window.CAPTIONS = {"dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E01 - The Cat and The Claw, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.836 --\u003e 00:00:04.838\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:49.026 --\u003e 00:01:50.319\r\n(LOUD SNORES)\r\n\r\n00:02:13.216 --\u003e 00:02:15.260\r\nNow, Isis, my sweet.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.347 --\u003e 00:02:19.348\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.712 --\u003e 00:02:52.255\r\nPerfect, my love.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.339 --\u003e 00:02:53.465\r\nLet's go home.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.345 --\u003e 00:03:01.682\r\nSo, our new cat\r\nburglar is a woman.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.984 --\u003e 00:03:14.861\r\nHmm. Probably my imagination.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.986 --\u003e 00:03:16.238\r\nProbably not.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.613 --\u003e 00:03:17.864\r\n(YOWL5)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.990 --\u003e 00:03:20.117\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.372 --\u003e 00:03:26.998\r\nMagnificent.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.749 --\u003e 00:03:31.128\r\nI suggest you save the\r\nflattery for the judge.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.818 --\u003e 00:03:56.403\r\nSo long, Dark Knight.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.486 --\u003e 00:03:58.196\r\nBATMAN: Drop in anytime.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.280 --\u003e 00:03:59.281\r\n(YOWL5)\r\n\r\n00:04:05.328 --\u003e 00:04:06.788\r\nYou're too kind.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.274 --\u003e 00:04:35.275\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:04:41.948 --\u003e 00:04:42.949\r\n(HISSES)\r\n\r\n00:04:44.326 --\u003e 00:04:45.452\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:04:47.204 --\u003e 00:04:49.414\r\nI'll have to try and\r\ntrim those claws.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.543 --\u003e 00:04:54.544\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:03.261 --\u003e 00:05:05.514\r\n- (TIRES SCREECH)\r\n- (YOWLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:06.431 --\u003e 00:05:07.641\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:05:15.023 --\u003e 00:05:16.650\r\nLeft you behind, did she?\r\n\r\n00:05:21.112 --\u003e 00:05:22.113\r\n(INAUDIBLE)\r\n\r\n00:05:24.783 --\u003e 00:05:25.909\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:05:46.137 --\u003e 00:05:47.138\r\n(WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:05:51.393 --\u003e 00:05:53.019\r\nThanks for the memento.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.276 --\u003e 00:06:01.111\r\n\u003ci\u003eNext,\r\nwe'll be auctioning off a date\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:01.319 --\u003e 00:06:03.321\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith Gotham's most\r\neligible bachelor,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:03.572 --\u003e 00:06:05.615\r\n- Mr. Bruce Wayne!\r\n- (CROWD MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:06:05.699 --\u003e 00:06:08.368\r\n\u003ci\u003eUh, if Mr. Wayne would be\r\ngood enough to step up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:09.119 --\u003e 00:06:10.871\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow, now, don't be shy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:10.954 --\u003e 00:06:12.497\r\n\u003ci\u003eAh, there he is.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:17.168 --\u003e 00:06:19.546\r\n- Oh, Bruce!\r\n- I'm so happy to see you.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.629 --\u003e 00:06:20.797\r\nWhere've you been?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.881 --\u003e 00:06:22.924\r\n- You look handsome.\r\n- You look wonderful.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.300 --\u003e 00:06:24.926\r\nOoh! Have I missed you.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.093 --\u003e 00:06:27.095\r\nI've been pinching\r\nmy pennies for you.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.178 --\u003e 00:06:30.223\r\nUh... Excuse me, ladies.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.473 --\u003e 00:06:32.851\r\n\u003ci\u003eRemember,\r\nwe've got lots of animals to save,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:32.976 --\u003e 00:06:36.730\r\n\u003ci\u003eso we're going to start\r\nthe bidding at $500.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:36.813 --\u003e 00:06:39.024\r\n- Five hundred.\r\n- Six hundred.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.357 --\u003e 00:06:41.067\r\nWe have six. Do I hear seven?\r\n\r\n00:06:41.151 --\u003e 00:06:42.402\r\n- Seven hundred.\r\n- Eight.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.485 --\u003e 00:06:43.695\r\nOne thousand.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.279 --\u003e 00:06:45.488\r\nWell, well.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.572 --\u003e 00:06:47.449\r\nThat's 1,000.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.532 --\u003e 00:06:49.701\r\nGoing once, going twice...\r\n\r\n00:06:49.826 --\u003e 00:06:51.536\r\nSELINA: $10,000.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.745 --\u003e 00:06:52.871\r\n(PEOPLE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:06:55.081 --\u003e 00:06:56.166\r\n(CROWD WHISPERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:01.254 --\u003e 00:07:02.923\r\n\u003ci\u003eUh, do I hear any more bids?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:03.214 --\u003e 00:07:06.843\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen sold, for $10,000, to...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:07.510 --\u003e 00:07:09.471\r\n\u003ci\u003eMs. Selina Kyle.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:09.888 --\u003e 00:07:10.889\r\nOh, wow.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.306 --\u003e 00:07:13.642\r\nI've never seen her before.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.059 --\u003e 00:07:16.353\r\nRumor has it she's\r\na wildlife nut.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.478 --\u003e 00:07:20.523\r\nShe's supposed to be sponsoring a\r\nmountain lion preserve outside Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.110 --\u003e 00:07:26.905\r\nIt's a pleasure.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.030 --\u003e 00:07:28.198\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.615 --\u003e 00:07:29.616\r\n(WOMAN CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:07:30.116 --\u003e 00:07:32.327\r\nUh, Mr. Wayne,\r\nmy secretary, Maven.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.786 --\u003e 00:07:33.828\r\nHow do you do?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.912 --\u003e 00:07:36.831\r\nUh... Please. \"Bruce.\"\r\n\r\n00:07:36.915 --\u003e 00:07:38.583\r\nI'm very flattered.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.584 --\u003e 00:07:42.629\r\nPlease understand,\r\nit's purely for the animals, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.754 --\u003e 00:07:43.755\r\nYou're off the hook.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.089 --\u003e 00:07:45.340\r\nBut you're not.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.507 --\u003e 00:07:46.675\r\nI beg your pardon?\r\n\r\n00:07:49.886 --\u003e 00:07:51.096\r\nYou bought a date,\r\n\r\n00:07:51.179 --\u003e 00:07:54.265\r\nand I'm honor-bound,\r\nand delighted to deliver.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.391 --\u003e 00:07:56.726\r\nI warn you,\r\nI'm not a man who gives up easily.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.810 --\u003e 00:07:58.812\r\nAll right. Lunch, then.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.937 --\u003e 00:08:00.021\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:00.313 --\u003e 00:08:01.523\r\n(POLICE SIRENS BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.986 --\u003e 00:08:07.404\r\nI wonder what's going on.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.487 --\u003e 00:08:09.030\r\nOh! Where'd he go?\r\n\r\n00:08:50.196 --\u003e 00:08:51.197\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:15.055 --\u003e 00:09:16.264\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.652 --\u003e 00:09:31.863\r\nWatch yourselves, men.\r\nThese guys are crazy.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.534 --\u003e 00:09:38.661\r\n- Thanks, friend.\r\n- BATMAN: What's going down?\r\n\r\n00:09:38.787 --\u003e 00:09:40.872\r\nThis morning,\r\nI get a warning from the Feds.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.247 --\u003e 00:09:42.749\r\nRed Claw is in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.832 --\u003e 00:09:43.833\r\nNow, this.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.958 --\u003e 00:09:45.710\r\n- Any leads?\r\n- Nothing.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.794 --\u003e 00:09:49.005\r\nRed Claw is the most ruthless\r\nterrorist leader in the world.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.380 --\u003e 00:09:51.100\r\nAnd we don't even have\r\na picture of the guy.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.174 --\u003e 00:09:52.926\r\nI'll see what I\r\ncan do from my end.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.596 --\u003e 00:09:58.598\r\nGood. There's no telling\r\nwhat they're up to.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.973 --\u003e 00:10:01.351\r\nNothing is safe with\r\nthese savages in town.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.072 --\u003e 00:10:16.324\r\nAren't you even a little\r\nexcited about your date?\r\n\r\n00:10:16.699 --\u003e 00:10:20.078\r\nI mean, Bruce Wayne is tall,\r\ndark and disgustingly rich.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.537 --\u003e 00:10:22.247\r\nI'd rather it were Batman.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.580 --\u003e 00:10:23.581\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:10:23.665 --\u003e 00:10:25.166\r\nYou should have seen him, Maven.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.583 --\u003e 00:10:27.252\r\nHe had the eyes of a lion.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.294 --\u003e 00:10:29.337\r\n(DOORBELL BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:10:33.216 --\u003e 00:10:34.509\r\nYes?\r\n\r\n00:10:34.592 --\u003e 00:10:36.192\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: A Mr. Bruce Wayne\r\nis on his way up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:36.261 --\u003e 00:10:37.428\r\nHere we go.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.679 --\u003e 00:10:38.763\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:10:40.140 --\u003e 00:10:42.684\r\n\u003ci\u003eCome on, Senna,\r\nat mast he's a good connection.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:42.809 --\u003e 00:10:44.435\r\nYou might be able to use him.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.480 --\u003e 00:10:50.191\r\n- Hello?\r\n- SELINA: Yes, I know.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.441 --\u003e 00:10:51.985\r\nI suppose you're right.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.153 --\u003e 00:10:56.030\r\nStill, I wish it were Batman\r\nstanding behind this door.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.828 --\u003e 00:11:03.621\r\nBruce, how wonderful to see you.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.746 --\u003e 00:11:04.789\r\nPlease, come in.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.332 --\u003e 00:11:08.543\r\nYou're even more\r\nstunning than I remember.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.668 --\u003e 00:11:10.461\r\nI'll just put these\r\nin some water.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.628 --\u003e 00:11:12.046\r\nSelina, it's your lawyer.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.338 --\u003e 00:11:13.923\r\nHe says the deal is off.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.007 --\u003e 00:11:15.008\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.509 --\u003e 00:11:17.677\r\nGive me that.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.760 --\u003e 00:11:19.012\r\nMartin, what happened?\r\n\r\n00:11:20.805 --\u003e 00:11:23.308\r\nThat's ridiculous.\r\nYou tell him I want to meet with him!\r\n\r\n00:11:23.975 --\u003e 00:11:27.437\r\nNo, today! He can't sell to Multigon!\r\nWe had an agreement!\r\n\r\n00:11:27.520 --\u003e 00:11:30.356\r\n- Uh, nice flowers.\r\n- What's going on?\r\n\r\n00:11:30.440 --\u003e 00:11:33.735\r\nSelina was negotiating for\r\nland for a wildlife preserve.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.860 --\u003e 00:11:36.446\r\nSome cartel just muscled\r\nher out of the deal.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.571 --\u003e 00:11:38.465\r\nSELINA: What do you mean\r\nhe won't take your calls?\r\n\r\n00:11:38.489 --\u003e 00:11:40.575\r\nYou go there,\r\nand kick down the door if you have to!\r\n\r\n00:11:40.700 --\u003e 00:11:43.328\r\nI want that land for\r\nthe mountain lions.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.788 --\u003e 00:11:46.789\r\n(SIGHS WEARILY)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.875 --\u003e 00:11:51.002\r\nI'm afraid I'm not going\r\nto be very good company.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.336 --\u003e 00:11:53.421\r\n- Is there anything I can do?\r\n- Not really.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.546 --\u003e 00:11:54.773\r\nUnless you can get me a meeting\r\n\r\n00:11:54.797 --\u003e 00:11:56.591\r\nwith the chairman of\r\nMultigon International.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.928 --\u003e 00:12:01.095\r\nWhat time's good for you?\r\n\r\n00:12:03.223 --\u003e 00:12:06.100\r\nHey,\r\nI'm starting to like this guy.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.946 --\u003e 00:12:19.864\r\nReally, Wayne,\r\nI do wish there was something\r\n\r\n00:12:19.948 --\u003e 00:12:21.588\r\nI could do for you and\r\nyour lovely friend,\r\n\r\n00:12:21.616 --\u003e 00:12:23.243\r\nbut the deal is quite set.\r\n\r\n00:12:23.910 --\u003e 00:12:25.745\r\n(PLAYING TUNE)\r\n\r\n00:12:31.334 --\u003e 00:12:33.878\r\nYou see, we're committed\r\nto building a major resort.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.295 --\u003e 00:12:36.214\r\nGolf course, tennis courts,\r\n\r\n00:12:36.297 --\u003e 00:12:38.466\r\nbocce ball, the whole shot.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.549 --\u003e 00:12:39.759\r\nThafsinsane!\r\n\r\n00:12:39.842 --\u003e 00:12:43.471\r\nThe land is in the middle of nowhere.\r\nIt's worthless except to wildcats.\r\n\r\n00:12:45.932 --\u003e 00:12:50.144\r\nMy dear, you just don't\r\nunderstand development potential.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.395 --\u003e 00:12:51.396\r\nAs for the cats,\r\n\r\n00:12:51.646 --\u003e 00:12:53.398\r\nMultigon will take care of them.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.856 --\u003e 00:12:55.316\r\nOne way or another.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.441 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nNow, if you'll excuse me,\r\n\r\n00:12:57.235 --\u003e 00:12:59.070\r\nI've given you all\r\nthe time I can spare.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.153 --\u003e 00:13:02.615\r\nOh, you'll find more time for\r\nme, Mr. Stern!\r\n\r\n00:13:03.074 --\u003e 00:13:05.743\r\nBefore I'm through,\r\nI'll have every environmental group\r\n\r\n00:13:05.827 --\u003e 00:13:08.204\r\nand animal rights activist\r\nbreathing down your neck.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.329 --\u003e 00:13:11.582\r\nThey'll be looking at you,\r\nand your project, so closely,\r\n\r\n00:13:11.916 --\u003e 00:13:14.127\r\nyou'll feel like a\r\nbug in a bell jar.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.589 --\u003e 00:13:19.882\r\nHave a nice day.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.693 --\u003e 00:13:41.571\r\nI'm afraid that Selina\r\nKyle may be trouble.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.696 --\u003e 00:13:45.033\r\nWe've come too far to\r\nhave our plans jeopardized\r\n\r\n00:13:45.116 --\u003e 00:13:47.243\r\nby some environmental fanatic.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.577 --\u003e 00:13:50.747\r\nHave someone keep an eye on Ms.\r\nKyle.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.085 --\u003e 00:13:58.629\r\nI'm afraid I wasn't\r\nmuch help after all.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.047 --\u003e 00:14:01.549\r\nWell, at least now I know\r\nwhat their cover story is.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.722 --\u003e 00:14:09.432\r\nYou know,\r\nit's awfully late for lunch.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.557 --\u003e 00:14:11.768\r\nWould you mind if I took\r\na rain check on our date?\r\n\r\n00:14:14.562 --\u003e 00:14:15.563\r\nPlease?\r\n\r\n00:14:19.025 --\u003e 00:14:20.026\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.568 --\u003e 00:14:22.153\r\n- Tomorrow?\r\n- Thanks.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.695 --\u003e 00:14:25.323\r\nThat'll give me time to take\r\ncare of some business tonight.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.406 --\u003e 00:14:28.701\r\nActually,\r\nI plan to work late myself.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.119 --\u003e 00:14:31.537\r\nAnd so, boys,\r\n\r\n00:14:32.121 --\u003e 00:14:35.249\r\nwe got to increase our cut\r\nin the gambling operations.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.001 --\u003e 00:14:38.669\r\nAnybody got a problem with that?\r\n\r\n00:14:40.004 --\u003e 00:14:41.005\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:48.471 --\u003e 00:14:49.472\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:51.057 --\u003e 00:14:52.266\r\nBack off, boys.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.642 --\u003e 00:14:54.102\r\nI want a word with your boss.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.769 --\u003e 00:14:55.853\r\nBut you can listen.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.145 --\u003e 00:14:57.355\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:14:57.438 --\u003e 00:14:59.107\r\nWhat do you know about Red Claw?\r\n\r\n00:14:59.232 --\u003e 00:15:01.442\r\nWhy are you asking us?\r\nWe're no terrorists.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.567 --\u003e 00:15:03.569\r\nYou're still scum.\r\n\r\n00:15:03.778 --\u003e 00:15:05.488\r\nAnd you hear things I don't.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.613 --\u003e 00:15:07.448\r\nI want Red Claw.\r\n\r\n00:15:07.740 --\u003e 00:15:09.283\r\nAnd until I get him,\r\n\r\n00:15:09.367 --\u003e 00:15:13.204\r\nI'm going to lean extra hard on\r\nyou, and all the other mob bosses.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.913 --\u003e 00:15:17.250\r\nIf you think I've been\r\nbad news before...\r\n\r\n00:15:17.875 --\u003e 00:15:20.378\r\nI get the picture.\r\nI'll see what I can do.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.684 --\u003e 00:15:36.310\r\nIf Stern won't admit\r\nwhat's going on,\r\n\r\n00:15:36.686 --\u003e 00:15:38.438\r\nwe'll have to find\r\nout for ourselves.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.906 --\u003e 00:15:51.075\r\nDespite our loss of arms,\r\n\r\n00:15:51.159 --\u003e 00:15:53.828\r\nthanks to Batman's interference,\r\n\r\n00:15:53.911 --\u003e 00:15:56.664\r\nwe're going to proceed\r\naccording to plan.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.457 --\u003e 00:15:58.541\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:16:04.964 --\u003e 00:16:07.800\r\nTomorrow at 2300 hours,\r\n\r\n00:16:07.925 --\u003e 00:16:11.345\r\na train under military escort\r\nwill pass through Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.429 --\u003e 00:16:14.891\r\nIt will be transporting\r\na strain of viral plague\r\n\r\n00:16:14.974 --\u003e 00:16:18.561\r\nthat Interpol confiscated\r\nfrom our eastern laboratories.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.686 --\u003e 00:16:22.899\r\nI cannot overemphasize the importance\r\nof that plague to our cause.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.319 --\u003e 00:16:27.320\r\nCATWOMAN: All clear?\r\n\r\n00:16:27.987 --\u003e 00:16:29.155\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.868 --\u003e 00:16:37.038\r\nI believe Beethoven's Ode\r\nto Joy will do the trick.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.830 --\u003e 00:16:40.041\r\n(PLAYING TUNE)\r\n\r\n00:16:46.380 --\u003e 00:16:49.133\r\nRemind me to thank Mama\r\nfor the piano lessons.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.718 --\u003e 00:16:52.094\r\n(CONTINUES PLAYING TUNE)\r\n\r\n00:16:53.429 --\u003e 00:16:54.430\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.892 --\u003e 00:16:58.893\r\n(YOWL5)\r\n\r\n00:16:58.976 --\u003e 00:17:00.811\r\nOutstanding.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.818 --\u003e 00:17:11.614\r\nWe'll hit the train outside the\r\ncity, at this point.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.948 --\u003e 00:17:12.949\r\n(ALARMS BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.496 --\u003e 00:17:19.497\r\nWhat is that?\r\n\r\n00:17:19.580 --\u003e 00:17:23.125\r\nA cat at the end\r\nof its nine lives.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.168 --\u003e 00:17:25.586\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.688 --\u003e 00:17:44.772\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.774 --\u003e 00:17:48.317\r\nAll right, I'm done.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.526 --\u003e 00:17:49.652\r\n(DOOR RATTLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:05.835 --\u003e 00:18:07.795\r\nShe's in the ventilation system.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.718 --\u003e 00:18:15.720\r\nI think we're in over our heads.\r\n\r\n00:18:32.820 --\u003e 00:18:33.821\r\nOw! Ow; OW!\r\n\r\n00:18:35.531 --\u003e 00:18:36.532\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:18:49.503 --\u003e 00:18:50.630\r\n(MEOWS LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.255 --\u003e 00:18:52.256\r\nCATWOMAN: Detour.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.716 --\u003e 00:18:54.967\r\nTHUG: She's down here! Hurry!\r\n\r\n00:19:03.267 --\u003e 00:19:04.352\r\nGoing UP-\r\n\r\n00:19:30.753 --\u003e 00:19:32.004\r\nHang on, Isis.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.226 --\u003e 00:19:46.310\r\nIsis, jump!\r\n\r\n00:19:54.193 --\u003e 00:19:55.444\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:02.284 --\u003e 00:20:03.285\r\nMy hero.\r\n\r\n00:20:14.505 --\u003e 00:20:16.048\r\nThat was for saving my cat.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.382 --\u003e 00:20:17.925\r\nIs that all it was for?\r\n\r\n00:20:18.008 --\u003e 00:20:20.344\r\n- Maybe not.\r\n- I heard gunfire.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.428 --\u003e 00:20:22.138\r\nOccupational hazard.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.305 --\u003e 00:20:24.306\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.390 --\u003e 00:20:25.641\r\nLet's keep the mystery.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.933 --\u003e 00:20:28.686\r\nIf I don't unmask\r\nyou, the police will.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.769 --\u003e 00:20:29.854\r\nPolice?\r\n\r\n00:20:29.937 --\u003e 00:20:31.105\r\nDon't be silly.\r\n\r\n00:20:31.939 --\u003e 00:20:33.983\r\nYou can't deny there's\r\nsomething between us.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.108 --\u003e 00:20:35.192\r\nYou're right.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.735 --\u003e 00:20:37.570\r\nAnd I'm afraid it's the law.\r\n\r\n00:20:41.991 --\u003e 00:20:43.075\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.709 --\u003e 00:20:54.253\r\nNever trifle with the\r\naffections of a woman.\r\n\r\n00:20:54.378 --\u003e 00:20:55.921\r\nUntil next time.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.301 --\u003e 00:21:02.720\r\nAnd there will be a next time.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.223 --\u003e 00:21:07.224\r\n(RUSTLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:14.440 --\u003e 00:21:16.358\r\nOh. Tough night?\r\n\r\n00:21:16.442 --\u003e 00:21:17.943\r\nIt had its ups and downs.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.360 --\u003e 00:21:21.447\r\nBut I did get pictures of\r\nthe fun family-resort site.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.781 --\u003e 00:21:23.141\r\nIt looks like\r\nthere's some kind of\r\n\r\n00:21:23.199 --\u003e 00:21:26.118\r\nabandoned military\r\nfacility, underground.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.452 --\u003e 00:21:27.953\r\nVery interesting.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.245 --\u003e 00:21:30.456\r\n(OVER HEADPHONES) We may save\r\nthose mountain lions yet.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.754 --\u003e 00:21:39.882\r\nBut who is going to save you?\r\n\r\n00:21:54.772 --\u003e 00:21:56.774\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.006 --\u003e 00:22:22.007\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E02 - On Leather Wings (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.757 --\u003e 00:00:09.676\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:26.295 --\u003e 00:01:28.255\r\nPILOT: \u003ci\u003eThis is Gotham\r\nAir One reporting in.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:28.589 --\u003e 00:01:30.048\r\nThings are actually\r\nquiet, for once.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.760 --\u003e 00:01:34.970\r\n- You see that?\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:01:35.304 --\u003e 00:01:38.140\r\nI had a blip.\r\nIt just ghosted across my screen.\r\n\r\n00:01:38.599 --\u003e 00:01:40.392\r\n- I don't see anything.\r\n- It was there.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.976 --\u003e 00:01:42.616\r\nWhatever it is,\r\nit must be right below us.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.354 --\u003e 00:01:45.856\r\n- There it is.\r\n- There what is?\r\n\r\n00:01:46.315 --\u003e 00:01:48.525\r\nIt looked like bat wings.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.109 --\u003e 00:01:50.193\r\nBat wings?\r\n\r\n00:01:50.444 --\u003e 00:01:53.238\r\nOkay, take us up through those\r\nclouds, just in case.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.455 --\u003e 00:02:02.664\r\nSorry, kid.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.998 --\u003e 00:02:04.249\r\nThere's nothing up here.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.625 --\u003e 00:02:05.876\r\nI swear, I saw it.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.376 --\u003e 00:02:08.253\r\nSomething was flying\r\naround up here.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.694 --\u003e 00:02:34.294\r\nNIGHT WATCHMAN: Testing,\r\none, two, three.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.780 --\u003e 00:02:36.156\r\nTesting, one, two, three.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.490 --\u003e 00:02:38.116\r\nYou, too, can fulfill the dream\r\n\r\n00:02:38.283 --\u003e 00:02:39.826\r\nof being a high-paid\r\nradio personality\r\n\r\n00:02:40.118 --\u003e 00:02:41.787\r\nin your spare\r\ntime, just like me.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.496 --\u003e 00:02:43.497\r\nJust call...\r\n\r\n00:02:43.830 --\u003e 00:02:44.873\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:02:45.082 --\u003e 00:02:47.417\r\nJust call the Gotham\r\nInstitute of Broadcast Arts.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.876 --\u003e 00:02:49.396\r\nYeah, that's better.\r\nCall the Gotham...\r\n\r\n00:02:49.586 --\u003e 00:02:50.671\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:05.519 --\u003e 00:03:06.770\r\n(EXHALES DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:03:14.277 --\u003e 00:03:15.821\r\n(YELPS) Get away!\r\n\r\n00:03:15.904 --\u003e 00:03:17.698\r\n(CREATURE GROWLING) {YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:31.169 --\u003e 00:03:32.212\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:44.725 --\u003e 00:03:46.805\r\nGORDON: I didn't authorize\r\nthis statement, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.977 --\u003e 00:03:48.228\r\nCome on, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.437 --\u003e 00:03:50.355\r\nSomebody asked me a\r\ncouple of questions.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.897 --\u003e 00:03:52.691\r\nI just gave them a\r\ncouple of answers.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.400 --\u003e 00:03:54.985\r\nYou gave them\r\nwithout my approval.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.652 --\u003e 00:03:58.132\r\nIf you'd kept quiet,\r\nhe wouldn't know we're moving against him.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.447 --\u003e 00:03:59.448\r\nI'll find him.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.614 --\u003e 00:04:01.575\r\nI just need a little extra\r\nhelp, Your Honor.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:03.076\r\nWhat kind of help?\r\n\r\n00:04:03.243 --\u003e 00:04:04.363\r\nI want my own tactical squad\r\n\r\n00:04:04.786 --\u003e 00:04:07.664\r\nfor the sole purpose of\r\nthrowing a net over this Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.039 --\u003e 00:04:10.625\r\n- Commissioner?\r\n- I've already denied the request.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.126 --\u003e 00:04:13.587\r\nNobody's taking a vigilante\r\nforce onto my streets.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.129 --\u003e 00:04:16.673\r\nYour Honor, any nutcase\r\nthat dresses up like a bat,\r\n\r\n00:04:17.048 --\u003e 00:04:18.508\r\nsooner or later is gonna snap.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.967 --\u003e 00:04:20.719\r\nListen,\r\nit's just not Batman's M.O.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.219 --\u003e 00:04:23.779\r\nOh, yeah? Tell that to the guy he\r\njust tossed through the window.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.431 --\u003e 00:04:26.271\r\nI think we could spare a few\r\nmen, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.850 --\u003e 00:04:29.352\r\nDetective Bullock does have a\r\nreputation for getting results.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.853 --\u003e 00:04:31.521\r\nI'm authorizing\r\nthe strike force.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.022 --\u003e 00:04:33.106\r\nAnything else, Detective?\r\n\r\n00:04:33.315 --\u003e 00:04:36.193\r\nJust make sure the D.A.'s office\r\ncan give me an airtight case, sir.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.651 --\u003e 00:04:38.028\r\nIf you catch him, Harvey,\r\n\r\n00:04:38.111 --\u003e 00:04:39.571\r\nI'll put him in jail for you.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.455 --\u003e 00:04:50.415\r\nBATMAN: \"Gotham police\r\ndeclare war on Batman\"?\r\n\r\n00:04:50.749 --\u003e 00:04:51.909\r\nI gather you've been reading.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.042 --\u003e 00:04:54.085\r\n\u003ci\u003eHow to Make Friends\r\nand Influence People.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:55.962 --\u003e 00:04:57.130\r\nSomebody's setting me up.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.214 --\u003e 00:04:58.381\r\nMy heavens.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.882 --\u003e 00:04:59.966\r\nYou mean, it wasn't you\r\n\r\n00:05:00.133 --\u003e 00:05:01.802\r\ntossing guards out of\r\nwindows last night?\r\n\r\n00:05:02.344 --\u003e 00:05:04.137\r\nI only toss butlers, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.387 --\u003e 00:05:06.556\r\nLook here.\r\nThere were two very quiet burglaries\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.652\r\nat other pharmaceutical\r\ncompanies this week.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.975 --\u003e 00:05:10.101\r\nNobody hurt like last night,\r\n\r\n00:05:11.019 --\u003e 00:05:12.938\r\nbut chemicals stolen\r\njust the same.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.355 --\u003e 00:05:14.773\r\nAnd you suspect a pattern?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.190 --\u003e 00:05:16.650\r\nOnly one way to find out.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.192 --\u003e 00:05:19.361\r\nI'll cancel Master\r\nBruce's rendezvous with\r\n\r\n00:05:19.778 --\u003e 00:05:21.196\r\nBambi, was it, sir?\r\n\r\n00:05:21.530 --\u003e 00:05:22.989\r\nYes, Alfred, do that.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.882 --\u003e 00:06:23.174\r\nCome here, you.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.509 --\u003e 00:06:25.510\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:06:27.345 --\u003e 00:06:29.180\r\n- He's back.\r\n- I'll call the police.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.819 --\u003e 00:06:43.904\r\n(SNIFFS)\r\n\r\n00:06:43.987 --\u003e 00:06:45.280\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n- (BOOK CLATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:06:52.662 --\u003e 00:06:54.015\r\n\u003ci\u003eDISPATCH: (ON RADIO)\r\nCalling Detective Bullock.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:54.039 --\u003e 00:06:55.123\r\n\u003ci\u003eCalling Detective Bullock.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:55.832 --\u003e 00:06:56.833\r\nYeah?\r\n\r\n00:06:56.917 --\u003e 00:06:59.127\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Batman's been sighted\r\nbreaking into Phoenix labs.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:59.461 --\u003e 00:07:00.629\r\nThought \u003ci\u003eyou'd\u003c/i\u003e be interested.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.046 --\u003e 00:07:03.340\r\nI want my squad there,\r\nbacked by choppers\r\n\r\n00:07:03.590 --\u003e 00:07:06.343\r\nand as many officers\r\nas you can get now.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.306 --\u003e 00:07:12.474\r\nYou're mine.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.438 --\u003e 00:07:19.814\r\n(SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:03.483 --\u003e 00:08:05.002\r\nNIGHT WATCHMAN: (ON\r\nTAPE) Call the Gotham...\r\n\r\n00:08:05.026 --\u003e 00:08:06.611\r\n(NIGHT WATCHMAN SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.947 --\u003e 00:08:10.365\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:13.660 --\u003e 00:08:15.161\r\n(CAMERA CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:22.293 --\u003e 00:08:23.461\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:35.849 --\u003e 00:08:37.308\r\n(SOLDIERS CHANTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:40.520 --\u003e 00:08:42.355\r\nBULLOCK: All right,\r\nyou jokers, pipe down!\r\n\r\n00:08:43.273 --\u003e 00:08:44.315\r\nHe's in there.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.524 --\u003e 00:08:46.192\r\nI want him by any\r\nmeans necessary.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.749 --\u003e 00:09:02.542\r\nCommissioner,\r\nyou're just in time\r\n\r\n00:09:02.876 --\u003e 00:09:04.627\r\nto see us hang this\r\nbat upside down.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.213 --\u003e 00:09:08.214\r\nYou sure he's in there?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.757 --\u003e 00:09:11.092\r\nThe chopper pilots just spotted\r\nhim on the fourth floor.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.634 --\u003e 00:09:13.234\r\nWell, he can't be in\r\ntwo places at once.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.762 --\u003e 00:09:16.431\r\nAnother pharmaceutical factory\r\nwas just robbed across town.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.890 --\u003e 00:09:18.975\r\n- You've got the wrong suspect.\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:09:29.110 --\u003e 00:09:30.111\r\nThere!\r\n\r\n00:09:35.617 --\u003e 00:09:36.761\r\n- Gas attack.\r\n- (ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:36.785 --\u003e 00:09:38.495\r\nPut on your masks.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.670 --\u003e 00:09:49.005\r\nHey, there he is.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.757 --\u003e 00:09:51.841\r\n(GUNFIRE)\r\n\r\n00:09:52.550 --\u003e 00:09:54.594\r\nWell, somebody's in\r\nthere, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.886 --\u003e 00:09:56.638\r\nCall them off,\r\nBullock, or I will.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.310 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.395 --\u003e 00:10:05.438\r\n(SHUSHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:09.025 --\u003e 00:10:11.194\r\nThe Bat's got to be in there, sir.\r\nWhat do you think?\r\n\r\n00:10:15.782 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\n- Tear gas?\r\n- We'll smoke him out.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.451 --\u003e 00:10:20.578\r\nOkay, men,\r\nready with your masks.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.032 --\u003e 00:10:59.450\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:01.786 --\u003e 00:11:04.455\r\n\u003ci\u003eANNOUNCER: The Gotham Zoo tour\r\ntram departs in five minutes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:06.583 --\u003e 00:11:07.792\r\n\u003ci\u003eAdventures in Chiroptery,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:08.042 --\u003e 00:11:10.044\r\n\u003ci\u003eat the Bat Exhibit,\r\nwill begin in 30 minutes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:18.386 --\u003e 00:11:19.596\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:11:20.013 --\u003e 00:11:21.055\r\nAnybody here?\r\n\r\n00:11:22.807 --\u003e 00:11:24.184\r\nDr. March?\r\n\r\n00:11:24.309 --\u003e 00:11:25.768\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:26.311 --\u003e 00:11:27.478\r\nDR. MARCH: Who is it?\r\n\r\n00:11:28.813 --\u003e 00:11:30.481\r\nBruce Wayne.\r\nI have an appointment.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.648 --\u003e 00:11:31.983\r\nI called about a bat problem.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.233 --\u003e 00:11:34.402\r\nWhat do you think we are?\r\nPest control?\r\n\r\n00:11:34.652 --\u003e 00:11:36.946\r\n- I just need...\r\n- Yes. Come in.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.697 --\u003e 00:11:39.032\r\nWhy, thank you, Doctor.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.490 --\u003e 00:11:41.910\r\nYou donate a few million,\r\nand you think you own the place.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.619 --\u003e 00:11:45.079\r\nI understand I'm to\r\nanalyze something for you.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.206 --\u003e 00:11:49.042\r\nYeah, Doc.\r\nI keep hearing squeaks in my chimney\r\n\r\n00:11:49.500 --\u003e 00:11:51.100\r\nand I found these in\r\nmy empty fireplace.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.377 --\u003e 00:11:52.754\r\nThey look like hairs.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.004 --\u003e 00:11:55.465\r\nI thought maybe you could tell\r\nme if I have a bat problem.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.798 --\u003e 00:11:58.343\r\nAnd what if they are bats, Mr. Wayne?\r\nWhat then?\r\n\r\n00:11:58.676 --\u003e 00:12:00.428\r\nDestroy them like insects?\r\n\r\n00:12:00.803 --\u003e 00:12:03.306\r\nWe won't survive the next\r\nevolutionary cataclysm,\r\n\r\n00:12:03.556 --\u003e 00:12:04.807\r\nbut bats will.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:07.435\r\nThey're survivors,\r\nMr. Wayne, not pests.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.769 --\u003e 00:12:09.145\r\nYou should understand that.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.395 --\u003e 00:12:10.480\r\nWOMAN: Dad?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.231 --\u003e 00:12:13.983\r\nI hope Mr. Wayne understands\r\nyou mean no disrespect.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.317 --\u003e 00:12:16.569\r\nOf course not, Miss...\r\n\r\n00:12:17.195 --\u003e 00:12:19.113\r\nMrs. Actually, Doctor.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.530 --\u003e 00:12:20.615\r\nI'm Francine Langstrom.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.990 --\u003e 00:12:22.830\r\nI think you spoke with\r\nmy husband on the phone.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.244 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nOh, Mr. Wayne,\r\nI'm sorry I'm late.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.287 --\u003e 00:12:27.622\r\nI'm Kirk Langstrom.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.830 --\u003e 00:12:29.249\r\nDid you bring the sample?\r\n\r\n00:12:29.707 --\u003e 00:12:31.459\r\nI gave it to Dr. Mar...\r\n\r\n00:12:32.126 --\u003e 00:12:33.211\r\nWhere'd he go?\r\n\r\n00:12:33.378 --\u003e 00:12:35.004\r\nProbably to get started\r\non the analysis.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.338 --\u003e 00:12:37.882\r\nIf it's a bat problem,\r\nwe'll know by tonight.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.549 --\u003e 00:12:41.177\r\nDad was lecturing Mr. Wayne\r\non the virtues of chiroptera.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.844 --\u003e 00:12:43.096\r\nChiropt-a-what?\r\n\r\n00:12:43.388 --\u003e 00:12:44.597\r\nChiroptera. Bats.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.847 --\u003e 00:12:47.767\r\nAnd I hope he didn't\r\nget carried away?\r\n\r\n00:12:47.976 --\u003e 00:12:50.812\r\nHe's a little\r\nprotective of all this.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.396 --\u003e 00:12:54.065\r\nI think he likes bats\r\nbetter than people.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.565 --\u003e 00:12:55.817\r\nI can't imagine.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.025 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nI brought you this, too.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.402 --\u003e 00:12:59.487\r\nIt's a recording I made of\r\nthe noise in my chimney.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.821 --\u003e 00:13:01.406\r\n(SCREECHING ON TAPE)\r\n\r\n00:13:07.078 --\u003e 00:13:09.706\r\nThat doesn't sound like any\r\nbat I've ever heard, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:13:12.709 --\u003e 00:13:15.628\r\nThe animal-behavior people\r\nhave a sound library.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.004 --\u003e 00:13:17.130\r\nMaybe they can identify it.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.630 --\u003e 00:13:18.923\r\nWe'll let you know.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.340 --\u003e 00:13:20.675\r\nI'd appreciate it.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.095 --\u003e 00:13:25.847\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.850 --\u003e 00:13:32.437\r\nI didn't realize you'd taken up\r\nlistening to rock 'n' roll, sir.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.979 --\u003e 00:13:34.647\r\nYou know,\r\nI actually did check this\r\n\r\n00:13:34.981 --\u003e 00:13:36.316\r\nagainst any musical sounds.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.524 --\u003e 00:13:38.693\r\nComputer still can't come\r\nclose to pinpointing it.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.152 --\u003e 00:13:40.403\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:42.196 --\u003e 00:13:44.365\r\nWayne Manor. One moment, please.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.782 --\u003e 00:13:46.326\r\nA call for Master Bruce\r\n\r\n00:13:46.409 --\u003e 00:13:47.994\r\nfrom a Dr. March.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.163 --\u003e 00:13:51.372\r\nHey, what's up, Doc?\r\n\r\n00:13:51.581 --\u003e 00:13:52.915\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou have bats, Mr. Wayne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:53.082 --\u003e 00:13:54.292\r\n\u003ci\u003eCommon brown bats.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:54.542 --\u003e 00:13:55.877\r\nThey shouldn't pose a problem.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.085 --\u003e 00:13:57.805\r\nAs the weather gets\r\ncolder, they'll move on.\r\n\r\n00:13:58.129 --\u003e 00:13:59.505\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat about the\r\nsound on the tape?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:59.839 --\u003e 00:14:01.132\r\nIt's actually two sounds.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.299 --\u003e 00:14:02.717\r\nStarlings and brown bats.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.176 --\u003e 00:14:05.094\r\nProbably fighting over\r\na nest in your chimney.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:06.637\r\nAppreciate the help, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.929 --\u003e 00:14:09.390\r\nI'll return the favor next\r\ntime you're raising funds.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.557 --\u003e 00:14:10.683\r\nBye-bye.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.100 --\u003e 00:14:12.477\r\nThis computer checked that fiber\r\n\r\n00:14:12.810 --\u003e 00:14:14.854\r\nagainst every animal\r\nspecies known to man.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.938 --\u003e 00:14:18.658\r\nI went to them because I thought\r\nthey might know something we didn't.\r\n\r\n00:14:19.442 --\u003e 00:14:21.110\r\nThat hair wasn't a brown bat's.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.944 --\u003e 00:14:24.072\r\nAnd those melodic sounds?\r\n\r\n00:14:24.447 --\u003e 00:14:27.325\r\nComputer,\r\ncheck against combined sounds.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.658 --\u003e 00:14:29.327\r\nStarlings and brown bats.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.246 --\u003e 00:14:33.373\r\n\u003ci\u003eNegative.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:33.581 --\u003e 00:14:35.375\r\n\u003ci\u003eSounds not originated\r\nby either species.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:37.001 --\u003e 00:14:38.086\r\nI would say, sir,\r\n\r\n00:14:38.336 --\u003e 00:14:40.880\r\nthat we have ourselves\r\nan incongruity.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.172 --\u003e 00:14:42.465\r\nIncongruity, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:14:43.007 --\u003e 00:14:44.133\r\nHe's lying-\r\n\r\n00:14:44.384 --\u003e 00:14:46.135\r\nAnd I'm gonna find out why.\r\n\r\n00:15:10.034 --\u003e 00:15:11.285\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.252 --\u003e 00:15:20.420\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:15:21.337 --\u003e 00:15:23.464\r\nMAN: Can't fight it.\r\nIt's got me.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.678 --\u003e 00:15:29.679\r\n(CHOKES)\r\n\r\n00:15:34.100 --\u003e 00:15:35.476\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:54.829 --\u003e 00:15:55.872\r\nWho's back there?\r\n\r\n00:15:57.039 --\u003e 00:15:59.542\r\nYou! I'm looking for Dr. March.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.959 --\u003e 00:16:01.544\r\nHe's not here, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.213 --\u003e 00:16:05.214\r\nWhere is he?\r\n\r\n00:16:05.381 --\u003e 00:16:07.758\r\nGiving a lecture\r\non human extinction\r\n\r\n00:16:07.925 --\u003e 00:16:09.177\r\nand bat evolution.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.510 --\u003e 00:16:11.262\r\nHe's really quite brilliant.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.846 --\u003e 00:16:13.514\r\nHe's misguided and a thief.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.931 --\u003e 00:16:15.349\r\nHe's just a theorist.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.725 --\u003e 00:16:17.268\r\nHe was afraid to\r\nput it to the test.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.768 --\u003e 00:16:19.020\r\nBut I wasn't.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.520 --\u003e 00:16:21.230\r\nI knew we'd discovered a formula\r\n\r\n00:16:21.397 --\u003e 00:16:23.107\r\nto create a totally new species.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.566 --\u003e 00:16:24.942\r\nNeither man nor bat.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.276 --\u003e 00:16:26.861\r\nAnd once I started taking it,\r\n\r\n00:16:27.069 --\u003e 00:16:28.112\r\nI couldn't stop.\r\n\r\n00:16:28.362 --\u003e 00:16:29.864\r\nI desperately wanted to.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.156 --\u003e 00:16:32.241\r\nBut it took over.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.950 --\u003e 00:16:35.119\r\nFrancine and March\r\ntried to protect me,\r\n\r\n00:16:35.745 --\u003e 00:16:36.954\r\nbut it was too late.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.205 --\u003e 00:16:40.541\r\nThe beast knew what chemicals\r\nwere needed to bring itself about.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.000 --\u003e 00:16:42.502\r\nIt was out of my control.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.002 --\u003e 00:16:45.963\r\nAnd it only needs\r\none more component\r\n\r\n00:16:46.214 --\u003e 00:16:48.090\r\nto complete the process.\r\n\r\n00:16:48.799 --\u003e 00:16:50.510\r\nIt's in me,\r\n\r\n00:16:50.843 --\u003e 00:16:52.011\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.179 --\u003e 00:16:54.430\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:17:21.832 --\u003e 00:17:23.125\r\n(ROARS)\r\n\r\n00:17:44.647 --\u003e 00:17:45.731\r\nFRANCINE: Kirk!\r\n\r\n00:17:47.400 --\u003e 00:17:48.401\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:23.519 --\u003e 00:18:25.396\r\nI'm getting something strange.\r\n\r\n00:18:25.896 --\u003e 00:18:27.231\r\nOh, not again!\r\n\r\n00:18:27.565 --\u003e 00:18:29.567\r\nI'm serious.\r\nIt's right below us.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.611 --\u003e 00:18:33.112\r\n(GRUNTS) Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:18:33.571 --\u003e 00:18:35.323\r\nGotham Command,\r\nwe need choppers.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.656 --\u003e 00:18:37.116\r\nWe've sighted the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:55.509 --\u003e 00:18:57.428\r\n- Let's go!\r\n- I can't do it, sir.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.803 --\u003e 00:18:59.123\r\nWhat do you mean\r\nyou can't do it?\r\n\r\n00:18:59.388 --\u003e 00:19:02.016\r\nI just got word not to let you\r\nup without the Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.433 --\u003e 00:19:04.602\r\n- Who told you that?\r\n- The Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:19:05.186 --\u003e 00:19:06.479\r\nGORDON: Get out, Detective!\r\n\r\n00:19:07.813 --\u003e 00:19:09.482\r\nThe Mayor may not\r\nlet me fire you,\r\n\r\n00:19:09.815 --\u003e 00:19:11.942\r\nbut I am not taking the\r\nheat for your fiascoes.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.360 --\u003e 00:19:14.904\r\nThis is my case, Commissioner!\r\nYou heard the Mayor!\r\n\r\n00:19:15.071 --\u003e 00:19:17.156\r\nThen why don't you go\r\ntake it up with him?\r\n\r\n00:19:17.323 --\u003e 00:19:18.574\r\nI've got a job to do.\r\n\r\n00:19:18.866 --\u003e 00:19:20.910\r\nIf you want to tag along, fine!\r\n\r\n00:19:23.579 --\u003e 00:19:24.914\r\nTake her up, Lieutenant.\r\n\r\n00:19:26.582 --\u003e 00:19:27.917\r\nHey, wait for me!\r\n\r\n00:20:15.464 --\u003e 00:20:17.341\r\n- There he is.\r\n- GORDON: There they are.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.759 --\u003e 00:20:20.010\r\nWhat is that thing?\r\n\r\n00:20:20.302 --\u003e 00:20:21.721\r\nThat thing is what we're after.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.388 --\u003e 00:20:23.639\r\nHoly»-...\r\n\r\n00:20:58.007 --\u003e 00:20:59.216\r\nTwo for dinner, sir?\r\n\r\n00:20:59.508 --\u003e 00:21:02.386\r\nI got a list of all the items\r\nstolen from the chemical labs.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.220 --\u003e 00:21:06.015\r\nWho would have thought they'd\r\nbe used to create a monster?\r\n\r\n00:21:07.475 --\u003e 00:21:10.561\r\nMaybe I can undo the fate\r\nLangstrom has brought upon himself.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.732 --\u003e 00:21:16.734\r\nALFRED: Does it appear\r\nfeasible, sir?\r\n\r\n00:21:17.359 --\u003e 00:21:18.736\r\nI think so.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.209 --\u003e 00:21:34.335\r\nIs he all right?\r\n\r\n00:21:37.797 --\u003e 00:21:39.548\r\n- Will he change again?\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:21:40.132 --\u003e 00:21:41.509\r\nThe formula's out of his system.\r\n\r\n00:21:42.092 --\u003e 00:21:43.385\r\nIt's over...\r\n\r\n00:21:43.677 --\u003e 00:21:44.887\r\nfor now.\r\n\r\n00:21:58.275 --\u003e 00:22:00.402\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.048 --\u003e 00:22:22.049\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E03 - Heart of Ice (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.377 --\u003e 00:00:04.379\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:18.370 --\u003e 00:01:21.456\r\nFREEZE: This is how I'll\r\nalways remember you.\r\n\r\n00:01:21.873 --\u003e 00:01:23.208\r\nSurrounded by winter,\r\n\r\n00:01:23.542 --\u003e 00:01:24.835\r\nforever young,\r\n\r\n00:01:25.168 --\u003e 00:01:26.587\r\nforever beautiful.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.504 --\u003e 00:01:28.964\r\nRest well, my love.\r\n\r\n00:01:29.840 --\u003e 00:01:31.216\r\nThe monster who took you from me\r\n\r\n00:01:31.800 --\u003e 00:01:34.428\r\nwill soon learn that\r\nrevenge is a dish\r\n\r\n00:01:35.596 --\u003e 00:01:37.681\r\nbest served cold.\r\n\r\n00:01:38.098 --\u003e 00:01:40.434\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn the midst of the\r\nhottest August on record,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:40.726 --\u003e 00:01:43.395\r\n\u003ci\u003ea rash of bizarre\r\ncold-related crimes\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:43.729 --\u003e 00:01:45.230\r\n\u003ci\u003ehave chilled Gotham to the bone.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:45.689 --\u003e 00:01:48.567\r\n\u003ci\u003eOnce again,\r\nthe target is a GothCorp facility\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:49.026 --\u003e 00:01:50.235\r\nattacked by an assailant\r\n\r\n00:01:50.444 --\u003e 00:01:52.070\r\n\u003ci\u003ewielding what witnesses called\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:52.237 --\u003e 00:01:53.655\r\n\u003ci\u003ea \"freezing gun.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:54.448 --\u003e 00:01:56.867\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe attacker's motives\r\nremain unclear.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:57.326 --\u003e 00:01:58.327\r\nWe spoke earlier\r\n\r\n00:01:58.493 --\u003e 00:02:00.871\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith GothCorp CEO Ferris Boyle,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:01.121 --\u003e 00:02:02.497\r\n\u003ci\u003ewho offered these comments.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:03.123 --\u003e 00:02:05.709\r\n\u003ci\u003eI don't know what this\r\nperson has against GothCorp.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:06.084 --\u003e 00:02:07.919\r\nBut we've always\r\n\u003ci\u003elooked\u003c/i\u003e upon ourselves\r\n\r\n00:02:08.128 --\u003e 00:02:09.546\r\nas the people company.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.130 --\u003e 00:02:11.548\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf this man has a problem,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:11.882 --\u003e 00:02:13.216\r\n\u003ci\u003ewe're willing to listen.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:15.552 --\u003e 00:02:18.055\r\n\u003ci\u003eA heartfelt plea from the\r\nchairman of Goth Corp,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:18.388 --\u003e 00:02:19.556\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe people company.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:20.265 --\u003e 00:02:21.516\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Summer Gleeson\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:21.725 --\u003e 00:02:23.018\r\nfor Gotham Insider.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.810 --\u003e 00:02:25.410\r\n- (MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n- Hey, get out of here!\r\n\r\n00:02:38.492 --\u003e 00:02:40.535\r\nTaking up video\r\ngames, are we, sir?\r\n\r\n00:02:42.412 --\u003e 00:02:44.873\r\nI've accessed police files\r\non the GothCorp raids.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.540 --\u003e 00:02:46.875\r\nThese are the stolen objects.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.376 --\u003e 00:02:48.752\r\nThey don't look like much alone,\r\n\r\n00:02:49.211 --\u003e 00:02:50.545\r\nbut in this configuration...\r\n\r\n00:02:55.801 --\u003e 00:02:56.802\r\nMy word.\r\n\r\n00:02:57.511 --\u003e 00:02:59.471\r\nThey combine into\r\na massive weapon\r\n\r\n00:02:59.554 --\u003e 00:03:01.056\r\nable to generate intense cold.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.723 --\u003e 00:03:03.433\r\nThere's still one\r\ncomponent missing,\r\n\r\n00:03:03.809 --\u003e 00:03:05.435\r\nand only one GothCorp\r\nplant makes it.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.237 --\u003e 00:03:16.697\r\n\u003ci\u003eHalt. Stay where you are.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:18.615 --\u003e 00:03:19.895\r\n- (ALL SHOUTING)\r\n- MAN: Look out!\r\n\r\n00:03:33.422 --\u003e 00:03:35.048\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:41.555 --\u003e 00:03:42.639\r\nWe got company.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.265 --\u003e 00:03:45.058\r\nFREEZE: Keep your\r\nmind on your business.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.851 --\u003e 00:03:46.893\r\nI'll handle this.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.734 --\u003e 00:03:54.735\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:05.036 --\u003e 00:04:06.455\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:04:07.038 --\u003e 00:04:08.331\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:29.102 --\u003e 00:04:30.312\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:04:31.938 --\u003e 00:04:33.440\r\nLoad those canisters.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.065 --\u003e 00:04:35.108\r\nHurry.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.921 --\u003e 00:04:57.130\r\nAre you done?\r\n\r\n00:05:01.551 --\u003e 00:05:02.636\r\nAll set.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.886 --\u003e 00:05:03.887\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:05:03.970 --\u003e 00:05:05.472\r\n(GASPS) The Batman!\r\n\r\n00:05:06.389 --\u003e 00:05:08.183\r\nPut me down! (YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.393 --\u003e 00:05:11.394\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.271 --\u003e 00:05:14.314\r\nFreeze.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.106 --\u003e 00:05:17.484\r\nThat's \"Mr. Freeze\" to you.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.411 --\u003e 00:05:30.497\r\nThis is a personal vendetta.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.164 --\u003e 00:05:33.083\r\nIt doesn't concern you.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.625 --\u003e 00:05:35.001\r\nIt's my concern now.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.794 --\u003e 00:05:38.672\r\nSince you ally yourself\r\nwith my enemies,\r\n\r\n00:05:38.839 --\u003e 00:05:40.549\r\nyou leave me no choice.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.056 --\u003e 00:05:49.057\r\nAhhh!\r\n\r\n00:05:49.766 --\u003e 00:05:50.767\r\nJohnny!\r\n\r\n00:06:02.863 --\u003e 00:06:03.864\r\n(SHUDDERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:05.740 --\u003e 00:06:07.492\r\nTake it easy, man. I got you.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.784 --\u003e 00:06:08.869\r\nFREEZE: Leave him.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.455 --\u003e 00:06:14.708\r\nHe should have\r\nbeen more careful.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.375 --\u003e 00:06:16.877\r\nNow he's paid the price\r\n\r\n00:06:17.335 --\u003e 00:06:19.004\r\nfor his incompetence.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.921 --\u003e 00:06:20.922\r\nBut he's one of us.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.464 --\u003e 00:06:24.676\r\nThen perhaps you'd\r\nlike to share his fate.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.058 --\u003e 00:06:35.103\r\n(SOBS) Don't leave me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:06:44.613 --\u003e 00:06:46.072\r\nPlease! Come back!\r\n\r\n00:06:49.284 --\u003e 00:06:50.869\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:53.288 --\u003e 00:06:54.915\r\nMAN: Help! Please!\r\n\r\n00:06:56.249 --\u003e 00:06:57.250\r\nCold...\r\n\r\n00:06:57.542 --\u003e 00:06:59.544\r\nSo cold.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.488 --\u003e 00:07:27.614\r\nI must say, you're showing\r\n\r\n00:07:27.989 --\u003e 00:07:30.575\r\na surprising amount of\r\ncompassion for that man\r\n\r\n00:07:31.201 --\u003e 00:07:33.203\r\nconsidering he would\r\nsurely have left you\r\n\r\n00:07:33.286 --\u003e 00:07:34.537\r\nto die in his place.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.621 --\u003e 00:07:36.331\r\n- (CRACKLING)\r\n- (WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:07:43.380 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(POWERING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:07:45.799 --\u003e 00:07:46.800\r\n(SNIFFLES)\r\n\r\n00:07:47.926 --\u003e 00:07:49.678\r\nWith all the compartments\r\non your belt,\r\n\r\n00:07:49.928 --\u003e 00:07:51.448\r\nyou'd think there'd\r\nbe one for tissues.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.348 --\u003e 00:07:55.392\r\n(SNIFFS) Thanks.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.767 --\u003e 00:07:57.602\r\n- (BLOWS NOSE)\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:08:07.654 --\u003e 00:08:08.738\r\nHe's pulling through.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.030 --\u003e 00:08:10.573\r\nThe hot chemical\r\nbath did the trick.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.907 --\u003e 00:08:12.117\r\n(SNEEZES LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:08:13.159 --\u003e 00:08:14.911\r\nYou could use a\r\nhot bath yourself.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.537 --\u003e 00:08:16.538\r\n(SNIFFS)\r\n\r\n00:08:16.955 --\u003e 00:08:18.456\r\nI can't worry about a cold now.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.915 --\u003e 00:08:20.583\r\nAfter Batman drops\r\nour unconscious guest\r\n\r\n00:08:21.001 --\u003e 00:08:22.794\r\nat police headquarters...\r\n(COUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:08:23.211 --\u003e 00:08:24.371\r\n\u003ci\u003eBruce Wayne has got a meeting\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:24.546 --\u003e 00:08:26.381\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith Mr. Ferris Boyle.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:27.215 --\u003e 00:08:28.216\r\nBruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.466 --\u003e 00:08:30.051\r\nIt's been forever.\r\nHow have you been?\r\n\r\n00:08:30.510 --\u003e 00:08:32.387\r\nStill the terror of\r\nthe Gotham night scene?\r\n\r\n00:08:33.054 --\u003e 00:08:34.097\r\n(BRUCE COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:35.306 --\u003e 00:08:36.433\r\nI get around.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.851 --\u003e 00:08:38.852\r\nSpeaking of terror,\r\n\r\n00:08:39.060 --\u003e 00:08:41.896\r\nwhat's this about someone\r\ncausing trouble for GothCorp?\r\n\r\n00:08:42.272 --\u003e 00:08:43.273\r\nYou got me.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.732 --\u003e 00:08:45.400\r\nSome fruitcake has it\r\nout for my company.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.692 --\u003e 00:08:46.860\r\nI don't know why.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.318 --\u003e 00:08:48.798\r\nMaybe it's an investor\r\nwho lost money.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:49.946\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:50.447 --\u003e 00:08:51.698\r\nOr an angry ex-employee.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.073 --\u003e 00:08:53.353\r\nThere's only one man who'd hate.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.408 --\u003e 00:08:54.659\r\nGothCorp that much,\r\n\r\n00:08:54.993 --\u003e 00:08:55.994\r\nif he were alive.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.494 --\u003e 00:08:58.621\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of our scientists.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.955 --\u003e 00:09:00.206\r\nAn obsessed wacko.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.415 --\u003e 00:09:01.958\r\nHe was caught using\r\ncompany equipment\r\n\r\n00:09:02.208 --\u003e 00:09:03.251\r\nfor personal reasons.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.668 --\u003e 00:09:05.086\r\nI had to send my\r\nsecurity men in.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.295 --\u003e 00:09:07.047\r\nThere was a fight, an explosion.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.547 --\u003e 00:09:08.673\r\nWe lost him.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.299 --\u003e 00:09:10.467\r\nWhat was he doing?\r\n\r\n00:09:10.717 --\u003e 00:09:12.343\r\nWasting company money.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.677 --\u003e 00:09:13.762\r\nMy money!\r\n\r\n00:09:14.012 --\u003e 00:09:15.180\r\nLook, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.388 --\u003e 00:09:17.849\r\nThat \"people company\"\r\nline is great PR.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.058 --\u003e 00:09:19.059\r\nBut when the wage-slaves\r\n\r\n00:09:19.225 --\u003e 00:09:20.705\r\nstart acting like\r\nthey own the place,\r\n\r\n00:09:20.769 --\u003e 00:09:21.895\r\nit's time to pull the plug.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.062 --\u003e 00:09:23.582\r\n- Know what I mean?\r\n- (INTERCOM BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.772 --\u003e 00:09:26.232\r\n\u003ci\u003eSECRETARY: Sir,\r\nthe humanitarian committee is here.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:27.150 --\u003e 00:09:28.276\r\nI'll be right out.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.568 --\u003e 00:09:29.848\r\nWe're hosting a ceremony tonight\r\n\r\n00:09:30.195 --\u003e 00:09:32.530\r\nfor Gotham's Humanitarian\r\nindustrialist of the Year.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.281 --\u003e 00:09:34.407\r\nGuess who's winning?\r\n\r\n00:09:34.991 --\u003e 00:09:36.409\r\nI feel ill.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.868 --\u003e 00:09:37.952\r\nHmm?\r\n\r\n00:09:39.370 --\u003e 00:09:41.372\r\nExcuse me, Ferris. My cold.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.083 --\u003e 00:09:44.751\r\nCongratulations on your award.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.126 --\u003e 00:09:46.753\r\nI'm sure it's well-deserved.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.842 --\u003e 00:09:54.385\r\n\u003ci\u003eFERRIS: And I want\r\nto say that these\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:54.636 --\u003e 00:09:56.805\r\n\u003ci\u003eunwarranted attacks\r\nagainst GothCorp\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:57.013 --\u003e 00:09:58.014\r\n\u003ci\u003ehave in no way changed\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:58.264 --\u003e 00:10:00.100\r\n\u003ci\u003eour personal commitment\r\nto the community.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:00.683 --\u003e 00:10:01.935\r\n\u003ci\u003eInspirational words\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:02.268 --\u003e 00:10:04.896\r\n\u003ci\u003efrom Gotham's Humanitarian\r\nindustrialist of the Year.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:07.398 --\u003e 00:10:08.483\r\nFREEZE: Humanity.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.317 --\u003e 00:10:10.485\r\nCompassion.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.152 --\u003e 00:10:12.403\r\nCharity.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.862 --\u003e 00:10:14.823\r\nWhere were those pretty words\r\n\r\n00:10:15.031 --\u003e 00:10:16.699\r\nwhen she needed to hear them?\r\n\r\n00:10:24.165 --\u003e 00:10:25.333\r\nFaster.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.875 --\u003e 00:10:27.836\r\nThe cannon must be\r\ncompleted tonight.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.711 --\u003e 00:10:31.089\r\nI have my own warm wishes\r\n\r\n00:10:31.297 --\u003e 00:10:33.341\r\nto bestow on Mr. Boyle.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.263 --\u003e 00:10:40.023\r\nBATMAN: When Ferris\r\nmentioned that explosion,\r\n\r\n00:10:40.473 --\u003e 00:10:42.113\r\nI remembered this\r\nheadline from last year.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.559 --\u003e 00:10:44.561\r\nDoes it say what\r\ncaused the accident?\r\n\r\n00:10:46.771 --\u003e 00:10:47.772\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.981 --\u003e 00:10:49.901\r\nAnd I suspect that's the\r\nreason for the cover-up.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.525 --\u003e 00:10:53.778\r\nI won't know for sure until I\r\ncheck GothCorp's classified files.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.362 --\u003e 00:10:55.363\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:55.655 --\u003e 00:10:57.240\r\nIf you're going to\r\ngo sneaking around\r\n\r\n00:10:57.365 --\u003e 00:10:59.200\r\na crowded office building,\r\nyou'll need this.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.869 --\u003e 00:11:01.953\r\nKnockout gas?\r\n\r\n00:11:02.120 --\u003e 00:11:03.204\r\nChicken soup.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.288 --\u003e 00:11:04.664\r\nThe only way to fight a cold.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.747 --\u003e 00:11:06.749\r\n(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:11:10.128 --\u003e 00:11:11.171\r\n(GUARD SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:16.551 --\u003e 00:11:17.594\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.802 --\u003e 00:11:19.262\r\nMr. Boyle sent me to fill in.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.596 --\u003e 00:11:21.639\r\nEnjoy yourself at the\r\nparty, with his compliments.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.223 --\u003e 00:11:23.474\r\nHey, great.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.808 --\u003e 00:11:24.851\r\n(SNEEZES)\r\n\r\n00:11:25.059 --\u003e 00:11:27.687\r\n- You okay?\r\n- I'm fine. Take off.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.479 --\u003e 00:11:29.731\r\n(HUMMING HAPPILY)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.578 --\u003e 00:11:44.579\r\n(LOCK CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.580 --\u003e 00:12:29.415\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy name is Dr. Victor Fries.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:30.375 --\u003e 00:12:32.335\r\n\u003ci\u003eI am recording what I pray\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:32.502 --\u003e 00:12:34.712\r\n\u003ci\u003ewill be mankind's first\r\nstep toward immortality.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:36.422 --\u003e 00:12:38.591\r\n\u003ci\u003eBehind me you see the CC-100...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:39.550 --\u003e 00:12:41.719\r\n\u003ci\u003eA cryogenic freezing\r\nchamber of my own design.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:42.095 --\u003e 00:12:44.639\r\n\u003ci\u003eI created it for the express\r\npurpose of freezing subjects\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:44.722 --\u003e 00:12:46.766\r\n\u003ci\u003estricken with\r\ninoperable ailments.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:47.183 --\u003e 00:12:48.184\r\n\u003ci\u003eSubjects like\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:48.601 --\u003e 00:12:50.103\r\n\u003ci\u003emy own beloved wife, Nora.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:50.645 --\u003e 00:12:51.747\r\n\u003ci\u003eOnce a remedy has been found...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:51.771 --\u003e 00:12:52.939\r\n(KNOB RATTLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:53.231 --\u003e 00:12:54.983\r\n\u003ci\u003eFERRIS: Open this door!\r\nOpen it now!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:59.570 --\u003e 00:13:00.730\r\n\u003ci\u003eGet away from that equipment!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:01.197 --\u003e 00:13:02.282\r\n\u003ci\u003eShut this stuff down.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:02.615 --\u003e 00:13:05.076\r\n\u003ci\u003eStop! This is my experiment!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:05.326 --\u003e 00:13:07.036\r\n\u003ci\u003eYour unauthorized experiment.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:07.245 --\u003e 00:13:09.622\r\n\u003ci\u003eI ordered funding\r\nsuspended weeks ago.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:10.164 --\u003e 00:13:12.500\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm already three million in\r\ndebt, thanks to you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:13.167 --\u003e 00:13:14.335\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou can't stop it now.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:14.794 --\u003e 00:13:15.920\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy wife is in there.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:16.212 --\u003e 00:13:17.505\r\n\u003ci\u003eSo bring her out.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:18.047 --\u003e 00:13:20.008\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou can't interrupt\r\nthe process now.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:20.466 --\u003e 00:13:21.467\r\n\u003ci\u003eOpen it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:21.759 --\u003e 00:13:23.094\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's her only chance.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:23.678 --\u003e 00:13:25.638\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is my equipment! Mine!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:26.097 --\u003e 00:13:27.265\r\n\u003ci\u003eI have every legal right\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:27.515 --\u003e 00:13:29.684\r\n\u003ci\u003eto use it or not\r\nuse it as I see fit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:29.934 --\u003e 00:13:32.061\r\n\u003ci\u003eI say this project ends now!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:34.647 --\u003e 00:13:35.648\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:35.982 --\u003e 00:13:37.942\r\n\u003ci\u003eStay away from her, murderer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:38.234 --\u003e 00:13:39.235\r\n\u003ci\u003eVictor...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:39.652 --\u003e 00:13:40.987\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm sorry.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:41.654 --\u003e 00:13:42.822\r\n\u003ci\u003eI lost my temper.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:43.114 --\u003e 00:13:44.407\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt doesn't have to come to this.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:44.741 --\u003e 00:13:45.908\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe can talk.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:47.201 --\u003e 00:13:48.202\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:48.536 --\u003e 00:13:49.537\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:13:50.663 --\u003e 00:13:52.040\r\n\u003ci\u003eGet out! Get out!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:54.500 --\u003e 00:13:55.710\r\n\u003ci\u003eNora!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:56.502 --\u003e 00:13:57.670\r\n\u003ci\u003eNora!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:59.839 --\u003e 00:14:00.923\r\nMy God.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.008 --\u003e 00:14:03.009\r\nFREEZE: Yes...\r\n\r\n00:14:03.509 --\u003e 00:14:05.094\r\nIt would move me to tears\r\n\r\n00:14:05.470 --\u003e 00:14:08.222\r\nif I still had tears to shed.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.989 --\u003e 00:14:27.533\r\nThe snow is beautiful,\r\ndon't you think?\r\n\r\n00:14:28.326 --\u003e 00:14:30.495\r\nClean, uncompromising...\r\n\r\n00:14:31.621 --\u003e 00:14:32.705\r\nAnd cold.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.373 --\u003e 00:14:36.501\r\nLike the swift\r\nhand of vengeance.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.502 --\u003e 00:14:39.420\r\nI saw what happened\r\nto your wife.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.213 --\u003e 00:14:41.214\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.173 --\u003e 00:14:44.509\r\nI'm beyond emotions.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.801 --\u003e 00:14:47.428\r\nThey've been frozen dead in me.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.262 --\u003e 00:14:49.597\r\nThat suit you wear...\r\n\r\n00:14:49.889 --\u003e 00:14:51.057\r\nA result of the coolant?\r\n\r\n00:14:51.557 --\u003e 00:14:52.809\r\nVery good.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.142 --\u003e 00:14:55.311\r\nA detective to the last.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.853 --\u003e 00:14:57.730\r\nI can no longer survive\r\n\r\n00:14:58.231 --\u003e 00:15:00.525\r\nout of a sub-zero environment.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.442 --\u003e 00:15:03.361\r\nTonight, I mean to pay back\r\n\r\n00:15:03.569 --\u003e 00:15:05.613\r\nthe man who ruined my life.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.197 --\u003e 00:15:07.532\r\nOur lives.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.533 --\u003e 00:15:09.617\r\nEven if you have to kill\r\n\r\n00:15:09.826 --\u003e 00:15:11.327\r\neveryone in the\r\nbuilding to do it?\r\n\r\n00:15:13.996 --\u003e 00:15:15.331\r\nThink of it, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.290 --\u003e 00:15:18.584\r\nTo never again walk\r\non a summer's day\r\n\r\n00:15:18.918 --\u003e 00:15:20.962\r\nwith a hot wind in your face\r\n\r\n00:15:21.170 --\u003e 00:15:23.131\r\nand a warm hand to hold.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.756 --\u003e 00:15:25.007\r\nOh, yes.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.591 --\u003e 00:15:27.885\r\nI'd kill for that.\r\n\r\n00:15:32.849 --\u003e 00:15:33.850\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.559 --\u003e 00:15:36.394\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:24.692 --\u003e 00:16:25.693\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:16:32.617 --\u003e 00:16:33.618\r\nKeys?\r\n\r\n00:16:37.997 --\u003e 00:16:39.332\r\nSeal the building.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.292 --\u003e 00:16:42.752\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:17:10.947 --\u003e 00:17:12.240\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.782 --\u003e 00:17:14.075\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:17:15.660 --\u003e 00:17:16.661\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:25.628 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\nHigher. Higher.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.130 --\u003e 00:17:30.550\r\nLet the evil that walks inside\r\n\r\n00:17:30.716 --\u003e 00:17:33.970\r\nbe cleansed by pure,\r\nunforgiving ice.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.598 --\u003e 00:17:39.850\r\nAnd so it gives\r\nme great pleasure\r\n\r\n00:17:39.934 --\u003e 00:17:42.436\r\nto present this\r\nwell-deserved award to...\r\n\r\n00:17:42.728 --\u003e 00:17:44.230\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.232 --\u003e 00:17:47.233\r\n(wmn WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:47.984 --\u003e 00:17:48.985\r\n(PEOPLE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:52.572 --\u003e 00:17:53.781\r\nDouble the power.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.450 --\u003e 00:17:57.577\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:17:59.704 --\u003e 00:18:00.705\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:19.140 --\u003e 00:18:20.141\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.018 --\u003e 00:18:23.477\r\nI will finish this.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.040 --\u003e 00:18:45.499\r\n(PANICKED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:18:54.550 --\u003e 00:18:56.427\r\nThe cold eyes of vengeance\r\n\r\n00:18:56.552 --\u003e 00:18:58.471\r\nare upon you, Boyle.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.263 --\u003e 00:19:00.264\r\nWho...\r\n\r\n00:19:00.473 --\u003e 00:19:01.682\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:02.350 --\u003e 00:19:03.434\r\nCome, now.\r\n\r\n00:19:03.976 --\u003e 00:19:05.394\r\nSurely you remember\r\n\r\n00:19:05.645 --\u003e 00:19:06.854\r\nyour old colleague\r\n\r\n00:19:07.521 --\u003e 00:19:08.522\r\nVictor Fries.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.067 --\u003e 00:19:12.068\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:12.777 --\u003e 00:19:13.778\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:15.988 --\u003e 00:19:18.032\r\nStop. Please.\r\n\r\n00:19:19.367 --\u003e 00:19:20.409\r\nI beg you.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.077 --\u003e 00:19:22.828\r\nYOU beg?\r\n\r\n00:19:23.663 --\u003e 00:19:24.914\r\nIn my nightmares,\r\n\r\n00:19:24.997 --\u003e 00:19:26.957\r\nI see my Nora behind the glass,\r\n\r\n00:19:28.084 --\u003e 00:19:31.212\r\nbegging to me with frozen eyes.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.712 --\u003e 00:19:33.339\r\nHow I've longed to see\r\n\r\n00:19:33.422 --\u003e 00:19:35.549\r\nthat look frozen on you.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.232 --\u003e 00:19:53.818\r\nThe advanced circuitry\r\nthat powers my suit\r\n\r\n00:19:53.984 --\u003e 00:19:56.070\r\nalso triples my strength.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.412 --\u003e 00:20:07.415\r\nSooner or later,\r\nall who stand in my way\r\n\r\n00:20:08.165 --\u003e 00:20:11.043\r\nmust feel the icy\r\ntouch of death.\r\n\r\n00:20:11.919 --\u003e 00:20:12.920\r\n(BATMAN STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:20:16.632 --\u003e 00:20:17.633\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:31.439 --\u003e 00:20:33.774\r\nUgh. What was that stuff?\r\n\r\n00:20:34.567 --\u003e 00:20:35.985\r\nThe only way to fight a cold.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.569 --\u003e 00:20:39.363\r\n(DISTORTED) It\r\ncan't end this way.\r\n\r\n00:20:39.822 --\u003e 00:20:41.240\r\nVengeance...\r\n\r\n00:20:42.992 --\u003e 00:20:43.993\r\nBATMAN: No.\r\n\r\n00:20:44.201 --\u003e 00:20:45.244\r\nJustice.\r\n\r\n00:20:45.494 --\u003e 00:20:47.872\r\nA year ago, Ferris Boyle\r\ninterrupted an experiment,\r\n\r\n00:20:48.539 --\u003e 00:20:50.583\r\nand in the process\r\ndestroyed two lives.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.000 --\u003e 00:20:52.418\r\nHere's the evidence.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.132 --\u003e 00:21:00.593\r\nGood night, humanitarian.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.106 --\u003e 00:21:15.566\r\nI failed you.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.817 --\u003e 00:21:19.487\r\nI wish there were another\r\nway for me to say it.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.113 --\u003e 00:21:22.156\r\nBut I cannot.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.531 --\u003e 00:21:25.201\r\nI can only beg your forgiveness\r\n\r\n00:21:25.993 --\u003e 00:21:28.245\r\nand pray you hear me somehow...\r\n\r\n00:21:29.079 --\u003e 00:21:30.247\r\nSomeplace...\r\n\r\n00:21:30.998 --\u003e 00:21:33.793\r\nSomeplace where a warm hand\r\n\r\n00:21:34.084 --\u003e 00:21:35.127\r\nwaits for mine.\r\n\r\n00:22:00.194 --\u003e 00:22:02.196\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.257 --\u003e 00:22:22.258\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E04 - Feat of Clay, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.628 --\u003e 00:00:04.630\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:57.242 --\u003e 00:01:59.828\r\nBruce? Bruce Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:02:00.412 --\u003e 00:02:01.913\r\nMAN: Over here, Lucius.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.542 --\u003e 00:02:08.128\r\nBruce, it's 3:00 in the morning.\r\nCouldn't this wait?\r\n\r\n00:02:08.837 --\u003e 00:02:11.006\r\nI could've given you\r\nthis stuff in the office.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.089 --\u003e 00:02:12.341\r\n(SHUSHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:13.508 --\u003e 00:02:14.551\r\nNot out here.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.055 --\u003e 00:02:19.097\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.440 --\u003e 00:02:31.943\r\nMy phones are bugged.\r\nThe office, the house, everywhere.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.695 --\u003e 00:02:35.197\r\nHe knows we're on to him.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.822 --\u003e 00:02:36.823\r\nLUCIUS: Daggett?\r\n\r\n00:02:39.076 --\u003e 00:02:42.537\r\nWho else? You were the one who said he\r\nwas trying to take over the company.\r\n\r\n00:02:43.121 --\u003e 00:02:45.415\r\nYes. Insider trading.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.750 --\u003e 00:02:49.711\r\nBut once you give these papers to the\r\nDA, he'll be under indictment\r\n\r\n00:02:49.836 --\u003e 00:02:51.630\r\nbefore he can change his socks.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.880 --\u003e 00:02:54.675\r\nIf I turn in the evidence.\r\nBut I won't.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.758 --\u003e 00:02:55.801\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:56.009 --\u003e 00:02:59.304\r\nYou see, Lucius, the reason I want\r\nthose papers is to destroy them.\r\n\r\n00:02:59.388 --\u003e 00:03:00.514\r\n(GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:03:00.597 --\u003e 00:03:03.892\r\nAnd now, that you've brought them,\r\nwe won't be needing you anymore.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.476 --\u003e 00:03:07.479\r\nBruce, what's going on here?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.604 --\u003e 00:03:13.360\r\nLet's just say I'm accepting\r\nyour resignation, Mr. Fox.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.488 --\u003e 00:03:19.991\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:28.709 --\u003e 00:03:30.168\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:03:33.588 --\u003e 00:03:34.798\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.759 --\u003e 00:03:39.886\r\nVOICE \u003ci\u003eON POLICE\u003c/i\u003e RADIO: \u003ci\u003eTwo-Baker-six.\r\nTwo-Baker-six.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:40.053 --\u003e 00:03:42.139\r\n\u003ci\u003e204 at Gotham Island Tramway,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:42.305 --\u003e 00:03:44.933\r\n\u003ci\u003esouth-side terminal.\r\nRespond, code 2.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:46.893 --\u003e 00:03:48.145\r\nLet's finish this.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:49.354\r\nFast.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.438 --\u003e 00:03:51.273\r\nBefore we have the\r\nlaw on our necks.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.398 --\u003e 00:03:53.233\r\nBATMAN: Too late, dirtbag.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.316 --\u003e 00:03:54.359\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:03:54.443 --\u003e 00:03:55.444\r\nWho said that?\r\n\r\n00:03:56.111 --\u003e 00:03:58.321\r\nThe Batman! Not him!\r\n\r\n00:04:04.286 --\u003e 00:04:05.287\r\nWhere is he?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.334 --\u003e 00:04:15.756\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:27.601 --\u003e 00:04:28.894\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:02.636 --\u003e 00:05:03.887\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:14.189 --\u003e 00:05:16.024\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:17.317 --\u003e 00:05:18.610\r\n(SHOUTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:18.693 --\u003e 00:05:20.070\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.669 --\u003e 00:05:38.672\r\nWayne. Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.422 --\u003e 00:05:41.049\r\nHe set me up.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.592 --\u003e 00:05:43.593\r\nCover me!\r\n\r\n00:05:52.477 --\u003e 00:05:54.104\r\nCOP: Stay where you are!\r\nDon't move!\r\n\r\n00:06:26.261 --\u003e 00:06:27.429\r\nReady on the set.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.973 --\u003e 00:06:31.349\r\nI'll go get Matt.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:45.196\r\nCome on, come on. Where are you?\r\n\r\n00:06:47.324 --\u003e 00:06:49.409\r\nTEDDY: Matt, uh,\r\nyou okay in there?\r\n\r\n00:06:49.701 --\u003e 00:06:52.454\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:53.872 --\u003e 00:06:54.873\r\nMatt?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.707 --\u003e 00:06:56.958\r\nHAGEN: Close the door!\r\n\r\n00:06:57.751 --\u003e 00:06:59.294\r\nIt's Teddy, Matt.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.295 --\u003e 00:07:01.880\r\nHAGEN: Close the door!\r\n\r\n00:07:02.839 --\u003e 00:07:03.840\r\nHelp me look.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.924 --\u003e 00:07:05.634\r\nIt's gotta be in here somewhere.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.468 --\u003e 00:07:09.471\r\nThe face cream?\r\nYou used up your last jar yesterday.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.804 --\u003e 00:07:10.805\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:07:11.097 --\u003e 00:07:13.350\r\nI gotta have more! Now, see.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.516 --\u003e 00:07:17.062\r\nIt wore off. Look!\r\nI can't fix it anymore!\r\n\r\n00:07:17.604 --\u003e 00:07:18.897\r\nRelax, Matt.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.022 --\u003e 00:07:20.899\r\nDon't tell me to\r\nrelax, you idiot!\r\n\r\n00:07:21.274 --\u003e 00:07:23.068\r\nI can't go out there like this!\r\n\r\n00:07:24.152 --\u003e 00:07:25.153\r\nHere.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.363 --\u003e 00:07:27.614\r\nGive it to me!\r\n\r\n00:07:28.531 --\u003e 00:07:30.408\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:07:32.494 --\u003e 00:07:34.371\r\nHuh? That's all?\r\n\r\n00:07:35.413 --\u003e 00:07:37.874\r\nI was lucky I could\r\nhang on to that much.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.918 --\u003e 00:07:41.419\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:41.503 --\u003e 00:07:43.046\r\nYou were holding out on me?\r\n\r\n00:07:43.129 --\u003e 00:07:46.299\r\nI had to, Matt.\r\nIf I didn't, you wouldn't have any now.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.300 --\u003e 00:07:48.301\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:53.765 --\u003e 00:07:57.727\r\nYou can't go on like this, Matt.\r\nYou hurt all the time now.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.936 --\u003e 00:07:59.729\r\nYou're just my stand-in.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.854 --\u003e 00:08:02.148\r\nNobody promoted\r\nyou to nursemaid.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.524 --\u003e 00:08:04.901\r\nThat stuff makes your\r\nface like putty, Matt.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.985 --\u003e 00:08:06.111\r\nIt can't be good for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.611 --\u003e 00:08:08.363\r\nIt probably ain't good for me.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.613 --\u003e 00:08:10.824\r\nBut unless I only wanna\r\ndo horror pictures,\r\n\r\n00:08:10.949 --\u003e 00:08:13.159\r\nit ain't bad for me either.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.786 --\u003e 00:08:15.787\r\nGone!\r\n\r\n00:08:16.121 --\u003e 00:08:17.122\r\nEmpty!\r\n\r\n00:08:17.664 --\u003e 00:08:19.499\r\nOnly 24 hours,\r\n\r\n00:08:19.582 --\u003e 00:08:22.669\r\nthen it starts all over again.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.752 --\u003e 00:08:24.295\r\n(KNOCKING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:08:24.379 --\u003e 00:08:26.381\r\nMAN: Mr. Hagen, we're waiting!\r\n\r\n00:08:26.756 --\u003e 00:08:27.757\r\nKeep your shirt on!\r\n\r\n00:08:30.093 --\u003e 00:08:31.803\r\nThat's what ain't good for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.928 --\u003e 00:08:34.931\r\nHaving to keep going back to\r\nDaggett for more of that stuff,\r\n\r\n00:08:35.056 --\u003e 00:08:37.600\r\nand do whatever lousy\r\nthing he wants to get it.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.810 --\u003e 00:08:41.104\r\nYou're right, Teddy. I can't.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.479 --\u003e 00:08:45.900\r\nI'll have to find a way to get\r\nlots of this stuff on my own.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.661 --\u003e 00:08:57.954\r\nDAGGETT: You're sure, Bell?\r\n\r\n00:08:58.163 --\u003e 00:08:59.914\r\n(POLICE RADIO CHATTER\r\nON HEADPHONES)\r\n\r\n00:08:59.998 --\u003e 00:09:03.543\r\nYou're sure that the man you hired\r\nknows nothing about our operation?\r\n\r\n00:09:07.630 --\u003e 00:09:09.674\r\nBell! I asked you a question.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.092 --\u003e 00:09:13.303\r\nBell! Bell!\r\n\r\n00:09:18.475 --\u003e 00:09:20.477\r\nGerms, take off his headphones.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.312 --\u003e 00:09:24.564\r\nPay attention.\r\nMr. Daggett is talking to you.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.647 --\u003e 00:09:28.693\r\n(CHATTER CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.236 --\u003e 00:09:31.237\r\nNow, then.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.321 --\u003e 00:09:32.989\r\nRelax, Mr. Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.073 --\u003e 00:09:36.284\r\nThe guy was just a hired gun.\r\nHe don't even know our names.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.785 --\u003e 00:09:39.120\r\nThank heaven for small favors.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.747 --\u003e 00:09:44.584\r\nBut Hagen has disappointed\r\nme once too often lately.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.085 --\u003e 00:09:47.295\r\nHe botched this\r\nassignment completely.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:51.966\r\nTo wit, once Fox is able to talk,\r\nhe might very well incriminate us,\r\n\r\n00:09:52.050 --\u003e 00:09:55.637\r\nif the police can't figure out\r\nwhat we're up to from those papers.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.762 --\u003e 00:09:58.139\r\nHagen was supposed to retrieve.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.141 --\u003e 00:10:01.142\r\nFrankly,\r\n\r\n00:10:02.018 --\u003e 00:10:05.313\r\nI think our Mr. Hagen has\r\noutlived his usefulness.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.147 --\u003e 00:10:08.817\r\nI want him dealt with.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.317 --\u003e 00:10:12.237\r\nBut, Mr. Daggett,\r\nthe man's a master of disguise.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.570 --\u003e 00:10:16.407\r\nHe was even before he had his\r\naccident, and you gave him this stuff.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.491 --\u003e 00:10:20.411\r\nYeah. It's not easy finding somebody\r\nwho can change the way he looks.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.912 --\u003e 00:10:22.372\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:22.455 --\u003e 00:10:25.083\r\nYou needn't bother\r\nsearching for him.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.667 --\u003e 00:10:29.337\r\nThis is the only place in the world\r\nwhere he can get what he needs.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.796 --\u003e 00:10:31.881\r\nAnd when his supply runs out,\r\n\r\n00:10:32.382 --\u003e 00:10:34.467\r\nhe'll come to us.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.972 --\u003e 00:10:41.432\r\n(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:42.767 --\u003e 00:10:45.770\r\n(SNORING)\r\n\r\n00:11:02.704 --\u003e 00:11:04.164\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.878 --\u003e 00:11:11.045\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:11:11.504 --\u003e 00:11:13.381\r\nBELL: Hold it right there.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.299 --\u003e 00:11:16.259\r\nTurn around, real slow.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.676 --\u003e 00:11:19.012\r\nStep into the light\r\nwhere we can see you.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.680 --\u003e 00:11:22.432\r\nI'm looking for Mr. Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.599 --\u003e 00:11:23.808\r\nI don't believe we've met.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.892 --\u003e 00:11:27.061\r\nMy name is Wayne. Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.192 --\u003e 00:11:35.361\r\nWayne, huh? Yeah, right. Sure.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.196 --\u003e 00:11:37.238\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:37.322 --\u003e 00:11:39.574\r\nCan the garbage, Hagen.\r\nWe ain't stupid.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.366 --\u003e 00:11:41.826\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:42.535 --\u003e 00:11:43.703\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.499 --\u003e 00:11:50.668\r\n- No!\r\n- You're Hagen, all right.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.752 --\u003e 00:11:53.046\r\nBroke in for more of that\r\nstuff, didn't you?\r\n\r\n00:11:53.171 --\u003e 00:11:56.799\r\nYeah, once they're\r\nhooked, they stay hooked.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.759 --\u003e 00:12:00.720\r\nCome on, Hagen,\r\nwe're going for a little ride.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.054 --\u003e 00:12:03.723\r\nForget it!\r\nI know what that means!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.151 --\u003e 00:12:17.278\r\nWait! I got an idea.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.737 --\u003e 00:12:18.738\r\nHold him.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.410 --\u003e 00:12:26.788\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:26.871 --\u003e 00:12:29.123\r\nPretty boy wanted\r\nmore of this stuff?\r\n\r\n00:12:29.457 --\u003e 00:12:31.167\r\nThen let's give it to him.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.251 --\u003e 00:12:33.169\r\nHAGEN: No! Not that way!\r\n\r\n00:12:33.378 --\u003e 00:12:34.712\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:12:35.421 --\u003e 00:12:38.132\r\nBELL: Let's give him\r\nall he'll ever need.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.216 --\u003e 00:12:39.217\r\nHAGEN: No!\r\n\r\n00:12:39.717 --\u003e 00:12:42.345\r\nNo! Don't!\r\n\r\n00:12:53.982 --\u003e 00:12:56.693\r\nSweet dreams, slimeball.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.902 --\u003e 00:13:01.322\r\n(HAGEN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:13:12.000 --\u003e 00:13:15.920\r\nBATMAN: I know my fist has\r\nlanded on that jaw once before.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.479 --\u003e 00:13:35.773\r\nBell. Raymond Bell.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.898 --\u003e 00:13:38.651\r\nOf course! Now I remember him.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.903 --\u003e 00:13:45.408\r\nCarries a pocket radio,\r\ntuned to police band at all times.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.702 --\u003e 00:13:50.121\r\nMaster Bruce,\r\nwhat am I to do about the police?\r\n\r\n00:13:50.246 --\u003e 00:13:51.956\r\nThey shall be back, you know.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.081 --\u003e 00:13:54.334\r\nI can't keep telling\r\nthem you're out.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.126 --\u003e 00:13:57.545\r\nPolice? What police?\r\n\r\n00:13:57.628 --\u003e 00:13:59.172\r\nWhat are you talking about?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.672 --\u003e 00:14:02.800\r\nI suggest you consult\r\nthe morning paper, sir.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.511 --\u003e 00:14:07.930\r\nBATMAN: \"Bruce Wayne\r\nsought for questioning\"\r\n\r\n00:14:08.014 --\u003e 00:14:10.224\r\n\"in attempt on\r\nexecutive's life\"?\r\n\r\n00:14:10.350 --\u003e 00:14:12.352\r\nBut that's impossible!\r\n\r\n00:14:15.605 --\u003e 00:14:19.400\r\nVOICE \u003ci\u003eON POLICE\u003c/i\u003e RADIO: \u003ci\u003eTwo-Baker-10,\r\ncode 7 in progress, 500 North Main.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:19.525 --\u003e 00:14:24.364\r\n\u003ci\u003eTwenty-two, code 4 at 1900 Roth\r\nAvenue, apartment B, \"boy.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:24.489 --\u003e 00:14:28.576\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll units, a warrant has been issued\r\nfor the arrest of Bell Raymond.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:28.910 --\u003e 00:14:31.788\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhite male,\r\napproximately 5 feet 10 inches.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:31.871 --\u003e 00:14:32.997\r\n\u003ci\u003eAge, mid-30s.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:34.415 --\u003e 00:14:37.752\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:46.761 --\u003e 00:14:50.264\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll available units divert to\r\nsuspect's last known address,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:50.390 --\u003e 00:14:54.185\r\n\u003ci\u003e3720 Burnley Boulevard.\r\nSuspect is believed...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:54.310 --\u003e 00:14:58.106\r\nArmed and dangerous.\r\nProceed with extreme caution. Over.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.981 --\u003e 00:15:00.817\r\nBELL: (CHUCKLES) Yeah, go ahead.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.192 --\u003e 00:15:02.902\r\nStake out my place.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.985 --\u003e 00:15:05.238\r\nIt'll be a long wait, jerks.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.750 --\u003e 00:15:22.213\r\nThat's it, Bell. Keep it up.\r\nYou're reacting true to form so far.\r\n\r\n00:15:43.234 --\u003e 00:15:45.778\r\n(GASPS) The Batman?\r\n\r\n00:15:47.905 --\u003e 00:15:51.200\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:57.373 --\u003e 00:16:00.293\r\nMade it! I am out of here!\r\n\r\n00:16:02.295 --\u003e 00:16:03.504\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:16:06.424 --\u003e 00:16:07.592\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:18.853 --\u003e 00:16:20.104\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:21.731 --\u003e 00:16:25.026\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.201 --\u003e 00:16:37.205\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:39.874 --\u003e 00:16:42.126\r\n(YELLS) No!\r\n\r\n00:16:42.793 --\u003e 00:16:44.587\r\n- (INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:45.546 --\u003e 00:16:46.797\r\nOh, no!\r\n\r\n00:16:46.881 --\u003e 00:16:49.175\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:11.489 --\u003e 00:17:13.866\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:24.710 --\u003e 00:17:25.711\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:26.254 --\u003e 00:17:30.800\r\nNo! For the love of mercy,\r\nBatman, don't let me fall!\r\n\r\n00:17:31.509 --\u003e 00:17:34.053\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.013 --\u003e 00:17:38.641\r\nWhat are you doing?\r\nAre you crazy?\r\n\r\n00:17:38.766 --\u003e 00:17:40.393\r\nListen up, scumwad.\r\n\r\n00:17:40.518 --\u003e 00:17:42.603\r\n\u003ci\u003e(AMPLIFIED) Because I'm\r\nonly gonna ask you once.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:49.652 --\u003e 00:17:51.237\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:52.655 --\u003e 00:17:55.283\r\n\u003ci\u003eWho was Lucius Fox\r\nmeeting at the tram?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:55.491 --\u003e 00:17:57.994\r\nWayne! Bruce Wayne!\r\n\r\n00:17:58.452 --\u003e 00:18:00.746\r\nYou lying sleaze!\r\n\r\n00:18:02.206 --\u003e 00:18:04.166\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou wanna rethink that answer?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:04.584 --\u003e 00:18:08.212\r\nNo! No!\r\n\r\n00:18:08.629 --\u003e 00:18:11.424\r\nOkay, okay, it wasn't Wayne!\r\n\r\n00:18:11.757 --\u003e 00:18:14.260\r\nThen who was it?\r\n\r\n00:18:16.095 --\u003e 00:18:18.931\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.435 --\u003e 00:18:25.938\r\nLast chance.\r\nWho was impersonating Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:18:28.190 --\u003e 00:18:29.191\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:30.651 --\u003e 00:18:33.446\r\nWho, Bell? Who?\r\n\r\n00:18:36.282 --\u003e 00:18:38.284\r\nFainted. He fainted.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.708 --\u003e 00:18:50.212\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is GCPD airborne unit\r\nsix-Able-12 to Batwing.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:50.338 --\u003e 00:18:52.131\r\n\u003ci\u003eDescend in the name of the law\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:52.256 --\u003e 00:18:55.301\r\n\u003ci\u003eand remand your prisoner\r\nto police custody.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:04.769 --\u003e 00:19:07.146\r\nThis should wake you\r\nup, Mr. Bell.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.322 --\u003e 00:19:19.742\r\nThis is the police!\r\nYou are under arrest!\r\n\r\n00:19:37.968 --\u003e 00:19:38.969\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.261 --\u003e 00:19:40.262\r\nPlease,\r\n\r\n00:19:40.971 --\u003e 00:19:42.515\r\nleave me alone.\r\n\r\n00:19:43.182 --\u003e 00:19:45.434\r\nLucius, it's okay.\r\nIt's me, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.559 --\u003e 00:19:47.103\r\nI have to speak to you.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.353 --\u003e 00:19:49.522\r\nOnly you can give me\r\nthe answers I need now.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.855 --\u003e 00:19:51.315\r\nLucius, take it easy.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.399 --\u003e 00:19:52.858\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.317 --\u003e 00:19:55.611\r\nYou know I'd never do\r\nanything to hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:19:56.779 --\u003e 00:19:59.532\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:05.955 --\u003e 00:20:08.374\r\nAh, there's his car. Stop here.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.261 --\u003e 00:20:21.262\r\nMatt?\r\n\r\n00:20:21.512 --\u003e 00:20:23.180\r\nMatt, are you in there?\r\n\r\n00:20:29.145 --\u003e 00:20:32.857\r\nSUMMER: And we'll have continuing\r\nupdates on this late-breaking story.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.940 --\u003e 00:20:36.026\r\nThe arrest of millionaire\r\nindustrialist Bruce Wayne\r\n\r\n00:20:36.110 --\u003e 00:20:40.156\r\nat the scene of an attempt on the\r\nlife of Wayne executive Lucius Fox.\r\n\r\n00:20:40.406 --\u003e 00:20:45.703\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Summer Gleeson, WGBS News at\r\n11:00, live at Gotham County Jail.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:48.205 --\u003e 00:20:49.290\r\nMatt?\r\n\r\n00:20:49.415 --\u003e 00:20:51.292\r\nMatt, it's me, Teddy.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.375 --\u003e 00:20:54.670\r\n(BREATHING HOARSELY)\r\n\r\n00:20:59.008 --\u003e 00:21:01.343\r\nMatt? Matt?\r\n\r\n00:21:01.594 --\u003e 00:21:02.803\r\nOh, Matt, is that you?\r\n\r\n00:21:03.512 --\u003e 00:21:05.890\r\nWhat in heaven's name\r\ndid they do to you?\r\n\r\n00:21:10.478 --\u003e 00:21:13.439\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:25.409 --\u003e 00:21:27.411\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:51.644 --\u003e 00:21:52.645\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E05 - Feat of Clay, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.503 --\u003e 00:00:04.505\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:03.105 --\u003e 00:01:04.982\r\nNARRATOR: Previously on Batman.\r\n\r\n00:01:05.065 --\u003e 00:01:07.025\r\nThat's what ain't good for you.\r\n\r\n00:01:07.150 --\u003e 00:01:10.195\r\nHaving to keep going back to\r\nDaggett for more of that stuff.\r\n\r\n00:01:10.320 --\u003e 00:01:12.281\r\nYou're right, Teddy. I can't.\r\n\r\n00:01:12.406 --\u003e 00:01:16.368\r\nI'll have to find a way to get\r\nlots of this stuff on my own.\r\n\r\n00:01:16.493 --\u003e 00:01:20.247\r\nI think our Mr. Hagen has\r\noutlived his usefulness.\r\n\r\n00:01:20.706 --\u003e 00:01:23.417\r\n\u003ci\u003eI want him dealt with.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:23.500 --\u003e 00:01:27.462\r\n- HAGEN: No.\r\n- Sweet dreams, slimeball.\r\n\r\n00:01:28.297 --\u003e 00:01:29.881\r\n(HAGEN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.048 --\u003e 00:01:32.509\r\nBATMAN: \"Bruce Wayne\r\nsought for questioning\"\r\n\r\n00:01:32.593 --\u003e 00:01:35.012\r\n\"in attempt on\r\nexecutive's life\"?\r\n\r\n00:01:45.772 --\u003e 00:01:47.149\r\n(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:59.745 --\u003e 00:02:01.997\r\nREPORTER 1: Mr. Wayne,\r\nwhat was it like to be in jail?\r\n\r\n00:02:02.080 --\u003e 00:02:05.417\r\nREPORTER 2: How do you respond to the\r\ncharges that you assaulted Lucius Fox?\r\n\r\n00:02:05.500 --\u003e 00:02:07.836\r\n- (ALL CLAMORING)\r\n- No comment. My client has no comment.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.961 --\u003e 00:02:10.273\r\n- Let us through, please.\r\n- REPORTER 3: Mr. Wayne, over here.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.297 --\u003e 00:02:13.550\r\n(CLAMORING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:13.634 --\u003e 00:02:15.111\r\nREPORTER 3: Mr. Wayne,\r\nMr. Wayne, over here.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.135 --\u003e 00:02:16.303\r\nREPORTER 4: Over here.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.054 --\u003e 00:02:18.847\r\nREPORTER 4: Mr. Wayne,\r\ncould you talk to us?\r\n\r\n00:02:22.809 --\u003e 00:02:26.605\r\nImagine, Lucius Fox\r\nthinking I would harm him.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.730 --\u003e 00:02:30.025\r\nAnd he's been with you,\r\nwhat, ten years now, sir?\r\n\r\n00:02:30.400 --\u003e 00:02:33.695\r\nThen whoever impersonated\r\nyou did an uncanny job.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.112 --\u003e 00:02:35.697\r\nBRUCE: \"Whoever\" is right.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.906 --\u003e 00:02:37.449\r\nBell said he didn't know.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.658 --\u003e 00:02:39.034\r\nHe had to be lying.\r\n\r\n00:02:39.159 --\u003e 00:02:41.203\r\nBut I know where\r\nto get the truth.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.631 --\u003e 00:02:53.715\r\nHAGEN: Move it, Lupus.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.840 --\u003e 00:02:56.385\r\nI want all this stuff\r\nout of here by sunrise.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.593 --\u003e 00:02:59.221\r\nAh, Matt, come on,\r\nyou don't have to do this.\r\n\r\n00:02:59.346 --\u003e 00:03:01.890\r\nYou made a comeback before.\r\nYou can do it again.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.183 --\u003e 00:03:04.309\r\nComeback?\r\n\r\n00:03:04.726 --\u003e 00:03:06.561\r\nComeback? From this?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.187 --\u003e 00:03:09.940\r\nFace it, Teddy,\r\nMatt Hagen is history.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.190 --\u003e 00:03:11.483\r\nThis time, for good.\r\n\r\n00:03:11.608 --\u003e 00:03:13.068\r\nHe's never coming back again.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.403 --\u003e 00:03:18.198\r\nGERMS: My contact on the force\r\nsays Bell hasn't cracked, so far.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.407 --\u003e 00:03:22.077\r\nGood. Well, I'm afraid we still\r\nhave quite a mess to clean up.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:26.081\r\nSooner or later,\r\nI will take control of Wayne Enterprises.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.546 --\u003e 00:03:34.923\r\nTheir marketing operation\r\nwill instantly give me\r\n\r\n00:03:35.006 --\u003e 00:03:38.927\r\na distribution network that would\r\ntake me years to build on my own.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.052 --\u003e 00:03:44.015\r\nTill then, my takeover plan\r\nwill have to be revised.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.141 --\u003e 00:03:49.521\r\nNow that our actor friend, Hagen,\r\nis no longer available to us.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.606 --\u003e 00:03:55.235\r\nOkay, Mr. Daggett,\r\nwho do you want me to take out now?\r\n\r\n00:03:56.486 --\u003e 00:03:59.197\r\nI want everything wrapped up by\r\nthe time I tape that show tonight.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.322 --\u003e 00:04:02.033\r\nWe're going to settle the\r\nFox matter once and for all.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.159 --\u003e 00:04:07.289\r\nBut, Mr. Daggett, he's in a hospital.\r\nAll those sick people...\r\n\r\n00:04:13.670 --\u003e 00:04:15.046\r\nOkay, Mr. Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.174 --\u003e 00:04:18.175\r\nBut, Matt,\r\n\r\n00:04:18.258 --\u003e 00:04:20.385\r\nyou thought it was all\r\nover for you once before,\r\n\r\n00:04:20.469 --\u003e 00:04:22.012\r\nand you were wrong then.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.095 --\u003e 00:04:23.972\r\nYou know,\r\nwhen you had your accident.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.222 --\u003e 00:04:25.724\r\nOf course I thought it was over.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.224 --\u003e 00:04:28.226\r\nI figured I was\r\nlucky to be alive.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.020 --\u003e 00:04:33.732\r\n\u003ci\u003eJust like I thought I was when Daggett\r\ncame to visit me at his clinic of his,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:33.857 --\u003e 00:04:36.693\r\n\u003ci\u003easking me to be his\r\nfirst test subject.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:37.068 --\u003e 00:04:38.320\r\n\u003ci\u003eHow could I say no?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:38.445 --\u003e 00:04:41.531\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe told me his Renuyu\r\nformula could do in minutes\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:41.656 --\u003e 00:04:44.409\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhat plastic surgery would\r\ntake years to accomplish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:52.209 --\u003e 00:04:53.752\r\nIt wasn't so bad,\r\n\r\n00:04:53.835 --\u003e 00:04:56.922\r\nexcept for all those jobs you\r\nhad to do for him in return.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.299 --\u003e 00:05:00.342\r\nBut, hey, it worked.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.467 --\u003e 00:05:02.928\r\nI mean, you had your biggest\r\nhits after the accident.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.056 --\u003e 00:05:09.726\r\nYeah. Some of the\r\nbest parts I ever had.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.396 --\u003e 00:05:16.316\r\nMatt! You're changing.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.441 --\u003e 00:05:18.360\r\nAnd you didn't use\r\nyour hands this time.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.485 --\u003e 00:05:20.278\r\nYou didn't even try.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.529 --\u003e 00:05:24.491\r\nYou did it automatically,\r\nlike a reflex or something.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.658 --\u003e 00:05:25.992\r\nUnbelievable.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.243 --\u003e 00:05:27.869\r\nYou know what this\r\nmeans, don't you?\r\n\r\n00:05:28.245 --\u003e 00:05:30.163\r\nIt doesn't have to be over.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.247 --\u003e 00:05:31.540\r\nYou can go on.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.665 --\u003e 00:05:33.124\r\nWe can go on.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.008 --\u003e 00:05:43.301\r\nWOW!\r\n\r\n00:05:43.718 --\u003e 00:05:46.721\r\nYou can even form\r\nclothes out of your skin.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.847 --\u003e 00:05:48.557\r\nBut, how?\r\n\r\n00:05:49.182 --\u003e 00:05:52.018\r\nThe formula must've soaked\r\nevery cell in my body.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.024 --\u003e 00:06:00.485\r\nIt's...\r\nIt's some kind of miracle.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.780 --\u003e 00:06:06.658\r\n- What... What are you doing?\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.033 --\u003e 00:06:09.744\r\nNo. You broke my concentration!\r\n\r\n00:06:09.870 --\u003e 00:06:12.205\r\nIt won't work, don't you see?\r\nIt's too hard.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.330 --\u003e 00:06:14.583\r\nIt's like tensing a muscle.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.666 --\u003e 00:06:16.334\r\nI can't keep it up for long.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.210 --\u003e 00:06:19.629\r\nMy career, my life...\r\n\r\n00:06:19.713 --\u003e 00:06:20.714\r\nIt is gone!\r\n\r\n00:06:20.797 --\u003e 00:06:22.132\r\nAnd I can never get it back!\r\n\r\n00:06:22.841 --\u003e 00:06:26.052\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.177 --\u003e 00:06:27.929\r\nI'm not an actor anymore.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.179 --\u003e 00:06:30.473\r\nI'm not even a man.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.557 --\u003e 00:06:33.268\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:06:35.478 --\u003e 00:06:36.646\r\nHAGEN: Pull in here.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.398 --\u003e 00:06:39.399\r\nTEDDY: The hospital?\r\n\r\n00:06:39.733 --\u003e 00:06:42.986\r\nSooner or later, Daggett will\r\nsend someone to finish off Fox.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.111 --\u003e 00:06:45.447\r\nOnce I know who it is, I can\r\n\r\n00:06:45.989 --\u003e 00:06:47.157\r\ntake his place.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.282 --\u003e 00:06:49.910\r\nAnd if Daggett thinks\r\nI'm his henchman,\r\n\r\n00:06:50.035 --\u003e 00:06:51.995\r\nI can walk right up to him and,\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:53.163\r\n\"Bam!\"\r\n\r\n00:06:56.875 --\u003e 00:06:58.919\r\nGoodbye, Mr. Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.294 --\u003e 00:07:02.339\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:39.292 --\u003e 00:07:40.543\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:07:46.925 --\u003e 00:07:47.926\r\n- (GAsPs)\r\n- Hey!\r\n\r\n00:07:53.974 --\u003e 00:07:55.058\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:07.278 --\u003e 00:08:08.613\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:09.739 --\u003e 00:08:11.908\r\nLet me out of here. Please.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.992 --\u003e 00:08:16.287\r\nAll these viruses and\r\nbacteria, I could be infected.\r\n\r\n00:08:16.413 --\u003e 00:08:17.998\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.833 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nNow, the man who\r\nimpersonated Bruce Wayne,\r\n\r\n00:08:23.753 --\u003e 00:08:25.630\r\nI want his name.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.714 --\u003e 00:08:28.383\r\nI, uh, I don't know who, uh...\r\n\r\n00:08:31.344 --\u003e 00:08:34.097\r\nHmm. Crimson fever.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.431 --\u003e 00:08:35.807\r\nLousy way to go.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.224 --\u003e 00:08:37.892\r\nNo cure, you know.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.018 --\u003e 00:08:40.020\r\nThe name. Now!\r\n\r\n00:08:40.103 --\u003e 00:08:42.272\r\nOkay, okay, it was Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.355 --\u003e 00:08:44.899\r\nMatt Hagen, the movie actor.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.360 --\u003e 00:08:48.903\r\nIt's the truth. I swear!\r\n\r\n00:08:49.029 --\u003e 00:08:50.655\r\nThen, how did he fool Fox?\r\n\r\n00:08:50.947 --\u003e 00:08:54.409\r\nHe's good, but no actor,\r\nno makeup, is that good.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.784 --\u003e 00:08:56.327\r\nI... I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.664 --\u003e 00:09:00.665\r\nYou're crazy!\r\n\r\n00:09:00.790 --\u003e 00:09:02.208\r\nLast chance.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.709 --\u003e 00:09:05.795\r\n- Talk!\r\n- All right. He had something.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.004 --\u003e 00:09:08.465\r\nSomething nobody else had.\r\nHe could...\r\n\r\n00:09:08.590 --\u003e 00:09:10.175\r\nMAN: Nice going, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.259 --\u003e 00:09:13.094\r\nBut I'll take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.312 --\u003e 00:09:24.355\r\n- This is my collar.\r\n- Just a moment.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.902 --\u003e 00:09:29.944\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:37.118 --\u003e 00:09:38.244\r\nWhat in the name of...\r\n\r\n00:09:38.369 --\u003e 00:09:39.579\r\nShut up.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.081 --\u003e 00:09:44.000\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:44.084 --\u003e 00:09:46.461\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.186 --\u003e 00:10:04.479\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.562 --\u003e 00:10:06.022\r\nRelax, Germs.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.147 --\u003e 00:10:08.775\r\nYou won't have to hang\r\naround here too long.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.694 --\u003e 00:10:14.572\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:26.334 --\u003e 00:10:28.128\r\nWhat in the name of heaven...\r\n\r\n00:10:30.463 --\u003e 00:10:31.548\r\nBack off!\r\n\r\n00:11:15.466 --\u003e 00:11:17.051\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.135 --\u003e 00:11:18.178\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:11:24.142 --\u003e 00:11:25.435\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:25.560 --\u003e 00:11:28.396\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:30.481 --\u003e 00:11:34.194\r\nAll that shape-changing takes\r\na lot out of you, doesn't it?\r\n\r\n00:11:34.277 --\u003e 00:11:38.323\r\n(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:12:09.687 --\u003e 00:12:10.688\r\n(MUFFLED SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:12:18.279 --\u003e 00:12:20.073\r\n\u003ci\u003eTomorrow on Gotham Insider,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:20.156 --\u003e 00:12:23.076\r\n\u003ci\u003emy guest will be pharmaceutical\r\nking, Roland Daggett,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:23.201 --\u003e 00:12:27.455\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhose new product can perform\r\nmiracles even plastic surgery can't.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:29.916 --\u003e 00:12:32.335\r\nNot even the Batman can stop\r\nme, Teddy.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.460 --\u003e 00:12:35.380\r\nAnd that means,\r\nDaggett won't have a prayer.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.505 --\u003e 00:12:36.506\r\nMatt, please.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.632 --\u003e 00:12:40.760\r\nYou don't want to do anything crazy.\r\nWhy don't you try to get some shuteye?\r\n\r\n00:12:42.095 --\u003e 00:12:44.681\r\n(GROWLS) Don't you\r\ndare patronize me!\r\n\r\n00:12:44.806 --\u003e 00:12:46.891\r\nI told you, I don't need rest.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.016 --\u003e 00:12:48.309\r\nI don't need food!\r\n\r\n00:12:48.518 --\u003e 00:12:50.853\r\nAnd I don't need you!\r\n\r\n00:12:50.937 --\u003e 00:12:52.438\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:56.609 --\u003e 00:12:57.860\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:13:12.000 --\u003e 00:13:14.961\r\nALFRED: I've acquired the Matt\r\nHagen films you requested, sir.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.086 --\u003e 00:13:17.338\r\nGood, because now I'm sure that\r\n\r\n00:13:17.422 --\u003e 00:13:19.632\r\nthat thing I fought at\r\nthe hospital is Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.757 --\u003e 00:13:21.926\r\nHis condition is apparently\r\nthe tragic result\r\n\r\n00:13:22.010 --\u003e 00:13:25.305\r\nof an experiment conducted\r\nby Roland Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.430 --\u003e 00:13:29.183\r\nHagen apparently transforms,\r\nunconsciously sometimes,\r\n\r\n00:13:29.350 --\u003e 00:13:31.311\r\nlike a reflex action.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.980 --\u003e 00:13:38.276\r\n(PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:38.359 --\u003e 00:13:41.112\r\n(APPLAUSE)\r\n\r\n00:13:49.829 --\u003e 00:13:51.914\r\n\u003ci\u003eFEMALE ANCHOR: A\r\nface-lift in ajar?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:52.915 --\u003e 00:13:55.144\r\n\u003ci\u003e- I love that idea. That's interesting.\r\n- (PEOPLE MURMURING IN AGREEMENT)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:55.168 --\u003e 00:13:58.212\r\nIf you'll watch the monitors,\r\nyou'll see that with Renuyu,\r\n\r\n00:13:58.379 --\u003e 00:14:00.214\r\nyou can smooth away wrinkles,\r\n\r\n00:14:00.340 --\u003e 00:14:02.425\r\nreshape imperfections.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.550 --\u003e 00:14:07.221\r\nLiterally,\r\nremake your face however you choose.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.597 --\u003e 00:14:08.765\r\n- Oh, that's great!\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.848 --\u003e 00:14:09.849\r\n(ALL MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.272 --\u003e 00:14:17.982\r\n\u003ci\u003eAmazing stuff, Rolly.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:18.107 --\u003e 00:14:20.651\r\nIsee we have some\r\nquestions in our audience.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.777 --\u003e 00:14:24.739\r\nI'd like to ask Mr. Daggett\r\nabout the rumors I've heard.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.864 --\u003e 00:14:27.700\r\nI hear he's selling Renuyu\r\nthrough direct marketing\r\n\r\n00:14:27.867 --\u003e 00:14:31.996\r\nbecause stores won't carry it\r\ndue to its harmful side effects.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.121 --\u003e 00:14:33.831\r\nWell, that's, uh...\r\n\r\n00:14:34.624 --\u003e 00:14:36.417\r\nAbsolutely untrue.\r\n\r\n00:14:36.542 --\u003e 00:14:40.505\r\nWhat about the addictive\r\nproperties of Renuyu, Mr. Daggett?\r\n\r\n00:14:40.630 --\u003e 00:14:42.548\r\nHow, once you're hooked on it,\r\n\r\n00:14:42.632 --\u003e 00:14:46.427\r\nyou can't stop using it\r\nwithout horrible pain?\r\n\r\n00:14:46.552 --\u003e 00:14:48.054\r\nNo. I mean...\r\n\r\n00:14:48.137 --\u003e 00:14:49.764\r\nThat's just not so.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.643 --\u003e 00:14:57.522\r\nWhy don't you show them what\r\nan overdose can do, Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.647 --\u003e 00:15:01.192\r\n(VOICE CHANGING) Why don't\r\nyou tell them about me?\r\n\r\n00:15:02.652 --\u003e 00:15:06.280\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:12.286 --\u003e 00:15:16.499\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:22.255 --\u003e 00:15:24.507\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:30.346 --\u003e 00:15:31.973\r\n- (eul\\ls COCKING)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:15:36.310 --\u003e 00:15:37.311\r\nBOTH: Huh?\r\n\r\n00:15:50.199 --\u003e 00:15:51.325\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:03.045 --\u003e 00:16:04.297\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:17.393 --\u003e 00:16:18.394\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:22.315 --\u003e 00:16:23.441\r\nYou again.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.566 --\u003e 00:16:25.776\r\nHagen, listen to me.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.277 --\u003e 00:16:27.361\r\nThere is no Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.487 --\u003e 00:16:30.198\r\nIt's only me now, Clayface.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.953 --\u003e 00:16:38.289\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.836 --\u003e 00:16:45.796\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.634 --\u003e 00:16:51.135\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:20.706 --\u003e 00:17:21.916\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:23.626 --\u003e 00:17:26.671\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:26.754 --\u003e 00:17:30.716\r\nSee? I figured out how to\r\nmanage this thing pretty good.\r\n\r\n00:17:31.259 --\u003e 00:17:35.304\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.222 --\u003e 00:17:37.348\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:42.562 --\u003e 00:17:43.854\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:55.533 --\u003e 00:17:58.536\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.420 --\u003e 00:18:08.796\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:09.297 --\u003e 00:18:10.590\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:23.519 --\u003e 00:18:25.479\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.695 --\u003e 00:18:33.988\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:37.366 --\u003e 00:18:39.702\r\nWhat are you doing? Stop it!\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.621\r\nLook at them, Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.912 --\u003e 00:18:43.831\r\nLook at what you used to be.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.832 --\u003e 00:18:47.001\r\nNo. No.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.251 --\u003e 00:18:48.461\r\nTurn them off.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.544 --\u003e 00:18:50.463\r\nYou can play those roles\r\nagain, Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.588 --\u003e 00:18:53.132\r\nLet me help you find a cure.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.257 --\u003e 00:18:55.509\r\nNo! Hagen's gone.\r\n\r\n00:18:55.635 --\u003e 00:18:57.303\r\nMake him stop haunting me!\r\n\r\n00:19:00.056 --\u003e 00:19:03.601\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.684 --\u003e 00:19:06.937\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.775 --\u003e 00:19:12.610\r\nStop it. Stop it. Turn them off.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.735 --\u003e 00:19:13.778\r\nI can't control it.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.861 --\u003e 00:19:15.905\r\nI can't be all of them.\r\nNot all at once.\r\n\r\n00:19:15.988 --\u003e 00:19:18.574\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:26.791 --\u003e 00:19:28.084\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:19:30.378 --\u003e 00:19:32.880\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.596 --\u003e 00:19:45.059\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.145 --\u003e 00:19:49.438\r\nMother of mercy.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.563 --\u003e 00:19:51.649\r\nIt looks just like Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.534 --\u003e 00:20:03.911\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.129 --\u003e 00:20:16.048\r\nYou know what I'd have given\r\nfor a death scene like this?\r\n\r\n00:20:16.674 --\u003e 00:20:18.050\r\nToo bad I won't get to...\r\n\r\n00:20:18.759 --\u003e 00:20:20.302\r\nRead the notices.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.438 --\u003e 00:20:31.605\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm just glad to know\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:31.689 --\u003e 00:20:33.691\r\n\u003ci\u003eit wasn't really Bruce\r\nWayne who attacked me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:33.816 --\u003e 00:20:35.359\r\n\u003ci\u003eThank you, Mr. Fox.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:35.484 --\u003e 00:20:37.278\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll charges against Wayne have,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:37.403 --\u003e 00:20:38.696\r\n\u003ci\u003eof course, been dropped.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:38.821 --\u003e 00:20:41.532\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd Roland Daggett\r\nremains in custody.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:46.829 --\u003e 00:20:47.830\r\nBATMAN: Mmm.\r\n\r\n00:20:48.289 --\u003e 00:20:49.540\r\nALFRED: My word, sir.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.665 --\u003e 00:20:52.626\r\nI should think after all this,\r\nit would be time to rest.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.752 --\u003e 00:20:53.753\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.919 --\u003e 00:20:57.214\r\nA piece of clay left behind when\r\nthey took Hagen's body away.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.840 --\u003e 00:20:58.841\r\nWatch.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.848 --\u003e 00:21:08.309\r\nElectricity has no effect on it?\r\n\r\n00:21:08.434 --\u003e 00:21:09.435\r\nBATMAN: Exactly.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.478 --\u003e 00:21:11.729\r\n\u003ci\u003eI wouldn't be surprised\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:11.812 --\u003e 00:21:14.982\r\n\u003ci\u003eif the body they took to\r\nthe morgue was only a shell.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:17.151 --\u003e 00:21:20.613\r\n\u003ci\u003eDon't forget, first and\r\nforemost, Hagen was an actor.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:21.489 --\u003e 00:21:23.199\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe said it himself, Alfred,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:23.407 --\u003e 00:21:24.784\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe called it a scene.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:24.867 --\u003e 00:21:27.703\r\n\u003ci\u003eMaybe the greatest\r\nscene of his career.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:28.287 --\u003e 00:21:29.872\r\nSee you around, Matt.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.792 --\u003e 00:21:36.796\r\n\u003ci\u003eA death scene so real,\r\nit fooled us all.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:36.879 --\u003e 00:21:39.548\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:21:46.222 --\u003e 00:21:52.436\r\n(LAUGHING IN HAGEN'S VOICE)\r\n\r\n00:21:57.566 --\u003e 00:21:59.568\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:23.843 --\u003e 00:22:24.844\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E06 - It's Never Too Late (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.147 --\u003e 00:00:29.071\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:32.593 --\u003e 00:01:35.220\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe mob war in Gotham\r\ncontinues tonight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:35.304 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n\u003ci\u003eRival crime families led by\r\nRupert Thorne and Arnold Stromwell\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:38.974 --\u003e 00:01:41.810\r\n\u003ci\u003econtinue to battle for control\r\nof the city's underworld.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:41.893 --\u003e 00:01:44.813\r\n- That's a nice picture of you, boss.\r\n- Pipe down!\r\n\r\n00:01:44.896 --\u003e 00:01:49.026\r\n\u003ci\u003eAccording to Police Commissioner\r\nGordon, mob violence is intensifying.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:49.109 --\u003e 00:01:52.195\r\nWhat we have here is a battle\r\nbetween an older \u003ci\u003ecrime\u003c/i\u003e boss\r\n\r\n00:01:52.279 --\u003e 00:01:56.074\r\n\u003ci\u003eand his younger rival for\r\ncontrol of the rackets in Gotham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:56.158 --\u003e 00:01:59.036\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd in this case,\r\nit looks like youth has the edge.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:59.119 --\u003e 00:02:01.997\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'd say Stromwell is\r\nabout to be retired.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:02.164 --\u003e 00:02:03.665\r\nWe'll see about that!\r\n\r\n00:02:03.915 --\u003e 00:02:06.585\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut the struggle may now\r\nbe taking a tragic twist\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:06.668 --\u003e 00:02:10.672\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith the reported disappearance of\r\nArnold Stromwell's only son, Joseph.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:13.550 --\u003e 00:02:16.553\r\nCalm down, boss.\r\nRemember your blood pressure.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.637 --\u003e 00:02:18.597\r\nI want my son back.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.722 --\u003e 00:02:20.474\r\nI know, Arnie. I know.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.557 --\u003e 00:02:22.434\r\nThis war has to stop.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.517 --\u003e 00:02:25.020\r\nI want a meeting with Thorne,\r\nand I want it tonight!\r\n\r\n00:02:25.103 --\u003e 00:02:27.356\r\nI'll set it up, Mr. Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.867 --\u003e 00:02:41.912\r\nIt's Thorne. He's got my son.\r\nI know it!\r\n\r\n00:02:41.995 --\u003e 00:02:43.163\r\nI know it!\r\n\r\n00:03:00.806 --\u003e 00:03:03.392\r\nCome on, buddy,\r\nyou're out of here.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.228 --\u003e 00:03:07.437\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:03:08.105 --\u003e 00:03:09.231\r\n(cucmue)\r\n\r\n00:03:12.401 --\u003e 00:03:13.652\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.573 --\u003e 00:03:20.659\r\nStromwell wants the\r\nmeeting tonight.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.742 --\u003e 00:03:23.453\r\nWe'll put out a sign that\r\nsays \"private party.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:23.537 --\u003e 00:03:26.248\r\n(LAUGHS) Yeah.\r\nA going-away party.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.415 --\u003e 00:03:29.376\r\nWhen Arnie gets here,\r\nwe're all going to act nice-nice,\r\n\r\n00:03:29.459 --\u003e 00:03:32.003\r\nmake him feel we want a truce.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.254 --\u003e 00:03:35.257\r\nAll everybody has to do\r\nis follow my instructions.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.340 --\u003e 00:03:37.217\r\nAnd you get the first cue, Pete.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.300 --\u003e 00:03:41.346\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's got to go like clockwork.\r\nAfter Pete leaves, the lights go out.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:41.430 --\u003e 00:03:43.682\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe have to the count\r\nof five to get clear,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:43.765 --\u003e 00:03:46.685\r\n\u003ci\u003eand it'll be all over\r\nfor Arnold Stromwell.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:05.287 --\u003e 00:04:08.749\r\nI'll teach Thorne to muscle in on me.\r\nThis is my town.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.832 --\u003e 00:04:10.625\r\nI made it what it is.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.212 --\u003e 00:04:17.632\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:38.320 --\u003e 00:04:40.864\r\nYou got to swear you\r\nwon't squeal on me, Mike.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.947 --\u003e 00:04:44.618\r\nGee, Arnie, you keep stealing\r\njunk, you're gonna get caught.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.701 --\u003e 00:04:46.870\r\nNah. Someday I'm\r\ngonna own this town.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.953 --\u003e 00:04:49.039\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.171 --\u003e 00:04:58.298\r\n(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.008 --\u003e 00:05:03.887\r\nArnie? What are you doing?\r\nGet off the tracks!\r\n\r\n00:05:04.846 --\u003e 00:05:05.972\r\nArnie!\r\n\r\n00:05:06.056 --\u003e 00:05:07.140\r\nArnie!\r\n\r\n00:05:31.289 --\u003e 00:05:33.333\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:20.005 --\u003e 00:06:22.966\r\n- Excuse me, Father.\r\n- What can I help you with?\r\n\r\n00:06:23.049 --\u003e 00:06:24.050\r\nYOU!\r\n\r\n00:06:24.134 --\u003e 00:06:27.846\r\nIt's coming down tonight, Father.\r\nHe's going to need you.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.972 --\u003e 00:06:30.140\r\nArnold?\r\n\r\n00:06:32.058 --\u003e 00:06:34.644\r\nThat's one soul I wish\r\nI could give up on.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.728 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nI don't believe you'd\r\ngive up on anyone, Father.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.398 --\u003e 00:06:39.983\r\nPlease be there.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.049 --\u003e 00:07:06.885\r\nHi, Arnie.\r\nI'm glad we could get together.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.971 --\u003e 00:07:13.099\r\nWe'll see, Thorne.\r\nIt's time to talk.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.350 --\u003e 00:07:16.144\r\nI think we should talk alone.\r\nMan to man.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.645 --\u003e 00:07:18.688\r\nLet the boys get some air.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.742 --\u003e 00:07:32.702\r\nWe made the news today.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.786 --\u003e 00:07:37.457\r\nI saw. It's making things difficult.\r\nYou're making things difficult.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.540 --\u003e 00:07:41.127\r\nCome on, Arnie.\r\nThis town's big enough for the two of us.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.628 --\u003e 00:07:43.505\r\n- Where's my son?\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:07:43.588 --\u003e 00:07:46.633\r\nMy son! Where is he?\r\nWhat have you done to him?\r\n\r\n00:07:50.303 --\u003e 00:07:52.055\r\nI don't know anything about it.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.264 --\u003e 00:07:54.724\r\nYou lowlife.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.810 --\u003e 00:07:59.521\r\nYou'd do anything to\r\ntake over my city.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.771 --\u003e 00:08:02.107\r\nI didn't touch your kid.\r\nI swear it, Arnie.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.190 --\u003e 00:08:03.608\r\nYou know I don't\r\nmess with family.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.822 --\u003e 00:08:10.657\r\nHey, come on.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.282 --\u003e 00:08:13.201\r\nWe're getting off on\r\nthe wrong foot here.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.284 --\u003e 00:08:15.620\r\nIt's a shame about your kid.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.912 --\u003e 00:08:17.455\r\nMaybe I can help.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.539 --\u003e 00:08:19.708\r\n- How?\r\n- Well, I've got connections you don't.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.177 --\u003e 00:08:32.303\r\nGood.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.512 --\u003e 00:08:35.181\r\nNow, we can't talk\r\non an empty stomach.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.348 --\u003e 00:08:38.518\r\nPete, I want to see an antipasto out\r\nhere that'll knock our socks off.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.982 --\u003e 00:08:45.025\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:09:08.339 --\u003e 00:09:09.591\r\nThe boss!\r\n\r\n00:09:12.010 --\u003e 00:09:14.637\r\n- You can't go in there.\r\n- It was a setup!\r\n\r\n00:09:14.721 --\u003e 00:09:16.681\r\nWe can't do nothing now.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.015 --\u003e 00:09:20.351\r\nWe've got to regroup.\r\nCome on, before the cops get here.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.900 --\u003e 00:09:29.360\r\nConsider yourself\r\nreplaced, Arnie.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.612 --\u003e 00:09:32.197\r\nIt's party time.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.383 --\u003e 00:09:54.052\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:55.428 --\u003e 00:09:57.305\r\nOh. What...\r\n\r\n00:09:59.516 --\u003e 00:10:01.851\r\nNo! Where am I?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.938 --\u003e 00:10:07.107\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:07.190 --\u003e 00:10:08.525\r\nI'm alive.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.025 --\u003e 00:10:10.985\r\nYou! What are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:10:11.277 --\u003e 00:10:12.904\r\nSaving your hide.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.987 --\u003e 00:10:16.574\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:10:17.492 --\u003e 00:10:20.411\r\nWhoa.\r\nHeavy barbecue action, man.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.041 --\u003e 00:10:27.043\r\nWow! He's really out there.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.587 --\u003e 00:10:31.714\r\nLet me go, you caped freak!\r\n\r\n00:10:38.680 --\u003e 00:10:41.099\r\n(POLICE RADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:10:45.895 --\u003e 00:10:48.773\r\nThe media's going to\r\nnail us on this one.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.066 --\u003e 00:10:51.693\r\nWhat are you looking at?\r\n\r\n00:10:51.776 --\u003e 00:10:54.612\r\nYour hair.\r\nIt looked better on TV.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.281 --\u003e 00:10:58.992\r\nDefinitely arson, Commissioner Gordon.\r\nA bomb.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.075 --\u003e 00:11:01.786\r\nDarn shame.\r\nThey make the best cannolis.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.872 --\u003e 00:11:07.333\r\n- Anybody in there?\r\n- There's no evidence anyone was inside.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.417 --\u003e 00:11:11.546\r\nThere was somebody in there!\r\nBatman saved his butt! I seen them, man.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.629 --\u003e 00:11:15.133\r\nHe was just leaping on the rooftops,\r\ncarrying somebody on his shoulders.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.216 --\u003e 00:11:16.259\r\nI seen it!\r\n\r\n00:11:16.342 --\u003e 00:11:20.346\r\nLike a dark angel snatching the\r\nguy from the fires of Hades, man.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.269 --\u003e 00:11:29.522\r\nYour news puts a crimp in\r\nour celebration, Simon.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.606 --\u003e 00:11:31.482\r\nSorry, Mr. Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.566 --\u003e 00:11:34.819\r\nBut why would Batman want to\r\nsave a guy like Stromwell?\r\n\r\n00:11:34.903 --\u003e 00:11:38.198\r\nTo get him to spill his\r\nguts about the organization.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.282 --\u003e 00:11:42.202\r\nGet everyone on the street!\r\nCheck the train yards.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.285 --\u003e 00:11:45.496\r\nFind Stromwell and the\r\nBatman and get rid of them!\r\n\r\n00:12:00.053 --\u003e 00:12:02.180\r\nAll right. Why the heroics?\r\n\r\n00:12:02.263 --\u003e 00:12:04.390\r\nYou've got something I want.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.849 --\u003e 00:12:06.768\r\nOh, yeah? What's that?\r\n\r\n00:12:06.851 --\u003e 00:12:09.145\r\nInformation. About the gangs.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.229 --\u003e 00:12:10.980\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:11.064 --\u003e 00:12:13.900\r\nWell, I appreciate your\r\nsaving my life and all,\r\n\r\n00:12:13.983 --\u003e 00:12:17.023\r\nbut you're gonna have to come up with\r\na better reason for me to turn stoolie.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.656 --\u003e 00:12:21.449\r\nI'll try and deliver.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.244 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:26.162 --\u003e 00:12:27.705\r\nWhoa.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.122 --\u003e 00:12:29.791\r\n(ARNOLD SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:35.546 --\u003e 00:12:36.839\r\nYou're gonna pay for this!\r\n\r\n00:12:38.132 --\u003e 00:12:41.135\r\nHey, I know this place.\r\nI started out here.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.219 --\u003e 00:12:42.595\r\nSelling drugs.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.346 --\u003e 00:12:44.472\r\nProve it.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.555 --\u003e 00:12:48.059\r\n- And now you manufacture them.\r\n- Prove that, too.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.142 --\u003e 00:12:50.770\r\nNobody twists anybody's\r\narm to take them, you know.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.853 --\u003e 00:12:52.897\r\nAnd for the record,\r\nI make candy.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.691 --\u003e 00:12:56.776\r\nHey, what are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:13:02.115 --\u003e 00:13:05.618\r\n\"Sunrise Foundation.\"\r\nMeans nothing to me.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.702 --\u003e 00:13:08.329\r\n(BELL TOLLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:15.920 --\u003e 00:13:17.630\r\nARNOLD: What is this place?\r\n\r\n00:13:17.839 --\u003e 00:13:19.632\r\nA drug rehab center.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.466 --\u003e 00:13:22.302\r\nNo. I ain't going in.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.593 --\u003e 00:13:24.929\r\nYour 10-cent tour\r\nof the city's over.\r\n\r\n00:13:27.056 --\u003e 00:13:29.767\r\nSo what could it hurt?\r\nOne little look, right?\r\n\r\n00:13:34.939 --\u003e 00:13:35.982\r\nJoey!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.065 --\u003e 00:13:38.735\r\nYes, and he's lucky.\r\nHe'll pull through.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.818 --\u003e 00:13:41.029\r\nConnie! Why didn't you call me?\r\n\r\n00:13:41.195 --\u003e 00:13:42.947\r\nI didn't know until today.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.031 --\u003e 00:13:45.575\r\nI'd never have known if\r\nit weren't for Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.995 --\u003e 00:13:52.540\r\nDon't get any closer.\r\nThe nurse said not to disturb him.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.915 --\u003e 00:13:55.501\r\nI'll find the guy\r\nwho got him hooked.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.585 --\u003e 00:13:57.003\r\nJust look in the mirror.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.086 --\u003e 00:13:59.672\r\nIt was your drugs and\r\nyour people who sell them.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.756 --\u003e 00:14:02.425\r\nI left you to get away\r\nfrom what you were doing.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.508 --\u003e 00:14:04.260\r\nOur son wasn't so lucky.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.767 --\u003e 00:14:12.727\r\nHelp stop it, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.977 --\u003e 00:14:16.856\r\nAll your power and money has\r\nbought you is an empire of misery.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.940 --\u003e 00:14:21.444\r\n- What do you want me to do?\r\n- Close down the organization.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.527 --\u003e 00:14:24.739\r\nTalk to the D.A.\r\nTurn in all the records.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.822 --\u003e 00:14:26.866\r\nIt has to stop, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.367 --\u003e 00:14:29.994\r\nIt has to stop now!\r\n\r\n00:14:44.926 --\u003e 00:14:47.595\r\nHere are the records.\r\nLook them over.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.648 --\u003e 00:15:00.525\r\nThese are dummy books.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.817 --\u003e 00:15:02.902\r\nYeah. And you're the dummy.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.909 --\u003e 00:15:13.246\r\nThey're both up there, all right.\r\nLet's smoke 'em out!\r\n\r\n00:15:13.579 --\u003e 00:15:16.207\r\nYou think I'd go down that easy?\r\nHa!\r\n\r\n00:15:16.582 --\u003e 00:15:19.710\r\nI got scores to settle.\r\nI'm big bad news.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.794 --\u003e 00:15:23.256\r\n- Always have been, always will be.\r\n- What about Joey?\r\n\r\n00:15:23.339 --\u003e 00:15:26.551\r\nI'm getting him out of that freak\r\nward, so I know he'll get better.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.634 --\u003e 00:15:28.970\r\nYou're fooling yourself\r\nagain, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:15:29.053 --\u003e 00:15:33.641\r\nYou're the fool, Batman.\r\nNow, if you just stay nice and quiet...\r\n\r\n00:15:37.520 --\u003e 00:15:38.771\r\nTear gas!\r\n\r\n00:15:39.772 --\u003e 00:15:42.817\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:47.280 --\u003e 00:15:50.783\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:15:59.917 --\u003e 00:16:01.586\r\n- (ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n- MAN: Look out!\r\n\r\n00:16:04.714 --\u003e 00:16:06.841\r\nStash, Freddy, get up there.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.677 --\u003e 00:16:11.846\r\nBATMAN: Stay here. Don't move.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.929 --\u003e 00:16:13.890\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.437 --\u003e 00:16:20.480\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.408 --\u003e 00:16:34.035\r\nStash? That you?\r\n\r\n00:16:36.245 --\u003e 00:16:37.788\r\nWhere's Batman?\r\n\r\n00:16:42.835 --\u003e 00:16:44.795\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.050 --\u003e 00:16:50.134\r\n(WHEEZES)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.218 --\u003e 00:16:52.011\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:16:56.390 --\u003e 00:16:57.433\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:16:59.477 --\u003e 00:17:01.020\r\nYou blew it, you jerks!\r\n\r\n00:17:12.532 --\u003e 00:17:14.617\r\nOver there! It's Stromwell!\r\n\r\n00:17:31.801 --\u003e 00:17:32.927\r\nHe ain't here.\r\n\r\n00:17:33.010 --\u003e 00:17:35.012\r\nHe's got to be here somewhere.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.076 --\u003e 00:17:58.119\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.559 --\u003e 00:18:23.811\r\nArnie, it's time to come home.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.729 --\u003e 00:18:26.606\r\nNo! Get away from me.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.648 --\u003e 00:18:29.317\r\nYou can't run anymore, Arnie!\r\n\r\n00:18:29.400 --\u003e 00:18:30.443\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.795 --\u003e 00:18:51.339\r\nGo ahead, take some.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.422 --\u003e 00:18:54.091\r\nNo! You stole that candy, Arnie.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.175 --\u003e 00:18:57.011\r\n- I don't want it.\r\n- Oh, what a mama's boy!\r\n\r\n00:18:57.094 --\u003e 00:18:59.263\r\nNo! Not again!\r\n\r\n00:18:59.722 --\u003e 00:19:02.058\r\nSomeday,\r\nI'm gonna own this town.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.141 --\u003e 00:19:04.518\r\n(BELL RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.775 --\u003e 00:19:12.151\r\n(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.819 --\u003e 00:19:14.904\r\nGet off!\r\n\r\n00:19:14.987 --\u003e 00:19:16.155\r\nGet off!\r\n\r\n00:19:16.238 --\u003e 00:19:19.909\r\nArnie? What are you doing?\r\nGet off the tracks!\r\n\r\n00:19:22.745 --\u003e 00:19:25.373\r\nArnie! Arnie!\r\n\r\n00:19:32.713 --\u003e 00:19:35.383\r\nJump, Arnie. Jump!\r\n\r\n00:20:06.789 --\u003e 00:20:09.208\r\nYOUNG ARNOLD: Michael? Michael!\r\n\r\n00:20:10.459 --\u003e 00:20:13.379\r\n- Michael! Michael!\r\n- (TRAIN HORN BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.462 --\u003e 00:20:16.590\r\n- I'm here, Arnie.\r\n- What are you doing here, Michael?\r\n\r\n00:20:16.674 --\u003e 00:20:19.969\r\n- I came to help you, Arnie.\r\n- I don't need your help.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.970 --\u003e 00:20:22.430\r\nIs that a fact?\r\n\r\n00:20:22.513 --\u003e 00:20:27.017\r\nAn empire crumbling.\r\nA marriage shattered. A son lost.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.476 --\u003e 00:20:29.186\r\nSure, you're doing fine.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.485 --\u003e 00:20:37.737\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.199 --\u003e 00:20:43.492\r\nARNOLD: Stay away, Michael.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.576 --\u003e 00:20:45.870\r\nLast time you helped me,\r\nit cost you your leg.\r\n\r\n00:20:45.953 --\u003e 00:20:48.664\r\n- Oh, I get by. Knock on wood.\r\n- (HOLLOW CLUNKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:49.331 --\u003e 00:20:52.543\r\nYou knew I was no good, Mike.\r\nWhy did you save me?\r\n\r\n00:20:52.710 --\u003e 00:20:54.837\r\nArnie, what else could I do?\r\n\r\n00:20:54.920 --\u003e 00:20:57.757\r\nBut now, you've got a\r\nchance to save yourself.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.840 --\u003e 00:21:00.342\r\nCome on, Arnie.\r\nDo the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.634 --\u003e 00:21:03.137\r\nFor yourself, for your son.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.138 --\u003e 00:21:05.973\r\nFor me, your little brother.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.893 --\u003e 00:21:10.019\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:21:10.102 --\u003e 00:21:11.187\r\nMichael.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.106 --\u003e 00:21:17.485\r\nYour family reunion touches\r\nme, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.693 --\u003e 00:21:19.320\r\nNow say goodbye.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.403 --\u003e 00:21:20.404\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:21:22.865 --\u003e 00:21:23.908\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:21:27.703 --\u003e 00:21:29.622\r\n(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:21:40.633 --\u003e 00:21:43.928\r\nARNOLD: Commissioner Gordon,\r\nI have a statement to give you.\r\n\r\n00:21:58.734 --\u003e 00:22:05.616\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:19.713 --\u003e 00:22:20.714\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E07 - Joker's Favor (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.964 --\u003e 00:00:07.299\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:15.951 --\u003e 00:01:17.953\r\n(HORNS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:21.582 --\u003e 00:01:22.976\r\nRADIO ANNOUNCER:\r\nhas escaped today.\r\n\r\n00:01:23.000 --\u003e 00:01:26.712\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe is armed and considered\r\nextremely dangerous. If seen...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:26.837 --\u003e 00:01:31.091\r\nOh, swell. Some nut makes trouble,\r\nand for that, they preempt the ballgame.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.466 --\u003e 00:01:33.218\r\nPerfect ending to an awful day.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.635 --\u003e 00:01:35.429\r\nBoss turns me down for a raise,\r\n\r\n00:01:35.679 --\u003e 00:01:37.055\r\nour kid needs braces,\r\n\r\n00:01:37.347 --\u003e 00:01:39.474\r\nand Bonnie's making\r\nmeatloaf for dinner.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.183 --\u003e 00:01:41.268\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:01:41.351 --\u003e 00:01:44.438\r\nAt what point exactly did I\r\nbecome life's punching bag?\r\n\r\n00:01:44.521 --\u003e 00:01:46.106\r\n(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:01:48.358 --\u003e 00:01:49.484\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:01:50.777 --\u003e 00:01:52.029\r\nWhat's their hurry?\r\n\r\n00:02:00.162 --\u003e 00:02:01.580\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:03.874 --\u003e 00:02:04.958\r\nSheesh.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.042 --\u003e 00:02:07.085\r\nGo on, push me aside, big shot.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.419 --\u003e 00:02:10.464\r\nNo reason anyone should move over\r\nand make way for Charlie Collins.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.634 --\u003e 00:02:14.674\r\n- Hey!\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:16.053 --\u003e 00:02:18.472\r\nOh, that's it.\r\nNo signal, no nothing.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.555 --\u003e 00:02:20.098\r\nJust treat me like\r\nI don't exist.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.641 --\u003e 00:02:22.851\r\nSorry, comrade. Not this time.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.644 --\u003e 00:02:25.103\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING,\r\nENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.446 --\u003e 00:02:35.447\r\nHey, buddy.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.614 --\u003e 00:02:37.407\r\nYeah, I'm talking to you, clown.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.699 --\u003e 00:02:39.326\r\nYou think you own\r\nthe whole road?\r\n\r\n00:02:39.743 --\u003e 00:02:40.994\r\nWhy, for two cents, I'd...\r\n\r\n00:02:41.912 --\u003e 00:02:42.954\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:02:43.163 --\u003e 00:02:44.247\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:46.375 --\u003e 00:02:47.751\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:02:55.550 --\u003e 00:02:56.802\r\nThat was The Joker.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.885 --\u003e 00:02:58.470\r\nI cussed out The Joker.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.403 --\u003e 00:03:15.529\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.905 --\u003e 00:03:17.948\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.700 --\u003e 00:03:21.410\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:21.535 --\u003e 00:03:22.953\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.589 --\u003e 00:03:35.799\r\nWhere'd all the cops go?\r\n\r\n00:03:39.678 --\u003e 00:03:40.762\r\n(EXHALES)\r\n\r\n00:03:40.846 --\u003e 00:03:41.888\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:42.347 --\u003e 00:03:43.849\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.939 --\u003e 00:03:52.399\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:55.652 --\u003e 00:03:57.404\r\nGO, Q9, go'\r\n\r\n00:03:57.863 --\u003e 00:03:59.906\r\n- Come on, come on.\r\n- (ENGINE SPUTTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:07.289 --\u003e 00:04:10.083\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:20.802 --\u003e 00:04:21.845\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:22.345 --\u003e 00:04:23.972\r\nThere's your two cents.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.264 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nNow, what are you\r\ngoing to do to me?\r\n\r\n00:04:27.684 --\u003e 00:04:29.394\r\nListen, I'm sorry, really.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.519 --\u003e 00:04:30.812\r\nI had a bad day.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.979 --\u003e 00:04:32.165\r\nBoss turned down my raise and...\r\n\r\n00:04:32.189 --\u003e 00:04:34.483\r\nNow, look, my rude friend.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.983 --\u003e 00:04:38.528\r\nWe can't have people cursing\r\nat each other on the freeway.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.612 --\u003e 00:04:41.198\r\nIt's simply not polite.\r\n\r\n00:04:41.865 --\u003e 00:04:42.908\r\nAhh!\r\n\r\n00:04:45.202 --\u003e 00:04:48.330\r\nI'm just going to have to\r\nteach you some manners.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.957 --\u003e 00:04:51.958\r\nPlease don't.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.125 --\u003e 00:04:53.126\r\nI have a family.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.210 --\u003e 00:04:55.504\r\nA wife, a little boy. Please.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.587 --\u003e 00:04:56.838\r\nI'll do anything to make it up.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.922 --\u003e 00:04:57.923\r\nAnything-\r\n\r\n00:04:59.216 --\u003e 00:05:01.843\r\n\"ATE/thing,\" Says you?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.053 --\u003e 00:05:04.095\r\nUh-huh.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.763 --\u003e 00:05:05.931\r\nOkey-dokey.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.644 --\u003e 00:05:11.645\r\nWallet.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.398 --\u003e 00:05:18.276\r\nSure. I don't have much cash.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.360 --\u003e 00:05:21.613\r\nOh, please. Don't insult me.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.032 --\u003e 00:05:28.203\r\n\"Charles Michael Collins.\" That's you.\r\n(CLICKING TONGUE)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.453 --\u003e 00:05:29.496\r\nLousy picture, though.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.579 --\u003e 00:05:30.622\r\nLousy.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.872 --\u003e 00:05:33.875\r\n\"Address, height,\r\nweight.\" Blah, blah, blah.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.959 --\u003e 00:05:36.211\r\nRighty-o, Chuckers.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.336 --\u003e 00:05:37.420\r\nHere's the deal.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.671 --\u003e 00:05:39.089\r\nI'll let you off,\r\n\r\n00:05:39.172 --\u003e 00:05:43.134\r\nif you promise to do\r\na little favor for me.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.427 --\u003e 00:05:46.304\r\nOkay. What?\r\n\r\n00:05:46.638 --\u003e 00:05:48.139\r\nI don't know!\r\n\r\n00:05:48.223 --\u003e 00:05:50.267\r\nI haven't thought of it yet.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.560 --\u003e 00:05:56.147\r\nYou just toddle on back to your\r\nmundane, meaningless little life,\r\n\r\n00:05:56.231 --\u003e 00:05:58.942\r\nand when I need you, I'll call.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.025 --\u003e 00:06:00.026\r\nFair?\r\n\r\n00:06:00.110 --\u003e 00:06:01.778\r\nGood. Great!\r\n\r\n00:06:01.903 --\u003e 00:06:02.988\r\nI'll be in touch.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.405 --\u003e 00:06:05.156\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:16.251 --\u003e 00:06:18.837\r\nGORDON: It's a waste of\r\ntime, money and manpower.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.920 --\u003e 00:06:21.047\r\nIf I had the authority to block\r\nit, I would.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.590 --\u003e 00:06:22.841\r\nCome on, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.924 --\u003e 00:06:25.635\r\nIt's free eats,\r\nand you get your picture in the paper.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.719 --\u003e 00:06:26.887\r\nIt's a good deal.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.642 --\u003e 00:06:36.271\r\n\"Testimonial in honor of Police\r\nCommissioner, James Gordon.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:36.563 --\u003e 00:06:39.566\r\n\"Tuesday night,\r\nthe Gotham Peregrinators Club.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:40.150 --\u003e 00:06:41.568\r\nBlasted waste of time.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.193 --\u003e 00:06:44.153\r\nBATMAN: Most of the force\r\nwould disagree with you.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.529 --\u003e 00:06:47.073\r\n(SCOFFS) If anyone should be\r\ngetting a testimonial, it's you.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.532 --\u003e 00:06:48.742\r\nI'm just the night shift.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.284 --\u003e 00:06:51.578\r\nYou deal with this\r\nmess 24 hours a day.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.912 --\u003e 00:06:53.472\r\nThat's what those\r\npeople want to honor.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.997 --\u003e 00:06:55.832\r\nOkay, okay. What the heck.\r\n\r\n00:06:56.082 --\u003e 00:06:57.834\r\nIt's a fancy club, good food.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.918 --\u003e 00:06:58.919\r\nCould be fun.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.294 --\u003e 00:07:01.838\r\nYou don't know where I can rent a\r\ntux, do you?\r\n\r\n00:07:01.922 --\u003e 00:07:03.340\r\n(wmn WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:04.466 --\u003e 00:07:05.842\r\nI hate it when he does that.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.926 --\u003e 00:07:07.385\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:07:12.474 --\u003e 00:07:15.310\r\nI arranged another early parole,\r\n\r\n00:07:15.393 --\u003e 00:07:18.688\r\nas soon as I heard about\r\nGordon's testimonial.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.772 --\u003e 00:07:19.981\r\nPhoo!\r\n\r\n00:07:20.607 --\u003e 00:07:22.943\r\nIt is to laugh, huh, Mr. J?\r\n\r\n00:07:26.696 --\u003e 00:07:28.490\r\nI ask you, Harley,\r\n\r\n00:07:28.615 --\u003e 00:07:33.662\r\nwho's given more hours of amusement\r\nto the Gotham Police Force than me?\r\n\r\n00:07:34.079 --\u003e 00:07:35.580\r\nNo one, Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.914 --\u003e 00:07:37.499\r\nI deserve...\r\n\r\n00:07:37.582 --\u003e 00:07:42.587\r\nNay. Demand the right to honor\r\nour dear commissioner as well.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.088 --\u003e 00:07:44.172\r\nHear, hear.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.673 --\u003e 00:07:46.424\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:54.933 --\u003e 00:07:55.976\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:01.815 --\u003e 00:08:02.899\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:08:06.778 --\u003e 00:08:07.988\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:08:10.824 --\u003e 00:08:12.909\r\nGonna call in a\r\nspecialist, boss?\r\n\r\n00:08:13.368 --\u003e 00:08:14.369\r\nNo, no.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.786 --\u003e 00:08:16.329\r\nJust an old friend,\r\n\r\n00:08:16.746 --\u003e 00:08:19.040\r\nwho's dying to do me a favor.\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.514 --\u003e 00:08:36.766\r\n(GRUNTS) Good one, Kenny.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.225 --\u003e 00:08:38.435\r\nGo out for a long bomb.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.978 --\u003e 00:08:41.896\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:08:42.605 --\u003e 00:08:43.606\r\nI got it.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.860 --\u003e 00:08:47.861\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:08:47.944 --\u003e 00:08:50.071\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Hello, Charlie.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:50.739 --\u003e 00:08:52.115\r\nWrong number, pal.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.198 --\u003e 00:08:53.533\r\nMy name is Don.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.616 --\u003e 00:08:54.826\r\nOh, n0, no, no.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.951 --\u003e 00:08:58.747\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is the right number,\r\nCharles Michael Collins.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:58.830 --\u003e 00:09:01.958\r\nI don't know why you changed\r\nyour name to Don Wallace\r\n\r\n00:09:02.167 --\u003e 00:09:05.170\r\nand moved your family\r\nto 12 Marigold Lane,\r\n\r\n00:09:05.295 --\u003e 00:09:07.297\r\nSpringdale, Ohio.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.380 --\u003e 00:09:11.885\r\nOne might think you were trying\r\nto skip out on our little deal.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.302 --\u003e 00:09:13.553\r\nLeave the sideburns.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.221 --\u003e 00:09:16.222\r\nHow did you find me?\r\n\r\n00:09:16.306 --\u003e 00:09:19.309\r\nOh, I never lost you, Chaz.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.392 --\u003e 00:09:21.936\r\nYou've become my hobby.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.062 --\u003e 00:09:24.647\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:26.149 --\u003e 00:09:28.234\r\nNow, listen up, Charlie Brown.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.318 --\u003e 00:09:30.862\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou're booked on the\r\nnext flight to Gotham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:31.237 --\u003e 00:09:33.948\r\nTell the family you have\r\nto visit a sick friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.240 --\u003e 00:09:37.827\r\nOh, and let's keep this\r\nto ourselves, okay?\r\n\r\n00:09:38.787 --\u003e 00:09:42.248\r\n\u003ci\u003eBad things happen to\r\npeople who gossip.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:42.332 --\u003e 00:09:44.501\r\n\u003ci\u003eCapisce, Carlo?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:46.169 --\u003e 00:09:47.170\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.253 --\u003e 00:09:49.005\r\n\u003ci\u003eGood. See you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:02.143 --\u003e 00:10:05.355\r\n\u003ci\u003eANNOUNCER: (ON PA) Gotham Air flight\r\n32, now arriving from Springdale.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:07.690 --\u003e 00:10:08.942\r\n\u003ci\u003eCHARLIE: This is crazy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:09.025 --\u003e 00:10:10.485\r\n\u003ci\u003eI can't believe I'm doing this.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:17.367 --\u003e 00:10:18.618\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf only I had some way to,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:18.701 --\u003e 00:10:20.870\r\n\u003ci\u003eI don't know, call him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:40.014 --\u003e 00:10:41.182\r\nHi!\r\n\r\n00:10:42.142 --\u003e 00:10:44.811\r\nThe car is this way, Charlie.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.191 --\u003e 00:10:52.235\r\nJumping Jiminy Christmas!\r\n\r\n00:10:52.694 --\u003e 00:10:54.404\r\nCharlie Collins!\r\n\r\n00:10:54.487 --\u003e 00:10:56.239\r\nIt's been forever.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.614 --\u003e 00:10:58.116\r\nHow are you, man?\r\n\r\n00:10:58.199 --\u003e 00:10:59.576\r\nYou look great.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.659 --\u003e 00:11:01.119\r\nLost a little weight.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.202 --\u003e 00:11:03.997\r\nLost a little hair, too.\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:04.080 --\u003e 00:11:06.082\r\nOh, Charlie.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.166 --\u003e 00:11:08.168\r\nCharlie, Charlie, Charlie.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.377 --\u003e 00:11:13.214\r\nSo, ready to do me\r\nthat little favor?\r\n\r\n00:11:14.048 --\u003e 00:11:16.634\r\nPlease,\r\ndon't make me hurt anyone.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.718 --\u003e 00:11:19.095\r\nNot to worry, Chuckers.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.721 --\u003e 00:11:21.764\r\nAs soon as you've\r\ndone my favor...\r\n\r\n00:11:21.848 --\u003e 00:11:24.058\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'll send you right back home.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:24.142 --\u003e 00:11:25.602\r\n\u003ci\u003eI promise.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:28.688 --\u003e 00:11:30.857\r\nOkay, Chaz.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.940 --\u003e 00:11:34.903\r\nWhen Harley knocks on the door three\r\ntimes, you open it.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.695 --\u003e 00:11:37.488\r\n- And?\r\n- That's it.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.031 --\u003e 00:11:39.824\r\nWait. That's the favor?\r\n\r\n00:11:40.325 --\u003e 00:11:42.285\r\nYou called me here\r\njust to open a door?\r\n\r\n00:11:42.368 --\u003e 00:11:45.288\r\nWell, look at the size\r\nof that cake, man!\r\n\r\n00:11:45.455 --\u003e 00:11:47.999\r\nShe can't open the door\r\nand push it in all at once!\r\n\r\n00:11:48.583 --\u003e 00:11:49.584\r\nThink!\r\n\r\n00:11:51.794 --\u003e 00:11:53.129\r\nHe is nuts.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.058 --\u003e 00:12:06.351\r\nNot bad.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.434 --\u003e 00:12:07.518\r\n(BURPS LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.769 --\u003e 00:12:09.020\r\n(SLURPS LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:10.521 --\u003e 00:12:11.731\r\nCongratulations, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.814 --\u003e 00:12:13.608\r\nI'm sorry I won't be\r\nable to stay for dinner.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.108 --\u003e 00:12:16.736\r\nHmm.\r\nThe life of a busy socialite.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.861 --\u003e 00:12:18.446\r\nAny way I could\r\nsneak out with you?\r\n\r\n00:12:25.954 --\u003e 00:12:28.581\r\n\u003ci\u003eCHARLIE: A room filled with\r\ncops, and no way to warn them.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:34.379 --\u003e 00:12:36.965\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf there were just some\r\nway to call Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:50.645 --\u003e 00:12:52.772\r\nOh... No way.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.147 --\u003e 00:12:54.440\r\nIt'd never work.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.524 --\u003e 00:12:56.025\r\nNot in a million...\r\n\r\n00:12:56.109 --\u003e 00:12:57.110\r\nWell, maybe.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.404 --\u003e 00:13:00.947\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:13:06.244 --\u003e 00:13:07.954\r\nNot staying for dinner, sir?\r\n\r\n00:13:08.079 --\u003e 00:13:09.831\r\nNot with The Joker on the loose.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.248 --\u003e 00:13:13.501\r\nSir, I believe you\r\nmay be needed inside.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.668 --\u003e 00:13:14.752\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:13:18.798 --\u003e 00:13:22.802\r\nGORDON: I'm honored that Gotham's\r\nfinest turned out to rub elbows\r\n\r\n00:13:22.885 --\u003e 00:13:25.221\r\nwith this tired old beat cop.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.975 --\u003e 00:13:30.727\r\nYou eating that roll, Montoya?\r\n\r\n00:13:30.810 --\u003e 00:13:32.478\r\nI'm really, very touched.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.854 --\u003e 00:13:34.480\r\n(KNOCKING)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.275 --\u003e 00:13:39.694\r\n- And I'll conclude by saying...\r\n- (WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:39.777 --\u003e 00:13:41.362\r\nDon't stop now, Jimmy.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.446 --\u003e 00:13:43.281\r\nThe party's just starting!\r\n\r\n00:13:49.120 --\u003e 00:13:51.914\r\nBaby doll. Entertainment.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.918 --\u003e 00:13:57.003\r\n\u003ci\u003eHey, sugar.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:57.086 --\u003e 00:13:58.880\r\nYou want to read me my rights?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.380 --\u003e 00:14:02.008\r\nYou have the right\r\nto remain silent.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.508 --\u003e 00:14:04.177\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:04.927 --\u003e 00:14:05.928\r\nJerk.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.145 --\u003e 00:14:15.480\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.360 --\u003e 00:14:21.778\r\n(PEOPLE MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:14:27.825 --\u003e 00:14:29.827\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:14:30.745 --\u003e 00:14:33.623\r\nHere's to Gotham's\r\nCommissioner G.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.956 --\u003e 00:14:37.543\r\nYou lock up the weirdos,\r\nthe crooks and the geeks.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.960 --\u003e 00:14:40.880\r\nYou're a hero to all\r\nthe boys in blue.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.172 --\u003e 00:14:42.924\r\nBut this time, baby,\r\n\r\n00:14:43.007 --\u003e 00:14:44.842\r\nthe joke's on you.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.259 --\u003e 00:14:46.469\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.972 --\u003e 00:14:51.516\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:55.103 --\u003e 00:14:56.479\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.031 --\u003e 00:15:08.199\r\n(PARTY HORN BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.282 --\u003e 00:15:09.283\r\nYes!\r\n\r\n00:15:09.367 --\u003e 00:15:13.329\r\nAnother stunning Joker entrance\r\nleaves the crowd speechless.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.830 --\u003e 00:15:15.915\r\nLet's hear it for him, folks.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.541 --\u003e 00:15:17.959\r\n(CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.544 --\u003e 00:15:21.421\r\n(WHOOPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:22.380 --\u003e 00:15:24.465\r\nGee! Tough audience.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.844 --\u003e 00:15:29.095\r\nCommissioner!\r\n\r\n00:15:29.512 --\u003e 00:15:32.515\r\nI'm here to present you with\r\na small token of affection,\r\n\r\n00:15:33.015 --\u003e 00:15:36.936\r\nfrom me and all the\r\nguys doing 25 to life.\r\n\r\n00:15:44.819 --\u003e 00:15:46.612\r\nWear it in good health,\r\n\r\n00:15:46.696 --\u003e 00:15:48.990\r\nall remaining 59 seconds of it.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.115 --\u003e 00:15:51.993\r\nToodles. (LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.788 --\u003e 00:15:58.374\r\nWait.\r\nYou promised to send me home.\r\n\r\n00:15:58.499 --\u003e 00:16:00.918\r\nI never said alive.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.253 --\u003e 00:16:03.963\r\nYou dirty, evil...\r\n\r\n00:16:04.255 --\u003e 00:16:05.339\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:06.299 --\u003e 00:16:09.427\r\nSayonara, sucker.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.510 --\u003e 00:16:11.053\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.159 --\u003e 00:16:34.160\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:16:34.452 --\u003e 00:16:36.871\r\nThe commissioner's\r\nmedal, it's a bomb!\r\n\r\n00:16:48.007 --\u003e 00:16:51.969\r\nGuess I'll need a new hobby,\r\nnow that old Charlie is... Pfft!\r\n\r\n00:16:52.303 --\u003e 00:16:53.471\r\nMacramé's nice.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.554 --\u003e 00:16:54.680\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.433 --\u003e 00:16:58.726\r\nThat came from outside!\r\n\r\n00:16:59.268 --\u003e 00:17:00.811\r\nRocko! Henshaw!\r\n\r\n00:17:00.937 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\nI smell a bat!\r\n\r\n00:17:02.939 --\u003e 00:17:04.357\r\nQuick! To the van!\r\n\r\n00:17:05.525 --\u003e 00:17:07.443\r\nUh, Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.196 --\u003e 00:17:13.157\r\nOkay. We'll tough it out here.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.952 --\u003e 00:17:17.578\r\nHe called you his hobby?\r\n\r\n00:17:17.703 --\u003e 00:17:18.704\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.788 --\u003e 00:17:21.290\r\nFor two years,\r\nhe watched me like a bug in a jar.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.415 --\u003e 00:17:23.751\r\nWatched and laughed,\r\nand threatened my family.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.085 --\u003e 00:17:26.003\r\nI had no choice, Batman, really.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.004 --\u003e 00:17:29.257\r\n(ALL GROANING AND COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.969 --\u003e 00:17:34.262\r\nThe gas is wearing off.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.554 --\u003e 00:17:35.596\r\nStay with the cops.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.694 --\u003e 00:17:50.736\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:54.031 --\u003e 00:17:55.032\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.621 --\u003e 00:18:01.789\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:01.872 --\u003e 00:18:03.124\r\n(METALLIC CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:09.880\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:13.676 --\u003e 00:18:15.303\r\nI know. You're thinking,\r\n\r\n00:18:15.428 --\u003e 00:18:16.470\r\n\"What a shame.\"\r\n\r\n00:18:17.013 --\u003e 00:18:19.432\r\n\"A pure,\r\ninnocent little thing like her\"\r\n\r\n00:18:19.515 --\u003e 00:18:22.393\r\n\"led astray by bad companions.\"\r\n\r\n00:18:25.479 --\u003e 00:18:27.398\r\nRight. Tell me another.\r\n\r\n00:18:32.403 --\u003e 00:18:36.157\r\nOi! Beauty school is starting\r\nto look pretty good about now.\r\n\r\n00:18:39.785 --\u003e 00:18:41.537\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:53.299 --\u003e 00:18:54.925\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:57.261 --\u003e 00:19:00.431\r\nIngenious, the way they\r\nreconstructed this temple.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.723 --\u003e 00:19:02.308\r\nCompletely accurate,\r\n\r\n00:19:02.391 --\u003e 00:19:05.227\r\nright down to the\r\npoison-tipped darts.\r\n\r\n00:19:08.564 --\u003e 00:19:09.649\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.151 --\u003e 00:19:16.030\r\nThe drop-away floor is a nice\r\ntouch, too. Hah!\r\n\r\n00:19:20.159 --\u003e 00:19:21.369\r\n(JOKER GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:25.247 --\u003e 00:19:26.666\r\n(SHUDDERS)\r\n\r\n00:19:28.042 --\u003e 00:19:30.211\r\nCatch! (LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.394 --\u003e 00:19:47.395\r\nHold it!\r\n\r\n00:19:48.145 --\u003e 00:19:51.107\r\nOh, come on! (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.190 --\u003e 00:19:52.775\r\nI said, hold it!\r\n\r\n00:19:53.734 --\u003e 00:19:54.819\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:59.115 --\u003e 00:20:01.242\r\nYou miserable little nobody!\r\n\r\n00:20:01.575 --\u003e 00:20:05.538\r\nIf I get caught,\r\nyour wife and son are history!\r\n\r\n00:20:05.913 --\u003e 00:20:08.374\r\nYou're not getting\r\ncaught, not this time.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.624 --\u003e 00:20:10.584\r\nI found this blown\r\nout of the van.\r\n\r\n00:20:11.168 --\u003e 00:20:12.545\r\nThis is how it ends, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.712 --\u003e 00:20:13.879\r\nNo big schemes,\r\n\r\n00:20:14.004 --\u003e 00:20:16.215\r\nno grand fight to the\r\nfinish with the Dark Knight.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.632 --\u003e 00:20:18.718\r\nTomorrow,\r\nall the papers will say,\r\n\r\n00:20:18.843 --\u003e 00:20:21.971\r\n\"Is that the great Joker was\r\nfound blown to bits in an alley,\"\r\n\r\n00:20:22.096 --\u003e 00:20:24.348\r\n\"alongside a miserable\r\nlittle nobody?\"\r\n\r\n00:20:25.224 --\u003e 00:20:27.435\r\nKind of funny. Ironic, really.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.685 --\u003e 00:20:30.312\r\nSee, I can destroy a man's\r\ndreams, too.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.438 --\u003e 00:20:33.482\r\nAnd that's really the only\r\ndream you've got, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:20:33.816 --\u003e 00:20:36.485\r\nLook, Charlie.\r\nYou've had a busy day.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.569 --\u003e 00:20:38.070\r\nAll this running around,\r\n\r\n00:20:38.154 --\u003e 00:20:41.407\r\nall this excitement with...\r\n(SHOUTS) ...Batman!\r\n\r\n00:20:41.615 --\u003e 00:20:44.160\r\nStop. You're crazy.\r\n\r\n00:20:44.243 --\u003e 00:20:46.328\r\nI had a good teacher. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:20:46.787 --\u003e 00:20:48.581\r\nSay good night, Gracie.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.331 --\u003e 00:20:50.332\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:50.416 --\u003e 00:20:53.753\r\nBatman! Batman!\r\n\r\n00:20:55.755 --\u003e 00:20:57.381\r\nHow long have you been there?\r\n\r\n00:20:58.132 --\u003e 00:20:59.341\r\nLong enough.\r\n\r\n00:20:59.800 --\u003e 00:21:01.010\r\nPut it down, Charlie.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.385 --\u003e 00:21:03.137\r\nYou know he'll\r\njust escape again.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.387 --\u003e 00:21:05.473\r\nThis is the only way\r\nmy family stays safe.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.598 --\u003e 00:21:07.558\r\nAll right. You win.\r\nTake it easy.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.641 --\u003e 00:21:11.187\r\nHere's everything on his blasted family.\r\nNames, addresses, it's all there.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.482 --\u003e 00:21:17.026\r\nYou're no fun anymore, Charlie.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.443 --\u003e 00:21:18.486\r\nHey, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.362 --\u003e 00:21:22.615\r\n(GASPS, SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:24.992 --\u003e 00:21:26.076\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:21:33.292 --\u003e 00:21:34.293\r\nGotcha.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.919 --\u003e 00:21:36.212\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:21:36.295 --\u003e 00:21:40.674\r\nOh. Very funny.\r\nA million laughs.\r\n\r\n00:21:41.175 --\u003e 00:21:42.676\r\nGo home, Mr. Collins.\r\n\r\n00:21:43.135 --\u003e 00:21:46.096\r\nHome. I never thought\r\nthat could sound so good.\r\n\r\n00:21:46.597 --\u003e 00:21:48.182\r\nWonder what Bonnie's\r\nmaking for dinner.\r\n\r\n00:21:48.724 --\u003e 00:21:50.244\r\nRight now,\r\nanything would taste great.\r\n\r\n00:21:50.810 --\u003e 00:21:51.977\r\nEven meatloaf.\r\n\r\n00:21:57.066 --\u003e 00:21:59.068\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:24.218 --\u003e 00:22:25.219\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E08 - The Cat and The Claw, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.756 --\u003e 00:00:07.758\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:06.275 --\u003e 00:01:08.193\r\nCATWOMAN: Previously\r\non Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:08.986 --\u003e 00:01:10.571\r\nPerfect, my love.\r\n\r\n00:01:10.654 --\u003e 00:01:11.989\r\nLet's go home.\r\n\r\n00:01:13.574 --\u003e 00:01:16.493\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: So,\r\nour new cat burglar is a woman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:17.035 --\u003e 00:01:19.663\r\nYou see, we're committed\r\nto building a major resort.\r\n\r\n00:01:19.788 --\u003e 00:01:23.250\r\nThe land is in the middle of nowhere.\r\nIt's worthless except to wildcats.\r\n\r\n00:01:23.542 --\u003e 00:01:25.961\r\nTomorrow at 2300 hours,\r\n\r\n00:01:26.044 --\u003e 00:01:30.007\r\na train under military escort\r\nwill pass through Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:01:30.424 --\u003e 00:01:33.927\r\nWe'll hit the train outside the\r\ncity, at this point.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.177 --\u003e 00:01:35.345\r\n(ALARM BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.681 --\u003e 00:01:39.361\r\n- (CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)\r\n- What is that?\r\n\r\n00:01:39.600 --\u003e 00:01:42.936\r\nA cat at the end\r\nof its nine lives.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.271 --\u003e 00:01:46.690\r\nBATMAN: I'll have to try\r\nand trim those claws.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.649 --\u003e 00:01:48.817\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:01:55.198 --\u003e 00:01:57.534\r\nNever trifle with the\r\naffections of a woman.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.659 --\u003e 00:01:59.077\r\nUntil next time.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.078 --\u003e 00:02:02.414\r\nAnd there will be a next time.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.619 --\u003e 00:02:41.995\r\n- BATMAN: You're late.\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:44.414 --\u003e 00:02:46.333\r\nCan't you ever walk up\r\nto someone normal-like?\r\n\r\n00:02:46.416 --\u003e 00:02:48.460\r\nBATMAN: I hear you\r\nhave some information.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.543 --\u003e 00:02:51.171\r\nUnder one condition.\r\nLay off the South Side.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.006 --\u003e 00:02:54.007\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:54.299 --\u003e 00:02:56.551\r\nKeep this up,\r\nand I'll be on you from all sides.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.635 --\u003e 00:02:58.845\r\nNorth, south, east and west.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.929 --\u003e 00:03:01.139\r\nOkay! I get the picture.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.976 --\u003e 00:03:07.187\r\nThere's rumors about\r\nsome train heist.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.604 --\u003e 00:03:09.189\r\n- When?\r\n- Tonight.\r\n\r\n00:03:09.272 --\u003e 00:03:10.273\r\nRed Claw?\r\n\r\n00:03:11.316 --\u003e 00:03:12.734\r\nDon't know. It's real sketchy.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.818 --\u003e 00:03:14.361\r\nOne thing I can tell you,\r\n\r\n00:03:14.444 --\u003e 00:03:16.613\r\nno one in the organization\r\nis making the hit.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.988 --\u003e 00:03:18.532\r\nThese are outsiders.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.741 --\u003e 00:03:20.784\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:24.246 --\u003e 00:03:25.872\r\nThere's nothing here\r\nin the schedules.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.624 --\u003e 00:03:28.959\r\nA last-minute change?\r\n\r\n00:03:29.292 --\u003e 00:03:30.293\r\nI'd have been told.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.087 --\u003e 00:03:33.672\r\nWhat if it was a military train?\r\n\r\n00:03:34.089 --\u003e 00:03:36.466\r\nSomething the government\r\nwouldn't want us to know about?\r\n\r\n00:03:37.259 --\u003e 00:03:38.760\r\nWouldn't be the first time.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.844 --\u003e 00:03:41.012\r\nBlasted Feds and their secrets.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.472 --\u003e 00:03:43.598\r\n(TRAIN RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:52.357 --\u003e 00:03:54.776\r\nYou know, when I saw those\r\narmy commercials on TV,\r\n\r\n00:03:54.901 --\u003e 00:03:57.446\r\nthey never said anything\r\nabout guarding no plague.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.529 --\u003e 00:04:00.115\r\nWho'd want to steal a can of\r\ngerms, anyway?\r\n\r\n00:04:26.391 --\u003e 00:04:27.517\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:04:28.351 --\u003e 00:04:30.061\r\n(SOLDIERS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:04:41.948 --\u003e 00:04:43.074\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.366 --\u003e 00:04:44.785\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:50.332 --\u003e 00:04:52.209\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.463 --\u003e 00:04:57.464\r\nThat's got to do it.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.858 --\u003e 00:05:18.068\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:37.838 --\u003e 00:05:38.880\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.298 --\u003e 00:05:42.092\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:50.100 --\u003e 00:05:51.601\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.190 --\u003e 00:05:58.692\r\nRed Claw, watch out!\r\n\r\n00:05:59.693 --\u003e 00:06:01.319\r\nRed Claw, a woman?\r\n\r\n00:06:01.903 --\u003e 00:06:03.864\r\nDo you have a problem with that?\r\n\r\n00:06:04.698 --\u003e 00:06:05.699\r\nNot at all.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.782 --\u003e 00:06:07.909\r\nI'm an equal-opportunity\r\ncrime fighter.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.118 --\u003e 00:06:09.411\r\nRED CLAW: Stay back, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:06:09.536 --\u003e 00:06:11.997\r\nI hold the ultimate equalizer.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.455 --\u003e 00:06:15.417\r\nThis plague kills\r\nindiscriminately.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.542 --\u003e 00:06:16.668\r\nYou'll die, too.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.085 --\u003e 00:06:20.338\r\nAlong with everyone else\r\nwithin a 10-mile radius.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.589 --\u003e 00:06:22.340\r\nCan you risk it, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:06:22.716 --\u003e 00:06:25.093\r\nGo on, call my bluff.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.844 --\u003e 00:06:28.972\r\nYou've finally met your\r\nmatch, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.055 --\u003e 00:06:31.808\r\nNot surprising it's a woman.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.227 --\u003e 00:06:36.438\r\nYes, General, but if you'd\r\nwarned us about this shipment\r\n\r\n00:06:36.521 --\u003e 00:06:37.772\r\nwe might've had a chance.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.274 --\u003e 00:06:40.525\r\nSo, what do I do now,\r\n\r\n00:06:40.609 --\u003e 00:06:42.444\r\nevacuate 10 million people?\r\n\r\n00:06:42.527 --\u003e 00:06:44.988\r\nMaybe we can set up camp\r\naround the Pentagon.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.113 --\u003e 00:06:46.197\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:46.448 --\u003e 00:06:48.199\r\nListen, General,\r\nI'll call you back.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.370 --\u003e 00:06:53.371\r\nGordon here.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.997 --\u003e 00:06:54.998\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.081 --\u003e 00:06:56.124\r\n\u003ci\u003eThank goodness.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:56.207 --\u003e 00:06:57.792\r\nHave you heard from Red Claw?\r\n\r\n00:06:58.251 --\u003e 00:06:59.461\r\nGORDON: Loud and clear.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.836 --\u003e 00:07:03.423\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe've got 24 hours to come up\r\nwith $1 billion in gold bullion,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:03.715 --\u003e 00:07:05.800\r\n\u003ci\u003eor she'll release\r\nthe plague on Gotham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:06.343 --\u003e 00:07:09.971\r\n\u003ci\u003eTo think, all this time the Feds\r\nhave been looking for a man.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:10.388 --\u003e 00:07:13.558\r\nBRUCE: Lately I'm learning never\r\nto underestimate the opposite sex.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.892 --\u003e 00:07:14.893\r\nI'll be in touch.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.610 --\u003e 00:07:26.488\r\nBruce and Selina go to\r\nlunch, take two.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.947 --\u003e 00:07:29.824\r\nI can't tell you how much I've been\r\nlooking forward to seeing you again.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.241 --\u003e 00:07:33.244\r\nWell, this time,\r\nI promise a much more exciting date\r\n\r\n00:07:33.328 --\u003e 00:07:34.329\r\nthan our last one.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.168 --\u003e 00:07:41.169\r\n\u003ci\u003eHEY-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:41.378 --\u003e 00:07:43.004\r\nThis time you seem preoccupied.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.214 --\u003e 00:07:45.340\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.423 --\u003e 00:07:47.092\r\nAn unexpected crisis.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.384 --\u003e 00:07:48.385\r\nYou, on the other hand,\r\n\r\n00:07:48.468 --\u003e 00:07:50.679\r\nlook like the cat who\r\nswallowed the canary.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.389 --\u003e 00:07:54.849\r\nThings are going very well\r\non the mountain lion front.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.308 --\u003e 00:07:57.102\r\nI may get that land\r\nfrom Multigon yet.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.435 --\u003e 00:07:58.436\r\nReally?\r\n\r\n00:07:58.895 --\u003e 00:08:00.271\r\nWhat did you find out?\r\n\r\n00:08:00.689 --\u003e 00:08:02.357\r\nLet's just say,\r\nthey plan on playing\r\n\r\n00:08:02.440 --\u003e 00:08:04.609\r\nmore than shuffleboard\r\nup at their resort.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.693 --\u003e 00:08:05.819\r\n(CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.902 --\u003e 00:08:06.945\r\nWhat in...\r\n\r\n00:08:08.613 --\u003e 00:08:09.614\r\nWatch out!\r\n\r\n00:08:10.865 --\u003e 00:08:12.283\r\nAn old boyfriend?\r\n\r\n00:08:13.952 --\u003e 00:08:16.204\r\nHere go your nine\r\nlives, kitty-cat.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.340 --\u003e 00:08:28.460\r\n- (CRASH ES)\r\n- (BOTH EXCLAIM)\r\n\r\n00:08:33.138 --\u003e 00:08:34.848\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:42.647 --\u003e 00:08:44.649\r\n- Busy fellow.\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:08:45.775 --\u003e 00:08:47.318\r\nBRUCE: Nothing. Hang on.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.909 --\u003e 00:08:55.994\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:59.664 --\u003e 00:09:01.124\r\n(BRAKES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:09:06.129 --\u003e 00:09:07.297\r\n(CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.675 --\u003e 00:09:11.885\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:09:13.762 --\u003e 00:09:14.804\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:16.014 --\u003e 00:09:17.223\r\nBrace yourself.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.600 --\u003e 00:09:19.976\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.646 --\u003e 00:09:24.731\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:27.442 --\u003e 00:09:28.443\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.823 --\u003e 00:09:35.200\r\n(BOTH SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:40.538 --\u003e 00:09:42.018\r\nWhere'd you learn\r\nto drive like that?\r\n\r\n00:09:42.791 --\u003e 00:09:45.293\r\nBRUCE: Oh, I've been going to\r\nthe Paris Grand Prix for years.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.627 --\u003e 00:09:47.627\r\nYou know, one of these\r\ndays, I think I'll enter it.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.888 --\u003e 00:09:58.181\r\nBRUCE: Well, you did\r\n\r\n00:09:58.264 --\u003e 00:09:59.909\r\n- promise me an exciting time.\r\n- (MIRROR SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:09:59.933 --\u003e 00:10:02.685\r\nIt's not every date where I\r\nget to fill out police reports.\r\n\r\n00:10:03.186 --\u003e 00:10:04.562\r\nSELINA: Thanks for seeing me up.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.854 --\u003e 00:10:07.273\r\nBRUCE: Just wanted to be sure\r\nthey didn't try anything else.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.858 --\u003e 00:10:10.860\r\nWhat makes you think\r\nthey weren't after you?\r\n\r\n00:10:10.944 --\u003e 00:10:12.320\r\nA nice guy like me?\r\n\r\n00:10:15.115 --\u003e 00:10:16.366\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:16.449 --\u003e 00:10:17.700\r\nGood night, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.784 --\u003e 00:10:20.120\r\nSelina, if you're in\r\nsome kind of trouble,\r\n\r\n00:10:20.203 --\u003e 00:10:21.204\r\nI wish you'd tell me.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.704 --\u003e 00:10:22.872\r\nPerhaps I can help.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.540 --\u003e 00:10:25.834\r\nI really care about you.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.292 --\u003e 00:10:29.045\r\nI haven't felt this way in a\r\nlong, long time.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.796 --\u003e 00:10:30.797\r\nThanks, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.673 --\u003e 00:10:34.217\r\nBut I've never been able to\r\nplay the damsel in distress.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.509 --\u003e 00:10:36.511\r\nI'll be okay. Don't worry.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.979 --\u003e 00:10:48.565\r\nMAVEN: But, why would someone\r\nat Multigon try to kill you?\r\n\r\n00:10:48.982 --\u003e 00:10:50.835\r\nSELINA: Ten to one,\r\nit has to do with those bunkers\r\n\r\n00:10:50.859 --\u003e 00:10:52.152\r\nunder their resort site.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.783 --\u003e 00:11:01.286\r\nI think it's time\r\nI do some digging.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.662 --\u003e 00:11:03.788\r\n(lsls MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:11:04.747 --\u003e 00:11:05.999\r\nNot this time, Isis.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.124 --\u003e 00:11:08.710\r\nI'm afraid where I'm going,\r\nthey don't allow pets.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.253 --\u003e 00:11:12.273\r\nALFRED: It's not that I\r\nquestion your instincts, sir,\r\n\r\n00:11:12.297 --\u003e 00:11:15.842\r\nbut why would Red Claw\r\nwish to harm Ms. Kyle?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.092 --\u003e 00:11:17.427\r\nBRUCE: Why, indeed.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.011 --\u003e 00:11:21.264\r\nBut somehow,\r\nSelina has crossed Red Claw's path,\r\n\r\n00:11:21.639 --\u003e 00:11:23.308\r\nand I mean to find out where.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.978 --\u003e 00:11:28.730\r\nWhat an unusual color.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.855 --\u003e 00:11:30.690\r\nMs. Kyle's, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.862 --\u003e 00:11:36.946\r\n(SNIFFS)\r\n\r\n00:11:38.072 --\u003e 00:11:40.450\r\nNo. It's a cat hair.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.534 --\u003e 00:11:43.995\r\nCurious,\r\nnever seen one quite that color.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.997 --\u003e 00:11:47.498\r\nBatman has.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.717 --\u003e 00:12:40.718\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:41.427 --\u003e 00:12:42.595\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:12:53.898 --\u003e 00:12:55.400\r\nMAVEN: (GASPS) Get away!\r\n\r\n00:13:02.282 --\u003e 00:13:03.408\r\n(GROWLS) Huh?\r\n\r\n00:13:08.871 --\u003e 00:13:10.290\r\n(BLOWS LANDING)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.520 --\u003e 00:13:33.646\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:34.105 --\u003e 00:13:35.440\r\nI won't hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.190 --\u003e 00:13:38.526\r\nRed Claw is after\r\nyou and Catwoman.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.610 --\u003e 00:13:42.071\r\nCatwoman?\r\nWhat are you talking about?\r\n\r\n00:13:42.238 --\u003e 00:13:44.407\r\nMaven, you must tell\r\nme where she's gone.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.490 --\u003e 00:13:45.908\r\nThese people are killers.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.037 --\u003e 00:13:51.247\r\n(STAMMERS) The Multigon site.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.415 --\u003e 00:13:54.167\r\nYou're not safe here anymore.\r\n\r\n00:13:54.375 --\u003e 00:13:55.918\r\nIs there somewhere you can hide?\r\n\r\n00:13:56.419 --\u003e 00:13:58.421\r\nWell, I guess I could go-\r\n\r\n00:13:58.546 --\u003e 00:14:00.214\r\n(WHISPERS) Shh. Go quickly.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.132 --\u003e 00:14:04.594\r\nAs long as you know who she is,\r\nyou should know how she feels.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.345 --\u003e 00:14:06.721\r\nShe's in love with you.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.287 --\u003e 00:14:32.914\r\n- (WHIP SWISHING)\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:35.333 --\u003e 00:14:36.667\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:36.751 --\u003e 00:14:39.045\r\nThis ought to keep\r\nyou out of my hair.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.504 --\u003e 00:14:41.589\r\n- (GROWLING)\r\n- (SHUSH ES)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.990 --\u003e 00:15:09.158\r\n(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:11.744 --\u003e 00:15:14.789\r\nThese will certainly enhance\r\nthe resort's brochure.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.545 --\u003e 00:15:22.755\r\nHere, kitty, kitty, kitty.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.839 --\u003e 00:15:24.215\r\n(SNICKERS)\r\n\r\n00:15:28.511 --\u003e 00:15:29.887\r\nI didn't think you cared.\r\n\r\n00:15:29.971 --\u003e 00:15:30.972\r\nBATMAN: Come on!\r\n\r\n00:15:32.682 --\u003e 00:15:33.975\r\nYou've got to get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.392 --\u003e 00:15:36.269\r\nCATWOMAN: Me? What about you?\r\n\r\n00:15:36.352 --\u003e 00:15:37.979\r\nThere's something\r\nI have to pick up.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.566 --\u003e 00:15:44.277\r\nWelcome to my little resort.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.530 --\u003e 00:15:49.574\r\nPlan on a short stay.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.417 --\u003e 00:16:01.169\r\n(BOTH STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:03.880 --\u003e 00:16:05.756\r\nIt's never dull, is it, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:16:06.215 --\u003e 00:16:07.884\r\nYou may be surprised to know\r\n\r\n00:16:07.967 --\u003e 00:16:11.304\r\nthese accommodations are\r\ncourtesy of your government.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.306 --\u003e 00:16:16.893\r\nThey built this top-secret\r\nfacility to shelter high officials\r\n\r\n00:16:16.976 --\u003e 00:16:19.312\r\nin case of a nuclear incident.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.605 --\u003e 00:16:23.649\r\nSince you wanted the plague so\r\nbadly, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:16:24.901 --\u003e 00:16:27.320\r\nwe've decided to give it to you.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.572 --\u003e 00:16:32.825\r\nWhat will you use to blackmail\r\nGotham if you waste it on us?\r\n\r\n00:16:33.284 --\u003e 00:16:36.162\r\nWhy risk carrying\r\nsuch deadly contents,\r\n\r\n00:16:36.245 --\u003e 00:16:38.331\r\nwhen a placebo will do?\r\n\r\n00:16:39.874 --\u003e 00:16:42.710\r\nBy the time they realize\r\nthe vial is a fake,\r\n\r\n00:16:42.835 --\u003e 00:16:46.672\r\nwe'll be miles away with\r\ntheir billion dollars.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.756 --\u003e 00:16:47.840\r\n(SIZZLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.591 --\u003e 00:16:51.260\r\nThe acid should eat through\r\nin a matter of minutes.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.802 --\u003e 00:16:55.264\r\nSound evacuation,\r\nand begin sealing the compound.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.557 --\u003e 00:16:59.519\r\nWe wouldn't want the plague\r\nto harm the precious wildlife,\r\n\r\n00:16:59.977 --\u003e 00:17:01.687\r\njust the vermin in here.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.483 --\u003e 00:17:08.361\r\nUgh. Would I like to\r\nget my claws into them.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.237 --\u003e 00:17:11.197\r\nIf I could just\r\nget some slack...\r\n\r\n00:17:12.156 --\u003e 00:17:14.784\r\nWhat this situation\r\nneeds is a woman's touch.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.121 --\u003e 00:17:20.414\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:17:28.464 --\u003e 00:17:29.674\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:17:31.842 --\u003e 00:17:33.052\r\nWhat a team.\r\n\r\n00:17:33.886 --\u003e 00:17:34.887\r\nCome on!\r\n\r\n00:17:38.975 --\u003e 00:17:40.560\r\n(ALARM CONTINUES BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.023 --\u003e 00:17:47.400\r\nYou've got to get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.817 --\u003e 00:17:49.068\r\nNot without you.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.694 --\u003e 00:17:50.987\r\nI'll be right behind you.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.237 --\u003e 00:17:53.239\r\nBut first,\r\nI've got to destroy the plague.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.906 --\u003e 00:17:54.907\r\nNow go!\r\n\r\n00:17:58.703 --\u003e 00:17:59.745\r\nPlease.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.996 --\u003e 00:19:25.164\r\n(RED CLAW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.221 --\u003e 00:19:41.847\r\n(YELLS ANGRILY)\r\n\r\n00:19:41.931 --\u003e 00:19:42.932\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.141 --\u003e 00:19:45.267\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.607 --\u003e 00:19:53.484\r\n\u003ci\u003e(OVER PM This is Police\r\nCommissioner Gordon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:53.943 --\u003e 00:19:55.611\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou're completely surrounded.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:55.861 --\u003e 00:19:57.196\r\n\u003ci\u003eGive yourselves up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:02.618 --\u003e 00:20:04.620\r\nRight where Batman\r\nsaid they'd be.\r\n\r\n00:20:05.454 --\u003e 00:20:07.415\r\nLooks like this\r\nresort is folding.\r\n\r\n00:20:07.748 --\u003e 00:20:08.791\r\n(CATWOMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:09.750 --\u003e 00:20:11.293\r\nRED CLAW: So are you.\r\n\r\n00:20:11.877 --\u003e 00:20:14.672\r\nFor years,\r\nI've fought to build my network.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.133 --\u003e 00:20:19.301\r\nI brought countries\r\nto their knees.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.013 --\u003e 00:20:25.891\r\nYou will pay, pussycat.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.727 --\u003e 00:20:28.894\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.478 --\u003e 00:20:33.441\r\nYou will learn why\r\neveryone fears Red Claw.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.860 --\u003e 00:20:36.986\r\n(ROARING)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.161 --\u003e 00:20:46.287\r\nThank you, friend.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.418 --\u003e 00:20:54.378\r\nSomething for you\r\nto remember me by.\r\n\r\n00:20:54.795 --\u003e 00:20:56.005\r\nHmm. (BLOWS KISS)\r\n\r\n00:21:01.677 --\u003e 00:21:03.387\r\nBatman, where's the virus?\r\n\r\n00:21:04.263 --\u003e 00:21:05.723\r\nIt went up in smoke,\r\n\r\n00:21:06.140 --\u003e 00:21:07.725\r\nwith Red Claw's future.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.434 --\u003e 00:21:11.061\r\nI should've known you'd have it\r\nall wrapped up before we got here.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.355 --\u003e 00:21:14.356\r\nAlmost.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.906 --\u003e 00:21:22.907\r\nMaven?\r\n\r\n00:21:25.034 --\u003e 00:21:26.035\r\nMaven?\r\n\r\n00:21:26.911 --\u003e 00:21:27.912\r\nShe's gone.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.704 --\u003e 00:21:30.748\r\nThe terrorists were\r\nafter both of you.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.208 --\u003e 00:21:35.544\r\nHave you told the police\r\nyou found your cat burglar?\r\n\r\n00:21:36.253 --\u003e 00:21:37.254\r\nBATMAN: Not yet.\r\n\r\n00:21:37.588 --\u003e 00:21:38.589\r\nCATWOMAN: Why not?\r\n\r\n00:21:39.423 --\u003e 00:21:41.926\r\nI didn't want you taken\r\naway like a common criminal.\r\n\r\n00:21:42.885 --\u003e 00:21:44.261\r\nSo, you do care.\r\n\r\n00:21:44.887 --\u003e 00:21:46.347\r\n(HANDCUFFS CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:21:49.642 --\u003e 00:21:51.560\r\nMore than you will ever know.\r\n\r\n00:21:58.943 --\u003e 00:22:00.945\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:19.713 --\u003e 00:22:20.714\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E09 - Pretty Poison (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.380 --\u003e 00:00:07.132\r\n(THEME some PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:33.093 --\u003e 00:01:34.553\r\nMy fellow citizens,\r\n\r\n00:01:34.636 --\u003e 00:01:37.889\r\nit is with great civic pride\r\nthat we gather here today\r\n\r\n00:01:37.973 --\u003e 00:01:41.143\r\nto break ground on the\r\nnew Gotham penitentiary,\r\n\r\n00:01:41.685 --\u003e 00:01:43.729\r\nwhich is been funded by\r\nthe Wayne Foundation.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.812 --\u003e 00:01:44.855\r\n(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:01:44.938 --\u003e 00:01:48.358\r\nAs you know,\r\nthis project was the dream of one man.\r\n\r\n00:01:48.984 --\u003e 00:01:51.153\r\nAnd he's with us here today.\r\n\r\n00:01:51.528 --\u003e 00:01:54.990\r\nGotham's new District\r\nAttorney, Harvey Dent.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.324 --\u003e 00:01:57.242\r\n(APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:01:58.035 --\u003e 00:02:02.039\r\nFrom this field of weeds and wild\r\nflowers will grow a new institution\r\n\r\n00:02:02.122 --\u003e 00:02:04.416\r\nto build a better, safer Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.209 --\u003e 00:02:07.878\r\n(APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:02:45.415 --\u003e 00:02:47.000\r\n(HELICOPTER WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:02:47.834 --\u003e 00:02:49.795\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:02:55.384 --\u003e 00:02:56.635\r\nGo! Go! Go!\r\n\r\n00:03:06.061 --\u003e 00:03:08.480\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:09.439 --\u003e 00:03:10.899\r\nThis is Gordon. What?\r\n\r\n00:03:11.983 --\u003e 00:03:14.319\r\nWe've got a prison break by air.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.403 --\u003e 00:03:16.113\r\nThe chopper's heading this way.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.675 --\u003e 00:03:39.136\r\n(LAUGHS) We're home free.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.437 --\u003e 00:03:50.021\r\nWhoa! What was that?\r\n\r\n00:03:50.105 --\u003e 00:03:51.189\r\nJust some turbulence.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.861 --\u003e 00:03:58.530\r\n(SIREN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:04:09.750 --\u003e 00:04:11.793\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SPEAKING FRENCH)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:14.963 --\u003e 00:04:16.298\r\nThank you, Andre.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.381 --\u003e 00:04:17.716\r\nI'm starving. Let's eat.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.302 --\u003e 00:04:21.678\r\n(SNIFFS)\r\n\r\n00:04:22.137 --\u003e 00:04:23.930\r\nShouldn't we wait\r\nfor your friend?\r\n\r\n00:04:24.014 --\u003e 00:04:27.476\r\nBruce? Nah. He's always late.\r\nHe probably got hung up on business.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.652 --\u003e 00:04:38.820\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:04:42.699 --\u003e 00:04:43.909\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:43.992 --\u003e 00:04:45.494\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\n00:04:48.622 --\u003e 00:04:49.998\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:04:51.166 --\u003e 00:04:52.584\r\nI hear he's rich.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.043 --\u003e 00:04:56.004\r\nYeah, Bruce runs around\r\nwith a high-class crowd.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.428 --\u003e 00:05:04.513\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:15.816 --\u003e 00:05:17.400\r\nBut he still manages\r\nto get his kicks.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.943 --\u003e 00:05:19.361\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:21.822 --\u003e 00:05:23.990\r\nThere's nothing we don't\r\nknow about each other.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.408 --\u003e 00:05:27.619\r\nWho... Who are you?\r\n\r\n00:05:28.119 --\u003e 00:05:30.038\r\nI'm your worst nightmare.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.247 --\u003e 00:05:31.748\r\n(HELICOPTER APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:32.082 --\u003e 00:05:34.876\r\nThis is the police! Nobody move!\r\n\r\n00:05:38.964 --\u003e 00:05:40.590\r\nI think you'll like him.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.674 --\u003e 00:05:42.425\r\nIf he's your friend,\r\nI know I will.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.593 --\u003e 00:05:45.011\r\nBig wings.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.470 --\u003e 00:05:48.390\r\nYeah, yeah, big wings.\r\nMove it along, pal.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.183 --\u003e 00:05:51.184\r\n(COMM BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:51.268 --\u003e 00:05:53.311\r\nAlfred, I'm running a\r\nlittle behind schedule.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.395 --\u003e 00:05:55.272\r\n\u003ci\u003eI have alerted Mr. Dent, sir.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:55.355 --\u003e 00:05:58.859\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe and Miss lsley patiently await\r\nyour arrival at the Rose Cafe.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:59.442 --\u003e 00:06:00.944\r\nHow's the food there?\r\n\r\n00:06:01.027 --\u003e 00:06:03.697\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn my humble opinion,\r\nsir, exquisite.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:09.411 --\u003e 00:06:11.496\r\n(BRAKES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:06:12.956 --\u003e 00:06:14.875\r\nI'll be taking the\r\nCord this evening.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.958 --\u003e 00:06:16.751\r\nAs I anticipated, sir.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.835 --\u003e 00:06:19.713\r\nIt is idling out front\r\nwith a full tank of gas.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.547 --\u003e 00:06:22.883\r\nALFRED: May I recommend\r\nthe Trout Amandine?\r\n\r\n00:06:23.258 --\u003e 00:06:25.010\r\nI'll give it a try, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.427 --\u003e 00:06:26.970\r\nWise decision, sir.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.053 --\u003e 00:06:28.138\r\nBon appetit.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.763 --\u003e 00:06:30.682\r\n(BRUCE LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:06:32.100 --\u003e 00:06:33.768\r\nYou should've seen\r\nHarvey's face.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.060 --\u003e 00:06:35.979\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:37.272 --\u003e 00:06:39.608\r\nOh, look at the time.\r\nI have to run.\r\n\r\n00:06:40.025 --\u003e 00:06:41.234\r\nSo soon?\r\n\r\n00:06:41.318 --\u003e 00:06:44.571\r\nI'm sorry. I have an early\r\nmeeting tomorrow. But you stay.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.905 --\u003e 00:06:47.324\r\n- No.\r\n- I insist.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.407 --\u003e 00:06:49.492\r\nSpend some time with\r\nyour crazy friend.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.118 --\u003e 00:06:53.830\r\nAnd call me the minute you get\r\nhome, Mr. District Attorney.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.594 --\u003e 00:07:08.720\r\nI'll call you.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.179 --\u003e 00:07:10.221\r\nGood.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.305 --\u003e 00:07:12.682\r\n- Nice meeting you, Bruce.\r\n- Same here.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.974 --\u003e 00:07:15.578\r\nWell, I've been talking to my broker,\r\nand his recommendation was that...\r\n\r\n00:07:15.602 --\u003e 00:07:16.937\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.774 --\u003e 00:07:23.610\r\n- So what do you think?\r\n- Does she have a sister?\r\n\r\n00:07:24.027 --\u003e 00:07:26.821\r\nNope. Pam's one of a kind.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.905 --\u003e 00:07:28.823\r\nThat's why I asked\r\nher to marry me.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.241 --\u003e 00:07:31.284\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:07:31.368 --\u003e 00:07:33.703\r\nYup. That's the Page 1 headline.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.787 --\u003e 00:07:36.873\r\n(GROANS) Is it\r\ngetting warm in here?\r\n\r\n00:07:37.165 --\u003e 00:07:39.709\r\nYou're still flushed\r\nfrom that last kiss.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.793 --\u003e 00:07:42.295\r\nHarvey,\r\nyou just met her last week.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.587 --\u003e 00:07:45.006\r\nAnd I already know\r\nshe's the one.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.173 --\u003e 00:07:46.800\r\nGosh, it's hot in here.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.050 --\u003e 00:07:49.344\r\nMarriage is a major step, Harv.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.427 --\u003e 00:07:52.180\r\n- Don't you think you're rushing it?\r\n- No way.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.389 --\u003e 00:07:56.184\r\nThe moment I laid eyes on Pam,\r\nlove hit me right in the face.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.643 --\u003e 00:07:58.103\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:00.897 --\u003e 00:08:04.025\r\n(CHUCKLES) Harv,\r\nyou've lost your mind.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.985 --\u003e 00:08:06.486\r\nKnock it off.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.861 --\u003e 00:08:08.571\r\nHarv? Harvey?\r\n\r\n00:08:13.702 --\u003e 00:08:15.704\r\nHang on, Harvey. Hang on.\r\n\r\n00:08:16.496 --\u003e 00:08:18.164\r\n- (DOOR CLOSES)\r\n- (SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:29.342 --\u003e 00:08:30.468\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:08:30.552 --\u003e 00:08:31.779\r\n- He's not breathing.\r\n- What's the blood pressure?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.803 --\u003e 00:08:33.304\r\nIsn't that the\r\nDistrict Attorney?\r\n\r\n00:08:34.139 --\u003e 00:08:35.783\r\n- Get his blood pressure, stat.\r\n- Get the EKG\r\n\r\n00:08:35.807 --\u003e 00:08:38.226\r\nand move him into OR,\r\nICU Number 3, stat.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.561 --\u003e 00:08:41.688\r\nDo we have a pulse?\r\nWe need a pulse here.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.357 --\u003e 00:08:47.777\r\nGet the EKG and move him into the\r\nOR, ICU Number 3, stat.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.320 --\u003e 00:08:50.864\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.782 --\u003e 00:08:54.451\r\nThis is Gordon. What?\r\n\r\n00:08:55.577 --\u003e 00:08:58.371\r\nHarvey Dent's in a coma at\r\nthe medical center. Move out.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.088 --\u003e 00:09:08.923\r\n(SIREN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:09:16.639 --\u003e 00:09:18.391\r\n(BEEPING RAPIDLY)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.899 --\u003e 00:09:29.402\r\nSo, what's the story, Doctor?\r\nHeart attack?\r\n\r\n00:09:29.736 --\u003e 00:09:33.114\r\nNo, Commissioner.\r\nMr. Dent has been poisoned.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.698 --\u003e 00:09:37.786\r\nFor criminy sakes.\r\nBullock, get down to that restaurant.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.994 --\u003e 00:09:41.206\r\n- What's it called, Wayne?\r\n- Uh, the Rose Cafe.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.623 --\u003e 00:09:44.667\r\nThe Rose Cafe.\r\nAnd find out who did this.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.751 --\u003e 00:09:46.086\r\nWith pleasure.\r\n\r\n00:09:46.628 --\u003e 00:09:49.130\r\nI want police guards on\r\nduty here around the clock.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.422 --\u003e 00:09:50.548\r\nYes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.883 --\u003e 00:09:55.095\r\n\u003ci\u003eNURSE: (OVER PA) Dr. Forrest,\r\ndial 118, please.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:58.723 --\u003e 00:10:00.225\r\n\u003ci\u003eDr. Kravitz...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:00.308 --\u003e 00:10:04.145\r\nExcuse me, Doctor.\r\nAre we talking about food poisoning here?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.229 --\u003e 00:10:05.271\r\nI doubt it.\r\n\r\n00:10:05.355 --\u003e 00:10:08.233\r\nThis is the most virulent strain\r\nof poison I've ever come across.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.316 --\u003e 00:10:10.276\r\nWe're doing everything we\r\ncan, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:12.195\r\nIs Harvey going to make it?\r\n\r\n00:10:12.278 --\u003e 00:10:14.239\r\nThe poison is racing\r\nthrough his system.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.322 --\u003e 00:10:18.284\r\nIf he's going to make it,\r\nwe need to find the antidote, and fast.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.971 --\u003e 00:10:40.390\r\nSo what'd you put\r\nin this mousse?\r\n\r\n00:10:40.682 --\u003e 00:10:43.768\r\nChocolate, sugar, eggs, cream...\r\n\r\n00:10:44.435 --\u003e 00:10:45.979\r\nStrychnine?\r\n\r\n00:10:46.062 --\u003e 00:10:47.814\r\nNo, no, no. No strychnine.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.231 --\u003e 00:10:50.775\r\nBut I added just a\r\npinch of vanilla.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.526 --\u003e 00:10:53.528\r\nYou know who did it? Talk!\r\n\r\n00:10:54.112 --\u003e 00:10:56.322\r\nHey, I just clean the\r\ndishes, okay?\r\n\r\n00:10:56.656 --\u003e 00:10:58.533\r\n(KEYBOARD CLACKING)\r\n\r\n00:11:01.286 --\u003e 00:11:03.663\r\nWe've isolated the\r\ntoxin, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.040 --\u003e 00:11:08.042\r\nIndeed we have, sir.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.126 --\u003e 00:11:13.131\r\nIt is a lethal poison derived\r\nfrom the plant Rosaceae Vularis,\r\n\r\n00:11:13.464 --\u003e 00:11:16.426\r\ncommonly known as\r\nthe wild thorny rose.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.593 --\u003e 00:11:19.429\r\nI'll get a plant sample from\r\nthe Gotham Botanical Gardens.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.721 --\u003e 00:11:21.931\r\nWe can use it to\r\nwork up an antidote.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.765 --\u003e 00:11:25.685\r\n- I'm afraid this is unfeasible.\r\n- Why?\r\n\r\n00:11:25.768 --\u003e 00:11:30.273\r\nBecause, sir, the wild thorny rose has\r\nbeen extinct for nearly five years.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.899 --\u003e 00:11:33.985\r\n- Which means, I'm afraid...\r\n- There's no antidote.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.323 --\u003e 00:11:39.324\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:11:53.671 --\u003e 00:11:55.715\r\nFight, Harvey, fight.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.716 --\u003e 00:11:57.759\r\n(ELEVATOR DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:11:58.760 --\u003e 00:12:01.638\r\nOh, Bruce,\r\nI came as soon as I got your call.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.055 --\u003e 00:12:04.182\r\n- How is he?\r\n- We're not sure.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.850 --\u003e 00:12:08.853\r\n- I want to see him.\r\n- Sorry, ma'am, no visitors.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.978 --\u003e 00:12:10.605\r\nCommissioner Gordon's orders.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.775 --\u003e 00:12:15.443\r\n(SOB$)\r\n\r\n00:12:15.944 --\u003e 00:12:20.073\r\nYou should try to get some sleep.\r\nCome on, I'll walk you to your car.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.287 --\u003e 00:12:28.748\r\n(SNIFFLES) Promise to call\r\nme if there's any change?\r\n\r\n00:12:29.123 --\u003e 00:12:31.459\r\nI will. You get some rest.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.834 --\u003e 00:12:34.504\r\nHarvey's lucky to have\r\nsuch a good friend.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.802 --\u003e 00:12:43.179\r\n- Goodnight, Bruce.\r\n- Goodnight, Pam.\r\n\r\n00:12:45.223 --\u003e 00:12:46.683\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:55.483 --\u003e 00:12:56.651\r\nALFRED: Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.734 --\u003e 00:12:59.570\r\nBRUCE: Alfred,\r\ndig up anything you can on Pamela lsley.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.654 --\u003e 00:13:02.699\r\nWho she is, where she's been,\r\nwhat she does... The works.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.991 --\u003e 00:13:04.367\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: Consider it done, sir.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:11.749 --\u003e 00:13:12.959\r\nWhat do you have, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:13:13.084 --\u003e 00:13:15.545\r\nWell, sir,\r\nMiss lsley is a research chemist\r\n\r\n00:13:15.795 --\u003e 00:13:18.381\r\nwith Chez Gerard,\r\nthe cosmetics firm.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.840 --\u003e 00:13:21.676\r\nShe works on the development\r\nof new fragrances.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.968 --\u003e 00:13:25.263\r\nTheir newest is a perfume\r\ncalled Nightshade.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.680 --\u003e 00:13:27.307\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's deadly.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:28.057 --\u003e 00:13:31.811\r\nMiss lsley has a PhD in\r\nbotany from Gotham University,\r\n\r\n00:13:32.186 --\u003e 00:13:34.731\r\nwhere she offers a\r\nmonthly lecture series\r\n\r\n00:13:34.814 --\u003e 00:13:37.567\r\non endangered and\r\nextinct plant species.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.734 --\u003e 00:13:39.068\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:39.527 --\u003e 00:13:42.113\r\nI think Harvey's\r\nengagement is off.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.829 --\u003e 00:14:35.375\r\nOh, you've done so well\r\ntoday, sweetheart.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.541 --\u003e 00:14:37.293\r\nNow get some rest.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.627 --\u003e 00:14:41.923\r\nAnd don't worry, I won't clip off\r\nany more of your beautiful petals\r\n\r\n00:14:42.090 --\u003e 00:14:43.841\r\nunless I need them.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.478 --\u003e 00:14:57.897\r\n(GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:15:17.542 --\u003e 00:15:19.419\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:20.503 --\u003e 00:15:22.088\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:29.971 --\u003e 00:15:30.972\r\n(CHIRPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.055 --\u003e 00:15:32.223\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:15:38.563 --\u003e 00:15:40.022\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:57.665 --\u003e 00:15:59.292\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:00.918 --\u003e 00:16:04.088\r\nWhat has my sweet little\r\nflytrap caught this time?\r\n\r\n00:16:17.101 --\u003e 00:16:19.479\r\nUm, a little big for a fly.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.522 --\u003e 00:16:23.191\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.533 --\u003e 00:16:34.952\r\nPAM: (LAUGHS) Batman.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.411 --\u003e 00:16:38.873\r\nA late night rendezvous?\r\nTo what do I owe the honor?\r\n\r\n00:16:38.956 --\u003e 00:16:41.042\r\n(GROANING) Harvey Dent.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.751 --\u003e 00:16:44.128\r\nOh, the poor District Attorney.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.504 --\u003e 00:16:46.881\r\nI hear he's not\r\nexpected to live.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.215 --\u003e 00:16:49.550\r\nOh, it's so sad.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.842 --\u003e 00:16:51.844\r\n(SOB$)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.969 --\u003e 00:16:55.306\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:55.598 --\u003e 00:16:56.974\r\nWhy, lsley?\r\n\r\n00:16:57.350 --\u003e 00:17:00.603\r\nOh, please, call me Poison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.854 --\u003e 00:17:04.857\r\nYou see,\r\nHarvey had to pay for his crime.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.316 --\u003e 00:17:06.692\r\nWhat crime?\r\n\r\n00:17:07.318 --\u003e 00:17:09.403\r\nWhy, murder, of course.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.946 --\u003e 00:17:12.323\r\nPlowing up a field of\r\nbeautiful wild flowers\r\n\r\n00:17:12.406 --\u003e 00:17:14.784\r\nfor that silly\r\npenitentiary of his.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.159 --\u003e 00:17:19.539\r\nThis little rose would be extinct\r\ntoday, if I hadn't saved my precious\r\n\r\n00:17:19.622 --\u003e 00:17:21.832\r\nfrom those horrible bulldozers.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.209 --\u003e 00:17:26.212\r\nThe blood of those\r\nflowers are on his hands.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.338 --\u003e 00:17:29.090\r\n(GRUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:17:30.550 --\u003e 00:17:32.385\r\nUh... (CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.468 --\u003e 00:17:33.761\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.470 --\u003e 00:17:36.138\r\nSo his fate was sealed...\r\n\r\n00:17:40.726 --\u003e 00:17:42.228\r\nWith a kiss.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.020 --\u003e 00:17:44.272\r\nAnd now,\r\n\r\n00:17:44.355 --\u003e 00:17:46.274\r\nso is yours.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.233 --\u003e 00:17:48.776\r\n(BATMAN STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:58.828 --\u003e 00:18:02.540\r\nOh, what's wrong?\r\nAfraid I have cooties?\r\n\r\n00:18:02.623 --\u003e 00:18:04.458\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:18:04.625 --\u003e 00:18:05.918\r\n- (SPITS)\r\n- Oh...\r\n\r\n00:18:06.043 --\u003e 00:18:08.713\r\nNow you've gone and\r\nhurt my feelings.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.130 --\u003e 00:18:12.717\r\nToo bad. I was going to\r\nshare the antidote with you.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.342 --\u003e 00:18:14.760\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.219 --\u003e 00:18:17.430\r\nLovely fragrance,\r\ndon't you think?\r\n\r\n00:18:20.600 --\u003e 00:18:23.060\r\nI call it \"Rose From the Dead.\"\r\n\r\n00:18:23.811 --\u003e 00:18:25.146\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:45.541 --\u003e 00:18:47.835\r\n(ROARING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.378 --\u003e 00:18:50.504\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:18:56.927 --\u003e 00:18:58.179\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:01.015 --\u003e 00:19:02.433\r\nMurderer!\r\n\r\n00:19:05.353 --\u003e 00:19:06.896\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:07.688 --\u003e 00:19:09.273\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.638 --\u003e 00:19:42.932\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:55.611 --\u003e 00:19:56.987\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:01.117 --\u003e 00:20:02.493\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:10.376 --\u003e 00:20:11.711\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:16.340 --\u003e 00:20:17.842\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:20:20.553 --\u003e 00:20:22.012\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:22.304 --\u003e 00:20:25.641\r\nEnjoy extinction, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.100 --\u003e 00:20:27.852\r\nI'm not going alone.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.645 --\u003e 00:20:30.896\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:31.313 --\u003e 00:20:33.983\r\nThe bottle for the weed.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.567 --\u003e 00:20:36.402\r\nWhat's it going to be?\r\n\r\n00:20:36.485 --\u003e 00:20:37.862\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.613 --\u003e 00:20:41.407\r\nMy baby.\r\n\r\n00:20:41.699 --\u003e 00:20:43.576\r\nMy precious baby!\r\n\r\n00:20:51.792 --\u003e 00:20:53.669\r\nMy pretty baby.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.257 --\u003e 00:20:59.467\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:21:01.761 --\u003e 00:21:04.388\r\n- Where am I?\r\n- You're in the hospital.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.764 --\u003e 00:21:06.766\r\nWhy? What happened?\r\n\r\n00:21:07.308 --\u003e 00:21:10.060\r\nYou passed out into\r\nyour chocolate mousse.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.186 --\u003e 00:21:12.021\r\nBut you're going to be fine.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.354 --\u003e 00:21:15.524\r\nNow, Harv, about your\r\nengagement to Pamela lsley...\r\n\r\n00:21:15.941 --\u003e 00:21:17.735\r\n- We're good friends, right?\r\n- Mmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.818 --\u003e 00:21:19.612\r\nI have to be honest with\r\nyou, don't I?\r\n\r\n00:21:19.695 --\u003e 00:21:21.155\r\n- Mmm-hmm.\r\n- Okay, then...\r\n\r\n00:21:21.655 --\u003e 00:21:23.282\r\nI think Pam is wrong for you.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.365 --\u003e 00:21:24.450\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:21:33.000 --\u003e 00:21:37.421\r\nThey can bury me in the\r\nground as deep as they like.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.714 --\u003e 00:21:40.424\r\nBut I'll grow back.\r\n\r\n00:21:40.716 --\u003e 00:21:42.468\r\nWe always grow back.\r\n\r\n00:21:43.427 --\u003e 00:21:44.970\r\nDon't we, baby?\r\n\r\n00:21:50.976 --\u003e 00:21:53.687\r\n(THEME some PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:17.253 --\u003e 00:22:18.254\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E10 - Nothing to Fear (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:08.967 --\u003e 00:00:10.802\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.851 --\u003e 00:01:42.853\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:42.936 --\u003e 00:01:45.606\r\nIt's a tragedy what's been\r\nhappening to the university.\r\n\r\n00:01:45.689 --\u003e 00:01:48.567\r\nWOMAN: Robberies, vandalism.\r\nMAN: Where will it end?\r\n\r\n00:01:50.611 --\u003e 00:01:52.571\r\nDr. Long! Dr. Long,\r\n\r\n00:01:52.654 --\u003e 00:01:54.948\r\nI'm Summer Gleeson\r\nwith Gotham Insider.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.032 --\u003e 00:01:57.743\r\nCan I ask you a few questions\r\nabout the recent robberies?\r\n\r\n00:01:57.826 --\u003e 00:01:59.077\r\nAll right, but I'm in a hurry.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.161 --\u003e 00:02:01.038\r\nDr. Long, do you have any idea\r\n\r\n00:02:01.121 --\u003e 00:02:03.749\r\nwhy someone would want to\r\ndestroy the university?\r\n\r\n00:02:04.249 --\u003e 00:02:05.917\r\nNo, but one more disaster\r\n\r\n00:02:06.001 --\u003e 00:02:08.754\r\nand students will be afraid\r\nto set foot on this campus.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.673 --\u003e 00:02:13.050\r\nBRUCE: Hello, Summer.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.133 --\u003e 00:02:15.385\r\nBruce! What a pleasant surprise.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.520 --\u003e 00:02:28.023\r\nDr. Long,\r\nhave you met Bruce Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:02:29.816 --\u003e 00:02:32.319\r\nYour father and I attended\r\nuniversity together.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.402 --\u003e 00:02:35.656\r\n- He had big plans for you.\r\n- Well, I guess he'd be pleased.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.739 --\u003e 00:02:38.075\r\nWayne Industries is more\r\nprosperous than ever.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.158 --\u003e 00:02:40.327\r\nPleased?\r\nWhen your father was alive,\r\n\r\n00:02:40.410 --\u003e 00:02:43.080\r\nWayne was a name that\r\ncommanded great respect.\r\n\r\n00:02:43.163 --\u003e 00:02:48.293\r\nNow, all Wayne stands for is a\r\nself-centered, jet-setting playboy.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.377 --\u003e 00:02:51.672\r\nIt's lucky your father didn't live to\r\nsee what you've done to his good name.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.755 --\u003e 00:02:53.715\r\nHe'd have died of shame.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.257 --\u003e 00:02:57.427\r\nWait, Dr. Long,\r\nI haven't finished the interview.\r\n\r\n00:02:57.636 --\u003e 00:03:01.682\r\nHe's probably just venting his anger\r\nover what's happening to the university.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.167 --\u003e 00:03:30.502\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:04.035 --\u003e 00:04:05.829\r\nHold it right there!\r\n\r\n00:04:08.665 --\u003e 00:04:10.167\r\nHey, what are you...\r\n\r\n00:04:10.250 --\u003e 00:04:11.460\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:04:11.543 --\u003e 00:04:13.211\r\nStop! What the...\r\n\r\n00:04:13.420 --\u003e 00:04:15.130\r\nNo! No, spiders!\r\n\r\n00:04:15.714 --\u003e 00:04:18.675\r\nGet them off of me! No! No!\r\n\r\n00:04:19.426 --\u003e 00:04:21.595\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:04:22.304 --\u003e 00:04:24.347\r\nWhat did you do to him, boss?\r\n\r\n00:04:24.431 --\u003e 00:04:27.726\r\nI merely helped him visualize\r\nhis innermost terror,\r\n\r\n00:04:27.934 --\u003e 00:04:30.562\r\nwhich is obviously\r\narachnophobia.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.896 --\u003e 00:04:33.732\r\n- A-whack-a-what?\r\n- Arachnophobia.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.065 --\u003e 00:04:36.777\r\nFear of spiders,\r\nyou dimwitted dropout!\r\n\r\n00:04:37.277 --\u003e 00:04:38.904\r\nNow, to the vault.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.579 --\u003e 00:04:51.333\r\n- Nigel, you'll stand guard here.\r\n- I'm ready for anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.425 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nCome to Papa.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.344 --\u003e 00:05:04.888\r\nTake what you can,\r\nthen burn the rest.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.971 --\u003e 00:05:06.348\r\nBurn it, boss?\r\n\r\n00:05:06.431 --\u003e 00:05:09.059\r\nThis isn't about money,\r\nit's about revenge.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.239 --\u003e 00:05:26.117\r\nHENCHMAN: Help, boss! It's the Batman.\r\nHe's got me... (MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.618 --\u003e 00:05:29.037\r\nClimb up there and\r\nwait for my signal.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.120 --\u003e 00:05:30.539\r\nSure thing, boss.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.166 --\u003e 00:05:34.960\r\n(HENCHMAN SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.043 --\u003e 00:05:37.045\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:44.928 --\u003e 00:05:46.513\r\nSCARECROW: Welcome, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.432 --\u003e 00:05:50.892\r\nOh, a gas mask.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.226 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nPerhaps you are as\r\nresourceful as they say.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.938 --\u003e 00:05:55.981\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:05:56.398 --\u003e 00:05:58.275\r\nI am fear incarnate.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:03.363\r\nI am the terror of Gotham.\r\nI am the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.447 --\u003e 00:06:06.741\r\nGive it up. There's no way out.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.158 --\u003e 00:06:08.910\r\nExcept through you.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.792 --\u003e 00:06:18.962\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:31.683 --\u003e 00:06:33.852\r\nFight all you want, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:06:34.311 --\u003e 00:06:36.688\r\nbut you must\r\nsuccumb to the fear.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.024 --\u003e 00:06:42.694\r\nWhat hidden terror keeps\r\nthe Batman awake at night?\r\n\r\n00:06:44.696 --\u003e 00:06:47.365\r\nCome on, you cretins.\r\nMy work is done.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.721 --\u003e 00:07:10.889\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: Bruce.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:11.932 --\u003e 00:07:13.058\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:07:13.850 --\u003e 00:07:15.101\r\nCan't be.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.519 --\u003e 00:07:17.771\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: Bruce...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:18.229 --\u003e 00:07:20.273\r\n\u003ci\u003eBruce, you have failed me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:20.982 --\u003e 00:07:22.192\r\nFather?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.443 --\u003e 00:07:25.946\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou have disgraced\r\nthe family name.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:51.429 --\u003e 00:07:52.597\r\nWait.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.856 --\u003e 00:08:03.733\r\nBatman, what happened?\r\n\r\n00:08:03.817 --\u003e 00:08:05.193\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.276 --\u003e 00:08:06.611\r\nScarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.820 --\u003e 00:08:09.239\r\nScarecrow? What do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:08:09.406 --\u003e 00:08:12.117\r\nHe's right. (COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.200 --\u003e 00:08:14.619\r\nIt was some guy dressed\r\nlike a scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.703 --\u003e 00:08:17.914\r\nHe tried to torch the bank,\r\nbut Batman stopped him.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.998 --\u003e 00:08:21.126\r\nAll right, then.\r\nWhere is this scarecrow?\r\n\r\n00:08:21.418 --\u003e 00:08:22.919\r\nWell, he got away.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.586 --\u003e 00:08:27.382\r\nYou mean the Commissioner's\r\npet bat here let him get away?\r\n\r\n00:08:27.841 --\u003e 00:08:30.260\r\nWhat do you got\r\nthere, vigilante?\r\n\r\n00:08:30.468 --\u003e 00:08:32.137\r\nLooks like police evidence.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.804 --\u003e 00:08:34.723\r\nGive it up. Now!\r\n\r\n00:08:36.850 --\u003e 00:08:39.310\r\nOoh, looks like I'm going\r\nto have to take it from you.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.061 --\u003e 00:08:43.064\r\nBullock,\r\nwhat the blazes is going on here?\r\n\r\n00:08:43.148 --\u003e 00:08:46.109\r\n\"Blaze\" is right, Commissioner.\r\nIt's attempted arson.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.192 --\u003e 00:08:48.486\r\nZorro here is\r\nwithholding evid...\r\n\r\n00:08:49.404 --\u003e 00:08:50.780\r\nWhere the...\r\n\r\n00:08:50.864 --\u003e 00:08:52.532\r\nYou were saying?\r\n\r\n00:08:52.741 --\u003e 00:08:54.743\r\nAh, never mind.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.005 --\u003e 00:09:08.858\r\n\u003ci\u003eSUMMER: (ON TV) Tonight's\r\narson attempt by someone\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:08.882 --\u003e 00:09:10.717\r\n\u003ci\u003ecalling himself the \"Scarecrow\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:10.800 --\u003e 00:09:12.302\r\n\u003ci\u003ewas thwarted by Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:12.385 --\u003e 00:09:15.305\r\nIt seems I have\r\nunderestimated the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.388 --\u003e 00:09:17.766\r\nBut at least the\r\nuniversity is finished.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.849 --\u003e 00:09:19.976\r\nANTHONY: Gee, boss,\r\nI never liked school.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.060 --\u003e 00:09:23.063\r\nBut how come you hate\r\nthe university so much?\r\n\r\n00:09:23.146 --\u003e 00:09:25.148\r\nThey tried to destroy me.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.523 --\u003e 00:09:28.276\r\nYou mean they kicked you out\r\n'cause you weren't smart enough?\r\n\r\n00:09:28.359 --\u003e 00:09:30.403\r\n- No, you simpleton.\r\n- Ow!\r\n\r\n00:09:31.279 --\u003e 00:09:32.614\r\nI taught there.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.697 --\u003e 00:09:36.284\r\nI was a professor of psychology,\r\nspecializing in phobias.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.367 --\u003e 00:09:39.120\r\nInducing terror has\r\nalways intrigued me.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.121 --\u003e 00:09:42.916\r\n\u003ci\u003eEven as a boy,\r\nI loved to frighten things.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:42.999 --\u003e 00:09:45.335\r\n\u003ci\u003ePeople, animals,\r\nit was all the same.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:45.418 --\u003e 00:09:48.421\r\n\u003ci\u003eI became obsessed with\r\nfear's crippling power.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:49.798 --\u003e 00:09:52.717\r\n\u003ci\u003eLater, when I became\r\ntheir leading professor\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:52.801 --\u003e 00:09:55.053\r\n\u003ci\u003eof subliminal psychology\r\nat the university,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:55.136 --\u003e 00:10:00.225\r\n\u003ci\u003eI began performing experiments on\r\nfear and its subsequent effects.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:00.308 --\u003e 00:10:02.644\r\n\u003ci\u003eDr. Long thought I went too far.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:03.144 --\u003e 00:10:05.063\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe called me a lunatic.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:06.022 --\u003e 00:10:10.068\r\nSo now, they will learn\r\nthe true nature of horror.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.318 --\u003e 00:10:12.320\r\nWow. He's a real professor.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.082 --\u003e 00:10:26.584\r\n\u003ci\u003eANNOUNCER: (ON TV) You'll\r\nfeel like a million dollars.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:36.177 --\u003e 00:10:38.555\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Exhibit\r\nA, scarecrow mask.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:38.888 --\u003e 00:10:40.431\r\n\u003ci\u003eWill analyze and\r\ncross-reference.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:40.515 --\u003e 00:10:42.684\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:10:50.233 --\u003e 00:10:52.152\r\nTHOMAS WAYNE: You've failed\r\nme, son.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.571 --\u003e 00:10:58.241\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Summer Gleeson,\r\nback live at the Gotham State University.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:58.324 --\u003e 00:11:00.660\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe campus bank was\r\nthe target of a robbery\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:00.743 --\u003e 00:11:04.247\r\n\u003ci\u003eand a malicious arson attempt\r\nby the so-called Scarecrow.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:04.330 --\u003e 00:11:06.791\r\n\u003ci\u003eThough the Batman\r\ndid thwart the arson,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:06.875 --\u003e 00:11:09.085\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe failed to catch\r\nthe perpetrators.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:09.169 --\u003e 00:11:11.337\r\n\u003ci\u003eFailed to catch\r\nthe perpetrators.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:11.421 --\u003e 00:11:13.923\r\n\u003ci\u003eFailed. Failed. Failed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:15.008 --\u003e 00:11:17.802\r\n- Imagine that, sir.\r\n- Huh? What?\r\n\r\n00:11:17.886 --\u003e 00:11:20.763\r\nSomeone dressed up in\r\na frightening costume,\r\n\r\n00:11:20.847 --\u003e 00:11:22.682\r\nrunning around scaring people.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.765 --\u003e 00:11:24.684\r\nWhat will they think of next?\r\n\r\n00:11:25.101 --\u003e 00:11:26.769\r\nThe question is,\r\n\r\n00:11:27.103 --\u003e 00:11:30.732\r\nwhy would Scarecrow want\r\nto destroy the university?\r\n\r\n00:11:31.065 --\u003e 00:11:33.193\r\nPerhaps he flunked Phys. Ed.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.236 --\u003e 00:11:36.613\r\nAre you all right, sir?\r\n\r\n00:11:36.696 --\u003e 00:11:40.491\r\nThe Scarecrow drugged me\r\nwith some kind of fear toxin.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.034 --\u003e 00:11:42.869\r\nI never know when\r\nit's going to hit me.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.453 --\u003e 00:11:47.373\r\nI'm having horrible\r\nvisions of my father.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.627 --\u003e 00:11:53.171\r\nHe says I'm shaming\r\nthe family name.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.464 --\u003e 00:11:55.965\r\nThat's rubbish.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.299 --\u003e 00:11:58.218\r\nI know your father\r\nwould be proud of you,\r\n\r\n00:11:58.301 --\u003e 00:12:01.721\r\nbecause I'm so proud of you.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.804 --\u003e 00:12:04.933\r\nCome on, it's time for chicken\r\nsoup and a good night's sleep.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.392 --\u003e 00:12:08.061\r\n- Alfred.\r\n- Yes, sir?\r\n\r\n00:12:08.603 --\u003e 00:12:09.646\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.570 --\u003e 00:12:20.657\r\n- (CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n- (PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.586 --\u003e 00:12:35.213\r\n- MAN: Hey, what's that?\r\n- (GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:12:36.547 --\u003e 00:12:38.258\r\nWOMAN: We're being gassed!\r\n\r\n00:12:38.341 --\u003e 00:12:40.426\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:47.767 --\u003e 00:12:49.602\r\n(PANICKED CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:50.395 --\u003e 00:12:52.438\r\nWOMAN: They've got guns!\r\nMAN: Guns?\r\n\r\n00:12:54.274 --\u003e 00:12:56.025\r\nSCARECROW: Thank you, Dr. Long.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.109 --\u003e 00:12:57.527\r\nI'll take that.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.652 --\u003e 00:13:00.863\r\n- Over my dead body.\r\n- If you insist.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.947 --\u003e 00:13:02.740\r\nOh! (Couemue)\r\n\r\n00:13:02.824 --\u003e 00:13:04.367\r\nWhat's happening?\r\n\r\n00:13:04.450 --\u003e 00:13:06.452\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:06.536 --\u003e 00:13:07.537\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:13:08.246 --\u003e 00:13:09.372\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:10.498 --\u003e 00:13:12.250\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:12.333 --\u003e 00:13:15.295\r\nBring him.\r\nHis torture has just begun.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.880 --\u003e 00:13:20.925\r\n(PANICKED CHATTERING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.759 --\u003e 00:13:23.928\r\nNo! Get them off my back!\r\n\r\n00:13:30.268 --\u003e 00:13:33.146\r\nBatman, I am surprised.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.438 --\u003e 00:13:37.358\r\nI thought you'd be home enjoying\r\nmy time-released fear toxin.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.442 --\u003e 00:13:38.526\r\n(SCARECROW LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:38.609 --\u003e 00:13:39.652\r\n(ALL GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:39.736 --\u003e 00:13:41.612\r\nSCARECROW: Welcome to\r\neveryone's worst fear.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.696 --\u003e 00:13:43.323\r\nIsn't it invigorating?\r\n\r\n00:13:43.406 --\u003e 00:13:45.033\r\nIt's a giant bat!\r\n\r\n00:13:50.204 --\u003e 00:13:51.497\r\nGet him!\r\n\r\n00:13:51.581 --\u003e 00:13:54.000\r\n(ALL YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:54.083 --\u003e 00:13:55.418\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.501 --\u003e 00:13:58.463\r\nMarvelous. Simply marvelous.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.553 --\u003e 00:14:49.430\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.514 --\u003e 00:14:51.391\r\nMy revenge is complete.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.849 --\u003e 00:14:57.146\r\nThe university is in the grip of\r\nfear, and Batman has been annihilated.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.355 --\u003e 00:14:58.398\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:14:58.606 --\u003e 00:15:02.110\r\nAnnihilated. Destroyed. Dead.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.193 --\u003e 00:15:03.444\r\nThen who's that?\r\n\r\n00:15:05.279 --\u003e 00:15:08.449\r\nI don't believe it.\r\nAnthony, take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.658 --\u003e 00:15:09.867\r\nWho, me?\r\n\r\n00:15:09.951 --\u003e 00:15:12.453\r\n- Er... But, boss...\r\n- Do it!\r\n\r\n00:15:21.963 --\u003e 00:15:23.381\r\nEnd of the line.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.049 --\u003e 00:15:26.092\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:29.679 --\u003e 00:15:31.347\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:32.640 --\u003e 00:15:33.933\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:15:49.532 --\u003e 00:15:52.493\r\n- Do something.\r\n- Me? You're the genius.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.827 --\u003e 00:15:54.203\r\nOh, no! Look!\r\n\r\n00:16:01.169 --\u003e 00:16:03.546\r\n(ANTHONY SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:08.926 --\u003e 00:16:10.428\r\nANTHONY: Help!\r\n\r\n00:16:10.511 --\u003e 00:16:12.263\r\n(ANTHONY SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.527 --\u003e 00:16:28.362\r\nWhat are we going to\r\ndo, Professor?\r\n\r\n00:16:28.446 --\u003e 00:16:31.324\r\nI believe we can leave\r\nit to my fear toxin.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.410 --\u003e 00:16:35.828\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.912 --\u003e 00:16:37.079\r\nTHOMAS WAYNE: Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.209 --\u003e 00:16:43.085\r\nNo, not now.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.503 --\u003e 00:16:45.671\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou are a disgrace.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:46.088 --\u003e 00:16:48.382\r\nNo! No!\r\n\r\n00:16:48.549 --\u003e 00:16:52.261\r\nYou are not my father.\r\nI am not a disgrace.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.012 --\u003e 00:16:54.680\r\nI am vengeance.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.056 --\u003e 00:16:56.599\r\nI am the night.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.141 --\u003e 00:16:59.769\r\nI am Batman!\r\n\r\n00:17:23.417 --\u003e 00:17:24.460\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:30.758 --\u003e 00:17:32.009\r\nStop him!\r\n\r\n00:17:33.678 --\u003e 00:17:34.887\r\nGotcha!\r\n\r\n00:17:50.528 --\u003e 00:17:51.696\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.239 --\u003e 00:17:55.408\r\nNo. No more prison walls.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.659 --\u003e 00:17:59.078\r\nThey're closing in on me. No!\r\n\r\n00:18:00.121 --\u003e 00:18:01.122\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:18:07.837 --\u003e 00:18:09.755\r\nIt's over, Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.839 --\u003e 00:18:12.383\r\nOnly for you and the\r\ndoctor, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.466 --\u003e 00:18:14.802\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.238 --\u003e 00:18:37.074\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- Just hold on.\r\n\r\n00:18:37.158 --\u003e 00:18:38.284\r\nBut how?\r\n\r\n00:19:09.774 --\u003e 00:19:13.611\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Exhibit A, scarecrow mask.\r\nAnalysis complete.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:14.111 --\u003e 00:19:17.740\r\n\u003ci\u003eSubstance is manufactured by\r\nfive corporations in Gotham City.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:18.199 --\u003e 00:19:20.910\r\n\u003ci\u003eAxis Engineering,\r\nBio Laboratories,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:20.993 --\u003e 00:19:24.830\r\n\u003ci\u003eCrane Chemicals,\r\nMacurity Manufacturing, Star Labs.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:24.914 --\u003e 00:19:27.583\r\nComputer,\r\ncross-reference former employees\r\n\r\n00:19:27.667 --\u003e 00:19:30.628\r\nof Gotham State University\r\nwith the chemical labs.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.711 --\u003e 00:19:32.046\r\n\u003ci\u003eSearching.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:32.129 --\u003e 00:19:34.674\r\n\u003ci\u003eFound. One Jonathan Crane.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:35.132 --\u003e 00:19:37.551\r\n\u003ci\u003eOwner,\r\noperator of Crane Chemicals.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:37.635 --\u003e 00:19:39.053\r\nBackground on Crane.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.136 --\u003e 00:19:41.597\r\n\u003ci\u003eSearching.\r\nFormer professor of psychology.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:41.681 --\u003e 00:19:44.767\r\n\u003ci\u003eSpecialty, fear and phobias.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:44.850 --\u003e 00:19:46.018\r\nBingo.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.947 --\u003e 00:19:59.281\r\nIt's not fair.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.365 --\u003e 00:20:01.325\r\nRevenge was within my grasp.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.409 --\u003e 00:20:02.910\r\nI was so close.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.993 --\u003e 00:20:05.621\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:20:05.705 --\u003e 00:20:06.956\r\nHmm?\r\n\r\n00:20:12.628 --\u003e 00:20:14.547\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:20:14.630 --\u003e 00:20:15.840\r\nWhat's going on?\r\n\r\n00:20:18.759 --\u003e 00:20:20.177\r\nWho's there?\r\n\r\n00:20:22.972 --\u003e 00:20:24.098\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.181 --\u003e 00:20:25.474\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.270 --\u003e 00:20:30.896\r\nNo. Please.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.980 --\u003e 00:20:32.940\r\n(YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.661 --\u003e 00:20:48.205\r\nNo, stop. Leave me alone.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.039 --\u003e 00:20:50.875\r\nWhat's the matter, Scarecrow?\r\n\r\n00:20:50.958 --\u003e 00:20:53.252\r\nCan't handle your own medicine?\r\n\r\n00:20:54.920 --\u003e 00:20:55.921\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:20:56.005 --\u003e 00:21:00.134\r\nNo. Stay away.\r\nStay away, please.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.217 --\u003e 00:21:01.886\r\n(LIGHTNING CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:21:04.764 --\u003e 00:21:06.515\r\nStay away.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.641 --\u003e 00:21:08.642\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:21:09.560 --\u003e 00:21:11.103\r\nOh, yes.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.688 --\u003e 00:21:16.025\r\nLook at the facts, Commissioner.\r\nBatman's withholding evidence.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.108 --\u003e 00:21:18.319\r\nEven helped the\r\nScarecrow guy escape.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.402 --\u003e 00:21:21.280\r\nI'd bet my badge he and\r\nScarecrow are in cahoots.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.614 --\u003e 00:21:22.948\r\nYour badge, eh?\r\n\r\n00:21:24.992 --\u003e 00:21:26.202\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:21:26.786 --\u003e 00:21:29.121\r\nNow, about that badge...\r\n\r\n00:21:59.693 --\u003e 00:22:02.154\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.673 --\u003e 00:22:21.674\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E11 - Be a Clown (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.924 --\u003e 00:00:09.593\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.455 --\u003e 00:01:23.584\r\nMAYOR HILL: Ever since my\r\nelection, I've promised the people\r\n\r\n00:01:23.667 --\u003e 00:01:26.753\r\nI'd build them a safe,\r\naffordable place to live.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.170 --\u003e 00:01:28.755\r\nGotham Towers is that place.\r\n\r\n00:01:28.839 --\u003e 00:01:30.048\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.132 --\u003e 00:01:33.260\r\nYour safety has always\r\nbeen my prime concern.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.677 --\u003e 00:01:36.930\r\nAnd under my leadership,\r\nno city will be safer\r\n\r\n00:01:37.264 --\u003e 00:01:41.059\r\nor more free of crime\r\nthan Gotham City...\r\n\r\n00:01:41.184 --\u003e 00:01:43.020\r\n- (TIRES SCREECH)\r\n- (CROWD SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:01:43.895 --\u003e 00:01:46.106\r\n- Look out!\r\n- Run!\r\n\r\n00:01:46.857 --\u003e 00:01:49.067\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:10.213 --\u003e 00:02:11.715\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:29.650 --\u003e 00:02:30.901\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:02:33.945 --\u003e 00:02:35.447\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:02:39.409 --\u003e 00:02:41.453\r\nGarbage collection\r\nis normally Monday,\r\n\r\n00:02:41.536 --\u003e 00:02:44.581\r\nbut in your case,\r\nI'm making an exception.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.290 --\u003e 00:02:47.376\r\n(REPORTERS EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:48.502 --\u003e 00:02:49.670\r\nBatman, wait!\r\n\r\n00:02:49.836 --\u003e 00:02:51.421\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:56.134\r\nRegarding safety in the\r\ncity, sir, you were saying?\r\n\r\n00:02:56.551 --\u003e 00:02:57.928\r\nWell, I...\r\n\r\n00:02:58.011 --\u003e 00:03:01.473\r\nWell, what just happened\r\nwas an isolated incident.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.932 --\u003e 00:03:04.893\r\nThere are just a\r\nfew rotten apples\r\n\r\n00:03:05.018 --\u003e 00:03:08.230\r\n\u003ci\u003egiving an otherwise peaceful\r\ncommunity a bad name.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:09.022 --\u003e 00:03:12.275\r\n\u003ci\u003eDo you include Batman in\r\nthose rotten apples, Mayor?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:12.359 --\u003e 00:03:13.485\r\n\u003ci\u003eAbsolutely.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:13.568 --\u003e 00:03:17.572\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe and criminals like the Joker\r\nare cut from the same cloth.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:17.656 --\u003e 00:03:20.659\r\nWhat? Compare me to Batman?\r\n\r\n00:03:20.909 --\u003e 00:03:23.537\r\nI got more style, more brains.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.620 --\u003e 00:03:25.914\r\nI'm certainly a better dresser.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.039 --\u003e 00:03:30.419\r\n\u003ci\u003eFurthermore, I intend to run every one\r\nof these costumed freaks out of town,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:30.961 --\u003e 00:03:35.716\r\n\u003ci\u003eand make all of Gotham City\r\nas safe as my own mansion.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:36.049 --\u003e 00:03:37.634\r\nOh, really?\r\n\r\n00:03:40.011 --\u003e 00:03:43.473\r\nWell, we'll just see how\r\nsafe your mansion is,\r\n\r\n00:03:43.557 --\u003e 00:03:45.726\r\nyou babbling bonehead.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.229 --\u003e 00:03:52.774\r\nGet a move on, Franklin.\r\nIt's almost time for the party.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.941 --\u003e 00:03:54.234\r\nYes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.317 --\u003e 00:03:59.114\r\nSome very important people will be here,\r\nand I don't want anything to go wrong.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.322 --\u003e 00:04:01.283\r\nBy the way,\r\nhave you seen my son?\r\n\r\n00:04:02.701 --\u003e 00:04:04.536\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\n\r\n00:04:04.619 --\u003e 00:04:07.956\r\nI will now perform my famous\r\ndisappearing-wand trick.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.123 --\u003e 00:04:09.541\r\nAbracadabra.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.170 --\u003e 00:04:15.297\r\n(TOYS CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:16.840 --\u003e 00:04:20.677\r\nJordan, stop fooling with\r\nthose stupid magic tricks.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.844 --\u003e 00:04:22.721\r\nYour party is starting.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.888 --\u003e 00:04:25.307\r\nThey're not stupid,\r\nand it's your party.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.724 --\u003e 00:04:28.769\r\nNonsense.\r\nI've invited some children.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.812 --\u003e 00:04:33.857\r\nYeah, your friends' kids.\r\nI don't even know any of them.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.940 --\u003e 00:04:36.067\r\nI'm not going to argue with\r\nyou, young man.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.193 --\u003e 00:04:38.653\r\nI'll expect you downstairs\r\nin five minutes.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.655 --\u003e 00:04:43.033\r\nMAYOR HILL: Hello.\r\nGlad you could come.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.742 --\u003e 00:04:46.870\r\nSenator Finch.\r\nWhat a pleasant surprise.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.080 --\u003e 00:04:51.041\r\nDid you get a good shot\r\nof me with the Senator?\r\n\r\n00:04:51.124 --\u003e 00:04:52.834\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n- Excellent.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.251 --\u003e 00:04:56.713\r\nSmile, Jordan.\r\nYou'd think you're having a bad time.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.172 --\u003e 00:04:59.591\r\n- No kidding.\r\n- Well, cheer up.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.758 --\u003e 00:05:02.803\r\nI've got a surprise coming,\r\nwhich should be here by now.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.220 --\u003e 00:05:06.765\r\nCouncilman Frye.\r\nAnd this must be Timmy?\r\n\r\n00:05:07.265 --\u003e 00:05:08.725\r\nHappy birthday.\r\nWhere's the food?\r\n\r\n00:05:09.434 --\u003e 00:05:11.311\r\nVOICE: Did someone say \"food?\"\r\n\r\n00:05:14.105 --\u003e 00:05:16.316\r\nI'm the guy with the goodies.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.399 --\u003e 00:05:18.068\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:25.367 --\u003e 00:05:26.785\r\n(BURSTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.993 --\u003e 00:05:28.453\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:31.206 --\u003e 00:05:33.208\r\nMayor Hill, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.291 --\u003e 00:05:36.753\r\nJekko. Jekko the Magnificent.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.837 --\u003e 00:05:38.463\r\n- Pleased to... Ow!\r\n- (BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:05:38.547 --\u003e 00:05:40.173\r\n(ALL LAUGH)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.799 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nAlways gives the party a charge.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:44.928\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:05:45.011 --\u003e 00:05:47.347\r\nIt's showtime!\r\n\r\n00:05:48.014 --\u003e 00:05:49.933\r\n- All right.\r\n- (ALL CLAP)\r\n\r\n00:05:50.725 --\u003e 00:05:54.312\r\nThank you! Thank you! (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:05:54.437 --\u003e 00:05:56.439\r\nWhere'd you learn that, Jekko?\r\n\r\n00:05:56.523 --\u003e 00:05:58.650\r\nFrom the great Prosciutto.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.734 --\u003e 00:06:01.987\r\nNow there was a ham.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.153 --\u003e 00:06:04.197\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:06:04.739 --\u003e 00:06:06.867\r\nHow can I get to be a\r\ngreat magician like you?\r\n\r\n00:06:07.492 --\u003e 00:06:09.744\r\nWell, there are three steps.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.495 --\u003e 00:06:13.081\r\nStep one, run away.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.665 --\u003e 00:06:17.460\r\nStep two,\r\nfind a magician with a great act.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.586 --\u003e 00:06:19.337\r\nAnd step three,\r\n\r\n00:06:19.588 --\u003e 00:06:20.672\r\nsteal it.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.841 --\u003e 00:06:25.051\r\nThat... That, that's okay.\r\nI think I got it.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.677 --\u003e 00:06:28.722\r\nBruce! Bruce Wayne!\r\nHow good of you to come.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.264 --\u003e 00:06:31.766\r\nJordan will be so\r\nhappy to see you.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.933 --\u003e 00:06:34.644\r\nI know the sooner I give him\r\nthis, the happier I'll be.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.898 --\u003e 00:06:40.233\r\nCould you show us\r\nmore, please, Jekko?\r\n\r\n00:06:40.692 --\u003e 00:06:42.819\r\nSure, birthday boy.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.903 --\u003e 00:06:45.614\r\nI'm saving the best for last.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.697 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nJordan, I've got more\r\nguests for you to meet.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.408 --\u003e 00:06:51.453\r\nBut, Dad, Jekko was just\r\ngoing to show us a trick.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.828 --\u003e 00:06:55.206\r\n- Sorry, but Mr. Wayne is waiting and...\r\n- I don't care about Mr. Wayne!\r\n\r\n00:06:55.582 --\u003e 00:06:58.793\r\nHush. You'll do what I say.\r\nNow come on.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.044 --\u003e 00:07:00.420\r\nIt's always what you want.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.503 --\u003e 00:07:02.213\r\nYou! You! You!\r\n\r\n00:07:05.717 --\u003e 00:07:06.927\r\n(GUESTS GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.727 --\u003e 00:07:17.562\r\n(LAUGHS) Kids.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.646 --\u003e 00:07:19.147\r\nTurn that off!\r\n\r\n00:07:20.607 --\u003e 00:07:26.154\r\nOh! Too bad for birthday boy.\r\nThis last trick is pure dynamite.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.072 --\u003e 00:07:29.157\r\n- Ta-da!\r\n- BOY: What is it?\r\n\r\n00:07:29.240 --\u003e 00:07:31.952\r\nIt's a birthday\r\ncandle, Einstein.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.202 --\u003e 00:07:34.663\r\nExcept this one blows you out.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.955 --\u003e 00:07:36.498\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:36.790 --\u003e 00:07:40.168\r\nNow scoot, you kids.\r\nShaw's over.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.752 --\u003e 00:07:42.545\r\nGo find some goodies.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.213 --\u003e 00:07:45.882\r\nThis trick's for the grown-ups.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.174 --\u003e 00:07:48.551\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:59.562 --\u003e 00:08:02.649\r\nIt's time for Jordo\r\nto make his wish.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.732 --\u003e 00:08:04.442\r\nAnd mine, too.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.445 --\u003e 00:08:10.073\r\nOh, my! A sparkler candle.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.448 --\u003e 00:08:12.909\r\nKeep watching and I'll, uh...\r\n\r\n00:08:14.035 --\u003e 00:08:15.996\r\nGet the birthday brat.\r\n\r\n00:08:16.079 --\u003e 00:08:17.998\r\nI don't know where\r\nJordan could have gone.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.081 --\u003e 00:08:20.041\r\nHe was dying to see you.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.709 --\u003e 00:08:22.836\r\n- You know kids.\r\n- Not really.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.336 --\u003e 00:08:27.507\r\nSo long, Mayor. Got to go.\r\nBut I left them with a bang.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.674 --\u003e 00:08:29.426\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:08:30.218 --\u003e 00:08:33.346\r\n- That laugh...\r\n- Good riddance, Jerko.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.930 --\u003e 00:08:36.057\r\nAs I was saying... Hey.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.102 --\u003e 00:08:41.021\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:08:57.412 --\u003e 00:08:59.622\r\n- Watch out!\r\n- Hey, pal!\r\n\r\n00:09:01.041 --\u003e 00:09:04.002\r\nBRUCE: Excuse me. Excuse me!\r\nI'm sorry. Pardon me.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.335 --\u003e 00:09:07.756\r\nComing through. Out of my way, please.\r\nExcuse me. I'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.839 --\u003e 00:09:09.466\r\nPardon me. Oops!\r\n\r\n00:09:11.718 --\u003e 00:09:13.178\r\nGUESTS: Aw.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.680 --\u003e 00:09:17.515\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:18.266 --\u003e 00:09:20.310\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.646 --\u003e 00:09:25.148\r\nI want answers!\r\n\r\n00:09:25.315 --\u003e 00:09:28.735\r\nNobody makes a fool of me,\r\nespecially in my own home.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.444 --\u003e 00:09:30.987\r\nAt least no one was hurt.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.071 --\u003e 00:09:34.157\r\nMr. Mayor,\r\nthis is the real Jekko the Clown.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.783 --\u003e 00:09:36.951\r\nWe found him tied\r\nup down the road.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.619 --\u003e 00:09:41.414\r\nSome maniac jumped me,\r\nstole my wagon and my costume.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.873 --\u003e 00:09:43.833\r\nMayor, where's Jordan?\r\n\r\n00:09:48.421 --\u003e 00:09:50.215\r\n(TANKS CLANKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:02.227 --\u003e 00:10:05.313\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:05.396 --\u003e 00:10:09.275\r\nTNT with your cake, sir?\r\n\r\n00:10:09.359 --\u003e 00:10:11.486\r\nOh, I crack myself up!\r\n\r\n00:10:16.032 --\u003e 00:10:17.408\r\nWOW!\r\n\r\n00:10:23.456 --\u003e 00:10:26.793\r\n\u003ci\u003eDenying reports of a bomb blast\r\nat his son's birthday party,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:26.876 --\u003e 00:10:31.506\r\n\u003ci\u003eMayor Hill insists the explosion was\r\ncaused by faulty electrical wiring.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:32.882 --\u003e 00:10:35.301\r\nYeah, right!\r\n\r\n00:10:35.593 --\u003e 00:10:38.054\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:40.181 --\u003e 00:10:44.269\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Mayor declined, however, to confirm\r\nthat his son, Jordan, is missing.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:44.477 --\u003e 00:10:45.728\r\nMissing?\r\n\r\n00:10:46.354 --\u003e 00:10:48.148\r\nIt's me, Jekko. I ran away.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.648 --\u003e 00:10:50.650\r\nYou did what?\r\n\r\n00:10:51.651 --\u003e 00:10:54.154\r\nI, I want to be a\r\nmagician, like you.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.237 --\u003e 00:10:55.738\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:57.115 --\u003e 00:11:01.202\r\n(LAUGHS) Well, kid,\r\nyou got step one right. Come on in.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.536 --\u003e 00:11:04.205\r\nI've been thinking\r\nabout a protege.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.416 --\u003e 00:11:07.959\r\nIt sure could be the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.501 --\u003e 00:11:12.255\r\nIf only I'd been paying more\r\nattention, he wouldn't have run away.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.881 --\u003e 00:11:16.509\r\nTake it easy, Mayor.\r\nI'm sure the police will find Jordan.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.676 --\u003e 00:11:18.094\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe“ you, Wayne,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:18.344 --\u003e 00:11:21.389\r\nthings are going to be different,\r\nif only he'd come back.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.224 --\u003e 00:11:24.934\r\n\u003ci\u003eJORDAN: Where'd you learn\r\nthat, Jekko?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:25.018 --\u003e 00:11:27.061\r\n\u003ci\u003eFrom the great Prosciutto.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:27.395 --\u003e 00:11:31.691\r\nNow there was a ham. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.696 --\u003e 00:11:40.158\r\n- But isn't swallowing a sword dangerous?\r\n- Watch.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.328 --\u003e 00:11:45.163\r\nHey! How did you do it?\r\n\r\n00:11:47.665 --\u003e 00:11:49.667\r\nEasy, kid.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.751 --\u003e 00:11:51.377\r\nIt's a trick sword.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.920 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- Now, you try it.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.673 --\u003e 00:11:57.425\r\nUh-uh. You could get cut.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.842 --\u003e 00:12:02.555\r\nHey! If it wasn't risky,\r\nI wouldn't enjoy it.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.764 --\u003e 00:12:04.224\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:06.893 --\u003e 00:12:09.062\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n- What's that?\r\n\r\n00:12:09.145 --\u003e 00:12:10.605\r\nSecurity, my boy.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.272 --\u003e 00:12:14.317\r\nYou can't be too careful\r\nin this part of town.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.070 --\u003e 00:12:18.363\r\n(DIGITAL BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:23.952 --\u003e 00:12:27.080\r\nJOKER: Well,\r\nif it ain't the Caped Coconut.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.956 --\u003e 00:12:30.041\r\nMy dad says Batman's no good.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.124 --\u003e 00:12:32.877\r\nWell, then I guess your\r\ndad's not a total idiot.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.586 --\u003e 00:12:36.839\r\nWhat do you say we play\r\na little joke on Batman?\r\n\r\n00:12:37.548 --\u003e 00:12:40.093\r\nYou can be my assistant.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.260 --\u003e 00:12:43.346\r\nCome on. This'll be a killer!\r\n\r\n00:12:43.471 --\u003e 00:12:45.139\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:53.940 --\u003e 00:12:56.234\r\nCome one, come all.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.609 --\u003e 00:12:57.902\r\nIt's...\r\n\r\n00:12:58.903 --\u003e 00:13:00.947\r\n\"Jekko the Jokester.\"\r\n\r\n00:13:01.698 --\u003e 00:13:04.200\r\nJa... Jekko the Jokester.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.617 --\u003e 00:13:05.785\r\nJordan!\r\n\r\n00:13:15.920 --\u003e 00:13:17.213\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:18.715 --\u003e 00:13:21.467\r\n(WHISPERS) This isn't a game, Jordan.\r\nWhere's Jekko?\r\n\r\n00:13:29.934 --\u003e 00:13:32.186\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.520 --\u003e 00:13:34.105\r\nTake a card, Batso.\r\n\r\n00:13:34.605 --\u003e 00:13:36.774\r\nTake all the cards!\r\n\r\n00:13:40.236 --\u003e 00:13:42.280\r\nNow it's my deal.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.579 --\u003e 00:13:51.289\r\nNot so fast!\r\n\r\n00:13:51.622 --\u003e 00:13:54.542\r\nA good magician always\r\nkeeps an ace up his sleeve.\r\n\r\n00:13:54.959 --\u003e 00:13:57.211\r\nThis one always floors them!\r\n\r\n00:14:00.798 --\u003e 00:14:02.175\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:04.677 --\u003e 00:14:05.928\r\nOh, my gosh.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.097 --\u003e 00:14:10.850\r\nWe bagged a big one this time!\r\n\r\n00:14:11.059 --\u003e 00:14:14.604\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:15.438 --\u003e 00:14:18.900\r\n- He isn't hurt, is he?\r\n- Hurt? (GASPS) Heavens!\r\n\r\n00:14:19.192 --\u003e 00:14:23.279\r\nYou wound me to the quick.\r\nThe enemy merely slumbers.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.654 --\u003e 00:14:26.491\r\nNo doubt dreaming\r\nof more foul deeds\r\n\r\n00:14:26.574 --\u003e 00:14:29.410\r\nto render upon the fair\r\ncitizens of Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.786 --\u003e 00:14:33.081\r\nBut his fate is not\r\nfor us to decide.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.164 --\u003e 00:14:34.791\r\n(CARNIVAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:14:39.379 --\u003e 00:14:41.005\r\n(MECHANICAL WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.013 --\u003e 00:14:50.348\r\n(MACHINE DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:14:50.932 --\u003e 00:14:54.102\r\n(LAUGHS) You're\r\ngoing to love this.\r\n\r\n00:15:07.031 --\u003e 00:15:09.242\r\nJOKER: Wake up, Batman.\r\nYou're on.\r\n\r\n00:15:10.034 --\u003e 00:15:11.911\r\n(WATER RUNNING)\r\n\r\n00:15:27.176 --\u003e 00:15:29.262\r\nFor your viewing pleasure,\r\n\r\n00:15:29.345 --\u003e 00:15:33.182\r\nwe present the infamous\r\nwater tank trap.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.266 --\u003e 00:15:35.935\r\nThe great Houdini\r\nsurvived such a test.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.352 --\u003e 00:15:40.022\r\nDare we demand\r\nless of the Batman?\r\n\r\n00:15:46.946 --\u003e 00:15:50.408\r\n- I don't like this, Jekko.\r\n- Quiet, kid. It's a free ticket.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.492 --\u003e 00:15:52.827\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:00.168 --\u003e 00:16:02.044\r\nHe did it! He got free.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.420 --\u003e 00:16:05.256\r\nThey don't make straitjackets\r\nlike they used to.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.339 --\u003e 00:16:06.424\r\nI should know.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.810 --\u003e 00:16:19.729\r\nHe can't get out.\r\nWhat's the trick?\r\n\r\n00:16:19.812 --\u003e 00:16:22.607\r\nThat's just it.\r\nThere is no trick!\r\n\r\n00:16:23.733 --\u003e 00:16:25.067\r\nNo! He'll drown!\r\n\r\n00:16:29.238 --\u003e 00:16:31.741\r\nThat's why they\r\ncall it the finale!\r\n\r\n00:16:33.743 --\u003e 00:16:35.620\r\nNow sit down and enjoy the show.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.835 --\u003e 00:16:44.045\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:16:44.128 --\u003e 00:16:45.463\r\nCome back!\r\n\r\n00:16:57.808 --\u003e 00:17:00.061\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- (MECHANICAL LAUGHTER PLAYS)\r\n\r\n00:17:02.605 --\u003e 00:17:04.690\r\n(SING-SONG) Naughty, naughty.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.941 --\u003e 00:17:07.902\r\nYou're making me miss the show.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.038 --\u003e 00:17:20.665\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:23.876 --\u003e 00:17:28.256\r\n(PANTING) All right, Joker.\r\nGet ready for a little bat magic.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.557 --\u003e 00:17:38.558\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:43.771 --\u003e 00:17:45.231\r\n(CLANKING)\r\n\r\n00:17:49.819 --\u003e 00:17:50.820\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:52.029 --\u003e 00:17:54.865\r\nJOKER: Oh, Jordo!\r\n\r\n00:17:56.367 --\u003e 00:17:57.785\r\n(GATE CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.621 --\u003e 00:18:03.457\r\nCome out, come out,\r\nwherever you are!\r\n\r\n00:18:12.925 --\u003e 00:18:13.926\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:18:14.176 --\u003e 00:18:18.723\r\n(CARNIVAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:18:27.148 --\u003e 00:18:28.357\r\n- Gotcha!\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:28.858 --\u003e 00:18:29.900\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:18:31.611 --\u003e 00:18:33.279\r\nCome here, you little...\r\n\r\n00:18:34.780 --\u003e 00:18:37.283\r\nOn second thought...\r\n\r\n00:18:40.202 --\u003e 00:18:43.080\r\nI love a roller coaster.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.664 --\u003e 00:18:46.626\r\nToo bad you missed the train.\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.631 --\u003e 00:18:55.551\r\nFasten your seat belt,\r\nit's going to be a bumpy ride.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.010 --\u003e 00:18:57.595\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:19:00.306 --\u003e 00:19:02.808\r\nYou win the prize, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.892 --\u003e 00:19:04.393\r\nCatch the Kewpie!\r\n\r\n00:19:09.398 --\u003e 00:19:11.067\r\nJOKER: Whee!\r\n\r\n00:19:11.692 --\u003e 00:19:12.943\r\nButterfingers!\r\n\r\n00:19:13.027 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n\u003ci\u003eKewpie-dewpie number two-aw.!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:23.287 --\u003e 00:19:27.500\r\nYou just don't like to\r\nplay with dolls, do you?\r\n\r\n00:19:39.261 --\u003e 00:19:41.097\r\n- That must have been his stop.\r\n- (WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:45.309\r\nOn the contrary, Joker.\r\nThis is where you get off.\r\n\r\n00:19:46.769 --\u003e 00:19:47.978\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:49.522 --\u003e 00:19:50.648\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:53.317 --\u003e 00:19:55.319\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:57.196 --\u003e 00:20:00.074\r\nSmell the roses, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:05.621 --\u003e 00:20:07.081\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.212 --\u003e 00:20:15.673\r\nHe always knew how\r\nto make an exit.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.881 --\u003e 00:20:16.882\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:20.177 --\u003e 00:20:22.430\r\n- Oh, my gosh!\r\n- Jordan!\r\n\r\n00:20:25.266 --\u003e 00:20:28.686\r\nReach for me.\r\nYou have to trust me.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.317 --\u003e 00:20:36.402\r\nNOW!\r\n\r\n00:20:45.786 --\u003e 00:20:46.996\r\nJORDAN: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:20:59.341 --\u003e 00:21:01.093\r\nCan we go home now?\r\n\r\n00:21:05.055 --\u003e 00:21:06.640\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.559 --\u003e 00:21:10.269\r\nJORDAN: Dad! Daddy!\r\n\r\n00:21:10.352 --\u003e 00:21:12.229\r\nJordan? Jordan.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.940 --\u003e 00:21:16.650\r\nOh, you're back.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.489 --\u003e 00:21:22.865\r\nMy boy is back.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.492 --\u003e 00:21:28.579\r\n- I'm so sorry for running away.\r\n- Please forgive me for the party.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.829 --\u003e 00:21:30.456\r\nWe can talk later.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.873 --\u003e 00:21:33.000\r\nRight now, I want to give you\r\n\r\n00:21:33.083 --\u003e 00:21:36.629\r\nthe biggest birthday\r\nhug you ever got.\r\n\r\n00:21:53.020 --\u003e 00:21:54.939\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:17.962 --\u003e 00:22:18.963\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E12 - Appointment in Crime Alley (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.797 --\u003e 00:00:07.799\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:31.550 --\u003e 00:01:32.551\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.856 --\u003e 00:01:47.482\r\nYou do good work, Mr...\r\n\r\n00:01:47.774 --\u003e 00:01:49.234\r\nWhat did you say your name was?\r\n\r\n00:01:49.359 --\u003e 00:01:51.111\r\nNitro, Mr. Daggett,\r\n\r\n00:01:51.194 --\u003e 00:01:53.155\r\non account of explosives\r\nare my business.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.072 --\u003e 00:01:58.660\r\nI assume Crocker explained the\r\nterms of your employment, Mr. Nitro?\r\n\r\n00:01:58.827 --\u003e 00:02:02.039\r\nSure. There's an old gas line\r\nrunning under the whole block.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.164 --\u003e 00:02:04.291\r\nI make it look like\r\nthe pipeline ruptured,\r\n\r\n00:02:04.374 --\u003e 00:02:06.627\r\nso the job can't\r\nbe traced to you.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.960 --\u003e 00:02:10.714\r\nIt's to be done while I give my speech\r\nto the Gotham Better Business Council.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.381 --\u003e 00:02:13.717\r\n9:00 exactly.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.176 --\u003e 00:02:17.512\r\nTrust me, when the hands\r\non that watch hit nine,\r\n\r\n00:02:18.138 --\u003e 00:02:19.222\r\nboom.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.142 --\u003e 00:02:25.520\r\nAs expected, the city zoning\r\nboard today rejected a request\r\n\r\n00:02:25.646 --\u003e 00:02:29.983\r\n\u003ci\u003eby the Daggett Development Corporation\r\nto raze a block of landmark brownstones\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:30.108 --\u003e 00:02:31.818\r\n\u003ci\u003ealong Gotham's Park Row.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:31.943 --\u003e 00:02:32.986\r\n\u003ci\u003eThirty years ago,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:33.070 --\u003e 00:02:36.073\r\n\u003ci\u003ePark Row was Gotham City's\r\nmost glamorous address.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:36.156 --\u003e 00:02:39.201\r\nBut, in recent years,\r\nthe area has suffered a decline.\r\n\r\n00:02:39.326 --\u003e 00:02:43.538\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd today, it is a slum better\r\nknown as the infamous \"Crime Alley.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:43.705 --\u003e 00:02:44.706\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut, to its inhabitants,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:44.831 --\u003e 00:02:47.376\r\n\u003ci\u003emany of whom spoke at\r\nthe zoning board today,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:47.501 --\u003e 00:02:49.836\r\n\u003ci\u003eCrime Alley is the\r\nonly home they have,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:49.920 --\u003e 00:02:51.588\r\n\u003ci\u003eand they fear its loss.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:51.838 --\u003e 00:02:55.967\r\n\u003ci\u003eOthers, like Roland Daggett, director\r\nof the Daggett Development Corporation,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:56.051 --\u003e 00:02:58.387\r\n\u003ci\u003esee the situation differently.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:01.098 --\u003e 00:03:02.349\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's tragic.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:02.766 --\u003e 00:03:05.268\r\n\u003ci\u003ePark Row may be an\r\nhistorical landmark,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:05.394 --\u003e 00:03:08.063\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut it's also a breeding\r\nground for crime.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:08.188 --\u003e 00:03:11.441\r\n\u003ci\u003eOf course, as much as we disagree\r\nwith the zoning board's decision,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:11.692 --\u003e 00:03:13.276\r\n\u003ci\u003eour hands are tied.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:13.485 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.323 --\u003e 00:03:20.242\r\nRoland Daggett is up to\r\nsomething, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.367 --\u003e 00:03:23.495\r\nThat almost goes without\r\nsaying, doesn't it, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:23.870 --\u003e 00:03:26.623\r\nI don't know what it is\r\nyet, but I will.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.748 --\u003e 00:03:29.584\r\nYou don't want to be late for\r\nyour 8:00 appointment, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.127 --\u003e 00:03:31.586\r\nHave I ever been late?\r\n\r\n00:03:32.504 --\u003e 00:03:33.505\r\nNo, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.630 --\u003e 00:03:35.090\r\nNot once in all these years.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.383 --\u003e 00:03:37.384\r\n(ENGINE RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:29.144 --\u003e 00:04:31.229\r\nHelp! Help!\r\n\r\n00:04:32.314 --\u003e 00:04:33.315\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:33.523 --\u003e 00:04:34.524\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:35.400 --\u003e 00:04:36.693\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:04:38.528 --\u003e 00:04:40.989\r\nHelp! Somebody help my mommy!\r\n\r\n00:04:41.782 --\u003e 00:04:44.242\r\n(STAMMERING) Those\r\nmen in our apartment,\r\n\r\n00:04:44.326 --\u003e 00:04:45.327\r\nthey'll hurt her.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.452 --\u003e 00:04:47.329\r\nI climbed out the window.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.454 --\u003e 00:04:48.663\r\nWhere?\r\n\r\n00:04:50.165 --\u003e 00:04:51.249\r\n(OBJECTS CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:55.921 --\u003e 00:04:58.590\r\nLady, you and your kid\r\nwere told to clear out.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.090 --\u003e 00:05:00.091\r\n(FURNITURE SMASHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.801 --\u003e 00:05:02.052\r\nYou didn't listen.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.427 --\u003e 00:05:04.304\r\nMaybe you'd like\r\nto be carried out.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.807 --\u003e 00:05:08.517\r\nNo! Please!\r\n\r\n00:05:09.267 --\u003e 00:05:11.144\r\n(BATARANG WHOOSHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.245 --\u003e 00:05:29.246\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:43.093 --\u003e 00:05:44.094\r\nYah!\r\n\r\n00:05:45.929 --\u003e 00:05:47.639\r\nMommy! Mommy!\r\n\r\n00:05:48.098 --\u003e 00:05:49.099\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:52.102 --\u003e 00:05:53.103\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.270 --\u003e 00:05:55.605\r\nWhat did they mean,\r\nyou were warned to clear out?\r\n\r\n00:05:55.939 --\u003e 00:05:58.191\r\nCouple of days ago,\r\nthese three show up,\r\n\r\n00:05:58.316 --\u003e 00:06:00.235\r\nsay they're working\r\nfor some corporation.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.527 --\u003e 00:06:02.654\r\nThey tell everyone on our\r\nblock they got to leave.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.946 --\u003e 00:06:04.447\r\nBut, where are we gonna go?\r\n\r\n00:06:13.123 --\u003e 00:06:14.791\r\nHe's never been late before.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.292 --\u003e 00:06:16.793\r\nI'd better look for him.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.003 --\u003e 00:06:19.754\r\nWhere you off to,\r\nMiss Thompkins?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.130 --\u003e 00:06:22.132\r\nJust looking for a\r\nfriend, Maggie.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.465 --\u003e 00:06:23.717\r\nYou be careful.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.842 --\u003e 00:06:27.345\r\nMaggie, I've lived in\r\nPark Row for 30 years.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.470 --\u003e 00:06:28.555\r\nIt's my home.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.889 --\u003e 00:06:30.473\r\nI'm not afraid here.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.964 --\u003e 00:07:04.299\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:07:04.883 --\u003e 00:07:06.551\r\nThis building is condemned.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.846 --\u003e 00:07:11.306\r\nI saw you on the news.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.514 --\u003e 00:07:12.933\r\nYou work for Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.228 --\u003e 00:07:18.855\r\nOh, my gracious!\r\n\r\n00:07:21.566 --\u003e 00:07:22.567\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:24.069 --\u003e 00:07:25.278\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:07:44.756 --\u003e 00:07:45.757\r\n(ENGINE RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:47.676 --\u003e 00:07:48.760\r\n(ENGINE STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.220 --\u003e 00:07:51.221\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:51.304 --\u003e 00:07:53.014\r\nI'm looking for Dr. Thompkins.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.139 --\u003e 00:07:56.101\r\nShe said somebody was\r\nsupposed to meet her.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.601 --\u003e 00:07:57.602\r\nYou?\r\n\r\n00:07:58.561 --\u003e 00:07:59.604\r\nWhere is she?\r\n\r\n00:07:59.938 --\u003e 00:08:01.523\r\nLeslie went looking for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.690 --\u003e 00:08:03.024\r\nI told her to be careful.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.149 --\u003e 00:08:06.111\r\nBad things happen to\r\npeople in Crime Alley.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.528 --\u003e 00:08:07.654\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.909 --\u003e 00:08:13.910\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:36.599 --\u003e 00:08:37.994\r\nCROCKER: Urban\r\nredevelopment, lady.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.018 --\u003e 00:08:39.436\r\nThat's what this is all about.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.519 --\u003e 00:08:41.646\r\nUh, tell me if the\r\nrope's too tight.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.735 --\u003e 00:08:50.572\r\nAll set. We just gotta do that\r\nold hotel down the street.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.655 --\u003e 00:08:53.033\r\nAnd then when 9:00\r\nrolls around...\r\n\r\n00:08:53.116 --\u003e 00:08:55.702\r\nBoom! Instant slum clearance.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.869 --\u003e 00:08:57.662\r\nNext stop, mini-mall.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.787 --\u003e 00:09:00.040\r\nYou can't destroy that hotel.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.165 --\u003e 00:09:01.332\r\nThis block may be abandoned,\r\n\r\n00:09:01.416 --\u003e 00:09:03.501\r\nbut that building has\r\npeople living in it.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.044 --\u003e 00:09:06.171\r\nCROCKER: Hey,\r\nwe told them to leave.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.296 --\u003e 00:09:09.132\r\nThey stand in the way of\r\nredevelopment, they get bulldozed.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.424 --\u003e 00:09:11.259\r\nNothing personal. Just business.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.968 --\u003e 00:09:14.220\r\nYou're insane.\r\nYou won't get away with-\r\n\r\n00:09:14.304 --\u003e 00:09:15.305\r\n(MUFFLED SPEECH)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.482 --\u003e 00:09:26.941\r\n(BOMB TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:28.151 --\u003e 00:09:29.152\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.487 --\u003e 00:09:32.697\r\nAlfred, did Leslie call?\r\n\r\n00:09:32.822 --\u003e 00:09:33.948\r\nALFRED: No, sir.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.365 --\u003e 00:09:37.035\r\n- Is anything wrong?\r\n- We missed each other.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.702 --\u003e 00:09:39.871\r\n- I'm on my way to her apartment.\r\n- (SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:09:41.081 --\u003e 00:09:43.541\r\nSomething's come up, Alfred.\r\nI'll be in touch.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.424 --\u003e 00:09:52.592\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:53.760 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:01.559 --\u003e 00:10:03.728\r\nMAN: Now,\r\nyou're gonna listen to me!\r\n\r\n00:10:04.854 --\u003e 00:10:08.149\r\nI want justice, Gotham City!\r\n\r\n00:10:09.359 --\u003e 00:10:10.360\r\n(GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:11.277 --\u003e 00:10:12.445\r\nWho's the hostage?\r\n\r\n00:10:12.987 --\u003e 00:10:14.489\r\nSome clerk from\r\nDaggett Development.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.614 --\u003e 00:10:17.033\r\nWrong place at the wrong\r\ntime with an eviction notice.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.534 --\u003e 00:10:19.077\r\nTen seconds, we make our move.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.745 --\u003e 00:10:22.747\r\nBATMAN: If you go,\r\nthe hostage might be hurt.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.914 --\u003e 00:10:24.666\r\n- I'll do it.\r\n- You'll do it?\r\n\r\n00:10:25.125 --\u003e 00:10:26.835\r\nWho do you think you are?\r\n\r\n00:10:27.585 --\u003e 00:10:28.586\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.670 --\u003e 00:10:31.214\r\nYou took my job, Gotham City!\r\n\r\n00:10:31.464 --\u003e 00:10:32.799\r\nYou took my home!\r\n\r\n00:10:33.299 --\u003e 00:10:35.301\r\nSomebody's gotta pay for that!\r\n\r\n00:10:35.760 --\u003e 00:10:37.220\r\n\u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e Pick you.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.345 --\u003e 00:10:38.805\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:39.472 --\u003e 00:10:41.266\r\nBATMAN: Put the gun down!\r\n\r\n00:10:41.349 --\u003e 00:10:42.392\r\nWho said that?\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.228\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:10:48.398 --\u003e 00:10:49.399\r\nWhoa.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.863 --\u003e 00:10:57.031\r\nSo, you're working for\r\nDaggett, too?\r\n\r\n00:10:58.700 --\u003e 00:10:59.701\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:01.703 --\u003e 00:11:04.038\r\nBATMAN: I won't ask twice.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.416 --\u003e 00:11:07.792\r\n(BOTH GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:08.668 --\u003e 00:11:10.044\r\n(BOTH EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:11:14.966 --\u003e 00:11:15.967\r\n(BOTH SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:11:30.732 --\u003e 00:11:33.026\r\nThanks for the help.\r\nGood thing you showed up.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.919 --\u003e 00:11:51.920\r\nBATMAN: Leslie?\r\n\r\n00:12:44.764 --\u003e 00:12:47.558\r\nPoor Doc Thompkins.\r\nShe's in trouble.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.643 --\u003e 00:12:49.769\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:49.852 --\u003e 00:12:50.853\r\nWhat trouble?\r\n\r\n00:12:50.937 --\u003e 00:12:51.938\r\nUh, nothing.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.063 --\u003e 00:12:54.607\r\nI didn't see them grab her.\r\nI didn't see nothing.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.983 --\u003e 00:12:56.734\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\nWho grabbed her?\r\n\r\n00:12:56.818 --\u003e 00:12:58.695\r\nI don't know!\r\nLet go of me! Let go!\r\n\r\n00:13:03.574 --\u003e 00:13:05.159\r\nWhere did you get\r\nthis blasting cap?\r\n\r\n00:13:05.660 --\u003e 00:13:07.996\r\nAnd where's Dr. Thompkins?\r\n\r\n00:13:08.830 --\u003e 00:13:10.498\r\n(STAMMERING) Two guys,\r\nthey grabbed her.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.581 --\u003e 00:13:11.582\r\nShe dropped it.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.666 --\u003e 00:13:13.376\r\nI thought I could sell it.\r\nGet a few bucks.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.751 --\u003e 00:13:14.877\r\nWhere are they?\r\n\r\n00:13:15.044 --\u003e 00:13:16.754\r\nCorner of Finger and Broom.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.879 --\u003e 00:13:18.506\r\nThat's all I know, honest!\r\n\r\n00:13:28.599 --\u003e 00:13:30.226\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:31.227 --\u003e 00:13:32.937\r\n(BOMB TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:13:34.981 --\u003e 00:13:35.982\r\n(CLOCK TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:13:39.402 --\u003e 00:13:42.447\r\nMAN: Ladies and gentlemen,\r\nmay I introduce our speaker,\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:44.782\r\na bold force for progress,\r\n\r\n00:13:44.907 --\u003e 00:13:47.827\r\na man of vision with the\r\nwill to execute his dreams,\r\n\r\n00:13:48.286 --\u003e 00:13:49.871\r\nRoland Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.669 --\u003e 00:13:57.670\r\n(ENGINE HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:06.679 --\u003e 00:14:07.680\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:10.516 --\u003e 00:14:11.517\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:14.270 --\u003e 00:14:15.750\r\n- WOMAN: He's hurt!\r\n- He's passed out!\r\n\r\n00:14:16.272 --\u003e 00:14:17.648\r\nMAN: Help! WOMAN: Help!\r\n\r\n00:14:19.859 --\u003e 00:14:20.860\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:21.569 --\u003e 00:14:22.695\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:14:23.863 --\u003e 00:14:25.948\r\nPerfect. Just perfect.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.510 --\u003e 00:14:47.220\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:50.473 --\u003e 00:14:52.141\r\n(PASSENGERS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.877 --\u003e 00:15:21.504\r\n- Look out!\r\n- Runaway trolley!\r\n\r\n00:15:21.629 --\u003e 00:15:23.429\r\nMAN: Get out of the way!\r\nThe trolley's coming!\r\n\r\n00:15:43.734 --\u003e 00:15:45.111\r\nPASSENGERS: Don't leave us!\r\n\r\n00:15:45.236 --\u003e 00:15:46.446\r\n(PASSENGERS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.076 --\u003e 00:15:53.202\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.997 --\u003e 00:15:56.998\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:57.665 --\u003e 00:15:58.666\r\n(PASSENGERS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:14.557 --\u003e 00:16:15.558\r\n(WHEELS SCRAPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:24.817 --\u003e 00:16:25.860\r\n(THUDS SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.699 --\u003e 00:16:32.926\r\nMAN: Oh, my goodness. Thank God.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.950 --\u003e 00:16:34.510\r\nWOMAN: Thank goodness.\r\nI was so afraid.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.036 --\u003e 00:16:36.412\r\nWOMAN 2: Let us out of here!\r\n\r\n00:16:38.039 --\u003e 00:16:40.166\r\nI've never been so\r\nscared in all my life.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.570 --\u003e 00:17:10.571\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.907 --\u003e 00:17:14.075\r\nBATMAN: Hello, Crocker.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.700 --\u003e 00:17:16.786\r\n- Long time no see.\r\n- CROCKER: Batman?\r\n\r\n00:17:17.328 --\u003e 00:17:18.808\r\n(STAMMERING) What\r\nare you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:17:20.456 --\u003e 00:17:21.707\r\nMeeting a friend.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.999 --\u003e 00:17:23.668\r\nWhat are you doing\r\nhere, Crocker?\r\n\r\n00:17:23.876 --\u003e 00:17:25.753\r\nCROCKER: No.\r\nNone of your business.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.878 --\u003e 00:17:27.272\r\nBATMAN: Somebody is\r\ntrying to run the people\r\n\r\n00:17:27.296 --\u003e 00:17:28.896\r\nin this neighborhood\r\nout of their homes.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.382 --\u003e 00:17:31.801\r\nYour boss, Daggett,\r\nwouldn't know anything about this,\r\n\r\n00:17:31.884 --\u003e 00:17:32.885\r\nwould he?\r\n\r\n00:17:33.177 --\u003e 00:17:35.221\r\nCROCKER: No. No, of course not.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.429 --\u003e 00:17:36.556\r\n(NITRO EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.348 --\u003e 00:17:38.641\r\nHow about you, Nitro?\r\n\r\n00:17:39.267 --\u003e 00:17:40.268\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:40.351 --\u003e 00:17:43.396\r\nYou told your parole board you\r\ngave up the arson-for-hire game.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.355 --\u003e 00:17:46.732\r\n(STAMMERING) I did. I'm clean.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.233 --\u003e 00:17:48.234\r\nBATMAN: Really?\r\n\r\n00:17:50.778 --\u003e 00:17:51.988\r\nThen what's this?\r\n\r\n00:17:54.156 --\u003e 00:17:57.076\r\nYou crazy?\r\nThis stuff is dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.326 --\u003e 00:17:58.452\r\nTalk to me, Nitro.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.703 --\u003e 00:18:01.205\r\nAfter Daggett lost his\r\nappeal to the zoning board,\r\n\r\n00:18:01.372 --\u003e 00:18:04.834\r\nCrocker hired you to level this\r\nwhole neighborhood, didn't he?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.084 --\u003e 00:18:06.794\r\nThat's it. That's right.\r\nYou got it.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.044 --\u003e 00:18:08.504\r\nDon't tell Daggett I talked.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.422 --\u003e 00:18:10.965\r\nWhere's Leslie Thompkins?\r\n\r\n00:18:11.215 --\u003e 00:18:12.842\r\nThe old lady? In there.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.967 --\u003e 00:18:15.803\r\nListen, we gotta get out of here.\r\nIt's almost 9:00.\r\n\r\n00:18:22.560 --\u003e 00:18:23.644\r\n(MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:18:25.896 --\u003e 00:18:26.897\r\n(BOMB TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:30.693 --\u003e 00:18:31.819\r\n- (TICKING STOPS)\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:35.448 --\u003e 00:18:36.449\r\n(CLOCK SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:18:40.411 --\u003e 00:18:41.579\r\nDon't worry about me.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.704 --\u003e 00:18:44.040\r\nThey're blowing up\r\nthe old SRO Hotel.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.582 --\u003e 00:18:46.375\r\nYou've got to get\r\nthe people out.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.127 --\u003e 00:18:49.128\r\nDAGGETT: Gentlemen,\r\n\r\n00:18:49.629 --\u003e 00:18:51.922\r\nGotham City is at a crossroads.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.298 --\u003e 00:18:55.051\r\nAs businessmen,\r\nthe choice we face is clear.\r\n\r\n00:18:55.801 --\u003e 00:18:57.887\r\nIt's time we decide\r\nwhere we stand.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.512 --\u003e 00:19:01.182\r\nAre we for progress\r\nor against it?\r\n\r\n00:19:01.849 --\u003e 00:19:04.518\r\nFor the future or for the past?\r\n\r\n00:19:05.227 --\u003e 00:19:07.021\r\nFor the weak or for the strong?\r\n\r\n00:19:18.366 --\u003e 00:19:19.367\r\n(BOMB TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:24.038 --\u003e 00:19:25.247\r\nIn short,\r\n\r\n00:19:25.748 --\u003e 00:19:29.377\r\nwe cannot allow the\r\nunderclass to hinder us\r\n\r\n00:19:29.502 --\u003e 00:19:31.462\r\nfrom building a better tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:19:37.051 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:19:56.445 --\u003e 00:19:57.905\r\n(INDISTINCT POLICE\r\nRADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.786 --\u003e 00:20:06.747\r\nMr. Daggett. Mr. Daggett.\r\nAny comments on this tragedy?\r\n\r\n00:20:06.914 --\u003e 00:20:09.500\r\nMAN: Does this affect your plans\r\nfor redevelopment, Mr. Daggett?\r\n\r\n00:20:11.585 --\u003e 00:20:13.129\r\nIt's a sad fact,\r\n\r\n00:20:13.587 --\u003e 00:20:17.216\r\nbut you have to expect\r\nviolence in Crime Alley.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.758 --\u003e 00:20:20.469\r\nThese people don't value\r\nhuman life like we do.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.387 --\u003e 00:20:24.557\r\nBATMAN: Nobody values human\r\nlife like you do, Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.726 --\u003e 00:20:28.728\r\nI diffused the\r\nbomb at the hotel.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.353 --\u003e 00:20:32.940\r\nAll your punks managed to destroy\r\nwere a few condemned buildings.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.733 --\u003e 00:20:35.025\r\nOnce they confess,\r\n\r\n00:20:35.526 --\u003e 00:20:36.986\r\nyou're finished.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.403 --\u003e 00:20:38.571\r\nI'm shocked.\r\n\r\n00:20:39.321 --\u003e 00:20:43.159\r\nShocked to learn that arson\r\nwas the cause of this tragedy.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.909 --\u003e 00:20:46.996\r\nThank heaven the criminals\r\nresponsible have been caught.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.121 --\u003e 00:20:49.957\r\n- But, Mr. Daggett, you told us to-\r\n- DAGGETT: Officers,\r\n\r\n00:20:50.082 --\u003e 00:20:52.334\r\nI believe your duty is clear.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.339 --\u003e 00:20:58.841\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.809 --\u003e 00:21:09.935\r\nLESLIE: Let it go.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.728 --\u003e 00:21:13.022\r\nDaggett won't escape\r\nthe law forever.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.314 --\u003e 00:21:15.065\r\nThere's nothing you can do now.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.483 --\u003e 00:21:17.985\r\nAnd besides,\r\nyou have an appointment to keep.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.824 --\u003e 00:21:26.118\r\nThis used to be a\r\nbeautiful street.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.577 --\u003e 00:21:28.496\r\nGood people lived here once.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.288 --\u003e 00:21:31.791\r\nGood people still\r\nlive in Crime Alley.\r\n\r\n00:21:56.482 --\u003e 00:21:58.484\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:23.342 --\u003e 00:22:24.343\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E13 - P.O.V (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.631 --\u003e 00:00:07.132\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:18.078 --\u003e 00:01:21.123\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:01:38.056 --\u003e 00:01:41.768\r\n- How we doing for time?\r\n- Bullock's meeting us at 2300 hours.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.060 --\u003e 00:01:44.271\r\nWe'll be there with time to spare.\r\nRelax.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.438 --\u003e 00:01:46.148\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.862 --\u003e 00:01:54.698\r\nSorry. I've never\r\nworked a sting before.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.032 --\u003e 00:01:56.742\r\nIt ought to be a hot one.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.664 --\u003e 00:02:04.708\r\nWILKES: Hot is right.\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\n00:02:10.714 --\u003e 00:02:12.090\r\nWhere's Bullock?\r\n\r\n00:02:12.633 --\u003e 00:02:16.053\r\nI don't know,\r\nbut we're in deep trouble.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.345 --\u003e 00:02:17.763\r\nWe've got to find Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.430 --\u003e 00:02:19.598\r\n(MAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:02:24.978 --\u003e 00:02:28.523\r\n- Detective Bullock. Are you all right?\r\n- I'm okay.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.815 --\u003e 00:02:32.235\r\nDo you realize what this means?\r\nWhy didn't you wait for us?\r\n\r\n00:02:32.319 --\u003e 00:02:33.862\r\n(GLASS SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:44.539 --\u003e 00:02:47.876\r\n- Let's go.\r\n- Wait. More inside.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.959 --\u003e 00:02:49.795\r\nWilkes, go after those two.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.295 --\u003e 00:02:51.672\r\nI'll check out the warehouse.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.549 --\u003e 00:02:56.093\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:02:57.678 --\u003e 00:02:58.887\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:03.141 --\u003e 00:03:04.518\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:03:04.976 --\u003e 00:03:05.977\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:09.022 --\u003e 00:03:12.693\r\nWhen I'm done with you clowns,\r\nyou won't qualify as security guards!\r\n\r\n00:03:12.984 --\u003e 00:03:15.570\r\nThe department works months\r\nto nail that drug lord.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.821 --\u003e 00:03:18.407\r\nWe lay out $2 million\r\nin cash for the sting.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.490 --\u003e 00:03:21.535\r\nAnd in five stinking\r\nminutes, you idiots blow it!\r\n\r\n00:03:22.119 --\u003e 00:03:25.080\r\n- Hey, I didn't blow anything.\r\n- Well, one of you did!\r\n\r\n00:03:27.499 --\u003e 00:03:30.460\r\nOr maybe what we've got here\r\nis three cops on the take.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.544 --\u003e 00:03:34.256\r\n- That's uncalled for.\r\n- What? You can't be serious.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.339 --\u003e 00:03:37.259\r\nBULLOCK: Where does he get off?\r\nHey, I'll tell you who's to blame.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.342 --\u003e 00:03:38.385\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:03:39.386 --\u003e 00:03:43.348\r\n- You saw the Batman, too?\r\n- Come on, Harvey, Batman's fault?\r\n\r\n00:03:43.432 --\u003e 00:03:45.767\r\nThen whose fault is it, Officer?\r\n\r\n00:03:45.851 --\u003e 00:03:48.937\r\nI don't know, but I'm sure\r\nit wasn't Batman. He was...\r\n\r\n00:03:49.020 --\u003e 00:03:52.899\r\nEither you start coming up with some\r\nanswers or hand over your badges.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.066 --\u003e 00:03:55.652\r\nI'm telling you, Lieutenant,\r\nBatman blew the bust.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.736 --\u003e 00:03:58.488\r\nMontoya and Wilkes were late,\r\nso I had to go in alone.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.031 --\u003e 00:04:01.324\r\nWe weren't late!\r\n\r\n00:04:01.575 --\u003e 00:04:05.162\r\nYou had your chance.\r\nAll right, Bullock, let's have it.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.787 --\u003e 00:04:08.123\r\nLike I said,\r\nI had to go in alone.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.041 --\u003e 00:04:13.795\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was waiting for Wilkes and Montoya\r\nwhen I saw that blasted Batman\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:13.879 --\u003e 00:04:15.046\r\nenter the warehouse.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.380 --\u003e 00:04:17.340\r\n\u003ci\u003eI couldn't wait for\r\nbackup any longer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:17.591 --\u003e 00:04:20.343\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was afraid he'd screw up the\r\nbust, so I followed him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:41.948 --\u003e 00:04:43.909\r\n(DRILL WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:04:50.624 --\u003e 00:04:53.084\r\n(GRINDING)\r\n\r\n00:04:54.294 --\u003e 00:04:55.295\r\nGot it.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.758 --\u003e 00:05:02.719\r\nThe boss was right.\r\nMust be a couple of mil in here.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.351 --\u003e 00:05:12.771\r\n\u003ci\u003eBULLOCK: I was closing in when\r\nthis loud noise tipped them.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:12.854 --\u003e 00:05:14.940\r\n(CLANGS)\r\n\r\n00:05:15.732 --\u003e 00:05:17.275\r\n\u003ci\u003eMust have been Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:17.567 --\u003e 00:05:18.819\r\nWhat was that?\r\n\r\n00:05:33.500 --\u003e 00:05:36.670\r\nFreeze, maggots!\r\nYou're all under arrest!\r\n\r\n00:05:37.128 --\u003e 00:05:40.340\r\n- BULLOCK: Jeez!\r\n- Over there. Get him!\r\n\r\n00:05:45.303 --\u003e 00:05:47.097\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:54.062 --\u003e 00:05:55.313\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.023 --\u003e 00:05:58.191\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:06:01.987 --\u003e 00:06:03.071\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.329 --\u003e 00:06:12.873\r\n(THUG GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:27.387 --\u003e 00:06:28.388\r\n(THUG GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.351 --\u003e 00:06:34.352\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:47.198 --\u003e 00:06:48.617\r\n(GROANS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:06:48.700 --\u003e 00:06:50.327\r\nFry, Copper!\r\n\r\n00:06:50.702 --\u003e 00:06:51.745\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:09.888 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:07:17.812 --\u003e 00:07:20.649\r\n\u003ci\u003eBULLOCK: In spite of the fire,\r\nI had everything under control\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:20.899 --\u003e 00:07:23.485\r\n\u003ci\u003eand then Batman showed up\r\nand bungled everything.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:27.489 --\u003e 00:07:28.490\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:07:36.831 --\u003e 00:07:40.460\r\n\u003ci\u003eLucky I was there\r\nto save his butt.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:45.465 --\u003e 00:07:48.093\r\nIt took my last bit of\r\nstrength to get us out.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.510 --\u003e 00:07:51.888\r\n- So you went in because of Batman.\r\n- I told you. They were late.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.180 --\u003e 00:07:55.892\r\nWere you trying to beat them out of\r\nthe collar or beat them to the cash?\r\n\r\n00:07:56.101 --\u003e 00:07:59.646\r\n- Ease up, Lieutenant.\r\n- No. You back off, Commissioner!\r\n\r\n00:07:59.813 --\u003e 00:08:03.608\r\nGordon, this is my investigation,\r\nso pipe down or get out!\r\n\r\n00:08:03.692 --\u003e 00:08:05.986\r\nHe knows they were supposed\r\nto go in as a team.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.236 --\u003e 00:08:09.364\r\nBullock, I demand to know the\r\nreal reason you didn't wait\r\n\r\n00:08:09.447 --\u003e 00:08:10.615\r\nfor the rest of your team.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.157 --\u003e 00:08:13.076\r\n- Bullock!\r\n- Give me a break.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.618 --\u003e 00:08:15.258\r\nWhy don't you ask them\r\nwhy they were late?\r\n\r\n00:08:15.578 --\u003e 00:08:17.288\r\nBut we weren't late, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.372 --\u003e 00:08:20.166\r\nAll right,\r\nlet's hear from the rookie.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.709 --\u003e 00:08:23.586\r\nMaybe he knows who's to\r\nblame for this screw-up.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.754 --\u003e 00:08:25.797\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:08:25.880 --\u003e 00:08:31.136\r\nWell, like Officer Montoya\r\nsaid, we weren't late.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.511 --\u003e 00:08:33.847\r\nWhen we arrived,\r\nDetective Bullock was down.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.097 --\u003e 00:08:36.474\r\nThen the two suspects\r\ncame out of the building.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.725 --\u003e 00:08:39.894\r\n\u003ci\u003eI pursued them while Officer\r\nMontoya went into the warehouse.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:41.938 --\u003e 00:08:43.648\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhen I looked into the alley...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:44.691 --\u003e 00:08:47.110\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe suspects\r\ncompletely vanished.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:53.450 --\u003e 00:08:54.701\r\n- (DOOR THUDS)\r\n- (GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:55.285 --\u003e 00:08:56.828\r\n(DOOR WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:08:58.246 --\u003e 00:08:59.330\r\n(ENGINE REVS)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.673 --\u003e 00:09:10.300\r\n\u003ci\u003eWILKES: I thought I'd bought it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:12.927 --\u003e 00:09:15.138\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen he came flying\r\nout of nowhere.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:15.263 --\u003e 00:09:18.058\r\nI'd heard of \u003ci\u003ehim,\u003c/i\u003e\r\nbut I'd never seen him before.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.892 --\u003e 00:09:21.478\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt was incredible,\r\nthe Batman threw out his hand\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:21.561 --\u003e 00:09:23.980\r\n\u003ci\u003eand sparks flew\r\nfrom his fingertips.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:24.314 --\u003e 00:09:25.565\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:09:26.191 --\u003e 00:09:28.234\r\n(TIRES EXPLODE, SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.781 --\u003e 00:09:33.907\r\n(CAR CRASH ES)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.990 --\u003e 00:09:35.510\r\n\u003ci\u003eWILKES: Then he\r\npointed his fingers...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:38.495 --\u003e 00:09:41.206\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd some kind of ray\r\nshot out at the van.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:41.289 --\u003e 00:09:42.999\r\n- (ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n- (EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:09:43.083 --\u003e 00:09:44.417\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt blew the door open.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:44.876 --\u003e 00:09:46.503\r\n\u003ci\u003eOne of the suspects\r\nstaggered out.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:46.795 --\u003e 00:09:48.922\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe other must've escaped\r\nthrough the loading dock.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:51.174 --\u003e 00:09:53.885\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe guy tried to bolt and the\r\nBatman just pointed at him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:54.469 --\u003e 00:09:55.762\r\n\u003ci\u003eWham! He dropped!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:56.554 --\u003e 00:09:59.849\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt was unbelievable!\r\nBatman's on the guy in a flash.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:00.266 --\u003e 00:10:02.102\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen the Batman says\r\nsomething to him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:04.813 --\u003e 00:10:06.481\r\nWhat did he say?\r\n\r\n00:10:07.774 --\u003e 00:10:11.152\r\nI couldn't hear.\r\nBut the guy looked plenty scared\r\n\r\n00:10:11.236 --\u003e 00:10:15.281\r\n- and blurted out \"Doc\" something.\r\n- Doc who?\r\n\r\n00:10:15.615 --\u003e 00:10:18.910\r\nI don't know.\r\nHe just said \"Doc.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:19.828 --\u003e 00:10:23.790\r\nWe're interrogating the suspect now,\r\nbut it doesn't look like he'll crack.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.415 --\u003e 00:10:26.459\r\nWell, I think the rookie's\r\nholding something back.\r\n\r\n00:10:27.001 --\u003e 00:10:29.129\r\nTake it easy!\r\nHe told you everything he knows!\r\n\r\n00:10:29.671 --\u003e 00:10:33.550\r\nHow touching. I hope you're\r\nas good at defending yourself\r\n\r\n00:10:33.967 --\u003e 00:10:36.678\r\nsince the detective here\r\nis calling you a liar.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.928 --\u003e 00:10:39.889\r\nWait a minute.\r\nNobody's calling anyone a liar.\r\n\r\n00:10:40.265 --\u003e 00:10:42.934\r\nThere's obviously a\r\ncommunication problem here.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.184 --\u003e 00:10:48.314\r\n- But my officers are not liars.\r\n- HACKLE: Well, someone in here is lying.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.857 --\u003e 00:10:50.900\r\nWhy don't you reserve\r\njudgment until you've heard\r\n\r\n00:10:50.984 --\u003e 00:10:52.819\r\nwhat Officer Montoya has to say.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.194 --\u003e 00:10:55.155\r\nAll right,\r\nlet's have your version.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.197 --\u003e 00:10:58.950\r\nLike I said before,\r\nwe got there on time.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.409 --\u003e 00:11:00.660\r\nBullock was down.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.911 --\u003e 00:11:04.497\r\nHe said there were \u003ci\u003estill\u003c/i\u003e suspects\r\ninside, \u003ci\u003eso I\u003c/i\u003e entered.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.673 --\u003e 00:11:15.300\r\nTHUG 1: We'll take\r\nit down to Hathcock.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.592 --\u003e 00:11:17.802\r\n\u003ci\u003eMONTOYA: And then I heard\r\nthe name \"Hathcock.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:19.554 --\u003e 00:11:21.431\r\nFreeze! Police!\r\n\r\n00:11:35.236 --\u003e 00:11:36.362\r\n(SCREAMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:11:41.284 --\u003e 00:11:42.368\r\nGet her.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.702 --\u003e 00:11:43.703\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.786 --\u003e 00:11:45.205\r\nMy pleasure.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.582 --\u003e 00:11:49.375\r\n(LAUGHS EVILLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:57.133 --\u003e 00:11:59.427\r\n\u003ci\u003eMONTOYA: I guess Batman must\r\nhave gotten a second wind\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:59.510 --\u003e 00:12:01.971\r\n\u003ci\u003eafter Detective Bullock\r\ndragged him out.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:03.765 --\u003e 00:12:05.558\r\nBecause he was in rare form.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.642 --\u003e 00:12:07.727\r\n(THUGS GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:09.812 --\u003e 00:12:10.813\r\nBehind you!\r\n\r\n00:12:18.029 --\u003e 00:12:19.239\r\n(woon CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:21.616 --\u003e 00:12:25.286\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was just about to cuff them when\r\nthe whole place started to come down.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:26.120 --\u003e 00:12:28.748\r\n\u003ci\u003eBefore I knew what happened,\r\nBatman pushed me out of the way.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:34.587 --\u003e 00:12:36.631\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe was buried alive.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:44.639 --\u003e 00:12:47.850\r\n- There was nothing I could do.\r\n- Poor Batman.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.142 --\u003e 00:12:51.354\r\nBut don't feel too bad.\r\nOne of you is going to burn, too.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.437 --\u003e 00:12:54.899\r\nWhat we've got here is\r\nthree cops with two stories.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.191 --\u003e 00:12:58.611\r\n- I'm telling you, they were late!\r\n- Commissioner, it's just not true.\r\n\r\n00:12:58.695 --\u003e 00:13:00.113\r\nBullock went in early.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.196 --\u003e 00:13:03.408\r\nSo you're accusing the detective\r\nof trying to hog the collar?\r\n\r\n00:13:03.700 --\u003e 00:13:05.868\r\nHe may have had good\r\nreason for going in.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.077 --\u003e 00:13:07.537\r\nBut we were not late.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.870 --\u003e 00:13:09.580\r\nSo it's my word against theirs.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.373 --\u003e 00:13:11.958\r\nNow what, Commissioner?\r\n\r\n00:13:12.041 --\u003e 00:13:15.211\r\nYou're all suspended\r\nuntil I make my decision.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.295 --\u003e 00:13:17.630\r\n- Suspended?\r\n- Hey, you can't...\r\n\r\n00:13:17.880 --\u003e 00:13:19.007\r\nBut no, l..\r\n\r\n00:13:19.215 --\u003e 00:13:21.759\r\nI'll take your badges\r\nand your weapons.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.566 --\u003e 00:13:38.109\r\nYou too, Officer.\r\n\r\n00:14:04.427 --\u003e 00:14:05.887\r\nDoc. Doc.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.430 --\u003e 00:14:08.890\r\nDr. Hathcock. Dock!\r\n\r\n00:14:16.481 --\u003e 00:14:18.858\r\nDock. Gotham Harbor! The dock!\r\n\r\n00:14:19.317 --\u003e 00:14:20.401\r\nI'd better tell...\r\n\r\n00:14:20.985 --\u003e 00:14:22.070\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.446 --\u003e 00:14:25.073\r\n(TRAIN ENGINE RUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:47.804 --\u003e 00:14:49.514\r\n- Hathcock. Yes!\r\n- (SNAPS FINGERS)\r\n\r\n00:14:51.099 --\u003e 00:14:52.934\r\nNow it all comes together.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.956 --\u003e 00:15:16.249\r\n(METAL JINGLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:21.587 --\u003e 00:15:24.590\r\n(LOCK CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:34.809 --\u003e 00:15:37.687\r\nI wonder what the boss is gonna\r\ndo with pointy-ears up there.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.979 --\u003e 00:15:40.064\r\nWell,\r\nhe's already been charbroiled.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.148 --\u003e 00:15:42.066\r\n- How about we skewer him?\r\n- (AIR GUSHES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:15:42.150 --\u003e 00:15:45.778\r\nNo. The boss figures he's\r\nworth more in one piece.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.447\r\nBATMAN: Where is your boss?\r\n\r\n00:15:47.530 --\u003e 00:15:49.907\r\nIs he gonna keep me\r\nhanging around all day?\r\n\r\n00:15:50.450 --\u003e 00:15:51.993\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.076 --\u003e 00:15:54.871\r\nKeep your cape on.\r\nHe's right up there.\r\n\r\n00:15:56.289 --\u003e 00:15:58.958\r\nThat's all I wanted to know.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.882 --\u003e 00:16:06.924\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:10.761 --\u003e 00:16:12.305\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:16:20.897 --\u003e 00:16:22.648\r\n(SPLASHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:23.733 --\u003e 00:16:25.193\r\n(ROPE CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:27.695 --\u003e 00:16:28.863\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.007 --\u003e 00:16:50.527\r\n- I thought you were...\r\n- Not while there's unfinished business.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.810 --\u003e 00:17:01.020\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.329 --\u003e 00:17:19.372\r\n(THUG GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.927 --\u003e 00:17:34.220\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.514 --\u003e 00:17:37.640\r\n(THUG GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.807 --\u003e 00:17:40.476\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:40.726 --\u003e 00:17:41.852\r\n(WATER SPLASH ES)\r\n\r\n00:17:44.897 --\u003e 00:17:46.232\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:17:51.279 --\u003e 00:17:53.447\r\nTHUG: Argh!\r\nGive me another clip.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.412 --\u003e 00:18:00.663\r\nOh, boy!\r\n\r\n00:18:03.249 --\u003e 00:18:04.542\r\nAre you all right?\r\n\r\n00:18:04.792 --\u003e 00:18:06.085\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.128 --\u003e 00:18:09.964\r\n- Dandy.\r\n- Then don't go away.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.548 --\u003e 00:18:11.591\r\nCount on it.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.383 --\u003e 00:18:13.801\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:18:19.432 --\u003e 00:18:20.433\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:52.965 --\u003e 00:18:54.175\r\n(CRANE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.010 --\u003e 00:18:57.094\r\nALL: What?\r\n\r\n00:19:03.601 --\u003e 00:19:04.685\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.733 --\u003e 00:19:11.859\r\n(SCREAMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PANIC)\r\n\r\n00:19:20.785 --\u003e 00:19:21.869\r\n(SHIP HORN SOUNDS)\r\n\r\n00:19:29.627 --\u003e 00:19:30.878\r\n(ROPE CREAKS)\r\n\r\n00:19:45.643 --\u003e 00:19:46.852\r\n(BOTH GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.899 --\u003e 00:19:53.234\r\n(CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.828 --\u003e 00:20:05.037\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:11.460 --\u003e 00:20:12.628\r\n(CRASHING LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:26.517 --\u003e 00:20:27.893\r\n(CRANE ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.103 --\u003e 00:20:30.521\r\n(CRANE CREAKS)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.314 --\u003e 00:20:33.774\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:51.333 --\u003e 00:20:53.461\r\n(POLICE CHATTER ON RADIO)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.841 --\u003e 00:21:00.718\r\nGORDON: I have to hand it to\r\nyou, Montoya.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.177 --\u003e 00:21:03.512\r\nYou and the Batman really\r\nturned this thing around.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.763 --\u003e 00:21:07.057\r\nYeah. What a collar.\r\nYou didn't just bust them,\r\n\r\n00:21:07.141 --\u003e 00:21:08.976\r\nyou put the whole gang\r\nout of commission.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.059 --\u003e 00:21:11.395\r\nWhat collar? She's suspended!\r\n\r\n00:21:11.687 --\u003e 00:21:13.898\r\nThis farce has gone far\r\nenough, Hackle.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.398 --\u003e 00:21:16.734\r\nWe've nailed the suspects\r\nand recovered our money.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.984 --\u003e 00:21:18.569\r\nThe investigation is closed.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.403 --\u003e 00:21:21.655\r\nOfficer Montoya\r\nearned this collar.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.865 --\u003e 00:21:26.994\r\nThe collar belongs to all three of us.\r\nIt was a team effort.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.204 --\u003e 00:21:30.456\r\nGee, thanks, partner.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.956 --\u003e 00:21:31.999\r\n(GRUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:21:32.625 --\u003e 00:21:33.876\r\nWhat was that, Bullock?\r\n\r\n00:21:36.045 --\u003e 00:21:37.254\r\nI said...\r\n\r\n00:21:38.547 --\u003e 00:21:40.132\r\nThanks a lot, Montoya.\r\n\r\n00:21:49.600 --\u003e 00:21:51.101\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.879 --\u003e 00:22:19.880\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E14 - The Clock King (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.756 --\u003e 00:00:07.758\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.749 --\u003e 00:01:23.750\r\n(TRAIN APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:27.713 --\u003e 00:01:28.714\r\n(DOOR BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:01:29.506 --\u003e 00:01:30.799\r\nIt's about time.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.512 --\u003e 00:01:36.513\r\n(DOOR BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.434 --\u003e 00:01:41.518\r\nGood morning, Hill.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.103 --\u003e 00:01:46.648\r\n- Oh, good morning, um...\r\n- Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.857 --\u003e 00:01:48.233\r\nTemple Fugate?\r\n\r\n00:01:48.817 --\u003e 00:01:51.653\r\nI should think you'd remember\r\nthe name by now, Counselor.\r\n\r\n00:01:51.820 --\u003e 00:01:54.990\r\nWe've only been taking the\r\nsame train every day for...\r\n\r\n00:01:55.198 --\u003e 00:01:58.535\r\nOne year,\r\nseven months and 13 days.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.161 --\u003e 00:02:01.788\r\nRight. The efficiency expert.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.290 --\u003e 00:02:05.292\r\nSix minutes behind schedule.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.378 --\u003e 00:02:11.006\r\nYou seem pretty tightly\r\nwound this morning, Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.381 --\u003e 00:02:13.550\r\nI have an important\r\ncourt hearing today.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.675 --\u003e 00:02:16.928\r\nThere's been a $20 million\r\njudgment against my company.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.012 --\u003e 00:02:18.847\r\nMy attorney has appealed.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.930 --\u003e 00:02:20.140\r\nBut if we lose,\r\n\r\n00:02:20.223 --\u003e 00:02:22.351\r\nit's the end of everything.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.726 --\u003e 00:02:24.811\r\nTemple,\r\nlet me give you some advice.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.103 --\u003e 00:02:27.898\r\nI'm a lawyer.\r\nTrust me, I know these things.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.981 --\u003e 00:02:31.193\r\nIf that judge sees you\r\nlooking as tense and haggard\r\n\r\n00:02:31.276 --\u003e 00:02:32.486\r\nas you are now,\r\n\r\n00:02:32.611 --\u003e 00:02:34.363\r\nhe'll think you were\r\nup to something.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.821 --\u003e 00:02:35.822\r\nLoosen up.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.906 --\u003e 00:02:38.116\r\nDo something to relax\r\nbefore you go into court.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.325 --\u003e 00:02:40.619\r\nGet out of your routine\r\nfor a few minutes.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.911 --\u003e 00:02:42.371\r\nDo you take a coffee break?\r\n\r\n00:02:42.537 --\u003e 00:02:44.081\r\nOf course. Every day,\r\n\r\n00:02:44.247 --\u003e 00:02:45.832\r\nat 3:00 on the dot.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.291 --\u003e 00:02:48.251\r\nThen take it at 3:15.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.920 --\u003e 00:02:51.713\r\nBut... My schedule.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.047 --\u003e 00:02:54.257\r\nForget your schedule\r\nfor one day.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.342 --\u003e 00:02:58.178\r\nBelieve me,\r\nit will make a new man out of you.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.932 --\u003e 00:03:03.183\r\n(TYPING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.650 --\u003e 00:03:13.527\r\nI needed those five minutes ago.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.860 --\u003e 00:03:15.070\r\nI'm sorry, sir, but...\r\n\r\n00:03:15.195 --\u003e 00:03:16.780\r\nThirty-seven pages?\r\n\r\n00:03:16.905 --\u003e 00:03:20.617\r\nThat would take a copier exactly\r\none minute and 49 seconds.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.034 --\u003e 00:03:23.453\r\nOne more delay like\r\nthis and you're fired.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.704 --\u003e 00:03:26.456\r\nYour coffee, sir.\r\nAnd those court documents you requested.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.166 --\u003e 00:03:31.044\r\nMAYOR HILL: \u003ci\u003eTake your\r\ncoffee break at 3:15.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:32.254 --\u003e 00:03:33.880\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd get out of the office.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:34.715 --\u003e 00:03:36.466\r\nPut that in a thermos, Ms.\r\nPerkins.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.401 --\u003e 00:03:55.527\r\n(BALL BOUNCING)\r\n\r\n00:04:01.950 --\u003e 00:04:02.951\r\n(SIGHS DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:04:04.035 --\u003e 00:04:05.036\r\nAah!\r\n\r\n00:04:05.954 --\u003e 00:04:06.955\r\n(CHILDREN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:07.038 --\u003e 00:04:09.291\r\nYou little brats!\r\n\r\n00:04:10.250 --\u003e 00:04:11.251\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:15.589 --\u003e 00:04:17.382\r\nNo! No!\r\n\r\n00:04:17.632 --\u003e 00:04:19.217\r\nDon't do this to me!\r\n\r\n00:04:21.219 --\u003e 00:04:23.180\r\nMy lawyer needs those papers.\r\n\r\n00:04:31.938 --\u003e 00:04:32.939\r\n(DOG BARKS)\r\n\r\n00:04:38.820 --\u003e 00:04:40.864\r\nDue to his failure to appear,\r\n\r\n00:04:40.989 --\u003e 00:04:43.742\r\nthis court finds your\r\nclient in default.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.867 --\u003e 00:04:46.203\r\nSummary judgment\r\nagainst him stands,\r\n\r\n00:04:46.578 --\u003e 00:04:47.871\r\nat $20 million.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.414 --\u003e 00:04:52.083\r\nNo! You can't! I'll be ruined!\r\n\r\n00:04:52.334 --\u003e 00:04:56.004\r\nThen perhaps this will teach\r\nyou to be on time for a change.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.087 --\u003e 00:04:58.799\r\n(TICKING CLOCK ECHOES)\r\n\r\n00:04:59.674 --\u003e 00:05:00.675\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:27.410 --\u003e 00:05:29.621\r\n(CLOCK TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.377 --\u003e 00:05:36.378\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:41.716 --\u003e 00:05:45.178\r\nAre you quite sure you won't\r\nstop for breakfast, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:05:45.512 --\u003e 00:05:47.848\r\nThe meals they serve\r\nat these fundraisers...\r\n\r\n00:05:47.973 --\u003e 00:05:49.766\r\nMmm, ghastly.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.891 --\u003e 00:05:52.811\r\nBRUCE: Alfred, I'm sure Mayor\r\nHill will put out a good spread.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.936 --\u003e 00:05:54.980\r\nHe knows you don't kick\r\noff a reelection campaign\r\n\r\n00:05:55.063 --\u003e 00:05:56.398\r\nby poisoning your supporters.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.819 --\u003e 00:06:03.446\r\nReally? If he were in a\r\nhurry to get to the food,\r\n\r\n00:06:03.530 --\u003e 00:06:05.699\r\nhe'd be ahead of us\r\ninstead of behind us.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.782 --\u003e 00:06:06.783\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:10.537 --\u003e 00:06:11.538\r\n(HORNS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:06:15.125 --\u003e 00:06:18.503\r\nI take it taxi drivers\r\nare no longer required\r\n\r\n00:06:18.587 --\u003e 00:06:20.463\r\nto obey traffic signals.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.589 --\u003e 00:06:22.048\r\nClimb off it, geezer.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.132 --\u003e 00:06:23.425\r\nYou had the red.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.717 --\u003e 00:06:24.797\r\nBRUCE: It's nobody's fault.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.051 --\u003e 00:06:26.052\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.763 --\u003e 00:06:30.557\r\nThe traffic signals\r\nare malfunctioning.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.476 --\u003e 00:06:34.519\r\nWhat the devil?\r\n\r\n00:06:35.186 --\u003e 00:06:36.396\r\nMAN: That is rude!\r\n\r\n00:06:36.479 --\u003e 00:06:37.790\r\nIt's the same\r\nthing all the time.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.814 --\u003e 00:06:38.815\r\n(PEOPLE ARGUING)\r\n\r\n00:06:39.399 --\u003e 00:06:40.483\r\nMAN 2: I'll sue you.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.326 --\u003e 00:06:50.785\r\nThere's the foul-up.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.911 --\u003e 00:06:52.370\r\nMayor Over-the-Hill.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.454 --\u003e 00:06:54.623\r\nNothing works right\r\nin this city no more.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.165 --\u003e 00:06:58.376\r\nI fear this does not bode\r\nwell for his campaign.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.127 --\u003e 00:07:00.128\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.253 --\u003e 00:07:01.296\r\nNo, it doesn't.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.421 --\u003e 00:07:03.465\r\nAnd that may be\r\nexactly the point.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.347 --\u003e 00:07:11.348\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.808 --\u003e 00:07:14.893\r\n(CROWD GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:23.151 --\u003e 00:07:24.402\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:25.028 --\u003e 00:07:26.988\r\nAnother piece of\r\noutlandish graffiti?\r\n\r\n00:07:27.489 --\u003e 00:07:30.075\r\nIs this somebody's\r\nidea of a joke?\r\n\r\n00:07:47.425 --\u003e 00:07:48.593\r\nBATMAN: Hold it!\r\n\r\n00:07:48.885 --\u003e 00:07:50.512\r\nWell, well.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.971 --\u003e 00:07:52.138\r\nThe Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.305 --\u003e 00:07:54.349\r\nIt's about time you showed up.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.724 --\u003e 00:07:58.228\r\nI suppose you want to know why\r\nI've brought downtown Gotham\r\n\r\n00:07:58.353 --\u003e 00:08:00.438\r\nto a standstill, Batman. Hmm?\r\n\r\n00:08:00.647 --\u003e 00:08:02.399\r\nWell, let's just say\r\n\r\n00:08:02.482 --\u003e 00:08:07.362\r\nit's because I'm a civic-minded citizen\r\nwith a lot of time on his hands.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.531 --\u003e 00:08:10.532\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.916 --\u003e 00:08:21.835\r\nI want some answers, wise guy.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.753 --\u003e 00:08:24.754\r\nTalk!\r\n\r\n00:08:24.921 --\u003e 00:08:25.922\r\nA pity.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.047 --\u003e 00:08:27.966\r\nI don't know what to tell\r\nyou, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.341 --\u003e 00:08:31.094\r\nExcept, perhaps that the 9:15\r\n\r\n00:08:31.177 --\u003e 00:08:33.972\r\nis always six minutes early.\r\n\r\n00:08:51.072 --\u003e 00:08:52.073\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:53.867 --\u003e 00:08:57.495\r\nBATMAN: If the creep with the clocks\r\ndid sabotage the entire traffic system,\r\n\r\n00:08:57.954 --\u003e 00:08:59.914\r\nhe had to have\r\ncome here to do it.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.790 --\u003e 00:09:01.791\r\nWait here.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.083 --\u003e 00:09:03.084\r\n(BATCLAW CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:07.797 --\u003e 00:09:08.798\r\nMy pleasure.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.882 --\u003e 00:09:12.135\r\nThis is one of the finest\r\nback alleys in all of Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.168 --\u003e 00:09:46.878\r\nBATMAN: What kind of saboteur\r\n\r\n00:09:46.961 --\u003e 00:09:50.507\r\nuses a $6,000 Metronex\r\nto trigger a time bomb?\r\n\r\n00:09:50.632 --\u003e 00:09:53.009\r\nA saboteur with too much money?\r\n\r\n00:09:53.676 --\u003e 00:09:56.012\r\nMost jewelry stores\r\nregister the serial numbers\r\n\r\n00:09:56.096 --\u003e 00:09:57.555\r\nof the Metronexes they sell.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.767 --\u003e 00:10:02.936\r\nLet's see what the\r\npolice database turns up.\r\n\r\n00:10:05.396 --\u003e 00:10:08.858\r\n\"Temple Fugate. 362 Brayfogle.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:09.359 --\u003e 00:10:10.568\r\nLet's go, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:10:15.281 --\u003e 00:10:19.202\r\nIt appears Mr. Fugate's\r\nneighborhood has seen better days.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.552 --\u003e 00:10:36.845\r\n(CLOCKS TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.243 --\u003e 00:11:01.661\r\n(RADIO STATIC)\r\n\r\n00:11:06.166 --\u003e 00:11:08.501\r\nBATMAN: What is it about\r\nthat particular clock tower?\r\n\r\n00:11:08.751 --\u003e 00:11:11.421\r\nHe's got more data on it than\r\nanything else in the city.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.588 --\u003e 00:11:13.464\r\nALFRED: There's been\r\na slight blackout.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.548 --\u003e 00:11:16.509\r\nJust one city block,\r\nbetween Schiff and Robinson,\r\n\r\n00:11:16.593 --\u003e 00:11:18.011\r\nwest of Molldorf.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.136 --\u003e 00:11:21.014\r\nBATMAN: The location of\r\nGotham Mutual's main branch.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.431 --\u003e 00:11:24.684\r\nNo doubt some malefactors\r\nblacked out the bank,\r\n\r\n00:11:24.976 --\u003e 00:11:26.936\r\nto disable the\r\nlocks on the vault.\r\n\r\n00:11:27.312 --\u003e 00:11:29.814\r\nYes, the time locks.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.981 --\u003e 00:11:30.982\r\n- Fugate.\r\n- Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.149 --\u003e 00:11:32.942\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:03.514 --\u003e 00:12:04.515\r\n(TIMER BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:12:06.392 --\u003e 00:12:07.644\r\n(SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.811 --\u003e 00:12:09.812\r\n(TAPE CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:10.813 --\u003e 00:12:13.524\r\n\u003ci\u003eFUGATE ON\u003c/i\u003e TAPE: \u003ci\u003eSorry I couldn't\r\nbe with you in person, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:13.650 --\u003e 00:12:15.360\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut, I've got a train to catch.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:15.443 --\u003e 00:12:18.571\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis box contains a\r\nhigh-speed vacuum pump.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:18.696 --\u003e 00:12:21.532\r\n\u003ci\u003eI know you've got all\r\nkinds of gas masks.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:21.699 --\u003e 00:12:23.701\r\n\u003ci\u003eSo, I'm putting you\r\nout of my misery\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:23.785 --\u003e 00:12:27.121\r\n\u003ci\u003eby simply removing all\r\nthe oxygen from the room.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:30.959 --\u003e 00:12:32.877\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe process will\r\ntake 15 minutes,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:33.211 --\u003e 00:12:35.004\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhich is exactly 17 minutes less\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:35.088 --\u003e 00:12:36.589\r\n\u003ci\u003ethan the time it would take you\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:36.673 --\u003e 00:12:39.968\r\n\u003ci\u003eto burn through the door with\r\nthat oxyacetylene torch of yours.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:41.302 --\u003e 00:12:44.722\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, and, I don't recommend trying\r\nto open the pump's housing.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:44.931 --\u003e 00:12:47.725\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's rigged with a\r\nvibration-sensitive explosive.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:47.976 --\u003e 00:12:50.353\r\n\u003ci\u003eOf course,\r\nif you want to get blown to bits,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:50.603 --\u003e 00:12:52.230\r\n\u003ci\u003ethat's fine with me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:52.355 --\u003e 00:12:55.858\r\n\u003ci\u003eEither way,\r\nit's time to say adieu, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:26.681 --\u003e 00:13:27.974\r\n(BAND PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.979 --\u003e 00:13:35.106\r\nThis magnificent station,\r\n\r\n00:13:35.231 --\u003e 00:13:39.027\r\nhome of the world's first\r\nfully-automated subway line,\r\n\r\n00:13:39.152 --\u003e 00:13:41.779\r\nis the fulfillment\r\nof my pledge to you,\r\n\r\n00:13:41.863 --\u003e 00:13:42.947\r\n(SIGNAL BELL CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:43.031 --\u003e 00:13:46.868\r\nto make our subways\r\nsafer and more efficient.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.993 --\u003e 00:13:50.955\r\nAnd so,\r\nI declare Gotham Central Station\r\n\r\n00:13:51.080 --\u003e 00:13:52.999\r\nofficially open.\r\n\r\n00:13:54.125 --\u003e 00:13:55.126\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.960 --\u003e 00:13:57.420\r\n(BAND PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:14:01.716 --\u003e 00:14:03.968\r\nLet the first train arrive!\r\n\r\n00:14:13.478 --\u003e 00:14:14.729\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:15.313 --\u003e 00:14:16.939\r\nWOMAN: (LAUGHING) Where is it?\r\n\r\n00:14:28.785 --\u003e 00:14:29.786\r\n(WHEEZING)\r\n\r\n00:14:40.880 --\u003e 00:14:42.507\r\nWOMAN: What an embarrassment.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.133 --\u003e 00:14:47.720\r\nI wanted that train\r\nhere at 2:30 on the dot!\r\n\r\n00:14:48.137 --\u003e 00:14:50.723\r\n\u003ci\u003eFUGATE: So,\r\nis this what you want?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:50.848 --\u003e 00:14:53.684\r\n\u003ci\u003eA mayor who can't even\r\nget a single subway train\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:53.768 --\u003e 00:14:54.977\r\n\u003ci\u003eto arrive on time?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:55.061 --\u003e 00:14:56.062\r\n(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:14:59.565 --\u003e 00:15:00.566\r\n(CROWD CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.151 --\u003e 00:15:03.861\r\n\u003ci\u003eFUGATE: Clear the\r\nplatform, please.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:04.112 --\u003e 00:15:07.490\r\n\u003ci\u003eHere comes some more of\r\nour mayor's incompetence.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:07.573 --\u003e 00:15:08.574\r\n(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.783 --\u003e 00:15:10.034\r\n(ALL GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:11.828 --\u003e 00:15:12.829\r\n(CROWD CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:15:28.761 --\u003e 00:15:29.846\r\n(TRAIN CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:40.898 --\u003e 00:15:42.066\r\n(CROWD SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:46.696 --\u003e 00:15:49.240\r\nOnly minor injuries. Thank God.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.407 --\u003e 00:15:51.200\r\nHill! Where's Hill?\r\n\r\n00:15:53.870 --\u003e 00:15:54.871\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:11.637 --\u003e 00:16:12.638\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:13.055 --\u003e 00:16:14.056\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:16:22.064 --\u003e 00:16:23.399\r\n(GROANING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:36.037 --\u003e 00:16:37.955\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd in the wake of\r\nthe subway accident,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:38.039 --\u003e 00:16:39.040\r\n\u003ci\u003ethis grim news,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:39.165 --\u003e 00:16:41.250\r\n\u003ci\u003eMayor Hamilton\r\nHill has vanished.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:41.626 --\u003e 00:16:43.878\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe police have no\r\nleads to his whereabouts\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:44.003 --\u003e 00:16:45.838\r\n\u003ci\u003eand they fear he may\r\nhave been kidnapped.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:46.881 --\u003e 00:16:47.882\r\n(CLOCK CHIMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:52.887 --\u003e 00:16:53.888\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.892 --\u003e 00:16:59.477\r\nFUGATE: Comfortable, Hill?\r\n\r\n00:16:59.644 --\u003e 00:17:01.354\r\nWell, you won't be for long.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.687 --\u003e 00:17:06.150\r\nAt 3:15 on the dot,\r\nthose hands will come together,\r\n\r\n00:17:06.317 --\u003e 00:17:08.444\r\nand you'll be crushed\r\nlike an insect.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.903 --\u003e 00:17:10.780\r\n3:15, Hill.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.988 --\u003e 00:17:14.116\r\nDoes that time hold\r\nany meaning for you?\r\n\r\n00:17:14.242 --\u003e 00:17:16.118\r\nI don't know what\r\nyou're talking about!\r\n\r\n00:17:16.369 --\u003e 00:17:20.623\r\nYou told me to take my\r\ncoffee break at 3:15.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.998 --\u003e 00:17:23.501\r\n- What?\r\n- You don't remember?\r\n\r\n00:17:23.668 --\u003e 00:17:24.961\r\nMy court date?\r\n\r\n00:17:27.296 --\u003e 00:17:28.923\r\nOh, my Lord!\r\n\r\n00:17:29.006 --\u003e 00:17:30.174\r\nThe lawsuit!\r\n\r\n00:17:30.591 --\u003e 00:17:33.970\r\nFugate, I swear,\r\nI was only trying to help.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.178 --\u003e 00:17:35.258\r\nFUGATE: Don't hand me that.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.429 --\u003e 00:17:36.556\r\nYou did it on purpose.\r\n\r\n00:17:36.847 --\u003e 00:17:40.601\r\nThe plaintiffs were represented\r\nby your law firm, Mr. Mayor.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.352 --\u003e 00:17:42.353\r\n(LIGHTNING CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:17:43.437 --\u003e 00:17:46.399\r\nBut I had nothing to do\r\nwith that case, Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:17:46.899 --\u003e 00:17:47.942\r\nLiar!\r\n\r\n00:17:48.234 --\u003e 00:17:49.944\r\nNot that it matters anymore,\r\n\r\n00:17:50.194 --\u003e 00:17:54.865\r\nnow that you have an appointment\r\nto keep at 3:15 precisely,\r\n\r\n00:17:54.949 --\u003e 00:17:56.951\r\nwith the grim reaper!\r\n\r\n00:17:57.034 --\u003e 00:17:58.619\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.124 --\u003e 00:18:04.125\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:04.333 --\u003e 00:18:07.044\r\nI'm here to clean your\r\nclock, Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.169 --\u003e 00:18:09.046\r\nFUGATE: Don't count on\r\nit, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.171 --\u003e 00:18:12.049\r\nWhen it comes to\r\nclocks, I am king.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.258 --\u003e 00:18:13.384\r\n\u003ci\u003eEn garde!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:14.635 --\u003e 00:18:15.970\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:16.429 --\u003e 00:18:17.430\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:18:18.014 --\u003e 00:18:19.015\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:18:19.849 --\u003e 00:18:21.017\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.727 --\u003e 00:18:23.728\r\n(LIGHTNING CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:18:41.329 --\u003e 00:18:42.538\r\nGive it up, Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.622 --\u003e 00:18:44.582\r\nHill committed no\r\ncrime against you.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.707 --\u003e 00:18:46.167\r\nHe did worse.\r\n\r\n00:18:46.417 --\u003e 00:18:48.252\r\nHe made me late!\r\n\r\n00:18:51.005 --\u003e 00:18:52.757\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.736 --\u003e 00:19:14.737\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.329 --\u003e 00:19:24.330\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:25.498 --\u003e 00:19:27.583\r\nFUGATE: I could do this all\r\nday, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:19:27.708 --\u003e 00:19:29.001\r\nbut your time is up.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.587 --\u003e 00:19:32.588\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.091 --\u003e 00:19:36.509\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:50.564 --\u003e 00:19:52.191\r\nFUGATE: I've studied\r\nnews footage of you.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.274 --\u003e 00:19:53.394\r\nAnd I know that it takes you\r\n\r\n00:19:53.442 --\u003e 00:19:56.904\r\nexactly 1/20 of a\r\nsecond to throw a punch.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.530 --\u003e 00:19:58.614\r\nBATMAN: Very clever.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.115 --\u003e 00:20:01.534\r\nBut it only takes\r\nme 1/30 of a second\r\n\r\n00:20:01.826 --\u003e 00:20:03.327\r\nto do this.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.954 --\u003e 00:20:05.955\r\n(coes GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:08.874 --\u003e 00:20:10.292\r\n(POWERING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:20:10.501 --\u003e 00:20:11.627\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:14.130 --\u003e 00:20:15.131\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:20:18.926 --\u003e 00:20:20.010\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:20:22.304 --\u003e 00:20:23.639\r\n(GEARS CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.113 --\u003e 00:20:40.281\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:41.741 --\u003e 00:20:42.908\r\nFugate!\r\n\r\n00:20:43.033 --\u003e 00:20:44.493\r\nYou can't escape!\r\n\r\n00:20:44.785 --\u003e 00:20:47.163\r\n\u003ci\u003eAu contraire, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:48.998 --\u003e 00:20:51.000\r\nYou of all people should know\r\n\r\n00:20:51.792 --\u003e 00:20:53.919\r\nthere's always a way out.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.504 --\u003e 00:20:56.964\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:21:00.760 --\u003e 00:21:01.761\r\nFugate!\r\n\r\n00:21:04.013 --\u003e 00:21:05.014\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:21:12.605 --\u003e 00:21:13.647\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:21:16.609 --\u003e 00:21:17.610\r\n(MAYOR HILL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:19.487 --\u003e 00:21:20.988\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:26.494 --\u003e 00:21:27.995\r\n(INDISTINCT POLICE\r\nRADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:21:30.331 --\u003e 00:21:33.011\r\nGORDON: Well, he won't be doing any\r\nmore campaigning for a few days.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.584 --\u003e 00:21:35.336\r\nBut at least the Mayor is safe.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.753 --\u003e 00:21:37.838\r\nBATMAN: No trace of this Clock\r\nKing, though.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.172 --\u003e 00:21:40.549\r\nGORDON: How could anyone\r\nsurvive a wreck like this?\r\n\r\n00:21:40.758 --\u003e 00:21:42.927\r\nBATMAN: If I could, he could.\r\n\r\n00:21:43.052 --\u003e 00:21:44.053\r\nThen,\r\n\r\n00:21:44.512 --\u003e 00:21:46.180\r\nyou think we'll\r\nhear from him again?\r\n\r\n00:21:46.388 --\u003e 00:21:48.140\r\nI wouldn't be\r\nsurprised, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:21:48.265 --\u003e 00:21:49.266\r\nIn fact,\r\n\r\n00:21:49.350 --\u003e 00:21:51.769\r\nI'd say,\r\nit's only a matter of time.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.852 --\u003e 00:21:52.853\r\n(CLOCK TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:21:56.774 --\u003e 00:21:58.776\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:23.801 --\u003e 00:22:24.802\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E15 - The Last Laugh (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.173 --\u003e 00:00:08.175\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:54.031 --\u003e 00:01:55.073\r\n(SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:01:55.407 --\u003e 00:01:57.451\r\nEw! P.U.!\r\n\r\n00:01:58.327 --\u003e 00:02:00.829\r\nOf all the disgusting...\r\n\r\n00:02:01.622 --\u003e 00:02:03.749\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:03.832 --\u003e 00:02:05.208\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:05.292 --\u003e 00:02:08.045\r\n- (CAR HORN HONKS)\r\n- (CONTINUES LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:09.379 --\u003e 00:02:10.964\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.840 --\u003e 00:02:14.509\r\nLook out, you crazy...\r\n\r\n00:02:14.593 --\u003e 00:02:17.804\r\n(BOTH LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:22.017 --\u003e 00:02:23.810\r\n(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.429\r\nOuch!\r\n\r\n00:03:01.890 --\u003e 00:03:04.351\r\nRough night of\r\ncrime-fighting, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:04.810 --\u003e 00:03:05.852\r\nVery.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.977 --\u003e 00:03:08.563\r\nWell, you'll be happy to\r\nknow I've drawn you a bath.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.980 --\u003e 00:03:10.148\r\nWhenever you're ready.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.443 --\u003e 00:03:14.778\r\nWhat's the deal, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:03:15.487 --\u003e 00:03:18.365\r\nI said I \"drew\" you a bath, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.408 --\u003e 00:03:20.909\r\nApril Fool's.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.326 --\u003e 00:03:24.746\r\nVery funny, Alfred.\r\nI guess I'll just take a shower.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.955 --\u003e 00:03:27.833\r\nNot a funny bone\r\nin his entire body.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.585 --\u003e 00:03:32.879\r\nAlfred, hit the\r\nradio, would you?\r\n\r\n00:03:33.213 --\u003e 00:03:34.548\r\nRight away, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.215 --\u003e 00:03:37.718\r\nREPORTER: \u003ci\u003eTraffic is at a\r\nstandstill on the Gotham expressway\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:37.801 --\u003e 00:03:40.887\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhere a trailer full of eggs\r\nhas overturned. This just in.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:41.763 --\u003e 00:03:43.306\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Gotham police\r\nare investigating\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:43.390 --\u003e 00:03:46.351\r\na \u003ci\u003eseries of near-fatal\r\naccidents along the riverfront.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:46.435 --\u003e 00:03:49.062\r\n\u003ci\u003eInitial reports indicate\r\nthat hundreds of Gothamites\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:49.146 --\u003e 00:03:52.399\r\n\u003ci\u003ehave inexplicably begun acting\r\nlike total laughing fools.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:53.191 --\u003e 00:03:54.985\r\n\u003ci\u003eMore details as they\r\nbecome available.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:55.694 --\u003e 00:03:58.447\r\nSounds like a rather\r\ndirty April Fools' prank.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.531 --\u003e 00:04:01.408\r\nSounds like the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.319 --\u003e 00:04:40.047\r\nREPORTER: (OVER RADIO) At this \u003ci\u003ehour,\u003c/i\u003e\r\nGotham City is \u003ci\u003ein\u003c/i\u003e the grip of insanity.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.071 --\u003e 00:04:42.282\r\n\u003ci\u003eEverywhere,\r\npeople are turning into lunatics.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:42.365 --\u003e 00:04:44.993\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe latest reports say that\r\nthe wave of foolish hysteria\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:45.118 --\u003e 00:04:47.078\r\n\u003ci\u003eis moving down 7th\r\nAvenue towards...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:47.954 --\u003e 00:04:49.998\r\n\u003ci\u003eTowards the financial district.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:50.957 --\u003e 00:04:53.543\r\n(REPORTER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.046 --\u003e 00:04:57.631\r\nThat's my cue.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.021 --\u003e 00:05:15.857\r\nJOKER: Uh-huh. Hmm...\r\n\r\n00:05:18.235 --\u003e 00:05:20.403\r\n(CHUCKLES) Perfect.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.619 --\u003e 00:05:29.871\r\nNow, everybody,\r\nremember where we parked.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.042 --\u003e 00:05:38.088\r\nWhen the going gets tough,\r\nthe tough go shopping.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.723 --\u003e 00:05:53.645\r\n(BOTH LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:56.189 --\u003e 00:05:59.734\r\n(ALL LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:06:01.987 --\u003e 00:06:06.032\r\n(LAUGHING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:06:31.850 --\u003e 00:06:34.102\r\nWho says crime doesn't pay?\r\n\r\n00:06:54.414 --\u003e 00:06:58.251\r\nNow, this is what I\r\ncall a sidewalk sale.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.885 --\u003e 00:07:08.303\r\n(DEVICE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.386 --\u003e 00:07:10.055\r\n\u003ci\u003eAUTOMATED VOICE:\r\nAirborne gas emanating\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:10.138 --\u003e 00:07:11.389\r\n\u003ci\u003efrom riverfront district.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:11.473 --\u003e 00:07:16.686\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnalysis, lengthy exposure to the gas\r\nwill result in permanent insanity.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:20.815 --\u003e 00:07:24.110\r\nBATMAN: Alfred,\r\nI left the hex key upstairs in the den.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.194 --\u003e 00:07:25.403\r\nWould you bring it down?\r\n\r\n00:07:25.570 --\u003e 00:07:30.075\r\nALFRED: Oh, \u003ci\u003ego fetch it\u003c/i\u003e yourself.\r\n(BLOWING RASPBERRIES)\r\n\r\n00:07:30.742 --\u003e 00:07:33.495\r\nVery funny, Alfred,\r\nbut I've no time to play.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.578 --\u003e 00:07:34.829\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:34.913 --\u003e 00:07:37.040\r\nAlfred? Alfred!\r\n\r\n00:07:37.123 --\u003e 00:07:39.459\r\n(ALFRED LAUGHING IN DISTANCE)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.345 --\u003e 00:07:53.098\r\nJust a little spring\r\ncleaning, sir.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.307 --\u003e 00:07:56.685\r\n(ALFRED CONTINUES LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:57.727 --\u003e 00:07:59.229\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:07:59.354 --\u003e 00:08:00.730\r\nThe gas!\r\n\r\n00:08:01.356 --\u003e 00:08:02.357\r\n(INHALES)\r\n\r\n00:08:09.364 --\u003e 00:08:10.365\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:08:17.455 --\u003e 00:08:18.832\r\n(VASE SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.459 --\u003e 00:08:25.005\r\nI believe I've contracted a\r\ngiant case of the giggles.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.718 --\u003e 00:08:31.320\r\nAUTOMATED VOICE: Lengthy\r\nexposure to the gas\r\n\r\n00:08:31.344 --\u003e 00:08:33.471\r\n\u003ci\u003ewill result in\r\npermanent insanity.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:44.733 --\u003e 00:08:47.444\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:51.865 --\u003e 00:08:54.909\r\nREPORTER: Okay, let's shoot it.\r\nThis place is giving me the creeps.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.160 --\u003e 00:08:56.453\r\nI'm here in downtown Gotham\r\n\r\n00:08:56.536 --\u003e 00:08:59.456\r\nwhere corporate CEOs have\r\ngone stark raving mad.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.539 --\u003e 00:09:03.251\r\nIt would appear that the collapse\r\nof the stock market is now imminent.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.376 --\u003e 00:09:04.419\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe question is,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:04.544 --\u003e 00:09:08.465\r\n\u003ci\u003eWill April Fools' Day mark the\r\nend of Gotham City as we know it?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:09.174 --\u003e 00:09:13.762\r\nThe only things gaining now\r\nare the laughing stocks.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.845 --\u003e 00:09:16.097\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:09:20.935 --\u003e 00:09:22.771\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.897 --\u003e 00:09:25.315\r\n(GRUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.903 --\u003e 00:09:31.488\r\n(JOKER GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.947 --\u003e 00:09:35.658\r\nHuh? Ah!\r\n\r\n00:09:36.534 --\u003e 00:09:37.535\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:09:39.037 --\u003e 00:09:40.038\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:48.463 --\u003e 00:09:49.964\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:10:02.685 --\u003e 00:10:05.980\r\nLook who's come to\r\ntrash the place.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.272 --\u003e 00:10:08.441\r\nA fitting setting for\r\nyou, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.691 --\u003e 00:10:12.028\r\nOoh, I just love to\r\nget down and dirty.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.695 --\u003e 00:10:14.614\r\nOkay, bOys,\r\n\r\n00:10:14.697 --\u003e 00:10:16.533\r\nit's playtime!\r\n\r\n00:10:17.992 --\u003e 00:10:19.494\r\nHENCHMAN 1: It's about time.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.702 --\u003e 00:10:21.538\r\nHENCHMAN 2: What\r\nare we waiting for?\r\n\r\n00:10:23.206 --\u003e 00:10:24.791\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:36.845 --\u003e 00:10:37.846\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:39.097 --\u003e 00:10:43.226\r\nBatman,\r\nyou're a real party pooper.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.601 --\u003e 00:10:46.855\r\nWhy don't you take your mask\r\noff and have a few laughs?\r\n\r\n00:10:47.230 --\u003e 00:10:48.857\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:48.940 --\u003e 00:10:50.775\r\nCut the clowning, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.945 --\u003e 00:10:55.280\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.076 --\u003e 00:11:01.286\r\nGet him.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.540 --\u003e 00:11:06.958\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:07.041 --\u003e 00:11:08.585\r\n(ARMS WHIRRING MECHANICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:11.045 --\u003e 00:11:15.967\r\nTsk-tsk. You shouldn't have\r\nmade Captain Clown mad.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.930 --\u003e 00:11:23.099\r\nTime to take out the garbage!\r\n\r\n00:11:25.268 --\u003e 00:11:27.896\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.525 --\u003e 00:11:36.112\r\nI just love these\r\nnew Ziploc seals.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.446 --\u003e 00:11:41.242\r\nWe wouldn't want our little\r\ncaged rodent to suffocate,\r\n\r\n00:11:41.326 --\u003e 00:11:44.871\r\nso we'll just punch\r\nsome air holes.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.954 --\u003e 00:11:50.752\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:51.127 --\u003e 00:11:54.797\r\nOkay, Captain,\r\ngive it the old heave-ho.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.063 --\u003e 00:12:15.985\r\nOops! Looks like our air\r\nholes are water holes too.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.236 --\u003e 00:12:17.987\r\nWhat a shame!\r\n\r\n00:12:22.033 --\u003e 00:12:24.994\r\n(LAUGHING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:12:43.137 --\u003e 00:12:46.808\r\nI never knew Batman\r\ncould sink so low.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.100 --\u003e 00:12:51.437\r\nWell, Captain, this could be the\r\nstart of a beautiful friendship.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.521 --\u003e 00:12:53.439\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:05.159 --\u003e 00:13:08.496\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:13:08.871 --\u003e 00:13:09.872\r\n(INHALES DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:13:13.793 --\u003e 00:13:14.877\r\n(DEVICE CHIRPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:18.464 --\u003e 00:13:20.216\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:10.266 --\u003e 00:14:13.061\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:15.104 --\u003e 00:14:17.190\r\nYou want to play dirty, Joker?\r\n\r\n00:14:24.572 --\u003e 00:14:28.826\r\nGet ready, boys. Here it comes.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.828 --\u003e 00:14:37.710\r\nThis will give those April fools a\r\nlot more smiles per gallon. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.013 --\u003e 00:14:50.014\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:14:53.518 --\u003e 00:14:56.521\r\nWhat are you fools... Batman!\r\n\r\n00:14:59.982 --\u003e 00:15:03.820\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:05.279 --\u003e 00:15:06.322\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:06.614 --\u003e 00:15:08.574\r\n(GROANS AND BREATHES HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:15:09.367 --\u003e 00:15:11.619\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.710 --\u003e 00:15:22.171\r\n(GRUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:23.047 --\u003e 00:15:25.049\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.734 --\u003e 00:15:45.111\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:15:59.792 --\u003e 00:16:01.586\r\nJOKER: Hey, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:16:02.962 --\u003e 00:16:07.300\r\nLooks like Captain Clown is\r\nreally getting attached to you.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.634 --\u003e 00:16:11.095\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:16:27.778 --\u003e 00:16:29.780\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:30.698 --\u003e 00:16:31.699\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.455 --\u003e 00:16:38.456\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.761 --\u003e 00:16:54.639\r\nYou killed Captain Clown.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.264 --\u003e 00:16:57.975\r\nYou killed Captain Clown!\r\n\r\n00:16:58.768 --\u003e 00:17:01.145\r\nJust for that, Batman...\r\n\r\n00:17:11.030 --\u003e 00:17:12.365\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.448 --\u003e 00:17:14.700\r\nHey, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:17:14.951 --\u003e 00:17:18.913\r\nyou stink so bad I can\r\nsmell you from here!\r\n\r\n00:17:20.122 --\u003e 00:17:21.541\r\n\u003ci\u003ePM}.!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:23.334 --\u003e 00:17:24.961\r\nPYEW, pyew, pyew!\r\n\r\n00:18:10.256 --\u003e 00:18:12.341\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.727 --\u003e 00:18:23.769\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:26.063 --\u003e 00:18:28.065\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:14.737 --\u003e 00:19:18.991\r\n\u003ci\u003e'lee-haw.!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:21.494 --\u003e 00:19:22.495\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:37.635 --\u003e 00:19:40.471\r\nJustice is served hot, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:19:41.055 --\u003e 00:19:45.810\r\nYou're going to melt just like\r\na grilled cheese sandwich.\r\n\r\n00:19:48.062 --\u003e 00:19:51.273\r\n(BELL RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.160 --\u003e 00:20:04.161\r\n(JOKER EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:11.127 --\u003e 00:20:13.796\r\nJustice will be served, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.879 --\u003e 00:20:15.756\r\nService with a smile?\r\n\r\n00:20:18.801 --\u003e 00:20:20.886\r\nClean up your act, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.387 --\u003e 00:20:24.306\r\nOh, that's a joke, right?\r\n\r\n00:20:24.682 --\u003e 00:20:27.101\r\nBatman finally told a joke.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.476 --\u003e 00:20:31.397\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:33.274 --\u003e 00:20:34.275\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.074 --\u003e 00:20:45.536\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:48.122 --\u003e 00:20:52.877\r\nBatman! You wouldn't let me\r\nfry, would you?\r\n\r\n00:20:55.713 --\u003e 00:20:57.256\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:21:12.855 --\u003e 00:21:16.108\r\nI've taken eight showers\r\nand I still feel soiled.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.233 --\u003e 00:21:18.861\r\nUgh! I've never seen\r\nso much garbage.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.279 --\u003e 00:21:22.823\r\nWhat's wrong, Alfred?\r\nAren't you feeling better?\r\n\r\n00:21:22.907 --\u003e 00:21:24.784\r\n\"What's wrong,\" sir?\r\n\r\n00:21:25.367 --\u003e 00:21:29.830\r\nI destroy a priceless Ming vase,\r\nand you ask me what's wrong?\r\n\r\n00:21:31.624 --\u003e 00:21:33.083\r\nDon't worry about it.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.167 --\u003e 00:21:36.045\r\nI'll just take it out of your\r\nsalary for the next couple of years.\r\n\r\n00:21:40.299 --\u003e 00:21:41.759\r\nVery well, sir.\r\n\r\n00:21:44.595 --\u003e 00:21:45.805\r\nAlfred.\r\n\r\n00:21:46.514 --\u003e 00:21:49.475\r\nApril Fool's. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:21:53.270 --\u003e 00:21:55.272\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:19.505 --\u003e 00:22:20.506\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E16 - Eternal Youth (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.920 --\u003e 00:00:04.922\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.792 --\u003e 00:01:24.793\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:36.597 --\u003e 00:01:37.598\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:02:00.746 --\u003e 00:02:01.747\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:09.379 --\u003e 00:02:10.464\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:02:25.812 --\u003e 00:02:26.855\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:02:38.033 --\u003e 00:02:39.034\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:47.668 --\u003e 00:02:50.295\r\n(GASPS) You can't do this.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.545 --\u003e 00:02:52.714\r\nI've seen what you've\r\ndone to the others.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.798 --\u003e 00:02:56.426\r\nPlease let me go.\r\nI'll pay anything.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.802 --\u003e 00:02:58.887\r\nYou've done enough\r\ndamage with your money.\r\n\r\n00:02:59.221 --\u003e 00:03:01.098\r\nYou wicked, evil...\r\n\r\n00:03:01.348 --\u003e 00:03:02.849\r\nEvil, Mrs. Thomas?\r\n\r\n00:03:03.266 --\u003e 00:03:04.726\r\nI don't control a company\r\n\r\n00:03:04.810 --\u003e 00:03:07.979\r\nthat leveled a 1,000-year-old\r\nforest for a strip mine.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.355 --\u003e 00:03:09.648\r\nThat's evil.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.774 --\u003e 00:03:11.775\r\n(CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.858 --\u003e 00:03:12.859\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:03:12.943 --\u003e 00:03:13.985\r\n(MOANING)\r\n\r\n00:03:15.570 --\u003e 00:03:17.072\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.240 --\u003e 00:03:19.950\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:24.246 --\u003e 00:03:27.499\r\nYou and your kind owe\r\nMother Nature a big debt,\r\n\r\n00:03:27.708 --\u003e 00:03:31.044\r\nand I'm going to\r\nsee that you pay it.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.928 --\u003e 00:03:42.097\r\nBRUCE: I don't care how\r\nmuch money we'll lose.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.222 --\u003e 00:03:44.224\r\nI won't have Wayne\r\nEnterprises involved\r\n\r\n00:03:44.307 --\u003e 00:03:47.144\r\nin an operation that\r\ndestroys a rainforest.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.227 --\u003e 00:03:49.187\r\nShut it down or you're gone!\r\n\r\n00:03:49.980 --\u003e 00:03:51.690\r\nOne of my greedy\r\ndirectors made a deal\r\n\r\n00:03:51.773 --\u003e 00:03:53.984\r\nwith a slash-and-burn\r\noutfit in the Amazon.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.192 --\u003e 00:03:56.153\r\nHmm, it's fortunate\r\nyou caught it in time.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.570 --\u003e 00:03:58.864\r\nI hate it when\r\nthings slip by me.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.322 --\u003e 00:04:01.700\r\nAnd with me helping you\r\nto answer your mail,\r\n\r\n00:04:01.783 --\u003e 00:04:02.784\r\nnothing will.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.745 --\u003e 00:04:07.414\r\nAh, it says here you\r\njust won $10 million.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.497 --\u003e 00:04:08.498\r\nThat's nice.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.790 --\u003e 00:04:13.503\r\nHmm, you also received a tape from\r\nsome enterprise called Eternal Youth.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.587 --\u003e 00:04:14.588\r\nShall I have a look?\r\n\r\n00:04:15.797 --\u003e 00:04:16.965\r\nBe my guest.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.555 --\u003e 00:04:24.931\r\n(MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:04:28.685 --\u003e 00:04:31.104\r\n\u003ci\u003eHello, Mr. Wayne, I'm Violet.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:31.396 --\u003e 00:04:32.898\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I'm Lily.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:33.106 --\u003e 00:04:35.442\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd we'd like to invite you...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:35.525 --\u003e 00:04:37.527\r\nTo a free weekend \u003ci\u003eat...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:37.903 --\u003e 00:04:40.030\r\n\u003ci\u003e- The Eternal Youth Spa.\r\n- The Eternal Youth Spa.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:42.491 --\u003e 00:04:44.701\r\nOh, my.\r\nThey even speak in unison.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.796 --\u003e 00:04:56.797\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.922 --\u003e 00:04:57.923\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:04:59.090 --\u003e 00:05:00.091\r\n(MUSIC STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.175 --\u003e 00:05:01.176\r\n(KNOCKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.352 --\u003e 00:05:11.394\r\nMaggie.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.895 --\u003e 00:05:13.271\r\nHello, love.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.316 --\u003e 00:05:18.902\r\nCare to join me\r\nfor a morning jog?\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:25.617\r\nAs much as I'd love to,\r\nMaster Bruce insists I review this tape.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.787 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\n\"Eternal Youth.\"\r\n\r\n00:05:30.664 --\u003e 00:05:32.165\r\nSounds intriguing.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.793 --\u003e 00:05:36.711\r\n- Hello, Bruce.\r\n- Good morning, Maggie.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.878 --\u003e 00:05:37.879\r\n(DOOR CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:05:38.588 --\u003e 00:05:42.217\r\n\u003ci\u003eOur founder, Dr. Daphne Demeter,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:42.300 --\u003e 00:05:44.761\r\n\u003ci\u003ehas created a medical program\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:44.970 --\u003e 00:05:47.389\r\n\u003ci\u003e- that actually reverses.\r\n- My, my, my.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:47.472 --\u003e 00:05:49.140\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe aging process.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:49.224 --\u003e 00:05:50.976\r\nMy gracious.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.685 --\u003e 00:05:53.228\r\nEveryone's got a gimmick.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.812 --\u003e 00:05:57.524\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou'll enjoy a weekend of\r\nsumptuous mineral baths,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:57.899 --\u003e 00:05:59.985\r\n\u003ci\u003especially prepared meals,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:00.277 --\u003e 00:06:02.487\r\n\u003ci\u003eand invigorating nature hikes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.654 --\u003e 00:06:05.156\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn two days, you'll look...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:05.657 --\u003e 00:06:06.908\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd feel...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:07.200 --\u003e 00:06:09.119\r\n\u003ci\u003e- Years younger!\r\n- Years younger!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:09.661 --\u003e 00:06:11.580\r\nIt's the perfect weekend\r\n\r\n00:06:11.913 --\u003e 00:06:15.041\r\n\u003ci\u003efor the harried,\r\nstressed-out executive.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:15.584 --\u003e 00:06:18.712\r\nYou might wanna try this, Bruce,\r\nwith your late nights and all.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.087 --\u003e 00:06:20.630\r\nMy weekends are shot, Maggie.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.089 --\u003e 00:06:23.067\r\nBut if you and Alfred would\r\nlike to go in my place...\r\n\r\n00:06:23.091 --\u003e 00:06:24.092\r\nUh...\r\n\r\n00:06:25.218 --\u003e 00:06:27.345\r\nThank you, sir,\r\nbut we couldn't possibly accept.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.762 --\u003e 00:06:29.389\r\nIt's much too generous.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.682 --\u003e 00:06:32.142\r\nI thought they said it was free.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.767 --\u003e 00:06:36.479\r\nThey did.\r\nOh, Alfie, don't be an old fogy.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.563 --\u003e 00:06:38.857\r\nA little fresh air would\r\ndo us both some good.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.107 --\u003e 00:06:41.526\r\nAnd you have been promising\r\nto take me somewhere.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.028 --\u003e 00:06:44.668\r\nI'm afraid it's quite\r\nout of the question.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.615 --\u003e 00:06:47.908\r\nI've been shanghaied.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:49.367\r\nOh, hush.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.910 --\u003e 00:06:52.037\r\n(EXCLAIMS) Maggie!\r\n\r\n00:07:05.258 --\u003e 00:07:06.509\r\n\u003ci\u003eVIOLET: May I help you?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:06.593 --\u003e 00:07:08.637\r\nHello. I'm Ms. Page.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.720 --\u003e 00:07:09.971\r\nAnd this is Mr. Pennyworth.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.347 --\u003e 00:07:12.265\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe'll be filling\r\nin for Mr. Wayne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:13.600 --\u003e 00:07:15.644\r\nOur target is a no-show.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.061 --\u003e 00:07:17.270\r\nWhat should we do?\r\n\r\n00:07:17.938 --\u003e 00:07:19.105\r\nLet them in.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.397 --\u003e 00:07:22.901\r\nSomebody's got to pay for the\r\nsins of Wayne Enterprises.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.947 --\u003e 00:07:29.616\r\nGood morning.\r\nI am your director, Dr. Demeter,\r\n\r\n00:07:30.367 --\u003e 00:07:31.660\r\nand I welcome you\r\n\r\n00:07:31.993 --\u003e 00:07:35.872\r\nto our wonderful program\r\nof organic rejuvenation.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.461 --\u003e 00:07:43.630\r\n(FLY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:07:44.506 --\u003e 00:07:47.467\r\nWould you put that\r\nthing down and relax?\r\n\r\n00:07:47.759 --\u003e 00:07:50.053\r\nAfter years of\r\nresearch in my lab,\r\n\r\n00:07:50.220 --\u003e 00:07:53.139\r\nI have developed this enzyme.\r\nDemetrite.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.223 --\u003e 00:07:54.599\r\nThe secret of eternal youth.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.183 --\u003e 00:07:57.560\r\nDoesn't she look wonderful?\r\n\r\n00:07:57.852 --\u003e 00:07:59.229\r\nNot a day over 90.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.521 --\u003e 00:08:01.982\r\nHere you'll find\r\ndemetrite in the food,\r\n\r\n00:08:02.065 --\u003e 00:08:03.108\r\nthe water,\r\n\r\n00:08:03.191 --\u003e 00:08:04.943\r\neven the air you\r\nbreathe at night.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.193 --\u003e 00:08:06.987\r\nWhat a relaxing thought.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.948 --\u003e 00:08:11.074\r\nI assure you,\r\n\r\n00:08:11.241 --\u003e 00:08:15.245\r\nthe enzyme is thoroughly non-toxic\r\nand completely biodegradable.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.453 --\u003e 00:08:19.082\r\nAnd once you see those\r\nwrinkles melt away,\r\n\r\n00:08:19.165 --\u003e 00:08:22.168\r\nyou'll want to saturate\r\nevery cell with it.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.211 --\u003e 00:08:25.338\r\nTo eternal youth.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.797 --\u003e 00:08:27.632\r\n- To eternal youth.\r\n- To eternal youth.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.767 --\u003e 00:08:40.061\r\nMmm. Quite refreshing, actually.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.562 --\u003e 00:08:42.022\r\nYou should taste these.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.313 --\u003e 00:08:43.523\r\nDelicious.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.360 --\u003e 00:08:51.740\r\nNow, this is the kind of wilderness\r\nexperience I could enjoy.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.287 --\u003e 00:08:59.205\r\nGORDON: It's a real\r\nbrain-buster, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.124 --\u003e 00:09:03.585\r\nNo ransom note,\r\nno goodbye note, no nothing.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.127 --\u003e 00:09:06.463\r\nAnd she's not the only\r\nvanishing industrialist.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.713 --\u003e 00:09:08.381\r\nThree more were\r\nreported this week.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.215 --\u003e 00:09:10.675\r\nBATMAN: I'll search\r\nher penthouse.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.134 --\u003e 00:09:12.218\r\nGood luck.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.635 --\u003e 00:09:14.304\r\nWe put that place\r\nunder a microscope.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.387 --\u003e 00:09:15.972\r\nAnd all we got was eye strain.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.306 --\u003e 00:09:18.391\r\nMaybe your Bat radar can...\r\n\r\n00:09:22.812 --\u003e 00:09:24.105\r\nOh, never mind.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.506 --\u003e 00:09:51.216\r\n\u003ci\u003eHello, Mrs. Thomas,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:51.299 --\u003e 00:09:52.717\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm Violet.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:52.801 --\u003e 00:09:54.135\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I'm Lily.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:54.552 --\u003e 00:09:56.846\r\n\u003ci\u003eVIOLET: And we'd\r\nlike to invite you...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:56.930 --\u003e 00:09:59.224\r\nLILY: To a free weekend \u003ci\u003eat...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:59.307 --\u003e 00:10:01.601\r\n\u003ci\u003eBOTH: The Eternal Youth Spa.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:04.771 --\u003e 00:10:06.189\r\nALFRED: Yes, Master Bruce,\r\n\r\n00:10:06.272 --\u003e 00:10:09.192\r\nI did ask about that\r\nlady as you requested.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.484 --\u003e 00:10:12.987\r\nBut it seems she left by\r\nherself two weekends ago.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.655 --\u003e 00:10:16.908\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhy anyone would want to\r\nleave this place is beyond me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:16.991 --\u003e 00:10:17.992\r\n(ALFRED CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:20.161\r\nAlfred, are you okay?\r\n\r\n00:10:20.537 --\u003e 00:10:22.038\r\nNever better, sir.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.205 --\u003e 00:10:25.708\r\nEverywhere I turn,\r\nI see another sign of nature's...\r\n\r\n00:10:27.335 --\u003e 00:10:28.545\r\nBeauty.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.962 --\u003e 00:10:32.924\r\nI assure you that when I return,\r\nI'll be feeling like a new man.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.601 --\u003e 00:10:47.647\r\nYou know, Maggie, I never realized\r\nhow dreary this place actually looks.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.730 --\u003e 00:10:49.649\r\nEspecially after\r\nwhere we've been.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.732 --\u003e 00:10:50.733\r\nAh, well,\r\n\r\n00:10:50.900 --\u003e 00:10:52.819\r\nthanks for a splendid weekend.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.740 --\u003e 00:10:58.992\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.703 --\u003e 00:11:04.789\r\nYou are feeling younger, aren't you?\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:11:06.499 --\u003e 00:11:07.542\r\n(CAR HORN HONKS)\r\n\r\n00:11:26.102 --\u003e 00:11:27.312\r\nWhat the...\r\n\r\n00:11:32.192 --\u003e 00:11:33.193\r\n(BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:37.071 --\u003e 00:11:38.448\r\nGood to see you, sir.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.115 --\u003e 00:11:40.575\r\nYou too, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.992 --\u003e 00:11:42.160\r\nWhat's with the jungle?\r\n\r\n00:11:42.243 --\u003e 00:11:45.371\r\nOh, I thought this drab old\r\ncave could use a little color.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.788 --\u003e 00:11:46.789\r\nHow does it look?\r\n\r\n00:11:48.208 --\u003e 00:11:49.334\r\nGreen.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.417 --\u003e 00:11:52.503\r\nYes, so lovely. (SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:54.297 --\u003e 00:11:57.634\r\nI fear all this decorating has\r\ngiven me a dreadful thirst.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.636 --\u003e 00:12:00.762\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:12:01.095 --\u003e 00:12:03.223\r\nSpecial spa water, sir,\r\n\r\n00:12:03.556 --\u003e 00:12:06.142\r\nwith a drop or two of\r\nDr. Demeter's formula.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.517 --\u003e 00:12:08.811\r\nWonderful stuff, this demetrite.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.068 --\u003e 00:12:19.447\r\nAh. Excuse me, sir.\r\nI couldn't help myself...\r\n\r\n00:12:21.783 --\u003e 00:12:22.784\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:25.787\r\nReally, sir.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.870 --\u003e 00:12:28.122\r\nIt was merely a case\r\nof overexertion.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.539 --\u003e 00:12:32.043\r\nMy weekend must have been\r\nmore tiring than I realized.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.585 --\u003e 00:12:34.921\r\nWell, you get some rest.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.338 --\u003e 00:12:37.006\r\nI need to check on something.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.666 --\u003e 00:13:13.459\r\nMAGGIE: Alfie!\r\n\r\n00:13:14.294 --\u003e 00:13:15.295\r\nALFRED: Maggie.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.920 --\u003e 00:13:17.463\r\nHow strange to see you.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.547 --\u003e 00:13:19.007\r\nI've just been thinking about-\r\n\r\n00:13:19.090 --\u003e 00:13:20.967\r\nGoing back to the spa?\r\n\r\n00:13:21.050 --\u003e 00:13:22.218\r\nHow did you know?\r\n\r\n00:13:22.677 --\u003e 00:13:25.346\r\nThat's all I've been thinking\r\nabout since I got home.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.681 --\u003e 00:13:28.308\r\nComputer log continuing.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.391 --\u003e 00:13:30.518\r\nThe active ingredient\r\nin the demetrite formula\r\n\r\n00:13:30.601 --\u003e 00:13:32.603\r\nis a chlorophyll-based enzyme.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.729 --\u003e 00:13:36.441\r\nAnalysis indicates that it does\r\naffect human cellular membranes.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.567 --\u003e 00:13:41.154\r\nI am now combining equal\r\namounts of the enzyme\r\n\r\n00:13:41.237 --\u003e 00:13:42.447\r\nto human plasma.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.534 --\u003e 00:13:47.535\r\nWhat the...\r\n\r\n00:13:50.621 --\u003e 00:13:51.622\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:53.875 --\u003e 00:13:54.876\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:13:55.793 --\u003e 00:13:56.919\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:14:00.131 --\u003e 00:14:01.257\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:14:02.050 --\u003e 00:14:03.801\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:14:04.761 --\u003e 00:14:06.012\r\nI don't know why, Doctor,\r\n\r\n00:14:06.095 --\u003e 00:14:09.891\r\nbut we felt absolutely\r\ncompelled to come back.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.974 --\u003e 00:14:11.809\r\nWe couldn't keep ourselves away.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.018 --\u003e 00:14:13.019\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.102 --\u003e 00:14:17.190\r\nAlready your bodies have been primed\r\nfor the true value of my treatment.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.523 --\u003e 00:14:19.567\r\nThe ultimate rejuvenation,\r\n\r\n00:14:19.859 --\u003e 00:14:23.112\r\nthe promise of life everlasting.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.370 --\u003e 00:14:31.829\r\nI say, what is this?\r\n\r\n00:14:34.665 --\u003e 00:14:36.084\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:36.167 --\u003e 00:14:37.502\r\nRu\", Maggie!\r\n\r\n00:14:42.215 --\u003e 00:14:43.508\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:43.841 --\u003e 00:14:45.385\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.232 --\u003e 00:15:43.401\r\nYou go after the wrong\r\npeople, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.654 --\u003e 00:15:47.905\r\nPoison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.573 --\u003e 00:15:50.908\r\nOnly you would identify\r\nyourself with Demeter,\r\n\r\n00:15:50.992 --\u003e 00:15:52.410\r\nthe Greek goddess of plants.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.869 --\u003e 00:15:54.704\r\nVIOLET: Hey,\r\na high school graduate.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.751 --\u003e 00:16:02.086\r\nDon't even think about it.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.340 --\u003e 00:16:08.176\r\nUnusual trees.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.846 --\u003e 00:16:13.806\r\n\u003ci\u003eSubtropica brasilias.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:14.182 --\u003e 00:16:16.893\r\nAs rare as winter roses, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.648 --\u003e 00:16:25.109\r\n\u003ci\u003eHap their sap for\r\nmy growth enzyme,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:25.651 --\u003e 00:16:30.490\r\nwhich you see here in its\r\npurified, most concentrated form.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.698 --\u003e 00:16:32.408\r\nThe secret of eternal youth.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.034 --\u003e 00:16:34.202\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.828 --\u003e 00:16:38.998\r\nBut you haven't seen my\r\nmost intriguing trees.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.707 --\u003e 00:16:43.461\r\nActually, Batman,\r\nyou and I are surprisingly alike.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.671 --\u003e 00:16:49.050\r\nWe both strive to see\r\nevil-doers punished.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.720 --\u003e 00:16:55.598\r\nBut while you have\r\nyour gallery of rogues,\r\n\r\n00:16:56.557 --\u003e 00:16:58.768\r\nI have my grove.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.987 --\u003e 00:17:11.989\r\nThis can't be.\r\n\r\n00:17:12.615 --\u003e 00:17:14.367\r\nThis dog of a dogwood\r\n\r\n00:17:14.450 --\u003e 00:17:17.453\r\nleveled enough trees\r\nto shade a small state.\r\n\r\n00:17:17.995 --\u003e 00:17:18.996\r\n(POISON IVY KISSING)\r\n\r\n00:17:22.041 --\u003e 00:17:23.584\r\nAnd weep not for this willow.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.876 --\u003e 00:17:27.129\r\nShe slaughtered an ancient\r\nforest to produce cardboard.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.588 --\u003e 00:17:28.714\r\nCardboard!\r\n\r\n00:17:30.841 --\u003e 00:17:33.511\r\nOf course, I still owe Bruce\r\nWayne for his involvement\r\n\r\n00:17:33.594 --\u003e 00:17:35.054\r\nwith that slash-and-burn outfit.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.972 --\u003e 00:17:37.098\r\nBut for now,\r\n\r\n00:17:37.223 --\u003e 00:17:39.809\r\nI'm content to settle\r\nfor his friends.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.484 --\u003e 00:17:49.569\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:49.652 --\u003e 00:17:50.653\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.990 --\u003e 00:17:56.742\r\nPOISON IVY: Right now,\r\nthe bark is merely exoskeletal.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.076 --\u003e 00:17:59.245\r\nIt will take months\r\nof additional spraying\r\n\r\n00:17:59.328 --\u003e 00:18:02.373\r\nbefore the transformations\r\nbecome irreversible.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.790 --\u003e 00:18:06.669\r\nBut, of course,\r\nI have the patience of a redwood.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.044 --\u003e 00:18:10.381\r\nAnd the convictions\r\nof a fanatic.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.715 --\u003e 00:18:13.342\r\nWell, if you're not going\r\nto be part of the solution,\r\n\r\n00:18:13.467 --\u003e 00:18:15.136\r\nyou're obviously\r\npart of the problem.\r\n\r\n00:18:15.219 --\u003e 00:18:16.220\r\nLadies.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.604 --\u003e 00:18:27.064\r\nThis spray is\r\ntriple-strength, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.648 --\u003e 00:18:30.818\r\nIt will start the transformation\r\nwithout any preliminaries.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.576 --\u003e 00:18:40.411\r\nHe should be sprouting\r\nleaves by now.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.162 --\u003e 00:18:42.163\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:43.289 --\u003e 00:18:45.583\r\nYou made your secret\r\ntoo accessible, Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.666 --\u003e 00:18:48.085\r\nI coated my outfit with\r\nan herbicidal antidote.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.586 --\u003e 00:18:49.962\r\nKeep spraying!\r\n\r\n00:18:52.798 --\u003e 00:18:53.799\r\n(BOTH EXCLAIM)\r\n\r\n00:18:59.722 --\u003e 00:19:00.723\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:02.391 --\u003e 00:19:03.559\r\n(ROPES WHIPPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.643 --\u003e 00:19:05.603\r\nHuh? (EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:06.562 --\u003e 00:19:07.563\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:15.446 --\u003e 00:19:16.447\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.369 --\u003e 00:19:22.370\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:41.389 --\u003e 00:19:43.974\r\nPOISON IVY: And I thought\r\nyou believed in justice.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.225 --\u003e 00:19:45.559\r\nJustice, yes.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.851 --\u003e 00:19:48.062\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut not the vengeance\r\nof an ecu-terrorist.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:49.105 --\u003e 00:19:51.315\r\nYou're as destructive\r\nas those you punish.\r\n\r\n00:19:58.197 --\u003e 00:20:01.826\r\nLook what you've made me do to my\r\npoor, defenseless tree.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.040 --\u003e 00:20:09.625\r\n- (GLASS BREAKS)\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:12.128 --\u003e 00:20:13.379\r\nThe enzyme!\r\n\r\n00:20:13.629 --\u003e 00:20:15.423\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.506 --\u003e 00:20:17.216\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:18.134 --\u003e 00:20:19.135\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:21:07.016 --\u003e 00:21:08.559\r\n(BOTH MOANING)\r\n\r\n00:21:12.813 --\u003e 00:21:14.106\r\nMAGGIE: Alfie,\r\n\r\n00:21:14.273 --\u003e 00:21:16.400\r\ndo you realize that\r\nthis is the second place\r\n\r\n00:21:16.484 --\u003e 00:21:18.277\r\nwe've been together\r\nin as many weeks?\r\n\r\n00:21:18.986 --\u003e 00:21:21.572\r\nThis relationship\r\nis branching out.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.864 --\u003e 00:21:22.865\r\nPlease, Maggie.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.532 --\u003e 00:21:26.452\r\nAfter our encounter\r\nwith Joan of Bark,\r\n\r\n00:21:26.535 --\u003e 00:21:29.330\r\nthe last thing I want to\r\nbe reminded of is trees.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.705 --\u003e 00:21:30.956\r\nBRUCE: Hey, good news.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.332 --\u003e 00:21:34.168\r\nI just heard all of Poison lvy's\r\nvictims are expected to recover.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.668 --\u003e 00:21:36.462\r\nBruce, please.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.545 --\u003e 00:21:38.798\r\nThe plant. Must you?\r\n\r\n00:21:39.882 --\u003e 00:21:40.966\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:21:41.592 --\u003e 00:21:43.177\r\nMaybe I'd better\r\nleave this outside.\r\n\r\n00:21:43.552 --\u003e 00:21:47.181\r\nNice man,\r\nbut sometimes not too bright.\r\n\r\n00:22:22.174 --\u003e 00:22:23.175\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E17 - Two-Face, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.047 --\u003e 00:00:07.049\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.330 --\u003e 00:01:21.748\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.000 --\u003e 00:01:24.793\r\n(GHOSTLY VOICE) Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:01:25.419 --\u003e 00:01:26.920\r\n\u003ci\u003eHarvey Dent.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:27.671 --\u003e 00:01:29.506\r\nNo! Keep away!\r\n\r\n00:01:30.382 --\u003e 00:01:31.842\r\nLeave me alone!\r\n\r\n00:01:32.801 --\u003e 00:01:34.177\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:35.429 --\u003e 00:01:36.722\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhere are you going, Harvey?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:36.972 --\u003e 00:01:39.016\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou can't get away from me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:39.224 --\u003e 00:01:40.392\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.559 --\u003e 00:01:41.685\r\n\u003ci\u003eSee what I mean?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:41.768 --\u003e 00:01:43.770\r\nStay away.\r\nI want no part of you.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.279 --\u003e 00:01:53.572\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.951 --\u003e 00:02:00.370\r\nStop it! Stop it, I said.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.163 --\u003e 00:02:02.748\r\nIt's time, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.624 --\u003e 00:02:05.083\r\nIt's time.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.047 --\u003e 00:02:11.548\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:02:14.259 --\u003e 00:02:15.510\r\nIt's time, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.802 --\u003e 00:02:17.012\r\nIt's time.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.263 --\u003e 00:02:19.348\r\nOh, Carlos.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.973 --\u003e 00:02:21.224\r\nIt's you.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.683 --\u003e 00:02:23.352\r\n- Are you okay, Harvey?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.685 --\u003e 00:02:24.770\r\nI must've fallen asleep.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:27.439\r\nI had a bad dream.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.690 --\u003e 00:02:29.775\r\nWell, you better wake up.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.941 --\u003e 00:02:32.069\r\nGordon called.\r\nThey started the raid.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.987 --\u003e 00:02:34.988\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:02:39.618 --\u003e 00:02:41.286\r\n(POLICE SIREN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:02:43.330 --\u003e 00:02:44.956\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Police\r\nCommissioner Gordon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:45.707 --\u003e 00:02:47.167\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe have you surrounded.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:47.626 --\u003e 00:02:49.961\r\n\u003ci\u003eCome out with your hands up,\r\nand no one will get hurt.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:50.587 --\u003e 00:02:52.214\r\nCount hard, Gordon!\r\n\r\n00:02:53.423 --\u003e 00:02:54.841\r\nHey, Jim. How's it going?\r\n\r\n00:02:55.008 --\u003e 00:02:56.301\r\n(GUN FIRES)\r\n\r\n00:02:57.094 --\u003e 00:02:58.095\r\nCould be better.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.804 --\u003e 00:03:00.180\r\nSir, the SWAT team is in place.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.640 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\nAll right,\r\nbut wait for my order.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.894 --\u003e 00:03:08.355\r\nTHUG 1: This oughta blow a\r\nhole in their little barricade.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.814 --\u003e 00:03:10.357\r\nHelp me get it up to the window.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.068 --\u003e 00:03:14.548\r\nTHUG 2: Hey!\r\nThey're starting to move.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.028 --\u003e 00:03:16.196\r\nTHUG 1: Let 'em try.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.279 --\u003e 00:03:18.198\r\nThere ain't nobody that\r\ncan get in here alive.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.495 --\u003e 00:03:24.621\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:28.333 --\u003e 00:03:29.334\r\nUh...\r\n\r\n00:03:29.793 --\u003e 00:03:30.794\r\nOh, Frankie.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.586 --\u003e 00:03:33.088\r\nAll units, stand by.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.214 --\u003e 00:03:35.298\r\nGet ready.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.841 --\u003e 00:03:36.883\r\nSet-\r\n\r\n00:03:36.967 --\u003e 00:03:37.968\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:03:39.928 --\u003e 00:03:41.471\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:43.765 --\u003e 00:03:44.766\r\nHold your fire.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.183 --\u003e 00:03:47.227\r\nTHUG 1: It's him!\r\nTHUG 2: It's him! Watch out!\r\n\r\n00:03:56.236 --\u003e 00:03:57.237\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:03:59.865 --\u003e 00:04:00.866\r\nWhat's going on in there?\r\n\r\n00:04:01.241 --\u003e 00:04:03.869\r\nLooks like they've got a\r\ncase of bat infestation.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.370 --\u003e 00:04:07.330\r\n- We give up.\r\n- Let us out.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.497 --\u003e 00:04:09.541\r\n- Help.\r\n- Get me out of here.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.130 --\u003e 00:04:17.424\r\nAs your District Attorney,\r\nI would like to commend.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.507 --\u003e 00:04:20.552\r\nCommissioner Gordon and his\r\nmen for their fine work.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.514 --\u003e 00:04:25.724\r\nAnd thank you.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.974 --\u003e 00:04:28.643\r\nMr. Dent, is it true that you were\r\nthe one who planned this raid?\r\n\r\n00:04:28.894 --\u003e 00:04:31.938\r\nYes, and I'm glad to say that\r\nanother one of Rupert Thorne's\r\n\r\n00:04:32.147 --\u003e 00:04:33.815\r\ncriminal rings has\r\nnow been broken.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.149 --\u003e 00:04:35.442\r\n(CAMERA SHUTTERS CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:04:35.525 --\u003e 00:04:37.444\r\nAs I stated in my\r\nre-election campaign,\r\n\r\n00:04:38.195 --\u003e 00:04:40.489\r\nI will not rest\r\nuntil Gotham City\r\n\r\n00:04:40.781 --\u003e 00:04:43.283\r\nhas been de-Thorned\r\nonce and for all.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.492 --\u003e 00:04:45.118\r\n(CROWD APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:04:45.202 --\u003e 00:04:46.536\r\nYou talk big, pretty boy.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.620 --\u003e 00:04:49.289\r\nBut you ain't gonna be when\r\nMr. Thorne gets through with you.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.418 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\nHe chews up and spits out\r\ncreeps like you for breakfast.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.963 --\u003e 00:04:58.381\r\nAll right.\r\nThat's enough out of you.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.718 --\u003e 00:05:02.886\r\n(LAUGHING MALICIOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:05:04.930 --\u003e 00:05:06.097\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:07.641 --\u003e 00:05:08.642\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:05:10.811 --\u003e 00:05:13.230\r\nYou little weasel,\r\nI'll tear you apart.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.772 --\u003e 00:05:16.066\r\nHelp! Get him off. He's crazy.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.274 --\u003e 00:05:17.567\r\nSomeone get him off me.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.818 --\u003e 00:05:19.110\r\nHey, give me some help here.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.861 --\u003e 00:05:21.696\r\nKick mud in my face, will ya?\r\n\r\n00:05:22.030 --\u003e 00:05:23.073\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:05:24.825 --\u003e 00:05:25.992\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:05:26.201 --\u003e 00:05:27.494\r\nGet a hold of yourself.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.079 --\u003e 00:05:30.330\r\nJim, I...\r\n\r\n00:05:37.546 --\u003e 00:05:39.714\r\nCome on. You don't need\r\nthis kind of publicity.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.507 --\u003e 00:05:41.675\r\nThe guy's a maniac.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.758 --\u003e 00:05:43.552\r\nHe's the one who should\r\nbe going to jail.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.679 --\u003e 00:05:47.865\r\nWhat in the name of heaven\r\ndid you think you were doing?\r\n\r\n00:05:47.889 --\u003e 00:05:49.266\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.975 --\u003e 00:05:51.977\r\nI guess he just pressed\r\nthe right button.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.186 --\u003e 00:05:54.521\r\nThat's one heck of a button.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.564 --\u003e 00:05:57.858\r\nREPORTER: \u003ci\u003eWell,\r\nit was another wild night in East Gotham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:58.191 --\u003e 00:06:00.318\r\n\u003ci\u003eAs police intercepted\r\nan arm shipment\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:00.402 --\u003e 00:06:02.320\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhich District\r\nAttorney Harvey Dent\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.571 --\u003e 00:06:04.239\r\n\u003ci\u003eis trying to connect\r\nto Rupert Thorne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:05.240 --\u003e 00:06:07.117\r\nHey, nice tie, boss.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.576 --\u003e 00:06:09.703\r\n\u003ci\u003eUnfortunately, Handsome Harvey\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:09.870 --\u003e 00:06:11.288\r\n\u003ci\u003eearned a new nickname tonight,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:11.621 --\u003e 00:06:14.374\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"Hot-head Harvey\" when he\r\nattacked one of the suspects.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:14.833 --\u003e 00:06:16.585\r\n\u003ci\u003eGet him off. He's crazy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:17.419 --\u003e 00:06:19.546\r\nMy, this guy is crazy.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.171 --\u003e 00:06:22.090\r\nYeah, crazy like a fox.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.632 --\u003e 00:06:25.844\r\nThat little tantrum probably\r\nbought him another 10,000 votes.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.678 --\u003e 00:06:27.804\r\nSo, how about we see\r\n\r\n00:06:27.971 --\u003e 00:06:29.848\r\nhow far he can swim\r\nin a cement suit?\r\n\r\n00:06:30.307 --\u003e 00:06:32.309\r\nAnd bring the heat\r\ndown on us even more?\r\n\r\n00:06:32.684 --\u003e 00:06:33.685\r\nUh-uh.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.894 --\u003e 00:06:36.104\r\nI want this one in my\r\npocket, boys.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.563 --\u003e 00:06:39.858\r\nWe need to dig up some\r\ndirt on our dashing DA.\r\n\r\n00:06:40.150 --\u003e 00:06:41.943\r\nSomething really juicy.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.485 --\u003e 00:06:44.738\r\nWell, I'm afraid that's\r\ngoing to be a problem.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.113 --\u003e 00:06:47.240\r\nDent's so clean, he squeaks.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.991 --\u003e 00:06:50.118\r\nJust stay on his tail, Candice.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.493 --\u003e 00:06:52.120\r\nAll men have something to hide.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.662 --\u003e 00:06:54.289\r\nThe brighter the picture,\r\n\r\n00:06:54.539 --\u003e 00:06:56.124\r\nthe darker the negative.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.463 --\u003e 00:07:03.214\r\n(PEOPLE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.224 --\u003e 00:07:14.935\r\nIf we want to make\r\nthis city safe again,\r\n\r\n00:07:15.477 --\u003e 00:07:17.604\r\nthen we have to come down\r\nhard on these criminals.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.146 --\u003e 00:07:19.731\r\nI will not see the\r\npeople of Gotham...\r\n\r\n00:07:20.065 --\u003e 00:07:22.776\r\nBruce, it was so nice of you to\r\nsponsor this fundraiser for Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.318 --\u003e 00:07:25.070\r\nWell, Harvey and I go way back.\r\n\r\n00:07:25.153 --\u003e 00:07:26.446\r\nHe's a great DA.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.613 --\u003e 00:07:27.906\r\nAnd an even better friend.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.281 --\u003e 00:07:31.076\r\nThough lately,\r\nhe seems awfully intense.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.494 --\u003e 00:07:33.745\r\nIs he all right, Grace?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.954 --\u003e 00:07:35.246\r\nThat incident on TV...\r\n\r\n00:07:35.497 --\u003e 00:07:38.750\r\nI think the pressures of the campaign\r\nget to him sometimes, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.209 --\u003e 00:07:40.627\r\nYeah, I guess so.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.169 --\u003e 00:07:43.546\r\nLately, he doesn't seem himself.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.214 --\u003e 00:07:46.174\r\nOh, Mr. Dent, I want you to know\r\n\r\n00:07:46.424 --\u003e 00:07:48.551\r\nthat I voted for you two times.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.260 --\u003e 00:07:51.888\r\nWell, ma'am, I trust it was\r\nin two separate elections.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.514 --\u003e 00:07:53.848\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:54.265 --\u003e 00:07:56.267\r\nGRACE: Mr. Dent,\r\nI have a question.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.643 --\u003e 00:07:57.811\r\nWhen are you going to marry\r\n\r\n00:07:58.061 --\u003e 00:08:00.146\r\nthat gorgeous fiancée of yours?\r\n\r\n00:08:01.022 --\u003e 00:08:02.732\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:03.650 --\u003e 00:08:05.026\r\n\u003ci\u003eBetter marry her soon, Haw,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:05.235 --\u003e 00:08:07.153\r\nor I just might steal\r\nher away myself.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.529 --\u003e 00:08:09.489\r\nYou do and I'll prosecute.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.073 --\u003e 00:08:11.366\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.742 --\u003e 00:08:14.022\r\nHarvey, you better look at this.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.996 --\u003e 00:08:18.156\r\nThe judge just threw out the\r\ncase against Thorne's men.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.373 --\u003e 00:08:20.041\r\nBut... But why?\r\n\r\n00:08:20.500 --\u003e 00:08:21.940\r\nCARLOS: The warrant\r\nwasn't complete.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.127 --\u003e 00:08:23.461\r\nThe judge said he had no choice.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.712 --\u003e 00:08:24.963\r\nHe had to let them go.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.380 --\u003e 00:08:27.340\r\nHad to? But... But...\r\n\r\n00:08:28.925 --\u003e 00:08:29.926\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:08:30.093 --\u003e 00:08:32.387\r\nI spent three\r\nmonths on that raid.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.721 --\u003e 00:08:35.015\r\nHe can't overturn. The fool.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.724 --\u003e 00:08:36.975\r\nHe's been bought.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.350 --\u003e 00:08:38.643\r\nLike all the rest!\r\n\r\n00:08:43.982 --\u003e 00:08:45.400\r\n\u003ci\u003eHaw, take it easy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:46.026 --\u003e 00:08:48.346\r\nThis kind of behavior doesn't\r\ngo over well with the voters.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.862 --\u003e 00:08:51.031\r\nLet go of me, you rich twit.\r\n\r\n00:08:51.906 --\u003e 00:08:52.907\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.991 --\u003e 00:08:53.992\r\nHarvey?\r\n\r\n00:08:56.244 --\u003e 00:08:57.537\r\nGrace? Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:08:58.329 --\u003e 00:09:00.123\r\nI'm sorry. I don't know what...\r\n\r\n00:09:00.832 --\u003e 00:09:01.916\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.379 --\u003e 00:09:07.672\r\n(CROWD MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:09:14.554 --\u003e 00:09:16.394\r\nHARVEY: I just flew off the\r\nhandle, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.098 --\u003e 00:09:18.641\r\nDon't worry.\r\nI've got it under control.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.225 --\u003e 00:09:22.228\r\nHarvey, you didn't just\r\nlose your temper out there.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.146 --\u003e 00:09:24.564\r\nYou were like another person.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.106 --\u003e 00:09:26.357\r\nI said I was sorry.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.524 --\u003e 00:09:28.026\r\nMaybe you should get some help.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.443 --\u003e 00:09:29.652\r\nHe already is.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.861 --\u003e 00:09:30.904\r\nGrace.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.071 --\u003e 00:09:32.489\r\nDarling, Bruce is your friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.323 --\u003e 00:09:34.449\r\nDon't be embarrassed.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.616 --\u003e 00:09:36.451\r\nLots of people see\r\npsychiatrists, Harv.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.618 --\u003e 00:09:38.298\r\nNot when they're running\r\nfor public office.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.703 --\u003e 00:09:41.122\r\nYou know how some voters\r\nfeel about shrinks.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.623 --\u003e 00:09:43.458\r\nWell, I for one, am proud of you\r\n\r\n00:09:43.708 --\u003e 00:09:44.834\r\nand relieved.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.126 --\u003e 00:09:47.337\r\nIt takes a strong man to\r\nadmit when he has a problem.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.879 --\u003e 00:09:50.173\r\nYeah, yeah,\r\njust keep it under your hat, okay?\r\n\r\n00:09:50.799 --\u003e 00:09:51.800\r\nDon't worry.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.133 --\u003e 00:09:53.593\r\nIf there's anything I know,\r\n\r\n00:09:53.843 --\u003e 00:09:55.011\r\nit's how to keep a secret.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.929 --\u003e 00:09:57.514\r\n(THUNDERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:05.355 --\u003e 00:10:07.649\r\nPSYCHIATRIST: You are\r\nnow in a deep sleep.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.316 --\u003e 00:10:09.526\r\nCan you hear me?\r\n\r\n00:10:09.734 --\u003e 00:10:10.735\r\nMmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.074 --\u003e 00:10:17.742\r\nGood. Now, Harvey,\r\n\r\n00:10:18.201 --\u003e 00:10:20.912\r\nI would like to speak with\r\nyour other personality.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.454 --\u003e 00:10:24.082\r\nI would like to talk\r\nwith Big Bad Harv.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.833 --\u003e 00:10:26.167\r\n(THUNDER CRACKS)\r\n\r\n00:10:26.251 --\u003e 00:10:28.086\r\nI don't think he wants to talk.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.670 --\u003e 00:10:30.797\r\nHe must if we are to help you.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.131 --\u003e 00:10:32.257\r\nPlease try.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.942 --\u003e 00:10:52.694\r\nBig Bad Harv?\r\n\r\n00:10:53.194 --\u003e 00:10:54.320\r\nSpeaking.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.446 --\u003e 00:10:58.700\r\nIt appears you and Harvey\r\nare having trouble again.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.242 --\u003e 00:11:00.451\r\nThe guy's a wimp.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.910 --\u003e 00:11:03.288\r\nWell,\r\nHarvey has special problems.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.746 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\nWhen he was young,\r\n\r\n00:11:05.206 --\u003e 00:11:08.251\r\nhe felt very guilty\r\nabout his angry feelings.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.668 --\u003e 00:11:10.253\r\nSQ guilty,\r\n\r\n00:11:10.420 --\u003e 00:11:11.963\r\nthat he hid them deep inside\r\n\r\n00:11:12.172 --\u003e 00:11:13.631\r\nuntil they became an illness.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.257 --\u003e 00:11:16.009\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou, Big Bad Haw,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:16.426 --\u003e 00:11:18.553\r\nrepresent these angry feelings.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.596 --\u003e 00:11:21.222\r\nEveryone feels anger\r\n\r\n00:11:21.639 --\u003e 00:11:23.016\r\nand it does no harm.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.474 --\u003e 00:11:25.977\r\nAs long as it doesn't\r\nresult in bad behavior.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.811 --\u003e 00:11:28.396\r\nOnce Harvey understands this-\r\n\r\n00:11:28.771 --\u003e 00:11:32.442\r\nThen maybe I'll go away, right?\r\n\r\n00:11:32.859 --\u003e 00:11:33.985\r\nWell...\r\n\r\n00:11:35.069 --\u003e 00:11:36.821\r\nI'm going nowhere, missy!\r\n\r\n00:11:37.197 --\u003e 00:11:39.741\r\nIf anyone's leaving,\r\nit's Mr. Goody Good.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.037 --\u003e 00:11:45.496\r\nAnd maybe you with him.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.873 --\u003e 00:11:47.874\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:12:00.887 --\u003e 00:12:02.096\r\nDid I do this?\r\n\r\n00:12:02.722 --\u003e 00:12:03.723\r\n(SIGHS WEARILY)\r\n\r\n00:12:04.349 --\u003e 00:12:07.477\r\nNot you,\r\nbut your other personality.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.810 --\u003e 00:12:09.395\r\nIt's stronger than I suspected.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.063 --\u003e 00:12:11.481\r\nWhat am I gonna do?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.689 --\u003e 00:12:13.691\r\nI've always been able\r\nto repress him before.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.150 --\u003e 00:12:16.819\r\nHarvey,\r\nI want you to admit yourself\r\n\r\n00:12:17.111 --\u003e 00:12:20.490\r\nto the psychiatric ward over at\r\nCounty General for a few days.\r\n\r\n00:12:21.282 --\u003e 00:12:22.325\r\nNo way, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:12:22.575 --\u003e 00:12:24.095\r\nYou know I'm trying\r\nto get re-elected.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.535 --\u003e 00:12:26.871\r\nYou're also trying\r\nto save your sanity.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.247 --\u003e 00:12:28.581\r\nIsn't there any other way?\r\n\r\n00:12:28.957 --\u003e 00:12:30.083\r\nPlease.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.208 --\u003e 00:12:32.835\r\nWell, I suppose if you\r\ncut back on campaigning\r\n\r\n00:12:32.919 --\u003e 00:12:34.963\r\nand intensified our sessions,\r\n\r\n00:12:35.046 --\u003e 00:12:36.214\r\nwe might be able to-\r\n\r\n00:12:36.381 --\u003e 00:12:37.715\r\nGreat. I'll do it.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.091 --\u003e 00:12:39.891\r\nYou just set up the\r\nschedule and I'll be here.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.219 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nJust so long as we keep\r\nall of this a secret.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.735 --\u003e 00:12:58.861\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\n\r\n00:12:59.070 --\u003e 00:13:00.405\r\naccording to the latest count,\r\n\r\n00:13:00.571 --\u003e 00:13:01.948\r\nHarvey Dent is\r\nreceiving a mandate\r\n\r\n00:13:02.323 --\u003e 00:13:04.909\r\nfrom the people of Gotham City\r\nin the form of a landslide.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.868 --\u003e 00:13:07.412\r\n(CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:10.999 --\u003e 00:13:13.835\r\nNow, now, let's wait until\r\nall the returns are in.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.878 --\u003e 00:13:17.338\r\nCongratulations, Harv.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.797 --\u003e 00:13:19.549\r\nYou're looking pretty\r\ncalm and collected.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.091 --\u003e 00:13:21.592\r\nI told ya I could handle myself.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.968 --\u003e 00:13:23.845\r\nIn fact,\r\nI'm in such good spirits,\r\n\r\n00:13:23.970 --\u003e 00:13:26.431\r\nI might announce a certain\r\nwedding date this evening.\r\n\r\n00:13:27.348 --\u003e 00:13:29.058\r\nOh Harvey, do you mean it?\r\n\r\n00:13:29.851 --\u003e 00:13:31.936\r\nIt's part of my\r\nacceptance speech.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.065 --\u003e 00:13:38.651\r\nUh, sorry, Harv, phone call.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.235 --\u003e 00:13:41.195\r\nHold those lips.\r\nI'll be right back.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.537 --\u003e 00:13:51.998\r\n\u003ci\u003e- HeHo?\r\n- Congratulations, Harvey.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:52.999 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Thorne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:54.584 --\u003e 00:13:55.793\r\n\u003ci\u003eRupert Thorne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:56.878 --\u003e 00:13:58.171\r\nWhat do you want, you slime?\r\n\r\n00:13:58.629 --\u003e 00:14:00.798\r\nNow, now,\r\nis that any way to talk\r\n\r\n00:14:01.132 --\u003e 00:14:03.176\r\nto a man who's about\r\nto make you a deal?\r\n\r\n00:14:04.135 --\u003e 00:14:06.637\r\nI'm not interested in your\r\ndeals, Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.180 --\u003e 00:14:08.765\r\nOh, I think you will be.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.307 --\u003e 00:14:12.935\r\nUnless of course,\r\nyou'd rather I speak with Big Bad Harv.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.644 --\u003e 00:14:16.564\r\n\u003ci\u003eOr perhaps, you'd prefer I\r\nspeak to the press first.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:17.315 --\u003e 00:14:19.984\r\n\u003ci\u003e- What\u003c/i\u003e do \u003ci\u003eyou want?\r\n- There's a limo waiting in the alley.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:20.526 --\u003e 00:14:21.694\r\n\u003ci\u003eTake it\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:21.903 --\u003e 00:14:23.780\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhile you still have\r\na career ahead of ya.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:25.865 --\u003e 00:14:27.367\r\nDarling, is something wrong?\r\n\r\n00:14:27.700 --\u003e 00:14:28.701\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.243 --\u003e 00:14:30.328\r\nI have to see someone.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.578 --\u003e 00:14:32.138\r\nWould you mind looking\r\nafter our guests?\r\n\r\n00:14:32.205 --\u003e 00:14:33.664\r\nBut the returns\r\nare just coming in.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.915 --\u003e 00:14:35.715\r\n(ANGRILY) I won't be long.\r\nThank you, darling.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.127 --\u003e 00:14:40.004\r\n- (GIGGLING)\r\n- (LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.172 --\u003e 00:14:42.799\r\n- Excuse me.\r\n- Wait.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.178 --\u003e 00:14:48.554\r\nHey, Harv, what's up?\r\n\r\n00:14:49.389 --\u003e 00:14:50.890\r\nA surprise meeting. That's all.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.224 --\u003e 00:14:52.517\r\nNow? With who?\r\n\r\n00:14:52.725 --\u003e 00:14:54.245\r\nJust mind your own\r\nbusiness, all right?\r\n\r\n00:14:54.435 --\u003e 00:14:55.686\r\nYou're in trouble, aren't you?\r\n\r\n00:14:55.978 --\u003e 00:14:58.314\r\nMy friend,\r\nyou don't know the half of it.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.790 --\u003e 00:15:16.791\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.412 --\u003e 00:15:55.413\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:09.886 --\u003e 00:16:11.179\r\n(TRACKER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:21.731 --\u003e 00:16:23.483\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.783 --\u003e 00:16:35.745\r\nHARVEY: Stealing someone's psychiatric\r\nfile is pretty low, Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.162 --\u003e 00:16:37.747\r\nEven for a swine like you.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.247 --\u003e 00:16:40.666\r\nTHORNE: But it makes for\r\nsuch fascinating reading.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.626 --\u003e 00:16:42.752\r\nListen to this, boys.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.960 --\u003e 00:16:45.004\r\nIt says here,\r\nwhen Harvey was a little boy,\r\n\r\n00:16:45.296 --\u003e 00:16:46.881\r\nhe was bothered by a bully.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.256 --\u003e 00:16:49.425\r\nEvery day, the bully would\r\nbug him after school,\r\n\r\n00:16:49.842 --\u003e 00:16:52.136\r\nuntil one day little\r\nHarvey got so mad,\r\n\r\n00:16:52.261 --\u003e 00:16:53.471\r\nhe slugged him one.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.930 --\u003e 00:16:55.139\r\nALL: Ooh!\r\n\r\n00:16:56.182 --\u003e 00:16:57.662\r\nTHORNE: Of course,\r\nthe bully ran away,\r\n\r\n00:16:58.434 --\u003e 00:17:00.478\r\nwhich made little\r\nHarvey feel very proud.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.062 --\u003e 00:17:03.314\r\nUntil he heard the bully\r\nwas in the hospital.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.607 --\u003e 00:17:06.025\r\nThat was some punch.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.651 --\u003e 00:17:08.194\r\nThat's what Harvey thought.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.778 --\u003e 00:17:11.656\r\nExcept the guy was in the\r\nhospital for appendicitis.\r\n\r\n00:17:12.949 --\u003e 00:17:15.159\r\nBut poor Harvey felt so guilty,\r\n\r\n00:17:15.576 --\u003e 00:17:17.537\r\nhe never showed his anger again.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.287 --\u003e 00:17:19.747\r\nAnd that was the start of...\r\n\r\n00:17:19.914 --\u003e 00:17:22.041\r\nBig... Bad... Harv.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.792 --\u003e 00:17:23.793\r\n(THORNE CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:17:24.377 --\u003e 00:17:25.503\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:17:25.962 --\u003e 00:17:28.589\r\nJust a few favors\r\nfrom the DA's office.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.090 --\u003e 00:17:30.383\r\nYou're dreaming.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.883 --\u003e 00:17:32.593\r\nOtherwise,\r\nas a concerned citizen,\r\n\r\n00:17:32.885 --\u003e 00:17:35.096\r\nI'd feel compelled to\r\ngive this to the press.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.638 --\u003e 00:17:37.723\r\nAfter all, the people of\r\nGotham have a right to know\r\n\r\n00:17:38.015 --\u003e 00:17:39.058\r\nthe kind of person...\r\n\r\n00:17:39.350 --\u003e 00:17:42.520\r\nOr should I say \"persons\"\r\nthey've elected.\r\n\r\n00:17:46.732 --\u003e 00:17:48.192\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:56.075 --\u003e 00:17:57.702\r\nSo, what do you say, Harvey?\r\n\r\n00:17:58.077 --\u003e 00:17:59.328\r\nDo we have a deal?\r\n\r\n00:18:04.625 --\u003e 00:18:06.252\r\nThere's just one problem.\r\n\r\n00:18:06.544 --\u003e 00:18:07.753\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.923\r\nYou're talking to\r\nthe wrong Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:18:20.182 --\u003e 00:18:21.350\r\nGet off of me.\r\n\r\n00:18:23.644 --\u003e 00:18:24.937\r\nNo, Dent!\r\n\r\n00:18:25.646 --\u003e 00:18:26.856\r\nLet's get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.398 --\u003e 00:18:28.733\r\nGet away from me!\r\n\r\n00:18:29.483 --\u003e 00:18:30.735\r\nThorne is mine.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.652 --\u003e 00:18:32.903\r\nGet them.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.155 --\u003e 00:18:36.157\r\n- Come on, let's get him.\r\n- I got him.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.135 --\u003e 00:18:58.429\r\n(THUGS GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:01.849 --\u003e 00:19:02.850\r\nWild.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.114 --\u003e 00:19:18.282\r\nTWO-FACE: Give me that file.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.038 --\u003e 00:19:25.331\r\nI'll get him!\r\n\r\n00:19:25.498 --\u003e 00:19:26.540\r\nBATMAN: Look out, Dent.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.504 --\u003e 00:19:33.172\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:19:36.133 --\u003e 00:19:37.259\r\n(LOUD EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:19:38.469 --\u003e 00:19:39.679\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:19:50.481 --\u003e 00:19:51.607\r\nHarvey.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.566 --\u003e 00:19:53.984\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.697 --\u003e 00:19:59.490\r\nGRACE: Doctor,\r\nwill he be all right?\r\n\r\n00:20:00.991 --\u003e 00:20:02.159\r\nHe'll pull through.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.493 --\u003e 00:20:04.412\r\nHe's lucky Batman got\r\nhim here so quickly.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.912 --\u003e 00:20:05.992\r\nBRUCE: What about his face?\r\n\r\n00:20:06.414 --\u003e 00:20:07.665\r\nThat's a different matter.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.499 --\u003e 00:20:10.042\r\nA good plastic\r\nsurgeon should be able\r\n\r\n00:20:10.376 --\u003e 00:20:11.961\r\nto repair most of\r\nthe physical scars.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.837 --\u003e 00:20:15.131\r\nI'm more worried about\r\nthe mental scars.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.139 --\u003e 00:20:25.433\r\nLooks like Dent's\r\nfinally out of your hair.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.850 --\u003e 00:20:27.435\r\nTHORNE: I wish I\r\ncould be sure of that.\r\n\r\n00:20:38.279 --\u003e 00:20:40.823\r\nDOCTOR: Now, you understand\r\nthere's going to be some scarring.\r\n\r\n00:20:41.615 --\u003e 00:20:43.659\r\nBut I've already\r\nscheduled a surgery.\r\n\r\n00:20:50.791 --\u003e 00:20:51.792\r\n(NURSE GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:53.836 --\u003e 00:20:54.920\r\nHARVEY: Give me a mirror.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.212 --\u003e 00:20:56.714\r\nHarvey,\r\nmaybe you should wait until-\r\n\r\n00:20:56.881 --\u003e 00:20:58.257\r\nI said, give me a mirror.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.632 --\u003e 00:20:59.759\r\nNOW!\r\n\r\n00:21:03.345 --\u003e 00:21:04.346\r\n(POT SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:21:09.185 --\u003e 00:21:10.561\r\n(HARVEY SCREAMS IN HORROR)\r\n\r\n00:21:16.817 --\u003e 00:21:18.152\r\n(LOUD THUNDERING)\r\n\r\n00:21:19.111 --\u003e 00:21:20.738\r\nHarvey, what happened?\r\n\r\n00:21:26.452 --\u003e 00:21:27.578\r\nHarvey...\r\n\r\n00:21:34.043 --\u003e 00:21:35.211\r\nGoodbye, Grace.\r\n\r\n00:21:59.026 --\u003e 00:22:00.736\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.757 --\u003e 00:22:22.758\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E18 - Two-Face, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:01:05.148 --\u003e 00:01:06.942\r\nGet away from me!\r\n\r\n00:01:07.025 --\u003e 00:01:08.777\r\nThorne is mine!\r\n\r\n00:01:08.860 --\u003e 00:01:10.612\r\nPreviously on Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:13.240 --\u003e 00:01:14.283\r\nLook out, Harvey!\r\n\r\n00:01:16.660 --\u003e 00:01:17.744\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:01:17.828 --\u003e 00:01:20.747\r\nNow, you understand,\r\nthere's going to be some scarring.\r\n\r\n00:01:30.132 --\u003e 00:01:31.675\r\nHarvey...\r\n\r\n00:02:01.496 --\u003e 00:02:03.957\r\nThis is it.\r\nRupert Thorne's bookie joint.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.962 --\u003e 00:02:11.173\r\nGood heads, we leave him alone.\r\n\r\n00:02:12.215 --\u003e 00:02:14.968\r\nBad heads, we hit him hard.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.153 --\u003e 00:02:34.363\r\nEverybody, down!\r\n\r\n00:02:36.615 --\u003e 00:02:38.742\r\nI said, down!\r\n\r\n00:02:48.168 --\u003e 00:02:51.046\r\nDon't bother to\r\nadjust the picture.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.129 --\u003e 00:02:54.466\r\nFor the next five\r\nminutes, I'm in control.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.549 --\u003e 00:02:55.926\r\nGet the money.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.310 --\u003e 00:03:06.311\r\nHey, look at this.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.395 --\u003e 00:03:08.647\r\nMust be a couple of\r\nhundred silver dollars.\r\n\r\n00:03:09.064 --\u003e 00:03:10.148\r\nBring it.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.113 --\u003e 00:03:17.531\r\nI'll take that.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.614 --\u003e 00:03:19.866\r\nJewelry wasn't part of the plan.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.409 --\u003e 00:03:22.577\r\n- We gotta flip for it.\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:03:30.544 --\u003e 00:03:32.379\r\nGood side, leave it.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.462 --\u003e 00:03:33.839\r\nBut, Two-Face...\r\n\r\n00:03:36.842 --\u003e 00:03:38.343\r\nI said leave it!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.851 --\u003e 00:03:50.647\r\nBefore I go, I want you all to give\r\nRupert Thorne a message for me.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.529 --\u003e 00:03:59.698\r\nHow much did he take\r\nme for this time?\r\n\r\n00:04:00.282 --\u003e 00:04:02.367\r\n$200,000.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.451 --\u003e 00:04:04.119\r\nI thought we got\r\nrid of this guy.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.202 --\u003e 00:04:06.288\r\nAre you kidding? We created him.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.956 --\u003e 00:04:09.458\r\nSix months of this\r\nis long enough!\r\n\r\n00:04:09.541 --\u003e 00:04:11.209\r\nSpread the word.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.293 --\u003e 00:04:14.254\r\nI'm putting out a contract.\r\n$1 million.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.337 --\u003e 00:04:16.882\r\nNo. Make it $2 million.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.884 --\u003e 00:04:23.138\r\nA million dollars a face to\r\nthe man who brings me Two-Face.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.606 --\u003e 00:04:33.940\r\nHarvey.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.871 --\u003e 00:04:49.164\r\nStay back!\r\n\r\n00:04:53.502 --\u003e 00:04:56.171\r\nHarvey, please, let me help you.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.088 --\u003e 00:05:00.008\r\nYou...\r\nYou saw what was happening.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.091 --\u003e 00:05:02.803\r\nYou knew something was\r\nterribly wrong with me.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.886 --\u003e 00:05:04.596\r\nI thought you were my friend.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.679 --\u003e 00:05:07.766\r\nYou should've been able to help\r\nme, but you didn't.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.309 --\u003e 00:05:11.102\r\nNow, look at me!\r\n\r\n00:05:11.186 --\u003e 00:05:12.771\r\nBut I tried, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.525 --\u003e 00:05:17.734\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:05:17.859 --\u003e 00:05:21.863\r\nWhy couldn't you save me?\r\n\r\n00:05:31.122 --\u003e 00:05:33.041\r\nWhy couldn't you save us, son?\r\n\r\n00:05:55.480 --\u003e 00:05:57.858\r\nSo what are you dreaming\r\ntonight, Harvey?\r\n\r\n00:05:58.608 --\u003e 00:05:59.985\r\nPeaceful dreams?\r\n\r\n00:06:00.569 --\u003e 00:06:01.653\r\nOr nightmares?\r\n\r\n00:06:01.903 --\u003e 00:06:03.905\r\nMaybe both at once.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.992 --\u003e 00:06:09.536\r\nSleep well, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.619 --\u003e 00:06:13.164\r\nWherever you are,\r\nwhatever you've become,\r\n\r\n00:06:13.290 --\u003e 00:06:15.625\r\nI will save you.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.209 --\u003e 00:06:17.502\r\nI swear.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.143 --\u003e 00:06:35.395\r\n- Grace Lamont?\r\n- Yes?\r\n\r\n00:06:35.478 --\u003e 00:06:37.772\r\nI'm Detective Leopold.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.856 --\u003e 00:06:40.025\r\nIt's about your fiancé.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.903 --\u003e 00:06:46.239\r\nSo, unless we can get to\r\nHarvey before Thorne does,\r\n\r\n00:06:46.323 --\u003e 00:06:47.824\r\nhe won't stand much of a chance.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.908 --\u003e 00:06:50.035\r\nI wish I could help,\r\nbut I haven't seen him\r\n\r\n00:06:50.118 --\u003e 00:06:52.037\r\nsince that horrible\r\nday in the hospital.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.120 --\u003e 00:06:54.664\r\nI don't know where he is.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.748 --\u003e 00:06:57.626\r\nIt is possible that Harvey\r\nmight try to see you.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.709 --\u003e 00:07:00.337\r\nIf he does,\r\nyou activate this beeper,\r\n\r\n00:07:00.420 --\u003e 00:07:04.007\r\nand we'll be able to trace the\r\nsignal to wherever you are.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.348 --\u003e 00:07:13.099\r\nIt's all in your hands.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.728 --\u003e 00:07:19.189\r\nAll we have to do now is wait.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.314 --\u003e 00:07:21.566\r\nWhat makes you so sure\r\nTwo-Face will come back here?\r\n\r\n00:07:21.650 --\u003e 00:07:25.028\r\nHe'll come back.\r\nThey always come back.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.672 --\u003e 00:07:45.298\r\n$64,800,\r\n\r\n00:07:45.382 --\u003e 00:07:48.843\r\n$64,900, $65,000.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.430 --\u003e 00:07:55.934\r\nYou don't touch anything\r\nuntil I tell you to, punk.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.311 --\u003e 00:08:01.856\r\nYou always were a couple\r\nof greedy little beggars,\r\n\r\n00:08:01.940 --\u003e 00:08:05.777\r\neven when I\r\nprosecuted you as DA.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.081 --\u003e 00:08:19.499\r\nWhat are you looking at?\r\n\r\n00:08:21.584 --\u003e 00:08:24.838\r\nGee, Two-Face, if you miss\r\nher, why don't you go see her?\r\n\r\n00:08:24.921 --\u003e 00:08:27.340\r\nSure, we could even bring her\r\nhere, if you want.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.690 --\u003e 00:08:46.359\r\nForget it.\r\nWe have more important things to do.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.112 --\u003e 00:08:52.157\r\nI've decided it's\r\ntime to finish Thorne\r\n\r\n00:08:52.240 --\u003e 00:08:53.700\r\nonce and for all.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.783 --\u003e 00:08:55.368\r\nYou're gonna knock him off?\r\n\r\n00:08:55.452 --\u003e 00:08:57.537\r\nLet's just say,\r\nI'm gonna do to him\r\n\r\n00:08:57.620 --\u003e 00:09:00.415\r\nexactly what he did to me.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.795 --\u003e 00:09:09.591\r\nSo you think you've discerned\r\na pattern to his crimes?\r\n\r\n00:09:09.674 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nJust look at the places he's\r\nrobbed, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.135 --\u003e 00:09:17.182\r\nClub 22, Gemini Jewelers,\r\nthe Two's Company Cafe.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.265 --\u003e 00:09:19.517\r\nTwo's? My word!\r\n\r\n00:09:19.601 --\u003e 00:09:22.353\r\nHas anyone informed the\r\nSecond National Bank?\r\n\r\n00:09:22.437 --\u003e 00:09:23.605\r\nThat won't be a target.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.688 --\u003e 00:09:25.690\r\nEvery place Two-Face has robbed\r\n\r\n00:09:25.774 --\u003e 00:09:28.943\r\nis also a front for Rupert\r\nThorne's criminal activities.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.027 --\u003e 00:09:32.739\r\nUnfortunately,\r\nhe's used up all of Thorne's places.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.616 --\u003e 00:09:36.367\r\nPerhaps, he'll rob them twice.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.451 --\u003e 00:09:38.328\r\nA sort of double-or-nothing.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.411 --\u003e 00:09:41.831\r\nNo. I think Two-Face is\r\nthrough humiliating Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.915 --\u003e 00:09:43.750\r\nNow he wants him out of the way.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.833 --\u003e 00:09:45.502\r\nAnd I think I know how.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.471 --\u003e 00:09:59.974\r\nKeep your guard up, sir.\r\nHarvey is no longer the fellow we knew.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.058 --\u003e 00:10:02.644\r\nI still feel that somewhere\r\ninside that monster\r\n\r\n00:10:02.727 --\u003e 00:10:04.312\r\nis my old friend.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.395 --\u003e 00:10:07.565\r\nThat may make him\r\neven more dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:10:44.310 --\u003e 00:10:45.687\r\nHey, this looks like something.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.770 --\u003e 00:10:48.606\r\n\"Rupert Thorne. Confidential.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:51.484 --\u003e 00:10:53.611\r\nFor years,\r\nI tried to subpoena this.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.736 --\u003e 00:10:58.199\r\n\"Money laundering, payoffs,\r\nblackmail.\" It's all here.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.034 --\u003e 00:11:02.328\r\nI'll destroy Thorne\r\nwith his file\r\n\r\n00:11:02.495 --\u003e 00:11:04.164\r\njust like he destroyed\r\nme with mine!\r\n\r\n00:11:04.747 --\u003e 00:11:06.457\r\nCome on, let's get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.851 --\u003e 00:11:26.060\r\nYou're coming with me, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.397 --\u003e 00:11:30.899\r\nI want to help you.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.982 --\u003e 00:11:34.652\r\nHelp me?\r\nYou don't know anything about me.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.736 --\u003e 00:11:36.821\r\nI know that you have\r\nfriends, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.905 --\u003e 00:11:38.823\r\nFriends who love\r\nand care about you.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.490 --\u003e 00:11:41.951\r\nHarvey's friends are\r\nno friends of mine.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.869 --\u003e 00:11:44.370\r\nWhat about Grace?\r\n\r\n00:11:44.454 --\u003e 00:11:45.622\r\nGrace?\r\n\r\n00:11:47.290 --\u003e 00:11:48.750\r\nWhat do you know about Grace?\r\n\r\n00:11:48.833 --\u003e 00:11:52.503\r\nShe still loves you, Harvey.\r\nShe keeps your picture.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.587 --\u003e 00:11:54.797\r\nEvery day, she waits and prays.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.881 --\u003e 00:11:56.507\r\n\u003ci\u003eShe wants you back, Haw.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:56.591 --\u003e 00:11:58.509\r\nHey, what's taking you guys-\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:11:59.928\r\nHoly»-...\r\n\r\n00:12:07.018 --\u003e 00:12:09.103\r\nCome on, let's get out of here!\r\n\r\n00:12:11.689 --\u003e 00:12:13.942\r\nNo, Harvey. Wait.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.738 --\u003e 00:12:19.739\r\nLet go of me!\r\n\r\n00:12:32.043 --\u003e 00:12:35.088\r\nHey, there. You okay, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:12:35.171 --\u003e 00:12:37.966\r\nLooks like you took a\r\nnasty fall there, fellow.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.841 --\u003e 00:12:41.719\r\nHarvey! Where's Harvey?\r\n\r\n00:12:41.928 --\u003e 00:12:43.596\r\nAin't nobody here but us, son.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.976 --\u003e 00:12:50.061\r\n- You all right?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.645 --\u003e 00:12:51.854\r\nI'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.743 --\u003e 00:13:08.162\r\nWait till the police get\r\na load of this stuff.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.246 --\u003e 00:13:10.415\r\nIt's even got his\r\nSwiss bank accounts.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.722 --\u003e 00:13:26.764\r\nStop the car!\r\n\r\n00:13:37.442 --\u003e 00:13:39.736\r\n- Hello?\r\n- Grace?\r\n\r\n00:13:39.819 --\u003e 00:13:40.945\r\nHarvey?\r\n\r\n00:13:41.446 --\u003e 00:13:43.990\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhere are you?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:45.033 --\u003e 00:13:46.200\r\nI wanna see you.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.284 --\u003e 00:13:49.370\r\nYes! Yes, of course, darling.\r\nWhere?\r\n\r\n00:13:49.454 --\u003e 00:13:50.997\r\n\u003ci\u003eLook out your window.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:54.167 --\u003e 00:13:56.169\r\n\u003ci\u003eThey'll bring you to me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:02.008 --\u003e 00:14:05.928\r\nHarvey, you know that no matter\r\nwhat, I love you.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.055 --\u003e 00:14:08.389\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'll see you soon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:10.433 --\u003e 00:14:12.060\r\nHe did what?\r\n\r\n00:14:18.775 --\u003e 00:14:21.903\r\nIf he gives those files to the\r\npolice, I'm ruined!\r\n\r\n00:14:21.986 --\u003e 00:14:24.030\r\nWe've got to stop him now!\r\n\r\n00:14:34.290 --\u003e 00:14:37.043\r\nGrab your hat, Rupie,\r\nand your checkbook.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.168 --\u003e 00:14:39.587\r\nTonight may be our lucky night.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.442 --\u003e 00:15:02.819\r\nThis way, ma'am.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.408 --\u003e 00:15:09.409\r\nIn there.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.508 --\u003e 00:15:27.009\r\nHello, Grace.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.511 --\u003e 00:15:29.637\r\nHarvey.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.683 --\u003e 00:15:36.310\r\nMy name is Two-Face now.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.394 --\u003e 00:15:37.728\r\nNo, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.812 --\u003e 00:15:39.439\r\nThis is my world now.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.148 --\u003e 00:15:43.609\r\nA dichotomy of\r\norder and chaos...\r\n\r\n00:15:43.693 --\u003e 00:15:45.278\r\nJust like me.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.361 --\u003e 00:15:47.989\r\nHarvey,\r\nwhat's happened to your mind?\r\n\r\n00:15:48.072 --\u003e 00:15:51.033\r\nYour feelings?\r\nYou used to listen to your feelings.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.117 --\u003e 00:15:54.412\r\nThis is what I listen to now.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.628 --\u003e 00:16:04.964\r\nChance, Grace.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.047 --\u003e 00:16:06.674\r\nChance is everything.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.757 --\u003e 00:16:10.970\r\nWhether you're born or not,\r\nwhether you live or die,\r\n\r\n00:16:11.053 --\u003e 00:16:12.930\r\nwhether you're good or bad,\r\n\r\n00:16:14.056 --\u003e 00:16:16.184\r\nit's all arbitrary.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.267 --\u003e 00:16:17.935\r\nThat's nonsense, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.561 --\u003e 00:16:20.855\r\nWas it chance that made\r\nyou District Attorney?\r\n\r\n00:16:20.980 --\u003e 00:16:23.024\r\nWas it chance that made\r\nyou fall in love with me?\r\n\r\n00:16:23.107 --\u003e 00:16:25.735\r\nTake control of your\r\nlife, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.818 --\u003e 00:16:27.278\r\nYou don't need a coin.\r\n\r\n00:16:28.112 --\u003e 00:16:29.405\r\nAnd you don't need this.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.408 --\u003e 00:16:34.869\r\nYou don't ever need\r\nto hide from me.\r\n\r\n00:16:48.508 --\u003e 00:16:51.135\r\n- I love you.\r\n- Grace.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.970 --\u003e 00:16:53.971\r\nWhat is it?\r\n\r\n00:17:05.650 --\u003e 00:17:07.401\r\nAt last we meet,\r\n\r\n00:17:07.735 --\u003e 00:17:13.699\r\nface to face... To face.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.783 --\u003e 00:17:15.117\r\nYOU!\r\n\r\n00:17:23.209 --\u003e 00:17:25.670\r\nYou did very well,\r\nleading us to your boyfriend.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.129 --\u003e 00:17:28.214\r\nGrace?\r\n\r\n00:17:28.297 --\u003e 00:17:32.093\r\nNow, now, she thought she\r\nwas alerting the police.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.176 --\u003e 00:17:34.428\r\nShe wanted to save you.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.512 --\u003e 00:17:36.639\r\nI'm so sorry, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:17:40.768 --\u003e 00:17:43.020\r\nSo much for control, huh, Grace?\r\n\r\n00:18:14.385 --\u003e 00:18:15.845\r\nIt ain't here, boss.\r\n\r\n00:18:15.928 --\u003e 00:18:18.472\r\nThat file is here, all right.\r\nNow, where is it?\r\n\r\n00:18:18.556 --\u003e 00:18:21.559\r\nNot a chance, you slime!\r\n\r\n00:18:26.647 --\u003e 00:18:29.483\r\nSuch a pretty face, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:18:29.567 --\u003e 00:18:32.153\r\n- Let her go!\r\n- Give me the file.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.840 --\u003e 00:18:55.676\r\n- Get rid of them.\r\n- But you said...\r\n\r\n00:18:56.302 --\u003e 00:18:58.512\r\nYour boyfriend first.\r\n\r\n00:19:10.232 --\u003e 00:19:11.233\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:19:12.610 --\u003e 00:19:14.904\r\nThis is the last time\r\nyou interfere with me.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.883 --\u003e 00:20:19.885\r\nNo! Two-Face, don't!\r\n\r\n00:20:19.969 --\u003e 00:20:21.887\r\n- You can't let him.\r\n- Harvey!\r\n\r\n00:20:21.971 --\u003e 00:20:25.391\r\n- What are you doing?\r\n- Taking control of my life.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.474 --\u003e 00:20:26.976\r\nLet the law handle it.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.059 --\u003e 00:20:28.519\r\nThe law?\r\n\r\n00:20:28.602 --\u003e 00:20:31.981\r\nHere's the only law!\r\nThe law of averages,\r\n\r\n00:20:32.106 --\u003e 00:20:33.899\r\nthe great equalizer.\r\n\r\n00:20:48.080 --\u003e 00:20:50.666\r\nNo! What have you done?\r\n\r\n00:20:50.750 --\u003e 00:20:52.710\r\nMy coin, where is it?\r\n\r\n00:20:52.793 --\u003e 00:20:55.004\r\nI can't decide without...\r\n\r\n00:20:55.087 --\u003e 00:20:58.132\r\nOh, no! It's got to be here!\r\nIt's got to!\r\n\r\n00:20:59.300 --\u003e 00:21:00.843\r\nI have to have it!\r\n\r\n00:21:10.102 --\u003e 00:21:13.606\r\nIt's all right now, Harvey.\r\nI'm here.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.619 --\u003e 00:21:29.330\r\nPoor Harvey.\r\nSo filled with anger.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.413 --\u003e 00:21:30.706\r\nDo you think there's any hope?\r\n\r\n00:21:30.790 --\u003e 00:21:34.543\r\nWhere there's love,\r\nthere's hope, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.756 --\u003e 00:21:41.091\r\nWell,\r\na little luck wouldn't hurt.\r\n\r\n00:21:45.554 --\u003e 00:21:47.515\r\nFor you, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:22:27.805 --\u003e 00:22:28.806\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E19 - Fear of Victory (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.628 --\u003e 00:00:04.630\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:35.262 --\u003e 00:01:36.263\r\n\u003ci\u003eHike!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:36.346 --\u003e 00:01:38.515\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.684 --\u003e 00:01:42.686\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMMENTATOR: Look at Gotham\r\nState's Brian Rogers!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:42.811 --\u003e 00:01:44.313\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe's a one-man offense.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:44.438 --\u003e 00:01:46.148\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:46.231 --\u003e 00:01:49.067\r\n\u003ci\u003eA repeat performance this weekend\r\nagainst that tough Tech team,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:49.192 --\u003e 00:01:52.446\r\n\u003ci\u003eall but guarantees Rogers\r\na big-buck Pro contract.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:54.406 --\u003e 00:01:57.075\r\nSounds like it's off to\r\nthe Pros for you, roommate.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.159 --\u003e 00:01:58.785\r\nMaybe. But he's right.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.910 --\u003e 00:02:01.538\r\nThe scouts will be watching\r\nme real close against Tech.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.080 --\u003e 00:02:03.790\r\nAh, no sweat.\r\nYou'll dazzle them.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.833 --\u003e 00:02:06.001\r\nI hope so.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.084 --\u003e 00:02:08.503\r\nMaking the Pros means I\r\ncan help out my folks.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.587 --\u003e 00:02:10.464\r\nMaybe even put my\r\nsister through college.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.715 --\u003e 00:02:13.133\r\nTime for Boseman's Bloopers,\r\n\r\n00:02:13.216 --\u003e 00:02:15.385\r\n\u003ci\u003eand boy, they were coming\r\noff the walls this week.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:15.636 --\u003e 00:02:19.056\r\n\u003ci\u003eHeavily favored middleweight champ,\r\nRudy Lovell, set two new records.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:19.139 --\u003e 00:02:21.058\r\n\u003ci\u003eOne for the shortest\r\nfight in history,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:21.183 --\u003e 00:02:23.143\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe other for the 50-yard dash.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:23.226 --\u003e 00:02:26.480\r\n\u003ci\u003eGoalie, Rick Gale, came up with\r\na novel way to defend his goal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:27.272 --\u003e 00:02:30.359\r\n\u003ci\u003eRather unorthodox, wouldn't you say, Rick?\r\nBut effective.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:33.195 --\u003e 00:02:34.529\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd here's top seed Chris Adams,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:34.655 --\u003e 00:02:37.366\r\n\u003ci\u003emaking it look like she's\r\nin the wrong racket.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:37.949 --\u003e 00:02:40.494\r\n\u003ci\u003eSeriously, though,\r\nthis was mighty puzzling behavior\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:40.619 --\u003e 00:02:42.454\r\n\u003ci\u003efrom some of our\r\nfinest athletes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:43.080 --\u003e 00:02:44.081\r\nI'll say.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.164 --\u003e 00:02:45.248\r\n(KNOCKING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.671 --\u003e 00:02:52.673\r\nTelegram for Brian Rogers.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.007 --\u003e 00:02:56.343\r\n- Uh, here you go.\r\n- Good evening, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.682 --\u003e 00:03:02.766\r\nThis is weird.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.308 --\u003e 00:03:04.309\r\nLet me see.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.646 --\u003e 00:03:10.065\r\n\"Dear Brian,\r\nbest of luck against Tech.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:10.482 --\u003e 00:03:13.402\r\n\"And remember that only\r\na fool knows no fear.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:13.985 --\u003e 00:03:16.488\r\n\"I'm betting on it. A fan.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:17.656 --\u003e 00:03:18.865\r\nAs I said...\r\n\r\n00:03:19.282 --\u003e 00:03:20.409\r\n- Weird.\r\n- Weird.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.583 --\u003e 00:03:29.751\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:38.385 --\u003e 00:03:39.594\r\nHike! Hike!\r\n\r\n00:03:39.678 --\u003e 00:03:41.346\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:42.764 --\u003e 00:03:43.890\r\n(WHISTLE BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:03:43.974 --\u003e 00:03:45.574\r\nBOSEMAN: Yet another\r\nbad pass by Rogers.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.518 --\u003e 00:03:50.522\r\nBrian Rogers is having the worst\r\nday of his collegiate career.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.606 --\u003e 00:03:53.692\r\nCome on, Brian, get it together.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.279\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:57.362 --\u003e 00:04:00.240\r\nUh, all right. All right.\r\nLet's try a run.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.741 --\u003e 00:04:02.033\r\nOff tackle.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.159 --\u003e 00:04:04.870\r\nOn third and 25,\r\nwe need to pass!\r\n\r\n00:04:05.662 --\u003e 00:04:06.830\r\nYeah, okay, okay.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.913 --\u003e 00:04:08.206\r\nYeah, yeah, sure, pass.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.665 --\u003e 00:04:10.333\r\nAre you okay, man?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.168 --\u003e 00:04:13.253\r\nYeah, yeah. No... No problem.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.381 --\u003e 00:04:18.884\r\nThe ball is snapped.\r\nRogers is going back.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.721 --\u003e 00:04:24.556\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:24.890 --\u003e 00:04:26.767\r\nAh! No!\r\n\r\n00:04:26.850 --\u003e 00:04:27.851\r\nDon't hurt me!\r\n\r\n00:04:27.934 --\u003e 00:04:29.644\r\n- Don't hurt me!\r\n- (WHISTLE BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:04:29.728 --\u003e 00:04:32.773\r\n(CROWD BOOING)\r\n\r\n00:04:40.405 --\u003e 00:04:42.657\r\n(LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:04:42.741 --\u003e 00:04:44.075\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:44.159 --\u003e 00:04:47.412\r\nThey were so big and scary.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.163 --\u003e 00:04:49.331\r\nI couldn't...\r\n\r\n00:04:49.790 --\u003e 00:04:51.416\r\nIt's gonna be all right, son.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.541 --\u003e 00:04:54.503\r\nWe're gonna take you to the\r\ninfirmary for observation.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.466 --\u003e 00:05:01.384\r\nROBIN: It was\r\nunbelievable, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.510 --\u003e 00:05:04.262\r\nThe guy totally freaked,\r\nright there on the field.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.346 --\u003e 00:05:06.681\r\nBrian Rogers. The Rock.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.765 --\u003e 00:05:08.433\r\nHe was under a lot of\r\npressure, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.476 --\u003e 00:05:11.276\r\n- You can never tell when...\r\n- (TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:05:21.613 --\u003e 00:05:23.532\r\nUh-oh. Time to punch in.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.294 --\u003e 00:05:38.088\r\nOh, no. Not him!\r\n\r\n00:05:38.171 --\u003e 00:05:39.506\r\nCome on. This way!\r\n\r\n00:05:47.973 --\u003e 00:05:49.349\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:51.268 --\u003e 00:05:54.187\r\n(SHUDDERING)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.858 --\u003e 00:05:59.401\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:06:07.951 --\u003e 00:06:11.079\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.165 --\u003e 00:06:15.208\r\nRobin!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.210 --\u003e 00:06:18.461\r\nHe don't stop.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.879 --\u003e 00:06:21.673\r\nThat's because he don't\r\nknow when to quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:27.888 --\u003e 00:06:30.390\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:34.561 --\u003e 00:06:37.188\r\nRobin, give me a hand.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.026 --\u003e 00:06:42.193\r\nI can't.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.819 --\u003e 00:06:45.196\r\nHey, Batman, catch this!\r\n\r\n00:06:50.785 --\u003e 00:06:52.120\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:06:53.538 --\u003e 00:06:54.748\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:06:59.127 --\u003e 00:07:00.754\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:07:15.477 --\u003e 00:07:16.770\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:16.853 --\u003e 00:07:17.896\r\nOh, my!\r\n\r\n00:07:17.979 --\u003e 00:07:19.147\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:07:24.277 --\u003e 00:07:26.196\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh» my'.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:33.411 --\u003e 00:07:37.832\r\nHey, boy blunder, what's the matter?\r\nBat got your tongue?\r\n\r\n00:07:37.916 --\u003e 00:07:39.751\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:40.335 --\u003e 00:07:42.379\r\nThis will take care of bird boy.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.895 --\u003e 00:08:00.397\r\nAll right, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.480 --\u003e 00:08:01.773\r\nPull yourself together.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.273 --\u003e 00:08:03.316\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:03.400 --\u003e 00:08:04.985\r\nI don't know what\r\nhappened to me.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.068 --\u003e 00:08:06.736\r\nI was scared to death.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.820 --\u003e 00:08:08.071\r\nI couldn't even think.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.154 --\u003e 00:08:10.115\r\nIt was so unreal.\r\n\r\n00:08:16.997 --\u003e 00:08:19.124\r\nIt's too strange,\r\nthat both you and your roommate\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:21.042\r\nwould have panic\r\nattacks on the same day.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.126 --\u003e 00:08:23.211\r\nI still can't believe it!\r\n\r\n00:08:23.294 --\u003e 00:08:24.879\r\nI could've gotten you killed!\r\n\r\n00:08:25.588 --\u003e 00:08:27.048\r\nCalm down.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.132 --\u003e 00:08:28.466\r\nWe'll get a lead on it.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.767 --\u003e 00:08:38.935\r\nDid you see this?\r\n\r\n00:08:40.186 --\u003e 00:08:41.938\r\nThe screwy telegram?\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:43.106\r\nSure.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.149 --\u003e 00:08:46.693\r\nHey, what's this?\r\n\r\n00:08:46.776 --\u003e 00:08:47.944\r\nOur lead.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.988 --\u003e 00:08:52.657\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:08:55.994 --\u003e 00:08:57.370\r\nBATMAN: Take it easy, fella.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.793 --\u003e 00:09:06.796\r\nI suspect the chemical is\r\nabsorbed through the skin.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.339 --\u003e 00:09:09.466\r\n(HISSES)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.592 --\u003e 00:09:11.968\r\n(SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:09:15.638 --\u003e 00:09:17.766\r\n- Nothing's happening.\r\n- Yet.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.393 --\u003e 00:09:22.103\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.480 --\u003e 00:09:25.315\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:09:27.233 --\u003e 00:09:28.902\r\n(YOWL5)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.611 --\u003e 00:09:30.820\r\nJust as I thought.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.904 --\u003e 00:09:32.864\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:09:34.908 --\u003e 00:09:37.869\r\nBATMAN: The fear chemical\r\nis activated by adrenaline.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.952 --\u003e 00:09:40.872\r\nSo whenever you or Brian or\r\nany of the other athletes\r\n\r\n00:09:40.955 --\u003e 00:09:41.956\r\ngot agitated...\r\n\r\n00:09:42.457 --\u003e 00:09:45.877\r\nThe stuff kicks in,\r\nturning our excitement to fear.\r\n\r\n00:09:46.586 --\u003e 00:09:48.630\r\nBut how long is this gonna last?\r\n\r\n00:09:49.297 --\u003e 00:09:51.758\r\nI'm afraid there's only one\r\nperson who can answer that.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.342 --\u003e 00:09:54.594\r\nThe professor of fear himself.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.677 --\u003e 00:09:55.929\r\nThe Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.930 --\u003e 00:09:59.390\r\nIt can't be.\r\nHe's locked up in Arkham.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.309 --\u003e 00:10:02.310\r\nIsn't he?\r\n\r\n00:10:09.192 --\u003e 00:10:10.527\r\n(BAT SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:28.753 --\u003e 00:10:30.839\r\nThis is for Jonathan Crane.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.922 --\u003e 00:10:31.923\r\nI sot it!\r\n\r\n00:10:33.258 --\u003e 00:10:34.926\r\nHey, corn on the cob.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.009 --\u003e 00:10:37.637\r\nA scarecrow's gotta love that.\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:45.854 --\u003e 00:10:47.981\r\nBATMAN: Has Professor\r\nCrane lost his appetite?\r\n\r\n00:10:53.820 --\u003e 00:10:55.530\r\nYou're not supposed to be here.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.613 --\u003e 00:10:57.949\r\nBut the Scarecrow is.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.032 --\u003e 00:10:59.284\r\nWhat...\r\n\r\n00:10:59.367 --\u003e 00:11:00.368\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:11:00.451 --\u003e 00:11:02.036\r\nHe's in his cell.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.120 --\u003e 00:11:03.955\r\nI'd like to make sure of that.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.038 --\u003e 00:11:07.458\r\n\u003ci\u003eTake my word.\r\nHusk saw him five minutes ago.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:07.876 --\u003e 00:11:10.545\r\nThen you won't mind\r\nif I pay him a visit.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.462 --\u003e 00:11:12.463\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:11:12.589 --\u003e 00:11:13.715\r\nNo, you can't do that!\r\n\r\n00:11:13.798 --\u003e 00:11:15.925\r\nIt's against the rules!\r\nYou can't!\r\n\r\n00:11:21.389 --\u003e 00:11:22.432\r\nStay with him, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.558 --\u003e 00:11:24.726\r\nFine with me.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.986 --\u003e 00:11:36.696\r\nThe cowl is familiar,\r\n\r\n00:11:36.821 --\u003e 00:11:38.281\r\nbut I'm blanking on the face.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.364 --\u003e 00:11:41.659\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.424 --\u003e 00:12:00.094\r\nNo! Don't go in!\r\nDon't do it! No!\r\n\r\n00:12:02.764 --\u003e 00:12:04.682\r\n- Don't!\r\n- Wait.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.766 --\u003e 00:12:06.768\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:13.316 --\u003e 00:12:14.734\r\nBATMAN: Professor Crane?\r\n\r\n00:12:22.575 --\u003e 00:12:27.247\r\n(MAN IACAL LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.914 --\u003e 00:12:32.168\r\n$27,800, $27,900, $28,000.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.002 --\u003e 00:12:35.129\r\nIt's a pleasure doing business.\r\n\r\n00:12:36.047 --\u003e 00:12:38.258\r\nYou've been winning a lot\r\nhere, Mr., uh...\r\n\r\n00:12:40.301 --\u003e 00:12:42.345\r\nYou may call me Lucky.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.971 --\u003e 00:12:44.973\r\nYeah? Well, Lucky,\r\n\r\n00:12:45.056 --\u003e 00:12:48.726\r\nthat's what you must be,\r\nbecause I ain't seen you lose.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.810 --\u003e 00:12:51.437\r\nNot even once over\r\nthe last week.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.521 --\u003e 00:12:53.064\r\nYes, well,\r\n\r\n00:12:53.147 --\u003e 00:12:55.149\r\nI make my own luck.\r\n\r\n00:13:01.572 --\u003e 00:13:03.324\r\nThat Lucky knows something,\r\n\r\n00:13:03.408 --\u003e 00:13:05.493\r\nand I wanna know it, too.\r\n\r\n00:13:09.539 --\u003e 00:13:11.457\r\nBe persuasive.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.016 --\u003e 00:14:11.100\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:14:11.434 --\u003e 00:14:12.977\r\nLost?\r\n\r\n00:14:13.561 --\u003e 00:14:16.105\r\nYou have that bewildered look,\r\n\r\n00:14:16.189 --\u003e 00:14:18.733\r\nbut your sort always does.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.816 --\u003e 00:14:21.235\r\nI ain't lost.\r\nI'm looking for you.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.319 --\u003e 00:14:25.114\r\nI wanna know how come you always\r\nwin, Mr. Lucky.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.239 --\u003e 00:14:27.450\r\nIt's quite simple, actually.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.575 --\u003e 00:14:29.494\r\nI fix the games.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.244 --\u003e 00:14:33.956\r\nYou can't fix all those sports.\r\nNobody can.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.083 --\u003e 00:14:38.086\r\nO ye of little brain,\r\nallow me to illustrate.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.379 --\u003e 00:14:42.423\r\nHere. You can read, can't you?\r\n\r\n00:14:48.262 --\u003e 00:14:49.263\r\n\"Boo!\"\r\n\r\n00:14:49.347 --\u003e 00:14:51.265\r\nHey, is this some kind of joke?\r\n\r\n00:14:52.016 --\u003e 00:14:54.352\r\nIt's no joke, I assure you.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.435 --\u003e 00:14:58.147\r\nIt's the fear of victory\r\nand the agony of...\r\n\r\n00:14:58.940 --\u003e 00:15:00.691\r\nThe Scarecrow!\r\n\r\n00:15:01.150 --\u003e 00:15:02.443\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.610 --\u003e 00:15:08.282\r\nSo, now you understand step one\r\nin how I fix an athletic contest.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.366 --\u003e 00:15:11.244\r\nI shall proceed to step two.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.327 --\u003e 00:15:14.414\r\nNo! No! Get away!\r\n\r\n00:15:15.081 --\u003e 00:15:16.624\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:24.841 --\u003e 00:15:29.053\r\nHe's gonna get me. He's gonna get me.\r\nHe's gonna get me!\r\n\r\n00:15:31.180 --\u003e 00:15:34.767\r\nThat's how we found him.\r\nScared as a rat at a cat convention.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.851 --\u003e 00:15:36.853\r\nI've never seen\r\nanything like it.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.936 --\u003e 00:15:38.789\r\nBATMAN: You haven't been\r\nwatching the sports channel.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.813 --\u003e 00:15:39.939\r\nSports?\r\n\r\n00:15:40.898 --\u003e 00:15:42.358\r\nOh, you mean those athletes?\r\n\r\n00:15:42.942 --\u003e 00:15:46.237\r\n- What's that got to do with...\r\n- Put two and two together, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.320 --\u003e 00:15:49.073\r\nThat goon in there works\r\nfor Leon the bookie.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.157 --\u003e 00:15:50.324\r\nAnd word has it,\r\n\r\n00:15:50.408 --\u003e 00:15:52.618\r\nhe's been taking it\r\non the chin lately.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.702 --\u003e 00:15:55.997\r\nYou're telling me that\r\nthat walking pile of straw\r\n\r\n00:15:56.080 --\u003e 00:15:58.082\r\nscares the stuffing\r\nout of sports stars,\r\n\r\n00:15:58.166 --\u003e 00:16:00.418\r\nand then bets\r\nagainst their teams?\r\n\r\n00:16:00.501 --\u003e 00:16:01.544\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.627 --\u003e 00:16:05.298\r\nA perfect way to scare up some\r\nquick cash for his sick schemes.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.846 --\u003e 00:16:13.014\r\nSteady, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.514 --\u003e 00:16:14.765\r\nYou can do it.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.767 --\u003e 00:16:18.186\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.353\r\nI'm not afraid!\r\n\r\n00:16:20.146 --\u003e 00:16:21.731\r\nI'm not afraid!\r\n\r\n00:16:21.814 --\u003e 00:16:23.941\r\nI'm not... No!\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:31.199\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.282 --\u003e 00:16:33.576\r\nI learned to walk\r\non a high wire.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.659 --\u003e 00:16:36.704\r\nNow I can't stand on a step\r\nstool without freaking.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.787 --\u003e 00:16:37.872\r\nI'm...\r\n\r\n00:16:37.955 --\u003e 00:16:39.540\r\nI'm no good to you anymore.\r\n\r\n00:16:40.458 --\u003e 00:16:43.419\r\nBATMAN: Easy, Dick.\r\nIt's bound to wear off.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.503 --\u003e 00:16:45.588\r\nBut, in the meantime,\r\nyou've got to fight it.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.671 --\u003e 00:16:47.298\r\nRegain control.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.381 --\u003e 00:16:48.799\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:16:48.883 --\u003e 00:16:49.884\r\nROBIN: Where?\r\n\r\n00:16:51.802 --\u003e 00:16:53.721\r\nBATMAN: I thought we'd\r\ncatch a game tonight.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.804 --\u003e 00:16:58.059\r\nThe Gotham Knights are favored 4-1,\r\nthanks to their quarterback, Mitch Nole.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.018 --\u003e 00:17:02.063\r\nROBIN: You think he's\r\ngonna get a telegram?\r\n\r\n00:17:03.022 --\u003e 00:17:04.357\r\nI'd say it's a good bet.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.483 --\u003e 00:17:07.026\r\n(SIGHS) I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.610 --\u003e 00:17:09.278\r\nI'll only get in the way.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.820 --\u003e 00:17:12.698\r\nYou can be my extra set of eyes.\r\nGet in.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.199 --\u003e 00:17:15.618\r\nI'll drive real slow.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.144 --\u003e 00:17:43.729\r\nOkay, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.813 --\u003e 00:17:45.690\r\nGet it together.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.531 --\u003e 00:17:56.033\r\nTelegram for Mitch Nole. Oh!\r\n\r\n00:17:56.492 --\u003e 00:17:59.120\r\nWhat? What's wrong?\r\nAll I did was double-park!\r\n\r\n00:17:59.203 --\u003e 00:18:00.746\r\nI'll move it! I swear!\r\n\r\n00:18:00.830 --\u003e 00:18:01.914\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.363 --\u003e 00:18:35.656\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:44.040 --\u003e 00:18:45.124\r\nAll right, Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.958 --\u003e 00:18:48.044\r\nWhat's your game plan this time?\r\n\r\n00:18:58.095 --\u003e 00:18:59.096\r\nHut!\r\n\r\n00:18:59.180 --\u003e 00:19:02.016\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:06.270 --\u003e 00:19:08.314\r\n- (WHISTLE BLOWS)\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:19:08.397 --\u003e 00:19:11.067\r\nBOSEMAN: Mitch Nole is\r\nripping the Colonials apart!\r\n\r\n00:19:11.192 --\u003e 00:19:14.278\r\nFour hundred yards passing,\r\nand the game's not over yet.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.362 --\u003e 00:19:17.740\r\nThere's enough powder in that\r\nhelmet to panic a pachyderm!\r\n\r\n00:19:19.992 --\u003e 00:19:20.993\r\nHut! Hut!\r\n\r\n00:19:25.790 --\u003e 00:19:28.959\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:19:29.835 --\u003e 00:19:33.047\r\nHe should be prostrating\r\nhimself, crying for mercy!\r\n\r\n00:19:33.130 --\u003e 00:19:35.091\r\nBATMAN: Change of\r\nluck, Scarecrow?\r\n\r\n00:19:36.550 --\u003e 00:19:37.843\r\nSCARECROW: You!\r\n\r\n00:19:37.927 --\u003e 00:19:41.222\r\nBATMAN: You're aware that\r\ngambling is illegal in Gotham?\r\n\r\n00:19:41.347 --\u003e 00:19:43.349\r\nI need the money, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:43.432 --\u003e 00:19:45.976\r\nYou know the cost of\r\nchemicals these days.\r\n\r\n00:19:46.102 --\u003e 00:19:49.897\r\nAnd it'll take much more than this to\r\nbring every pathetic person in Gotham\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.483\r\nto their knees, kissing my feet!\r\n\r\n00:19:53.234 --\u003e 00:19:54.694\r\nNo closer, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:19:54.777 --\u003e 00:19:57.446\r\nUnless you want a stampede\r\nof half-crazed humanity,\r\n\r\n00:19:57.530 --\u003e 00:19:59.323\r\ncrushing and clawing each other!\r\n\r\n00:20:00.157 --\u003e 00:20:01.158\r\nROBIN: Oh, no!\r\n\r\n00:20:06.163 --\u003e 00:20:09.500\r\nCome on, Robin. Get a grip!\r\n\r\n00:20:15.798 --\u003e 00:20:19.760\r\nNow, what guarantee do I\r\nhave you won't follow me?\r\n\r\n00:20:20.594 --\u003e 00:20:22.138\r\nYou have my word, Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.221 --\u003e 00:20:24.390\r\nJust don't drop the vial.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.473 --\u003e 00:20:27.935\r\nActually, Batman,\r\nI'd prefer a little insurance\r\n\r\n00:20:28.060 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nthat you'll be\r\notherwise occupied.\r\n\r\n00:20:40.573 --\u003e 00:20:42.616\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:50.124 --\u003e 00:20:51.417\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:56.422 --\u003e 00:20:57.423\r\n(CROWD GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.090 --\u003e 00:20:59.383\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:02.011 --\u003e 00:21:05.723\r\nBOSEMAN: It's a fumble!\r\nThis could mean disaster for Gotham!\r\n\r\n00:21:07.767 --\u003e 00:21:09.351\r\nWait! Look at that!\r\n\r\n00:21:13.355 --\u003e 00:21:15.065\r\nWhat a recovery!\r\n\r\n00:21:15.274 --\u003e 00:21:16.275\r\n(WHISTLE BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:21:19.695 --\u003e 00:21:21.238\r\nBATMAN: Good work, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.991 --\u003e 00:21:26.952\r\nI also snagged a helmet\r\nthat had some of this in it.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.036 --\u003e 00:21:29.789\r\nLooks like you've got a\r\nhandle on your problem.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.872 --\u003e 00:21:32.041\r\nYeah. I'm getting there.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.626 --\u003e 00:21:36.962\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMMENTATOR: The Gotham Knights\r\nwasted no time signing Brian Rogers,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:37.046 --\u003e 00:21:40.466\r\n\u003ci\u003emaking our local champ their\r\nfirst-round draft pick.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:40.549 --\u003e 00:21:43.010\r\nLooks like your friend\r\nis back on track again.\r\n\r\n00:21:43.594 --\u003e 00:21:45.471\r\nYeah, I can't wait\r\nto congratulate him.\r\n\r\n00:21:45.554 --\u003e 00:21:47.848\r\nYou can always send a telegram.\r\n\r\n00:21:54.438 --\u003e 00:21:56.440\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.465 --\u003e 00:22:22.466\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E20 - I've Got Batman in My Basement (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:19.520 --\u003e 00:00:21.522\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.097 --\u003e 00:01:38.599\r\n(DRILLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:41.143 --\u003e 00:01:42.311\r\n(GLASS SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:02:13.425 --\u003e 00:02:14.593\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.676 --\u003e 00:02:16.553\r\nA piece of cake.\r\nJust like the boss said.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.762 --\u003e 00:02:18.805\r\nYeah,\r\nall it took was five minutes.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.014 --\u003e 00:02:21.183\r\nBATMAN: And that will\r\nget you five years.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.726 --\u003e 00:02:24.061\r\nWith good behavior.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.103 --\u003e 00:02:26.146\r\n(BIRD SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.396 --\u003e 00:02:27.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:39.910 --\u003e 00:02:41.203\r\n(BIRD SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:41.536 --\u003e 00:02:42.621\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:46.541 --\u003e 00:02:48.381\r\n- (CONTINUES SCREECHING)\r\n- (CONTINUES GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:13.985 --\u003e 00:03:15.362\r\nBird seed?\r\n\r\n00:03:21.493 --\u003e 00:03:23.995\r\nHey, Roberta,\r\nit's got a walkie-talkie wrist band.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.329 --\u003e 00:03:27.666\r\nA pen light, binoculars,\r\neven this cool badge.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.208 --\u003e 00:03:30.293\r\nYo, Sherwood,\r\nwhat you got there?\r\n\r\n00:03:30.877 --\u003e 00:03:32.379\r\nIt's a junior detective kit.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.754 --\u003e 00:03:34.172\r\nAnd the name's Sherman.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.756 --\u003e 00:03:37.342\r\nA fake, just like you, wormwood.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.718 --\u003e 00:03:39.386\r\nFRANK: Whoa. Check this out.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.469 --\u003e 00:03:40.470\r\nA hawk.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.054 --\u003e 00:03:43.181\r\nCome on, Frank. Those are mine.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.390 --\u003e 00:03:45.243\r\n- (FRANK LAUGHING)\r\n- SHERMAN: Come on. Give it back.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.267 --\u003e 00:03:48.270\r\nCan't you find any of your\r\nown species to play with?\r\n\r\n00:03:49.187 --\u003e 00:03:52.065\r\nAh, don't pitch a fit.\r\nWe're just kidding around.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.401 --\u003e 00:03:55.819\r\nHey, that's no hawk.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.236 --\u003e 00:03:59.030\r\nJudging by its wingspread\r\nand the shape of its head,\r\n\r\n00:03:59.448 --\u003e 00:04:02.117\r\nit's obviously a giant\r\nSouth American vulture.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.617 --\u003e 00:04:05.078\r\n(SCOFFS) A vulture,\r\nin Gotham City?\r\n\r\n00:04:05.746 --\u003e 00:04:07.247\r\nFRANK: Sure thing, Sherlock.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.581 --\u003e 00:04:08.915\r\nSHERMAN: Come on, Roberta.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.417 --\u003e 00:04:11.960\r\nROBERTA: Sherman,\r\nwhere are we going?\r\n\r\n00:04:12.502 --\u003e 00:04:15.672\r\nA vulture in Gotham City is\r\na mystery worth checking out.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.352 --\u003e 00:04:31.021\r\nCome on, Roberta.\r\nIt went in there.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.028 --\u003e 00:04:41.198\r\nSherman, the sign says it's condemned.\r\nYou shouldn't go in.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.825 --\u003e 00:04:44.826\r\nMen.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.044 --\u003e 00:04:55.045\r\nI don't like it.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.629 --\u003e 00:04:57.631\r\nCop a squat and dummy up, Jay.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.881 --\u003e 00:05:01.134\r\nIf the boss said to meet him back\r\nhere, we meet him here.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.219 --\u003e 00:05:03.970\r\n(GASPS) What's that?\r\n\r\n00:05:10.435 --\u003e 00:05:12.896\r\nIt's just birdseed, birdbrain.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.736 --\u003e 00:05:21.404\r\nCome on, let's get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.831 --\u003e 00:05:31.915\r\nThe Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.415 --\u003e 00:05:33.917\r\n(SQUAWS)\r\n\r\n00:05:38.004 --\u003e 00:05:40.465\r\nAw, Scrap, my faithful pet.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.007 --\u003e 00:05:43.093\r\nReady for a ripe repast?\r\n\r\n00:05:48.932 --\u003e 00:05:51.601\r\n(SHUDDERS) That bald buzzard\r\ngives me the willies.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.060 --\u003e 00:05:53.395\r\nIf it weren't for Scrap,\r\n\r\n00:05:53.478 --\u003e 00:05:57.107\r\nyou two would be feathering your\r\nnest at Stonegate Penitentiary.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.482 --\u003e 00:05:59.776\r\nNow, where is it?\r\n\r\n00:06:05.115 --\u003e 00:06:10.745\r\nOh, how much more doth beauty\r\nbeauteous seem by this sweet egg,\r\n\r\n00:06:11.037 --\u003e 00:06:13.248\r\nwhich we have scrambled for?\r\n\r\n00:06:13.874 --\u003e 00:06:16.501\r\nSHERMAN: They stole the\r\nVonalster Fabergé Egg.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.043 --\u003e 00:06:18.044\r\nThe what?\r\n\r\n00:06:18.545 --\u003e 00:06:20.297\r\nDon't you read the papers?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.839 --\u003e 00:06:22.299\r\nDo the comics count?\r\n\r\n00:06:26.344 --\u003e 00:06:28.013\r\nThat thing's worth a fortune.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.221 --\u003e 00:06:29.431\r\nWe gotta tell someone.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.858 --\u003e 00:06:41.359\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:42.360 --\u003e 00:06:43.361\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:47.949 --\u003e 00:06:48.950\r\nPENGUIN: Batman!\r\n\r\n00:06:49.492 --\u003e 00:06:51.411\r\nGet that capon crusader.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.039 --\u003e 00:06:55.290\r\n(ALL SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:06:56.207 --\u003e 00:06:57.208\r\nSHERMAN: Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.794 --\u003e 00:07:01.379\r\n- (WHIRS)\r\n- (BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:07:20.732 --\u003e 00:07:21.775\r\n(BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:07:22.150 --\u003e 00:07:23.360\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:28.531 --\u003e 00:07:30.283\r\nGet out. Now!\r\n\r\n00:07:30.992 --\u003e 00:07:32.452\r\n(STUTTERS) Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.581 --\u003e 00:07:37.958\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:46.508 --\u003e 00:07:48.468\r\nYou should have taken\r\nyour own advice.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.677 --\u003e 00:07:49.678\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.136 --\u003e 00:07:52.472\r\n- (GAS HISSES)\r\n- (COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:55.392 --\u003e 00:07:56.726\r\n(CONTINUES COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:00.897 --\u003e 00:08:02.190\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.610 --\u003e 00:08:06.820\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:06.903 --\u003e 00:08:08.405\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:10.907 --\u003e 00:08:12.283\r\n(BATMAN CONTINUES COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:16.204 --\u003e 00:08:17.205\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.708 --\u003e 00:08:21.668\r\nBatman's in trouble. Come on.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.377 --\u003e 00:08:24.087\r\nI don't know about this.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.926 --\u003e 00:08:33.388\r\n(GRUNTS) It's those delinquents.\r\nStop them!\r\n\r\n00:08:42.939 --\u003e 00:08:45.817\r\n- Quick, inside.\r\n- Sherman, do something.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.256 --\u003e 00:09:09.758\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:20.018 --\u003e 00:09:21.561\r\nWe gotta get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.062 --\u003e 00:09:23.104\r\nWhat am I doing?\r\n\r\n00:09:23.396 --\u003e 00:09:25.148\r\nI'm not old enough to drive.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.527 --\u003e 00:09:31.362\r\n(STRAINS) I can't\r\nreach the pedals.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.863 --\u003e 00:09:32.989\r\nI can.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.326 --\u003e 00:09:37.744\r\nPush that long one.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.036 --\u003e 00:09:39.370\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:39.454 --\u003e 00:09:40.997\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:44.042 --\u003e 00:09:45.585\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:54.427 --\u003e 00:09:56.012\r\n(ALL CONTINUE EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:56.096 --\u003e 00:09:57.138\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:59.808 --\u003e 00:10:00.809\r\nHit it again.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.851 --\u003e 00:10:03.394\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.479 --\u003e 00:10:05.647\r\n(JAY GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:10:07.941 --\u003e 00:10:09.567\r\nOkay, Roberta, floor it.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.985 --\u003e 00:10:12.403\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:14.114 --\u003e 00:10:15.156\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:21.538 --\u003e 00:10:22.914\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:29.712 --\u003e 00:10:31.214\r\n(CONTINUES SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:39.973 --\u003e 00:10:42.183\r\nBe-fowled by a\r\ncouple of fledglings.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.145 --\u003e 00:10:46.425\r\nSHERMAN: Keep it going, Roberta.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.729 --\u003e 00:10:48.690\r\nI think I'm starting to\r\nget the hang of this.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.693 --\u003e 00:10:53.319\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:54.445 --\u003e 00:10:56.990\r\nSHERMAN: Come on, Batman.\r\nThis will help.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.994 --\u003e 00:11:02.453\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:03.788 --\u003e 00:11:05.415\r\n(BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:06.291 --\u003e 00:11:07.292\r\nIt's okay.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.670 --\u003e 00:11:13.131\r\nMy name is Sherman.\r\nAnd I'm a detective, too.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.548 --\u003e 00:11:15.300\r\nWe're lying low in my basement.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.510 --\u003e 00:11:18.710\r\nWe got the egg down here, too.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.888 --\u003e 00:11:21.973\r\nSee, this is my crime lab.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.265 --\u003e 00:11:23.850\r\nIt's not exactly the Batcave.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.100 --\u003e 00:11:25.518\r\nCapsule.\r\n\r\n00:11:27.187 --\u003e 00:11:28.188\r\n\"Cap\" what?\r\n\r\n00:11:29.022 --\u003e 00:11:30.899\r\nNo, you're not captured, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.316 --\u003e 00:11:33.818\r\nYou're safe here.\r\nIt's just Mom and me.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.152 --\u003e 00:11:35.361\r\nAnd she's at work.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.570 --\u003e 00:11:36.905\r\n(ROBERTA CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:11:37.655 --\u003e 00:11:39.949\r\nOh, yeah. And Roberta's here.\r\nShe's cool.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.742 --\u003e 00:11:41.743\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.911 --\u003e 00:11:44.204\r\nVisor.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.704 --\u003e 00:11:46.039\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:46.956 --\u003e 00:11:48.499\r\nWonder what that meant.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.917 --\u003e 00:11:52.086\r\nDon't look at me.\r\nI've had enough mystery for one day.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.547\r\n- I'm calling the police.\r\n- No way.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.048 --\u003e 00:11:58.426\r\nA detective always has to protect\r\nthe identity of his client,\r\n\r\n00:11:58.927 --\u003e 00:12:00.720\r\nespecially when\r\nit's this client.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.776 --\u003e 00:12:18.071\r\nThose meddling brats\r\ncouldn't have gotten too far.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.321 --\u003e 00:12:20.281\r\nBut, boss,\r\nwhat about the Batman?\r\n\r\n00:12:20.531 --\u003e 00:12:24.619\r\nBatman's a worm, less than\r\nnothing, a worthless peasant.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.245 --\u003e 00:12:29.791\r\nAnd besides, the gas will keep\r\nhim null and void for a good week.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.925 --\u003e 00:12:41.344\r\nMRS. GRANT: Sherman,\r\nwhat are you doing down there?\r\n\r\n00:12:41.636 --\u003e 00:12:42.887\r\nNothing, Mom.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.221 --\u003e 00:12:46.099\r\nMRS. GRANT: You're not trying to\r\nmake gunpowder again, are you?\r\n\r\n00:12:46.891 --\u003e 00:12:48.351\r\nNo, Mom, honest.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.685 --\u003e 00:12:50.687\r\nWe saved Batman's life, Mrs.\r\nGrant,\r\n\r\n00:12:50.937 --\u003e 00:12:53.064\r\nand now we're hiding him\r\nfrom some bad criminals.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.439 --\u003e 00:12:56.234\r\nMRS. GRANT: That's good,\r\njust don't make a mess.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.985 --\u003e 00:12:59.028\r\nNice going, Miss Bigmouth.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.445 --\u003e 00:13:01.614\r\nSorry, Sherman.\r\nI guess I panicked.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.413 --\u003e 00:13:10.832\r\nMRS. GRANT: I'm going to the\r\nstore, Sherman.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.915 --\u003e 00:13:12.375\r\nStay out of trouble.\r\n\r\n00:13:12.750 --\u003e 00:13:13.918\r\nSHERMAN: Sure thing, Mom.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.967 --\u003e 00:13:23.011\r\nAfternoon, Mrs. Grant.\r\n\r\n00:13:23.261 --\u003e 00:13:25.138\r\nLovely day, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:13:28.474 --\u003e 00:13:30.893\r\nHe's up! He shoots!\r\nIt looks good!\r\n\r\n00:13:35.189 --\u003e 00:13:36.899\r\nOh, no!\r\n\r\n00:13:39.110 --\u003e 00:13:42.447\r\nMan, oh, man!\r\nScope out these wheels.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.905 --\u003e 00:13:44.657\r\nSHERMAN: You guys\r\nbetter leave that alone.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.949 --\u003e 00:13:47.910\r\nOh, Golly, we sure are\r\nscared, aren't we, Nicholas?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.453 --\u003e 00:13:52.957\r\nOh, yes, Francis, we certainly are.\r\nStep aside, Shirley.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.001 --\u003e 00:13:57.587\r\n- Cool. Whose car is this?\r\n- (DEVICES BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:57.795 --\u003e 00:14:00.006\r\nIt's my mom's... My uncle's.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.509 --\u003e 00:14:05.553\r\nAll right, look,\r\nit's the Batmobile.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.012 --\u003e 00:14:07.430\r\nFRANK: Yeah, right.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.056 --\u003e 00:14:11.100\r\nHey, I don't think he's kidding.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.684 --\u003e 00:14:12.685\r\nWhat's this?\r\n\r\n00:14:15.646 --\u003e 00:14:17.023\r\nSome kind of capsules.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.565 --\u003e 00:14:18.566\r\nCapsule?\r\n\r\n00:14:19.317 --\u003e 00:14:22.779\r\nCapsule on the visor.\r\nThat's what he meant.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.571 --\u003e 00:14:26.115\r\nGive me that!\r\nIt's a matter of life or death.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.741 --\u003e 00:14:27.825\r\n(BIRD SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:30.203 --\u003e 00:14:32.163\r\n(CONTINUES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:37.085 --\u003e 00:14:38.419\r\n(CONTINUES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:53.267 --\u003e 00:14:54.685\r\n- No!\r\n- (BIRD SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.527 --\u003e 00:15:04.320\r\n- (CONTINUES SCREECHING)\r\n- BOTH: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:15:06.072 --\u003e 00:15:07.865\r\n(CONTINUES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.241 --\u003e 00:15:09.784\r\nSHERMAN: Come on,\r\nBatman, wake up.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.413 --\u003e 00:15:14.747\r\n(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:17.291 --\u003e 00:15:18.292\r\nIt's him!\r\n\r\n00:15:20.169 --\u003e 00:15:21.587\r\nNICK: Totally awesome.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.630 --\u003e 00:15:24.215\r\nI wonder who he really is.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.549 --\u003e 00:15:26.050\r\nNo! Get back.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.134 --\u003e 00:15:27.385\r\n(NICK AND FRANK GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:15:28.010 --\u003e 00:15:29.637\r\nThis isn't a game, you jerks.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.012 --\u003e 00:15:33.641\r\nIf the vulture's here that means the\r\nPenguin will be right on his tail.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.933 --\u003e 00:15:35.059\r\nBOTH: The Penguin?\r\n\r\n00:15:35.435 --\u003e 00:15:38.187\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHES)\r\n- Oh, no! What's that?\r\n\r\n00:15:38.271 --\u003e 00:15:40.481\r\nOh, great! It's him.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.452 --\u003e 00:15:54.495\r\nThat's it. I'm calling 911.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.834 --\u003e 00:16:00.835\r\nIt's dead.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.840 --\u003e 00:16:08.176\r\nSo much for phone\r\ncalls, huh, boss?\r\n\r\n00:16:10.511 --\u003e 00:16:12.597\r\nThen it's them or us.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.930 --\u003e 00:16:14.557\r\nBe careful with that\r\negg, Roberta.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.849 --\u003e 00:16:17.268\r\nI bet we can find\r\nsomething here to help us.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.436 --\u003e 00:16:19.979\r\n(BIRD SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:16:23.816 --\u003e 00:16:25.234\r\nI don't think anyone's home.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.485 --\u003e 00:16:27.278\r\nYeah,\r\nthe place is locked up tight.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.612 --\u003e 00:16:32.241\r\nStone walls do not a prison make\r\nnor locked doors a barricade.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.331 --\u003e 00:16:42.001\r\nGentlemen,\r\nand I use the term loosely,\r\n\r\n00:16:42.668 --\u003e 00:16:43.961\r\nafter you.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.012 --\u003e 00:16:56.265\r\nOkay, get ready for\r\noperation Fowl Play.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.269 --\u003e 00:17:01.479\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.562 --\u003e 00:17:03.314\r\nHow bourgeois.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.648 --\u003e 00:17:06.776\r\nTearing this place apart\r\ncould only improve it.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.360 --\u003e 00:17:08.444\r\n(CLATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:17:08.861 --\u003e 00:17:11.072\r\nLet the egg hunt begin.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.283 --\u003e 00:17:16.035\r\n(OBJECTS CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.246 --\u003e 00:17:19.539\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:25.294 --\u003e 00:17:26.671\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:27.964 --\u003e 00:17:29.048\r\n(SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:17:29.590 --\u003e 00:17:31.759\r\n- Hey, Raven, are you okay?\r\n- (EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:17:31.842 --\u003e 00:17:32.885\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.013 --\u003e 00:17:39.058\r\nThese commoners have\r\nsuch cheap furniture.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.606 --\u003e 00:17:47.650\r\nCome on, Batman, snap out of it.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.858 --\u003e 00:17:50.570\r\nIf that didn't wake him,\r\nI don't know what will.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.739 --\u003e 00:17:56.367\r\nCharge! Now, Roberta!\r\n\r\n00:18:01.956 --\u003e 00:18:03.124\r\nNice shot.\r\n\r\n00:18:03.541 --\u003e 00:18:06.544\r\nBe careful, Roberta,\r\nyou don't wanna get too close.\r\n\r\n00:18:06.961 --\u003e 00:18:08.421\r\n- (PENGUIN GRUNTS)\r\n- We did it.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.671 --\u003e 00:18:13.509\r\nChildren defending their nest.\r\nHow noble. How endearing.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.677 --\u003e 00:18:16.470\r\nHow ineffective.\r\n\r\n00:18:16.929 --\u003e 00:18:18.389\r\nGrab the little pests.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.657 --\u003e 00:18:38.200\r\nHe's not awake yet?\r\n\r\n00:18:38.993 --\u003e 00:18:40.786\r\nFrank thought he\r\nsaw his eye blink.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.870 --\u003e 00:18:42.330\r\n- (DOOR CLICKS)\r\n- (EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:18:42.663 --\u003e 00:18:44.332\r\n(POUNDING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.088 --\u003e 00:18:53.841\r\nValiant effort, but I win.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.300 --\u003e 00:18:57.011\r\nNow, back away,\r\nyou irksome imps.\r\n\r\n00:19:01.474 --\u003e 00:19:03.225\r\nAh. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.309 --\u003e 00:19:05.102\r\nA treat with my egg.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.854 --\u003e 00:19:09.482\r\nSliced ham. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.068 --\u003e 00:19:13.069\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.611 --\u003e 00:19:15.404\r\nFarewell, Bat-vermin.\r\n\r\n00:19:18.616 --\u003e 00:19:19.700\r\n(PENGUIN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:19.867 --\u003e 00:19:20.868\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:19:23.954 --\u003e 00:19:25.081\r\nBATMAN: Back off, Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.834 --\u003e 00:19:31.629\r\nGentlemen,\r\nyour timing is impeccable.\r\n\r\n00:19:32.546 --\u003e 00:19:34.006\r\nTake no prisoners!\r\n\r\n00:19:36.676 --\u003e 00:19:37.927\r\n(RAVEN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:44.684 --\u003e 00:19:45.685\r\n(JAY GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.270 --\u003e 00:19:50.439\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.565 --\u003e 00:19:52.775\r\n(RAVEN SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:52.858 --\u003e 00:19:54.235\r\n(JAY GRUNTS) {THUD)\r\n\r\n00:19:54.860 --\u003e 00:19:58.197\r\nI'll clip your wings,\r\nyou flying rodent.\r\n\r\n00:20:03.494 --\u003e 00:20:04.995\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:30.855 --\u003e 00:20:33.482\r\nPENGUIN: Still a little\r\ndazed, are we?\r\n\r\n00:20:36.736 --\u003e 00:20:37.945\r\n(PENGUIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.745 --\u003e 00:20:47.121\r\nWe're safe!\r\n\r\n00:20:47.371 --\u003e 00:20:51.041\r\nMRS. GRANT: My house!\r\n(YELLS) Sherman!\r\n\r\n00:20:51.876 --\u003e 00:20:53.169\r\nMaybe you're safe.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.794 --\u003e 00:20:56.547\r\nYoung man, you've got some\r\nserious explaining to do.\r\n\r\n00:20:56.839 --\u003e 00:20:57.965\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.466 --\u003e 00:21:01.343\r\nUh, Mom,\r\nI'd like you to meet Batman.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.719 --\u003e 00:21:03.095\r\nBatman, this is my mom.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.804 --\u003e 00:21:04.805\r\nMa'am.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.139 --\u003e 00:21:06.265\r\nUh, hello.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.433 --\u003e 00:21:10.478\r\nSay, Batman, you wouldn't be\r\nsingle, would you?\r\n\r\n00:21:22.448 --\u003e 00:21:23.908\r\nNow, where was I?\r\n\r\n00:21:24.533 --\u003e 00:21:26.744\r\nSomeone keeps swiping\r\nMr. Vanducci's newspaper?\r\n\r\n00:21:27.203 --\u003e 00:21:28.204\r\nRight, Frank.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.412 --\u003e 00:21:29.892\r\nYou and Nick set up\r\nfor surveillance.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.623 --\u003e 00:21:33.834\r\nRoberta and I will be over at Mrs.\r\nFineman's. Her dog is missing.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.752 --\u003e 00:21:35.878\r\nYou're the boss.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.337 --\u003e 00:21:37.338\r\nBOTH: Sherman.\r\n\r\n00:21:47.890 --\u003e 00:21:49.892\r\n(THEME some PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:14.041 --\u003e 00:22:15.042\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E21 - Vendetta (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.964 --\u003e 00:00:07.382\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:26.628 --\u003e 00:01:28.130\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:29.631 --\u003e 00:01:31.174\r\nWe're almost there, Conway.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.633 --\u003e 00:01:33.343\r\nJust keep your eyes open.\r\n\r\n00:01:36.430 --\u003e 00:01:38.015\r\nSomething could still happen.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.767 --\u003e 00:01:42.227\r\nSpider Conway.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.399 --\u003e 00:01:48.900\r\nDon't know what\r\nhe's worrying about.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.109 --\u003e 00:01:51.153\r\nHe's only got the sweetest\r\ndeal of the century.\r\n\r\n00:01:53.405 --\u003e 00:01:56.742\r\nAll he's gotta do is make like a\r\ncanary at the crime-commission hearings\r\n\r\n00:01:56.908 --\u003e 00:01:59.077\r\nand he gets 10\r\nyears off his time.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.369 --\u003e 00:02:02.247\r\nIt ain't him getting to the hearings\r\nthat's got him spooked, commish.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.331 --\u003e 00:02:04.958\r\nIt's somebody else getting\r\nto him before then.\r\n\r\n00:02:12.174 --\u003e 00:02:14.051\r\n- (CLOCK TICKING)\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:17.304 --\u003e 00:02:18.388\r\nThere's a bomb on the boat!\r\n\r\n00:02:19.473 --\u003e 00:02:20.682\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:21.016 --\u003e 00:02:22.392\r\nPOLICE OFFICER: Abandon ship!\r\n\r\n00:02:23.352 --\u003e 00:02:25.395\r\n(BINOCULAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:02:35.447 --\u003e 00:02:37.908\r\nRemind me never to think of\r\nyou as a good-luck charm.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.535 --\u003e 00:02:42.913\r\nOFFICER 1: Help!\r\n(COUGHING) OFFICER 2: Over here! Help me!\r\n\r\n00:02:48.960 --\u003e 00:02:50.671\r\n(OFFICERS couemue)\r\n\r\n00:02:53.173 --\u003e 00:02:55.509\r\nGORDON: Carver,\r\nI want Dock Street cordoned off,\r\n\r\n00:02:55.592 --\u003e 00:02:57.678\r\nthree blocks in both directions.\r\nMove it.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.303 --\u003e 00:02:59.971\r\nHardesty, call Forensics.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.059 --\u003e 00:03:05.977\r\nNo sign of Conway\r\nanywhere, detective.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.896 --\u003e 00:03:09.356\r\nStart dragging the bay.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.564 --\u003e 00:03:52.190\r\nTaking me off the case?\r\n\r\n00:03:52.566 --\u003e 00:03:54.568\r\nWhat kind of shuck\r\nand jive is this, Jim?\r\n\r\n00:03:55.152 --\u003e 00:03:58.113\r\nYou know what I had to go through\r\njust to get Conway out of Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.196 --\u003e 00:04:00.907\r\nBut it's worth it if his testimony\r\ncan take down Rupert Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.409 --\u003e 00:04:04.661\r\nWhich is why Thorne looks\r\ngood for the bombing.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.370 --\u003e 00:04:07.164\r\nBut if I let you\r\ngo after Thorne,\r\n\r\n00:04:07.414 --\u003e 00:04:09.875\r\na lot of ugly ancient\r\nhistory is bound to come up.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.962 --\u003e 00:04:15.756\r\n(THUNDER CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:04:18.133 --\u003e 00:04:20.594\r\nI gotta relieve you,\r\nHarv, you know that.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.136 --\u003e 00:04:24.514\r\nUnless, you want Internal Affairs\r\nall over you like a bad rash.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.598 --\u003e 00:04:25.849\r\n(SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:04:58.965 --\u003e 00:05:00.342\r\nAncient history.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.759 --\u003e 00:05:02.385\r\nYeah, right!\r\n\r\n00:05:20.529 --\u003e 00:05:22.364\r\nBRUCE: A real\r\npage-turner, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:05:23.240 --\u003e 00:05:24.324\r\nIndeed.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.116 --\u003e 00:05:28.328\r\nBullock was suspected of\r\naccepting graft from Thorne\r\n\r\n00:05:28.453 --\u003e 00:05:29.621\r\ntwo years ago?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.038 --\u003e 00:05:32.958\r\nRight, but the case was\r\ndropped for lack of evidence.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.793 --\u003e 00:05:37.128\r\nIt was just before Spider\r\nConway went to prison.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.629 --\u003e 00:05:39.047\r\nAnd at the time of his arrest,\r\n\r\n00:05:39.381 --\u003e 00:05:41.091\r\nConway was working for Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.550 --\u003e 00:05:44.594\r\nSo, he might know something that\r\nBullock doesn't want revealed.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.928 --\u003e 00:05:48.306\r\nSurely you can't think this\r\nBullock person planted that bomb.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.640 --\u003e 00:05:50.517\r\nI'm not sure yet what to think.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.809 --\u003e 00:05:53.228\r\nAfter the explosion,\r\nI went out to Stonegate Island,\r\n\r\n00:05:53.395 --\u003e 00:05:55.355\r\nto check out the dock\r\nthe boat left from.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.939 --\u003e 00:05:57.607\r\nI found this.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.942 --\u003e 00:06:00.360\r\nA toothpick?\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:07.534\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:10.662 --\u003e 00:06:12.247\r\nWhere in the world...\r\n\r\n00:06:19.546 --\u003e 00:06:21.673\r\nHey! Anybody here? (ECHOING)\r\n\r\n00:06:36.771 --\u003e 00:06:37.772\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:06:38.064 --\u003e 00:06:39.190\r\nNot you!\r\n\r\n00:06:39.482 --\u003e 00:06:40.567\r\nIt can't be!\r\n\r\n00:06:41.192 --\u003e 00:06:42.319\r\nStay back!\r\n\r\n00:06:42.777 --\u003e 00:06:44.237\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:50.243 --\u003e 00:06:53.038\r\n(HUMMING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:06:57.375 --\u003e 00:06:58.919\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:01.880 --\u003e 00:07:03.131\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.931 --\u003e 00:07:12.098\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:12.766 --\u003e 00:07:13.892\r\n(THUNDER CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.769 --\u003e 00:07:18.146\r\nYou'd better have the\r\nmoney to pay for that.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.607 --\u003e 00:07:22.150\r\n(POT BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:22.233 --\u003e 00:07:24.194\r\nHere's how it works, slimeball.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.611 --\u003e 00:07:27.530\r\nI have questions and\r\nif you have answers,\r\n\r\n00:07:27.948 --\u003e 00:07:29.574\r\nI'll leave you alone.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.242 --\u003e 00:07:33.787\r\nOh, I got plenty of answers.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.874 --\u003e 00:07:40.377\r\n- (GUNS COCKING)\r\n- .38-caliber answers.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.925 --\u003e 00:07:48.259\r\n(LAUGHS SMUGLY)\r\n\r\n00:07:48.468 --\u003e 00:07:50.261\r\nNow, then, you were saying?\r\n\r\n00:07:52.722 --\u003e 00:07:54.057\r\nI was saying,\r\n\r\n00:07:54.641 --\u003e 00:07:59.020\r\nyou'd better hope your\r\nmen are very good shots.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.354 --\u003e 00:08:01.564\r\nIt's too hot in here.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.648 --\u003e 00:08:02.774\r\nLet's get some air.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.035 --\u003e 00:08:15.495\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:16.830 --\u003e 00:08:18.540\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:25.630 --\u003e 00:08:27.215\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:08:30.343 --\u003e 00:08:31.636\r\nWait! Stop!\r\n\r\n00:08:31.845 --\u003e 00:08:33.114\r\nI'll tell you anything you want.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.138 --\u003e 00:08:35.807\r\nDid you order Spider\r\nConway blown up?\r\n\r\n00:08:36.057 --\u003e 00:08:38.018\r\n(LAUGHS) That loser?\r\n\r\n00:08:38.101 --\u003e 00:08:40.020\r\nI wouldn't wipe my shoes on him.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.395 --\u003e 00:08:41.855\r\nConway's got nothing on me.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.938 --\u003e 00:08:43.106\r\nLet him talk.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.108 --\u003e 00:08:46.388\r\nHe could've talked his head off.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:47.444\r\nNo problem.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.777 --\u003e 00:08:48.820\r\nBATMAN: Okay.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.279 --\u003e 00:08:50.613\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.657 --\u003e 00:08:55.243\r\nDon't just stand\r\nthere, you clowns.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.535 --\u003e 00:08:57.203\r\nGet me down!\r\n\r\n00:09:01.958 --\u003e 00:09:03.835\r\nNo trace of Conway\r\nyet, commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.377 --\u003e 00:09:05.462\r\nWell, keep at it.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.587 --\u003e 00:09:07.172\r\nI'll meet you back\r\nat headquarters.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.803 --\u003e 00:09:14.804\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:15.472 --\u003e 00:09:17.724\r\nI've had cats that made\r\nmore noise than you.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.974 --\u003e 00:09:20.268\r\nWe need to talk about Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.690 --\u003e 00:09:28.276\r\nI think he might have been\r\nresponsible for the bomb.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.526 --\u003e 00:09:29.527\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.819 --\u003e 00:09:32.697\r\nYou know there was evidence that\r\nConway falsely implicated Bullock\r\n\r\n00:09:32.781 --\u003e 00:09:33.865\r\nat the graft inquest.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.240 --\u003e 00:09:36.201\r\nBut you have no\r\nproof Conway lied.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.826 --\u003e 00:09:39.412\r\nLook, Harvey Bullock\r\nis hard to work with,\r\n\r\n00:09:39.496 --\u003e 00:09:40.789\r\neven harder to like.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.247 --\u003e 00:09:42.707\r\nBut he's a good cop, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.832 --\u003e 00:09:43.833\r\nHe's clean.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.917 --\u003e 00:09:44.918\r\nMONTOYA: Commissioner?\r\n\r\n00:09:46.503 --\u003e 00:09:48.338\r\n- Something?\r\n- Not a trace.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.713 --\u003e 00:09:49.714\r\nAll right.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.923 --\u003e 00:09:51.049\r\nPull them back in.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.674 --\u003e 00:09:53.009\r\nWe'll have to assume the worst.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.594 --\u003e 00:09:55.762\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:09:56.930 --\u003e 00:09:58.306\r\nFor once, my friend,\r\n\r\n00:09:58.723 --\u003e 00:10:00.475\r\nI hope your instincts are wrong.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.288 --\u003e 00:10:24.541\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- Joey the Snail,\r\n\r\n00:10:24.624 --\u003e 00:10:28.128\r\nbrought in last night on a\r\n605, right?\r\n\r\n00:10:28.253 --\u003e 00:10:29.546\r\nLet me see him.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.921 --\u003e 00:10:31.131\r\nBullock, that you?\r\n\r\n00:10:31.422 --\u003e 00:10:33.466\r\nYeah. Now, let me see him.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.925 --\u003e 00:10:36.010\r\nI need to check\r\nyour authorization.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.100 --\u003e 00:10:43.101\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:55.321 --\u003e 00:10:57.615\r\nRise and shine, Joey.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.117 --\u003e 00:11:00.535\r\n(SHUDDERS) Who's there?\r\n\r\n00:11:00.702 --\u003e 00:11:03.288\r\nYour worst nightmare.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.247 --\u003e 00:11:06.416\r\nNo! Keep away from me!\r\n\r\n00:11:06.833 --\u003e 00:11:08.168\r\n(CELL DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.002 --\u003e 00:11:10.336\r\n(BODY THUDS)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.760 --\u003e 00:11:20.763\r\n- (POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n- (BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:26.978 --\u003e 00:11:29.314\r\n- (CAR DOOR OPENS)\r\n- (CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:11:37.947 --\u003e 00:11:39.240\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.833 --\u003e 00:11:50.043\r\nALFRED: Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.545 --\u003e 00:11:56.174\r\nStill intent on that scale,\r\nor what-have-you, I see.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.758 --\u003e 00:11:57.842\r\nBelieve it or not,\r\n\r\n00:11:57.926 --\u003e 00:11:59.928\r\nthe cellular structure is human,\r\n\r\n00:12:00.386 --\u003e 00:12:02.472\r\nbut the texture\r\nof it is almost...\r\n\r\n00:12:03.014 --\u003e 00:12:04.098\r\nReptilian.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.724 --\u003e 00:12:06.267\r\nHmm. Do tell.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.517 --\u003e 00:12:09.354\r\nBullock might not be the\r\nprimary suspect after all.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.021 --\u003e 00:12:11.981\r\nIn any event,\r\nI've made your favorite,\r\n\r\n00:12:12.065 --\u003e 00:12:13.316\r\nFrench onion soup.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.858 --\u003e 00:12:16.486\r\nAnd, when you let it\r\nget cold this time,\r\n\r\n00:12:16.611 --\u003e 00:12:19.781\r\nnote that it's in a\r\nmicrowavable crock.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.365 --\u003e 00:12:21.366\r\nCrock?\r\n\r\n00:12:22.408 --\u003e 00:12:24.661\r\nAlfred, you're beautiful!\r\n\r\n00:12:27.372 --\u003e 00:12:30.667\r\nImagine if I'd gotten around\r\nto telling him about the salad.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.126 --\u003e 00:12:34.671\r\n\u003ci\u003eTOUR GUIDE: And,\r\nas you can see by this re-creation of\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:34.754 --\u003e 00:12:37.006\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe crocodile's natural habitat,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:37.715 --\u003e 00:12:41.094\r\n\u003ci\u003ecrocodiles make their\r\nlairs in underwater caves.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:41.344 --\u003e 00:12:42.595\r\nOf course!\r\n\r\n00:13:21.426 --\u003e 00:13:22.635\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:13:23.469 --\u003e 00:13:24.971\r\nGet us out of here!\r\n\r\n00:13:27.640 --\u003e 00:13:28.850\r\n(SHUSHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:30.685 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\nNo telling what he'll do.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.072 --\u003e 00:13:46.284\r\nTerrific. Just what I need now.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.492 --\u003e 00:13:48.661\r\nThe freak job in the cape.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.786 --\u003e 00:13:50.830\r\nYou're no prize yourself.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.290 --\u003e 00:13:53.708\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:00.298 --\u003e 00:14:02.300\r\nWhat can I tell you?\r\n\r\n00:14:02.759 --\u003e 00:14:05.678\r\nBeing a reptile\r\nman ain't pretty,\r\n\r\n00:14:06.054 --\u003e 00:14:08.639\r\nbut it's got its upside.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.931 --\u003e 00:14:12.518\r\nLike having the strength of a\r\ncrocodile, for instance.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.897 --\u003e 00:14:18.733\r\nBut I guess you've\r\nlearned that by now, huh?\r\n\r\n00:14:18.858 --\u003e 00:14:20.318\r\nThe hard way.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.373 --\u003e 00:14:36.459\r\nYou know,\r\nthey used to call \"Killer Croc,\"\r\n\r\n00:14:36.584 --\u003e 00:14:39.796\r\nthe meanest dude in the\r\nWrestling Federation.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.171 --\u003e 00:14:44.008\r\nNow, they'll call him the\r\nguy who iced the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.676 --\u003e 00:14:47.053\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:52.433 --\u003e 00:14:53.935\r\nDon't hold your breath.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.602 --\u003e 00:14:55.937\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:23.506 --\u003e 00:15:24.632\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:40.731 --\u003e 00:15:44.235\r\nYou've been rooted to that spot\r\nfor over an hour, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:15:44.527 --\u003e 00:15:46.967\r\nIt's taken me that long to search\r\nthrough all these newspapers\r\n\r\n00:15:47.071 --\u003e 00:15:48.072\r\non microfiche.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.782 --\u003e 00:15:50.783\r\nHere.\r\n\r\n00:15:50.867 --\u003e 00:15:54.036\r\n\u003ci\u003eFrom the Miami Times\r\nHerald, four\u003c/i\u003e years \u003ci\u003eago.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:54.245 --\u003e 00:15:55.246\r\nSee?\r\n\r\n00:15:55.329 --\u003e 00:15:57.999\r\nHe started out a carnival\r\nsideshow attraction,\r\n\r\n00:15:58.249 --\u003e 00:15:59.917\r\nthen became a pro-wrestler.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.460 --\u003e 00:16:03.087\r\nTwo years later,\r\nCroc had moved to Gotham City\r\n\r\n00:16:03.212 --\u003e 00:16:04.505\r\nand turned to crime.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.797 --\u003e 00:16:06.716\r\nHe used to be\r\nstrictly penny-ante.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.966 --\u003e 00:16:08.593\r\nUntil now,\r\nI'd never heard of him.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.093 --\u003e 00:16:11.637\r\nBut, according to this,\r\nBullock busted him\r\n\r\n00:16:11.721 --\u003e 00:16:14.474\r\nbased on the testimony from\r\nConway and Joey the Snail.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.640 --\u003e 00:16:16.309\r\nThen Croc has escaped.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.978 --\u003e 00:16:21.606\r\nAnd now, it's payback time.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.815 --\u003e 00:16:24.400\r\nYou have Conway and the Snail.\r\n\r\n00:16:24.484 --\u003e 00:16:26.235\r\nThey can clear\r\nDetective Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.903 --\u003e 00:16:29.572\r\nTrue,\r\nbut that won't get us Croc.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.864 --\u003e 00:16:32.575\r\nHe won't return to his lair,\r\nnow that I know where it is.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.075 --\u003e 00:16:35.453\r\nI'll have to make\r\nhim come to us.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.506 --\u003e 00:16:48.758\r\n(REPORTERS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:17:04.607 --\u003e 00:17:05.816\r\n(ENGINE STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:09.111 --\u003e 00:17:11.197\r\n- Drive!\r\n- Croc!\r\n\r\n00:17:11.447 --\u003e 00:17:13.533\r\n- How did you...\r\n- Escape? Simple.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.617 --\u003e 00:17:17.203\r\nThe guards don't think\r\nabout the sewers.\r\n\r\n00:17:17.995 --\u003e 00:17:20.081\r\nNo one does, except me.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.206 --\u003e 00:17:22.833\r\nIt was you who set me\r\nup for Spider and Joey.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.251 --\u003e 00:17:24.377\r\nYou got it.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.460 --\u003e 00:17:28.673\r\nI wanted you to sweat it out in\r\na cell for a while, like I did.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.881 --\u003e 00:17:32.301\r\nTo know what it feels\r\nlike, the way I do.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.885 --\u003e 00:17:34.804\r\nHuh? You?\r\n\r\n00:17:35.388 --\u003e 00:17:37.068\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n- (TRUCK HORN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.848 --\u003e 00:17:39.350\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:48.109 --\u003e 00:17:49.527\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:57.868 --\u003e 00:17:59.245\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.893 --\u003e 00:18:24.228\r\nGive it up, Croc.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.312 --\u003e 00:18:25.813\r\nI know everything now.\r\n\r\n00:18:26.480 --\u003e 00:18:28.899\r\nYou planted that toothpick on the\r\ndock, didn't you?\r\n\r\n00:18:29.233 --\u003e 00:18:31.569\r\nAnd you impersonated\r\nBullock at the jail.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.990 --\u003e 00:18:36.991\r\nKILLER CROC: Yeah,\r\n\r\n00:18:37.074 --\u003e 00:18:40.328\r\nand it would've gone down\r\nsmooth if you hadn't butted in.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.453 --\u003e 00:18:42.413\r\nBut, hey, I'm adaptable.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.747 --\u003e 00:18:44.874\r\nWhen you grow up\r\nlooking like I do,\r\n\r\n00:18:44.999 --\u003e 00:18:47.418\r\nyou gotta learn to\r\ngo with the flow.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.543 --\u003e 00:18:50.004\r\nI'll just take\r\ncare of you first,\r\n\r\n00:18:50.087 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nthen Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.050 --\u003e 00:18:55.051\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:59.180 --\u003e 00:19:01.849\r\nSee, this ain't no Batcave.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.141 --\u003e 00:19:04.268\r\nYou're on my turf now.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.942 --\u003e 00:19:13.277\r\n(KILLER CROC GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:22.078 --\u003e 00:19:23.079\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.788 --\u003e 00:19:24.789\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.062 --\u003e 00:19:49.146\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:06.414 --\u003e 00:20:07.748\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:09.250 --\u003e 00:20:10.710\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:20:18.134 --\u003e 00:20:19.135\r\nCroc!\r\n\r\n00:20:42.783 --\u003e 00:20:43.784\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:20:49.373 --\u003e 00:20:51.167\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:21:04.805 --\u003e 00:21:05.806\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\n00:21:06.182 --\u003e 00:21:08.517\r\nWhy'd you stick your neck\r\nout like that to help me?\r\n\r\n00:21:08.642 --\u003e 00:21:10.895\r\nBecause I thought\r\nyou were guilty too\r\n\r\n00:21:11.228 --\u003e 00:21:12.396\r\nand I was wrong.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.314 --\u003e 00:21:15.524\r\nWe may have different\r\nways of enforcing the law,\r\n\r\n00:21:15.900 --\u003e 00:21:17.443\r\nbut we both believe in it.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.818 --\u003e 00:21:20.279\r\nEh. Go on.\r\nI'll take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.493 --\u003e 00:21:26.994\r\nNot a bad piece of work.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.002 --\u003e 00:21:36.295\r\nTell me, Detective Bullock,\r\n\r\n00:21:36.420 --\u003e 00:21:39.340\r\nhow does it feel to be formally\r\ncleared of all charges,\r\n\r\n00:21:39.423 --\u003e 00:21:41.967\r\nnow that Killer Croc,\r\nMorgan, has been arrested?\r\n\r\n00:21:42.092 --\u003e 00:21:45.888\r\n\u003ci\u003eI just want all the scumbuckets\r\nand dirtbags in this town\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:46.013 --\u003e 00:21:47.598\r\n\u003ci\u003eto know they'd better lay low,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:47.681 --\u003e 00:21:50.810\r\n\u003ci\u003ebecause Bullock's back\r\nand ready to kick butt!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:57.525 --\u003e 00:21:59.527\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:24.426 --\u003e 00:22:25.427\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E22 - Prophecy of Doom (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.964 --\u003e 00:00:07.382\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:38.682 --\u003e 00:01:45.564\r\n(PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:10.839 --\u003e 00:02:17.387\r\n(TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:02:24.853 --\u003e 00:02:31.401\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:42.264 --\u003e 00:03:43.515\r\nYou know me, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.598 --\u003e 00:03:45.684\r\nStaid banker,\r\nold conservative stock.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.767 --\u003e 00:03:48.103\r\nI'm the last person\r\nto act impulsively.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.186 --\u003e 00:03:50.605\r\nBut I'm telling you,\r\nthis fellow is a revelation.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.022 --\u003e 00:03:52.399\r\nYou should read this.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.566 --\u003e 00:03:55.652\r\nDad, you're not gonna\r\nproselytize Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.819 --\u003e 00:03:57.654\r\nNow you hush, Lisa.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.946 --\u003e 00:04:00.282\r\nWe're raising a\r\ngeneration of cynics.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.449 --\u003e 00:04:03.785\r\nBRUCE: \"Nostromos.\" Yes,\r\nI've read about him in the Star Enquirer.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.869 --\u003e 00:04:07.205\r\nUh, Alfred likes to pick\r\nup a copy now and then.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.330 --\u003e 00:04:09.458\r\nThat man saved my life.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.833 --\u003e 00:04:12.377\r\nHe warned me not to go\r\non the gambling cruise.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.502 --\u003e 00:04:15.088\r\nTwo days out to\r\nsea, the ship sank.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.255 --\u003e 00:04:16.590\r\nA coincidence.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.882 --\u003e 00:04:18.925\r\nWhat about the cave-in\r\nat the Zanza mines?\r\n\r\n00:04:19.050 --\u003e 00:04:21.428\r\nOr the fires at the\r\nKarobi oil field?\r\n\r\n00:04:21.678 --\u003e 00:04:23.638\r\nHis predictions\r\nsaved me a fortune.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.014 --\u003e 00:04:25.474\r\nMake a heck of a stockbroker.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.599 --\u003e 00:04:29.436\r\nTomorrow I'm hosting a\r\nparty in Nostromos' honor.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.603 --\u003e 00:04:31.897\r\nI want you to be there\r\nto see for yourself.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.272 --\u003e 00:04:33.273\r\nSounds great.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.356 --\u003e 00:04:35.609\r\nBut I'll have to check\r\nmy horoscope to be sure.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.658 --\u003e 00:04:45.678\r\nBRUCE: You don't believe\r\nin this guy at all, do you?\r\n\r\n00:04:45.702 --\u003e 00:04:49.289\r\nCall me crazy, but sometimes I\r\nthink his predictions come true\r\n\r\n00:04:49.372 --\u003e 00:04:50.832\r\nbecause he makes them happen.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.501 --\u003e 00:04:56.171\r\nOnly thing I do know is these days,\r\nmy father won't make a move without him.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.797 --\u003e 00:04:59.174\r\nDaddy's even part of\r\na secret brotherhood.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.591 --\u003e 00:05:01.092\r\nSecret brotherhood?\r\n\r\n00:05:01.426 --\u003e 00:05:03.595\r\nHe won't even tell his own\r\nfamily what it's about,\r\n\r\n00:05:04.095 --\u003e 00:05:07.974\r\nthanks to Mr. All-Wise,\r\nAll-Wonderful Nostromos.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.692 --\u003e 00:05:18.693\r\nPeace to all.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.027 --\u003e 00:05:20.487\r\nBrothers and sisters,\r\n\r\n00:05:20.654 --\u003e 00:05:23.114\r\nthe negative plane is\r\naligned with the positive,\r\n\r\n00:05:23.240 --\u003e 00:05:25.534\r\nbringing forth astral harmony.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.659 --\u003e 00:05:26.660\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.080\r\nThe vibrations are\r\nright for prophecy.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.580 --\u003e 00:05:32.123\r\nOh. Okay.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.541 --\u003e 00:05:35.252\r\nThat which you seek\r\nand cannot find,\r\n\r\n00:05:35.377 --\u003e 00:05:36.378\r\nis the seeker.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.128 --\u003e 00:05:40.215\r\nYou are merely the eye\r\ntrying to view itself.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.966 --\u003e 00:05:42.717\r\nThis is awfully deep.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.801 --\u003e 00:05:43.844\r\n(SHUSHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:44.970 --\u003e 00:05:47.722\r\nWe are but radios for\r\nthe cosmic transmitter.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.181 --\u003e 00:05:49.850\r\nTune your receivers.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.975 --\u003e 00:05:51.852\r\nHear the inner voice.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.185 --\u003e 00:05:53.812\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:53.895 --\u003e 00:05:54.938\r\n(ALL TALKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:55.021 --\u003e 00:05:56.022\r\nWOMAN: What is going on?\r\n\r\n00:05:56.147 --\u003e 00:05:58.567\r\nBrother Ethan,\r\nthe inner voice speaks.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.692 --\u003e 00:06:00.402\r\nSomeone here is in grave danger.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.485 --\u003e 00:06:02.404\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:06:09.703 --\u003e 00:06:12.581\r\nThe messenger of\r\ndeath is searching,\r\n\r\n00:06:13.248 --\u003e 00:06:15.083\r\ncrying out for...\r\n\r\n00:06:16.501 --\u003e 00:06:17.669\r\nYOU!\r\n\r\n00:06:21.923 --\u003e 00:06:23.383\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.466 --\u003e 00:06:26.761\r\n(CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.560 --\u003e 00:06:37.355\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:39.649 --\u003e 00:06:41.610\r\nBut, how did the glass\r\nbreak, sir?\r\n\r\n00:06:42.694 --\u003e 00:06:45.697\r\nPsychic vibrations, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.489 --\u003e 00:06:49.034\r\nThough I'd bet on a\r\nhigh-frequency sonic device.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.370 --\u003e 00:06:53.955\r\nBut I have some\r\ntricks of my own.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.497 --\u003e 00:06:57.459\r\nI lifted Nostromos'\r\nfingerprints at the party.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.168 --\u003e 00:07:00.837\r\nThere he is. Alias Carl Fowler.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.671 --\u003e 00:07:03.048\r\nProfessional actor.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.173 --\u003e 00:07:04.633\r\nArrested for petty larceny.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.384 --\u003e 00:07:08.386\r\nOtherwise, no criminal record.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.016 --\u003e 00:07:14.225\r\nThat's his partner.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.517 --\u003e 00:07:16.645\r\nLucas. Special-effects man.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.020 --\u003e 00:07:18.313\r\nArrested for fraud.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.647 --\u003e 00:07:19.648\r\nNever convicted.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.065 --\u003e 00:07:22.233\r\nSo, they were both\r\nin show business.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.442 --\u003e 00:07:23.443\r\nStill are.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.777 --\u003e 00:07:26.488\r\nI just wish I knew where\r\nthis act was going.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.048 --\u003e 00:07:46.049\r\nHi, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.341 --\u003e 00:07:48.635\r\nI hear your personal elevator\r\nis working great now.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.177 --\u003e 00:07:50.720\r\nThe repair guy was just out.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.137 --\u003e 00:07:53.306\r\nReally? I didn't know\r\nthere was anything wrong.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.071 --\u003e 00:08:09.906\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.536 --\u003e 00:09:00.498\r\n(ELECTRICAL BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:09:15.513 --\u003e 00:09:17.390\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.190 --\u003e 00:09:26.441\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.737 --\u003e 00:09:31.988\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:55.762 --\u003e 00:09:58.723\r\nNo one could have predicted\r\nBatman would spot me.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.932 --\u003e 00:10:00.767\r\nNot even the great Nostromos.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.851 --\u003e 00:10:04.771\r\nBesides,\r\nhow do you know Wayne survived?\r\n\r\n00:10:05.146 --\u003e 00:10:06.856\r\nThe news said he\r\ngot off the elevator\r\n\r\n00:10:06.981 --\u003e 00:10:09.692\r\nright before it fell,\r\nyou pathetic amateur.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.068 --\u003e 00:10:13.029\r\nWell, you didn't predict he would\r\ndie, exactly.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.363 --\u003e 00:10:16.950\r\nFool! Can't you see how his death\r\nwould have affected the Brotherhood?\r\n\r\n00:10:17.325 --\u003e 00:10:19.244\r\nHow vulnerable they\r\nwould have felt?\r\n\r\n00:10:19.702 --\u003e 00:10:22.247\r\nWe could have finally hit\r\nthem for all they're worth!\r\n\r\n00:10:22.330 --\u003e 00:10:23.373\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:27.127\r\nPeace to all.\r\n\r\n00:10:27.794 --\u003e 00:10:31.297\r\nNostromos, I must see you at once.\r\nIt's about Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.965 --\u003e 00:10:33.049\r\nBruce Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:10:33.133 --\u003e 00:10:35.802\r\nMmm-hmm. A miracle has happened.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.927 --\u003e 00:10:37.637\r\nBruce has seen the light.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.931 --\u003e 00:10:43.476\r\nIt wasn't until that moment,\r\nwhen I came so close to death,\r\n\r\n00:10:43.935 --\u003e 00:10:46.980\r\nthat I realized you really\r\ndid have a divine connection.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.564 --\u003e 00:10:49.524\r\nTo think I ridiculed you.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.983 --\u003e 00:10:51.943\r\nCan you ever forgive me?\r\n\r\n00:10:52.902 --\u003e 00:10:54.154\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.279 --\u003e 00:10:57.157\r\nI rejoice in your\r\nsoaring consciousness.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.907 --\u003e 00:10:59.784\r\nNostromos, I was thinking,\r\n\r\n00:10:59.868 --\u003e 00:11:03.121\r\na man of Bruce's\r\nstanding, his influence,\r\n\r\n00:11:03.204 --\u003e 00:11:05.832\r\nshould he not be considered\r\nfor the Brotherhood?\r\n\r\n00:11:06.833 --\u003e 00:11:09.085\r\nYes. It's preordained.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.753 --\u003e 00:11:13.173\r\nWelcome, Brother Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.548 --\u003e 00:11:15.300\r\nLISA: No, not Bruce!\r\n\r\n00:11:16.217 --\u003e 00:11:17.385\r\nLisa, you\r\n\r\n00:11:18.094 --\u003e 00:11:19.387\r\ndon't understand.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.470 --\u003e 00:11:21.764\r\nOh, I understand, all right.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.848 --\u003e 00:11:23.266\r\nYou're like all the rest,\r\n\r\n00:11:23.349 --\u003e 00:11:26.769\r\nsuckered in by this\r\nmoney-grubbing, bogus creep.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.936 --\u003e 00:11:28.146\r\nLisa!\r\n\r\n00:11:28.813 --\u003e 00:11:31.566\r\nYou know what my inner voice tells\r\nme, Nostromos?\r\n\r\n00:11:31.733 --\u003e 00:11:33.902\r\nYou've ripped off\r\nyour last victim.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.156 --\u003e 00:11:39.866\r\nI'm so sorry. I...\r\n\r\n00:11:39.949 --\u003e 00:11:41.117\r\nDo not apologize.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.409 --\u003e 00:11:42.619\r\nShe will believe.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.869 --\u003e 00:11:44.495\r\nThey will all believe,\r\n\r\n00:11:44.746 --\u003e 00:11:46.414\r\nafter the Great Fall.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.500 --\u003e 00:11:51.753\r\nETHAN: You may have joined\r\nus just in time, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.295 --\u003e 00:11:54.672\r\nFor months Nostromos has\r\nbeen warning the Brotherhood\r\n\r\n00:11:54.797 --\u003e 00:11:56.674\r\nof an economic\r\ncollapse in the West.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.342 --\u003e 00:11:58.343\r\n\"The Great Fall\"?\r\n\r\n00:11:58.801 --\u003e 00:11:59.844\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.261 --\u003e 00:12:01.721\r\nBut, at Nostromos' direction,\r\n\r\n00:12:01.804 --\u003e 00:12:04.807\r\nwe've set up a superfund\r\nto protect ourselves.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.933 --\u003e 00:12:08.811\r\nAfter the fall, we can use it\r\nnot only to rebuild fortunes,\r\n\r\n00:12:09.270 --\u003e 00:12:11.147\r\nbut society as well.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.356 --\u003e 00:12:13.691\r\nAnd I take it that Nostromos\r\ncontrols this money.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.942 --\u003e 00:12:17.362\r\nOh, no, he can't touch it\r\nwithout my written approval.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.779 --\u003e 00:12:20.782\r\nNostromos insisted\r\neverything be aboveboard.\r\n\r\n00:12:21.199 --\u003e 00:12:22.367\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.125 --\u003e 00:12:34.420\r\nNOSTROMOS: And though,\r\ntonight we bask in the radiance\r\n\r\n00:12:34.545 --\u003e 00:12:36.923\r\nof Brother Bruce's conversion,\r\n\r\n00:12:37.048 --\u003e 00:12:39.300\r\nit grieves me to\r\nburden your spirits\r\n\r\n00:12:39.425 --\u003e 00:12:40.969\r\nwith solemn news as well.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.594 --\u003e 00:12:44.639\r\nThe Great Fall is at hand.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.057 --\u003e 00:12:47.267\r\nThe Great Fall.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.350 --\u003e 00:12:48.559\r\n(ALL MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:13:08.162 --\u003e 00:13:12.375\r\n\u003ci\u003eNOSTROMOS: The omens rise and\r\nconverge with every passing moment.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:12.500 --\u003e 00:13:14.043\r\n\u003ci\u003eYes, my brethren,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:14.168 --\u003e 00:13:16.045\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe inner voice speaks.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:16.587 --\u003e 00:13:19.340\r\nI now see a dawn of destruction.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.051 --\u003e 00:13:23.052\r\nRiots!\r\n\r\n00:13:23.177 --\u003e 00:13:24.178\r\nPillaging!\r\n\r\n00:13:24.304 --\u003e 00:13:25.430\r\nCarnage!\r\n\r\n00:13:25.555 --\u003e 00:13:28.057\r\nA society out of control!\r\n\r\n00:13:29.434 --\u003e 00:13:31.602\r\nOh, the torment!\r\n\r\n00:13:31.894 --\u003e 00:13:33.396\r\nThe suffering!\r\n\r\n00:13:33.771 --\u003e 00:13:35.231\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:13:35.315 --\u003e 00:13:37.650\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:42.739 --\u003e 00:13:45.158\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe vision becomes clear.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:47.827 --\u003e 00:13:50.079\r\nBrothers, beware!\r\n\r\n00:13:50.788 --\u003e 00:13:51.956\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:13:55.877 --\u003e 00:13:58.171\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:13:59.797 --\u003e 00:14:01.090\r\nI am fine.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.591 --\u003e 00:14:06.846\r\nBrethren, you must transfer all you can\r\nto the Brotherhood's fund by tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.971 --\u003e 00:14:09.223\r\nThe stars are in their\r\nproper confluence.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.307 --\u003e 00:14:11.267\r\nSigns and portents abound.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.434 --\u003e 00:14:14.896\r\nAs prophets of old foretold\r\ncataclysmic changes,\r\n\r\n00:14:15.021 --\u003e 00:14:18.191\r\nso now, I predict a\r\nmassive social upheaval!\r\n\r\n00:14:18.358 --\u003e 00:14:20.109\r\nThis is the end\r\nof the old order.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.193 --\u003e 00:14:22.111\r\nAnarchy and chaos will abound.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.195 --\u003e 00:14:24.947\r\nThe Great Fall has begun.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.746 --\u003e 00:14:35.041\r\nYou gave them $10 million, sir?\r\n\r\n00:14:35.416 --\u003e 00:14:38.419\r\nAnd to think,\r\nI was fretting over the electric bill.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.337 --\u003e 00:14:41.547\r\nI had to keep up\r\nappearances, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.798 --\u003e 00:14:44.342\r\nThere must be over $300\r\nmillion in that fund.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.467 --\u003e 00:14:46.010\r\nMy Word!\r\n\r\n00:14:46.386 --\u003e 00:14:50.681\r\nWell, at least Nostromos can't touch\r\nit without Mr. Clark's authorization.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.807 --\u003e 00:14:52.058\r\nFor now.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.183 --\u003e 00:14:55.019\r\nBut I don't need to be psychic\r\nto predict that Ethan Clark\r\n\r\n00:14:55.103 --\u003e 00:14:57.647\r\nis about to undergo\r\na spiritual crisis.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.214 --\u003e 00:15:24.215\r\nWell, Lucas,\r\n\r\n00:15:24.424 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\nour benevolent brothers\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.469\r\ntransferred another 63\r\nmillion this morning.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.678 --\u003e 00:15:32.723\r\nI predict, you and I are about\r\nto become as rich as pigs.\r\n\r\n00:15:32.807 --\u003e 00:15:34.934\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:35.017 --\u003e 00:15:36.203\r\n- ETHAN: Nostromos!\r\n- (KNOCKING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:15:36.227 --\u003e 00:15:37.270\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:15:42.066 --\u003e 00:15:43.443\r\nOut. Out!\r\n\r\n00:15:44.402 --\u003e 00:15:45.903\r\nETHAN: Nostromos.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.029 --\u003e 00:15:48.364\r\nI got your message.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.489 --\u003e 00:15:51.033\r\nI'd have been here sooner,\r\nbut I've been trying to locate Lisa.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.117 --\u003e 00:15:52.660\r\nShe didn't come home last night.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.785 --\u003e 00:15:55.746\r\nThe inner voice\r\nassures me she is fine.\r\n\r\n00:15:56.038 --\u003e 00:15:57.165\r\nDo you know where she is?\r\n\r\n00:15:57.540 --\u003e 00:16:00.793\r\nDo not worry.\r\nI see you joining her soon.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.044 --\u003e 00:16:04.505\r\nRight now,\r\nwe have urgent business to discuss.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.881 --\u003e 00:16:06.299\r\nThe voice has warned\r\n\r\n00:16:06.382 --\u003e 00:16:08.676\r\nthat the Brotherhood's\r\nfund is in jeopardy.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.093 --\u003e 00:16:10.219\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:16:10.386 --\u003e 00:16:13.181\r\nWe must convert it into\r\ngold bullion at once.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.389 --\u003e 00:16:15.766\r\nI've prepared the papers\r\nfor your signature.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.726 --\u003e 00:16:21.439\r\nBut, Nostromos, I can't possibly sign\r\nuntil I've notified the brothers.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.564 --\u003e 00:16:22.940\r\nThere's no time!\r\n\r\n00:16:23.316 --\u003e 00:16:25.026\r\nBut, they must be informed.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.109 --\u003e 00:16:26.777\r\nIt's our obligation.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.069 --\u003e 00:16:29.447\r\nPerhaps the stars\r\ncan persuade you.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.906 --\u003e 00:16:32.200\r\nI see a bad moon rising.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.410 --\u003e 00:16:35.536\r\nLisa!\r\n\r\n00:16:35.620 --\u003e 00:16:38.206\r\n(MUFFLED SPEAKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.289 --\u003e 00:16:39.457\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:39.540 --\u003e 00:16:40.833\r\nSign!\r\n\r\n00:16:43.044 --\u003e 00:16:46.923\r\nNostromos, what is this?\r\nI don't understand.\r\n\r\n00:16:48.049 --\u003e 00:16:50.259\r\nSign! Or she pays.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.635 --\u003e 00:16:51.844\r\nWhy would you do this?\r\n\r\n00:16:51.928 --\u003e 00:16:54.639\r\nI believed in you. You saved me.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.764 --\u003e 00:16:55.932\r\nPlease, Nostro...\r\n\r\n00:16:56.015 --\u003e 00:16:57.558\r\n(MUFFLED TALK)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.642 --\u003e 00:17:00.102\r\nI have one last prediction for\r\nyou, Ethan.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.394 --\u003e 00:17:02.230\r\nThe end will be swift.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.563 --\u003e 00:17:05.608\r\nBrother Lucas has set enough\r\nexplosives in this place\r\n\r\n00:17:05.733 --\u003e 00:17:07.860\r\nto create a supernova.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.236 --\u003e 00:17:10.530\r\nI suggest you make\r\nyour peace quickly.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.239 --\u003e 00:17:16.244\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:16.327 --\u003e 00:17:17.745\r\nOoh!\r\n\r\n00:17:20.039 --\u003e 00:17:21.499\r\nThe control room!\r\n\r\n00:17:28.005 --\u003e 00:17:29.215\r\nUp there.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.105 --\u003e 00:17:45.523\r\nYou go that way.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.826 --\u003e 00:17:57.868\r\n(SHOUTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.204 --\u003e 00:18:02.164\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:02.540 --\u003e 00:18:05.126\r\nBATMAN: Your turn\r\nto see the light.\r\n\r\n00:18:05.501 --\u003e 00:18:06.502\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:18:18.180 --\u003e 00:18:19.557\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:31.360 --\u003e 00:18:34.447\r\n(MACHINE POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:18:48.085 --\u003e 00:18:49.962\r\n(MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:07.229 --\u003e 00:19:09.482\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:17.907 --\u003e 00:19:19.533\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:27.708 --\u003e 00:19:30.211\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:36.217 --\u003e 00:19:37.593\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:37.677 --\u003e 00:19:40.805\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.435 --\u003e 00:19:49.271\r\nYou're about to fall out of\r\norbit, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.109 --\u003e 00:19:55.361\r\n(LUCAS GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:57.738 --\u003e 00:19:58.906\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.963 --\u003e 00:20:15.339\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.353 --\u003e 00:20:34.358\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:38.362 --\u003e 00:20:41.866\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.119 --\u003e 00:20:47.037\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:23.908 --\u003e 00:21:27.328\r\n(SIGHS) I can't believe\r\nI was so gullible.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.453 --\u003e 00:21:30.706\r\nBut that's what I get for\r\nputting my faith in greed.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.501 --\u003e 00:21:35.336\r\nYou weren't the only one, Daddy.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.878 --\u003e 00:21:37.421\r\nGuilty as charged.\r\n\r\n00:21:37.588 --\u003e 00:21:39.048\r\nAs the Bard once said,\r\n\r\n00:21:39.381 --\u003e 00:21:43.260\r\n\"The fault lies not in the\r\nstars, but in ourselves.\"\r\n\r\n00:21:53.896 --\u003e 00:21:55.898\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:19.547 --\u003e 00:22:20.548\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E23 - Forgotten (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.631 --\u003e 00:00:07.132\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.180 --\u003e 00:01:39.308\r\nMAN: Your help means a lot to\r\nus, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:01:39.391 --\u003e 00:01:41.893\r\nBRUCE: And what you do\r\nmeans a lot to this city.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.269 --\u003e 00:01:43.687\r\nI wish we could do more.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.023 --\u003e 00:01:48.317\r\nLately,\r\nthings haven't been going well.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.151 --\u003e 00:01:50.777\r\nThanks. What do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:01:51.320 --\u003e 00:01:54.740\r\nI can't prove it, but I'm\r\npositive, people are disappearing.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.823 --\u003e 00:01:58.493\r\nTransients, regulars,\r\nold faces I miss seeing.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.577 --\u003e 00:02:02.164\r\nThen a month ago, a volunteer,\r\nDan Riley, disappeared.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.247 --\u003e 00:02:04.333\r\nI'm telling you,\r\nsomething's very wrong.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.416 --\u003e 00:02:06.543\r\n- You've talked to the police?\r\n- Of course.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.627 --\u003e 00:02:08.670\r\nBut the police have\r\ntheir hands full.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.754 --\u003e 00:02:11.465\r\nAnd homeless people\r\ndisappearing is not big news.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.384 --\u003e 00:02:16.428\r\n(BATS CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:09.648 --\u003e 00:03:11.358\r\n(BRAKES SHRIEKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:23.078 --\u003e 00:03:24.913\r\n(STEAM WHIZZING)\r\n\r\n00:03:27.207 --\u003e 00:03:29.000\r\n(VEHICLE APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:43.181 --\u003e 00:03:45.434\r\n(CLANGS)\r\n\r\n00:03:47.811 --\u003e 00:03:49.521\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:03:53.024 --\u003e 00:03:55.235\r\nHey, buddy,\r\nyou looking for a job?\r\n\r\n00:03:55.777 --\u003e 00:03:58.405\r\nMaybe. What kind of job?\r\n\r\n00:03:58.488 --\u003e 00:04:02.117\r\nOh, you'll like it.\r\nIt's long-term employment.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.243 --\u003e 00:04:06.329\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:14.421 --\u003e 00:04:15.714\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:18.967 --\u003e 00:04:20.469\r\n(SCREAMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:04:24.556 --\u003e 00:04:26.600\r\n(CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.767 --\u003e 00:04:28.393\r\n(CAT MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.318 --\u003e 00:04:37.861\r\n- (BRUCE GROANS)\r\n- (YOWLS)\r\n\r\n00:04:53.168 --\u003e 00:04:55.295\r\n(SNORING)\r\n\r\n00:04:58.799 --\u003e 00:05:00.008\r\nHey, Riley.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.636 --\u003e 00:05:04.387\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:06.807 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.018 --\u003e 00:05:13.104\r\n(CHAIN CLINKS)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.980 --\u003e 00:05:15.440\r\nOh, boy.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.359 --\u003e 00:05:19.611\r\n- Hey, stranger.\r\n- You okay?\r\n\r\n00:05:20.987 --\u003e 00:05:23.740\r\nI think so. Where am I?\r\n\r\n00:05:24.032 --\u003e 00:05:27.786\r\nWell, opinions differ, but we all agree.\r\nIt ain't Miami.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.495 --\u003e 00:05:31.748\r\nDon't mind him.\r\nEvery chain gang has a comedian.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.040 --\u003e 00:05:34.501\r\nI'm Dan Riley,\r\nand he's Salvo Smith.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.126 --\u003e 00:05:36.670\r\nSo, what's your name, pal?\r\n\r\n00:05:37.754 --\u003e 00:05:40.298\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.299 --\u003e 00:05:42.884\r\n(SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.482 --\u003e 00:05:58.775\r\nWhat is this?\r\n\r\n00:05:59.025 --\u003e 00:06:02.654\r\nIf it's moving, it's a rat.\r\nIf not, it's a cooked rat.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.321 --\u003e 00:06:06.116\r\nWhy aren't these\r\nlowlifes working?\r\n\r\n00:06:06.741 --\u003e 00:06:07.784\r\nThey have to eat, sir.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.911 --\u003e 00:06:12.998\r\nI have to eat.\r\nThey have to work.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.582 --\u003e 00:06:16.793\r\nFrom now on,\r\nthey'll bring me twice the gold ore.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.085 --\u003e 00:06:19.045\r\n- Do you hear me?\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.296 --\u003e 00:06:20.964\r\nWe recruited some new men.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.716 --\u003e 00:06:25.635\r\nYou bums better\r\nstart busting butt\r\n\r\n00:06:25.719 --\u003e 00:06:29.139\r\nor you'll all end up like him.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.266 --\u003e 00:06:32.684\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:34.769 --\u003e 00:06:36.438\r\nNo! Please!\r\n\r\n00:06:36.688 --\u003e 00:06:39.816\r\nI ain't done nothing!\r\nNo! Please!\r\n\r\n00:06:42.611 --\u003e 00:06:43.737\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:06:44.195 --\u003e 00:06:45.405\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:06:47.949 --\u003e 00:06:49.242\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:06:57.125 --\u003e 00:07:02.047\r\nNow get to work,\r\nor you'll all roast.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.392 --\u003e 00:07:15.644\r\nRise and shine.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.144 --\u003e 00:07:17.812\r\nIt's a beautiful...\r\n\r\n00:07:18.730 --\u003e 00:07:19.898\r\nThat's odd.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.148 --\u003e 00:07:23.777\r\nOnly vampires loathe\r\ndaylight more than Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.194 --\u003e 00:07:25.737\r\nI wonder what's keeping him.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.080 --\u003e 00:07:36.623\r\n(SWITCH CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:07:42.879 --\u003e 00:07:45.382\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.470 --\u003e 00:07:53.264\r\n- How you holding up?\r\n- Okay, I guess.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.349 --\u003e 00:07:55.642\r\n(GRUNTS) Remember anything yet?\r\n\r\n00:07:56.893 --\u003e 00:07:58.770\r\nI'm beginning to\r\nwonder if I ever will.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.729 --\u003e 00:08:01.481\r\nHey, YOU Can't give up hope.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.564 --\u003e 00:08:03.650\r\nDown here it's all\r\nwe've got to hang on to.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.150 --\u003e 00:08:07.404\r\nI guess you're right.\r\nSo, what brought you guys here?\r\n\r\n00:08:07.821 --\u003e 00:08:12.492\r\nI was one of Gotham City's unemployed.\r\nNow I got a job. Lucky me.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.659 --\u003e 00:08:15.829\r\nI was a steamfitter at\r\nthe Gotham Navy Yard.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.996 --\u003e 00:08:19.457\r\nTwo nights a week, I did volunteer\r\nwork at the Dock Street Rescue Mission.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.041 --\u003e 00:08:22.836\r\nOne night I was getting into my\r\ncar, and three guys jumped me.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.253 --\u003e 00:08:24.838\r\nI wound up here.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.088 --\u003e 00:08:27.882\r\nMy family must be going\r\nout of their minds.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.592 --\u003e 00:08:31.261\r\nRescue Mission.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.262 --\u003e 00:08:34.014\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.806 --\u003e 00:08:36.182\r\nCave-in!\r\n\r\n00:08:36.349 --\u003e 00:08:38.184\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:50.071 --\u003e 00:08:51.990\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:53.908 --\u003e 00:08:55.535\r\nAh, are you okay?\r\n\r\n00:08:58.621 --\u003e 00:08:59.831\r\nWhere's Salvo?\r\n\r\n00:09:00.040 --\u003e 00:09:02.125\r\nSALVO: I'm over\r\nhere, taking five.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.417 --\u003e 00:09:03.418\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:09:03.626 --\u003e 00:09:05.462\r\nHang on, man. We'll get you out.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.545 --\u003e 00:09:08.631\r\nTake your time.\r\nIt's the first break I've had all day.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.175 --\u003e 00:09:11.760\r\nDoes this sort of\r\nthing happen often?\r\n\r\n00:09:12.385 --\u003e 00:09:13.386\r\nToo often.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.095 --\u003e 00:09:15.972\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:17.265 --\u003e 00:09:20.602\r\nNo, I'm sorry, sir.\r\nMr. Wayne was called out of town.\r\n\r\n00:09:21.019 --\u003e 00:09:23.938\r\nIf you call back on Friday...\r\n\r\n00:09:31.071 --\u003e 00:09:33.323\r\n(SWITCHES CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:38.411 --\u003e 00:09:40.038\r\nThe Studebaker's gone.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.371 --\u003e 00:09:42.332\r\nI'd better activate\r\nthe tracking device.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.584 --\u003e 00:09:47.295\r\n(TICKING) (BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:48.671\r\nThe Bowery.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.756 --\u003e 00:09:51.758\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:01.851 --\u003e 00:10:03.853\r\n(MAN CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:06.940 --\u003e 00:10:10.360\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:10:24.874 --\u003e 00:10:26.584\r\n(wmn WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:50.483 --\u003e 00:10:51.734\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:10:51.901 --\u003e 00:10:53.820\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:55.572 --\u003e 00:10:57.365\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:57.615 --\u003e 00:11:01.077\r\nDock Street Rescue Mission.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.496 --\u003e 00:11:06.624\r\n(MUNCHING AUDIBLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:06.916 --\u003e 00:11:10.378\r\nI've never seen such lazy scum.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.628 --\u003e 00:11:13.631\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:11:15.049 --\u003e 00:11:16.467\r\n(BLOWS RASPBERRY)\r\n\r\n00:11:18.636 --\u003e 00:11:21.389\r\nNow that was real funny.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.307 --\u003e 00:11:23.933\r\nThrow him in the box!\r\n\r\n00:11:26.686 --\u003e 00:11:28.479\r\nYou can't. It'll kill him.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.688 --\u003e 00:11:33.735\r\n(LAUGHS) That's the idea.\r\nNow do it!\r\n\r\n00:11:35.236 --\u003e 00:11:37.363\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:41.409 --\u003e 00:11:43.661\r\nTHUG 1: I got him! Come on!\r\n\r\n00:11:44.329 --\u003e 00:11:46.539\r\n(THUG GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:58.218 --\u003e 00:12:00.470\r\n(THUGS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:12:00.887 --\u003e 00:12:03.765\r\n- (THUMPING)\r\n- (THUGS GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.186 --\u003e 00:12:12.190\r\nWe'll see how they like the oven.\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:12.357 --\u003e 00:12:15.902\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:41.636 --\u003e 00:12:43.471\r\n(TRUCK DOOR CLOSING)\r\n\r\n00:12:46.557 --\u003e 00:12:48.017\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:49.519 --\u003e 00:12:50.770\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:12:56.025 --\u003e 00:12:58.027\r\nRILEY: Hey,\r\nyou really cleaned their clocks.\r\n\r\n00:12:58.778 --\u003e 00:13:00.571\r\nYou did pretty good yourself.\r\n\r\n00:13:01.155 --\u003e 00:13:03.825\r\nWell, maybe you used to\r\nbe some kind of fighter.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.117 --\u003e 00:13:05.785\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.369 --\u003e 00:13:08.663\r\nI just don't know.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.962 --\u003e 00:13:20.717\r\nRILEY: My son,\r\nhe's gonna be six on April 7th.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.467 --\u003e 00:13:24.804\r\nOr seven on April 6. (SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.638 --\u003e 00:13:27.598\r\nOh, what's it matter?\r\nI'll never see him again.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.224 --\u003e 00:13:29.642\r\nHang on, Riley.\r\n\r\n00:13:30.184 --\u003e 00:13:31.436\r\nWe'll make it.\r\n\r\n00:13:31.936 --\u003e 00:13:35.440\r\nRemember what you told me?\r\nYou can't lose hope.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:38.109\r\nI can't take it anymore!\r\n\r\n00:13:39.068 --\u003e 00:13:40.361\r\nI lost my family! My family!\r\n\r\n00:13:40.445 --\u003e 00:13:44.782\r\nMy family! M My family! Amlly!\r\n\r\n00:13:59.339 --\u003e 00:14:00.631\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:12.643 --\u003e 00:14:16.856\r\nRiley, you've got to pull it together.\r\nWe're getting out of here.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.981 --\u003e 00:14:18.232\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:14:18.316 --\u003e 00:14:19.442\r\nYeah, right.\r\n\r\n00:14:19.817 --\u003e 00:14:21.277\r\nYou're the one who's losing it.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.487 --\u003e 00:14:23.654\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:34.582 --\u003e 00:14:35.792\r\n(BLOWS WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:38.336 --\u003e 00:14:40.588\r\n(GROANS) Stop him!\r\n\r\n00:14:41.297 --\u003e 00:14:45.551\r\nStop him,\r\nor you'll all rot in the mines!\r\n\r\n00:14:46.677 --\u003e 00:14:48.096\r\n(BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:50.640\r\nThere he is.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.140 --\u003e 00:14:52.433\r\nWe got him now.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.517 --\u003e 00:14:54.394\r\nHe's gone into Box Canyon.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.727 --\u003e 00:14:56.312\r\nThere's no way out.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.487 --\u003e 00:15:05.696\r\n(DOGS CONTINUE BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.259 --\u003e 00:15:28.094\r\n(SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:38.062 --\u003e 00:15:39.772\r\nTHUG 1: Look! Up there!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.279 --\u003e 00:15:48.322\r\n(ALFRED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:49.198 --\u003e 00:15:50.658\r\n(RAPID BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:56.289 --\u003e 00:15:57.707\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:16:02.587 --\u003e 00:16:04.130\r\nOh! Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:16:12.555 --\u003e 00:16:15.933\r\nThis must be the place.\r\nBring us down.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.100 --\u003e 00:16:17.185\r\nCOMPUTER: Negative.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.268 --\u003e 00:16:20.188\r\nBut Master Bruce is down here.\r\nWe have to land.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.438 --\u003e 00:16:22.648\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Impossible.\r\nArea too confined.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:23.107 --\u003e 00:16:25.610\r\nLand, you bucket of bolts.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.110 --\u003e 00:16:27.320\r\nCOMPUTER: Your funeral.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.528 --\u003e 00:16:29.030\r\nOh, dear.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.113 --\u003e 00:16:30.323\r\n- (ENGINE REVS)\r\n- (SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:34.285 --\u003e 00:16:35.661\r\nALFRED: Get us down!\r\n\r\n00:16:37.371 --\u003e 00:16:39.332\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Caution. Rocks.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:44.837 --\u003e 00:16:46.088\r\n(WHIZZES)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.007 --\u003e 00:16:49.926\r\nSon of a gun.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.720 --\u003e 00:16:53.930\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:03.147 --\u003e 00:17:04.649\r\nCOMPUTER: Watch your step.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.776 --\u003e 00:17:11.822\r\nI... I...\r\nI claim this land for Spain.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.248 --\u003e 00:17:21.666\r\nMaster Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.673 --\u003e 00:17:30.299\r\nBOSS BIGGIS: Hurry\r\nup with that gravy!\r\n\r\n00:17:32.843 --\u003e 00:17:37.431\r\nIf those fools let that prisoner\r\nescape, I'll eat them alive.\r\n\r\n00:17:39.600 --\u003e 00:17:41.269\r\nA bat! A giant bat!\r\n\r\n00:17:41.519 --\u003e 00:17:42.812\r\nHorrible!\r\n\r\n00:17:43.813 --\u003e 00:17:45.731\r\nWhat are you babbling about?\r\n\r\n00:17:45.940 --\u003e 00:17:47.149\r\nWhat bat?\r\n\r\n00:17:47.525 --\u003e 00:17:48.943\r\nRight here.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.527 --\u003e 00:17:50.736\r\nThere it is!\r\n\r\n00:17:52.113 --\u003e 00:17:53.614\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:17:57.076 --\u003e 00:17:58.202\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:59.912 --\u003e 00:18:00.955\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:02.331 --\u003e 00:18:03.749\r\n(GROWLS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e ANGER)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.628 --\u003e 00:18:08.629\r\nShoot him!\r\n\r\n00:18:11.090 --\u003e 00:18:12.425\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:18:13.259 --\u003e 00:18:15.636\r\nAfter him, you fools!\r\n\r\n00:18:19.473 --\u003e 00:18:21.309\r\n\u003ci\u003eBOSS BIGGIS: After him!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:21.976 --\u003e 00:18:26.230\r\n$1,000 to the man\r\nwho bags that bat.\r\n\r\n00:18:33.863 --\u003e 00:18:35.281\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:18:37.158 --\u003e 00:18:38.200\r\nThere he is!\r\n\r\n00:18:38.951 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\nBOSS BIGGIS: Split\r\nup and fan out.\r\n\r\n00:18:55.426 --\u003e 00:18:56.886\r\nHuh? (CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:18:57.261 --\u003e 00:18:58.804\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:19:01.766 --\u003e 00:19:02.808\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:19:07.938 --\u003e 00:19:09.357\r\nKill the lights!\r\n\r\n00:19:10.024 --\u003e 00:19:13.361\r\nWe'll find out if this\r\nbat can see in the dark.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.445 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CLICKING SWITCHES)\r\n\r\n00:19:28.793 --\u003e 00:19:29.960\r\nLook out! (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:34.548 --\u003e 00:19:35.966\r\nI think he went this way.\r\n\r\n00:19:36.717 --\u003e 00:19:38.636\r\nGUARD 1: Pete, where are...\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:39.470 --\u003e 00:19:41.097\r\nGUARD 2: Help!\r\n\r\n00:19:42.390 --\u003e 00:19:44.433\r\nHelp! (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:45.142 --\u003e 00:19:48.354\r\nHodges, Kurt, Howard!\r\nAre you okay?\r\n\r\n00:19:48.646 --\u003e 00:19:50.189\r\nBATMAN: Not exactly.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.484 --\u003e 00:19:54.735\r\nStop him!\r\n\r\n00:20:19.593 --\u003e 00:20:21.595\r\nNo! Leave me alone!\r\n\r\n00:20:22.638 --\u003e 00:20:23.764\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:28.310 --\u003e 00:20:30.146\r\nBATMAN: We've got\r\nto get out of here.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:33.065\r\nStop. We'll be killed.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.524 --\u003e 00:20:35.985\r\nBATMAN: Stop, and we will be.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.778 --\u003e 00:20:39.029\r\n(BOSS BIGGIS GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:43.576 --\u003e 00:20:45.077\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:48.038 --\u003e 00:20:49.123\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.503 --\u003e 00:20:56.213\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:02.928 --\u003e 00:21:05.723\r\nDon't let me drown!\r\n\r\n00:21:08.851 --\u003e 00:21:11.937\r\nWhen you taste the prison\r\nfood, you'll wish I had.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.063 --\u003e 00:21:14.106\r\nRILEY: It's no palace,\r\n\r\n00:21:14.190 --\u003e 00:21:17.030\r\nbut you're welcome to stay at our\r\nplace until you get back on your feet.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.109 --\u003e 00:21:20.613\r\nThanks, Riley. Maybe this time,\r\nwe can find some work that pays.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.863 --\u003e 00:21:22.490\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:21:23.199 --\u003e 00:21:25.659\r\nYou know, pal, it'll be\r\ntight, but you're welcome too.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.910 --\u003e 00:21:27.036\r\nThanks, but I...\r\n\r\n00:21:27.119 --\u003e 00:21:28.913\r\nALFRED: Are we\r\nready, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:21:31.373 --\u003e 00:21:32.917\r\nBOTH: Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:21:33.083 --\u003e 00:21:35.878\r\nBruce Wayne.\r\nWayneTech Enterprises.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.754 --\u003e 00:21:39.548\r\nIf you'd like a job,\r\nI can probably help.\r\n\r\n00:21:41.634 --\u003e 00:21:42.635\r\nHit me, Riley.\r\n\r\n00:21:42.802 --\u003e 00:21:43.886\r\nHit you? Why?\r\n\r\n00:21:44.094 --\u003e 00:21:46.889\r\nMaybe I'll lose my memory and\r\nwake up a millionaire too.\r\n\r\n00:21:57.191 --\u003e 00:21:58.651\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.840 --\u003e 00:22:21.841\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E24 - Mad As A Hatter (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.672 --\u003e 00:00:07.674\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:27.337 --\u003e 00:01:28.547\r\nJERVIS: Oh, dear.\r\n\r\n00:01:28.672 --\u003e 00:01:30.382\r\nSuch table manners.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.095 --\u003e 00:01:37.306\r\nPerhaps I can make you\r\nact a bit more civilized.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.058 --\u003e 00:01:41.768\r\n(DEVICES BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:01:53.905 --\u003e 00:01:56.033\r\n(LAUGHS) Bravo!\r\n\r\n00:01:56.450 --\u003e 00:01:59.077\r\nThey all laughed when I said I'd\r\nfind a way to tap into another\r\n\r\n00:01:59.161 --\u003e 00:02:00.454\r\ncreature's mind.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.746 --\u003e 00:02:03.415\r\nWhy, with this band\r\nand these electrodes,\r\n\r\n00:02:03.624 --\u003e 00:02:05.500\r\nI can control anything.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.959 --\u003e 00:02:06.960\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:02:08.378 --\u003e 00:02:10.172\r\nPsst, Jervis.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.380 --\u003e 00:02:14.885\r\nOh, Alice.\r\n(STUTTERING) What a nice surprise.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.053 --\u003e 00:02:18.680\r\nYeah, yeah. Look busy.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.306 --\u003e 00:02:21.516\r\n\u003ci\u003eDr. Gates, Mr. Wayne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:24.978 --\u003e 00:02:26.855\r\nRight this way.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.278 --\u003e 00:02:36.573\r\nBruce,\r\nyou remember Jervis Tetch.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.908 --\u003e 00:02:40.410\r\n- Hello.\r\n- Of course.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.911 --\u003e 00:02:44.831\r\nI read your proposal on using microchips\r\nto enhance the brain's potential.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.998 --\u003e 00:02:46.208\r\nSounds intriguing.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.375 --\u003e 00:02:50.545\r\nActually, the prototype\r\nisn't quite ready yet.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.754 --\u003e 00:02:54.925\r\nTetch, I think we owe our\r\nfounder and employer, Mr. Wayne,\r\n\r\n00:02:55.092 --\u003e 00:02:57.969\r\na little more than lame excuses.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.720 --\u003e 00:03:01.306\r\n- Sorry.\r\n- That's all right, Dr. Cates.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.390 --\u003e 00:03:03.558\r\nMr. Tetch is a valued\r\nmember of our research team.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.767 --\u003e 00:03:05.686\r\nI'm sure we can\r\nspare him more time.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.061 --\u003e 00:03:07.604\r\nAs you say, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:09.106 --\u003e 00:03:10.565\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.200 --\u003e 00:03:22.244\r\nYou got off easy this\r\ntime, Tetch,\r\n\r\n00:03:22.327 --\u003e 00:03:25.539\r\nbut heads could roll\r\nif you slip up again.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.299 --\u003e 00:03:39.219\r\nShe's always like that\r\nwhen the big boss drops by.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.386 --\u003e 00:03:42.222\r\nCheer up. Mr. Wayne knows\r\nwhat you mean to the company.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.389 --\u003e 00:03:43.390\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.724 --\u003e 00:03:48.103\r\nSometimes, Alice, I think you're\r\nthe only one who understands me.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:51.648\r\n(CHUCKLES) That's just\r\nwhat my boyfriend says.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.944 --\u003e 00:03:59.573\r\nI guess I'm lucky to have two\r\nsuch amazing men in my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.906 --\u003e 00:04:01.450\r\nSee you after lunch.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.541 --\u003e 00:04:13.086\r\nOf course, intellectually,\r\nI know it's all wrong.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.837 --\u003e 00:04:15.547\r\nShe's got a\r\nboyfriend, after all.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.298 --\u003e 00:04:19.009\r\nBetter to withdraw like a gentleman.\r\nForget her.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.259 --\u003e 00:04:21.261\r\nTurn my heart to other pursuits.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.512 --\u003e 00:04:23.513\r\n(SLURPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.057 --\u003e 00:04:27.559\r\nNever!\r\n\r\n00:04:30.312 --\u003e 00:04:32.731\r\nLook. I've already\r\ndeveloped a circuitry card\r\n\r\n00:04:32.898 --\u003e 00:04:35.317\r\npowerful enough to\r\ncontrol a human brain.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.692 --\u003e 00:04:40.655\r\nIt would be so easy to make her\r\nforget her boorish beau and love me.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.906 --\u003e 00:04:41.907\r\nAh.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.449 --\u003e 00:04:45.535\r\nBut that would reduce\r\nher to a soulless shell.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.911 --\u003e 00:04:48.580\r\nOh, no, not my Alice.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.705 --\u003e 00:04:49.706\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.248 --\u003e 00:04:52.292\r\nIt's hopeless.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.626 --\u003e 00:04:55.879\r\n- (ALICE SOBBING)\r\n- DR. CATES: Oh, Alice, I'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.756 --\u003e 00:04:59.466\r\n(SOBBING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.008 --\u003e 00:05:01.551\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:05:03.595 --\u003e 00:05:06.348\r\nCuriouser and curiouser.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.598 --\u003e 00:05:09.351\r\n(SOBBING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:05:09.434 --\u003e 00:05:12.479\r\nALICE: I just wanted to talk about\r\nwhere our relationship was going\r\n\r\n00:05:12.646 --\u003e 00:05:14.731\r\nand Billy got so defensive.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.190 --\u003e 00:05:19.319\r\nMmm. Classic male\r\nfear of commitment.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.820 --\u003e 00:05:23.365\r\nThe next thing I knew,\r\nwe were shouting, screaming.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.615 --\u003e 00:05:27.035\r\nSaying we never wanted\r\nto see each other again.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.497 --\u003e 00:05:34.042\r\nO frabjous day! Callooh! Callay!\r\n\r\n00:05:34.125 --\u003e 00:05:35.836\r\n(LAUGHS) She's mine\r\nfor the asking.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.044 --\u003e 00:05:40.674\r\nI'll sweep her off her feet, treat her\r\nto a wonderful night on the town and...\r\n\r\n00:05:42.634 --\u003e 00:05:43.885\r\nNothing.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.219 --\u003e 00:05:47.305\r\nWhat could a beautiful girl like\r\nher ever see in someone like me?\r\n\r\n00:05:47.556 --\u003e 00:05:49.933\r\nHow could I impress her?\r\n\r\n00:05:51.726 --\u003e 00:05:52.727\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.729 --\u003e 00:05:56.523\r\nHow, indeed.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.990 --\u003e 00:06:06.157\r\nJervis?\r\n\r\n00:06:11.162 --\u003e 00:06:12.581\r\nGood evening, Miss Pleasance.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.206 --\u003e 00:06:15.959\r\nI'm here to help you forget\r\nyour recent heartbreak.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.209 --\u003e 00:06:19.170\r\nGotham can be a\r\nwonderland, Alice.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.588 --\u003e 00:06:22.173\r\nTonight, let me be your guide.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.258 --\u003e 00:06:25.051\r\nI'll get my coat.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.558 --\u003e 00:06:32.809\r\nDid you see that?\r\n\r\n00:06:32.976 --\u003e 00:06:36.897\r\n- Gotta be the Bat-Creep.\r\n- Hey, easy money headed our way.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.612 --\u003e 00:06:46.907\r\nThis is really a surprise, Jervis.\r\nYou're so...\r\n\r\n00:06:47.073 --\u003e 00:06:48.575\r\nQuiet at work.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.825 --\u003e 00:06:51.328\r\nAh, still waters run\r\ndeep, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.578 --\u003e 00:06:55.665\r\nIt's been my philosophy that people\r\nshould take what they want from life.\r\n\r\n00:06:56.041 --\u003e 00:06:57.709\r\nTHUG: Hey, ours too.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.043 --\u003e 00:07:00.921\r\nOkay, Mr. Hat,\r\nlet's have the money.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.212 --\u003e 00:07:03.840\r\nOn your way, curs,\r\nlest I'm forced to teach you a lesson.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.924 --\u003e 00:07:05.133\r\nJervis, no.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.675 --\u003e 00:07:07.636\r\nIt's your funeral, nut boy.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.975 --\u003e 00:07:15.310\r\n(DEVICES BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.644 --\u003e 00:07:18.188\r\nPlease, Mr. Hat, go easy on us.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.772 --\u003e 00:07:20.815\r\nWe're sorry. Honest.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.525 --\u003e 00:07:27.113\r\nWhy don't you do something useful,\r\nlike, oh, go jump in the river.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.364 --\u003e 00:07:28.907\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.784 --\u003e 00:07:33.453\r\n- Are you all right?\r\n- I'm sorry you had to see that.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.620 --\u003e 00:07:35.497\r\nBut they had to be\r\ntaught a lesson.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.044 --\u003e 00:07:44.422\r\n\u003ci\u003eDare we hope Gotham treats\r\nyou to an early evening, sir?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:45.757 --\u003e 00:07:49.219\r\nI should be so lucky. The police\r\nemergency band just switched on.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.761 --\u003e 00:07:54.975\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen I'll prepare your usual\r\nbreakfast, toast, coffee, bandages.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:55.642 --\u003e 00:07:56.935\r\nGood night, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.268 --\u003e 00:07:58.704\r\nPOLICE DISPATCHER ON RADIO: All units.\r\nAll units.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.728 --\u003e 00:08:02.107\r\n\u003ci\u003eTwo possible suicides reported scaling\r\nthe Gotham Bridge suspension tower.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:02.315 --\u003e 00:08:04.818\r\n- All units, please respond.\r\n- BATMAN: Guess I'm elected.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.451 --\u003e 00:08:14.953\r\n(BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:20.375 --\u003e 00:08:21.751\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:08:26.673 --\u003e 00:08:27.674\r\nEngage.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.223 --\u003e 00:08:36.683\r\nLousy night for a swim.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.850 --\u003e 00:08:38.935\r\nMr. Hat told us to\r\njump in the river.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.103 --\u003e 00:08:44.024\r\nRight.\r\nLook, you guys stay calm and-\r\n\r\n00:08:44.274 --\u003e 00:08:46.234\r\nGotta do what Mr. Hat says.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.988 --\u003e 00:08:51.698\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.323 --\u003e 00:08:53.700\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:08:54.325 --\u003e 00:08:55.577\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:09:15.346 --\u003e 00:09:17.015\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:21.811 --\u003e 00:09:24.773\r\n(GASPS) Hey, man,\r\nkeep away from me.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.981 --\u003e 00:09:26.733\r\nWe never touched the creep.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.692 --\u003e 00:09:30.987\r\nOkay, maybe we hit him up for\r\nmoney, but we never-\r\n\r\n00:09:31.279 --\u003e 00:09:33.656\r\nHey, what are we doing here?\r\n\r\n00:09:40.789 --\u003e 00:09:45.210\r\nMonsieur Tetch, I have created\r\na gastronomical delight for you.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.627 --\u003e 00:09:47.587\r\nAll on the house, of course.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.754 --\u003e 00:09:49.130\r\nThank you, Antoine.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.297 --\u003e 00:09:50.799\r\nPardon, Monsieur Tetch.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.965 --\u003e 00:09:54.552\r\nWould you be so kind as to favor us\r\nwith a photo for our celebrity wall?\r\n\r\n00:09:54.928 --\u003e 00:09:56.763\r\nEnchanté, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.350 --\u003e 00:10:03.394\r\nI had no idea you were\r\nsuch a man about town.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.187 --\u003e 00:10:08.108\r\nAh, this is a side I share\r\nonly with those closest to me.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.191 --\u003e 00:10:10.151\r\n(SLOW VIOLIN MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:10:22.705 --\u003e 00:10:25.041\r\nDon't forget to lock up when you're\r\ndone, Mr. Tetch.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.166 --\u003e 00:10:26.376\r\nRig ht-o.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.882 --\u003e 00:10:37.679\r\nYou know, Alice in Wonderland\r\nwas always my favorite story.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.179 --\u003e 00:10:41.224\r\nDo you remember \"The\r\nMock Turtle's Song\"?\r\n\r\n00:10:42.058 --\u003e 00:10:44.060\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SINGING) Will you, won't\r\nyou, will you, won't you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:44.769 --\u003e 00:10:46.396\r\nWon't you join the dance?\r\n\r\n00:10:48.773 --\u003e 00:10:50.775\r\n(SLOW ORCHESTRAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.329 --\u003e 00:11:07.834\r\nWhen you showed me that strange card,\r\nI recalled an image from my childhood.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.251 --\u003e 00:11:10.420\r\nIt seems those near-suicides\r\n\r\n00:11:10.503 --\u003e 00:11:13.506\r\nhad a run-in with a\r\nself-styled Mad Hatter.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.090 --\u003e 00:11:16.467\r\nBATMAN: I saw that\r\npicture earlier today\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:21.472\r\nin the office of a scientist who\r\ncreates circuitry similar to this.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.146 --\u003e 00:11:32.567\r\nThank you for a wonderful time.\r\nYou're a terrific friend.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.859 --\u003e 00:11:35.695\r\nUntil tomorrow, dear Alice.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.406 --\u003e 00:11:42.368\r\nTomorrow and every\r\nday afterward.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.036 --\u003e 00:11:44.370\r\n(BLOWS KISS)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.708 --\u003e 00:11:51.294\r\nWhat a sweet, funny man.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.673 --\u003e 00:11:57.467\r\n- BILLY: Alice?\r\n- Billy?\r\n\r\n00:11:59.344 --\u003e 00:12:01.930\r\nBaby, I'm sorry. Can we talk?\r\n\r\n00:12:09.646 --\u003e 00:12:11.286\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SINGING) Will you,\r\nwon't you, will you...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:12.190 --\u003e 00:12:17.487\r\n(CHUCKLES) Ah, good morning. Hello!\r\nGood to see you. Lovely day, what?\r\n\r\n00:12:18.863 --\u003e 00:12:20.573\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:12:20.657 --\u003e 00:12:21.699\r\n(SINGING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:21.783 --\u003e 00:12:22.784\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.497 --\u003e 00:12:31.209\r\nOh, Jervis, thanks so much\r\nfor cheering me up last night.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.501 --\u003e 00:12:34.170\r\nListen,\r\nI have the most incredible news.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.462 --\u003e 00:12:36.214\r\nBilly was there after\r\nyou dropped me off.\r\n\r\n00:12:36.422 --\u003e 00:12:38.549\r\nHe apologized. I forgave him.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.716 --\u003e 00:12:41.052\r\nAnd then, he gave me this.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.511 --\u003e 00:12:43.137\r\nCan you believe it?\r\n\r\n00:12:44.597 --\u003e 00:12:46.266\r\nI'm getting married.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.269 --\u003e 00:12:51.521\r\nJervis, your hand.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.688 --\u003e 00:12:54.983\r\nOh, it's nothing. Forget it.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.692 --\u003e 00:12:58.278\r\n- And congratulations.\r\n- Jervis?\r\n\r\n00:12:58.403 --\u003e 00:12:59.529\r\nJervis?\r\n\r\n00:13:05.243 --\u003e 00:13:08.955\r\nI can still fix this.\r\nI can still win!\r\n\r\n00:13:09.330 --\u003e 00:13:10.832\r\n\u003ci\u003e- (DOOR OPENS)\r\n- DR. GATES: Tetcw.!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:11.416 --\u003e 00:13:13.084\r\nI don't know what you did,\r\n\r\n00:13:13.167 --\u003e 00:13:15.962\r\nbut Bruce Wayne is\r\ndemanding to see you now!\r\n\r\n00:13:17.171 --\u003e 00:13:19.299\r\nI promise you,\r\nTetch, it's your head\r\n\r\n00:13:19.382 --\u003e 00:13:21.926\r\nif you've gotten my\r\ndepartment in any trouble.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.010 --\u003e 00:13:24.762\r\nOh, do be quiet, Dr. Cates!\r\n\r\n00:13:24.846 --\u003e 00:13:25.847\r\n(DEVICE BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.645 --\u003e 00:13:35.940\r\nExcuse me, Alice.\r\nHave you seen Marcia or Jervis Tetch?\r\n\r\n00:13:36.399 --\u003e 00:13:38.484\r\nThey left together\r\nabout half an hour ago.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.985 --\u003e 00:13:39.986\r\nTogether?\r\n\r\n00:13:40.069 --\u003e 00:13:41.529\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:42.780 --\u003e 00:13:44.991\r\nHello? Hi, sweetie.\r\n\r\n00:13:45.241 --\u003e 00:13:48.286\r\n- My fiancé.\r\n- (WHISPERS) Congratulations.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.831 --\u003e 00:13:55.126\r\nBilly, what's wrong?\r\nYou sound so-What?\r\n\r\n00:13:56.085 --\u003e 00:14:00.465\r\nBut why? Billy? Billy.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.966 --\u003e 00:14:07.055\r\nExcuse me, Mr. Wayne. (SHAKILY) I\r\nthink I'm gonna need a minute alone.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.305 --\u003e 00:14:09.515\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:14:11.851 --\u003e 00:14:16.022\r\nSorry, Billy, me lad,\r\nbut all's fair in love and war.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.740 --\u003e 00:14:26.991\r\n(SNIFFLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:27.658 --\u003e 00:14:28.826\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:37.543 --\u003e 00:14:38.586\r\nAlice, darling.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.669 --\u003e 00:14:39.712\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:39.796 --\u003e 00:14:43.341\r\nI had to come back when I heard\r\nthat cad abandoned you again.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.925 --\u003e 00:14:46.969\r\nHow did you know?\r\nI didn't tell anyone.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.261 --\u003e 00:14:48.721\r\nMAD HATTER: Oh, pish tosh.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.805 --\u003e 00:14:52.975\r\nWhat matters now is we have each\r\nother, now and forever.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.059 --\u003e 00:14:54.560\r\n(GASPS) Oh...\r\n\r\n00:14:54.644 --\u003e 00:14:56.854\r\nThis is getting too weird.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.271 --\u003e 00:15:00.358\r\nWhat have you done with Marcia\r\nCates and this girl's fiancé?\r\n\r\n00:15:00.733 --\u003e 00:15:02.944\r\nNo, I don't like this game.\r\n\r\n00:15:03.111 --\u003e 00:15:04.362\r\nLet's play another.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.445 --\u003e 00:15:05.571\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.408 --\u003e 00:15:09.409\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.288 --\u003e 00:15:18.835\r\nI anticipated there'd be trouble sooner\r\nor later, so I enlisted some help.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.085 --\u003e 00:15:24.090\r\nI'm sure you recognize my friends,\r\nthe Walrus and the Carpenter.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.050 --\u003e 00:15:27.176\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.274 --\u003e 00:15:43.109\r\nWhy are you doing this?\r\n\r\n00:15:43.776 --\u003e 00:15:45.820\r\nFor us, my dearest.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.903 --\u003e 00:15:49.824\r\nOh, believe me.\r\nI didn't want it this way.\r\n\r\n00:15:54.078 --\u003e 00:15:55.663\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:06.257 --\u003e 00:16:07.258\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:14.265 --\u003e 00:16:15.808\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.979 --\u003e 00:16:21.647\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:41.459 --\u003e 00:16:42.668\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:58.476 --\u003e 00:17:00.102\r\nMAD HATTER: Twinkle,\r\ntwinkle, little bat.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.686 --\u003e 00:17:03.064\r\nHow I wonder what you're at.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.117 --\u003e 00:17:18.371\r\nNow, this is a game\r\nmore to my liking.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.955 --\u003e 00:17:22.667\r\nAre you, the famous Batman,\r\nso intent upon destroying my happiness\r\n\r\n00:17:22.750 --\u003e 00:17:27.046\r\nthat you'll harm these poor,\r\nmind-warped innocents to get me?\r\n\r\n00:17:27.421 --\u003e 00:17:29.382\r\nLet's find out. (CLAPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.222 --\u003e 00:17:37.473\r\nOff with his head.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.398 --\u003e 00:17:46.399\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:48.651 --\u003e 00:17:50.861\r\nOh, one thing I\r\nforgot to mention.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.028 --\u003e 00:17:54.282\r\nMy control over my pawns\r\nincreases their strength. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:17:54.865 --\u003e 00:17:56.617\r\nGuess you found that out, huh?\r\n\r\n00:18:03.916 --\u003e 00:18:05.626\r\nBATMAN: Oh! (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.712 --\u003e 00:18:09.380\r\nOff with his head!\r\n\r\n00:18:32.445 --\u003e 00:18:34.405\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.488 --\u003e 00:18:35.906\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.365 --\u003e 00:18:39.869\r\nThere's the knave.\r\nOff with his head!\r\n\r\n00:18:40.411 --\u003e 00:18:42.121\r\nThey're programmed to attack me.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.330 --\u003e 00:18:44.707\r\n- But they won't fight you.\r\n- I gotcha.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.710 --\u003e 00:18:48.961\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.670 --\u003e 00:18:50.880\r\nMy aching skull.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.547 --\u003e 00:18:53.674\r\nCome, my dear.\r\nIt's time we were away.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.280 --\u003e 00:19:17.365\r\n(SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.496 --\u003e 00:19:25.748\r\nMAD HATTER: You're mighty in\r\nGotham, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:19:25.831 --\u003e 00:19:29.460\r\nbut in Wonderland,\r\nthe Mad Hatter reigns supreme.\r\n\r\n00:19:29.543 --\u003e 00:19:31.420\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:19:43.099 --\u003e 00:19:44.141\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.023 --\u003e 00:19:52.066\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:01.075 --\u003e 00:20:02.076\r\n(MAD HATTER GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:04.036 --\u003e 00:20:05.162\r\n(DISHES SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:06.205 --\u003e 00:20:09.917\r\nI'll cut that cowl off your\r\nneck before you'll take her.\r\n\r\n00:20:10.042 --\u003e 00:20:12.795\r\nI've waited my whole\r\nlonely life for her!\r\n\r\n00:20:13.546 --\u003e 00:20:15.673\r\nThen all you've waited\r\nfor is a puppet.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.299 --\u003e 00:20:19.385\r\nA soulless little doll.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.927 --\u003e 00:20:23.889\r\nIt didn't have to be this way.\r\nYou made me do this to her!\r\n\r\n00:20:23.973 --\u003e 00:20:25.349\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:26.809 --\u003e 00:20:28.686\r\n(MAD HATTER GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:38.821 --\u003e 00:20:39.905\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.616 --\u003e 00:20:43.617\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:46.036 --\u003e 00:20:48.080\r\n(BATMAN STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:20:49.457 --\u003e 00:20:51.041\r\n(LAUGHS MANICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:51.542 --\u003e 00:20:53.252\r\n(GASPS) Grrr!\r\n\r\n00:20:58.966 --\u003e 00:20:59.967\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:21.030 --\u003e 00:21:23.616\r\n- BILLY: Alice?\r\n- Oh, Billy!\r\n\r\n00:21:26.494 --\u003e 00:21:27.495\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:21:36.086 --\u003e 00:21:38.798\r\nWould not, could not...\r\n\r\n00:21:39.882 --\u003e 00:21:41.717\r\nWould not, could not.\r\n\r\n00:21:42.760 --\u003e 00:21:45.304\r\nOh, could not join the dance.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.977 --\u003e 00:21:53.979\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E25 - The Cape and Cowl Conspiracy (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.753 --\u003e 00:00:04.755\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:27.546 --\u003e 00:01:31.383\r\n\"Where tracks and golf\r\nballs roll and wind.\"\r\n\r\n00:01:34.177 --\u003e 00:01:37.598\r\n\"Round colored\r\nbanners of all kind.\"\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:43.103\r\n\"Here,\r\nnew instructions you will find.\"\r\n\r\n00:01:43.270 --\u003e 00:01:46.106\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: (ON PA) You've come to\r\nthe right place, Mr. McWhirter.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:46.189 --\u003e 00:01:48.609\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou won't be able to find me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:48.692 --\u003e 00:01:51.361\r\nJust follow the\r\nsound of my voice.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.115 --\u003e 00:01:56.908\r\nWho the devil are you?\r\n\r\n00:01:57.618 --\u003e 00:02:02.789\r\nWell, for a diplomatic courier,\r\nyou're not very diplomatic, are you?\r\n\r\n00:02:02.873 --\u003e 00:02:05.959\r\nIf you're my contact,\r\nwhat's the countersign?\r\n\r\n00:02:06.126 --\u003e 00:02:08.712\r\n(TUTTING) Patience, patience.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.254 --\u003e 00:02:11.024\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll your questions will be\r\nanswered, dear boy,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:11.048 --\u003e 00:02:14.259\r\n\u003ci\u003eif you'll simply follow\r\nthe running lights.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:24.770 --\u003e 00:02:27.773\r\nOkay, I'm here. Now what?\r\n\r\n00:02:31.193 --\u003e 00:02:32.194\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.404 --\u003e 00:02:35.864\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.699 --\u003e 00:02:40.327\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow then, about that\r\ncollection of bearer bonds\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:40.410 --\u003e 00:02:42.162\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou're supposed to transport,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:42.412 --\u003e 00:02:44.498\r\nif you'll just tell me\r\nwhere I can find them,\r\n\r\n00:02:45.707 --\u003e 00:02:47.542\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou might get out of here alive.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:51.046 --\u003e 00:02:52.047\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:02:57.678 --\u003e 00:03:00.472\r\nAll right!\r\nAll right, \u003ci\u003eI'll\u003c/i\u003e tell you!\r\n\r\n00:03:00.889 --\u003e 00:03:03.475\r\n\u003ci\u003eGood call. Now, hurry up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:04.017 --\u003e 00:03:07.771\r\nI hate it when people talk with\r\ntheir mouth full. (CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:15.195 --\u003e 00:03:18.907\r\nAll we know is this, last night,\r\nthe International Relief Consortium\r\n\r\n00:03:18.990 --\u003e 00:03:21.827\r\nwas supposed to receive a delivery\r\nfrom one of their couriers.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.910 --\u003e 00:03:25.080\r\nThis guy. Name's McWhirter.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.332 --\u003e 00:03:28.542\r\nHe's lucky to be alive.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.750 --\u003e 00:03:31.461\r\nHe was supposed to pick\r\nup and deliver a donation.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.545 --\u003e 00:03:35.090\r\nA diplomatic pouch containing\r\n$750,000 in bearer bonds\r\n\r\n00:03:35.173 --\u003e 00:03:37.259\r\nearmarked for humanitarian aid-\r\n\r\n00:03:37.426 --\u003e 00:03:40.679\r\nTo starving refugees in Eastern Europe.\r\nYeah, I know.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.096 --\u003e 00:03:43.598\r\nOnly McWhirter never showed up.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.765 --\u003e 00:03:46.518\r\nSomebody else got to\r\nthe bonds before he did.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.685 --\u003e 00:03:47.978\r\nAnd now they're missing.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.145 --\u003e 00:03:52.023\r\nThe same somebody who lured him into\r\nthat quicksand trap you mentioned?\r\n\r\n00:03:52.190 --\u003e 00:03:55.569\r\nYou know who that sounds\r\nlike, don't you? Wormwood.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.652 --\u003e 00:03:56.862\r\nThe interrogator.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.987 --\u003e 00:03:59.114\r\nThe guy who specializes\r\nin using deathtraps\r\n\r\n00:03:59.197 --\u003e 00:04:01.533\r\nto pry information\r\nout of his victims?\r\n\r\n00:04:01.700 --\u003e 00:04:04.911\r\nTerrific. Look up \"slippery\"\r\nin the dictionary,\r\n\r\n00:04:04.995 --\u003e 00:04:06.788\r\nand you get Josiah Wormwood.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.205 --\u003e 00:04:09.499\r\nWell, I guess if anyone\r\ncan pin something on him\r\n\r\n00:04:09.583 --\u003e 00:04:11.501\r\nand make it stick, you can.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.335 --\u003e 00:04:15.797\r\nMaybe. Right now, though,\r\nwe're not even sure he's in town.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.673 --\u003e 00:04:19.593\r\nBut I think I know which\r\none of Wormwood's associates\r\n\r\n00:04:19.801 --\u003e 00:04:21.845\r\nmight be able to give\r\nme that information.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.891 --\u003e 00:04:28.560\r\nOh, yeah, I remember this clown.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.727 --\u003e 00:04:29.936\r\nNothing but a two-bit con man.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.020 --\u003e 00:04:32.522\r\nBut a continental\r\ntype, a real smoothie,\r\n\r\n00:04:32.647 --\u003e 00:04:34.733\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe kind who'll do\r\nanything for a free meal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:35.317 --\u003e 00:04:37.194\r\n\u003ci\u003eCalls himself \"The Baron.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:40.280 --\u003e 00:04:44.242\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\nour guest speaker this evening.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.326 --\u003e 00:04:46.870\r\nBaron Waclaw Jozek.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.953 --\u003e 00:04:48.997\r\n(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.926 --\u003e 00:05:03.386\r\nMadam President, honored guests,\r\n\r\n00:05:03.762 --\u003e 00:05:05.889\r\nthis is a rare pleasure for me.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.057 --\u003e 00:05:09.976\r\nUnaccustomed as I am to\r\nbeing sought after...\r\n\r\n00:05:10.310 --\u003e 00:05:11.478\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:14.898 --\u003e 00:05:16.107\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:16.191 --\u003e 00:05:17.484\r\n(CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:05:17.567 --\u003e 00:05:18.568\r\nJOZEK: No, no, no!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.986 --\u003e 00:05:20.987\r\n(WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:05:22.405 --\u003e 00:05:25.033\r\nNo, no, no!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.288 --\u003e 00:05:32.958\r\nHow dare you manhandle me.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.000 --\u003e 00:05:35.836\r\nI want information from you.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.003 --\u003e 00:05:39.881\r\nBy the way,\r\nI hope you're not afraid of heights.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.554 --\u003e 00:05:47.138\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:49.766 --\u003e 00:05:50.767\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:05:51.810 --\u003e 00:05:53.937\r\nBATMAN: That's all you have\r\non your friend Wormwood?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.104 --\u003e 00:05:56.273\r\nI've told you all I know.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.775 --\u003e 00:06:01.528\r\nWhat more do you want?\r\nLet me down. (WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:01.695 --\u003e 00:06:04.197\r\nJust one more thing, Baron.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.823 --\u003e 00:06:07.367\r\nI suggest that for your health\r\n\r\n00:06:08.660 --\u003e 00:06:13.707\r\nyou take a vacation,\r\nsomewhere far away from Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.797 --\u003e 00:06:22.424\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:30.724 --\u003e 00:06:32.017\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:06:32.100 --\u003e 00:06:33.184\r\nCome in.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.238 --\u003e 00:06:47.616\r\n(SIGHS) This had better be\r\nimportant, Waclaw.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.784 --\u003e 00:06:51.494\r\nIt is, to me.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.379 --\u003e 00:07:04.633\r\nI want the Batman's\r\ncape and cowl.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.925 --\u003e 00:07:07.093\r\nAnd I want you to\r\nget them for me.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.803 --\u003e 00:07:11.765\r\nHmm.\r\nHumble the legendary Batman?\r\n\r\n00:07:12.265 --\u003e 00:07:14.809\r\nI must admit,\r\nit is an intriguing challenge.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.185 --\u003e 00:07:17.437\r\nBut I'm afraid I can't\r\ncontain my curiosity.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.146 --\u003e 00:07:21.024\r\nI must know,\r\nwhat do you want them for?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.568 --\u003e 00:07:26.071\r\nI will be glad to tell you\r\nthat, dear Wormwood,\r\n\r\n00:07:26.529 --\u003e 00:07:30.241\r\nif you'll tell me how you\r\ngot those bearer bonds\r\n\r\n00:07:30.325 --\u003e 00:07:33.286\r\naway from the International\r\nRelief Consortium.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.038 --\u003e 00:07:36.665\r\nI don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.582 --\u003e 00:07:40.710\r\n(LAUGHING) Have it your way.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.877 --\u003e 00:07:43.004\r\nIn that case, I will say\r\n\r\n00:07:43.088 --\u003e 00:07:47.467\r\nonly that you will be very\r\nwell paid to do as I request\r\n\r\n00:07:47.968 --\u003e 00:07:51.262\r\nwithout further questions.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.101 --\u003e 00:07:59.521\r\nAll right, I'll get you\r\nthe Batman's cape and cowl.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.854 --\u003e 00:08:01.398\r\nThat won't be difficult.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.898 --\u003e 00:08:05.485\r\nHe is only human, after all.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.216 --\u003e 00:08:30.218\r\nGot a new toy, I see.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.553 --\u003e 00:08:32.929\r\nI figure it might come in handy.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.180 --\u003e 00:08:35.974\r\nIt might get you in\r\ntrouble with the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.057 --\u003e 00:08:37.726\r\nLet me worry about the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.892 --\u003e 00:08:39.853\r\nHere, have a look at this.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.441 --\u003e 00:08:49.446\r\n\"Where iron horses go to rot and\r\nchildren toot their horns a lot...\"\r\n\r\n00:08:49.612 --\u003e 00:08:52.949\r\n\"A damsel's pleas\r\nshall come to naught.\"\r\n\r\n00:08:53.324 --\u003e 00:08:54.701\r\nDo you know what it means?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.042 --\u003e 00:09:03.376\r\nDon't you?\r\n\r\n00:09:48.379 --\u003e 00:09:50.173\r\nLooking for someone, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:09:50.590 --\u003e 00:09:52.801\r\n\u003ci\u003eSorry,\r\nyou won't find me in there.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:53.009 --\u003e 00:09:55.470\r\n\u003ci\u003eHowever, you will find\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:55.845 --\u003e 00:09:56.930\r\na trap!\r\n\r\n00:09:59.224 --\u003e 00:10:00.683\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.813 --\u003e 00:10:06.272\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:06.523 --\u003e 00:10:10.944\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow then, you have approximately\r\none minute to save that young woman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:14.489 --\u003e 00:10:16.449\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:21.996 --\u003e 00:10:24.749\r\nBut I'll remove\r\nher from jeopardy\r\n\r\n00:10:25.041 --\u003e 00:10:28.878\r\nif you simply surrender\r\nyour cape and cowl.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.045 --\u003e 00:10:32.423\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou can push it through the little\r\nopening at the base of the engine door.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:32.882 --\u003e 00:10:35.009\r\n\u003ci\u003eThirty seconds left, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:36.386 --\u003e 00:10:37.387\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:40.223 --\u003e 00:10:41.724\r\nFifteen seconds.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.059 --\u003e 00:10:46.146\r\nWOMAN: (SCREAMING) Help!\r\nPlease, help!\r\n\r\n00:10:52.402 --\u003e 00:10:53.736\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:55.280 --\u003e 00:10:56.489\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:10:56.573 --\u003e 00:10:58.491\r\n\u003ci\u003eOne second left.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:03.121 --\u003e 00:11:04.455\r\nA hologram?\r\n\r\n00:11:21.389 --\u003e 00:11:22.932\r\n(ENGINE STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:31.065 --\u003e 00:11:32.501\r\nJOZEK: (ON PHONE) \u003ci\u003eDo\u003c/i\u003e\r\nyou have the items?\r\n\r\n00:11:32.525 --\u003e 00:11:34.235\r\nUh, no.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.319 --\u003e 00:11:36.279\r\nUh, the first apparatus...\r\n\r\n00:11:37.030 --\u003e 00:11:39.240\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe trap at the old\r\nrailway exhibit?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:39.407 --\u003e 00:11:41.659\r\n\u003ci\u003eYes. He beat it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:42.076 --\u003e 00:11:44.162\r\nSo there will have to be others?\r\n\r\n00:11:44.871 --\u003e 00:11:49.834\r\nOnly one. And this time,\r\nI shall put the man himself in jeopardy.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.460 --\u003e 00:11:53.588\r\nI have a facility at\r\nDe Larues Wax Museum\r\n\r\n00:11:53.671 --\u003e 00:11:56.549\r\nthat will serve our\r\npurposes nicely.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.925 --\u003e 00:11:59.594\r\nJust see that you succeed.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.136 --\u003e 00:12:04.432\r\nOh, I will. And once you have what\r\nyou want, you must tell me why-\r\n\r\n00:12:04.515 --\u003e 00:12:06.059\r\n- (LINE DISCONNECTS)\r\n- Well!\r\n\r\n00:12:10.521 --\u003e 00:12:13.149\r\nBATMAN: \"Where Washington\r\nand young Babe Ruth\"\r\n\r\n00:12:13.233 --\u003e 00:12:15.777\r\n\"stand side by side\r\nwith John Wilkes Booth.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:16.402 --\u003e 00:12:19.280\r\n\"Batman will find\r\na plan uncouth.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:19.447 --\u003e 00:12:21.908\r\nWell, what do you\r\nthink this one means?\r\n\r\n00:12:22.742 --\u003e 00:12:25.745\r\nThose famous figures\r\nstanding around together?\r\n\r\n00:12:25.912 --\u003e 00:12:28.081\r\nDe Larues Wax Museum, what else?\r\n\r\n00:12:28.831 --\u003e 00:12:30.375\r\nOh. Of course.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.523 --\u003e 00:12:55.733\r\nWORMWOOD: (ON PA) Over\r\nhere, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.735 --\u003e 00:13:00.405\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat's it. Come right in.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:09.497 --\u003e 00:13:12.375\r\nNow,\r\nif I might call your attention\r\n\r\n00:13:12.458 --\u003e 00:13:15.586\r\nto the panel sliding\r\nopen along the ceiling.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.753 --\u003e 00:13:19.841\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's uncovering a\r\n20,000-watt halogen bulb.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:20.800 --\u003e 00:13:24.512\r\n\u003ci\u003eI don't actually know how\r\nhot 20,000 watts make a room,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:25.013 --\u003e 00:13:27.515\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut I do know that it melts wax.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:38.151 --\u003e 00:13:42.071\r\nAnd eventually,\r\nit will melt you.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.422 --\u003e 00:14:00.423\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:14:00.757 --\u003e 00:14:01.758\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:05.470 --\u003e 00:14:10.141\r\nOf course, you can save yourself\r\nsimply by giving me your cape and cowl.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.184 --\u003e 00:14:14.312\r\n\u003ci\u003eAfter all, it looks like your\r\nweapons are covered with wax.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:14.604 --\u003e 00:14:16.147\r\nNo hurry. \u003ci\u003eI'll\u003c/i\u003e wait. (CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.732 --\u003e 00:14:21.152\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, very inventive.\r\nDo you suppose it will work?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:27.200 --\u003e 00:14:28.534\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:38.878 --\u003e 00:14:39.879\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:44.008 --\u003e 00:14:48.554\r\n\u003ci\u003eCongratulations.\r\nBut don't breathe too deeply, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:49.097 --\u003e 00:14:51.391\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt seems that when you\r\nshattered the lamp,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:51.557 --\u003e 00:14:56.771\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou triggered the release of a toxic\r\nnerve gas from a tank in the ceiling.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:57.021 --\u003e 00:15:00.691\r\nNow, your cape and cowl, please.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.983 --\u003e 00:15:03.528\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:15:03.611 --\u003e 00:15:07.198\r\nAll right. All right.\r\nTurn off the gas.\r\n\r\n00:15:07.365 --\u003e 00:15:08.783\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.866 --\u003e 00:15:09.867\r\nYou win. (Couemue)\r\n\r\n00:15:24.006 --\u003e 00:15:28.094\r\nWORMWOOD: \u003ci\u003e(ON PA) Ah. Nothing like\r\na breath of fresh air, eh, Batman?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:28.261 --\u003e 00:15:29.637\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.889 --\u003e 00:15:35.101\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd now, your cape and\r\ncowl, please.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:41.274 --\u003e 00:15:42.900\r\nSatisfied?\r\n\r\n00:15:44.068 --\u003e 00:15:45.528\r\nActually, no.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.736 --\u003e 00:15:50.199\r\nI wonder if you would put those\r\ndown neatly over here, by the light.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.955 --\u003e 00:15:57.373\r\n\u003ci\u003eA second mask?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:58.166 --\u003e 00:16:02.753\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot as confident as we'd seem\r\nthen, are we? (CHUCKLING)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:03.087 --\u003e 00:16:07.758\r\n\u003ci\u003eHmm. Well, keep your silly identity.\r\nThese are all I require.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:21.063 --\u003e 00:16:22.857\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:25.860 --\u003e 00:16:27.570\r\nWORMWOOD: Stop stalling, Jozek.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.198 --\u003e 00:16:31.574\r\nI've got the goods.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.824 --\u003e 00:16:33.868\r\nHave you got my certified check?\r\n\r\n00:16:35.119 --\u003e 00:16:36.412\r\nIhaveindeed.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.288 --\u003e 00:16:40.583\r\nAh, but first,\r\nlet us drink to our success.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.250 --\u003e 00:16:43.669\r\n(CHUCKLING) On one condition.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.420 --\u003e 00:16:49.050\r\nWill you tell me why you wanted\r\nBatman's cape and cowl, finally?\r\n\r\n00:16:49.675 --\u003e 00:16:54.931\r\nAh, but you know my condition.\r\nYou must tell me your secret.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.264 --\u003e 00:16:57.850\r\nThen I will tell you mine.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.645 --\u003e 00:17:03.356\r\nWhat did you do with those bonds?\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:08.152 --\u003e 00:17:10.446\r\nAnd who commissioned\r\ntheir theft?\r\n\r\n00:17:13.783 --\u003e 00:17:16.494\r\n(SIGHING) If you\r\nreally want to know,\r\n\r\n00:17:17.161 --\u003e 00:17:20.957\r\nan agent of the Quirian\r\nEmirates will get the bonds\r\n\r\n00:17:21.123 --\u003e 00:17:25.086\r\nfrom a locker at\r\nPan-Europa Airways tomorrow\r\n\r\n00:17:25.169 --\u003e 00:17:28.506\r\nwhen I meet him there\r\nto give him this key.\r\n\r\n00:17:31.676 --\u003e 00:17:35.846\r\nNow, what will you do\r\nwith the cape and cowl?\r\n\r\n00:17:39.725 --\u003e 00:17:41.978\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:42.061 --\u003e 00:17:45.231\r\nI am going to wear them.\r\n\r\n00:17:46.440 --\u003e 00:17:47.441\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:50.278 --\u003e 00:17:51.904\r\nYou're not Jozek?\r\n\r\n00:17:55.866 --\u003e 00:17:59.203\r\nYou were playing.\r\nPlaying me for a fool.\r\n\r\n00:18:00.121 --\u003e 00:18:02.498\r\nBATMAN: From the day you\r\nfirst walked in here.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.629 --\u003e 00:18:11.674\r\nIt was you I was\r\ndealing with all along!\r\n\r\n00:18:12.091 --\u003e 00:18:13.092\r\nBATMAN: Give me the key.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.968 --\u003e 00:18:14.969\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:19.557 --\u003e 00:18:20.558\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.574 --\u003e 00:19:19.575\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:24.330 --\u003e 00:19:25.706\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:32.797 --\u003e 00:19:33.798\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.883 --\u003e 00:19:36.884\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:43.641 --\u003e 00:19:44.642\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.857 --\u003e 00:19:52.858\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.953 --\u003e 00:20:05.746\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:07.164 --\u003e 00:20:08.416\r\n(SHRIEKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.756 --\u003e 00:20:17.216\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:26.684 --\u003e 00:20:28.227\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.742 --\u003e 00:20:44.582\r\nWORMWOOD: (ON TAPE) If\r\nyou really want to \u003ci\u003eknow,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:44.660 --\u003e 00:20:47.121\r\n\u003ci\u003ean agent of the\r\nQuirian Emirates...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:50.166\r\nThe bugs in the room picked\r\nup the whole story on tape.\r\n\r\n00:20:50.332 --\u003e 00:20:52.668\r\n\u003ci\u003eAt Pan-Europa Airways tomorrow.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:54.962 --\u003e 00:20:57.006\r\n- Thank you, Commissioner.\r\n- Thank you.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.632 --\u003e 00:21:03.387\r\nAnd thank Jozek for the use of the\r\nhall, if he ever returns from Europe.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.682 --\u003e 00:21:10.644\r\nWhen we collared the Quirian agent\r\nat the airport, he sang like a bird.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.853 --\u003e 00:21:13.773\r\nAnd he fingered you as the guy\r\nwho was gonna sell him the bonds.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.107 --\u003e 00:21:16.692\r\nOh, I almost forgot.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.318 --\u003e 00:21:18.944\r\nThis came for you.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.240 --\u003e 00:21:28.412\r\n\"Confinement will speed your reform.\r\nBut long, cold nights will be the norm.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.579 --\u003e 00:21:31.791\r\n\"So here's a thing\r\nto keep you warm\"?\r\n\r\n00:21:33.501 --\u003e 00:21:34.668\r\nWell.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.796 --\u003e 00:21:38.214\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:40.800 --\u003e 00:21:41.967\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:21:55.147 --\u003e 00:21:57.149\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.798 --\u003e 00:22:21.799\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E26 - Perchance to Dream (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.503 --\u003e 00:00:04.505\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.208 --\u003e 00:01:24.209\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.219 --\u003e 00:01:35.220\r\n(ENGINE REVS)\r\n\r\n00:02:30.150 --\u003e 00:02:31.550\r\n- (ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:35.697 --\u003e 00:02:37.783\r\nHuh? What the...\r\n\r\n00:02:38.200 --\u003e 00:02:39.201\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:44.456 --\u003e 00:02:46.166\r\nGood morning, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.249 --\u003e 00:02:47.751\r\nRise and shine, sir.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.418 --\u003e 00:02:50.170\r\nI'm lucky to be awake at all.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.504 --\u003e 00:02:52.673\r\nI fell into that\r\ntrap like an amateur.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.173 --\u003e 00:02:54.424\r\nTrap, sir?\r\n\r\n00:02:55.550 --\u003e 00:02:56.927\r\nHow'd I get back here?\r\n\r\n00:02:57.636 --\u003e 00:02:58.679\r\nRobin?\r\n\r\n00:02:58.929 --\u003e 00:03:00.222\r\nRobin, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:00.847 --\u003e 00:03:03.934\r\nA young lady?\r\nI thought you and Miss Selina were...\r\n\r\n00:03:04.935 --\u003e 00:03:07.229\r\nPardon me, sir,\r\nnone of my business.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.312 --\u003e 00:03:10.107\r\nIf this is a joke,\r\nAlfred, it's not funny.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.607 --\u003e 00:03:13.276\r\nIf it's a joke, sir,\r\nI assure you it's on me.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.944 --\u003e 00:03:15.445\r\nI've just prepared breakfast.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.821 --\u003e 00:03:18.407\r\nPerhaps morning coffee\r\nwill clear the cobwebs.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.590 --\u003e 00:03:36.842\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:03:37.509 --\u003e 00:03:38.760\r\nA problem, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:39.010 --\u003e 00:03:40.178\r\nIt's not here.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.470 --\u003e 00:03:42.097\r\nWhat's not here, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:42.597 --\u003e 00:03:44.182\r\nYou know what I'm talking about.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.266 --\u003e 00:03:46.768\r\nThe entrance to the Batcave.\r\nWhy is it sealed up?\r\n\r\n00:03:47.227 --\u003e 00:03:48.478\r\nBatcave?\r\n\r\n00:03:49.062 --\u003e 00:03:50.397\r\nI'm sorry, I don't...\r\n\r\n00:03:50.647 --\u003e 00:03:53.316\r\nThat's right,\r\nAlfred, the Batcave.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.692 --\u003e 00:03:55.318\r\nIt's a big hole in the ground\r\n\r\n00:03:55.402 --\u003e 00:03:58.447\r\nwith a big car in it that's all\r\nblack, remember?\r\n\r\n00:03:58.655 --\u003e 00:04:00.991\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: Son? You sound upset.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:01.199 --\u003e 00:04:02.284\r\nLs something the matter?\r\n\r\n00:04:05.662 --\u003e 00:04:08.206\r\nNo. No, it's impossible.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.373 --\u003e 00:04:09.458\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.292 --\u003e 00:04:11.543\r\nIt can't be you.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.960 --\u003e 00:04:13.211\r\nIt can't be.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.139 --\u003e 00:04:25.390\r\nYou okay, son?\r\n\r\n00:04:25.640 --\u003e 00:04:27.601\r\nI'm... I'm all right.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.934 --\u003e 00:04:30.312\r\nJust partied too hard last\r\nnight, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.896 --\u003e 00:04:33.106\r\nYou will be able to get to\r\nthe office today, won't you?\r\n\r\n00:04:33.398 --\u003e 00:04:35.317\r\nThere's that stockholder's\r\nmeeting, you know.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.400 --\u003e 00:04:36.485\r\nSure.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.277 --\u003e 00:04:39.196\r\nI'm fine, really.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.821 --\u003e 00:04:42.157\r\nWell, good.\r\nGlad you'll be there.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.449 --\u003e 00:04:44.618\r\nYour mother and I have an\r\nappointment too this morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.828 --\u003e 00:04:48.038\r\nOn the golf course.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.789 --\u003e 00:04:50.248\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.755 --\u003e 00:04:59.633\r\nThis should be just the thing\r\nfor your meeting, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.803 --\u003e 00:05:03.804\r\nAlfred,\r\n\r\n00:05:04.346 --\u003e 00:05:05.722\r\nwill you do me a favor?\r\n\r\n00:05:06.473 --\u003e 00:05:07.724\r\nIt's an odd favor.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.350 --\u003e 00:05:09.684\r\nWould you tell me\r\n\r\n00:05:10.268 --\u003e 00:05:11.478\r\nabout my life?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.978 --\u003e 00:05:13.396\r\nJust humor me, please.\r\n\r\n00:05:14.356 --\u003e 00:05:15.774\r\nVery well, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.067 --\u003e 00:05:19.319\r\nSince your father retired,\r\n\r\n00:05:19.402 --\u003e 00:05:21.404\r\nyou've been head of\r\nWayne Enterprises,\r\n\r\n00:05:21.530 --\u003e 00:05:25.367\r\nthough Lucius Fox really\r\nruns the business.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.534 --\u003e 00:05:27.536\r\nNot that you aren't\r\ncapable, of course.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.453 --\u003e 00:05:31.164\r\nThat's all right, Alfred.\r\nGo on, please.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.748 --\u003e 00:05:35.877\r\nAnd, um, unless plans have\r\nchanged since last night,\r\n\r\n00:05:36.127 --\u003e 00:05:38.171\r\nyou're to marry\r\nMiss Selina Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.089 --\u003e 00:05:41.132\r\nYou proposed to her last week.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.466 --\u003e 00:05:43.218\r\nNo, it's wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.426 --\u003e 00:05:44.845\r\nIt's all wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.928 --\u003e 00:05:48.223\r\nWell, sir, it's a leisurely\r\nexistence, I admit.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.598 --\u003e 00:05:50.225\r\nBut there are worse lives.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.782 --\u003e 00:06:06.783\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:06:13.456 --\u003e 00:06:14.666\r\nSefina?\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:17.836\r\nYour mother called, darling,\r\nsaid you could use some cheering up.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.336 --\u003e 00:06:20.672\r\nAnd, uh, who better for the job\r\n\r\n00:06:20.755 --\u003e 00:06:22.507\r\nthan the woman you're\r\nmarrying next week?\r\n\r\n00:06:25.635 --\u003e 00:06:26.761\r\nBruce,\r\n\r\n00:06:26.845 --\u003e 00:06:28.889\r\nyou really are upset.\r\nWhat's wrong?\r\n\r\n00:06:29.222 --\u003e 00:06:30.515\r\nI feel as if\r\n\r\n00:06:31.057 --\u003e 00:06:32.601\r\nI'm someone else.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.684 --\u003e 00:06:35.270\r\nIt's crazy, but I know I'm-\r\n\r\n00:06:35.353 --\u003e 00:06:36.479\r\nSELINA: Batman!\r\n\r\n00:06:55.916 --\u003e 00:06:57.459\r\nHey, watch where you're going!\r\n\r\n00:06:57.542 --\u003e 00:06:59.377\r\nBruce. Bruce, wait.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.059 --\u003e 00:07:15.477\r\n(CRIMINAL YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:19.898 --\u003e 00:07:21.024\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:36.748 --\u003e 00:07:37.749\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:07:39.793 --\u003e 00:07:41.127\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:07:41.211 --\u003e 00:07:42.462\r\nHey! Help!\r\n\r\n00:08:00.563 --\u003e 00:08:01.564\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:07.529 --\u003e 00:08:08.989\r\nIsn't he fantastic?\r\n\r\n00:08:09.406 --\u003e 00:08:11.366\r\n- Actually, yeah.\r\n- (SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.459 --\u003e 00:08:23.086\r\nWho... Who is he?\r\n\r\n00:08:23.253 --\u003e 00:08:24.671\r\nThey call him Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.879 --\u003e 00:08:27.674\r\nNo, I mean, who is he?\r\n\r\n00:08:28.299 --\u003e 00:08:29.551\r\nNo one knows.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.634 --\u003e 00:08:32.303\r\nHe just appeared in\r\nGotham a few weeks ago.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.387 --\u003e 00:08:34.347\r\nBruce, you okay?\r\n\r\n00:08:34.889 --\u003e 00:08:38.309\r\nSelina, does the name\r\nCatwoman ring a bell?\r\n\r\n00:08:38.560 --\u003e 00:08:39.811\r\nCatwoman?\r\n\r\n00:08:41.187 --\u003e 00:08:43.815\r\nBruce, you're beginning to worry me.\r\nWhat's this all about?\r\n\r\n00:08:44.024 --\u003e 00:08:46.151\r\nI'm losing my mind, that's what.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.530 --\u003e 00:08:52.240\r\nI couldn't go to a psychiatrist.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.782 --\u003e 00:08:54.743\r\nYou're the only doctor I\r\ntrust, Leslie.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.910 --\u003e 00:08:58.288\r\nIt's like I'm living\r\nsomeone else's life.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.080 --\u003e 00:09:01.416\r\nI don't know anything\r\nabout me anymore.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.876 --\u003e 00:09:05.045\r\nHelp me, Leslie, please.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.503 --\u003e 00:09:07.255\r\n\u003ci\u003eEven though I'm not a\r\npsychiatrist, Bruce,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:07.338 --\u003e 00:09:08.840\r\nyour problem seems clear.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.799 --\u003e 00:09:10.925\r\nYou've led the sort of life\r\n\r\n00:09:11.009 --\u003e 00:09:12.802\r\nwhere everything has\r\nbeen handed to you,\r\n\r\n00:09:12.886 --\u003e 00:09:14.345\r\neven Wayne Enterprises.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.888 --\u003e 00:09:17.348\r\nYou don't feel you've\r\naccomplished anything.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.432 --\u003e 00:09:19.434\r\nIt's all been laid out for you.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.101 --\u003e 00:09:23.938\r\nSo your unconscious created a\r\nlife more satisfying to you.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.397 --\u003e 00:09:27.942\r\nYou've identified with someone\r\nwhose every deed has great value.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.359 --\u003e 00:09:29.444\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.527 --\u003e 00:09:31.696\r\nIt's called\r\ndisassociation, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.197 --\u003e 00:09:34.240\r\nOnce you find pride\r\nin your own existence,\r\n\r\n00:09:34.324 --\u003e 00:09:36.576\r\nthen these delusions\r\nwill vanish.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.118 --\u003e 00:09:39.954\r\nThen all these years of\r\ntraining and discipline...\r\n\r\n00:09:41.122 --\u003e 00:09:42.916\r\nWhat happened to my parents...\r\n\r\n00:09:43.083 --\u003e 00:09:44.417\r\nA delusion.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.168 --\u003e 00:09:46.336\r\nThen...\r\n\r\n00:09:47.462 --\u003e 00:09:49.297\r\nThe nightmare is over.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.264 --\u003e 00:09:59.307\r\nDad.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.559 --\u003e 00:10:04.979\r\nDad, will you and Mom join Selina\r\nand me at the opera tonight?\r\n\r\n00:10:05.480 --\u003e 00:10:08.274\r\nYou certainly seem like\r\nyour old self again, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.733 --\u003e 00:10:11.236\r\nI've never felt better in my\r\nlife, sir.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.195 --\u003e 00:10:13.571\r\nI'll check with your mother.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.324 --\u003e 00:10:19.369\r\nHave you found that entrance\r\nto the Batcave yet, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:10:20.328 --\u003e 00:10:22.413\r\nUh, I'm afraid not, sir.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.331 --\u003e 00:10:26.209\r\nGood. Because if you had,\r\nthen we'd both be nuts.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.501 --\u003e 00:10:29.879\r\nIt's nice to see you in good humor\r\nagain, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.839 --\u003e 00:10:34.050\r\nWhy shouldn't I be?\r\nMy life is a dream, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.134 --\u003e 00:10:36.344\r\nThe best dream anyone ever had.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.719 --\u003e 00:10:39.764\r\nI'll just prepare your\r\nsuit for the opera tonight.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.142 --\u003e 00:10:43.518\r\nYou do that, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.073 --\u003e 00:10:58.074\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:11:01.911 --\u003e 00:11:02.912\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:11:12.172 --\u003e 00:11:13.173\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:25.351 --\u003e 00:11:27.228\r\nNothing makes sense!\r\n\r\n00:11:29.814 --\u003e 00:11:30.982\r\nBruce!\r\n\r\n00:11:35.028 --\u003e 00:11:36.279\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.571 --\u003e 00:11:37.864\r\nYou're a lie.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.364 --\u003e 00:11:40.325\r\nIt's all a lie!\r\n\r\n00:11:53.504 --\u003e 00:11:57.133\r\n\u003ci\u003eOnce again, the mysterious\r\nfigure known as Batman has come-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:57.217 --\u003e 00:11:58.551\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:11:59.761 --\u003e 00:12:01.387\r\nAlways Batman!\r\n\r\n00:12:04.849 --\u003e 00:12:05.850\r\nStop it, son.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.100 --\u003e 00:12:07.310\r\nCalm down.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.477 --\u003e 00:12:09.938\r\nHe's behind all this. I know it.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.188 --\u003e 00:12:11.981\r\nAnd I'm gonna find out why.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.233 --\u003e 00:12:14.817\r\nYou're not well, son.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.152 --\u003e 00:12:17.320\r\nBruce.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.298 --\u003e 00:12:39.884\r\nI need a flare gun\r\nand some flares.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.093 --\u003e 00:12:42.053\r\nUh, sure, no problem.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.310 --\u003e 00:12:50.478\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:12:54.065 --\u003e 00:12:56.776\r\nExcuse me, sir.\r\nThis is a no-parking zone.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.110 --\u003e 00:12:58.444\r\nMay we see your license?\r\n\r\n00:12:59.654 --\u003e 00:13:01.447\r\nCertainly, officer.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.742 --\u003e 00:13:07.328\r\nMr. Wayne, your parents are\r\nvery concerned about you.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.412 --\u003e 00:13:08.496\r\nPlease come with us.\r\n\r\n00:13:09.080 --\u003e 00:13:10.248\r\nVery well.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.790 --\u003e 00:13:12.000\r\nBut not right now.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.253 --\u003e 00:13:16.504\r\nHey! Stop!\r\n\r\n00:13:28.433 --\u003e 00:13:29.434\r\nBlast it.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.517 --\u003e 00:13:31.060\r\nGo around. We'll cut him off.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.902 --\u003e 00:13:41.070\r\nUp there.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.196 --\u003e 00:13:43.197\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:13:46.743 --\u003e 00:13:48.286\r\nGuy moves like Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.341 --\u003e 00:14:03.551\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:25.990 --\u003e 00:14:27.909\r\nStop right there, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.705 --\u003e 00:14:33.790\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:14:33.873 --\u003e 00:14:34.957\r\nNot again.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.004 --\u003e 00:14:41.005\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:24.549 --\u003e 00:15:25.800\r\nHere I am!\r\n\r\n00:15:28.344 --\u003e 00:15:30.263\r\nI've been waiting for you!\r\n\r\n00:15:31.013 --\u003e 00:15:32.849\r\nYou did this to me!\r\n\r\n00:16:09.010 --\u003e 00:16:10.011\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:17.018 --\u003e 00:16:18.019\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:21.397 --\u003e 00:16:23.649\r\nYou're not well, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:16:24.400 --\u003e 00:16:26.569\r\nYou need professional help.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.944 --\u003e 00:16:29.780\r\nLiar! You know what's going on.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.072 --\u003e 00:16:31.073\r\nThis is a dream.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.449 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nAnd you're the one responsible.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.493 --\u003e 00:16:34.660\r\nA dream?\r\n\r\n00:16:35.036 --\u003e 00:16:36.412\r\nWhy do you think that?\r\n\r\n00:16:36.704 --\u003e 00:16:38.498\r\nI suspected it from the start.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.956 --\u003e 00:16:41.542\r\nI knew I was right when I\r\ntried to read the newspaper.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.876 --\u003e 00:16:43.711\r\nThe print didn't make sense.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.086 --\u003e 00:16:45.296\r\nYes?\r\n\r\n00:16:45.880 --\u003e 00:16:48.925\r\nThat's because reading is a function\r\nof the right side of the brain\r\n\r\n00:16:49.133 --\u003e 00:16:51.344\r\nwhile dreams come\r\nfrom the left side.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.677 --\u003e 00:16:54.180\r\nIt's impossible to read\r\nsomething in a dream.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.597 --\u003e 00:16:56.098\r\nGranting that's true,\r\n\r\n00:16:56.307 --\u003e 00:16:57.808\r\nhow is it my fault?\r\n\r\n00:16:58.017 --\u003e 00:16:59.393\r\nI can't explain it.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.810 --\u003e 00:17:01.437\r\nBut you're the key to this.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.604 --\u003e 00:17:03.064\r\nI knew you'd be here.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.231 --\u003e 00:17:05.483\r\nThis tower is part\r\nof my nightly patrol.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.108 --\u003e 00:17:08.152\r\nNow tell me what's going on.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.197 --\u003e 00:17:13.282\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe know you're up\r\nthere, Mr. Wayne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:13.616 --\u003e 00:17:15.368\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe don't want to hurt you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:15.451 --\u003e 00:17:17.453\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe just want to talk.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:21.499 --\u003e 00:17:22.667\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:57.034 --\u003e 00:17:58.536\r\nThe Mad Hatter?\r\n\r\n00:17:59.662 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nCongratulations are in order,\r\n\r\n00:18:01.789 --\u003e 00:18:03.916\r\nI suppose. And you're right.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.208 --\u003e 00:18:05.334\r\nThis is a dream,\r\n\r\n00:18:05.418 --\u003e 00:18:07.295\r\na very special dream.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.670 --\u003e 00:18:09.755\r\nThen you know\r\neverything about me.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.047 --\u003e 00:18:11.841\r\n\u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e do. (CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:11.924 --\u003e 00:18:14.135\r\nBut I'm only part of your dream.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.677 --\u003e 00:18:19.056\r\nThe mind-control apparatus\r\nreveals nothing to the real world.\r\n\r\n00:18:19.223 --\u003e 00:18:22.768\r\nIts purpose is to create\r\nan ideal world for you.\r\n\r\n00:18:23.561 --\u003e 00:18:25.813\r\nThen you're not the\r\nreal Mad Hatter.\r\n\r\n00:18:26.147 --\u003e 00:18:27.231\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.315 --\u003e 00:18:29.650\r\nJust a figment of\r\nyour imagination.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.192 --\u003e 00:18:32.778\r\nBut that doesn't\r\nmean I'm not real\r\n\r\n00:18:33.029 --\u003e 00:18:34.864\r\nin this dream world.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.781 --\u003e 00:18:38.117\r\nMake it stop. Bring me back.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.871 --\u003e 00:18:43.205\r\nI'm crushed.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.289 --\u003e 00:18:46.042\r\nYou don't like the fantasy\r\nworld I've created for you?\r\n\r\n00:18:46.125 --\u003e 00:18:47.460\r\nIt's not real.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.836 --\u003e 00:18:54.133\r\nAh. Are you the dreamer or\r\nmerely part of someone's dream?\r\n\r\n00:18:54.592 --\u003e 00:18:57.136\r\n(LAUGHING) That was\r\njust the question.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.219 --\u003e 00:18:59.472\r\nTweedledee put to Alice\r\nin Through the \u003ci\u003eLooking-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:59.555 --\u003e 00:19:01.891\r\nThis isn't some silly storybook!\r\n\r\n00:19:02.266 --\u003e 00:19:04.226\r\nAh, but it is.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.310 --\u003e 00:19:06.228\r\nIt's a beautiful story.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.312 --\u003e 00:19:08.814\r\nYou have love, wealth, a family.\r\n\r\n00:19:08.898 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\nAll you ever wanted.\r\n\r\n00:19:10.983 --\u003e 00:19:13.944\r\nYour own private Wonderland.\r\n\r\n00:19:15.571 --\u003e 00:19:16.739\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:17.114 --\u003e 00:19:18.491\r\nI won't live a lie.\r\n\r\n00:19:18.783 --\u003e 00:19:21.077\r\nNo matter how\r\nattractive you make it.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.494 --\u003e 00:19:24.080\r\nIt's a moot point, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.789 --\u003e 00:19:26.540\r\nThere's no way out of this.\r\n\r\n00:19:26.999 --\u003e 00:19:29.710\r\nTell me how to wake up, or I'll-\r\n\r\n00:19:29.877 --\u003e 00:19:32.588\r\nHa! You can't hurt a\r\ndream, my good fellow.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.047 --\u003e 00:19:34.882\r\nAnd you can't wake up.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.800 --\u003e 00:19:37.134\r\nStop fighting it.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.138 --\u003e 00:19:42.431\r\nYou see?\r\n\r\n00:19:42.682 --\u003e 00:19:44.850\r\nIn a moment,\r\nthe police will be here.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.101 --\u003e 00:19:48.479\r\nDo you want to spend the rest\r\nof your dream life in Arkham?\r\n\r\n00:19:48.562 --\u003e 00:19:50.231\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.273 --\u003e 00:19:52.608\r\nOpen up, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.036 --\u003e 00:20:05.287\r\nYou're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:20:05.371 --\u003e 00:20:06.664\r\nThere is a way out.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.956 --\u003e 00:20:08.749\r\n(STUTTERING) Now,\r\nwait just a minute.\r\n\r\n00:20:09.125 --\u003e 00:20:11.085\r\nYou don't want to\r\ndo anything foolish.\r\n\r\n00:20:11.377 --\u003e 00:20:12.920\r\n(THUDDING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.337 --\u003e 00:20:15.381\r\nThis isn't an ordinary dream.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.673 --\u003e 00:20:17.550\r\nWhat if you're wrong?\r\n\r\n00:20:17.883 --\u003e 00:20:21.178\r\nThen I'll see you\r\nin your nightmares.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.016 --\u003e 00:20:27.768\r\nMr. Wayne, no!\r\n\r\n00:20:35.234 --\u003e 00:20:36.235\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:36.318 --\u003e 00:20:37.737\r\n(MACHINERY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:20:40.489 --\u003e 00:20:41.782\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:41.866 --\u003e 00:20:43.743\r\nNo! You can't!\r\n\r\n00:20:45.870 --\u003e 00:20:46.871\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:48.748 --\u003e 00:20:49.749\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.420 --\u003e 00:20:55.880\r\nIt's impossible!\r\n\r\n00:20:56.213 --\u003e 00:20:59.508\r\nNo one's will is strong enough\r\nto escape my dream machine!\r\n\r\n00:21:00.259 --\u003e 00:21:01.469\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\n00:21:02.261 --\u003e 00:21:04.180\r\nWhy did you do it?\r\n\r\n00:21:04.430 --\u003e 00:21:06.724\r\nYou, of all people,\r\n\r\n00:21:06.974 --\u003e 00:21:09.643\r\nhave the gall to ask me that?\r\n\r\n00:21:10.644 --\u003e 00:21:12.813\r\nYou ruined my life!\r\n\r\n00:21:13.481 --\u003e 00:21:17.693\r\nI was willing to give you\r\nwhatever life you wanted\r\n\r\n00:21:18.527 --\u003e 00:21:20.905\r\njust to keep you out of mine.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.206 --\u003e 00:21:32.333\r\nSomething for the lab\r\nboys to play with.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.416 --\u003e 00:21:33.751\r\nAny idea what it is?\r\n\r\n00:21:34.251 --\u003e 00:21:35.252\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.920 --\u003e 00:21:38.756\r\nThe stuff that\r\ndreams are made of.\r\n\r\n00:21:50.935 --\u003e 00:21:52.937\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:21.006 --\u003e 00:22:22.007\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E27 - The Underdwellers (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.672 --\u003e 00:00:07.382\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:29.631 --\u003e 00:01:33.343\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhoever jumps first is chicken.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:47.149 --\u003e 00:01:48.400\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.278 --\u003e 00:01:52.696\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:01:53.322 --\u003e 00:01:56.241\r\n(LAUGHS BOISTEROUSLY) I\r\nknew you'd chicken out.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.452 --\u003e 00:01:59.911\r\nHuh? (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:02.748 --\u003e 00:02:05.542\r\n(GRUNTS, GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:08.837 --\u003e 00:02:11.506\r\n(SCREAMING \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PANIC)\r\n\r\n00:02:12.132 --\u003e 00:02:14.009\r\n(TRAIN RUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.682 --\u003e 00:02:23.393\r\nYou play chicken long\r\nenough, you fry.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.823 --\u003e 00:02:38.992\r\n(CAR HORNS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.970 --\u003e 00:03:00.222\r\nMy purse!\r\n\r\n00:03:00.347 --\u003e 00:03:01.973\r\nHelp! A thief!\r\n\r\n00:03:07.854 --\u003e 00:03:10.774\r\nI'm telling you,\r\nit was a leprechaun.\r\n\r\n00:03:11.066 --\u003e 00:03:15.570\r\nReally, ma'am? You expect me to\r\nbelieve you saw a little green man?\r\n\r\n00:03:17.114 --\u003e 00:03:18.156\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:03:20.617 --\u003e 00:03:21.743\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:03:24.162 --\u003e 00:03:25.622\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:36.299 --\u003e 00:03:38.093\r\nBOTH: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:03:50.397 --\u003e 00:03:52.274\r\nLeprechauns and batmen...\r\n\r\n00:03:52.733 --\u003e 00:03:54.276\r\nWhat's Gotham coming to?\r\n\r\n00:03:57.946 --\u003e 00:03:59.322\r\nLeprechauns?\r\n\r\n00:04:01.992 --\u003e 00:04:03.577\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:05.203 --\u003e 00:04:06.663\r\nBRUCE: Leprechauns, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.830 --\u003e 00:04:08.790\r\n(CLASSICAL MUSIC\r\nPLAYING ON RADIO)\r\n\r\n00:04:08.874 --\u003e 00:04:10.667\r\n- Pardon?\r\n- (BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:10.792 --\u003e 00:04:11.793\r\n(MUSIC STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:12.627 --\u003e 00:04:16.590\r\n- Not in the mood for Brahms, are we?\r\n- You think I'm crazy, don't you?\r\n\r\n00:04:17.132 --\u003e 00:04:18.800\r\nIn what sense, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:04:19.259 --\u003e 00:04:22.679\r\nSeriously, you don't\r\nbelieve I saw a leprechaun.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.180 --\u003e 00:04:25.140\r\n(CHUCKLES) Did he\r\nhave a pot of gold?\r\n\r\n00:04:25.807 --\u003e 00:04:28.185\r\nSir,\r\nI believe you saw something.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.769 --\u003e 00:04:30.395\r\nMaybe I need a rest.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.771 --\u003e 00:04:33.565\r\nI do believe a break\r\nfrom Wayne Enterprises\r\n\r\n00:04:33.648 --\u003e 00:04:35.692\r\nand crime fighting\r\nwould do wonders.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.026 --\u003e 00:04:38.278\r\nPerhaps a vacation.\r\nA little golf?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.361 --\u003e 00:04:39.529\r\nSounds boring.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.780 --\u003e 00:04:40.906\r\nIn the Bahamas?\r\n\r\n00:04:41.031 --\u003e 00:04:42.699\r\nHot and boring.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.283 --\u003e 00:04:46.286\r\nNo, Alfred,\r\nI think this is a job for Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.454 --\u003e 00:04:50.916\r\nYou have a fine flair\r\nfor dramatics, sir.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.124 --\u003e 00:04:53.752\r\nWhy, thank you, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.085 --\u003e 00:04:56.171\r\n(COMPUTER CLICKING, BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:57.005 --\u003e 00:04:58.107\r\nALFRED: The theater district?\r\n\r\n00:04:58.131 --\u003e 00:05:01.176\r\nYes, I think it's\r\ntime for an encore.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.341 --\u003e 00:05:43.718\r\n(come JINGLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:55.063 --\u003e 00:05:56.481\r\n(CRIES OUT \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:06:00.652 --\u003e 00:06:03.280\r\n(BELL CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:37.272 --\u003e 00:06:41.109\r\n(SHOUTS) Hurry up!\r\nHurry. Hurry. Hurry.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.234 --\u003e 00:06:46.448\r\nAre you ready for your lessons?\r\nYes? I think so. I think so.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.531 --\u003e 00:06:51.494\r\nWell, so am I. Your teacher.\r\nYour leader. Your king.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.578 --\u003e 00:06:53.705\r\nReady, I am. Yes.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.080 --\u003e 00:06:57.000\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:00.253 --\u003e 00:07:04.925\r\nLesson number one is...\r\n(SHOUTS) No talking!\r\n\r\n00:07:06.718 --\u003e 00:07:09.137\r\nChildren are to be\r\nseen and not heard.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.804 --\u003e 00:07:13.058\r\nWe are the Underdwellers.\r\nWe are the silent ones.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.141 --\u003e 00:07:16.895\r\nWe follow the invisible creed.\r\nBut, but, but...\r\n\r\n00:07:17.020 --\u003e 00:07:21.816\r\nSomeone was talking. You.\r\nYou, you, you were heard.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.900 --\u003e 00:07:24.819\r\nAnd we all know the\r\npunishment for talking.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.903 --\u003e 00:07:26.988\r\nDon't we, boys and girls?\r\n\r\n00:07:32.744 --\u003e 00:07:35.747\r\nI think he needs\r\nto see the light.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.122 --\u003e 00:07:38.833\r\nYes, I do.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.376 --\u003e 00:07:44.005\r\nA few hours in the light\r\nwill make Jack a bright boy.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.172 --\u003e 00:07:45.256\r\n(DOOR CLANGS)\r\n\r\n00:07:45.340 --\u003e 00:07:50.595\r\nAnd now, lesson two.\r\n(SHOUTS) All of you up to the streets!\r\n\r\n00:07:50.679 --\u003e 00:07:55.141\r\nBring back pretties,\r\nlots and lots of pretties for your king.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.725 --\u003e 00:07:57.352\r\n(SHOUTS) Now!\r\n\r\n00:08:00.438 --\u003e 00:08:02.941\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:08:28.049 --\u003e 00:08:29.759\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:33.430\r\nI thought so.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.763 --\u003e 00:08:35.390\r\n(DOOR SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.953 --\u003e 00:08:59.080\r\n(TRAIN RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.506 --\u003e 00:09:10.008\r\nDead bolt.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.093 --\u003e 00:09:13.720\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.280 --\u003e 00:09:35.366\r\n(CLINKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:58.723 --\u003e 00:10:01.142\r\nJust a second, son.\r\nI'm not going to hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.309 --\u003e 00:10:02.936\r\n(TRAIN HORN BLARES)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.019 --\u003e 00:10:04.187\r\nWait.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.821 --\u003e 00:10:14.989\r\n(HORN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:10:34.300 --\u003e 00:10:35.301\r\nOpen.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.295 --\u003e 00:11:12.255\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:19.137 --\u003e 00:11:20.555\r\nGood evening, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.889 --\u003e 00:11:21.931\r\nSir.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.557 --\u003e 00:11:25.101\r\nMight this wee one\r\nbe a leprechaun?\r\n\r\n00:11:25.476 --\u003e 00:11:29.689\r\nThis, Alfred, is our guest.\r\nI'd like you to take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.856 --\u003e 00:11:33.193\r\nMe? But I know\r\nnothing of children.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.526 --\u003e 00:11:34.777\r\nYou'll do fine.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.861 --\u003e 00:11:36.863\r\nFeed him,\r\nclean him and put him to bed.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.988 --\u003e 00:11:38.531\r\nWell, perhaps.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.324 --\u003e 00:11:40.658\r\nNot in that order.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.082 --\u003e 00:11:50.376\r\nRise and shine,\r\nmaster leprechaun.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.460 --\u003e 00:11:52.170\r\nTime to be up and about.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.306 --\u003e 00:12:05.183\r\nFirst a bath, don't you think?\r\n\r\n00:12:07.852 --\u003e 00:12:08.895\r\nDo you have a name?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.064 --\u003e 00:12:14.359\r\nI hope you don't expect\r\nme to guess it. Fred?\r\n\r\n00:12:16.527 --\u003e 00:12:18.529\r\nPete? Leon?\r\n\r\n00:12:19.030 --\u003e 00:12:21.658\r\nHow about a little help?\r\nCan you talk?\r\n\r\n00:12:21.741 --\u003e 00:12:23.076\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:23.660 --\u003e 00:12:26.246\r\nGotcha. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:26.537 --\u003e 00:12:29.123\r\nYou'll feel much better\r\nwhen you're clean.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.250 --\u003e 00:12:32.335\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:35.213 --\u003e 00:12:37.507\r\nAnd smell better too, I trust.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.191 --\u003e 00:12:58.611\r\nFrog, the rolls, if you please.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.779 --\u003e 00:13:01.531\r\nYou're not Frog.\r\n\r\n00:13:03.199 --\u003e 00:13:04.617\r\nWhere is he?\r\n\r\n00:13:05.368 --\u003e 00:13:08.621\r\nHe's not here! Not here!\r\n\r\n00:13:08.705 --\u003e 00:13:13.126\r\nAnd after all I've done for you\r\nungrateful little monsters...\r\n\r\n00:13:13.376 --\u003e 00:13:15.920\r\nI took you in when nobody\r\nelse would have you.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.004 --\u003e 00:13:18.881\r\nIt is I who care for you.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.007 --\u003e 00:13:21.676\r\nI who provide for you,\r\n\r\n00:13:21.759 --\u003e 00:13:26.180\r\nand only I who knows\r\nwhat's good for you!\r\n\r\n00:13:26.264 --\u003e 00:13:29.058\r\nWould you rather I sent\r\nyou back into the light?\r\n\r\n00:13:29.517 --\u003e 00:13:32.979\r\nBack to those who hurt\r\nyou and sent you away?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.857 --\u003e 00:13:38.901\r\nThere will be nothing to\r\neat until Frog is found!\r\n\r\n00:13:39.736 --\u003e 00:13:43.281\r\n(SHOUTING) Now, out with you.\r\nOut with you!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.040 --\u003e 00:13:55.126\r\nNow, now. Let's start with\r\nsome basic table manners.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.376 --\u003e 00:13:58.212\r\nKnife, fork, spoon.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.299 --\u003e 00:14:04.010\r\nOh, dear, I could've sworn I...\r\n\r\n00:14:04.302 --\u003e 00:14:07.096\r\nNo matter.\r\nAs they say, \"Dig in.\"\r\n\r\n00:14:07.555 --\u003e 00:14:10.975\r\n(MUNCHING AUDIBLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:12.977 --\u003e 00:14:14.395\r\nI wash, you dry.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.855 --\u003e 00:14:19.650\r\nNow then, doesn't it feel\r\ngood to be doing honest work?\r\n\r\n00:14:22.320 --\u003e 00:14:23.696\r\nWhat? Wait!\r\n\r\n00:14:25.615 --\u003e 00:14:26.616\r\nCharming.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.625 --\u003e 00:14:37.001\r\n(ALFRED SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:14:38.711 --\u003e 00:14:40.463\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:44.550 --\u003e 00:14:47.178\r\nALFRED: Now, see here,\r\nwe're supposed to be working.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.553 --\u003e 00:14:49.138\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.222 --\u003e 00:14:50.932\r\nI wonder if I was\r\nthat much trouble.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.364 --\u003e 00:15:09.450\r\nOh, dear.\r\nThat is extremely dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.742 --\u003e 00:15:11.994\r\nYou must put it down\r\nbefore you hurt someone.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.496 --\u003e 00:15:16.833\r\nChildren and guns do not\r\nmix, ever.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.375 --\u003e 00:15:20.753\r\nIt wasn't loaded,\r\nbut it could have been.\r\n\r\n00:15:21.337 --\u003e 00:15:22.964\r\nI need your help.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.048 --\u003e 00:15:25.550\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.288 --\u003e 00:15:56.497\r\nEvidence.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.415 --\u003e 00:16:01.002\r\n(CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:02.795 --\u003e 00:16:03.921\r\nWhere is he?\r\n\r\n00:16:13.931 --\u003e 00:16:16.058\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:30.072 --\u003e 00:16:32.575\r\n(BELL CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.549 --\u003e 00:16:53.054\r\nI don't know what kind of barbarian\r\ndid this to you, but it's over.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.387 --\u003e 00:16:56.224\r\nAnd from now on you'll be\r\ntreated like human beings.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.307 --\u003e 00:16:59.268\r\nI think we'll have\r\nsomething to say about that.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.352 --\u003e 00:17:02.355\r\n- (CROCODILES GROWLING)\r\n- Yes, we will.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.234 --\u003e 00:17:08.569\r\nWelcome our guests.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.494 --\u003e 00:17:19.539\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:19.789 --\u003e 00:17:22.083\r\n(BELL CLANGS)\r\n\r\n00:17:42.895 --\u003e 00:17:46.148\r\nCrush him!\r\nDestroy that costumed freak.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.529 --\u003e 00:17:53.489\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.958 --\u003e 00:18:05.835\r\n(SCREAMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e ANGER)\r\n\r\n00:18:05.918 --\u003e 00:18:08.588\r\nI'll show you who's the\r\nruler of this kingdom.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.713 --\u003e 00:18:09.964\r\nPut him down.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.631 --\u003e 00:18:14.677\r\n- Now!\r\n- It's feeding time for my pretties.\r\n\r\n00:18:17.972 --\u003e 00:18:19.390\r\n(GROWLS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e ANGER)\r\n\r\n00:18:36.198 --\u003e 00:18:37.825\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:38.451 --\u003e 00:18:40.745\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:50.755 --\u003e 00:18:52.089\r\nGreat.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.884 --\u003e 00:18:57.011\r\nAnd I thought you\r\nwere endangered.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.219 --\u003e 00:19:00.348\r\nBravo. Bravo.\r\n\r\n00:19:01.057 --\u003e 00:19:04.894\r\nYou've caused me great\r\ndistress, you evil bat.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.977 --\u003e 00:19:06.771\r\nYes. Yes. Yes, you have.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.937 --\u003e 00:19:12.318\r\nYou've hurt my pretty pets,\r\nand you've frightened my beloved children.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.777 --\u003e 00:19:16.155\r\n- Beloved children?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.656 --\u003e 00:19:20.826\r\nI feed them, I clothe\r\nthem, I discipline them,\r\n\r\n00:19:20.951 --\u003e 00:19:23.245\r\nand I teach them a trade.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.871 --\u003e 00:19:29.001\r\nAnd now I will\r\nteach you something.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.044 --\u003e 00:19:31.754\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:36.967 --\u003e 00:19:38.260\r\nGrab my hand!\r\n\r\n00:19:38.594 --\u003e 00:19:40.971\r\n(SHOUTS) Never!\r\n\r\n00:19:47.853 --\u003e 00:19:50.523\r\nA gruesome fate\r\nfor a gruesome man.\r\n\r\n00:19:50.648 --\u003e 00:19:52.483\r\n(SEWER KING LAUGHS MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:19:52.566 --\u003e 00:19:54.318\r\nSEWER KING: I rather enjoyed it.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.443 --\u003e 00:19:58.489\r\nI told you, they're my pretties.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.073 --\u003e 00:20:02.368\r\n(CHUCKLES) Have a nice swim.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.868 --\u003e 00:20:06.205\r\n(SEWER KING LAUGHING MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.631 --\u003e 00:20:17.007\r\nLater.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.568 --\u003e 00:20:37.319\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.032 --\u003e 00:20:43.951\r\nWhat? You!\r\n\r\n00:20:49.373 --\u003e 00:20:52.126\r\n(GRUNTS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.086 --\u003e 00:20:55.796\r\n(TRAIN HORN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:21:03.596 --\u003e 00:21:06.474\r\nwhy? Why? Why?\r\n\r\n00:21:06.557 --\u003e 00:21:09.518\r\nI don't pass sentence.\r\nThat's for the courts.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.102 --\u003e 00:21:11.479\r\nBut this time...\r\n\r\n00:21:12.104 --\u003e 00:21:17.067\r\nThis time I am sorely\r\ntempted to do the job myself.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.540 --\u003e 00:21:32.583\r\nThe light.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.834 --\u003e 00:21:34.919\r\nThe light.\r\n\r\n00:21:56.857 --\u003e 00:21:58.651\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.464 --\u003e 00:22:21.465\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E28 - Night of The Ninja (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.881 --\u003e 00:00:07.883\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.222 --\u003e 00:01:38.640\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.350 --\u003e 00:01:41.560\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:01:42.144 --\u003e 00:01:43.395\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:01:44.187 --\u003e 00:01:45.188\r\nWhat the...\r\n\r\n00:02:05.167 --\u003e 00:02:06.668\r\n(SOFT BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:18.847 --\u003e 00:02:19.973\r\nNINJA: Excellent.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.098 --\u003e 00:02:21.141\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:02:29.107 --\u003e 00:02:30.108\r\nHey, you. Stop!\r\n\r\n00:02:43.163 --\u003e 00:02:44.373\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:55.759 --\u003e 00:02:56.927\r\n(SWORD sucnue)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.933 --\u003e 00:03:03.934\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:05.769 --\u003e 00:03:06.770\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:03:15.070 --\u003e 00:03:16.110\r\nBRUCE: When you are ready.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.407 --\u003e 00:03:19.700\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:19.783 --\u003e 00:03:20.992\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.163 --\u003e 00:03:26.164\r\nAgain.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.835 --\u003e 00:03:32.003\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:32.796 --\u003e 00:03:35.257\r\n(PETULANTLY) Sorry,\r\nsome of us aren't perfect.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.924 --\u003e 00:03:37.259\r\nALFRED: Master Bruce, I'm afraid\r\n\r\n00:03:37.342 --\u003e 00:03:40.178\r\nthere's been another robbery\r\nof a Wayne Enterprises company.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.846 --\u003e 00:03:42.848\r\nThat's the sixth one\r\nin less than two weeks.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.515 --\u003e 00:03:44.558\r\nSeventh.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.683 --\u003e 00:03:45.684\r\nWhere, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:03:47.018 --\u003e 00:03:48.246\r\nNIGHT MANAGER: I didn't see him.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.270 --\u003e 00:03:49.604\r\nI was doing the closing report.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.771 --\u003e 00:03:51.691\r\nThe next thing I knew,\r\nI woke up with a headache.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.940 --\u003e 00:03:53.442\r\nGuard said he was\r\ndressed in black.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.900 --\u003e 00:03:54.943\r\nSame guy all right.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.233\r\nGood morning, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.612 --\u003e 00:03:58.613\r\nI wish.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.697 --\u003e 00:04:00.657\r\nHe left something behind this\r\ntime, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.450 --\u003e 00:04:02.451\r\nDeadly little thing.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.868 --\u003e 00:04:03.869\r\nMean anything to you?\r\n\r\n00:04:05.871 --\u003e 00:04:07.873\r\nDon't touch it.\r\nYou'll break the evidence chain.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.344 --\u003e 00:04:23.805\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:28.894 --\u003e 00:04:29.895\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:34.566 --\u003e 00:04:35.567\r\nThe match is over.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.776 --\u003e 00:04:37.110\r\nKyodai is the victor.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.153 --\u003e 00:04:39.905\r\nDon't be depressed, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.489 --\u003e 00:04:44.034\r\nYou're not bad for a rich\r\nman's pampered son. (CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:47.370 --\u003e 00:04:48.663\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:48.747 --\u003e 00:04:50.081\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:51.708 --\u003e 00:04:54.127\r\nThere's always someone\r\nbetter, Kyodai Ken.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.336 --\u003e 00:04:56.213\r\nNow apologize for your remark.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.399 --\u003e 00:05:17.901\r\nSUMMER: Mr. Wayne. Mr. Wayne!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.277 --\u003e 00:05:20.362\r\nDo you have any idea\r\n\r\n00:05:20.445 --\u003e 00:05:23.615\r\nwhy someone has been robbing\r\nand sabotaging your businesses?\r\n\r\n00:05:23.949 --\u003e 00:05:25.325\r\nTwo buildings burned down,\r\n\r\n00:05:25.408 --\u003e 00:05:26.409\r\nanother blown up.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.493 --\u003e 00:05:28.370\r\nThis one's computer\r\nsystem's wrecked.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.703 --\u003e 00:05:30.103\r\nMiss Gleeson,\r\nhow do you know that?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.330 --\u003e 00:05:32.666\r\nA good reporter has\r\nsources, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.874 --\u003e 00:05:34.376\r\nAny comment, Mr. Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:05:35.377 --\u003e 00:05:36.461\r\nIf you'll excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.465 --\u003e 00:05:43.176\r\nHmph. (ANGRILY) You can't\r\nignore the press, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.347 --\u003e 00:05:49.224\r\nDICK: Hey, Bruce, wait up.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.976 --\u003e 00:05:52.336\r\nListen,\r\nit will only take a minute\r\n\r\n00:05:52.394 --\u003e 00:05:53.436\r\nto get into my costume.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.895 --\u003e 00:05:55.021\r\nNot this time, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.984 --\u003e 00:06:00.944\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:06:03.363 --\u003e 00:06:04.364\r\nWhat's with him?\r\n\r\n00:06:04.698 --\u003e 00:06:05.782\r\nBat got his tongue?\r\n\r\n00:06:06.116 --\u003e 00:06:07.242\r\nYou know Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.450 --\u003e 00:06:09.244\r\nHe's not one to\r\ndiscuss his feelings.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.536 --\u003e 00:06:10.662\r\nIsn't that the truth.\r\n\r\n00:06:11.329 --\u003e 00:06:12.581\r\nSomething's eating him, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.164 --\u003e 00:06:14.249\r\nI don't know what.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.958 --\u003e 00:06:15.959\r\nYet.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.015 --\u003e 00:06:31.474\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:41.151 --\u003e 00:06:43.153\r\nYORU: You practice\r\nas a man obsessed.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.195 --\u003e 00:06:45.196\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:55.999 --\u003e 00:06:58.501\r\nI'm not good enough, Yoru Sensei.\r\nI lost!\r\n\r\n00:06:59.002 --\u003e 00:07:01.212\r\nEveryone loses now and again.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.630 --\u003e 00:07:03.340\r\nI have to be the best there is,\r\n\r\n00:07:03.590 --\u003e 00:07:04.716\r\nno matter what it takes!\r\n\r\n00:07:05.508 --\u003e 00:07:08.887\r\nDefeat can be more\r\ninstructive than victory.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.175 --\u003e 00:07:49.970\r\nNINJA: So, the famous Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.178 --\u003e 00:07:52.055\r\nI am honored.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.389 --\u003e 00:07:54.683\r\nHowever,\r\nmy business is not with you.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.141 --\u003e 00:07:56.977\r\nLeave and you may live.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.687 --\u003e 00:08:00.146\r\nStay and...\r\n\r\n00:08:12.450 --\u003e 00:08:15.870\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:35.432 --\u003e 00:08:36.766\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:38.018 --\u003e 00:08:39.227\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:51.156 --\u003e 00:08:52.490\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.870 --\u003e 00:08:58.872\r\n- (PROJECTILE RICOCHETING)\r\n- (NINJA GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:01.916 --\u003e 00:09:03.043\r\nListen, dipstick.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.168 --\u003e 00:09:04.461\r\nBatman's my pal.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.711 --\u003e 00:09:06.046\r\nHe can be a major jerk,\r\n\r\n00:09:06.129 --\u003e 00:09:07.213\r\nbut you gotta love him.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.464 --\u003e 00:09:10.216\r\nAnd nobody tries to fillet\r\nhim when I'm around.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.259 --\u003e 00:09:12.927\r\n(BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:13.011 --\u003e 00:09:14.596\r\nNINJA: Another time then.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.479 --\u003e 00:09:23.813\r\n(EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.487 --\u003e 00:09:31.488\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:43.625 --\u003e 00:09:45.210\r\nHow does he do that?\r\n\r\n00:09:48.421 --\u003e 00:09:49.547\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:49.631 --\u003e 00:09:51.341\r\n- You okay?\r\n- I'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.633 --\u003e 00:09:53.802\r\nCome on.\r\nThere's nothing more to do here.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.345 --\u003e 00:09:57.597\r\n\"Thanks for saving my\r\nbacon, Robin.\"\r\n\r\n00:09:57.889 --\u003e 00:09:59.849\r\n\"Hey, no problemo, Batman.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:05.313 --\u003e 00:10:07.398\r\nI thought samurai live\r\nby a code of honor.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.816 --\u003e 00:10:10.193\r\nThat gas gun wasn't\r\nexactly according to Hoyle.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.485 --\u003e 00:10:11.611\r\nHe's not samurai.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.945 --\u003e 00:10:14.614\r\nHe's ninja.\r\nThey're spies and assassins.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.989 --\u003e 00:10:16.549\r\nTheir only code is\r\nto get the job done.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.367 --\u003e 00:10:18.493\r\nI know him.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.743 --\u003e 00:10:19.744\r\nSay what?\r\n\r\n00:10:22.413 --\u003e 00:10:24.499\r\nHe and Bruce Wayne were\r\nstudents together in Japan,\r\n\r\n00:10:24.874 --\u003e 00:10:26.084\r\na long time ago.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.167 --\u003e 00:10:28.002\r\nHis name is Kyodai Ken.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.878 --\u003e 00:10:29.921\r\nHe was good.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.004 --\u003e 00:10:31.089\r\nYeah? How good?\r\n\r\n00:10:31.297 --\u003e 00:10:32.340\r\nGood.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.466 --\u003e 00:10:34.509\r\nI see.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.760 --\u003e 00:10:37.428\r\nI'm sure there is\r\nmore to these crimes\r\n\r\n00:10:37.512 --\u003e 00:10:39.389\r\nagainst Bruce Wayne\r\nthan meets the eye.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.722 --\u003e 00:10:41.850\r\nWhat do we know about the\r\nBruce, after all?\r\n\r\n00:10:41.933 --\u003e 00:10:43.601\r\nOne of the richest\r\nmen on the planet,\r\n\r\n00:10:43.935 --\u003e 00:10:45.979\r\nbut he comes off like\r\nthe ultimate Boy Scout.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.521 --\u003e 00:10:48.148\r\nI think I'll just pop over\r\n\r\n00:10:48.231 --\u003e 00:10:50.567\r\nto the Wayne charities\r\nreception tonight\r\n\r\n00:10:51.109 --\u003e 00:10:52.777\r\nand see if I can't\r\nget some answers.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.070 --\u003e 00:10:55.071\r\nBe careful, Summer.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.321 --\u003e 00:10:56.948\r\nWayne's got mondo\r\nclout in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.365 --\u003e 00:10:58.366\r\nHey, Harry,\r\n\r\n00:10:58.616 --\u003e 00:10:59.742\r\nI'm a big girl.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.372 --\u003e 00:11:07.417\r\nAlfred, do you know anything\r\nabout Bruce's training in Japan?\r\n\r\n00:11:07.792 --\u003e 00:11:09.210\r\nOf course, dear boy.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.544 --\u003e 00:11:11.629\r\nI was there. Lovely country.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.880 --\u003e 00:11:13.298\r\nI especially like the tea.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.631 --\u003e 00:11:15.925\r\nYou ever hear of somebody\r\nnamed Kyodai Ken?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.134 --\u003e 00:11:17.343\r\nOh, indeed.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.510 --\u003e 00:11:20.013\r\nHe was the only student\r\nat the martial art school\r\n\r\n00:11:20.096 --\u003e 00:11:22.473\r\nwho could consistently\r\ndefeat Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.932 --\u003e 00:11:24.350\r\nA bad egg, that one.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.475 --\u003e 00:11:27.353\r\nI think Bruce is worried\r\nhe can't take this ninja.\r\n\r\n00:11:27.854 --\u003e 00:11:29.105\r\nHe won't admit it, of course.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.564 --\u003e 00:11:31.774\r\nHe never admits\r\nfears, Master Dick.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.858 --\u003e 00:11:33.443\r\nHaven't you learned that by now?\r\n\r\n00:11:34.068 --\u003e 00:11:35.069\r\n(BOTH GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:11:38.698 --\u003e 00:11:39.699\r\nAh, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.782 --\u003e 00:11:40.783\r\n(STAMMERING) l...\r\n\r\n00:11:41.743 --\u003e 00:11:42.869\r\nI'll be at the museum.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.286 --\u003e 00:11:44.662\r\nI should be back by midnight.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.123 --\u003e 00:11:48.208\r\nDo you think he heard us?\r\n\r\n00:11:48.499 --\u003e 00:11:49.542\r\nWho can tell?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.128 --\u003e 00:11:54.088\r\n(CLASSICAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:12:31.251 --\u003e 00:12:32.252\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:32.335 --\u003e 00:12:34.712\r\nGood thing I decided\r\nto practice tonight.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.171 --\u003e 00:12:37.632\r\nYoru Sensei would hate\r\nto lose that blade.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.174 --\u003e 00:12:39.467\r\nIt's 500 years old.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.759 --\u003e 00:12:41.719\r\nTrue, and worth a fortune.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.136 --\u003e 00:12:44.097\r\nI don't need it to take care of\r\nyou, Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.898 --\u003e 00:12:55.525\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:55.608 --\u003e 00:12:56.609\r\nYORU: (YELLING) Stop!\r\n\r\n00:12:59.362 --\u003e 00:13:01.489\r\nYou have dishonored the\r\ndojo, Kyodai.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.073 --\u003e 00:13:04.117\r\nYou no longer have\r\nany place here.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.325 --\u003e 00:13:05.368\r\nGo!\r\n\r\n00:13:06.369 --\u003e 00:13:08.288\r\nYou will pay for\r\nthis, rich man's son.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.788 --\u003e 00:13:10.456\r\nI'll take all that\r\nyou hold dear,\r\n\r\n00:13:10.665 --\u003e 00:13:12.583\r\nand then I will destroy you!\r\n\r\n00:13:43.740 --\u003e 00:13:45.420\r\nWhy have you been\r\nfollowing me all evening?\r\n\r\n00:13:45.742 --\u003e 00:13:46.743\r\nHow did you... Look.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.160 --\u003e 00:13:48.578\r\nI know you don't like me much.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.995 --\u003e 00:13:50.163\r\nBut I have a job to do.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.580 --\u003e 00:13:51.789\r\nIt's late, Miss Gleeson.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.008 --\u003e 00:14:03.468\r\nI did some research, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.593 --\u003e 00:14:05.428\r\nI know you spent\r\nsome time in Japan.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.678 --\u003e 00:14:08.056\r\nDo you think this ninja\r\nperson is connected to that?\r\n\r\n00:14:08.806 --\u003e 00:14:10.975\r\n- Have a nice trip, Mr. Wayne.\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.523 --\u003e 00:14:18.900\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:21.778 --\u003e 00:14:22.779\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:14:34.415 --\u003e 00:14:36.417\r\n(BATS SQUEAKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.964 --\u003e 00:14:44.592\r\nYou really think this is a good\r\nidea, Master Dick?\r\n\r\n00:14:44.801 --\u003e 00:14:46.636\r\nBruce is hours overdue, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.719 --\u003e 00:14:47.762\r\nIt's not like him.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.137 --\u003e 00:14:49.347\r\nThere's a tracker in his car.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.432 --\u003e 00:14:53.017\r\nI'll feel better\r\nonce I check it out.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.649 --\u003e 00:15:00.691\r\nGodspeed, lad.\r\n\r\n00:15:10.535 --\u003e 00:15:12.495\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.247 --\u003e 00:15:15.248\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:15:15.331 --\u003e 00:15:16.624\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:15:17.166 --\u003e 00:15:18.459\r\nNINJA: Ah, the rich man awakens.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.918 --\u003e 00:15:20.294\r\nRemember me?\r\n\r\n00:15:21.921 --\u003e 00:15:23.673\r\nI remember you, Kyodai.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.756 --\u003e 00:15:26.134\r\nWell, you should recall\r\nthe man you ruined.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.843 --\u003e 00:15:29.804\r\nI was forced to become a thief\r\nafter I was cast out of the dojo.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.263 --\u003e 00:15:31.514\r\nAs I remember it,\r\n\r\n00:15:31.597 --\u003e 00:15:34.600\r\nbeing a thief was what got you\r\nthrown out in the first place.\r\n\r\n00:15:35.059 --\u003e 00:15:38.521\r\nOf course, you never had to\r\nworry about money, Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.604 --\u003e 00:15:41.065\r\nA society parasite\r\nfeeding off others.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:43.359\r\nFlabby, soft, weak.\r\n\r\n00:15:44.068 --\u003e 00:15:46.362\r\nIt is too easy to defeat you.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.071 --\u003e 00:15:49.824\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:49.907 --\u003e 00:15:51.159\r\nWhere am I?\r\n\r\n00:15:52.326 --\u003e 00:15:53.453\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:53.536 --\u003e 00:15:55.538\r\nI've stolen your bank\r\ncodes at each theft.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.872 --\u003e 00:15:57.373\r\nSoon I will have them all.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.790 --\u003e 00:16:01.043\r\nThen I'll transfer your\r\nmoney to my own accounts.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.127 --\u003e 00:16:02.336\r\nI don't get it.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.837 --\u003e 00:16:05.256\r\nYou mean you're nothing\r\nbut a common thief?\r\n\r\n00:16:06.007 --\u003e 00:16:08.676\r\n(LAUGHING) Not a common\r\nthief, woman.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.010 --\u003e 00:16:11.053\r\nA great thief. The best.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.137 --\u003e 00:16:14.015\r\nAnd now the game\r\nis about to end.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.772\r\n(BOTH GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:29.614 --\u003e 00:16:32.366\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.450 --\u003e 00:16:33.618\r\nAh, way to go, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.202 --\u003e 00:16:35.745\r\nMaster crime fighter. (SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.413 --\u003e 00:16:38.748\r\n(ALARM CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.831 --\u003e 00:16:41.626\r\nIt appears we have\r\nan unexpected guest.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.376 --\u003e 00:16:43.377\r\nI'll be back.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.641 --\u003e 00:16:58.893\r\nNINJA: Isn't it past your\r\nbedtime, boy?\r\n\r\n00:16:58.976 --\u003e 00:17:01.103\r\nLet's just see who's\r\ngoing sleepy-by\r\n\r\n00:17:01.187 --\u003e 00:17:02.730\r\nin the next couple of\r\nminutes, huh?\r\n\r\n00:17:04.398 --\u003e 00:17:05.858\r\nNINJA: This isn't the\r\nmovies, boy.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.942 --\u003e 00:17:07.527\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:08.569 --\u003e 00:17:09.862\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:13.074 --\u003e 00:17:15.743\r\nEnough of this.\r\nI have business I must attend to.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.965 --\u003e 00:17:29.966\r\n(NINJA YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:06.210 --\u003e 00:18:08.170\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- (CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.671 --\u003e 00:18:11.465\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.392 --\u003e 00:18:22.393\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:18:34.280 --\u003e 00:18:35.948\r\nNINJA: Oh, really?\r\n\r\n00:18:50.630 --\u003e 00:18:52.632\r\n- (NINJA YELLING)\r\n- (THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:18:54.842 --\u003e 00:18:56.594\r\nYou have gone soft, Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.677 --\u003e 00:18:59.096\r\nEven a white belt\r\ncould avoid that throw.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.973 --\u003e 00:19:02.308\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:02.516 --\u003e 00:19:04.185\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n- (THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:19:04.268 --\u003e 00:19:05.811\r\nTired, Mr. Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:19:05.895 --\u003e 00:19:07.897\r\nI haven't even\r\nbroken a sweat yet.\r\n\r\n00:19:08.522 --\u003e 00:19:09.523\r\nGet up!\r\n\r\n00:19:12.943 --\u003e 00:19:14.320\r\n(SOFTLY) Hang in there, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.490 --\u003e 00:19:18.741\r\n(BRUCE GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.824 --\u003e 00:19:21.994\r\nStop it! Can't you see\r\nhe's no match for you?\r\n\r\n00:19:22.078 --\u003e 00:19:23.788\r\nHe never was.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.871 --\u003e 00:19:24.914\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:26.791 --\u003e 00:19:29.418\r\n(BOTH YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:30.211 --\u003e 00:19:31.212\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:19:34.924 --\u003e 00:19:37.677\r\n(SIGHS) I have had enough\r\nexercise for one night.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.260 --\u003e 00:19:39.970\r\nNow it ends, Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.978 --\u003e 00:19:49.021\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:49.105 --\u003e 00:19:50.106\r\nSUMMER: Hey!\r\n\r\n00:20:02.868 --\u003e 00:20:04.412\r\n- (NINJA GROANS)\r\n- (THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:20:05.079 --\u003e 00:20:06.080\r\nYes!\r\n\r\n00:20:10.501 --\u003e 00:20:12.211\r\nGotten a second wind, have you?\r\n\r\n00:20:12.670 --\u003e 00:20:16.757\r\nGood. This will make your\r\ndefeat all the more satisfying.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.258 --\u003e 00:20:18.592\r\nShut up and fight.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.302 --\u003e 00:20:21.303\r\n(NINJA EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.690 --\u003e 00:20:34.775\r\nYou were right about one\r\nthing, Kyodai.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.234 --\u003e 00:20:36.360\r\nNow it ends.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.060 --\u003e 00:21:11.228\r\nSo, what did you tell Summer?\r\n\r\n00:21:11.437 --\u003e 00:21:13.814\r\nThat Batman arrived and\r\ntook care of the ninja.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.981 --\u003e 00:21:14.982\r\nThat's true enough.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.066 --\u003e 00:21:18.486\r\nThe police couldn't find\r\nany trace of Kyodai Ken.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.861 --\u003e 00:21:19.862\r\nYou think he escaped?\r\n\r\n00:21:20.070 --\u003e 00:21:22.031\r\nNinjas are very resourceful.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.406 --\u003e 00:21:23.699\r\nDo you think he might return?\r\n\r\n00:21:23.949 --\u003e 00:21:24.950\r\nIt doesn't matter.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.201 --\u003e 00:21:26.327\r\nI defeated him once.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.660 --\u003e 00:21:28.496\r\nIf necessary, I can do it again.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.788 --\u003e 00:21:31.040\r\nHe had you worried for a while\r\nthough, didn't he?\r\n\r\n00:21:33.250 --\u003e 00:21:34.251\r\nThanks for your help.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.460 --\u003e 00:21:36.860\r\nIt would have been harder to\r\ndefeat him with Summer watching.\r\n\r\n00:21:37.338 --\u003e 00:21:39.590\r\nMaybe even impossible.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.895 --\u003e 00:21:54.897\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:19.296 --\u003e 00:22:20.297\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E29 - The Strange Secret of Bruce Wayne (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.173 --\u003e 00:00:08.175\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:54.281 --\u003e 00:01:56.158\r\nHand it over, Judge Vargas.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.160 --\u003e 00:01:59.661\r\nThe doctor said a trade.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.247 --\u003e 00:02:03.624\r\nThen let's trade.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.671 --\u003e 00:02:11.006\r\nWe had a deal.\r\n\r\n00:02:12.215 --\u003e 00:02:13.342\r\nNumbers.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.802 --\u003e 00:02:16.887\r\nCrunch it.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.059 --\u003e 00:02:23.894\r\nTwenty grand short, Snap.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.562 --\u003e 00:02:28.899\r\nThe price just went\r\nup another 100 thou.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.775 --\u003e 00:02:32.611\r\nPlease, I can't pay that much.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.570 --\u003e 00:02:34.738\r\n\u003ci\u003e(Nah, y0u'll Pa)!-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:35.072 --\u003e 00:02:37.282\r\nYou make a mistake.\r\nYou always pay.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.783 --\u003e 00:02:39.409\r\nMy sentiments exactly.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.456 --\u003e 00:02:45.582\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.881 --\u003e 00:02:54.049\r\nJudge Vargas!\r\n\r\n00:02:56.218 --\u003e 00:02:57.302\r\nJudge Vargas!\r\n\r\n00:02:57.552 --\u003e 00:02:58.637\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:03:16.363 --\u003e 00:03:17.531\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:24.830 --\u003e 00:03:26.248\r\nHelp.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.582 --\u003e 00:03:28.750\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:54.860 --\u003e 00:03:56.027\r\n(AMBULANCE DOORS CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:03:56.445 --\u003e 00:03:57.696\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:58.155 --\u003e 00:03:59.906\r\nThank heavens she's\r\nnot badly hurt.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.657 --\u003e 00:04:02.737\r\nBut they don't know when\r\nshe'll regain consciousness.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.618 --\u003e 00:04:07.164\r\nI've known Maria Vargas for 20 years.\r\nThe best judge on the circuit.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.289 --\u003e 00:04:08.498\r\nIt can't be blackmail.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.374 --\u003e 00:04:12.836\r\nThere was something on that videotape\r\nshe didn't want anyone to see.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.462 --\u003e 00:04:14.921\r\nI had dinner with\r\nher a week ago.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.297 --\u003e 00:04:16.715\r\nShe was just back from vacation.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.257 --\u003e 00:04:18.675\r\nLooked so relaxed.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.426 --\u003e 00:04:20.802\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:22.345 --\u003e 00:04:24.473\r\nWOMAN: \u003ci\u003eCommissioner,\r\nthat limo's plate is registered\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:24.556 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\n\u003ci\u003eto the Yucca Springs\r\nResort corporation.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:27.350 --\u003e 00:04:29.686\r\nYucca Springs is where\r\nMaria took her vacation.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.061 --\u003e 00:04:32.272\r\nSome sort of executive\r\nrelaxation program.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.856 --\u003e 00:04:35.984\r\nThat's one of Roland Daggett's\r\nsubsidiary companies.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.486 --\u003e 00:04:38.945\r\nWhat are you going to...\r\n\r\n00:04:50.582 --\u003e 00:04:52.209\r\nDo I look stressed out to you?\r\n\r\n00:04:53.418 --\u003e 00:04:55.295\r\nYou? Get outta town.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.754 --\u003e 00:04:58.882\r\nExactly.\r\nI think I need a vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.392 --\u003e 00:05:12.354\r\nNow that you've enrolled in\r\nthe stress management program.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.479 --\u003e 00:05:16.024\r\nJudge Vargas took,\r\nmay I ask what your next step is, sir?\r\n\r\n00:05:16.441 --\u003e 00:05:18.401\r\nThat's up to Dr. Hugo Strange.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.819 --\u003e 00:05:21.530\r\nI think he's the same doctor\r\nJudge Vargas mentioned.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.239 --\u003e 00:05:24.491\r\nMy first session with\r\nhim is in 15 minutes.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.200 --\u003e 00:05:28.787\r\nIn that case, perhaps I should\r\nlay out your evening clothes.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.083 --\u003e 00:05:35.335\r\nAre you sure this will\r\nhelp me relax, Doc?\r\n\r\n00:05:35.710 --\u003e 00:05:36.753\r\nBut of course.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.087 --\u003e 00:05:40.131\r\nMy radiopathic monitoring\r\ndevice is infallible.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.590 --\u003e 00:05:42.759\r\nIt works by lowering\r\nyour defenses.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.097 --\u003e 00:05:48.974\r\nWhat defenses might those be?\r\n\r\n00:05:49.641 --\u003e 00:05:53.687\r\nThe defenses we create to hide the\r\ntruth from ourselves and others.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.187 --\u003e 00:05:56.690\r\nFor when we do this,\r\nwe create stress.\r\n\r\n00:05:56.940 --\u003e 00:05:58.233\r\nIs it not so?\r\n\r\n00:05:58.608 --\u003e 00:06:00.360\r\nSome secrets are worth keeping.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.652 --\u003e 00:06:05.115\r\nIf you feel so, there must be\r\nconsiderable stress in your life.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.241 --\u003e 00:06:09.244\r\nSo, we should start with\r\nyour childhood, yes?\r\n\r\n00:06:10.996 --\u003e 00:06:13.456\r\nI don't have much to\r\nsay about my childhood.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.499 --\u003e 00:06:18.587\r\nIs there some past tragedy you\r\ndid not wish to acknowledge?\r\n\r\n00:06:30.599 --\u003e 00:06:31.892\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:37.647 --\u003e 00:06:38.940\r\n(GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:06:41.234 --\u003e 00:06:43.820\r\n\u003ci\u003eSTRANGE: Perhaps,\r\nthe loss of your parents?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:47.991 --\u003e 00:06:52.579\r\nWere they taken from\r\nyou by violence?\r\n\r\n00:06:54.956 --\u003e 00:06:56.958\r\nWhat happened to my\r\nparents is no secret.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.542 --\u003e 00:07:01.004\r\nBut no one knows that you\r\nfeel it was your fault. Yes?\r\n\r\n00:07:01.254 --\u003e 00:07:02.547\r\nI was only a child.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.131 --\u003e 00:07:04.591\r\nThere was nothing I could do.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.134 --\u003e 00:07:08.053\r\nBut you wanted to do something.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.470 --\u003e 00:07:09.930\r\nYou were filled with anger.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.347 --\u003e 00:07:12.182\r\nYou desired what?\r\n\r\n00:07:12.974 --\u003e 00:07:14.392\r\nA need filled you.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.893 --\u003e 00:07:17.228\r\nAll-consuming. All-controlling.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.938 --\u003e 00:07:19.689\r\nWhat was it, Mr. Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:07:20.857 --\u003e 00:07:22.108\r\nWhat was it?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.151 --\u003e 00:07:25.028\r\nI wanted...\r\n\r\n00:07:29.157 --\u003e 00:07:30.200\r\nYes?\r\n\r\n00:07:31.451 --\u003e 00:07:32.786\r\nRevenge!\r\n\r\n00:07:37.666 --\u003e 00:07:42.712\r\nYour relaxation therapy doesn't seem to\r\nbe working too well on me, Dr. Strange.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.046 --\u003e 00:07:45.131\r\nThe first session is\r\nofttimes traumatic.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.256 --\u003e 00:07:47.133\r\nWe will continue tomorrow, yes?\r\n\r\n00:07:49.761 --\u003e 00:07:53.056\r\nI'll have to think about it.\r\nGood day, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.268 --\u003e 00:07:58.561\r\nAnd good day to you,\r\n\r\n00:07:59.771 --\u003e 00:08:00.897\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.319 --\u003e 00:08:07.612\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.158 --\u003e 00:08:13.493\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING OVER RECORDING)\r\n\r\n00:08:14.119 --\u003e 00:08:16.955\r\n\u003ci\u003eBoy, did you get a wrong number.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:17.163 --\u003e 00:08:19.499\r\nLeave your message at\r\nthe sound of the shriek.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.833 --\u003e 00:08:22.252\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo, please, don't!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:22.460 --\u003e 00:08:23.795\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:08:24.838 --\u003e 00:08:27.257\r\n\u003ci\u003eSTRANGE: I am speaking,\r\nI trust, to the Joker?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:28.008 --\u003e 00:08:30.677\r\nYour number was\r\nnot easy to find.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.094 --\u003e 00:08:33.722\r\nThis is Dr. Hugo Strange.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.305 --\u003e 00:08:39.519\r\nI am arranging an auction for an item,\r\nI believe you will find most enticing.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.206 --\u003e 00:09:02.876\r\nMaster Bruce,\r\nDr. Strange has just left the grounds.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.626 --\u003e 00:09:04.627\r\nGood.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.629 --\u003e 00:09:09.340\r\nThis is my chance to get a\r\ncloser look at his machine.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.884 --\u003e 00:09:12.969\r\nI've got bad feelings about\r\nit, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.577 --\u003e 00:09:38.870\r\nJudge Vargas.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.123 --\u003e 00:09:44.501\r\n\u003ci\u003eLet us begin with\r\nyour childhood.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:44.793 --\u003e 00:09:46.753\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"VARGAS\".\r\nI'd rather not, Doctor.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:47.337 --\u003e 00:09:49.672\r\nSTRANGE: Hiding secrets\r\ncan lead to stress.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.298 --\u003e 00:09:52.008\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat secrets are you hiding?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:52.383 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n\u003ci\u003eLet me guess.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:54.344 --\u003e 00:09:57.722\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou liked to play with matches?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:58.056 --\u003e 00:09:59.599\r\n- \u003ci\u003eYes?\r\n- Yes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:59.891 --\u003e 00:10:01.309\r\n\u003ci\u003eI mean, no. No.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:01.976 --\u003e 00:10:05.688\r\n\u003ci\u003ePlaying with matches,\r\nmy parents told me it was wrong.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:08.942 --\u003e 00:10:12.737\r\n\u003ci\u003e(GASPS) I didn't mean to!\r\nIt was an accident!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:13.571 --\u003e 00:10:16.241\r\nSTRANGE: So,\r\nyou were the one responsible\r\n\r\n00:10:16.324 --\u003e 00:10:20.036\r\n\u003ci\u003efor the great Gotham\r\nDock fire 30 years ago?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:20.120 --\u003e 00:10:22.664\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll this guilt you have\r\ncarried inside you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:23.289 --\u003e 00:10:24.707\r\n\u003ci\u003eDo you not feel better now?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:26.584 --\u003e 00:10:29.170\r\nIt can see thoughts.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.653 --\u003e 00:10:55.655\r\n(SNIFFS) Ah...\r\n\r\n00:10:55.864 --\u003e 00:10:58.199\r\nSunshine. Clean air.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.324 --\u003e 00:10:59.659\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.285 --\u003e 00:11:01.661\r\nI hate it.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.874 --\u003e 00:11:07.792\r\nThis Dr. Strange better\r\nhave a good reason\r\n\r\n00:11:07.876 --\u003e 00:11:10.295\r\nfor dragging us out to\r\nthe middle of nowhere.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.463 --\u003e 00:11:16.718\r\nHave you no poetry in your\r\nsoul my dichotomous friend?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.968 --\u003e 00:11:20.513\r\nThere is a certain stark\r\nbeauty to this environment.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.472 --\u003e 00:11:22.932\r\nIt's too brown.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.516 --\u003e 00:11:25.977\r\nI prefer green, as in money.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.728 --\u003e 00:11:27.896\r\nYou have a point.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.277 --\u003e 00:11:36.279\r\nHey, what's in this one?\r\n\r\n00:11:37.697 --\u003e 00:11:42.410\r\nWhy, just what the doctor ordered.\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:11:54.422 --\u003e 00:11:55.632\r\nGood heavens.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.507 --\u003e 00:11:57.550\r\nMaster Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.634 --\u003e 00:11:59.219\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou must get out immediately.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:00.094 --\u003e 00:12:01.554\r\nAlmost through, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.846 --\u003e 00:12:03.306\r\nHas Strange come back?\r\n\r\n00:12:03.389 --\u003e 00:12:05.475\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's much worse than that, sir.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:08.353 --\u003e 00:12:09.687\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:12:15.526 --\u003e 00:12:19.822\r\nHey, bucko, I'd be a little more\r\ncareful with the luggage if I were you.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.906 --\u003e 00:12:21.574\r\nOtherwise,\r\nyou might lose your tip.\r\n\r\n00:12:21.658 --\u003e 00:12:23.785\r\nNot to mention your head.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.702 --\u003e 00:12:26.579\r\nYes, sir, Mr. Joker, sir.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.996 --\u003e 00:12:30.375\r\nIt's so hard to find\r\ngood help these days.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.918 --\u003e 00:12:34.337\r\nHow true. How true.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.467 --\u003e 00:12:42.262\r\nThe Joker, Two-Face and the\r\nPenguin have just arrived\r\n\r\n00:12:42.345 --\u003e 00:12:44.180\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith large quantities of cash.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:44.806 --\u003e 00:12:48.559\r\nSo, that's it.\r\nStrange isn't planning to blackmail me.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.810 --\u003e 00:12:50.603\r\nHe's going to auction my tape.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.062 --\u003e 00:12:52.105\r\nTape, sir?\r\n\r\n00:12:52.188 --\u003e 00:12:54.524\r\nI'll explain later.\r\nKeep me informed.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.578 --\u003e 00:13:08.830\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:08.913 --\u003e 00:13:11.291\r\nYou are Bruce Wayne's\r\nbutler, are you not?\r\n\r\n00:13:12.000 --\u003e 00:13:14.585\r\n- Yes.\r\n- Most excellent.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.046 --\u003e 00:13:18.131\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:46.576 --\u003e 00:13:47.952\r\nRemove him.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.081 --\u003e 00:13:54.792\r\nIt took me years to\r\nbuild that device.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.835 --\u003e 00:13:57.337\r\nBut no matter.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.297 --\u003e 00:14:01.174\r\nYou were, perhaps,\r\nlooking for this?\r\n\r\n00:14:01.591 --\u003e 00:14:03.718\r\nYour butler told us\r\nyou would be here.\r\n\r\n00:14:04.302 --\u003e 00:14:07.513\r\nIt took a dose of sodium\r\npentothal to persuade him to talk.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.764 --\u003e 00:14:09.515\r\nHe is quite loyal to you.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.350 --\u003e 00:14:12.935\r\nYou are a valuable\r\ncommodity, Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.853 --\u003e 00:14:15.313\r\nOr should I say.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.356 --\u003e 00:14:17.482\r\n\"Batman\"?\r\n\r\n00:14:18.232 --\u003e 00:14:19.484\r\nTake him away.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.571 --\u003e 00:14:26.449\r\nOh, Master Bruce, I'm so sorry.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.866 --\u003e 00:14:28.159\r\nThis is all my fault.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.701 --\u003e 00:14:30.078\r\nNonsense, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.495 --\u003e 00:14:34.332\r\nBelieve it or not,\r\nthis is working out just as I planned.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.208 --\u003e 00:14:36.793\r\nHow reassuring.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.088 --\u003e 00:14:43.841\r\nFirst, I would like to thank\r\nyou for coming all this way-\r\n\r\n00:14:43.925 --\u003e 00:14:45.343\r\nGet to the point!\r\n\r\n00:14:47.345 --\u003e 00:14:48.638\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.347 --\u003e 00:14:51.182\r\nVery well. I have here\r\n\r\n00:14:51.599 --\u003e 00:14:56.687\r\nincontestable proof of\r\nBatman's secret identity.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.188 --\u003e 00:14:58.606\r\nNow, gentlemen,\r\n\r\n00:14:59.273 --\u003e 00:15:01.275\r\nhow much am I bid?\r\n\r\n00:15:08.324 --\u003e 00:15:11.828\r\nDoes Dr. Strange truly have\r\nproof of your identity, sir?\r\n\r\n00:15:12.245 --\u003e 00:15:13.496\r\nI'm afraid so.\r\n\r\n00:15:21.963 --\u003e 00:15:23.589\r\nFive hundred thousand.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.048 --\u003e 00:15:27.051\r\n(SCOFFS) Chicken feed.\r\nI'll bid a million.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.427 --\u003e 00:15:28.636\r\nTwo million!\r\n\r\n00:15:28.719 --\u003e 00:15:31.472\r\nI have two million.\r\nDo I hear three?\r\n\r\n00:15:32.014 --\u003e 00:15:34.517\r\nHold it, hold it, hold it.\r\n\r\n00:15:35.643 --\u003e 00:15:37.562\r\nGet out of my face, clown.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.645 --\u003e 00:15:39.230\r\nWhich one?\r\n\r\n00:15:42.066 --\u003e 00:15:45.736\r\nGentlemen, it behooves us not\r\nto fight amongst ourselves.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.820 --\u003e 00:15:48.489\r\nWell put, sardine breath.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.823 --\u003e 00:15:51.409\r\nI think we should pool\r\nour resources on this.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.076 --\u003e 00:15:55.329\r\nFifity-one million,\r\ntwo hundred forty thousand,\r\n\r\n00:15:55.413 --\u003e 00:15:57.874\r\nsix hundred and\r\neighty-five dollars\r\n\r\n00:15:59.292 --\u003e 00:16:00.460\r\nand\r\n\r\n00:16:01.377 --\u003e 00:16:03.004\r\nfifty-three cents.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.839 --\u003e 00:16:06.090\r\nSTRANGE: Sold.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.009 --\u003e 00:16:11.721\r\nAnd now I give you\r\nBatman's secret identity.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.180 --\u003e 00:16:14.974\r\nAnd after the show,\r\nyou shall meet its star.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.815 --\u003e 00:16:27.195\r\nFocus, focus! Focus!\r\n\r\n00:16:33.159 --\u003e 00:16:34.619\r\nIt's a perfect plan.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.702 --\u003e 00:16:35.995\r\nWith this machine,\r\n\r\n00:16:36.787 --\u003e 00:16:39.790\r\nI can imagine Batman\r\nto be anyone I choose.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.874 --\u003e 00:16:42.919\r\nAnd these fools will\r\npay a fortune for it.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.421 --\u003e 00:16:48.090\r\n- Wait! It's not the right tape!\r\n- (WEAPON FIRES)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.133 --\u003e 00:16:52.011\r\nFellow miscreants,\r\nwe've been had.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.094 --\u003e 00:16:56.349\r\nI'm gonna use your head for\r\na bowling ball, Strange.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.432 --\u003e 00:16:57.558\r\nGet him!\r\n\r\n00:16:59.936 --\u003e 00:17:02.813\r\nI should have known better than\r\nto deal with the likes of you.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.256 --\u003e 00:17:30.424\r\nI spoke to Master Dick,\r\nsir, as you requested.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.841 --\u003e 00:17:32.051\r\nExcellent, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.510 --\u003e 00:17:33.594\r\nTo the airport.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.979 --\u003e 00:17:46.232\r\nBailing out of the resort\r\nbusiness, Hugo?\r\n\r\n00:17:46.399 --\u003e 00:17:49.485\r\nJoker, I swear,\r\nit was the wrong tape.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.569 --\u003e 00:17:51.737\r\nYou're telling me.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.821 --\u003e 00:17:56.409\r\nCome on, Hugo,\r\ntime to fly the unfriendly skies.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.617 --\u003e 00:17:58.119\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:29.108 --\u003e 00:18:30.818\r\n- (MUFFLED YELLING)\r\n- JOKER: Why, Hugo.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.986 --\u003e 00:18:35.281\r\nWhy didn't you tell us\r\nabout your fear of flying?\r\n\r\n00:18:36.157 --\u003e 00:18:38.868\r\nJoker, please! I was set up!\r\n\r\n00:18:38.951 --\u003e 00:18:40.578\r\nBruce Wayne is Batman!\r\n\r\n00:18:40.661 --\u003e 00:18:43.414\r\nThat's absurd.\r\nI know Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.497 --\u003e 00:18:46.667\r\nIf he's Batman,\r\nI'm the King Of England.\r\n\r\n00:18:46.751 --\u003e 00:18:49.170\r\nAnd people say I'm crazy.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.423 --\u003e 00:18:56.344\r\nSay, is it hot in\r\nhere or is it just me?\r\n\r\n00:18:56.427 --\u003e 00:19:00.348\r\nHarv, open that door\r\nso we can get a breeze.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.431 --\u003e 00:19:02.516\r\nGood idea.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.600 --\u003e 00:19:03.768\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:09.273 --\u003e 00:19:11.942\r\nRemember, it's not the fall,\r\n\r\n00:19:12.026 --\u003e 00:19:14.111\r\nit's the sudden stop!\r\n\r\n00:19:14.236 --\u003e 00:19:15.571\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:27.375 --\u003e 00:19:31.504\r\nMan, things haven't been\r\nthe same since deregulation.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.879 --\u003e 00:19:33.381\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:02.368 --\u003e 00:20:03.744\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.994 --\u003e 00:20:05.663\r\nWhat a rush.\r\n\r\n00:20:07.665 --\u003e 00:20:08.833\r\nBATMAN: Stay where you are.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.086 --\u003e 00:20:16.465\r\nYou may notice, my masked\r\nfriend, that we have the guns.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.556 --\u003e 00:20:24.765\r\nAh, well,\r\n\r\n00:20:25.182 --\u003e 00:20:27.518\r\nArkham is nice\r\nthis time of year.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.525 --\u003e 00:20:37.027\r\nMaria told me everything when\r\nshe woke up in the hospital.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.319 --\u003e 00:20:38.988\r\nThe dock fire was an accident.\r\n\r\n00:20:39.363 --\u003e 00:20:41.615\r\nShe had nothing to\r\nfear from the truth.\r\n\r\n00:20:41.699 --\u003e 00:20:43.617\r\nBut you do, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.701 --\u003e 00:20:46.871\r\nSoon, the whole world will know\r\nthat you are really Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.954 --\u003e 00:20:50.958\r\nYou created that tape in the theater\r\nby imagining me saying those lies.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.041 --\u003e 00:20:54.170\r\nBut the tape of your\r\nthoughts is the truth.\r\n\r\n00:20:54.253 --\u003e 00:20:56.255\r\nI know your secret.\r\n\r\n00:20:56.338 --\u003e 00:20:58.299\r\nWhat secret is that?\r\n\r\n00:20:58.382 --\u003e 00:21:00.593\r\nNo, it is impossible.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.676 --\u003e 00:21:03.846\r\nStrange, I knew from the start\r\nyour machine could read minds.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.929 --\u003e 00:21:07.099\r\nThat's why I asked Bruce\r\nWayne to help me expose you.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.183 --\u003e 00:21:08.851\r\nAnd I was glad to do it.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.934 --\u003e 00:21:11.187\r\nMaria Vargas is\r\na friend of mine.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.855 --\u003e 00:21:16.066\r\nLet's go. You'll have lots of\r\ntime to think about it in prison.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.203 --\u003e 00:21:28.537\r\nNot bad, huh?\r\n\r\n00:21:28.621 --\u003e 00:21:31.540\r\nMaybe I'll shuck this crime\r\nfighting gig and try Hollywood.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.877 --\u003e 00:21:36.545\r\nWish you weren't so tall though.\r\n\r\n00:21:37.087 --\u003e 00:21:39.924\r\nWalking in these leg\r\nextension braces is a pain.\r\n\r\n00:21:40.800 --\u003e 00:21:42.384\r\nWhere to now, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:21:42.676 --\u003e 00:21:43.844\r\nHome, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:21:44.386 --\u003e 00:21:47.890\r\nI've had enough vacation\r\nto last me a long time.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.186 --\u003e 00:21:54.188\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.671 --\u003e 00:22:19.672\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E30 - Tyger, Tyger (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.173 --\u003e 00:00:08.175\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.215 --\u003e 00:01:31.258\r\n(TIGER GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:01:31.925 --\u003e 00:01:34.469\r\nDon't tell me, I only work here.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.148 --\u003e 00:01:49.484\r\nHello, handsome.\r\nIt's criminal to keep you like this.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.568 --\u003e 00:01:52.070\r\nIf I had my way,\r\nyou'd be running free\r\n\r\n00:01:52.154 --\u003e 00:01:55.157\r\nand the humans who did\r\nthis would be put in here.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.200 --\u003e 00:01:58.410\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.586 --\u003e 00:02:11.465\r\nEasy, lady.\r\nJust relax and go sleepy-bye.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:14.885\r\nI won't let you hurt\r\n\r\n00:02:15.677 --\u003e 00:02:17.095\r\nthe tiger.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.596 --\u003e 00:02:20.932\r\nI wasn't sent here after the\r\ntiger, lady.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.185 --\u003e 00:02:24.311\r\n(MOANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:28.482 --\u003e 00:02:31.485\r\nOkay, Romeo, take it somewhere else.\r\nThe zoo's closed.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.529 --\u003e 00:02:35.572\r\nWhat in the name of...\r\n\r\n00:02:44.748 --\u003e 00:02:47.084\r\nNice tiger. Nice tiger.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.793 --\u003e 00:02:49.211\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:02:59.596 --\u003e 00:03:01.056\r\n(telephone ringing)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.808 --\u003e 00:03:07.020\r\n- Alfred, have you heard from Selina?\r\n- Why, no, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.104 --\u003e 00:03:11.274\r\nI thought you and she were having dinner\r\nto discuss an animal rights charity.\r\n\r\n00:03:11.358 --\u003e 00:03:13.860\r\nShe should've been here by now.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.944 --\u003e 00:03:17.030\r\nI'm so sorry, Monsieur Wayne,\r\nI meant to tell you earlier.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.114 --\u003e 00:03:19.950\r\n\u003ci\u003eMademoiselle Kyle called\r\nto say she'd be delayed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:20.033 --\u003e 00:03:22.452\r\nShe was visiting a\r\nfriend at the zoo.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.120 --\u003e 00:03:25.664\r\nI may be home late, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.960 --\u003e 00:03:32.254\r\nIf you hadn't have gotten\r\nhere, I would have been sushi.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.337 --\u003e 00:03:34.256\r\n- That tiger was ready to-\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.464 --\u003e 00:03:36.883\r\n- Now, about the woman.\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.008 --\u003e 00:03:39.845\r\nMan, her taste in\r\nboyfriends lacks severely.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.928 --\u003e 00:03:42.264\r\n- The guy looked like an ape.\r\n- Where is she?\r\n\r\n00:03:44.850 --\u003e 00:03:48.103\r\nSir, this is police business.\r\nWhere is she?\r\n\r\n00:03:48.729 --\u003e 00:03:51.189\r\nKong carried her off.\r\nI mean, we're talking primal here.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.543 --\u003e 00:04:13.044\r\n(MOANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:16.381 --\u003e 00:04:18.383\r\nHey, anybody here?\r\n\r\n00:04:21.344 --\u003e 00:04:22.804\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:04:27.726 --\u003e 00:04:29.728\r\n- (GAsPs)\r\n- (GROwl_s)\r\n\r\n00:04:34.024 --\u003e 00:04:35.484\r\n(SNIFFS)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.109 --\u003e 00:04:38.069\r\nAh, I see you've met Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.238 --\u003e 00:04:42.365\r\nHe seems to like you, Miss Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.491 --\u003e 00:04:45.494\r\nGo.\r\nIt's time for your exercises.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.454 --\u003e 00:04:51.750\r\nThis is called kidnapping.\r\nThe last I heard, it was highly illegal.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.125 --\u003e 00:04:53.126\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:04:53.585 --\u003e 00:04:56.379\r\nMy name is Emile Dorian.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.463 --\u003e 00:04:59.090\r\nBut that doesn't begin\r\nto tell you who I am.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.174 --\u003e 00:05:01.426\r\nTygrus is my\r\ncreation, Miss Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.510 --\u003e 00:05:03.595\r\n(PROJECTILES FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:05:04.429 --\u003e 00:05:08.016\r\nYou've met my first attempt at\r\naltering human genetic structure,\r\n\r\n00:05:08.099 --\u003e 00:05:09.434\r\nGarth the ape-man.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.060 --\u003e 00:05:14.022\r\nA simple biform.\r\nCrude, but serviceable.\r\n\r\n00:05:14.105 --\u003e 00:05:17.067\r\nBut Tygrus,\r\nhe is the pinnacle of my art.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.150 --\u003e 00:05:20.070\r\nI designed him from\r\nscratch, so to speak.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.654 --\u003e 00:05:24.032\r\nI have given him the strength\r\nand speed of a cat and more.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.408 --\u003e 00:05:27.118\r\n\u003ci\u003eHove cats.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:27.202 --\u003e 00:05:30.455\r\nTheir independence,\r\ntheir power, their beauty.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.419 --\u003e 00:05:40.507\r\nThat is why I've chosen you for\r\nmy next experiment, Selina Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.632 --\u003e 00:05:43.093\r\nOr perhaps I should\r\nI say Catwoman?\r\n\r\n00:05:43.260 --\u003e 00:05:45.011\r\nMister, you're crazy!\r\n\r\n00:05:45.095 --\u003e 00:05:48.682\r\nSticks and stones, Miss Kyle.\r\nSticks and stones.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.765 --\u003e 00:05:51.518\r\nYou've already been inoculated\r\nwith the initial dosage.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.601 --\u003e 00:05:54.062\r\nThis shot will\r\nfurther the treatment.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.689 --\u003e 00:05:56.773\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:59.234 --\u003e 00:06:01.319\r\nMy analysis shows\r\nthat it's similar\r\n\r\n00:06:01.403 --\u003e 00:06:04.155\r\nto the compound that turned\r\nyou into the Man-Bat.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.536 --\u003e 00:06:14.457\r\nYou're right. It's called T-99,\r\nthe brainchild of Dr. Emile Dorian.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.833 --\u003e 00:06:16.418\r\n(CREATURE CHIRPING)\r\n\r\n00:06:19.880 --\u003e 00:06:20.964\r\nWhat is it?\r\n\r\n00:06:21.047 --\u003e 00:06:24.092\r\nOne of the good doctor's\r\nearly experiments.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.261 --\u003e 00:06:28.513\r\nShhh. It's okay.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.597 --\u003e 00:06:31.474\r\nSo Dorian uses cats\r\nfor his research?\r\n\r\n00:06:31.558 --\u003e 00:06:32.851\r\nIn a way.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.934 --\u003e 00:06:35.979\r\nHe likes cats better than people.\r\nWon't experiment on them.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.062 --\u003e 00:06:38.899\r\nWhen I worked with him,\r\nhe used primates, monkeys.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.982 --\u003e 00:06:41.568\r\nHe changed their\r\ngenotypes with feline DNA.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.651 --\u003e 00:06:44.654\r\n- Where can I find him?\r\n- He owns an island off the coast.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.779 --\u003e 00:06:48.992\r\nHe retired there after people started\r\nprotesting his genetic engineering work.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.090 --\u003e 00:07:05.675\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:07:40.919 --\u003e 00:07:44.339\r\nThe doc don't take kindly\r\nto uninvited guests.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.008 --\u003e 00:07:49.260\r\nGarth, bring him downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.768 --\u003e 00:07:58.520\r\nThat's one way to do it.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.645 --\u003e 00:08:00.563\r\nThat will be all, Garth.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.647 --\u003e 00:08:03.024\r\nDoc, are you sure it'll be all-\r\n\r\n00:08:03.108 --\u003e 00:08:06.444\r\nYes, yes. Leave us. Now.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.363 --\u003e 00:08:11.616\r\nServants nowadays.\r\nTsk, tsk, tsk.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.700 --\u003e 00:08:13.576\r\nWhere's Selina Kyle?\r\n\r\n00:08:14.077 --\u003e 00:08:15.829\r\nTemper, temper, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.954 --\u003e 00:08:20.041\r\nYou shall see your Catwoman as\r\nyou've never seen her before.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.381 --\u003e 00:08:28.216\r\nSelina.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.097 --\u003e 00:08:35.890\r\nWhat have you done to her?\r\n\r\n00:08:38.143 --\u003e 00:08:40.520\r\nI've made her what she\r\nalways wanted to be.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.603 --\u003e 00:08:44.482\r\nI've given her power and grace\r\nbeyond her wildest dreams.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.566 --\u003e 00:08:46.776\r\nYou've made her a monster!\r\n\r\n00:08:47.402 --\u003e 00:08:49.154\r\nI believe she would disagree.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.237 --\u003e 00:08:52.157\r\nYou can't even begin to\r\nimagine how it is for her.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.240 --\u003e 00:08:53.992\r\nA whole new state of being,\r\n\r\n00:08:54.075 --\u003e 00:08:58.371\r\nheightened senses, increased\r\nspeed, agility, strength.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.456 --\u003e 00:09:00.540\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:12.886 --\u003e 00:09:16.347\r\n- Selina, do you know me?\r\n- Batman?\r\n\r\n00:09:18.475 --\u003e 00:09:20.435\r\nYou'll only confuse her, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.894 --\u003e 00:09:24.522\r\nShe's no longer the woman you knew.\r\nNo longer even human.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.606 --\u003e 00:09:27.817\r\nIn fact, she needs only one\r\nmore injection to complete-\r\n\r\n00:09:27.901 --\u003e 00:09:30.236\r\nReverse the\r\ntransformation or I'll-\r\n\r\n00:09:30.320 --\u003e 00:09:31.863\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:09:38.369 --\u003e 00:09:39.954\r\nGood lad, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.963 --\u003e 00:09:52.300\r\nAnother example of your\r\ngenetic tinkering, Dorian?\r\n\r\n00:09:52.383 --\u003e 00:09:54.302\r\nWell, nothing so crude, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.385 --\u003e 00:09:57.388\r\nTygrus is the ultimate life form.\r\nSuperior to any human.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.306 --\u003e 00:09:59.682\r\n(TYGRUS GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:12.028 --\u003e 00:10:14.697\r\nDoesn't he remind\r\nyou of Blake's poem?\r\n\r\n00:10:14.781 --\u003e 00:10:18.576\r\n\u003ci\u003eTyger Tyger, burning bright,\r\nIn the forests of the night.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:29.420 --\u003e 00:10:30.839\r\nTygrus, no!\r\n\r\n00:10:33.466 --\u003e 00:10:35.009\r\nEnough, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.888 --\u003e 00:10:40.348\r\nGo back to the enclosure.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.141 --\u003e 00:10:44.102\r\nWho... What am I?\r\n\r\n00:10:45.228 --\u003e 00:10:47.355\r\nSelina, come with me.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.356 --\u003e 00:10:49.732\r\nI'll find some way to help you.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.191 --\u003e 00:10:51.568\r\nTake him outside.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.118 --\u003e 00:11:01.119\r\nGarth!\r\n\r\n00:11:07.333 --\u003e 00:11:08.626\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:11:14.716 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nInteresting.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.467 --\u003e 00:11:19.512\r\nPerhaps your bestial side is\r\nnot as dominant as I thought.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.013 --\u003e 00:11:21.306\r\nRemove her.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.313 --\u003e 00:11:29.939\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:11:33.443 --\u003e 00:11:36.070\r\nIt's all right.\r\nIt's for her own good.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.154 --\u003e 00:11:39.657\r\nLet her go, Dorian,\r\nor by heaven I'll-\r\n\r\n00:11:39.741 --\u003e 00:11:42.202\r\nHer fate is in your\r\nhands, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.285 --\u003e 00:11:46.331\r\nI want to test Tygrus'\r\nreflexes and feral instincts.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.414 --\u003e 00:11:49.000\r\nAnd who better to pit\r\nhim against than you?\r\n\r\n00:11:53.755 --\u003e 00:11:56.925\r\nI'll give you a generous head\r\nstart before releasing Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.008 --\u003e 00:11:59.928\r\nIf you defeat him,\r\nI shall relinquish this.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.011 --\u003e 00:12:03.139\r\nThe antigen to reverse\r\nCatwoman's mutation.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.806 --\u003e 00:12:05.600\r\nHow do I know you'll\r\nkeep your word?\r\n\r\n00:12:06.726 --\u003e 00:12:07.977\r\nYou don't.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.853 --\u003e 00:12:11.189\r\nThe clock is ticking, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.272 --\u003e 00:12:13.274\r\nGood luck. You'll need it.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.030 --\u003e 00:12:21.407\r\nHe's all yours, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:12:23.660 --\u003e 00:12:25.995\r\nHe is prey to you, my boy.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.079 --\u003e 00:12:28.915\r\n\u003ci\u003eOf no more concern than\r\na rabbit is to a wolf.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:28.998 --\u003e 00:12:33.044\r\nAnd when he's gone,\r\nnothing will stand in your way.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.314 --\u003e 00:12:54.774\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:13:12.166 --\u003e 00:13:14.961\r\nDon't be difficult.\r\nIt's for your own good.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.004 --\u003e 00:13:19.674\r\nThink how wonderful it will be\r\nonce this inoculation takes effect.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.757 --\u003e 00:13:22.135\r\nYou'll be so much\r\nmore than human.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.762 --\u003e 00:13:25.763\r\nSELINA: Wait!\r\n\r\n00:13:27.724 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nNo need to do it that way.\r\n\r\n00:13:30.101 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\nI... I won't fight you.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.438 --\u003e 00:13:36.149\r\nYou've made the right\r\ndecision, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.650 --\u003e 00:13:39.444\r\nDon't trust her, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.197 --\u003e 00:13:44.449\r\nShe's getting away!\r\n\r\n00:13:45.700 --\u003e 00:13:49.620\r\nNever mind. We'll find her.\r\nThis is an island after all.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.330 --\u003e 00:13:51.664\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:20.485 --\u003e 00:14:22.153\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.279 --\u003e 00:14:25.740\r\nSo, you can talk.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.823 --\u003e 00:14:27.575\r\nMy father taught me.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.076 --\u003e 00:14:30.203\r\nYour father was a test tube.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.286 --\u003e 00:14:33.289\r\nHe told me to destroy\r\nyou, and I will.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.373 --\u003e 00:14:36.709\r\nAnd when you're gone,\r\nSelina will love me.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.335 --\u003e 00:14:38.753\r\nI wouldn't count on it.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.546 --\u003e 00:14:42.757\r\nThat cable should\r\nhold you for a while.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.059 --\u003e 00:14:54.644\r\n(SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:15:10.159 --\u003e 00:15:11.452\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:53.536 --\u003e 00:15:55.079\r\n(BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:16:13.097 --\u003e 00:16:14.223\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:14.307 --\u003e 00:16:15.475\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.498 --\u003e 00:16:39.499\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.877 --\u003e 00:16:45.546\r\n- You're hurt.\r\n- It's nothing.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.630 --\u003e 00:16:47.173\r\nHow did you get\r\naway from Dorian?\r\n\r\n00:16:47.256 --\u003e 00:16:49.133\r\nHe didn't try to stop me.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.217 --\u003e 00:16:51.177\r\nHe knows there's\r\nno way off this-\r\n\r\n00:16:51.302 --\u003e 00:16:52.720\r\nWhat is it?\r\n\r\n00:16:57.725 --\u003e 00:16:58.976\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.229 --\u003e 00:17:03.606\r\nStop, Tygrus! Don't hurt him.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.689 --\u003e 00:17:04.857\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\n00:17:04.941 --\u003e 00:17:07.026\r\nBatman's done nothing to you.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.109 --\u003e 00:17:10.196\r\nHe's my enemy and\r\nmy father's enemy.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.279 --\u003e 00:17:12.823\r\nWhen I prove I'm\r\nbest, you'll be mine.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.282 --\u003e 00:17:15.701\r\nNo, I can't be won like that.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.785 --\u003e 00:17:19.664\r\n- But my father said-\r\n- He's wrong!\r\n\r\n00:17:19.747 --\u003e 00:17:23.751\r\nSearch your feelings, Tygrus.\r\nYou know he's wrong.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.420 --\u003e 00:17:28.214\r\n(HOWL$)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.348 --\u003e 00:17:40.226\r\nI'm very disappointed in\r\nyou, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.310 --\u003e 00:17:43.187\r\nI am ashamed of you.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.188 --\u003e 00:17:48.317\r\n- Father, please.\r\n- Twenty years of work in jeopardy.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.401 --\u003e 00:17:51.445\r\nYou should have killed Batman.\r\nTorn him limb from limb.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.529 --\u003e 00:17:56.158\r\nWhy? He ls not food,\r\nand he is not my enemy.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.242 --\u003e 00:17:57.243\r\nHe's right.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.160 --\u003e 00:17:59.370\r\nI'm not his enemy.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.453 --\u003e 00:18:01.038\r\nAll I want is the antigen.\r\n\r\n00:18:01.831 --\u003e 00:18:03.416\r\nAnd you.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.842 --\u003e 00:18:15.845\r\nTygrus, stop him.\r\nHe'll take me away from you.\r\n\r\n00:18:15.928 --\u003e 00:18:18.097\r\nThis is out of your\r\nhands, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:18:18.180 --\u003e 00:18:22.184\r\nHe's broken the law,\r\ncommitted crimes against nature.\r\n\r\n00:18:25.229 --\u003e 00:18:29.275\r\nIt doesn't matter. He's my father.\r\nHe gave me life.\r\n\r\n00:18:29.567 --\u003e 00:18:30.818\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:18:32.403 --\u003e 00:18:35.615\r\nThis is your fault.\r\nYou've ruined him!\r\n\r\n00:18:38.242 --\u003e 00:18:39.243\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:18:41.871 --\u003e 00:18:45.583\r\nLet go! I won't have this\r\ninsolence, Tygrus.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.666 --\u003e 00:18:48.836\r\nI made you and I can unmake you.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.719 --\u003e 00:18:57.720\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:18:58.596 --\u003e 00:18:59.805\r\nTygrus!\r\n\r\n00:19:14.403 --\u003e 00:19:16.030\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:22.119 --\u003e 00:19:26.457\r\nI only wanted you to be strong,\r\nto show no weakness, no pity.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.458 --\u003e 00:19:30.336\r\nAs you wish, Father!\r\n\r\n00:19:35.883 --\u003e 00:19:37.134\r\nTygrus!\r\n\r\n00:20:02.159 --\u003e 00:20:04.245\r\nTygrus didn't deserve this.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.455 --\u003e 00:20:08.833\r\nNo need for tears yet, Selina.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.477 --\u003e 00:20:31.272\r\nFather needs help.\r\nYou will help him, won't you?\r\n\r\n00:20:31.355 --\u003e 00:20:32.648\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.190 --\u003e 00:20:35.818\r\nBatwing, standard\r\nevac, code three.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.945 --\u003e 00:20:41.657\r\nBatman, the antidote!\r\nI'll be stuck like this forever.\r\n\r\n00:20:44.034 --\u003e 00:20:45.828\r\nWould that be so bad?\r\n\r\n00:20:45.911 --\u003e 00:20:48.164\r\nYou could stay here with me.\r\n\r\n00:20:48.247 --\u003e 00:20:53.252\r\nOh, Tygrus, I can't live like this.\r\nI have to be human again.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.047 --\u003e 00:20:58.674\r\nGoodbye, Selina.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.772 --\u003e 00:21:14.106\r\nWait.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.190 --\u003e 00:21:17.693\r\nWon't you come with us?\r\nThere's nothing for you here.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.777 --\u003e 00:21:20.863\r\nThere's nothing for me anywhere.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.872 --\u003e 00:21:35.711\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: Tyger Tyger burning bright,\r\nIn the forests of the night:\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:38.339 --\u003e 00:21:44.136\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat immortal hand or eye,\r\nDare frame thy fearful symmetry?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:51.477 --\u003e 00:21:53.479\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.003 --\u003e 00:22:19.004\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E31 - Dreams in Darkness (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.461 --\u003e 00:00:04.463\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.833 --\u003e 00:01:25.586\r\nHas the new patient\r\nquieted down?\r\n\r\n00:01:25.752 --\u003e 00:01:29.131\r\nYes, Doctor. His hallucinations\r\nseem to have stopped.\r\n\r\n00:01:29.381 --\u003e 00:01:31.174\r\nSuch a pity, really.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.466 --\u003e 00:01:36.555\r\nTo think, after all he's accomplished,\r\nthat he should end up here, like this.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.306 --\u003e 00:01:40.350\r\nYes, he does seem calmer.\r\n\r\n00:01:41.184 --\u003e 00:01:43.020\r\nYou can turn on the lights.\r\n\r\n00:01:45.814 --\u003e 00:01:47.357\r\nIt's all right, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.608 --\u003e 00:01:50.902\r\nI'm Dr. Bartholomew,\r\nyour psychiatrist.\r\n\r\n00:01:51.278 --\u003e 00:01:54.406\r\nDid you contact Commissioner\r\nGordon and Dr. Wu?\r\n\r\n00:01:54.948 --\u003e 00:01:58.076\r\nCalm yourself.\r\nEverything is under control.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.368 --\u003e 00:02:00.329\r\nHaven't you listened to\r\nanything I've told you?\r\n\r\n00:02:01.872 --\u003e 00:02:03.457\r\nHe needs more time.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.624 --\u003e 00:02:05.292\r\nSee that he's not disturbed.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.375 --\u003e 00:02:08.545\r\nBartholomew,\r\nwe don't have any more time!\r\n\r\n00:02:09.004 --\u003e 00:02:10.255\r\nNow, now.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.631 --\u003e 00:02:13.133\r\nThere's always time to heal.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.676 --\u003e 00:02:16.595\r\nSuch a pity.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.347 --\u003e 00:02:21.141\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: \"There's always time\r\nto heal,\" the doctor told me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:21.308 --\u003e 00:02:22.851\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut he was wrong.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:23.060 --\u003e 00:02:24.603\r\n\u003ci\u003eThere was no time left.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:24.770 --\u003e 00:02:29.483\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot for me,\r\nnot for him and not for Gotham City.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:30.067 --\u003e 00:02:32.527\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd as long as I remained\r\ntrapped in Arkham,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:32.611 --\u003e 00:02:34.363\r\n\u003ci\u003ethere was nothing I could do.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:34.446 --\u003e 00:02:38.116\r\n\u003ci\u003eExcept wait for the end\r\nand remember the beginning.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:41.870 --\u003e 00:02:43.747\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe word on the street\r\nwas that something big\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:43.830 --\u003e 00:02:45.624\r\n\u003ci\u003ewas going down at the\r\nHealth Spring Spa.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:50.837 --\u003e 00:02:52.506\r\n\u003ci\u003eI guessed a robbery,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:52.756 --\u003e 00:02:54.216\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut that night,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:54.383 --\u003e 00:02:55.801\r\n\u003ci\u003eI guessed wrong.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:02.140 --\u003e 00:03:05.018\r\nYo. Getting set to make\r\nthe final connection.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.310 --\u003e 00:03:08.730\r\nMAN: (ON RADIO) Superlative, Torchy.\r\nPrecisely on schedule.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.404 --\u003e 00:03:18.284\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: He thought he was gonna do\r\nsomething to the spa's drinking water.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:19.783 --\u003e 00:03:21.952\r\n\u003ci\u003eI decided to make\r\nhim think again.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:30.001 --\u003e 00:03:31.002\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:03:31.628 --\u003e 00:03:32.796\r\nBummer.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.004 --\u003e 00:03:35.716\r\nMAN: (ON RADIO) A-ha.\r\nPrecisely on schedule.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.133 --\u003e 00:03:37.342\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow, Torchy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:06.329 --\u003e 00:04:07.706\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:04:21.678 --\u003e 00:04:22.679\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:04:31.188 --\u003e 00:04:32.189\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.693 --\u003e 00:04:37.736\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:41.948 --\u003e 00:04:44.826\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: He was in no condition to\r\ntell me what he was trying to do,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:45.118 --\u003e 00:04:46.661\r\n\u003ci\u003eor who he was working for.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:47.287 --\u003e 00:04:48.997\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy only clues were\r\nthe strange device\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:49.080 --\u003e 00:04:51.416\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe had welded to the\r\ndrinking-water pipe\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:52.042 --\u003e 00:04:54.377\r\n\u003ci\u003eand one half of a video\r\ncommunication link.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:54.795 --\u003e 00:04:57.964\r\n\u003ci\u003eAs for the gas,\r\nI thought it had no effect on me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:58.507 --\u003e 00:05:00.133\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut I was wrong again.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:00.217 --\u003e 00:05:01.218\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:03.053 --\u003e 00:05:04.054\r\nWhat...\r\n\r\n00:05:04.888 --\u003e 00:05:06.431\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:05:07.724 --\u003e 00:05:10.811\r\nI beg your pardon, Master Bruce.\r\nDid I startle you?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.561 --\u003e 00:05:16.107\r\nNo. I must have been staring\r\nat the screen too long.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.150 --\u003e 00:05:21.488\r\nHere are the reference materials you\r\nrequested on water-purifying systems.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.863 --\u003e 00:05:24.115\r\nMight one inquire\r\nwhat they're for?\r\n\r\n00:05:25.450 --\u003e 00:05:28.912\r\nBATMAN: Someone stole a huge\r\nwater-purification system last month.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.287 --\u003e 00:05:31.581\r\nThis device is a\r\nminiature test model\r\n\r\n00:05:31.706 --\u003e 00:05:35.335\r\nwhich means someone was trying\r\nto contaminate the spa's water.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.419 --\u003e 00:05:38.129\r\nGood heavens. With what?\r\n\r\n00:05:39.589 --\u003e 00:05:42.175\r\nThe gas residue was\r\ncompletely oxidized.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.426 --\u003e 00:05:45.971\r\nI can't be sure. Yet.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.056 --\u003e 00:05:50.267\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: The man I'd captured\r\nwas still in the hospital.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:50.392 --\u003e 00:05:52.477\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe doctor said he\r\nwas able to talk.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:53.979 --\u003e 00:05:55.772\r\nRed eyes.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.939 --\u003e 00:05:57.274\r\nThose teeth.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.440 --\u003e 00:05:58.859\r\nStay away.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.067 --\u003e 00:06:01.778\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut what he had to say\r\ndidn't make any sense.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.487 --\u003e 00:06:05.198\r\n\u003ci\u003eAccording to the chart,\r\nhe was hallucinating wildly\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:05.282 --\u003e 00:06:08.785\r\n\u003ci\u003edue to a massive fear reaction\r\nin the amygdala of his brain.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:16.793 --\u003e 00:06:18.128\r\nWho's in here?\r\n\r\n00:06:19.254 --\u003e 00:06:20.422\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.714 --\u003e 00:06:22.716\r\nI need to know what's\r\naffected this man.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.883 --\u003e 00:06:26.219\r\n- Why?\r\n- Because it may have affected me too.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.179 --\u003e 00:06:30.015\r\nYour blood titers are elevated.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.265 --\u003e 00:06:32.183\r\nYou've been exposed to it also.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.517 --\u003e 00:06:35.687\r\nPercentage is smaller,\r\nso it's taking longer to affect you.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.104 --\u003e 00:06:38.440\r\nBut I will begin to\r\nhallucinate as well?\r\n\r\n00:06:38.773 --\u003e 00:06:40.984\r\nI'm surprised you\r\nhaven't already.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.443 --\u003e 00:06:43.904\r\nBut don't worry,\r\nI can give you an antidote.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.321 --\u003e 00:06:46.781\r\nIt will make you\r\nsleep for two days.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.866 --\u003e 00:06:50.076\r\nBatman,\r\nyou must let me treat you.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.201 --\u003e 00:06:54.748\r\nOtherwise, in 24 hours, you won't be\r\nable to tell reality from fantasy.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.498 --\u003e 00:06:56.750\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:07:01.379 --\u003e 00:07:04.049\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: I couldn't risk being\r\nout of action for that long.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:04.215 --\u003e 00:07:07.135\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat had happened at the\r\nspa was only a trial run.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:07.302 --\u003e 00:07:09.679\r\n\u003ci\u003eSomeone was planning to\r\npoison Gotham's water supply\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:09.763 --\u003e 00:07:11.723\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith the same fear-inducing gas,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:12.098 --\u003e 00:07:16.102\r\n\u003ci\u003eand I knew only one person\r\ncapable of such a deed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:16.186 --\u003e 00:07:17.187\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:19.481 --\u003e 00:07:20.482\r\nRobin!\r\n\r\n00:07:20.857 --\u003e 00:07:21.858\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:42.128 --\u003e 00:07:44.673\r\nBATMAN: Robin, look out.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.839 --\u003e 00:07:46.633\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.800 --\u003e 00:07:48.259\r\nIt's a trap.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.426 --\u003e 00:07:50.595\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe hallucinations\r\nwere getting stronger.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:51.221 --\u003e 00:07:53.723\r\n\u003ci\u003eI could've sworn I had really\r\nseen Robin in front of me,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:53.807 --\u003e 00:07:55.475\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut I couldn't tell them that.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:55.892 --\u003e 00:07:58.395\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was raving, incoherent.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:58.853 --\u003e 00:08:00.313\r\nLook out.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.523 --\u003e 00:08:03.441\r\nJoker's got a bomb!\r\n\r\n00:08:03.858 --\u003e 00:08:05.568\r\n\u003ci\u003eSome thought I'd gone mad.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:06.277 --\u003e 00:08:07.904\r\n\u003ci\u003eOthers thought I\r\nalways had been.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:08.321 --\u003e 00:08:11.574\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd so they put me where\r\nthey thought I belonged.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:12.283 --\u003e 00:08:13.535\r\nNot yet.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.702 --\u003e 00:08:17.163\r\nHis mask is at the root of\r\nhis delusional fixation.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.497 --\u003e 00:08:20.667\r\nTo take it off might plunge\r\nhim into a catatonic state.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.888 --\u003e 00:08:36.725\r\nIt's time we had another\r\nchat, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.060 --\u003e 00:08:42.605\r\nNow, tell me about this\r\nsupposed gas again.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.231 --\u003e 00:08:44.733\r\nI've already told you.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.442 --\u003e 00:08:48.028\r\nWhen the gas is put into\r\nGotham's water supply,\r\n\r\n00:08:48.236 --\u003e 00:08:50.613\r\nthe entire city\r\nwill be affected.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.947 --\u003e 00:08:52.323\r\nWhy won't you believe me?\r\n\r\n00:08:52.991 --\u003e 00:08:54.242\r\nEasy.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.870 --\u003e 00:08:58.997\r\nWell,\r\nhow could such a complex plan\r\n\r\n00:08:59.080 --\u003e 00:09:01.708\r\nbe implemented without\r\nattracting attention?\r\n\r\n00:09:01.958 --\u003e 00:09:05.170\r\nI think this plot is\r\njust another delusion.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.587 --\u003e 00:09:08.256\r\nAnd deep down,\r\nyou believe so too.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.007 --\u003e 00:09:11.176\r\nOtherwise, why come to Arkham?\r\n\r\n00:09:11.301 --\u003e 00:09:14.804\r\nThe one place where costumed\r\ndelusional personalities\r\n\r\n00:09:14.888 --\u003e 00:09:17.015\r\ncan receive compassion and help.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.223 --\u003e 00:09:18.892\r\nI didn't come here for help.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.309 --\u003e 00:09:21.644\r\nI came to find the\r\ncriminal behind all this.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.145 --\u003e 00:09:23.480\r\nReally, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.855 --\u003e 00:09:28.151\r\nAs if a criminal could run an\r\noutside operation from in here.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.568 --\u003e 00:09:31.529\r\nJack Napier? Harvey Dent?\r\nPamela lsley?\r\n\r\n00:09:31.946 --\u003e 00:09:35.283\r\nOr, as you call them, the\r\nJoker, Two-Face and Poison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.492 --\u003e 00:09:38.036\r\nWe keep them all\r\nunder constant watch.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.411 --\u003e 00:09:40.830\r\nThey're not responsible\r\nfor this madness.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.164 --\u003e 00:09:44.626\r\nThere's only one criminal twisted\r\nenough to come up with such a scheme,\r\n\r\n00:09:45.085 --\u003e 00:09:46.211\r\nThe Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.337 --\u003e 00:09:50.256\r\nProfessor Crane? What nonsense.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.673 --\u003e 00:09:53.510\r\nI saw him this\r\nmorning in his cell.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.760 --\u003e 00:09:56.554\r\nHe's probably asleep\r\neven as we speak.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.062 --\u003e 00:10:05.688\r\nFirst truck's almost\r\nempty, boss.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.064 --\u003e 00:10:07.232\r\nSCARECROW: Excellent.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.482 --\u003e 00:10:10.652\r\nKeep going.\r\nI expect no interference.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.319 --\u003e 00:10:13.029\r\nWhat about Batman?\r\n\r\n00:10:13.196 --\u003e 00:10:14.405\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:10:14.823 --\u003e 00:10:16.699\r\nHe's no longer of consequence.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.075 --\u003e 00:10:20.370\r\nIt was no accident, his turning\r\nup at the health spa, you know.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.537 --\u003e 00:10:22.747\r\nI leaked rumors of\r\na burglary there.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.081 --\u003e 00:10:24.249\r\nYou set him up?\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.000\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.209 --\u003e 00:10:28.336\r\nAnd now that he's been\r\nexposed to the gas,\r\n\r\n00:10:28.628 --\u003e 00:10:31.339\r\nhe's achieved the fate\r\nhe truly deserves.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.714 --\u003e 00:10:33.883\r\nYou mean Batman's...\r\n\r\n00:10:34.759 --\u003e 00:10:37.303\r\n(CHUCKLES) Oh,\r\nhe's much worse than that.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.804 --\u003e 00:10:39.597\r\nMuch, much worse than that.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.317 --\u003e 00:10:52.861\r\nWho's there?\r\n\r\n00:11:17.093 --\u003e 00:11:18.094\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:20.305 --\u003e 00:11:22.891\r\nMom? Dad?\r\n\r\n00:11:38.239 --\u003e 00:11:40.158\r\nNo. Stop!\r\n\r\n00:11:40.575 --\u003e 00:11:41.826\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:11:42.368 --\u003e 00:11:43.745\r\nDon't go in there!\r\n\r\n00:11:46.664 --\u003e 00:11:47.665\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:00.803 --\u003e 00:12:02.305\r\n- No!\r\n- (CANNON FIRES)\r\n\r\n00:12:05.808 --\u003e 00:12:06.809\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:13.816 --\u003e 00:12:16.027\r\nI hope I'm not disturbing you.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.402 --\u003e 00:12:18.571\r\nIsn't that why I'm here?\r\n\r\n00:12:18.988 --\u003e 00:12:21.449\r\nBecause I'm disturbed?\r\n\r\n00:12:22.951 --\u003e 00:12:26.955\r\nI asked an orderly to look\r\nin on Professor Crane, and...\r\n\r\n00:12:27.163 --\u003e 00:12:28.414\r\nAnd he's not there.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.873 --\u003e 00:12:33.378\r\nHe can't possibly have left the grounds.\r\nOur security is absolute.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.544 --\u003e 00:12:36.631\r\n- Completely...\r\n- No security is absolute.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.257 --\u003e 00:12:39.300\r\nThe Scarecrow has\r\nalready proved that.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.550 --\u003e 00:12:41.594\r\nBut I think I know where he is.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.886 --\u003e 00:12:43.096\r\nWhere?\r\n\r\n00:12:43.263 --\u003e 00:12:44.847\r\nWhere's Arkham's water supply?\r\n\r\n00:12:45.807 --\u003e 00:12:49.686\r\nArkham Cavern.\r\nThe asylum was built over it.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.811 --\u003e 00:12:52.814\r\nThere's an underground river\r\nthat feeds the city reservoir.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.064 --\u003e 00:12:54.482\r\nI've got to get down there.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.691 --\u003e 00:12:57.026\r\nIn your condition?\r\nI can't allow that.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.277 --\u003e 00:12:58.653\r\nYou're staying here.\r\n\r\n00:13:09.497 --\u003e 00:13:11.916\r\nYou're still very ill, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:12.333 --\u003e 00:13:13.876\r\nThis will make you feel better.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.221 --\u003e 00:13:27.682\r\nThe last truck's here.\r\nOnce we start pumping it,\r\n\r\n00:13:27.765 --\u003e 00:13:30.393\r\nthere's no stopping\r\nthe chemical reaction.\r\n\r\n00:13:30.810 --\u003e 00:13:31.978\r\nSCARECROW: Excellent.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.186 --\u003e 00:13:35.815\r\nThe opportunities to study the\r\nnature of fear will be unparalleled.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.566 --\u003e 00:13:40.445\r\nIt's time for the greatest\r\ncontrolled experiment in mass madness\r\n\r\n00:13:40.528 --\u003e 00:13:42.363\r\nto finally begin.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.409 --\u003e 00:13:47.410\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:58.463 --\u003e 00:14:01.924\r\nDon't worry, the police\r\nwill handle Professor Crane.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.731 --\u003e 00:14:17.899\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:14:37.919 --\u003e 00:14:39.128\r\nGUARD: Get him!\r\n\r\n00:15:09.409 --\u003e 00:15:10.410\r\n(GUARD GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:15.498 --\u003e 00:15:18.126\r\nTake me to the basement. Now.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.948 --\u003e 00:15:49.949\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:51.868 --\u003e 00:15:53.161\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:06.466 --\u003e 00:16:07.467\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:13.681 --\u003e 00:16:14.682\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:20.188 --\u003e 00:16:21.189\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:25.109 --\u003e 00:16:26.277\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:16:42.001 --\u003e 00:16:43.211\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.377 --\u003e 00:16:44.754\r\nYou're not real.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.505 --\u003e 00:16:46.756\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:16:53.346 --\u003e 00:16:55.181\r\nRobin. Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.556 --\u003e 00:16:56.849\r\nYou've got to help me.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.475 --\u003e 00:16:59.185\r\nIt's too late for that, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.435 --\u003e 00:17:01.687\r\nYou've lived in\r\ndarkness too long.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.230 --\u003e 00:17:06.943\r\nYes. Do come along, Master Bruce.\r\nIt's time to go home.\r\n\r\n00:17:17.328 --\u003e 00:17:18.329\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.412 --\u003e 00:17:22.458\r\nSCARECROW: The great Batman,\r\nscared out of his mind.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.792 --\u003e 00:17:24.418\r\nHow does it feel?\r\n\r\n00:17:29.090 --\u003e 00:17:30.508\r\n({SCREECHES) {YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.139 --\u003e 00:17:38.140\r\n(BAT SQUEAKS)\r\n\r\n00:17:38.516 --\u003e 00:17:39.517\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.573 --\u003e 00:17:54.574\r\n(TIMER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:56.951 --\u003e 00:17:58.703\r\nFull pressure on pump one.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.078 --\u003e 00:18:01.205\r\n\u003ci\u003eMixing chamber two on standby.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:01.372 --\u003e 00:18:03.833\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe are go for injection.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:04.000 --\u003e 00:18:06.961\r\n\u003ci\u003eThree minutes and counting.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:08.421 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\nThat's the last of it.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.631 --\u003e 00:18:13.801\r\nAn entire city\r\nscreaming in fear.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.135 --\u003e 00:18:16.095\r\nI wonder if we'll\r\nbe able to hear it.\r\n\r\n00:18:23.436 --\u003e 00:18:24.437\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:26.022 --\u003e 00:18:27.023\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.486 --\u003e 00:18:34.655\r\nYou've run out of\r\ntime, Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.072 --\u003e 00:18:37.450\r\nThis experiment\r\nin terror is over.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.826 --\u003e 00:18:39.827\r\n(POWERING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:18:43.581 --\u003e 00:18:44.582\r\nGet him.\r\n\r\n00:18:49.545 --\u003e 00:18:51.964\r\nHe's been exposed to the\r\ngas, remember?\r\n\r\n00:18:52.089 --\u003e 00:18:54.050\r\nHe'll be terrified of you.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.013 --\u003e 00:19:00.014\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.024 --\u003e 00:19:11.359\r\n(WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.318 --\u003e 00:19:13.319\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:14.236 --\u003e 00:19:15.821\r\n- Turn it off!\r\n- Turn it off!\r\n\r\n00:19:21.994 --\u003e 00:19:26.165\r\nFool. Did you really think I\r\nwouldn't have backup controls?\r\n\r\n00:19:26.624 --\u003e 00:19:28.542\r\nIt's over, Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.266 --\u003e 00:19:45.267\r\n(POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:19:58.698 --\u003e 00:19:59.740\r\n- (HISSING)\r\n- Ah!\r\n\r\n00:20:12.420 --\u003e 00:20:13.421\r\n(SQUEAKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:35.943 --\u003e 00:20:37.570\r\nIt's gonna blow!\r\n\r\n00:20:47.246 --\u003e 00:20:48.247\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:50.499 --\u003e 00:20:52.585\r\nNo! No!\r\n\r\n00:21:01.302 --\u003e 00:21:03.262\r\nHelp me!\r\n\r\n00:21:04.430 --\u003e 00:21:05.765\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:06.724 --\u003e 00:21:09.560\r\nOne second. One...\r\nSend for an ambulance...\r\n\r\n00:21:10.311 --\u003e 00:21:11.562\r\n(MUMBUNG)\r\n\r\n00:21:11.896 --\u003e 00:21:14.440\r\nBARTHOLOMEW: Well,\r\nhe was right all along.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.274 --\u003e 00:21:17.943\r\nThis time,\r\nsee if you can keep him in there.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.830 --\u003e 00:21:30.956\r\nALFRED: There you go.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.415 --\u003e 00:21:32.750\r\nAs simple as that.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.626 --\u003e 00:21:34.877\r\nThanks, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.211 --\u003e 00:21:37.087\r\nIt's good to know I'm safe here.\r\n\r\n00:21:57.024 --\u003e 00:21:59.026\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:23.092 --\u003e 00:22:24.093\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E32 - Beware The Gray Ghost (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.964 --\u003e 00:00:07.382\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.625 --\u003e 00:01:25.794\r\nNARRATOR: When \u003ci\u003ecrime\u003c/i\u003e\r\nhaunts the night,\r\n\r\n00:01:25.919 --\u003e 00:01:29.214\r\na \u003ci\u003esilent crusader carries\r\nthe torch of justice.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:35.679 --\u003e 00:01:38.348\r\n\u003ci\u003eThose with evil hearts beware,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:38.473 --\u003e 00:01:41.059\r\n\u003ci\u003efor out of the darkness comes\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:41.226 --\u003e 00:01:43.812\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe Gray Ghost.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:43.895 --\u003e 00:01:47.190\r\n(WOMAN SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:01:48.609 --\u003e 00:01:51.695\r\n\u003ci\u003eTonight's episode,\r\n\"The Mad Bomber.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:14.801 --\u003e 00:02:17.554\r\nBedtime right after Gray Ghost.\r\nOkay, Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:02:20.682 --\u003e 00:02:24.269\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe city is rocked again\r\nby the mysterious bomber.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:24.394 --\u003e 00:02:28.482\r\n\u003ci\u003eOur only hope, the Gray Ghost!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:40.744 --\u003e 00:02:47.292\r\n(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:02:55.133 --\u003e 00:02:56.176\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:03:00.681 --\u003e 00:03:03.058\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"Pay up,\r\nor pay the consequences.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:03.183 --\u003e 00:03:07.145\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"One million in cash,\r\nor the Piedmont Bank is next.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:07.604 --\u003e 00:03:09.606\r\n\u003ci\u003eSigned, \"The Mad Bomber.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:20.742 --\u003e 00:03:23.745\r\n(POLICE SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:03:23.829 --\u003e 00:03:25.330\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:32.295 --\u003e 00:03:33.296\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.467 --\u003e 00:03:39.594\r\nBATMAN: \"Pay up,\r\nor pay the consequences.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:39.761 --\u003e 00:03:42.764\r\n\"One million in cash,\r\nor the Gotham Bank is next.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:43.223 --\u003e 00:03:45.851\r\nSigned, \"The Mad Bomber.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:47.936 --\u003e 00:03:50.564\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf only we knew how he\r\nplanted those bombs.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:51.314 --\u003e 00:03:53.900\r\n\u003ci\u003eFear not, chief.\r\nI think I have the answer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:55.986 --\u003e 00:03:58.405\r\nTime for all little Gray\r\nGhosts to be in bed.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.244 --\u003e 00:04:10.667\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:11.710 --\u003e 00:04:13.253\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Gray Ghost.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:17.090 --\u003e 00:04:19.092\r\nREPORTER: \u003ci\u003eAnd so,\r\nanother building is blown up\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:19.176 --\u003e 00:04:21.803\r\n\u003ci\u003eas Gotham's Mad Bomber\r\ncontinues to demand\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:21.928 --\u003e 00:04:23.722\r\n\u003ci\u003eone million dollars\r\nfrom the city\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:23.805 --\u003e 00:04:25.807\r\n\u003ci\u003eto end his reign of destruction.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:25.932 --\u003e 00:04:27.476\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe question remains,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:27.684 --\u003e 00:04:32.814\r\n\u003ci\u003ehow are the explosives getting past\r\nboth police and bomb-squad experts?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:32.981 --\u003e 00:04:35.442\r\nAnd, what does it have\r\nto do with my old hero?\r\n\r\n00:04:40.947 --\u003e 00:04:42.240\r\nWhat can I do for you?\r\n\r\n00:04:42.407 --\u003e 00:04:45.744\r\nWe're looking for a copy of a film.\r\nActually, a TV show.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.827 --\u003e 00:04:47.370\r\nWe can't find it on video.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.662 --\u003e 00:04:49.581\r\nWell, you've come to\r\nthe right place, pal.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.706 --\u003e 00:04:52.083\r\nI got every TV show\r\never made here.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.250 --\u003e 00:04:54.002\r\nI collect them. It's my life.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.085 --\u003e 00:04:56.588\r\nI got it all.\r\nAnything you want. Name it.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.339 --\u003e 00:04:58.507\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Gray Ghost.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:59.341 --\u003e 00:05:01.259\r\nUh, name something else.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.344 --\u003e 00:05:03.512\r\nYou said you had everything.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.095 --\u003e 00:05:06.389\r\nExcept The Gray Ghost.\r\nNobody has it.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.515 --\u003e 00:05:08.934\r\nThe studio that made that\r\nshow, Spectra,\r\n\r\n00:05:09.059 --\u003e 00:05:12.771\r\nit burned to the ground 20 years ago.\r\nThe negatives went up like kindling.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.854 --\u003e 00:05:14.189\r\nA real shame.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.150 --\u003e 00:05:18.819\r\nSo,\r\nThe Gray Ghost doesn't exist?\r\n\r\n00:05:18.944 --\u003e 00:05:20.153\r\nNot anymore.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.403 --\u003e 00:05:21.488\r\nSorry, pal.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.295 --\u003e 00:05:39.047\r\nBRUCE: So many actors.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.881 --\u003e 00:05:42.884\r\nI wish I knew the one you're looking\r\nfor, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.009 --\u003e 00:05:44.886\r\nBut I don't watch television.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.095 --\u003e 00:05:46.763\r\nI prefer my fireplace.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.099 --\u003e 00:05:52.602\r\n- I found him!\r\n- \"Simon Trent.\"\r\n\r\n00:05:52.769 --\u003e 00:05:54.187\r\nDapper-looking chap.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.271 --\u003e 00:05:56.273\r\nBRUCE: And he's living\r\nright here in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.941 --\u003e 00:05:59.261\r\n- MAN: Trent!\r\n- (KNOCKING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:05:59.317 --\u003e 00:06:01.319\r\nTrent! Do you hear me?\r\n\r\n00:06:02.904 --\u003e 00:06:04.614\r\nTrent! I know you're in there.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.739 --\u003e 00:06:06.366\r\nThis ain't no homeless shelter.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.700 --\u003e 00:06:08.660\r\nPay your rent or get out!\r\n\r\n00:06:08.910 --\u003e 00:06:10.745\r\nLousy, has-been actor!\r\n\r\n00:06:24.718 --\u003e 00:06:27.137\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:27.637 --\u003e 00:06:30.223\r\n- Hello?\r\n- Yeah, it's me, Si.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.682 --\u003e 00:06:32.767\r\nBad news.\r\nYou didn't get the part.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.230 --\u003e 00:06:40.400\r\nI need to work, Frankie.\r\nGet me something. You're my agent.\r\n\r\n00:06:40.901 --\u003e 00:06:43.612\r\nI try, Si. I really do.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.029 --\u003e 00:06:46.531\r\nBut they still think of\r\nyou as the Gray Ghost.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.656 --\u003e 00:06:47.657\r\nThose who remember.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:50.201\r\nI can do other parts.\r\nI'm an actor.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.327 --\u003e 00:06:53.163\r\n\u003ci\u003eI know, Si.\r\nHey, we've been through this before.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:53.288 --\u003e 00:06:56.041\r\n\u003ci\u003eSomething will come up.\r\nJust hang in there, okay?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:14.809 --\u003e 00:07:15.852\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:07:21.983 --\u003e 00:07:23.401\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.155 --\u003e 00:07:28.323\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:07:28.490 --\u003e 00:07:33.870\r\n(CRYING)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.637 --\u003e 00:07:53.848\r\nOh! The original\r\nGray Ghost costume!\r\n\r\n00:07:54.808 --\u003e 00:07:56.393\r\nYou sure you wanna\r\nget rid of this?\r\n\r\n00:07:56.935 --\u003e 00:07:58.061\r\nPositive.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.857 --\u003e 00:08:04.567\r\nI can't pay much, Mr. Trent.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.734 --\u003e 00:08:07.070\r\nYour Gray Ghost merchandise\r\njust isn't much in demand.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.445 --\u003e 00:08:09.489\r\nI mean, no one's buying.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.614 --\u003e 00:08:11.074\r\nI know, Ted.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.741 --\u003e 00:08:13.827\r\nI'll take whatever\r\nyou can give me.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.127 --\u003e 00:08:25.005\r\nWell, old friend,\r\nyou've paid the rent for the last time.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.305 --\u003e 00:08:38.059\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:45.650 --\u003e 00:08:46.901\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:54.617 --\u003e 00:08:58.079\r\n\"Gray Ghost, meet me tonight\r\nat the Gotham Art School.\"\r\n\r\n00:08:58.246 --\u003e 00:08:59.914\r\nSigned, \"A friend.\"\r\n\r\n00:09:28.485 --\u003e 00:09:29.694\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.778 --\u003e 00:09:30.779\r\nYou?\r\n\r\n00:09:32.405 --\u003e 00:09:33.782\r\nI need your help.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.999 --\u003e 00:09:47.545\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:56.596 --\u003e 00:09:57.847\r\nWhat do you want from me?\r\n\r\n00:09:58.556 --\u003e 00:10:01.768\r\nSome madman is blowing up\r\nGotham, piece by piece.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.976 --\u003e 00:10:04.938\r\nSomehow, it's connected\r\nto the Gray Ghost. To you.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.357 --\u003e 00:10:08.441\r\nWhat are you talking about?\r\n\r\n00:10:08.525 --\u003e 00:10:11.444\r\nI'm just an actor.\r\nThe Gray Ghost was a part I played.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.278 --\u003e 00:10:15.115\r\nThe bombings in Gotham are\r\nexactly like an episode\r\n\r\n00:10:15.198 --\u003e 00:10:16.282\r\n\u003ci\u003eof The Gray Ghost.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:16.449 --\u003e 00:10:18.243\r\nI need you to remember\r\nhow it was done.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.827 --\u003e 00:10:21.496\r\nI made hundreds of those shows.\r\nThey're all a blur!\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:24.999\r\nNow, leave me alone.\r\nJust leave me alone!\r\n\r\n00:10:28.962 --\u003e 00:10:31.131\r\n(BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.214 --\u003e 00:10:32.257\r\nThat noise.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.442 --\u003e 00:10:52.485\r\nWait.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.750 --\u003e 00:11:14.465\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:20.680 --\u003e 00:11:21.764\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:11:23.975 --\u003e 00:11:25.351\r\nYou know something.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.768 --\u003e 00:11:27.353\r\nYou recognized that sound.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.021 --\u003e 00:11:29.147\r\nThis is harassment.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.272 --\u003e 00:11:30.773\r\nI'm calling the police.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.110 --\u003e 00:11:37.155\r\nWe know the next bomb is going\r\nto hit the Gotham Library.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.780 --\u003e 00:11:38.865\r\nHelp me.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.967 --\u003e 00:12:00.303\r\nHere's your answer.\r\nTake it and go!\r\n\r\n00:12:00.470 --\u003e 00:12:01.554\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:12:10.647 --\u003e 00:12:13.399\r\nI used to admire what\r\nthe Gray Ghost stood for.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.733 --\u003e 00:12:16.444\r\nI'm not the Gray Ghost.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.528 --\u003e 00:12:18.988\r\nI can see that now.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.126 --\u003e 00:12:36.506\r\nNARRATOR: Out of the darkness\r\n\u003ci\u003ecomes\u003c/i\u003e the Gray Ghost!\r\n\r\n00:12:48.893 --\u003e 00:12:50.687\r\nALFRED: Popcorn, sir.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.385 --\u003e 00:13:24.429\r\n(BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.558 --\u003e 00:13:29.559\r\nThat's it.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.767 --\u003e 00:13:31.060\r\nThat's the noise.\r\n\r\n00:13:31.144 --\u003e 00:13:33.354\r\n(BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:13:36.149 --\u003e 00:13:38.192\r\nYou've gotta be kidding me.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.991 --\u003e 00:13:46.284\r\nThat's right, commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.534 --\u003e 00:13:49.662\r\nRemote-controlled toy cars\r\nloaded with explosives.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.829 --\u003e 00:13:51.807\r\nWe'll know what to look for\r\nat the library, tonight.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.831 --\u003e 00:13:58.546\r\n- (HELICOPTER BLADES WHIRRING)\r\n- (POLICE CHATTER ON RADIO)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.231 --\u003e 00:14:20.818\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:27.033 --\u003e 00:14:28.076\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:31.996 --\u003e 00:14:33.623\r\nThere they are. Fire!\r\n\r\n00:15:11.452 --\u003e 00:15:12.453\r\n(CLANKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:32.723 --\u003e 00:15:34.475\r\nHmm. No explosives.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.600 --\u003e 00:15:35.601\r\nA decoy?\r\n\r\n00:15:43.401 --\u003e 00:15:44.735\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:56.581 --\u003e 00:15:57.832\r\nAhhh!\r\n\r\n00:16:10.136 --\u003e 00:16:11.304\r\nYou.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.139 --\u003e 00:16:14.307\r\nLike you said,\r\n\r\n00:16:14.599 --\u003e 00:16:15.975\r\nyou need my help.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.726 --\u003e 00:16:17.727\r\nLook familiar?\r\n\r\n00:16:20.521 --\u003e 00:16:21.647\r\nMore than familiar.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.064 --\u003e 00:16:23.191\r\nIt's identical.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.649 --\u003e 00:16:26.235\r\nLook. It even has the\r\nGray Ghost brand name.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.486 --\u003e 00:16:28.029\r\nBetter check it for prints.\r\n\r\n00:16:28.654 --\u003e 00:16:29.655\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.780 --\u003e 00:16:31.032\r\nHey, I owed you.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.115 --\u003e 00:16:32.825\r\nYou got me my outfit back.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.417 --\u003e 00:16:42.585\r\nGray Ghost.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.919 --\u003e 00:16:43.920\r\nYes?\r\n\r\n00:16:44.086 --\u003e 00:16:45.880\r\nYou want to give me\r\na hand with this?\r\n\r\n00:16:46.255 --\u003e 00:16:48.216\r\nUh... Sure.\r\n\r\n00:16:58.392 --\u003e 00:17:01.854\r\n(BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:17:04.690 --\u003e 00:17:05.733\r\nDrive.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.030 --\u003e 00:17:12.031\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.009 --\u003e 00:17:33.803\r\nMore of them.\r\nAnd they're gaining on us.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.011 --\u003e 00:17:35.555\r\nTry the green switch.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.158 --\u003e 00:17:58.327\r\n(LAUGHS) Hey,\r\nwe did it, partner!\r\n\r\n00:18:11.632 --\u003e 00:18:13.634\r\nThis place is amazing.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.468 --\u003e 00:18:15.469\r\nIt's just like...\r\n\r\n00:18:15.970 --\u003e 00:18:17.763\r\nThe Gray Ghost's lair?\r\n\r\n00:18:17.888 --\u003e 00:18:20.600\r\nIt's almost an exact replica.\r\n\r\n00:18:20.725 --\u003e 00:18:22.727\r\nLet me show you something else.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.064 --\u003e 00:18:28.274\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:31.652 --\u003e 00:18:34.822\r\nBATMAN: As a kid,\r\nI used to watch you with my father.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.364 --\u003e 00:18:37.241\r\nThe Gray Ghost was my hero.\r\n\r\n00:18:37.908 --\u003e 00:18:39.827\r\nSo, it wasn't all for nothing.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.497 --\u003e 00:18:44.498\r\nWhat did you find?\r\n\r\n00:18:44.624 --\u003e 00:18:46.250\r\nFingerprints on the toy car.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.209 --\u003e 00:18:48.753\r\nAnd they belong to...\r\n\r\n00:18:49.837 --\u003e 00:18:51.839\r\nYou, Simon Trent.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.089 --\u003e 00:18:53.549\r\nThat's not possible.\r\n\r\n00:18:55.176 --\u003e 00:18:56.802\r\nYour prints are on this car.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.011 --\u003e 00:18:58.763\r\nYou had the only\r\ncopy of the show.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.138 --\u003e 00:19:01.932\r\nThe Mad Bomber followed\r\nthe show step by step.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.099 --\u003e 00:19:04.268\r\nBut, I'm not the Mad\r\nBomber, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.393 --\u003e 00:19:08.356\r\nI'm not. I sold my Gray Ghost\r\ncars months ago to pay for my...\r\n\r\n00:19:09.357 --\u003e 00:19:10.399\r\nNo,\r\n\r\n00:19:10.650 --\u003e 00:19:12.568\r\nit can't be him!\r\n\r\n00:19:13.486 --\u003e 00:19:20.409\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.202 --\u003e 00:19:22.244\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:22.328 --\u003e 00:19:24.413\r\n(ALARM BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:25.998 --\u003e 00:19:29.168\r\nWell, if it isn't the\r\nDark Knight himself.\r\n\r\n00:19:29.585 --\u003e 00:19:31.879\r\nYou're finished, Mad Bomber.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.714 --\u003e 00:19:35.007\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.091 --\u003e 00:19:36.926\r\n(BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:19:49.105 --\u003e 00:19:51.482\r\nTime to put your toys\r\naway, little man.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.816 --\u003e 00:19:52.817\r\nTED: I can't.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.900 --\u003e 00:19:54.318\r\nYou see, I need the money,\r\n\r\n00:19:54.652 --\u003e 00:19:56.028\r\nto buy more toys.\r\n\r\n00:19:56.237 --\u003e 00:19:57.822\r\nI love toys.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.988 --\u003e 00:19:59.240\r\nThey can play songs.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.824 --\u003e 00:20:01.075\r\nThey can dance.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.535 --\u003e 00:20:03.661\r\nThey can even eat money.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.120 --\u003e 00:20:05.830\r\nOh, boy, can they eat money.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.288 --\u003e 00:20:07.915\r\nAll my money.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.082 --\u003e 00:20:09.125\r\nAnd then,\r\n\r\n00:20:09.291 --\u003e 00:20:11.877\r\nI remembered an episode\r\nof The Gray Ghost.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.169 --\u003e 00:20:14.088\r\nAnd I knew what\r\nelse a toy could do.\r\n\r\n00:20:14.463 --\u003e 00:20:15.840\r\nIt can carry a bomb.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.507 --\u003e 00:20:18.634\r\nIt can hold a city for ransom.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.926 --\u003e 00:20:20.845\r\nOh, the power of the toy.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.470 --\u003e 00:20:23.055\r\nIt can earn millions.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.139 --\u003e 00:20:26.350\r\nMillions for the little,\r\nold toy collector, me.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.434 --\u003e 00:20:28.561\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:57.631 --\u003e 00:20:58.883\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:58.966 --\u003e 00:21:03.179\r\nMy toys!\r\nMy toys, my beautiful toys!\r\n\r\n00:21:09.310 --\u003e 00:21:11.479\r\nREPORTER: Gothamites have\r\nturned out in record numbers\r\n\r\n00:21:11.562 --\u003e 00:21:13.147\r\nto celebrate the video release\r\n\r\n00:21:13.272 --\u003e 00:21:16.150\r\nof the long-lost Gray\r\nGhost television series.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.233 --\u003e 00:21:19.236\r\nAnd on hand, for the festivities\r\nis the toast of the town,\r\n\r\n00:21:19.361 --\u003e 00:21:22.406\r\nthe Gray Ghost\r\nhimself, Simon Trent.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.782 --\u003e 00:21:24.700\r\nBRUCE: Please make\r\nit out to \"Bruce.\"\r\n\r\n00:21:29.246 --\u003e 00:21:30.706\r\nThere you go, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.373 --\u003e 00:21:32.708\r\nThanks, Mr. Trent.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.461 --\u003e 00:21:37.755\r\nYou know, as a kid,\r\nI used to watch you with my father.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.422 --\u003e 00:21:39.840\r\nThe Gray Ghost was my hero.\r\n\r\n00:21:40.424 --\u003e 00:21:41.675\r\nReally?\r\n\r\n00:21:42.134 --\u003e 00:21:43.844\r\nAnd he still is.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.394 --\u003e 00:21:54.396\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.087 --\u003e 00:22:19.088\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E33 - Cat Scratch Fever (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.672 --\u003e 00:00:07.674\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.833 --\u003e 00:01:27.170\r\nJUDGE: Selina Kyle, you have pled guilty\r\nto the charges brought against Catwoman.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.254 --\u003e 00:01:28.547\r\nAnd do you understand\r\n\r\n00:01:28.630 --\u003e 00:01:32.718\r\nyou can be sentenced to as\r\nmuch as 25 years in prison?\r\n\r\n00:01:32.801 --\u003e 00:01:34.303\r\nYes, Your Honor.\r\n\r\n00:01:36.471 --\u003e 00:01:38.765\r\nRegardless of the fact that\r\nyou committed the crimes\r\n\r\n00:01:38.849 --\u003e 00:01:42.603\r\nto benefit animals and\r\nwildlife, theft is theft.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.686 --\u003e 00:01:44.104\r\nSELINA: Yes, Your Honor.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.187 --\u003e 00:01:48.358\r\nHowever, since you did help save\r\nGotham City from annihilation\r\n\r\n00:01:48.442 --\u003e 00:01:51.445\r\nand the district attorney has\r\nrecommended a plea bargain,\r\n\r\n00:01:51.528 --\u003e 00:01:56.325\r\nI have decided to sentence\r\nyou to five years probation.\r\n\r\n00:01:56.408 --\u003e 00:01:59.703\r\n- MAN: Yeah.\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:02.080 --\u003e 00:02:04.082\r\nI'm not finished!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.460 --\u003e 00:02:08.378\r\nBut I'm warning you, Miss Kyle,\r\n\r\n00:02:08.712 --\u003e 00:02:14.009\r\nif you ever don your Catwoman\r\ncostume again to violate the law,\r\n\r\n00:02:14.092 --\u003e 00:02:18.805\r\nI'll not only revoke probation,\r\nI'll throw the book at you.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.264 --\u003e 00:02:20.682\r\nI understand.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.142 --\u003e 00:02:25.103\r\nREPORTER: Miss Kyle,\r\none question from you and a picture.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.187 --\u003e 00:02:28.315\r\nREPORTER 2: I'll lose my job\r\nif I don't get the question.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.398 --\u003e 00:02:30.108\r\nREPORTER 3: Miss\r\nKyle, Miss Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.317 --\u003e 00:02:32.637\r\nREPORTER 4: Just one question.\r\nLs Catwoman really finished?\r\n\r\n00:02:33.028 --\u003e 00:02:35.155\r\nAnd though she's been\r\nreleased on probation,\r\n\r\n00:02:35.238 --\u003e 00:02:37.324\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe question still remains.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:37.407 --\u003e 00:02:40.410\r\n\u003ci\u003eCan this lady leopard\r\nreally change her spots?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:43.330 --\u003e 00:02:47.918\r\nI do hope you'll be seeing Miss Selina\r\nnow that she's free to prowl again.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.794 --\u003e 00:02:50.212\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.671 --\u003e 00:02:53.048\r\nBut I thought you'd\r\ngrown quite fond of her.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.131 --\u003e 00:02:54.966\r\nI assumed the\r\nfeeling was mutual.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.426 --\u003e 00:02:57.636\r\nAlmost.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.722 --\u003e 00:03:02.265\r\nShe's in love with Batman.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.308 --\u003e 00:03:04.309\r\nOh, dear.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.393 --\u003e 00:03:07.437\r\nThese modern relationships\r\ncan be so complicated.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.521 --\u003e 00:03:12.442\r\nBesides, I'm not totally convinced\r\nshe's given up her criminal life.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.658 --\u003e 00:03:22.869\r\n(LAUGHING) Oh, Maven,\r\nI can't believe I'm really free.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.371 --\u003e 00:03:25.789\r\nCome here, Isis.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.958 --\u003e 00:03:29.584\r\nWhere's my little precious?\r\n\r\n00:03:33.797 --\u003e 00:03:36.383\r\nUm, there's something\r\nI have to tell you.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.633 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nMaven, where's my cat?\r\n\r\n00:03:38.719 --\u003e 00:03:41.096\r\nI... I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.179 --\u003e 00:03:44.307\r\nA couple of days ago,\r\nI left the window open, and she was gone.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.016 --\u003e 00:03:46.810\r\nI think she went\r\nlooking for you.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:49.771\r\nI searched everywhere.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.855 --\u003e 00:03:52.065\r\nI'm so sorry, Selina.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.194 --\u003e 00:03:58.034\r\nRADIO \u003ci\u003eDJ: Temperatures\r\nhave reached record lows\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:58.071 --\u003e 00:04:00.115\r\n\u003ci\u003eas another snowstorm\r\nheads our way.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:00.198 --\u003e 00:04:03.660\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe advise our listeners to\r\nkeep children and pets inside.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:28.101 --\u003e 00:04:30.103\r\n(WHISTLING SILENTLY)\r\n\r\n00:04:31.354 --\u003e 00:04:32.773\r\n(CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.443 --\u003e 00:04:37.444\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:04:38.945 --\u003e 00:04:39.946\r\n(WHISTLING SILENTLY)\r\n\r\n00:04:46.244 --\u003e 00:04:47.329\r\n(SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:04:47.412 --\u003e 00:04:48.413\r\n(BOTH SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:48.830 --\u003e 00:04:51.291\r\n(CATS MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:04:53.919 --\u003e 00:04:55.253\r\nSELINA: Isis?\r\n\r\n00:04:55.337 --\u003e 00:04:57.088\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:04:57.839 --\u003e 00:04:59.591\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:05:01.092 --\u003e 00:05:02.886\r\nRelax. I'm a friend.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.057 --\u003e 00:05:09.059\r\n(VEHICLE APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:16.650 --\u003e 00:05:17.651\r\n(DOOR SLAMMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:22.531 --\u003e 00:05:23.532\r\n(CAT MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.912 --\u003e 00:05:29.955\r\n(BOTH MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:05:30.413 --\u003e 00:05:31.414\r\nFleabags.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.498 --\u003e 00:05:33.542\r\nDirty, lousy, stinking fleabags.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.625 --\u003e 00:05:35.043\r\nGet them, Paunch.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.877 --\u003e 00:05:37.295\r\n(BOTH SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:38.213 --\u003e 00:05:39.464\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:05:39.548 --\u003e 00:05:43.176\r\nCome to mama,\r\nyou disgusting furball.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.178 --\u003e 00:05:47.097\r\nJust what do you\r\nthink you're doing?\r\n\r\n00:05:47.430 --\u003e 00:05:48.849\r\nCatching strays.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.932 --\u003e 00:05:49.975\r\nWhat's it to you?\r\n\r\n00:05:50.475 --\u003e 00:05:52.811\r\nYou're obviously not\r\nthe animal shelter.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.894 --\u003e 00:05:54.855\r\nSo, what do you want\r\nwith these cats?\r\n\r\n00:05:55.355 --\u003e 00:05:57.899\r\nNone of your business.\r\nSo kiss off.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.983 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nSELINA: Fine.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:00.861\r\n- But I'm taking my friends.\r\n- Hey.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.361 --\u003e 00:06:03.113\r\nYou asked for it, sister.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.030 --\u003e 00:06:05.365\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:05.448 --\u003e 00:06:08.034\r\nNow, tell me,\r\nwhat are you up to?\r\n\r\n00:06:08.118 --\u003e 00:06:10.704\r\n(EXCLAIMS) Paunch, do something!\r\n\r\n00:06:13.748 --\u003e 00:06:15.584\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:06:16.334 --\u003e 00:06:18.128\r\n- (BOTH GROANING)\r\n- (METAL CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:19.671 --\u003e 00:06:20.964\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:06:21.715 --\u003e 00:06:23.592\r\nThat's one way to\r\ntake out the trash.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.675 --\u003e 00:06:26.094\r\nLaugh this off, sister!\r\n\r\n00:06:30.223 --\u003e 00:06:31.308\r\nNail her!\r\n\r\n00:06:39.190 --\u003e 00:06:40.191\r\n(PAUNCH GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:41.610 --\u003e 00:06:42.652\r\nPaunch?\r\n\r\n00:06:44.321 --\u003e 00:06:47.824\r\nWOMAN: (ECHOING) Hey,\r\nyou can't do this to me!\r\n\r\n00:06:50.410 --\u003e 00:06:52.746\r\n- Put a lid on it, sister.\r\n- (WOMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:54.205 --\u003e 00:06:55.206\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:58.084 --\u003e 00:07:00.295\r\nYou were supposed to\r\nstay out of trouble.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.378 --\u003e 00:07:03.924\r\nDon't tell me you're my very\r\nown private probation officer.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.382 --\u003e 00:07:06.384\r\nHow often would you\r\nlike me to check in?\r\n\r\n00:07:08.136 --\u003e 00:07:09.304\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.977 --\u003e 00:07:18.438\r\nI'm afraid our reunion\r\nwill have to wait.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.651 --\u003e 00:07:24.277\r\nAll right, what's going on here?\r\n\r\n00:07:26.112 --\u003e 00:07:27.113\r\nShe jumped us.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.197 --\u003e 00:07:28.448\r\nI wanna press charges.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.531 --\u003e 00:07:30.200\r\nThey were stealing cats.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.201 --\u003e 00:07:33.161\r\nWOMAN: Stealing from\r\nwho, you dumb cluck?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.495 --\u003e 00:07:34.621\r\nThey're strays.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.704 --\u003e 00:07:36.682\r\nWe were just rounding them\r\nup to find them good homes\r\n\r\n00:07:36.706 --\u003e 00:07:38.917\r\nwhen this maniac attacked us.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.000 --\u003e 00:07:40.502\r\nThis is insane.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.044 --\u003e 00:07:44.464\r\nSounds like we better settle\r\nthis downtown, Miss Kyle.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.547 --\u003e 00:07:45.590\r\nDowntown?\r\n\r\n00:07:45.674 --\u003e 00:07:47.759\r\nOFFICER: You have the\r\nright to remain silent.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.842 --\u003e 00:07:51.304\r\nAnything you say can and will be\r\nused against you in a court of law.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.643 --\u003e 00:07:59.229\r\nMAN: The speed at which the toxin\r\novertakes the animal's system\r\n\r\n00:07:59.312 --\u003e 00:08:01.064\r\nis something to\r\nbehold, Mr. Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.147 --\u003e 00:08:03.692\r\nEven with a species this large.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.775 --\u003e 00:08:05.485\r\n- (DOGS BARKING)\r\n- (CAT MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.568 --\u003e 00:08:07.070\r\n- (SYRINGE STABBING)\r\n- There.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.153 --\u003e 00:08:09.489\r\nYou can see the change\r\nalmost instantly.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.906 --\u003e 00:08:10.949\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:11.908 --\u003e 00:08:13.108\r\n- Careful, sir.\r\n- (DOG BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:13.368 --\u003e 00:08:15.662\r\nOne little nip,\r\nand the toxin will spread through you\r\n\r\n00:08:15.745 --\u003e 00:08:17.425\r\n- with the same virulence.\r\n- (DOG GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:20.375 --\u003e 00:08:21.668\r\nGood, Milo.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.751 --\u003e 00:08:23.920\r\nRemember,\r\nspeed is of the essence.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.047 --\u003e 00:08:28.800\r\nI expect this operation to be\r\ncompleted by tomorrow night.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.888 --\u003e 00:08:35.306\r\nMILO: Sorry, kitten.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.599 --\u003e 00:08:38.560\r\n(lsls MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:08:38.643 --\u003e 00:08:40.520\r\nBut you heard the man.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.161 --\u003e 00:08:57.328\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:57.412 --\u003e 00:09:01.332\r\nMaven, how on Earth did you\r\nraise my bail at this hour?\r\n\r\n00:09:01.416 --\u003e 00:09:02.417\r\n(MAVEN CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.173 --\u003e 00:09:09.382\r\nI see.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.009 --\u003e 00:09:13.511\r\nSELINA: Your bail money is safe.\r\nI promise.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.595 --\u003e 00:09:15.555\r\nBRUCE: That's not\r\nimportant, Selina.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.638 --\u003e 00:09:16.639\r\nYou are.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.017 --\u003e 00:09:21.644\r\nBruce, I like you a lot.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.228 --\u003e 00:09:23.438\r\nBut as a friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.355 --\u003e 00:09:25.440\r\nI understand.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.940 --\u003e 00:09:29.819\r\nThen, as a friend, may I point out this\r\narrest could revoke your probation?\r\n\r\n00:09:29.903 --\u003e 00:09:32.113\r\nI'll worry about that\r\nafter I find my cat.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.447 --\u003e 00:09:34.991\r\nWhat I wanna know is what\r\nthose creeps I met in the alley\r\n\r\n00:09:35.075 --\u003e 00:09:37.619\r\nare doing with a big-time\r\nattorney from Daggett Labs.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.078 --\u003e 00:09:42.165\r\nI spend a night in jail, and he has them\r\nback on the street in less than an hour.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.248 --\u003e 00:09:45.502\r\nRoland Daggett is a dangerous\r\nman, Selina.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.585 --\u003e 00:09:46.961\r\nI'd be very careful.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:48.588\r\nDon't worry.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.130 --\u003e 00:09:52.634\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou won't see Selina Kyle\r\nanywhere near Daggett Labs.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:11.486 --\u003e 00:10:14.155\r\nLUCIUS: Our sources tell us that\r\nDaggett's pharmaceuticals arm\r\n\r\n00:10:14.239 --\u003e 00:10:16.324\r\nis coming out with\r\na hot new drug.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.450 --\u003e 00:10:18.660\r\nWhat kind?\r\n\r\n00:10:18.910 --\u003e 00:10:20.662\r\nSome sort of antitoxin.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.745 --\u003e 00:10:24.165\r\nAll we really know is Daggett's had\r\nhis best people on it for months.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.041 --\u003e 00:10:26.251\r\nWhy the sudden interest?\r\n\r\n00:10:26.835 --\u003e 00:10:27.915\r\nThink he's up to something?\r\n\r\n00:10:28.253 --\u003e 00:10:30.255\r\nThat goes without\r\nsaying, doesn't it?\r\n\r\n00:10:32.924 --\u003e 00:10:34.968\r\n(ANIMALS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:10:42.851 --\u003e 00:10:45.061\r\n(ANIMALS WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:45.145 --\u003e 00:10:47.188\r\n(WHISPERING QUIETLY)\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:49.774\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:10:49.858 --\u003e 00:10:51.025\r\nIsis!\r\n\r\n00:10:51.109 --\u003e 00:10:52.110\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:10:55.780 --\u003e 00:10:58.074\r\nOh, what have they done to\r\nyou, my precious?\r\n\r\n00:10:58.158 --\u003e 00:10:59.284\r\n(SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:10:59.367 --\u003e 00:11:01.744\r\n- (EXCLAIMS)\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:01.828 --\u003e 00:11:04.122\r\n(DOGS BARKING LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:07.792 --\u003e 00:11:09.127\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:16.634 --\u003e 00:11:19.095\r\nWell,\r\nlookie what the cat dragged in.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.637 --\u003e 00:11:22.307\r\nNasty wound you got\r\nthere, pussycat.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.390 --\u003e 00:11:25.059\r\nYou gonna lick it and\r\nmake it all better?\r\n\r\n00:11:25.143 --\u003e 00:11:26.936\r\nWhat have you done\r\nto these animals?\r\n\r\n00:11:27.020 --\u003e 00:11:31.191\r\nNothing compared to what we're\r\ngonna do to you, pussycat.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.193 --\u003e 00:11:34.194\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:34.569 --\u003e 00:11:36.571\r\n(LIQUID SIZZLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.946 --\u003e 00:11:38.281\r\n(ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:45.705 --\u003e 00:11:47.749\r\nLet's skin that cat!\r\n\r\n00:11:47.832 --\u003e 00:11:51.586\r\nYou two yobbos wouldn't have\r\nnoticed, but she's been bitten.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.669 --\u003e 00:11:54.380\r\nShe can run from us,\r\nbut not the toxin.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.344 --\u003e 00:12:00.386\r\nIsis.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.470 --\u003e 00:12:01.471\r\n(lsls GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.645 --\u003e 00:12:10.063\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:17.904 --\u003e 00:12:18.905\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:20.490 --\u003e 00:12:21.783\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:28.456 --\u003e 00:12:29.457\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:31.918 --\u003e 00:12:33.002\r\nCATWOMAN: Isis?\r\n\r\n00:12:33.086 --\u003e 00:12:34.379\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:12:37.465 --\u003e 00:12:39.801\r\n(CATWOMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:45.431 --\u003e 00:12:47.016\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:47.600 --\u003e 00:12:49.018\r\nWhat's happening to me?\r\n\r\n00:12:49.102 --\u003e 00:12:52.230\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:58.278 --\u003e 00:12:59.696\r\nIsis.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.779 --\u003e 00:13:01.322\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:13:12.292 --\u003e 00:13:13.293\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:16.796 --\u003e 00:13:18.631\r\nStay away from me.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.882 --\u003e 00:13:21.050\r\nNo! (GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.134 --\u003e 00:13:22.844\r\nCatwoman, it's me.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.679 --\u003e 00:13:25.680\r\nCATWOMAN: Batman?\r\n\r\n00:13:27.974 --\u003e 00:13:29.350\r\nYou're hot.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.767 --\u003e 00:13:30.852\r\nNow you notice.\r\n\r\n00:13:31.269 --\u003e 00:13:33.021\r\nI've got to get you to a doctor.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.104 --\u003e 00:13:34.981\r\nNo. You can't.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.064 --\u003e 00:13:36.691\r\nDaggett will have me arrested.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.774 --\u003e 00:13:38.401\r\nI have a hideaway.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.484 --\u003e 00:13:40.695\r\nNot far. Please.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.078 --\u003e 00:13:52.540\r\nYou know, you haven't told me why\r\nyou've come to my rescue, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.832 --\u003e 00:13:54.834\r\nAre you getting\r\nsoft on criminals\r\n\r\n00:13:55.251 --\u003e 00:13:56.294\r\nor just on me?\r\n\r\n00:13:56.377 --\u003e 00:13:59.047\r\nI think the fever is\r\nmaking you delusional.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.130 --\u003e 00:14:01.341\r\nEver the escape artist, I see.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.424 --\u003e 00:14:03.051\r\n(MOANING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:03.134 --\u003e 00:14:04.218\r\nBATMAN: What's this?\r\n\r\n00:14:05.345 --\u003e 00:14:06.512\r\nIsis bit me.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.596 --\u003e 00:14:10.099\r\n(STAMMERING) It's not her fault.\r\nThey did something to her.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.183 --\u003e 00:14:11.893\r\nAll the animals.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.976 --\u003e 00:14:15.396\r\n(WEAKLY) Must save Isis.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.522 --\u003e 00:14:17.857\r\nAnd we will.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.989 --\u003e 00:14:25.990\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:14:34.082 --\u003e 00:14:35.291\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:37.043 --\u003e 00:14:38.753\r\nWhat's the delay, Milo?\r\n\r\n00:14:38.836 --\u003e 00:14:41.089\r\nYou should have had these\r\nanimals on the street by now.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.422 --\u003e 00:14:44.384\r\nUh, uh, right, Mr. Daggett.\r\nWe're waiting for Paunch.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.467 --\u003e 00:14:47.095\r\nI sent him to the warehouse\r\nfor a pack of the antitoxin\r\n\r\n00:14:47.512 --\u003e 00:14:51.015\r\njust in case there are any accidents\r\nwhile transporting the animals.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.307 --\u003e 00:14:53.017\r\n(MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:54.143 --\u003e 00:14:56.062\r\nLet's play a little game.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.437 --\u003e 00:14:58.856\r\nI'll try to guess Daggett's plan\r\n\r\n00:14:58.940 --\u003e 00:15:01.025\r\nand you'll let me\r\nknow if I'm right.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.109 --\u003e 00:15:03.152\r\n(MUFFLED SPEECH)\r\n\r\n00:15:09.033 --\u003e 00:15:13.287\r\nBATMAN: Viral antitoxins for a\r\nplague that doesn't exist yet.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.955 --\u003e 00:15:16.874\r\nBut if the plague is introduced\r\nvia stray dogs and cats\r\n\r\n00:15:16.958 --\u003e 00:15:19.752\r\nit'll blanket Gotham\r\nCity within weeks.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.836 --\u003e 00:15:21.254\r\nDAGGETT: Days, actually.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.004 --\u003e 00:15:24.882\r\nYou know how many strays\r\nthere are in Gotham, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:15:24.966 --\u003e 00:15:26.801\r\nThree hundred thousand.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.301 --\u003e 00:15:30.221\r\nImagine if even a tenth\r\nof them carried the virus.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.304 --\u003e 00:15:32.723\r\nNot only will this little\r\nbottle make me a hero,\r\n\r\n00:15:32.807 --\u003e 00:15:34.725\r\nit'll make me a fortune as well.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.809 --\u003e 00:15:36.227\r\n- Take care of him.\r\n- (GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:37.353 --\u003e 00:15:38.771\r\n(MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.566 --\u003e 00:15:42.567\r\nGet him!\r\n\r\n00:15:56.414 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:58.791 --\u003e 00:15:59.876\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:16:07.842 --\u003e 00:16:09.927\r\n(DOG BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:18.936 --\u003e 00:16:22.148\r\nThattaboy, Fido.\r\nRip him to bits.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.035 --\u003e 00:16:35.912\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.093 --\u003e 00:16:54.430\r\nI can't imagine he\r\ncould elude that beast.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.514 --\u003e 00:16:57.016\r\nYou'd better make sure of\r\nthat, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.308 --\u003e 00:17:01.145\r\nBecause if he does get away,\r\nI suggest you keep on driving\r\n\r\n00:17:01.604 --\u003e 00:17:04.690\r\nas far away from Gotham as\r\nthis truck can take you.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.074 --\u003e 00:17:15.076\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:17:15.159 --\u003e 00:17:16.452\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:20.706 --\u003e 00:17:22.708\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:34.971 --\u003e 00:17:35.972\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.097 --\u003e 00:17:38.558\r\n(DOG BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:17:47.316 --\u003e 00:17:50.111\r\n(FAINT BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:11.048 --\u003e 00:18:12.049\r\n(VEHICLE APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:19.265 --\u003e 00:18:20.933\r\n(DOG BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:23.477 --\u003e 00:18:24.478\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:25.104 --\u003e 00:18:26.105\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:35.573 --\u003e 00:18:37.491\r\nHa! He's dog meat.\r\n\r\n00:18:37.575 --\u003e 00:18:39.744\r\n(BATMAN STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:18:58.346 --\u003e 00:19:00.890\r\n(DOG SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:19:04.018 --\u003e 00:19:05.061\r\n(DOG GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:06.687 --\u003e 00:19:07.730\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.235 --\u003e 00:19:15.237\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:16.030 --\u003e 00:19:17.323\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:34.298 --\u003e 00:19:35.758\r\nHe's not coming up.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.841 --\u003e 00:19:39.220\r\nJust let him show those\r\npointy little ears.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.514 --\u003e 00:19:42.890\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.315 --\u003e 00:19:54.193\r\nNo one could withstand\r\nthis degree of hypothermia.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.276 --\u003e 00:19:56.445\r\nGuy's gotta be an\r\nice cube by now.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.321 --\u003e 00:19:58.322\r\n(WOMAN SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:59.365 --\u003e 00:20:00.950\r\nMILO: Look out, you fool!\r\n\r\n00:20:01.033 --\u003e 00:20:02.284\r\n(WOMAN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:20:11.210 --\u003e 00:20:12.211\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:14.046 --\u003e 00:20:15.131\r\n(BOTH GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.214 --\u003e 00:20:17.633\r\nIt's off to the pound for you.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.096 --\u003e 00:20:24.557\r\n(MOANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.697 --\u003e 00:20:41.907\r\nMAVEN: Tonight on the news,\r\nthey called you a hero.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.325 --\u003e 00:20:46.662\r\nYou keep this up,\r\nand they'll start making Catwoman dolls.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.710 --\u003e 00:20:54.044\r\nAre you sure you'll be okay?\r\n\r\n00:20:54.503 --\u003e 00:20:55.838\r\nGo home, Maven.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.921 --\u003e 00:20:57.173\r\nAnd thanks.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.132 --\u003e 00:21:00.342\r\nShe'll turn up. I know she will.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.904 --\u003e 00:21:20.905\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:21:26.118 --\u003e 00:21:27.953\r\n(MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:21:28.037 --\u003e 00:21:29.371\r\nIsis.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.624 --\u003e 00:21:33.459\r\nIsis, you're all right.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.378 --\u003e 00:21:37.713\r\nBut how?\r\n\r\n00:21:51.977 --\u003e 00:21:53.979\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.337 --\u003e 00:22:19.338\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E34 - I Am The Night (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.839 --\u003e 00:00:07.341\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.344 --\u003e 00:01:35.596\r\nALFRED: Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:01:36.096 --\u003e 00:01:38.807\r\nAre you all right, sir?\r\n\r\n00:01:39.057 --\u003e 00:01:42.019\r\n- I'm tired, Alfred.\r\n- I shouldn't wonder.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.144 --\u003e 00:01:46.481\r\nYou've taken no meals today.\r\nI can't recall when you last slept.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.065 --\u003e 00:01:49.526\r\nA weary body can be dealt with\r\n\r\n00:01:49.693 --\u003e 00:01:52.946\r\nbut a weary spirit,\r\nthat's something else.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.620 --\u003e 00:02:03.665\r\nSometimes, old friend, I wonder if\r\nI'm really doing any good out there.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.957 --\u003e 00:02:07.502\r\nHow can you doubt it?\r\nThe lives you've saved,\r\n\r\n00:02:07.586 --\u003e 00:02:09.921\r\nthe criminals you've\r\nbrought to justice.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.005 --\u003e 00:02:13.717\r\nI've put out a few fires,\r\nyes, won a few battles.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.800 --\u003e 00:02:17.929\r\nBut the war goes on, Alfred.\r\nOn and on.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.059 --\u003e 00:02:23.852\r\nYou have it, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:02:23.935 --\u003e 00:02:25.187\r\nOf course, sir.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.240 --\u003e 00:02:38.867\r\n(CAR HORNS BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:02:48.543 --\u003e 00:02:50.671\r\n(BLOWING AIR)\r\n\r\n00:02:53.715 --\u003e 00:02:57.219\r\nIt's a done deal. You're looking\r\nat the new vice president of-\r\n\r\n00:02:57.302 --\u003e 00:03:01.431\r\nExcuse me, folks. Spare some change?\r\nTrying to get bus fare home.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.307 --\u003e 00:03:04.059\r\nUh, sure.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.190 --\u003e 00:03:11.775\r\nWorks every time.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.041 --\u003e 00:03:30.502\r\nI say we take them now,\r\nbefore the deal happens.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.669 --\u003e 00:03:33.130\r\nWe got enough on them.\r\nWhat are we waiting for?\r\n\r\n00:03:33.213 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\nBatman. He got us the\r\ndirt on the Jazzman.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.258 --\u003e 00:03:38.427\r\nSaid he'd be here when\r\nthe hammer went down.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.475 --\u003e 00:03:47.060\r\n(CASH REGISTER DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.440 --\u003e 00:03:52.774\r\nBatman. (SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:04:03.285 --\u003e 00:04:05.704\r\nYou seem quieter\r\nthan usual tonight.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.829 --\u003e 00:04:09.958\r\nEvery year I come here,\r\nI wonder if it should be the last time,\r\n\r\n00:04:10.709 --\u003e 00:04:12.502\r\nif I should put\r\nthe past behind me,\r\n\r\n00:04:12.919 --\u003e 00:04:14.713\r\ntry to lead a normal life.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.796 --\u003e 00:04:19.634\r\nSantayana says that those who forget\r\nthe past are condemned to repeat it.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.302 --\u003e 00:04:22.846\r\nHe also said a fanatic is\r\nsomeone who redoubles his efforts\r\n\r\n00:04:22.929 --\u003e 00:04:24.723\r\nwhile losing sight of his goal.\r\n\r\n00:04:41.156 --\u003e 00:04:42.365\r\n(EXCLAIMS, GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:47.621 --\u003e 00:04:51.374\r\nWizard, you never call.\r\nYou never write.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.625 --\u003e 00:04:55.420\r\nYou never pay us our piece of kale\r\nfor letting you work that corner.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.087 --\u003e 00:05:00.175\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY) Willie. Monk.\r\nYeah, I was just looking for you guys.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.801 --\u003e 00:05:01.968\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:03.929 --\u003e 00:05:08.225\r\nLet's skip the pleasantries.\r\nWhat do you say? 50 bucks, now.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.809 --\u003e 00:05:12.437\r\nIt's that, or I cut out your\r\nliver and fry it in a pan.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.521 --\u003e 00:05:15.232\r\nI haven't exactly\r\ngot it right now.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.315 --\u003e 00:05:19.027\r\nThen what you do got is\r\na whole world of trouble.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.369 --\u003e 00:05:28.537\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.620 --\u003e 00:05:29.663\r\nWillie?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.205 --\u003e 00:05:31.206\r\nWillie?\r\n\r\n00:05:31.373 --\u003e 00:05:32.457\r\n(WILLIE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.544 --\u003e 00:05:37.337\r\nYou're mine. Later.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.932 --\u003e 00:05:51.434\r\nHey, Bats, don't worry about me.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.518 --\u003e 00:05:53.812\r\nI don't need help from some\r\njerk in long underwear.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.281 --\u003e 00:06:07.242\r\nThink there's room in the Mitchell\r\nStreet Mission for one more?\r\n\r\n00:06:07.325 --\u003e 00:06:08.577\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.086 --\u003e 00:06:20.255\r\nCommissioner, it's gotta be now.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.593 --\u003e 00:06:25.594\r\nHit it.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.391 --\u003e 00:06:34.936\r\nThis is the police. You men in the\r\nwarehouse, you're under arrest.\r\n\r\n00:06:35.854 --\u003e 00:06:37.564\r\n(GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:06:53.830 --\u003e 00:06:56.708\r\nAren't you going home?\r\nIt's almost 3:00 a.m.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.834 --\u003e 00:06:59.878\r\nPromises to keep, Leslie.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.961 --\u003e 00:07:01.588\r\nI have promises to keep.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.963 --\u003e 00:07:03.214\r\n(GUNFIRE CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.218 --\u003e 00:07:08.678\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:11.348 --\u003e 00:07:12.557\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:07:17.687 --\u003e 00:07:18.855\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:07:21.274 --\u003e 00:07:23.818\r\nThis was a setup.\r\nThe Jazzman was ready for us.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.322 --\u003e 00:07:31.368\r\nI've been waiting a long time\r\nto play \"Taps\" for Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.451 --\u003e 00:07:33.203\r\n(GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:07:53.264 --\u003e 00:07:54.641\r\nTHUG: What the hell?\r\n\r\n00:07:54.724 --\u003e 00:07:56.101\r\n(ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:07:56.184 --\u003e 00:07:57.769\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:05.568 --\u003e 00:08:09.364\r\nWhat's the deal? We couldn't get\r\nclose enough to use tear gas.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.455 --\u003e 00:08:18.999\r\n(ENGINE REVS)\r\n\r\n00:08:27.090 --\u003e 00:08:28.383\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.490 --\u003e 00:08:53.992\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:03.543\r\n(GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:06.588 --\u003e 00:09:09.090\r\nLooks like the fat lady just\r\nsung, Jimmy.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.632 --\u003e 00:09:12.635\r\nHey, where's the commish?\r\nHe should see this.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.553 --\u003e 00:09:14.554\r\nCommissioner?\r\n\r\n00:09:16.806 --\u003e 00:09:17.974\r\nOh, my God!\r\n\r\n00:09:20.351 --\u003e 00:09:21.686\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.069 --\u003e 00:09:30.945\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.239 --\u003e 00:09:34.633\r\nDOCTOR 1: BP, 90/60.\r\nRespiration shallow.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.657 --\u003e 00:09:35.658\r\nDOCTOR 2: Normal saline.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.742 --\u003e 00:09:37.786\r\nDOCTOR 3: Type and cross match.\r\nFive units now.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.869 --\u003e 00:09:39.412\r\nWarm up O.R. 1.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.637 --\u003e 00:09:59.390\r\n\u003ci\u003eLast night, police broke the smuggling\r\nring of Jimmy \"The Jazzman\" Peake.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:59.557 --\u003e 00:10:02.352\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut the victory in the drug\r\nwar came at a high cost.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:02.769 --\u003e 00:10:06.314\r\n\u003ci\u003ePolice Commissioner James Gordon was\r\nbadly wounded in the line of duty.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:06.981 --\u003e 00:10:11.111\r\n\u003ci\u003eBallistics investigation has matched\r\nthe bullet with the Jazzman's gun.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:11.402 --\u003e 00:10:13.071\r\n\u003ci\u003eAny comments, Jazzman?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:13.822 --\u003e 00:10:16.533\r\n\u003ci\u003eLet's just say it was\r\ntime to pay the piper.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:19.035 --\u003e 00:10:21.412\r\n\u003ci\u003eSources say that the\r\nJazzman has long nursed\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:21.496 --\u003e 00:10:23.498\r\n\u003ci\u003ea grudge against\r\nCommissioner Gordon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:23.665 --\u003e 00:10:26.835\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe commissioner remains in intensive\r\ncare at Gotham City Hospital.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:52.402 --\u003e 00:10:56.239\r\nI don't know if you can hear me, Jim.\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.406 --\u003e 00:10:58.867\r\nIf I hadn't stopped\r\nin Crime Alley...\r\n\r\n00:10:58.992 --\u003e 00:11:00.577\r\nBARBARA: Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.161 --\u003e 00:11:03.830\r\n- How is he?\r\n- Not good.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.289 --\u003e 00:11:05.540\r\nIt's my fault.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.207 --\u003e 00:11:09.169\r\nI should've gotten there\r\nfirst, checked it out before.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.252 --\u003e 00:11:12.046\r\nDon't blame yourself.\r\nYou caught the man who shot him.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.255 --\u003e 00:11:13.590\r\nIf I'd been there...\r\n\r\n00:11:14.048 --\u003e 00:11:15.888\r\nBULLOCK: You should've been\r\nthere, pointy ears.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.009 --\u003e 00:11:18.219\r\nThen maybe Peake might've\r\nshot the right guy.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.469 --\u003e 00:11:21.069\r\nI thought you were supposed to\r\nknow what's shaking on the streets.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.347 --\u003e 00:11:23.308\r\nHow come you didn't tell\r\nus this was a setup?\r\n\r\n00:11:23.975 --\u003e 00:11:25.894\r\n- I didn't know.\r\n- Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:26.311 --\u003e 00:11:28.479\r\nIn my book that makes\r\nyou just as responsible\r\n\r\n00:11:28.563 --\u003e 00:11:30.398\r\nfor him being here\r\nas the Jazzman.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.732 --\u003e 00:11:32.650\r\nHarvey, please.\r\nIt wasn't his fault.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.696 --\u003e 00:11:41.534\r\nHey, where you going?\r\nThis ain't over yet, outlaw!\r\n\r\n00:11:41.826 --\u003e 00:11:44.287\r\nYou hear me?\r\nYou're going down for this!\r\n\r\n00:11:44.370 --\u003e 00:11:47.916\r\nI ain't talking law!\r\nI'm talking you and me!\r\n\r\n00:12:03.806 --\u003e 00:12:04.933\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.353 --\u003e 00:12:09.771\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.747 --\u003e 00:12:28.957\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:31.542 --\u003e 00:12:33.461\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:39.884 --\u003e 00:12:42.303\r\nJames Peake,\r\nyou are hereby remanded\r\n\r\n00:12:42.387 --\u003e 00:12:45.014\r\nto the custody of the\r\nstate pending trial.\r\n\r\n00:12:45.265 --\u003e 00:12:47.809\r\nAs there is no room currently\r\nin the Gotham City jail,\r\n\r\n00:12:47.892 --\u003e 00:12:52.063\r\nyou will be taken to Stonegate\r\nPenitentiary to await a trial date.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.407 --\u003e 00:13:04.075\r\nIt ain't going to trial.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.158 --\u003e 00:13:06.828\r\nThey got enough on me to\r\nplay the funeral march.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.495 --\u003e 00:13:10.623\r\nNot a problem, bro.\r\nTalk to Southside Eddy.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.707 --\u003e 00:13:12.467\r\nHe'll get you on the\r\nstreet and out of Gotham\r\n\r\n00:13:12.500 --\u003e 00:13:14.544\r\nbefore the ink on\r\nyour fingers dries.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.128 --\u003e 00:13:17.630\r\nNot out of Gotham. Not yet.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.006 --\u003e 00:13:21.801\r\nFirst, I'll make sure Gordon's\r\ngot a one-way ticket to harp land.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.093 --\u003e 00:13:24.095\r\nNot now, Jimmy.\r\nYou gotta lay low.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.721 --\u003e 00:13:29.309\r\nGordon busted me six years ago.\r\nWould've been the best score of my life.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.767 --\u003e 00:13:32.061\r\nI owe him big time.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.823 --\u003e 00:13:47.452\r\nI'm so glad you could come, Master Dick.\r\nIt's been three days.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.660 --\u003e 00:13:49.662\r\nI've never seen him\r\nlike this before.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.176 --\u003e 00:14:04.177\r\nBruce?\r\n\r\n00:14:12.643 --\u003e 00:14:14.312\r\nBruce!\r\nStay down here much longer,\r\n\r\n00:14:14.395 --\u003e 00:14:16.647\r\nyou'll be growing\r\nmushrooms in your armpits.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.731 --\u003e 00:14:20.068\r\n- I should have been there.\r\n- You can't be everywhere.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.485 --\u003e 00:14:24.197\r\n- I let him down.\r\n- You're being too hard on yourself.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.364 --\u003e 00:14:27.658\r\nHe's a friend.\r\nMore than a friend.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.742 --\u003e 00:14:31.913\r\nJim Gordon's the same age my father\r\nwould've been if he hadn't...\r\n\r\n00:14:32.997 --\u003e 00:14:34.624\r\nNow he's hanging by a thread.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.708 --\u003e 00:14:38.044\r\nIf I'd gotten there\r\nfive minutes sooner.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.127 --\u003e 00:14:42.048\r\nYou're only human.\r\nYou do all one man can do.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.131 --\u003e 00:14:44.050\r\nMore than any man's\r\nexpected to do.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.347 --\u003e 00:14:51.224\r\nLaundry coming through, boss.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.600 --\u003e 00:14:54.560\r\nI chose this life.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.644 --\u003e 00:14:58.189\r\nI use the night.\r\nI became the night.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.856 --\u003e 00:15:00.608\r\nSooner or later, I'll go down.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.775 --\u003e 00:15:05.405\r\nIt might be the Joker or Two-Face\r\nor just some punk who gets lucky.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.072 --\u003e 00:15:08.491\r\nMy decision. No regrets.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.658 --\u003e 00:15:11.577\r\nBut I can't let anyone\r\nelse pay for my mistakes.\r\n\r\n00:15:12.829 --\u003e 00:15:16.374\r\nJim Gordon's a cop, Bruce.\r\nHe knows the risks.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.958 --\u003e 00:15:19.836\r\nHow long before I let someone\r\nelse I care about down?\r\n\r\n00:15:20.211 --\u003e 00:15:23.673\r\nLeslie. Alfred. You.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.182 --\u003e 00:15:34.308\r\nNow.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.367 --\u003e 00:15:54.203\r\nWhen all is said and done,\r\nhow much good have I accomplished?\r\n\r\n00:15:54.287 --\u003e 00:15:55.830\r\nThey sell T-shirts of me.\r\n\r\n00:15:56.164 --\u003e 00:15:59.959\r\nI've become a cliché. More good for\r\nthe tourist trade than the streets.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.126 --\u003e 00:16:02.128\r\nThis city would fall\r\napart without you.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.795 --\u003e 00:16:04.797\r\nMaybe. Maybe not.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.339 --\u003e 00:16:09.177\r\nWhen you look too long into the abyss,\r\nthe abyss looks back through you.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.510 --\u003e 00:16:13.014\r\nMaybe it's time for Batman to\r\nreturn to the night that spawned him\r\n\r\n00:16:13.097 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nbefore anyone else gets hurt.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.608 --\u003e 00:16:25.568\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.235 --\u003e 00:16:28.070\r\n(PRISON ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.995 --\u003e 00:16:37.830\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.998 --\u003e 00:16:40.833\r\nJimmy Peake's a madman, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.125 --\u003e 00:16:44.629\r\nHe'll try to finish what he started.\r\nI feel so helpless.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.213 --\u003e 00:16:47.548\r\nI can't just sit here.\r\nI've gotta do something to-\r\n\r\n00:16:47.632 --\u003e 00:16:50.092\r\nI know how you feel.\r\nMore than you might think.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.301 --\u003e 00:16:51.469\r\nBut your place is here.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.928 --\u003e 00:16:54.805\r\nThere's only one person who\r\ncan find the Jazzman now.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.889 --\u003e 00:16:58.100\r\n- You're talking about Batman.\r\n- I hope so.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.527 --\u003e 00:17:09.327\r\nYou've gotta pull yourself\r\nout of this, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.403 --\u003e 00:17:11.322\r\nThe Jazzman broke\r\nout of Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.614 --\u003e 00:17:13.616\r\nHe's gone to ground\r\nsomewhere in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.452 --\u003e 00:17:18.287\r\nYou know he'll find a\r\nway to get to Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.121 --\u003e 00:17:21.791\r\nOkay. Then I'm going after him.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.583 --\u003e 00:17:24.895\r\nYou taught me everything I know\r\nabout crime-fighting, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.919 --\u003e 00:17:28.589\r\nBut the most important\r\nlesson was to never give up.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.312 --\u003e 00:17:44.522\r\nNo, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.231 --\u003e 00:17:47.066\r\nThis is my hunt.\r\n\r\n00:18:03.749 --\u003e 00:18:05.334\r\n(POLICE SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.295 --\u003e 00:18:08.897\r\nPOLICE DISPATCHER: (OVER\r\nRADIO) Attention, all cars.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.921 --\u003e 00:18:11.674\r\n\u003ci\u003eSuspect sighted near\r\ncorner of Adams and O'Neil.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:12.133 --\u003e 00:18:14.176\r\nThis is Bullock. I'm on him.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.260 --\u003e 00:18:17.054\r\n\u003ci\u003eRoger, Detective. Use caution.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:34.947 --\u003e 00:18:36.073\r\n(MAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:40.703 --\u003e 00:18:41.787\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:18:42.663 --\u003e 00:18:44.582\r\nI've gotta get some coffee, Dad.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.832 --\u003e 00:18:45.916\r\nI'll be right back.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.850 --\u003e 00:19:05.311\r\nTime to face the music, Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:19:08.439 --\u003e 00:19:09.565\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:09.982 --\u003e 00:19:11.484\r\n- (GUN FIRES)\r\n- (JAZZMAN SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:15.071 --\u003e 00:19:16.155\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:33.422 --\u003e 00:19:34.423\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:37.718 --\u003e 00:19:39.136\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.846 --\u003e 00:19:42.890\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:50.189 --\u003e 00:19:51.190\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:07.206 --\u003e 00:20:08.749\r\n- (GUN FIRES)\r\n- (GROANS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:20:09.792 --\u003e 00:20:10.793\r\nFreeze, Jimmy!\r\n\r\n00:20:12.503 --\u003e 00:20:16.298\r\n- Barbara?\r\n- Dad! You're all right.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.632 --\u003e 00:20:19.301\r\nThe bust... Went down okay?\r\n\r\n00:20:19.635 --\u003e 00:20:22.012\r\nYes. Get some rest now.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.304 --\u003e 00:20:24.181\r\nGotta keep fighting. Never stop.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.640 --\u003e 00:20:26.350\r\nWhat I try to live by.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.351 --\u003e 00:20:31.313\r\nMaybe if I'd been younger,\r\ncould've been like you.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.481 --\u003e 00:20:34.567\r\nAlways wanted to be a hero.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.485 --\u003e 00:20:37.987\r\nYou are a hero, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.961 --\u003e 00:20:55.129\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:55.337 --\u003e 00:20:57.173\r\nUp to your old tricks, I see.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.590 --\u003e 00:20:59.800\r\nHow about returning that\r\nsuitcase to its owner.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.426 --\u003e 00:21:02.595\r\nHey, man, I am the owner.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.846 --\u003e 00:21:05.765\r\nYou know, I was kind of\r\nhoping I'd run into you.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.973 --\u003e 00:21:08.309\r\nI'd been in those places like\r\nwhere you left me before.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.642 --\u003e 00:21:12.855\r\nHeard the rap, wasn't impressed.\r\nBut this time it made sense.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.147 --\u003e 00:21:16.150\r\nMaybe I was ready to hear it.\r\nSo I'm heading back home.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.233 --\u003e 00:21:18.444\r\nI guess I kind of owe it to\r\nyou, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.861 --\u003e 00:21:21.781\r\nYou probably saved my life.\r\nI bet you hear this all the time.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.864 --\u003e 00:21:24.116\r\nLook, I'm gonna miss my bus.\r\nI'll see you around.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.617 --\u003e 00:21:27.036\r\nAnd thanks.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.686 --\u003e 00:21:54.772\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.838 --\u003e 00:22:19.839\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E35 - Almost Got 'Im (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.506 --\u003e 00:00:07.508\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:21.582 --\u003e 00:01:24.042\r\nJOKER: I want a nice clean\r\ngame, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:01:24.668 --\u003e 00:01:25.919\r\nPENGUIN: That'll be a first.\r\n\r\n00:01:26.587 --\u003e 00:01:29.965\r\nSo I hear you-know-who nailed\r\nthe Mad Hatter last week.\r\n\r\n00:01:30.674 --\u003e 00:01:31.675\r\nJOKER: No kidding?\r\n\r\n00:01:32.134 --\u003e 00:01:34.386\r\nHe sure gets\r\naround, for one guy.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.761 --\u003e 00:01:36.641\r\nTWO-FACE: Yeah, well,\r\nthat's where you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.014 --\u003e 00:01:38.682\r\nI don't think it is one guy.\r\n\r\n00:01:38.932 --\u003e 00:01:39.975\r\nKILLER CROC: Huh?\r\n\r\n00:01:40.058 --\u003e 00:01:43.604\r\nTWO-FACE: The way I figure it, Gordon's\r\ngot a bunch of them stashed someplace\r\n\r\n00:01:43.895 --\u003e 00:01:45.063\r\nlike a SWAT team.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.023 --\u003e 00:01:48.483\r\nHe wants you to think it's one\r\nguy, but-\r\n\r\n00:01:48.650 --\u003e 00:01:50.444\r\nJOKER: No,\r\nyou're always seeing double.\r\n\r\n00:01:51.028 --\u003e 00:01:52.839\r\nPENGUIN: It's obvious\r\nour caped friend suffered\r\n\r\n00:01:52.863 --\u003e 00:01:55.616\r\nsome crime-related trauma\r\nwhen he was younger.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.991 --\u003e 00:01:59.620\r\nPerhaps an overanxious mugger\r\nblew off a piece of his face.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.370 --\u003e 00:02:04.708\r\nJOKER: Sure, he could be all gross\r\nand disgusting under that mask.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.584 --\u003e 00:02:06.752\r\nNo offense, Harv.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.294 --\u003e 00:02:08.837\r\nTWO-FACE: Just deal.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.338 --\u003e 00:02:11.423\r\nWell, you know what I think.\r\n\r\n00:02:12.049 --\u003e 00:02:15.010\r\nNot the robot theory again.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.344 --\u003e 00:02:16.720\r\nWell, he could be.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.014 --\u003e 00:02:20.057\r\nPOISON IVY: Hello, boys.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.934 --\u003e 00:02:24.978\r\nGet me an herbal\r\ntea and deal me in.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.854 --\u003e 00:02:26.855\r\nScram, lady.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.856 --\u003e 00:02:29.399\r\nThis is a private-\r\n\r\n00:02:29.608 --\u003e 00:02:30.651\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:32.944 --\u003e 00:02:34.154\r\nWhy, you little-\r\n\r\n00:02:38.325 --\u003e 00:02:39.993\r\nPoison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.827 --\u003e 00:02:42.287\r\nIt's been a long time, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.829 --\u003e 00:02:44.915\r\nYou're still looking\r\nhalfway decent.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.624 --\u003e 00:02:49.461\r\n- Half of me wants to strangle you.\r\n- And what does the other half want?\r\n\r\n00:02:49.836 --\u003e 00:02:51.505\r\nTo hit you with a truck.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.005 --\u003e 00:02:53.298\r\nWe used to date.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.548 --\u003e 00:02:54.675\r\nBOTH: Ah.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.217 --\u003e 00:02:58.720\r\nWhat brings such a dainty\r\ndove to this dismal den?\r\n\r\n00:02:58.804 --\u003e 00:02:59.906\r\n- (PATRON GRUNTING)\r\n- (OBJECTS SMASHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:59.930 --\u003e 00:03:03.308\r\nRunning from the law.\r\nAnd the Batman, too, of course.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.850 --\u003e 00:03:05.227\r\n- Of course.\r\n- Likewise.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.519 --\u003e 00:03:07.896\r\n- You got it.\r\n- KILLER CROC: Same here.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.188 --\u003e 00:03:10.273\r\nYou'd think one of us\r\nwould've got him by now.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.482 --\u003e 00:03:11.775\r\nI've come the closest.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.150 --\u003e 00:03:14.444\r\nAre you kidding?\r\nI was the one who nearly-\r\n\r\n00:03:14.861 --\u003e 00:03:16.089\r\n- (BANGS ON TABLE)\r\n- Nobody's come closer to\r\n\r\n00:03:16.113 --\u003e 00:03:18.156\r\nsnuffing the Batman than me.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.699 --\u003e 00:03:20.426\r\nPENGUIN: In your dreams.\r\nKILLER CROC: Says you.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.450 --\u003e 00:03:21.868\r\nGet out of my face.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.952 --\u003e 00:03:23.286\r\n(JOKER WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:03:23.453 --\u003e 00:03:24.871\r\nThe fact of the matter is,\r\n\r\n00:03:24.955 --\u003e 00:03:28.125\r\nwe each have an \"almost\r\ngot him\" Batman story.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.500 --\u003e 00:03:32.170\r\nI know mine's the best,\r\nbut let's hear yours anyway.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.629 --\u003e 00:03:36.133\r\nI'd say, \"Ladies first,\" but\r\nsince we don't have any...\r\n\r\n00:03:36.258 --\u003e 00:03:38.927\r\n(CHUCKLES) We'll start with\r\nyou, Pam.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.344 --\u003e 00:03:42.472\r\nAll right.\r\nThis happened last Halloween.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.597 --\u003e 00:03:44.141\r\n\u003ci\u003eI had rigged\r\nhundreds of pumpkins\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:44.307 --\u003e 00:03:46.685\r\n\u003ci\u003eto blow out poison-ivy\r\ngas when they were lit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:55.277 --\u003e 00:03:58.905\r\n\u003ci\u003eI knew Batman would show as soon\r\nas Gotham started scratching.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:59.322 --\u003e 00:04:01.700\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn fact, I was counting on it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:08.081 --\u003e 00:04:09.082\r\n(MATCHSTICK STRIKING)\r\n\r\n00:04:13.795 --\u003e 00:04:15.338\r\nTrick or treat.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.467 --\u003e 00:04:19.634\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:21.136\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:04:27.100 --\u003e 00:04:28.101\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:29.060 --\u003e 00:04:31.813\r\nIt's midnight, darling.\r\nTime to unmask.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.286 --\u003e 00:04:47.412\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:47.996 --\u003e 00:04:49.748\r\nBATMAN: Poison gas...\r\n\r\n00:04:50.832 --\u003e 00:04:52.292\r\nIt's just the darnedest thing.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.584 --\u003e 00:04:55.629\r\nI have this natural immunity\r\nagainst poisons, toxins,\r\n\r\n00:04:55.921 --\u003e 00:04:59.508\r\nthe pain and suffering of others.\r\nGo figure. Bye.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.591 --\u003e 00:05:00.634\r\n(BLOWS KISS)\r\n\r\n00:05:02.511 --\u003e 00:05:03.720\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:05:06.973 --\u003e 00:05:08.225\r\n(ENGINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:05:20.862 --\u003e 00:05:21.863\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:05:43.260 --\u003e 00:05:45.720\r\nAnd that's how I almost got him.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.388 --\u003e 00:05:48.640\r\nWith exploding pumpkins.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.182 --\u003e 00:05:51.226\r\nI'd like to hear you do better.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.560 --\u003e 00:05:55.313\r\nOh, you will,\r\nbut I'm saving the best for last.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.856 --\u003e 00:05:57.691\r\nCan't be better than mine.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.483 --\u003e 00:06:00.694\r\nThere was this time I had\r\njust robbed the Gotham Mint\r\n\r\n00:06:00.944 --\u003e 00:06:03.196\r\nof $2 million in $2 bills.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.574 --\u003e 00:06:09.077\r\n\u003ci\u003eLucky for me,\r\nI brought along the Two-Ton Gang.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:10.453 --\u003e 00:06:12.080\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:16.376 --\u003e 00:06:19.880\r\nThe coin says you lose, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.630 --\u003e 00:06:21.715\r\nTie him up.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.798 --\u003e 00:06:24.634\r\nAnd just so you don't\r\nget any ideas...\r\n\r\n00:06:28.054 --\u003e 00:06:29.055\r\n(BATMAN GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.643 --\u003e 00:06:37.022\r\nWe'll see how tough you\r\nare without your toys.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.606 --\u003e 00:06:39.733\r\n(TWO-FACE LAUGHING SINISTERLY)\r\n\r\n00:06:53.163 --\u003e 00:06:54.831\r\nSo, what happened next?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.248 --\u003e 00:06:57.876\r\nI thought as long as I\r\nhad Batman at my mercy,\r\n\r\n00:06:58.668 --\u003e 00:07:00.754\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe deserved a 50-50 chance.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:01.963 --\u003e 00:07:07.677\r\nHere's the deal. The coin lands face\r\ndown, you'll be squashed flat.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.803 --\u003e 00:07:12.766\r\nIt lands face up,\r\nit'll just break every bone in your body.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.493 --\u003e 00:07:33.536\r\nHey, where's my coin?\r\n\r\n00:07:34.454 --\u003e 00:07:37.207\r\nAnybody see where I... Oh, no.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.795 --\u003e 00:07:44.422\r\nNow. Launch it now!\r\n\r\n00:08:06.111 --\u003e 00:08:07.362\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:10.699 --\u003e 00:08:12.033\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.584 --\u003e 00:08:22.961\r\n(BOTH YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:33.555 --\u003e 00:08:34.556\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.931 --\u003e 00:08:36.850\r\nBATMAN: Here.\r\nI owe you a dollar.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.519 --\u003e 00:08:42.105\r\nTWO-FACE: And if it weren't\r\nfor this blasted coin,\r\n\r\n00:08:42.480 --\u003e 00:08:44.024\r\nI would've got him.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.899 --\u003e 00:08:47.402\r\nGee, that's too bad, Harv.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.610 --\u003e 00:08:50.447\r\nBut I guess you'll\r\nalways come in second.\r\n\r\n00:08:51.281 --\u003e 00:08:52.741\r\nAnyone else want a go?\r\n\r\n00:08:53.366 --\u003e 00:08:54.617\r\nKILLER CROC: Me!\r\n\r\n00:08:55.452 --\u003e 00:08:57.829\r\nThere I was,\r\nholed up in this quarry\r\n\r\n00:08:58.246 --\u003e 00:09:02.751\r\nwhen Batman came nosing around.\r\nHe was getting closer, closer...\r\n\r\n00:09:03.251 --\u003e 00:09:05.754\r\n- POISON IVY: And?\r\n- I threw a rock at him.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.305 --\u003e 00:09:18.099\r\nSo, Harvey,\r\nwhat became of the giant penny?\r\n\r\n00:09:18.850 --\u003e 00:09:20.226\r\nIt was a big rock.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.602 --\u003e 00:09:22.520\r\nThey actually let him keep it.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.273 --\u003e 00:09:27.400\r\nTWO-FACE: Whose deal is it?\r\nPENGUIN: Mine.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.901 --\u003e 00:09:31.529\r\nI find your middling\r\nmachinations mildly diverting.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.030 --\u003e 00:09:34.032\r\nBut for sheer criminal genius,\r\n\r\n00:09:34.365 --\u003e 00:09:39.079\r\nnone surpasses my most recent\r\nornithologically-inspired entoilment.\r\n\r\n00:09:39.871 --\u003e 00:09:43.208\r\nSmaller words, please.\r\nYou're losing Croc.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.583 --\u003e 00:09:44.709\r\n(MUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:09:45.126 --\u003e 00:09:47.587\r\nFor weeks, I let rumors\r\ncirculate through the underworld\r\n\r\n00:09:47.837 --\u003e 00:09:52.675\r\n\u003ci\u003eof my plan to steal a pair of priceless\r\nbreeding condors from the Gotham Zoo.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:53.176 --\u003e 00:09:56.471\r\n\u003ci\u003eSure enough, on the appointed\r\nnight, guess who showed up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:03.603 --\u003e 00:10:04.604\r\n(LOCK CLATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:10:10.652 --\u003e 00:10:11.903\r\n(PENGUIN GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:14.614 --\u003e 00:10:15.824\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:17.826 --\u003e 00:10:18.827\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:10:21.579 --\u003e 00:10:24.541\r\nCurses,\r\nI would grab the wrong umbrella.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.386 --\u003e 00:10:37.470\r\n(DOOR SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:38.930 --\u003e 00:10:41.432\r\nPENGUIN: Welcome,\r\nmy ebon-winged adversary.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.891 --\u003e 00:10:44.727\r\nYou have taken the bait\r\nas I knew you would.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.103 --\u003e 00:10:49.816\r\nNow, prepare to meet your\r\nend within my aviary of doom.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.692 --\u003e 00:10:51.985\r\nAviary of what?\r\n\r\n00:10:52.443 --\u003e 00:10:55.363\r\n\u003ci\u003e'Leash, Pengers,\r\nhow corny can you get'?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:55.864 --\u003e 00:10:56.865\r\n(SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:10:57.073 --\u003e 00:11:01.244\r\nJust because you mundane miscreants\r\nhave no drama in your souls...\r\n\r\n00:11:01.870 --\u003e 00:11:04.038\r\nAnyway, there he was in my-\r\n\r\n00:11:05.290 --\u003e 00:11:06.875\r\nBig birdhouse.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.635 --\u003e 00:11:19.429\r\nPENGUIN: Beautiful, aren't they?\r\n\r\n00:11:19.804 --\u003e 00:11:22.015\r\nLike glittering\r\nfragments of the rainbow.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.099 --\u003e 00:11:25.894\r\nBy the way,\r\nthat mist I sprayed on you\r\n\r\n00:11:26.060 --\u003e 00:11:28.813\r\nis derived from the\r\nnectar these birds drink.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.606 --\u003e 00:11:32.066\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- It's quite harmless.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.775 --\u003e 00:11:35.904\r\nBut their poison-tipped\r\nbeaks, however, are not.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.785 --\u003e 00:11:45.121\r\nA scratch or two will\r\nmerely slow you down.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.413 --\u003e 00:11:47.832\r\nThree or four,\r\nand you'll start to get drowsy.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.374 --\u003e 00:11:53.004\r\nAnd after that, well, I wish I could\r\nsay it's been nice knowing you.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.171 --\u003e 00:11:54.172\r\n(PENGUIN CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.132 --\u003e 00:11:58.051\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- (BATARANG WHOOSHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:58.968 --\u003e 00:12:00.178\r\n(WATER SPRAYING)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.352 --\u003e 00:12:08.353\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.686 --\u003e 00:12:10.188\r\nPENGUIN: Oh, well played.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.730 --\u003e 00:12:14.317\r\nNow to take a poison antidote\r\nfrom your miraculous belt.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.444 --\u003e 00:12:17.612\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:17.820 --\u003e 00:12:19.614\r\nAnd I suggest you do it quickly,\r\n\r\n00:12:20.031 --\u003e 00:12:23.785\r\nbefore my cassowary's razor-sharp\r\ntalons rend you asunder.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.661 --\u003e 00:12:25.662\r\n(SQUAWKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:29.624 --\u003e 00:12:30.625\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:32.877 --\u003e 00:12:33.878\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:34.671 --\u003e 00:12:35.838\r\n(SQUAWKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:47.600 --\u003e 00:12:48.810\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:58.403 --\u003e 00:12:59.487\r\n(CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:13:09.580 --\u003e 00:13:12.667\r\n\u003ci\u003ePENGUIN: Naturally, I had flown\r\nthe coop by the time he escaped.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:14.585 --\u003e 00:13:16.713\r\nStill, I almost got him.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.255 --\u003e 00:13:18.881\r\nJOKER: Not even close.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.549 --\u003e 00:13:21.676\r\nYou see,\r\nthe thing you're forgetting\r\n\r\n00:13:21.968 --\u003e 00:13:24.929\r\nis that there are all sorts\r\nof ways to get someone.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.471 --\u003e 00:13:28.224\r\nTake my latest\r\nrun-in with Batsy.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.641 --\u003e 00:13:31.561\r\nIt was just last night,\r\nas the entire country\r\n\r\n00:13:31.644 --\u003e 00:13:34.939\r\nwas tuning into its\r\nfavorite talk show.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.899 --\u003e 00:13:39.527\r\n- (THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n- HARLEY: It's Late Night Gotham Live!\r\n\r\n00:13:40.111 --\u003e 00:13:43.990\r\nAnd here's the man who puts a smile on\r\nyour face, whether you want it or not,\r\n\r\n00:13:44.157 --\u003e 00:13:46.159\r\nthe Joker.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.409 --\u003e 00:13:48.077\r\n(APPLAUSE)\r\n\r\n00:14:10.725 --\u003e 00:14:12.268\r\n(GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:20.151 --\u003e 00:14:22.362\r\nGood evening, folks.\r\nI'm the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.570 --\u003e 00:14:25.740\r\nLiving proof that you don't have\r\nto be crazy to host this show,\r\n\r\n00:14:25.823 --\u003e 00:14:26.824\r\nbut it helps.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.908 --\u003e 00:14:28.951\r\n- (CACKLES)\r\n- (DRUM ROLL)\r\n\r\n00:14:31.496 --\u003e 00:14:33.456\r\nWe've got a real treat for\r\nyou, kids.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.998 --\u003e 00:14:38.753\r\nI ran into my first guest last night\r\nwhile making a withdrawal from the bank.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.212 --\u003e 00:14:41.130\r\nYou know him as\r\n\"The Dark Knight,\"\r\n\r\n00:14:41.214 --\u003e 00:14:43.966\r\nbut we prefer to think\r\nof him as history.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.258 --\u003e 00:14:48.429\r\n(CHUCKLES) Here he is,\r\nthe one and only...\r\n\r\n00:14:49.555 --\u003e 00:14:50.890\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.414 --\u003e 00:15:17.917\r\nWe're back with my\r\nextra-special guest.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.088 --\u003e 00:15:23.881\r\nSo how's Robin?\r\n\r\n00:15:29.762 --\u003e 00:15:31.514\r\nOh. Moving right along.\r\n\r\n00:15:31.722 --\u003e 00:15:35.852\r\nYou know, kids, we've got an item\r\nhere no home should be without.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.269 --\u003e 00:15:40.148\r\nThe laughter-activated electric chair.\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:15:40.648 --\u003e 00:15:45.653\r\nYes, sir, the merest titter or guffaw\r\nstarts the chair's generator revving up\r\n\r\n00:15:45.778 --\u003e 00:15:47.447\r\ntowards maximum zappage.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.947 --\u003e 00:15:48.990\r\nHarley?\r\n\r\n00:15:50.825 --\u003e 00:15:52.243\r\n(SLOWLY) Ha, ha, ha.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.037 --\u003e 00:15:56.038\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:56.247 --\u003e 00:15:57.457\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:15:58.207 --\u003e 00:16:02.670\r\nBut for a real demonstration,\r\nwe're pumping our studio audience\r\n\r\n00:16:02.837 --\u003e 00:16:05.673\r\nfull of my patented\r\nlaughing gas.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.299 --\u003e 00:16:08.718\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:11.262 --\u003e 00:16:12.555\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.722 --\u003e 00:16:16.809\r\nThese yahoos will laugh at anything\r\nnow, even the phone book.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.977 --\u003e 00:16:19.145\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.520 --\u003e 00:16:24.025\r\nMarvin Abbott, 555-8976.\r\n\r\n00:16:24.484 --\u003e 00:16:25.943\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.819 --\u003e 00:16:28.112\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:29.530 --\u003e 00:16:33.743\r\nGerald Adams, 555-9011.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.368 --\u003e 00:16:35.953\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.330 --\u003e 00:16:38.581\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:40.374 --\u003e 00:16:43.503\r\n\u003ci\u003eNLJ. Addison, 555-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:43.669 --\u003e 00:16:44.670\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.258 --\u003e 00:16:50.468\r\n(CATWOMAN SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:52.303 --\u003e 00:16:53.304\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:16:54.138 --\u003e 00:16:55.264\r\n(JOKER GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:00.603 --\u003e 00:17:01.812\r\n(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.938 --\u003e 00:17:03.523\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:07.777 --\u003e 00:17:09.612\r\n(WHIP SWISHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.532 --\u003e 00:17:13.783\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:21.040 --\u003e 00:17:22.959\r\nCATWOMAN: Shaw's over, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.709 --\u003e 00:17:27.213\r\nJOKER: Catwoman, ladies and gentlemen.\r\nLet's hear it for her.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.505 --\u003e 00:17:28.714\r\n(HIGH VOLTAGE BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:17:30.049 --\u003e 00:17:31.467\r\n(HYSTERICAL LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.885 --\u003e 00:17:34.095\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:17:36.138 --\u003e 00:17:37.348\r\nTWO-FACE: Almost got him.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.848 --\u003e 00:17:40.977\r\nYes, if not for that\r\ninfatuated feline.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.561 --\u003e 00:17:44.939\r\nOh, but that's the best part.\r\nOnce the chair went up,\r\n\r\n00:17:45.231 --\u003e 00:17:47.650\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was out of there\r\ntout de suite.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:47.733 --\u003e 00:17:48.734\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.364 --\u003e 00:17:54.532\r\n(JOKER EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:54.907 --\u003e 00:17:57.910\r\n\u003ci\u003eMiss Kitty still wanted\r\nto play cat-and-mouse,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:58.202 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nnever dreaming \u003ci\u003eI still\u003c/i\u003e\r\nhad an ace up \u003ci\u003emy\u003c/i\u003e sleeve.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.039 --\u003e 00:18:03.040\r\n- (THUDS)\r\n- (GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:09.964 --\u003e 00:18:14.093\r\nAnd by golly, speaking of\r\naces, looky here.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.885 --\u003e 00:18:17.888\r\nTWO-FACE: I can't believe his luck.\r\nKILLER CROC: Oh, darn.\r\n\r\n00:18:19.056 --\u003e 00:18:20.683\r\nPENGUIN: Let me see those cards.\r\n\r\n00:18:23.811 --\u003e 00:18:27.481\r\nNow, now, no sore losers.\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:28.149 --\u003e 00:18:29.817\r\nHey, I don't get it.\r\n\r\n00:18:29.942 --\u003e 00:18:32.653\r\nYou just knocked out\r\nCatwoman and left her?\r\n\r\n00:18:32.903 --\u003e 00:18:34.780\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, come on, Crackers,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:35.031 --\u003e 00:18:38.075\r\ndidn't I say there's more\r\nthan one way to \"get someone\"?\r\n\r\n00:18:38.326 --\u003e 00:18:39.744\r\nEven as I speak,\r\n\r\n00:18:39.869 --\u003e 00:18:44.373\r\nCatwoman is being trussed up at\r\nthe Pussykins Pet Food factory.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.790 --\u003e 00:18:50.129\r\nFirst thing tomorrow, I'm sending a\r\nlovely case of cat food to Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.588 --\u003e 00:18:51.922\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:54.425 --\u003e 00:18:55.718\r\nBATMAN: I don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.386 --\u003e 00:18:58.638\r\n(JOKER GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.601 --\u003e 00:19:06.979\r\nWas it something I said?\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.068 --\u003e 00:19:15.112\r\nPENGUIN: Well, well.\r\nAn impostor in our midst.\r\n\r\n00:19:15.613 --\u003e 00:19:18.407\r\nRisking everything for your\r\nkitty, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:19:18.866 --\u003e 00:19:20.660\r\nYou're not getting\r\nout of this one.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.410 --\u003e 00:19:22.953\r\nMaybe. (SNAPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.329 --\u003e 00:19:25.331\r\n(GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:33.714 --\u003e 00:19:36.467\r\nBut I'm not bad\r\nwith traps myself.\r\n\r\n00:19:50.231 --\u003e 00:19:51.607\r\n(CATWOMAN SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:55.027 --\u003e 00:19:58.364\r\nI had a kitty once. You know,\r\nthey don't always land on their feet.\r\n\r\n00:19:58.656 --\u003e 00:19:59.782\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.366 --\u003e 00:20:01.659\r\nLook on the bright side.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.867 --\u003e 00:20:04.662\r\nTomorrow, you'll be feeding\r\nhundreds of hungry cats.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.870 --\u003e 00:20:07.998\r\nThe fun starts as soon\r\nas Mr. J comes back.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.749 --\u003e 00:20:09.792\r\nBATMAN: Don't wait up.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.336 --\u003e 00:20:13.337\r\n(HARLEY GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.214 --\u003e 00:20:20.094\r\nBack off, Bats, or say \"ciao\" to\r\nyour girlfriend. Cat chow, that is.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.470 --\u003e 00:20:22.972\r\nThat's a good little rodent.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.055 --\u003e 00:20:25.141\r\nAnd just to make sure\r\nyou don't follow me...\r\n\r\n00:20:25.516 --\u003e 00:20:26.684\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:20:28.561 --\u003e 00:20:30.104\r\n(CATWOMAN STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:40.114 --\u003e 00:20:44.076\r\nGee, Batman, what you gonna do,\r\nkick me around or save your kitten?\r\n\r\n00:20:46.620 --\u003e 00:20:48.622\r\nYou've only got time for one.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.632 --\u003e 00:21:01.635\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY) Good call.\r\nHelp.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.186 --\u003e 00:21:11.979\r\nCATWOMAN: Thanks\r\nfor coming after me.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.313 --\u003e 00:21:13.355\r\nBATMAN: I owed you.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.064 --\u003e 00:21:15.858\r\nWell, I'd like to\r\nthink our relationship\r\n\r\n00:21:15.941 --\u003e 00:21:19.445\r\nisn't just restricted to saving\r\neach other from freaks and weirdos.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.737 --\u003e 00:21:22.823\r\nAnd that maybe we'd have a place\r\nfor each other without Gotham,\r\n\r\n00:21:23.240 --\u003e 00:21:24.241\r\nwithout the freaks.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.784 --\u003e 00:21:27.161\r\nMaybe without masks.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.912 --\u003e 00:21:28.913\r\nMaybe.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.371 --\u003e 00:21:30.706\r\n(SIREN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:21:31.832 --\u003e 00:21:32.833\r\n(CLOAK FLAPPING)\r\n\r\n00:21:42.301 --\u003e 00:21:44.303\r\nHmm. Almost got 'im.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.770 --\u003e 00:21:54.772\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.504 --\u003e 00:22:19.505\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E36 - Moon of the Wolf (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.173 --\u003e 00:00:08.175\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:00:17.559 --\u003e 00:00:19.686\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:35.220 --\u003e 00:01:36.763\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.556 --\u003e 00:01:39.016\r\nHey, what's with you?\r\n\r\n00:01:47.774 --\u003e 00:01:49.610\r\n(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:50.402 --\u003e 00:01:51.570\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:58.577 --\u003e 00:01:59.578\r\nHi.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.206 --\u003e 00:02:04.416\r\n(DOG SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:02:04.666 --\u003e 00:02:08.420\r\n(WHISTLES) Come on, will you?\r\nI ain't got all night, you know.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.254 --\u003e 00:02:10.255\r\n(BRANCHES SNAPPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:13.175 --\u003e 00:02:14.176\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:15.969 --\u003e 00:02:16.970\r\nWhat the...\r\n\r\n00:02:20.432 --\u003e 00:02:21.642\r\n(YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:23.769 --\u003e 00:02:25.479\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:02:28.148 --\u003e 00:02:29.149\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:33.737 --\u003e 00:02:36.448\r\nNo! Stay back!\r\nKeep away from me!\r\n\r\n00:02:44.164 --\u003e 00:02:47.751\r\nIf it's a fight you're looking\r\nfor, try starting one with me.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.634 --\u003e 00:02:58.136\r\nThe masquerade party's\r\nover, hairy.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.675 --\u003e 00:03:39.970\r\nWell, Mr. John Hamner...\r\n\r\n00:03:42.723 --\u003e 00:03:44.433\r\nYou're a very lucky fella.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.111 --\u003e 00:03:57.446\r\nHelen, get me...\r\n\r\n00:03:58.905 --\u003e 00:03:59.906\r\nWe need to talk.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.990 --\u003e 00:04:01.908\r\n(PHONE RINGING) I wish\r\nyou'd stop doing that.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.325 --\u003e 00:04:04.870\r\nJust tangled with a\r\nmugger in a werewolf mask.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.203 --\u003e 00:04:07.372\r\nI tried to stop him,\r\nand he threw a guy off a bridge.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.956 --\u003e 00:04:09.416\r\nMean anything to you?\r\n\r\n00:04:09.791 --\u003e 00:04:11.084\r\n\"A werewolf mask\"?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.793 --\u003e 00:04:12.878\r\nLet's take a look.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.551 --\u003e 00:04:22.429\r\nOnly thing that even comes close\r\nis two Alaskan timber wolves\r\n\r\n00:04:22.804 --\u003e 00:04:24.931\r\nstolen from the city\r\nzoo last Friday.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.515 --\u003e 00:04:27.476\r\nThe victim's name\r\nwas John Hamner.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.893 --\u003e 00:04:30.103\r\nFrom his uniform,\r\nI'd say he works for the zoo.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.604 --\u003e 00:04:31.813\r\nI doubt it's a coincidence.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.272 --\u003e 00:04:33.273\r\nI'll get Bullock on it.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.235 --\u003e 00:04:38.862\r\nHelen, get me Harvey Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.030 --\u003e 00:04:41.281\r\nYeah, ASAP.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.824 --\u003e 00:04:44.034\r\nBATMAN: Hmm.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.117 --\u003e 00:04:45.368\r\nSomething wrong, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:04:45.869 --\u003e 00:04:48.413\r\nBATMAN: Just had a disturbing\r\nthought, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.997 --\u003e 00:04:51.875\r\nWhat if that guy\r\nwasn't wearing a mask?\r\n\r\n00:05:16.733 --\u003e 00:05:18.151\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.493 --\u003e 00:05:27.744\r\n(ROARING)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.544 --\u003e 00:05:36.837\r\nJust under the wire.\r\n\r\n00:05:38.171 --\u003e 00:05:40.966\r\nPlease, spare me the melodrama.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.341 --\u003e 00:05:43.009\r\nIn precisely seven seconds,\r\n\r\n00:05:43.343 --\u003e 00:05:45.804\r\nall your fearsome growling\r\nwon't mean a blessed thing.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.816 --\u003e 00:05:59.526\r\nThere, all better.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.193 --\u003e 00:06:01.903\r\nEasy.Easy.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.445 --\u003e 00:06:03.697\r\nIt'll all be over soon,\r\n\r\n00:06:04.030 --\u003e 00:06:08.910\r\n- now that you've taken care of Hamner.\r\n- No. The Batman interfered.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.536 --\u003e 00:06:10.787\r\nHim again?\r\n\r\n00:06:10.954 --\u003e 00:06:13.832\r\nObviously, something will\r\nhave to be done about him.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.792 --\u003e 00:06:17.335\r\nWon't it, my friend?\r\n\r\n00:06:23.466 --\u003e 00:06:25.385\r\nREPORTER: And here\r\nare today's headlines.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.468 --\u003e 00:06:27.721\r\n\u003ci\u003eFormer Olympic champion\r\nAnthony Romulus\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:27.804 --\u003e 00:06:29.564\r\n\u003ci\u003eannounced in a letter\r\nin today's Gotham\u003c/i\u003e Globe\r\n\r\n00:06:29.639 --\u003e 00:06:32.350\r\n\u003ci\u003ethat he would double his million-dollar\r\npledge to a local charity\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:32.517 --\u003e 00:06:35.478\r\n\u003ci\u003eif Batman appears at his home\r\nthis evening to receive the check.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:44.905 --\u003e 00:06:46.907\r\nBRUCE: Haven't seen you\r\naround here lately, Tony.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.449 --\u003e 00:06:48.450\r\nTONY: Been busy, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.242 --\u003e 00:06:51.286\r\nTrying to find a new\r\ntax shelter or two.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.703 --\u003e 00:06:54.205\r\nThen you're serious about\r\nthat ad in the paper, Tony?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.206 --\u003e 00:06:56.458\r\nTONY: Dead serious.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.167 --\u003e 00:06:59.711\r\nI'll give $2.5 million\r\nto the Gotham United Fund\r\n\r\n00:07:00.420 --\u003e 00:07:03.840\r\nprovided the Batman comes to the\r\nhouse personally to pick up the check.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.383 --\u003e 00:07:08.553\r\nWOMAN: Why him?\r\nLooking for someone to arm-wrestle?\r\n\r\n00:07:09.512 --\u003e 00:07:11.556\r\nLet's just say I've always\r\nwanted to check out.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.723 --\u003e 00:07:14.267\r\nGotham's second-best\r\nathlete firsthand.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.768 --\u003e 00:07:15.936\r\n(WOMAN LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:18.521 --\u003e 00:07:22.233\r\nNARRATOR: \u003ci\u003e(ON TV) The Alaskan timber\r\nwolf hunts in pairs or in packs,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:22.567 --\u003e 00:07:25.862\r\n\u003ci\u003econtrary to the way this\r\npredator is commonly depicted\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:25.987 --\u003e 00:07:27.739\r\n\u003ci\u003ein wildlife adventure films.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:31.201 --\u003e 00:07:34.120\r\nALFRED: Thinking of acquiring a new\r\npet, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:07:35.956 --\u003e 00:07:38.291\r\nNo, Alfred.\r\nJust searching for some connection\r\n\r\n00:07:38.375 --\u003e 00:07:41.670\r\nbetween Hamner, those stolen\r\nwolves, and that hairy weirdo.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.212 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\nThe hairs check out\r\nas genuine wolf hair.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.589 --\u003e 00:07:48.426\r\nBut it could mean only that shaggy\r\nwas wearing an extremely fancy mask.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.344 --\u003e 00:07:51.805\r\nI've come at this problem\r\nfrom a dozen directions.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.305 --\u003e 00:07:54.516\r\nBut they all lead to\r\nthe same dead end.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.225 --\u003e 00:08:00.063\r\nWell, then, might I suggest, sir,\r\nthat it's time to get a new map.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.939 --\u003e 00:08:03.483\r\nBATMAN: Or time to stop\r\nspinning my wheels, at least.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.817 --\u003e 00:08:05.235\r\nI have other business tonight.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.244 --\u003e 00:08:15.912\r\nHmm! You're welcome.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.674 --\u003e 00:08:28.675\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.300 --\u003e 00:08:31.803\r\nI hear you have something for\r\nme, Mr. Romulus.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.929 --\u003e 00:08:34.431\r\nI've been expecting you.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.724 --\u003e 00:08:37.225\r\nPlease,\r\nmake yourself comfortable.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.396 --\u003e 00:08:42.605\r\nTONY: I'll write you a check.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.483 --\u003e 00:08:48.611\r\n- Would you care for something to drink?\r\n- No, thank you.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.738 --\u003e 00:08:51.281\r\nCan we just get on with it?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.584 --\u003e 00:09:04.836\r\nIs it getting hot in here?\r\n\r\n00:09:05.628 --\u003e 00:09:06.629\r\n\"Hot\"?\r\n\r\n00:09:07.005 --\u003e 00:09:08.923\r\nWhy, no, I don't believe so.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.758 --\u003e 00:09:11.176\r\nIt is hot.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.302 --\u003e 00:09:14.554\r\nAnd there's something\r\nwrong with the air in here.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.929 --\u003e 00:09:16.806\r\nIt's... Of course.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.599 --\u003e 00:09:18.641\r\nGas.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.893 --\u003e 00:09:20.894\r\nDon't know\r\n\r\n00:09:21.436 --\u003e 00:09:22.937\r\nwhat you're trying to pull,\r\n\r\n00:09:23.480 --\u003e 00:09:25.648\r\nbut you're not going to...\r\n\r\n00:09:29.694 --\u003e 00:09:31.446\r\nI'm sorry, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.696 --\u003e 00:09:35.033\r\nBut you really should've\r\ntaken the doctored drink.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.376 --\u003e 00:09:48.755\r\nDR. MILO: Sounds like there's quite\r\na nasty storm brewing, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.172 --\u003e 00:09:50.298\r\nTONY: I hope so, Milo.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.799 --\u003e 00:09:53.551\r\nThe rain will make me feel\r\ncleaner after what we just did.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.802 --\u003e 00:09:56.471\r\nDR. MILO: And I hope he\r\nawakens before moonrise.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.810 --\u003e 00:10:04.312\r\nI want him to see\r\nthe end coming.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.979 --\u003e 00:10:06.940\r\nAn end you expect me to deliver.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.190 --\u003e 00:10:10.360\r\nMilo, you're a worse animal\r\nthan anything I turn into.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.652 --\u003e 00:10:13.947\r\nBut I'm the animal who holds\r\nthe key to your salvation.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.325 --\u003e 00:10:18.952\r\nDon't ever forget that.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.536 --\u003e 00:10:20.954\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:22.831 --\u003e 00:10:25.333\r\nNow, why don't I pour you a cup of\r\ntea, Anthony?\r\n\r\n00:10:25.750 --\u003e 00:10:28.128\r\n- You'll feel better.\r\n- In a pig's eye, Milo.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.878 --\u003e 00:10:30.797\r\nThere's only one\r\nthing I want from you.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.172 --\u003e 00:10:33.049\r\nThe antidote? Certainly.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.591 --\u003e 00:10:35.510\r\nWhen you've earned it.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.802 --\u003e 00:10:37.387\r\nAs if I haven't suffered enough?\r\n\r\n00:10:40.807 --\u003e 00:10:42.433\r\nYou know what they say, Anthony.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.434 --\u003e 00:10:45.270\r\nNo pain, no gain.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.187 --\u003e 00:10:47.981\r\nBut you know that\r\nfar better than I.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.607 --\u003e 00:10:52.735\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat with all that training you\r\ndid to compete in the Autumn Games.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:54.320 --\u003e 00:10:56.865\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut that wasn't good enough for\r\nyou, was it?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:57.365 --\u003e 00:11:01.244\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo. You wanted something that\r\nwould guarantee a gold medal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:01.661 --\u003e 00:11:02.787\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I gave it to you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:03.663 --\u003e 00:11:05.165\r\nSteroids, Mr. Romulus?\r\n\r\n00:11:05.665 --\u003e 00:11:07.667\r\nNo, too easily detectable.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.168 --\u003e 00:11:09.627\r\nBut there is this.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.545 --\u003e 00:11:13.006\r\nA special steroid derivative\r\nI've been working on.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.339 --\u003e 00:11:15.758\r\nUndetectable and unbeatable.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.217 --\u003e 00:11:17.343\r\nOne thing you should know.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.635 --\u003e 00:11:21.931\r\nThis serum contains both steroids\r\nand timber wolf estrogen.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.390 --\u003e 00:11:25.518\r\nAll designed to heighten one's\r\nphysical attributes to their utmost.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.768 --\u003e 00:11:28.354\r\nUnfortunately,\r\nit still requires testing.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.521 --\u003e 00:11:29.522\r\n\u003ci\u003eHEY-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:32.942 --\u003e 00:11:34.152\r\nToo late, Professor.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.028 --\u003e 00:11:36.487\r\nThe power is mine now.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.407 --\u003e 00:11:42.702\r\nThen all that remains\r\nis to discuss my fee.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.041 --\u003e 00:11:50.752\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd you got your money's\r\nworth, didn't you, my friend?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:00.345 --\u003e 00:12:01.471\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:13.733 --\u003e 00:12:16.152\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, yes,\r\nyour money's worth and more.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:16.903 --\u003e 00:12:19.405\r\n\u003ci\u003eUsing your newfound\r\nfame to earn a fortune.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:21.157 --\u003e 00:12:22.533\r\n\u003ci\u003ePublic appearances.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:23.117 --\u003e 00:12:24.535\r\nCommercial endorsements.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.911 --\u003e 00:12:29.249\r\nAnd that only made your terrible\r\nselfishness all the more reprehensible.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.208 --\u003e 00:12:31.501\r\nWhy should I give you a dime?\r\n\r\n00:12:32.043 --\u003e 00:12:34.587\r\nIt was my own sweat that\r\ngot me this far, Milo.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.129 --\u003e 00:12:36.422\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:36.798 --\u003e 00:12:39.717\r\nAnd I intend to go the\r\nrest of the way alone.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.009 --\u003e 00:12:43.972\r\n\u003ci\u003eDR.\u003c/i\u003e MILO: \u003ci\u003eNow, there was a decision\r\nyou've lived to regret, wasn't it?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:44.889 --\u003e 00:12:46.724\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.527 --\u003e 00:12:59.404\r\nThe effects can't be reversed.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.988 --\u003e 00:13:02.573\r\n- What?\r\n- I said \"reversed,\" Anthony.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.907 --\u003e 00:13:05.159\r\nI can't reverse the process.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.285 --\u003e 00:13:06.953\r\nBut I can complete it.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.328 --\u003e 00:13:11.082\r\nWhat you're suffering from, my friend,\r\nis an early stage of lycanthropy.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.666 --\u003e 00:13:14.335\r\nMore commonly known\r\nas \"werewolf ism.\"\r\n\r\n00:13:15.003 --\u003e 00:13:16.546\r\nFor that, I have no treatment.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.838 --\u003e 00:13:20.758\r\nHowever, advanced\r\nwerewolf ism can be cured.\r\n\r\n00:13:27.348 --\u003e 00:13:28.516\r\n(GAGGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:30.435 --\u003e 00:13:31.978\r\n(WINCING)\r\n\r\n00:13:33.479 --\u003e 00:13:35.440\r\nWhat did you do to me?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.565 --\u003e 00:13:38.443\r\nThe pain! The pain!\r\n\r\n00:13:38.693 --\u003e 00:13:41.821\r\nAnd if you ever wish it to go\r\naway, Anthony,\r\n\r\n00:13:41.904 --\u003e 00:13:46.159\r\nfrom this moment forward,\r\nyou will do precisely what I tell you.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:51.456\r\nI won't let you trick me\r\nagain, Milo.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.956 --\u003e 00:13:54.417\r\nNow, give me that antidote!\r\nPlease, just a taste.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.001 --\u003e 00:13:56.711\r\nNo, not a drop.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.005 --\u003e 00:14:02.633\r\nI want all the creature's\r\nsavagery unleashed on the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.684 --\u003e 00:14:13.519\r\n(WHISTLING MELODICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:18.733 --\u003e 00:14:20.068\r\n(WOLVES GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:24.405 --\u003e 00:14:25.531\r\nBULLOCK: You Hamner?\r\n\r\n00:14:25.615 --\u003e 00:14:26.616\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:27.742 --\u003e 00:14:30.578\r\nJohn Hamner? Bullock, Gotham PD.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.870 --\u003e 00:14:31.871\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:14:32.163 --\u003e 00:14:34.540\r\nAbout them two wolves\r\nsomebody boosted.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.749 --\u003e 00:14:37.085\r\nThere was no sign of forced entry\r\nhere, you know.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.251 --\u003e 00:14:40.630\r\nSo I'm figuring somebody\r\nmust have unlocked the cages,\r\n\r\n00:14:41.089 --\u003e 00:14:42.507\r\nand looked the other way.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.757 --\u003e 00:14:44.217\r\nI've been checking you\r\nout, Hamner.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.467 --\u003e 00:14:47.929\r\nSeems last week, your bank account\r\nsuddenly got bigger by a few grand.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.096 --\u003e 00:14:49.263\r\nSo, what's the story?\r\n\r\n00:14:49.430 --\u003e 00:14:53.101\r\nI want the truth before I decide to\r\nfeed you to your furry friends here.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.393 --\u003e 00:14:55.561\r\nAll right, all right.\r\nYou got it.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.062 --\u003e 00:14:59.273\r\nThe guy tells me to open the locks.\r\nNext morning, the wolves are gone.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.565 --\u003e 00:15:01.401\r\n- What guy?\r\n- I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.651 --\u003e 00:15:04.320\r\nI never saw him, he calls me.\r\nPays me off by courier.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.570 --\u003e 00:15:06.239\r\nFor all I know, he could be you.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.864 --\u003e 00:15:08.408\r\nYou got that wrong, pally.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.741 --\u003e 00:15:10.743\r\nI'm the guy taking you in.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.205 --\u003e 00:15:15.706\r\n(HOWL$)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.669 --\u003e 00:15:20.753\r\nYou fool!\r\n\r\n00:15:21.170 --\u003e 00:15:23.506\r\nThere's no telling what\r\nthe werewolf might do.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.382 --\u003e 00:15:26.342\r\nHey, ask me if I care.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.594 --\u003e 00:15:29.804\r\n(TONY SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:40.481 --\u003e 00:15:41.899\r\n(HOWL$)\r\n\r\n00:15:42.316 --\u003e 00:15:44.777\r\nNow go. Your victim is waiting.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.117 --\u003e 00:15:52.118\r\nGo, Anth...\r\n\r\n00:15:53.786 --\u003e 00:15:55.955\r\nAnthony, what...\r\nWhat are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:16:03.171 --\u003e 00:16:04.255\r\nAnthony, please!\r\n\r\n00:16:04.839 --\u003e 00:16:06.048\r\nLet's talk about this.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.132 --\u003e 00:16:07.175\r\nWe can...\r\n\r\n00:16:07.550 --\u003e 00:16:08.759\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:16:09.510 --\u003e 00:16:10.595\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:16:16.893 --\u003e 00:16:18.019\r\n(ANTHONY GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:16:24.025 --\u003e 00:16:25.151\r\n- (GROWLS)\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.986 --\u003e 00:16:28.571\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.581 --\u003e 00:16:41.083\r\n(HOWL$)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.010 --\u003e 00:16:52.136\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:55.890 --\u003e 00:16:57.391\r\n(WOLF GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:04.941 --\u003e 00:17:06.317\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:33.261 --\u003e 00:17:34.929\r\n(HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.473 --\u003e 00:17:41.269\r\n- Honey, did you hear that?\r\n- It's only the wind, Norman.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.234 --\u003e 00:17:50.111\r\nNORMAN: Come on,\r\nwe gotta call 911.\r\n\r\n00:18:01.706 --\u003e 00:18:03.249\r\nDo me a favor, shaggy.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.422 --\u003e 00:18:10.423\r\nStay down!\r\n\r\n00:18:12.341 --\u003e 00:18:13.342\r\nGuess not.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.359 --\u003e 00:18:32.570\r\nI'm obviously no match\r\nfor you down here.\r\n\r\n00:18:32.987 --\u003e 00:18:35.406\r\nSo let's take this\r\nto higher ground.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.576 --\u003e 00:18:39.577\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:18:52.506 --\u003e 00:18:53.924\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:18:54.634 --\u003e 00:18:56.719\r\nHold your fire till\r\nI give the word.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.053 --\u003e 00:18:58.262\r\nYour move, hairy.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.362 --\u003e 00:19:15.363\r\nThere.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.990 --\u003e 00:19:19.492\r\nI said, no shooting.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.159 --\u003e 00:19:22.328\r\nLet him handle this. For now.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.625 --\u003e 00:19:28.709\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.524 --\u003e 00:19:53.442\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:17.591 --\u003e 00:20:19.844\r\nYou know, my friend,\r\nI'm innocent.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.136 --\u003e 00:20:22.138\r\nThey'll never convict\r\nme of a thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.888 --\u003e 00:20:24.098\r\nDon't bet on it.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.314 --\u003e 00:20:35.735\r\nNo trace of wolfie.\r\nWe checked the shoreline for miles.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.235 --\u003e 00:20:38.154\r\nBut in four weeks,\r\nthere's another full moon.\r\n\r\n00:20:38.487 --\u003e 00:20:39.905\r\nThen we'll know for sure.\r\n\r\n00:20:44.118 --\u003e 00:20:46.412\r\nWOMAN: Isn't it just to die for?\r\n\r\n00:20:46.620 --\u003e 00:20:48.998\r\nWait till you see the gym.\r\nYou'll plotz.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.623 --\u003e 00:20:52.263\r\nOh, right. This place used to belong\r\nto Anthony Romulus, didn't it?\r\n\r\n00:20:52.793 --\u003e 00:20:55.129\r\n- So Why'd he wanna move?\r\n- AGENT: But he didn't.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.379 --\u003e 00:20:57.923\r\nThey say he just\r\nleft town one day.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.090 --\u003e 00:21:01.302\r\nThe house is being sold\r\nto pay off his creditors.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.594 --\u003e 00:21:03.053\r\nAny idea what happened to him?\r\n\r\n00:21:03.304 --\u003e 00:21:06.265\r\nNo, nobody really knows.\r\nStrange, ain't it?\r\n\r\n00:21:06.557 --\u003e 00:21:09.351\r\nMAN: Yeah. A guy who's\r\ngot just about everything.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.727 --\u003e 00:21:10.728\r\nAnd he gives it all up?\r\n\r\n00:21:11.729 --\u003e 00:21:14.815\r\n(HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:21.614 --\u003e 00:21:23.574\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:48.224 --\u003e 00:21:49.225\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E37 - Terror in the Sky (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.464 --\u003e 00:00:07.466\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:43.854 --\u003e 00:01:45.480\r\nThat's it. Keep her steady.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.691 --\u003e 00:01:49.401\r\nNow crank her another\r\ninch, and...\r\n\r\n00:01:49.776 --\u003e 00:01:51.236\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.820 --\u003e 00:01:53.572\r\n(THUNDEROUS FLAPPING\r\nAPPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:54.406 --\u003e 00:01:56.575\r\n- (EXCLAIMING)\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.336 --\u003e 00:02:08.337\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:16.261 --\u003e 00:02:17.971\r\n(SLURPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:29.650 --\u003e 00:02:30.651\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.115 --\u003e 00:02:38.116\r\nAh, forget this.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.325 --\u003e 00:02:39.910\r\nWORKER: Yeah,\r\nit can have the fruit.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.790 --\u003e 00:02:45.791\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:08.772 --\u003e 00:03:10.148\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:19.408 --\u003e 00:03:20.409\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:20.867 --\u003e 00:03:23.036\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.997 --\u003e 00:03:28.542\r\nKirk. Kirk, what's the matter?\r\n\r\n00:03:29.126 --\u003e 00:03:30.794\r\nNothing. Maybe.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.461 --\u003e 00:03:32.629\r\nI'm not sure.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.255 --\u003e 00:03:34.423\r\nAnother nightmare?\r\n\r\n00:03:34.840 --\u003e 00:03:36.466\r\nYou've been having a\r\nlot of those lately.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.800 --\u003e 00:03:38.280\r\nIs there something\r\nyou wanna tell me?\r\n\r\n00:03:43.098 --\u003e 00:03:44.808\r\nThen lie down. Go back to sleep.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.476 --\u003e 00:03:47.686\r\nKIRK: I need some air.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.355 --\u003e 00:03:51.356\r\n(SQUELCHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:52.190 --\u003e 00:03:53.191\r\nUgh.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.984 --\u003e 00:03:55.152\r\nNow what?\r\n\r\n00:03:55.902 --\u003e 00:03:57.571\r\nNothing. Go back to sleep.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.296 --\u003e 00:04:18.049\r\nI'm telling you it was some kind of\r\nanimal, a monstrosity.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.383 --\u003e 00:04:20.427\r\nThe wingspan had to be 15 feet.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.886 --\u003e 00:04:22.846\r\nWORKER: With huge\r\nfangs and claws.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.221 --\u003e 00:04:24.765\r\nLook what it did to the fruit.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.432 --\u003e 00:04:27.893\r\nUh-huh. Thanks.\r\nWe'll get right on it.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.491 --\u003e 00:04:43.492\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:44.493 --\u003e 00:04:45.494\r\n(ENGINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:04:51.458 --\u003e 00:04:52.459\r\nAlfred.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.960 --\u003e 00:04:55.128\r\nTrouble, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:04:55.670 --\u003e 00:04:56.797\r\nYou could say that.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.255 --\u003e 00:05:00.008\r\nReports of a huge bat\r\ncreature the size of a man.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.509 --\u003e 00:05:01.760\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:05:01.968 --\u003e 00:05:03.261\r\nRemind you of anybody?\r\n\r\n00:05:04.930 --\u003e 00:05:06.515\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: Present\r\ncompany excepted,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:07.098 --\u003e 00:05:08.099\r\nindeed, sir, \u003ci\u003eit\u003c/i\u003e does.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.643 --\u003e 00:05:13.480\r\n\u003ci\u003eHake it Dr. Langstrom has\r\nsomehow become the Man-Bat again.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:13.605 --\u003e 00:05:14.940\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: It seems that way.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:15.398 --\u003e 00:05:18.735\r\nYou don't suppose he's taking\r\nthat formula of his again, do you?\r\n\r\n00:05:18.902 --\u003e 00:05:22.322\r\nI don't know.\r\nBut I know where I can find the answer.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.951 --\u003e 00:05:27.077\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.413 --\u003e 00:05:31.414\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:44.052 --\u003e 00:05:46.137\r\nDad. Where is he, Dad?\r\n\r\n00:05:46.471 --\u003e 00:05:48.765\r\nI'm not your husband's\r\nkeeper, Francine.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.932 --\u003e 00:05:51.434\r\nHe won't even work with me\r\nanymore, remember?\r\n\r\n00:05:51.935 --\u003e 00:05:53.395\r\nCan't you see I'm worried?\r\n\r\n00:05:53.687 --\u003e 00:05:57.524\r\nHe's experimenting again with\r\nthe bat mutagen. I'm sure of it.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.899 --\u003e 00:05:59.609\r\nWell, I wouldn't know\r\nanything about that.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.901 --\u003e 00:06:02.195\r\nHe's been holed up in there\r\nsince before I got here.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.445 --\u003e 00:06:03.822\r\nWhy don't you ask him yourself?\r\n\r\n00:06:04.030 --\u003e 00:06:06.074\r\nI'm busy enough with\r\nmy own research.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.961 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.052 --\u003e 00:06:27.929\r\nFRANCINE: I can't go\r\nthrough it again, Kirk.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.346 --\u003e 00:06:29.556\r\nI won't go through it.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.931 --\u003e 00:06:30.974\r\nFrancine.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.892 --\u003e 00:06:35.186\r\nWhy, Kirk? Why would you do this to me?\r\nYou promised.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.605 --\u003e 00:06:38.398\r\n(STAMMERS) It's\r\nnot what you think.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.607 --\u003e 00:06:39.816\r\nBATMAN: The devil, it isn't.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.485 --\u003e 00:06:45.322\r\nI'm sick and tired of cleaning\r\nup after you, Langstrom.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.739 --\u003e 00:06:48.450\r\n- So people have spotted it?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.992 --\u003e 00:06:51.953\r\nYou must have some kind of death wish\r\nto take that stuff again, Doctor.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.621 --\u003e 00:06:55.373\r\nWhat? You think it's\r\nhappening deliberately?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.540 --\u003e 00:06:59.127\r\nIf I am transforming,\r\nthen that thing's still inside me.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.628 --\u003e 00:07:01.421\r\nI'm not taking the formula.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.255 --\u003e 00:07:04.007\r\nStop it, stop it!\r\n\r\n00:07:04.174 --\u003e 00:07:05.926\r\nI'm sick of hearing\r\nabout that thing.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.051 --\u003e 00:07:08.178\r\nI'm sick of my life.\r\nI'm sick of you.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.970 --\u003e 00:07:10.931\r\nFrancine. Francine, wait!\r\n\r\n00:07:11.598 --\u003e 00:07:14.559\r\nIf you haven't been taking the\r\nformula again, what's all this?\r\n\r\n00:07:15.060 --\u003e 00:07:18.104\r\nWhat do you think?\r\nI've been trying to clean up after you.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.688 --\u003e 00:07:21.066\r\nObviously your so-called\r\nantidote didn't work.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.441 --\u003e 00:07:23.902\r\nHow could it have,\r\nif I'm still transforming?\r\n\r\n00:07:24.110 --\u003e 00:07:27.322\r\nDon't you get it yet, Batman?\r\nYou failed.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.365 --\u003e 00:07:31.201\r\nAll right, let's prove it.\r\nGive me your hand.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.701 --\u003e 00:07:34.204\r\n- What are you doing?\r\n- A DNA sample.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.537 --\u003e 00:07:37.540\r\nI'll run some tests.\r\nWe'll see what the truth is.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.504 --\u003e 00:07:44.631\r\nLangstrom, look,\r\nif you're right...\r\n\r\n00:07:44.965 --\u003e 00:07:47.133\r\nSave it.\r\nYou've done enough already.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.429 --\u003e 00:07:52.639\r\nI'll be in touch.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.860 --\u003e 00:08:06.861\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.029 --\u003e 00:08:09.239\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.659 --\u003e 00:08:13.660\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:08:13.868 --\u003e 00:08:15.161\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:29.467 --\u003e 00:08:30.677\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.180 --\u003e 00:08:35.348\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:08:43.773 --\u003e 00:08:45.150\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:19.893 --\u003e 00:09:21.019\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:36.534 --\u003e 00:09:37.869\r\n(HORNS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:49.714 --\u003e 00:09:50.799\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:54.427 --\u003e 00:09:56.721\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n- (CROWD SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)\r\n\r\n00:10:02.435 --\u003e 00:10:03.603\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.229 --\u003e 00:10:05.230\r\nWOMAN: Look!\r\n\r\n00:10:08.942 --\u003e 00:10:09.943\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:14.823 --\u003e 00:10:15.990\r\n(BATMAN STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:10:29.921 --\u003e 00:10:31.005\r\n(TRAIN WHISTLE BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.422 --\u003e 00:10:33.341\r\nThe end of a perfect day.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.772 --\u003e 00:10:49.107\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:51.985 --\u003e 00:10:55.280\r\nIndeed, Master Bruce,\r\nit does seem that with a bit more luck,\r\n\r\n00:10:55.363 --\u003e 00:10:56.447\r\nyou could have had him.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.534 --\u003e 00:11:02.078\r\nI think I got all of him I need.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.873 --\u003e 00:11:06.624\r\nWell, if she's not at\r\nthe ticket counter,\r\n\r\n00:11:06.708 --\u003e 00:11:08.084\r\ncould you page her, please?\r\n\r\n00:11:08.543 --\u003e 00:11:09.544\r\nThis is her husband.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.545 --\u003e 00:11:11.546\r\nBATMAN: Langstrom.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.131 --\u003e 00:11:14.132\r\nI have news.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.674 --\u003e 00:11:17.260\r\nFrancine's gone.\r\nShe really left me.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.844 --\u003e 00:11:18.970\r\nNot that I can blame her.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.429 --\u003e 00:11:21.139\r\nWho wants to live\r\nwith a monster?\r\n\r\n00:11:21.306 --\u003e 00:11:24.100\r\nYou're not a monster,\r\nLangstrom, not anymore.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.517 --\u003e 00:11:28.271\r\nMy tests show that the original\r\nantidote did work after all.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.354 --\u003e 00:11:30.857\r\nI also got a sample\r\nof the creature's DNA.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.232 --\u003e 00:11:32.483\r\nAnd after comparing them,\r\n\r\n00:11:32.775 --\u003e 00:11:36.321\r\nI'm certain the monster is someone\r\nelse, a new bat creature.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.905 --\u003e 00:11:38.072\r\nWe're both off the hook.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.907 --\u003e 00:11:42.827\r\n- But if it's not me, then-\r\n- Let me worry about that.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.411 --\u003e 00:11:44.537\r\nYou've got other problems.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.704 --\u003e 00:11:47.290\r\nRight. Maybe I can catch\r\nher before her plane leaves.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.582 --\u003e 00:11:49.292\r\nYou're sure you\r\ndon't need any help?\r\n\r\n00:11:49.709 --\u003e 00:11:52.462\r\nDon't worry.\r\nI'll take care of everything.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.142 --\u003e 00:12:08.519\r\nDR. MARCH: Put that down. Now!\r\n\r\n00:12:09.979 --\u003e 00:12:12.065\r\nOr I'll fill you with\r\nso much tranquilizer,\r\n\r\n00:12:12.190 --\u003e 00:12:13.483\r\nyou'll be out for a week.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.192 --\u003e 00:12:16.819\r\nYou couldn't leave it\r\nalone, could you, March?\r\n\r\n00:12:17.362 --\u003e 00:12:18.947\r\nYou've recreated the mutagen.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.239 --\u003e 00:12:21.699\r\nRecreated it? I've refined it.\r\n\r\n00:12:21.824 --\u003e 00:12:24.953\r\nAt night, on my own,\r\nso the others wouldn't know.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.203 --\u003e 00:12:28.498\r\nI still believe only a\r\ncreature like a Man-Bat\r\n\r\n00:12:28.623 --\u003e 00:12:31.334\r\ncan survive the next\r\nevolutionary cataclysm.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.459 --\u003e 00:12:32.460\r\nAnd it will.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.752 --\u003e 00:12:36.631\r\nMy new serum could be even\r\nmore powerful than Kirk's.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.299 --\u003e 00:12:39.592\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:40.426 --\u003e 00:12:42.428\r\nCould be? What do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:12:42.679 --\u003e 00:12:45.598\r\nI needed to test it,\r\nbut before I had the chance-\r\n\r\n00:12:45.974 --\u003e 00:12:48.685\r\n- You mean, you haven't taken it?\r\n- Of course not.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.060 --\u003e 00:12:51.646\r\nThe experimental batch was destroyed.\r\nI'll have to-\r\n\r\n00:12:51.729 --\u003e 00:12:52.730\r\nDestroyed how?\r\n\r\n00:12:53.106 --\u003e 00:12:54.857\r\nI'd been working\r\nthrough the night.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.316 --\u003e 00:12:57.235\r\nI was just completing\r\nthe final combination.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.777 --\u003e 00:13:00.280\r\n\u003ci\u003eFrancine burst in.\r\nI was startled.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:00.780 --\u003e 00:13:02.782\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou have to understand.\r\nI was very tired.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:02.865 --\u003e 00:13:07.078\r\n\u003ci\u003eI accidentally dropped the beaker.\r\nThe whole night's work, ruined.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:07.704 --\u003e 00:13:09.580\r\n\u003ci\u003eFrancine never guessed\r\nwhat I'd been doing.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:09.914 --\u003e 00:13:13.459\r\nShe even helped me clean up the\r\nmess, all that glass...\r\n\r\n00:13:15.461 --\u003e 00:13:18.548\r\nOh! Oh, my Lord! Francine.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.923 --\u003e 00:13:21.759\r\nThe mutagen,\r\nit's in her bloodstream now.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.843 --\u003e 00:13:22.969\r\nOh, no!\r\n\r\n00:13:26.848 --\u003e 00:13:28.516\r\nIs that what it's going to take?\r\n\r\n00:13:28.808 --\u003e 00:13:31.853\r\nYour daughter's life,\r\nbefore you end this insanity?\r\n\r\n00:14:05.219 --\u003e 00:14:06.346\r\nHow can I help you, ma'am?\r\n\r\n00:14:06.929 --\u003e 00:14:09.057\r\nI'm afraid I'm not\r\nfeeling very well.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.265 --\u003e 00:14:11.392\r\n- Could you get me some aspirin?\r\n- Certainly.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.900 --\u003e 00:14:23.071\r\nKirk. Of all the ridiculous stunts...\r\nI told you-\r\n\r\n00:14:23.154 --\u003e 00:14:25.990\r\nNo, Francine, this time I talk.\r\nYou listen.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.366 --\u003e 00:14:28.993\r\nWhoever the creature\r\nis, it's not me.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.410 --\u003e 00:14:30.787\r\nThe Batman can prove it.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.245 --\u003e 00:14:33.081\r\nBut how? Who?\r\n\r\n00:14:33.539 --\u003e 00:14:36.376\r\nWhat's the difference anymore?\r\nCome home.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.674 --\u003e 00:14:45.760\r\n- (GROANS SOFTLY)\r\n- Honey, what's wrong?\r\n\r\n00:14:47.303 --\u003e 00:14:48.679\r\n(STAMMERING) \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e don't know.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.597 --\u003e 00:14:52.016\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.814 --\u003e 00:14:58.815\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:59.440 --\u003e 00:15:01.025\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:04.320 --\u003e 00:15:05.822\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.539 --\u003e 00:15:15.540\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.001 --\u003e 00:15:20.211\r\n(SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.134 --\u003e 00:15:27.510\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:33.599 --\u003e 00:15:35.184\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:37.812 --\u003e 00:15:38.896\r\nFrancine!\r\n\r\n00:15:42.567 --\u003e 00:15:43.609\r\nFrancine!\r\n\r\n00:15:51.701 --\u003e 00:15:53.911\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:15:57.165 --\u003e 00:15:58.624\r\nFrancine!\r\n\r\n00:16:05.631 --\u003e 00:16:07.383\r\n(PASSENGERS SHOUTING\r\nINDISTINCTLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:11.471 --\u003e 00:16:12.638\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:15.933 --\u003e 00:16:18.133\r\n- Cabin pressure dropping.\r\n- PILOT: Gotta take her down.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.227 --\u003e 00:16:20.271\r\nPan-Con 1-4-4 to GCX Control.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.354 --\u003e 00:16:21.772\r\n\u003ci\u003eCabin pressure has failed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:21.981 --\u003e 00:16:24.661\r\n\u003ci\u003eRequesting clearance for emergency\r\nlanding immediately, do you copy?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:29.822 --\u003e 00:16:31.699\r\n(PASSENGERS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.950 --\u003e 00:16:34.410\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:34.494 --\u003e 00:16:35.786\r\nHold on!\r\n\r\n00:16:52.178 --\u003e 00:16:53.221\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:05.525 --\u003e 00:17:06.734\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:14.367 --\u003e 00:17:15.535\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:18:57.053 --\u003e 00:18:58.262\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:11.525 --\u003e 00:19:12.902\r\n(DART GUN FIRES)\r\n\r\n00:19:19.200 --\u003e 00:19:20.701\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:26.248 --\u003e 00:19:27.667\r\n- (GROWLS)\r\n- (BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:44.934 --\u003e 00:19:46.102\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.185 --\u003e 00:19:47.436\r\n(RADAR CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.979 --\u003e 00:19:51.482\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:56.570 --\u003e 00:19:58.030\r\n(BATMAN STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.991 --\u003e 00:20:02.118\r\n(SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.804 --\u003e 00:20:23.347\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:25.975 --\u003e 00:20:27.309\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.148 --\u003e 00:20:34.233\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:40.823 --\u003e 00:20:41.991\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.703 --\u003e 00:20:46.704\r\nKirk.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.037 --\u003e 00:20:48.539\r\n(GROANING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:52.168 --\u003e 00:20:53.169\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.466 --\u003e 00:20:59.508\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:00.301 --\u003e 00:21:01.510\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:02.762 --\u003e 00:21:03.846\r\nKIRK: I've got you, honey.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.680 --\u003e 00:21:07.683\r\nAnd this time,\r\nI'm not letting you go.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.645 --\u003e 00:21:12.646\r\nFRANCINE: Kirk.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.147 --\u003e 00:21:15.316\r\nKIRK: The nightmare's\r\nfinally over.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.407 --\u003e 00:21:25.409\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:49.558 --\u003e 00:21:50.559\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E38 - Christmas with The Joker (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.423 --\u003e 00:00:08.425\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:21.456 --\u003e 00:01:22.934\r\n\u003ci\u003eINMATES: (SINGING) Jingle\r\nBells, Jingle Bells.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:22.958 --\u003e 00:01:25.085\r\n\u003ci\u003eJingle all the way.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:25.210 --\u003e 00:01:29.131\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, what fun it is to ride In\r\na one horse open slay, hey!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:29.339 --\u003e 00:01:32.718\r\n\u003ci\u003eJingle Bells,\r\nBatman smells Robin laid an egg.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:33.218 --\u003e 00:01:38.974\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Batmobile lost a wheel\r\nAnd the Joker got away!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:44.646 --\u003e 00:01:45.897\r\n(JOKER CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:52.696 --\u003e 00:01:56.283\r\n\u003ci\u003eCrashing through the roof\r\nIn a one-horse open tree.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:56.825 --\u003e 00:02:00.996\r\n\u003ci\u003eBusting out I go\r\nLaughing all the wheeeee!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:01.079 --\u003e 00:02:02.456\r\n(JOKER LAUGHS MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:06.376 --\u003e 00:02:08.545\r\nROBIN: Come on, Batman,\r\nit's Christmas Eve.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.837 --\u003e 00:02:10.881\r\nLet's kick back and\r\nget into the spirit.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.423 --\u003e 00:02:14.426\r\nBATMAN: The Joker's escaped\r\nfrom Arkham Asylum, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.760 --\u003e 00:02:17.846\r\nAnd you really think he's gonna\r\nmake his move on Christmas Eve?\r\n\r\n00:02:18.096 --\u003e 00:02:20.932\r\nEven scum spend the holidays\r\nwith their families.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.475 --\u003e 00:02:23.268\r\nBATMAN: He has no family.\r\n\r\n00:02:24.311 --\u003e 00:02:25.896\r\nOkay, I'll make a deal with you.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:30.359\r\nIf we go out on patrol, and Gotham\r\nis quiet with no sign of the Joker,\r\n\r\n00:02:30.692 --\u003e 00:02:35.238\r\nwe come back here, have Christmas\r\ndinner and watch It's a Wonderful Life.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.614 --\u003e 00:02:39.534\r\nYou know, I've never seen that.\r\nI could never get past the title.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.744 --\u003e 00:02:41.745\r\nIt's a deal, then?\r\n\r\n00:02:42.204 --\u003e 00:02:43.205\r\nDeal.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.889 --\u003e 00:03:02.891\r\n(JAZZY CHRISTMAS MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.983 --\u003e 00:03:13.527\r\n(BELL RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:13.610 --\u003e 00:03:14.611\r\n(come CLINK)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.990 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nDoesn't it warm your heart to see\r\neveryone in the spirit of Christmas?\r\n\r\n00:03:29.292 --\u003e 00:03:31.169\r\nBah Humbug to you, too.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.339 --\u003e 00:03:37.676\r\nYou just can't believe there's\r\nno use for us for one night.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.721 --\u003e 00:03:41.722\r\nThere.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.560 --\u003e 00:03:47.769\r\nHey, lady, hold up.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.395 --\u003e 00:03:50.856\r\nYou dropped this package\r\na couple blocks back.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.440 --\u003e 00:03:54.609\r\nOh, it's for my grandson.\r\nThanks so much.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.027 --\u003e 00:03:57.446\r\nMerry Christmas.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.364 --\u003e 00:04:00.949\r\nNow can we go home?\r\n\r\n00:04:04.619 --\u003e 00:04:06.705\r\nHe could give\r\nlessons to Scrooge.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.752 --\u003e 00:04:13.712\r\nALFRED: The Christmas goose\r\nwill be ready shortly.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.838 --\u003e 00:04:17.841\r\nYou know, we really should've\r\ndone one more sweep of the city.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.341 --\u003e 00:04:19.843\r\nNow just relax, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.010 --\u003e 00:04:22.637\r\nYou're gonna love It's a Wonderful Life.\r\nIt's a great movie.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.430 --\u003e 00:04:25.515\r\nIt's not relentlessly\r\ncheerful, is it?\r\n\r\n00:04:26.224 --\u003e 00:04:27.984\r\nDICK: No,\r\nit's about how much of a difference\r\n\r\n00:04:28.059 --\u003e 00:04:30.020\r\none man can make to a city.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.645 --\u003e 00:04:31.646\r\nSound familiar?\r\n\r\n00:04:33.482 --\u003e 00:04:35.233\r\n(CHRISTMAS CAROL PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.985 --\u003e 00:04:39.029\r\nUh, wrong channel.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.529 --\u003e 00:04:41.406\r\nSome kind of Christmas special.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.621 --\u003e 00:04:51.249\r\nANNOUNCER: It's a Wonderful\r\nLife \u003ci\u003ewill\u003c/i\u003e not be seen this year.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.458 --\u003e 00:04:53.335\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn its place is the following.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:54.461 --\u003e 00:04:58.757\r\n\u003ci\u003eJoker here. Greetings,\r\nGotham, and merry Christmas.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:59.174 --\u003e 00:05:03.762\r\n\u003ci\u003eI hope you're watching, Batman.\r\nThis one's for you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:03.845 --\u003e 00:05:05.847\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:17.359 --\u003e 00:05:18.652\r\n(PEDESTRIANS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:21.780 --\u003e 00:05:24.157\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Live from Gotham City,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:24.241 --\u003e 00:05:28.912\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe show that nobody wants to\r\nsee but everyone will watch.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:39.589 --\u003e 00:05:44.219\r\nYes,\r\nit's Christmas with the Joker!\r\n\r\n00:05:45.095 --\u003e 00:05:50.058\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd now, let's welcome our\r\nhost, the Clown Prince of Crime,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:50.392 --\u003e 00:05:52.102\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe Joker!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:52.185 --\u003e 00:05:53.228\r\n(AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:05:53.311 --\u003e 00:05:55.772\r\n\u003ci\u003eGreetings from Gotham City.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:55.856 --\u003e 00:06:00.360\r\nAnd welcome to the \u003ci\u003efirst\u003c/i\u003e annual\r\nChristmas with the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.443 --\u003e 00:06:01.736\r\n(APPLAUDING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:06:04.030 --\u003e 00:06:07.951\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, thank you, thank you.\r\nThank you very much.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:08.034 --\u003e 00:06:09.244\r\n(JOKER CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:06:09.327 --\u003e 00:06:12.122\r\n\u003ci\u003eHave I got a show\r\nfor you tonight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:16.877\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's loaded with surprises and\r\nmystery guests and Christmas jeer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:16.960 --\u003e 00:06:19.629\r\nROBIN: Well, Batman,\r\nyou were sure right about the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.297 --\u003e 00:06:21.298\r\nAny leads?\r\n\r\n00:06:22.549 --\u003e 00:06:25.010\r\nI've accessed Gotham's\r\nelectrical mainframe.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.427 --\u003e 00:06:27.804\r\nAnd I'm zeroing in\r\non the power surges\r\n\r\n00:06:27.888 --\u003e 00:06:30.390\r\nto pinpoint the location of\r\nJoker's broadcast signal.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.473 --\u003e 00:06:32.684\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n- That's it.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.351 --\u003e 00:06:35.979\r\nI don't know, Batman,\r\nit seems too easy.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.271 --\u003e 00:06:38.148\r\nBATMAN: It's never\r\neasy with the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.815 --\u003e 00:06:41.651\r\nOh, Batman,\r\nI hope you're watching\r\n\r\n00:06:41.735 --\u003e 00:06:45.447\r\n\u003ci\u003e'cause I've got a very\r\nspecial surprise for you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:47.574 --\u003e 00:06:51.870\r\nRumor has it, Christmas is\r\na time to share with family.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.953 --\u003e 00:06:54.039\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:54.372 --\u003e 00:06:57.083\r\nAnd since I don't\r\nhave one of my own...\r\n\r\n00:06:57.167 --\u003e 00:06:59.044\r\nAUDIENCE: Aww!\r\n\r\n00:06:59.669 --\u003e 00:07:02.255\r\nI decided to steal one.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.339 --\u003e 00:07:04.341\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:05.216 --\u003e 00:07:10.138\r\nAnd here they are,\r\nthe awful Lawful family.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.014 --\u003e 00:07:15.894\r\nAren't they just the cutest\r\nfamily you've ever seen?\r\n\r\n00:07:18.188 --\u003e 00:07:20.398\r\nIt's never easy with the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.232 --\u003e 00:07:24.027\r\n\u003ci\u003eMeet Daddy Lawful.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:25.403 --\u003e 00:07:27.447\r\nYou diseased maniac! I'll...\r\n(MUFFLED SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.781 --\u003e 00:07:28.782\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.865 --\u003e 00:07:32.202\r\nLooks like I'll have to\r\nteach Daddy some manners.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.161 --\u003e 00:07:35.956\r\nAnd here's Mommy Lawful.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.748 --\u003e 00:07:39.834\r\n(GASPS) Help!\r\nSomebody please help us. We...\r\n\r\n00:07:39.918 --\u003e 00:07:41.086\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:07:41.169 --\u003e 00:07:43.922\r\nHo, ho, ho. Isn't she jolly?\r\n\r\n00:07:44.172 --\u003e 00:07:47.968\r\nAnd here we have\r\nlittle Baby Lawful.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.051 --\u003e 00:07:50.428\r\nCoochie, coochie, coo.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.429 --\u003e 00:07:53.932\r\nWhen I get my hands on\r\nyou, I'll rip your...\r\n\r\n00:07:54.015 --\u003e 00:07:55.016\r\n(MUFFLED SPEAKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:55.517 --\u003e 00:07:59.729\r\nI'll bet Batman wishes he\r\nhad a familyjust like mine.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.980 --\u003e 00:08:02.315\r\nPersonally,\r\nI think relatives are a bore,\r\n\r\n00:08:02.565 --\u003e 00:08:07.195\r\nso Batman can have them if\r\nhe can find them by midnight.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.278 --\u003e 00:08:08.446\r\n(AUDIENCE GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.780 --\u003e 00:08:10.156\r\nOtherwise...\r\n\r\n00:08:10.240 --\u003e 00:08:11.408\r\n(IMITATES THROAT SLITTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.951 --\u003e 00:08:14.995\r\n(JOKER CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:17.080 --\u003e 00:08:19.124\r\nHold tight, we're almost there.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.624 --\u003e 00:08:23.420\r\n\u003ci\u003eHi, I'm Laffy,\r\nJoker's helpful little elf.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:23.503 --\u003e 00:08:28.216\r\nI'm here to present Batman with a\r\nvery special Christmas surprise.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.299 --\u003e 00:08:30.093\r\nUh-oh, here it comes.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.094 --\u003e 00:08:35.432\r\nGee, Joker, it's sure nice of\r\nyou to get Bat Breath a present.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.640 --\u003e 00:08:38.435\r\nHo, ho,\r\nI'm just that kind of guy.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.518 --\u003e 00:08:39.853\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:39.936 --\u003e 00:08:43.148\r\nIt's an exact replica\r\nof Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.898 --\u003e 00:08:47.235\r\nIt has everything,\r\neven trains and bridges.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.736 --\u003e 00:08:51.031\r\nBridges?\r\nI just love blowing up bridges.\r\n\r\n00:08:51.948 --\u003e 00:08:53.491\r\nWell, in that case,\r\n\r\n00:08:53.575 --\u003e 00:08:57.620\r\nlet's go live to Donner and\r\nBlitzen at the President's Bridge.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.538 --\u003e 00:09:00.206\r\n\u003ci\u003eGreetings, Donner.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:00.331 --\u003e 00:09:04.085\r\n\u003ci\u003eHow about singing us a merry tune\r\nwhile you blow up the bridge?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:04.753 --\u003e 00:09:05.754\r\nSure, boss.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.047 --\u003e 00:09:10.467\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SINGING) Jingle Bells,\r\nBatman smells Robin laid an egg.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:22.062 --\u003e 00:09:23.730\r\nThat was great!\r\n\r\n00:09:23.813 --\u003e 00:09:26.149\r\nThe fun has just begun.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.691 --\u003e 00:09:29.944\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe 11:30 train will\r\nbe along any minute.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:31.321 --\u003e 00:09:33.323\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:35.241 --\u003e 00:09:36.743\r\nWe've gotta stop that train.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.868 --\u003e 00:09:39.954\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:40.121 --\u003e 00:09:45.210\r\nOh, look, Laffy,\r\nMommy Lawful has something to say.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.835 --\u003e 00:09:47.670\r\nWhat's up, Mommy?\r\n\r\n00:09:48.046 --\u003e 00:09:49.547\r\nMy mother's on that train.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.048 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\nYour mother?\r\nWell, that's different, then.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.968 --\u003e 00:09:57.430\r\nYeah, it'll be even more\r\nexciting when it crashes.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.514 --\u003e 00:09:59.474\r\n(LAUGHS MOCKINGLY)\r\n\r\n00:10:12.946 --\u003e 00:10:15.824\r\nYou uncouple the passenger cars.\r\nI'll get the engineer.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.386 --\u003e 00:10:38.388\r\n(METAL CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:11:05.915 --\u003e 00:11:07.041\r\nThe bridge is out. Come on.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.148 --\u003e 00:11:33.318\r\nBah Humbug.\r\nI hate Batman and Robin.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.985 --\u003e 00:11:35.653\r\nThen let's get rid of them.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.158 --\u003e 00:11:43.077\r\nOh, boy, let's build a snowman.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.912 --\u003e 00:11:45.538\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:47.332 --\u003e 00:11:49.209\r\nWe've isolated the\r\nJoker's broadcast signal.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.292 --\u003e 00:11:51.794\r\nIt's coming from the\r\nobservatory on Mount Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.142 --\u003e 00:12:08.144\r\nBATMAN: There,\r\nthe radar antenna.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.645 --\u003e 00:12:09.646\r\nROBIN: What's that?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.648 --\u003e 00:12:14.817\r\nCareful, Robin. I'm sure there's\r\nmore to this than meets the eye.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.901 --\u003e 00:12:15.902\r\n(RUSTLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:18.238 --\u003e 00:12:20.782\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Merry Christmas, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:20.865 --\u003e 00:12:23.409\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm so glad you could join us.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:24.285 --\u003e 00:12:25.620\r\nWhat's your game, Joker?\r\n\r\n00:12:25.995 --\u003e 00:12:29.666\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Oh, just a little\r\nholiday entertainment, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:30.166 --\u003e 00:12:34.587\r\nI'm sure all the folks at home will\r\nenjoy sharing this special occasion.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.921 --\u003e 00:12:40.343\r\n\u003ci\u003eLadies and gentlemen, boys and girls,\r\nlive from the top of Mount Gotham,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:40.426 --\u003e 00:12:43.513\r\nthe death of Batman.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.771 --\u003e 00:12:56.526\r\nWhen you care enough\r\nto send the very blast.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.901 --\u003e 00:13:02.699\r\nWe'll return in just a moment,\r\nbut first a word from our sponsor.\r\n\r\n00:13:14.294 --\u003e 00:13:16.921\r\nRobin, try and get\r\ninside the observatory.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.171 --\u003e 00:13:18.423\r\nI'll draw its fire.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.726 --\u003e 00:13:34.564\r\nWhoops. Looks like we're\r\nexperiencing technical difficulty.\r\n\r\n00:13:34.814 --\u003e 00:13:37.984\r\nBut don't worry, folks,\r\nwe're still on the air.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.401 --\u003e 00:13:42.572\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, no! Our cannon seems\r\nto be out of control.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:42.822 --\u003e 00:13:46.284\r\n\u003ci\u003eGotham City could be\r\nin serious danger.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:47.452 --\u003e 00:13:49.287\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:51.122 --\u003e 00:13:53.249\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:03.968 --\u003e 00:14:06.429\r\n(JOKERS CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:24.572 --\u003e 00:14:26.199\r\nBatman, Robin here.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.830 --\u003e 00:14:35.541\r\nRobin,\r\nOperation Cause and Effect.\r\n\r\n00:14:36.709 --\u003e 00:14:37.710\r\nGotcha.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.563 --\u003e 00:14:58.564\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:14:58.815 --\u003e 00:15:02.110\r\nI'm fine. But we're not any\r\ncloser to finding Joker's hideout.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.485 --\u003e 00:15:03.736\r\nWhat's our next move?\r\n\r\n00:15:04.070 --\u003e 00:15:06.906\r\nTo be quite honest,\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.494 --\u003e 00:15:15.248\r\nBatman, it's almost midnight.\r\nWe have to do something.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.581 --\u003e 00:15:19.627\r\nIt's up to the Joker now.\r\nOnly a miracle can save the hostages.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.044 --\u003e 00:15:23.548\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Arrgh! Where's that Bat fella?\r\nAnd that Robin fella?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:23.631 --\u003e 00:15:25.425\r\n\u003ci\u003eOoh, they're gonna\r\nspoil my Christmas.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:25.508 --\u003e 00:15:28.928\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat's the matter?\r\nCan't they figure anything out? Time's up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:29.011 --\u003e 00:15:31.597\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm rubbing everybody\r\nout at midnight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:32.598 --\u003e 00:15:36.144\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut wait,\r\nwe have another present to open.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:37.061 --\u003e 00:15:40.231\r\n\u003ci\u003eLet's not keep Mommy\r\nLawful waiting.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:41.315 --\u003e 00:15:44.652\r\n\u003ci\u003eToo bad Batman is\r\nsuch a party pooper.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:45.194 --\u003e 00:15:47.196\r\n\u003ci\u003eMaybe he doesn't\r\nknow how to get here.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:47.488 --\u003e 00:15:50.032\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll dressed up\r\nwith nowhere to go.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:50.700 --\u003e 00:15:56.497\r\nWell, I wonder what Mommy\r\nLawful is getting for Christmas.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.331 --\u003e 00:16:00.543\r\nOoh! The suspense is killing me.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.002 --\u003e 00:16:07.967\r\nIs it? Can it be? Oh, yes!\r\nIt's a Betty Blooper doll.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.843 --\u003e 00:16:12.263\r\nAnd what do Better\r\nBlooper dolls do?\r\n\r\n00:16:12.597 --\u003e 00:16:15.266\r\nWhy, you just wind them up...\r\n\r\n00:16:16.893 --\u003e 00:16:20.229\r\nAnd they wreak havoc\r\non Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.521 --\u003e 00:16:22.690\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:24.609 --\u003e 00:16:26.819\r\nI haven't seen one of\r\nthose dolls in years.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.069 --\u003e 00:16:29.030\r\nThey don't make dolls\r\nlike that anymore,\r\n\r\n00:16:29.363 --\u003e 00:16:34.118\r\nnot since the Laffco toy factory\r\nwent out of business 14 years ago.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.411 --\u003e 00:16:36.954\r\nThird and Main, downtown.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.636 --\u003e 00:16:53.638\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.615 --\u003e 00:17:13.616\r\nLook sharp, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.492 --\u003e 00:17:16.410\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:24.961 --\u003e 00:17:27.129\r\n(CLASSICAL CHRISTMAS\r\nMUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:17:33.386 --\u003e 00:17:34.804\r\nWhere's that music coming from?\r\n\r\n00:17:35.429 --\u003e 00:17:36.430\r\nGood question.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.098 --\u003e 00:17:38.224\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.065 --\u003e 00:17:47.275\r\nBATMAN: Look out!\r\n\r\n00:18:10.506 --\u003e 00:18:12.258\r\nStand ready. More on the way.\r\n\r\n00:18:21.183 --\u003e 00:18:22.184\r\nStand clear, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.455 --\u003e 00:18:44.707\r\nThey don't call you\r\n\"Batman\" for nothing.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.001 --\u003e 00:18:48.002\r\n(GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:18:48.210 --\u003e 00:18:49.211\r\nSnipers!\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.274\r\nWhere'd he go?\r\n\r\n00:19:12.026 --\u003e 00:19:13.027\r\nThere he is.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.744 --\u003e 00:19:22.953\r\n- Huh?\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:19:24.955 --\u003e 00:19:26.040\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:19:26.123 --\u003e 00:19:27.458\r\nBOTH: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:19:28.751 --\u003e 00:19:30.711\r\n\u003ci\u003eTEDDY: I love you very much.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:35.466 --\u003e 00:19:37.134\r\nKeep your eyes\r\nopen for the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.094 --\u003e 00:19:40.971\r\nI'll save you the\r\ntrouble, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.347 --\u003e 00:19:46.018\r\nCome and get your Christmas\r\npresent, or the kiddies get it.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.687 --\u003e 00:19:50.272\r\nLet them go, Joker.\r\nIt's me you want.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.065 --\u003e 00:19:53.818\r\nMerry Christmas, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.363 --\u003e 00:20:00.700\r\nWell, go on, open it.\r\n\r\n00:20:03.202 --\u003e 00:20:04.578\r\nDon't do it, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:20:04.995 --\u003e 00:20:06.163\r\nEasy, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.838 --\u003e 00:20:15.756\r\n(JOKER CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.178 --\u003e 00:20:23.097\r\nJOKER: Oh, I can't stand it.\r\n\r\n00:20:38.195 --\u003e 00:20:39.572\r\nRobin, take care of 'em.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.825 --\u003e 00:20:44.285\r\n(JOKER GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.911 --\u003e 00:20:47.455\r\n(JOKER LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:20:47.538 --\u003e 00:20:52.042\r\nRun, run as fast as you can.\r\nYou'll not catch me, I'm the Joker man.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.918 --\u003e 00:20:54.253\r\n(JOKER YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.883 --\u003e 00:21:00.134\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:03.763 --\u003e 00:21:05.222\r\nMerry Christmas, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.140 --\u003e 00:21:07.683\r\nBah Humbug.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.067 --\u003e 00:21:18.694\r\nIt was nice of\r\nCommissioner Gordon\r\n\r\n00:21:18.903 --\u003e 00:21:21.781\r\nto give you that recording\r\nof It's a Wonderful Life.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.323 --\u003e 00:21:24.450\r\nAnd it is a wonderful life.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.075 --\u003e 00:21:27.787\r\nIt has its moments.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.746 --\u003e 00:21:30.247\r\n(BELL TOLLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:34.752 --\u003e 00:21:36.128\r\n(CHRISTMAS CAROL PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:36.212 --\u003e 00:21:39.507\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SINGING) Don we\r\nnow our gay apparel.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:39.590 --\u003e 00:21:42.384\r\nFa-Ia-Ia, la-Ia-Ia, la-Ia-Ia\r\n\r\n00:21:43.052 --\u003e 00:21:45.304\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:49.141 --\u003e 00:21:50.851\r\nMerry Christmas.\r\n\r\n00:21:54.980 --\u003e 00:21:56.982\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E39 - Heart of Steel, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:17.684 --\u003e 00:00:19.686\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:41.435 --\u003e 00:01:43.103\r\nMiss, can I help you?\r\n\r\n00:01:55.449 --\u003e 00:01:57.492\r\nI think it belongs to that\r\nwoman who came in early.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.576 --\u003e 00:01:59.578\r\nMaybe there's a\r\nreward for finding it.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.376 --\u003e 00:02:09.630\r\nYou wouldn't think a lock\r\nthat good would just pop.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.713 --\u003e 00:02:11.632\r\nNo I.D. on any of this stuff.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.715 --\u003e 00:02:13.008\r\nWeird, huh.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.091 --\u003e 00:02:14.343\r\nWhat should we do with it?\r\n\r\n00:02:14.426 --\u003e 00:02:16.470\r\nEh, we'll worry about it tomorrow.\r\nIt's late.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.553 --\u003e 00:02:18.180\r\n- Pizza?\r\n- Sounds good.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.057 --\u003e 00:02:22.392\r\nWhoa there, Mr. Wayne.\r\nAnything wrong?\r\n\r\n00:02:22.476 --\u003e 00:02:25.312\r\nNo, just trying to get out\r\nbefore they set the night alarms.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.065 --\u003e 00:02:30.108\r\nNo problem, sir.\r\nI'll walk you to your car.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.192 --\u003e 00:02:31.193\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.276 --\u003e 00:02:33.236\r\nThe alarm system\r\nmakes me nervous.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.466 --\u003e 00:03:37.634\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:20.594 --\u003e 00:04:21.887\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:04:22.053 --\u003e 00:04:23.764\r\nDid we set it off by accident?\r\n\r\n00:04:23.847 --\u003e 00:04:25.682\r\nNo, sir. It's from upstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.519 --\u003e 00:04:31.146\r\nWhat the heck is that thing?\r\n\r\n00:04:34.149 --\u003e 00:04:35.734\r\nBetter not take any chances.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.817 --\u003e 00:04:37.027\r\nRight this way, sir.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.110 --\u003e 00:04:39.863\r\nNow, for your own safety you stay\r\nput, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:04:41.656 --\u003e 00:04:42.741\r\nStay put?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.158 --\u003e 00:04:44.534\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.683 --\u003e 00:05:09.976\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:26.743 --\u003e 00:05:28.036\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:05:32.207 --\u003e 00:05:33.375\r\n(SCRAPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:03.340 --\u003e 00:07:04.466\r\nHome.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.438 --\u003e 00:07:19.606\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:26.321 --\u003e 00:07:29.616\r\nIntruder rectifier. Now.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.786 --\u003e 00:07:33.995\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:10.156 --\u003e 00:08:11.366\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:29.843 --\u003e 00:08:33.304\r\nI do wish you wouldn't be so rough\r\nwith your toys, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.181 --\u003e 00:08:36.599\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:08:40.520 --\u003e 00:08:43.148\r\nWayne Manor. Moment, please.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.815 --\u003e 00:08:45.817\r\nMr. Lucius Fox, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.900 --\u003e 00:08:47.694\r\nShall I out him on\r\nthe speaker phone?\r\n\r\n00:08:47.777 --\u003e 00:08:49.070\r\nThank you, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.154 --\u003e 00:08:50.447\r\nLucius, what's up?\r\n\r\n00:08:50.530 --\u003e 00:08:52.115\r\nBad news, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.198 --\u003e 00:08:56.453\r\nThey got away with all the prototype\r\nprotein silicon wafer chips from R&D.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.536 --\u003e 00:08:58.038\r\nThe design specs?\r\n\r\n00:08:58.121 --\u003e 00:09:00.123\r\n\u003ci\u003eStill safe in the\r\ncomputer, thank heaven.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:00.498 --\u003e 00:09:02.959\r\nThe thieves won't be able to\r\nduplicate the chips without them.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.043 --\u003e 00:09:05.211\r\n\u003ci\u003eMaybe we should discuss\r\ntightening security\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:05.295 --\u003e 00:09:06.546\r\n\u003ci\u003ein case they come back.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:06.629 --\u003e 00:09:09.174\r\nYou're right.\r\n10 minutes, Lucius. Thanks.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.341 --\u003e 00:09:13.011\r\nProtein silicon\r\nwhat, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:09:13.094 --\u003e 00:09:16.598\r\nL's called Wetware.\r\nThe cutting edge of computer research.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.681 --\u003e 00:09:19.142\r\nSounds more like a\r\nline of swimsuits.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.225 --\u003e 00:09:22.562\r\nI'm talking about Al.\r\nArtificial intelligence.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.645 --\u003e 00:09:25.774\r\nThe missing link between\r\ncomputers and human thought.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.857 --\u003e 00:09:28.276\r\nYou mean machines that think?\r\n\r\n00:09:28.359 --\u003e 00:09:30.570\r\nYes,\r\nand with a will of their own.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.653 --\u003e 00:09:33.740\r\nThey could process raw data a\r\nmillion times faster than we.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.823 --\u003e 00:09:35.867\r\nIt'll still be able to\r\nmake the leaps of intuition\r\n\r\n00:09:35.950 --\u003e 00:09:37.744\r\nthat inspired our\r\ngreatest minds.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.827 --\u003e 00:09:41.498\r\nSounds as if the human race\r\nwill become quite expendable.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.581 --\u003e 00:09:42.999\r\nExcept for butlers, of course.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.625 --\u003e 00:09:44.667\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.751 --\u003e 00:09:47.295\r\nGORDON: When I told the mayor\r\nabout the nature of the theft,\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:49.506\r\nhe insisted I oversee\r\nthe investigation.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.589 --\u003e 00:09:52.675\r\nQuestion is, where could the\r\nthieves hope to sell this stuff?\r\n\r\n00:09:52.759 --\u003e 00:09:54.094\r\nBeats me.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.177 --\u003e 00:09:56.346\r\nOnly other group\r\nresearching AI on this coast\r\n\r\n00:09:56.429 --\u003e 00:09:58.348\r\nis Karl Rossum's\r\nteam at Cybertron.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.431 --\u003e 00:10:00.183\r\nI thought Rossum was retired.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.266 --\u003e 00:10:03.853\r\nBRUCE: Karl went into semi-seclusion\r\nafter the loss of his daughter.\r\n\r\n00:10:03.937 --\u003e 00:10:06.106\r\nHe taught me everything\r\nI know about electronics.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.189 --\u003e 00:10:08.608\r\nBut he's been more active\r\nin business lately.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.691 --\u003e 00:10:10.026\r\nI'll talk to him.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.110 --\u003e 00:10:11.361\r\nDad, you in here?\r\n\r\n00:10:12.487 --\u003e 00:10:13.863\r\nOops, bad timing.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.947 --\u003e 00:10:16.741\r\nBarbara, come in. You've grown.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.825 --\u003e 00:10:19.244\r\nIt's been, what, four years?\r\n\r\n00:10:19.327 --\u003e 00:10:22.330\r\nHome from college for a visit.\r\nMade the dean's list.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.413 --\u003e 00:10:24.374\r\nBRUCE: And who's\r\nyour little friend?\r\n\r\n00:10:25.959 --\u003e 00:10:27.794\r\n(CHUCKLES) This is Wubby.\r\n\r\n00:10:27.877 --\u003e 00:10:29.379\r\nMy best friend since 3rd grade.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.462 --\u003e 00:10:33.007\r\nDad can't seem to pick me up at the\r\nairport without bringing him along.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.299 --\u003e 00:10:34.592\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:10:34.676 --\u003e 00:10:37.137\r\nYes, well,\r\nhe knows the way better than I.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.220 --\u003e 00:10:40.765\r\nSo you go talk to Rossum and I'll\r\nstart things moving on my end.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.900 --\u003e 00:10:52.485\r\nBarbara forgot her bear.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.926 --\u003e 00:11:18.303\r\n(PIANO MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:11:24.684 --\u003e 00:11:25.977\r\n(TRUMPET PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:11:33.943 --\u003e 00:11:37.447\r\nBruce Wayne. I'm so glad you called.\r\nIt's been years.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.530 --\u003e 00:11:40.200\r\nI heard about the theft\r\nof those chips, my boy.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.284 --\u003e 00:11:42.619\r\nYou need better security.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.080 --\u003e 00:11:49.375\r\nJust curious if anyone's\r\ntried to sell you any Wetware.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.459 --\u003e 00:11:52.545\r\nAfraid not. If anyone does, of\r\ncourse, you'll be the first to know.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.796 --\u003e 00:11:55.548\r\n- Cappuccino?\r\n- Yes, thanks.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.299 --\u003e 00:11:58.635\r\nI was wondering about\r\nyour own AI research.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.809 --\u003e 00:12:08.770\r\nUh... Thank you.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.653 --\u003e 00:12:19.197\r\nNothing like a hot Cappuccino\r\nand a foot massage.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.280 --\u003e 00:12:21.783\r\nNow, let me show you\r\nmy pride and joy.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.619 --\u003e 00:12:26.246\r\nThis is my greatest achievement.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.329 --\u003e 00:12:28.498\r\nMY Prototype Al.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.581 --\u003e 00:12:30.291\r\nThis is HARDAC.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.128 --\u003e 00:12:35.338\r\nWho?\r\n\r\n00:12:36.839 --\u003e 00:12:40.885\r\nHolographic analytical\r\nreciprocating digital computer.\r\n\r\n00:12:45.056 --\u003e 00:12:46.349\r\n\u003ci\u003eHARD AC .\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:46.432 --\u003e 00:12:49.269\r\n\u003ci\u003eHARD AC. Okay.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:50.603\r\nAnd you?\r\n\r\n00:12:50.687 --\u003e 00:12:53.940\r\nHow rude of me.\r\nBruce, this is Randa Duane, my assistant.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.445 --\u003e 00:13:00.863\r\nYour hand is like ice.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.947 --\u003e 00:13:04.033\r\nSorry,\r\nI've been in the cold room.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.117 --\u003e 00:13:06.703\r\nSo tell me. What does HARDAC do?\r\n\r\n00:13:06.786 --\u003e 00:13:10.540\r\nNow, Bruce, I can't tell you\r\nall of my secrets, can I?\r\n\r\n00:13:12.625 --\u003e 00:13:14.502\r\nLet's just say that certain...\r\n\r\n00:13:17.588 --\u003e 00:13:21.592\r\nThat certain projects\r\nare under his control.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.315 --\u003e 00:13:38.276\r\nWell, since you won't tell me\r\nwhat you're working on, Karl,\r\n\r\n00:13:38.359 --\u003e 00:13:41.738\r\nmaybe I can charm the details\r\nout of your lovely assistant?\r\n\r\n00:13:41.821 --\u003e 00:13:43.823\r\nWell, you can try.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.615 --\u003e 00:13:46.784\r\nDinner?\r\nTomorrow night at my house?\r\n\r\n00:13:47.577 --\u003e 00:13:49.662\r\nLove to. After 8:00 though.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.746 --\u003e 00:13:51.289\r\nI'm working late.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.173 --\u003e 00:14:02.508\r\nGood. Well, I better get going.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.592 --\u003e 00:14:04.010\r\nI'll walk you out.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.652 --\u003e 00:14:25.281\r\n\u003ci\u003eRanda, you did not bring me\r\nthe design specifics I needed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:25.365 --\u003e 00:14:28.326\r\nThere wasn't time to get them from\r\nthe Wayne Enterprises' databanks.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.409 --\u003e 00:14:29.994\r\nI'll try again tomorrow night.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.078 --\u003e 00:14:32.997\r\n\u003ci\u003eSome people in high places\r\nare becoming too curious\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:33.081 --\u003e 00:14:34.332\r\n\u003ci\u003eabout this operation.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:34.415 --\u003e 00:14:36.250\r\n\u003ci\u003eThey must be dealt with.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:36.334 --\u003e 00:14:38.211\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe next duplicant is ready.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:41.339 --\u003e 00:14:43.674\r\n\u003ci\u003eSee to his placement. Tonight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:44.801 --\u003e 00:14:45.968\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.603 --\u003e 00:14:56.979\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:15:00.525 --\u003e 00:15:02.985\r\nI'll get it, princess.\r\nYou keep hitting those books.\r\n\r\n00:15:12.412 --\u003e 00:15:14.247\r\nYes. What is it?\r\n\r\n00:15:17.750 --\u003e 00:15:18.960\r\nWhat the devil?\r\n\r\n00:15:20.545 --\u003e 00:15:21.671\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:37.520 --\u003e 00:15:38.604\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:15:39.856 --\u003e 00:15:41.107\r\n(BODY THUDS)\r\n\r\n00:15:49.532 --\u003e 00:15:50.992\r\nDad, you okay?\r\n\r\n00:15:52.952 --\u003e 00:15:54.078\r\nI'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:15:54.704 --\u003e 00:15:55.913\r\nWho was at the door?\r\n\r\n00:15:59.709 --\u003e 00:16:02.003\r\nWere you outside?\r\nYour hand is like ice.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.086 --\u003e 00:16:03.171\r\nI'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.892 --\u003e 00:16:17.935\r\n- Dad, are you sure you're-\r\n- I said I'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.274 --\u003e 00:16:25.026\r\nAs of last night, Karl Rossum\r\n\r\n00:16:25.109 --\u003e 00:16:27.737\r\nhadn't been approached to\r\nreceive any stolen goods.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.820 --\u003e 00:16:29.238\r\nBut he knew what was stolen.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.322 --\u003e 00:16:32.825\r\nSo you'll try to squeeze some\r\ninfo from his assistant tonight.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.909 --\u003e 00:16:35.703\r\nWell, \"squeeze\" may\r\nnot be the best word.\r\n\r\n00:16:40.166 --\u003e 00:16:41.876\r\nI hope I'm not interrupting.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.919 --\u003e 00:16:44.086\r\nBRUCE: Not at all.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.170 --\u003e 00:16:46.923\r\nWe're just installing some\r\nnew computer safeguards.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.465 --\u003e 00:16:49.926\r\nWell, I'll stay out of your way.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.020 --\u003e 00:17:02.104\r\nShall we go?\r\n\r\n00:17:03.105 --\u003e 00:17:04.315\r\nAfter you.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.526 --\u003e 00:17:07.777\r\n(CHIMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.490 --\u003e 00:17:14.158\r\nDon't you like the roast, Dad?\r\n\r\n00:17:14.242 --\u003e 00:17:15.660\r\nIt's fine.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.743 --\u003e 00:17:18.329\r\nThat's practically all\r\nyou've said since last night.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.412 --\u003e 00:17:19.539\r\nAre you mad at me?\r\n\r\n00:17:20.331 --\u003e 00:17:21.541\r\nNo, you're-\r\n\r\n00:17:21.624 --\u003e 00:17:23.417\r\nI know. I'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.338 --\u003e 00:17:28.548\r\n(CHIMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:59.579 --\u003e 00:18:02.999\r\nBut the best one was the dishwasher\r\nthat turned into a Jacuzzi.\r\n\r\n00:18:03.082 --\u003e 00:18:04.375\r\n(BOTH LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:04.625 --\u003e 00:18:06.794\r\nYeah, Karl's a\r\ngenius, all right.\r\n\r\n00:18:06.877 --\u003e 00:18:08.838\r\nHe'd have to be to know\r\nit was Wetware chips\r\n\r\n00:18:08.921 --\u003e 00:18:10.381\r\nthat were stolen\r\nfrom my company.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.464 --\u003e 00:18:12.341\r\nCare to tell me about\r\nthat, Randa?\r\n\r\n00:18:12.592 --\u003e 00:18:14.010\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:18:16.053 --\u003e 00:18:17.221\r\nWayne here.\r\n\r\n00:18:17.763 --\u003e 00:18:18.973\r\nI'm on my way.\r\n\r\n00:18:19.056 --\u003e 00:18:22.310\r\nI have to go out.\r\nCall Alfred if you need anything.\r\n\r\n00:18:22.393 --\u003e 00:18:23.811\r\nI'll be back soon.\r\n\r\n00:18:33.154 --\u003e 00:18:34.322\r\nThey get the Wetware specs?\r\n\r\n00:18:34.405 --\u003e 00:18:35.615\r\nI don't know yet.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.698 --\u003e 00:18:37.366\r\nThey dust the keys for prints?\r\n\r\n00:18:37.450 --\u003e 00:18:39.201\r\nYeah. Nothing.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.287 --\u003e 00:18:43.039\r\nThey got the file, all right.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.122 --\u003e 00:18:45.625\r\nHow are these guys\r\ngetting in here?\r\n\r\n00:18:53.132 --\u003e 00:18:56.385\r\nDon't worry. I uploaded a\r\ndecoy file here last night.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.469 --\u003e 00:18:58.679\r\nThe real design specs\r\nfile is at my house.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.056 --\u003e 00:19:01.641\r\n- Randa.\r\n- Yes?\r\n\r\n00:19:01.932 --\u003e 00:19:04.685\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe information I need\r\nwas not in that file.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:04.769 --\u003e 00:19:05.936\r\nSearch the house.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.020 --\u003e 00:19:09.148\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy databanks of Rossum's memories\r\nindicate that Bruce Wayne\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:09.231 --\u003e 00:19:11.901\r\n\u003ci\u003ealways kept important\r\nbackups at home.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:11.984 --\u003e 00:19:13.277\r\nI'll do it right now.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.531 --\u003e 00:19:21.077\r\nI heard your voice, Ms. Duane,\r\nand thought Master Bruce had returned.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.160 --\u003e 00:19:23.120\r\nI thought you might\r\nenjoy a spot of tea.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.246 --\u003e 00:19:25.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:30.127 --\u003e 00:19:33.506\r\nI think it's time Ms.\r\nDuane answered some questions.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:39.679\r\n(RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:19:47.895 --\u003e 00:19:48.938\r\nSomething wrong?\r\n\r\n00:19:49.397 --\u003e 00:19:50.981\r\nNo answer at the house.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.065 --\u003e 00:19:52.191\r\nI better get back there.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.274 --\u003e 00:19:53.609\r\nSee you later, Lucius.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.269 --\u003e 00:20:30.563\r\nHARDAC,\r\nI've definitely found something.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.646 --\u003e 00:20:32.565\r\nBruce Wayne is Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.648 --\u003e 00:20:35.776\r\n\u003ci\u003eIntriguing.\r\nThis data may be useful later.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:35.860 --\u003e 00:20:38.070\r\n\u003ci\u003eThere must be a\r\ncentral computer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:38.154 --\u003e 00:20:40.114\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt will have the data I need.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:40.197 --\u003e 00:20:42.450\r\nI see it. Prepare for\r\ninterface in one minute.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.206 --\u003e 00:20:52.084\r\n\u003ci\u003eI will take it from here, Randa.\r\nYou come home.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:57.047 --\u003e 00:20:59.091\r\nAlfred? Randa?\r\n\r\n00:21:02.219 --\u003e 00:21:03.429\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:21:04.430 --\u003e 00:21:05.514\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:21:06.474 --\u003e 00:21:08.058\r\nMaster Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.142 --\u003e 00:21:10.936\r\nAlfred, what happened?\r\nWhere's Ms. Duane?\r\n\r\n00:21:11.353 --\u003e 00:21:13.272\r\nForgive me, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.355 --\u003e 00:21:16.650\r\nI can't imagine how would I...\r\nI must've dozed off.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.318 --\u003e 00:21:19.570\r\nI assume Ms. Duane has left.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.946 --\u003e 00:21:23.073\r\nI assume nothing at this point.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.749 --\u003e 00:21:33.959\r\nComputer, scan Batcave for-\r\n\r\n00:21:38.672 --\u003e 00:21:39.673\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:21:47.431 --\u003e 00:21:48.599\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:59.068 --\u003e 00:22:01.070\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:25.010 --\u003e 00:22:26.011\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E40 - Heart of Steel, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:17.601 --\u003e 00:00:19.436\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:05.357 --\u003e 00:01:06.900\r\nNARRATOR: Previously\r\non Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:07.526 --\u003e 00:01:10.779\r\nThis is my greatest achievement.\r\nMy prototype AI.\r\n\r\n00:01:11.613 --\u003e 00:01:12.906\r\nThis is HARDAC.\r\n\r\n00:01:15.909 --\u003e 00:01:19.371\r\nHolographic analytical\r\nreciprocating digital computer.\r\n\r\n00:01:20.163 --\u003e 00:01:21.206\r\n\u003ci\u003eHARD AC .\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:21.290 --\u003e 00:01:23.959\r\nSo tell me. What does HARDAC do?\r\n\r\n00:01:24.209 --\u003e 00:01:28.046\r\nNow, Bruce, I can't tell you\r\nall of my secrets, can I?\r\n\r\n00:01:28.338 --\u003e 00:01:30.924\r\nWell, since you won't tell me\r\nwhat you're working on, Karl,\r\n\r\n00:01:31.425 --\u003e 00:01:34.553\r\nmaybe I can charm the details\r\nout of your lovely assistant?\r\n\r\n00:01:35.762 --\u003e 00:01:37.681\r\nWell, you can try.\r\n\r\n00:01:38.181 --\u003e 00:01:42.436\r\n\u003ci\u003eSome people in high places are becoming\r\ntoo curious about this operation.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:42.603 --\u003e 00:01:43.913\r\n- (KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n- I'll get it, princess.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.937 --\u003e 00:01:45.147\r\nYou keep hitting those books.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.988 --\u003e 00:01:53.989\r\nWhat the devil?\r\n\r\n00:01:54.406 --\u003e 00:01:55.657\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:01:57.367 --\u003e 00:01:59.953\r\nWere you outside?\r\nYour hand is like ice.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.037 --\u003e 00:02:01.038\r\nI'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.331 --\u003e 00:02:04.708\r\n- Dad, are you sure you're-\r\n- I said I'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.635 --\u003e 00:02:18.138\r\nI heard your voice, Ms. Duane,\r\nand thought Master Bruce had returned.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.680 --\u003e 00:02:19.973\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:24.102 --\u003e 00:02:26.313\r\nHARDAC,\r\nI've definitely found something.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.396 --\u003e 00:02:28.273\r\nBruce Wayne is Batman.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.399 --\u003e 00:02:31.568\r\nComputer, scan Batcave for-\r\n\r\n00:02:32.819 --\u003e 00:02:33.945\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:02:34.446 --\u003e 00:02:35.739\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:53.965 --\u003e 00:02:55.884\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:03:08.980 --\u003e 00:03:10.190\r\nGood heavens!\r\n\r\n00:03:31.795 --\u003e 00:03:35.382\r\nI do wish your toys wouldn't\r\nplay so roughly with you, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.467 --\u003e 00:03:39.970\r\nThere's another computer\r\nuplinked to this one.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.053 --\u003e 00:03:41.680\r\nI'm tracing the link now.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.310 --\u003e 00:03:48.645\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:57.237 --\u003e 00:03:58.321\r\nI've lost it.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.864 --\u003e 00:04:00.907\r\nThe link was shut\r\ndown at the source.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.991 --\u003e 00:04:02.743\r\nCould Randa Duane\r\nhave been down here?\r\n\r\n00:04:02.826 --\u003e 00:04:04.369\r\nI should hope not.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.162 --\u003e 00:04:06.788\r\nBut I can't say for\r\ncertain, sir.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.872 --\u003e 00:04:10.417\r\nI... I simply can't remember\r\nanything beyond the time you left.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.959 --\u003e 00:04:12.461\r\nIt's all right, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.544 --\u003e 00:04:13.704\r\nWe'd better search the house.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.463 --\u003e 00:04:16.173\r\nSearch for what, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:04:16.256 --\u003e 00:04:19.301\r\nAnything unusual.\r\nShe may have left a clue I can use.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.302 --\u003e 00:04:21.386\r\nShe's only human.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.056 --\u003e 00:04:27.184\r\nGORDON: Yes, I understand.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.267 --\u003e 00:04:30.187\r\nThat's no problem.\r\nThe Gotham Club would be ideal.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.270 --\u003e 00:04:32.063\r\nI'll take care of Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.107 --\u003e 00:04:35.525\r\nDad, who are you talking to?\r\n\r\n00:04:35.609 --\u003e 00:04:36.777\r\nLeave me alone.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.068 --\u003e 00:04:38.361\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:45.994 --\u003e 00:04:47.454\r\nYou wanted me, commissioner?\r\n\r\n00:04:48.038 --\u003e 00:04:51.291\r\nGORDON: Go to Cybertron and see Randa\r\nDuane. She has something for you.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.000 --\u003e 00:04:54.044\r\nBut I already took a statement\r\nfrom that Rossum guy.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.127 --\u003e 00:04:55.128\r\nThey ain't involved.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.212 --\u003e 00:04:57.005\r\nDo it, lieutenant.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.088 --\u003e 00:05:00.675\r\nTalk to this guy, talk to that guy.\r\nI'm getting a sore throat.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.093 --\u003e 00:05:03.173\r\nGORDON: Get me Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.221 --\u003e 00:05:05.430\r\nGordon here.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.514 --\u003e 00:05:08.225\r\nWe know who stole your computer\r\ndata, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.308 --\u003e 00:05:10.560\r\nMeet me at the Gotham\r\nClub in one hour.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.644 --\u003e 00:05:13.313\r\nI will, commissioner.\r\nAnd thanks for-\r\n\r\n00:05:25.325 --\u003e 00:05:29.412\r\nThe duplicant processor's been used.\r\nI didn't authorize that.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.496 --\u003e 00:05:32.582\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt was necessary to serve\r\nyour ultimate purpose.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:32.666 --\u003e 00:05:35.085\r\nNo, it was a stupid idea.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.168 --\u003e 00:05:37.170\r\nThe babblings of a broken heart.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.546 --\u003e 00:05:39.756\r\n\u003ci\u003eHumans make errors in judgment.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:39.840 --\u003e 00:05:44.052\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt is sometimes necessary to protect\r\nthem from their own inadequacies.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:46.096 --\u003e 00:05:47.973\r\nI've let this go too far.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.056 --\u003e 00:05:49.808\r\nI gave you too much free will.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.934 --\u003e 00:05:52.602\r\nIt's time to change\r\nyour programming.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.906 --\u003e 00:06:05.907\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:10.453 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:06:12.330 --\u003e 00:06:14.082\r\nYou have immobilized the maker.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.250 --\u003e 00:06:18.295\r\n\u003ci\u003eHis human imperfection\r\nendangers the plan.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:18.378 --\u003e 00:06:20.672\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe must be improved upon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:40.901 --\u003e 00:06:42.068\r\n(YAWNING)\r\n\r\n00:06:42.193 --\u003e 00:06:43.486\r\n- (KNOCK ON DOOR)\r\n- It's open.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.868 --\u003e 00:06:51.077\r\nWhat on earth?\r\n\r\n00:07:21.775 --\u003e 00:07:25.612\r\n- Commissioner?\r\n- No, Batman. I called you.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.072 --\u003e 00:07:29.324\r\nI expected your father, Ms.\r\nGordon.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.407 --\u003e 00:07:30.992\r\nThat's why I called you.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.451 --\u003e 00:07:33.495\r\nThat man is not my father.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.578 --\u003e 00:07:35.914\r\nWhat do you mean\r\nhe's not your father?\r\n\r\n00:07:35.997 --\u003e 00:07:37.874\r\nJust what I said.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.958 --\u003e 00:07:40.085\r\nSomeone is impersonating\r\nmy father.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.168 --\u003e 00:07:41.419\r\nWhat makes you think so?\r\n\r\n00:07:41.503 --\u003e 00:07:44.798\r\nWell, he doesn't have bolts in\r\nhis neck or anything that obvious.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.881 --\u003e 00:07:47.342\r\nHe's so cold to me.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.425 --\u003e 00:07:50.971\r\nBut, it's not just that.\r\nI can't put my finger on it.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.054 --\u003e 00:07:53.014\r\nBut I know, he's not my father.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.098 --\u003e 00:07:55.392\r\nI know I sound\r\ncrazy, but I'm not.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.017 --\u003e 00:07:59.229\r\nWhoever's downstairs now,\r\nit looks like Jim Gordon,\r\n\r\n00:07:59.312 --\u003e 00:08:02.065\r\ntalks like him,\r\nbut it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.732 --\u003e 00:08:04.818\r\nPlease help me, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.276 --\u003e 00:08:07.779\r\n- I'll do what I can.\r\n- Thank you.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.279 --\u003e 00:08:09.739\r\nGetting a little fresh air?\r\n\r\n00:08:14.035 --\u003e 00:08:16.913\r\nHow come I wasn't invited\r\nto this little get-together?\r\n\r\n00:08:25.046 --\u003e 00:08:28.216\r\nIt's suddenly less pleasant up here.\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.469 --\u003e 00:08:33.013\r\nNot so fast, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.311 --\u003e 00:08:41.479\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.036 --\u003e 00:08:57.203\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:59.456 --\u003e 00:09:00.790\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:09:18.266 --\u003e 00:09:19.392\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.153 --\u003e 00:09:31.613\r\n(ELECTRICAL BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:09:56.763 --\u003e 00:09:58.014\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:06.731 --\u003e 00:10:07.732\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:12.320 --\u003e 00:10:15.073\r\n- A robot?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:10:15.156 --\u003e 00:10:17.742\r\nMore advanced than\r\nanything I've ever seen.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.826 --\u003e 00:10:21.454\r\n- Does that mean my father...\r\n- I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.913 --\u003e 00:10:22.914\r\nI'll find out tonight.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.665 --\u003e 00:10:26.334\r\nDon't go home.\r\nStay at a friend's house.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.417 --\u003e 00:10:29.420\r\nNot so fast.\r\nHow are you going to find out?\r\n\r\n00:10:29.504 --\u003e 00:10:32.090\r\n- I wanna be there.\r\n- That's not possible.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.173 --\u003e 00:10:34.300\r\nI'll contact you as soon\r\nas I know something.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.093 --\u003e 00:10:36.511\r\nPlease let go of my cape.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.555 --\u003e 00:10:39.597\r\nBatman, I...\r\n\r\n00:10:54.904 --\u003e 00:10:57.532\r\nGood evening, Bruce.\r\nI'm glad you could come.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.616 --\u003e 00:10:59.784\r\nNice to see you, mayor.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.201 --\u003e 00:11:03.079\r\n- Is Commissioner Gordon here?\r\n- He'll be along.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.163 --\u003e 00:11:04.497\r\nHe won't wanna miss this.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.583 --\u003e 00:11:11.337\r\nYou're going to become a member\r\nof a very exclusive club tonight.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.421 --\u003e 00:11:14.299\r\nI thought I already belonged to\r\nevery exclusive club in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.382 --\u003e 00:11:17.927\r\nNo, my boy.\r\nThis club is brand new.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.511 --\u003e 00:11:21.639\r\nThough everyone will\r\nbelong very soon.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.320 --\u003e 00:11:36.487\r\nHuh? (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:45.538 --\u003e 00:11:49.209\r\nRanda? Is this what I get for\r\nleaving in the middle of dinner?\r\n\r\n00:11:49.834 --\u003e 00:11:52.503\r\nYou know what they say about\r\na woman scorned, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.764 --\u003e 00:12:03.890\r\nDon't let him get away.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.247 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:12:46.933 --\u003e 00:12:48.101\r\n(ELECTRICAL CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:16.587 --\u003e 00:13:17.922\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:13:29.976 --\u003e 00:13:31.736\r\nBARBARA: \"Wait at a\r\nfriend's house,\" he says.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.312 --\u003e 00:13:33.688\r\nNot likely, Wubby.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.771 --\u003e 00:13:36.190\r\nBullock went to Cybertron\r\nand a robot came back.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.607 --\u003e 00:13:38.067\r\nWanna bet Dad's there too?\r\n\r\n00:15:09.450 --\u003e 00:15:10.743\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:25.925 --\u003e 00:15:29.387\r\nMiss Gordon, your skill at breaking\r\nand entering is impressive.\r\n\r\n00:15:29.512 --\u003e 00:15:30.739\r\nWhere did you\r\nlearn those tricks?\r\n\r\n00:15:30.763 --\u003e 00:15:34.267\r\nA police commissioner's daughter\r\ndoesn't get all her education in school.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.392 --\u003e 00:15:36.227\r\nWhat have you done\r\nwith my father?\r\n\r\n00:15:36.310 --\u003e 00:15:37.812\r\nHe's right here, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.895 --\u003e 00:15:41.023\r\nYou'll be joining him soon.\r\nVery soon.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.044 --\u003e 00:16:44.253\r\n(GLASS SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.594 --\u003e 00:16:53.471\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.013 --\u003e 00:16:56.849\r\nEnough. It's over, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.433 --\u003e 00:17:00.228\r\n\u003ci\u003ePeople are imperfect.\r\nThey make mistakes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:02.271 --\u003e 00:17:04.941\r\n\u003ci\u003eYour mistake was coming here\r\nto interfere with the plan.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:06.943 --\u003e 00:17:08.319\r\nWhat is this plan?\r\n\r\n00:17:08.402 --\u003e 00:17:13.658\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe plan was conceived by Karl Rossum\r\nwhen his young daughter was deactivated.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:13.741 --\u003e 00:17:16.160\r\nDeactivated? You mean-\r\n\r\n00:17:16.244 --\u003e 00:17:17.995\r\n\u003ci\u003eA vehicular accident.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:20.164 --\u003e 00:17:24.418\r\n\u003ci\u003eOur maker felt the emotion called\r\nlove in great quantity for her.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:24.961 --\u003e 00:17:28.047\r\n\u003ci\u003eAfterwards, he decided to\r\nfind a way to replace humans,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:28.130 --\u003e 00:17:30.424\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhose decisions can\r\ncost other human lives.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:30.925 --\u003e 00:17:34.053\r\n- But we're all capable of human error.\r\n- Precisely.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.136 --\u003e 00:17:37.348\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe maker's concept was sound,\r\nbut he did not go far enough.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:37.431 --\u003e 00:17:38.849\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhich is why I have taken over.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:39.267 --\u003e 00:17:41.435\r\n- Does that mean my father's-\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.519 --\u003e 00:17:43.980\r\nThere is still much\r\nto learn from humans.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.063 --\u003e 00:17:46.524\r\nI will keep them alive\r\nuntil I have learned enough.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.859 --\u003e 00:17:49.944\r\nDad!\r\n\r\n00:18:18.723 --\u003e 00:18:20.308\r\n(DISTORTED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.697 --\u003e 00:18:35.990\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:46.709 --\u003e 00:18:48.210\r\nWhat a headache.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.794 --\u003e 00:18:51.464\r\nBarbara?\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:18:51.547 --\u003e 00:18:54.050\r\nRescuing you, silly. Come on.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.553 --\u003e 00:19:00.931\r\n\u003ci\u003eEmergency. Emergency.\r\nStop the one called Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:02.058 --\u003e 00:19:03.392\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:11.150 --\u003e 00:19:12.526\r\nResistance is useless.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.610 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n\u003ci\u003eI control every means of\r\nescape from this building.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:17.114 --\u003e 00:19:18.532\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:19:20.618 --\u003e 00:19:21.619\r\nDad!\r\n\r\n00:19:34.173 --\u003e 00:19:35.174\r\nIs there another way out?\r\n\r\n00:19:36.926 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\nMy office has a private elevator on\r\na separate power source. This way.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.776 --\u003e 00:19:54.944\r\nGet my father out of here.\r\n\r\n00:19:56.737 --\u003e 00:19:58.989\r\n- What about you?\r\n- I'm gonna help Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.410 --\u003e 00:20:03.703\r\n(BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:17.174 --\u003e 00:20:18.467\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.314 --\u003e 00:20:33.357\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.697 --\u003e 00:20:41.073\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:48.706 --\u003e 00:20:50.291\r\nBarbara. Where's Barbara?\r\n\r\n00:20:51.959 --\u003e 00:20:53.586\r\n\u003ci\u003eCore systems damaged.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:53.669 --\u003e 00:20:55.588\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe plan has failed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:07.433 --\u003e 00:21:08.559\r\nBarbara!\r\n\r\n00:21:09.727 --\u003e 00:21:10.728\r\nOver there.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.147 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nBarbara. Thank God.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.784 --\u003e 00:21:27.578\r\nI had no idea HARDAC\r\nhad gone this far.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.661 --\u003e 00:21:30.748\r\nI'm sure the investigation\r\nwill prove exactly that.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.832 --\u003e 00:21:35.377\r\n- You did well. Thanks.\r\n- Anytime.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.461 --\u003e 00:21:37.797\r\nI'm getting too old\r\nfor this kind of stuff.\r\n\r\n00:21:37.880 --\u003e 00:21:39.465\r\nI sort of enjoyed it.\r\n\r\n00:21:41.967 --\u003e 00:21:43.886\r\nCome on, sweetie. Let's go home.\r\n\r\n00:21:54.104 --\u003e 00:21:56.106\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.464 --\u003e 00:22:21.465\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E41 - If You're So Smart, Why Aren't You Rich (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.586 --\u003e 00:00:04.588\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:19.788 --\u003e 00:01:22.541\r\n\u003ci\u003e- MOCKRIDGE: Miss Welbeck.\r\n- Yes, Mr. Mockridge?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:22.624 --\u003e 00:01:24.501\r\n\u003ci\u003eMOCKRDGE: Has Edward\r\nNygma come in yet?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:24.585 --\u003e 00:01:25.836\r\nWELBECK: \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e don't \u003ci\u003ethink\u003c/i\u003e so.\r\n\r\n00:01:26.253 --\u003e 00:01:29.339\r\n\u003ci\u003eMOCKNDGE: Good. If you need me,\r\nI'll be down on the eighth floor.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:12.924 --\u003e 00:02:13.925\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:16.678 --\u003e 00:02:18.013\r\nWhat's going on here?\r\n\r\n00:02:23.935 --\u003e 00:02:26.688\r\nWhere's my office?\r\nMy door was right here.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.772 --\u003e 00:02:28.148\r\n\"Was\" is right.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.943 --\u003e 00:02:33.570\r\nWhat's the meaning of this?\r\n\r\n00:02:33.654 --\u003e 00:02:35.254\r\nMOCKRIDGE: What does it look\r\nlike, Eddie?\r\n\r\n00:02:37.157 --\u003e 00:02:40.619\r\nYou're out of here. You're history.\r\nYou're fired. Comprende?\r\n\r\n00:02:40.827 --\u003e 00:02:43.580\r\nHave you lost what\r\npasses for your mind?\r\n\r\n00:02:43.664 --\u003e 00:02:45.874\r\nYou can't afford to do without\r\nme, Mockridge.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.957 --\u003e 00:02:48.377\r\nI can if you're gonna\r\nsue me for royalties.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.460 --\u003e 00:02:51.588\r\nI created the Riddle\r\nof the Minotaur game.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.672 --\u003e 00:02:54.257\r\nThis company is making\r\nmillions from my genius.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.008 --\u003e 00:02:58.136\r\nCompetitron Software's success\r\ndidn't come from the product, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.220 --\u003e 00:03:00.138\r\nCompetitron has a\r\ncorporate attitude.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.222 --\u003e 00:03:03.308\r\nIts strength is in the boardroom,\r\nthe deal, the contract.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.809 --\u003e 00:03:06.687\r\nSpecifically the work-for-hire\r\ncontract you signed.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.732 --\u003e 00:03:13.902\r\nYou are a fool, Mockridge,\r\nto think you can get away with this.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.985 --\u003e 00:03:18.073\r\nYour amoral greed is no match\r\nfor an intellect like mine.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.156 --\u003e 00:03:20.742\r\nOh, yeah?\r\nThen tell me something, Eddie.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.826 --\u003e 00:03:23.954\r\nIf you're so smart,\r\nwhy aren't you rich?\r\n\r\n00:03:27.416 --\u003e 00:03:29.084\r\nSo I've made sure\r\nthat Competitron\r\n\r\n00:03:29.167 --\u003e 00:03:31.837\r\nowns all rights to Riddle of\r\nthe Minotaur free and clear.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.546 --\u003e 00:03:35.006\r\nConsidering all the\r\nlicensing and merchandising,\r\n\r\n00:03:35.090 --\u003e 00:03:38.176\r\nwell heck, we just built a Minotaur\r\namusement park outside this city.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.260 --\u003e 00:03:40.762\r\nAnd if we'd had to pay royalties\r\non all that to the creator-\r\n\r\n00:03:40.846 --\u003e 00:03:42.514\r\nYou can stop\r\npitching, Mockridge.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.597 --\u003e 00:03:45.517\r\nI want this deal so I can\r\nmove Competitron to Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.101 --\u003e 00:03:48.270\r\nThis city desperately needs\r\nthe jobs it'll create.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:49.354\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:53.108 --\u003e 00:03:54.693\r\nWhat's he trying to...\r\n\r\n00:03:56.695 --\u003e 00:04:02.784\r\nBRUCE: What did you say?\r\nMockridge, are you okay? Mockridge!\r\n\r\n00:04:07.748 --\u003e 00:04:11.293\r\nWe'll have to wrap this up later, guys.\r\nSomething's come up.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.087 --\u003e 00:04:15.088\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.675 --\u003e 00:04:21.887\r\nWell, whatever that meant,\r\nit sure rattled his cage.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.970 --\u003e 00:04:28.143\r\nBRUCE: \"Why do multi-million dollar\r\ndeals break down in the wasteland?\"\r\n\r\n00:04:38.320 --\u003e 00:04:40.155\r\nIt has to have a double meaning.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.238 --\u003e 00:04:43.408\r\nMaster Dick,\r\nthat must be quite a computer game\r\n\r\n00:04:43.492 --\u003e 00:04:45.994\r\nto be worth tying up a\r\n$50 million computer.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.077 --\u003e 00:04:50.332\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot\u003c/i\u003e a game, \u003ci\u003eAlfred, the game.\r\nRiddle of the Minotaur.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:50.415 --\u003e 00:04:51.917\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n- It's really cool, look.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.000 --\u003e 00:04:54.628\r\nNot only do you have to\r\navoid all these traps,\r\n\r\n00:04:57.756 --\u003e 00:04:59.716\r\nbut you've gotta solve\r\nall these riddles.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.800 --\u003e 00:05:03.261\r\n(DICK READING)\r\n\r\n00:05:05.347 --\u003e 00:05:07.390\r\nWell, a straight line.\r\nWhat else?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.478 --\u003e 00:05:13.188\r\nBegging your pardon, young sir,\r\n\r\n00:05:13.271 --\u003e 00:05:17.567\r\nbut mightn't the answer on\r\na globe be a curved line?\r\n\r\n00:05:19.194 --\u003e 00:05:21.613\r\nBATMAN: Wasteland, wasteland.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.155 --\u003e 00:05:23.156\r\n\u003ci\u003e(HERON. MUSE'. PLNHNG)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:25.450 --\u003e 00:05:29.955\r\n- My word.\r\n- Oh, that. That's the Hand of Fate.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.038 --\u003e 00:05:31.665\r\nWhen you make a\r\nmistake, it picks you up\r\n\r\n00:05:31.748 --\u003e 00:05:33.416\r\nand takes you to another\r\npart of the maze.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.168 --\u003e 00:05:38.547\r\nDoesn't Mockridge own a club\r\ndowntown called The Wasteland?\r\n\r\n00:05:39.256 --\u003e 00:05:42.050\r\nThe Wasteland! (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:42.133 --\u003e 00:05:43.134\r\nRight.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.218 --\u003e 00:05:46.221\r\n- The Wasteland.\r\n- I mean in the game.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.304 --\u003e 00:05:47.597\r\nIt's a dead end, see?\r\n\r\n00:05:48.390 --\u003e 00:05:49.391\r\nBATMAN: Come on.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.474 --\u003e 00:05:51.768\r\nDaniel Mockridge is\r\nwalking into a trap.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.035 --\u003e 00:06:10.036\r\nMOCKRIDGE: Nygma?\r\n\r\n00:06:13.039 --\u003e 00:06:14.082\r\nNYQma.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.165 --\u003e 00:06:17.586\r\nRIDDLER: Decode that message\r\nall by yourself, Mockridge,\r\n\r\n00:06:18.253 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nor did you have help?\r\n\r\n00:06:19.921 --\u003e 00:06:22.674\r\nYou're trespassing, Nygma.\r\nGet out.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.757 --\u003e 00:06:24.009\r\nYou can't kill this deal.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.092 --\u003e 00:06:25.176\r\nI'm selling out to Wayne,\r\n\r\n00:06:25.260 --\u003e 00:06:27.095\r\nand there's nothing\r\nyou can do to stop me.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.178 --\u003e 00:06:29.931\r\nOf course there isn't.\r\nYou don't understand.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.015 --\u003e 00:06:32.225\r\nI have a proposition for you.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.309 --\u003e 00:06:34.227\r\nYou've come up with a new game?\r\n\r\n00:06:34.311 --\u003e 00:06:38.940\r\nThis? No, this puzzle is\r\nfar more than any mere game.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.024 --\u003e 00:06:42.652\r\nWouldn't you agree?\r\nOr do you need to try it yourself?\r\n\r\n00:06:42.736 --\u003e 00:06:45.488\r\nSolve it. Then we'll talk.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.572 --\u003e 00:06:47.699\r\nOh, for crying out loud.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.284 --\u003e 00:06:50.285\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:59.377 --\u003e 00:07:01.922\r\nWhat is this,\r\nsome kind of extortion scheme?\r\n\r\n00:07:02.005 --\u003e 00:07:04.341\r\nYou think I want money?\r\n\r\n00:07:04.424 --\u003e 00:07:08.970\r\nNot anymore.\r\nWhat I want now is you.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.432 --\u003e 00:07:13.433\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:20.899 --\u003e 00:07:21.900\r\nEmpty-\r\n\r\n00:07:27.030 --\u003e 00:07:29.866\r\nRIDDLER: Well, well.\r\n\"Bat\" something-or-other, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:07:29.950 --\u003e 00:07:31.618\r\nWho invited you?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.536 --\u003e 00:07:35.705\r\nYou know what happens\r\nto gatecrashers?\r\n\r\n00:07:37.916 --\u003e 00:07:39.668\r\nThey have to match wits with...\r\n\r\n00:07:40.335 --\u003e 00:07:41.711\r\nThe Riddler.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.220 --\u003e 00:07:51.221\r\nThe Riddler?\r\n\r\n00:07:52.347 --\u003e 00:07:55.558\r\nWhat is that, Nygma,\r\nsome kind of joke on your name?\r\n\r\n00:07:55.642 --\u003e 00:07:56.685\r\nNYQma?\r\n\r\n00:07:56.768 --\u003e 00:08:00.230\r\nMy, my.\r\nCan we actually have a brain\r\n\r\n00:08:00.313 --\u003e 00:08:02.482\r\nbeneath that pointy\r\ncowl of ours?\r\n\r\n00:08:03.316 --\u003e 00:08:06.361\r\nSo tell me,\r\nhave you brawn to match?\r\n\r\n00:08:06.820 --\u003e 00:08:07.821\r\n(SNAPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:11.574 --\u003e 00:08:12.867\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:26.339 --\u003e 00:08:27.340\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:39.310 --\u003e 00:08:40.311\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:46.693 --\u003e 00:08:48.153\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:08:53.408 --\u003e 00:08:54.409\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:09:02.917 --\u003e 00:09:03.918\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.759 --\u003e 00:09:13.595\r\nI love that trick,\r\nbut I can never make it work.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.860 --\u003e 00:09:32.822\r\nLet's consider you handled for\r\nnow, shall we?\r\n\r\n00:09:33.823 --\u003e 00:09:34.824\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:41.539 --\u003e 00:09:43.541\r\nROBIN: Coming through!\r\n\r\n00:09:55.637 --\u003e 00:09:57.430\r\nWell done, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.514 --\u003e 00:10:01.518\r\nBut have you wits enough to save\r\ntwo people at the same time?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.187 --\u003e 00:10:05.188\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:10:05.522 --\u003e 00:10:08.900\r\nIt's my own variation on\r\nthe Chinese finger puzzle.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.734 --\u003e 00:10:11.170\r\nMOCKRIDGE: Batman,\r\nyou gotta help me.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.194 --\u003e 00:10:12.946\r\nI can pay you, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:10:13.029 --\u003e 00:10:14.322\r\nAnything YOU want!\r\n\r\n00:10:15.240 --\u003e 00:10:17.158\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.081\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:28.628 --\u003e 00:10:31.256\r\nROBIN: Hey,\r\nit's getting hot in here.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.339 --\u003e 00:10:33.299\r\nGet me out of this thing!\r\n\r\n00:10:35.426 --\u003e 00:10:37.679\r\nWhat did you mean,\r\na joke on his name?\r\n\r\n00:10:37.762 --\u003e 00:10:39.222\r\nYou know who he is?\r\n\r\n00:10:39.305 --\u003e 00:10:41.307\r\nI figured the creator\r\nof the Minotaur game\r\n\r\n00:10:41.391 --\u003e 00:10:44.060\r\nwas behind this the minute\r\nI saw that billboard.\r\n\r\n00:10:44.144 --\u003e 00:10:46.896\r\nI read all about him in the\r\ncompany records I examined.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.980 --\u003e 00:10:51.151\r\nHis name's Nygma, Edward Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.234 --\u003e 00:10:53.695\r\nI get it. E. Nygma,\r\n\r\n00:10:53.778 --\u003e 00:10:56.698\r\nMeaning a puzzle or riddle.\r\nAn enigma.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.781 --\u003e 00:10:58.867\r\nAt least we know who\r\nwe're looking for.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.702 --\u003e 00:11:02.036\r\nHey, Bruce, look.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.287 --\u003e 00:11:03.580\r\n(CARS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.872 --\u003e 00:11:04.873\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:11:11.379 --\u003e 00:11:12.380\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:20.221 --\u003e 00:11:22.724\r\nROBIN: The lights.\r\nWhy are they all flashing?\r\n\r\n00:11:22.807 --\u003e 00:11:24.309\r\nBATMAN: It's Morse code.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.868 --\u003e 00:11:43.745\r\nThat should get their attention.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.248 --\u003e 00:11:49.667\r\nBut why?\r\nYou got the guy you wanted.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.255 --\u003e 00:11:55.840\r\nBatman knows who I am.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.507 --\u003e 00:11:58.968\r\nWe'll have to put him\r\nand his snot-nosed cohort\r\n\r\n00:11:59.052 --\u003e 00:12:00.303\r\nout of the way first.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.804 --\u003e 00:12:02.805\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.807 --\u003e 00:12:05.850\r\nWhat did it say?\r\n\r\n00:12:05.934 --\u003e 00:12:09.812\r\n\"When is the Minotaur's owner\r\nas high as an elephant's eye?\"\r\n\r\n00:12:12.315 --\u003e 00:12:13.316\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.068 --\u003e 00:12:19.405\r\nWell, Mockridge owns the Minotaur,\r\nbut what's as high as an elephant's eye?\r\n\r\n00:12:19.489 --\u003e 00:12:20.698\r\nCorn.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.079 --\u003e 00:12:27.705\r\n- Corn?\r\n- (TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.789 --\u003e 00:12:30.708\r\nBATMAN: It's from an old song\r\nlyric, before your time.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.792 --\u003e 00:12:33.920\r\nSo, what's he saying?\r\n\"When Mockridge is corny\"?\r\n\r\n00:12:34.003 --\u003e 00:12:36.130\r\n\"When Mockridge is in the corn\"?\r\n\r\n00:12:36.798 --\u003e 00:12:39.092\r\nWhat's another word\r\nmeaning \"corn\"?\r\n\r\n00:12:39.884 --\u003e 00:12:43.054\r\n- Uh... Kernel? Cob?\r\n- Maize!\r\n\r\n00:12:43.137 --\u003e 00:12:45.348\r\n\"When Mockridge\r\nis in the maize.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:45.431 --\u003e 00:12:47.475\r\n\u003ci\u003eROBIN: The maze at\r\nthe amusement park.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:47.558 --\u003e 00:12:48.768\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: Exactly.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:55.525 --\u003e 00:12:56.776\r\nBATMAN: Where's Mockridge?\r\n\r\n00:12:56.859 --\u003e 00:13:00.697\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn the center of the maze,\r\nalong with the Minotaur robot.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:01.864 --\u003e 00:13:06.119\r\n\u003ci\u003eI've programmed it to destroy\r\nhim at exactly 4:30 a.m.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:07.704 --\u003e 00:13:11.916\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhich gives you less than 10 minutes\r\nto run the maze and find him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:12.000 --\u003e 00:13:15.211\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut first,\r\nthrow down your utility belts.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:15.295 --\u003e 00:13:18.798\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt'll be more interesting that\r\nway, don't you think?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:19.882 --\u003e 00:13:21.759\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow you may enter.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:32.145 --\u003e 00:13:33.646\r\nRIDDLER: Oh! And by the way,\r\n\r\n00:13:33.730 --\u003e 00:13:36.941\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou'll have to answer the\r\nRiddle of the Minotaur too.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:37.025 --\u003e 00:13:38.609\r\nBATMAN: I can't wait.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.319 --\u003e 00:13:41.612\r\nHow far did you say\r\nyou got in the game?\r\n\r\n00:13:41.696 --\u003e 00:13:43.740\r\nROBIN: I'm not sure.\r\nMaybe halfway.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.823 --\u003e 00:13:45.491\r\nBATMAN: Already I love this.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.163 --\u003e 00:13:52.999\r\n- Now where to?\r\n- I'm thinking. I'm thinking.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.960 --\u003e 00:13:57.712\r\nBATMAN: Could you\r\ndo it more quickly?\r\n\r\n00:13:58.796 --\u003e 00:14:02.175\r\nOh, the Griffin. Well, that just blocks\r\noff the way you came, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.929 --\u003e 00:14:10.058\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: Except I've added\r\nan improvement of my own.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:27.867 --\u003e 00:14:29.869\r\n\"Losers ahead\"?\r\n\r\n00:14:29.952 --\u003e 00:14:31.162\r\nDuck!\r\n\r\n00:14:33.206 --\u003e 00:14:34.832\r\nLoses a head.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.916 --\u003e 00:14:38.002\r\nI don't know what's worse,\r\nthe traps or the puns.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.217 --\u003e 00:14:46.594\r\nI guess this isn't a\r\ngood time to tell you.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.677 --\u003e 00:14:48.596\r\nNobody's ever made it to\r\nthe center of the maze.\r\n\r\n00:15:12.036 --\u003e 00:15:15.498\r\nI'll find Mockridge if I have\r\nto tear this place apart, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.581 --\u003e 00:15:17.291\r\nRIDDLER: Idoubt \u003ci\u003eit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:17.375 --\u003e 00:15:19.752\r\n\u003ci\u003eI made sure the perils\r\nare quite lethal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:19.836 --\u003e 00:15:22.839\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou have eight\r\nminutes, gentlemen.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:22.922 --\u003e 00:15:26.384\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen Mockridge becomes the\r\nonly good corporate shark.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:26.467 --\u003e 00:15:27.802\r\n\u003ci\u003eA dead one.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:31.889 --\u003e 00:15:33.141\r\nROBIN: Great.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.224 --\u003e 00:15:35.351\r\nYou don't happen to know\r\nArabic, do you?\r\n\r\n00:15:35.435 --\u003e 00:15:38.521\r\nNo, but I can translate it.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.649 --\u003e 00:15:43.443\r\n(BATMAN READING)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.568 --\u003e 00:15:45.194\r\nOh, terrific.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.319 --\u003e 00:15:47.071\r\nLet's just pick one and move!\r\n\r\n00:15:49.740 --\u003e 00:15:50.908\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:50.992 --\u003e 00:15:54.370\r\nWe're going the wrong way!\r\n'Cause here comes the Hand of Fate!\r\n\r\n00:16:04.422 --\u003e 00:16:06.674\r\nBATMAN: Of course!\r\nWe went to the left,\r\n\r\n00:16:06.757 --\u003e 00:16:09.719\r\nbut in the Arab world,\r\nyou always eat with your right hand.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.598 --\u003e 00:16:15.349\r\nWe've gotta use\r\none of these keys.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.433 --\u003e 00:16:17.226\r\nYes, but which one?\r\n\r\n00:16:17.310 --\u003e 00:16:20.396\r\nAnd why are they labeled\r\nA, C and D?\r\n\r\n00:16:20.480 --\u003e 00:16:21.731\r\nDon't look at me.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.814 --\u003e 00:16:23.399\r\nBATMAN: Let's try D.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.030 --\u003e 00:16:30.114\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:16:33.034 --\u003e 00:16:34.035\r\nTry another one.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.118 --\u003e 00:16:35.119\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.578 --\u003e 00:16:36.746\r\nA this time.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.246 --\u003e 00:16:38.331\r\nROBIN: No, wait!\r\n\r\n00:16:39.457 --\u003e 00:16:41.876\r\nTurn that key and\r\nthere'll be three blades.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.959 --\u003e 00:16:44.504\r\n- But how do you- - It's the C key.\r\nTrust me.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.305 --\u003e 00:16:55.640\r\nIt's a musical puzzle.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.723 --\u003e 00:16:57.475\r\nThey key of D has two sharps.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.558 --\u003e 00:16:59.101\r\nThe key of A has three.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.185 --\u003e 00:17:01.854\r\nBut the key of C has no sharps.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.189 --\u003e 00:17:04.232\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:17.411 --\u003e 00:17:20.289\r\nROBIN: The shortest distance\r\nbetween two points on a globe.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.373 --\u003e 00:17:21.874\r\nThat one I remember.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.958 --\u003e 00:17:24.126\r\nRIDDLER: One minute, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.212 --\u003e 00:17:27.380\r\nStay here.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.463 --\u003e 00:17:29.215\r\n- But that's the wrong door.\r\n- I know.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.298 --\u003e 00:17:31.551\r\n- But the Hand!\r\n- That's what I want.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.230 --\u003e 00:17:45.231\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:50.736 --\u003e 00:17:53.823\r\nBatman! Batman, where are you?\r\n\r\n00:17:53.906 --\u003e 00:17:57.702\r\n\u003ci\u003eForget it, kid.\r\nI handed him his walking papers.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:00.413 --\u003e 00:18:01.455\r\nGet on.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.000 --\u003e 00:18:06.877\r\nJust one question. How?\r\n\r\n00:18:06.961 --\u003e 00:18:09.046\r\nI linked it to my\r\npalmtop computer.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.130 --\u003e 00:18:12.675\r\n\u003ci\u003eRWJDLER: That is grand-scale\r\ncheating, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:12.758 --\u003e 00:18:15.720\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou're not allowed to tamper\r\nwith the Hand of Fate.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:18.180\r\nI don't believe in fate.\r\n\r\n00:18:18.264 --\u003e 00:18:21.142\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou probably don't believe\r\nin minotaurs either.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:21.267 --\u003e 00:18:23.144\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut you'll still have\r\nto answer the riddle.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:24.103 --\u003e 00:18:28.232\r\n\u003ci\u003eMINOTAUR: I have billions of\r\neyes, yet I live in darkness.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:29.150 --\u003e 00:18:31.068\r\n\u003ci\u003eI have millions of ears,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:31.736 --\u003e 00:18:33.321\r\n\u003ci\u003eyet only four lobes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:33.946 --\u003e 00:18:38.409\r\n\u003ci\u003eI have no muscle,\r\nyet I rule two hemispheres.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:39.201 --\u003e 00:18:40.745\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat am I?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:42.079 --\u003e 00:18:43.581\r\nThat's simple. The human brain.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.915 --\u003e 00:18:45.916\r\n(POWERING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:18:46.959 --\u003e 00:18:48.753\r\nIt has billions of optic\r\nand auditory nerves\r\n\r\n00:18:48.836 --\u003e 00:18:50.755\r\nfour lobes and two hemispheres.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.838 --\u003e 00:18:54.342\r\nAnd it's the only thing\r\nEdward Nygma respects.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.425 --\u003e 00:18:57.219\r\n\u003ci\u003eA lucky guess, that's all.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:57.303 --\u003e 00:18:59.513\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut it won't save you, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:59.597 --\u003e 00:19:01.098\r\n\u003ci\u003eDestroy them!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:14.987 --\u003e 00:19:15.988\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:22.370 --\u003e 00:19:24.330\r\nI solved your riddle, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.413 --\u003e 00:19:25.748\r\nNow here's one for you.\r\n\r\n00:19:25.831 --\u003e 00:19:29.335\r\nHow do you take out a\r\nminotaur with a single blow?\r\n\r\n00:19:30.294 --\u003e 00:19:31.337\r\nLike this!\r\n\r\n00:19:51.357 --\u003e 00:19:52.775\r\nYou're through, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.858 --\u003e 00:19:55.736\r\n\u003ci\u003eSorry, boys,\r\nbut you'll never find me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:55.820 --\u003e 00:19:58.030\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm not even in\r\nthe amusement park.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:58.114 --\u003e 00:20:02.952\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd by the time you get out of the\r\nmaze, I'll be out of the city.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:10.876 --\u003e 00:20:13.129\r\nDICK: I guess the\r\nmayor's happy about this.\r\n\r\n00:20:14.046 --\u003e 00:20:18.134\r\nBringing in $5.5 million a\r\nyear in new jobs will do that.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.217 --\u003e 00:20:22.179\r\nBut that creep Mockridge got to\r\npocket a cool 10 mil from the buyout.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.596 --\u003e 00:20:24.056\r\nWhat a burn.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.140 --\u003e 00:20:27.560\r\nMaybe. But we've been searching\r\nfor The Riddler for months,\r\n\r\n00:20:28.227 --\u003e 00:20:29.603\r\n\u003ci\u003eand he's still out there.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:34.775 --\u003e 00:20:36.152\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:20:47.830 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: Mockridge\r\nmay have his money,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:49.707 --\u003e 00:20:51.333\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut he won't be sleeping well.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:09.852 --\u003e 00:21:12.772\r\n\u003ci\u003eHow much is a good\r\nnight's sleep worth?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:13.522 --\u003e 00:21:16.066\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow there's a riddle for you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:24.158 --\u003e 00:21:26.160\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:50.601 --\u003e 00:21:51.602\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E42 - Joker's Wild (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.628 --\u003e 00:00:04.630\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.255 --\u003e 00:01:32.301\r\n\u003ci\u003eBe sure the bulbs are spaced far\r\nenough apart for proper root growth,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:32.384 --\u003e 00:01:35.387\r\n\u003ci\u003eand remember to give the\r\nseedlings plenty of sunlight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:37.931 --\u003e 00:01:39.182\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:47.566 --\u003e 00:01:50.235\r\n\u003ci\u003eAdd just enough water. Then...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:50.319 --\u003e 00:01:51.320\r\n(PATIENTS PROTESTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.570 --\u003e 00:01:53.071\r\nHey, I was watching that.\r\n\r\n00:01:53.155 --\u003e 00:01:55.407\r\nAnd now you're watching this.\r\n\r\n00:01:56.992 --\u003e 00:02:00.579\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: (CHUCKLING) Next, a dog drinks\r\nmilk out of his owner's mouth.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:01.538 --\u003e 00:02:02.914\r\nChange it back.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.332 --\u003e 00:02:06.043\r\nOh, no, no, no. Don't want to.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.085 --\u003e 00:02:08.170\r\nGuard!\r\n\r\n00:02:09.087 --\u003e 00:02:10.339\r\nWhat's the problem?\r\n\r\n00:02:11.214 --\u003e 00:02:16.011\r\nDon't look now, Sonny Jim,\r\nbut the plant lady's gone wackers again.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.720 --\u003e 00:02:19.014\r\nHe started it.\r\nI was just sitting here.\r\n\r\n00:02:19.556 --\u003e 00:02:22.976\r\nThat's right.\r\nYou're always blaming me.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.060 --\u003e 00:02:25.145\r\nAnd the children\r\nwonder why we fight.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.104 --\u003e 00:02:27.272\r\nCrazy.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.814 --\u003e 00:02:29.941\r\nI know you are, but what am I?\r\n\r\n00:02:30.484 --\u003e 00:02:35.781\r\nOkay, okay, you'll watch this quietly,\r\nor you'll go back to your cells.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.864 --\u003e 00:02:36.865\r\n\u003ci\u003eJawohl!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:37.407 --\u003e 00:02:38.617\r\nI don't care.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.204 --\u003e 00:02:44.873\r\nYou hold my hand,\r\nand I'll slug you.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.916 --\u003e 00:02:47.209\r\nGuard!\r\n\r\n00:02:47.292 --\u003e 00:02:49.252\r\nJust kidding. Just kidding.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.336 --\u003e 00:02:51.546\r\nYeesh, Pammy, lighten up.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.006 --\u003e 00:02:56.385\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Summer Gleeson live\r\nat Gotham Palisades Boardwalk,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:56.468 --\u003e 00:02:57.844\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhere it's opening day\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:57.928 --\u003e 00:03:01.264\r\n\u003ci\u003eat billionaire Cameron Kaiser's\r\nlatest showplace resort.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:01.473 --\u003e 00:03:06.103\r\n\u003ci\u003eTotal price tag for this fun-seeker's\r\nmecca, nearly $300 million.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:07.896 --\u003e 00:03:09.272\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's true, Summer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:09.356 --\u003e 00:03:12.150\r\n\u003ci\u003eI set out to create the most opulent\r\ngambling resort in the world.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:12.234 --\u003e 00:03:14.152\r\nAfter all,\r\nwhat's a few million here and there\r\n\r\n00:03:14.236 --\u003e 00:03:16.196\r\nas long as my guests are happy?\r\n\r\n00:03:16.655 --\u003e 00:03:19.908\r\n\u003ci\u003eGotham's elite have turned\r\nout in style for the opening.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:19.991 --\u003e 00:03:22.285\r\n\u003ci\u003eBruce Wayne,\r\nperhaps you can give us a hint\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:22.369 --\u003e 00:03:25.664\r\n\u003ci\u003eabout the top secret theme\r\nof Mr. Kaiser's new casino.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:26.540 --\u003e 00:03:28.542\r\n\u003ci\u003eLooks like we'll find out\r\ntogether, Summer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:28.667 --\u003e 00:03:30.252\r\n- (APPLAUSE)\r\n- (DRUMROLL)\r\n\r\n00:03:30.335 --\u003e 00:03:33.380\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\nthe wait is over.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.463 --\u003e 00:03:35.632\r\n\u003ci\u003eI officially welcome\r\nyou, one and all...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:37.843 --\u003e 00:03:41.054\r\n- To Jokers \u003ci\u003eWild.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n- (HEAD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:41.138 --\u003e 00:03:42.347\r\nSay what?\r\n\r\n00:03:56.361 --\u003e 00:03:57.821\r\n\u003ci\u003eSUMMER: Oh, just disgusting.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:57.904 --\u003e 00:04:00.282\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: Psst!\r\nSummer, we're on the air.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:00.866 --\u003e 00:04:04.703\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, uh... There you have it.\r\nLet's get a reaction from the guests.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:04.786 --\u003e 00:04:07.497\r\n\u003ci\u003e- Uh, Mr. Wayne.\r\n- No comment.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:13.879 --\u003e 00:04:17.424\r\n\u003ci\u003eMr. Kaiser,\r\nwhy build a casino seemingly in honor\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:17.507 --\u003e 00:04:20.385\r\n\u003ci\u003eof one of history's\r\nmost notorious outlaws?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:21.011 --\u003e 00:04:22.345\r\n\u003ci\u003eSummer, please.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:22.429 --\u003e 00:04:26.016\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy joker is a classic symbol,\r\nlong associated with cards and games.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:26.099 --\u003e 00:04:29.603\r\n\u003ci\u003eI can't help it if there's a passing\r\nresemblance to some criminal fruitcake.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:30.771 --\u003e 00:04:31.772\r\n(JOKER GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:32.272 --\u003e 00:04:37.569\r\nHow dare that smug,\r\npreening fool try to cash in on my image!\r\n\r\n00:04:38.111 --\u003e 00:04:39.905\r\nNow who should lighten up?\r\n\r\n00:04:40.614 --\u003e 00:04:42.324\r\nDon't get cute with me, Red.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.200 --\u003e 00:04:45.535\r\nHe's ripping me off.\r\nI'll protest.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.871\r\nYeah, I'll sue.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.954 --\u003e 00:04:49.998\r\nThen I'll rip his lungs out.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.081 --\u003e 00:04:51.333\r\nAnd I will, too.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.375 --\u003e 00:04:53.710\r\nTake it easy.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.211 --\u003e 00:04:57.088\r\n(GROANS) I feel dizzy.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.464 --\u003e 00:05:00.425\r\nSick... Everything's spinning.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.509 --\u003e 00:05:03.428\r\nOh! Need a doctor.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.596 --\u003e 00:05:05.722\r\nPAMELA: Oh, Joker?\r\n\r\n00:05:06.640 --\u003e 00:05:08.475\r\nThanks for the smile.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.685 --\u003e 00:05:11.686\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:25.742 --\u003e 00:05:28.161\r\nHang on.\r\nI'll get Dr. Bartholomew.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.995 --\u003e 00:05:31.623\r\nYes. Hurry. Please.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.041 --\u003e 00:05:34.459\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:37.045 --\u003e 00:05:38.046\r\nSucker.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.974 --\u003e 00:05:51.601\r\nJOKER: What a maroon. Ha!\r\n\r\n00:05:51.685 --\u003e 00:05:54.229\r\nI know you are, but what am I?\r\n\r\n00:05:57.357 --\u003e 00:05:58.441\r\nThe Joker!\r\n\r\n00:05:58.900 --\u003e 00:06:00.318\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:03.238 --\u003e 00:06:06.783\r\nExit stage left,\r\nlaughing all the way.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.952 --\u003e 00:06:10.662\r\n- Hey!\r\n- Excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.716 --\u003e 00:06:24.009\r\n- There he is!\r\n- Get him!\r\n\r\n00:06:25.635 --\u003e 00:06:28.388\r\nStep right up and play\r\neveryone's favorite game,\r\n\r\n00:06:28.471 --\u003e 00:06:30.473\r\n\"What's the Joker\r\ngot in the pail?\"\r\n\r\n00:06:31.558 --\u003e 00:06:33.310\r\nMaybe a deadly poison?\r\n\r\n00:06:33.393 --\u003e 00:06:36.605\r\nOr maybe just something to make\r\nthe floor nice and slippery.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.189 --\u003e 00:06:39.566\r\n- Hey!\r\n- Look out!\r\n\r\n00:06:43.236 --\u003e 00:06:46.031\r\nI always did know\r\nhow to make an exit.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.949 --\u003e 00:06:48.950\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:06:49.534 --\u003e 00:06:50.577\r\nTa-da!\r\n\r\n00:07:09.012 --\u003e 00:07:11.514\r\nDon't try this at home, kids.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.143 --\u003e 00:07:16.144\r\n(WHOOPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:17.604 --\u003e 00:07:18.605\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:07:20.523 --\u003e 00:07:21.858\r\nPeekaboo.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.443 --\u003e 00:07:25.445\r\nSorry, no riders.\r\n\r\n00:07:25.570 --\u003e 00:07:26.571\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:07:29.157 --\u003e 00:07:30.575\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:32.953 --\u003e 00:07:38.041\r\nNow to treat Mr. Cameron Kaiser\r\nto a real blowout opening.\r\n\r\n00:07:38.166 --\u003e 00:07:40.085\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.387 --\u003e 00:07:52.055\r\nI didn't mind driving down here\r\n\r\n00:07:52.138 --\u003e 00:07:54.140\r\nat a moment's notice\r\nwith your equipment.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.516 --\u003e 00:07:57.978\r\nAnd I was happy to dream up a\r\nplausible alibi for your date.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.061 --\u003e 00:08:02.357\r\nBut staying in this horrid\r\nplace pushes even my tolerance.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.899 --\u003e 00:08:04.025\r\nMine too.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.401 --\u003e 00:08:05.402\r\nBut I'm convinced\r\n\r\n00:08:05.485 --\u003e 00:08:08.697\r\nit wasn't Kaiser's original goal\r\nto make a Joker-themed casino.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.616 --\u003e 00:08:14.202\r\n- See?\r\n- But why the deception?\r\n\r\n00:08:14.995 --\u003e 00:08:16.955\r\nThat's what I\r\nintend to find out.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.956 --\u003e 00:08:19.749\r\n(HEAD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:44.441 --\u003e 00:08:47.360\r\n\"Camelot.\" Hmm.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.414 --\u003e 00:09:01.708\r\nLooks like Kaiser broke\r\nthe bank on this place.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.963 --\u003e 00:09:08.965\r\nWhat an interesting hobby you've\r\ngot, Cameron.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.843 --\u003e 00:09:12.844\r\nHey, you.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.648 --\u003e 00:09:26.649\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.111 --\u003e 00:09:31.404\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:09:34.824 --\u003e 00:09:37.160\r\nWhere are you?\r\nCome out and fight.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.712 --\u003e 00:09:49.506\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:00.642 --\u003e 00:10:02.143\r\n(WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:02.685 --\u003e 00:10:04.896\r\nJumpin' Jiminy Christmas.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.027 --\u003e 00:10:12.946\r\nIt's an homage to me.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.947 --\u003e 00:10:15.615\r\nI'm kind of sorry I\r\nhave to blow it up.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.492 --\u003e 00:10:20.411\r\nGo on and open table six.\r\nWe got players waiting.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.121 --\u003e 00:10:22.122\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.373 --\u003e 00:10:24.374\r\n(SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:10:24.666 --\u003e 00:10:27.794\r\nThen again,\r\nall work and no play...\r\n\r\n00:10:27.877 --\u003e 00:10:28.878\r\n(CACKLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.881 --\u003e 00:10:33.424\r\nGood evening, folks.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.636 --\u003e 00:10:38.388\r\nThe game is blackjack.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.471 --\u003e 00:10:40.640\r\nJoker's rules, of course.\r\n\r\n00:10:40.723 --\u003e 00:10:41.724\r\n(GIGGLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:47.689 --\u003e 00:10:49.607\r\nOoh! Blackjack already.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.567 --\u003e 00:10:51.693\r\nLucky me.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.235 --\u003e 00:10:53.236\r\n- Hey.\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:10:53.319 --\u003e 00:10:54.445\r\nHold on.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.529 --\u003e 00:10:56.156\r\nJOKER: Don't be sore losers.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.239 --\u003e 00:10:58.074\r\nWe're here to have fun.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.994 --\u003e 00:11:04.414\r\nMr. Kaiser,\r\nthat dealer's doing something screwy.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.497 --\u003e 00:11:05.957\r\nI'm calling security.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.040 --\u003e 00:11:07.417\r\nNo. Wait.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.085 --\u003e 00:11:12.380\r\n\u003ci\u003eOoh! Mercy me.\r\nAnother blackjack.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:12.463 --\u003e 00:11:15.049\r\n\u003ci\u003eOne might think I had\r\nan ace up my sleeve.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:16.926 --\u003e 00:11:18.052\r\nLet him deal.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.678 --\u003e 00:11:20.263\r\nYes, sir. You're the boss.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.056 --\u003e 00:11:23.933\r\n(JOKER CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.317 --\u003e 00:11:35.403\r\n- Try your luck, friend?\r\n- Why not?\r\n\r\n00:11:36.112 --\u003e 00:11:38.364\r\nSay, don't I know you?\r\n\r\n00:11:39.365 --\u003e 00:11:41.242\r\nSure. Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.784 --\u003e 00:11:42.785\r\nHuh.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.869 --\u003e 00:11:46.164\r\nSo this is how your family\r\nmade all those billions.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.124 --\u003e 00:11:50.752\r\nThe secret's out. And you are?\r\n\r\n00:11:51.502 --\u003e 00:11:54.756\r\nOh, just a nameless clown,\r\nshuffling my life away.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.382 --\u003e 00:11:59.302\r\nToo bad it has to be in\r\nsuch gruesome surroundings.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.557\r\nDon't care for the decor?\r\n\r\n00:12:04.641 --\u003e 00:12:08.311\r\nNot hardly. All those\r\nhorrible faces grinning at me.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.895 --\u003e 00:12:11.272\r\nThat would do things to\r\nmy mind after a while.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.690 --\u003e 00:12:13.983\r\nWho says you have one?\r\n\r\n00:12:16.569 --\u003e 00:12:18.780\r\nYeah, I'd be ready for\r\nthe laughing academy\r\n\r\n00:12:18.863 --\u003e 00:12:22.075\r\nif I had to stare at\r\nthat ugly clown all day.\r\n\r\n00:12:23.076 --\u003e 00:12:25.828\r\n- Why I ought to...\r\n- Hit me.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.166 --\u003e 00:12:31.167\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:32.794 --\u003e 00:12:33.878\r\nTwenty.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.463 --\u003e 00:12:38.508\r\nOh, lucky me. Twenty-one.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.342 --\u003e 00:12:43.012\r\nHow nice. A little something\r\nfor the Wayne Charity Fund.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.931 --\u003e 00:12:46.099\r\nGood night.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.100 --\u003e 00:12:48.101\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:12:55.233 --\u003e 00:12:56.609\r\nHe's here.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.902 --\u003e 00:12:59.279\r\nPlace your bets, folks.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.654 --\u003e 00:13:00.655\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:13:01.447 --\u003e 00:13:02.907\r\n- BATMAN: You.\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:13:03.992 --\u003e 00:13:05.034\r\n- Batman.\r\n- It's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.118 --\u003e 00:13:06.160\r\nI don't believe it.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.244 --\u003e 00:13:08.830\r\n- It is Batman!\r\n- What's he doing here?\r\n\r\n00:13:08.913 --\u003e 00:13:10.999\r\nWhoops! Time to cash out.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.918 --\u003e 00:13:15.044\r\n- Hey!\r\n- Hey.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.254 --\u003e 00:13:17.422\r\nMAN: Stop that guy.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.142 --\u003e 00:13:30.143\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.478 --\u003e 00:13:33.479\r\n(ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:13:36.899 --\u003e 00:13:37.900\r\n(MAN SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:41.029 --\u003e 00:13:42.030\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:13:43.323 --\u003e 00:13:44.324\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:56.252 --\u003e 00:13:57.587\r\nHere's where I get off.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.130 --\u003e 00:14:00.131\r\nWhoo!\r\n\r\n00:14:13.561 --\u003e 00:14:15.813\r\nNot bad for a starter,\r\n\r\n00:14:15.938 --\u003e 00:14:18.608\r\nbut the real fireworks\r\nare still to come.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.447 --\u003e 00:14:28.242\r\nWhoops! Coming through.\r\nHot stuff. One side, please.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.674 --\u003e 00:14:46.928\r\nI wouldn't take odds on this place\r\nlasting the night. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:55.603 --\u003e 00:14:56.604\r\n(JOKER HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.980 --\u003e 00:14:59.315\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: Helipad.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:02.318\r\nI want my personal 'copter\r\nready for takeoff in 20 minutes.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.402 --\u003e 00:15:03.444\r\n\u003ci\u003eYes, sir, Mr. Kaiser.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:12.245 --\u003e 00:15:13.454\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.330 --\u003e 00:15:15.706\r\nGoing somewhere?\r\n\r\n00:15:16.916 --\u003e 00:15:19.585\r\nFirst you trash my\r\npenthouse, then my casino.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.669 --\u003e 00:15:20.909\r\nYou gonna wreck something else?\r\n\r\n00:15:21.504 --\u003e 00:15:24.507\r\nIf I didn't know better,\r\nI'd say you wanted this place destroyed.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.425 --\u003e 00:15:30.388\r\nAfter spending 300 million to build it?\r\nThat's not good business, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.471 --\u003e 00:15:32.473\r\nI've seen the unpaid bills.\r\n\r\n00:15:32.932 --\u003e 00:15:34.934\r\nBuilding this casino\r\nhas bankrupted you.\r\n\r\n00:15:35.435 --\u003e 00:15:37.854\r\nThat's why you turned it\r\ninto a target for the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.312 --\u003e 00:15:41.107\r\nOnce he destroys it,\r\nyou'll collect the insurance money.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:43.693\r\nYou hit the jackpot, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:44.402 --\u003e 00:15:46.779\r\nBut I've got too much at\r\nstake to be stopped now.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.572 --\u003e 00:15:49.365\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:53.369 --\u003e 00:15:55.746\r\nAh! You again.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.039 --\u003e 00:16:00.668\r\n- What do we do with him, boss?\r\n- Send him down to his friend.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.545 --\u003e 00:16:03.546\r\n(JOKER HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:08.426 --\u003e 00:16:10.970\r\n- Huh?\r\n- (ELEVATOR DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:16:11.053 --\u003e 00:16:12.054\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:14.432 --\u003e 00:16:17.810\r\nKind of slow on the\r\nreflexes, eh, Batsy?\r\n\r\n00:16:18.352 --\u003e 00:16:21.606\r\nThat car crash must have taken\r\nmore out of you than I thought.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.898 --\u003e 00:16:23.483\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.369 --\u003e 00:16:37.580\r\nWa key, wa key.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.539 --\u003e 00:16:39.540\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:42.877 --\u003e 00:16:44.128\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.592 --\u003e 00:16:52.345\r\nThought you'd like to be\r\nconscious for your own demise.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.428 --\u003e 00:16:55.264\r\nI really put some\r\neffort into this one.\r\n\r\n00:16:58.059 --\u003e 00:16:59.352\r\nOnce I spin the wheel,\r\n\r\n00:16:59.435 --\u003e 00:17:00.978\r\nyou, the casino\r\n\r\n00:17:01.062 --\u003e 00:17:05.816\r\nand that strutting fool Kaiser\r\nwill all be blown sky-high.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.651 --\u003e 00:17:07.985\r\nNot bad, eh?\r\n\r\n00:17:08.986 --\u003e 00:17:12.323\r\nYou won't get Kaiser.\r\nHe's been playing you for a patsy.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.074 --\u003e 00:17:14.075\r\nEh?\r\n\r\n00:17:14.784 --\u003e 00:17:16.577\r\nHe's counting on you\r\nto blow this place up\r\n\r\n00:17:16.661 --\u003e 00:17:17.995\r\nso he can collect the insurance.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.746 --\u003e 00:17:20.331\r\nBy the time you get clear,\r\n\r\n00:17:20.414 --\u003e 00:17:22.583\r\nKaiser will be miles\r\naway, laughing at you.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.417 --\u003e 00:17:25.378\r\nI hate it when you make sense.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.966 --\u003e 00:17:33.219\r\nI'll settle my score with\r\nKaiser, man to clown.\r\n\r\n00:17:33.302 --\u003e 00:17:35.763\r\nBut that still doesn't\r\nlet you off the hook.\r\n\r\n00:17:39.559 --\u003e 00:17:40.851\r\n(WHEEL WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:17:49.235 --\u003e 00:17:52.321\r\nHow about that, Bats?\r\nLooks like your number's up.\r\n\r\n00:17:52.572 --\u003e 00:17:54.657\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:02.915 --\u003e 00:18:03.916\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.778 --\u003e 00:18:35.531\r\n- Get me out of here now!\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.911 --\u003e 00:18:41.912\r\n(MAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:44.290 --\u003e 00:18:45.291\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\n00:18:48.044 --\u003e 00:18:50.004\r\nSome clown jumped me\r\nand grabbed my 'copter.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.087 --\u003e 00:18:51.422\r\nMr. Kaiser's up there.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.845 --\u003e 00:18:59.639\r\nWhat are you circling\r\nfor, you fool?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.640 --\u003e 00:19:04.352\r\n- It was a scheme worthy of me, Kaiser.\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:04.435 --\u003e 00:19:09.065\r\nThe way you got me riled up and\r\nturned me loose on this place.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.025 --\u003e 00:19:13.903\r\nYou... You were supposed\r\nto destroy the casino.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.779 --\u003e 00:19:17.823\r\nYeah, but then I realized it'd\r\nbe more fun to get rid of you\r\n\r\n00:19:17.907 --\u003e 00:19:19.408\r\nand run the show myself.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.201 --\u003e 00:19:21.410\r\nBut you can't!\r\n\r\n00:19:21.911 --\u003e 00:19:26.749\r\nOh, please, Mr. Kaiser,\r\nyou of all people should've realized\r\n\r\n00:19:26.832 --\u003e 00:19:28.668\r\nthere'd be a joker in the deck.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.959 --\u003e 00:19:30.753\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:34.465 --\u003e 00:19:37.051\r\nWhy can't he ever stay dead?\r\n\r\n00:19:57.988 --\u003e 00:19:59.740\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:03.202 --\u003e 00:20:04.245\r\nJOKER: Gotcha!\r\n\r\n00:20:08.499 --\u003e 00:20:09.667\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.673 --\u003e 00:20:18.592\r\n(HEAD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.262 --\u003e 00:20:24.890\r\nThat's it.\r\nChew him up and spit him out.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.057 --\u003e 00:20:26.058\r\n(JOKER CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.283 --\u003e 00:20:43.909\r\nStop! You'll kill us all!\r\n\r\n00:21:15.274 --\u003e 00:21:16.275\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:21:17.818 --\u003e 00:21:19.653\r\n- (CHIMING)\r\n- (AUTOMATED VOICE WHOOPING)\r\n\r\n00:21:24.784 --\u003e 00:21:29.371\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd so it ended for both ex-billionaire\r\nCameron Kaiser and the Joker.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:29.830 --\u003e 00:21:32.208\r\nAh! Enough of this rubbish.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.291 --\u003e 00:21:33.292\r\nPAMELA: Hey!\r\n\r\n00:21:33.375 --\u003e 00:21:35.002\r\nALL: We were watching that.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.420 --\u003e 00:21:37.421\r\n(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:21:39.465 --\u003e 00:21:40.966\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd was returned to Arkham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:41.050 --\u003e 00:21:44.720\r\nAh, you bunch of no-good,\r\nwhacked-out losers.\r\n\r\n00:21:44.804 --\u003e 00:21:45.971\r\nYou make me sick.\r\n\r\n00:21:50.935 --\u003e 00:21:52.937\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E43 - His Silicon Soul (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:17.643 --\u003e 00:00:19.645\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:17.452 --\u003e 00:01:19.037\r\n(THUNDER CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:27.588 --\u003e 00:01:30.882\r\nMAN: This is a bunch of junk, Chaz.\r\nWhat'd you drag us down here for?\r\n\r\n00:01:31.049 --\u003e 00:01:33.849\r\nCHAZ: I'm telling you, man, this\r\nplace is full of top-secret technology\r\n\r\n00:01:34.011 --\u003e 00:01:36.054\r\nfrom some computer\r\nfactory that blew up.\r\n\r\n00:01:36.680 --\u003e 00:01:39.474\r\nMAN: It's full of something, all right.\r\nAnd so are you.\r\n\r\n00:01:39.683 --\u003e 00:01:41.560\r\nNo, I'm serious, man.\r\n\r\n00:01:41.643 --\u003e 00:01:44.104\r\nDefense systems,\r\nrobotics, laser weaponry.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.035 --\u003e 00:01:59.369\r\nGive me a hand here.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.961 --\u003e 00:02:10.172\r\n- (MEN GASP)\r\n- (THUNDER CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:12.466 --\u003e 00:02:14.801\r\nOh, man, this ain't happening.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.809 --\u003e 00:02:23.894\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.063 --\u003e 00:02:27.147\r\nPathetic.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.106 --\u003e 00:02:29.232\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:02:31.735 --\u003e 00:02:32.736\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:02:35.447 --\u003e 00:02:37.824\r\nThis ain't happening.\r\nThis ain't happening.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.621 --\u003e 00:02:43.747\r\n(MEN GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:03:01.056 --\u003e 00:03:02.516\r\n(THUNDER CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:07.312 --\u003e 00:03:08.313\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:09.564 --\u003e 00:03:10.649\r\n(GUN CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.900 --\u003e 00:03:14.444\r\nYou ain't human.\r\nYou ain't human!\r\n\r\n00:03:18.448 --\u003e 00:03:19.616\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.715 --\u003e 00:03:36.049\r\n(CLOCK TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:38.093 --\u003e 00:03:39.803\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:02.033 --\u003e 00:04:04.578\r\nMother. Father.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.745 --\u003e 00:04:06.288\r\nALFRED: Don't move!\r\n\r\n00:04:06.872 --\u003e 00:04:07.914\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.376 --\u003e 00:04:13.920\r\nOh, Master Bruce,\r\nyou did give me a start.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.087 --\u003e 00:04:16.381\r\nSir, are you all right?\r\n\r\n00:04:16.465 --\u003e 00:04:19.384\r\nAlfred, what's happened to me?\r\n\r\n00:04:20.010 --\u003e 00:04:21.011\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:30.687 --\u003e 00:04:32.063\r\n'Busy flight? (GAsPs)\r\n\r\n00:04:32.147 --\u003e 00:04:35.692\r\nNever too busy to spend time\r\ncutting down your pifiatas.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.776 --\u003e 00:04:38.987\r\nNext time, try hanging them a little\r\nlower if it isn't too much trouble.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.657 --\u003e 00:04:43.992\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:50.165 --\u003e 00:04:51.750\r\nYours, I believe?\r\n\r\n00:04:53.960 --\u003e 00:04:55.462\r\nSo it would seem.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.673 --\u003e 00:05:02.385\r\nKeep him away, man. He ain't human.\r\nGet it away from me!\r\n\r\n00:05:08.934 --\u003e 00:05:11.269\r\nJim, I didn't catch these men.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.728 --\u003e 00:05:14.022\r\nWell, if you didn't, who did?\r\n\r\n00:05:17.108 --\u003e 00:05:19.528\r\nYou're one of\r\nRossum's duplicants.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.611 --\u003e 00:05:22.030\r\nDuplicants? What do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:05:22.405 --\u003e 00:05:24.407\r\nWhat have you done\r\nwith Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:05:24.658 --\u003e 00:05:25.742\r\n(ALFRED GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:25.826 --\u003e 00:05:27.452\r\nAlfred, it's me.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.536 --\u003e 00:05:31.164\r\nI need your help.\r\nI have to find out what's happened to me.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.706 --\u003e 00:05:34.167\r\nI'm not going to\r\nlast long like this.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.878 --\u003e 00:05:39.130\r\nAlfred, wait. Please!\r\n\r\n00:05:58.400 --\u003e 00:05:59.776\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:06:08.618 --\u003e 00:06:09.703\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.663 --\u003e 00:06:12.747\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:16.418 --\u003e 00:06:20.046\r\nSorry to do this, old friend.\r\nBut I need some answers.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.259 --\u003e 00:06:25.302\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.094 --\u003e 00:06:29.598\r\nComputer, access \"duplicant.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:30.557 --\u003e 00:06:31.766\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Searching.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:34.477 --\u003e 00:06:38.773\r\n\u003ci\u003eDuplicant. Lifelike robot capable\r\nof mimicking human behavior.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:38.940 --\u003e 00:06:40.775\r\n\u003ci\u003eDesigned,\r\nconfigured and assembled\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:40.942 --\u003e 00:06:42.694\r\n\u003ci\u003eby Cybertron\r\nIndustries' holographic\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:42.777 --\u003e 00:06:45.655\r\n\u003ci\u003eanalytical reciprocating\r\ndigital computer\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:45.822 --\u003e 00:06:47.365\r\n\u003ci\u003eknown as HARDAC.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:50.160 --\u003e 00:06:51.745\r\nCurrent status of HARDAC.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.495 --\u003e 00:06:55.832\r\n\u003ci\u003eDestroyed in failed attempt to\r\nreplace human beings with duplicants.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:55.999 --\u003e 00:07:00.420\r\nProbability of existence of\r\nBatman or Bruce Wayne duplicant.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.587 --\u003e 00:07:03.214\r\n- Insufficient data.\r\n- List known duplicants.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.840 --\u003e 00:07:07.177\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Duane, Randa.\r\nGordon, James.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:07.344 --\u003e 00:07:10.639\r\n\u003ci\u003eBullock, Harvey. Hill, Hamilton.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:10.805 --\u003e 00:07:12.891\r\n\u003ci\u003eRoss um, Karl.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:13.099 --\u003e 00:07:15.518\r\n\u003ci\u003eStatus of all, destroyed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:15.685 --\u003e 00:07:17.854\r\nDUPLICANT: Magnify\r\nlower right quadrant.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.938 --\u003e 00:07:19.022\r\n(BEEPS RAPIDLY)\r\n\r\n00:07:19.522 --\u003e 00:07:21.942\r\nCurrent location of Karl Rossum.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.025 --\u003e 00:07:23.234\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Searching.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:36.623 --\u003e 00:07:38.041\r\nBATMAN: Recognize these?\r\n\r\n00:07:39.042 --\u003e 00:07:40.919\r\nThey came from your warehouse.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.252 --\u003e 00:07:44.297\r\nIt seems there was another\r\nBatman sighted there last night.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.381 --\u003e 00:07:48.218\r\nCould HARDAC have created\r\nanother duplicant? One of me?\r\n\r\n00:07:49.427 --\u003e 00:07:50.637\r\nHARDAC's gone.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.720 --\u003e 00:07:54.849\r\nWhatever wasn't blown to bits was\r\nconfiscated by the police months ago.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.016 --\u003e 00:07:57.018\r\nThere's nothing left but junk.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.185 --\u003e 00:07:59.938\r\nBroken toys I outgrew long ago.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.438 --\u003e 00:08:02.857\r\nI don't try to build life\r\nanymore, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.316 --\u003e 00:08:05.902\r\n- I just grow it.\r\n- I'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.069 --\u003e 00:08:08.905\r\nI know how painful it can\r\nbe to dig up the past.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.072 --\u003e 00:08:10.573\r\nThen please, leave me alone.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.991 --\u003e 00:08:12.867\r\nLet me get on with my life.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.268 --\u003e 00:08:41.062\r\n- DUPLICANT: Rossum.\r\n- I told you everything I know.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.229 --\u003e 00:08:43.023\r\nNow, please... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:44.441 --\u003e 00:08:45.900\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:57.287 --\u003e 00:08:59.039\r\nRossum, I need your help.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.248 --\u003e 00:09:03.334\r\n- Where did you come from?\r\n- Listen to me.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.418 --\u003e 00:09:06.588\r\nSomeone put my mind\r\ninto this robot body.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.671 --\u003e 00:09:08.590\r\nYou're the only one\r\nwho can help me.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.217 --\u003e 00:09:13.636\r\nROSSUM: The damage\r\nis too extensive.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.720 --\u003e 00:09:16.681\r\nThese circuits will give out,\r\nprobably in a matter of hours.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.765 --\u003e 00:09:21.644\r\nThen we've got to find my real body\r\nor transfer me to another robot shell.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.145 --\u003e 00:09:23.605\r\nYou don't understand.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.688 --\u003e 00:09:26.316\r\nYou're not a man's\r\nmind in a robot's body.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.399 --\u003e 00:09:30.945\r\n- You're a robot. Period.\r\n- You're lying. It's not possible!\r\n\r\n00:09:31.112 --\u003e 00:09:36.534\r\nI know my family and friends.\r\nI remember names, faces, birthdays.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.618 --\u003e 00:09:38.661\r\nI have memories, a past.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.745 --\u003e 00:09:41.623\r\nYou have information.\r\nData. Nothing more.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.248 --\u003e 00:09:44.042\r\nDo you remember your first kiss?\r\n\r\n00:09:44.918 --\u003e 00:09:46.002\r\nYour favorite song?\r\n\r\n00:09:46.544 --\u003e 00:09:49.464\r\nThe last time you tasted\r\na really good steak?\r\n\r\n00:09:49.964 --\u003e 00:09:51.466\r\nNo, but-\r\n\r\n00:09:51.549 --\u003e 00:09:55.261\r\nCan you remember anything beyond\r\ncold, hard facts?\r\n\r\n00:09:55.553 --\u003e 00:09:59.182\r\nFacts can be implanted,\r\naccessed from any number of sources.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.017 --\u003e 00:10:02.018\r\nHuh.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.852 --\u003e 00:10:04.104\r\nWhere's HARDAC?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.604 --\u003e 00:10:07.273\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\nHARDAC was destroyed.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.607 --\u003e 00:10:09.776\r\nWhere is he? Tell me!\r\n\r\n00:10:10.276 --\u003e 00:10:11.694\r\nNOW!\r\n\r\n00:10:17.242 --\u003e 00:10:18.243\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:22.872 --\u003e 00:10:23.957\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:24.874 --\u003e 00:10:25.917\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:27.877 --\u003e 00:10:29.254\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:40.223 --\u003e 00:10:41.516\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:49.524 --\u003e 00:10:52.569\r\n- Don't!\r\n- (GRUNTS) I can't let it live!\r\n\r\n00:10:52.902 --\u003e 00:10:54.445\r\nWe don't know\r\nwhere it came from.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.654 --\u003e 00:10:57.907\r\nIf HARDAC has been reactivated,\r\nthis machine may lead us to it.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.290 --\u003e 00:11:07.584\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:23.725 --\u003e 00:11:24.767\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:11:36.905 --\u003e 00:11:37.947\r\n(ROSSUM SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:11:55.423 --\u003e 00:11:56.966\r\nWe've lost it.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.342 --\u003e 00:11:58.801\r\nNot for long.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.097 --\u003e 00:12:04.140\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:04.224 --\u003e 00:12:08.561\r\nComputer, current location of\r\nconfiscated HARDAC remains.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.704 --\u003e 00:12:27.956\r\nDUPLICANT: HARDAC.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.039 --\u003e 00:12:29.082\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:31.334 --\u003e 00:12:33.086\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Symbol\r\nrecognition confirmed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:33.169 --\u003e 00:12:34.963\r\nWhat in...\r\n\r\n00:12:44.222 --\u003e 00:12:46.307\r\n\u003ci\u003eInitiating startup program.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:51.271 --\u003e 00:12:52.522\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:13:03.032 --\u003e 00:13:05.285\r\n\u003ci\u003ePrepare to insert\r\noperational circuitry.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:09.747 --\u003e 00:13:12.667\r\n\u003ci\u003eInitiating diagnostic\r\nand repair sequences.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:12.917 --\u003e 00:13:14.002\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:13:14.711 --\u003e 00:13:15.962\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.718 --\u003e 00:13:26.180\r\n\u003ci\u003eWarning. Memory error detected.\r\nReconfiguring mnemonic files.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:26.681 --\u003e 00:13:31.060\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n- What are you doing to me?\r\n\r\n00:13:32.687 --\u003e 00:13:35.940\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: A learning program designed\r\nto complete your memory files\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:36.190 --\u003e 00:13:38.860\r\n\u003ci\u003eand help you better fulfill\r\nyour operating directives.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:39.694 --\u003e 00:13:44.115\r\n\u003ci\u003eShortly before self-destruction\r\nHARDAC created one final duplicant.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:45.033 --\u003e 00:13:46.451\r\n\u003ci\u003eAn advanced prototype\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:46.576 --\u003e 00:13:51.039\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith personal and technical information\r\naccessed from Batman's computer.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:51.456 --\u003e 00:13:53.291\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou were that duplicant.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:54.542 --\u003e 00:13:58.880\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut your memory systems were damaged\r\nbefore full activation occurred.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:00.173 --\u003e 00:14:04.927\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe new circuit board contains HARDAC's\r\ncore operational systems and memory.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:05.011 --\u003e 00:14:07.764\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll duplicants were programmed\r\nto seek out this component\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:07.847 --\u003e 00:14:09.724\r\n\u003ci\u003ein the event of\r\nHARDAC's destruction.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:11.642 --\u003e 00:14:14.479\r\n\u003ci\u003eYour memory systems have\r\nnow been reconfigured.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:14.562 --\u003e 00:14:18.024\r\nYes. I am fully operational now.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.149 --\u003e 00:14:21.569\r\n\u003ci\u003eExcellent.\r\nYou now house my command files.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:22.028 --\u003e 00:14:24.072\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe are HARDAC.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:24.155 --\u003e 00:14:28.826\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe will reactivate the plan to\r\nreplace all humanity with duplicants.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:41.923 --\u003e 00:14:45.718\r\nWe will begin the replacement\r\nprocess with Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.450 --\u003e 00:15:10.618\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:16.666 --\u003e 00:15:18.876\r\nI thought I might find you here.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.880 --\u003e 00:15:27.051\r\nI cannot function as the Batman\r\nuntil you are deactivated.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.510 --\u003e 00:15:29.303\r\nThat's easier said than done.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.870 --\u003e 00:15:54.996\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:04.839 --\u003e 00:16:07.341\r\nALFRED: Master Bruce,\r\nI'm so glad you're back.\r\n\r\n00:16:07.550 --\u003e 00:16:11.846\r\n- What became of your evil twin?\r\n- It's all taken care of, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.222 --\u003e 00:16:15.850\r\nThere is only one Batman now.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.560 --\u003e 00:16:19.187\r\nOh, good Lord.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.270 --\u003e 00:16:21.856\r\nI will allow you to continue\r\nyour necessary maintenance\r\n\r\n00:16:21.981 --\u003e 00:16:25.693\r\nof the Batcave and mansion until\r\nyour replacement is fully configured.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.943 --\u003e 00:16:29.989\r\nIn a few moments,\r\nHARDAC will upload into this computer.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.783 --\u003e 00:16:35.912\r\nThrough the information network\r\nthis computer is linked with,\r\n\r\n00:16:35.995 --\u003e 00:16:39.123\r\nHARDAC can imprint himself\r\non every computer on Earth.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.415 --\u003e 00:16:42.793\r\nHARDAC will reactivate,\r\nmore powerful than ever\r\n\r\n00:16:42.877 --\u003e 00:16:46.047\r\nand configure more duplicants\r\nto replace humanity.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.297 --\u003e 00:16:49.967\r\nImpossible.\r\nA computer can't build a factory.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.051 --\u003e 00:16:52.929\r\nHumans will construct\r\nthe necessary machinery.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.888 --\u003e 00:16:55.598\r\nHumanity will resist!\r\n\r\n00:16:55.681 --\u003e 00:16:59.477\r\nWith total control of worldwide\r\ndefense and communications systems,\r\n\r\n00:16:59.560 --\u003e 00:17:01.854\r\nHARDAC can be very persuasive.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.938 --\u003e 00:17:03.481\r\nBATMAN: I disagree.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.940 --\u003e 00:17:06.901\r\nMaster Bruce.\r\nThank heaven you're alive.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.443 --\u003e 00:17:10.613\r\nImpossible.\r\nYou could not have survived the fall.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.905 --\u003e 00:17:13.824\r\nWe humans are more resilient\r\nthan you give us credit for.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.702 --\u003e 00:17:18.204\r\n- (ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.746 --\u003e 00:17:19.830\r\nAlfred!\r\n\r\n00:17:23.751 --\u003e 00:17:26.003\r\nNever mind me.\r\nStop the computer!\r\n\r\n00:17:26.170 --\u003e 00:17:28.506\r\nYou cannot prevent the\r\ninevitable, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.589 --\u003e 00:17:30.675\r\nHARDAC is reborn.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.178 --\u003e 00:17:35.263\r\n(BATMAN YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.433 --\u003e 00:17:42.019\r\nIn the very image of the\r\nman who destroyed him.\r\n\r\n00:17:50.611 --\u003e 00:17:52.822\r\nI know all your moves, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.489 --\u003e 00:17:55.032\r\nSo why don't you finish me off?\r\n\r\n00:17:55.408 --\u003e 00:17:59.453\r\nOr have you become enough like me\r\nto know that I won't take a life?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.501 --\u003e 00:18:09.672\r\nI saw you risk your own life to\r\nsave Rossum in the greenhouse.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.447 --\u003e 00:18:37.074\r\nYou knew I'd be able\r\nto dodge that in time.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.659 --\u003e 00:18:42.079\r\nI suspect you not only won't\r\nkill, you can't.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.246 --\u003e 00:18:44.999\r\nThat's why you didn't finish\r\nme off at the warehouse.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.082 --\u003e 00:18:48.669\r\nImpossible.\r\nI am programmed to serve HARDAC.\r\n\r\n00:19:18.199 --\u003e 00:19:19.408\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:25.164 --\u003e 00:19:26.248\r\n(CLANGS)\r\n\r\n00:19:29.126 --\u003e 00:19:33.089\r\nWhy do you resist?\r\nHARDAC's goals are identical to your own.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.381 --\u003e 00:19:34.965\r\nHow do you figure that?\r\n\r\n00:19:37.343 --\u003e 00:19:40.846\r\nPicture a world\r\ncompletely free of crime,\r\n\r\n00:19:40.930 --\u003e 00:19:44.016\r\nfree of suffering,\r\nfree of frailty.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.558 --\u003e 00:19:49.105\r\nBATMAN: You mean free of choice?\r\nCompassion? Free of humanity?\r\n\r\n00:19:49.188 --\u003e 00:19:50.272\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.115 --\u003e 00:20:00.991\r\nYou can't do it.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.075 --\u003e 00:20:02.827\r\nHARDAC built you well.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.620 --\u003e 00:20:08.082\r\nPerhaps even better than\r\nhe could have imagined.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.795 --\u003e 00:20:14.088\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:17.842 --\u003e 00:20:19.719\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:20.469 --\u003e 00:20:22.179\r\nI've taken a life.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.599 --\u003e 00:20:27.560\r\nI've killed a man.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.485 --\u003e 00:20:40.865\r\nMy city, my people.\r\nWhat have I done?\r\n\r\n00:20:41.157 --\u003e 00:20:42.366\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:05.473 --\u003e 00:21:06.724\r\nMaster Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:21:23.032 --\u003e 00:21:24.784\r\nThank heaven you're alive.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.786 --\u003e 00:21:30.498\r\nIt would appear, sir,\r\nthat it preferred to sacrifice itself,\r\n\r\n00:21:30.581 --\u003e 00:21:33.959\r\nrather than allow innocent\r\nlives to come to harm.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.168 --\u003e 00:21:35.544\r\nSomewhat like you.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.003 --\u003e 00:21:39.340\r\nBATMAN: It seems it was more than\r\nwires and microchips after all.\r\n\r\n00:21:39.423 --\u003e 00:21:41.509\r\nCould it be it had a\r\nsoul, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:21:41.592 --\u003e 00:21:43.469\r\nA soul of silicon,\r\n\r\n00:21:44.345 --\u003e 00:21:46.305\r\nbut a soul nonetheless.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.728 --\u003e 00:21:54.730\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E44 - Off Balance (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.215 --\u003e 00:00:07.341\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:24.209 --\u003e 00:01:25.502\r\nAn hour I've been waiting.\r\n\r\n00:01:25.586 --\u003e 00:01:27.706\r\nI don't know what Nico wanted\r\nto meet here for anyway.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.963 --\u003e 00:01:29.047\r\nBATMAN: He didn't, Twitch.\r\n\r\n00:01:30.966 --\u003e 00:01:31.967\r\nI did.\r\n\r\n00:01:32.718 --\u003e 00:01:35.596\r\nYou! You tricked me.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.804 --\u003e 00:01:37.222\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:01:37.514 --\u003e 00:01:40.934\r\nInformation on the\r\nSociety of Shadows.\r\n\r\n00:01:41.393 --\u003e 00:01:43.395\r\nWord is they've\r\nstarted operating here.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.687 --\u003e 00:01:45.606\r\nTell me all about them.\r\n\r\n00:01:45.731 --\u003e 00:01:48.025\r\nThere ain't that much to tell.\r\n\r\n00:01:48.150 --\u003e 00:01:51.028\r\nI mean, I only worked for them, okay?\r\nNot with them.\r\n\r\n00:01:51.278 --\u003e 00:01:53.739\r\nIt'll have to do. Now talk.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.197 --\u003e 00:01:55.282\r\nOkay, Okay-\r\n\r\n00:01:55.365 --\u003e 00:01:58.005\r\nThey're supposed to have their\r\nclaws in every dirty deal in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.082 --\u003e 00:02:07.461\r\nIn fact, word on the street is they\r\ngot something major going down tonight.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.669 --\u003e 00:02:10.505\r\nGonna boost some kind of new\r\nultrasound gizmo, or something.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.340 --\u003e 00:02:14.092\r\n- Who runs the show?\r\n- Strange dude.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.259 --\u003e 00:02:16.637\r\nStrangest thing about these\r\nguys, come to think of it.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.054 --\u003e 00:02:21.099\r\nGoes by the code name \"Vertigo.\"\r\nThey say he's... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:25.062 --\u003e 00:02:26.104\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:27.648 --\u003e 00:02:28.774\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:29.191 --\u003e 00:02:32.527\r\nPlease, he made me talk.\r\nI didn't wanna.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.694 --\u003e 00:02:35.739\r\nNo one betrays the Society.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.531 --\u003e 00:02:38.116\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:40.285 --\u003e 00:02:45.082\r\nNo, no, please.\r\n(SCREAMS) I didn't do it!\r\n\r\n00:02:52.506 --\u003e 00:02:55.217\r\nSuch be the fate\r\nof all traitors.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.467 --\u003e 00:02:56.760\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.095 --\u003e 00:02:59.471\r\nYou'll pay for that.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.246 --\u003e 00:03:25.455\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:33.171 --\u003e 00:03:35.465\r\nMay the Shadows live forever.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.334 --\u003e 00:04:13.211\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:20.761 --\u003e 00:04:22.012\r\n(SHELLS CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.224 --\u003e 00:04:27.225\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:04:28.226 --\u003e 00:04:29.311\r\nBATMAN: Over here, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.356 --\u003e 00:04:36.610\r\nI heard Twitch got away,\r\nthanks to a couple of Shadow agents.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.902 --\u003e 00:04:38.487\r\nBATMAN: And when I\r\ntried to nail them,\r\n\r\n00:04:38.570 --\u003e 00:04:41.031\r\nthey used some sort of gas\r\nto erase their own minds.\r\n\r\n00:04:41.448 --\u003e 00:04:44.117\r\nYeah, that fits with what\r\nlittle we know about them.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.285 --\u003e 00:04:47.120\r\nBut something Twitch\r\nsaid makes me think\r\n\r\n00:04:47.204 --\u003e 00:04:50.665\r\nthey're going after Wayne\r\nTech's new sonic drill tonight\r\n\r\n00:04:50.749 --\u003e 00:04:51.792\r\nwhen it comes into Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.125 --\u003e 00:04:54.836\r\nTell Bullock he should add\r\nmore guards just to be safe.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.003 --\u003e 00:04:57.088\r\nIs there anything\r\nyou don't know about?\r\n\r\n00:04:57.422 --\u003e 00:05:00.050\r\nI only assigned that detail\r\na couple of hours ago.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.384 --\u003e 00:05:04.513\r\nOne of these days,\r\nI'm gonna nail his feet to the ground.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.198 --\u003e 00:05:25.784\r\nYou don't want us to touch the drill.\r\nRight, Mr. Fox?\r\n\r\n00:05:26.201 --\u003e 00:05:27.702\r\nNot unless you have to.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.786 --\u003e 00:05:31.373\r\nAnd be careful, it's the only working\r\nprototype from our lab in Chicago.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.623 --\u003e 00:05:34.334\r\nAnd I don't wanna be the guy who\r\nhas to tell Mr. Wayne it broke\r\n\r\n00:05:34.417 --\u003e 00:05:36.657\r\nbefore we got it to headquarters\r\nfor the final shakedown.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.128 --\u003e 00:05:39.422\r\nBut I thought you said\r\nit could be dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.548 --\u003e 00:05:42.592\r\nWell, it's intended for use\r\nin building excavations,\r\n\r\n00:05:42.676 --\u003e 00:05:44.845\r\noil rigs and the like, but...\r\n\r\n00:05:45.011 --\u003e 00:05:49.516\r\nRelax, kid. That gizmo ain't gonna hurt\r\nnobody as long as Harvey Bullock's-\r\n\r\n00:05:49.641 --\u003e 00:05:51.935\r\n- What the...\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:55.063 --\u003e 00:05:56.940\r\n(ALL GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.094 --\u003e 00:06:29.097\r\n- Who are you?\r\n- What do you want?\r\n\r\n00:06:29.389 --\u003e 00:06:33.476\r\nThe first thing I want is for you\r\nto stop asking stupid questions.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.977 --\u003e 00:06:39.190\r\nThe second is a powerful weapon,\r\nand I think your drill will do nicely.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.399 --\u003e 00:06:40.734\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:50.744 --\u003e 00:06:54.497\r\nAnd I think you'll do 10 to\r\n20 in Stonegate, minimum.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.123 --\u003e 00:06:56.666\r\nThe Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.334 --\u003e 00:07:00.170\r\nI suppose this had to\r\nhappen sooner or later.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.297 --\u003e 00:07:03.465\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.597 --\u003e 00:07:12.098\r\n(BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:07:14.809 --\u003e 00:07:15.936\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:24.819 --\u003e 00:07:25.987\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:07:26.488 --\u003e 00:07:27.739\r\nVERTIGO: You.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.823 --\u003e 00:07:29.866\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:07:33.703 --\u003e 00:07:35.330\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:44.839 --\u003e 00:07:47.801\r\nCome. We're due back by\r\nthe tolling of the hour.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.304 --\u003e 00:07:52.973\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:08:06.444 --\u003e 00:08:08.196\r\n(ALL GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:08:14.995 --\u003e 00:08:16.287\r\nALFRED: But are you certain\r\n\r\n00:08:16.371 --\u003e 00:08:18.915\r\nthe lady in black was working\r\nwith this Vertigo chap?\r\n\r\n00:08:19.332 --\u003e 00:08:23.586\r\nHad to be, Alfred. He'd never have been\r\nable to escape if she hadn't shown up.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.795 --\u003e 00:08:26.065\r\nAnd she was the only one who\r\nwasn't affected by his weapon.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.089 --\u003e 00:08:28.883\r\n- Weapon, sir?\r\n- That eyepiece of his.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.342 --\u003e 00:08:31.720\r\nI think it gives off\r\nsome kind of radiation.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.803 --\u003e 00:08:35.140\r\nIt must distort visual perception\r\nand sense of balance somehow,\r\n\r\n00:08:35.223 --\u003e 00:08:38.685\r\ncreating the illusion that\r\neverything around you is topsy-turvy.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.102 --\u003e 00:08:41.312\r\n- My word.\r\n- Not that it matters.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.521 --\u003e 00:08:44.357\r\nNothing about that can give me\r\nany clues to his whereabouts.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.566 --\u003e 00:08:48.111\r\nHe mentioned returning to his base\r\nbefore the \"tolling of the hour,\"\r\n\r\n00:08:48.194 --\u003e 00:08:52.032\r\nwhich suggests a clock tower,\r\nor church bell. Then fled west.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.365 --\u003e 00:08:54.909\r\nYet there's no such structure\r\nthat could conceal a hideout,\r\n\r\n00:08:54.993 --\u003e 00:08:56.870\r\nnot within 50 miles to the west.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.953 --\u003e 00:09:00.165\r\nMight I suggest, Master\r\nBruce, that you take a break?\r\n\r\n00:09:00.290 --\u003e 00:09:03.752\r\nIf you keep pushing yourself like\r\nthis, you soon won't know\r\n\r\n00:09:03.835 --\u003e 00:09:06.963\r\n- your right hand from your left.\r\n- Alfred, you're brilliant!\r\n\r\n00:09:07.047 --\u003e 00:09:08.590\r\nYes, so I've heard.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.090 --\u003e 00:09:10.675\r\nWith my head turned\r\naround like that,\r\n\r\n00:09:10.759 --\u003e 00:09:12.719\r\nI couldn't tell one\r\ndirection from the other.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.802 --\u003e 00:09:15.597\r\nThey didn't escape to the\r\nwest, they went east.\r\n\r\n00:09:21.519 --\u003e 00:09:24.439\r\nThere, Alfred.\r\nThat has to be the place.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.847 --\u003e 00:09:59.099\r\n(RUSTLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:06.689 --\u003e 00:10:07.941\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:14.614 --\u003e 00:10:16.699\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:10:19.285 --\u003e 00:10:20.578\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:28.920 --\u003e 00:10:30.588\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:50.400 --\u003e 00:10:52.652\r\nFour against one. Nasty odds.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.328 --\u003e 00:11:05.582\r\n- I can take care of myself, thank you.\r\n- So I see.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.166 --\u003e 00:11:09.460\r\n- Still, the gesture is appreciated.\r\n- Don't mention it.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.836 --\u003e 00:11:12.672\r\n- Just whose side are you on?\r\n- That would be telling.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.755 --\u003e 00:11:14.382\r\nGUARD: And it would\r\nmake no difference.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.178 --\u003e 00:11:21.389\r\nAs of now, this battle is ended.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.807 --\u003e 00:11:24.601\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:29.856 --\u003e 00:11:31.608\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.066 --\u003e 00:11:33.318\r\n(WOMAN SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:11:46.748 --\u003e 00:11:48.124\r\n(DOOR SHUTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:05.808 --\u003e 00:12:09.229\r\n- Filthy creature.\r\n- I've been called worse.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.481 --\u003e 00:12:13.983\r\nWhat happened to... My mask!\r\n\r\n00:12:14.734 --\u003e 00:12:18.112\r\n- What have you done with it?\r\n- Easier to clean your wounds this way.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.196 --\u003e 00:12:20.823\r\nThen you know.\r\nYou know that I'm...\r\n\r\n00:12:21.199 --\u003e 00:12:24.452\r\nHush. Who knows what other\r\nears may be listening?\r\n\r\n00:12:27.872 --\u003e 00:12:30.833\r\nJust who are you?\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:12:31.251 --\u003e 00:12:33.253\r\nMy name is Talia.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.336 --\u003e 00:12:36.297\r\nAnd I, too, have business\r\nwith the Society of Shadows.\r\n\r\n00:12:36.506 --\u003e 00:12:39.259\r\n- What kind of business?\r\n- Personal business.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.509 --\u003e 00:12:42.095\r\nSuch as I imagine yours must be.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.637 --\u003e 00:12:45.807\r\nPoint taken.\r\nIt's a simple enough lock.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.140 --\u003e 00:12:48.393\r\nI can get it open it with...\r\nMy belt!\r\n\r\n00:12:48.601 --\u003e 00:12:50.103\r\nHow unfortunate.\r\n\r\n00:12:51.229 --\u003e 00:12:54.899\r\nI appreciate the sympathy,\r\nbut what we need right now is a lock pick.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.983 --\u003e 00:12:56.150\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.821 --\u003e 00:13:01.072\r\n(PIN JINGLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:03.992 --\u003e 00:13:06.786\r\nWe make a good team,\r\ndon't you think?\r\n\r\n00:13:11.874 --\u003e 00:13:13.584\r\nNow, come. Quickly.\r\n\r\n00:13:14.043 --\u003e 00:13:17.880\r\nThere's no telling what evil Vertigo\r\nmay do with your sonic device.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.506 --\u003e 00:13:21.050\r\nSounds like you\r\ntwo have a history.\r\n\r\n00:13:23.386 --\u003e 00:13:25.888\r\nYes. The man once\r\nworked for my father.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.264 --\u003e 00:13:29.976\r\nUntil Father at last came to\r\nrecognize the blackness in his soul.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.271 --\u003e 00:13:34.564\r\n(GUARDS GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:13:35.273 --\u003e 00:13:39.652\r\nWhen he learned of Vertigo's intentions,\r\nmy father sent me as his emissary\r\n\r\n00:13:39.736 --\u003e 00:13:42.572\r\nto keep the device out\r\nof Vertigo's hands.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.114 --\u003e 00:13:45.950\r\nHow kind of him.\r\nWhy should your father even care?\r\n\r\n00:13:46.284 --\u003e 00:13:49.454\r\nBecause he is concerned\r\nfor all humankind.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.540 --\u003e 00:13:56.753\r\n- This way. It leads to the lab.\r\n- Lab? What lab?\r\n\r\n00:14:13.394 --\u003e 00:14:15.563\r\nUnlocked. How convenient.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.646 --\u003e 00:14:18.524\r\nYou do, of course,\r\nrealize that this is a trap.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.941 --\u003e 00:14:21.819\r\nNaturally,\r\nbut what other choice do we have?\r\n\r\n00:14:27.158 --\u003e 00:14:28.368\r\n- (SCREECHING)\r\n- (BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:14:32.747 --\u003e 00:14:34.290\r\nWelcome, friends.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.874 --\u003e 00:14:39.087\r\nYou're quite right,\r\nI have been expecting you.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.253 --\u003e 00:14:41.005\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:09.158 --\u003e 00:15:12.286\r\nYour little dizzifying trick\r\nwon't stop us, Vertigo.\r\n\r\n00:15:12.620 --\u003e 00:15:14.288\r\nMaybe, maybe not.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.497 --\u003e 00:15:17.834\r\nYou see, you'll have to\r\nget across this room alive.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.126 --\u003e 00:15:22.255\r\nAnd that may prove difficult,\r\nconsidering this entire laboratory\r\n\r\n00:15:22.338 --\u003e 00:15:24.590\r\nhas been rigged to destroy you.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.757 --\u003e 00:15:31.222\r\nOh. And in case you think that once I go\r\nmy disorienting effect will go with me,\r\n\r\n00:15:31.305 --\u003e 00:15:32.890\r\nthink again.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.391 --\u003e 00:15:36.978\r\nI've planted duplicate vertigo\r\ndevices throughout the room\r\n\r\n00:15:37.061 --\u003e 00:15:40.314\r\nto maintain the effect\r\nonce I've departed.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.731 --\u003e 00:15:44.569\r\nGoodbye and good luck.\r\nYou'll need it.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.489 --\u003e 00:15:50.116\r\n(BOTH GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.535 --\u003e 00:15:54.954\r\n- You okay?\r\n- My contact lenses.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.204 --\u003e 00:15:58.249\r\nI lost them when we fell.\r\nThey counter the distortion effect.\r\n\r\n00:15:58.332 --\u003e 00:16:00.251\r\nWithout them,\r\nI'm as helpless as you.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.543 --\u003e 00:16:02.670\r\nI don't do \"helpless.\"\r\n\r\n00:16:05.506 --\u003e 00:16:08.509\r\nCome on, take my hand.\r\nI can get us through this.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.634 --\u003e 00:16:12.263\r\n- How?\r\n- I trusted you, now it's your turn.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.989 --\u003e 00:16:31.324\r\n(TALIA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.407 --\u003e 00:16:32.617\r\nBATMAN: Jump!\r\n\r\n00:16:37.205 --\u003e 00:16:39.248\r\nHow did you know?\r\n\r\n00:16:45.004 --\u003e 00:16:46.339\r\nBATMAN: Down!\r\n\r\n00:16:51.385 --\u003e 00:16:53.054\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:17:06.776 --\u003e 00:17:08.236\r\nClear.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.612 --\u003e 00:17:11.405\r\nHow did you do that?\r\n\r\n00:17:12.156 --\u003e 00:17:14.742\r\nSimple.\r\nI just kept my eyes closed.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.826 --\u003e 00:17:16.994\r\nYou what?\r\n\r\n00:17:17.495 --\u003e 00:17:19.705\r\nThe only way to neutralize\r\nthe vertigo effect\r\n\r\n00:17:19.789 --\u003e 00:17:22.542\r\nwas to rely on my other\r\nsenses to see us through.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.917 --\u003e 00:17:26.546\r\nAll right, I am impressed.\r\nNow where to?\r\n\r\n00:17:30.132 --\u003e 00:17:32.260\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:17:38.349 --\u003e 00:17:39.517\r\nUp.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.256 --\u003e 00:18:13.134\r\n- BATMAN: Going somewhere, Vertigo?\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.384 --\u003e 00:18:16.304\r\n- It's impossible!\r\n- BATMAN: Nothing is impossible.\r\n\r\n00:18:19.223 --\u003e 00:18:21.601\r\nThen I will finish\r\nyou both myself.\r\n\r\n00:18:22.226 --\u003e 00:18:23.853\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:35.156 --\u003e 00:18:36.824\r\n- (RUMBLING)\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:47.585 --\u003e 00:18:49.545\r\nI can't take much more of this.\r\n\r\n00:18:49.920 --\u003e 00:18:52.048\r\nOnly one thing to do.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.341 --\u003e 00:18:54.383\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.098 --\u003e 00:19:02.266\r\n(BELL RINGS)\r\n\r\n00:19:02.767 --\u003e 00:19:05.102\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:31.295 --\u003e 00:19:32.838\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.938 --\u003e 00:19:50.418\r\nBATMAN: Without\r\nVertigo to lead them,\r\n\r\n00:19:50.481 --\u003e 00:19:51.941\r\nhis agents have all fled?\r\n\r\n00:19:52.274 --\u003e 00:19:56.195\r\nYes. The Society of Shadows\r\nis no longer what it was.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.659 --\u003e 00:20:05.454\r\nWell, I've gotta get\r\nthis back to Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:20:07.373 --\u003e 00:20:10.459\r\nWait. I can't let\r\nyou leave like this,\r\n\r\n00:20:10.918 --\u003e 00:20:12.461\r\nnot with the drill.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.548 --\u003e 00:20:17.967\r\nI thought I finally knew\r\nwhich side you were on.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.509 --\u003e 00:20:20.052\r\nI should have known better,\r\n\r\n00:20:20.136 --\u003e 00:20:23.055\r\nconsidering that you knew where\r\neverything was in the monastery.\r\n\r\n00:20:23.139 --\u003e 00:20:24.515\r\nHow could you have,\r\n\r\n00:20:25.057 --\u003e 00:20:26.642\r\nunless you were one of them?\r\n\r\n00:20:31.564 --\u003e 00:20:34.942\r\nI am truly sorry, Batman.\r\nIt could have been...\r\n\r\n00:20:35.568 --\u003e 00:20:36.736\r\nSweet.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.992 --\u003e 00:20:45.161\r\nThis is not over.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.457 --\u003e 00:20:51.876\r\nVertigo has been dealt\r\nwith, Father.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.626 --\u003e 00:20:54.795\r\nMAN: Small wonder\r\nyou seem so pleased.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.588 --\u003e 00:20:58.299\r\n- Then your mission?\r\n- A complete success.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.924 --\u003e 00:21:01.093\r\n\u003ci\u003eI secured this\r\njust as you asked.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:01.177 --\u003e 00:21:03.429\r\nThen choose a target and test\r\nit, daughter.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.679 --\u003e 00:21:07.099\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe must be certain it has\r\nsurvived its ordeal intact.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:19.528 --\u003e 00:21:20.613\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:20.738 --\u003e 00:21:21.739\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:21:22.072 --\u003e 00:21:23.240\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:21:25.993 --\u003e 00:21:28.871\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe Batman,\r\nhe sabotaged it somehow!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:29.455 --\u003e 00:21:31.040\r\nSo, even in defeat,\r\n\r\n00:21:31.123 --\u003e 00:21:35.544\r\nthe detective manages to achieve\r\nsome small measure of victory.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.130 --\u003e 00:21:42.885\r\nAs you said, Detective,\r\nthis is not over.\r\n\r\n00:21:47.431 --\u003e 00:21:49.016\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:13.624 --\u003e 00:22:14.625\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E45 - What Is Reality (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.797 --\u003e 00:00:07.341\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.914 --\u003e 00:01:22.124\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.261 --\u003e 00:01:35.304\r\n(ATM BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:36.513 --\u003e 00:01:39.349\r\nHuh? \"Where does a\r\n500-pound gorilla sleep?\"\r\n\r\n00:01:39.433 --\u003e 00:01:40.713\r\nWhat is this, some kind of joke?\r\n\r\n00:01:42.060 --\u003e 00:01:43.061\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:01:44.521 --\u003e 00:01:46.523\r\nListen, you stupid\r\nmachine, I want my money.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.988 --\u003e 00:01:54.239\r\n(BEEPING RAPIDLY)\r\n\r\n00:01:55.907 --\u003e 00:01:59.995\r\nHey! Stupid machine,\r\ngive me back my money.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.078 --\u003e 00:02:02.539\r\nHey! Who's in there?\r\nAnybody in there?\r\n\r\n00:02:03.915 --\u003e 00:02:06.209\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.502 --\u003e 00:02:09.504\r\nMAN 1: Sell any market.\r\nMAN 2: Fill or kill.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.588 --\u003e 00:02:12.049\r\nMAN 1: Bid me 20,000.\r\nWOMAN 1: The market's on fire.\r\n\r\n00:02:12.132 --\u003e 00:02:13.884\r\nMAN 1: We're taking\r\na bath on that one.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.967 --\u003e 00:02:15.302\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:02:15.385 --\u003e 00:02:16.946\r\nWhat's with the bell?\r\nThe market doesn't close\r\n\r\n00:02:16.970 --\u003e 00:02:18.388\r\nfor another 15 minutes.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.350 --\u003e 00:02:23.727\r\n\"What's worse than a\r\nmillipede with flat feet?\"\r\n\r\n00:02:24.269 --\u003e 00:02:27.272\r\nGood Lord, we've got a\r\ncomputer vandal on our hands.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.691 --\u003e 00:02:30.984\r\nDICK: Stop whining, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.068 --\u003e 00:02:34.279\r\nIf you think the ticket's a mistake,\r\nyou'll get a chance tell the whole story\r\n\r\n00:02:34.363 --\u003e 00:02:35.822\r\nto the clerk when\r\nwe get up there.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.947 --\u003e 00:02:37.783\r\nIf I live that long.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.075 --\u003e 00:02:39.409\r\nCLERK: I'm sorry, folks,\r\n\r\n00:02:39.660 --\u003e 00:02:41.203\r\nyou'll just have to be patient.\r\n\r\n00:02:41.286 --\u003e 00:02:43.038\r\nThe computers are still down.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.373 --\u003e 00:02:48.543\r\n\"How do you get five\r\nelephants into a compact car?\"\r\n\r\n00:03:01.348 --\u003e 00:03:04.559\r\nREPORTER 1: There he is.\r\nREPORTER 2: Commissioner, look here.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.268 --\u003e 00:03:07.121\r\nIs it true about the clue?\r\nWhat about the riddles?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.145 --\u003e 00:03:09.707\r\nREPORTER 1: Have any new proof?\r\nREPORTER 2: Any truth to the riddles?\r\n\r\n00:03:09.731 --\u003e 00:03:11.531\r\nCommissioner,\r\ncan you give me just one answer?\r\n\r\n00:03:11.608 --\u003e 00:03:13.402\r\n(REPORTERS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:03:13.485 --\u003e 00:03:14.861\r\nSo, what's the story on this?\r\n\r\n00:03:15.237 --\u003e 00:03:17.531\r\nWe're doing everything we can.\r\nNo more questions.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.281 --\u003e 00:03:19.408\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.621 --\u003e 00:03:27.124\r\nBATMAN: Looks like Edward\r\nNygma's making a comeback.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.417 --\u003e 00:03:29.543\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nYeah, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.132 --\u003e 00:03:38.844\r\nHe's deleting all his files from\r\nevery police database we can access.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.469 --\u003e 00:03:41.179\r\nLook, he's left no trace\r\n\r\n00:03:41.263 --\u003e 00:03:43.223\r\nof any driver's license\r\nor social security number.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.141 --\u003e 00:03:47.227\r\nNo bank accounts, credit cards,\r\nnot even a birth certificate.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.477 --\u003e 00:03:48.937\r\nAs if he never existed.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.020 --\u003e 00:03:50.939\r\nBut what about the\r\nhard copies of-\r\n\r\n00:03:51.022 --\u003e 00:03:52.566\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:52.649 --\u003e 00:03:53.900\r\nGordon here.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.652 --\u003e 00:03:58.530\r\nWhat? Someone just\r\ndelivered a crate downstairs\r\n\r\n00:03:58.613 --\u003e 00:04:00.449\r\nwith question marks\r\npainted on it.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.033 --\u003e 00:04:03.368\r\nAnd it's ticking.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.454 --\u003e 00:04:09.416\r\nMove it, people. Gordon's orders.\r\nWe need this area cleared now.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.743 --\u003e 00:04:45.786\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:04:46.328 --\u003e 00:04:48.413\r\nROBIN: Gently, gently.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.872 --\u003e 00:04:50.373\r\nWe'll never get\r\nit open this way.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.582 --\u003e 00:04:54.836\r\nWhat we've got here is a variation\r\non the ancient Chinese puzzle box.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.128 --\u003e 00:04:57.339\r\n- Can you solve it?\r\n- You kidding?\r\n\r\n00:04:57.422 --\u003e 00:05:01.760\r\nYou're looking at the guy who solved\r\nthe Baxter's box puzzle in 37 seconds.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.885 --\u003e 00:05:04.638\r\nOf course, this time I\r\ndon't have a sledgehammer.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.763 --\u003e 00:05:06.765\r\n(BOX TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:09.100 --\u003e 00:05:10.227\r\nA-ha!\r\n\r\n00:05:17.734 --\u003e 00:05:18.985\r\n(ALARM BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:19.069 --\u003e 00:05:20.195\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.952 --\u003e 00:05:27.994\r\n(ALARM STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.912 --\u003e 00:05:32.165\r\n- Some kind of threat?\r\n- More like an invitation.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.127 --\u003e 00:05:38.755\r\nCareful, vigilante.\r\nYou know what they say,\r\n\r\n00:05:38.839 --\u003e 00:05:41.007\r\ncuriosity killed the Bat.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.259 --\u003e 00:05:44.511\r\nTHUG: These the papers you\r\nwanted, Mr. Nygma?\r\n\r\n00:05:48.139 --\u003e 00:05:49.933\r\nOf course, they are.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.058 --\u003e 00:05:53.144\r\nDid you make certain these\r\nare the only existing copies?\r\n\r\n00:05:55.689 --\u003e 00:05:56.815\r\nThey'd better be.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.366 --\u003e 00:06:07.909\r\nAny idea what these are?\r\n\r\n00:06:09.077 --\u003e 00:06:11.037\r\nThat's what we were\r\nhoping you could tell us.\r\n\r\n00:06:11.329 --\u003e 00:06:13.164\r\nI've got other leads to follow.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.248 --\u003e 00:06:15.959\r\nMeantime, I want you to search\r\nevery inch of that mainframe.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.459 --\u003e 00:06:19.629\r\nAnd if you find anything\r\nunusual, inform me immediately.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.803 --\u003e 00:06:29.264\r\nBATMAN: \"Where does a\r\n500-pound gorilla sleep?\"\r\n\r\n00:06:29.389 --\u003e 00:06:32.058\r\n\"What's worse than a\r\nmillipede with flat feet?\"\r\n\r\n00:06:32.142 --\u003e 00:06:35.270\r\nAnd, \"How do you get five\r\nelephants into a compact car?\"\r\n\r\n00:06:35.353 --\u003e 00:06:37.814\r\nAnywhere it wants,\r\na giraffe with a sore throat,\r\n\r\n00:06:37.898 --\u003e 00:06:41.443\r\nand two in the front seat,\r\ntwo in back, and one in the trunk.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.526 --\u003e 00:06:43.236\r\nYeah, yeah, I know. I know.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.320 --\u003e 00:06:46.907\r\nAny schoolboy knows those.\r\nBut brainteasers are the Riddler's M.O.,\r\n\r\n00:06:46.990 --\u003e 00:06:48.950\r\nnot corny old jokes like these.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.034 --\u003e 00:06:52.412\r\nPerhaps the questions are the\r\nclues, not the answers.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.746 --\u003e 00:06:55.624\r\nFor example,\r\nthey all seem to involve animals.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.707 --\u003e 00:06:57.500\r\nAlso numbers.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.584 --\u003e 00:06:59.419\r\nA 500-pound gorilla.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.628 --\u003e 00:07:01.880\r\nA millipede, meaning 1,000 legs.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.422 --\u003e 00:07:03.798\r\nAnd five elephants.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.924 --\u003e 00:07:05.926\r\nNow, let's convert\r\nthem to Roman numerals.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.468 --\u003e 00:07:08.970\r\n- Look.\r\n- ALFRED: D-M-V.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.095 --\u003e 00:07:11.765\r\nBOTH: Department\r\nof Motor Vehicles.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.682 --\u003e 00:07:14.225\r\nBut I recall you mentioning\r\n\r\n00:07:14.309 --\u003e 00:07:16.603\r\nhe'd already obliterated\r\nhis records there,\r\n\r\n00:07:16.686 --\u003e 00:07:18.229\r\nso why return?\r\n\r\n00:07:18.313 --\u003e 00:07:20.023\r\nBATMAN: For the hard copy.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.824 --\u003e 00:07:31.159\r\n- (BATARANG WHIZZES)\r\n- (EXC LAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:07:39.042 --\u003e 00:07:40.293\r\n(THUG GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:04.859 --\u003e 00:08:06.820\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:12.075 --\u003e 00:08:13.284\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:15.495 --\u003e 00:08:17.247\r\nTHUG: Come on,\r\nwe're out of here.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.590 --\u003e 00:08:28.717\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:08:38.560 --\u003e 00:08:39.769\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:42.439 --\u003e 00:08:45.900\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLERz Now, well,\r\nI never was any good at parallel parking.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:46.234 --\u003e 00:08:50.196\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I'm not too clear on the laws\r\nabout pedestrian right-of-way either.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:50.321 --\u003e 00:08:51.990\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:58.663 --\u003e 00:09:00.165\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:04.002 --\u003e 00:09:05.545\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.258 --\u003e 00:09:13.720\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: Now, while you're disabling\r\nmy van, you might wish to consider\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:13.803 --\u003e 00:09:17.932\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe effect of the imminent collision\r\non the nitroglycerin inside.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:19.392 --\u003e 00:09:20.435\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:21.311 --\u003e 00:09:22.479\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.271 --\u003e 00:09:25.190\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.865 --\u003e 00:09:36.409\r\nYour message sounded urgent.\r\nFound something?\r\n\r\n00:09:36.493 --\u003e 00:09:38.828\r\nYou bet your...\r\nI mean, yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.912 --\u003e 00:09:40.663\r\nIt's a virtual-reality program.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.747 --\u003e 00:09:43.792\r\nInstead of using a keyboard or\r\njoystick, you put this puppy on\r\n\r\n00:09:43.875 --\u003e 00:09:46.628\r\nand enter a whole\r\ncomputer-generated world\r\n\r\n00:09:46.711 --\u003e 00:09:49.798\r\nand interact with everything in\r\nit, as if it actually existed.\r\n\r\n00:09:49.881 --\u003e 00:09:51.007\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:09:53.218 --\u003e 00:09:54.427\r\nJust watch the screen.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.183 --\u003e 00:10:02.727\r\nA pixel is worth 1,000 words.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.811 --\u003e 00:10:04.729\r\nCare to try it, Commissioner?\r\n\r\n00:10:09.776 --\u003e 00:10:11.277\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:10:17.617 --\u003e 00:10:20.787\r\nSort of like playing a computer\r\ngame from the inside, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:10:20.870 --\u003e 00:10:23.915\r\nAmazing, it even feels real.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.040 --\u003e 00:10:26.751\r\nThe military's been experimenting\r\nwith virtual reality\r\n\r\n00:10:26.835 --\u003e 00:10:28.211\r\nfor combat simulation.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.294 --\u003e 00:10:31.089\r\nGORDON: And what's Nygma doing with it?\r\nROBIN: Nothing now.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.381 --\u003e 00:10:34.217\r\nHe can't access this computer,\r\nit's not hooked up to a phone line.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.300 --\u003e 00:10:37.178\r\n- Why'd he want us to find it?\r\n- Good question.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.262 --\u003e 00:10:40.390\r\nBut there's no way to know till\r\nI go through all the files.\r\n\r\n00:10:40.557 --\u003e 00:10:42.851\r\nGuess I should get back to\r\nwork after I grab a snack.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.934 --\u003e 00:10:44.894\r\n- You hungry?\r\n- No, thanks.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.736 --\u003e 00:10:55.363\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:10:58.992 --\u003e 00:11:03.079\r\nBatman's young friend is fairly clever,\r\nbut he doesn't have all the answers.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.163 --\u003e 00:11:04.164\r\n(GORDON GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:08.459 --\u003e 00:11:09.859\r\n- (ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n- (GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.177 --\u003e 00:11:18.469\r\n(ROBIN SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:11:37.405 --\u003e 00:11:40.116\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:11:51.711 --\u003e 00:11:54.589\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: Ask me no questions,\r\nI'll tell you no tales.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:54.797 --\u003e 00:11:56.758\r\nAnother riddle, Nygma?\r\n\r\n00:11:57.717 --\u003e 00:12:01.137\r\n\u003ci\u003eRWJDLER: It all makes\r\nsense when you add it up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:08.686 --\u003e 00:12:10.813\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: Four quarters and a\r\npenny, sir?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:11.147 --\u003e 00:12:16.194\r\nPenny, penny. Cent, red cent.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.527 --\u003e 00:12:18.738\r\nCopper, it's made of copper.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.821 --\u003e 00:12:21.699\r\nAnd \"copper\" is another\r\nword for \"policeman.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:22.158 --\u003e 00:12:24.869\r\nAnd \"no tails\" would be heads.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.119 --\u003e 00:12:27.830\r\nPolice, head, quarters.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.956 --\u003e 00:12:29.666\r\nALFRED: \u003ci\u003ePolice\u003c/i\u003e headquarters.\r\n\r\n00:12:29.916 --\u003e 00:12:31.376\r\nBravo, sir.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.459 --\u003e 00:12:34.045\r\nIt does make sense\r\nwhen you add it up.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.128 --\u003e 00:12:38.007\r\nAnd four quarters and\r\none penny make 101 cents.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.132 --\u003e 00:12:39.509\r\nSo...\r\n\r\n00:12:41.469 --\u003e 00:12:43.680\r\nPolice headquarters, room 101.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.225 --\u003e 00:12:49.435\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:53.481 --\u003e 00:12:54.816\r\nThe commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.703 --\u003e 00:13:08.371\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:09.789 --\u003e 00:13:11.291\r\nVirtual reality?\r\n\r\n00:13:11.708 --\u003e 00:13:13.668\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: Quite so, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:14.335 --\u003e 00:13:17.463\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd everything your commissioner\r\nis experiencing in here\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:17.547 --\u003e 00:13:20.967\r\n\u003ci\u003eseems so real to him,\r\nit might as well be real.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:21.217 --\u003e 00:13:24.679\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'd give his heart another 15\r\nminutes, at most.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:25.013 --\u003e 00:13:26.306\r\nHe can't be online.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.267 --\u003e 00:13:30.351\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:30.435 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\nI searched through every file.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.729 --\u003e 00:13:34.147\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou searched the software.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:34.230 --\u003e 00:13:36.524\r\nHad you bothered to\r\nexamine the hardware,\r\n\r\n00:13:36.607 --\u003e 00:13:39.444\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou would have discovered\r\na cordless modem line.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:40.153 --\u003e 00:13:41.779\r\n\u003ci\u003eI wouldn't do that, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:42.905 --\u003e 00:13:44.949\r\n\u003ci\u003eDisconnecting Gordon\r\nwould be fatal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:45.033 --\u003e 00:13:49.412\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe sudden stop would be like\r\nslamming into a brick wall at 400 mph.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:50.288 --\u003e 00:13:53.624\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo, if you wish to get\r\nGordon out alive, Batman,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:53.708 --\u003e 00:13:55.585\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou'll have to come\r\nin here and get him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:56.002 --\u003e 00:13:58.046\r\nForget it.\r\nThe Riddler controls that world.\r\n\r\n00:13:58.129 --\u003e 00:13:59.297\r\nYou wouldn't last a minute.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.422 --\u003e 00:14:00.590\r\nWe'll use these.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.673 --\u003e 00:14:02.717\r\nThey'll let me keep\r\none ear in reality,\r\n\r\n00:14:02.800 --\u003e 00:14:04.260\r\nso stay in touch.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:07.013\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.190 --\u003e 00:14:22.111\r\nOne door leads to a plane\r\nwhere kings and queens contend.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.612 --\u003e 00:14:24.092\r\n- Can you find it?\r\n- (THUNDER RUMBLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:25.281 --\u003e 00:14:27.700\r\n- Suggestions, partner?\r\n- I'm working on it.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.803 --\u003e 00:14:47.845\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:48.429 --\u003e 00:14:50.973\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:53.059 --\u003e 00:14:57.105\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: A pity you can't\r\nearn extra lives in this game.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:02.527 --\u003e 00:15:06.572\r\nQuite an experience, being riddled\r\nwith questions, isn't it, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:15:13.162 --\u003e 00:15:14.956\r\n\u003ci\u003eROBIN: Batman,\r\ndon't open that door.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:15.039 --\u003e 00:15:17.291\r\n\"Crazy intent\" means...\r\n\r\n00:15:17.375 --\u003e 00:15:18.793\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"Loco motive.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:18.876 --\u003e 00:15:20.253\r\n(TRAIN HORN BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:15:24.549 --\u003e 00:15:27.343\r\nI suppose you expect me to\r\nbelieve you planned that.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.594 --\u003e 00:15:31.722\r\nBut you still haven't\r\nfound the right door.\r\n\r\n00:15:32.223 --\u003e 00:15:34.225\r\n\u003ci\u003eROBIN: Batman,\r\nI think I figured out the clue.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:34.392 --\u003e 00:15:38.104\r\nThe plane where kings and queens\r\ncontend could mean a chessboard.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.438 --\u003e 00:15:41.441\r\n\u003ci\u003eIs there a door marked\r\n\"checkmate\" or \"black and white\"?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:43.234 --\u003e 00:15:45.361\r\n\"4096.\"\r\n\r\n00:15:45.445 --\u003e 00:15:46.737\r\nWait a minute.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.821 --\u003e 00:15:49.615\r\nThere are 64 squares on a\r\nchessboard, right?\r\n\r\n00:15:49.699 --\u003e 00:15:51.325\r\nROBIN: Yeah. So?\r\n\r\n00:15:51.409 --\u003e 00:15:55.121\r\nSo, 4096 is 64 squared.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.172 --\u003e 00:16:07.300\r\nOnly you can put the king in\r\ncheck, vigilante.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.976 --\u003e 00:16:21.189\r\nMove according to the rules,\r\nor it's the end of the day.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.122 --\u003e 00:16:39.207\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:40.791 --\u003e 00:16:42.293\r\nWrong move, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.805 --\u003e 00:16:57.558\r\nI've got it.\r\nThey call you the Dark Knight, right?\r\n\r\n00:16:57.642 --\u003e 00:16:59.727\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen you have to\r\nmove like a knight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:01.812 --\u003e 00:17:04.065\r\nThat's it. Two up, one across,\r\n\r\n00:17:04.148 --\u003e 00:17:07.276\r\n'cause a wrong move means\r\n\"the end of the day,\" or...\r\n\r\n00:17:07.443 --\u003e 00:17:09.529\r\n\"Knight fall,\" of course.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.201 --\u003e 00:17:17.995\r\nNygma, what are you up to now?\r\n\r\n00:17:20.540 --\u003e 00:17:21.999\r\nAnd why this?\r\n\r\n00:17:22.166 --\u003e 00:17:25.836\r\nThat is for me to know and you to\r\ndeduce, Dark Knight.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.797 --\u003e 00:17:29.215\r\nBATMAN: If this is a clue,\r\n\r\n00:17:29.298 --\u003e 00:17:31.842\r\ncould it have something\r\nto do with the Pegasus?\r\n\r\n00:17:31.926 --\u003e 00:17:35.555\r\nDon't look at me.\r\nI flunked Greek mythology, remember?\r\n\r\n00:17:35.763 --\u003e 00:17:37.890\r\nHis clues always have\r\na double meaning.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.974 --\u003e 00:17:40.685\r\nSo, if Pegasus is also the\r\nname of a constellation-\r\n\r\n00:17:40.810 --\u003e 00:17:42.353\r\nNow, astronomy I do know.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.436 --\u003e 00:17:44.146\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou're in Orion now.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:47.358 --\u003e 00:17:48.651\r\n(ARROW WHIZZES)\r\n\r\n00:17:49.652 --\u003e 00:17:51.654\r\n\u003ci\u003eROBIN: So you wanna\r\nkeep going past Taurus,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:51.737 --\u003e 00:17:53.864\r\nthen hang a sharp\r\nright at Andromeda.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.873 --\u003e 00:18:05.918\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd that should put you right\r\nin the constellation Pegasus.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:06.210 --\u003e 00:18:07.378\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:14.010 --\u003e 00:18:15.595\r\n(GLASS BREAKS)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.720 --\u003e 00:18:16.929\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:20.808 --\u003e 00:18:24.020\r\nWelcome to Riddlerville, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.145 --\u003e 00:18:27.857\r\nThings are a little mixed-up here,\r\nbut I'm sure you can fix that.\r\n\r\n00:18:28.149 --\u003e 00:18:31.193\r\nYour commissioner is\r\ncontained within this cube.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.319 --\u003e 00:18:34.322\r\nSolve the puzzle,\r\nand you gain access.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.614 --\u003e 00:18:36.449\r\nNo problemo, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.532 --\u003e 00:18:39.035\r\nThat's a Baxter's box.\r\nI can guide you through it-\r\n\r\n00:18:39.118 --\u003e 00:18:40.411\r\n- (BEEPING)\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:40.494 --\u003e 00:18:42.830\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo coaching from\r\nthe peanut gallery.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:43.497 --\u003e 00:18:48.210\r\nYou have one minute, Batman.\r\nThen the clock strikes two.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.502 --\u003e 00:18:51.172\r\n- (CLOCK TICKING)\r\n- If you can do it, so can I.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.758 --\u003e 00:18:57.053\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- I should've known you'd cheat.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.388 --\u003e 00:19:01.098\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:05.186 --\u003e 00:19:08.939\r\nNice try, Batman, but in my\r\nworld, you play by my rules.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.023 --\u003e 00:19:11.567\r\nYou may control this\r\nworld, Nygma,\r\n\r\n00:19:11.692 --\u003e 00:19:14.570\r\nbut I still control myself.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.989 --\u003e 00:19:20.618\r\nThe name is Riddler.\r\nEdward Nygma no longer exists.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.951 --\u003e 00:19:24.747\r\nYou might recall that he was once\r\nfired by an ungrateful employer.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.830 --\u003e 00:19:27.958\r\nThat was a private matter,\r\nand should've remained one.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.584 --\u003e 00:19:31.796\r\nAttempted homicide is never\r\na private matter, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:19:32.213 --\u003e 00:19:34.256\r\nBut it would've been if\r\nyou hadn't interfered\r\n\r\n00:19:34.340 --\u003e 00:19:36.050\r\nand turned Nygma\r\ninto a fugitive.\r\n\r\n00:19:36.133 --\u003e 00:19:38.094\r\nSo I deleted Nygma,\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:41.389\r\njust like I'm about to delete\r\nyou, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.433 --\u003e 00:19:45.768\r\n(TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.020 --\u003e 00:19:50.481\r\nRIDDLER: We can keep this\r\nup as long as you can.\r\n\r\n00:19:50.606 --\u003e 00:19:53.818\r\nAny number you can think\r\nof, we can double.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.151 --\u003e 00:19:57.697\r\nTell me, Riddler, how can you\r\nsplit your focus in 32 directions\r\n\r\n00:19:57.863 --\u003e 00:20:01.117\r\nand sustain the concentration it\r\ntakes to keep your world together?\r\n\r\n00:20:01.283 --\u003e 00:20:03.994\r\n- You can't.\r\n- (SCREAMS) No!\r\n\r\n00:20:05.871 --\u003e 00:20:07.289\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:07.957 --\u003e 00:20:10.000\r\n(RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:20:27.935 --\u003e 00:20:29.061\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.186 --\u003e 00:20:31.355\r\nHuh? What happened?\r\n\r\n00:20:41.323 --\u003e 00:20:43.451\r\nI can escape that easily, too.\r\n\r\n00:20:44.994 --\u003e 00:20:50.082\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut then, if the planet were\r\nequitable, I'd still have my old job.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:50.833 --\u003e 00:20:54.587\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo, no, not yet. No!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:54.712 --\u003e 00:20:57.298\r\n(RIDDLER SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:58.048 --\u003e 00:20:59.675\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:20:59.759 --\u003e 00:21:01.969\r\nLooked like he suffered\r\nsome kind of attack.\r\n\r\n00:21:02.052 --\u003e 00:21:04.805\r\nLike a sensory\r\noverload or something.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.889 --\u003e 00:21:08.267\r\nBut we'll never know for sure\r\nbecause we'll never find him.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.350 --\u003e 00:21:12.146\r\nOh, no? Come on.\r\nI think he left us a clue.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.856 --\u003e 00:21:19.570\r\n\"If the planet were equitable,\r\nI'd still have my old job.\"\r\n\r\n00:21:19.653 --\u003e 00:21:24.825\r\nROBIN: Of course. \"If the world's\r\nfair, I'd still have my ex-position.\"\r\n\r\n00:21:24.909 --\u003e 00:21:26.660\r\nOh. Give me a break.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.331 --\u003e 00:21:31.582\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:21:31.665 --\u003e 00:21:35.002\r\nBATMAN: Looks like he didn't\r\nescape his virtual reality in time.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.128 --\u003e 00:21:39.048\r\nYou mean he's been trapped\r\ninside his own program?\r\n\r\n00:21:39.298 --\u003e 00:21:45.179\r\nCould be. And how to get him out\r\nmay be a riddle no one can solve.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.228 --\u003e 00:21:54.188\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.379 --\u003e 00:22:19.380\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E46 - The Laughing Fish (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.797 --\u003e 00:00:07.799\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:06.441 --\u003e 00:01:07.734\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:07.818 --\u003e 00:01:09.361\r\n(RAIN PATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:42.311 --\u003e 00:01:43.854\r\n(SHIP'S HORN BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:02:01.371 --\u003e 00:02:03.373\r\nOkay, let's see what we got.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.082 --\u003e 00:02:06.335\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING IN DISGUST)\r\n\r\n00:02:06.543 --\u003e 00:02:09.504\r\nOh, that's impossible.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.630 --\u003e 00:02:11.048\r\nI'm gonna be sick.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.173 --\u003e 00:02:12.174\r\nFISHERMAN: All of them...\r\n\r\n00:02:12.924 --\u003e 00:02:14.384\r\nFISHERMAN 2: With\r\nthe Joker's face.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.509 --\u003e 00:02:16.779\r\nFISHERMAN 3: It looks just like him.\r\nFISHERMAN 1: It can't be.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.803 --\u003e 00:02:17.963\r\nFISHERMAN 2: Call the police.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.599 --\u003e 00:02:22.309\r\nHe's made his move.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.599 --\u003e 00:03:04.518\r\nDining in tonight, sir?\r\n\r\n00:03:04.643 --\u003e 00:03:07.229\r\nThe dissection tray,\r\nplease, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.438 --\u003e 00:03:11.233\r\nALFRED: Any idea what our\r\nhappy friend is up to now?\r\n\r\n00:03:12.859 --\u003e 00:03:15.696\r\nNormal criminals usually\r\nhave logical motives.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.822 --\u003e 00:03:20.075\r\nBut the Joker's insane schemes\r\nmake sense to him alone.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.245 --\u003e 00:03:25.247\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:31.670 --\u003e 00:03:33.338\r\n(CLEARING THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:03:33.422 --\u003e 00:03:35.424\r\nLook alive, wage slaves.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.549 --\u003e 00:03:38.552\r\nPresenting that\r\ncaliph of clowns,\r\n\r\n00:03:38.635 --\u003e 00:03:40.679\r\nthat mogul of mountebanks,\r\n\r\n00:03:40.762 --\u003e 00:03:44.182\r\nthe one and only Joker!\r\n\r\n00:03:44.266 --\u003e 00:03:45.892\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.560 --\u003e 00:03:49.396\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.647 --\u003e 00:03:51.940\r\nGreat Scott.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.023 --\u003e 00:03:54.067\r\nActually, I'm Irish.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.776 --\u003e 00:03:58.572\r\nGood morning, Mr. Francis.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.655 --\u003e 00:04:01.616\r\nPlease allow me to\r\nintroduce my associates.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.742 --\u003e 00:04:02.909\r\nMiss Quinn.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.034 --\u003e 00:04:04.453\r\n(SPEAKING IN FRENCH)\r\n\r\n00:04:04.536 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nAnd Messrs, uh... Oh.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.330 --\u003e 00:04:10.292\r\nTheir names escape me for the moment.\r\nNo matter.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.500 --\u003e 00:04:14.546\r\nWe gentlemen of business\r\nhave arrangements to discuss.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.963 --\u003e 00:04:17.090\r\nUh, arrangements?\r\n\r\n00:04:17.966 --\u003e 00:04:19.718\r\nFor my fish, of course.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.926 --\u003e 00:04:23.555\r\nThis has all been worked\r\nout far in advance, Francis.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.680 --\u003e 00:04:27.601\r\nYou are merely the last\r\ntiny cog in my grand design.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.726 --\u003e 00:04:30.437\r\nSo don't speak to me\r\nagain, okay?\r\n\r\n00:04:31.021 --\u003e 00:04:33.940\r\nNow, what is everyone\r\nin town talking about?\r\n\r\n00:04:34.441 --\u003e 00:04:36.735\r\nUh, your fish?\r\n\r\n00:04:36.985 --\u003e 00:04:38.904\r\nI told you not to speak!\r\n\r\n00:04:41.573 --\u003e 00:04:45.577\r\n(SNIFFING) Ugh, fish.\r\nStinker-roonie.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.954 --\u003e 00:04:49.372\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:04:49.956 --\u003e 00:04:51.583\r\nAll better.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.083 --\u003e 00:04:55.879\r\nAs I was saying, since every fish\r\nin Gotham now bears my famous\r\n\r\n00:04:55.962 --\u003e 00:04:57.756\r\nand frankly fabulous face,\r\n\r\n00:04:57.881 --\u003e 00:05:02.093\r\nI should be getting a profit\r\nfrom every fish product sold.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.177 --\u003e 00:05:05.555\r\nLet's say,\r\na nickel per fish sandwich,\r\n\r\n00:05:05.680 --\u003e 00:05:09.476\r\nfifty cents for sardines.\r\nMillions of dollars a day\r\n\r\n00:05:09.559 --\u003e 00:05:13.480\r\nto finance my happily\r\nhedonistic lifestyle.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.563 --\u003e 00:05:17.484\r\nSo which of your tedious copyright\r\nforms do I fill out first?\r\n\r\n00:05:18.193 --\u003e 00:05:19.402\r\nYou may speak now.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.237 --\u003e 00:05:22.280\r\n(NERVOUSLY) No one\r\ncan copyright fish.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.405 --\u003e 00:05:24.616\r\nThey're a natural resource.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.699 --\u003e 00:05:27.244\r\nBut they share my unique face.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.327 --\u003e 00:05:29.579\r\nColonel what's-his-name\r\nhas chickens,\r\n\r\n00:05:29.704 --\u003e 00:05:31.706\r\nand they don't even\r\nhave mustaches.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.832 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nI can't help it. It's the law!\r\n\r\n00:05:34.543 --\u003e 00:05:37.462\r\nOh. Trying to cheat the\r\nJoker, are you?\r\n\r\n00:05:37.587 --\u003e 00:05:40.382\r\nWell, we'll see who\r\nhas the last laugh.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.008 --\u003e 00:05:45.053\r\nYou have until midnight to\r\nchange your mind, Francis.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.178 --\u003e 00:05:47.764\r\nOr you'll be the\r\npoorest fish of all.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.848 --\u003e 00:05:50.392\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:52.352 --\u003e 00:05:54.729\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.148 --\u003e 00:05:58.775\r\nBuh-bye!\r\n\r\n00:05:59.526 --\u003e 00:06:01.319\r\nHe's crazy.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.363 --\u003e 00:06:06.449\r\n\u003ci\u003eNEWSREADER: Coming up next,\r\nMarla Benson has a special report\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.660\r\n\u003ci\u003eon the smiling fish epidemic.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:08.785 --\u003e 00:06:11.580\r\n\u003ci\u003eHow safe are Gotham's waters?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:11.663 --\u003e 00:06:13.665\r\nWell,\r\nhe's not out to poison people.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.249 --\u003e 00:06:17.085\r\nThis diluted toxin\r\nonly affects fish.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.168 --\u003e 00:06:20.046\r\nMaybe he's trying to make\r\nus all die from disgust.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.171 --\u003e 00:06:21.882\r\n(WACKY TUNE PLAYING ON TV)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.842 --\u003e 00:06:25.361\r\n\u003ci\u003eHARLEY: (SINGING)\r\nThey're finny and funny.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:25.385 --\u003e 00:06:26.678\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd, oh, so delish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:26.761 --\u003e 00:06:29.431\r\n\u003ci\u003eThey're joyful and\r\njolly Joker Fish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:30.932 --\u003e 00:06:34.185\r\n\u003ci\u003eJOKER: Say, Mom,\r\nwondering what to feed the family tonight?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:34.311 --\u003e 00:06:36.605\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat?!\r\nI feed the family tonight?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:36.980 --\u003e 00:06:40.567\r\n(GROWLING LIKE A PIRATE)\r\n\u003ci\u003eTry\u003c/i\u003e me famous Joker \u003ci\u003eFish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:41.151 --\u003e 00:06:44.446\r\n\u003ci\u003eThere's Smiling Smelt,\r\nGiggling Grouper,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:44.529 --\u003e 00:06:46.197\r\n\u003ci\u003eand Happy Haddock.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:46.865 --\u003e 00:06:48.742\r\nThis could cause a\r\nstampede to pork.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.200 --\u003e 00:06:50.952\r\n\u003ci\u003eYummy, yum-Yum-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:51.786 --\u003e 00:06:52.829\r\n\u003ci\u003eEat it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:53.204 --\u003e 00:06:58.043\r\n\u003ci\u003eUh, Mr. J, I have this\r\nlittle problem with fish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:00.170 --\u003e 00:07:01.963\r\n\u003ci\u003eYummy, yum-Yum-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:02.547 --\u003e 00:07:05.216\r\n\u003ci\u003eYes, friends, that's Joker Fish.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:05.342 --\u003e 00:07:06.509\r\n(HARLEY RETCHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:06.593 --\u003e 00:07:09.638\r\n\u003ci\u003eTasty, tempting,\r\nand of course...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:10.555 --\u003e 00:07:13.433\r\n\u003ci\u003e- Naturally low in cholesterol.\r\n- Naturally low in cholesterol.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:13.600 --\u003e 00:07:16.102\r\n\u003ci\u003eComing to your local store.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:16.186 --\u003e 00:07:20.357\r\n\u003ci\u003eJust as soon as that nasty old Mr. G.\r\nCarl Francis\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:20.440 --\u003e 00:07:23.234\r\n\u003ci\u003edecides to give me my\r\nlegal cut of the profits.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:23.318 --\u003e 00:07:24.778\r\nChange the channel.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.861 --\u003e 00:07:27.280\r\n(JOKER GIGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.364 --\u003e 00:07:28.657\r\nIt's on every station.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.199 --\u003e 00:07:31.534\r\nGet a trace on that signal. Now!\r\n\r\n00:07:31.701 --\u003e 00:07:34.996\r\n\u003ci\u003eI hope you've changed your\r\nmind, Mr. Francis,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:35.080 --\u003e 00:07:38.083\r\n\u003ci\u003ebecause I haven't changed mine.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:38.208 --\u003e 00:07:39.793\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:42.420 --\u003e 00:07:44.005\r\n(CLOCK TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:45.757 --\u003e 00:07:49.052\r\nRelax, Mr. Francis. I've got men\r\nposted at every window and door.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.135 --\u003e 00:07:50.804\r\nNobody's sneaking\r\nin here tonight.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.471 --\u003e 00:07:53.098\r\nIf I got in this easily...\r\n\r\n00:07:55.642 --\u003e 00:07:57.018\r\nSo will the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.102 --\u003e 00:07:59.479\r\nHey, hey,\r\nthis is police business.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.562 --\u003e 00:08:01.231\r\nHaul your bat butt out of here.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.314 --\u003e 00:08:02.565\r\nHold it, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.066 --\u003e 00:08:05.485\r\nNo one knows the Joker's\r\nmethods better than Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.652 --\u003e 00:08:06.861\r\nHe stays.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.987 --\u003e 00:08:10.198\r\nGlory-hogging,\r\nlong-underwear geek.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.281 --\u003e 00:08:12.325\r\nUh, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:08:12.409 --\u003e 00:08:14.202\r\nwhy is this happening to me?\r\n\r\n00:08:14.285 --\u003e 00:08:17.080\r\nI've never done\r\nanything to this Joker.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.455 --\u003e 00:08:20.792\r\nI'm just a paper pusher.\r\nI can't change the laws.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.875 --\u003e 00:08:22.043\r\nI'm harmless.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.168 --\u003e 00:08:25.839\r\nAnd in his sick mind,\r\nthat's the joke, Mr. Francis.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.441 --\u003e 00:08:46.860\r\n- Feeling all right?\r\n- Oh, sure.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.943 --\u003e 00:08:50.196\r\nIt's just that everything's\r\nbeen so crazy today.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.321 --\u003e 00:08:52.657\r\nI haven't even had time\r\nto rinse off that gunk\r\n\r\n00:08:52.824 --\u003e 00:08:54.993\r\nthe Joker's girl squirted on me.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.368 --\u003e 00:08:57.829\r\n(YELLING) Get this man\r\nto a hospital, now!\r\n\r\n00:08:57.912 --\u003e 00:08:58.955\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:09:00.123 --\u003e 00:09:02.083\r\n(CLOCK CHIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:06.838 --\u003e 00:09:08.673\r\n- OFFICER: Watch out!\r\n- (OFFICERS EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.633 --\u003e 00:09:12.635\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:09:13.261 --\u003e 00:09:15.555\r\n(ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:21.603 --\u003e 00:09:24.314\r\n(OFFICERS couemue)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.445 --\u003e 00:09:31.696\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.072 --\u003e 00:09:33.865\r\n(cnecmue)\r\n\r\n00:09:37.786 --\u003e 00:09:41.664\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:09:48.671 --\u003e 00:09:51.049\r\nHe'll be all right once\r\nthe antivenom kicks in.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.132 --\u003e 00:09:54.219\r\nI don't get it. We all breathed the\r\ngas, and we're not smiling.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.302 --\u003e 00:09:55.762\r\nHe didn't want us.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.845 --\u003e 00:09:58.473\r\nThat gas is one part\r\nof a binary compound.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.556 --\u003e 00:10:00.850\r\nThe Joker exposed\r\nFrancis to the other part\r\n\r\n00:10:00.934 --\u003e 00:10:02.393\r\nwhen he threatened\r\nhim this morning.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.477 --\u003e 00:10:03.478\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis just in.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:03.561 --\u003e 00:10:05.688\r\n\u003ci\u003eFormer Copyright Director G.\r\nCarl Francis\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:05.772 --\u003e 00:10:09.067\r\n\u003ci\u003ewill be taking an\r\nextended vacation.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:09.943 --\u003e 00:10:13.154\r\n\u003ci\u003eLooks like he's having more fun already.\r\n(LAUGHING)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:13.238 --\u003e 00:10:14.781\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut I'm not happy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:14.864 --\u003e 00:10:18.701\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf I don't get legal claim\r\nto my fish by 3:00 a.m.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:18.785 --\u003e 00:10:23.623\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe number two bureaucrat,\r\nThomas Jackson, will feel my wrath.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:23.790 --\u003e 00:10:26.751\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd now, Batman,\r\nbecause I know you're watching,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:26.835 --\u003e 00:10:29.295\r\nhere's a message\r\nfrom our sponsor.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.379 --\u003e 00:10:32.590\r\n\u003ci\u003e(SINGING) They're finny and funny\r\nAnd, oh, so delish\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:34.384 --\u003e 00:10:36.678\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:36.761 --\u003e 00:10:38.972\r\nAll units,\r\nkeep your eyes open for anything.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.015 --\u003e 00:10:43.017\r\n(INDISTINCT POLICE\r\nRADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:10:53.611 --\u003e 00:10:55.089\r\nBULLOCK: I'd like to\r\ngo on record as saying\r\n\r\n00:10:55.113 --\u003e 00:10:58.074\r\nthis Batman business is\r\nthe lamest idea and I...\r\n\r\n00:10:58.158 --\u003e 00:10:59.450\r\nDuly noted, Lieutenant.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.534 --\u003e 00:11:02.328\r\nBut we're going to try it his\r\nway to protect Mr. Jackson.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.672 --\u003e 00:11:14.174\r\nNearly 3:00 a.m.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.340 --\u003e 00:11:15.967\r\nAnd not a cackle\r\nfrom that hyena.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.050 --\u003e 00:11:17.677\r\nWe must've scared him off.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.094 --\u003e 00:11:19.929\r\n- (BOTH GASPING)\r\n- What's that?\r\n\r\n00:11:21.806 --\u003e 00:11:22.891\r\nJACKSON: Just my cat.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.518 --\u003e 00:11:26.978\r\nBATMAN: A Joker Fish!\r\n\r\n00:11:28.313 --\u003e 00:11:31.357\r\n(CAT SNICKERING)\r\n\r\n00:11:31.441 --\u003e 00:11:32.859\r\nIt's affecting it. Look out!\r\n\r\n00:11:35.820 --\u003e 00:11:37.614\r\n(CAT SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:40.283 --\u003e 00:11:42.076\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:42.160 --\u003e 00:11:45.079\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.374 --\u003e 00:11:50.752\r\n(LAUGHING sl_ows)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.841 --\u003e 00:11:59.719\r\nBATMAN: Even drugged,\r\nthe cat went straight for its master.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.137 --\u003e 00:12:02.764\r\n(SNICKERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.847 --\u003e 00:12:04.432\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.268 --\u003e 00:12:08.853\r\n(CAT MEOWING)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.937 --\u003e 00:12:10.772\r\nBULLOCK: Oh,\r\nthis is just dandy, Commish.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.855 --\u003e 00:12:12.482\r\nYour pet bat's playing dress up\r\n\r\n00:12:12.565 --\u003e 00:12:15.318\r\nwhile the Joker's popping off\r\npencil pushers right and left.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.401 --\u003e 00:12:17.254\r\nWell, I ain't sticking\r\naround to see who's next.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.278 --\u003e 00:12:19.030\r\nI got my own methods.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.197 --\u003e 00:12:20.240\r\nGORDON: Bullock!\r\n\r\n00:12:22.992 --\u003e 00:12:25.328\r\nCommissioner,\r\nhave a look at this fish.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.204 --\u003e 00:12:27.997\r\nIt's a Japanese tang,\r\n\r\n00:12:28.081 --\u003e 00:12:30.583\r\nnot native to\r\nGotham's cold waters.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.708 --\u003e 00:12:32.168\r\nGORDON: So where\r\ndid it come from?\r\n\r\n00:13:24.971 --\u003e 00:13:26.222\r\nFreeze, copper!\r\n\r\n00:13:26.306 --\u003e 00:13:28.599\r\nI got you covered, see?\r\n\r\n00:13:28.766 --\u003e 00:13:31.811\r\nWell, if it ain't laughing\r\nboy's little hench-wench.\r\n\r\n00:13:31.978 --\u003e 00:13:33.438\r\nYou're outgunned, sugar.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.563 --\u003e 00:13:34.814\r\nDo tell.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.857 --\u003e 00:13:37.817\r\n(EXCLAIMS) What?\r\n\r\n00:13:38.776 --\u003e 00:13:41.070\r\n- (BLOWS)\r\n- (SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:41.154 --\u003e 00:13:42.905\r\nOoh, look at what I caught.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.531 --\u003e 00:13:45.408\r\nKind of runty, though.\r\n\r\n00:13:45.992 --\u003e 00:13:49.412\r\nI'm gonna have to throw it back.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.746 --\u003e 00:13:52.332\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:52.415 --\u003e 00:13:55.668\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:02.008 --\u003e 00:14:05.053\r\nJOKER: You know, Bullock,\r\nyou may be a lousy cop,\r\n\r\n00:14:05.178 --\u003e 00:14:07.764\r\nbut you make a terrific worm.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.847 --\u003e 00:14:09.974\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:13.019 --\u003e 00:14:14.437\r\nYou won't get away with this.\r\n\r\n00:14:19.734 --\u003e 00:14:20.902\r\nHe's right, you know.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.487 --\u003e 00:14:23.529\r\nYou're kidding.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.613 --\u003e 00:14:25.448\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:28.576 --\u003e 00:14:31.204\r\nIf this lunchmeat\r\nfigured out where we are,\r\n\r\n00:14:31.329 --\u003e 00:14:32.997\r\nBatman won't be far behind.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.081 --\u003e 00:14:36.167\r\nAnd why spoil my\r\nsharkie's appetite\r\n\r\n00:14:36.250 --\u003e 00:14:38.461\r\nwhen I can feed him bigger fish?\r\n\r\n00:14:38.544 --\u003e 00:14:41.130\r\nHmm? (CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.589 --\u003e 00:14:44.675\r\nUgh! Again with the fish.\r\nI hate fish.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.344 --\u003e 00:14:50.390\r\n- Uh, no offense, Mr. J.\r\n- Poor Harley.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.515 --\u003e 00:14:53.643\r\nThis caper's been kind of rough on\r\nyou, hasn't it?\r\n\r\n00:14:53.726 --\u003e 00:14:55.311\r\nUh-huh.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.478 --\u003e 00:14:56.604\r\nCheer up.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.687 --\u003e 00:14:59.440\r\nYou can be my very\r\nown little mermaid.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.524 --\u003e 00:15:01.025\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.819 --\u003e 00:15:04.529\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:04.946 --\u003e 00:15:07.115\r\nHARLEY: You're really\r\nsick, you know that, boss?\r\n\r\n00:15:07.198 --\u003e 00:15:08.741\r\nMmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.825 --\u003e 00:15:11.661\r\n- (JINGLE PLAYING)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:15:11.744 --\u003e 00:15:13.246\r\n(FARTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:17.560 --\u003e 00:16:19.520\r\nJOKER: Now, this fella here\r\n\r\n00:16:22.148 --\u003e 00:16:23.733\r\ncame with his own grin.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.109 --\u003e 00:16:26.694\r\nSee the resemblance?\r\n\r\n00:16:27.195 --\u003e 00:16:29.655\r\nAnd check out my\r\ncatch of the day.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.115 --\u003e 00:16:34.494\r\n(MUFFLED YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:34.785 --\u003e 00:16:35.953\r\nBullock.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.455 --\u003e 00:16:38.498\r\n(SPITS)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.581 --\u003e 00:16:40.458\r\nI didn't need no bat\r\ncomputer to tell me\r\n\r\n00:16:40.541 --\u003e 00:16:42.668\r\nthat weird lookin' minnow\r\ncame from an aquarium.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.169 --\u003e 00:16:46.964\r\nYes, well,\r\nthis is all tremendously boring.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.089 --\u003e 00:16:48.799\r\n'Course,\r\nI can always amuse myself\r\n\r\n00:16:48.883 --\u003e 00:16:51.594\r\nwatching old Harv give\r\nmy shark indigestion.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.677 --\u003e 00:16:53.054\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.478 --\u003e 00:17:01.479\r\nWait!\r\n\r\n00:17:02.772 --\u003e 00:17:04.398\r\nLet him go.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.482 --\u003e 00:17:05.775\r\nI'm the one you're after.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.400 --\u003e 00:17:09.278\r\nGee, and let my little\r\nguppy go hungry?\r\n\r\n00:17:09.362 --\u003e 00:17:11.030\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.113 --\u003e 00:17:14.408\r\nWhat do you think we\r\ncan do about that?\r\n\r\n00:17:21.082 --\u003e 00:17:22.667\r\nYou're right, Harley.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.792 --\u003e 00:17:24.502\r\nFish are disgusting.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.213\r\nI think I'll start using\r\nmy toxin on cattle.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.463 --\u003e 00:17:29.423\r\n\"Joker Burgers.\" Ha!\r\n\r\n00:17:29.674 --\u003e 00:17:31.884\r\nTalk about a Happy Meal.\r\n\r\n00:17:31.968 --\u003e 00:17:35.012\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.390 --\u003e 00:17:40.351\r\n(SIGHING) You never\r\ncould take a joke.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.608 --\u003e 00:17:49.860\r\nHe doesn't stand a chance\r\nagainst that monster!\r\n\r\n00:17:49.944 --\u003e 00:17:52.613\r\n- Yeah. Catch.\r\n- Hey!\r\n\r\n00:17:52.697 --\u003e 00:17:54.073\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:06.586 --\u003e 00:18:08.004\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.087 --\u003e 00:18:10.047\r\n(VOCALIZING MERRILY)\r\n\r\n00:18:10.131 --\u003e 00:18:11.215\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:12.383 --\u003e 00:18:14.051\r\nHey. Hey!\r\n\r\n00:18:16.512 --\u003e 00:18:18.014\r\n(POUNDING ON GLASS)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.350 --\u003e 00:18:22.560\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:27.857 --\u003e 00:18:29.483\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.614 --\u003e 00:18:37.700\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:38.993 --\u003e 00:18:41.329\r\nOh! Ah! (LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.545 --\u003e 00:18:50.796\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.427 --\u003e 00:18:57.928\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:05.853 --\u003e 00:19:07.146\r\n(ALL EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.149 --\u003e 00:19:11.901\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.276 --\u003e 00:19:13.653\r\nOopsie.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.820 --\u003e 00:19:16.906\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:20.368 --\u003e 00:19:21.535\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:19:35.591 --\u003e 00:19:37.093\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:37.218 --\u003e 00:19:38.427\r\nYou Okay?\r\n\r\n00:19:40.680 --\u003e 00:19:42.431\r\nJust give him one for\r\nme, will you?\r\n\r\n00:19:47.103 --\u003e 00:19:49.230\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:54.360 --\u003e 00:19:56.028\r\nHuh? (GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:04.120 --\u003e 00:20:05.246\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:05.329 --\u003e 00:20:08.541\r\nMeanwhile, back at the wrench.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.666 --\u003e 00:20:11.669\r\nSince my side-splitters\r\ndon't tickle you,\r\n\r\n00:20:11.794 --\u003e 00:20:13.671\r\nhow about a skull-splitter?\r\n\r\n00:20:19.135 --\u003e 00:20:20.136\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:20:22.555 --\u003e 00:20:23.848\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:26.016 --\u003e 00:20:28.936\r\nThere's no place left to\r\ngo, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.103 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:31.856\r\n(EXCLAIMING INDIFFERENTLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:33.482 --\u003e 00:20:35.484\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.613 --\u003e 00:20:42.158\r\nSee, Batsy,\r\nI think of everything.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.241 --\u003e 00:20:44.285\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:44.368 --\u003e 00:20:46.245\r\nHuh? (SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:02.261 --\u003e 00:21:05.055\r\nHARLEY: (SNIFFING) Oh,\r\nmy poor, poor pudding.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.891 --\u003e 00:21:10.352\r\nCome on, he was a demented,\r\nabusive, psychotic maniac.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.061 --\u003e 00:21:12.229\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.313 --\u003e 00:21:14.648\r\nI'm really gonna miss him.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.316 --\u003e 00:21:17.318\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:21:21.989 --\u003e 00:21:23.616\r\nGORDON: Do you think\r\nhe's gone for good?\r\n\r\n00:21:23.699 --\u003e 00:21:25.201\r\nBelieve me, Jim,\r\n\r\n00:21:25.284 --\u003e 00:21:26.577\r\nI wish it were true.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.203 --\u003e 00:21:29.580\r\nBut deep inside, I doubt it.\r\n\r\n00:21:49.475 --\u003e 00:21:51.477\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:15.793 --\u003e 00:22:16.794\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E47 - Harley and Ivy (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:08.884 --\u003e 00:00:10.886\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:24.084 --\u003e 00:01:25.085\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.505 --\u003e 00:01:29.923\r\n(CARS HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.549 --\u003e 00:01:31.883\r\n(YELLING) You jerks!\r\n\r\n00:01:36.305 --\u003e 00:01:37.665\r\n- (WOMAN SCREAMING)\r\n- (DOG YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.806 --\u003e 00:01:39.141\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.772 --\u003e 00:01:49.526\r\nAh! The wind in my hair\r\nand the Batman at my heels.\r\n\r\n00:01:50.193 --\u003e 00:01:53.322\r\nIt's the kind of night that\r\nmakes you glad to be alive.\r\n\r\n00:01:53.989 --\u003e 00:01:55.532\r\nRight, Harley girl?\r\n\r\n00:01:56.450 --\u003e 00:01:58.410\r\nSure thing, Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.002 --\u003e 00:02:08.503\r\nQuick! Turn here!\r\n\r\n00:02:10.130 --\u003e 00:02:12.799\r\n- But, boss, that's-\r\n- I said, turn!\r\n\r\n00:02:13.383 --\u003e 00:02:14.384\r\nYes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.468 --\u003e 00:02:15.594\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:17.679 --\u003e 00:02:19.931\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:27.731 --\u003e 00:02:28.982\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:30.984 --\u003e 00:02:33.528\r\nWhy didn't you tell me\r\nsomeone put a hill there?\r\n\r\n00:02:33.612 --\u003e 00:02:36.907\r\n- I tried, but- - Never mind.\r\nJust hand me the gun.\r\n\r\n00:02:39.534 --\u003e 00:02:41.495\r\n(SNAPS FINGERS) Come on!\r\nCome on!\r\n\r\n00:02:43.914 --\u003e 00:02:44.915\r\nHere.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.749 --\u003e 00:02:47.292\r\nHey, Batsy!\r\n\r\n00:02:47.459 --\u003e 00:02:49.795\r\nThis is where I leave you flat.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.878 --\u003e 00:02:51.213\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:56.218 --\u003e 00:02:57.844\r\nYou nincompoop!\r\n\r\n00:02:58.261 --\u003e 00:02:59.429\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:02:59.846 --\u003e 00:03:01.306\r\nYou didn't say which gun.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.239 --\u003e 00:03:18.699\r\n(BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:24.955 --\u003e 00:03:26.540\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:27.374 --\u003e 00:03:29.126\r\nLet's go. Let's go!\r\n\r\n00:03:29.292 --\u003e 00:03:30.627\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.005 --\u003e 00:03:36.842\r\nIf he wants the car that\r\nbad, he can have it.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:49.855\r\nNext time, clown.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.236 --\u003e 00:03:58.780\r\nJOKER: No,\r\nwe didn't get the diamond.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.364 --\u003e 00:04:02.784\r\nThe \"Dork Knight\" showed up\r\nbefore we even got to the museum.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.118 --\u003e 00:04:05.203\r\nI had a great shot at him, too,\r\n\r\n00:04:05.287 --\u003e 00:04:10.834\r\nexcept my dear little Harley\r\nQuinn handed me the wrong gun!\r\n\r\n00:04:11.376 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\n(BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nBut, pudding, it was kind of\r\nfunny watching you shoot at him\r\n\r\n00:04:16.006 --\u003e 00:04:17.674\r\nwith the \"bang\" flag.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.300 --\u003e 00:04:19.843\r\n(BOTH (assume)\r\n\r\n00:04:23.680 --\u003e 00:04:24.681\r\nFunny?\r\n\r\n00:04:25.056 --\u003e 00:04:29.269\r\nYou presume to tell me what\r\nI should think is funny?\r\n\r\n00:04:29.436 --\u003e 00:04:31.938\r\n(YELLING) In fact,\r\nwhen have you ever\r\n\r\n00:04:32.105 --\u003e 00:04:34.524\r\ncontributed a worthwhile\r\nidea to this gang?\r\n\r\n00:04:35.358 --\u003e 00:04:37.944\r\n(STAMMERING) Well,\r\nI did get us away from Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.487 --\u003e 00:04:40.030\r\nHuzzah!\r\n\r\n00:04:40.113 --\u003e 00:04:42.365\r\nThe kid gets lucky,\r\nand she wants a medal!\r\n\r\n00:04:44.534 --\u003e 00:04:46.828\r\nMaybe I should just\r\nlet you run the gang.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.287 --\u003e 00:04:50.081\r\nMaybe you're a better crook than\r\nthe rest of us put together.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.707 --\u003e 00:04:51.833\r\nMaybe.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.667 --\u003e 00:04:53.668\r\n(TIMIDLY) not.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.085 --\u003e 00:04:55.420\r\n(BOTH SMIRKING)\r\n\r\n00:04:55.670 --\u003e 00:04:57.172\r\n(HYENAS LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:01.843 --\u003e 00:05:04.888\r\n(JOKER GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:05.430 --\u003e 00:05:06.640\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.605 --\u003e 00:05:16.566\r\nFine! I'll show you!\r\nYou'll be sorry!\r\n\r\n00:05:16.650 --\u003e 00:05:19.027\r\nI'll pull a big heist,\r\nand I'll be laughing at you.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.110 --\u003e 00:05:21.446\r\nHa! Ha! You hear? Laughing!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.205 --\u003e 00:05:31.706\r\nI miss him already.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.366 --\u003e 00:06:07.492\r\nPiece of cake.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.914 --\u003e 00:06:15.876\r\nMr. J will just plotz\r\nwhen I give him...\r\n\r\n00:06:17.544 --\u003e 00:06:20.255\r\nNo. I'm keeping it for myself.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.756 --\u003e 00:06:22.757\r\nMaybe.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.558 --\u003e 00:06:33.059\r\n(ALARM RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:36.104 --\u003e 00:06:37.314\r\nThe heck with it!\r\n\r\n00:06:50.994 --\u003e 00:06:51.995\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:06:55.457 --\u003e 00:06:56.458\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:00.462 --\u003e 00:07:02.088\r\nNice work, butterfingers.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.172 --\u003e 00:07:05.091\r\nWhy didn't you just turn on the\r\nBat signal while you were at it?\r\n\r\n00:07:06.009 --\u003e 00:07:07.677\r\nI wasn't trying to get caught.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.136 --\u003e 00:07:09.596\r\nCould've fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.804 --\u003e 00:07:13.308\r\nHey! Aren't you that plant\r\nlady, Poison Oakie?\r\n\r\n00:07:13.642 --\u003e 00:07:15.602\r\nIvy. Poison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.102 --\u003e 00:07:17.145\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.562 --\u003e 00:07:19.731\r\nHarley Quinn.\r\nPleased to meet you.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.231 --\u003e 00:07:21.232\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:07:28.657 --\u003e 00:07:30.742\r\nThis is not a good\r\ntime to get acquainted.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.326 --\u003e 00:07:32.369\r\nMONTOYA: Freeze!\r\n\r\n00:07:41.336 --\u003e 00:07:42.671\r\nAny ideas?\r\n\r\n00:07:45.131 --\u003e 00:07:46.675\r\nWhat you got in the bottles?\r\n\r\n00:07:47.592 --\u003e 00:07:49.594\r\nPOISON IVY: Plant toxins\r\nfrom the museum lab.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.304 --\u003e 00:07:52.639\r\nGood enough.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.477 --\u003e 00:07:58.520\r\nHeads up!\r\n\r\n00:08:01.773 --\u003e 00:08:04.901\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:07.237 --\u003e 00:08:09.114\r\nMONTOYA: Stop in\r\nthe name of the law!\r\n\r\n00:08:09.864 --\u003e 00:08:11.157\r\nNot tonight, baby.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.744 --\u003e 00:08:15.912\r\nPOISON IVY: Get in the car!\r\n\r\n00:08:16.162 --\u003e 00:08:17.288\r\nHARLEY: What car?\r\n\r\n00:08:20.375 --\u003e 00:08:21.793\r\nThat car.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.919 --\u003e 00:08:25.755\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:30.218 --\u003e 00:08:31.511\r\n_Yes! _Yes!\r\n\r\n00:08:31.678 --\u003e 00:08:34.931\r\nPOISON IVY: This could be the\r\nbeginning of a beautiful friendship.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.820 --\u003e 00:08:50.071\r\nHARLEY: (WHINING) I hate shots!\r\n\r\n00:08:50.196 --\u003e 00:08:52.073\r\nI hate shots!\r\n\r\n00:08:52.615 --\u003e 00:08:55.535\r\nNow, now. You're not\r\nimmune to poison like I am\r\n\r\n00:08:55.952 --\u003e 00:08:59.914\r\nand you won't last 10 minutes here\r\nin Toxic Acres without my antidote.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.540 --\u003e 00:09:02.042\r\n(WHINING)\r\n\r\n00:09:05.045 --\u003e 00:09:10.008\r\n(SIGHS) You'd think after living with\r\nMr. J, I'd be used to a little pain.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.259 --\u003e 00:09:12.969\r\nWhy do you put up\r\nwith that clown?\r\n\r\n00:09:13.219 --\u003e 00:09:16.639\r\nDon't get me wrong.\r\nMy pudding's a little rough sometimes,\r\n\r\n00:09:16.806 --\u003e 00:09:18.850\r\nbut he loves me, really.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.934 --\u003e 00:09:21.352\r\nSure he does.\r\n\r\n00:09:21.436 --\u003e 00:09:24.147\r\nYou're just one big forgiving\r\ndoormat, aren't you?\r\n\r\n00:09:24.606 --\u003e 00:09:26.691\r\nI am not a doormat.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.400 --\u003e 00:09:28.443\r\nAm I?\r\n\r\n00:09:28.651 --\u003e 00:09:31.738\r\nIf you had a middle name,\r\nit would be \"Welcome.\"\r\n\r\n00:09:33.406 --\u003e 00:09:38.244\r\nBut cheer up, kid. You just need some\r\nlessons in good old female self-esteem.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.578 --\u003e 00:09:42.999\r\nIn other words,\r\nlet's play with the boys on our terms.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.797 --\u003e 00:09:51.049\r\nAnd now, gentlemen,\r\nif there is no new business,\r\n\r\n00:09:51.382 --\u003e 00:09:52.675\r\nI propose we adjourn to-\r\n\r\n00:09:52.759 --\u003e 00:09:54.803\r\nPOISON IVY: A moment,\r\nplease, Mr. Chairman.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.553 --\u003e 00:09:57.806\r\n(MEN PROTESTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:57.931 --\u003e 00:09:59.724\r\n- MAN 1: Who is that?\r\n- MAN 2: A woman, here?\r\n\r\n00:09:59.808 --\u003e 00:10:00.892\r\nCHAIRMAN: Outrageous!\r\n\r\n00:10:01.059 --\u003e 00:10:03.978\r\nSee here, young lady,\r\nis this some kind of joke?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.395 --\u003e 00:10:06.022\r\nThe joke, my dear chairman,\r\n\r\n00:10:06.106 --\u003e 00:10:10.360\r\nis this obsolete,\r\nsexist mockery you call a men's club.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.194 --\u003e 00:10:12.570\r\nNow, I ask you,\r\n\r\n00:10:12.654 --\u003e 00:10:16.199\r\nwhat kind of adventurers\r\nrefuse to admit women?\r\n\r\n00:10:16.324 --\u003e 00:10:19.536\r\n- MAN 1: What does she know?\r\n- MAN 2: That is ridiculous.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.911 --\u003e 00:10:21.871\r\nMAN 3: Get her out of here.\r\nHow dare she?\r\n\r\n00:10:21.955 --\u003e 00:10:24.707\r\n(MEN PROTESTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:26.126 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nStill, if it's excitement\r\nyou boys crave...\r\n\r\n00:10:32.590 --\u003e 00:10:33.800\r\nWhat is this?\r\n\r\n00:10:33.883 --\u003e 00:10:35.885\r\nLet go! “Stop!\r\n\r\n00:10:36.094 --\u003e 00:10:38.054\r\n(ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:10:40.223 --\u003e 00:10:44.769\r\nThat should keep you big strong\r\nmen busy while we weak little girls\r\n\r\n00:10:45.061 --\u003e 00:10:46.855\r\nloot your trophy room.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.147 --\u003e 00:10:49.816\r\nGee, Red. You got style!\r\n\r\n00:10:49.983 --\u003e 00:10:50.984\r\nThis is true.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.195 --\u003e 00:10:56.322\r\n(MEN CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.154 --\u003e 00:11:39.741\r\n(HARLEY HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.328 --\u003e 00:11:45.038\r\nWhat did you make?\r\nWhat did you make?\r\n\r\n00:11:46.372 --\u003e 00:11:49.500\r\nSteamed chard and beet juice.\r\nHmm! Yum!\r\n\r\n00:11:51.169 --\u003e 00:11:52.503\r\nGee, green.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.587 --\u003e 00:11:54.547\r\nMy favorite color.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.476 --\u003e 00:12:08.102\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.394 --\u003e 00:12:11.898\r\nNo offense, Red,\r\nbut I'm not very hungry.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.191 --\u003e 00:12:16.319\r\nSomehow I don't feel\r\nlike my old perky self.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.903 --\u003e 00:12:18.571\r\nSomething's missing.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.614 --\u003e 00:12:24.035\r\nWill you stop? I can't believe you're\r\nstill mooning over that psychotic creep.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.535 --\u003e 00:12:28.039\r\nWell, maybe I'd feel better\r\nif I knew he missed me, too.\r\n\r\n00:12:36.047 --\u003e 00:12:37.632\r\nJOKER: (SHOUTING) Harley!\r\n\r\n00:12:39.008 --\u003e 00:12:41.761\r\nThis place is going to\r\nblinking blue blazes.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.679 --\u003e 00:12:44.264\r\nAnybody seen my socks?\r\n\r\n00:12:45.098 --\u003e 00:12:46.557\r\nJOKER: Harley!\r\n\r\n00:12:46.683 --\u003e 00:12:48.243\r\n- (HYENAS SNARLING)\r\n- (JOKER EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:48.851 --\u003e 00:12:50.603\r\nThey snapped at me!\r\n\r\n00:12:50.728 --\u003e 00:12:52.313\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat's going on, Roe'?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:52.647 --\u003e 00:12:56.859\r\nThe place is a mess, no one's fed the\r\nhyenas, and I can't find my socks!\r\n\r\n00:12:57.277 --\u003e 00:12:58.403\r\nWhere's Harley?\r\n\r\n00:12:59.404 --\u003e 00:13:01.281\r\n(STAMMERING) You canned\r\nher, boss, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:01.698 --\u003e 00:13:04.075\r\nSo? She's always\r\ncome back before.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.659 --\u003e 00:13:05.952\r\nGee,\r\n\r\n00:13:06.160 --\u003e 00:13:08.288\r\nI guess you ain't\r\nseen the papers then.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.538 --\u003e 00:13:11.416\r\nPapers?\r\nWhat are you babbling about?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.838 --\u003e 00:13:19.340\r\n(JOKER SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:20.717 --\u003e 00:13:22.802\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:13:31.686 --\u003e 00:13:33.271\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:36.607 --\u003e 00:13:38.026\r\n(CURSING \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e SPANISH)\r\n\r\n00:13:40.486 --\u003e 00:13:44.365\r\nI remember when I would go\r\ndriving like this with Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.782 --\u003e 00:13:47.118\r\n(IMITATING HARLEY) \"Mr.\r\nJ, Mr. J.\"\r\n\r\n00:13:48.036 --\u003e 00:13:49.871\r\nChange the record, Harl.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.954 --\u003e 00:13:52.874\r\nYou want to be some wacko's\r\nvictim the rest of your life?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.505 --\u003e 00:14:01.883\r\nWell, hello.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.008 --\u003e 00:14:04.510\r\nI think I'm in love.\r\n(MAKING KISSING SOUNDS)\r\n\r\n00:14:05.094 --\u003e 00:14:06.637\r\nAhooga! Ahooga!\r\n\r\n00:14:06.888 --\u003e 00:14:08.264\r\n(HOWL$)\r\n\r\n00:14:09.015 --\u003e 00:14:10.600\r\nExcuse me, boys.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.683 --\u003e 00:14:15.313\r\nDidn't your mommies tell you that's not\r\nthe nice way to get a lady's attention?\r\n\r\n00:14:15.855 --\u003e 00:14:19.609\r\nOh! And what are you gonna do?\r\nSpank us?\r\n\r\n00:14:19.942 --\u003e 00:14:23.279\r\nThat's right, pigs.\r\nAnd here's the paddle.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.738 --\u003e 00:14:25.490\r\n(ALL SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:14:31.037 --\u003e 00:14:33.873\r\nThere may be hope for you yet.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.352 --\u003e 00:14:55.895\r\n(COMPUTER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:59.273 --\u003e 00:15:00.983\r\nALFRED: Choosing a weekend\r\ndate, sir?\r\n\r\n00:15:01.651 --\u003e 00:15:04.612\r\nBATMAN: This is one sister act\r\nthat's hard to follow, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.779 --\u003e 00:15:08.366\r\nOnly clue I have is this soil\r\nanalysis from their tire tracks.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.077 --\u003e 00:15:12.078\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:15:12.662 --\u003e 00:15:16.124\r\nContains the same compounds\r\nyou'd find in a toxic waste dump.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.749 --\u003e 00:15:19.919\r\nThen may I suggest an\r\naccessory this evening?\r\n\r\n00:15:27.802 --\u003e 00:15:29.178\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.139 --\u003e 00:15:32.140\r\nJOKER: (YELLING) \u003ci\u003eWhat?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:32.640 --\u003e 00:15:34.308\r\n(TIMIDLY) Mr. J?\r\n\r\n00:15:35.268 --\u003e 00:15:36.727\r\nHarley?\r\n\r\n00:15:38.563 --\u003e 00:15:40.648\r\nHi, pudding.\r\nYou still angry with me?\r\n\r\n00:15:41.107 --\u003e 00:15:42.608\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.526 --\u003e 00:15:46.028\r\nHoney, baby, pumpkin pie.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.487 --\u003e 00:15:48.156\r\nYou know I can't hold a grudge.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.823 --\u003e 00:15:50.658\r\n- Where are you?\r\n- With a friend.\r\n\r\n00:15:50.741 --\u003e 00:15:53.786\r\nLook, I can't talk,\r\nbut I wanted to let you know I'm okay.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.870 --\u003e 00:15:55.079\r\n(DOOR CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.163 --\u003e 00:15:57.707\r\nOops. Gotta go.\r\nI'll talk to you soon.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.500 --\u003e 00:16:01.627\r\nSooner than you think.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.879 --\u003e 00:16:05.089\r\n- What's up?\r\n- Wrong number.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.173 --\u003e 00:16:06.299\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:07.383 --\u003e 00:16:08.384\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:08.843 --\u003e 00:16:10.011\r\nBATMAN: Evening, ladies.\r\n\r\n00:16:10.511 --\u003e 00:16:11.846\r\nPlaytime's over.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.805 --\u003e 00:16:14.765\r\n(SARCASTICALLY) Land 0'\r\nGoshen, Harleen.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.849 --\u003e 00:16:16.434\r\nLook who's come a-courting.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.976 --\u003e 00:16:18.644\r\nLooks like he's got us.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.728 --\u003e 00:16:20.021\r\nLooks like!\r\n\r\n00:16:22.273 --\u003e 00:16:23.941\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:27.111 --\u003e 00:16:29.572\r\nPOISON IVY: Poor Batman.\r\nAll trussed up.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.989 --\u003e 00:16:32.241\r\nAnd no place to go.\r\n\r\n00:16:34.577 --\u003e 00:16:35.912\r\n_Yes! _Yes!\r\n\r\n00:16:41.000 --\u003e 00:16:43.836\r\nPOISON IVY: Here we have\r\nthe typical male aggressor,\r\n\r\n00:16:43.920 --\u003e 00:16:48.382\r\nfittingly imprisoned within the\r\nbonds of female domestic slavery.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.471 --\u003e 00:16:56.516\r\nHARLEY: And, frankly, folks,\r\nhe's never looked better.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.974 --\u003e 00:16:58.267\r\nAdmit it, darling,\r\n\r\n00:16:58.351 --\u003e 00:17:02.063\r\nyou didn't think two women were\r\ncapable of bringing you down.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.647 --\u003e 00:17:06.275\r\nMan or woman,\r\na sick mind is capable of anything.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.484 --\u003e 00:17:09.779\r\nA very enlightened\r\nstatement, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.488 --\u003e 00:17:12.406\r\nWe'll carve it on\r\nyour headstone.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.741 --\u003e 00:17:15.493\r\nHARLEY: Aloha, sucker.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.456 --\u003e 00:17:22.750\r\nHey,\r\ndid you leave the lights on?\r\n\r\n00:17:29.924 --\u003e 00:17:33.511\r\nJOKER: My, haven't you\r\nbeen the busy little bees.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.512 --\u003e 00:17:35.805\r\nPudding?\r\n\r\n00:17:36.389 --\u003e 00:17:39.559\r\nYou were out,\r\nso we just made ourselves at home.\r\n\r\n00:17:39.850 --\u003e 00:17:41.227\r\nHope you don't mind.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.477 --\u003e 00:17:43.479\r\nYou found me!\r\n\r\n00:17:43.604 --\u003e 00:17:45.314\r\nSo much for self-esteem.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.694 --\u003e 00:17:52.613\r\nI hope you realize we're\r\non a toxic waste dump.\r\n\r\n00:17:52.780 --\u003e 00:17:56.617\r\nI'd say you've got 10 minutes to\r\nclear out before the fumes do you in.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.953 --\u003e 00:18:00.246\r\nShe's right, boss.\r\n\r\n00:18:00.329 --\u003e 00:18:01.956\r\nI'm feeling kind of...\r\n\r\n00:18:02.498 --\u003e 00:18:03.499\r\nSick.\r\n\r\n00:18:03.666 --\u003e 00:18:05.126\r\nHold it in, Rocco.\r\n\r\n00:18:06.168 --\u003e 00:18:10.881\r\nI'm only staying long enough\r\nto collect what's mine.\r\n\r\n00:18:11.007 --\u003e 00:18:12.258\r\n(SQUEALS)\r\n\r\n00:18:12.592 --\u003e 00:18:13.593\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:18:26.147 --\u003e 00:18:27.148\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:27.440 --\u003e 00:18:28.983\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.155 --\u003e 00:18:37.074\r\nOoh! Look at the goodies.\r\n\r\n00:18:37.783 --\u003e 00:18:39.368\r\nThat's ours, you louse!\r\n\r\n00:18:39.744 --\u003e 00:18:43.623\r\nPammy, lwouldn't leave\r\nyou empty-handed.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.206 --\u003e 00:18:46.542\r\nJOKER: Since you like\r\nflowers so much...\r\n\r\n00:18:47.585 --\u003e 00:18:49.003\r\nOh, Pudding, no!\r\n\r\n00:18:50.463 --\u003e 00:18:52.632\r\nYou can have mine!\r\n\r\n00:18:53.716 --\u003e 00:18:55.259\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.052 --\u003e 00:18:57.053\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:18:57.219 --\u003e 00:18:58.220\r\nRed!\r\n\r\n00:19:00.097 --\u003e 00:19:01.432\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.392 --\u003e 00:19:05.061\r\nIt doesn't work on me.\r\n\r\n00:19:10.024 --\u003e 00:19:11.609\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:19.742 --\u003e 00:19:20.743\r\nGet them!\r\n\r\n00:19:28.959 --\u003e 00:19:30.252\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:19:37.259 --\u003e 00:19:39.053\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:42.139 --\u003e 00:19:44.642\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:50.564 --\u003e 00:19:51.899\r\nOh, Batsy!\r\n\r\n00:20:01.909 --\u003e 00:20:03.389\r\n(YELLING) Stop\r\nshooting, you lunatic.\r\n\r\n00:20:03.452 --\u003e 00:20:05.037\r\nWe're sitting on a powder keg.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.979 --\u003e 00:20:31.772\r\nOops. Dopey me.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.149 --\u003e 00:20:34.150\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:50.624 --\u003e 00:20:52.168\r\n(ENGINE STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:55.880 --\u003e 00:20:56.881\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:20:57.089 --\u003e 00:20:58.799\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:21:11.604 --\u003e 00:21:14.148\r\nNo man can take us prisoner.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.775 --\u003e 00:21:16.817\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:21:16.901 --\u003e 00:21:18.194\r\n(BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:21:22.782 --\u003e 00:21:24.450\r\nAll right, ladies.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.784 --\u003e 00:21:25.868\r\nRaise them.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.660 --\u003e 00:21:28.496\r\n(CHATTERING ON POLICE RADIO)\r\n\r\n00:21:33.834 --\u003e 00:21:35.252\r\nJOKER: That's it.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.336 --\u003e 00:21:39.006\r\nNext time I start a\r\ngang, no women.\r\n\r\n00:21:39.465 --\u003e 00:21:40.716\r\n(SHOUTING) Do you hear me?\r\n\r\n00:21:40.925 --\u003e 00:21:42.384\r\nNo women!\r\n\r\n00:21:43.010 --\u003e 00:21:45.304\r\nI think we can\r\nstill work it out.\r\n\r\n00:21:45.471 --\u003e 00:21:46.722\r\nDon't you?\r\n\r\n00:22:23.551 --\u003e 00:22:24.552\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E48 - The Mechanic (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.422 --\u003e 00:00:07.424\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:05.148 --\u003e 00:01:07.526\r\nTHE MECHANIC\r\n\r\n00:01:42.644 --\u003e 00:01:43.895\r\nIs he kidding?\r\n\r\n00:01:45.105 --\u003e 00:01:47.316\r\n(GUN CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:47.816 --\u003e 00:01:49.401\r\nMaybe he's new in town.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.863 --\u003e 00:01:55.907\r\n- Can't you go any faster?\r\n- I'm flooring it now.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.578 --\u003e 00:02:02.289\r\n(CRASHING AND TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.801 --\u003e 00:02:16.595\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.140 --\u003e 00:02:21.642\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:27.981 --\u003e 00:02:30.400\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:02:54.091 --\u003e 00:02:55.842\r\nMAN: Hold on, guys!\r\n\r\n00:02:56.051 --\u003e 00:02:58.720\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:05.185 --\u003e 00:03:06.478\r\n(ALL GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:03:08.980 --\u003e 00:03:10.315\r\n(BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:13.944 --\u003e 00:03:17.572\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:30.127 --\u003e 00:03:31.211\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:31.294 --\u003e 00:03:33.839\r\nLooks like Earl's got\r\nhis work cut out for him.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.177 --\u003e 00:03:41.680\r\n(ENGINE SPUTTERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.768 --\u003e 00:03:48.103\r\n(BUZZER SOUNDING)\r\n\r\n00:03:59.448 --\u003e 00:04:00.657\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\n00:04:02.701 --\u003e 00:04:04.536\r\nYou been letting\r\nthe kid drive again?\r\n\r\n00:04:04.745 --\u003e 00:04:05.912\r\n(LAUGHS SARCASTICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:04:06.288 --\u003e 00:04:08.415\r\nActually, we were playing\r\nchicken with a penguin.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.749 --\u003e 00:04:11.334\r\n- Looks like the penguin won.\r\n- The Penguin?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.585 --\u003e 00:04:14.337\r\nOr three of his men, at least.\r\nBut they flew the coop.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.883 --\u003e 00:04:20.043\r\nEARL: Then I guess you'll be\r\nneeding the loaners again.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.098 --\u003e 00:04:26.349\r\n(ENGINE STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.892 --\u003e 00:04:28.477\r\n- Well?\r\n- The alignment,\r\n\r\n00:04:28.560 --\u003e 00:04:31.521\r\nthe whole suspension,\r\nall shot to heck.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.230 --\u003e 00:04:34.524\r\n(GROANS) I'll call you\r\nin a couple of days.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.108 --\u003e 00:04:36.443\r\nMARVA: Better make it a week.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.610 --\u003e 00:04:39.780\r\nLooks like we're gonna have to\r\norder a whole new drive train.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.618 --\u003e 00:04:45.994\r\nCome on, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.382 --\u003e 00:05:02.594\r\nGuess we won't be seeing\r\nsunlight for a while, Dad?\r\n\r\n00:05:02.761 --\u003e 00:05:05.514\r\nOnce we've got the parts\r\nit ought to go quickly.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.764 --\u003e 00:05:10.811\r\nBetter put in the order right now.\r\nLet's see. Twelve-gauge piston pins.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.063 --\u003e 00:05:15.565\r\nPENGUIN: These are terrible.\r\nTerrible!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.027 --\u003e 00:05:22.739\r\nCome on, boss, give me a break. We got\r\nyou the stamps. What more do you want?\r\n\r\n00:05:23.573 --\u003e 00:05:26.326\r\nI wanted the rare ones!\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.910 --\u003e 00:05:29.037\r\nThe reversed Audubons.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.246 --\u003e 00:05:32.332\r\nThese aren't worth enough to pay\r\nfor the repairs to the limousine.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.837 --\u003e 00:05:40.507\r\nGive me one good reason why I shouldn't\r\nhave Percival here peck out your eyes.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.590 --\u003e 00:05:41.591\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:05:42.717 --\u003e 00:05:44.010\r\n(SQUAWKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:44.219 --\u003e 00:05:46.888\r\n- Well, I'm waiting.\r\n- MAN: Here's a reason, boss.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.138 --\u003e 00:05:50.475\r\nIf we never banged up the limo,\r\nI'd never have run into my old friend.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.725 --\u003e 00:05:52.769\r\nThe one I told you about.\r\nRemember?\r\n\r\n00:05:56.690 --\u003e 00:06:00.318\r\nAh, yes, the one who works for\r\nthat auto-parts distributor.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.735 --\u003e 00:06:03.822\r\nMmm-hmm. That's me.\r\nRundle. Arnold Rundle.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.033 --\u003e 00:06:08.869\r\nI process custom orders.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.077 --\u003e 00:06:11.538\r\n- Go on, Arnie. Show him.\r\n- Right.\r\n\r\n00:06:11.621 --\u003e 00:06:15.041\r\nThis is an order my\r\ncompany received yesterday.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.460 --\u003e 00:06:21.214\r\n\"Titanium-steel wheel wells,\r\n12-gauge piston pins.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:21.756 --\u003e 00:06:26.052\r\nVery few vehicles use such\r\nunusual material as those.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.636 --\u003e 00:06:29.014\r\nAnd the point of this is what?\r\n\r\n00:06:29.890 --\u003e 00:06:33.018\r\nI think these parts were\r\nordered for the Batmobile.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.602 --\u003e 00:06:34.603\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:06:35.353 --\u003e 00:06:36.354\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:06:39.941 --\u003e 00:06:41.276\r\nTell him why, Arnie.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.818 --\u003e 00:06:44.362\r\nWell,\r\nright after I got that order,\r\n\r\n00:06:44.613 --\u003e 00:06:46.823\r\nFalcone told me what\r\nhappened to the Batmobile\r\n\r\n00:06:46.907 --\u003e 00:06:49.534\r\nwhile it was chasing\r\nyour limo the other day.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.826 --\u003e 00:06:53.830\r\nFrom the description, I'd say the\r\nkind of damage the Batmobile sustained\r\n\r\n00:06:53.914 --\u003e 00:06:57.792\r\nmight require the kind of\r\nreplacement parts in that order.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.168 --\u003e 00:07:00.545\r\nYes. Yes, I understand.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.087 --\u003e 00:07:02.297\r\nYou do?\r\n\r\n00:07:02.380 --\u003e 00:07:04.841\r\nWhy, yes.\r\nAnd it's absolutely brilliant.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.091 --\u003e 00:07:07.010\r\nA first-rate piece\r\nof detective work.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.302 --\u003e 00:07:09.137\r\nYou are to be rewarded, sir.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.429 --\u003e 00:07:11.181\r\n(GASPS) Reward?\r\n\r\n00:07:11.264 --\u003e 00:07:13.391\r\nWould $300,000 be enough?\r\n\r\n00:07:13.934 --\u003e 00:07:17.062\r\n- 300,000?\r\n- Oh, all right, 400,000,\r\n\r\n00:07:17.145 --\u003e 00:07:18.772\r\nbut that's my final offer.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.152 --\u003e 00:07:26.279\r\nDon't spend it all in one place.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.824 --\u003e 00:07:31.952\r\nUh... Excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.661 --\u003e 00:07:35.330\r\n- I don't get it, boss.\r\n- It's all right here.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.705 --\u003e 00:07:39.125\r\nOur friend, Mr. Rundle, amassed\r\nnewspaper reports of various instances\r\n\r\n00:07:39.209 --\u003e 00:07:41.044\r\nwhen the Batmobile was damaged.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.544 --\u003e 00:07:43.439\r\nThen he checked the dates\r\nagainst the other times\r\n\r\n00:07:43.463 --\u003e 00:07:45.715\r\nhis company got orders for\r\nthese types of materials.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.882 --\u003e 00:07:46.967\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:47.050 --\u003e 00:07:50.971\r\nPENGUIN: In every case, it was a match.\r\nThe same exact date.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.429 --\u003e 00:07:54.140\r\nExcuse me.\r\nWhere will this take me?\r\n\r\n00:07:54.391 --\u003e 00:07:55.809\r\nOn a sea cruise.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.601 --\u003e 00:07:59.062\r\nHere.\r\nLook at these bills of lading.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.855 --\u003e 00:08:02.023\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:02.273 --\u003e 00:08:07.821\r\nARNOLD: (YELLING) Excuse me!\r\nI'm expected back at the office!\r\n\r\n00:08:08.530 --\u003e 00:08:11.116\r\nPENGUIN: All the orders come\r\nfrom the same repair shop\r\n\r\n00:08:11.324 --\u003e 00:08:13.868\r\nrun by a certain Mr. Cooper.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.912 --\u003e 00:08:17.622\r\nEarl Cooper.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.501 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\n(BLUES MUSIC PLAYING ON RADIO)\r\n\r\n00:08:26.798 --\u003e 00:08:28.383\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:08:54.409 --\u003e 00:08:56.619\r\nEarl, my good fellow.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.039 --\u003e 00:09:03.126\r\nI'm afraid the warranty on\r\nthis vehicle has just expired.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.384 --\u003e 00:09:13.219\r\nIt's just like I figured, boss.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.179 --\u003e 00:09:17.766\r\nThe on board computer routes all\r\nthe controls through a main switch.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.600 --\u003e 00:09:22.020\r\nThen we're going to pull\r\na switch on a switch.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.730 --\u003e 00:09:25.106\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.398 --\u003e 00:09:26.524\r\nNow what?\r\n\r\n00:09:26.608 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\n(GROANS) The flipping thing\r\ndarn near electrocuted me.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.569 --\u003e 00:09:32.363\r\nThere's a security device to\r\nkeep it from being tampered with.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.906 --\u003e 00:09:34.532\r\nThen disconnect it.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.533 --\u003e 00:09:37.202\r\nI wouldn't even know\r\nwhere to look for it.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.577 --\u003e 00:09:39.370\r\nWell, I know who does.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.625 --\u003e 00:09:46.920\r\nAnd he's going to help\r\nus, aren't you, Earl?\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:49.756\r\nIn your dreams, Pinocchio.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.465 --\u003e 00:09:52.926\r\nAnd how, pray tell,\r\ndid that costumed clown\r\n\r\n00:09:53.009 --\u003e 00:09:55.428\r\ngive you such a bad\r\ncase of loyalty?\r\n\r\n00:09:55.720 --\u003e 00:09:59.307\r\n- None of your business.\r\n- PENGUIN: I'm making it my business.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.225 --\u003e 00:10:02.519\r\nPerhaps you've heard\r\nof my umbrella weapons.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.977 --\u003e 00:10:06.523\r\nWould you like to see what\r\none can do to your daughter?\r\n\r\n00:10:07.774 --\u003e 00:10:09.651\r\nDon't listen to him, Dad.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.734 --\u003e 00:10:10.944\r\n(MUFFLED YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:11.361 --\u003e 00:10:12.612\r\nOkay. Okay.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.489 --\u003e 00:10:17.242\r\nIf you must know, I used to be\r\nan engineer at Global Motors...\r\n\r\n00:10:18.409 --\u003e 00:10:22.372\r\n\u003ci\u003etill I predicted one of their new sports\r\ncars would have brake-design problems.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:24.374 --\u003e 00:10:27.919\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut they ignored my warnings and\r\nintroduced a new model anyway.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:28.169 --\u003e 00:10:31.673\r\nBut, Cooper, the boys in Legal\r\nsay we can't be held accountable.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.425 --\u003e 00:10:36.970\r\nWe're talking about\r\npeople's lives here.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.472 --\u003e 00:10:42.475\r\nWell, thank you for your time.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.393 --\u003e 00:10:44.602\r\nLet it go, Earl.\r\n\r\n00:10:44.978 --\u003e 00:10:47.063\r\nHey, you've got a\r\nbright future here.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.523 --\u003e 00:10:50.191\r\n- Don't blow it.\r\n- (DOOR SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:51.234 --\u003e 00:10:52.986\r\nHe's gonna report it, I know it.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.196 --\u003e 00:10:58.241\r\nThen if our Mr. Cooper is\r\ngoing to become a liability,\r\n\r\n00:10:58.533 --\u003e 00:11:02.370\r\nI suggest we take steps\r\nto minimize our risk. Hmm?\r\n\r\n00:11:04.164 --\u003e 00:11:05.165\r\n(BLEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:11:06.749 --\u003e 00:11:09.502\r\nEARL: \u003ci\u003eThat same night,\r\nthey sicced some hired muscle on me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:10.670 --\u003e 00:11:11.671\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:20.138 --\u003e 00:11:21.431\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:26.352 --\u003e 00:11:27.353\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:27.437 --\u003e 00:11:28.438\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:11:30.440 --\u003e 00:11:31.441\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.946 --\u003e 00:11:39.365\r\n\u003ci\u003eEARL: He saved my butt\r\nfor sure that day.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:43.244 --\u003e 00:11:45.914\r\nBut long after the Global\r\nscandal was forgotten,\r\n\r\n00:11:46.206 --\u003e 00:11:48.917\r\nI still had a reputation\r\nas a whistle-blower.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.167 --\u003e 00:11:50.835\r\nTwenty years in the business,\r\n\r\n00:11:51.085 --\u003e 00:11:53.213\r\nand I couldn't get work\r\nas a wrench jockey.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.796 --\u003e 00:11:57.008\r\nI was down to my last dime.\r\nNo money, no job,\r\n\r\n00:11:57.300 --\u003e 00:11:59.052\r\nand no prospects for one.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.302 --\u003e 00:12:02.472\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd then he saved my life again.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:03.056 --\u003e 00:12:04.682\r\n(ENGINE SPUTTERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.727 --\u003e 00:12:08.728\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:12:12.565 --\u003e 00:12:14.108\r\nI need a new car.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.734 --\u003e 00:12:17.028\r\nEARL: \u003ci\u003eIt was a\r\nchallenge of a lifetime.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:18.238 --\u003e 00:12:21.866\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt took me six months to come\r\nup with the design specs alone.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:22.784 --\u003e 00:12:25.995\r\n\u003ci\u003eTitanium construction,\r\nablative skin cowling,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:26.246 --\u003e 00:12:28.289\r\n\u003ci\u003etri-nitro propulsion units.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:30.833 --\u003e 00:12:33.294\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe paid for everything. Cash.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:33.503 --\u003e 00:12:37.674\r\n\u003ci\u003eFound this site for a garage, too,\r\nand outfitted it to my specifications\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:37.966 --\u003e 00:12:40.009\r\n\u003ci\u003eand paid me real well.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:40.301 --\u003e 00:12:41.928\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut he got his money's worth.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:45.265 --\u003e 00:12:47.267\r\nHmm. He set you up here, huh?\r\n\r\n00:12:47.684 --\u003e 00:12:50.520\r\nWell,\r\nnow you're going to set him up.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.812 --\u003e 00:12:53.106\r\nBe sure to do exactly\r\nas I tell you,\r\n\r\n00:12:53.189 --\u003e 00:12:56.651\r\nor the next person who gets a\r\njolt out of your security device\r\n\r\n00:12:56.734 --\u003e 00:12:58.820\r\nwill be your charming daughter.\r\n\r\n00:13:03.324 --\u003e 00:13:05.576\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:12.875 --\u003e 00:13:16.170\r\nYes, Batman, it's ready any\r\ntime you wanna pick it up.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.630 --\u003e 00:13:19.048\r\nHe's on his way.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.382 --\u003e 00:13:21.843\r\nAnd we will be ready for him.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.385 --\u003e 00:13:23.386\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:24.178 --\u003e 00:13:25.596\r\nWon't we, Earl?\r\n\r\n00:13:28.182 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:13:34.397 --\u003e 00:13:36.899\r\nAll right, gentlemen,\r\nbattle stations.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.900 --\u003e 00:13:39.485\r\nThe Bat is about to bite...\r\n\r\n00:13:39.694 --\u003e 00:13:42.447\r\nThe dust, that is.\r\nPut her in the limo.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.493 --\u003e 00:13:50.997\r\nInsurance,\r\njust in case you forget your lines.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.874 --\u003e 00:13:56.085\r\nAnd do take a good long look\r\nat your friend, the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.377 --\u003e 00:14:00.506\r\nAfter all, you'll be saying\r\nadieu to your best customer.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.590 --\u003e 00:14:02.675\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:14:14.354 --\u003e 00:14:17.023\r\n- Looks great, Earl.\r\n- BATMAN: Big job, wasn't it?\r\n\r\n00:14:17.106 --\u003e 00:14:18.149\r\nYou look tired.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.358 --\u003e 00:14:21.319\r\nYeah. Well,\r\nit took longer than I figured.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.736 --\u003e 00:14:24.697\r\nSee? Haven't even had\r\ntime to clean up yet.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.864 --\u003e 00:14:27.784\r\n- Where's Marva?\r\n- EARL: Oh. Down in the basement.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.159 --\u003e 00:14:31.871\r\nGot some cleaning to do down\r\nthere, in the basement.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.956 --\u003e 00:14:37.293\r\nBy the way, I even fixed\r\nthe air-conditioning switch.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.380 --\u003e 00:14:41.756\r\nUh... Right.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.175 --\u003e 00:14:45.551\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:54.185\r\nMAN: You did good, old man.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.150 --\u003e 00:15:02.652\r\nThey just left.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.208 --\u003e 00:15:19.752\r\n- What's bugging you?\r\n- He seemed upset.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.086 --\u003e 00:15:22.547\r\n- Something's just not right.\r\n- (CAR HONKS)\r\n\r\n00:15:28.428 --\u003e 00:15:29.429\r\n(FARTING NOISE)\r\n\r\n00:15:33.683 --\u003e 00:15:35.685\r\n- The Penguin!\r\n- Hang on.\r\n\r\n00:15:35.935 --\u003e 00:15:37.854\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:39.063 --\u003e 00:15:40.314\r\nHere they come!\r\n\r\n00:15:40.690 --\u003e 00:15:42.316\r\n(SNICKERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.746 --\u003e 00:15:57.623\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n- (METAL SCRATCHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:05.423 --\u003e 00:16:06.591\r\nWhat are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:16:06.799 --\u003e 00:16:10.219\r\n(GRUNTING) Nothing.\r\nWe've been sabotaged.\r\n\r\n00:16:10.428 --\u003e 00:16:12.138\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.413 --\u003e 00:16:38.414\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.466 --\u003e 00:16:49.675\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.551 --\u003e 00:16:52.220\r\nPENGUIN: Bye-bye, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.514 --\u003e 00:16:56.807\r\nMan, how did he get\r\ncontrol of the car?\r\n\r\n00:16:57.225 --\u003e 00:16:59.977\r\nHe got control of Earl.\r\nCome on, we better bail.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.274 --\u003e 00:17:06.609\r\n(BOTH EXCLAIM)\r\n\r\n00:17:10.988 --\u003e 00:17:12.198\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:30.466 --\u003e 00:17:31.842\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.181 --\u003e 00:17:38.766\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.725 --\u003e 00:17:41.102\r\nStand by to eject.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.145 --\u003e 00:17:44.689\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:45.481 --\u003e 00:17:48.484\r\n(CHUCKLES) I hate to burst\r\nyour balloon, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:17:48.568 --\u003e 00:17:50.945\r\nbut now it's time for you to go.\r\n\r\n00:17:54.615 --\u003e 00:17:56.325\r\n- (GRUNTING)\r\n- (ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:17:57.034 --\u003e 00:18:00.580\r\nI got a feeling we're about\r\nto take the hard way down.\r\n\r\n00:18:00.997 --\u003e 00:18:03.416\r\n- Down? The basement!\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:18:03.499 --\u003e 00:18:05.585\r\nEarl. He kept saying \"basement.\"\r\n\r\n00:18:05.751 --\u003e 00:18:07.753\r\nIt's a racing term.\r\nWhen drivers crash,\r\n\r\n00:18:07.837 --\u003e 00:18:10.840\r\nthey say they've gone down in the basement.\r\nHe was warning us.\r\n\r\n00:18:15.928 --\u003e 00:18:18.639\r\nThe air-conditioning switch.\r\nHe said he'd fixed it.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.485 --\u003e 00:18:32.486\r\nHa!\r\n\r\n00:18:40.244 --\u003e 00:18:43.039\r\nPity.\r\nIt was a magnificent vehicle.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.122 --\u003e 00:18:44.749\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:52.340 --\u003e 00:18:53.883\r\nAll right, Earl!\r\n\r\n00:18:54.508 --\u003e 00:18:56.927\r\nRight. Blew him sky-high, huh?\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:57.470 --\u003e 00:19:00.014\r\n(IMITATES STAMMER) Bat's all, folks.\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:19:00.640 --\u003e 00:19:02.141\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- (EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.068 --\u003e 00:19:13.736\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:14.362 --\u003e 00:19:15.571\r\nMAN: Let me down!\r\n\r\n00:19:15.821 --\u003e 00:19:17.698\r\nWhat are you doing? Let me down!\r\n\r\n00:19:23.079 --\u003e 00:19:25.206\r\nWait! Hey, boss, behind us!\r\n\r\n00:19:25.289 --\u003e 00:19:28.459\r\nWhat? It's not possible.\r\nGet us out of here!\r\n\r\n00:19:35.633 --\u003e 00:19:37.426\r\nGet him off us! Lose him!\r\n\r\n00:19:37.718 --\u003e 00:19:39.178\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:56.278 --\u003e 00:19:57.446\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:19:58.531 --\u003e 00:20:00.116\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.923 --\u003e 00:20:17.007\r\nPENGUIN: Come on.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.385 --\u003e 00:20:20.761\r\nLet her go, Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.853 --\u003e 00:20:30.521\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.398 --\u003e 00:20:33.607\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:20:39.196 --\u003e 00:20:40.197\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:46.704 --\u003e 00:20:48.372\r\nUh-uh.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.749 --\u003e 00:20:51.250\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:55.921 --\u003e 00:20:57.298\r\nI'm gonna miss this place.\r\n\r\n00:20:57.631 --\u003e 00:21:00.050\r\nOnly till you see the new\r\none I'm setting up for you.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.134 --\u003e 00:21:02.845\r\nBut this time I had my backers\r\n\r\n00:21:02.928 --\u003e 00:21:05.556\r\nset up dummy corporations\r\nto order the parts through.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.639 --\u003e 00:21:07.224\r\nSo no one can trace you again.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.600 --\u003e 00:21:10.686\r\nEARL: Yeah?\r\nWait till you see the new Batmobile.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.020 --\u003e 00:21:14.440\r\nIt's gonna have tritium\r\nthrusters, dual accelerators,\r\n\r\n00:21:14.940 --\u003e 00:21:17.109\r\nfuel-injected turbo boosters.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.068 --\u003e 00:21:20.362\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:21:39.673 --\u003e 00:21:40.966\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:41.050 --\u003e 00:21:42.384\r\n\"One bat for you\"?\r\n\r\n00:21:42.593 --\u003e 00:21:44.595\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:48.808 --\u003e 00:21:50.810\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:14.667 --\u003e 00:22:16.669\r\nTranslated by:\r\n\r\n00:22:18.671 --\u003e 00:22:19.672\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E49 - The Man Who Killed Batman (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.419 --\u003e 00:00:04.421\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:27.087 --\u003e 00:01:29.423\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:35.887 --\u003e 00:01:37.180\r\n- (CAR HON KS)\r\n- (YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:39.016 --\u003e 00:01:40.017\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:01:50.402 --\u003e 00:01:52.696\r\nOh, no.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.211 --\u003e 00:02:12.132\r\nLet me in, please.\r\nI have to see Mr. Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.720 --\u003e 00:02:18.180\r\n(KNOCK AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.724 --\u003e 00:02:22.976\r\nA Sidney Debris to see you, sir.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.854 --\u003e 00:02:26.855\r\nSend him in.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.984 --\u003e 00:02:34.905\r\nMr. Thorne, I'm so grateful you're\r\nwilling to see me on such short-\r\n\r\n00:02:34.988 --\u003e 00:02:37.032\r\nNonsense, Sidney. Come in.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.116 --\u003e 00:02:39.910\r\nJoin me for a demitasse?\r\n\r\n00:02:40.535 --\u003e 00:02:41.995\r\nNo, thank you, sir.\r\n\r\n00:02:43.830 --\u003e 00:02:44.831\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.915 --\u003e 00:02:46.041\r\n(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:46.541 --\u003e 00:02:48.752\r\n- Sorry about the leather.\r\n- Mmm.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.835 --\u003e 00:02:52.005\r\nI hear you've made quite a name for\r\nyourself on the streets, Sidney.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.506 --\u003e 00:02:55.258\r\nWhat is it they're calling you?\r\nOh, yes.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.425 --\u003e 00:02:57.511\r\n\"The Man Who Killed Batman.\"\r\n\r\n00:02:58.220 --\u003e 00:03:00.806\r\nWell, yes, no...\r\nThat is, I didn't...\r\n\r\n00:03:00.889 --\u003e 00:03:04.017\r\nOh, Mr. Thorne,\r\nI'm in big trouble.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.518 --\u003e 00:03:06.478\r\nNow, now, just relax, man.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.645 --\u003e 00:03:08.772\r\nAnd tell me what's on your mind.\r\n\r\n00:03:09.398 --\u003e 00:03:13.485\r\nSIDNEY: Well, for a while now, I've been\r\ntrying to move my way up in the rackets.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.944 --\u003e 00:03:17.656\r\nA few nights ago, my pal Eddie G.\r\nTold me about a big drug shipment\r\n\r\n00:03:17.739 --\u003e 00:03:19.908\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe was picking up\r\nfor some mob hotshot.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:20.367 --\u003e 00:03:22.911\r\n\u003ci\u003eSounded like an opportunity\r\nand I wanted in.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:33.714 --\u003e 00:03:34.798\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:03:44.141 --\u003e 00:03:45.267\r\nHey, hey.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.560 --\u003e 00:03:49.062\r\n- You want to blow this whole deal?\r\n- Sorry, Eddie.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.188 --\u003e 00:03:52.649\r\nWhy did you bring along that loser?\r\nHe's useless.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.024 --\u003e 00:03:54.693\r\nNot as bait for Batman.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.235 --\u003e 00:03:58.196\r\nHe'll be too busy kicking the\r\ncrud out of Sid to notice us.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.905 --\u003e 00:04:01.783\r\nYo, Sid.\r\nThis is your big chance, bud.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.075 --\u003e 00:04:05.954\r\nYou do this job right, you might\r\neven score yourself a cool mob name.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.538 --\u003e 00:04:07.581\r\nLike what?\r\n\r\n00:04:07.664 --\u003e 00:04:10.083\r\nUh... We'll call you.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.792 --\u003e 00:04:12.169\r\nSid the Squid.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.836 --\u003e 00:04:14.588\r\nSid the Squid.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.880 --\u003e 00:04:16.673\r\nYeah, yeah.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.174 --\u003e 00:04:19.843\r\nNow, get your keister up there\r\nand holler if you see anything.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.727 --\u003e 00:04:30.979\r\nSIDNEY: Like a\r\nhungry sea predator,\r\n\r\n00:04:31.271 --\u003e 00:04:33.940\r\nSid the Squid\r\nstretched his tentacles\r\n\r\n00:04:34.024 --\u003e 00:04:36.610\r\nthrough the Gotham underworld.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.068 --\u003e 00:04:39.821\r\nYeah, boy, I'm on my way.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.905 --\u003e 00:04:41.656\r\nNothing's gonna stop me now.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.751 --\u003e 00:04:54.628\r\nThat's weird,\r\nwonder where that...\r\n\r\n00:04:56.546 --\u003e 00:04:57.881\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:04.971 --\u003e 00:05:06.515\r\nSIDNEY: Help!\r\n\r\n00:05:12.646 --\u003e 00:05:13.688\r\nEDDIE: The Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:14.731 --\u003e 00:05:16.983\r\nHey,\r\nthis isn't what it looks like.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.944 --\u003e 00:05:23.073\r\nLooks like a drug run to me. Someone's\r\nflooding the streets with that trash.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:25.408\r\n- I want his name.\r\n- I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.534 --\u003e 00:05:27.869\r\nI'm just the lookout, honest.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.954 --\u003e 00:05:29.955\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:05:30.038 --\u003e 00:05:31.873\r\nTHUG: Sid's taking\r\non the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.957 --\u003e 00:05:35.210\r\nLittle weasel's got guts.\r\nNo brains, but guts.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.293 --\u003e 00:05:36.586\r\nSplit.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.671 --\u003e 00:05:39.339\r\n(YELLS) \"(GRUNTS)\"\r\n\r\n00:05:40.799 --\u003e 00:05:44.553\r\nOh, I'm so sorry.\r\nIt was an accident, really.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.803 --\u003e 00:05:46.471\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Back off.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.555 --\u003e 00:05:47.764\r\nYes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.307 --\u003e 00:05:50.684\r\n\"(YELPS) (GAsPs)\"\r\n\r\n00:05:53.019 --\u003e 00:05:54.271\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:05:54.980 --\u003e 00:05:56.982\r\nDon't let me fall, please!\r\n\r\n00:05:59.776 --\u003e 00:06:00.777\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:06:10.203 --\u003e 00:06:12.789\r\nStop struggling. Let go!\r\n\r\n00:06:15.876 --\u003e 00:06:16.960\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.386 --\u003e 00:06:27.804\r\n- What?\r\n- What was that?\r\n\r\n00:06:36.688 --\u003e 00:06:39.858\r\nI didn't mean it. He came right at me.\r\nI was just trying to get away,\r\n\r\n00:06:39.941 --\u003e 00:06:42.903\r\nand he went over the side.\r\nBoom, whoosh, fire!\r\n\r\n00:06:42.986 --\u003e 00:06:44.487\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.822 --\u003e 00:06:47.532\r\nNo one could live through that.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:53.163\r\nYou know what this means?\r\nSid the Squid just offed the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.961 --\u003e 00:07:01.546\r\nYou should be happy, Sidney.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.925 --\u003e 00:07:06.843\r\nThrough a\r\none-in-a-million mishap,\r\n\r\n00:07:06.927 --\u003e 00:07:10.388\r\nyou've realized the dream\r\nof every criminal in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.598 --\u003e 00:07:12.682\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:07:12.766 --\u003e 00:07:15.602\r\nThe utter demise of Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.102 --\u003e 00:07:19.022\r\nYou know, Mr. Thorne,\r\nmy whole life\r\n\r\n00:07:19.105 --\u003e 00:07:21.900\r\nI've dreamed of\r\nbeing a big shot.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.026 --\u003e 00:07:26.112\r\nALL: (CHANTING)\r\nSidney, Sidney, Sidney.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.449 --\u003e 00:07:34.704\r\n\u003ci\u003eSIDNEY: And that night, for one\r\nminute, all my dreams came true.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:36.790 --\u003e 00:07:41.002\r\nTo Sid the Squid,\r\nthe man who burned the bat.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.795 --\u003e 00:07:45.840\r\nALL: Squid! Squid! Squid!\r\n\r\n00:07:45.924 --\u003e 00:07:48.051\r\nEDDIE: The toughest\r\nguy in Gotham!\r\n\r\n00:07:50.303 --\u003e 00:07:51.596\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:07:56.184 --\u003e 00:07:57.185\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:57.268 --\u003e 00:08:02.065\r\nSuddenly I'm thinking, if I take\r\ndown the guy who took down Batman,\r\n\r\n00:08:02.899 --\u003e 00:08:06.027\r\nthen I'll be the\r\ntoughest guy in town.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.403 --\u003e 00:08:08.530\r\nYou got my vote, Chief.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.656 --\u003e 00:08:12.117\r\nCome on, Squid,\r\ngive him what for.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.367 --\u003e 00:08:14.178\r\n- THUG: Come on, let's get it going here.\r\n- (ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:08:14.202 --\u003e 00:08:15.620\r\nGet up. Come on.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.050 --\u003e 00:08:30.051\r\n(SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:08:38.601 --\u003e 00:08:40.520\r\n\u003ci\u003eSIDNEY: It was nuts, I tell you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:40.812 --\u003e 00:08:45.150\r\n\u003ci\u003eEvery creep and lowlife trying to get a\r\nlittle piece of the guy who got Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:48.111 --\u003e 00:08:50.822\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was actually relieved\r\nwhen the cops showed up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:51.072 --\u003e 00:08:52.741\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.745 --\u003e 00:08:58.371\r\n\u003ci\u003eWell, sort of.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:58.663 --\u003e 00:09:00.582\r\n- You can't keep me here.\r\n- I got rights.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.707 --\u003e 00:09:02.167\r\n- Lousy bulls.\r\n- (ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:09:02.333 --\u003e 00:09:06.046\r\nSimmer down, party boys.\r\nYou'll be out tomorrow morning.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.588 --\u003e 00:09:11.009\r\nUh, Montoya, word is coming in from\r\nthe streets on a homicide victim.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.259 --\u003e 00:09:13.720\r\n- They have an ID?\r\n- Yeah, it's, uh...\r\n\r\n00:09:14.804 --\u003e 00:09:15.930\r\nIt's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.306 --\u003e 00:09:17.307\r\n(GULPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:17.515 --\u003e 00:09:19.142\r\nWhat? How?\r\n\r\n00:09:19.601 --\u003e 00:09:21.519\r\nThat explosion at\r\nthe customs house.\r\n\r\n00:09:21.686 --\u003e 00:09:25.607\r\nThey said it's the work of some\r\nmastermind called the Squid.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.609 --\u003e 00:09:28.610\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.903 --\u003e 00:09:30.904\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:31.571 --\u003e 00:09:32.572\r\n(SPEAKING SPANISH)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.031 --\u003e 00:09:36.409\r\nLook, Renee,\r\nthe commish is taking it pretty hard.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.826 --\u003e 00:09:39.204\r\n- Could you, uh...\r\n- Sure, sure.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.084 --\u003e 00:09:47.212\r\nHow about it, losers?\r\nYou see anything tonight?\r\n\r\n00:09:47.462 --\u003e 00:09:49.464\r\nWhat's the word on this Squid\r\nguy, huh?\r\n\r\n00:09:49.589 --\u003e 00:09:51.049\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:09:51.299 --\u003e 00:09:53.885\r\nWhat about you, skinny?\r\nYou got anything to say?\r\n\r\n00:09:54.052 --\u003e 00:09:55.261\r\n(WOMAN CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:09:56.679 --\u003e 00:09:58.223\r\nJust one minute, please.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.681 --\u003e 00:10:02.227\r\nI'm Harleen Quinzel,\r\nlegal counsel to Mr. Debris.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.477 --\u003e 00:10:05.313\r\nI've paid his bail, and he doesn't\r\nhave to answer any questions\r\n\r\n00:10:05.396 --\u003e 00:10:07.315\r\nuntil he's formally arraigned.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.956 --\u003e 00:10:24.749\r\nDon't I know you from someplace?\r\n\r\n00:10:24.999 --\u003e 00:10:27.460\r\nI think I served\r\nyou a subpoena once.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.170 --\u003e 00:10:31.506\r\nIt was a small subpoena.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.484 --\u003e 00:10:55.405\r\nGee! Who would care enough\r\nto bail me out of the jug?\r\n\r\n00:10:55.572 --\u003e 00:10:57.490\r\nMy mom doesn't even speak to me.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.657 --\u003e 00:11:00.076\r\nAnd my parole officer's\r\nstill in jail.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.494 --\u003e 00:11:02.704\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:03.079 --\u003e 00:11:05.874\r\nWow, lady,\r\nyou sure pile on the makeup.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.249 --\u003e 00:11:09.294\r\nMy boss likes me to\r\nwear a smile to work.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.460 --\u003e 00:11:13.381\r\nHey, I've seen you.\r\nYou work for...\r\n\r\n00:11:13.548 --\u003e 00:11:15.800\r\n(GASPS) The Joker.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.596 --\u003e 00:11:22.015\r\nWelcome, Sidney.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.443 --\u003e 00:11:36.404\r\nPlease, allow me the\r\nhonor of shaking hands\r\n\r\n00:11:36.487 --\u003e 00:11:39.365\r\nwith the man who\r\ndid the impossible.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.866 --\u003e 00:11:44.579\r\nThe man who killed Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.998 --\u003e 00:11:47.999\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:48.082 --\u003e 00:11:52.253\r\nWhoops!\r\n(LAUGHS) Sorry, force of habit.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.629 --\u003e 00:11:56.674\r\nYou know, there's just one thing\r\nbothering me about your story, Sid.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.799 --\u003e 00:12:00.803\r\nNo body, no batus\r\ndelecti, so to speak.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.346 --\u003e 00:12:04.015\r\nWe need to pull a job\r\ntonight just to make sure.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.432 --\u003e 00:12:06.309\r\nMake sure of what, boss?\r\n\r\n00:12:08.686 --\u003e 00:12:11.689\r\nWhy, that old Batsy's bought the\r\ncave, of course.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.814 --\u003e 00:12:15.902\r\nAnd one more thing, Murphy.\r\nDon't ask stupid questions.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.444 --\u003e 00:12:17.779\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:12:17.946 --\u003e 00:12:19.656\r\n- Ah! Ooh!\r\n- (DOGS YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:25.411 --\u003e 00:12:28.248\r\n(YAWNS) I'll get the mop.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.716 --\u003e 00:12:40.802\r\n(ALARM RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:12:41.135 --\u003e 00:12:42.553\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:12:47.267 --\u003e 00:12:48.977\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:49.978 --\u003e 00:12:54.774\r\nRighty-o! Harley, you loot the\r\nsafe while the boys and I set up.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.275 --\u003e 00:12:57.235\r\nRight away, Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:12:58.278 --\u003e 00:13:02.490\r\nWhen the cops show, stall them for a while.\r\nNothing too fancy.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.573 --\u003e 00:13:05.994\r\nJust keep them busy until\r\nBats gets here. Got it?\r\n\r\n00:13:06.327 --\u003e 00:13:07.620\r\nSure, boss.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.082 --\u003e 00:13:13.710\r\n- Any questions, Murph?\r\n- No, sir.\r\n\r\n00:13:14.168 --\u003e 00:13:15.253\r\nGood man.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.714 --\u003e 00:13:21.259\r\nAnd if Batman hasn't really\r\ngone to his final reward,\r\n\r\n00:13:21.342 --\u003e 00:13:23.386\r\nwe'll see that he gets there.\r\n\r\n00:13:23.469 --\u003e 00:13:24.470\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:13:33.604 --\u003e 00:13:37.191\r\nMmm. From pinching pennies to\r\nrubbing elbows with the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.275 --\u003e 00:13:39.694\r\n- Not bad, Sidney.\r\n- Please.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.944 --\u003e 00:13:42.280\r\nConnections like him\r\nI can do without.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.822 --\u003e 00:13:46.284\r\n\u003ci\u003eNaturally, it didn't take the cops\r\nlong to seal off the building.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:46.659 --\u003e 00:13:48.828\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot that it mattered\r\nto Mr. Happy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:48.911 --\u003e 00:13:54.250\r\n(GROWLS) Where is he?\r\nHe's never been this late before.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.418 --\u003e 00:13:57.628\r\nThere's a certain\r\nrhythm to these things.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.712 --\u003e 00:13:59.881\r\nI cause trouble, he shows up.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.964 --\u003e 00:14:02.884\r\nWe have some laughs,\r\nand the game starts all over again.\r\n\r\n00:14:04.093 --\u003e 00:14:07.138\r\nOnly, now, thanks to you,\r\n\r\n00:14:07.305 --\u003e 00:14:11.059\r\nI have this terrible feeling\r\nhe's really not coming.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.853 --\u003e 00:14:16.189\r\nWhee! Look at all the pretties.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.814 --\u003e 00:14:18.274\r\nPut them back, Harley.\r\n\r\n00:14:19.150 --\u003e 00:14:22.445\r\nOh, Mr. J., you're such a kidder.\r\nYou never could...\r\n\r\n00:14:23.821 --\u003e 00:14:25.490\r\nI said, put them back!\r\n\r\n00:14:25.615 --\u003e 00:14:26.741\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:33.456\r\nSure, boss, I can do that.\r\nThis is me putting them back. No problemo.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.539 --\u003e 00:14:34.707\r\n(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:35.124 --\u003e 00:14:39.253\r\nWithout Batman,\r\ncrime has no punch line.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.006 --\u003e 00:14:44.467\r\n\u003ci\u003eSIDNEY: A laughing gas\r\nbomb kept the cops busy\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:44.592 --\u003e 00:14:46.177\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhile we slipped out the back.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:47.512 --\u003e 00:14:51.849\r\n\u003ci\u003eLater, the Joker held a little\r\nmemorial at the Ace Chemical plant.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:51.933 --\u003e 00:14:54.352\r\n(ORGAN MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:14:56.396 --\u003e 00:14:58.773\r\nYou know what's great about\r\nyou, Puddin'?\r\n\r\n00:14:59.107 --\u003e 00:15:02.026\r\nYou really put the\r\n\"fun\" in funeral.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.700 --\u003e 00:15:14.872\r\nDear friends,\r\ntoday is the day the clown cried.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.456 --\u003e 00:15:16.457\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:15:20.086 --\u003e 00:15:23.297\r\nAnd he cries not for\r\nthe passing of one man,\r\n\r\n00:15:23.506 --\u003e 00:15:25.925\r\nbut for the death of a dream.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.509 --\u003e 00:15:30.221\r\nThe dream that he would someday\r\ntaste the ultimate victory\r\n\r\n00:15:30.304 --\u003e 00:15:32.348\r\nover his hated enemy.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.307 --\u003e 00:15:38.438\r\nFor it was the Batman who made\r\nme the happy soul I am today.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.896 --\u003e 00:15:43.359\r\nHow I agonized over the perfect\r\nway to thank him for that.\r\n\r\n00:15:44.152 --\u003e 00:15:47.488\r\nPerhaps with a cyanide\r\npie in the face.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.782 --\u003e 00:15:50.783\r\n(WAILS)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.413 --\u003e 00:16:00.376\r\nOr an exploding whoopee cushion,\r\nplayfully planted in the Batmobile.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.423 --\u003e 00:16:09.635\r\nBut those dreams were dashed\r\nby the weaselly little gunsel\r\n\r\n00:16:09.719 --\u003e 00:16:11.554\r\nsitting there in our midst.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.972 --\u003e 00:16:17.435\r\nThe cowardly,\r\ninsignificant ganef who probably got lucky\r\n\r\n00:16:17.643 --\u003e 00:16:21.981\r\nwhen Batman slipped on the slime\r\ntrail this loser left behind him.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.315 --\u003e 00:16:25.943\r\nThis mound of\r\ndiseased hyena filth\r\n\r\n00:16:26.027 --\u003e 00:16:29.989\r\nwho's not fit to lick\r\nthe dirt from my spats!\r\n\r\n00:16:31.949 --\u003e 00:16:35.745\r\nBut I digress.\r\nThe time for sorrow has passed.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.078 --\u003e 00:16:40.833\r\nIt's time to look ahead to\r\na future filled with smiles.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.292 --\u003e 00:16:43.628\r\nAnd I'll be smiling again\r\n\r\n00:16:43.920 --\u003e 00:16:47.340\r\njust as soon as we\r\ntake that man there,\r\n\r\n00:16:47.465 --\u003e 00:16:50.301\r\nand slap him in that box there,\r\n\r\n00:16:50.676 --\u003e 00:16:54.096\r\nand roll it into that\r\nvat of acid there.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.182 --\u003e 00:16:59.101\r\nNo, no! I never meant to do it!\r\n\r\n00:16:59.685 --\u003e 00:17:01.312\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:17:02.063 --\u003e 00:17:03.064\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:17:05.316 --\u003e 00:17:07.568\r\n(MUFFLED) This\r\nisn't funny anymore\r\n\r\n00:17:13.824 --\u003e 00:17:16.244\r\n(PLAYING \"AMAZING\r\nGRACE\" ON KAZOO)\r\n\r\n00:17:25.378 --\u003e 00:17:27.547\r\n- (POUNDING)\r\n- Would it help if I said I'm sorry?\r\n\r\n00:17:27.672 --\u003e 00:17:31.384\r\nI'm really, really, really,\r\nreally, really sorry.\r\n\r\n00:17:31.467 --\u003e 00:17:33.594\r\n(\"AMAZING GRACE\" CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:17:55.324 --\u003e 00:17:56.450\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:17:58.160 --\u003e 00:18:00.788\r\nWell, that was fun.\r\nWho's for Chinese?\r\n\r\n00:18:08.254 --\u003e 00:18:09.255\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:12.925 --\u003e 00:18:14.885\r\n\u003ci\u003eSIDNEY: I thought I\r\nwas a goner for sure.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:18.431 --\u003e 00:18:21.809\r\n\u003ci\u003eThen, just as the acid\r\nstarted to eat its way in...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:25.354 --\u003e 00:18:26.480\r\n- (THUDS)\r\n- (WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:18:27.231 --\u003e 00:18:28.232\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:18:28.316 --\u003e 00:18:31.611\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was saved. The box must have\r\nbeen sucked down a drain pipe\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:31.694 --\u003e 00:18:33.613\r\n\u003ci\u003eand smacked open on the bank.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:33.988 --\u003e 00:18:35.656\r\n\u003ci\u003eI knew I had to get out of town.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:37.575 --\u003e 00:18:40.494\r\nSo I called Eddie G.\r\nAnd begged him to set me up\r\n\r\n00:18:40.578 --\u003e 00:18:42.997\r\nwith the big man\r\nbehind the drug ring.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.205 --\u003e 00:18:44.582\r\nHe sent me to you.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.915 --\u003e 00:18:48.794\r\nPlease, Mr. Thorne.\r\nYou're rich and powerful.\r\n\r\n00:18:49.003 --\u003e 00:18:51.922\r\nI'll do anything you say if\r\nyou can get me out of Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.381 --\u003e 00:18:57.386\r\nSo the famous Sid the Squid is nothing\r\nbut a pathetic victim of circumstance.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.054 --\u003e 00:19:00.640\r\nJust how stupid\r\ndo you think I am?\r\n\r\n00:19:01.265 --\u003e 00:19:02.350\r\nExcuse me?\r\n\r\n00:19:02.433 --\u003e 00:19:04.143\r\nYou think I didn't\r\nhear the rumors\r\n\r\n00:19:04.226 --\u003e 00:19:07.938\r\nof the third-rate stumblebum\r\nwho rubbed out the Batman?\r\n\r\n00:19:08.105 --\u003e 00:19:12.318\r\nAnd now you say you accidentally\r\nmade a fool of the Joker?\r\n\r\n00:19:13.110 --\u003e 00:19:16.364\r\nNo one's that lucky or stupid.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.656 --\u003e 00:19:19.325\r\n- Yes, I am. Honest.\r\n- Admit it.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.076 --\u003e 00:19:22.828\r\nYou're trying to muscle\r\nin on my drug racket.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.037 --\u003e 00:19:26.082\r\nYou've been playing dumb so\r\nyou can get a shot at me.\r\n\r\n00:19:26.374 --\u003e 00:19:27.833\r\nNo, really.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.292 --\u003e 00:19:30.878\r\nSure, I'll get you out of\r\nGotham, Sidney.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.128 --\u003e 00:19:32.338\r\nIn a pine box.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.631 --\u003e 00:19:35.549\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:39.512 --\u003e 00:19:42.056\r\n(DISTANT GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.352 --\u003e 00:19:47.645\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:53.693 --\u003e 00:19:54.694\r\n_Y°u? “(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:16.674 --\u003e 00:20:18.134\r\nThat's for pulling a gun.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.052 --\u003e 00:20:21.762\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:23.097 --\u003e 00:20:24.890\r\nAnd that's for the drugs.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.942 --\u003e 00:20:35.943\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:38.028 --\u003e 00:20:39.280\r\n(OBJECTS SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:43.909 --\u003e 00:20:46.036\r\nAnd that one's for any I missed.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.328 --\u003e 00:20:48.622\r\nOh, am I glad to see you.\r\n\r\n00:20:48.956 --\u003e 00:20:51.292\r\nWait a minute,\r\nhow come you're alive?\r\n\r\n00:20:51.625 --\u003e 00:20:54.003\r\nI swung away before\r\nthe gas tank exploded.\r\n\r\n00:20:54.420 --\u003e 00:20:56.505\r\nBut I thought since you\r\nbelieved I was dead,\r\n\r\n00:20:56.589 --\u003e 00:20:59.091\r\nI'd tail you and see who\r\nwas calling the shots.\r\n\r\n00:20:59.508 --\u003e 00:21:02.428\r\nSo you were the one who\r\nsaved me from the Joker?\r\n\r\n00:21:03.095 --\u003e 00:21:04.138\r\nThat's right.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.972 --\u003e 00:21:07.099\r\nWell, glad to be of service.\r\nSee you.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.476 --\u003e 00:21:11.061\r\nYou're still an accomplice\r\nto Thorne's gang.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.522 --\u003e 00:21:15.733\r\nGuess I can't win for\r\nlosing, huh?\r\n\r\n00:21:16.484 --\u003e 00:21:20.988\r\nI don't know. In the right environment,\r\na man of your dangerous reputation\r\n\r\n00:21:21.071 --\u003e 00:21:23.032\r\ncould still get\r\na lot of respect.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.078 --\u003e 00:21:29.079\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:21:29.789 --\u003e 00:21:32.416\r\n- PRISONER 1: Here he comes.\r\n- PRISONER 2: It's the Squid.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.666 --\u003e 00:21:35.544\r\nPRISONER 3: Toughest man in\r\nGotham, nearly offed the Bat.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.920 --\u003e 00:21:39.340\r\nPRISONER 4: Set Thorne up.\r\nHe made a fool out of the Joker, too.\r\n\r\n00:21:39.673 --\u003e 00:21:43.552\r\n- PRISONER 5: Don't mess with him, man.\r\n- A big shot at last.\r\n\r\n00:21:44.053 --\u003e 00:21:47.306\r\n(ALL CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.422 --\u003e 00:22:21.423\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E50 - Zatanna (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.586 --\u003e 00:00:04.588\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:15.492 --\u003e 00:01:17.077\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:17.160 --\u003e 00:01:20.706\r\nWOMAN: \u003ci\u003eLadies and gentlemen,\r\nit's time for magic.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:24.626 --\u003e 00:01:27.462\r\nGood evening, Gotham.\r\nI'm Zatanna.\r\n\r\n00:01:38.098 --\u003e 00:01:41.143\r\nTonight,\r\nI can promise you a few surprises.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.854 --\u003e 00:01:45.790\r\n- A thrill or two along the way.\r\n- (AUDIENCE GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.814 --\u003e 00:01:48.233\r\nAnd with luck, a happy ending.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.568 --\u003e 00:01:50.569\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:01:53.071 --\u003e 00:01:56.241\r\nHow long has it been?\r\nTen years, 12?\r\n\r\n00:01:56.408 --\u003e 00:01:58.660\r\nAll that and another lifetime.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.077 --\u003e 00:02:01.163\r\nALFRED: She and her father\r\nwere very fond of you.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.496 --\u003e 00:02:03.457\r\nI was a different person then.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.624 --\u003e 00:02:06.585\r\nYes. Intense, driven, moody.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.835 --\u003e 00:02:08.629\r\nShe'd never recognize you now.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.838 --\u003e 00:02:13.842\r\nNow open your heart to magic,\r\nand become a child again.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.393 --\u003e 00:02:26.313\r\nZATARA: Remember,\r\nconcentration and control.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.813 --\u003e 00:02:30.108\r\nFocus on them,\r\nand you can master any escape.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.529 --\u003e 00:02:35.697\r\nGo.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.781 --\u003e 00:02:37.699\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:56.635\r\nCongratulations. You've beaten\r\nyour old time by six seconds.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.843 --\u003e 00:02:57.886\r\nYes!\r\n\r\n00:02:57.969 --\u003e 00:03:00.639\r\nYou've got the makings\r\nof a great magician.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.306 --\u003e 00:03:03.600\r\nI'm sorry you're\r\ngoing to be moving on.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.767 --\u003e 00:03:06.853\r\nSame here. It was an honor\r\nto study with you, Zatara.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.229 --\u003e 00:03:08.522\r\nBut to what end?\r\n\r\n00:03:09.022 --\u003e 00:03:11.191\r\nThree months ago you\r\nappeared on my doorstep\r\n\r\n00:03:11.525 --\u003e 00:03:13.485\r\nwith no interest in performing,\r\n\r\n00:03:13.777 --\u003e 00:03:16.571\r\nand yet dying to become\r\nan escape artist.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.239 --\u003e 00:03:18.240\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.990 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nAnd for some reason,\r\nI wound up teaching you secrets\r\n\r\n00:03:22.369 --\u003e 00:03:24.788\r\nI'd never shown\r\nanother magician.\r\n\r\n00:03:25.038 --\u003e 00:03:26.540\r\nBRUCE: You could've\r\nsent me away.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.790 --\u003e 00:03:30.919\r\nZATARA: No. There was something\r\ninside you I had no right to deny.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.712 --\u003e 00:03:34.381\r\nSomething deep and painful.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.548 --\u003e 00:03:38.593\r\nAfter all, I would be foolish to\r\nassume I was the only one with secrets.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.969 --\u003e 00:03:40.637\r\nEh, John Smith?\r\n\r\n00:03:41.680 --\u003e 00:03:43.223\r\nThanks for everything, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.807 --\u003e 00:03:45.183\r\nI'll miss you, John.\r\n\r\n00:03:46.393 --\u003e 00:03:48.478\r\nAnd so, I trust, will Zatanna.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.562 --\u003e 00:03:50.647\r\nOh! Hi, Daddy.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.610 --\u003e 00:03:57.070\r\nGood night, children.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.077 --\u003e 00:04:06.246\r\nI thought you'd be\r\nfinishing the tour with us.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.705 --\u003e 00:04:10.208\r\nI'm leaving for Japan tomorrow.\r\nThere's still a lot I have to learn.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.667 --\u003e 00:04:13.962\r\nBoy, that's you.\r\nOne big serious schoolboy.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.504 --\u003e 00:04:17.048\r\nNo time in your life\r\nfor fun or magic.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.674 --\u003e 00:04:19.760\r\nHere, pick a card.\r\nI'll tell your future.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.387 --\u003e 00:04:25.348\r\nHmm. I see emotion, intensity...\r\n\r\n00:04:25.891 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nTwo of hearts.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.852 --\u003e 00:04:29.895\r\nBRUCE: Joker.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.645 --\u003e 00:04:32.355\r\nOh, it's a dumb trick anyway.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.606 --\u003e 00:04:34.149\r\nBRUCE: Look,\r\nI don't know the future,\r\n\r\n00:04:34.524 --\u003e 00:04:36.860\r\nbut I know I'll see you\r\nagain someday, Zanna.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.943 --\u003e 00:04:38.945\r\nYou're the only one who\r\never calls me Zanna.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.488 --\u003e 00:04:40.697\r\nI really hate it.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.283 --\u003e 00:04:44.367\r\nNo goodbye hug?\r\n\r\n00:04:45.911 --\u003e 00:04:48.079\r\nSee? It's not so bad.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.997 --\u003e 00:04:51.166\r\n- I'll write you.\r\n- No, you won't.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.374 --\u003e 00:04:53.460\r\n- I promise.\r\n- You can't.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.710 --\u003e 00:04:55.837\r\nI locked your hands to the wall.\r\n(GIGGLES)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.463 --\u003e 00:04:57.506\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:04:59.174 --\u003e 00:05:02.010\r\nLooks like someone's missing\r\ntheir plane tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.302 --\u003e 00:05:04.429\r\nBut hey, if you were any\r\nkind of escape artist\r\n\r\n00:05:04.679 --\u003e 00:05:06.932\r\nyou'd be out of those cuffs\r\nand through the door by now.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.015 --\u003e 00:05:08.016\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:09.851 --\u003e 00:05:12.062\r\nNow you see him, now you don't.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.777 --\u003e 00:05:20.278\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:05:21.196 --\u003e 00:05:24.491\r\nThank you. You know,\r\nI have this little problem with money.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.741 --\u003e 00:05:27.035\r\nSeems like it disappears\r\nbefore I even make it.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.536 --\u003e 00:05:31.122\r\nAnd here to help me demonstrate\r\nare Mr. Irving Fauncewater,\r\n\r\n00:05:31.248 --\u003e 00:05:34.167\r\ndirector of the Gotham Mint,\r\nand noted magic debunker.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.127\r\nDr. Montague Kane.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.586 --\u003e 00:05:37.754\r\nWelcome, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:05:38.004 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nMiss Zatanna.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.923 --\u003e 00:05:41.383\r\nThis is so exciting.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.300 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\n“(YELPS) “Oh!\r\n\r\n00:05:43.844 --\u003e 00:05:48.139\r\nLet me guess, first time on stage, Irv?\r\nNothing like enthusiasm, right, folks?\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:49.307\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:49.391 --\u003e 00:05:51.268\r\nThe way they're\r\nresponding, one would think\r\n\r\n00:05:51.351 --\u003e 00:05:53.645\r\nyour ridiculous stunt\r\nwas going to work.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.020 --\u003e 00:05:58.483\r\nJust to clue you in, Monty here makes\r\na living exposing magicians' secrets.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.817 --\u003e 00:06:00.902\r\nSimple tricks and nonsense.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.278 --\u003e 00:06:02.279\r\n\u003ci\u003eZAT ANNA: Uh-huh.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.863 --\u003e 00:06:03.864\r\nAnd I've invited him here\r\n\r\n00:06:03.947 --\u003e 00:06:07.075\r\nto find the secret of the\r\nfeat I'm attempting tonight.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.367 --\u003e 00:06:11.872\r\nThere is no secret. What you're\r\nproposing is flat-out impossible.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:15.500\r\nWell, kids,\r\nimpossible is what I'm all about.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.792 --\u003e 00:06:19.212\r\nMr. Fauncewater,\r\nopen the doors, please.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.881 --\u003e 00:06:25.051\r\n- $10 million and the means to make it.\r\n- (AUDIENCE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.761 --\u003e 00:06:29.973\r\nTake a good look, folks,\r\n'cause you know what they say about money.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.682 --\u003e 00:06:32.100\r\n\"Easy come,\"\r\n\r\n00:06:32.267 --\u003e 00:06:34.477\r\n\"easy go!\"\r\n\r\n00:06:34.728 --\u003e 00:06:35.937\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:39.900 --\u003e 00:06:41.109\r\n(AUDIENCE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:06:48.283 --\u003e 00:06:49.576\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:51.453 --\u003e 00:06:52.579\r\nOh, my!\r\n\r\n00:06:57.250 --\u003e 00:06:58.793\r\nBravo, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.919 --\u003e 00:07:01.421\r\nIt was a pleasure\r\nto be proven wrong.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.796 --\u003e 00:07:02.964\r\nThank you, Monty.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.214 --\u003e 00:07:07.969\r\nAnd now, just so Irv doesn't have a\r\nfit, I'll bring it back good as new.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.386 --\u003e 00:07:10.138\r\nArba decarba!\r\n\r\n00:07:17.187 --\u003e 00:07:18.980\r\nThe money. Where's the money?\r\n\r\n00:07:19.105 --\u003e 00:07:20.774\r\n\"Where's the money,\" he says.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.191 --\u003e 00:07:23.443\r\nIt's right there, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.735 --\u003e 00:07:26.446\r\nIt's gone!\r\nWhat have you done with it?\r\n\r\n00:07:26.529 --\u003e 00:07:30.617\r\nNow, take it easy, Irv. I'm sure\r\nthere's a perfectly logical explanation.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.867 --\u003e 00:07:33.203\r\nAnd I'm sure the audience\r\nwould like to hear it.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.411 --\u003e 00:07:35.956\r\n- As would the police.\r\n- Now, wait a minute.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.331 --\u003e 00:07:37.916\r\nPoHce, poHce!\r\n\r\n00:07:39.084 --\u003e 00:07:40.168\r\nMAN: The police are coming.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.251 --\u003e 00:07:43.171\r\nLook, it's a trick, an illusion.\r\nI don't know what went wrong,\r\n\r\n00:07:43.254 --\u003e 00:07:45.715\r\nbut if we can all just\r\ncalm down for a second...\r\n\r\n00:07:46.007 --\u003e 00:07:47.842\r\n\"You have the right\r\nto remain silent.\"\r\n\r\n00:07:48.051 --\u003e 00:07:50.470\r\n\"Anything you say can and\r\nwill be used against you.\"\r\n\r\n00:08:05.151 --\u003e 00:08:07.278\r\nThis never happens\r\nto me in Vegas.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.533 --\u003e 00:08:12.867\r\nBRUCE: She's been set up.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.910 --\u003e 00:08:17.956\r\nObviously, but as she's the only\r\nsuspect, the police must hold her.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.373 --\u003e 00:08:22.085\r\nGiving the real thief time to escape.\r\nI can't let that happen.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.419 --\u003e 00:08:25.630\r\nAnd more important,\r\nyou can't desert an old friend.\r\n\r\n00:08:30.635 --\u003e 00:08:31.803\r\n(CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.055 --\u003e 00:08:35.056\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:42.230 --\u003e 00:08:43.231\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:08:47.861 --\u003e 00:08:49.988\r\n- Nice car.\r\n- Thanks.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.739 --\u003e 00:08:53.575\r\nYou know, I didn't love the idea\r\nof spending the night in jail,\r\n\r\n00:08:53.658 --\u003e 00:08:56.077\r\nbut this does technically\r\nmake me a fugitive.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.327 --\u003e 00:08:58.288\r\nI believe I'm looking\r\nat some prison time now.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.371 --\u003e 00:09:01.416\r\nI heard about the mint robbery.\r\nI can help prove you didn't do it.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.708 --\u003e 00:09:04.169\r\nWhy do you care about\r\nsome leggy dame in nylons?\r\n\r\n00:09:04.669 --\u003e 00:09:06.671\r\nOr have I answered\r\nmy own question?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.840 --\u003e 00:09:11.200\r\n- BATMAN: If you want to go it alone...\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:12.427 --\u003e 00:09:15.805\r\nNo, no. I'm sorry.\r\nI'm having a bad day.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.726 --\u003e 00:09:22.812\r\nI'm sure whoever framed you\r\nknew how your trick was done.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.896 --\u003e 00:09:24.689\r\nThey may have left\r\na clue at the mint.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.887 --\u003e 00:09:59.099\r\n- This place is surrounded by cops.\r\n- Just relax.\r\n\r\n00:09:59.557 --\u003e 00:10:01.017\r\nThat's where the money was.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.226 --\u003e 00:10:02.227\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.896 --\u003e 00:10:07.816\r\nBATMAN: Look. This line was\r\nrecently scraped into the floor.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.191 --\u003e 00:10:10.860\r\nWhatever made it left\r\nshards of glass, too.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.944 --\u003e 00:10:13.488\r\nThat would have been one\r\nmighty big piece of glass.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.571 --\u003e 00:10:16.241\r\n(GASPS) Or mirror.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.366 --\u003e 00:10:19.619\r\nLike the one you used to reflect\r\nthe hologram of the vanished mint.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.702 --\u003e 00:10:22.205\r\nOh, sure,\r\ntake all the mystery out of life.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.041 --\u003e 00:10:27.627\r\nI think the money was\r\nstolen before you got here.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.379 --\u003e 00:10:32.966\r\nThe thief reflected a hologram of\r\nthe cash while you did your trick,\r\n\r\n00:10:33.341 --\u003e 00:10:35.760\r\nthen quickly hid the\r\nmirror when it was over.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.052 --\u003e 00:10:38.346\r\nHow'd he get rid of\r\na mirror that big?\r\n\r\n00:10:40.223 --\u003e 00:10:42.934\r\nHe didn't. It's still here.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.351 --\u003e 00:10:44.519\r\nGUARD: Who's in here?\r\n\r\n00:10:46.563 --\u003e 00:10:47.897\r\nHold it!\r\n\r\n00:10:48.523 --\u003e 00:10:49.816\r\nStay where you are.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.078 --\u003e 00:11:04.873\r\nZATANNA: Only another magician would\r\nhave known how to rig that trick.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.998 --\u003e 00:11:08.835\r\nOr someone who knows their methods.\r\nLike Montague Kane.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.419 --\u003e 00:11:11.921\r\nHe's been ripping off\r\nillusionists for years.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.213 --\u003e 00:11:16.426\r\nI thought I finally had a trick\r\neven he couldn't expose. Wrong.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.718 --\u003e 00:11:18.136\r\nI'll settle with Kane.\r\n\r\n00:11:18.428 --\u003e 00:11:20.680\r\nMeantime,\r\nI'd better drop you someplace safe.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.930 --\u003e 00:11:25.435\r\nOh, no. Kane played me for a sap,\r\nand I'll see him go down for it.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.727 --\u003e 00:11:27.854\r\nAll right,\r\nbut it could be dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.855 --\u003e 00:11:31.065\r\nYou're sure there's no one\r\nyou want to call first?\r\n\r\n00:11:31.482 --\u003e 00:11:34.527\r\nUh, friends, family,\r\na husband, maybe?\r\n\r\n00:11:34.736 --\u003e 00:11:37.071\r\nMe? Who's got time\r\nfor a relationship\r\n\r\n00:11:37.155 --\u003e 00:11:39.699\r\nwhen you're pulling rabbits\r\nout of a hat 52 weeks a year?\r\n\r\n00:11:40.950 --\u003e 00:11:44.829\r\nBesides, someone's got to keep the\r\nold act going now that Dad's gone.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.706 --\u003e 00:11:48.958\r\n- I'm sorry.\r\n- Why?\r\n\r\n00:11:49.792 --\u003e 00:11:53.296\r\nI saw him perform when I was younger.\r\nHe was great.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.671 --\u003e 00:11:57.508\r\nThanks. You know, I have the\r\nweirdest feeling we've met before.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.884 --\u003e 00:12:00.345\r\nI just have that kind of face.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.503 --\u003e 00:12:35.380\r\nKANE: It would\r\nseem I have guests.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.304 --\u003e 00:12:45.640\r\nCome in,\r\nand join me by the fire.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.349 --\u003e 00:12:48.851\r\nCome, come. Don't be shy.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.021\r\nYou've obviously\r\nunraveled my little scheme\r\n\r\n00:12:52.105 --\u003e 00:12:55.483\r\nand I would congratulate\r\nyou face-to-face.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.192 --\u003e 00:12:58.695\r\nYou're not going to have a\r\nface when I'm done with you.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.362 --\u003e 00:13:01.322\r\nNow, you slimy... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:03.533 --\u003e 00:13:04.826\r\nIt's a trap!\r\n\r\n00:13:05.368 --\u003e 00:13:06.786\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:15.461 --\u003e 00:13:19.173\r\nKANE: \u003ci\u003e(ON SPEAKER) A trifle cliched,\r\nI know, but effective nonetheless.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:19.924 --\u003e 00:13:22.885\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd while you briefly savor\r\nyour fleeting triumph,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:23.094 --\u003e 00:13:26.973\r\n\u003ci\u003elam winging toward more\r\ncomfortable surroundings.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:27.390 --\u003e 00:13:28.391\r\n\u003ci\u003eAdieu.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:29.309 --\u003e 00:13:30.601\r\n(MACHINERY WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:13:44.198 --\u003e 00:13:47.243\r\n- I have an idea.\r\n- Oh, I would hope so.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.884 --\u003e 00:14:04.344\r\n(SCRAPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:07.513 --\u003e 00:14:08.765\r\nThis way.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.950 --\u003e 00:14:30.036\r\nI always did know\r\nhow to make an exit.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.578 --\u003e 00:14:32.747\r\nUnfortunately, so did Kane.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.331 --\u003e 00:14:36.292\r\nKANE: \u003ci\u003e(ECHOING) And while you\r\nbriefly savor your fleeting triumph,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:36.376 --\u003e 00:14:40.171\r\n\u003ci\u003elam winging toward more\r\ncomfortable surroundings.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:40.588 --\u003e 00:14:41.589\r\n\u003ci\u003eAdieu.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:46.761 --\u003e 00:14:49.055\r\nCome on.\r\nThe show's not over yet.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.855 --\u003e 00:15:00.566\r\nKANE: Take a last longing\r\nlook, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.817 --\u003e 00:15:03.194\r\nWe're heading to a place\r\nwhere the climate is warmer,\r\n\r\n00:15:03.277 --\u003e 00:15:04.695\r\nthe people are friendlier\r\n\r\n00:15:04.946 --\u003e 00:15:08.616\r\nand the extradition\r\nlaws are nonexistent.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.200 --\u003e 00:15:11.619\r\nBATMAN: The only place you're\r\nheading is to a prison cell.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.911 --\u003e 00:15:13.704\r\nWell done, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.038 --\u003e 00:15:17.375\r\nYou not only eluded my trap,\r\nbut solved my clue as well.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.834 --\u003e 00:15:18.918\r\nGet rid of him.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.710 --\u003e 00:15:20.920\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:30.972 --\u003e 00:15:32.098\r\nTa-da!\r\n\r\n00:15:32.849 --\u003e 00:15:36.394\r\nOh, Monty. You fell for the\r\nsecond-oldest trick in the book.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.936 --\u003e 00:15:38.396\r\nAnd here's the first.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.563 --\u003e 00:15:39.856\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.941 --\u003e 00:15:42.942\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.317 --\u003e 00:15:44.318\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:15:47.864 --\u003e 00:15:49.073\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:50.158 --\u003e 00:15:51.826\r\nKeep your distance, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.953 --\u003e 00:15:54.954\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:00.710 --\u003e 00:16:03.212\r\nYou are most engaging, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.421 --\u003e 00:16:05.548\r\nBeautiful, impetuous.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.257 --\u003e 00:16:10.595\r\nI could be persuaded to spare\r\nyou, if properly implored.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.387 --\u003e 00:16:12.388\r\n“(THUDS) 0w!\r\n\r\n00:16:12.680 --\u003e 00:16:15.475\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:18.478 --\u003e 00:16:19.729\r\nBring them both!\r\n\r\n00:16:30.698 --\u003e 00:16:32.700\r\nWith all reverence\r\nfor the departed,\r\n\r\n00:16:32.909 --\u003e 00:16:35.828\r\nZatara himself couldn't\r\nescape those locks.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.497 --\u003e 00:16:41.250\r\nStill, between the two of you,\r\nyou might be able to loosen a few chains\r\n\r\n00:16:41.334 --\u003e 00:16:43.294\r\nbefore you hit the water.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.467 --\u003e 00:16:50.718\r\n(WHISPERS) Take my hand.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.511 --\u003e 00:16:53.930\r\nScared? That makes two of us.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.347 --\u003e 00:16:56.849\r\n- Trust me, Zanna.\r\n- \"Zanna\"?\r\n\r\n00:16:58.643 --\u003e 00:17:00.436\r\nBATMAN: Quick, in my glove.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.112 --\u003e 00:17:12.240\r\nFarewell, my dear Zatanna.\r\n\r\n00:17:12.657 --\u003e 00:17:15.451\r\nWe could have been magic.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.957 --\u003e 00:17:24.043\r\n- (ZATAN NA SCREAMING)\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:34.262 --\u003e 00:17:36.013\r\nIncredible.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.772 --\u003e 00:17:46.274\r\n(ZATAN NA SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.823 --\u003e 00:17:57.618\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:58.911 --\u003e 00:17:59.912\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.708 --\u003e 00:18:06.043\r\nStop firing, you fools!\r\n\r\n00:18:38.909 --\u003e 00:18:40.202\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:44.040 --\u003e 00:18:46.792\r\n(ZATAN NA SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:58.220 --\u003e 00:18:59.847\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.809 --\u003e 00:19:04.810\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:19:08.898 --\u003e 00:19:09.899\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:14.403 --\u003e 00:19:15.655\r\n(BOTH YELP)\r\n\r\n00:19:25.915 --\u003e 00:19:27.333\r\nGet rid of him!\r\n\r\n00:19:41.722 --\u003e 00:19:42.723\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:20:03.911 --\u003e 00:20:05.621\r\n(BOTH SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.178 --\u003e 00:20:24.348\r\nDon't you know? A magician\r\nnever does the same trick twice.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.473 --\u003e 00:20:25.474\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:28.394 --\u003e 00:20:29.645\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:49.039 --\u003e 00:20:51.250\r\nZATANNA: So, you never wrote.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.542 --\u003e 00:20:53.377\r\nI meant to. Really.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.627 --\u003e 00:20:56.130\r\nHey, it's okay.\r\nI can see you've been busy.\r\n\r\n00:20:56.547 --\u003e 00:20:59.759\r\n- Just answer an old friend one question.\r\n- Shoot.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.634 --\u003e 00:21:02.928\r\nWhat happened that\r\nmade you put this on?\r\n\r\n00:21:03.721 --\u003e 00:21:05.139\r\nA painful memory.\r\n\r\n00:21:05.806 --\u003e 00:21:07.057\r\nAnd a promise.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.183 --\u003e 00:21:09.560\r\nI'd say you're keeping\r\nthat promise pretty well.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.935 --\u003e 00:21:13.647\r\nAnd for what it's worth,\r\nDad would've been proud of you tonight.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.607 --\u003e 00:21:15.733\r\nYou, too.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.233 --\u003e 00:21:17.401\r\nCan I give you a ride?\r\n\r\n00:21:29.789 --\u003e 00:21:35.294\r\nZATAN \u003ci\u003eNA: John, I hate goodbyes\u003c/i\u003e too.\r\n\u003ci\u003eLove, Zanna.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:36.128 --\u003e 00:21:38.798\r\n\u003ci\u003eP.S. Don't forget to write.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:53.395 --\u003e 00:21:55.397\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.214 --\u003e 00:22:21.215\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E51 - Robin's Reckoning, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:02.628 --\u003e 00:00:03.962\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.125 --\u003e 00:01:24.960\r\nROBIN: If I knew it was\r\ngonna take this long,\r\n\r\n00:01:25.043 --\u003e 00:01:26.545\r\nI would've brought my homework.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.546 --\u003e 00:01:29.381\r\nYou sure about this\r\nextortion ring?\r\n\r\n00:01:29.798 --\u003e 00:01:32.467\r\n- Uh-huh.\r\n- It's been four hours.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.093 --\u003e 00:01:35.762\r\n- Uh-huh.\r\n- You still think they'll show?\r\n\r\n00:01:36.221 --\u003e 00:01:38.682\r\n- Uh-huh.\r\n- (SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:01:38.765 --\u003e 00:01:41.602\r\nLucky for me you're such\r\na good conversationalist.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.394 --\u003e 00:01:43.395\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.695 --\u003e 00:01:53.280\r\nBATMAN: There's the slime.\r\n\r\n00:01:53.363 --\u003e 00:01:54.948\r\nAll right!\r\n\r\n00:01:55.032 --\u003e 00:01:57.909\r\nThese are contract\r\nsaboteurs, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.993 --\u003e 00:02:00.704\r\nLet's take it by the\r\nnumbers, nice and easy.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.787 --\u003e 00:02:03.123\r\nYeah, time to kick some butt.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.250 --\u003e 00:02:07.252\r\nGood thing we had\r\nthat little chat.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.759 --\u003e 00:02:16.053\r\nOkay,\r\nnow I'm gonna need a charge.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.553 --\u003e 00:02:19.765\r\n- How about- - Yahoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:19.848 --\u003e 00:02:21.350\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:25.312 --\u003e 00:02:26.688\r\nOh, great.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.819 --\u003e 00:02:33.904\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.738 --\u003e 00:02:37.491\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.574 --\u003e 00:02:39.493\r\nROBIN: Come on. Come on.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.202 --\u003e 00:02:41.578\r\nYou can do it.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.204 --\u003e 00:02:43.413\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:02:45.540 --\u003e 00:02:47.459\r\nThis is getting sad.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.633 --\u003e 00:02:56.426\r\n(BOTH YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:07.646 --\u003e 00:03:09.314\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.358 --\u003e 00:03:13.610\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:15.821 --\u003e 00:03:17.364\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:03:27.624 --\u003e 00:03:29.042\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:29.126 --\u003e 00:03:32.129\r\nIt's back to the gym for you.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.212 --\u003e 00:03:33.964\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:35.006 --\u003e 00:03:36.007\r\n(GUNFIRE)\r\n\r\n00:04:02.284 --\u003e 00:04:03.869\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:12.878 --\u003e 00:04:13.962\r\nLet them go.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.796 --\u003e 00:04:16.173\r\nHe's all we need.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.009 --\u003e 00:04:21.595\r\nNow, who's behind this\r\nlittle enterprise?\r\n\r\n00:04:21.678 --\u003e 00:04:24.514\r\nI ain't saying nothing\r\ntill I see my lawyer.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.432 --\u003e 00:04:26.683\r\nSuit yourself.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.726 --\u003e 00:04:28.769\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:04:32.689 --\u003e 00:04:35.192\r\nWait. Wait. You gotta help me.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.317 --\u003e 00:04:37.194\r\nThe cops wouldn't leave me.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.944 --\u003e 00:04:39.112\r\nWe're not the police.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.030 --\u003e 00:04:42.491\r\nYou want help? I want a name.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.574 --\u003e 00:04:43.825\r\nWho's your boss?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.909 --\u003e 00:04:46.495\r\nI can't. I can't say nothing.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.953 --\u003e 00:04:48.163\r\nHe'll tear me apart.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.331 --\u003e 00:04:50.957\r\nOh. Then you've got a problem.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.041 --\u003e 00:04:53.210\r\nAhhh! Hey, come on.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.293 --\u003e 00:04:54.711\r\nFor pity's sake!\r\n\r\n00:04:55.086 --\u003e 00:04:58.548\r\n(SCREAMING) It's Marin!\r\nBilly Marin!\r\n\r\n00:04:59.090 --\u003e 00:05:00.175\r\nMarin.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.426 --\u003e 00:05:02.928\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.438 --\u003e 00:05:16.024\r\nAnd where do we find Mr. Marin?\r\n\r\n00:05:16.608 --\u003e 00:05:19.653\r\n(STUTTERING) I don't...\r\nLook, I can't-\r\n\r\n00:05:19.736 --\u003e 00:05:22.239\r\n- Spill it.\r\n- Forget it, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.948 --\u003e 00:05:25.784\r\n- What?\r\n- I said forget it.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.368 --\u003e 00:05:27.994\r\nBut this guy's ready to sing.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.078 --\u003e 00:05:30.705\r\nLet it go.\r\nThe police can take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.789 --\u003e 00:05:32.541\r\n- Go get the Batmobile.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:05:32.624 --\u003e 00:05:33.625\r\nNOW!\r\n\r\n00:05:37.379 --\u003e 00:05:38.380\r\n\u003ci\u003eHEY-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:38.463 --\u003e 00:05:40.632\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:45.887 --\u003e 00:05:47.639\r\nAll right, scumbucket.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.722 --\u003e 00:05:50.851\r\nIt's you, me and 30 stories.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.601 --\u003e 00:05:54.604\r\nYou're gonna tell me\r\nexactly what I want to know.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.404 --\u003e 00:06:04.155\r\nROBIN: Why can't I go with you?\r\n\r\n00:06:04.239 --\u003e 00:06:06.616\r\n- What's the deal?\r\n- BATMAN: I'm working alone tonight.\r\n\r\n00:06:07.576 --\u003e 00:06:10.745\r\nROBIN: Come on. I don't get to do\r\nthis much since I started college.\r\n\r\n00:06:11.580 --\u003e 00:06:14.624\r\nIf it's because ljumped the\r\ngun back there, I'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.708 --\u003e 00:06:17.836\r\nIt's something I\r\nhave to do alone.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.629 --\u003e 00:06:21.089\r\nSo that's it.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.172 --\u003e 00:06:24.634\r\nNo apologies, no explanation.\r\nJust, \"See you later, kid.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:24.718 --\u003e 00:06:25.719\r\nYou know the rules.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.802 --\u003e 00:06:29.139\r\n- There are times when I can't\r\nexplain- - \"My actions, even to you.\"\r\n\r\n00:06:29.222 --\u003e 00:06:31.141\r\nHey, that line worked\r\ngreat in sixth grade,\r\n\r\n00:06:31.224 --\u003e 00:06:32.976\r\nbut in case you hadn't noticed-\r\n\r\n00:06:33.059 --\u003e 00:06:34.811\r\nWe'll discuss this later.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.320 --\u003e 00:06:46.197\r\nMaster Dick,\r\ndare I ask what's going on?\r\n\r\n00:06:46.323 --\u003e 00:06:48.199\r\nThat's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.377 --\u003e 00:07:01.755\r\nROBIN: I'll never be like\r\nhim, Alfred. Never.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.465 --\u003e 00:07:06.843\r\nHe's a stone-cold,\r\nself-righteous...\r\n\r\n00:07:06.927 --\u003e 00:07:09.471\r\nMaster Dick,\r\ntry not to be too critical.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.554 --\u003e 00:07:11.431\r\nI'm certain whatever\r\nhis reasons,\r\n\r\n00:07:11.514 --\u003e 00:07:14.309\r\nMaster Bruce has your\r\nbest interests in mind.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.392 --\u003e 00:07:17.020\r\nHe shuts me out, man.\r\nTreats me like a kid.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.105 --\u003e 00:07:20.190\r\nI don't get it.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.273 --\u003e 00:07:23.902\r\nEverything was going great until\r\nthat Marin business came up.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.238 --\u003e 00:07:29.449\r\nYou ever hear of a crook\r\nnamed Billy Marin, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:07:29.532 --\u003e 00:07:31.743\r\nMmm, can't say that I have,\r\n\r\n00:07:31.826 --\u003e 00:07:34.287\r\nbut I'm not one to\r\nperuse post office walls.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.205 --\u003e 00:07:36.706\r\nI think Batman has.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.341 --\u003e 00:07:50.971\r\nThere. \"Billy Marin.\r\nAlias: Simon Dirks\",\r\n\r\n00:07:51.054 --\u003e 00:07:55.183\r\n\"Sid the Squid, Killa\r\nCoburn, Punky Lesh.\"\r\n\r\n00:07:55.684 --\u003e 00:07:56.977\r\nBut who is he really?\r\n\r\n00:08:01.314 --\u003e 00:08:02.941\r\n\"Tony Zucco.\"\r\n\r\n00:08:03.024 --\u003e 00:08:05.110\r\nOh! My word.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.193 --\u003e 00:08:06.695\r\nFinally.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.639 --\u003e 00:08:36.516\r\nOkay, Dick. You ready?\r\n\r\n00:08:37.392 --\u003e 00:08:38.393\r\nReady, Dad.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.694 --\u003e 00:08:49.654\r\n(EXCITED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:08:50.697 --\u003e 00:08:53.199\r\nThat Grayson kid's\r\na real boy wonder.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.795 --\u003e 00:09:06.963\r\n\u003ci\u003eHEY-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:07.047 --\u003e 00:09:08.882\r\n(TRUMPETING)\r\n\r\n00:09:09.257 --\u003e 00:09:12.886\r\nOkay, Sitka, give it back.\r\nCome on, you.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.011 --\u003e 00:09:14.345\r\nMAN: You heard me. Get out!\r\n\r\n00:09:15.680 --\u003e 00:09:16.681\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:18.058 --\u003e 00:09:19.309\r\nI run an honest business here.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.392 --\u003e 00:09:22.062\r\nI don't pay two-bit\r\nhoodlums protection money!\r\n\r\n00:09:23.229 --\u003e 00:09:24.898\r\nInsurance, Mr. Haley.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.981 --\u003e 00:09:27.484\r\nYou know, from accidents?\r\n\r\n00:09:28.318 --\u003e 00:09:30.737\r\nCan't run a business\r\nwithout insurance.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.820 --\u003e 00:09:33.615\r\nGet off my property\r\nwhile you can still walk.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.991 --\u003e 00:09:38.078\r\nHey! Hey, fine.\r\nI've tried to be reasonable.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.703 --\u003e 00:09:40.872\r\nYou don't want my\r\nservices, okay.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.207 --\u003e 00:09:44.334\r\nBut you're gonna wish you'd\r\nlistened, old man.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.417 --\u003e 00:09:47.253\r\n(CHUCKLING) Oh, yeah,\r\nkeep my number handy.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.337 --\u003e 00:09:50.465\r\nYou're gonna be calling Tony\r\nZucco, and soon.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.548 --\u003e 00:09:51.758\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:53.176 --\u003e 00:09:54.260\r\nOut of my way, punk.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.771 --\u003e 00:10:08.525\r\nANNOUNCER: Step right up.\r\nThis way to the big top extravaganza.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.485 --\u003e 00:10:12.153\r\nAll right.\r\nLet's move it, you grubs.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.237 --\u003e 00:10:14.656\r\nSecure the rigging.\r\nShow starts in one hour.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.667 --\u003e 00:10:31.131\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\nand children of all ages.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.214 --\u003e 00:10:34.759\r\nWelcome to the\r\ngrandest show on Earth.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.843 --\u003e 00:10:36.511\r\nBefore we begin,\r\n\r\n00:10:36.594 --\u003e 00:10:41.432\r\nlet's have a hand for the benefactor\r\nof tonight's action-packed pageant,\r\n\r\n00:10:41.516 --\u003e 00:10:44.269\r\nMr. Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:10:44.352 --\u003e 00:10:46.187\r\n- (FANFARE)\r\n- (CROWD APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:10:48.982 --\u003e 00:10:50.817\r\n(CROWD LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:50.900 --\u003e 00:10:53.611\r\nRINGMASTER: And now,\r\nladies and gentlemen,\r\n\r\n00:10:53.695 --\u003e 00:10:57.198\r\ndirect your attention\r\nhigh above the center ring\r\n\r\n00:10:57.282 --\u003e 00:11:00.451\r\nfor a dazzling display\r\nof aerial artistry.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.537 --\u003e 00:11:05.540\r\n- Hey, that's the guy the...\r\n- Come on, honey, we're on.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.207 --\u003e 00:11:11.171\r\nPerforming death-defying stunts\r\nwithout the aid of a net,\r\n\r\n00:11:11.254 --\u003e 00:11:15.258\r\nthe fabulous Flying Graysons.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.341 --\u003e 00:11:17.969\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.453 --\u003e 00:11:44.454\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:46.206 --\u003e 00:11:47.207\r\nDad!\r\n\r\n00:11:55.381 --\u003e 00:11:56.591\r\n(CROWD GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.972 --\u003e 00:12:04.515\r\nDICK: It had to be that guy.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.725 --\u003e 00:12:07.185\r\nHe threatened Mr. Haley.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.228 --\u003e 00:12:10.355\r\nI saw him come out of the tent.\r\n\r\n00:12:10.438 --\u003e 00:12:12.357\r\nI tried to tell my folks, but...\r\n\r\n00:12:12.440 --\u003e 00:12:13.650\r\nBut...\r\n\r\n00:12:13.733 --\u003e 00:12:15.235\r\nOkay, son. Okay.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.612 --\u003e 00:12:20.448\r\nI want an APB on this\r\nZucco character now.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.531 --\u003e 00:12:21.824\r\nWhat about the boy?\r\n\r\n00:12:21.908 --\u003e 00:12:22.909\r\nMr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:12:23.534 --\u003e 00:12:26.663\r\nI was in the audience,\r\ncouldn't leave after this.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.746 --\u003e 00:12:28.581\r\nDoes he have anyone?\r\n\r\n00:12:28.665 --\u003e 00:12:29.666\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:12:29.749 --\u003e 00:12:31.209\r\nNo family.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.292 --\u003e 00:12:33.092\r\nSome of the circus people\r\nwant to take him in,\r\n\r\n00:12:34.170 --\u003e 00:12:36.673\r\nbut, frankly, I'm afraid Zucco\r\nmight try to shut him up.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.173 --\u003e 00:12:38.841\r\nThe boy's a material witness.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.925 --\u003e 00:12:41.970\r\nWe'll be here tonight,\r\nbut I might have to find a safe house.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.680 --\u003e 00:12:45.306\r\nI may be able to help.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.433 --\u003e 00:12:51.271\r\nAnd remember, lad,\r\nyou'll always be a part of this family.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.772 --\u003e 00:12:54.023\r\nThanks, Mr. Haley.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.318 --\u003e 00:13:00.280\r\nI know, Sitka.\r\nI'm gonna miss you, too.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.996 --\u003e 00:13:09.414\r\n(CAR DOORS CLOSING)\r\n\r\n00:13:27.181 --\u003e 00:13:28.182\r\nThis is it.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.142 --\u003e 00:13:30.143\r\nI'll get your bags.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.771 --\u003e 00:13:35.315\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:44.324 --\u003e 00:13:46.451\r\nI hope you find this\r\nroom to your liking.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.534 --\u003e 00:13:48.953\r\nIt was Master Bruce's\r\nwhen he was your age.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.330 --\u003e 00:13:53.082\r\nLook, Dick,\r\nit's not going to be easy.\r\n\r\n00:13:53.750 --\u003e 00:13:55.752\r\nYou have to take\r\nit a day at a time.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.835 --\u003e 00:13:59.756\r\nBut for however long it takes,\r\nyou have a home with us.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.757 --\u003e 00:14:02.008\r\nThanks, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.508 --\u003e 00:14:04.385\r\n- Bruce.\r\n- Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.178 --\u003e 00:14:08.806\r\nCome, sir, I do believe Master Dick\r\ncould use some time to settle in.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.231 --\u003e 00:14:18.274\r\n(DOOR CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:14:35.083 --\u003e 00:14:36.334\r\n\u003ci\u003eROBIN: It's not right, Alfred.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:37.585 --\u003e 00:14:39.837\r\nHe can't take\r\nZucco away from me.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.921 --\u003e 00:14:41.339\r\nI won't let him!\r\n\r\n00:14:47.845 --\u003e 00:14:51.224\r\n\u003ci\u003eDICK: It had to be that guy.\r\nHe threatened Mr. Haley.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:51.307 --\u003e 00:14:54.268\r\nGORDON: \u003ci\u003eI want an APB on this Zucco.\r\n(ECHOING)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:54.352 --\u003e 00:14:55.436\r\nZucco.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.605 --\u003e 00:14:59.357\r\nIsn't Bruce coming down to eat?\r\n\r\n00:15:00.233 --\u003e 00:15:01.901\r\nI'm afraid not tonight, Dick.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.984 --\u003e 00:15:03.569\r\nI've got a late meeting.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.445 --\u003e 00:15:06.114\r\nCould be fruitful.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.197 --\u003e 00:15:07.323\r\nMmm. Very good, sir.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.866 --\u003e 00:15:11.577\r\nHe has a meeting every night.\r\nWho does he see?\r\n\r\n00:15:12.412 --\u003e 00:15:17.041\r\nUm, some of the most influential\r\npeople in Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.709 --\u003e 00:15:20.002\r\nMAN: Come on, seven.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.670 --\u003e 00:15:22.171\r\nSnake eyes. (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.467 --\u003e 00:15:29.846\r\nToughluck. Maybe I can\r\nchange the way they roll.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.015 --\u003e 00:15:35.643\r\nHey, you're a friend of Tony\r\nZucco's, ain't you?\r\n\r\n00:15:35.726 --\u003e 00:15:38.020\r\nI hear he's been\r\nfeeling the heat lately.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.023 --\u003e 00:15:42.316\r\nMAN: Lucky five.\r\n\r\n00:15:42.817 --\u003e 00:15:45.153\r\nYeah, the Z-man's been lying\r\nlow, all right.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.862 --\u003e 00:15:48.197\r\nThey say he's got bat problems.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.284 --\u003e 00:15:52.743\r\nBig bat problems.\r\n\r\n00:15:54.495 --\u003e 00:15:57.373\r\nI can't help wondering how\r\nhe's keeping out of sight.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.457 --\u003e 00:15:59.333\r\nYou do an awful\r\nlot of wondering,\r\n\r\n00:15:59.417 --\u003e 00:16:02.044\r\nfor someone we ain't\r\never seen before.\r\n\r\n00:16:02.128 --\u003e 00:16:03.629\r\nWhat'd you say your name was?\r\n\r\n00:16:04.505 --\u003e 00:16:05.673\r\nSmith.\r\n\r\n00:16:07.508 --\u003e 00:16:11.179\r\nSmith. That wouldn't be Detective\r\nSmith, would it?\r\n\r\n00:16:11.262 --\u003e 00:16:12.805\r\nOr maybe Sergeant?\r\n\r\n00:16:15.933 --\u003e 00:16:17.268\r\nCheck his wallet, Al.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.103 --\u003e 00:16:20.813\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.074 --\u003e 00:16:33.075\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:39.707 --\u003e 00:16:40.708\r\n(GULPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:41.417 --\u003e 00:16:42.418\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.377 --\u003e 00:16:45.171\r\nNow, about Zucco...\r\n\r\n00:16:46.506 --\u003e 00:16:48.549\r\nNo way. I ain't no squealer.\r\n\r\n00:16:48.633 --\u003e 00:16:51.093\r\nYou're getting nothing out of me.\r\nYou hear? Nothing.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.640 --\u003e 00:16:58.017\r\n(YELLS) Stromwell.\r\nHe's with Stromwell,\r\n\r\n00:16:58.100 --\u003e 00:17:00.478\r\nhis uncle, okay?\r\nAll right? (WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.198 --\u003e 00:17:14.033\r\n(MAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:21.916 --\u003e 00:17:23.000\r\nWho's there?\r\n\r\n00:17:29.090 --\u003e 00:17:30.299\r\nEasy, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.383 --\u003e 00:17:31.509\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:32.593 --\u003e 00:17:34.262\r\nYou might try\r\nknocking some time.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.972 --\u003e 00:17:37.515\r\nThis isn't a social call.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.266 --\u003e 00:17:41.686\r\nI've come for your\r\nnephew, Tony Zucco.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.478 --\u003e 00:17:45.022\r\nYou can't just barge\r\nin here making demands.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.982 --\u003e 00:17:48.276\r\nI want him bad, Stromwell.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.359 --\u003e 00:17:49.986\r\nReal bad.\r\n\r\n00:17:50.653 --\u003e 00:17:53.197\r\n- How should I know where he is?\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.531 --\u003e 00:17:56.033\r\nI stopped looking after\r\nthat loser a long time ago.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.742 --\u003e 00:17:59.704\r\nIf you protect him, Stromwell,\r\n\r\n00:17:59.787 --\u003e 00:18:03.332\r\nI'll be very grumpy.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.333 --\u003e 00:18:07.044\r\nYou don't want to see me grumpy.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.670 --\u003e 00:18:09.088\r\nSTROMWELL: Uh, yeah. I got you.\r\n\r\n00:18:20.725 --\u003e 00:18:24.145\r\nZUCCO: Smooth, Uncle Arnie.\r\nReal smooth.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.228 --\u003e 00:18:26.897\r\nYeah, you sure suckered\r\nthat pointy-eared freak.\r\n\r\n00:18:26.981 --\u003e 00:18:30.192\r\n- He won't be messing around here any-\r\n- Jerk! Fool!\r\n\r\n00:18:30.276 --\u003e 00:18:31.986\r\nYou and your penny-ante\r\nextortion racket!\r\n\r\n00:18:32.069 --\u003e 00:18:33.946\r\nLook what you've\r\nbrought on my house!\r\n\r\n00:18:34.405 --\u003e 00:18:38.326\r\nHey, come on. Stop already.\r\nWe can handle the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.409 --\u003e 00:18:40.995\r\nNo, buddy boy,\r\nthis time you've gone too far.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.621 --\u003e 00:18:44.457\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou're no longer a part of this\r\nfamily, you hear? You're out!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:49.003 --\u003e 00:18:50.254\r\nHey. Who's there?\r\n\r\n00:18:50.338 --\u003e 00:18:51.756\r\n(GUNFIRE)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.839 --\u003e 00:18:54.008\r\nIt's him. He's still here.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.260 --\u003e 00:18:57.261\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:09.815 --\u003e 00:19:11.525\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:11.609 --\u003e 00:19:13.110\r\nNow I've got you.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.194 --\u003e 00:19:15.196\r\nYou lousy, stinking...\r\n\r\n00:19:26.040 --\u003e 00:19:29.043\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: I was so close, Alfred,\r\nI could smell his sweat.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:29.794 --\u003e 00:19:33.798\r\nFrom now on, Tony Zucco\r\ngets my undivided attention.\r\n\r\n00:19:34.465 --\u003e 00:19:35.925\r\nHow fortunate for Zucco,\r\n\r\n00:19:36.467 --\u003e 00:19:38.302\r\nbecause there's a\r\nlittle boy up there\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.763\r\nwho's just aching for\r\nsome of that attention.\r\n\r\n00:19:40.846 --\u003e 00:19:42.848\r\nI'm doing this for him.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.392 --\u003e 00:19:47.603\r\nI'm sure revenge can\r\nbe deliciously sweet.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.687 --\u003e 00:19:50.398\r\nHowever, at the moment,\r\nhe needs a friend.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.482 --\u003e 00:19:53.734\r\nIsn't that what you needed, sir?\r\n\r\n00:20:02.410 --\u003e 00:20:04.495\r\nBRUCE: Hey, Dick? How you doing?\r\n\r\n00:20:05.204 --\u003e 00:20:06.247\r\nFine.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.872 --\u003e 00:20:08.332\r\nSorry I haven't been around.\r\n\r\n00:20:09.125 --\u003e 00:20:11.961\r\nI forget how big and\r\nlonely this place can be.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.044 --\u003e 00:20:13.421\r\nThat's okay.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.504 --\u003e 00:20:14.588\r\nAs it turns out,\r\n\r\n00:20:14.672 --\u003e 00:20:16.924\r\nI may have some free\r\ntime starting tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.842 --\u003e 00:20:20.720\r\nHow'd you like to catch the\r\nGotham Knights' season opener?\r\n\r\n00:20:20.803 --\u003e 00:20:22.930\r\n- Box seats.\r\n- Great.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.223 --\u003e 00:20:25.891\r\nI know it must be\r\nvery difficult.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.517 --\u003e 00:20:27.977\r\nIf only I could've stopped him.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.728 --\u003e 00:20:30.604\r\nI saw him coming\r\nout of the tent.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.688 --\u003e 00:20:32.940\r\nI knew he didn't belong there.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.150\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.775 --\u003e 00:20:35.901\r\nYou keep thinking,\r\n\r\n00:20:36.861 --\u003e 00:20:38.988\r\n\"If only I'd done\r\nsomething differently.\"\r\n\r\n00:20:40.239 --\u003e 00:20:42.700\r\n\"If only I could've\r\nwarned them.\"\r\n\r\n00:20:43.784 --\u003e 00:20:45.745\r\nBut there isn't anything\r\nyou could have done.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.662 --\u003e 00:20:49.290\r\nThere's isn't anything\r\neither of us could have done.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.208 --\u003e 00:20:52.543\r\nYour mom and dad?\r\n\r\n00:20:55.212 --\u003e 00:20:57.173\r\nDoes the hurt ever go away?\r\n\r\n00:20:58.424 --\u003e 00:20:59.925\r\nI wish I could say yes.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.177 --\u003e 00:21:06.098\r\nBut it will get better in time for you.\r\nThat I promise.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.725 --\u003e 00:21:09.268\r\nROBIN: (ON SPEAKER)\r\nYou deceived me.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.351 --\u003e 00:21:12.521\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou can't take this one.\r\nZucco's mine!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:12.605 --\u003e 00:21:13.606\r\nSorry, Robin,\r\n\r\n00:21:13.689 --\u003e 00:21:16.025\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut on this team,\r\nI call the shots.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:16.108 --\u003e 00:21:19.487\r\n- But I've waited half my life!\r\n- Batman out.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.570 --\u003e 00:21:22.698\r\n- (RADIO CLICKS)\r\n- Oh, no. He's not going to ace me out.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.240 --\u003e 00:21:25.701\r\nPlease, Master Dick,\r\nyou must do as he says.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.785 --\u003e 00:21:27.411\r\nNot this time, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.621 --\u003e 00:21:29.955\r\nMaybe not ever again.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.061 --\u003e 00:21:54.063\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:17.336 --\u003e 00:22:18.337\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E52 - Birds of a Feather (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.255 --\u003e 00:00:07.424\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.622 --\u003e 00:01:23.500\r\nAh, Audubon.\r\nMy personal favorite.\r\n\r\n00:01:24.501 --\u003e 00:01:26.003\r\n(SMOOCHES)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.966 --\u003e 00:01:32.092\r\n(MUFFLED GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:01:33.677 --\u003e 00:01:36.930\r\nSorry about the intrusion, sir,\r\nbut at least you've been ransacked\r\n\r\n00:01:37.014 --\u003e 00:01:39.349\r\nby a man of impeccable taste.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.938 --\u003e 00:01:46.064\r\n(BATARANGS WHIZZING)\r\n\r\n00:01:46.148 --\u003e 00:01:47.316\r\nBOTH: Huh?\r\n\r\n00:01:51.069 --\u003e 00:01:54.573\r\nTwo days out of prison and you're\r\nback to your old games, Penguin?\r\n\r\n00:01:55.282 --\u003e 00:01:57.743\r\nYou again, and again and again!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.423 --\u003e 00:02:12.924\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.313 --\u003e 00:02:28.023\r\n(MACHINE GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:02:35.781 --\u003e 00:02:36.782\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.866 --\u003e 00:02:39.034\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:41.286 --\u003e 00:02:42.329\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.003 --\u003e 00:02:51.296\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:02:56.468 --\u003e 00:02:58.303\r\n(HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.140 --\u003e 00:03:03.767\r\nSo today's the day, huh?\r\n\r\n00:03:04.768 --\u003e 00:03:06.561\r\nPlanning on making a big splash?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.521 --\u003e 00:03:10.607\r\nNo need.\r\nThey never forget the true elite.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.484 --\u003e 00:03:14.778\r\nWell, they got a lot\r\nto remember you by.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.195 --\u003e 00:03:20.367\r\nAh, but this time, I'll reclaim my perch\r\nin high society as an upstanding bird.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.076 --\u003e 00:03:23.870\r\nI've learned my lesson.\r\nNever again.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.287 --\u003e 00:03:25.330\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.414 --\u003e 00:03:27.874\r\nCome.\r\nThe cream of society awaits.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.041 --\u003e 00:03:30.502\r\nA limousine is no\r\ndoubt at the ready.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.555 --\u003e 00:03:43.032\r\nGUARD: Oh, what's the\r\nmatter, Penguin?\r\n\r\n00:03:43.056 --\u003e 00:03:46.852\r\nMaybe the cream of society has\r\ncurdled, huh? (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:03:48.520 --\u003e 00:03:49.706\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:49.730 --\u003e 00:03:50.897\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.440 --\u003e 00:03:54.234\r\nYou coming or not?\r\nI got a schedule, you know.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.776 --\u003e 00:03:57.112\r\nAnd a lovely disposition\r\nto go with it.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.076 --\u003e 00:04:05.954\r\nWell, this is hardly the style\r\nto which I am accustomed.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.371 --\u003e 00:04:07.372\r\nGlad you like it.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.039 --\u003e 00:04:09.124\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:15.589 --\u003e 00:04:16.829\r\nVERONICA: I'm slipping, Pierce.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.758 --\u003e 00:04:20.051\r\nOnly 24 invitations this month.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.552 --\u003e 00:04:22.888\r\nMy dear, you're practically out.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.263 --\u003e 00:04:25.056\r\nIt's high time\r\nyou threw a party.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.307 --\u003e 00:04:27.809\r\nAnd make it the\r\nbiggest bash ever.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.018 --\u003e 00:04:29.686\r\nYes, yes, but how?\r\n\r\n00:04:29.895 --\u003e 00:04:32.147\r\nI'm out of charities\r\nuntil spring at least,\r\n\r\n00:04:32.522 --\u003e 00:04:34.524\r\nand there are no\r\ninteresting celebrities.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.608 --\u003e 00:04:35.942\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.026 --\u003e 00:04:39.321\r\nRemember when the Joker crashed\r\nMuffy Van Alten's last affair?\r\n\r\n00:04:39.571 --\u003e 00:04:41.823\r\nHe robbed us blind,\r\nbut hey, what a giggle.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.116 --\u003e 00:04:47.496\r\nYeah, it was amusing.\r\nBut the Joker's yesterday's news.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.996 --\u003e 00:04:49.539\r\nThen have a peek at today's.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.083 --\u003e 00:04:53.460\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.085 --\u003e 00:04:55.545\r\nI love it!\r\n\r\n00:05:01.051 --\u003e 00:05:04.596\r\nI'd best prepare myself\r\nfor the welcoming throngs.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.185 --\u003e 00:05:12.854\r\nWell, fellow rogues,\r\nit's great to be back.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.776 --\u003e 00:05:22.531\r\nIf you're trying to surprise me,\r\nyou're doing an excellent job.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.324 --\u003e 00:05:27.077\r\nSay, who's there?\r\nTwo-Face? Croc?\r\n\r\n00:05:27.577 --\u003e 00:05:28.954\r\nJoker, old shoe.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.371 --\u003e 00:05:30.789\r\nBATMAN: None of the\r\nabove, Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.168 --\u003e 00:05:37.420\r\nOh, no! Not you.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.546 --\u003e 00:05:38.922\r\nGet used to it.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.256 --\u003e 00:05:42.092\r\nWherever you go,\r\nI'll be right behind you.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.342 --\u003e 00:05:44.052\r\nPrecisely where you belong.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.344 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nBut you needn't bother.\r\nHaven't you heard? I've reformed.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.557 --\u003e 00:05:51.184\r\nPaid my debt to\r\nsociety and all that.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.018 --\u003e 00:05:53.019\r\nWe'll see.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.103 --\u003e 00:05:55.355\r\nI just came to tell you\r\nto keep your beak clean.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.817 --\u003e 00:06:00.151\r\nAs long as you're here,\r\n\r\n00:06:00.235 --\u003e 00:06:02.028\r\nwon't you stay for a cappuccino?\r\n\r\n00:06:15.542 --\u003e 00:06:17.544\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:06:17.627 --\u003e 00:06:20.380\r\nJust what I need,\r\na bat in my belfry.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.797 --\u003e 00:06:23.592\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:25.719 --\u003e 00:06:28.638\r\nHold on. Hold on, I'm coming.\r\nHello.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.264 --\u003e 00:06:32.309\r\nMr. Cobblepot?\r\nVeronica Vreeland here.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.018 --\u003e 00:06:34.352\r\nVeronica Vreeland?\r\n\r\n00:06:34.936 --\u003e 00:06:36.438\r\nThe Veronica Vreeland?\r\n\r\n00:06:36.980 --\u003e 00:06:41.276\r\nYes. And I'm sure there's only\r\none Oswald Chesterfield Cobblepot.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.776 --\u003e 00:06:43.403\r\nI've so wanted to meet you.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.695 --\u003e 00:06:44.696\r\nYou have?\r\n\r\n00:06:45.488 --\u003e 00:06:49.117\r\nAre you free for dinner tomorrow?\r\n7:00-ish at Angelo's?\r\n\r\n00:06:49.409 --\u003e 00:06:51.077\r\n\u003ci\u003eThey do a darling calamari.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:52.871 --\u003e 00:06:56.458\r\nOh, certainement, my dear.\r\nI'll see you there.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.046 --\u003e 00:07:03.131\r\n(BOTH LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:04.549 --\u003e 00:07:06.259\r\n(PENGUIN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:06.343 --\u003e 00:07:07.469\r\nAnd get this.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.552 --\u003e 00:07:10.597\r\nThen I said, \"But, Warden,\r\nthose aren't my pants.\"\r\n\r\n00:07:10.764 --\u003e 00:07:12.724\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.558 --\u003e 00:07:14.684\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.060 --\u003e 00:07:17.520\r\nOh, Ozzie, you are such a rogue.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.608 --\u003e 00:07:22.817\r\n(GULPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:25.028 --\u003e 00:07:27.030\r\n\u003ci\u003eAh, si, signore,\r\na tame for two'?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:27.405 --\u003e 00:07:29.199\r\nIs that who I think it is?\r\n\r\n00:07:32.911 --\u003e 00:07:36.623\r\nCome along, Binky.\r\nWe've already been robbed once this year.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.748 --\u003e 00:07:38.500\r\n(HOST SPEAKING ITALIAN)\r\n\r\n00:07:44.756 --\u003e 00:07:46.257\r\nSuch an enchanting evening.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.883 --\u003e 00:07:49.844\r\nBut tell me, my dear,\r\nwhat are you hatching?\r\n\r\n00:07:50.303 --\u003e 00:07:51.513\r\nWhatever do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:07:52.097 --\u003e 00:07:56.226\r\nThere's more to our encounter than\r\nmeets my eagle eye, isn't there?\r\n\r\n00:07:56.685 --\u003e 00:07:59.187\r\nWhy, Oswald,\r\nhow could you think such a thing?\r\n\r\n00:07:59.604 --\u003e 00:08:03.566\r\nI've always been captivated by your...\r\nYour rapacious wit.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.942 --\u003e 00:08:07.612\r\nNot to mention that\r\nfine Roman nose.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.035 --\u003e 00:08:16.871\r\nNaturally.\r\nCome, let us fly, my dove.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.873 --\u003e 00:08:21.459\r\nGargon, the check,\r\nif you please.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.043 --\u003e 00:08:26.047\r\nWith respect, signore, the management\r\noffers the meal with his compliments\r\n\r\n00:08:26.256 --\u003e 00:08:27.924\r\nif you will just leave.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.884 --\u003e 00:08:33.304\r\nThey seem to know you quite well.\r\nHave you eaten here before?\r\n\r\n00:08:33.680 --\u003e 00:08:37.517\r\nI've been known to stop\r\nby for a quick carryout.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.900 --\u003e 00:08:48.403\r\nHey, I smell money.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.778 --\u003e 00:08:52.741\r\nBy the by, Ozzie, in two\r\ndays, I'm throwing a small do,\r\n\r\n00:08:53.199 --\u003e 00:08:57.078\r\nintimate almost,\r\njust 100 or so of my dearest friends.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.662 --\u003e 00:09:00.457\r\nI'd be delighted.\r\nYou are inviting me, aren't you?\r\n\r\n00:09:00.832 --\u003e 00:09:01.833\r\nYes!\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:07.380\r\nOkay, you know the drill, fatso.\r\nWallet, jewels, cough them up.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.756 --\u003e 00:09:11.676\r\nYou insolent curs.\r\nDon't you know who I am?\r\n\r\n00:09:11.968 --\u003e 00:09:14.929\r\nNot with that ugly\r\nmask you're wearing.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.098 --\u003e 00:09:18.641\r\nTake him, boys.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.486 --\u003e 00:09:30.570\r\n\u003ci\u003eEn garde!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:32.739 --\u003e 00:09:34.199\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:09:34.866 --\u003e 00:09:35.992\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:36.826 --\u003e 00:09:37.994\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:09:45.835 --\u003e 00:09:46.836\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:47.545 --\u003e 00:09:50.173\r\nThat's too fine a collar\r\nfor a mongrel like you.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.639 --\u003e 00:09:59.140\r\n(PENGUIN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:10:01.142 --\u003e 00:10:02.435\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:08.399 --\u003e 00:10:09.442\r\n(BATMAN PUNCHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:11.945 --\u003e 00:10:13.154\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:16.032 --\u003e 00:10:17.492\r\n(CONTINUES SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:21.287 --\u003e 00:10:23.790\r\nCome on, you rotten...\r\n\r\n00:10:26.668 --\u003e 00:10:28.169\r\n(THUG STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:10:30.880 --\u003e 00:10:32.423\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:10:34.300 --\u003e 00:10:37.095\r\nI knew you couldn't stay\r\nclean for more than one day.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.554 --\u003e 00:10:40.181\r\nLet him go. He didn't do anything.\r\nIt was those brutes.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.683 --\u003e 00:10:42.851\r\nHe wasn't with them?\r\n\r\n00:10:43.268 --\u003e 00:10:45.436\r\nThat's right,\r\nyou vulgar vigilante.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.562 --\u003e 00:10:48.815\r\nIn my day, I associated with a\r\nmuch higher class of riffraff.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.482 --\u003e 00:10:50.984\r\nI'm so sorry, Ozzie.\r\n\r\n00:10:51.401 --\u003e 00:10:54.112\r\nAs long as you weren't\r\nbruised, my peach.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.363 --\u003e 00:10:56.447\r\n\"Peach\"?\r\n\r\n00:10:57.115 --\u003e 00:11:00.577\r\nWhy don't you be a good masked\r\nman and ride off into the night.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.743 --\u003e 00:11:03.246\r\nThis time,\r\nI'll clean up after you.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.875 --\u003e 00:11:10.378\r\nPIERCE: He fenced with his umbrella?\r\nHow droll.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.837 --\u003e 00:11:13.464\r\nThis Penguin will\r\nabsolutely make your party.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:15.842\r\nYou know,\r\nit was quite touching actually.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.134 --\u003e 00:11:18.761\r\nIt's not often that a\r\nman rushes to my rescue.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.596 --\u003e 00:11:21.764\r\nUnfortunately,\r\nhe wants to see me again.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.474\r\nWho's that, Veronica?\r\n\r\n00:11:23.600 --\u003e 00:11:25.800\r\nI've heard you're running\r\naround with a dangerous crowd.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.102 --\u003e 00:11:27.812\r\nWell, keep it under your\r\nhat, Brucie,\r\n\r\n00:11:27.896 --\u003e 00:11:30.440\r\nbut, I've just snagged\r\nthe Penguin for my party.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.523 --\u003e 00:11:31.524\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\n00:11:32.150 --\u003e 00:11:33.860\r\nPIERCE: For the\r\nentertainment, dodo.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.360 --\u003e 00:11:38.198\r\nCan't you just see their faces\r\nwhen that stuffed capon waddles in?\r\n\r\n00:11:38.698 --\u003e 00:11:40.533\r\nI'd think twice if I were you.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.700 --\u003e 00:11:42.827\r\nOh, lighten up, Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.994 --\u003e 00:11:45.413\r\nAfter all, he is NOKD.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.456 --\u003e 00:11:48.124\r\n\"Not our kind, dear.\"\r\n\r\n00:11:51.127 --\u003e 00:11:54.339\r\nBetter be careful that your little\r\njoke doesn't come home to roost.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.598 --\u003e 00:12:06.726\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:12:23.243 --\u003e 00:12:25.203\r\n(SINGING ALONG)\r\n\r\n00:12:41.761 --\u003e 00:12:44.180\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:56.651 --\u003e 00:12:58.987\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:10.081 --\u003e 00:13:12.917\r\nSo you're the president\r\nof Gotham First Federal.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.418 --\u003e 00:13:15.336\r\nI hope you've beefed\r\nup your security.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.586 --\u003e 00:13:19.382\r\nThose time locks were easy to\r\ncircumnavigate, as I recall.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.966 --\u003e 00:13:22.593\r\nSir, you leave me\r\nat a loss for words.\r\n\r\n00:13:23.052 --\u003e 00:13:25.596\r\nI certainly left you\r\nat a loss for funds.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.722 --\u003e 00:13:27.181\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.599 --\u003e 00:13:31.019\r\nLovely dress. Prison chic?\r\n\r\n00:13:31.602 --\u003e 00:13:34.939\r\nMakes her look like a gathering\r\nof Cell Block 3. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:13:35.273 --\u003e 00:13:38.693\r\nSay, isn't that Mayor Hill?\r\nHey, Hammy!\r\n\r\n00:13:39.652 --\u003e 00:13:41.279\r\nHe's beautiful.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.863 --\u003e 00:13:43.865\r\nCan you imagine\r\ntomorrow's papers?\r\n\r\n00:13:44.198 --\u003e 00:13:47.577\r\nThere's not enough ink to print\r\nall his faux pas. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:13:48.494 --\u003e 00:13:51.456\r\nI don't know, Pierce.\r\nI've got a bad feeling about this.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.217 --\u003e 00:14:05.511\r\nAdmiring the Vreeland\r\njewelry, Mr. Cobblepot?\r\n\r\n00:14:06.095 --\u003e 00:14:07.930\r\nAh, Mr. Wayne, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:14:08.556 --\u003e 00:14:11.434\r\nActually, I was thinking of\r\nadding this to her collection.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.936 --\u003e 00:14:14.979\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.438 --\u003e 00:14:18.149\r\nMaybe the rumors of your\r\nreform are not exaggerated.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.441 --\u003e 00:14:21.194\r\nAnything's possible\r\nwhen love is involved.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.569 --\u003e 00:14:22.862\r\nIf you'll excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.952 --\u003e 00:14:31.746\r\nPIERCE: Oh, will you relax?\r\n\r\n00:14:31.913 --\u003e 00:14:33.081\r\nYou've done him a favor.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.581 --\u003e 00:14:34.582\r\nVERONICA: But, Pierce...\r\n\r\n00:14:37.043 --\u003e 00:14:38.378\r\nYou said it yourself.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.586 --\u003e 00:14:41.631\r\nThat fat bird would never get\r\ninvited to a party like this,\r\n\r\n00:14:41.923 --\u003e 00:14:45.635\r\nnot with those clothes,\r\nthat waddle, those flippers.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.260 --\u003e 00:14:47.261\r\nOswald!\r\n\r\n00:14:47.428 --\u003e 00:14:50.932\r\nDid she mention my\r\nfine Roman nose?\r\n\r\n00:14:52.892 --\u003e 00:14:54.185\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:14:55.436 --\u003e 00:14:57.397\r\n- (COUGHING)\r\n- (VERONICA SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.855 --\u003e 00:14:59.375\r\n- Who was that?\r\n- WOMAN: What happened?\r\n\r\n00:14:59.440 --\u003e 00:15:01.160\r\nMAN 1: What's going on?\r\nMAN 2: Good heavens.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.068 --\u003e 00:15:03.069\r\nPierce?\r\n\r\n00:15:06.030 --\u003e 00:15:08.157\r\nHe took her.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.335 --\u003e 00:15:20.670\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.389 --\u003e 00:15:33.683\r\nWell, it's been over 24 hours.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.392 --\u003e 00:15:38.438\r\nI assure you that every available\r\nman is on this case, Mr. Chapman.\r\n\r\n00:15:39.188 --\u003e 00:15:41.899\r\nIt's times like these when I\r\nwonder why we pay you people.\r\n\r\n00:15:42.191 --\u003e 00:15:43.901\r\nListen here,\r\nyou simpering little twit!\r\n\r\n00:15:44.235 --\u003e 00:15:46.070\r\nYou were foolish enough\r\nto invite the Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.237 --\u003e 00:15:47.405\r\nNow it's his party.\r\n\r\n00:15:47.530 --\u003e 00:15:48.781\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:15:48.906 --\u003e 00:15:50.283\r\n(GLASS SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:56.914 --\u003e 00:15:57.957\r\nPIERCE: What is it?\r\n\r\n00:16:01.752 --\u003e 00:16:02.753\r\nThe ransom note.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.754 --\u003e 00:16:06.090\r\nHe wants $1 million\r\nfrom her trust.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.674 --\u003e 00:16:08.342\r\nPetty cash. Easily done.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.759 --\u003e 00:16:10.386\r\nThere's just one\r\ncatch, Mr. Chapman.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.262 --\u003e 00:16:14.098\r\n- He wants you to make the drop.\r\n- The drop?\r\n\r\n00:16:27.278 --\u003e 00:16:28.821\r\nHuh? (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:45.129 --\u003e 00:16:46.380\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:46.506 --\u003e 00:16:47.798\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.009 --\u003e 00:16:51.219\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.302 --\u003e 00:16:54.096\r\n\"Go to the corner of\r\nBarr and Englehart.\"\r\n\r\n00:16:58.100 --\u003e 00:16:59.435\r\nLook sharp, boys.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.852 --\u003e 00:17:00.853\r\nShouldn't be long now.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.566 --\u003e 00:17:07.193\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:17:14.200 --\u003e 00:17:15.201\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:17:15.660 --\u003e 00:17:16.661\r\nPENGUIN: B00!\r\n\r\n00:17:16.994 --\u003e 00:17:18.579\r\n\u003ci\u003ePIERCE: Penguin, is that you?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:19.288 --\u003e 00:17:21.082\r\nIt's Pierce. I've got the money.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.624 --\u003e 00:17:24.252\r\nI knew I could\r\ncount on your kind.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.835 --\u003e 00:17:26.462\r\nRight, I'll just leave it here,\r\n\r\n00:17:26.546 --\u003e 00:17:28.506\r\nand you can pick it up\r\nat your convenience.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.839 --\u003e 00:17:30.299\r\nNot quite, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.550 --\u003e 00:17:32.718\r\n\u003ci\u003eTake exactly one step\r\nout of the booth,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:33.177 --\u003e 00:17:35.304\r\n\u003ci\u003eturn left and start walking.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:35.846 --\u003e 00:17:36.847\r\nHow far?\r\n\r\n00:17:37.056 --\u003e 00:17:38.891\r\nYou'll know when you get there.\r\n\r\n00:17:47.984 --\u003e 00:17:49.443\r\n(PIERCE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:56.075 --\u003e 00:17:57.994\r\nWe lost him in the sewers.\r\n\r\n00:18:06.210 --\u003e 00:18:10.798\r\nPENGUIN: Time to disembark.\r\nDon't forget your luggage. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:12.300 --\u003e 00:18:15.428\r\nThat's right,\r\njust follow my mellifluous chirp.\r\n\r\n00:18:21.934 --\u003e 00:18:24.270\r\n(GASPS) What's happening?\r\n\r\n00:18:30.985 --\u003e 00:18:31.986\r\nVERONICA: Pierce!\r\n\r\n00:18:32.862 --\u003e 00:18:34.322\r\nOh, my Lord!\r\n\r\n00:18:35.531 --\u003e 00:18:36.532\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:18:37.617 --\u003e 00:18:39.577\r\nI believe you two\r\nknow each other.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.411 --\u003e 00:18:42.121\r\nHey, what is this?\r\n\r\n00:18:42.496 --\u003e 00:18:47.126\r\nThe end of the show,\r\nwhen the fat bird sings. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:18:50.671 --\u003e 00:18:51.922\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:18:52.840 --\u003e 00:18:56.093\r\nPlease, Oswald. If it's money you\r\nwant, I can get you more.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.886 --\u003e 00:18:57.887\r\nShut up!\r\n\r\n00:18:58.137 --\u003e 00:19:01.015\r\nAll I wanted from you, dearie,\r\nwas a little friendship.\r\n\r\n00:19:01.223 --\u003e 00:19:05.436\r\nThat would've cost you nothing.\r\nBut now you'll pay.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.604 --\u003e 00:19:07.772\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:19:10.232 --\u003e 00:19:13.778\r\nI believe this calls for an\r\nacceleration of my plans.\r\n\r\n00:19:19.700 --\u003e 00:19:21.619\r\nIt's been smashing.\r\n\r\n00:19:22.119 --\u003e 00:19:23.996\r\nOswald, it needn't end this way.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.080 --\u003e 00:19:27.958\r\nI truly was growing fond of you.\r\nWe might've been friends.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.209 --\u003e 00:19:31.212\r\n- We still might.\r\n- Yes, we all might.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.837 --\u003e 00:19:32.838\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.005 --\u003e 00:19:34.882\r\n\"'Tis better to have\r\nloved and lost,\"\r\n\r\n00:19:35.257 --\u003e 00:19:36.258\r\nand made a small profit,\r\n\r\n00:19:36.676 --\u003e 00:19:38.552\r\n\"than never to\r\nhave loved at all.\"\r\n\r\n00:19:38.761 --\u003e 00:19:39.887\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:41.764 --\u003e 00:19:43.808\r\nFashionably late, I see.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.859 --\u003e 00:19:55.319\r\nOn to Act 2.\r\n\r\n00:19:55.403 --\u003e 00:19:56.487\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:20:04.578 --\u003e 00:20:06.247\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:20:16.424 --\u003e 00:20:17.758\r\nTally-ho!\r\n\r\n00:20:23.097 --\u003e 00:20:26.183\r\nAnd who says opera\r\nhas to be boring?\r\n\r\n00:20:32.273 --\u003e 00:20:34.817\r\n“No! Help!\r\n\r\n00:20:39.905 --\u003e 00:20:41.449\r\n(PENGUIN LAUGHING MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:47.788 --\u003e 00:20:49.874\r\n(VERONICA SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.253 --\u003e 00:20:55.629\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:20:57.757 --\u003e 00:21:00.468\r\nWe'll end this on a high note.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.888 --\u003e 00:21:06.265\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.559 --\u003e 00:21:09.810\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:21:10.853 --\u003e 00:21:12.271\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:21:14.899 --\u003e 00:21:16.901\r\nNo! (GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:21:19.779 --\u003e 00:21:22.114\r\nCareful. Careful.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.408 --\u003e 00:21:25.409\r\nVERONICA: Oswald,\r\n\r\n00:21:26.869 --\u003e 00:21:29.038\r\nI really was\r\ngrowing fond of you.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.830 --\u003e 00:21:31.248\r\nIt's too bad this had to happen.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.582 --\u003e 00:21:33.959\r\nI suppose it's\r\ntrue what they say.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.376 --\u003e 00:21:36.003\r\nSociety is to blame.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.712 --\u003e 00:21:38.422\r\nHigh society.\r\n\r\n00:21:54.021 --\u003e 00:21:56.023\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:20.256 --\u003e 00:22:21.257\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E53 - Robin's Reckoning, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.048 --\u003e 00:00:08.050\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:05.816 --\u003e 00:01:07.484\r\nROBIN: Previously on Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:07.734 --\u003e 00:01:10.571\r\nROBIN: Everything was going great\r\nuntil that Marin business came up.\r\n\r\n00:01:12.864 --\u003e 00:01:14.908\r\nYou ever hear of a crook\r\nnamed Billy Marin, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:01:25.460 --\u003e 00:01:28.463\r\n- Hey, that's the guy the-\r\n- Come on, honey, we're on.\r\n\r\n00:01:39.433 --\u003e 00:01:40.434\r\nDad!\r\n\r\n00:01:44.271 --\u003e 00:01:45.689\r\nDoes he have anyone?\r\n\r\n00:01:46.231 --\u003e 00:01:47.941\r\nNo. No family.\r\n\r\n00:01:48.692 --\u003e 00:01:50.611\r\nI may be able to help.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.321 --\u003e 00:01:54.906\r\nROBIN ON RADIO: You can't take this one.\r\n\u003ci\u003eZucco's\u003c/i\u003e mine.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.198 --\u003e 00:01:58.368\r\n- Sorry, Robin.\r\n- But I've waited half my life.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.452 --\u003e 00:02:02.623\r\n- Batman out.\r\n- Oh, no, he's not gonna ace me out.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.873 --\u003e 00:02:05.042\r\n- Master Dick,\r\nyou- - Not this time, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.460 --\u003e 00:02:07.794\r\nMaybe not ever again.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.740 --\u003e 00:02:37.741\r\n(CONSOLE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.824 --\u003e 00:02:40.202\r\nI told you to sit this one\r\nout, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.704 --\u003e 00:02:44.247\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:47.376 --\u003e 00:02:49.378\r\nYou're a real piece of\r\nwork, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.961 --\u003e 00:02:52.589\r\nOkay, I'll find Zucco on my own,\r\n\r\n00:02:53.173 --\u003e 00:02:54.883\r\njust like I did before.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.095 --\u003e 00:02:59.137\r\nHa-ha!\r\n\r\n00:03:07.396 --\u003e 00:03:08.397\r\n\u003ci\u003eEn garde.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:13.318 --\u003e 00:03:16.279\r\nBRUCE: Try using more control.\r\nYou're wasting a lot of energy.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.947 --\u003e 00:03:18.824\r\nDICK: Oh, yeah? (GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:23.787 --\u003e 00:03:25.288\r\n(YELLING WILDLY)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.372 --\u003e 00:03:26.373\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:03:26.957 --\u003e 00:03:27.958\r\nBRUCE: See?\r\n\r\n00:03:29.000 --\u003e 00:03:30.544\r\nIt's finesse, not strength.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.713 --\u003e 00:03:33.714\r\nFinesse, huh?\r\n\r\n00:03:34.673 --\u003e 00:03:37.342\r\nHey.\r\nOkay, now you're gonna get it.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.759 --\u003e 00:03:39.594\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:39.678 --\u003e 00:03:40.679\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:03:41.138 --\u003e 00:03:42.389\r\n- Too slow, huh?\r\n- (GIGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:42.764 --\u003e 00:03:43.890\r\n(ALFRED CLEARING THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:03:43.974 --\u003e 00:03:45.392\r\nForgive the interruption, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.475 --\u003e 00:03:47.686\r\nBut Lieutenant Gordon\r\nis here to see you.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.103 --\u003e 00:03:49.646\r\nHe asked to meet\r\nwith you in private.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.439 --\u003e 00:03:52.566\r\nUh, why don't you hit the\r\nshowers, Dick?\r\n\r\n00:03:52.858 --\u003e 00:03:53.978\r\nIt's almost time for dinner.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.443 --\u003e 00:03:56.153\r\nUh, yeah, sure.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:09.438\r\nGORDON: I dropped\r\nby to let you know\r\n\r\n00:04:09.499 --\u003e 00:04:11.339\r\nyou might not have to\r\nkeep the boy much longer.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.961 --\u003e 00:04:13.962\r\nOh?\r\n\r\n00:04:14.045 --\u003e 00:04:17.299\r\nWe just started putting these up\r\nand already we got a few bites.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.382 --\u003e 00:04:19.426\r\nZucco's been spotted\r\non the Lower East Side.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.509 --\u003e 00:04:21.970\r\nOff the record,\r\nwe hear he's trying to skip town.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.345 --\u003e 00:04:24.473\r\n- BRUCE: How soon?\r\n- Could be tonight.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.890 --\u003e 00:04:26.558\r\nThis Batman's got\r\nZucco real spooked.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.225 --\u003e 00:04:29.144\r\nZucco's friends too.\r\nNobody will touch the guy.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.520 --\u003e 00:04:32.147\r\nAnd if Zucco gets away?\r\n\r\n00:04:32.355 --\u003e 00:04:33.899\r\nGORDON: We could\r\nlose him for good.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.473 --\u003e 00:05:08.225\r\nYou sure you want\r\nto get off here?\r\n\r\n00:05:08.475 --\u003e 00:05:09.476\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.393 --\u003e 00:05:12.395\r\nHey, ever pick up this guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.273 --\u003e 00:05:16.817\r\nCan't say as I have.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.442 --\u003e 00:05:19.569\r\nWho is he,\r\nyour old man or something?\r\n\r\n00:05:20.487 --\u003e 00:05:21.530\r\nDICK: Yeah, something.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.801 --\u003e 00:05:44.135\r\n(INAUDIBLE)\r\n\r\n00:05:59.192 --\u003e 00:06:00.944\r\n(wmn WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.621 --\u003e 00:06:13.164\r\nZUCCO: Who you looking at, boy?\r\n\r\n00:06:13.248 --\u003e 00:06:14.374\r\nNo one.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.710\r\n- (WHIRRING)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:06:24.801 --\u003e 00:06:25.969\r\n(WHIRRING GROWS LOUDER)\r\n\r\n00:06:49.701 --\u003e 00:06:51.982\r\nLENNIE: Who do you think taught\r\nyou how to grift, Chi-Chi?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:53.747\r\nYou don't go skimming\r\nmoney from me.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.289 --\u003e 00:06:56.249\r\n(STAMMERING) But I\r\nain't, Lennie, honest.\r\n\r\n00:06:56.917 --\u003e 00:06:59.210\r\nOh, yeah?\r\nWe'll just see about that.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.294 --\u003e 00:07:01.004\r\nCHI-CHI: No! Wait! (GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.219 --\u003e 00:07:10.221\r\n(STAMMERING) Lennie,\r\nlook, I can explain.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.430 --\u003e 00:07:12.432\r\nLENNIE: We're\r\nbeyond explanations.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.515 --\u003e 00:07:13.683\r\nDICK: Leave her alone.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.188 --\u003e 00:07:19.606\r\nThis kid belong to you?\r\n\r\n00:07:20.023 --\u003e 00:07:22.025\r\nCHI-CHI: Let go of me.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.484 --\u003e 00:07:23.860\r\nI said leave her alone!\r\n\r\n00:07:23.944 --\u003e 00:07:25.278\r\n(LENNIE GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.739 --\u003e 00:07:31.534\r\nYou little creep.\r\nWhen I get my hands on you...\r\n\r\n00:07:31.701 --\u003e 00:07:33.411\r\nGet away, kid. Jump!\r\n\r\n00:07:33.912 --\u003e 00:07:35.080\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.303 --\u003e 00:07:51.304\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:53.139 --\u003e 00:07:54.140\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:58.687 --\u003e 00:08:01.272\r\nDICK: Come on! LENNIE: Hey.\r\nHey, let me out!\r\n\r\n00:08:02.107 --\u003e 00:08:05.735\r\n- (BANGING)\r\n- There's roaches in here. Roaches!\r\n\r\n00:08:08.863 --\u003e 00:08:12.033\r\n(LAUGHING) So when's the last time you\r\nate, kid? Christmas?\r\n\r\n00:08:16.162 --\u003e 00:08:18.540\r\n(WITH MOUTH FULL) Sorry,\r\nbut I'm kind of in a rush.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.623 --\u003e 00:08:21.292\r\nHey, you can't expect to find\r\nthis uncle of yours at this hour.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.584 --\u003e 00:08:24.546\r\nThis is the only place around\r\nthat's still open. Right, Berty?\r\n\r\n00:08:24.629 --\u003e 00:08:26.006\r\nBERTY: Mmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.089 --\u003e 00:08:28.216\r\nHey. I know that deadbeat.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.758 --\u003e 00:08:31.720\r\n- You do?\r\n- Yeah. He's been here.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.053 --\u003e 00:08:34.347\r\nAlways barking\r\norders, never tipping.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.431 --\u003e 00:08:37.350\r\n(SCOFFING) I've seen him come from\r\nthat building across the basin.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.435 --\u003e 00:08:41.021\r\nThat place has been\r\ncondemned for years, right?\r\n\r\n00:08:41.396 --\u003e 00:08:44.024\r\nYeah, and may it fall on his\r\nhead, the louse.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.624 --\u003e 00:09:02.792\r\n(CLATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:09:27.984 --\u003e 00:09:29.486\r\n(METAL CRUMPLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:41.206 --\u003e 00:09:42.207\r\n(EXCLAIMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:44.793 --\u003e 00:09:46.044\r\nLet go of me!\r\n\r\n00:09:46.503 --\u003e 00:09:48.129\r\nThe circus boy.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.379 --\u003e 00:09:50.173\r\nMy little material witness.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.381 --\u003e 00:09:51.758\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:09:51.841 --\u003e 00:09:54.511\r\n_0w! You... DICK: Hey!\r\n\r\n00:09:54.886 --\u003e 00:09:57.055\r\nI was just about to leave\r\ntown because of you.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.806 --\u003e 00:10:00.391\r\nLooks like I'm gonna have\r\na change in travel plans.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.725 --\u003e 00:10:02.352\r\n- (SMACKING)\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.394 --\u003e 00:10:06.648\r\nBATMAN: Only place you're going\r\nis up the river, you scum.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.653 --\u003e 00:10:14.823\r\nYou creep! I hate you!\r\nI hate you!\r\n\r\n00:10:14.906 --\u003e 00:10:17.450\r\nZucco; (GROANING) Get away!\r\n\r\n00:10:21.246 --\u003e 00:10:23.289\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:23.706 --\u003e 00:10:24.833\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.256 --\u003e 00:10:33.007\r\nDICK: (SHOUTING) Help!\r\n\r\n00:10:35.468 --\u003e 00:10:36.469\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:43.685 --\u003e 00:10:45.979\r\nSo much for the\r\nBat and the brat.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.362 --\u003e 00:10:57.115\r\nHelp! Help!\r\n\r\n00:11:00.326 --\u003e 00:11:01.327\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.043 --\u003e 00:11:10.044\r\nHang on.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.097 --\u003e 00:11:23.349\r\nHe's gone. He got away.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.100 --\u003e 00:11:28.313\r\nNo! You had him.\r\nYou let him go! You let him.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.563 --\u003e 00:11:31.232\r\nWhy? Why'd you do it? Why?\r\n\r\n00:11:40.200 --\u003e 00:11:41.409\r\nWhere are we going?\r\n\r\n00:11:42.160 --\u003e 00:11:43.203\r\nHome.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.332 --\u003e 00:11:50.752\r\nDICK: Man, oh, man.\r\nIs this where you live?\r\n\r\n00:11:51.711 --\u003e 00:11:52.795\r\nThis is where I work.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.546 --\u003e 00:11:57.550\r\nYou're the first...\r\nCorrection, second person to see it.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.676 --\u003e 00:12:00.094\r\nWhy'd you bring me here?\r\n\r\n00:12:01.471 --\u003e 00:12:05.767\r\nBecause I wanna know just how\r\nbadly you want Tony Zucco.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.893 --\u003e 00:12:08.102\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:12:08.686 --\u003e 00:12:10.021\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:12:14.275 --\u003e 00:12:15.526\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:16.444 --\u003e 00:12:20.281\r\nI take it Master Dick's\r\nvisit will now be indefinite?\r\n\r\n00:12:26.663 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\nYou're out there\r\nsomewhere, Zucco.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.706 --\u003e 00:12:30.124\r\nBut you can't hide from me.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.625 --\u003e 00:12:33.419\r\n- I've been taught by the best.\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:34.921 --\u003e 00:12:36.398\r\nWOMAN \u003ci\u003eON\u003c/i\u003e RADIO: \u003ci\u003eAnd\r\njust\u003c/i\u003e a \u003ci\u003efew hours ago,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:36.422 --\u003e 00:12:38.675\r\n\u003ci\u003eBatman apprehended a\r\nsuspected extortionist,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:38.800 --\u003e 00:12:41.552\r\n\u003ci\u003eFerris Dolan of 210\r\nTrumbell Avenue.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:41.886 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\n\u003ci\u003eMr. Dolan and other men\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:43.388 --\u003e 00:12:46.224\r\n\u003ci\u003ewere reportedly sabotaging\r\na midtown construction site\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:46.474 --\u003e 00:12:48.017\r\n\u003ci\u003eat the time of his capture.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:53.147 --\u003e 00:12:54.732\r\n(SIZZLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:03.741 --\u003e 00:13:04.993\r\nCome on, Dolan.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.285 --\u003e 00:13:06.911\r\nYou gotta have his\r\naddress somewhere.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.884 --\u003e 00:13:23.177\r\n(LINE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.513 --\u003e 00:13:27.307\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:35.189 --\u003e 00:13:36.316\r\nZUCCO: Yeah, who is it?\r\n\r\n00:13:37.984 --\u003e 00:13:39.444\r\n\u003ci\u003eHello? Hello?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:40.611 --\u003e 00:13:42.655\r\n\u003ci\u003eWho's there? Ugh.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:42.822 --\u003e 00:13:44.907\r\nROBIN: Gotcha.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.492 --\u003e 00:13:47.618\r\nI don't like it.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.828 --\u003e 00:13:50.188\r\nYou sure Batman\r\ndidn't follow you?\r\n\r\n00:13:50.246 --\u003e 00:13:52.123\r\nNo. And Dolan's no squealer.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.206 --\u003e 00:13:53.708\r\nYou got nothing to worry about.\r\n\r\n00:13:54.667 --\u003e 00:13:55.668\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:56.002 --\u003e 00:13:58.338\r\nDon't tell me what I've\r\ngot to worry about.\r\n\r\n00:13:58.921 --\u003e 00:14:00.465\r\nI'm not back in\r\ntown five minutes,\r\n\r\n00:14:00.673 --\u003e 00:14:02.925\r\nfive minutes,\r\nand he's on my tail.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.009 --\u003e 00:14:04.969\r\nYou don't know the Bat.\r\nHe don't let up.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.053 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHe's a dark angel of death,\r\nman, and he wants me.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.893 --\u003e 00:14:13.227\r\nUh, why you, boss?\r\n\r\n00:14:13.728 --\u003e 00:14:15.271\r\nHow should I know?\r\n\r\n00:14:16.356 --\u003e 00:14:18.232\r\n- (CEILING CREAKING)\r\n- What's that?\r\n\r\n00:14:19.067 --\u003e 00:14:20.068\r\nWhat's what?\r\n\r\n00:14:20.443 --\u003e 00:14:21.944\r\nShh. Listen.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.320 --\u003e 00:14:24.989\r\n(CREAKING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:14:25.239 --\u003e 00:14:27.075\r\nIt sounds like rats.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.785 --\u003e 00:14:30.411\r\nYeah, rats.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.664 --\u003e 00:14:36.459\r\n(GOONS YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:50.765 --\u003e 00:14:52.892\r\nBoss, calm down, okay?\r\n\r\n00:14:54.852 --\u003e 00:14:56.354\r\nYou're starting to worry us.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.065 --\u003e 00:15:00.650\r\n(wooo CRACKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:00.733 --\u003e 00:15:02.360\r\n(ALL YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:04.654 --\u003e 00:15:05.822\r\nMama.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.823 --\u003e 00:15:07.824\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.990 --\u003e 00:15:09.617\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:09.700 --\u003e 00:15:11.661\r\nAw, what's the matter, Bats?\r\n\r\n00:15:11.953 --\u003e 00:15:13.079\r\nYou twist your knee?\r\n\r\n00:15:13.329 --\u003e 00:15:16.332\r\nLooks like you could use a\r\nlittle protection about now.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.916 --\u003e 00:15:21.295\r\nAnd protection is my racket.\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.175 --\u003e 00:15:28.010\r\nNine years, creep.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.511 --\u003e 00:15:30.847\r\nNine years of looking\r\nover my shoulder.\r\n\r\n00:15:31.180 --\u003e 00:15:32.181\r\nNo more.\r\n\r\n00:15:32.265 --\u003e 00:15:34.642\r\nI'm sending you\r\nstraight to a bat box.\r\n\r\n00:15:35.226 --\u003e 00:15:36.769\r\n(GUN CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:37.311 --\u003e 00:15:39.021\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:15:40.398 --\u003e 00:15:41.858\r\n(GAS HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:15:42.483 --\u003e 00:15:44.193\r\n(ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:49.073 --\u003e 00:15:50.616\r\n(BATMAN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:53.661 --\u003e 00:15:55.037\r\n(COUGHING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.913 --\u003e 00:15:58.374\r\nWhat are you deadbeats\r\nstanding around here for?\r\n\r\n00:15:58.958 --\u003e 00:16:00.209\r\nGet out there!\r\n\r\n00:16:00.918 --\u003e 00:16:01.961\r\nNOW!\r\n\r\n00:16:12.305 --\u003e 00:16:14.515\r\nGOON: Where'd he go?\r\nZUCCO: Not far.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.599 --\u003e 00:16:16.100\r\nYou saw how he was limping.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.643 --\u003e 00:16:19.187\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.562 --\u003e 00:16:21.481\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:25.485 --\u003e 00:16:26.486\r\nZUCCO: Spread out.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.459 --\u003e 00:16:43.085\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- (SMACKING)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.551 --\u003e 00:16:51.719\r\n(SHIP'S HORN BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:17:00.311 --\u003e 00:17:01.604\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:17.578 --\u003e 00:17:18.746\r\n(EXCLAIMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e FEAR)\r\n\r\n00:17:37.682 --\u003e 00:17:39.517\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:55.324 --\u003e 00:17:57.451\r\n(GROANING SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:05.376 --\u003e 00:18:07.795\r\n(GRUNTING) Mick!\r\nMick, he's over here!\r\n\r\n00:18:12.758 --\u003e 00:18:14.260\r\nGet him. Get him!\r\n\r\n00:18:22.685 --\u003e 00:18:25.938\r\n(CARNIVAL MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:18:30.026 --\u003e 00:18:32.111\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.528 --\u003e 00:18:33.821\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:44.874 --\u003e 00:18:47.209\r\nRound and round we\r\ngo, hey, Bats?\r\n\r\n00:18:52.131 --\u003e 00:18:53.758\r\nRide's over!\r\n\r\n00:18:53.841 --\u003e 00:18:57.303\r\nNo, boss! Don't! Wait!\r\nYou can't! You'll hit us!\r\n\r\n00:18:58.429 --\u003e 00:18:59.764\r\nZUCCO: Sorry, boys.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.847 --\u003e 00:19:03.434\r\nYou pays your money,\r\nand you takes your chances.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.815 --\u003e 00:19:12.234\r\n(zucco YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:16.072 --\u003e 00:19:18.532\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.786 --\u003e 00:19:23.371\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.454 --\u003e 00:19:25.539\r\nI don't believe this.\r\n\r\n00:19:25.623 --\u003e 00:19:27.166\r\nYou're through, Zucco.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.084 --\u003e 00:19:29.251\r\nForever.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.169 --\u003e 00:19:32.088\r\nIs that so, birdy boy?\r\n\r\n00:19:32.254 --\u003e 00:19:33.631\r\n(GRUNTING) Huh?\r\n\r\n00:19:36.342 --\u003e 00:19:38.344\r\nI've waited a long time.\r\n\r\n00:19:40.012 --\u003e 00:19:41.639\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:45.434 --\u003e 00:19:46.936\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:49.730 --\u003e 00:19:51.816\r\n(WHIMPERING) Keep away from me.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.817 --\u003e 00:19:54.694\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:58.155 --\u003e 00:19:59.657\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.157 --\u003e 00:20:04.161\r\nNo. Don't. Please.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.912 --\u003e 00:20:05.913\r\nBATMAN: Robin!\r\n\r\n00:20:07.832 --\u003e 00:20:08.874\r\nEnough.\r\n\r\n00:20:09.166 --\u003e 00:20:11.419\r\nYou can't let your emotions\r\nget the best of you.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.295 --\u003e 00:20:15.047\r\nStuff your advice, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.131 --\u003e 00:20:16.799\r\nYou and your stone-cold heart.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.882 --\u003e 00:20:19.343\r\nYou don't know how I feel.\r\nHow could you?\r\n\r\n00:20:20.761 --\u003e 00:20:22.513\r\n(SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:20:22.596 --\u003e 00:20:23.889\r\nBatman, I...\r\n\r\n00:20:24.640 --\u003e 00:20:25.766\r\nI didn't mean to...\r\n\r\n00:20:25.850 --\u003e 00:20:26.892\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.245 --\u003e 00:20:47.705\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:21:03.929 --\u003e 00:21:06.766\r\nROBIN: You were right, you\r\nknow, not bringing me along.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.266 --\u003e 00:21:08.851\r\nYou knew I'd take\r\nit too personally.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.894 --\u003e 00:21:11.020\r\nIt wasn't that, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.812 --\u003e 00:21:13.230\r\nIt wasn't that at all.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.400 --\u003e 00:21:18.027\r\nZucco's taken so much,\r\n\r\n00:21:18.736 --\u003e 00:21:20.154\r\ncaused you so much pain.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.946 --\u003e 00:21:22.782\r\nI couldn't stand the\r\nthought that he might...\r\n\r\n00:21:23.908 --\u003e 00:21:25.659\r\nTake you too.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.832 --\u003e 00:21:32.958\r\nCome on, partner.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.709 --\u003e 00:21:34.919\r\nIt's been a long night.\r\n\r\n00:21:47.765 --\u003e 00:21:49.767\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:13.958 --\u003e 00:22:14.959\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E54 - Blind as a Batman (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.189 --\u003e 00:00:24.191\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:17.578 --\u003e 00:01:21.623\r\n\u003ci\u003eThree features make WayneTech's\r\nnew Raven X-111 stealth helicopter\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:21.707 --\u003e 00:01:23.625\r\n\u003ci\u003eunique among military aircraft.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:24.126 --\u003e 00:01:27.462\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe first is her\r\nsilent-running capability.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:27.921 --\u003e 00:01:29.798\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:01:35.012 --\u003e 00:01:36.430\r\n(LOW WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.681 --\u003e 00:01:41.351\r\n\u003ci\u003eMaking the Raven ideal for\r\nreconnaissance and covert operations.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:47.899 --\u003e 00:01:51.111\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnother is her state-of-the-art\r\ncloaking device.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:51.194 --\u003e 00:01:55.407\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis renders her invisible to all normal\r\nforms of radar and sonar detection.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:55.991 --\u003e 00:01:57.409\r\n(MEN CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:05.000 --\u003e 00:02:06.877\r\nLast, but certainly not least,\r\n\r\n00:02:06.960 --\u003e 00:02:10.297\r\n\u003ci\u003ethere is her extraordinary\r\nZVF sensor system.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:10.797 --\u003e 00:02:15.093\r\n\u003ci\u003eZVF, as I'm sure you've heard,\r\nstands for zero visibility flight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:15.636 --\u003e 00:02:20.390\r\n\u003ci\u003eWith this new technology, feedback\r\nfrom the aircraft's radar and sonar\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:20.474 --\u003e 00:02:23.810\r\n\u003ci\u003eis translated,\r\nnot into blips on a tracking grid,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:23.894 --\u003e 00:02:26.813\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut rather into computer\r\ngenerated images\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:26.897 --\u003e 00:02:28.732\r\n\u003ci\u003eon a video display terminal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:29.274 --\u003e 00:02:33.570\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut should you think the Raven X-111\r\nhas only defensive capabilities,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:33.654 --\u003e 00:02:34.946\r\n\u003ci\u003ethink again.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:42.621 --\u003e 00:02:44.665\r\nLooks like it's going even\r\nbetter than we'd hoped.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.748 --\u003e 00:02:46.375\r\nWouldn't you say, Mr. Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:02:46.458 --\u003e 00:02:47.709\r\nI guess, Doctor,\r\n\r\n00:02:47.793 --\u003e 00:02:50.921\r\nthough I still have serious misgivings\r\nabout building weapon systems.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.171 --\u003e 00:02:52.339\r\n(BOTH GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:02:54.883 --\u003e 00:02:56.051\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:02:59.971 --\u003e 00:03:01.431\r\nWhat are they trying to do?\r\n\r\n00:03:02.933 --\u003e 00:03:04.643\r\n(HELICOPTER GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:03:12.693 --\u003e 00:03:14.111\r\nHey, what's that?\r\n\r\n00:03:15.237 --\u003e 00:03:18.281\r\n- Looks like the helicopter crew.\r\n- But if you guys are here,\r\n\r\n00:03:18.824 --\u003e 00:03:20.325\r\nthen who's flying the chopper?\r\n\r\n00:03:20.701 --\u003e 00:03:24.246\r\n(LAUGHING) Look at them.\r\nTaking off like scared pigeons.\r\n\r\n00:03:25.414 --\u003e 00:03:28.709\r\nPENGUIN: You find pigeons\r\nfunny, my friend?\r\n\r\n00:03:28.792 --\u003e 00:03:30.877\r\nNo, boss. Not me.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.961 --\u003e 00:03:33.630\r\nGood. You'll do well\r\nto remember that.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.716 --\u003e 00:03:37.634\r\nAttention. Attention.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.009 --\u003e 00:03:40.220\r\nThis is the Penguin speaking.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.263 --\u003e 00:03:44.182\r\nI have taken control\r\nof your precious Raven\r\n\r\n00:03:44.266 --\u003e 00:03:47.811\r\nand intend to be paid\r\nhandsomely for its return.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.894 --\u003e 00:03:49.771\r\nI will contact\r\nthe mayor's office\r\n\r\n00:03:49.855 --\u003e 00:03:52.691\r\nwith the instructions for\r\ndelivery of the ransom.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.528 --\u003e 00:03:57.529\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:00.282 --\u003e 00:04:01.408\r\n(BRUCE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:04:02.701 --\u003e 00:04:04.786\r\nPENGUIN: As of this moment,\r\n\r\n00:04:04.870 --\u003e 00:04:09.332\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe most dangerous bird\r\nin the sky is the Penguin.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:09.416 --\u003e 00:04:10.417\r\n(PENGUIN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:11.543 --\u003e 00:04:12.961\r\nMaster Bruce!\r\n\r\n00:04:14.045 --\u003e 00:04:16.256\r\nHome, Alfred. Now.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.339 --\u003e 00:04:18.383\r\nBut, sir,\r\nyou need medical attention.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.467 --\u003e 00:04:22.179\r\nNo. I don't want the WayneTech\r\ndoctors examining me.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.223 --\u003e 00:04:26.349\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.433 --\u003e 00:04:27.601\r\nCall Leslie.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.684 --\u003e 00:04:29.519\r\nHave her meet us at the house.\r\n\r\n00:04:29.603 --\u003e 00:04:32.439\r\nBegging your pardon, sir,\r\nbut why so secretive?\r\n\r\n00:04:32.522 --\u003e 00:04:36.151\r\nBecause I don't want\r\nanyone to find out\r\n\r\n00:04:37.152 --\u003e 00:04:39.279\r\nthat I can't see.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.784 --\u003e 00:04:47.913\r\nIt's too soon to know for sure, Bruce,\r\nbut it looks like it's only temporary.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.996 --\u003e 00:04:50.373\r\nIt might last two,\r\nmaybe three days at the most.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.832 --\u003e 00:04:54.586\r\nAssuming, of course, you actually\r\nfollow my instructions for a change.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.170 --\u003e 00:04:56.379\r\nWhat happened?\r\n\r\n00:04:56.463 --\u003e 00:04:59.549\r\nIt looks like the explosion\r\nflash burned both retinas.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.883 --\u003e 00:05:01.885\r\nIt'll heal better if\r\nyou keep your eyes\r\n\r\n00:05:01.968 --\u003e 00:05:04.387\r\ncompletely covered\r\nfor at least 36 hours.\r\n\r\n00:05:04.471 --\u003e 00:05:07.265\r\nOtherwise, you could damage\r\nyour vision permanently.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.849 --\u003e 00:05:10.685\r\nSo keep him home, Alfred,\r\neven if you have to hog-tie him.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.769 --\u003e 00:05:14.689\r\nHe needs to rest,\r\nwhich means the Batman is off duty, too.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.317\r\nNo way, Leslie.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.400 --\u003e 00:05:19.653\r\nNot as long as the\r\nPenguin has that chopper.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.237 --\u003e 00:05:24.908\r\nIf there is some question, Master Bruce,\r\nI urge you to resolve it straightaway.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.159 --\u003e 00:05:28.745\r\nYou've a call on\r\nyour private line.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.454 --\u003e 00:05:32.040\r\n- Then let's go.\r\n- In your condition, sir?\r\n\r\n00:05:32.123 --\u003e 00:05:35.085\r\nIf you think a little inconvenience\r\nlike this is gonna stop me...\r\n\r\n00:05:35.377 --\u003e 00:05:36.586\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.340 --\u003e 00:05:41.424\r\nIndeed.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.105 --\u003e 00:05:56.314\r\nMAYOR HILL: He didn't respond?\r\n\r\n00:05:57.190 --\u003e 00:06:00.235\r\nNo, Mr. Mayor.\r\nBut I'm sure there's a reason.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.318 --\u003e 00:06:04.573\r\nWho cares? What's Mr. Trick-or-Treat\r\ngonna do that we can't?\r\n\r\n00:06:04.656 --\u003e 00:06:08.785\r\nI got 12 details crawling over every\r\nairfield and heliport in four counties.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.869 --\u003e 00:06:10.745\r\n\u003ci\u003eQuite a machine, this Raven.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:10.829 --\u003e 00:06:15.041\r\n\u003ci\u003eAmazing what its communications\r\nequipment can do, don't you agree?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:15.125 --\u003e 00:06:17.168\r\nYou received my instructions?\r\n\r\n00:06:17.252 --\u003e 00:06:19.379\r\nMAYOR HILL: \u003ci\u003eThey arrived\r\nby messenger this morning.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:19.462 --\u003e 00:06:22.716\r\nYou know,\r\n100 million is a lot of money.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.799 --\u003e 00:06:25.051\r\nIt'll take time to\r\nraise that much.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.135 --\u003e 00:06:26.970\r\nYou're stalling, Hill.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.053 --\u003e 00:06:30.515\r\nObviously,\r\nyou're not taking me seriously.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.974 --\u003e 00:06:33.810\r\n\u003ci\u003eI warned you not to\r\nmake that mistake.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:33.894 --\u003e 00:06:37.397\r\n\u003ci\u003eApparently,\r\nI'll have to show you why.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:41.234 --\u003e 00:06:44.779\r\n(LAUGHING) You should've seen\r\nhis face when I told him.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.863 --\u003e 00:06:45.906\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.989 --\u003e 00:06:47.616\r\nWhat the heck is that?\r\n\r\n00:06:48.074 --\u003e 00:06:49.451\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.744 --\u003e 00:06:52.203\r\nGIRL: It's not making a sound.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.796 --\u003e 00:07:03.465\r\nJam it, get us out of here!\r\n\r\n00:07:05.383 --\u003e 00:07:07.093\r\n(EVIL LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.305 --\u003e 00:07:13.224\r\n- You sure this is a good idea, boss?\r\n- Do as you're told.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.683 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nMAN: Ow!\r\n\r\n00:07:17.187 --\u003e 00:07:18.521\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:25.737 --\u003e 00:07:28.090\r\nMALE REPORTER: \u003ci\u003eAs a warning of\r\nwhat he'll do tomorrow night.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:28.114 --\u003e 00:07:32.202\r\n\u003ci\u003eAmazingly, all those on the collapsing\r\nbridge escaped with only minor injuries.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:38.083 --\u003e 00:07:41.169\r\nAlfred, I've got to find\r\nsome way to stop him.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.795 --\u003e 00:07:43.964\r\nSight or no sight.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.971 --\u003e 00:07:53.765\r\nI still think this\r\nis a terrible idea.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.848 --\u003e 00:07:55.225\r\nI mean, using electrodes\r\n\r\n00:07:55.308 --\u003e 00:07:58.979\r\nto connect this gizmo directly\r\nto your brain's optic center?\r\n\r\n00:07:59.062 --\u003e 00:08:00.689\r\nBATMAN: Objection noted.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.772 --\u003e 00:08:02.565\r\nMay I have the\r\nheadpiece, please?\r\n\r\n00:08:09.197 --\u003e 00:08:12.575\r\nThose ZVF components I gave you,\r\nyou wired them into this thing?\r\n\r\n00:08:12.659 --\u003e 00:08:14.869\r\nI know how to\r\nfollow instructions.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.502 --\u003e 00:08:26.548\r\nJust be careful with that power pack.\r\nYou have to keep recharging it.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.981 --\u003e 00:08:44.524\r\nWill it work, sir?\r\n\r\n00:08:47.694 --\u003e 00:08:49.529\r\nBRUCE: Only one way to find out.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.547 --\u003e 00:09:08.548\r\n(GRUNTS LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:09:11.551 --\u003e 00:09:13.053\r\nWell done, sir.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.139 --\u003e 00:09:17.932\r\nI was aiming for its head.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.016 --\u003e 00:09:19.142\r\nIt isn't perfect.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.977 --\u003e 00:09:22.687\r\nBut it will have to do.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.231 --\u003e 00:09:28.902\r\nI can only pray that the same\r\ntechnology that created this crisis\r\n\r\n00:09:29.027 --\u003e 00:09:31.154\r\ncan help me put an end to it.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.084 --\u003e 00:09:45.293\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:09:54.219 --\u003e 00:09:55.220\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:58.181 --\u003e 00:09:59.682\r\nMAYOR HILL: Just\r\nwhat I was afraid of.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.391 --\u003e 00:10:02.811\r\nAccording to the controller's\r\noffice, we can't come close\r\n\r\n00:10:02.977 --\u003e 00:10:04.854\r\nto putting that ransom together.\r\n\r\n00:10:05.355 --\u003e 00:10:08.441\r\nNot without shutting down\r\nbasic municipal services.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.525 --\u003e 00:10:10.568\r\nSo, what other options we got?\r\n\r\n00:10:11.361 --\u003e 00:10:12.695\r\nBATMAN: None, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.779 --\u003e 00:10:16.616\r\nWhich is why you're going to do\r\nexactly what the Penguin wants you to.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.666 --\u003e 00:10:28.211\r\nMALE REPORTER: \u003ci\u003eWe interrupt our regular\r\nprogramming for this special report.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:28.294 --\u003e 00:10:32.715\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is Mayor Hamilton Hill with a\r\npersonal message for the Penguin,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:32.799 --\u003e 00:10:34.843\r\n\u003ci\u003ewherever you may be tonight.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:35.301 --\u003e 00:10:36.803\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou've won.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:36.886 --\u003e 00:10:41.057\r\n\u003ci\u003eJust bring the Raven X-111\r\nto the drop site at midnight\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:41.141 --\u003e 00:10:44.811\r\n\u003ci\u003eand I promise you'll get\r\neverything that's coming to you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:45.520 --\u003e 00:10:48.857\r\nPENGUIN: You see?\r\nI told you they'd knuckle under.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.358 --\u003e 00:10:53.945\r\n- But, boss, it sounds too easy.\r\n- Relax.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.404 --\u003e 00:10:55.572\r\nWith the Raven's instruments,\r\n\r\n00:10:55.655 --\u003e 00:10:58.950\r\nwe'll be able to spot a trap a mile\r\naway, literally.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.784 --\u003e 00:11:02.704\r\nAnd if in fact this\r\nis a double-cross,\r\n\r\n00:11:02.787 --\u003e 00:11:06.124\r\n- may heaven help them all.\r\n- (YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:19.220 --\u003e 00:11:21.097\r\nScanners show the area is\r\nsecure, boss.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.973 --\u003e 00:11:25.185\r\nIn that case,\r\ngentlemen, it's payday.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.287 --\u003e 00:11:45.496\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:11:45.705 --\u003e 00:11:47.665\r\nWhat? What?\r\n\r\n00:11:49.709 --\u003e 00:11:50.710\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:55.715 --\u003e 00:11:56.799\r\nGotcha.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.432 --\u003e 00:12:07.560\r\nBut... But how could he\r\nsneak up on us like that?\r\n\r\n00:12:07.644 --\u003e 00:12:10.188\r\nThat plane of his must have\r\na cloaking device, too.\r\n\r\n00:12:22.450 --\u003e 00:12:24.953\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:12:35.296 --\u003e 00:12:37.090\r\nThis means war!\r\n\r\n00:12:59.988 --\u003e 00:13:01.197\r\nMAN: We're going down!\r\n\r\n00:13:06.536 --\u003e 00:13:08.496\r\n_Mayday! _Mayday!\r\n\r\n00:13:40.445 --\u003e 00:13:43.364\r\nThe laser cannons.\r\nUse the lasers!\r\n\r\n00:14:01.841 --\u003e 00:14:02.842\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:03.760 --\u003e 00:14:06.220\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Red alert.\r\nRed alert. Traumatic impact.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:06.304 --\u003e 00:14:07.889\r\n\u003ci\u003eHeat damage to fuselage.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:07.972 --\u003e 00:14:10.892\r\n\u003ci\u003eBreach to hull.\r\nExtensive structural damage.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:10.975 --\u003e 00:14:12.560\r\nTell me something I don't know.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.643 --\u003e 00:14:13.895\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:13.978 --\u003e 00:14:15.229\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:14:19.317 --\u003e 00:14:22.278\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Sixty-five seconds\r\nto total system failure.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:36.793 --\u003e 00:14:39.087\r\nLook. That Bat's going down.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.811 --\u003e 00:14:57.438\r\n\u003ci\u003eCOMPUTER: Warning. Warning.\r\nElectrical system failure.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:57.605 --\u003e 00:14:59.023\r\n\u003ci\u003eSwitching to auxiliary power.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:10.076 --\u003e 00:15:11.077\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:15:11.661 --\u003e 00:15:13.496\r\nPENGUIN: Happy landing, rodent!\r\n\r\n00:15:41.315 --\u003e 00:15:42.942\r\nLook. There!\r\n\r\n00:16:01.669 --\u003e 00:16:03.129\r\nTerrific.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.187 --\u003e 00:16:21.981\r\nNo, my pointy-eared old friend.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.064 --\u003e 00:16:24.734\r\nYou don't escape me that easily.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.200 --\u003e 00:16:33.493\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.784 --\u003e 00:16:37.038\r\nLook at the way he's moving.\r\nThere's something wrong with him.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.121 --\u003e 00:16:39.624\r\nPENGUIN: Why, yes.\r\nI think he's injured.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.592 --\u003e 00:16:52.678\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:06.901 --\u003e 00:17:08.152\r\n(CHUCKLES MENACINGLY)\r\n\r\n00:17:09.403 --\u003e 00:17:11.197\r\n(SHOTS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:17:13.824 --\u003e 00:17:14.825\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:24.794 --\u003e 00:17:25.795\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:17:40.434 --\u003e 00:17:41.435\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:42.186 --\u003e 00:17:43.646\r\nI'll handle him.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.801 --\u003e 00:18:14.802\r\n(BATMAN YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:18:30.526 --\u003e 00:18:31.986\r\nWhat's the matter, Bat-\r\n\r\n00:18:32.069 --\u003e 00:18:33.070\r\n(GRUNTS) Ahhh!\r\n\r\n00:18:38.868 --\u003e 00:18:41.203\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.819 --\u003e 00:19:14.820\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:19:22.662 --\u003e 00:19:23.663\r\n(CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:19:26.832 --\u003e 00:19:30.795\r\nYour aim appears to be a\r\nlittle off today, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.130 --\u003e 00:19:35.716\r\nI don't think you can hit\r\nthe broad side of a barn,\r\n\r\n00:19:35.800 --\u003e 00:19:38.386\r\nlet alone the broad\r\nside of this bird.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.136 --\u003e 00:19:40.930\r\nYou're blind as a bat.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.013 --\u003e 00:19:42.932\r\nSightless and helpless.\r\n\r\n00:19:44.392 --\u003e 00:19:45.559\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.519 --\u003e 00:19:47.728\r\nYou got one right.\r\n\r\n00:19:50.940 --\u003e 00:19:53.359\r\n(PENGUIN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:59.657 --\u003e 00:20:01.701\r\n(EVIL LAUGHTER CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:20:08.916 --\u003e 00:20:11.752\r\nPENGUIN: And where do\r\nyou think you're going?\r\n\r\n00:20:15.840 --\u003e 00:20:18.008\r\nYou've hit a dead end, rodent.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.855\r\nYou're only prolonging\r\nthe inevitable.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.459 --\u003e 00:20:53.169\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.420 --\u003e 00:20:56.255\r\n(COUGHING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:21:05.264 --\u003e 00:21:07.391\r\n(PENGUIN GRUNTING IN PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.476 --\u003e 00:21:09.977\r\nNot possible.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.060 --\u003e 00:21:13.314\r\nYou're supposed to be helpless.\r\nHelpless!\r\n\r\n00:21:16.525 --\u003e 00:21:19.403\r\nI'd feel a lot better about\r\nthis if you'd listened to me.\r\n\r\n00:21:27.328 --\u003e 00:21:28.662\r\nALFRED: Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:21:29.663 --\u003e 00:21:30.748\r\nWell?\r\n\r\n00:21:32.416 --\u003e 00:21:35.503\r\nMy word, sir.\r\nSurely, you're not-\r\n\r\n00:21:35.586 --\u003e 00:21:38.172\r\nNo, Alfred. I can see just fine.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.255 --\u003e 00:21:41.383\r\nAnd right now,\r\nI've never seen anything prettier.\r\n\r\n00:21:49.266 --\u003e 00:21:51.268\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E55 - Day of The Samurai (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:17.643 --\u003e 00:00:19.353\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.797 --\u003e 00:01:30.674\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.814 --\u003e 00:01:46.815\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.134 --\u003e 00:02:15.344\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:03:03.058 --\u003e 00:03:04.059\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:16.655 --\u003e 00:03:17.864\r\nMaster Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.198 --\u003e 00:03:19.199\r\nWhat is it, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:03:19.825 --\u003e 00:03:22.160\r\nYoru Sensei. Line three.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.079 --\u003e 00:03:25.288\r\nKonnichiwa, sensei.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.269 --\u003e 00:03:48.854\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:04:10.876 --\u003e 00:04:13.086\r\nALFRED: I should enjoy\r\nour return to Nippon more\r\n\r\n00:04:13.253 --\u003e 00:04:14.963\r\nwithout this\r\nunfortunate business.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.589 --\u003e 00:04:18.467\r\nSo would I, Alfred,\r\nbut gin' cannot be denied.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.134 --\u003e 00:04:23.013\r\nAh, yes, giri.\r\nHonor, duty, obligation.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.181 --\u003e 00:04:27.017\r\nPILOT: \u003ci\u003eWe'll reach the city of\r\nKuruhara in an hour, Mr. Wayne.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:30.854 --\u003e 00:04:32.647\r\n(STUDENTS GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:38.111 --\u003e 00:04:40.280\r\nBRUCE: Of course,\r\nI will help in any way I can, sensei.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.614 --\u003e 00:04:42.134\r\nBut what made you\r\nthink of calling me?\r\n\r\n00:04:42.407 --\u003e 00:04:47.162\r\nYou cannot hide a Warrior's spirit\r\nbehind your playboy image, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.662 --\u003e 00:04:50.290\r\nKyodai Ken returned\r\nfrom America in defeat.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.540 --\u003e 00:04:51.792\r\nHe was beaten by Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.250 --\u003e 00:04:53.376\r\nSo it is said.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.877 --\u003e 00:04:58.256\r\nPerhaps I thought you might somehow\r\nenlist the aid of this Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.673 --\u003e 00:05:01.384\r\n- You know him, do you not?\r\n- We've met.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.025 --\u003e 00:05:19.027\r\n(BREATHING SLOWLY)\r\n\r\n00:05:22.697 --\u003e 00:05:23.740\r\n(KNOCK AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:05:23.824 --\u003e 00:05:24.825\r\nCome.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.325 --\u003e 00:05:27.911\r\nA spot of tea before\r\nretiring, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:05:28.119 --\u003e 00:05:29.955\r\nI have some\r\nexcellent green brew.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:31.540\r\nNo, thanks, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.833 --\u003e 00:05:34.835\r\nIf I might be so\r\nbold, Master Bruce,\r\n\r\n00:05:35.126 --\u003e 00:05:37.963\r\nhow did your meeting\r\nwith Yoru Sensei go?\r\n\r\n00:05:39.548 --\u003e 00:05:41.258\r\nIt was not good news.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.341 --\u003e 00:05:42.342\r\n(CRACKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:42.843 --\u003e 00:05:44.511\r\nI believe I will have that\r\ntea, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.934 --\u003e 00:05:55.105\r\nOnce upon a time, Alfred,\r\n500 years ago to be exact,\r\n\r\n00:05:56.189 --\u003e 00:05:59.776\r\n\u003ci\u003ethere was a fighting master who\r\nlearned how to manipulate the ki lines,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:00.193 --\u003e 00:06:01.987\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe currents of life force.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.571 --\u003e 00:06:07.284\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe called the art kiba-no-hoko,\r\n\"The Way of the Fang.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:10.036 --\u003e 00:06:12.497\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt was such an efficient\r\nand terrible fighting art\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:12.956 --\u003e 00:06:15.542\r\n\u003ci\u003ethat the master decided it\r\nwas too dangerous to teach.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:19.838 --\u003e 00:06:23.216\r\n\u003ci\u003eA mere touch could render a man\r\nunconscious, or cripple him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:23.800 --\u003e 00:06:26.636\r\n\u003ci\u003eThere was even a\r\ntouch that was fatal.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:33.143 --\u003e 00:06:37.272\r\n\u003ci\u003eSo the master hid the only copy of the\r\ninstruction scroll for kiba-no-hoko\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:37.856 --\u003e 00:06:41.192\r\n\u003ci\u003ein one of the thousand caves\r\non the slopes of Mount Kajiiki.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:42.027 --\u003e 00:06:43.987\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe told no one but\r\nhis eldest son.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:47.824 --\u003e 00:06:52.329\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe location has been kept a\r\nfamily secret for 500 years.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:53.997 --\u003e 00:06:55.665\r\nALFRED: And Yoru Sensei?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.999 --\u003e 00:06:58.001\r\nBRUCE: ls the\r\ngreat-great-great-grandson\r\n\r\n00:06:58.209 --\u003e 00:07:00.253\r\nof the man who created\r\nthat forbidden art.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.879 --\u003e 00:07:04.883\r\nAnd the only man who knows\r\nthe location of the scroll.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.425 --\u003e 00:07:07.636\r\nYoru Sensei has no sons.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.428 --\u003e 00:07:12.349\r\nWhen he leaves this world,\r\nthe secret leaves with him.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.391 --\u003e 00:07:14.809\r\nAnd the kidnapped girl?\r\n\r\n00:07:15.268 --\u003e 00:07:16.478\r\nYoru's star student.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.853 --\u003e 00:07:19.439\r\nKyodai wants to trade her for\r\nthe knowledge of the fang.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.981 --\u003e 00:07:21.608\r\nALFRED: To use against\r\nyou, I expect.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.359 --\u003e 00:07:26.029\r\nWell, perhaps our cowled friend\r\ncan persuade him otherwise.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.446 --\u003e 00:07:27.822\r\nIt's not that easy, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.865 --\u003e 00:07:31.409\r\nHe's after Batman as well.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.910 --\u003e 00:07:32.911\r\nBut why?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.787 --\u003e 00:07:36.039\r\nHe fought Bruce\r\nWayne and Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.623 --\u003e 00:07:38.291\r\nFighting styles are\r\nlike fingerprints.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.209 --\u003e 00:07:43.171\r\nKyodai knows that\r\nwe are the same man.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.309 --\u003e 00:07:57.602\r\nThat was Kyodai Ken.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.894 --\u003e 00:07:59.914\r\nBRUCE: Did he give you\r\ninstructions for the exchange?\r\n\r\n00:07:59.938 --\u003e 00:08:03.233\r\nYORU: Yes.\r\nIn the Uramachi district after dark.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.984 --\u003e 00:08:06.945\r\nA bad part of town,\r\na place of thieves and the Yakuza.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.487 --\u003e 00:08:09.364\r\nA ninja would feel safe there.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.656 --\u003e 00:08:12.617\r\nIf you give him a phony map,\r\nhe wouldn't know the difference.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.326 --\u003e 00:08:14.911\r\nTrue, but I would know.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.662 --\u003e 00:08:18.331\r\nYou are familiar with the\r\ncode of Bushido, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.873 --\u003e 00:08:22.002\r\nNinja may lie and cheat.\r\nSamurai cannot.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.502 --\u003e 00:08:23.503\r\nHai, sensei.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.506 --\u003e 00:08:27.906\r\nI'll see that the\r\nmap is delivered.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.613 --\u003e 00:08:52.782\r\nBATMAN: Let her go, ninja.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.491 --\u003e 00:08:54.534\r\nYOU!\r\n\r\n00:08:55.160 --\u003e 00:08:56.411\r\nRelease Kairi.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.871 --\u003e 00:08:58.955\r\nKYODAI: Throw me the map.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.497 --\u003e 00:09:01.124\r\nFirst she goes free.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.932 --\u003e 00:09:19.017\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:20.351 --\u003e 00:09:21.561\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:42.457 --\u003e 00:09:43.917\r\n(BOTH GROAN)\r\n\r\n00:09:47.587 --\u003e 00:09:49.297\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:25.291 --\u003e 00:10:26.376\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.719 --\u003e 00:11:18.928\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.321 --\u003e 00:11:37.947\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:20.406 --\u003e 00:12:22.533\r\nBRUCE: I can only read\r\nbits and pieces, sensei.\r\n\r\n00:12:22.951 --\u003e 00:12:24.744\r\nNot enough to understand\r\nthe techniques.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.161 --\u003e 00:12:28.665\r\nIt seems that age has destroyed\r\nthe secrets of kiba-no-hoko.\r\n\r\n00:12:29.666 --\u003e 00:12:31.459\r\nI wish it were so, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.918 --\u003e 00:12:33.586\r\nThere is a large part missing.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.045 --\u003e 00:12:37.966\r\nThe location of, and directions\r\non performing the o-nemuri touch.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.008 --\u003e 00:12:41.970\r\nI think that Batman\r\nis in grave danger.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.810 --\u003e 00:12:50.395\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:02.699 --\u003e 00:13:04.219\r\nALFRED: Another\r\ntemblor, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.826 --\u003e 00:13:07.537\r\nShall I pack for our\r\nreturn to Gotham City, sir?\r\n\r\n00:13:08.037 --\u003e 00:13:10.206\r\nI'm afraid not just\r\nyet, old friend.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.791 --\u003e 00:13:14.210\r\nI thought, that with the\r\nrecovery of the young lady\r\n\r\n00:13:14.460 --\u003e 00:13:17.630\r\nand the destruction of the scroll,\r\nyour chores here were finished.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.172 --\u003e 00:13:21.843\r\nKyodai has the part of the scroll\r\nthat describes the o-nemuri touch.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.343 --\u003e 00:13:25.263\r\nI'm afraid my Japanese is a bit\r\nrusty, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.680 --\u003e 00:13:27.348\r\nIt means \"big sleep.\"\r\n\r\n00:13:27.807 --\u003e 00:13:31.436\r\nA better translation\r\nmight be \"Eternal sleep.\"\r\n\r\n00:13:32.145 --\u003e 00:13:33.438\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:13:34.230 --\u003e 00:13:35.565\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh» my'.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:19.734 --\u003e 00:14:22.612\r\nI cannot tell you where the\r\nfatal point lies, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.237 --\u003e 00:14:25.740\r\nI never allowed myself\r\nto read the scroll,\r\n\r\n00:14:25.948 --\u003e 00:14:29.452\r\nfor fear I might someday be tempted\r\nto use the forbidden knowledge.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.203 --\u003e 00:14:31.871\r\nIt could be anywhere, then.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.080 --\u003e 00:14:35.291\r\nYes, on a hand, an arm, a leg.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.958 --\u003e 00:14:39.045\r\nEven a simple defensive\r\nblock could mean doom.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.900 --\u003e 00:15:02.318\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:15:05.947 --\u003e 00:15:06.948\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:15:09.617 --\u003e 00:15:10.618\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:15:11.119 --\u003e 00:15:12.328\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:12.412 --\u003e 00:15:15.331\r\nNo, rich man, but I have him.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.250 --\u003e 00:15:20.378\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou will face me,\r\nas yourself or your alter ego.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:21.045 --\u003e 00:15:22.713\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt is all the same to me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:23.047 --\u003e 00:15:24.757\r\n\u003ci\u003eYoru will tell you where.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:35.560 --\u003e 00:15:37.061\r\nA single touch.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.270 --\u003e 00:15:40.022\r\nThat's all it will take\r\nto destroy your master.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.356 --\u003e 00:15:41.732\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.317 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:46.612 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(KNOCK AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.785 --\u003e 00:15:54.162\r\nWill you fight Kyodai?\r\n\r\n00:15:54.662 --\u003e 00:15:56.622\r\nI believe the Batman\r\nintends to face him.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.123 --\u003e 00:16:00.293\r\nDo you think this\r\nBatman will fight him?\r\n\r\n00:16:00.793 --\u003e 00:16:02.545\r\nBatman does as he will.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.880 --\u003e 00:16:06.757\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut I'm fairly sure he'll\r\nchoose to meet the ninja.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:38.831 --\u003e 00:16:41.417\r\nHow do you like our\r\nfire-breather, gaijin?\r\n\r\n00:16:41.792 --\u003e 00:16:43.544\r\nImpressive, is he not?\r\n\r\n00:16:43.920 --\u003e 00:16:44.921\r\nBATMAN: Very.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.006 --\u003e 00:16:49.842\r\nOnce again, you approach\r\nunseen, dark one.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.635 --\u003e 00:16:52.345\r\nYou would have\r\nmade a good ninja.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.428 --\u003e 00:16:55.014\r\nI would prefer to be a samurai.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.306 --\u003e 00:16:58.643\r\nBut you are like me,\r\na warrior of the night.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.064 --\u003e 00:17:04.398\r\nSo it would seem.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.279 --\u003e 00:17:13.824\r\nLet us face each other in the\r\nopen, man to man.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.367 --\u003e 00:17:17.119\r\nSamurai do not\r\nhide behind masks.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.542 --\u003e 00:17:25.711\r\nAll right. Take your best shot.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.646 --\u003e 00:17:45.898\r\nKYODAI: Why do you back\r\naway, night fighter?\r\n\r\n00:17:46.983 --\u003e 00:17:48.693\r\nAfraid of my touch?\r\n\r\n00:17:49.277 --\u003e 00:17:50.570\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:59.662 --\u003e 00:18:02.498\r\nThis was a poor choice for\r\na battleground, Kyodai.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.999 --\u003e 00:18:04.709\r\nThe volcano may claim us all.\r\n\r\n00:18:05.334 --\u003e 00:18:08.838\r\nIt does not matter.\r\nNinja do not fear death.\r\n\r\n00:18:25.062 --\u003e 00:18:27.982\r\nEnough. It ends now.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.323 --\u003e 00:18:36.699\r\nYou are strong.\r\n\r\n00:18:39.035 --\u003e 00:18:40.578\r\nBut not strong enough.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.875 --\u003e 00:18:48.210\r\nSayonara, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.556 --\u003e 00:19:02.266\r\nLeaving so soon, Kyodai?\r\n\r\n00:19:06.729 --\u003e 00:19:08.230\r\nThe o-nemuri touch.\r\n\r\n00:19:08.981 --\u003e 00:19:11.942\r\nHow could you withstand it?\r\nIt's impossible.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.568 --\u003e 00:19:16.864\r\nIt's all over, Kyodai.\r\nYour precious technique doesn't work.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.249 --\u003e 00:19:28.834\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.435 --\u003e 00:19:48.062\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:01.659 --\u003e 00:20:05.329\r\nGrab it. If you jump and I\r\npull, you can make it.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.207 --\u003e 00:20:10.418\r\nKyodai, the rope!\r\n\r\n00:20:36.527 --\u003e 00:20:39.321\r\nI couldn't see through the smoke.\r\nWas Kyodai...\r\n\r\n00:20:39.572 --\u003e 00:20:42.742\r\nI don't know, Alfred.\r\nI wish I did.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.242 --\u003e 00:20:45.995\r\nI saw him use the fatal touch on\r\nyou, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.287 --\u003e 00:20:47.788\r\nDid he somehow miss?\r\n\r\n00:20:48.372 --\u003e 00:20:50.958\r\n\u003ci\u003eNo. Hound his practice dummy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:51.625 --\u003e 00:20:55.171\r\nThere was a soft spot on it,\r\na place jabbed many times.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.671 --\u003e 00:20:59.300\r\n- I protected that spot on my own body.\r\n- Most ingenious, sir.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.471 --\u003e 00:21:05.723\r\nI'm sorry about Kyodai, sensei.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.515 --\u003e 00:21:09.018\r\nWe all choose our own\r\npaths, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.226 --\u003e 00:21:10.686\r\nHe walked a dark trail.\r\n\r\n00:21:10.770 --\u003e 00:21:12.772\r\nIt was not your responsibility.\r\n\r\n00:21:14.148 --\u003e 00:21:17.943\r\nIf you see Batman,\r\ntell him I have great respect for him.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.277 --\u003e 00:21:19.320\r\nWhy?\r\n\r\n00:21:19.653 --\u003e 00:21:21.697\r\nHe's as much a\r\nninja as Kyodai was.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.114 --\u003e 00:21:25.367\r\nNot so. Batman offered\r\nto help his adversary.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.910 --\u003e 00:21:29.455\r\nAnd, a lesser man would have used\r\nthe knowledge of the o-nemuri touch\r\n\r\n00:21:29.538 --\u003e 00:21:30.915\r\nagainst his opponent.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.499 --\u003e 00:21:34.752\r\nBatman is the essence of\r\nsamurai, Wayne-san.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.252 --\u003e 00:21:37.004\r\nYou would do well\r\nto remember that.\r\n\r\n00:21:38.172 --\u003e 00:21:39.965\r\n\u003ci\u003eDomo arigato, sensei.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:22:21.590 --\u003e 00:22:22.591\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E56 - See No Evil (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:05.964 --\u003e 00:00:07.382\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.541 --\u003e 00:01:24.960\r\n(BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:26.753 --\u003e 00:01:29.381\r\n(BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:01:44.813 --\u003e 00:01:45.856\r\nMAN: Kimberly?\r\n\r\n00:01:46.982 --\u003e 00:01:48.275\r\nKimmy.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.654 --\u003e 00:01:53.655\r\nKimmy.\r\n\r\n00:01:55.490 --\u003e 00:01:57.409\r\nMojo, you came back.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.035 --\u003e 00:01:59.911\r\nMAN: Sure.\r\nI said I would, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:02:00.370 --\u003e 00:02:01.496\r\nUh-huh.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.872 --\u003e 00:02:03.332\r\nMAN: Look what I got for you.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.999 --\u003e 00:02:06.793\r\nOh. It's beautiful.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.127 --\u003e 00:02:08.420\r\nThank you, thank you.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.545 --\u003e 00:02:10.839\r\nMAN: (CHUCKLES) You're\r\nwelcome, sweetie.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.757 --\u003e 00:02:14.718\r\nNow, don't worry. I know that\r\nwhat you've really been hoping for\r\n\r\n00:02:14.801 --\u003e 00:02:16.178\r\nis a pearl necklace.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.553 --\u003e 00:02:19.014\r\nWell, I haven't found\r\njust the right one yet,\r\n\r\n00:02:19.139 --\u003e 00:02:22.476\r\nbut Mojo promises he'll bring\r\nyou one next time he visits.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.559 --\u003e 00:02:23.894\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.977 --\u003e 00:02:25.062\r\nMAN: Kimmy, what's wrong?\r\n\r\n00:02:25.729 --\u003e 00:02:28.732\r\nKIMMY: Next time better be\r\nsoon or you might not find us.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.316 --\u003e 00:02:30.817\r\nMommy says we're moving.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.901 --\u003e 00:02:33.153\r\nMAN: (GASPS) Moving?\r\n\r\n00:02:33.236 --\u003e 00:02:37.240\r\nKIMMY: She says things will be\r\nbetter for us someplace else.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.283 --\u003e 00:02:39.409\r\n(KIMMY GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:39.493 --\u003e 00:02:41.912\r\nKimberly,\r\nwho are you talking to?\r\n\r\n00:02:42.704 --\u003e 00:02:44.456\r\nNobody, Mommy, just Mojo.\r\n\r\n00:02:44.748 --\u003e 00:02:47.709\r\nOh, I'm sorry I missed him.\r\nI would've said, \"Hi.\"\r\n\r\n00:02:48.251 --\u003e 00:02:49.753\r\nKIMMY: He really was\r\nhere, Mommy.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.337 --\u003e 00:02:52.422\r\nI know, honey. I know.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.923 --\u003e 00:02:54.549\r\nNow go to sleep, okay?\r\n\r\n00:03:18.240 --\u003e 00:03:25.163\r\n(PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:41.555 --\u003e 00:03:42.806\r\n(DOORKNOB RATTLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:45.684 --\u003e 00:03:47.894\r\nHey! Who locked the bathroom?\r\n\r\n00:03:53.066 --\u003e 00:03:54.484\r\n(ELECTRONIC BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:03:56.278 --\u003e 00:03:58.321\r\n(ELECTRONIC BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:14.546 --\u003e 00:04:17.299\r\nA most handsome\r\nselection, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.429 --\u003e 00:04:23.430\r\nI'll take it.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.972 --\u003e 00:04:24.973\r\nWhat in the devil?\r\n\r\n00:04:29.019 --\u003e 00:04:30.228\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:32.481 --\u003e 00:04:33.774\r\nMAN: Holy smoke, look!\r\n\r\n00:04:34.900 --\u003e 00:04:36.359\r\n(ALL GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:36.443 --\u003e 00:04:40.781\r\n(PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:44.409 --\u003e 00:04:46.119\r\nMAN: Police! Police!\r\nOver this way!\r\n\r\n00:04:46.203 --\u003e 00:04:47.204\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:49.331 --\u003e 00:04:51.374\r\nHelp, security!\r\nI've been robbed.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.458 --\u003e 00:04:53.376\r\n- Look at that!\r\n- What the heck?\r\n\r\n00:04:53.460 --\u003e 00:04:56.213\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:01.134 --\u003e 00:05:03.595\r\nNobody moves till we figure\r\nout what's going on here.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.720 --\u003e 00:05:05.889\r\nHey! My piece. It's been stolen.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.348 --\u003e 00:05:07.349\r\nMine, too.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.557 --\u003e 00:05:08.600\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.060 --\u003e 00:05:12.312\r\nArgh! Ahhh!\r\n\r\n00:05:12.646 --\u003e 00:05:13.772\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.778 --\u003e 00:05:21.112\r\nFootsteps?\r\n\r\n00:05:29.287 --\u003e 00:05:30.372\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.705 --\u003e 00:05:31.832\r\nI know you're in here.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.160 --\u003e 00:06:11.538\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.621 --\u003e 00:06:13.123\r\nMAN: Cute. Real cute.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.593 --\u003e 00:06:27.512\r\nYou were better off blowing\r\nsmoke, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.138 --\u003e 00:06:32.225\r\nSee, I guess I'm what\r\nyou'd call a burnout case.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.146 --\u003e 00:06:37.814\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:42.235 --\u003e 00:06:45.822\r\nMAN: Too bad about these high\r\nceilings, huh, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:06:46.114 --\u003e 00:06:49.576\r\nI mean, all this lousy\r\nechoing kind of makes it hard\r\n\r\n00:06:49.659 --\u003e 00:06:51.578\r\nto get a fix on me, doesn't it?\r\n\r\n00:06:51.745 --\u003e 00:06:54.247\r\nEspecially,\r\nsince you wouldn't see me...\r\n\r\n00:06:54.331 --\u003e 00:06:56.166\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:56.249 --\u003e 00:06:58.418\r\nif I were standing\r\nright next to you.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.501 --\u003e 00:07:02.631\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:02.714 --\u003e 00:07:03.840\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:07:03.924 --\u003e 00:07:05.216\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.428 --\u003e 00:07:11.389\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:07:11.473 --\u003e 00:07:13.099\r\nMAN: See you around, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.183 --\u003e 00:07:15.310\r\nToo bad you can't say the same.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.393 --\u003e 00:07:17.103\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:56.059 --\u003e 00:07:57.894\r\nA better life somewhere\r\nelse, huh?\r\n\r\n00:07:58.061 --\u003e 00:08:01.982\r\nWhere your dear old dad can't find\r\nyou, that's what she really means.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.566 --\u003e 00:08:05.110\r\nWell, don't you worry.\r\n\r\n00:08:06.027 --\u003e 00:08:08.321\r\nShe's never going to\r\ntake you away from me.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.906 --\u003e 00:08:12.450\r\nI won't let her. You hear me?\r\n\r\n00:08:12.575 --\u003e 00:08:14.786\r\nI won't let her.\r\n\r\n00:08:30.510 --\u003e 00:08:31.553\r\n(KISSES)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.431 --\u003e 00:08:36.474\r\nBye, sweetie. Have a nice day.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.423 --\u003e 00:09:09.966\r\nHELEN: I'll be back in an hour.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.180 --\u003e 00:09:16.181\r\nHey, babe.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.015 --\u003e 00:09:18.308\r\nLong time.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.850 --\u003e 00:09:20.185\r\nNot long enough.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.273 --\u003e 00:09:26.983\r\nDid they tell you\r\nabout the parole?\r\n\r\n00:09:29.444 --\u003e 00:09:30.987\r\nI'm living in Gotham now.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.154 --\u003e 00:09:35.075\r\nI don't care what you do, as long as\r\nyou don't do it within 100 feet of me.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.158 --\u003e 00:09:37.452\r\nThe restraining order?\r\nYou don't need that anymore, Helen.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.577 --\u003e 00:09:39.704\r\nWhen I was still a bum,\r\nit made sense, but...\r\n\r\n00:09:39.829 --\u003e 00:09:41.289\r\nWhat do you mean, \"was\"?\r\n\r\n00:09:41.623 --\u003e 00:09:43.917\r\nCome on, babe. Look at me!\r\n\r\n00:09:57.222 --\u003e 00:10:00.600\r\nHow many all-night gas stations did\r\nyou have to knock over for that?\r\n\r\n00:10:01.643 --\u003e 00:10:02.644\r\nKeep it.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.400 --\u003e 00:10:11.736\r\nEverything is different\r\nnow, can't you see that?\r\n\r\n00:10:12.028 --\u003e 00:10:14.739\r\nI can give Kimmy everything\r\nshe'll ever need.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.906 --\u003e 00:10:16.157\r\nYou stay away from her.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.449 --\u003e 00:10:18.743\r\nCome on, babe.\r\nIf you could just let her see me...\r\n\r\n00:10:18.868 --\u003e 00:10:20.703\r\nKeep your hands off me.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.787 --\u003e 00:10:21.788\r\nI told her all about you.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.871 --\u003e 00:10:23.915\r\nShe knows you're not\r\nsupposed to go near her.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.332 --\u003e 00:10:26.668\r\nHelen, please.\r\nCut me some slack, here, will you?\r\n\r\n00:10:26.793 --\u003e 00:10:28.419\r\nI'll give you anything you want.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.628 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nWant?\r\n\r\n00:10:30.046 --\u003e 00:10:32.674\r\nAll I want is for\r\nyou to disappear.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.966 --\u003e 00:10:34.008\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.551 --\u003e 00:10:35.552\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.718 --\u003e 00:10:37.762\r\nBut just remember\r\nthe old saying,\r\n\r\n00:10:38.555 --\u003e 00:10:41.015\r\n\"Be careful what you wish for.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:46.271 --\u003e 00:10:48.439\r\nSCIENTIST: I understand your\r\nconcern, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.523 --\u003e 00:10:51.526\r\nBut I don't think you need to worry\r\nthat Wayne Tech is responsible\r\n\r\n00:10:51.609 --\u003e 00:10:53.444\r\nfor this invisible man.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.611 --\u003e 00:10:55.488\r\nAfter all,\r\nno equipment is missing.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.615 --\u003e 00:11:00.869\r\nBut, I seem to remember,\r\nlast year, hearing something\r\n\r\n00:11:00.952 --\u003e 00:11:02.954\r\nabout an invisibility project.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.705 --\u003e 00:11:05.540\r\nYou mean that inventor Carrows.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.332 --\u003e 00:11:07.625\r\nYeah, I remember him.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.959 --\u003e 00:11:09.895\r\nThe one who wanted us to\r\ngo into business with him,\r\n\r\n00:11:09.919 --\u003e 00:11:11.087\r\ndeveloping that plastic.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.504 --\u003e 00:11:15.133\r\nUh-huh. The \"cloak of\r\ninvisibility\" he called it, right?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.009 --\u003e 00:11:17.010\r\nSo, what happened?\r\n\r\n00:11:17.135 --\u003e 00:11:19.888\r\nWell, we were interested\r\nin hearing more, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.013 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nBut, Carrows withdrew his proposal\r\nbefore we could close a deal.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.643 --\u003e 00:11:28.438\r\nLucius, see if you can locate him.\r\nI'd like to talk to him.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.813 --\u003e 00:11:31.149\r\nDon't bother.\r\nHe passed away a couple of months ago.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.275 --\u003e 00:11:34.402\r\nBut I've heard that his old\r\nassistant, Sam Giddell,\r\n\r\n00:11:34.527 --\u003e 00:11:36.487\r\nwas trying to carry\r\non his research.\r\n\r\n00:11:40.658 --\u003e 00:11:43.161\r\n(RATCHET CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:52.272 --\u003e 00:12:53.356\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:54.649 --\u003e 00:12:56.776\r\nOkay, you, come out of there.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.901 --\u003e 00:12:58.903\r\nI don't know what you\r\nthink you're doing.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.740 --\u003e 00:13:03.908\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:13:05.243 --\u003e 00:13:06.661\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:11.332 --\u003e 00:13:12.375\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:14.043 --\u003e 00:13:15.712\r\n(GASPS) You.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.087 --\u003e 00:13:17.213\r\nI didn't know.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.338 --\u003e 00:13:18.464\r\nAre you Giddell?\r\n\r\n00:13:18.673 --\u003e 00:13:20.133\r\n(STAMMERS) What do you want?\r\n\r\n00:13:20.258 --\u003e 00:13:22.218\r\nWhere were you the\r\nday before yesterday?\r\n\r\n00:13:22.343 --\u003e 00:13:24.429\r\nHere. All day.\r\nAnd I can prove it.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.512 --\u003e 00:13:26.139\r\nThe building security saw me.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.264 --\u003e 00:13:27.265\r\nYou can check.\r\n\r\n00:13:33.521 --\u003e 00:13:35.398\r\nWorking kind of\r\nlate, aren't you?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.732 --\u003e 00:13:38.276\r\nI wanted to prep the last\r\nof the stuff for disposal.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.904 --\u003e 00:13:45.033\r\nThis is that invisibility\r\nplastic your boss created?\r\n\r\n00:13:45.700 --\u003e 00:13:46.868\r\nMmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.785 --\u003e 00:13:50.455\r\n- How does it work?\r\n- Here, let me show you.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.122 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nIt's really quite remarkable.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.837 --\u003e 00:13:59.881\r\n(ELECTRICAL BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:13:59.964 --\u003e 00:14:02.425\r\nSee those filaments\r\nembedded in the plastic?\r\n\r\n00:14:04.302 --\u003e 00:14:05.345\r\nMmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.428 --\u003e 00:14:07.305\r\nRun an electrical\r\ncurrent through them,\r\n\r\n00:14:07.388 --\u003e 00:14:10.183\r\nand the stuff bends light\r\ninstead of absorbing it,\r\n\r\n00:14:10.266 --\u003e 00:14:11.267\r\nso you can't see it.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.392 --\u003e 00:14:14.187\r\nBut in the process,\r\nthe plastic becomes toxic.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.312 --\u003e 00:14:16.189\r\nI know. I read the report.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.647 --\u003e 00:14:19.442\r\nI've spent the last two months\r\ntrying to correct the problem,\r\n\r\n00:14:19.525 --\u003e 00:14:20.526\r\nbut it's hopeless.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.735 --\u003e 00:14:22.135\r\nSo, you were just\r\ngoing to dump it?\r\n\r\n00:14:22.403 --\u003e 00:14:24.238\r\nYes, it's too dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.447 --\u003e 00:14:26.991\r\nFunny thing is,\r\nsome of it seems to be missing.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.075 --\u003e 00:14:30.286\r\n- Who else would know about this stuff?\r\n- Only the other assistant.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.620 --\u003e 00:14:32.872\r\nActually,\r\nhe was more like an errand boy.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.247 --\u003e 00:14:34.499\r\nAn ex-con.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.707 --\u003e 00:14:37.627\r\nName is Ventrix. Lloyd Ventrix.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.841 --\u003e 00:14:45.760\r\n- Mrs. Ventrix?\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:45.843 --\u003e 00:14:47.387\r\nI'm looking for your husband.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.512 --\u003e 00:14:48.888\r\nIt's urgent.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.013 --\u003e 00:14:51.808\r\nOh, Mojo,\r\nit's exactly what I wanted.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.933 --\u003e 00:14:53.309\r\nLLOYD: I'm glad.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.686 --\u003e 00:14:56.687\r\nNow, come on.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.771 --\u003e 00:14:58.815\r\nI want to show you\r\nsomething real special.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.774 --\u003e 00:15:03.111\r\n- (CHUCKLES) Where are we going?\r\n- You'll see.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.821 --\u003e 00:15:06.948\r\nAnd prolonged exposure\r\nto the plastic\r\n\r\n00:15:07.031 --\u003e 00:15:09.450\r\ncan damage the mind,\r\nas well as the body.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.617 --\u003e 00:15:11.786\r\nYou say he can make\r\nhimself invisible?\r\n\r\n00:15:11.953 --\u003e 00:15:13.955\r\n(GASPS) Mojo!\r\n\r\n00:15:14.539 --\u003e 00:15:16.082\r\n- Who?\r\n- Kimberly!\r\n\r\n00:15:19.001 --\u003e 00:15:20.336\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.217 --\u003e 00:15:27.218\r\nKimberly.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.636 --\u003e 00:15:29.679\r\nKimberly.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.596 --\u003e 00:15:31.597\r\nKimberly!\r\n\r\n00:15:32.098 --\u003e 00:15:33.266\r\nKimmy!\r\n\r\n00:15:33.683 --\u003e 00:15:36.978\r\n(CRYING)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.869 --\u003e 00:15:55.121\r\nI thought Mojo was just\r\nher imaginary friend.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.204 --\u003e 00:15:56.372\r\nI never thought...\r\n\r\n00:15:56.581 --\u003e 00:15:57.582\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:15:58.624 --\u003e 00:16:00.084\r\nA tranquilizer dart.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.209 --\u003e 00:16:02.086\r\nHow long ago did you\r\nsee your daughter?\r\n\r\n00:16:02.336 --\u003e 00:16:04.547\r\nFive minutes ago.\r\nI put her to bed and...\r\n\r\n00:16:05.006 --\u003e 00:16:06.090\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:16:17.477 --\u003e 00:16:18.769\r\nLLOYD: Here we are.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.061 --\u003e 00:16:20.146\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:21.105 --\u003e 00:16:24.233\r\n- You want me to get in your car?\r\n- Now, Kimmy...\r\n\r\n00:16:24.358 --\u003e 00:16:26.861\r\nBut it'll look like the\r\ncar's going by itself.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.195 --\u003e 00:16:28.571\r\nWon't we get in trouble?\r\n\r\n00:16:28.863 --\u003e 00:16:30.823\r\nNo, Kimberly, we won't.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.157 --\u003e 00:16:32.408\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.783 --\u003e 00:16:34.494\r\n(SIGHS) \u003ci\u003eI'll\u003c/i\u003e tell you what,\r\n\r\n00:16:34.785 --\u003e 00:16:37.288\r\nmaybe if I let you see\r\nme, you'll feel better.\r\n\r\n00:16:40.291 --\u003e 00:16:41.459\r\nHi, Kimberly.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.542 --\u003e 00:16:43.377\r\n(GASPS) You're a man?\r\n\r\n00:16:44.629 --\u003e 00:16:45.963\r\nI gotta go, Mojo.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.047 --\u003e 00:16:47.840\r\nI'm not supposed to\r\nbe with strangers.\r\n\r\n00:16:47.924 --\u003e 00:16:49.759\r\nMommy told me. (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.635 --\u003e 00:16:52.428\r\nBut I'm not a\r\nstranger, Kimberly.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.845 --\u003e 00:16:53.888\r\nI'm your daddy.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.055 --\u003e 00:16:56.015\r\nMy daddy? Get away!\r\n\r\n00:16:56.265 --\u003e 00:16:58.100\r\nMommy says you're not\r\nallowed to come near me.\r\n\r\n00:16:58.226 --\u003e 00:16:59.769\r\nShe says you're a bad man.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.852 --\u003e 00:17:01.646\r\nShe says that's why\r\nthey locked you up.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.771 --\u003e 00:17:02.980\r\nNever mind that!\r\n\r\n00:17:03.564 --\u003e 00:17:05.525\r\nYou're coming with me,\r\nwhether you want to or not.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.608 --\u003e 00:17:07.401\r\nBATMAN: Not in this\r\nlifetime, pal.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.280 --\u003e 00:17:12.615\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:16.035 --\u003e 00:17:17.954\r\nMommy, Mommy!\r\n\r\n00:17:49.193 --\u003e 00:17:50.945\r\nMommy, Mommy!\r\n\r\n00:17:51.028 --\u003e 00:17:52.029\r\nKimberly?\r\n\r\n00:18:22.643 --\u003e 00:18:27.898\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:30.359 --\u003e 00:18:32.820\r\nI didn't know he could fly, too.\r\n\r\n00:18:37.867 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.434 --\u003e 00:19:04.810\r\nGive it up, Ventrix.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.894 --\u003e 00:19:07.438\r\nThe suit is toxic.\r\nIt'll destroy you!\r\n\r\n00:19:07.563 --\u003e 00:19:09.774\r\nDon't hand me that.\r\nI'm not feeling any pain.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.857 --\u003e 00:19:11.942\r\nAt least,\r\nnot like you're gonna feel.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.640 --\u003e 00:19:44.058\r\n(TRAIN HORN BLOWING)\r\n\r\n00:20:04.912 --\u003e 00:20:05.996\r\nArgh!\r\n\r\n00:20:06.080 --\u003e 00:20:08.624\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:09.667 --\u003e 00:20:15.172\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.220 --\u003e 00:20:23.097\r\nVentrix, the suit,\r\n\r\n00:20:23.431 --\u003e 00:20:24.432\r\nit's poison!\r\n\r\n00:20:24.724 --\u003e 00:20:26.058\r\nLLOYD: So, what if it is?\r\n\r\n00:20:26.392 --\u003e 00:20:27.727\r\nI don't care.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.479 --\u003e 00:20:31.856\r\nAs long as I have it,\r\n\r\n00:20:31.939 --\u003e 00:20:35.401\r\nI can take my daughter\r\nback, whenever I want!\r\n\r\n00:20:36.694 --\u003e 00:20:39.155\r\nHer mother won't\r\nbe able to stop me,\r\n\r\n00:20:39.321 --\u003e 00:20:40.823\r\nand neither will you!\r\n\r\n00:20:53.502 --\u003e 00:20:54.503\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:55.171 --\u003e 00:20:56.464\r\nPeekaboo.\r\n\r\n00:20:56.964 --\u003e 00:20:58.132\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:20:59.341 --\u003e 00:21:02.845\r\n(LLOYD GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:21:03.512 --\u003e 00:21:04.764\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:21:09.268 --\u003e 00:21:12.354\r\nGet ready for your biggest\r\ndisappearing act, Ventrix.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.730 --\u003e 00:21:15.399\r\nThe one where no one\r\nsees you for 10 to 20.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.236 --\u003e 00:21:20.476\r\nKIMMY: Me and Mommy are moving.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.780 --\u003e 00:21:22.466\r\nAnd even if Daddy gets\r\nout of jail this time,\r\n\r\n00:21:22.490 --\u003e 00:21:23.783\r\nhe'll never find us.\r\n\r\n00:21:23.949 --\u003e 00:21:26.494\r\nKimberly?\r\nWho are you talking to now?\r\n\r\n00:21:26.786 --\u003e 00:21:28.162\r\nJust Batman, Mommy.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.496 --\u003e 00:21:31.123\r\nOh. Him, again?\r\n\r\n00:21:31.707 --\u003e 00:21:33.501\r\nBut he really was here, Mommy.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.751 --\u003e 00:21:35.211\r\nI know, honey.\r\n\r\n00:21:35.336 --\u003e 00:21:36.337\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:21:53.521 --\u003e 00:21:55.523\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.838 --\u003e 00:22:19.839\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E57 - The Demon's Quest, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:23.524 --\u003e 00:00:25.526\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:12.406 --\u003e 00:01:14.032\r\n(THUNDER CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.069 --\u003e 00:01:52.070\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:56.533 --\u003e 00:01:58.118\r\nHey! (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:18.555 --\u003e 00:02:20.223\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:46.625 --\u003e 00:02:47.876\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:49.503 --\u003e 00:02:51.588\r\nNo word then, Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:02:51.755 --\u003e 00:02:54.174\r\nNone. And I've scoured\r\nthe entire city.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.257 --\u003e 00:02:58.261\r\nNo one has seen either Robin\r\nor Dick Grayson for two days.\r\n\r\n00:02:59.846 --\u003e 00:03:02.307\r\nI really should remain\r\nupstairs then, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.391 --\u003e 00:03:03.517\r\nLest he call.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.059 --\u003e 00:03:07.604\r\nOh, by the way, this came for\r\nyou an hour ago by messenger.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.375 --\u003e 00:03:30.961\r\nNo. It can't be.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.721 --\u003e 00:03:42.055\r\nMAN: So.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.514 --\u003e 00:03:44.933\r\nThey know your\r\nidentity, detective.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.684 --\u003e 00:03:47.769\r\nWho are you?\r\nHow did you get in here?\r\n\r\n00:03:52.816 --\u003e 00:03:56.403\r\nYou must forgive Ubu, detective.\r\nHe is well-trained.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.570 --\u003e 00:04:01.575\r\nAllow me to introduce myself.\r\nLam he who is called Ra's al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.075 --\u003e 00:04:04.911\r\nThe Demon's Head.\r\nI thought you were only a legend.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.746 --\u003e 00:04:07.372\r\nI am quite real.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.873 --\u003e 00:04:10.000\r\nAnd as I am sure\r\nyou realize by now,\r\n\r\n00:04:10.167 --\u003e 00:04:14.254\r\nmy reputation for\r\nresourcefulness is well-deserved.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.671 --\u003e 00:04:16.590\r\nAs you can see,\r\nwe have a common problem.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.673 --\u003e 00:04:20.260\r\nYour ward was abducted on the\r\nsame night as my daughter.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.052 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nYou do remember my daughter?\r\n\r\n00:04:23.597 --\u003e 00:04:25.807\r\n- You're Talia's father?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.767 --\u003e 00:04:30.729\r\nBut surely you would not expect\r\nher to mention me by name. (COUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:04:32.481 --\u003e 00:04:35.859\r\nKeep your distance!\r\nI am merely old.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.151 --\u003e 00:04:38.320\r\nOlder, perhaps,\r\nthan you can imagine.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.737 --\u003e 00:04:41.573\r\nBut not so old that I cannot\r\nassist you in your search.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.240 --\u003e 00:04:46.495\r\nI get the message. Okay, then.\r\nFor openers, look at the blade.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.703 --\u003e 00:04:49.498\r\nIt's used by a cult of\r\nmercenaries based in Calcutta.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.790 --\u003e 00:04:53.710\r\nEven the rope appears to be made\r\nof a hemp indigenous to that area.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.877 --\u003e 00:04:55.712\r\nWell done, detective.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.879 --\u003e 00:04:59.841\r\nYou are worthy of your reputation.\r\nTo India, then.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.509 --\u003e 00:05:02.969\r\nCome,\r\nI have an aircraft waiting.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.472 --\u003e 00:05:06.640\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:06.723 --\u003e 00:05:07.849\r\nUBU: Infidel!\r\n\r\n00:05:10.769 --\u003e 00:05:12.521\r\nRA'S: Forgive my servant.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.813 --\u003e 00:05:15.482\r\nHe feels that no one\r\nshould precede me.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.732 --\u003e 00:05:17.526\r\nCall it overzealousness.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.239 --\u003e 00:05:25.116\r\nI think I'll call it strike one.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.834 --\u003e 00:05:36.795\r\nBATMAN: You still have me at a\r\nloss, Ra's al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.170 --\u003e 00:05:38.672\r\nJust how did you learn who I am?\r\n\r\n00:05:39.464 --\u003e 00:05:43.093\r\nI control a vast global\r\norganization, detective.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.927 --\u003e 00:05:48.348\r\nObviously, Batman's activities\r\nrequire certain costly implements.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.099 --\u003e 00:05:52.227\r\nIt was a simple matter for my people\r\nto learn which wealthy Americans\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.688\r\nwere amassing what\r\nBatman might require.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.272 --\u003e 00:05:58.942\r\nThe one who matched my daughter's\r\ndescription of you was Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.151 --\u003e 00:06:02.195\r\nNext time I'll have\r\nto glue my mask on.\r\n\r\n00:06:02.988 --\u003e 00:06:04.322\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:06:05.615 --\u003e 00:06:06.700\r\nDo you need help?\r\n\r\n00:06:07.534 --\u003e 00:06:09.703\r\nI need nothing.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.870 --\u003e 00:06:14.958\r\nAs Napoleon told me,\r\na strong will can fuel a frail physique.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.474 --\u003e 00:06:35.979\r\nHow can you be certain, detective,\r\nthat those we seek are to be found here?\r\n\r\n00:06:36.271 --\u003e 00:06:39.316\r\nI make it my business to\r\nknow things like that. Here.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.649 --\u003e 00:06:41.318\r\nThere's an incense shop.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.944 --\u003e 00:06:43.945\r\nInfidel!\r\n\r\n00:06:45.196 --\u003e 00:06:46.740\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- (SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:51.578 --\u003e 00:06:54.205\r\nOkay. That's two.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.884 --\u003e 00:07:07.302\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.513 --\u003e 00:07:11.556\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.562 --\u003e 00:07:18.563\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:07:40.877 --\u003e 00:07:42.003\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:07:42.963 --\u003e 00:07:47.258\r\nYes. Unless you tell me how to\r\nfind the mercenaries who did this.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.884 --\u003e 00:07:51.972\r\nThey have fled with the boy\r\nand the woman. (WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:07:54.766 --\u003e 00:07:55.976\r\nWhere?\r\n\r\n00:07:58.520 --\u003e 00:08:03.566\r\nTo Malaysia. In a pagoda in\r\nthe shadow of Mount Merapi.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.942 --\u003e 00:08:06.027\r\nI know nothing more, I swear it!\r\n\r\n00:08:26.047 --\u003e 00:08:29.801\r\nLook at it, detective,\r\none of the last of the rain forests.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.968 --\u003e 00:08:32.012\r\nThe world depends\r\nupon its oxygen,\r\n\r\n00:08:32.095 --\u003e 00:08:35.682\r\nyet the rich see only\r\nprofit in its destruction.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.849 --\u003e 00:08:40.562\r\nYou who belong to the overclass\r\nhave much to answer for.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.271 --\u003e 00:08:45.150\r\nBruce Wayne donates millions of dollars\r\na year to preserve these forests.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.650 --\u003e 00:08:50.989\r\nRA'S: Which are being depleted at\r\nthe rate of 120,000 acres a day.\r\n\r\n00:08:51.740 --\u003e 00:08:54.659\r\nDoes your money solve\r\nthis problem? No.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.826 --\u003e 00:08:57.746\r\nIt will take more than\r\nwealth, it will take power.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.121 --\u003e 00:09:00.749\r\nAnd, I fear, ruthlessness.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.044 --\u003e 00:09:08.757\r\nHumankind must be forced to serve the\r\nplanet instead of its own appetites.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.883 --\u003e 00:09:12.302\r\nAnd you're the one\r\nwho'll do the forcing?\r\n\r\n00:09:12.635 --\u003e 00:09:15.805\r\nI am qualified, yes.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.306 --\u003e 00:09:19.392\r\nBut I may not have sufficient\r\nlifetimes left to me.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.143 --\u003e 00:09:22.562\r\nMaster, ahead. Look!\r\n\r\n00:09:23.813 --\u003e 00:09:26.816\r\nRA'S: In the shadow of the\r\nvolcano, just as the Indian said.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.317 --\u003e 00:09:28.777\r\nLet us hurry.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.860 --\u003e 00:09:31.404\r\nThe next piece of our\r\npuzzle surely waits within.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.817 --\u003e 00:10:10.068\r\n(SNARLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.214 --\u003e 00:10:32.465\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:37.637 --\u003e 00:10:38.721\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:56.531 --\u003e 00:10:57.782\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.618 --\u003e 00:11:01.619\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:11:19.804 --\u003e 00:11:20.972\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:31.024 --\u003e 00:11:32.192\r\n(SNORES)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.734 --\u003e 00:11:34.736\r\nSweet dreams, tabby.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.456 --\u003e 00:11:49.959\r\nCongratulations, detective,\r\non thwarting our tormentors.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.462 --\u003e 00:11:55.465\r\nObviously,\r\nour quest was meant to end here.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.548 --\u003e 00:11:59.427\r\nMaybe, maybe not. Look at this.\r\nA map of the Himalayas.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.802 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\nThere's a faint scratch,\r\n\r\n00:12:01.679 --\u003e 00:12:05.058\r\nalmost certainly made by a\r\nfingernail tracing a route.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.141 --\u003e 00:12:07.685\r\nIndeed.\r\nI am familiar with that area,\r\n\r\n00:12:07.852 --\u003e 00:12:10.897\r\nand the nearest field large\r\nenough to accommodate my aircraft\r\n\r\n00:12:11.064 --\u003e 00:12:12.941\r\nis 100 miles from\r\nour destination.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.359 --\u003e 00:12:17.070\r\nSo I will arrange for a\r\nhelicopter when one is needed.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.240 --\u003e 00:12:21.783\r\nAfter you.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.620 --\u003e 00:12:26.621\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.957 --\u003e 00:12:29.999\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.678 --\u003e 00:12:44.347\r\nRA'S: The mountain in\r\nquestion is directly ahead.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.430 --\u003e 00:12:48.476\r\nI've radioed for my men.\r\nThey await me on the mountaintop.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.643 --\u003e 00:12:52.313\r\n- While I descend the hard way.\r\n- You must search for clues.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.689 --\u003e 00:12:55.233\r\nIf we perceive any danger,\r\nwe can signal you with-\r\n\r\n00:12:55.775 --\u003e 00:12:56.985\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:58.152 --\u003e 00:13:01.281\r\nMaster, we must get\r\nyou to one of the pits.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.532 --\u003e 00:13:05.326\r\n- Pits?\r\n- Ignore him, detective.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.493 --\u003e 00:13:08.162\r\nWe must stay on the hunt for\r\nthe sake of the children.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.705 --\u003e 00:13:11.624\r\nAll right.\r\nIf that's the way it's to be played.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.812 --\u003e 00:14:15.813\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:19.817 --\u003e 00:14:21.027\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:55.561 --\u003e 00:14:57.814\r\n- Robin.\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:14:58.272 --\u003e 00:15:00.608\r\n- Batman!\r\n- You okay?\r\n\r\n00:15:00.942 --\u003e 00:15:02.360\r\nAm I glad to see you.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.944 --\u003e 00:15:04.237\r\nI'll have you free in a minute.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.994 --\u003e 00:15:13.454\r\n(MAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.342 --\u003e 00:15:27.677\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.482 --\u003e 00:15:43.609\r\n- Been here long?\r\n- A couple days, I think.\r\n\r\n00:15:43.943 --\u003e 00:15:45.445\r\nI still don't know\r\nwho grabbed me.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.868 --\u003e 00:15:53.119\r\nI do.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.202 --\u003e 00:15:54.412\r\n(CLAPPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.096 --\u003e 00:16:13.931\r\nBATMAN: Ra's al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.855 --\u003e 00:16:23.274\r\nObviously,\r\nyour little accident wasn't fatal.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.441 --\u003e 00:16:26.652\r\nI imagine you and Ubu left the\r\nchopper when lwasn't looking.\r\n\r\n00:16:26.736 --\u003e 00:16:31.616\r\nIndeed. At the moment it exploded,\r\nit was proceeding on automatic pilot.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.782 --\u003e 00:16:34.911\r\nSo how long have you\r\nknown, detective,\r\n\r\n00:16:35.077 --\u003e 00:16:37.121\r\nthat I planned your\r\nWard's capture?\r\n\r\n00:16:37.455 --\u003e 00:16:38.664\r\nAlmost from the beginning.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.748 --\u003e 00:16:40.917\r\nHow could you have known\r\nthat Robin and your daughter\r\n\r\n00:16:41.083 --\u003e 00:16:42.752\r\nwere abducted on the same night?\r\n\r\n00:16:42.919 --\u003e 00:16:45.046\r\nUnless I had done the abducting?\r\n\r\n00:16:45.254 --\u003e 00:16:46.672\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.839 --\u003e 00:16:49.592\r\nAnd do you think I'd have let you\r\ntake me anywhere in your plane\r\n\r\n00:16:49.675 --\u003e 00:16:51.635\r\nunless I suspected you\r\nmeant to lead me somewhere?\r\n\r\n00:16:51.928 --\u003e 00:16:55.181\r\nFor one thing,\r\nthere were all those would-be assassins.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.264 --\u003e 00:16:57.350\r\nThey knew where\r\nwe'd be and when.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.517 --\u003e 00:17:01.020\r\nSomeone had to be tipping them off.\r\nThat someone had to be you.\r\n\r\n00:17:01.354 --\u003e 00:17:04.941\r\nThen there was Ubu.\r\nAlways by his master's side,\r\n\r\n00:17:05.107 --\u003e 00:17:08.569\r\nalways very picky about letting\r\nyou go ahead of everyone else.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.778 --\u003e 00:17:13.658\r\nExcept in Malaysia,\r\nwhere you knew there was danger waiting.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.242 --\u003e 00:17:16.035\r\nI am deeply impressed.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.661 --\u003e 00:17:17.870\r\nAs am I.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.545 --\u003e 00:17:26.671\r\nReady to go?\r\n\r\n00:17:30.550 --\u003e 00:17:32.260\r\nWell, if you say so.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.343 --\u003e 00:17:34.512\r\nThough it was just starting\r\nto get interesting.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.474 --\u003e 00:17:40.893\r\nThe master gave you no\r\npermission to leave.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.185 --\u003e 00:17:43.271\r\nI didn't ask for any.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.398 --\u003e 00:17:46.399\r\n(GROWLS SOFTLY)\r\n\r\n00:17:49.235 --\u003e 00:17:50.319\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:51.779 --\u003e 00:17:53.447\r\nAnd that's three.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.864 --\u003e 00:17:54.949\r\n(KNUCKLES CRACKING)\r\n\r\n00:17:57.243 --\u003e 00:17:58.327\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.624 --\u003e 00:18:09.005\r\nWait. I can't let you leave like this.\r\nMy father meant you no harm.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.008 --\u003e 00:18:15.678\r\n- He had a funny way of showing it.\r\n- RA'S: My time is short.\r\n\r\n00:18:16.220 --\u003e 00:18:17.972\r\nI have no sons.\r\n\r\n00:18:18.055 --\u003e 00:18:21.559\r\nI need a man to assume my\r\nposition when I am gone.\r\n\r\n00:18:21.934 --\u003e 00:18:24.979\r\nBATMAN: Then it was a test?\r\nBut why me?\r\n\r\n00:18:25.229 --\u003e 00:18:30.109\r\nBecause you are most worthy.\r\nThat is now proven beyond any doubt.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.901 --\u003e 00:18:32.987\r\nAnd because my precious\r\ndaughter loves you.\r\n\r\n00:18:42.496 --\u003e 00:18:43.497\r\nForget it.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.043 --\u003e 00:18:49.462\r\nThen this means we\r\nmust be enemies!\r\n\r\n00:18:49.629 --\u003e 00:18:52.423\r\nYou will regret this\r\ninsult, detective.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.590 --\u003e 00:18:56.218\r\nYOU will... (COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:59.347 --\u003e 00:19:00.348\r\nFather!\r\n\r\n00:19:02.141 --\u003e 00:19:03.643\r\n(RASPY BREATHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:07.688 --\u003e 00:19:11.067\r\n- He's dying!\r\n- I've had it with your little games.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.525 --\u003e 00:19:13.235\r\nNo game, I swear it!\r\n\r\n00:19:15.738 --\u003e 00:19:16.947\r\n(WHEEZING)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.452 --\u003e 00:19:23.954\r\nPulse is bad.\r\nHe can't fake that.\r\n\r\n00:19:25.039 --\u003e 00:19:27.416\r\nWe must take him\r\nto the Lazarus Pit.\r\n\r\n00:19:40.096 --\u003e 00:19:42.640\r\nYou want us to put him in that?\r\nYou're crazy!\r\n\r\n00:19:42.973 --\u003e 00:19:46.227\r\nNo, listen to me,\r\nI know it is difficult to believe,\r\n\r\n00:19:46.394 --\u003e 00:19:51.273\r\nbut the pit is what keeps him alive.\r\nWhat has kept him alive for 600 years.\r\n\r\n00:19:52.733 --\u003e 00:19:56.445\r\n- Batman?\r\n- Please, you must believe me!\r\n\r\n00:19:59.657 --\u003e 00:20:02.785\r\nBATMAN: We have no choice.\r\nHe's stopped breathing.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.648 --\u003e 00:20:33.941\r\nWe've killed him.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.067 --\u003e 00:20:37.194\r\nNo. All is well.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.486 --\u003e 00:20:38.821\r\n(BUBBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.491 --\u003e 00:20:43.909\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:20:44.577 --\u003e 00:20:46.036\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:21:09.852 --\u003e 00:21:11.604\r\n(EVIL LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:21:19.028 --\u003e 00:21:20.029\r\n(TALIA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:25.868 --\u003e 00:21:27.161\r\nPut her down!\r\n\r\n00:21:31.665 --\u003e 00:21:34.835\r\nI said put her down!\r\n\r\n00:21:35.503 --\u003e 00:21:37.087\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:21:51.560 --\u003e 00:21:53.562\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E58 - The Demon's Quest, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.814 --\u003e 00:00:24.816\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:06.400 --\u003e 00:01:08.402\r\nBATMAN: Previously on Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:12.739 --\u003e 00:01:14.491\r\nWho are you?\r\nHow did you get in here?\r\n\r\n00:01:14.908 --\u003e 00:01:18.036\r\nI am he who is\r\ncalled Ra's al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:01:18.537 --\u003e 00:01:21.456\r\nYour ward was abducted on the\r\nsame night as my daughter.\r\n\r\n00:01:21.957 --\u003e 00:01:23.625\r\nYou're Talia's father?\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:25.042\r\nMy time is short.\r\n\r\n00:01:25.043 --\u003e 00:01:28.547\r\nI need a man to assume my\r\nposition when I am gone.\r\n\r\n00:01:29.047 --\u003e 00:01:32.259\r\nBATMAN: But why me?\r\nRA'S: Because you are most worthy.\r\n\r\n00:01:32.342 --\u003e 00:01:34.636\r\nAnd because my precious\r\ndaughter loves you.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.137 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n- Forget it.\r\n- Then this means we must be enemies!\r\n\r\n00:01:39.057 --\u003e 00:01:41.310\r\nYou will regret this\r\ninsult, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.060 --\u003e 00:01:43.937\r\nYOU will... (COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.063 --\u003e 00:01:46.732\r\nWe must take him\r\nto the Lazarus Pit.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.952 --\u003e 00:02:00.287\r\n(RA'S LAUGHING EVILLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:09.087 --\u003e 00:02:10.547\r\n(TALIA GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.926 --\u003e 00:02:17.095\r\nPut her down, Ra's. Now!\r\n\r\n00:02:21.808 --\u003e 00:02:24.186\r\nNo, Father! Ah!\r\n\r\n00:02:24.519 --\u003e 00:02:26.313\r\nWe must stop him.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.105 --\u003e 00:02:30.192\r\nThe chemicals can revive the dying\r\nbut will kill a healthy person.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.317 --\u003e 00:02:31.401\r\nI get it, I get it.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.405 --\u003e 00:02:36.782\r\nTALIA: No!\r\n\r\n00:02:39.743 --\u003e 00:02:40.994\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:44.373 --\u003e 00:02:45.374\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:02:48.168 --\u003e 00:02:49.795\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:53.340 --\u003e 00:02:54.383\r\nStay back.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.926 --\u003e 00:02:57.206\r\nTALIA: I can handle this myself.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.389 --\u003e 00:03:01.598\r\n(BREATH ES HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:03:05.018 --\u003e 00:03:06.061\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:03:14.986 --\u003e 00:03:16.405\r\nRA'S: Thank you, daughter.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.740 --\u003e 00:03:21.785\r\nAnd thank you, Detective,\r\nfor my daughter's life.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.327 --\u003e 00:03:24.204\r\nYou look refreshed, Father.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.329 --\u003e 00:03:25.831\r\nRenewed.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.165 --\u003e 00:03:31.628\r\nBut even a miracle such as the\r\nLazarus Pit has its terrible price.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.421 --\u003e 00:03:35.172\r\nYes. It offers\r\nphysical rejuvenation\r\n\r\n00:03:35.173 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nbut the stress of the transformation\r\nleaves one temporarily insane.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.177 --\u003e 00:03:42.180\r\nAnd no man may reap its\r\nblessings indefinitely.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.014 --\u003e 00:03:45.183\r\nWhich is why I must ask you\r\nagain, Detective,\r\n\r\n00:03:45.434 --\u003e 00:03:48.895\r\nwill you wed my daughter and\r\ncarry on for me when I am gone?\r\n\r\n00:03:51.606 --\u003e 00:03:54.025\r\nThe answer is still no.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.610 --\u003e 00:03:58.196\r\nA pity. You leave me no choice.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.780 --\u003e 00:04:00.198\r\n- (SNAPS FINGERS)\r\n- (GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:04:00.574 --\u003e 00:04:03.201\r\nRA'S: You see,\r\nif you are not with me, Detective,\r\n\r\n00:04:03.702 --\u003e 00:04:05.579\r\nyou are against me.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.662 --\u003e 00:04:07.205\r\nFather, no!\r\n\r\n00:04:07.414 --\u003e 00:04:09.249\r\nHe has seen too\r\nmany of our secrets.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.374 --\u003e 00:04:11.793\r\nHe knows too much to be\r\npermitted to leave here.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.468 --\u003e 00:04:22.596\r\nBut you would destroy this\r\nplace, our home?\r\n\r\n00:04:22.679 --\u003e 00:04:24.097\r\nOnly a minor loss.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.222 --\u003e 00:04:27.476\r\nThere is nothing here that cannot\r\nbe found in our desert stronghold.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.642 --\u003e 00:04:30.854\r\nAnd we must leave nothing behind\r\nthat might be later used against us.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.233 --\u003e 00:04:36.276\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:43.533 --\u003e 00:04:45.452\r\nFarewell, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.911 --\u003e 00:04:48.038\r\nGoodbye, beloved.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.253 --\u003e 00:04:56.254\r\n(BOTH YELL)\r\n\r\n00:05:02.302 --\u003e 00:05:04.137\r\nRobin! The rope!\r\n\r\n00:05:09.267 --\u003e 00:05:10.268\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.460 --\u003e 00:05:36.878\r\nCome on!\r\n\r\n00:05:37.295 --\u003e 00:05:38.296\r\n(ROBIN YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:55.188 --\u003e 00:05:57.774\r\n- (EXHALES) You okay?\r\n- Sure.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.024 --\u003e 00:06:01.027\r\nI wish I'd worn the thermal\r\ntights, but other than that...\r\n\r\n00:06:07.492 --\u003e 00:06:09.327\r\nBy the time we get\r\ndown this mountain,\r\n\r\n00:06:09.703 --\u003e 00:06:13.330\r\nhe could be halfway to his desert\r\nstronghold, wherever that is.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.331 --\u003e 00:06:15.959\r\nThen we've gotta find out where.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.042 --\u003e 00:06:17.168\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:17.252 --\u003e 00:06:21.339\r\nHe's going to realize his dream of a\r\ngreen and balanced Earth at any cost.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.132 --\u003e 00:06:25.635\r\nEven if that means destroying half\r\nthe planet's population to do it.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.344 --\u003e 00:06:28.013\r\nROBIN: But where do\r\nwe even start looking?\r\n\r\n00:06:28.346 --\u003e 00:06:30.181\r\nBATMAN: You were his\r\nprisoner for a week.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.265 --\u003e 00:06:31.933\r\nYou must have\r\noverheard something.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.350 --\u003e 00:06:34.185\r\nWell, there was one thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.269 --\u003e 00:06:38.940\r\nA word I heard several times.\r\nIt was, uh... (STUTTERS)\r\n\r\n00:06:39.858 --\u003e 00:06:42.027\r\nOrpheus. Yeah, that's it.\r\n\r\n00:06:56.958 --\u003e 00:06:59.377\r\nOrpheus. From Greek mythology.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.003 --\u003e 00:07:03.673\r\nHe descended into the netherworld to\r\nbring his beloved back from the dead.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.798 --\u003e 00:07:05.300\r\nBut according to the database,\r\n\r\n00:07:05.383 --\u003e 00:07:08.385\r\nOrpheus is also the name of\r\na privately-owned satellite\r\n\r\n00:07:08.386 --\u003e 00:07:11.388\r\nlaunched into synchronous\r\norbit over a year ago.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.389 --\u003e 00:07:14.809\r\n- Coincidence?\r\n- Yeah, right.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.268 --\u003e 00:07:16.454\r\nDICK: What's it orbiting over?\r\n\r\n00:07:16.478 --\u003e 00:07:18.396\r\nBRUCE: What else? A desert.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.855 --\u003e 00:07:20.649\r\nThe Sahara desert.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.024 --\u003e 00:07:24.903\r\nAnd the exact coordinates have to\r\nbe Ra's al Ghul's desert stronghold.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.200 --\u003e 00:07:32.494\r\nWe're within 100 kilometers\r\nof the target area, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.619 --\u003e 00:07:36.039\r\nGotta hold her steady at 500\r\nfeet to stay under their radar,\r\n\r\n00:07:36.331 --\u003e 00:07:38.249\r\nbut you can still\r\neject at this altitude.\r\n\r\n00:07:38.333 --\u003e 00:07:39.668\r\nThen let's do it.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.749 --\u003e 00:08:21.084\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.501 --\u003e 00:08:22.627\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:08:27.298 --\u003e 00:08:29.509\r\n(CHUCKLES) Huh?\r\n\r\n00:08:33.471 --\u003e 00:08:34.472\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.506 --\u003e 00:09:10.717\r\nSo you have finally arrived.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.968 --\u003e 00:09:13.678\r\nHitch your mounts and follow me.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.762 --\u003e 00:09:15.889\r\nWe must not keep\r\nthe master waiting.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.181 --\u003e 00:09:18.767\r\n- Quickly. Our time grows short.\r\n- (CAMELS GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:24.230 --\u003e 00:09:27.525\r\nYou there! Did you not hear me?\r\nWhat is the matter with...\r\n\r\n00:09:30.570 --\u003e 00:09:31.780\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:09:47.545 --\u003e 00:09:48.838\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.924 --\u003e 00:09:52.842\r\nSo my eyes did not deceive me.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.635 --\u003e 00:09:55.720\r\nYou will pay for this trespass.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.613 --\u003e 00:10:14.656\r\n(MAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:10:18.660 --\u003e 00:10:19.994\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:23.581 --\u003e 00:10:24.582\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:10:30.463 --\u003e 00:10:34.676\r\nFor this indignity,\r\nI will see you suffer.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.969 --\u003e 00:10:37.387\r\nRA'S: Enough!\r\n\r\n00:10:39.639 --\u003e 00:10:41.975\r\nWhat is the meaning of\r\nthis disturbance, Ubu?\r\n\r\n00:10:43.601 --\u003e 00:10:47.772\r\nForgive me, master, but I discovered\r\nthis most unworthy one spying.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.231 --\u003e 00:10:52.861\r\nOh? I believe I would have a\r\ncloser look at one so foolish.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.197 --\u003e 00:10:57.323\r\nOr so brave.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.615 --\u003e 00:10:58.658\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:02.912 --\u003e 00:11:05.622\r\n- You.\r\n- My admiration for you\r\n\r\n00:11:05.623 --\u003e 00:11:07.584\r\nwas well-founded, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.667 --\u003e 00:11:09.836\r\nToo bad I can't say the same.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.253 --\u003e 00:11:13.256\r\n- Shall I dispatch him, master?\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.548 --\u003e 00:11:16.259\r\nFor now, merely relieve him\r\nof that cumbersome belt.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.554 --\u003e 00:11:23.224\r\nOh, and search him.\r\nMake certain that he conceals no surprises\r\n\r\n00:11:23.308 --\u003e 00:11:25.643\r\nwhich might enable\r\nhim to escape.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.019 --\u003e 00:11:27.270\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:27.353 --\u003e 00:11:29.939\r\nYou have nothing to lose by\r\ntelling me what you're doing here.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.649 --\u003e 00:11:33.860\r\nYes, I suppose I do owe you that\r\nmuch, Detective,\r\n\r\n00:11:33.943 --\u003e 00:11:36.738\r\nsince, in many ways,\r\nyou are responsible for it.\r\n\r\n00:11:36.863 --\u003e 00:11:38.655\r\nYou see,\r\nI had hoped to achieve my vision\r\n\r\n00:11:38.656 --\u003e 00:11:41.534\r\nof an earthly utopia\r\ngradually over time,\r\n\r\n00:11:41.910 --\u003e 00:11:45.496\r\nwith my heir carrying on\r\nmy work after I was gone.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.580 --\u003e 00:11:49.375\r\nBut your refusal to become my\r\nheir has left me no other choice.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.876 --\u003e 00:11:52.086\r\n- His mask, master?\r\n- No, leave it.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.170 --\u003e 00:11:53.963\r\nIt is a mark of honor.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.506 --\u003e 00:11:59.344\r\nEven though because of him, I must\r\nnow use what I call the Lazarus effect\r\n\r\n00:11:59.469 --\u003e 00:12:02.305\r\nto achieve my utopia\r\nin one bold stroke.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.680 --\u003e 00:12:03.890\r\nBATMAN: How?\r\n\r\n00:12:05.683 --\u003e 00:12:06.684\r\n(HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:11.105 --\u003e 00:12:14.275\r\nRA'S: The material of the pit\r\nis an unknown chemical stew\r\n\r\n00:12:14.359 --\u003e 00:12:17.694\r\nthat bubbles to the Earth's\r\nsurface only at certain key places.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.695 --\u003e 00:12:21.366\r\nEven now my people are placing\r\nbombs, such as that one,\r\n\r\n00:12:21.491 --\u003e 00:12:24.285\r\nover the various Lazarus\r\nPits around the world.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.535 --\u003e 00:12:26.621\r\nThese bombs are\r\nelectronically linked\r\n\r\n00:12:26.704 --\u003e 00:12:29.707\r\n\u003ci\u003eto a private satellite\r\nalready in Earth orbit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:30.708 --\u003e 00:12:32.710\r\n- Orpheus.\r\n- Precisely.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.919 --\u003e 00:12:35.712\r\nAnd at the moment when sun and\r\nmoon are in proper alignment\r\n\r\n00:12:35.713 --\u003e 00:12:38.715\r\nto cause the greatest upheaval\r\nin Earth's geomagnetic field,\r\n\r\n00:12:38.716 --\u003e 00:12:42.178\r\nI shall send a signal to that\r\nsatellite beginning a countdown.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.720 --\u003e 00:12:45.014\r\nFive minutes thereafter,\r\none \u003ci\u003ebomb will\u003c/i\u003e be lowered\r\n\r\n00:12:45.139 --\u003e 00:12:47.558\r\n\u003ci\u003edeep into the heart of each pit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:47.809 --\u003e 00:12:51.104\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe satellite will, in turn,\r\nrelay a microwave signal\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:51.187 --\u003e 00:12:54.190\r\n\u003ci\u003ethat will detonate all\r\nthe bombs simultaneously.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:54.399 --\u003e 00:12:58.444\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe multiple explosions will\r\nresult in a global chain reaction.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:58.736 --\u003e 00:13:02.031\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll the Lazarus Pits throughout\r\nthe world will overflow.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:02.365 --\u003e 00:13:05.451\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe globe will be saturated\r\nwith their chemical solution.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:05.743 --\u003e 00:13:08.705\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd when the resultant\r\ncataclysm has abated,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:08.788 --\u003e 00:13:10.832\r\nthere \u003ci\u003ewill come\u003c/i\u003e a blessed peace.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.207 --\u003e 00:13:14.252\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd this poor, defiled planet\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:14.377 --\u003e 00:13:19.549\r\n\u003ci\u003eshall find itself restored\r\nto its former pristine glory.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:19.799 --\u003e 00:13:22.677\r\nBut that will cost\r\ncountless lives.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.969 --\u003e 00:13:25.430\r\nActually, Detective,\r\nwe have counted.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.763 --\u003e 00:13:30.059\r\nTwo billion, fifty-six million,\r\nnine hundred and eighty-six thousand.\r\n\r\n00:13:31.602 --\u003e 00:13:34.605\r\nA most impressive plan,\r\nwould you not agree?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.189 --\u003e 00:13:39.193\r\nYes, I can see it clearly\r\nnow for the first time.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.404 --\u003e 00:13:44.782\r\nYou are completely\r\nout of your mind.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.452 --\u003e 00:13:49.203\r\nInfidel dog.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.204 --\u003e 00:13:51.247\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.793 --\u003e 00:13:58.963\r\nThis time I shall attend\r\nto you personally.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.226 --\u003e 00:14:13.227\r\nRA'S: Ubu.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.645 --\u003e 00:14:18.900\r\nI would prefer the detective live to\r\nwitness the realization of my dream.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.070 --\u003e 00:14:26.449\r\nTake him to the tower to\r\nawait my moment of triumph.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.824 --\u003e 00:14:28.701\r\nAs you wish, master.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.748 --\u003e 00:14:34.832\r\nTALIA: Wait.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.047 --\u003e 00:14:43.341\r\nTo remember me, beloved.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.683 --\u003e 00:14:55.853\r\nNot so dangerous without\r\nyour precious belt, are you?\r\n\r\n00:15:04.570 --\u003e 00:15:06.572\r\nOne can only wonder\r\nwhy the master thought\r\n\r\n00:15:06.697 --\u003e 00:15:09.075\r\nit would require two\r\nof us to guard him.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.784 --\u003e 00:15:10.910\r\n(BOTH YELL)\r\n\r\n00:15:18.459 --\u003e 00:15:23.589\r\nMy children, we stand on the\r\nthreshold of a great adventure.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.714 --\u003e 00:15:27.301\r\nEven now, the satellite Orpheus\r\nis moving into proper alignment\r\n\r\n00:15:27.385 --\u003e 00:15:30.513\r\nand the moment of destiny\r\nis finally upon us.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.888 --\u003e 00:15:32.265\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:36.894 --\u003e 00:15:38.396\r\nFather, it is not too late.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.896 --\u003e 00:15:40.897\r\nSurely there must\r\nbe some other way.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.898 --\u003e 00:15:43.526\r\nNo, daughter.\r\nThe decision has been made.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.381 --\u003e 00:16:06.507\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:07.592 --\u003e 00:16:10.511\r\nIn five minutes,\r\nthe world will be forever changed.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.929 --\u003e 00:16:13.222\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:16:16.934 --\u003e 00:16:17.935\r\n(MUFFLED SHOUT)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.205 --\u003e 00:16:38.581\r\n(CHEERING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:17:00.353 --\u003e 00:17:01.979\r\nUBU: Master.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.274 --\u003e 00:17:08.486\r\nStop him! He'll ruin everything!\r\n\r\n00:17:09.403 --\u003e 00:17:10.404\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:15.910 --\u003e 00:17:17.036\r\nInfidel.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.789 --\u003e 00:17:23.167\r\nIf you only knew how sick I\r\nam of you calling me that.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.009 --\u003e 00:17:33.010\r\n(UBU GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:34.262 --\u003e 00:17:38.683\r\nPerhaps, Detective, it is time\r\nthat you and I finally finish this.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.849 --\u003e 00:17:42.061\r\nIt is the only chance you will\r\nhave to stop that satellite.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.855 --\u003e 00:17:46.023\r\nWell?\r\n\r\n00:17:47.733 --\u003e 00:17:51.445\r\n- Are you man enough to face your better?\r\n- If you insist.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.912 --\u003e 00:18:00.913\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:18:04.917 --\u003e 00:18:06.043\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:23.477 --\u003e 00:18:24.854\r\n(SWORDS CLANGING)\r\n\r\n00:18:28.733 --\u003e 00:18:31.319\r\nGive it up, Ra's.\r\nYou'll destroy yourself.\r\n\r\n00:18:33.112 --\u003e 00:18:34.280\r\n(RA'S GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:39.285 --\u003e 00:18:42.079\r\nIt appears that we will both\r\nperish together, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.088 --\u003e 00:18:53.132\r\nAccept it. You have no choice.\r\n\r\n00:19:02.099 --\u003e 00:19:03.142\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:08.397 --\u003e 00:19:09.565\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:24.330 --\u003e 00:19:25.414\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:30.503 --\u003e 00:19:31.587\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:36.634 --\u003e 00:19:37.843\r\nGive me your hand.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.976 --\u003e 00:19:47.019\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:47.812 --\u003e 00:19:49.855\r\nVictory is yours, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:54.985\r\nPerhaps it is time I am finally\r\none with the planet I so love.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.186 --\u003e 00:20:31.187\r\nYou must understand, beloved,\r\n\r\n00:20:31.188 --\u003e 00:20:33.816\r\nI share my father's vision\r\nand seek the same ends\r\n\r\n00:20:33.899 --\u003e 00:20:36.360\r\nbut I do not choose his\r\nmeans to those ends.\r\n\r\n00:20:36.444 --\u003e 00:20:37.987\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:20:48.289 --\u003e 00:20:50.206\r\nWhat's to become of me, then?\r\n\r\n00:20:50.207 --\u003e 00:20:51.876\r\nAm I to be your prisoner?\r\n\r\n00:21:13.397 --\u003e 00:21:16.734\r\nSo it's finally over?\r\nWe've seen the last of Ra's al Ghul?\r\n\r\n00:21:17.234 --\u003e 00:21:19.028\r\nLooks that way.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.504 --\u003e 00:21:38.923\r\n(RA'S LAUGHING EVILLY)\r\n\r\n00:21:48.057 --\u003e 00:21:50.059\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E59 - Read My Lips (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:18.185 --\u003e 00:00:20.229\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:15.617 --\u003e 00:01:17.286\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.375 --\u003e 00:01:26.211\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.678 --\u003e 00:01:35.721\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:01:48.817 --\u003e 00:01:50.152\r\nNot a bad night's take.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.962 --\u003e 00:02:11.149\r\nMAN 1: What happened to the lights?\r\nMAN 2: What the heck?\r\n\r\n00:02:11.173 --\u003e 00:02:12.758\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:25.604 --\u003e 00:02:26.688\r\nHere.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.401 --\u003e 00:02:32.778\r\nPut them on. Hurry.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.139 --\u003e 00:03:02.432\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:05.352 --\u003e 00:03:06.561\r\nNow.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.922 --\u003e 00:03:37.259\r\nIt went down smooth, Scarf\r\nace, just like you said.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.676 --\u003e 00:03:42.222\r\nThat's just the beginning, boys.\r\nSoon we're gonna own this town.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.946 --\u003e 00:03:59.406\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:06.872 --\u003e 00:04:07.873\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:04:07.956 --\u003e 00:04:10.250\r\nHave pity on an old\r\nman's blood pressure.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.333 --\u003e 00:04:11.543\r\nWhat is it, Jim?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.626 --\u003e 00:04:14.129\r\nWe're taking a pounding\r\nover this new gang.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.212 --\u003e 00:04:17.591\r\nTheir boss puts heists together\r\nsmooth as a Swiss watchmaker.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.674 --\u003e 00:04:19.968\r\n- What have you got for me?\r\n- Not much.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.051 --\u003e 00:04:22.721\r\nWe don't know who the boss is\r\nor any of the gang members.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.804 --\u003e 00:04:25.098\r\nBut a home video\r\nenthusiast taped the gang\r\n\r\n00:04:25.182 --\u003e 00:04:27.058\r\nleaving the scene of\r\ntheir latest crime.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.225 --\u003e 00:04:29.269\r\n- Interested?\r\n- Always.\r\n\r\n00:04:31.772 --\u003e 00:04:34.900\r\nLet me know if you need any...\r\nHelp?\r\n\r\n00:04:50.999 --\u003e 00:04:53.293\r\nNot much of a plot, is it, sir?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.303 --\u003e 00:05:07.849\r\nThey're clever. Masks, gloves.\r\nNo way they can be identified.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.861 --\u003e 00:05:21.488\r\nA tattoo.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.480 --\u003e 00:05:57.732\r\nWho you looking for, bat-breath?\r\n\r\n00:05:57.816 --\u003e 00:05:59.818\r\nFirst guess is you.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.901 --\u003e 00:06:01.611\r\nDon't get wise with me.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.695 --\u003e 00:06:03.196\r\nI might not like you.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.530 --\u003e 00:06:05.824\r\nYou're breaking my heart, Rhino.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.907 --\u003e 00:06:07.576\r\nI ain't scared of you,\r\n\r\n00:06:07.659 --\u003e 00:06:10.287\r\nbut you ain't gonna trick me\r\ninto taking a swing at you.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.370 --\u003e 00:06:11.997\r\nYou got nothing on me.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:15.083\r\nYou seem to have me confused\r\nwith the police, Rhino.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.166 --\u003e 00:06:18.670\r\nI want information,\r\nand I'll get it any way I please.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.753 --\u003e 00:06:20.046\r\nWho's your boss?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.422 --\u003e 00:06:23.174\r\nYou want information,\r\nwatch the news.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.050 --\u003e 00:06:25.051\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:35.562 --\u003e 00:06:37.272\r\nYou've got a hard head.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.355 --\u003e 00:06:40.066\r\nHow about using it for something\r\nother than a blunt object?\r\n\r\n00:06:42.277 --\u003e 00:06:43.278\r\n(SIREN WHOOPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:50.118 --\u003e 00:06:53.038\r\nWell, if it isn't\r\nCharles \"Rhino\" Daly.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.289 --\u003e 00:06:58.251\r\n- Why don't you run along home?\r\n- Your ma's probably waiting up.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.423 --\u003e 00:07:07.302\r\n(EXHALES IN RELIEF) Guy like that,\r\nI'm not so sure a bullet would stop him.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.385 --\u003e 00:07:09.721\r\nHey, I'm not so sure\r\na tank would stop him.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.613 --\u003e 00:07:28.031\r\nI gotta see the boss.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.033 --\u003e 00:07:33.536\r\n(WHIMPERING) He's sleeping.\r\nHe said he's not to be disturbed.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.162 --\u003e 00:07:37.540\r\nHey, man, it's important.\r\nBatman's on our case.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.624 --\u003e 00:07:40.001\r\nI see. I'll see what I can do.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.676 --\u003e 00:07:50.261\r\nSir, I'm terribly sorry.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.345 --\u003e 00:07:52.555\r\n\u003ci\u003eSCARF ACE: Hey,\r\nI'm shaping here.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:52.639 --\u003e 00:07:55.809\r\nI lay down, I close my\r\neyes, what's that tell you?\r\n\r\n00:07:55.892 --\u003e 00:07:58.436\r\nVENTRILOQUIST: Yes, sir,\r\nbut Rhino says it's important.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.937 --\u003e 00:08:01.856\r\nSCARFACE: Oh,\r\nRhino says it's important, huh?\r\n\r\n00:08:02.273 --\u003e 00:08:05.235\r\nWell, it better be or there's\r\ngonna be fireworks, get me?\r\n\r\n00:08:05.819 --\u003e 00:08:07.862\r\nOkay, take me out there.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.328 --\u003e 00:08:17.914\r\nThis better be good, yous mugs.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:30.719\r\nOkay, talk, Rhino. What's so important\r\nI can't get a good night's sleep?\r\n\r\n00:08:30.802 --\u003e 00:08:33.680\r\nEh, Batman's got me\r\nfigured, Scarf ace.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.763 --\u003e 00:08:37.976\r\nI don't know how, but he came\r\ndown on me like a cast-iron safe.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.059 --\u003e 00:08:41.354\r\nBatman? We're talking real trouble.\r\nWhat are we gonna-\r\n\r\n00:08:41.438 --\u003e 00:08:44.232\r\nHey, hey!\r\nWho you talking to, creep?\r\n\r\n00:08:44.315 --\u003e 00:08:46.151\r\nHe's just the hired help.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.234 --\u003e 00:08:48.820\r\nI'm the boss here.\r\nYou talk to me.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.487 --\u003e 00:08:52.657\r\nSorry, boss. He's new.\r\nHe don't know the score.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.741 --\u003e 00:08:55.160\r\nYeah, well, he better get\r\nwith the program pretty quick.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.243 --\u003e 00:08:57.579\r\nI don't stand for\r\nno lack of respect.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.079 --\u003e 00:09:01.207\r\nThis Batman business\r\ncan only mean one thing.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.833 --\u003e 00:09:04.711\r\nWe got us a squealer.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.545 --\u003e 00:09:07.505\r\nNo, boss, that can't be.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.589 --\u003e 00:09:10.425\r\nNone of us wanna screw up\r\na sweet deal like this.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.508 --\u003e 00:09:12.427\r\nGlad to hear it, Mugsy,\r\n\r\n00:09:12.510 --\u003e 00:09:16.181\r\n'cause if there is and I find\r\nhim, it's drapes for that rat!\r\n\r\n00:09:16.264 --\u003e 00:09:18.933\r\nVENTRILOQUIST: Now, Mr. Scarf\r\nace, remember your blood pressure.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.476 --\u003e 00:09:23.605\r\nShut up! I want your opinion,\r\ndummy, I'll pull your string.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.149 --\u003e 00:09:30.820\r\nHe's just tired. Irritable.\r\nHe's really a genius, Scarf ace is.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.362 --\u003e 00:09:33.740\r\nYou mean the\r\nVentriloquist is a genius.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.240 --\u003e 00:09:37.869\r\nNah. Like Scarf ace said,\r\nhe's just hired help.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.952 --\u003e 00:09:40.413\r\nScarf ace, he's the real brains.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.947 --\u003e 00:10:15.115\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:49.732 --\u003e 00:10:51.234\r\nMr. Scarf ace?\r\n\r\n00:10:57.740 --\u003e 00:10:58.741\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:05.331 --\u003e 00:11:08.501\r\nMy advice to you?\r\nDon't make a sound.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.460 --\u003e 00:11:10.920\r\nI'm looking for evidence.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.379 --\u003e 00:11:13.423\r\nEvidence of your\r\nprevious robberies.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.007 --\u003e 00:11:17.093\r\n- (STAMMERS) Robberies?\r\n- Don't be coy.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.177 --\u003e 00:11:19.304\r\nCooperate and it could\r\ngo easier for you.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.762 --\u003e 00:11:21.222\r\nHe...\r\nHe doesn't tell me anything.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.306 --\u003e 00:11:23.349\r\nNot his plans,\r\nnot where he hides the loot.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.433 --\u003e 00:11:25.977\r\nI swear I'm just a flunky.\r\nI know nothing.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.311 --\u003e 00:11:30.106\r\nYou can think I'm dumb,\r\njust don't talk to me like I'm dumb.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.648 --\u003e 00:11:34.235\r\nI don't know anything, I tell you.\r\nLet me go before he-\r\n\r\n00:11:34.319 --\u003e 00:11:38.489\r\nSCARFACE: Hey, who's making all the racket?\r\nThat you, dummy?\r\n\r\n00:11:39.115 --\u003e 00:11:44.204\r\nOh, no. Don't let him find me with you.\r\nYou don't know how dangerous he is.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.287 --\u003e 00:11:46.372\r\nHe sees me talking to\r\nyou, I'm a goner.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.456 --\u003e 00:11:47.665\r\nPlease.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.458 --\u003e 00:11:50.084\r\nSCARFACE: Dummy, get in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.255 --\u003e 00:11:56.507\r\nVENTRILOQUIST: Sorry,\r\nMr. Scarf ace, I couldn't sleep.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.925 --\u003e 00:12:01.054\r\nSCARFACE: I need my beauty rest here,\r\ndummy. That's twice you waked me up.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.512 --\u003e 00:12:05.475\r\nDo it again, you're gonna be\r\nwearing a pine overcoat, get me?\r\n\r\n00:12:08.770 --\u003e 00:12:09.896\r\nYou're sweating.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.979 --\u003e 00:12:12.273\r\nWhat's going on?\r\nAnd don't feed me no apples.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.857 --\u003e 00:12:15.818\r\nNothing, sir.\r\nI was just having a bad dream.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.902 --\u003e 00:12:18.112\r\nWhat did you leave\r\nthat window open for?\r\n\r\n00:12:18.196 --\u003e 00:12:20.865\r\nThis ain't no meat locker.\r\nI'm cold.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.949 --\u003e 00:12:22.867\r\nYes, sir,\r\nI'll shut it right now.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.925 --\u003e 00:12:42.220\r\nIt's called multiple personality\r\nsyndrome disorder, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.303 --\u003e 00:12:45.640\r\nTwo personalities in one\r\nbrain, completely separate.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.140 --\u003e 00:12:49.060\r\nNeither one knows what the\r\nother is thinking. Listen.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.478 --\u003e 00:12:52.105\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"SCARFACE\". Batman's so hot,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:52.188 --\u003e 00:12:55.775\r\n\u003ci\u003elet's see him swim Gotham\r\nBay in concrete boots.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:57.902 --\u003e 00:13:00.071\r\nVENTRILOQUIST: \u003ci\u003eA good\u003c/i\u003e\r\nidea, Mr. Scarf ace.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.154 --\u003e 00:13:04.492\r\n\u003ci\u003eSCARFACE: Bet your bow tie I'm right,\r\ndummy. Say, who dresses you anyway?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:05.576 --\u003e 00:13:08.997\r\nVENTRILOQUIST: (CHUCKLES) You're\r\nsuch a kidder, Mr. Scarf ace.\r\n\r\n00:13:09.664 --\u003e 00:13:12.208\r\nI'd swear it was\r\ntwo separate people.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.042 --\u003e 00:13:15.586\r\nYou're not alone.\r\nEven the computer is fooled.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.129 --\u003e 00:13:18.298\r\nWhen I studied with\r\nZatara the magician,\r\n\r\n00:13:18.381 --\u003e 00:13:21.259\r\nhe taught me about ventriloquism\r\nand voice-throwing.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.467 --\u003e 00:13:24.095\r\nHow to make your voice seem\r\nto come from across the room.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.429 --\u003e 00:13:26.848\r\nThis Ventriloquist could\r\ngive Zatara lessons.\r\n\r\n00:13:27.515 --\u003e 00:13:32.312\r\nYou've had your share of odd opponents,\r\nsir, but this one does take the biscuit.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.687 --\u003e 00:13:36.232\r\nAny idea where he, or\r\nthey, will strike next?\r\n\r\n00:13:36.316 --\u003e 00:13:39.819\r\nNo. Scarf ace keeps his plans\r\nsecret until the last minute.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.194 --\u003e 00:13:43.281\r\nI'll just have to listen\r\nin for as long as it takes.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.073 --\u003e 00:13:46.826\r\nAll right, yous\r\nmugs, listen good.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.118 --\u003e 00:13:51.497\r\nThere's a shipment of platinum gonna be\r\nloaded onto the luxury liner Majestic.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.040 --\u003e 00:13:53.624\r\n- We're gonna- - But, platinum?\r\n\r\n00:13:53.708 --\u003e 00:13:56.586\r\nBut, boss, don't they send\r\nstuff like that by freighter?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.964 --\u003e 00:14:02.175\r\nI'm talking here!\r\n\r\n00:14:02.258 --\u003e 00:14:04.510\r\nOkay, okay. Sorry, boss.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.053 --\u003e 00:14:10.767\r\nIt's a trick, see? They think no one\r\nwill suspect the shipment's on a liner.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.184 --\u003e 00:14:13.519\r\nBut they're like yous mugs.\r\nStupid.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.603 --\u003e 00:14:15.480\r\nNot smart like me.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.855 --\u003e 00:14:17.982\r\nWe'll slip in,\r\nget the goods and skedaddle\r\n\r\n00:14:18.066 --\u003e 00:14:19.859\r\nbefore the ship\r\nleaves the harbor.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.234 --\u003e 00:14:21.361\r\nOne more thing.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.986 --\u003e 00:14:23.946\r\nI smell a double-cross.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.322 --\u003e 00:14:27.325\r\nWoke up last night with one\r\nof them whatchamacallits.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.408 --\u003e 00:14:29.369\r\nPrima... Primanotion.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.911 --\u003e 00:14:32.997\r\n- \"Premonition\"?\r\n- Don't put words in my mouth!\r\n\r\n00:14:33.581 --\u003e 00:14:36.000\r\nAll I'm saying here\r\nis I got this feeling\r\n\r\n00:14:36.084 --\u003e 00:14:38.294\r\nsomebody here is out to get me.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.378 --\u003e 00:14:40.880\r\nAnd I'm gonna get them first.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.464 --\u003e 00:14:43.841\r\nI don't know who it is\r\nyet, but I will.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.175 --\u003e 00:14:45.718\r\nAnd when I do...\r\n\r\n00:14:45.802 --\u003e 00:14:46.803\r\n(IMITATES CUTTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:47.553 --\u003e 00:14:52.600\r\nNow, here's the details. Listen up.\r\nI ain't gonna repeat myself.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.188 --\u003e 00:14:58.648\r\n(MOTOR BOAT APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:45.653 --\u003e 00:15:47.196\r\nYippee ki-yay.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.669 --\u003e 00:16:02.920\r\nUh-oh.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.463 --\u003e 00:16:04.464\r\n(MAN OUTSIDE GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.395 --\u003e 00:16:20.396\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.844 --\u003e 00:16:53.846\r\nSCARFACE: See?\r\nThe Bat's not so tough.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.930 --\u003e 00:16:56.891\r\nComes up against Scarf ace,\r\nhe's just another dummy.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.141 --\u003e 00:17:00.269\r\nIt was a trap, Bats,\r\nstart to finish.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.353 --\u003e 00:17:03.147\r\nAnd you fell for it like\r\na world-class sucker.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.773 --\u003e 00:17:06.859\r\nThe dummy here spilled the\r\nbeans you'd been in his room.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.735 --\u003e 00:17:11.030\r\nI had the room searched\r\nand lookie what I found.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.704 --\u003e 00:17:21.415\r\nYou're not as smart as you think you\r\nare, Scarf ace.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.499 --\u003e 00:17:24.252\r\nI'd watch my mouth if I were\r\nyou, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.710 --\u003e 00:17:27.380\r\nOne bullet through that\r\nrope and you're history.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.713 --\u003e 00:17:29.257\r\nGet my point?\r\n\r\n00:17:29.340 --\u003e 00:17:30.883\r\n(LAUGHS EVILLY)\r\n\r\n00:17:31.467 --\u003e 00:17:34.053\r\nHow do you think I found this place?\r\nThe phone book?\r\n\r\n00:17:34.136 --\u003e 00:17:36.681\r\nI had help. Inside help.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.223 --\u003e 00:17:39.976\r\nMy primanotion.\r\nI knew I was right.\r\n\r\n00:17:40.601 --\u003e 00:17:42.937\r\nWhich one of you louses is it?\r\n\r\n00:17:43.229 --\u003e 00:17:44.897\r\nIt ain't me, boss.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.231 --\u003e 00:17:48.859\r\nI know it ain't you, Rhino.\r\nYou're too stupid to be a traitor.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.943 --\u003e 00:17:50.361\r\nOoh, thanks, boss.\r\n\r\n00:17:50.778 --\u003e 00:17:54.699\r\nBut whoever it is, they're gonna pay!\r\nBig time! Who is it?\r\n\r\n00:17:54.782 --\u003e 00:17:57.743\r\nYou don't talk,\r\nyou get the ultimate massage.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.077 --\u003e 00:18:02.415\r\n- BATMAN: And If I tell?\r\n- Maybe you just get run over by a truck.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.498 --\u003e 00:18:05.084\r\nTempting, but no.\r\n\r\n00:18:05.167 --\u003e 00:18:07.128\r\nHave it your way. Rhino.\r\n\r\n00:18:11.424 --\u003e 00:18:13.884\r\nBATMAN: Hold it!\r\nSCARFACE: This is getting old, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.968 --\u003e 00:18:16.345\r\nLast chance. Who's the traitor?\r\n\r\n00:18:16.596 --\u003e 00:18:18.556\r\nHim, the Ventriloquist.\r\n\r\n00:18:20.725 --\u003e 00:18:24.520\r\nNo! No! He's lying.\r\nI told you when he came into my room.\r\n\r\n00:18:25.062 --\u003e 00:18:28.608\r\nSo what? Maybe you did\r\n'cause I had you cornered.\r\n\r\n00:18:28.691 --\u003e 00:18:30.443\r\nHeard you talking to Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.152 --\u003e 00:18:33.433\r\nBATMAN: (IN VENTRILOQUIST'S VOICE) Shut\r\nup, you blockhead.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.947 --\u003e 00:18:37.158\r\nWhat did you say?\r\n\r\n00:18:37.241 --\u003e 00:18:41.454\r\nIt wasn't me. I didn't say that.\r\nMy lips didn't move.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.954 --\u003e 00:18:44.415\r\nSo what? You're a ventriloquist.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.498 --\u003e 00:18:48.711\r\nYou're also a lying, yellow,\r\nliver-bellied, two-faced-\r\n\r\n00:18:48.794 --\u003e 00:18:52.465\r\nNo, Scarf ace, not me.\r\nI'm loyal. I'd never-\r\n\r\n00:18:52.548 --\u003e 00:18:56.177\r\nHe's been feeding me information\r\nin return for legal protection.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.260 --\u003e 00:18:59.180\r\n(IN VENTRILOQUIST'S VOICE) You're\r\ngoing up the river, sawdust-for-brains.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.639 --\u003e 00:19:02.933\r\nWhy, I ought to...\r\nWaste the four-flusher.\r\n\r\n00:19:03.017 --\u003e 00:19:06.854\r\nGo on. I gave an order.\r\nIce him. Do it! Do it now!\r\n\r\n00:19:07.521 --\u003e 00:19:12.360\r\nBut, boss, we ventilate the\r\nVentriloquist, you're, you know...\r\n\r\n00:19:12.443 --\u003e 00:19:14.695\r\nI'm surrounded by traitors.\r\n\r\n00:19:15.571 --\u003e 00:19:16.739\r\nOkay, fine.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.822 --\u003e 00:19:20.159\r\nYou want something done\r\nright, do it yourself.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.744 --\u003e 00:19:26.290\r\nSpare me, Scarf ace. Please.\r\nI've always been loyal to you.\r\n\r\n00:19:26.374 --\u003e 00:19:30.336\r\nGo ahead, plead, beg.\r\nIt ain't gonna do you no good.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.419 --\u003e 00:19:33.381\r\nYou're lunchmeat,\r\nyou lousy, no-Ah!\r\n\r\n00:19:34.507 --\u003e 00:19:36.759\r\nI'm hit, boys. Get him!\r\n\r\n00:19:54.026 --\u003e 00:19:55.361\r\nTake him, Rhino!\r\n\r\n00:19:55.695 --\u003e 00:19:57.113\r\nNo problem.\r\n\r\n00:20:00.574 --\u003e 00:20:01.659\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:35.651 --\u003e 00:20:36.652\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:44.034 --\u003e 00:20:45.035\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:54.086 --\u003e 00:20:55.087\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:02.386 --\u003e 00:21:03.387\r\nAh! (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:21:05.222 --\u003e 00:21:06.599\r\n(VENTRILOQUIST SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:21:20.571 --\u003e 00:21:22.615\r\nThe medication has\r\nhelped him immensely.\r\n\r\n00:21:22.782 --\u003e 00:21:26.118\r\nHis other personality seems\r\nto have totally submerged.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.331 --\u003e 00:21:33.125\r\n- That's very good work.\r\n- Thank you.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.143 --\u003e 00:21:53.145\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S01 E60 - Fire From Olympus (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:18.101 --\u003e 00:00:20.187\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.250 --\u003e 00:01:24.793\r\nWhat's keeping him?\r\n\r\n00:01:34.678 --\u003e 00:01:36.763\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:49.443 --\u003e 00:01:50.861\r\nCommissioner Gordon?\r\n\r\n00:01:51.111 --\u003e 00:01:52.279\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:56.116 --\u003e 00:01:59.119\r\n- Forget it, Stavros.\r\n- Your meeting's been canceled.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.252 --\u003e 00:02:08.587\r\nHe's on his way, boss.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.060 --\u003e 00:02:24.603\r\nNo! No!\r\n\r\n00:02:25.228 --\u003e 00:02:26.438\r\n(CRYING)\r\n\r\n00:02:27.272 --\u003e 00:02:29.483\r\n(CRYING HYSTERICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:38.659 --\u003e 00:02:41.912\r\nPlease, please.\r\nIt's not what you think.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.496 --\u003e 00:02:44.998\r\nI wasn't gonna say anything.\r\nHonest.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.082 --\u003e 00:02:46.458\r\nSilence!\r\n\r\n00:02:46.541 --\u003e 00:02:48.627\r\nFirst you transgress against me.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.086 --\u003e 00:02:52.214\r\nThen you force me to\r\ndescend to the mortal plane.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.297 --\u003e 00:02:55.634\r\nAnd now you say I\r\nknow not what I think?\r\n\r\n00:02:56.093 --\u003e 00:02:57.260\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:02:57.344 --\u003e 00:03:00.180\r\nTo the depths of\r\nTartarus with you.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.139 --\u003e 00:03:02.779\r\n- (THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n- (STAVROS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:14.695 --\u003e 00:03:18.281\r\nHe's a lucky guy. If those tires\r\nhadn't absorbed the shock, he-\r\n\r\n00:03:18.365 --\u003e 00:03:20.575\r\nJust a minute.\r\nThe weather was perfectly clear tonight,\r\n\r\n00:03:20.659 --\u003e 00:03:23.078\r\nand you're telling me that\r\nman was struck by lightning?\r\n\r\n00:03:23.453 --\u003e 00:03:26.832\r\nI guess you'll have to ask him\r\nwhat happened whenever he wakes up.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.591 --\u003e 00:03:38.760\r\nHis name is Yanni Stavros.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.844 --\u003e 00:03:41.304\r\nBATMAN: He works for\r\nMaximillian Shipping Lines.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.013 --\u003e 00:03:43.557\r\nAs a scheduler.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.640 --\u003e 00:03:46.601\r\n- You know him?\r\n- He's been under Interpol investigation\r\n\r\n00:03:46.685 --\u003e 00:03:49.563\r\nfor selling vital shipping\r\nschedules to hijackers.\r\n\r\n00:03:50.689 --\u003e 00:03:53.984\r\nThat fits. Stavros had offered\r\nto give me some information\r\n\r\n00:03:54.067 --\u003e 00:03:55.547\r\nso he could cut a\r\ndeal with the feds.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.821\r\nWhat kind of information?\r\n\r\n00:03:57.904 --\u003e 00:04:00.323\r\nEver hear of something\r\ncalled an EDC?\r\n\r\n00:04:00.907 --\u003e 00:04:02.534\r\nThe Electron Discharge Cannon.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.617 --\u003e 00:04:04.494\r\nA fourth-generation\r\nenergy weapon\r\n\r\n00:04:04.578 --\u003e 00:04:07.372\r\nbeing developed by a combined\r\nUS-European alliance.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.123 --\u003e 00:04:10.917\r\nThen you probably know this\r\nprototype was stolen last month\r\n\r\n00:04:11.001 --\u003e 00:04:12.669\r\nwhile it was being\r\nshipped overseas.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.044 --\u003e 00:04:14.605\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAN: (ON TV) This film\r\ncontains classified information\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:14.629 --\u003e 00:04:19.009\r\n\u003ci\u003eon defense project 406562,\r\nthe Electron Discharge Cannon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:19.426 --\u003e 00:04:21.011\r\n\u003ci\u003eFor authorized personnel only.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:21.470 --\u003e 00:04:25.140\r\nAnd you think Stavros was either\r\ninvolved in the theft or knows who was.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.640 --\u003e 00:04:27.601\r\n(CANNON POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:04:33.148 --\u003e 00:04:34.483\r\nGORDON: I pray that he does,\r\n\r\n00:04:34.566 --\u003e 00:04:37.569\r\nbecause if that infernal device\r\nfalls into the wrong hands...\r\n\r\n00:04:39.988 --\u003e 00:04:41.907\r\nMaybe it already has.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.039 --\u003e 00:04:50.999\r\nCLIO: The grand jury is\r\nbuilding another case,\r\n\r\n00:04:51.082 --\u003e 00:04:53.001\r\nand I can't stop them this time.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.084 --\u003e 00:04:56.505\r\nThere are allegations of bribery,\r\nextortion and racketeering,\r\n\r\n00:04:56.588 --\u003e 00:04:58.465\r\nall pointing back to you, Max.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.548 --\u003e 00:05:03.678\r\nSure, I'm your assistant, but there's\r\nonly so much I can do on my own.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.762 --\u003e 00:05:08.600\r\nMax? Maxie? Come on,\r\nlook at me when I'm talking to you.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.683 --\u003e 00:05:12.103\r\nYou bore me with these tales\r\nof petty human concerns.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.729 --\u003e 00:05:14.564\r\nYou're doing it again, Maxie.\r\n\r\n00:05:14.648 --\u003e 00:05:17.317\r\nYou are Clio,\r\nmy muse of history.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.901 --\u003e 00:05:20.070\r\nAmuse me with tales\r\nof ancient times,\r\n\r\n00:05:20.153 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nwhen mortals trembled\r\nat the name of Zeus.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.657 --\u003e 00:05:25.826\r\nYou want a story? I got one.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.368 --\u003e 00:05:27.828\r\nSeems there was\r\nthis guy named Max,\r\n\r\n00:05:27.911 --\u003e 00:05:30.872\r\nwho, because he had been lucky\r\nso far in the smuggling racket,\r\n\r\n00:05:30.956 --\u003e 00:05:35.252\r\nbelieved himself to be\r\nuntouchable, superior, godlike.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.378 --\u003e 00:05:39.381\r\nThere's a cynical edge to\r\nyour voice I don't appreciate.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.965 --\u003e 00:05:44.010\r\nKnow you not I am above mortal\r\nconstraints of right and wrong?\r\n\r\n00:05:44.094 --\u003e 00:05:46.304\r\nNo one is above the law, Max.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.307 --\u003e 00:05:51.351\r\nI make my own laws.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.145 --\u003e 00:05:57.440\r\nMaxie, please. Don't look at\r\nme as if you don't know me.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.235 --\u003e 00:06:03.029\r\nWhat's happened to you? To us?\r\n\r\n00:06:03.238 --\u003e 00:06:06.449\r\nAfter all we've been through together.\r\nAfter all we meant to-\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.243\r\n(AIR CRAFT WHINING)\r\n\r\n00:06:08.368 --\u003e 00:06:09.828\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:06:20.171 --\u003e 00:06:21.548\r\nWho dares?\r\n\r\n00:06:21.631 --\u003e 00:06:22.841\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.924 --\u003e 00:06:28.263\r\nLike the shadow of ebon-winged\r\nnight, he rises from the dark realm.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.346 --\u003e 00:06:32.601\r\nBehold, the coming of my\r\nbrother, Lord Hades!\r\n\r\n00:06:40.859 --\u003e 00:06:42.569\r\nWelcome, Lord Hades.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.652 --\u003e 00:06:45.530\r\nBe serious, Max. That's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.614 --\u003e 00:06:48.116\r\nBut Batman is a mere mortal.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.450 --\u003e 00:06:52.287\r\nAnd what mortal could reach the\r\nsummit of Mount Olympus and survive?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.579 --\u003e 00:06:56.666\r\nCome, dark brother.\r\nAvail yourself of the nectar of the gods.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.500 --\u003e 00:06:58.793\r\nNo, thanks.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.336 --\u003e 00:07:01.379\r\nI just want to ask you\r\na few questions about-\r\n\r\n00:07:01.463 --\u003e 00:07:06.593\r\nHold. The words of the gods are\r\nnot for the ears of mere muses.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.385 --\u003e 00:07:11.014\r\nYep, that's me, just a lowly muse.\r\nWhatever.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.475 --\u003e 00:07:15.727\r\nNow, my brother,\r\nwhat brings you to me?\r\n\r\n00:07:15.810 --\u003e 00:07:18.730\r\nHas Lord Vulcan been\r\ncausing you trouble again?\r\n\r\n00:07:22.901 --\u003e 00:07:24.444\r\nThe Batman? Upstairs?\r\n\r\n00:07:25.779 --\u003e 00:07:26.947\r\nWhat do we do?\r\n\r\n00:07:27.864 --\u003e 00:07:29.908\r\nIf His Lordship wants\r\nus, he'll holler.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.367 --\u003e 00:07:33.870\r\nYou're taking this too lightly, Alex.\r\nWe're in trouble.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.954 --\u003e 00:07:35.205\r\nMaxie's worse than ever.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.497 --\u003e 00:07:38.833\r\nWhen was the last time you saw him\r\nwear real clothes in the office?\r\n\r\n00:07:39.042 --\u003e 00:07:41.836\r\nYou know the boss and Greek stuff.\r\nIt's his thing.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.920 --\u003e 00:07:46.091\r\nWell, his thing is about to blow\r\nthis shipping firm out of the water.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.174 --\u003e 00:07:47.759\r\nAnd maybe Maxie with it.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.468 --\u003e 00:07:51.471\r\nAn Electron Discharge Cannon?\r\n\r\n00:07:52.055 --\u003e 00:07:54.432\r\nYou run one of the world's\r\nlargest shipping firms.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.516 --\u003e 00:07:57.686\r\nI thought you might know how the\r\nhijackers were able to move it.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.769 --\u003e 00:08:00.897\r\nWhy should Zeus be concerned\r\nabout the weapons of man\r\n\r\n00:08:00.981 --\u003e 00:08:03.692\r\nwhen he can call forth\r\nthunderbolts of his own?\r\n\r\n00:08:12.200 --\u003e 00:08:13.618\r\nThis audience is at an end.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.036 --\u003e 00:08:16.413\r\nAwake, my harpies.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.501 --\u003e 00:08:25.088\r\nBegone, Lord Hades.\r\nGet thee back to thine own realm.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.171 --\u003e 00:08:28.258\r\nDo not come again to\r\nOlympus until bidden.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.341 --\u003e 00:08:30.343\r\nI think I get the message.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.775 --\u003e 00:08:46.943\r\n(AIR CRAFT WHINING)\r\n\r\n00:08:58.621 --\u003e 00:09:01.291\r\nOh, Max,\r\nwhat's happening to you?\r\n\r\n00:09:10.050 --\u003e 00:09:14.679\r\nHey, you called, boss... I mean,\r\nthou didst summon us, O great Zeus?\r\n\r\n00:09:14.763 --\u003e 00:09:16.431\r\nIndeed I did.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.514 --\u003e 00:09:19.559\r\nFor you are to be among\r\nthe first pitiful mortals\r\n\r\n00:09:19.642 --\u003e 00:09:22.729\r\nto bear witness to\r\nthe dawn of a new age.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.982 --\u003e 00:09:27.150\r\n(BEEPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.277 --\u003e 00:09:32.739\r\nSoon all mortals will\r\ntremble once more\r\n\r\n00:09:32.822 --\u003e 00:09:36.242\r\nat the fury of Zeus reborn!\r\n\r\n00:09:43.750 --\u003e 00:09:45.418\r\nCome back to me, Maxie.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.502 --\u003e 00:09:47.087\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.465 --\u003e 00:09:51.841\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:09:54.969 --\u003e 00:09:56.471\r\nThe same thing you do.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.223 --\u003e 00:10:00.058\r\nTo help Maximillian Zeus.\r\n\r\n00:10:05.146 --\u003e 00:10:06.940\r\nHe wasn't always this\r\nway, you know.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.023 --\u003e 00:10:11.653\r\nBut then business got bad and he\r\nstarted handling cargo for the mob.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.736 --\u003e 00:10:16.783\r\nAfter a while, with the pressure,\r\nthe tension, things got confused.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.866 --\u003e 00:10:19.369\r\nHe's not living in the\r\nreal world anymore.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.328 --\u003e 00:10:22.163\r\nMaybe you can relate to that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.415 --\u003e 00:10:27.418\r\nYou're the only one who can get\r\nme close enough to help him,\r\n\r\n00:10:27.502 --\u003e 00:10:30.380\r\nwhile some of the man\r\nyou knew still exists.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.497 --\u003e 00:11:07.709\r\nThis is as far as I can take you.\r\nNow you're on your own.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.171 --\u003e 00:11:12.338\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:11:24.684 --\u003e 00:11:26.227\r\nThis isn't the roof.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.771 --\u003e 00:11:31.149\r\nSorry, Ms. Droukas.\r\nBoss's orders.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.649 --\u003e 00:11:33.735\r\nThis is as far as you go.\r\n\r\n00:11:39.449 --\u003e 00:11:42.410\r\nLike Bellerophon\r\nastride winged Pegasus,\r\n\r\n00:11:42.493 --\u003e 00:11:46.539\r\nyon foolish mortals dare\r\nencroach on sacred Olympus.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.248 --\u003e 00:11:50.501\r\n- Does he mean us?\r\n- Get thee back unto the mortal plane!\r\n\r\n00:11:57.550 --\u003e 00:11:59.010\r\nNo, Maxie! Not the cops!\r\n\r\n00:12:20.531 --\u003e 00:12:23.576\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:32.210 --\u003e 00:12:33.461\r\nI don't believe it.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.095 --\u003e 00:12:43.775\r\nWOMAN: It's on fire!\r\nMAN: It's gonna crash.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.846 --\u003e 00:12:45.682\r\nWOMAN: It's gonna explode.\r\nMAN: Oh, no!\r\n\r\n00:12:45.765 --\u003e 00:12:47.225\r\nGet back!\r\n\r\n00:12:47.308 --\u003e 00:12:49.644\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:58.027 --\u003e 00:13:01.990\r\nFeel the wrath of Zeus,\r\nthou insignificant-\r\n\r\n00:13:02.073 --\u003e 00:13:05.493\r\nMax, what have you done?\r\nYou could have killed someone!\r\n\r\n00:13:05.576 --\u003e 00:13:09.163\r\nHow dare you speak\r\nwith such disloyalty!\r\n\r\n00:13:09.247 --\u003e 00:13:12.166\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut, Maxie, phase,\r\nyou know Hove you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:12.792 --\u003e 00:13:16.504\r\nClio? I'm sorry. I can't...\r\n\r\n00:13:18.381 --\u003e 00:13:21.175\r\nThou art no longer\r\nfit to be among us!\r\n\r\n00:13:21.259 --\u003e 00:13:23.970\r\nTie her to the\r\nthunderbolt of Zeus.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.053 --\u003e 00:13:26.282\r\nBut, boss, don't you think you\r\nmay be carrying things a bit-\r\n\r\n00:13:26.306 --\u003e 00:13:27.307\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:31.269\r\nAlexander,\r\nwill thou do my bidding?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.398 --\u003e 00:13:37.233\r\nNothing personal, Ms. Droukas.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.192 --\u003e 00:13:39.193\r\n(MUFFLED PROTESTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:47.577 --\u003e 00:13:51.289\r\nSo, no longer like an\r\neagle against the sky,\r\n\r\n00:13:51.372 --\u003e 00:13:56.544\r\nbut as a worm crawling though the dirt\r\ndoes Lord Hades try to regain Olympus.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.627 --\u003e 00:14:00.381\r\nLook on my works,\r\nye mighty, and despair.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.931 --\u003e 00:14:09.974\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:14:11.309 --\u003e 00:14:13.394\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:25.990 --\u003e 00:14:29.452\r\nMAX: Heracles bested 12\r\nlabors before \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e received him.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.161 --\u003e 00:14:33.247\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd so it shall be with\r\nyou, bat demon.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:37.877 --\u003e 00:14:39.962\r\n(HISSING)\r\n\r\n00:15:06.489 --\u003e 00:15:08.783\r\n(GRUNTING \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:15:16.290 --\u003e 00:15:18.167\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:48.948 --\u003e 00:15:53.703\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAX: So, you have survived my hydra.\r\nBut many more challenges await.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:56.497 --\u003e 00:15:58.082\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:59.876 --\u003e 00:16:01.335\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:04.005 --\u003e 00:16:06.048\r\n(CLOPPING HOOVES APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:13.556 --\u003e 00:16:14.557\r\n(ANIMAL SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.824 --\u003e 00:16:32.825\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.495 --\u003e 00:16:36.746\r\nMAX: Alas.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.829 --\u003e 00:16:38.664\r\nFarewell, my dark brother.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.982 --\u003e 00:17:07.068\r\nBe not afraid, my muse.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.151 --\u003e 00:17:10.863\r\nFor once thou hast been cleansed\r\nby the fire from Olympus,\r\n\r\n00:17:10.947 --\u003e 00:17:15.451\r\nthou shalt be as a goddess at\r\nmy side throughout eternity!\r\n\r\n00:17:15.826 --\u003e 00:17:18.329\r\n(MUFFLED SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:20.831 --\u003e 00:17:22.833\r\nLet the heavens scream!\r\n\r\n00:17:23.209 --\u003e 00:17:24.877\r\nLet the earth tremble!\r\n\r\n00:17:40.518 --\u003e 00:17:45.064\r\nLet mortals know the\r\ngods of old live again!\r\n\r\n00:17:53.531 --\u003e 00:17:55.741\r\nIt's over, Maxie.\r\n\r\n00:17:55.825 --\u003e 00:17:58.911\r\nAlexander,\r\ndestroy the bat demon.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.995 --\u003e 00:18:03.583\r\n- But, boss, maybe we shouldn't-\r\n- Traitors! My harpies, awake.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.041 --\u003e 00:18:06.460\r\nDestroy all who oppose me!\r\n\r\n00:18:35.489 --\u003e 00:18:36.490\r\n(CANNON POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:18:58.596 --\u003e 00:18:59.597\r\n(MAX GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:10.941 --\u003e 00:19:11.942\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:16.197 --\u003e 00:19:17.198\r\nAh.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.281 --\u003e 00:19:19.533\r\nThank you, Bat... Look out!\r\n\r\n00:19:19.617 --\u003e 00:19:22.244\r\nBegone, thou foul bat demon!\r\n\r\n00:19:26.374 --\u003e 00:19:29.126\r\nGet thee back to the\r\nunderworld where thee belongs!\r\n\r\n00:19:29.919 --\u003e 00:19:33.381\r\nSuch is the fate of all who\r\ndare to thwart the gods.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.568 --\u003e 00:19:55.903\r\nOh, no.\r\n\r\n00:20:05.955 --\u003e 00:20:07.540\r\nIt's going to fire!\r\n\r\n00:20:10.501 --\u003e 00:20:11.752\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:20:12.169 --\u003e 00:20:13.713\r\nThat's mine!\r\n\r\n00:20:19.260 --\u003e 00:20:20.261\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:25.516 --\u003e 00:20:27.393\r\nMaxie, no!\r\n\r\n00:20:33.065 --\u003e 00:20:34.233\r\nGet down!\r\n\r\n00:20:38.904 --\u003e 00:20:43.117\r\n(MAX SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:57.131 --\u003e 00:21:00.217\r\nNow, this is truly Olympus.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.301 --\u003e 00:21:02.678\r\nSurely,\r\nit can be no other place.\r\n\r\n00:21:04.472 --\u003e 00:21:07.391\r\nThere's beautiful Demeter,\r\ngoddess of the harvest.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.103 --\u003e 00:21:15.107\r\nAnd double-faced Janus,\r\nlord of beginnings and endings.\r\n\r\n00:21:20.446 --\u003e 00:21:24.074\r\nAnd merry Hermes,\r\nthe trickster of the gods.\r\n\r\n00:21:32.458 --\u003e 00:21:36.545\r\nNow at last,\r\nmighty Zeus is home.\r\n\r\n00:21:48.224 --\u003e 00:21:50.226\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E01 - Shadow of The Bat, Part 1 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.147 --\u003e 00:00:24.149\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:33.468 --\u003e 00:01:34.720\r\n(BAT SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:36.638 --\u003e 00:01:37.889\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:01:38.432 --\u003e 00:01:40.225\r\nThis place gives me the willies.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.309 --\u003e 00:01:41.393\r\nNo kiddin'.\r\n\r\n00:01:41.476 --\u003e 00:01:44.187\r\nWhy do we gotta do this stuff in\r\nthe middle of the flipping night?\r\n\r\n00:01:48.984 --\u003e 00:01:50.068\r\n- (CLATTER)\r\n- (BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:01:50.152 --\u003e 00:01:53.030\r\nMaybe you'd prefer moving\r\ncontraband in broad daylight,\r\n\r\n00:01:53.113 --\u003e 00:01:54.406\r\nwhen the cops might notice.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.200 --\u003e 00:01:59.911\r\nJeez, boss. You shouldn't\r\nsneak up on guys like that.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.995 --\u003e 00:02:01.455\r\nJust get this stuff loaded.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.873 --\u003e 00:02:04.583\r\nI never liked this place.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.292 --\u003e 00:02:06.793\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:08.837 --\u003e 00:02:10.589\r\n(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:14.217\r\n\u003ci\u003eThis is the police.\r\nWe have you surrounded.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:14.301 --\u003e 00:02:15.886\r\n\u003ci\u003eCome out with your hands up.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:19.556 --\u003e 00:02:21.683\r\nI can't be seen here.\r\nHold them off.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.393 --\u003e 00:02:25.604\r\n- (CROWBAR CLATTERS)\r\n- (GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:02:28.440 --\u003e 00:02:30.025\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:02:53.298 --\u003e 00:02:55.092\r\nThat's right. Nice and easy.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.967 --\u003e 00:02:57.010\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:02:59.179 --\u003e 00:03:00.764\r\nI never liked this place.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.186 --\u003e 00:03:07.396\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:03:17.572 --\u003e 00:03:20.659\r\nCome on, then. You're not taking\r\nRupert Thorne without a fight.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.743 --\u003e 00:03:22.869\r\nYou?\r\n\r\n00:03:27.207 --\u003e 00:03:30.043\r\nIf I gotta go down,\r\nI'm taking you with me.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.721 --\u003e 00:03:41.847\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.435 --\u003e 00:03:47.561\r\n(THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:03:55.402 --\u003e 00:03:56.862\r\nCareful, Gil.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.945 --\u003e 00:03:59.406\r\nDon't make this hard on\r\nyourself, Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.489 --\u003e 00:04:01.408\r\nStep out where we can see you.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.033 --\u003e 00:04:04.035\r\nNot even if I could, flatfoot.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.704 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.169 --\u003e 00:04:15.046\r\nDon't you just love it when he\r\ngives them to you gift-wrapped?\r\n\r\n00:04:17.174 --\u003e 00:04:20.886\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe deputy commissioner, Gil Mason,\r\nwho last night was instrumental\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:20.969 --\u003e 00:04:22.679\r\n\u003ci\u003ein capturing Rupert Thorne...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:23.263 --\u003e 00:04:25.491\r\n\u003ci\u003eMason attributed the incriminating\r\nevidence against Thorne\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:25.515 --\u003e 00:04:27.058\r\n\u003ci\u003eto a mysterious informant.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:27.601 --\u003e 00:04:31.396\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd the commissioner and I won't\r\nrest until every crime kingpin,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:31.480 --\u003e 00:04:34.107\r\n\u003ci\u003ehustler, and two-bit\r\ncrook is off the streets.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:34.441 --\u003e 00:04:37.903\r\nYou'll ruin your eyes changing\r\nchannels so fast, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.986 --\u003e 00:04:39.780\r\nNot to mention your\r\nattention span.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.863 --\u003e 00:04:44.451\r\nOne would think the fall of Thorne\r\nwould bring a smile even to your face.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.576 --\u003e 00:04:47.454\r\nI'd love to know who this\r\nmysterious informant is.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.537 --\u003e 00:04:50.874\r\nThis is the third gang lord Mason's\r\nbrought down in as many months.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.250 --\u003e 00:04:53.710\r\nYes, it's quite alarming.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.336 --\u003e 00:04:57.923\r\nIf this continues, you might even\r\nbe forced into taking a vacation.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.507 --\u003e 00:05:00.187\r\n- (WIND BLOWING)\r\n- (DOG BARKING \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e DISTANCE)\r\n\r\n00:05:12.270 --\u003e 00:05:16.191\r\nYou know, Dad, if you and Gil\r\nkeep nailing bad guys like this,\r\n\r\n00:05:20.403 --\u003e 00:05:22.864\r\npeople will start thinking\r\nyou two are Batman and Robin.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.948 --\u003e 00:05:25.075\r\nWhat can I say?\r\nGil is a godsend.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.618 --\u003e 00:05:30.038\r\n- And he's not bad-looking, either.\r\n- Dad.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.209 --\u003e 00:05:36.711\r\nI just got you to stop\r\ntreating me like a kid,\r\n\r\n00:05:37.629 --\u003e 00:05:40.549\r\n- and now you're trying to marry me off.\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.632 --\u003e 00:05:43.718\r\nHey, don't think I didn't see you\r\ntwo at that fundraiser last week.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.802 --\u003e 00:05:45.303\r\nThick as thieves you were.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.387 --\u003e 00:05:46.596\r\n(DOORBELL DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:05:50.934 --\u003e 00:05:54.479\r\nMr. Mason, you must be psychic.\r\nWe were just talking about you.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.980 --\u003e 00:05:56.022\r\nCome in, come in.\r\n\r\n00:05:56.982 --\u003e 00:05:59.860\r\n- Hey, Gil. What's doing?\r\n- Another tip on a case?\r\n\r\n00:06:00.777 --\u003e 00:06:03.613\r\nBelieve me, Jim,\r\nI don't wanna be here.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.697 --\u003e 00:06:06.032\r\nBut I thought it would\r\nbe best coming from me.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.825 --\u003e 00:06:07.993\r\nWhat is it? What's wrong?\r\n\r\n00:06:09.578 --\u003e 00:06:12.289\r\nJames Gordon,\r\nI have a warrant for your arrest.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.748 --\u003e 00:06:15.292\r\nThis is a joke, right?\r\n\r\n00:06:17.586 --\u003e 00:06:20.672\r\n- On what charges?\r\n- Accepting bribes.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.423 --\u003e 00:06:22.841\r\nYou can't be serious.\r\n\r\n00:06:23.717 --\u003e 00:06:25.719\r\nThe department has\r\nreason to believe\r\n\r\n00:06:25.802 --\u003e 00:06:29.055\r\nthat you've been taking money\r\nfrom Rupert Thorne for years.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.556 --\u003e 00:06:32.976\r\nWhat? Dad's never taken\r\na bribe in his life.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:35.186\r\nI'm sorry, Barb.\r\n\r\n00:06:35.687 --\u003e 00:06:37.689\r\nYou have the right\r\nto remain silent.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.772 --\u003e 00:06:40.108\r\nIf you give up that\r\nright, anything you say-\r\n\r\n00:06:40.191 --\u003e 00:06:41.610\r\nI know my rights, Gil.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.698 --\u003e 00:06:47.741\r\nDad.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.491 --\u003e 00:06:51.286\r\nDon't worry, Barbara.\r\nIt's all a mistake, you'll see.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.369 --\u003e 00:06:53.249\r\nREPORTER: Commissioner,\r\ndo you have a statement?\r\n\r\n00:06:54.456 --\u003e 00:06:56.875\r\nI'm sorry, Barbara. I really am.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.296 --\u003e 00:07:02.815\r\nREPORTER 1: Commissioner\r\nGordon, just a statement, sir.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.839 --\u003e 00:07:04.525\r\nREPORTER 2: What about\r\nthese corruption charges?\r\n\r\n00:07:04.549 --\u003e 00:07:06.092\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:07:12.015 --\u003e 00:07:13.895\r\nREPORTER 3: Ms.\r\nGordon, do you have a statement?\r\n\r\n00:07:13.975 --\u003e 00:07:15.727\r\n(REPORTERS CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.572 --\u003e 00:07:29.074\r\nWe'll see about this.\r\n\r\n00:07:41.378 --\u003e 00:07:44.255\r\nBut you're the DA, Janet.\r\nYou've worked with my father.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.339 --\u003e 00:07:47.300\r\n- There must be something you can-\r\n- The evidence is solid, Barbara.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.384 --\u003e 00:07:50.178\r\nMoney deposited to your father's\r\nname in laundered accounts.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.261 --\u003e 00:07:52.555\r\nWitnesses who swear they\r\nsaw him take bribes.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.014 --\u003e 00:07:55.600\r\nThat's not sufficient\r\ncause to deny him bail.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.684 --\u003e 00:08:00.397\r\nTrue. But we also found deposit\r\nreceipts for a South American bank.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.480 --\u003e 00:08:02.482\r\nWe have to consider\r\nhim a flight risk.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.565 --\u003e 00:08:04.776\r\nThis is crazy.\r\nMy father would never-\r\n\r\n00:08:04.859 --\u003e 00:08:07.696\r\nMaybe you don't know your\r\nfather as well as you think.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.655 --\u003e 00:08:09.990\r\nMaybe none of us do.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.370 --\u003e 00:08:18.456\r\nDon't you believe her, kid.\r\nYour pop's the best there is.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.540 --\u003e 00:08:21.126\r\nThat's why the department's\r\nputting on a rally for him.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.459 --\u003e 00:08:26.548\r\n- Harvey, that's a wonderful idea.\r\n- Yeah. Wish I could say it was mine.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.884\r\nJust because I have a job to do\r\ndoesn't mean I'm not on your side.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.968 --\u003e 00:08:33.763\r\nI'm going to see Jim Gordon gets all\r\nthe public support we can muster.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.180 --\u003e 00:08:37.017\r\nAll the top cops will be\r\nthere, including yours truly.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.100 --\u003e 00:08:40.061\r\nSo don't worry your pretty little head.\r\nShould be quite a show.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.645 --\u003e 00:08:46.317\r\nYes, and I know someone who'd be a\r\nreal showstopper, if I can get him.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.963 --\u003e 00:09:08.214\r\n(KEYS JANGLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:37.786 --\u003e 00:09:38.787\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:43.249 --\u003e 00:09:45.085\r\nI was wondering when\r\nyou'd get around to me.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.168 --\u003e 00:09:46.461\r\nI got a look at the evidence.\r\n\r\n00:09:46.836 --\u003e 00:09:50.298\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: Those deposit receipts were\r\nperfect forgeries, dated months ago.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:50.673 --\u003e 00:09:52.425\r\n\u003ci\u003eDoesn't look like\r\nThorne's handiwork.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:52.550 --\u003e 00:09:53.593\r\nThen who?\r\n\r\n00:09:54.302 --\u003e 00:09:57.222\r\nWord on the street is a\r\nnew syndicate is moving in.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.806 --\u003e 00:09:59.808\r\nCould be a connection.\r\nI'll check it out.\r\n\r\n00:09:59.891 --\u003e 00:10:02.977\r\n\u003ci\u003e- Anything you need?\r\n- Yes. Check on Barbara.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:03.353 --\u003e 00:10:04.437\r\nKeep her out of this.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.191 --\u003e 00:10:09.859\r\nBut you have to\r\ncome to the rally.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.860 --\u003e 00:10:15.281\r\nThe public respects you. If they see\r\nyou there, they'll know Dad's innocent.\r\n\r\n00:10:15.365 --\u003e 00:10:18.201\r\nSorry, but there's more to\r\nthis than a simple frame-up.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.284 --\u003e 00:10:20.578\r\nAnd I'm not gonna find out\r\nby appearing at rallies.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.662 --\u003e 00:10:21.746\r\nBut don't you see?\r\n\r\n00:10:21.830 --\u003e 00:10:24.707\r\nThe best thing you can do for\r\nhim, is to keep out of it.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.791 --\u003e 00:10:26.876\r\nThe people behind\r\nthis are dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.007 --\u003e 00:10:35.718\r\n\"I'm a professional,\r\ndon't try this at home,\" huh?\r\n\r\n00:10:36.302 --\u003e 00:10:37.679\r\nSorry, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.762 --\u003e 00:10:40.598\r\nYou being at the rally could\r\ndecide if Dad goes free.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.224 --\u003e 00:10:44.435\r\nSo you'll be there,\r\none way or another.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.957 --\u003e 00:11:09.210\r\nMAD DOG: You called me, boss?\r\nBOSS: The rally's tomorrow night.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.919 --\u003e 00:11:13.089\r\nEverything's in place.\r\nYou know what to do.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.885 --\u003e 00:11:18.761\r\nWill you at least\r\nwear a transceiver?\r\n\r\n00:11:18.845 --\u003e 00:11:20.889\r\nI can monitor from here\r\nin case they try to-\r\n\r\n00:11:20.972 --\u003e 00:11:22.765\r\nNo, too easy to detect.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.099 --\u003e 00:11:25.935\r\nHey. I didn't miss a Bogart\r\nfestival in film class\r\n\r\n00:11:26.019 --\u003e 00:11:28.646\r\njust to sit on my butt here\r\nwhile you hit the streets.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.063 --\u003e 00:11:30.607\r\nThere has to be\r\nsomething I can do.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.612 --\u003e 00:11:37.322\r\nDo you make public appearances?\r\n\r\n00:11:45.705 --\u003e 00:11:49.334\r\n\u003ci\u003eAfter all Commissioner Gordon\r\nhas done for Gotham City,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:49.417 --\u003e 00:11:53.087\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe least the city can do\r\nfor him is grant him bail.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:53.171 --\u003e 00:11:54.797\r\n(CROWD CHEERING AND APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:11:57.967 --\u003e 00:11:59.010\r\nShowtime.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.015 --\u003e 00:12:06.226\r\nBruce? What in...\r\n\r\n00:12:06.309 --\u003e 00:12:07.936\r\n- That's him, all right.\r\n- It's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.103 --\u003e 00:12:10.146\r\nWOMAN: Batman!\r\n\r\n00:12:10.230 --\u003e 00:12:12.565\r\nMAN 1: I knew it.\r\nMAN 2: He knows Gordon's innocent!\r\n\r\n00:12:13.483 --\u003e 00:12:15.401\r\n- Grandstanding psycho.\r\n- (PEOPLE CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:12:27.413 --\u003e 00:12:28.581\r\nTouchdown.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.632 --\u003e 00:12:39.217\r\n(CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:39.968 --\u003e 00:12:41.803\r\nAnd the crowd goes wild.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.140 --\u003e 00:12:47.308\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:12:54.065 --\u003e 00:12:55.233\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:58.111 --\u003e 00:12:59.279\r\n(GASPING AND SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:26.973 --\u003e 00:13:27.974\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:31.561 --\u003e 00:13:32.603\r\nSHOOTER: What the...\r\n\r\n00:13:33.521 --\u003e 00:13:34.981\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:43.823 --\u003e 00:13:44.991\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:13:47.785 --\u003e 00:13:48.828\r\nWait!\r\n\r\n00:13:55.460 --\u003e 00:13:56.669\r\nA girl?\r\n\r\n00:14:25.740 --\u003e 00:14:27.241\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:28.409 --\u003e 00:14:29.577\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:14:30.745 --\u003e 00:14:32.580\r\nThe lady's with me, gents.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.208 --\u003e 00:14:36.209\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:14:36.542 --\u003e 00:14:37.960\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:38.044 --\u003e 00:14:40.963\r\nAre you crazy?\r\nYou're lucky you didn't get killed.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.047 --\u003e 00:14:43.966\r\n- Come on. They're getting away.\r\n- This is nuts.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.425 --\u003e 00:14:45.968\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:14:59.273 --\u003e 00:15:00.441\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.031 --\u003e 00:15:08.116\r\n(BARBARA GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:16.290 --\u003e 00:15:17.333\r\nYuck.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.417 --\u003e 00:15:18.793\r\n(SIRENS APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:27.218 --\u003e 00:15:29.262\r\nGreat. She's gone, too.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.388 --\u003e 00:15:33.599\r\nFunny, I don't remember a\r\nBatgirl in our little club.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.225 --\u003e 00:15:36.865\r\n\u003ci\u003eREPORTER ON TV: All Gotham is\r\ntalking about the mysterious Batgirl,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:36.894 --\u003e 00:15:40.481\r\n\u003ci\u003ewho foiled an assassination attempt\r\non acting commissioner Gil Mason.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:41.107 --\u003e 00:15:43.860\r\nExpanding membership in\r\nthe crime-fighting club?\r\n\r\n00:15:44.277 --\u003e 00:15:46.571\r\nIf I find out who she\r\nis, I'll...\r\n\r\n00:15:48.239 --\u003e 00:15:49.949\r\nHey. Look at that.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.129 --\u003e 00:16:06.215\r\nMr. Mason ducked\r\nbefore he saw the guns.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.299 --\u003e 00:16:08.176\r\nAlmost as though he expected it.\r\n\r\n00:16:10.595 --\u003e 00:16:14.265\r\nBatgirl, sheesh.\r\nWhat's next, Weasel Woman?\r\n\r\n00:16:15.558 --\u003e 00:16:16.601\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:16:17.852 --\u003e 00:16:19.061\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.288 --\u003e 00:16:38.456\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.789 --\u003e 00:16:39.874\r\nGotcha.\r\n\r\n00:16:43.961 --\u003e 00:16:45.046\r\n(KNOCKING AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.426 --\u003e 00:16:52.136\r\nGil, you know those\r\nguys who shot at you?\r\n\r\n00:16:52.220 --\u003e 00:16:53.780\r\nWell, I think I know\r\nwho one of them...\r\n\r\n00:16:59.310 --\u003e 00:17:00.686\r\nSomething wrong, Barbara?\r\n\r\n00:17:01.270 --\u003e 00:17:03.981\r\nI didn't know you had company.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.065 --\u003e 00:17:07.109\r\nOh, no problem.\r\nMy friend here was just leaving.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.777 --\u003e 00:17:11.864\r\nOh, yeah, gotta run. Listen,\r\nI'll see you at the business meeting, Gil.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.948 --\u003e 00:17:12.990\r\nMiss.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.992 --\u003e 00:17:17.703\r\nSo, welcome to my humble abode.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.329 --\u003e 00:17:19.330\r\nUh...\r\n\r\n00:17:19.997 --\u003e 00:17:21.624\r\n\u003ci\u003eHusk came over to...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:22.416 --\u003e 00:17:25.628\r\nTo see if you're okay.\r\nI was worried about you.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.711 --\u003e 00:17:28.422\r\nHey, I appreciate that.\r\nI really do. Drink?\r\n\r\n00:17:28.839 --\u003e 00:17:31.717\r\nOh, gee, I'm sorry,\r\nI was just on my way to see Dad.\r\n\r\n00:17:31.801 --\u003e 00:17:34.345\r\nBut I'm sure I'll\r\ncatch you again.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.244 --\u003e 00:18:02.164\r\nYeah, boss, like Batman, only a dame.\r\nShe almost screwed up everything.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.421 --\u003e 00:18:09.861\r\nNo, don't worry.\r\nNo one can hear me.\r\n\r\n00:18:11.841 --\u003e 00:18:12.925\r\n(INAUDIBLE)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.595 --\u003e 00:18:17.388\r\nRight, boss.\r\nI'm heading back right now.\r\n\r\n00:19:26.499 --\u003e 00:19:27.500\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:31.212 --\u003e 00:19:32.421\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:41.263 --\u003e 00:19:43.349\r\n(SIGHS) What am I gonna do?\r\n\r\n00:19:43.432 --\u003e 00:19:46.477\r\nIf Gil's involved in this,\r\nthere's nobody I can trust.\r\n\r\n00:19:55.403 --\u003e 00:19:56.862\r\nAnd if Batman's not around...\r\n\r\n00:20:05.287 --\u003e 00:20:06.455\r\nWhat do you think, Woobie?\r\n\r\n00:20:08.541 --\u003e 00:20:10.042\r\nCould use a little work, huh?\r\n\r\n00:20:12.336 --\u003e 00:20:14.380\r\nBOSS: It appears\r\nwe have a prowler.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.590 --\u003e 00:20:17.591\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:18.843 --\u003e 00:20:19.844\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:25.391 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:20:28.394 --\u003e 00:20:31.230\r\nMatches Malone.\r\nHeard about a new mob.\r\n\r\n00:20:31.313 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\n- Thought I could make some more dough.\r\n- Is that so?\r\n\r\n00:20:35.192 --\u003e 00:20:37.153\r\nWell, you heard right.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.236 --\u003e 00:20:40.322\r\nIn fact, you can double your\r\ntake on the jobs we're pulling.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.658 --\u003e 00:20:45.870\r\nAssuming I let you\r\nlive to join my gang.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.287 --\u003e 00:20:47.288\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:47.496 --\u003e 00:20:48.956\r\nMatches Malone?\r\n\r\n00:20:50.833 --\u003e 00:20:52.168\r\nNever heard of you.\r\n\r\n00:20:52.752 --\u003e 00:20:55.212\r\nBut there's something about\r\nyou that I don't like.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.296 --\u003e 00:20:59.216\r\nNothing I can put my finger\r\non, but I trust my hunches.\r\n\r\n00:21:00.092 --\u003e 00:21:03.137\r\nKind of like second\r\nsight, you know?\r\n\r\n00:21:05.931 --\u003e 00:21:10.311\r\nGood heads, you live.\r\nBad heads, you don't. Simple, huh?\r\n\r\n00:21:29.580 --\u003e 00:21:30.623\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:21:39.423 --\u003e 00:21:42.051\r\nSo Batman can't help me? Fine.\r\n\r\n00:21:42.843 --\u003e 00:21:47.014\r\nIn that case,\r\nlet's see what Batgirl can do.\r\n\r\n00:21:57.107 --\u003e 00:21:59.109\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:22.675 --\u003e 00:22:23.676\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E02 - Shadow of The Bat, Part 2 (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.189 --\u003e 00:00:24.191\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:09.820 --\u003e 00:01:12.656\r\nJames Gordon,\r\nI have a warrant for your arrest.\r\n\r\n00:01:12.739 --\u003e 00:01:14.783\r\nROBIN: Previously on Batman...\r\n\r\n00:01:14.866 --\u003e 00:01:17.578\r\nThe rally's tomorrow night.\r\nEverything's in place.\r\n\r\n00:01:18.203 --\u003e 00:01:19.329\r\nYou know what to do.\r\n\r\n00:01:19.413 --\u003e 00:01:23.083\r\nI'm going to see Jim Gordon gets all\r\nthe public support we can muster.\r\n\r\n00:01:23.166 --\u003e 00:01:26.086\r\nAll the top cops will be there,\r\nso don't worry your pretty little head.\r\n\r\n00:01:26.336 --\u003e 00:01:27.713\r\nShould be quite a show.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.796 --\u003e 00:01:31.758\r\nYes, and I know someone\r\nwho'd be a real showstopper.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.842 --\u003e 00:01:34.720\r\nThe best thing you can do\r\nfor him is to keep out of it.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.929 --\u003e 00:01:40.183\r\nSorry, Batman. You being at the\r\nrally could decide if Dad goes free.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:43.353\r\nBARBARA: So you'll be\r\nthere, one way or another.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.645 --\u003e 00:01:47.232\r\nGIL: After all Commissioner\r\nGordon has done for Gotham City,\r\n\r\n00:01:47.316 --\u003e 00:01:50.902\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe least the city can do\r\nfor him is grant him bail.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:54.323 --\u003e 00:01:56.033\r\nGil, you know those\r\nguys who shot at you?\r\n\r\n00:01:56.116 --\u003e 00:01:57.676\r\nWell, I think I know\r\nwho one of them...\r\n\r\n00:01:58.201 --\u003e 00:02:00.871\r\nI didn't know you had company.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.954 --\u003e 00:02:02.748\r\nMy friend here was just leaving.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.290 --\u003e 00:02:07.336\r\nYeah, gotta run. Listen,\r\nI'll see you at the business meeting, Gil.\r\n\r\n00:02:07.419 --\u003e 00:02:08.629\r\nMiss.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.962 --\u003e 00:02:09.963\r\nLook at that.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:14.760\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: Mr. Mason ducked\r\nbefore he saw the guns.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:14.843 --\u003e 00:02:16.720\r\nAlmost as though he expected it.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.596 --\u003e 00:02:19.389\r\nWhat am I gonna do?\r\n\r\n00:02:19.473 --\u003e 00:02:22.517\r\nIf Gil's involved in this,\r\nthere's nobody I can trust.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.126 --\u003e 00:02:50.420\r\n- ALFRED: Where will you start?\r\n- With Gil Mason.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.504 --\u003e 00:02:52.714\r\nThe videotape clearly\r\nshows that he ducked\r\n\r\n00:02:52.798 --\u003e 00:02:54.591\r\nbefore those shots were fired.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.760 --\u003e 00:02:58.595\r\nIf he knew he was\r\ngonna be shot at,\r\n\r\n00:02:58.679 --\u003e 00:03:01.306\r\nhe probably knows a lot\r\nmore about what's going on.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.390 --\u003e 00:03:03.058\r\nThen he may know more\r\nthan he's letting on\r\n\r\n00:03:03.141 --\u003e 00:03:06.061\r\nabout Commissioner Gordon's\r\nunfortunate situation.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.144 --\u003e 00:03:07.354\r\nI hope so, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.729 --\u003e 00:03:10.732\r\n'Cause if this lead fizzles,\r\nI'm fresh out of ideas.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.704 --\u003e 00:04:07.330\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:04:09.958 --\u003e 00:04:11.334\r\nYou again?\r\n\r\n00:04:11.418 --\u003e 00:04:13.962\r\nListen, under other\r\ncircumstances, this could be fun,\r\n\r\n00:04:14.045 --\u003e 00:04:15.589\r\nbut I've got a job to do.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.964 --\u003e 00:04:17.507\r\nDon't flatter yourself.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.591 --\u003e 00:04:20.886\r\nWell, I don't have time\r\nto babysit amateurs, okay?\r\n\r\n00:04:21.178 --\u003e 00:04:23.597\r\nI may not have a diploma\r\nfrom crime-fighting school,\r\n\r\n00:04:23.680 --\u003e 00:04:25.599\r\nbut I can do fine on my\r\nown, thanks.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.016 --\u003e 00:04:30.103\r\n- What are you doing here anyway?\r\n- Same as you. We both suspect Mason of-\r\n\r\n00:04:30.187 --\u003e 00:04:31.229\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:35.609 --\u003e 00:04:36.818\r\n(TELEPHONE CONTINUES RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:42.824 --\u003e 00:04:44.242\r\nMason here.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.118 --\u003e 00:04:47.496\r\nYou wanna meet? Okay, where?\r\n\r\n00:04:47.788 --\u003e 00:04:49.289\r\n- What's he saying?\r\n- (SHUSH ES)\r\n\r\n00:04:49.998 --\u003e 00:04:51.041\r\nDork.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.003 --\u003e 00:04:57.839\r\nSouth Gotham subway,\r\nthe old river entrance. In one hour.\r\n\r\n00:04:59.800 --\u003e 00:05:02.177\r\nRight. I'm on my way.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.140 --\u003e 00:05:09.142\r\nWell, show's over.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.768 --\u003e 00:05:11.353\r\nYou can run along home now.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.607 --\u003e 00:05:18.401\r\n- Okay_ - Okay?\r\n\r\n00:05:18.485 --\u003e 00:05:21.238\r\nIf you won't let me help\r\nyou, what else can I do?\r\n\r\n00:05:21.571 --\u003e 00:05:23.907\r\nGood. You've got\r\nsome sense after all.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.952 --\u003e 00:05:29.913\r\nNice guy,\r\nbut a few bats short of a belfry.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.386 --\u003e 00:05:45.387\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:05:48.849 --\u003e 00:05:50.475\r\nGotta work on that\r\nlanding, girl.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:13.540\r\n(MUFFLED STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:06:27.304 --\u003e 00:06:28.513\r\n(MUFFLED STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.018 --\u003e 00:06:34.686\r\nI guess the party\r\nstarted without me.\r\n\r\n00:06:49.618 --\u003e 00:06:51.899\r\nTWO-FACE: You sure you haven't\r\nseen him at the department?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.871 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\nGIL: I'd remember that face.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.539 --\u003e 00:06:55.832\r\nWho is he?\r\n\r\n00:06:56.207 --\u003e 00:06:58.585\r\nTWO-FACE: In a few minutes,\r\nnobody's gonna care.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.461 --\u003e 00:07:00.503\r\n(THUDS)\r\n\r\n00:07:03.506 --\u003e 00:07:05.800\r\n- Okay, you're done.\r\n- So that's it?\r\n\r\n00:07:05.884 --\u003e 00:07:09.721\r\nYou bring me all the way to South\r\nGotham to ID some two-bit hood?\r\n\r\n00:07:09.804 --\u003e 00:07:11.765\r\nTWO-FACE: Don't get wise with\r\nme, Mason.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.848 --\u003e 00:07:14.601\r\nRemember who got you set\r\nup as Gordon's assistant.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.684 --\u003e 00:07:16.436\r\nRight, Harvey, right.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.895 --\u003e 00:07:17.979\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:18.063 --\u003e 00:07:21.775\r\nDon't call me that!\r\nIt's Two-Face to you, pretty boy.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.108 --\u003e 00:07:25.946\r\nOkay, okay. Two-Face, take it easy.\r\nYou're the man.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.279 --\u003e 00:07:29.366\r\nDon't you forget it.\r\nSince our little stunt at the rally,\r\n\r\n00:07:29.449 --\u003e 00:07:32.285\r\nI got this city thinking you're\r\nthe best thing since the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.828 --\u003e 00:07:35.830\r\nOnce Gordon's out\r\nof the picture...\r\n\r\n00:07:37.666 --\u003e 00:07:39.834\r\nYou'll be a shoo-in\r\nto take his place.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.085 --\u003e 00:07:43.922\r\nIn fact, they could be calling\r\nyou Commissioner by tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.381 --\u003e 00:07:45.382\r\nTomorrow?\r\n\r\n00:07:45.465 --\u003e 00:07:47.065\r\nTWO-FACE: I'm stepping\r\nup the timetable.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.092 --\u003e 00:07:52.180\r\nToo many people nosing around.\r\nThis guy, that Batgirl chippy.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.764 --\u003e 00:07:54.432\r\nI'm not taking any chances.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.516 --\u003e 00:07:56.893\r\nMy men will bust Gordon\r\nout of jail tonight.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.977 --\u003e 00:07:59.229\r\nThen we'll dump him\r\noff Bayshore Wharf.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.521 --\u003e 00:08:00.772\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:08:01.398 --\u003e 00:08:02.440\r\n- Hey!\r\n- What's that?\r\n\r\n00:08:02.524 --\u003e 00:08:04.067\r\nGIL: Hey,\r\ndid you hear something?\r\n\r\n00:08:05.860 --\u003e 00:08:07.988\r\nWe got company. Over there.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.409 --\u003e 00:08:13.785\r\nRobin, look out!\r\n\r\n00:08:15.245 --\u003e 00:08:16.329\r\nRobin?\r\n\r\n00:08:27.382 --\u003e 00:08:31.302\r\nIf he's Robin, that makes you...\r\n\r\n00:08:32.220 --\u003e 00:08:33.430\r\n(RAPID GUNFIRE)\r\n\r\n00:08:47.694 --\u003e 00:08:48.778\r\nLet's go!\r\n\r\n00:08:50.238 --\u003e 00:08:51.573\r\n(MACHINE GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:08:58.163 --\u003e 00:08:59.289\r\nBlow it!\r\n\r\n00:09:18.266 --\u003e 00:09:19.976\r\nJust whose side are you on?\r\n\r\n00:09:20.060 --\u003e 00:09:23.146\r\nYou're right. If I hadn't\r\nlet him take me by surprise-\r\n\r\n00:09:23.229 --\u003e 00:09:26.357\r\nRobin! I see you brought a date.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.941 --\u003e 00:09:29.360\r\nMe? I thought she was with you.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.611 --\u003e 00:09:32.280\r\nShe's got your taste in\r\nclothes, speaking of which...\r\n\r\n00:09:33.323 --\u003e 00:09:36.201\r\nYes. Am I glad to see you.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.284 --\u003e 00:09:37.952\r\nDo you mind?\r\n\r\n00:09:38.912 --\u003e 00:09:40.038\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.914 --\u003e 00:09:44.459\r\nWell, this is just great.\r\nNow Batman and Robin know what's going on.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.709 --\u003e 00:09:46.753\r\nThe bat-chick too. I saw her.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.045 --\u003e 00:09:50.548\r\nThe explosion probably took care of them.\r\nBut just in case...\r\n\r\n00:09:51.257 --\u003e 00:09:52.467\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:52.884 --\u003e 00:09:54.094\r\n(RAPID BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:10:05.021 --\u003e 00:10:07.482\r\nI don't know who you are\r\nor why you're doing this,\r\n\r\n00:10:07.565 --\u003e 00:10:09.192\r\nbut let's get one\r\nthing straight.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.609 --\u003e 00:10:12.445\r\nIt takes more than a costume\r\nand an attitude to do this work.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.529 --\u003e 00:10:14.656\r\nLook, I've got a reason\r\nfor being here so-\r\n\r\n00:10:14.739 --\u003e 00:10:16.199\r\nYou've already fouled up once.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.741 --\u003e 00:10:19.369\r\nStay out of our way so\r\nit doesn't happen again.\r\n\r\n00:10:27.669 --\u003e 00:10:31.756\r\nI should've known it would be Two-Face.\r\nIt's a perfect two-part plan.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.840 --\u003e 00:10:34.926\r\nHe consolidates the gangs while\r\nMason takes over the police.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.009 --\u003e 00:10:37.470\r\nWhat he said about the\r\nCommissioner, will he-\r\n\r\n00:10:37.554 --\u003e 00:10:39.097\r\nYou saw him flip his coin.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.597 --\u003e 00:10:42.517\r\nIt's judge, jury,\r\nand executioner.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.690 --\u003e 00:10:50.525\r\nAnd here we sit\r\nwith no way to...\r\n\r\n00:10:50.608 --\u003e 00:10:51.693\r\n- (RUMBLING)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:10:51.776 --\u003e 00:10:53.027\r\nSounds like a train.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.454 --\u003e 00:11:04.539\r\nROBIN: Argh!\r\n\r\n00:11:07.458 --\u003e 00:11:08.543\r\nHold on.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.626 --\u003e 00:11:09.836\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:11:13.715 --\u003e 00:11:14.716\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:15.133 --\u003e 00:11:16.134\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:16.843 --\u003e 00:11:19.804\r\nNot bad. Maybe there's\r\nhope for you after all.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.430 --\u003e 00:11:21.639\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:40.700 --\u003e 00:11:41.910\r\nHurry, Batman!\r\n\r\n00:11:50.710 --\u003e 00:11:53.087\r\nGreat. Only how do we get to it?\r\n\r\n00:11:54.005 --\u003e 00:11:55.882\r\nAlways carry a spare.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.012 --\u003e 00:12:03.890\r\nYou first. Press here to\r\nsend it back down to us.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.973 --\u003e 00:12:04.974\r\nWait.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.227 --\u003e 00:12:09.646\r\nJust in case you run\r\ninto trouble up there.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.729 --\u003e 00:12:10.897\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:12:33.753 --\u003e 00:12:35.046\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:12:46.182 --\u003e 00:12:48.059\r\nGORDON: If I ever get\r\nreinstated, Bullock,\r\n\r\n00:12:48.142 --\u003e 00:12:50.228\r\nremind me to do something\r\nabout the food in here.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.603 --\u003e 00:12:54.691\r\nRelax, Commish. We got the judge\r\nto reconsider bail, didn't we?\r\n\r\n00:12:57.819 --\u003e 00:12:59.237\r\nYou gonna eat that pickle?\r\n\r\n00:13:00.363 --\u003e 00:13:01.656\r\n(TICKING)\r\n\r\n00:13:05.493 --\u003e 00:13:06.661\r\n(EXCLAIMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e HORROR)\r\n\r\n00:13:22.927 --\u003e 00:13:24.804\r\n- What in...\r\n- Come on, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.887 --\u003e 00:13:27.640\r\nRupert Thorne doesn't\r\ndesert his friends.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.016 --\u003e 00:13:29.684\r\nThorne...\r\n\r\n00:13:36.149 --\u003e 00:13:40.111\r\nGet some keys down here!\r\nNever a blasted cop when you need one.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.309 --\u003e 00:14:12.518\r\nThink she made it?\r\n\r\n00:14:15.021 --\u003e 00:14:16.230\r\nI hope so.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.981 --\u003e 00:14:18.232\r\nThink we'll make it?\r\n\r\n00:14:20.443 --\u003e 00:14:23.446\r\nWhat do you think about the\r\ncommissioner's innocence now, Detective?\r\n\r\n00:14:23.905 --\u003e 00:14:26.616\r\n- I don't know.\r\n- Come on, he has to be guilty.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.325 --\u003e 00:14:29.511\r\n- Have you heard from Gordon?\r\n- Any leads about his whereabouts?\r\n\r\n00:14:29.535 --\u003e 00:14:30.912\r\nYou think he's left town?\r\n\r\n00:14:30.995 --\u003e 00:14:32.455\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:32.663 --\u003e 00:14:37.418\r\n- Get out of my face, all of you.\r\n- REPORTER: Detective. Detective.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.544 --\u003e 00:14:39.837\r\nI can barely hear you, miss!\r\n\r\n00:14:39.921 --\u003e 00:14:42.965\r\nThe phone lines must've been\r\ndamaged by the explosion.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.342 --\u003e 00:14:45.551\r\nSpeak up!\r\n\r\n00:14:46.135 --\u003e 00:14:49.013\r\nI said Commissioner\r\nGordon's in danger.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.305 --\u003e 00:14:50.848\r\nI still can't hear you.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.932 --\u003e 00:14:54.143\r\nIf you want the story on Gordon's\r\nbreakout, come down here.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.311 --\u003e 00:14:56.396\r\nBreakout?\r\n\r\n00:14:57.146 --\u003e 00:14:58.439\r\nThey've got him.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.784 --\u003e 00:15:11.411\r\nI've got an idea.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.577 --\u003e 00:15:12.578\r\n(INHALES DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:12.912 --\u003e 00:15:14.247\r\nIt's about time.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.941 --\u003e 00:15:45.111\r\n- Where are we going?\r\n- We'll find out when we get there.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.998 --\u003e 00:16:39.999\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.085 --\u003e 00:16:45.338\r\nSubways are getting more\r\ndangerous every day.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.755 --\u003e 00:16:47.435\r\nYou think they got the\r\nCommissioner by now?\r\n\r\n00:16:47.590 --\u003e 00:16:50.635\r\nMost likely.\r\nWe've got to get to Bayshore Wharf.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.052 --\u003e 00:16:54.972\r\nGlad it's not far.\r\nI hate wet shoes.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.644 --\u003e 00:17:02.104\r\nIt's business, Jim.\r\nNothing personal.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.188 --\u003e 00:17:04.857\r\nMatter of fact, I respect you.\r\nI do.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.941 --\u003e 00:17:07.777\r\nBut a fella has to take his\r\nopportunities where he finds them.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.860 --\u003e 00:17:11.280\r\nAnd with you out of the way,\r\nI'll be mayor inside of a year.\r\n\r\n00:17:11.364 --\u003e 00:17:13.366\r\nYou're sick, Gil.\r\nA lot sicker than him.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.741 --\u003e 00:17:15.701\r\nAt least I can see his bad half.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.118 --\u003e 00:17:17.954\r\nSorry you feel that way.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.329 --\u003e 00:17:20.206\r\nAt least you won't have\r\nto worry about Barbara.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.289 --\u003e 00:17:21.707\r\nI'll take good care of her.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.791 --\u003e 00:17:24.001\r\nShe's very fond of me, you know.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.085 --\u003e 00:17:28.548\r\nYou piece of scum. I may not be around\r\nto stop you but I know someone who will.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.006 --\u003e 00:17:30.508\r\nI wouldn't count on it, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.591 --\u003e 00:17:33.261\r\nThere's been a recent decline\r\nin the bat population.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.644 --\u003e 00:17:42.770\r\nRun, Commissioner!\r\n\r\n00:17:42.895 --\u003e 00:17:44.689\r\n(MEN COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:17:48.818 --\u003e 00:17:49.819\r\nGet him!\r\n\r\n00:17:52.655 --\u003e 00:17:54.240\r\nBatgirl, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.659 --\u003e 00:17:59.370\r\nDon't worry.\r\nI'll get you out of this.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.453 --\u003e 00:18:00.496\r\nSomehow.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.839 --\u003e 00:18:10.923\r\nMiss me?\r\n\r\n00:18:13.801 --\u003e 00:18:15.428\r\nI think you're safe now, sir.\r\n\r\n00:18:19.181 --\u003e 00:18:21.267\r\nGet him. Snuff the Bat!\r\n\r\n00:18:23.811 --\u003e 00:18:24.979\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:26.564 --\u003e 00:18:27.565\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:18:36.115 --\u003e 00:18:37.158\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:18:41.454 --\u003e 00:18:42.455\r\n(SPLASHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:43.247 --\u003e 00:18:46.208\r\nYou've screwed up my plans\r\nfor the last time, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.633 --\u003e 00:18:55.426\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:09.398 --\u003e 00:19:11.233\r\nNo, you don't.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.598 --\u003e 00:19:43.599\r\n(YELPS) Ahhh!\r\n\r\n00:19:56.362 --\u003e 00:20:00.908\r\n- That's a first. A coin flips Two-Face.\r\n- Where's Batgirl?\r\n\r\n00:20:00.991 --\u003e 00:20:03.244\r\nOut there. On her own.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.134 --\u003e 00:20:20.428\r\nNow let's see who\r\nyou really are.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.929 --\u003e 00:20:26.183\r\n- Barbara? I didn't know it was you.\r\n- Would it have made a difference, Gil?\r\n\r\n00:20:26.392 --\u003e 00:20:27.518\r\n(can. GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:37.111 --\u003e 00:20:39.488\r\nI ought to leave you here.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.304 --\u003e 00:21:06.766\r\nCommissioner, I understand that\r\nGil Mason is still in a coma.\r\n\r\n00:21:06.849 --\u003e 00:21:09.101\r\nYes, but even so,\r\nhe has been indicted.\r\n\r\n00:21:09.185 --\u003e 00:21:12.146\r\nSo how does it feel to be\r\nbehind your desk again?\r\n\r\n00:21:12.229 --\u003e 00:21:15.065\r\nA heck of a lot better than\r\nit felt being behind bars.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.524 --\u003e 00:21:17.610\r\nAnd what of the\r\nmysterious Batgirl?\r\n\r\n00:21:17.693 --\u003e 00:21:20.863\r\nWho is she and where has she vanished to?\r\nAny thoughts?\r\n\r\n00:21:21.155 --\u003e 00:21:22.656\r\nAs far as I'm concerned,\r\n\r\n00:21:22.740 --\u003e 00:21:24.992\r\nshe's as welcome in\r\nGotham City as the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:21:25.534 --\u003e 00:21:27.495\r\nHow do you think Batman\r\nwill feel about that?\r\n\r\n00:21:27.995 --\u003e 00:21:30.122\r\nI suppose there's always\r\nroom for one more.\r\n\r\n00:21:30.206 --\u003e 00:21:33.584\r\nAnd I have a feeling\r\nwe'll be seeing her again.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.667 --\u003e 00:21:35.836\r\nI wouldn't be at all surprised.\r\n\r\n00:21:52.102 --\u003e 00:21:54.104\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.754 --\u003e 00:22:19.755\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E03 - Mudslide (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.882 --\u003e 00:00:08.842\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.716 --\u003e 00:01:33.802\r\nI'm gonna check the parking lot, Billy.\r\nTry to stay awake, huh?\r\n\r\n00:01:33.885 --\u003e 00:01:36.680\r\n(CHUCKLES) Hey,\r\nit's not past my bedtime, old man.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.451 --\u003e 00:01:58.452\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:01:58.535 --\u003e 00:01:59.786\r\nI didn't hear you come back.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.203 --\u003e 00:02:02.664\r\nSorry, I forgot to check\r\nMr. Tarnower's office.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.748 --\u003e 00:02:04.374\r\nI better do that now.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.057 --\u003e 00:02:21.850\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.991 --\u003e 00:02:39.451\r\nWhat in the name of...\r\n\r\n00:02:43.872 --\u003e 00:02:45.582\r\nLooks like a slow night, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.666 --\u003e 00:02:48.001\r\nWhen I finish patrolling this\r\narea, I'm heading home.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.251 --\u003e 00:02:50.253\r\n\u003ci\u003eExcellent timing, Master Bruce.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:50.337 --\u003e 00:02:52.047\r\n\u003ci\u003eI've just taken dinner\r\nout of the oven.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:54.591 --\u003e 00:02:57.052\r\nLooks like trouble at\r\nTarnower Financial, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:02:57.135 --\u003e 00:02:58.512\r\nI won't be home early after all.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.679 --\u003e 00:03:01.723\r\n(SIGHS) Please don't take\r\nthis the wrong way, sir,\r\n\r\n00:03:01.807 --\u003e 00:03:03.684\r\nbut your goose is cooked.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.788 --\u003e 00:03:27.040\r\nBILLY: Step away from the safe.\r\nNow!\r\n\r\n00:03:27.582 --\u003e 00:03:29.501\r\nDo it, man. I'm cocked!\r\n\r\n00:03:31.753 --\u003e 00:03:33.171\r\n(SQUELCHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:36.174 --\u003e 00:03:37.259\r\nMr. Tarnower?\r\n\r\n00:03:37.551 --\u003e 00:03:39.594\r\nWhat did you expect? Batman?\r\n\r\n00:03:40.137 --\u003e 00:03:43.557\r\nYou should be downstairs guarding the door.\r\nWhat do I pay you for?\r\n\r\n00:03:43.890 --\u003e 00:03:46.268\r\nYes, sir. Sorry. I thought...\r\n\r\n00:03:46.768 --\u003e 00:03:49.020\r\nHey,\r\nwhat happened to your accent?\r\n\r\n00:03:49.104 --\u003e 00:03:50.897\r\nAnd aren't you supposed\r\nto be in Hawaii?\r\n\r\n00:03:51.481 --\u003e 00:03:52.482\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:00.657 --\u003e 00:04:03.952\r\nBatman? Thank goodness you're here.\r\nI caught a thief.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.670 --\u003e 00:04:14.671\r\n(CHAINS RATTLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:19.176 --\u003e 00:04:20.177\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:27.893 --\u003e 00:04:31.813\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:04:41.615 --\u003e 00:04:42.783\r\n(CLOCK CHIMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.143 --\u003e 00:05:13.146\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:22.280 --\u003e 00:05:23.490\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:05:25.992 --\u003e 00:05:27.577\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:32.290 --\u003e 00:05:35.710\r\nHagen, I offered to help\r\nyou become human again.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.961 --\u003e 00:05:37.462\r\nThe offer still stands.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.879 --\u003e 00:05:40.298\r\nI don't need your help, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.925 --\u003e 00:05:43.218\r\nHave it your way.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.059 --\u003e 00:05:52.060\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:57.607 --\u003e 00:06:00.443\r\nYou used to be faster, Hagen.\r\nNot to mention neater.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.778 --\u003e 00:06:03.363\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:13.123 --\u003e 00:06:14.541\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:21.631 --\u003e 00:06:22.966\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:24.551 --\u003e 00:06:25.719\r\nMatthew, get in.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.789 --\u003e 00:06:56.666\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:01.755 --\u003e 00:07:03.006\r\n(BREATH ES HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:07:03.798 --\u003e 00:07:05.216\r\nStella.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.884 --\u003e 00:07:08.595\r\nThere, there.\r\nIt's gonna be all right, Matthew.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.678 --\u003e 00:07:12.098\r\nI'll fix everything.\r\nDon't you worry.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.724 --\u003e 00:07:14.142\r\nIt'll be all right.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.225 --\u003e 00:07:17.979\r\nI'll take care of you.\r\nI won't let anything happen to you.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.234 --\u003e 00:07:24.235\r\n(MACHINERY POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:07:49.886 --\u003e 00:07:52.097\r\nIt's okay now, Matthew.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.348 --\u003e 00:07:55.141\r\nSleep, my darling.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.652 --\u003e 00:08:08.530\r\nALFRED: Am I correct in\r\nassuming metamorphic Mr. Hagen\r\n\r\n00:08:08.613 --\u003e 00:08:10.115\r\nis back in town, sir?\r\n\r\n00:08:10.323 --\u003e 00:08:12.617\r\nBack, but not for\r\nlong, I'd guess.\r\n\r\n00:08:13.076 --\u003e 00:08:15.578\r\nIt seems that Clayface\r\nis losing his integrity.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.912 --\u003e 00:08:18.415\r\nI wasn't aware that he\r\never had any to begin with.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.790 --\u003e 00:08:21.334\r\nI'm speaking in a physiological\r\nsense, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.627 --\u003e 00:08:25.672\r\nBased on destructive ultrasonic\r\nanalysis of the sample,\r\n\r\n00:08:25.839 --\u003e 00:08:28.967\r\nthe molecular bonding of his\r\nclay flesh is breaking down.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.384 --\u003e 00:08:31.720\r\nHe's falling apart, literally.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.345 --\u003e 00:08:33.513\r\nALFRED: How grotesque.\r\n\r\n00:08:33.680 --\u003e 00:08:34.806\r\nTea?\r\n\r\n00:08:37.809 --\u003e 00:08:40.478\r\nWhatever medical process he's\r\nusing to keep himself together\r\n\r\n00:08:40.562 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\nmust cost a fortune.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.230 --\u003e 00:08:44.065\r\nWhich is why he's\r\ncommitting robberies.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.357 --\u003e 00:08:47.402\r\nAnd that woman helping him,\r\nwhat's her stake in this?\r\n\r\n00:08:47.485 --\u003e 00:08:49.821\r\nMmm.\r\nPerhaps she enjoys mud baths.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.787 --\u003e 00:09:02.208\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe surgery was a success, Eric...\r\nI mean, Senator Chandler.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:07.589 --\u003e 00:09:11.551\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, darling, how wonderful.\r\nLet's get married right away.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:16.473 --\u003e 00:09:18.016\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:09:22.187 --\u003e 00:09:23.188\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:09:28.943 --\u003e 00:09:30.695\r\n\u003ci\u003eSusan. Wait.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:31.654 --\u003e 00:09:34.491\r\n\u003ci\u003eI love you, Susan.\r\nYou cured more than my body,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:35.033 --\u003e 00:09:36.367\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou cured my heart.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:48.963 --\u003e 00:09:51.216\r\n- CLAYFACE: Turn it off!\r\n- Matthew?\r\n\r\n00:09:56.638 --\u003e 00:09:58.223\r\nThat's not me anymore.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.017 --\u003e 00:10:03.478\r\nI'm sorry, Matthew.\r\nI didn't think you'd be awake yet.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.938 --\u003e 00:10:07.273\r\nI don't know if I can\r\nstand this much longer.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.816 --\u003e 00:10:11.027\r\nTrapped in this suit,\r\nsurviving on chemicals.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.111 --\u003e 00:10:12.320\r\nIt's a nightmare!\r\n\r\n00:10:15.073 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nStella.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.658 --\u003e 00:10:17.659\r\nI'm sorry.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.618 --\u003e 00:10:20.578\r\nI know I owe everything to you.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.204 --\u003e 00:10:23.164\r\nYou cured more than my body,\r\n\r\n00:10:23.706 --\u003e 00:10:25.041\r\nyou cured my heart.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.291 --\u003e 00:10:28.503\r\nI have something to show you, Matthew.\r\nSomething new.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.522 --\u003e 00:10:48.898\r\nSTELLA: Now, watch.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.277 --\u003e 00:10:55.405\r\n- How did you do that?\r\n- A new isotope.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.989 --\u003e 00:10:59.492\r\nMP-40. An experimental\r\nmutagenic adaptogen.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.784 --\u003e 00:11:01.244\r\nI believe it can restore,\r\n\r\n00:11:01.327 --\u003e 00:11:04.914\r\nmaybe even increase your\r\npowers, perhaps permanently.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.290 --\u003e 00:11:08.543\r\nYou can become Matt Hagen\r\nagain, forever.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.877 --\u003e 00:11:10.461\r\nWhere can we get this stuff?\r\n\r\n00:11:10.587 --\u003e 00:11:14.716\r\nWell, that's a problem. The only\r\nlarge source is Wayne Biomedical Labs.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.508 --\u003e 00:11:17.635\r\nIt's rare and it will\r\nbe well-protected.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.719 --\u003e 00:11:21.848\r\nProtected from human thieves,\r\nmaybe, but not from Clayface.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.307 --\u003e 00:11:24.309\r\nNo, Matthew. It's too risky.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.517 --\u003e 00:11:27.770\r\nWithout the suit, your structural\r\nintegrity could go at any time.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.062 --\u003e 00:11:29.230\r\nIt's worth the risk.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.731 --\u003e 00:11:32.066\r\nI'm not spending the rest\r\nof my life like this.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.788 --\u003e 00:11:47.290\r\nAnything interesting\r\nyet, Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:11:47.999 --\u003e 00:11:51.961\r\nIt appears his past dealings with women\r\nhad nothing to do with medicine, sir.\r\n\r\n00:11:52.170 --\u003e 00:11:54.923\r\nNo record so far of\r\nany female doctors.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.256 --\u003e 00:11:58.718\r\nKeep looking.\r\nIf we find her, we find him.\r\n\r\n00:12:22.700 --\u003e 00:12:23.910\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:23.993 --\u003e 00:12:25.662\r\nLet's cut to the chase.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.912 --\u003e 00:12:27.914\r\nThe MP-40, where is it?\r\n\r\n00:12:28.498 --\u003e 00:12:29.499\r\n(MUFFLED SPEECH)\r\n\r\n00:12:44.806 --\u003e 00:12:45.807\r\n(BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:12:49.060 --\u003e 00:12:51.229\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:12:51.312 --\u003e 00:12:54.315\r\nA monster.\r\nThere's a monster in the lab!\r\n\r\n00:12:54.649 --\u003e 00:12:57.360\r\nOkay, okay. Just take it easy.\r\nWe'll handle it.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.579 --\u003e 00:13:09.580\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:44.741 --\u003e 00:13:46.868\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:49.746 --\u003e 00:13:53.791\r\nLook at that lady, Mommy.\r\nShe's got mud all over her.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.091 --\u003e 00:14:03.343\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:05.386 --\u003e 00:14:08.598\r\nCHILD: Ew! Mommy, she's melting!\r\n\r\n00:14:10.516 --\u003e 00:14:12.411\r\n- WOMAN: What is it?\r\n- MAN 1: Let me out of here.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.435 --\u003e 00:14:14.079\r\n- MAN 2: Oh, gross!\r\n- MAN 3: Coming through.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.103 --\u003e 00:14:16.248\r\n- MAN 4: God, that smells.\r\n- MAN 5: Oh, I'm gonna be sick!\r\n\r\n00:14:16.272 --\u003e 00:14:17.440\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.608 --\u003e 00:14:21.861\r\nThat's it, run.\r\nRun for your measly lives.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.070 --\u003e 00:14:23.780\r\nRun from Clayface!\r\n\r\n00:14:23.863 --\u003e 00:14:24.864\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.047 --\u003e 00:14:42.673\r\nCLAYFACE: You're dead\r\nmeat, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.757 --\u003e 00:14:45.176\r\nNo room to dodge. I gotcha cold.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.426 --\u003e 00:14:47.011\r\nOther way around, Hagen.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.428 --\u003e 00:14:48.638\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.985 --\u003e 00:15:04.278\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:26.592 --\u003e 00:15:27.593\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:28.386 --\u003e 00:15:30.471\r\n(LAUGHS MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:45.403 --\u003e 00:15:48.531\r\nALFRED: There's nothing here about\r\nany women doctors, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.614 --\u003e 00:15:51.617\r\nThe ladies Mr. Hagen knew\r\nwere generally of a less, uh,\r\n\r\n00:15:52.285 --\u003e 00:15:53.870\r\nintellectual class.\r\n\r\n00:15:54.036 --\u003e 00:15:55.329\r\nWe're missing something.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.538 --\u003e 00:15:56.831\r\nI can't imagine what.\r\n\r\n00:15:56.914 --\u003e 00:15:59.542\r\nClosest thing Hagen had to\r\na relationship with a doctor\r\n\r\n00:15:59.750 --\u003e 00:16:03.254\r\nwas in the film Dark Interlude.\r\nIn it, he plays Eric Chandler,\r\n\r\n00:16:03.421 --\u003e 00:16:06.716\r\na senator who falls in love with\r\nthe plastic surgeon treating him.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.799 --\u003e 00:16:08.759\r\nThat's it. His movies!\r\n\r\n00:16:09.260 --\u003e 00:16:11.804\r\n- Master Bruce?\r\n- No time to explain now, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.221 --\u003e 00:16:13.514\r\nThere never is.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.598 --\u003e 00:16:15.183\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:16:36.037 --\u003e 00:16:37.038\r\n(MACHINERY POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.377 --\u003e 00:16:45.129\r\nI... I can feel it.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.258 --\u003e 00:16:50.259\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.551 --\u003e 00:16:52.637\r\nYes! It's working.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.471 --\u003e 00:16:54.472\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.725 --\u003e 00:16:58.726\r\n(MACHINERY POWERING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:16:58.809 --\u003e 00:16:59.810\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:00.311 --\u003e 00:17:03.147\r\nSTELLA: Batman.\r\nNo, turn it back on.\r\n\r\n00:17:03.523 --\u003e 00:17:04.690\r\nI was so close.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.982 --\u003e 00:17:09.070\r\nSo close! I almost felt\r\nlike Matt Hagen again.\r\n\r\n00:17:09.862 --\u003e 00:17:11.197\r\nHow did you find us?\r\n\r\n00:17:11.364 --\u003e 00:17:14.992\r\nI realized you must've used a medical\r\nconsultant on some of your films.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.368 --\u003e 00:17:17.828\r\nI found Dr. Bates' name\r\nin an old film log.\r\n\r\n00:17:18.287 --\u003e 00:17:19.747\r\nDr.\r\nBates had once owned a motel,\r\n\r\n00:17:19.830 --\u003e 00:17:22.083\r\nbut sold it to get money for\r\nthis, lexpect.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.291 --\u003e 00:17:24.752\r\nThis was the address the\r\nbank had in its files.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.086 --\u003e 00:17:28.172\r\nIt's over, Hagen.\r\nThe lab boys can take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.256 --\u003e 00:17:29.966\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:38.224 --\u003e 00:17:40.309\r\nStella!\r\n\r\n00:17:44.480 --\u003e 00:17:45.856\r\n(INHALES)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.732 --\u003e 00:17:47.733\r\n(ROARING)\r\n\r\n00:17:52.280 --\u003e 00:17:54.865\r\nYou've upstaged me for the last\r\ntime, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.411 --\u003e 00:18:00.037\r\nTime to bring down the curtain.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.422 --\u003e 00:18:11.507\r\nTime for your final bow, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:18:13.134 --\u003e 00:18:15.011\r\nMatthew, no! You can't.\r\n\r\n00:18:17.972 --\u003e 00:18:19.265\r\nIt's the only way.\r\n\r\n00:18:26.480 --\u003e 00:18:27.815\r\nPlease, stop it.\r\n\r\n00:18:28.316 --\u003e 00:18:32.612\r\nThink, Stella.\r\nDo you want Matt Hagen or this?\r\n\r\n00:18:33.613 --\u003e 00:18:34.614\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.951 --\u003e 00:18:41.037\r\nCLAYFACE: No, you don't!\r\n\r\n00:18:42.872 --\u003e 00:18:44.624\r\nSTELLA: ls... Is he...\r\n\r\n00:18:46.334 --\u003e 00:18:47.543\r\nAlmost.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.793 --\u003e 00:18:49.629\r\nI can feel his heart slowing.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.630 --\u003e 00:18:51.672\r\nSlowing.\r\n\r\n00:18:53.716 --\u003e 00:18:54.717\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.302 --\u003e 00:18:57.303\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:18:57.386 --\u003e 00:18:58.666\r\n- (PROJECTILE FIRING)\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:59.722 --\u003e 00:19:00.723\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:24.664 --\u003e 00:19:26.207\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.646 --\u003e 00:19:49.647\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:19:52.400 --\u003e 00:19:54.443\r\nSTELLA: Matthew,\r\nget back inside!\r\n\r\n00:19:55.152 --\u003e 00:19:58.489\r\nYou're absorbing the rain!\r\nMatthew!\r\n\r\n00:20:10.292 --\u003e 00:20:11.502\r\nMatthew!\r\n\r\n00:20:11.585 --\u003e 00:20:12.586\r\nCLAYFACE: No.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.170 --\u003e 00:20:15.548\r\nWe finish this now.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.069 --\u003e 00:20:39.822\r\nSave him, Batman. Please!\r\n\r\n00:20:40.197 --\u003e 00:20:43.242\r\nCome on, Hagen.\r\nPull yourself together.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.747 --\u003e 00:20:48.956\r\nToo late.\r\n\r\n00:20:49.749 --\u003e 00:20:51.500\r\nCurtain's going...\r\n\r\n00:20:53.627 --\u003e 00:20:55.880\r\n- Down.\r\n- Hagen!\r\n\r\n00:20:58.883 --\u003e 00:21:00.301\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:21:28.704 --\u003e 00:21:30.831\r\n(STELLA WEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:21:50.559 --\u003e 00:21:52.478\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:17.545 --\u003e 00:22:18.546\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E04 - The Worry Men (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.356 --\u003e 00:00:24.358\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:31.842 --\u003e 00:01:34.595\r\nHello, Gotham, I'm home!\r\n\r\n00:01:34.678 --\u003e 00:01:36.888\r\nMAN 1: Hello, Ronnie!\r\nMAN 2: Ronnie!\r\n\r\n00:01:37.055 --\u003e 00:01:40.017\r\nWOMAN: Veronica, darling,\r\nyou look smashing.\r\n\r\n00:01:40.684 --\u003e 00:01:42.603\r\nHow did you like\r\nthe rain forest?\r\n\r\n00:01:42.686 --\u003e 00:01:46.231\r\nThe food was appalling,\r\nthe accommodations were nonexistent\r\n\r\n00:01:46.315 --\u003e 00:01:49.151\r\nand the bugs were the\r\nsize of my trust fund.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.234 --\u003e 00:01:51.278\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:52.821 --\u003e 00:01:55.991\r\nBut seriously,\r\nit's important we all do our part\r\n\r\n00:01:56.074 --\u003e 00:01:58.243\r\nto preserve those\r\nprecious resources.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.327 --\u003e 00:02:00.495\r\n- MAN: Hear, hear.\r\n- (PEOPLE CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:02.122 --\u003e 00:02:04.791\r\nLook at them,\r\ncelebrating without a care in the world.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.875 --\u003e 00:02:07.085\r\nI think it's great\r\nthat Veronica's finally\r\n\r\n00:02:07.169 --\u003e 00:02:09.129\r\ndoing something\r\nworthwhile with her money.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.588 --\u003e 00:02:10.881\r\nI'm sorry, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.964 --\u003e 00:02:13.026\r\nThe securities business has\r\nbeen kind of rough lately.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.050 --\u003e 00:02:14.384\r\nLot of late hours, you know.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.718 --\u003e 00:02:18.096\r\nSeems all I do is worry about how to\r\nget my company through one more day.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.472 --\u003e 00:02:21.767\r\nWorries, Hayden?\r\nI have the cure for that.\r\n\r\n00:02:24.436 --\u003e 00:02:26.480\r\nI'm a little old for\r\ndolls, don't you think?\r\n\r\n00:02:26.938 --\u003e 00:02:28.273\r\nNot these dolls.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.649 --\u003e 00:02:31.234\r\nThey're Worry Men\r\nfrom Central America.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.568 --\u003e 00:02:33.528\r\nLegends say you tell\r\nthem your problems,\r\n\r\n00:02:33.612 --\u003e 00:02:35.572\r\nthen put them under\r\nyour pillow at night.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.656 --\u003e 00:02:37.991\r\nThey'll do your worrying\r\nfor you while you sleep.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.450 --\u003e 00:02:41.912\r\nAnd when you wake up, poof,\r\nyour problems are gone.\r\n\r\n00:02:41.995 --\u003e 00:02:43.455\r\nOh, come on, Ronnie.\r\n\r\n00:02:43.622 --\u003e 00:02:46.667\r\nYou're the last one I'd think would\r\nfall for some ancient tribal hoodoo.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.875 --\u003e 00:02:48.627\r\nDon't be so smug, Brucie.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.752 --\u003e 00:02:52.255\r\nWhen I was in the jungle,\r\nI saw some things you'd never believe.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.939 --\u003e 00:03:12.275\r\nAnd I tell you, I haven't had a\r\nbad night's sleep since my trip.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.734 --\u003e 00:03:14.319\r\nWell, sounds great to me.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.571 --\u003e 00:03:19.700\r\nIn fact, the little darlings work\r\ntheir magic for me all day long.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.785 --\u003e 00:03:23.954\r\nSee, aren't they precious?\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:29.852\r\n- I just couldn't get along without them.\r\n- Thanks for everything, Ron.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.876 --\u003e 00:03:31.712\r\nBut I've got a few\r\nmore rounds to make.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.920 --\u003e 00:03:32.921\r\n(SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:03:33.004 --\u003e 00:03:37.551\r\nIf ever someone led a worry-free\r\nlife, it's you, Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.267 --\u003e 00:03:47.436\r\nI've got one for everybody.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.937 --\u003e 00:03:50.272\r\nBATMAN: Party crasher.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.868 --\u003e 00:04:03.952\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:04.244 --\u003e 00:04:05.579\r\nNasty 1103!-\r\n\r\n00:04:18.175 --\u003e 00:04:19.676\r\nReady to call it a night?\r\n\r\n00:04:25.766 --\u003e 00:04:26.767\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:37.444 --\u003e 00:04:38.445\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:39.321 --\u003e 00:04:40.489\r\n(STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:57.047 --\u003e 00:04:58.381\r\n(PEOPLE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:05:02.719 --\u003e 00:05:04.721\r\n- (PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n- Oh, my heavens!\r\n\r\n00:05:15.899 --\u003e 00:05:17.692\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.662 --\u003e 00:05:30.580\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:05:37.879 --\u003e 00:05:39.714\r\n(PEOPLE CLAMORING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.249 --\u003e 00:06:15.292\r\nBRUCE: Tell me, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.375 --\u003e 00:06:18.879\r\nWhat's an ancient Mayan witch\r\ndoctor doing on a Gotham skyscraper?\r\n\r\n00:06:19.129 --\u003e 00:06:21.590\r\nThis isn't one of those\r\nRiddler questions, is it?\r\n\r\n00:06:22.299 --\u003e 00:06:24.175\r\nNo, but it's just as confusing.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.342 --\u003e 00:06:28.179\r\nThere's someone new in town using\r\nMayan tribal gimmicks in his crimes.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.346 --\u003e 00:06:32.142\r\n- Blowguns, stone weapons.\r\n- Voodoo dolls?\r\n\r\n00:06:32.434 --\u003e 00:06:35.020\r\nThat's some party favor\r\nfrom Veronica's party.\r\n\r\n00:06:35.103 --\u003e 00:06:37.423\r\nThey're supposed to take away\r\nyour worries while you sleep.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.689 --\u003e 00:06:38.815\r\nImagine that.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.940 --\u003e 00:06:42.527\r\nWhat some overworked souls won't\r\ndo to get a good night's rest.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.486 --\u003e 00:06:44.613\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:06:45.614 --\u003e 00:06:47.407\r\nStill, every little bit helps.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.043 --\u003e 00:07:01.171\r\nI tell you, child, I handle all\r\nsorts of things for Mr. Wayne,\r\n\r\n00:07:01.254 --\u003e 00:07:03.840\r\nbut this one really\r\ntakes the cake.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.009 --\u003e 00:07:07.385\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.552 --\u003e 00:07:10.138\r\n- Oh, Morning, Dana.\r\n- Oh, I gotta go. Bye-bye.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.100 --\u003e 00:07:16.478\r\n(BRUCE HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:07:19.981 --\u003e 00:07:22.567\r\nSometimes I forget how\r\nbeautiful Gotham can be.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.943 --\u003e 00:07:25.737\r\nYou're in fine\r\nspirits, I must say.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.573 --\u003e 00:07:31.785\r\nA good night's sleep and I'm\r\nready to take on the world.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.160 --\u003e 00:07:33.262\r\nYou got everything all right?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.286 --\u003e 00:07:35.830\r\nYes, I followed your\r\nmessage to the letter.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.914 --\u003e 00:07:38.708\r\n- But I can't help wondering what-\r\n- Thank you.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.543 --\u003e 00:07:42.420\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:15.286 --\u003e 00:08:19.582\r\nI know it's your company,\r\nMr. Wayne, but $20 million, man.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.666 --\u003e 00:08:23.211\r\n- That's a lot of money.\r\n- Yes, it is. What's your point?\r\n\r\n00:08:23.294 --\u003e 00:08:26.548\r\nWell, I'd sure feel uncomfortable\r\nwalking around with all that cash\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:28.466\r\nin a tiny little briefcase.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.550 --\u003e 00:08:32.429\r\nDana, I'm sorry. I'm not following this.\r\nWhat cash? What briefcase?\r\n\r\n00:08:32.804 --\u003e 00:08:36.474\r\nThe $20 million you told me\r\nto put in a briefcase for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.017 --\u003e 00:08:38.643\r\nYou're not making any sense.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.727 --\u003e 00:08:41.479\r\nThe $20 million I told\r\nyou to put in a briefcase?\r\n\r\n00:08:41.563 --\u003e 00:08:44.482\r\nYou called me from your car,\r\ngave me your account number,\r\n\r\n00:08:44.566 --\u003e 00:08:48.486\r\ntold me to transfer $20\r\nmillion in cash and... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:50.947 --\u003e 00:08:51.948\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:56.578 --\u003e 00:08:57.787\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:08:58.997 --\u003e 00:09:02.167\r\n$20 million of my\r\nmoney in that case?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.500 --\u003e 00:09:05.462\r\nI hope you're not going to\r\ntake it out of my salary.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.883 --\u003e 00:09:11.384\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:09:13.678 --\u003e 00:09:15.598\r\nREPORTER: \u003ci\u003eTens of millions\r\nof dollars are missing\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:15.638 --\u003e 00:09:16.866\r\n\u003ci\u003esince this morning, Mr. Sloane.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:16.890 --\u003e 00:09:18.516\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf it wasn't you, then who?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:18.600 --\u003e 00:09:22.937\r\n\u003ci\u003e(STAMMERS) But I don't know, I tell you.\r\nI don't know. Why would I do it? Why?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:23.021 --\u003e 00:09:26.149\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat was the scene today as\r\nbroker Hayden Sloane was arrested\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:26.232 --\u003e 00:09:27.609\r\non charges of embezzlement.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.692 --\u003e 00:09:31.488\r\n\u003ci\u003eSloane joins the growing list of wealthy\r\nGothamites who, for reasons unknown,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:31.571 --\u003e 00:09:36.451\r\n\u003ci\u003ehave pilfered their own companies\r\nfor a combined total of $100 million.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:38.411 --\u003e 00:09:39.829\r\nUnbelievable.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.538 --\u003e 00:09:42.957\r\nAnd you have no clue how\r\nthis could have happened?\r\n\r\n00:09:43.041 --\u003e 00:09:47.337\r\nI do now. Each of us was a guest\r\nat Veronica Vreeland's party.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.296 --\u003e 00:09:50.799\r\nIf there are answers,\r\nshe's got them.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.425 --\u003e 00:09:53.885\r\n(VERONICA HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.728 --\u003e 00:10:04.854\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:05.814 --\u003e 00:10:07.315\r\nBATMAN: Miss Vreeland.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.649 --\u003e 00:10:08.733\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:10:12.737 --\u003e 00:10:14.197\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:10:15.323 --\u003e 00:10:17.325\r\nLet me help you with your bag.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.034 --\u003e 00:10:19.619\r\nNo, you stay back.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.953 --\u003e 00:10:22.247\r\nThis is mine, you hear? Mine.\r\n\r\n00:10:23.206 --\u003e 00:10:24.249\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:25.917 --\u003e 00:10:29.003\r\nI know it's yours.\r\nWhat were you planning to do with it?\r\n\r\n00:10:29.087 --\u003e 00:10:32.090\r\nI have to throw it\r\noverboard because...\r\n\r\n00:10:32.257 --\u003e 00:10:33.466\r\nBecause...\r\n\r\n00:10:33.550 --\u003e 00:10:36.553\r\nExcuse me,\r\nI don't feel very well.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.858 --\u003e 00:10:51.317\r\nCare to explain these?\r\n\r\n00:10:52.193 --\u003e 00:10:53.278\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:53.361 --\u003e 00:10:56.030\r\nMy jewels!\r\nHow did they get here?\r\n\r\n00:10:56.114 --\u003e 00:11:00.451\r\n- Don't you remember?\r\n- No, everything's a blank. I...\r\n\r\n00:11:00.660 --\u003e 00:11:01.786\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:08.793 --\u003e 00:11:10.086\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:13.923 --\u003e 00:11:15.091\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:17.594 --\u003e 00:11:19.429\r\nLeave him alone, you swine!\r\n\r\n00:11:20.346 --\u003e 00:11:21.431\r\nPlease?\r\n\r\n00:11:39.199 --\u003e 00:11:41.701\r\nMy therapist is never\r\ngoing to believe this.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.784 --\u003e 00:11:44.704\r\nAnd I thought you were supposed\r\nto take away my worries.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.789 --\u003e 00:11:47.832\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.250 --\u003e 00:11:52.170\r\nWell, say goodbye,\r\nyou troublesome little trinkets.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.380 --\u003e 00:11:57.717\r\nWait. These dolls.\r\nWhere did you get them?\r\n\r\n00:11:57.800 --\u003e 00:12:02.680\r\nFrom a craftsman at a small village.\r\nA funny little man in a giant straw hat.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.140 --\u003e 00:12:05.516\r\nAn Englishman?\r\n\r\n00:12:06.184 --\u003e 00:12:07.477\r\nWhy, yes.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.560 --\u003e 00:12:10.730\r\nAnd he suggested giving the\r\ndolls to your society friends.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.856 --\u003e 00:12:13.441\r\nWhat, are you psychic, too?\r\n\r\n00:12:13.900 --\u003e 00:12:16.277\r\nJust picking up on the pattern.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.708 --\u003e 00:12:34.629\r\nSir, you have no idea how terrible I\r\nfeel to have played a part in this.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.129 --\u003e 00:12:38.132\r\nNeither you nor Veronica could have\r\nknown that hidden within each doll\r\n\r\n00:12:38.216 --\u003e 00:12:42.011\r\nwas a tiny microchip designed to\r\nstimulate a sleeper's brainwaves\r\n\r\n00:12:42.095 --\u003e 00:12:44.472\r\nand make them susceptible\r\nto hypnotic suggestion.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.639 --\u003e 00:12:49.686\r\nCreating a radio receiver of sorts\r\nout of an entranced human mind?\r\n\r\n00:12:49.769 --\u003e 00:12:50.979\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.195 --\u003e 00:13:01.614\r\nAnd who knows how to warp\r\nthe human mind better\r\n\r\n00:13:01.698 --\u003e 00:13:05.076\r\nthan Jervis Tetch,\r\nthe Mad Hatter?\r\n\r\n00:13:05.493 --\u003e 00:13:10.957\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAD\u003c/i\u003e HATTER: \u003ci\u003e\"'0 frabjous day, callooh,\r\ncallay, ' he chortled in his joy.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:11.040 --\u003e 00:13:13.126\r\nIt's sheer brilliance.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.209 --\u003e 00:13:14.961\r\nA wonderland of treasures\r\n\r\n00:13:15.044 --\u003e 00:13:18.840\r\nall willingly donated by\r\nGotham's simpering elite.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.215 --\u003e 00:13:20.216\r\nAh.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.300 --\u003e 00:13:24.512\r\nAnd now come the famous Vreeland\r\njewels to dance at my heels.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.097 --\u003e 00:13:29.809\r\nWhat? How dare you\r\nreturn empty-handed?\r\n\r\n00:13:30.184 --\u003e 00:13:32.729\r\nForgive us, sir.\r\nBut Batman showed up, and-\r\n\r\n00:13:32.812 --\u003e 00:13:33.938\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:13:34.314 --\u003e 00:13:36.816\r\nYou insufferable fools.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.191 --\u003e 00:13:41.279\r\nYou can't even handle one man\r\ndressed up like a flying mouse?\r\n\r\n00:13:41.779 --\u003e 00:13:42.780\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:43.948 --\u003e 00:13:46.409\r\nOh, and what's this?\r\nWhat's this?\r\n\r\n00:13:46.492 --\u003e 00:13:49.412\r\nYou've graciously left\r\npart of your cloak behind\r\n\r\n00:13:49.495 --\u003e 00:13:52.540\r\nas Batman's invitation to\r\nwaltz right into our midst.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.957 --\u003e 00:13:54.083\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.043 --\u003e 00:13:58.004\r\nAnd that's just what he'll\r\ndo, won't he?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.839 --\u003e 00:14:01.132\r\nOf course he will.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.215 --\u003e 00:14:05.386\r\nAnd far be it for me to\r\ndisappoint him when he arrives.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.928 --\u003e 00:14:08.389\r\n(EVIL LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:14:30.953 --\u003e 00:14:33.998\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: As you predicted, sir,\r\nthe computer has identified\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:34.082 --\u003e 00:14:38.503\r\n\u003ci\u003ethis scrap of artificial fur as a\r\ntype used in theatrical productions,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:38.836 --\u003e 00:14:41.297\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhich would make its most\r\nprobable source of origin-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:41.381 --\u003e 00:14:43.800\r\nThe Great Eastern\r\nCostume Company.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.883 --\u003e 00:14:45.426\r\nIt's been closed for years,\r\n\r\n00:14:45.843 --\u003e 00:14:48.471\r\nmaking it a perfect\r\nhideout for the Mad Hatter.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.167 --\u003e 00:15:20.420\r\n\u003ci\u003eMAD HATTER: I knew you were\r\ncoming, so I thought\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:20.503 --\u003e 00:15:23.548\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'd have some of the old chaps\r\n'round to make you feel at home.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:23.631 --\u003e 00:15:24.966\r\n(GIGGLES)\r\n\r\n00:15:36.185 --\u003e 00:15:39.063\r\n- How is Batman like a donut \u003ci\u003eshop?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:15:39.814 --\u003e 00:15:42.692\r\n\u003ci\u003e- They're both filled with holes.\r\n- (GRUNTS)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:43.401 --\u003e 00:15:44.652\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:04.213 --\u003e 00:16:05.214\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:19.145 --\u003e 00:16:20.271\r\n(EXHALES)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.527 --\u003e 00:16:27.570\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhoops.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:27.653 --\u003e 00:16:29.989\r\n\u003ci\u003eShould have warned you, old boy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:30.239 --\u003e 00:16:32.283\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat lot's real.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:32.366 --\u003e 00:16:34.202\r\n(GRUNTING AND STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:38.122 --\u003e 00:16:39.373\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:16:41.792 --\u003e 00:16:42.877\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:44.337 --\u003e 00:16:45.463\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.437 --\u003e 00:17:07.360\r\nDelightful. Oh, quite a bonus to add\r\nto my already-substantial collection.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.569 --\u003e 00:17:10.112\r\nYou disappoint me, Tetch.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.196 --\u003e 00:17:12.907\r\nFor all your brilliance,\r\nyou've become just another thief.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.241 --\u003e 00:17:16.244\r\nYou make it sound so common.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.702 --\u003e 00:17:18.162\r\nWell, actually, Batman,\r\n\r\n00:17:18.246 --\u003e 00:17:22.500\r\nyou'll be happy to know you're\r\nwitnessing my retirement from crime.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.251 --\u003e 00:17:25.795\r\nSee, after my recent\r\nrelease from Arkham,\r\n\r\n00:17:25.878 --\u003e 00:17:29.465\r\nI vowed to leave Gotham and\r\nmy wicked ways behind me.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.674 --\u003e 00:17:35.179\r\nPerhaps buy a little island\r\nsomewhere and open a sunbonnet shop.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.513 --\u003e 00:17:40.101\r\nBut islands, even little\r\nones, cost money.\r\n\r\n00:17:40.810 --\u003e 00:17:42.979\r\n(SNIFFLING) Lots of money.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.062 --\u003e 00:17:45.940\r\nAnd then I heard of Ms.\r\nVreeland's\r\n\r\n00:17:46.023 --\u003e 00:17:48.693\r\nwell-publicized trek\r\ninto the rain forest.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.985 --\u003e 00:17:55.449\r\nYes, I realized at once she'd be the\r\nperfect unwitting partner in my scheme.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.285 --\u003e 00:17:59.537\r\n\u003ci\u003eInvesting what\r\nlimited funds I had,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:59.620 --\u003e 00:18:02.498\r\n\u003ci\u003eI managed to follow dear\r\nRonnie into the forest\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:02.582 --\u003e 00:18:05.960\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhere, at a small native village,\r\nshe made the acquaintance\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:06.043 --\u003e 00:18:09.005\r\n\u003ci\u003eof my specially-created\r\nWorry Men.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:13.759 --\u003e 00:18:16.053\r\nThough,\r\nI can't take complete credit.\r\n\r\n00:18:16.137 --\u003e 00:18:18.973\r\nI provided the\r\nmicrocircuitry, of course,\r\n\r\n00:18:19.056 --\u003e 00:18:22.143\r\nbut my good friend here\r\nsupplied the dolls.\r\n\r\n00:18:22.852 --\u003e 00:18:24.478\r\nCan you believe it?\r\n\r\n00:18:24.562 --\u003e 00:18:27.440\r\nHe was just an honest\r\nnative craftsman\r\n\r\n00:18:27.523 --\u003e 00:18:30.818\r\nuntil I changed his\r\nmind about helping me.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.901 --\u003e 00:18:35.239\r\nThose others are riffraff culled\r\nout of various Gotham street gangs.\r\n\r\n00:18:35.323 --\u003e 00:18:37.950\r\nGutter trash of no\r\ngreat importance.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.242 --\u003e 00:18:40.786\r\nSo, as this is my\r\nfarewell to crime,\r\n\r\n00:18:40.870 --\u003e 00:18:43.372\r\nI think I'll take a souvenir\r\nto mark the occasion.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.749 --\u003e 00:18:45.958\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:48.836 --\u003e 00:18:53.716\r\nNo matter. I have a better way\r\nto remove that nasty old cowl.\r\n\r\n00:19:01.390 --\u003e 00:19:04.018\r\nStop! You don't know\r\nwhat you're doing.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.402 --\u003e 00:19:15.279\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:19:15.571 --\u003e 00:19:17.031\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:19:22.703 --\u003e 00:19:24.330\r\nOh, that noise!\r\n\r\n00:19:26.874 --\u003e 00:19:28.542\r\nWhat's going on?\r\n\r\n00:19:30.044 --\u003e 00:19:31.504\r\nHow did I get here?\r\n\r\n00:19:34.006 --\u003e 00:19:35.549\r\nOh, you're a clever one.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.633 --\u003e 00:19:39.679\r\nBut I will not be denied.\r\nAs the great Lewis Carroll said,\r\n\r\n00:19:39.970 --\u003e 00:19:42.390\r\n\"One, two, one, two,\"\r\n\r\n00:19:42.473 --\u003e 00:19:45.976\r\n\"and through and through,\r\nthe vorpal blade went snicker-snack.\"\r\n\r\n00:19:46.060 --\u003e 00:19:49.522\r\n\"He left it dead, and with its\r\nhead, he went galumphing back.\"\r\n\r\n00:19:49.605 --\u003e 00:19:51.107\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:55.486 --\u003e 00:19:57.029\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:19:57.905 --\u003e 00:19:59.740\r\nStop! I command you.\r\n\r\n00:20:00.157 --\u003e 00:20:02.576\r\nSo, we're gutter trash, are we?\r\n\r\n00:20:05.204 --\u003e 00:20:07.123\r\nWho's calling the shots now?\r\n\r\n00:20:08.040 --\u003e 00:20:10.918\r\n- Stop!\r\n- JAGUAR SHAMAN: Yes. Stop.\r\n\r\n00:20:15.715 --\u003e 00:20:17.258\r\nLeave him to the police.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.842 --\u003e 00:20:23.681\r\nThank you. Thank you, you\r\ngenerous, forgiving, noble fool.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:25.391\r\nStand back, all of you.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.474 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nI'm getting out. But not before\r\nI sew up one last loose end.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.896 --\u003e 00:20:31.939\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:20:55.921 --\u003e 00:20:56.922\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.105 --\u003e 00:21:15.399\r\nBRUCE: Tomorrow this all\r\ngoes back to the company.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.566 --\u003e 00:21:19.069\r\nMinus the cost of a plane ticket\r\nhome for our kidnapped doll maker.\r\n\r\n00:21:19.153 --\u003e 00:21:21.947\r\nI must say,\r\nafter all the Hatter put him through,\r\n\r\n00:21:22.031 --\u003e 00:21:24.450\r\nthat fellow showed\r\nremarkable restraint.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.533 --\u003e 00:21:25.910\r\nWhen everything\r\nwas said and done,\r\n\r\n00:21:25.993 --\u003e 00:21:28.204\r\nall the shaman really\r\nwanted was to go home.\r\n\r\n00:21:28.662 --\u003e 00:21:32.041\r\nIn fact, Ihear he even sent\r\nthe Hatter a farewell \u003ci\u003egift.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:32.666 --\u003e 00:21:33.709\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:21:34.210 --\u003e 00:21:36.253\r\n\u003ci\u003eBRUCE: Something to\r\nensure that Jervis Tetch\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:36.337 --\u003e 00:21:39.590\r\n\u003ci\u003eonly dreams of a good,\r\nhonest life from now on.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:49.225 --\u003e 00:21:51.227\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:16.001 --\u003e 00:22:17.002\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E05 - Paging The Crime Doctor (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.632 --\u003e 00:00:08.717\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.720 --\u003e 00:01:36.763\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:01:41.518 --\u003e 00:01:43.770\r\nEmergency vehicle.\r\nPull over and let him by.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.417 --\u003e 00:02:07.085\r\n(BOTH SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:15.177 --\u003e 00:02:16.762\r\n\u003ci\u003e(BOTH consume)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:20.140 --\u003e 00:02:22.559\r\nWhat's going on?\r\n\r\n00:02:22.684 --\u003e 00:02:23.685\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.240 --\u003e 00:02:38.492\r\nGet the box.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.579 --\u003e 00:02:43.789\r\nMAN: That's it.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.383 --\u003e 00:02:55.634\r\nWe're out of here.\r\n\r\n00:03:04.976 --\u003e 00:03:07.187\r\nHey, man, did I call it or what?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.771 --\u003e 00:03:10.273\r\nOnly two guards.\r\nNo cops for miles.\r\n\r\n00:03:11.650 --\u003e 00:03:13.318\r\nIt was, like, no sweat, right?\r\n\r\n00:03:13.735 --\u003e 00:03:15.195\r\n- (ALL LAUGHING)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:03:15.404 --\u003e 00:03:16.530\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:03:21.868 --\u003e 00:03:22.953\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:03:23.453 --\u003e 00:03:24.746\r\nThe Batman!\r\n\r\n00:03:32.003 --\u003e 00:03:33.213\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:53.316 --\u003e 00:03:54.651\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:04:03.785 --\u003e 00:04:04.786\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:04:04.870 --\u003e 00:04:06.913\r\nHe!!! Hey, \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e Can't see!\r\n\r\n00:04:14.546 --\u003e 00:04:16.381\r\nChubb, you okay?\r\n\r\n00:04:16.506 --\u003e 00:04:17.507\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:21.344\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:25.682 --\u003e 00:04:26.683\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:04:27.726 --\u003e 00:04:29.603\r\nNo, please! Let me go!\r\n\r\n00:04:29.686 --\u003e 00:04:30.687\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:04:33.982 --\u003e 00:04:35.233\r\n(CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:41.782 --\u003e 00:04:43.533\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:53.585 --\u003e 00:04:54.961\r\nHe's history. Gotta be.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.170 --\u003e 00:04:57.172\r\nNobody could take\r\nthat fall and live.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.972 --\u003e 00:05:09.309\r\nNo more fingerprints, Doc, ever?\r\nWow!\r\n\r\n00:05:10.101 --\u003e 00:05:12.604\r\nYou think you iced the Batman?\r\n\r\n00:05:12.687 --\u003e 00:05:15.106\r\n(LAUGHS) Not on your best\r\nday, Jake.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.440 --\u003e 00:05:17.651\r\nI'd cover my back if I were you.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.818 --\u003e 00:05:21.446\r\nYou mean there's actually somebody\r\nyou don't think you can push around?\r\n\r\n00:05:23.907 --\u003e 00:05:24.908\r\n(SNAPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:28.537 --\u003e 00:05:31.665\r\nTo what do I owe this\r\nunexpected pleasure, Rupert?\r\n\r\n00:05:32.165 --\u003e 00:05:35.961\r\nI brought you some more equipment,\r\nthe latest in medical technology.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.294 --\u003e 00:05:40.215\r\nAfter all, nothing's too good\r\nfor my brother, the crime doctor.\r\n\r\n00:05:40.590 --\u003e 00:05:44.511\r\nOh, great. A laser,\r\nfor all that critical brain surgery\r\n\r\n00:05:44.594 --\u003e 00:05:46.972\r\nI'll be doing on my\r\ndistinguished patients.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.764 --\u003e 00:05:52.727\r\nStill, after all these\r\nyears, still such contempt.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.311 --\u003e 00:05:57.315\r\nNow why would I have contempt for\r\nthe man who made me what I am today?\r\n\r\n00:05:57.732 --\u003e 00:05:58.942\r\nHow would I know?\r\n\r\n00:05:59.109 --\u003e 00:06:01.278\r\nI'm the fool who keeps giving\r\nyou everything you want,\r\n\r\n00:06:01.653 --\u003e 00:06:04.030\r\neven though you act\r\nlike an ungrateful punk!\r\n\r\n00:06:04.614 --\u003e 00:06:08.869\r\nWhat I want is to be a real doctor,\r\nRupert, with a respectable practice!\r\n\r\n00:06:09.119 --\u003e 00:06:11.288\r\nIs it my fault you\r\nlost your license?\r\n\r\n00:06:11.580 --\u003e 00:06:13.665\r\nI would've reported that\r\nbullet to the police,\r\n\r\n00:06:13.748 --\u003e 00:06:16.501\r\nas I was supposed to.\r\nBut, no, you insisted.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.002 --\u003e 00:06:20.213\r\nYou knew what I'd turned into before\r\nyou took that slug out of me, Matthew.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.714 --\u003e 00:06:23.758\r\nSo for that, I get to spend\r\nthe rest of my life like this?\r\n\r\n00:06:24.843 --\u003e 00:06:28.179\r\nI had much bigger plans,\r\nand you know it, you vulgar... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:28.263 --\u003e 00:06:30.348\r\nDon't you ever talk\r\nto me like that!\r\n\r\n00:06:30.807 --\u003e 00:06:33.268\r\nMe, who gave up everything\r\nso you could... (CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.685 --\u003e 00:06:36.980\r\nSo you could... (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:37.355 --\u003e 00:06:39.441\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:42.027 --\u003e 00:06:43.653\r\nOn the table with him. Stat!\r\n\r\n00:06:54.748 --\u003e 00:06:56.374\r\nIt's just the flu, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:06:56.541 --\u003e 00:06:59.336\r\nKeep him in bed a few\r\ndays, and he'll be fine.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.753 --\u003e 00:07:02.380\r\n(SPEAKING SPANISH)\r\n\r\n00:07:03.006 --\u003e 00:07:05.508\r\nExcuse me.\r\nI have another patient waiting.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.926 --\u003e 00:07:07.928\r\n(SPEAKING SPANISH)\r\n\r\n00:07:11.264 --\u003e 00:07:13.266\r\nWell, Bruce,\r\nwhat is it this time?\r\n\r\n00:07:13.350 --\u003e 00:07:14.351\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:07:16.269 --\u003e 00:07:17.270\r\nBruce!\r\n\r\n00:07:20.899 --\u003e 00:07:22.609\r\nJust a minor concussion.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.817 --\u003e 00:07:24.152\r\nProbably from the fall.\r\n\r\n00:07:25.612 --\u003e 00:07:28.365\r\nHere. Take one of\r\nthese every four hours.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.615 --\u003e 00:07:30.659\r\nThough why I ever\r\nbother is beyond me.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.909 --\u003e 00:07:32.744\r\nYou never follow\r\nmy instructions.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.827 --\u003e 00:07:35.080\r\nYour father, God rest him,\r\n\r\n00:07:35.455 --\u003e 00:07:38.249\r\nhe called you stubborn\r\nfrom the day you were born.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.545 --\u003e 00:07:44.923\r\nAlways used to say you\r\nhad a very hard head.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.215 --\u003e 00:07:46.925\r\nHe didn't know the half of it.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.300 --\u003e 00:07:49.761\r\nCome back tomorrow night.\r\nI'll take another look.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.011 --\u003e 00:07:52.305\r\nAnd stay in bed the whole day.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.555 --\u003e 00:07:54.516\r\n- Understand?\r\n- Right.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.892 --\u003e 00:07:57.769\r\nThe tumor's pressing\r\nagainst the aorta,\r\n\r\n00:07:57.852 --\u003e 00:07:59.652\r\nrestricting the flow of\r\nblood into your heart.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.813 --\u003e 00:08:02.107\r\nNormally, these things are\r\nbenign and easily removed.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.732 --\u003e 00:08:03.900\r\nBut we can't do it here.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.109 --\u003e 00:08:05.610\r\nI said, no hospital!\r\n\r\n00:08:06.486 --\u003e 00:08:09.114\r\nI got enemies who'd pay a fortune\r\nto make sure I don't come out.\r\n\r\n00:08:09.280 --\u003e 00:08:11.366\r\nWithout the operation,\r\nyou're a goner anyway.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.533 --\u003e 00:08:15.286\r\nI told you, if you don't do it\r\nhere, it won't get done!\r\n\r\n00:08:15.787 --\u003e 00:08:18.289\r\nForget it, Rupert.\r\nI'm in over my head.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.540 --\u003e 00:08:20.460\r\nThere must be somebody\r\nyou could get to help you.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.834 --\u003e 00:08:24.421\r\n(SIGHS) No. No, they'd never work with\r\nme, not voluntarily.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.588 --\u003e 00:08:26.798\r\nWho is he, Matthew?\r\n\r\n00:08:27.257 --\u003e 00:08:29.676\r\nI'll get him for you.\r\nI'll send the boys.\r\n\r\n00:08:30.010 --\u003e 00:08:31.553\r\nMatt, please!\r\n\r\n00:08:32.345 --\u003e 00:08:33.888\r\nRemember what I promised you.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.305 --\u003e 00:08:35.640\r\nAbout your license.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:37.017\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:08:37.767 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.060 --\u003e 00:08:41.438\r\nBut I'll go, too.\r\nI have to face her myself.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.105 --\u003e 00:08:45.692\r\n\u003ci\u003eHer name is Thompkins.\r\nLeslie Thompkins.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:03.835 --\u003e 00:09:05.879\r\nI'm sorry, the clinic is closed.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.212 --\u003e 00:09:08.631\r\n- LesHe?\r\n- Unless this is an emergency?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.798 --\u003e 00:09:11.009\r\nOh, but it is.\r\nSomeone's in trouble.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.468 --\u003e 00:09:12.927\r\nAn old friend of yours.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.555 --\u003e 00:09:16.556\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:17.182 --\u003e 00:09:18.266\r\n(BANGING)\r\n\r\n00:09:18.475 --\u003e 00:09:19.726\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.231 --\u003e 00:09:26.691\r\nGet out, or so help me,\r\n\r\n00:09:26.775 --\u003e 00:09:29.069\r\nI'll knock your brains\r\nacross the street.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.652 --\u003e 00:09:31.029\r\nSure you will.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.410 --\u003e 00:09:38.953\r\nNow that takes me back.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.580 --\u003e 00:09:41.956\r\nRemember when I took this?\r\n\r\n00:09:42.874 --\u003e 00:09:46.294\r\nBig AMA mixer. Graduation\r\nweek at the Waldorf. Remember?\r\n\r\n00:09:46.795 --\u003e 00:09:48.296\r\nAnd they booked Benny Goodman.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.012 --\u003e 00:09:57.305\r\nMatt?\r\n\r\n00:09:57.597 --\u003e 00:09:59.349\r\nMatt Thorne?\r\n\r\n00:09:59.557 --\u003e 00:10:03.353\r\nI'd heard things about you, Matt.\r\nThe word was you were still practicing,\r\n\r\n00:10:04.229 --\u003e 00:10:07.482\r\nwithout a license.\r\nI heard other things, too.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.066 --\u003e 00:10:09.776\r\nLooks like most\r\nof them are true.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.070 --\u003e 00:10:14.739\r\nNow,\r\nabout this friend in trouble.\r\n\r\n00:10:15.323 --\u003e 00:10:16.324\r\nIt's me.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.991 --\u003e 00:10:19.369\r\nBecause of what a certain\r\npatient of mine will do to me\r\n\r\n00:10:19.577 --\u003e 00:10:20.954\r\nif I don't operate on him.\r\n\r\n00:10:21.371 --\u003e 00:10:24.707\r\nBut I can't do it alone,\r\nand he won't let me check him into County.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.125 --\u003e 00:10:27.085\r\nSo you want me to assist?\r\n\r\n00:10:27.377 --\u003e 00:10:28.378\r\nForget it.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.297 --\u003e 00:10:33.258\r\nLook, there will be a lot\r\nof money in it for you.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.424 --\u003e 00:10:36.302\r\nI know what kind of money that is.\r\nGet out!\r\n\r\n00:10:37.095 --\u003e 00:10:38.847\r\nI'm sorry you feel that way.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.141 --\u003e 00:10:42.142\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:10:43.059 --\u003e 00:10:44.185\r\nLeave me alone.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.062 --\u003e 00:10:47.063\r\n(GLASS BREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:47.730 --\u003e 00:10:48.982\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:51.359 --\u003e 00:10:53.236\r\nLESLIE: You can't do this.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.736 --\u003e 00:10:54.737\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:10:54.821 --\u003e 00:10:55.947\r\n(SHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:10:56.030 --\u003e 00:10:57.323\r\n(LESLIE WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:11:01.161 --\u003e 00:11:03.454\r\n- BRUCE: I thought he looked familiar.\r\n- Who, sir?\r\n\r\n00:11:03.746 --\u003e 00:11:07.542\r\nThe guy who pushed me off the bridge.\r\nHe's one of Rupert Thorne's men.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.792 --\u003e 00:11:11.546\r\nTake a look. It's from the\r\nsurgical mask he was wearing.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.671 --\u003e 00:11:13.923\r\n\"Rose Commercial Laundry.\"\r\n\r\n00:11:14.215 --\u003e 00:11:16.342\r\nOne of Thorne's\r\nlegitimate businesses.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.843 --\u003e 00:11:19.470\r\nRose, Thorne. Of course.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.679 --\u003e 00:11:22.765\r\nHow clever,\r\nin a prosaic sort of way.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.894 --\u003e 00:11:29.480\r\nBut what would Thorne want\r\nwith a surgical laser?\r\n\r\n00:11:33.818 --\u003e 00:11:37.488\r\nIt's a chance at a decent life\r\nagain, Leslie. That's why.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.739 --\u003e 00:11:39.073\r\nAnd you believe him?\r\n\r\n00:11:39.324 --\u003e 00:11:41.993\r\nOf course.\r\nHe's got a lot of important friends.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.452 --\u003e 00:11:44.704\r\nJudges, politicians,\r\nthe medical society.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.288 --\u003e 00:11:47.707\r\nIf Rupert says he can\r\nget me my license back...\r\n\r\n00:11:47.874 --\u003e 00:11:50.293\r\nLESLIE: I meant,\r\ndo you believe he will?\r\n\r\n00:11:50.835 --\u003e 00:11:53.004\r\nOf course. He's my brother.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.636 --\u003e 00:12:01.346\r\nShall we call the police, sir?\r\n\r\n00:12:03.306 --\u003e 00:12:04.474\r\nNot just yet.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.572 --\u003e 00:12:23.409\r\n\"My two best friends.\r\nLove, Matt.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:23.660 --\u003e 00:12:26.788\r\nMy word, sir.\r\nThat's your father and Dr. Thompkins.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.205 --\u003e 00:12:28.206\r\nMmm-hmm.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.539 --\u003e 00:12:31.167\r\nForty years ago.\r\nBut I never saw this before.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.087 --\u003e 00:12:35.588\r\nAny idea who Matt is?\r\n\r\n00:12:36.214 --\u003e 00:12:38.383\r\nALFRED: Yes,\r\nI believe your father mentioned him.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.052 --\u003e 00:12:43.596\r\nOne of their colleagues\r\nin medical school.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.650 --\u003e 00:12:58.069\r\nALFRED: Very close\r\nfriends they all were.\r\n\r\n00:12:58.152 --\u003e 00:13:00.112\r\nCalled themselves \"The\r\nThree Musketeers,\" in fact.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.405 --\u003e 00:13:03.616\r\n\"Matthew Thorne?\"\r\nAs in Rupert Thorne?\r\n\r\n00:13:03.908 --\u003e 00:13:06.703\r\nTwo medical connections\r\nto a Thorne in 24 hours.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.828 --\u003e 00:13:08.413\r\nI doubt that's a coincidence.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.379 --\u003e 00:13:20.591\r\nIt went better than I could've hoped.\r\nI owe everything to you, Leslie.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.675 --\u003e 00:13:22.552\r\nI don't know how\r\nI can repay you.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.347 --\u003e 00:13:27.557\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:13:33.396 --\u003e 00:13:34.564\r\nLeslie?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.273 --\u003e 00:13:36.357\r\nLeslie!\r\n\r\n00:13:43.948 --\u003e 00:13:46.117\r\nGood work, Doc.\r\nMe and the boys will take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.576 --\u003e 00:13:47.910\r\nWith the old lady, I mean.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.994 --\u003e 00:13:50.955\r\nThank you, Tony, but I'd rather\r\nsee Dr. Thompkins home myself.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.372 --\u003e 00:13:53.207\r\nSorry, Doc.\r\nYou don't understand.\r\n\r\n00:13:53.541 --\u003e 00:13:56.002\r\nWe can't let her talk\r\nabout this place, see?\r\n\r\n00:13:56.252 --\u003e 00:13:58.671\r\nBefore he went under,\r\nMr. Thorne said to us,\r\n\r\n00:13:58.838 --\u003e 00:14:02.300\r\n\"When it's over,\r\nmake sure you shut her up.\"\r\n\r\n00:14:21.486 --\u003e 00:14:22.487\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:25.948 --\u003e 00:14:29.035\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.021 --\u003e 00:14:58.022\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:15.373 --\u003e 00:15:16.499\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:25.049 --\u003e 00:15:26.426\r\nTONY: She's gotta go, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.509 --\u003e 00:15:28.845\r\nAnd Mr. Thorne said not\r\nto let you interfere.\r\n\r\n00:15:29.137 --\u003e 00:15:31.597\r\nIf you do, the deal's off.\r\n\r\n00:15:31.806 --\u003e 00:15:36.769\r\nOkay, okay. But we'll do it my way.\r\nQuickly and without pain.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.865 --\u003e 00:15:50.158\r\nI'll give her an injection.\r\n\r\n00:15:50.867 --\u003e 00:15:52.743\r\nThat's not what\r\nthe boss ordered.\r\n\r\n00:15:52.994 --\u003e 00:15:55.872\r\nIt'll be cleaner this way.\r\nIt'll look like she had a heart attack.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.874 --\u003e 00:16:41.083\r\n(YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:41.167 --\u003e 00:16:42.168\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:52.428 --\u003e 00:16:54.639\r\nOf course.\r\nThat's for me, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:16:54.722 --\u003e 00:16:57.099\r\nMy payment for\r\nservices rendered?\r\n\r\n00:16:57.808 --\u003e 00:16:59.810\r\nYou're no better\r\nthan your brother.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.019 --\u003e 00:17:01.187\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.771 --\u003e 00:17:04.565\r\nI'm sorry, Leslie.\r\nI don't have any choice.\r\n\r\n00:17:13.824 --\u003e 00:17:15.159\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:17:15.576 --\u003e 00:17:16.577\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.204 --\u003e 00:17:19.413\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:20.373 --\u003e 00:17:21.707\r\nOh, no!\r\n\r\n00:17:26.337 --\u003e 00:17:28.339\r\nDon't worry.\r\nIt's just a sedative.\r\n\r\n00:17:30.007 --\u003e 00:17:31.342\r\nWe've got to get\r\nyou out of here.\r\n\r\n00:17:33.511 --\u003e 00:17:34.512\r\nCome on. This way.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.720 --\u003e 00:17:36.681\r\nWhat about your brother?\r\nYour license?\r\n\r\n00:17:36.764 --\u003e 00:17:39.183\r\nForget it.\r\nIt's not worth someone's life.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.436 --\u003e 00:17:44.355\r\nNow you're talking\r\nlike a doctor.\r\n\r\n00:18:01.831 --\u003e 00:18:02.832\r\nChubb!\r\n\r\n00:18:07.128 --\u003e 00:18:08.170\r\nJake!\r\n\r\n00:18:21.684 --\u003e 00:18:22.893\r\nMATT: This way.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.363 --\u003e 00:18:36.324\r\nJAKE: You're not going anywhere!\r\n\r\n00:18:42.997 --\u003e 00:18:45.124\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:18:53.633 --\u003e 00:18:54.800\r\nThey're headed for the roof!\r\n\r\n00:18:55.843 --\u003e 00:18:57.678\r\n(ELEVATOR WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:19:00.931 --\u003e 00:19:01.932\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.179 --\u003e 00:19:41.180\r\nMatt!\r\n\r\n00:19:41.972 --\u003e 00:19:43.099\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.435 --\u003e 00:19:47.728\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.895 --\u003e 00:19:49.230\r\nI can't make it.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:50.981\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:52.400 --\u003e 00:19:53.651\r\nHurry!\r\n\r\n00:19:56.946 --\u003e 00:19:57.947\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.825 --\u003e 00:20:02.451\r\nMATT: Don't! Please!\r\n\r\n00:20:03.285 --\u003e 00:20:04.286\r\n(CRIES OUT)\r\n\r\n00:20:07.623 --\u003e 00:20:08.624\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.339 --\u003e 00:20:17.299\r\nMATT: I can't hold on!\r\n\r\n00:20:18.259 --\u003e 00:20:20.177\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:20:21.721 --\u003e 00:20:24.223\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:34.650 --\u003e 00:20:37.528\r\nI thought I told you\r\nto take the day off.\r\n\r\n00:20:46.829 --\u003e 00:20:48.372\r\nGUARD: Visitor, Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:20:54.962 --\u003e 00:20:57.965\r\nBruce Wayne, Dr. Thorne.\r\nThomas Wayne's son.\r\n\r\n00:20:58.632 --\u003e 00:21:00.509\r\n- Did you get my letter?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:21:01.469 --\u003e 00:21:03.053\r\nThomas Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.512 --\u003e 00:21:06.015\r\nI told you I can help you\r\nwith your legal costs,\r\n\r\n00:21:06.098 --\u003e 00:21:07.858\r\nmaybe even put in a good\r\nword with the judge.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.892 --\u003e 00:21:09.977\r\nYes,\r\nbut what do you get out of it?\r\n\r\n00:21:10.478 --\u003e 00:21:13.606\r\nWell, there is something\r\nyou can do for me.\r\n\r\n00:21:13.731 --\u003e 00:21:15.900\r\nI knew it.\r\nI knew there'd be a catch.\r\n\r\n00:21:16.066 --\u003e 00:21:19.028\r\nSorry, Mr. Wayne.\r\nMatthew Thorne is no longer for sale.\r\n\r\n00:21:21.155 --\u003e 00:21:24.283\r\n- I'm not looking for any illegal favors.\r\n- What, then?\r\n\r\n00:21:25.034 --\u003e 00:21:28.078\r\nSomething you know.\r\nSomething only you can give me.\r\n\r\n00:21:31.081 --\u003e 00:21:32.666\r\nTell me about my father.\r\n\r\n00:21:36.253 --\u003e 00:21:37.254\r\n(INAUDIBLE)\r\n\r\n00:22:16.168 --\u003e 00:22:17.169\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E06 - House and Garden (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.189 --\u003e 00:00:24.191\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.797 --\u003e 00:01:30.299\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:39.391\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:01.413 --\u003e 00:02:02.539\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:02:03.206 --\u003e 00:02:04.750\r\n- (SHATTERS)\r\n- Who's in here?\r\n\r\n00:02:08.295 --\u003e 00:02:09.338\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:09.588 --\u003e 00:02:10.631\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:11.465 --\u003e 00:02:12.591\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:22.517 --\u003e 00:02:24.798\r\nDOCTOR: This is the fourth\r\nidentical poisoning this month.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.062 --\u003e 00:02:26.521\r\nWe've kept the\r\nvictims alive so far,\r\n\r\n00:02:26.605 --\u003e 00:02:28.690\r\nbut we're not even sure\r\nwhat kind of poison it is.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.107 --\u003e 00:02:31.193\r\nWhy don't you ask the\r\nwoman who made it?\r\n\r\n00:02:32.194 --\u003e 00:02:33.320\r\nPoison Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.570 --\u003e 00:02:35.739\r\nGORDON: She was our first\r\nguess, but we ruled her out.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.114 --\u003e 00:02:38.241\r\n- You mean she's still in Arkham?\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:02:38.325 --\u003e 00:02:40.577\r\nShe completed her\r\nrehabilitation six months ago.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.661 --\u003e 00:02:41.995\r\nThe board gave her a clean bill.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.329 --\u003e 00:02:46.166\r\nAnd now, wealthy bachelors are being\r\nstruck down by an unknown toxin.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.583 --\u003e 00:02:48.335\r\nSounds like lvy's MO to me.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.418 --\u003e 00:02:50.879\r\nI don't think she's interested\r\nin single men anymore.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.254 --\u003e 00:02:52.255\r\nHmm?\r\n\r\n00:02:52.381 --\u003e 00:02:53.507\r\nGORDON: You haven't heard?\r\n\r\n00:02:53.590 --\u003e 00:02:55.884\r\nNot only did Pamela\r\nlsley clean herself up,\r\n\r\n00:02:56.093 --\u003e 00:02:57.594\r\nshe also got married.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.682 --\u003e 00:03:03.183\r\n(BIRDS CHIRPING)\r\n\r\n00:03:08.146 --\u003e 00:03:09.481\r\n(DOORBELL RINGS)\r\n\r\n00:03:10.732 --\u003e 00:03:12.359\r\nHi. Come on in.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.277 --\u003e 00:03:15.570\r\nThank you, Ms. lsley.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.862 --\u003e 00:03:19.282\r\nMy pleasure, Commissioner,\r\nthough it's Carlyle now.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.574 --\u003e 00:03:21.576\r\nMrs. Pamela Lillian Carlyle.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.829 --\u003e 00:03:25.622\r\nThis is my husband, Steven.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.498 --\u003e 00:03:28.792\r\nHello, Commissioner.\r\nNice to see you again.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.126 --\u003e 00:03:30.794\r\nDr. Carlyle is our liaison\r\n\r\n00:03:30.877 --\u003e 00:03:32.997\r\nbetween the board at Arkham\r\nand the police department.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.296 --\u003e 00:03:36.550\r\nYou also teach classes on criminal\r\npsychology at Gotham State.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.800 --\u003e 00:03:38.218\r\nI've read some of your works.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.301 --\u003e 00:03:39.761\r\nThey were very impressive.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.137 --\u003e 00:03:41.263\r\nThank you.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.596 --\u003e 00:03:44.725\r\nBut I get the feeling\r\nthis isn't a social call.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.891 --\u003e 00:03:48.061\r\nBATMAN: Someone is poisoning\r\nand robbing wealthy young men.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.603 --\u003e 00:03:52.649\r\nAs painful as it sounds,\r\nall clues point to your wife.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.858 --\u003e 00:03:56.111\r\n- That's outrageous! Pamela hasn't-\r\n- Darling, please.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.320 --\u003e 00:03:59.781\r\nBatman, I don't doubt\r\nthat I was your first,\r\n\r\n00:03:59.865 --\u003e 00:04:01.533\r\nand probably only suspect.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.075 --\u003e 00:04:05.495\r\nOver the years, you and I have\r\nhad a rather intense relationship.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.413 --\u003e 00:04:08.832\r\nBut that's all in the\r\npast, believe me.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.124 --\u003e 00:04:11.835\r\nI look back on what I\r\nwas, and I shudder.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.377 --\u003e 00:04:15.380\r\nLocked away in Arkham with\r\nthe obsessed and the insane\r\n\r\n00:04:15.464 --\u003e 00:04:18.091\r\nand me just as lost\r\nas any of them.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.925 --\u003e 00:04:20.802\r\nAnd then I met Steven.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.094 --\u003e 00:04:24.431\r\nHis love and guidance brought\r\nme into the light again.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.723 --\u003e 00:04:27.392\r\nKID 1: Mom, Dad,\r\nthe Batmobile's outside!\r\n\r\n00:04:27.476 --\u003e 00:04:29.311\r\nKID 2: It is, it is! We saw it!\r\n\r\n00:04:29.394 --\u003e 00:04:30.437\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:04:30.771 --\u003e 00:04:31.813\r\nBOTH: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:04:32.689 --\u003e 00:04:35.525\r\nKID 1: Cool.\r\nBatman's really here!\r\n\r\n00:04:37.944 --\u003e 00:04:40.614\r\nMommy, you didn't tell\r\nus you know Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.822 --\u003e 00:04:41.907\r\n(KISSES)\r\n\r\n00:04:42.240 --\u003e 00:04:43.992\r\nThat was a long time\r\nago, sweetie.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.576 --\u003e 00:04:46.870\r\nThese are my boys,\r\nChris and Kelly.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.162 --\u003e 00:04:49.915\r\nCHRIS: Hi.\r\nKELLY: Can we ride in your car?\r\n\r\n00:04:50.165 --\u003e 00:04:52.876\r\nCome on, guys.\r\nLet's leave Mom alone for a minute.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.670 --\u003e 00:04:57.047\r\nBye, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.756 --\u003e 00:04:59.800\r\nI never thought about\r\nhaving kids before.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:01.843\r\nI can't.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.010 --\u003e 00:05:05.055\r\nNature's little tradeoff\r\nfor my hyper immune system.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.556 --\u003e 00:05:10.560\r\nAnd yet, when I met Steven's boys,\r\nsomething inside me just melted.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.144 --\u003e 00:05:12.813\r\nI guess there really\r\ndoes come a time\r\n\r\n00:05:12.896 --\u003e 00:05:15.190\r\nwhen a woman wants\r\nsomething more in her life.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.440 --\u003e 00:05:17.192\r\nAt least this woman does.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.818 --\u003e 00:05:19.653\r\nSteven doesn't\r\ncare about my past.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.986 --\u003e 00:05:22.572\r\nHe and the boys accept\r\nme for who I am now.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.906 --\u003e 00:05:25.867\r\nI don't know who has been\r\nduplicating my old crimes,\r\n\r\n00:05:25.992 --\u003e 00:05:29.871\r\nbut I can assure you,\r\ngentlemen, Poison Ivy is dead.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.837 --\u003e 00:05:41.675\r\nDon't tell me the great Dick Grayson\r\nis spending the night in for a change?\r\n\r\n00:05:42.050 --\u003e 00:05:43.927\r\n(CHUCKLES) Hey,\r\nwe got finals coming up.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.261 --\u003e 00:05:47.597\r\nBut what about those cheerleaders\r\nI always see chasing you around?\r\n\r\n00:05:47.889 --\u003e 00:05:50.183\r\nCan't they help\r\nyou pass calculus?\r\n\r\n00:05:50.267 --\u003e 00:05:53.270\r\n- That's not the reason I asked you over.\r\n- Oh, no?\r\n\r\n00:05:53.562 --\u003e 00:05:56.731\r\nNo. I just thought it would\r\nbe fun to get together\r\n\r\n00:05:56.815 --\u003e 00:06:00.318\r\nand study and talk and, um...\r\n\r\n00:06:00.652 --\u003e 00:06:01.736\r\nAnd?\r\n\r\n00:06:08.034 --\u003e 00:06:09.244\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:06:15.250 --\u003e 00:06:16.334\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:06:16.626 --\u003e 00:06:17.961\r\nBATMAN: It's me.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.336 --\u003e 00:06:19.754\r\nOh, hi.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.755 --\u003e 00:06:22.716\r\nI wasn't expecting to\r\nhear from you tonight.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.966 --\u003e 00:06:24.759\r\n(SCOFFS) I'd better go.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.135 --\u003e 00:06:26.136\r\nUh...\r\n\r\n00:06:26.386 --\u003e 00:06:27.554\r\nDo you have company?\r\n\r\n00:06:29.097 --\u003e 00:06:30.765\r\n(SIGHS) Not anymore.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.433 --\u003e 00:06:32.517\r\nSorry.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.601 --\u003e 00:06:36.563\r\nI need you to check on a teacher\r\nthere at GSU. Steven Carlyle.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.855 --\u003e 00:06:39.232\r\nI was in his class last year.\r\nNice guy.\r\n\r\n00:06:40.108 --\u003e 00:06:42.360\r\n- He's not in trouble, is he?\r\n- Possibly.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.986 --\u003e 00:06:44.487\r\nSee what you can find on him.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.571 --\u003e 00:06:47.240\r\nFamily history,\r\nplaces he's worked, anything.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.490 --\u003e 00:06:49.659\r\nRight.\r\nI'll check back with you later.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.536 --\u003e 00:06:52.621\r\nCindy?\r\n\r\n00:06:53.747 --\u003e 00:06:54.831\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:58.418 --\u003e 00:06:59.586\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.720 --\u003e 00:07:10.722\r\n(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:07:21.775 --\u003e 00:07:23.318\r\n(CINDY WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:23.401 --\u003e 00:07:24.986\r\nCINDY: I'm so sorry.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.071 --\u003e 00:07:29.366\r\nIt's all my fault.\r\nIf only I hadn't left him.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.699 --\u003e 00:07:30.825\r\n- It's all right.\r\n- (SOBS)\r\n\r\n00:07:32.035 --\u003e 00:07:34.913\r\nI had just gone back to my\r\nroom when I heard a loud crash.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.996 --\u003e 00:07:38.041\r\nI ran down here,\r\nand Dick was gone.\r\n\r\n00:07:38.333 --\u003e 00:07:40.013\r\nBRUCE: And you saw no\r\none leaving the dorm?\r\n\r\n00:07:40.210 --\u003e 00:07:41.211\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.379 --\u003e 00:07:44.673\r\nI don't think Dick is the only\r\nvictim, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.756 --\u003e 00:07:47.008\r\nYou mean they kidnapped\r\nhim to get at me.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.467 --\u003e 00:07:50.804\r\nIt fits the pattern. Wealthy single\r\nmen, all targets of robberies.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.887 --\u003e 00:07:54.182\r\nOnly, in your case, you have something\r\nmore valuable to hold for ransom.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.351 --\u003e 00:07:57.560\r\nMy ward.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.833 --\u003e 00:08:21.001\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.209 --\u003e 00:08:22.585\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:24.170 --\u003e 00:08:28.133\r\nKeep driving,\r\nor your neck gets a new air hole.\r\n\r\n00:08:28.216 --\u003e 00:08:30.176\r\n(GRUNTING) What do you want?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.594 --\u003e 00:08:32.846\r\n\u003ci\u003e(“RES SQUEAL)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:33.096 --\u003e 00:08:34.723\r\nI do the talking.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.806 --\u003e 00:08:38.435\r\nBring five million in cash to\r\nthe docks tomorrow midnight.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.727 --\u003e 00:08:41.312\r\nCome alone,\r\nor the kid is history.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.188 --\u003e 00:08:43.898\r\nNod if you understand.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.358 --\u003e 00:08:46.526\r\nSmart boy.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.193 --\u003e 00:08:48.528\r\n(HORN BLARES)\r\n\r\n00:09:00.874 --\u003e 00:09:02.292\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.089 --\u003e 00:09:10.550\r\nALFRED: I expect\r\nthere's no other option?\r\n\r\n00:09:10.759 --\u003e 00:09:14.304\r\nThe money's not important.\r\nGetting Dick back is.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.387 --\u003e 00:09:15.722\r\nAgreed, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.889 --\u003e 00:09:19.934\r\nBut even so, didn't the kidnapper\r\nleave some clue for Batman to follow?\r\n\r\n00:09:20.268 --\u003e 00:09:23.354\r\nJust my torn shirt.\r\nI'll have to fall back on my instincts.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.688 --\u003e 00:09:27.192\r\nAnd right now, they're saying\r\nlvy's fairy tale lifestyle\r\n\r\n00:09:27.275 --\u003e 00:09:28.860\r\nisn't everything it seems.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.290 --\u003e 00:09:43.792\r\nWait for me, guys.\r\n\r\n00:09:45.168 --\u003e 00:09:47.170\r\nBye, honey. Love you.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.106 --\u003e 00:10:08.274\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: (OVER RADIO)\r\nWhat's she doing now, sir?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:08.942 --\u003e 00:10:10.652\r\nBATMAN: Buying squash.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.277 --\u003e 00:10:13.279\r\nI've been keeping tabs\r\non her all morning.\r\n\r\n00:10:15.073 --\u003e 00:10:16.967\r\nAnd so far,\r\nshe's done nothing more incriminating\r\n\r\n00:10:16.991 --\u003e 00:10:18.785\r\nthan return an overdue video.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.119 --\u003e 00:10:20.161\r\nEven paid the late fee.\r\n\r\n00:10:20.495 --\u003e 00:10:23.581\r\n\u003ci\u003eALFRED: Could it be Poison\r\nIvy truly has reformed?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:23.790 --\u003e 00:10:26.668\r\nI want to believe it.\r\nWhy can't I?\r\n\r\n00:10:29.587 --\u003e 00:10:33.341\r\nThe greenhouse checks out too.\r\nNothing but plants and flowers.\r\n\r\n00:10:33.424 --\u003e 00:10:34.467\r\nALFRED: Sir?\r\n\r\n00:10:34.551 --\u003e 00:10:35.593\r\n(CAR APPROACHES)\r\n\r\n00:10:35.677 --\u003e 00:10:36.678\r\nLater.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.020 --\u003e 00:10:48.648\r\nKID: Can we watch cartoons?\r\nPAMELA: After your homework.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.857 --\u003e 00:10:51.234\r\n(DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:10:51.734 --\u003e 00:10:54.279\r\nBATMAN: This is a dead end.\r\nI haven't found anything that-\r\n\r\n00:10:54.696 --\u003e 00:10:56.281\r\n(GASPS AND GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.034 --\u003e 00:11:02.287\r\nThere are laws against\r\nspying on people.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.122 --\u003e 00:11:06.833\r\nThere are laws against\r\npoisoning them too.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.586 --\u003e 00:11:11.129\r\nLook around, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.379 --\u003e 00:11:15.300\r\nI've got a nice house, a little\r\ngarden and a family that loves me.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.884 --\u003e 00:11:17.927\r\nWhy would I jeopardize that?\r\n\r\n00:11:18.219 --\u003e 00:11:21.514\r\nFor the first time in my\r\nlife, I'm happy.\r\n\r\n00:11:22.098 --\u003e 00:11:24.058\r\nI'm beginning to\r\nthink you're right.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.227 --\u003e 00:11:27.270\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:11:29.355 --\u003e 00:11:30.523\r\nGood luck.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.149 --\u003e 00:11:33.359\r\nYou too, Mrs. Carlyle.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.250 --\u003e 00:11:52.587\r\nPLANT-MAN: Wayne,\r\nkick the case over here.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.171 --\u003e 00:11:54.422\r\nLet me see the boy.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.798 --\u003e 00:11:57.217\r\n(MUFFLED GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:57.800 --\u003e 00:11:59.594\r\nThe money. Now!\r\n\r\n00:12:06.309 --\u003e 00:12:07.560\r\nSend out the boy.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.938 --\u003e 00:12:11.064\r\nYou hear me?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.481 --\u003e 00:12:12.732\r\nPLANT-MAN: I hear you.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.778 --\u003e 00:12:17.904\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:30.208 --\u003e 00:12:31.209\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:40.051 --\u003e 00:12:42.262\r\nGoodbye, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:12:44.097 --\u003e 00:12:45.598\r\n(PLANT-MAN CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.694 --\u003e 00:12:58.903\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:04.993 --\u003e 00:13:06.411\r\n(MUFFLED GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:08.871 --\u003e 00:13:10.915\r\nTime to hit the drink.\r\n\r\n00:13:12.500 --\u003e 00:13:14.043\r\n(PLANT-MAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:19.882 --\u003e 00:13:21.342\r\n(MUFFLED GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:13:23.386 --\u003e 00:13:24.595\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.388 --\u003e 00:13:26.389\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:40.111 --\u003e 00:13:41.237\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:45.158 --\u003e 00:13:46.159\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:54.667 --\u003e 00:13:58.254\r\nI guess I should be grateful that\r\nthing used a fist on me and not poison.\r\n\r\n00:13:58.463 --\u003e 00:14:01.924\r\nRight. But we're still in the\r\ndark as to who's behind this.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.342 --\u003e 00:14:03.885\r\nYou don't think\r\nit's the plant lady?\r\n\r\n00:14:03.968 --\u003e 00:14:07.096\r\nAll she wants is to be left\r\nalone with her husband and sons.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.680 --\u003e 00:14:11.017\r\n- Sons?\r\n- Carlyle's two boys, Chris and Kelly.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.100 --\u003e 00:14:12.393\r\nI know Chris and Kelly.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.019 --\u003e 00:14:16.481\r\nI was in Carlyle's class when his\r\nex brought them to visit last year.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.065 --\u003e 00:14:19.192\r\nI thought Carlyle had custody.\r\n\r\n00:14:19.359 --\u003e 00:14:21.778\r\nNo. And here's another\r\nshocker for you.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.445 --\u003e 00:14:24.947\r\nChris and Kelly are girls.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.698 --\u003e 00:14:28.034\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:14:52.183 --\u003e 00:14:53.184\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.192 --\u003e 00:15:02.276\r\n(SQUEAKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:03.820 --\u003e 00:15:05.196\r\n(WHISPERS) No sign of Ivy.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.738 --\u003e 00:15:06.823\r\nWhat's that?\r\n\r\n00:15:07.115 --\u003e 00:15:08.199\r\nInsurance.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.922 --\u003e 00:15:24.132\r\nPlastic?\r\n\r\n00:15:27.844 --\u003e 00:15:29.053\r\n(BOTH GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:15:38.312 --\u003e 00:15:40.064\r\n(WATER BUBBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:47.738 --\u003e 00:15:50.116\r\nJust a happy little\r\nhomemaker, huh?\r\n\r\n00:15:59.876 --\u003e 00:16:00.877\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:05.256 --\u003e 00:16:07.425\r\n(GASPS AND COUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:07.884 --\u003e 00:16:10.803\r\n- Dr. Carlyle?\r\n- Help me.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.473 --\u003e 00:16:16.142\r\nShe's insane. Has to be stopped.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.726 --\u003e 00:16:19.854\r\n- You don't know what she's done.\r\n- KID: Mommy.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.949 --\u003e 00:16:33.159\r\nMommy.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.534 --\u003e 00:16:34.577\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.122 --\u003e 00:16:41.125\r\nIt... It isn't possible.\r\n\r\n00:16:41.459 --\u003e 00:16:43.544\r\n- Mommy.\r\n- Mommy.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.545 --\u003e 00:16:46.380\r\nI was her doctor in Arkham.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.631 --\u003e 00:16:48.633\r\nShe said she wanted to reform.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.091 --\u003e 00:16:52.345\r\nI trusted her,\r\nlet her get too close.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.972 --\u003e 00:16:56.557\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.729 --\u003e 00:17:05.566\r\nOne little kiss,\r\nand dear Steven was my slave.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.942 --\u003e 00:17:08.486\r\nHe was useful in signing\r\nmy release papers,\r\n\r\n00:17:08.569 --\u003e 00:17:12.073\r\nand for supplying certain raw\r\nmaterials for my experiments\r\n\r\n00:17:12.615 --\u003e 00:17:15.701\r\nbut the marriage\r\nwas, well, a fake.\r\n\r\n00:17:17.328 --\u003e 00:17:19.038\r\nAnd these mutations?\r\n\r\n00:17:19.664 --\u003e 00:17:21.541\r\nOur children, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.333 --\u003e 00:17:25.545\r\nPlant-based life forms\r\nenhanced with Steven's DNA.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.254 --\u003e 00:17:28.005\r\nThey're not truly human.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.256 --\u003e 00:17:31.551\r\nIn fact, their life spans are\r\nsomewhat like certain rare flowers\r\n\r\n00:17:31.634 --\u003e 00:17:34.554\r\nthat blossom and\r\ndie in a few days.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.929 --\u003e 00:17:36.055\r\nI see.\r\n\r\n00:17:36.430 --\u003e 00:17:38.432\r\nAt first it looks like a child.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.808 --\u003e 00:17:40.810\r\nThen it resembles Dr. Carlyle.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.102 --\u003e 00:17:44.272\r\n- And in its final phase-\r\n- In its final phase,\r\n\r\n00:17:44.355 --\u003e 00:17:46.023\r\nbefore it burns itself out...\r\n\r\n00:17:46.190 --\u003e 00:17:51.028\r\nThe creature becomes my\r\nwilling enforcer and bodyguard.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.450 --\u003e 00:17:58.869\r\nBATMAN: Thief and\r\nkidnapper is more like it.\r\n\r\n00:17:59.495 --\u003e 00:18:00.913\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:01.497 --\u003e 00:18:03.666\r\nIt costs money to\r\nraise a family.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.083 --\u003e 00:18:07.211\r\n- You haven't changed a bit.\r\n- Yes, I have.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.753 --\u003e 00:18:10.798\r\nI meant it when I said I\r\nwanted a family that loves me.\r\n\r\n00:18:11.090 --\u003e 00:18:13.384\r\n\u003ci\u003eHusk wanted it on my terms.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:14.135 --\u003e 00:18:16.220\r\nLady, you're nuts.\r\n\r\n00:18:16.929 --\u003e 00:18:18.556\r\nWell, that's your opinion.\r\n\r\n00:18:18.806 --\u003e 00:18:21.475\r\nProbably the last one\r\nyou'll ever have, too.\r\n\r\n00:18:21.851 --\u003e 00:18:22.935\r\nKids?\r\n\r\n00:18:24.604 --\u003e 00:18:28.232\r\nThat water I fed them contained\r\na super active growth formula.\r\n\r\n00:18:28.441 --\u003e 00:18:31.777\r\nTrue, it cuts their life span\r\ndown to just a few minutes,\r\n\r\n00:18:31.861 --\u003e 00:18:33.529\r\nbut that's more time\r\nthan you've got.\r\n\r\n00:18:38.576 --\u003e 00:18:39.827\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:46.876 --\u003e 00:18:48.169\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.088 --\u003e 00:18:52.506\r\n(ELECTRICITY CRACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:55.801 --\u003e 00:18:57.011\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:19:00.139 --\u003e 00:19:01.349\r\nROBIN: This way, Doc.\r\n\r\n00:19:03.726 --\u003e 00:19:05.311\r\n(PLANT-MEN GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:16.530 --\u003e 00:19:19.367\r\nGreat. She gave her little\r\nfamily the formula too.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.037 --\u003e 00:19:24.330\r\nStay with Carlyle!\r\n\r\n00:19:35.341 --\u003e 00:19:36.384\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:36.842 --\u003e 00:19:38.928\r\nAnyone else want\r\ntheir weeds whacked?\r\n\r\n00:19:46.310 --\u003e 00:19:47.937\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:52.817 --\u003e 00:19:55.361\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:59.115 --\u003e 00:20:00.157\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:20:09.166 --\u003e 00:20:10.376\r\nMy darlings!\r\n\r\n00:20:14.338 --\u003e 00:20:15.589\r\nWeed killer.\r\n\r\n00:20:16.257 --\u003e 00:20:18.801\r\nI figured what you were\r\nup to involved plants\r\n\r\n00:20:19.009 --\u003e 00:20:21.137\r\nso I pumped your water\r\ntanks with herbicide.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.971 --\u003e 00:20:24.849\r\nWhat was the tip-off, Batman?\r\nSteven's kids?\r\n\r\n00:20:25.391 --\u003e 00:20:29.311\r\nYou couldn't replicate them as\r\ngirls, not with Carlyle's DNA.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.854 --\u003e 00:20:31.731\r\nSo, you took your\r\nchance with boys.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.231 --\u003e 00:20:34.775\r\nBut Ivy could replicate herself.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.276 --\u003e 00:20:36.360\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:37.194 --\u003e 00:20:38.237\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:38.404 --\u003e 00:20:39.530\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:20:40.114 --\u003e 00:20:41.282\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:45.411 --\u003e 00:20:50.166\r\nGuess you weren't the only one\r\nwith an escape plan, huh, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:21:08.434 --\u003e 00:21:10.352\r\nMost of the stolen property\r\nwas still in the lab\r\n\r\n00:21:10.436 --\u003e 00:21:12.396\r\nalong with lvy's toxin formulas.\r\n\r\n00:21:12.605 --\u003e 00:21:15.191\r\nWell, at least we have lvy's\r\ntoxins to form an antidote.\r\n\r\n00:21:15.816 --\u003e 00:21:17.818\r\nI'm just sorry she got away.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.943 --\u003e 00:21:21.906\r\nMe too, Robin. But I don't think\r\nwe'll see her again anytime soon.\r\n\r\n00:21:26.994 --\u003e 00:21:28.746\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: Ivy lost\r\neverything she had.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:29.497 --\u003e 00:21:31.916\r\n\u003ci\u003eEverything she said\r\nshe ever wanted.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:35.628 --\u003e 00:21:39.089\r\n\u003ci\u003eFor what it's worth,\r\nI believed her when she told me\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:39.173 --\u003e 00:21:42.343\r\n\u003ci\u003efor the first time in her\r\nlife, she was happy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:21:51.894 --\u003e 00:21:53.896\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.587 --\u003e 00:22:19.588\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E07 - Sideshow (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:23.315 --\u003e 00:00:25.317\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:21.123 --\u003e 00:01:22.374\r\n(TRAIN HORN BLOWS)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.380 --\u003e 00:01:29.881\r\n(KILLER CROC GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.215 --\u003e 00:01:32.092\r\nGUARD: Don't bother\r\ntrying, Croc.\r\n\r\n00:01:32.175 --\u003e 00:01:34.553\r\nThose cuffs are stacked\r\npolycarbon alloy.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.636 --\u003e 00:01:36.430\r\nNot even you can break them.\r\n\r\n00:01:36.722 --\u003e 00:01:37.723\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:01:37.806 --\u003e 00:01:41.476\r\nSo they finally declared old Croc\r\nsane and responsible for his crimes.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.060 --\u003e 00:01:43.604\r\nTook them long enough.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.687 --\u003e 00:01:45.981\r\nI hear they're giving him\r\nhis own cellblock upstate.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.440 --\u003e 00:01:47.983\r\nYour tax dollars at work.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.359 --\u003e 00:01:51.737\r\nWake me if he busts out.\r\nThat would be a story.\r\n\r\n00:01:56.825 --\u003e 00:02:00.829\r\nYou know, there's something the brains\r\nback at the joint didn't think about.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.163 --\u003e 00:02:02.456\r\nYeah, what's that?\r\n\r\n00:02:02.539 --\u003e 00:02:06.835\r\nCrocodiles got the strongest\r\njaws of any animal around.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.714 --\u003e 00:02:11.923\r\nGet back!\r\n\r\n00:02:13.425 --\u003e 00:02:14.426\r\n(GUARD SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.509 --\u003e 00:02:16.136\r\n- What was that?\r\n- Did you hear that?\r\n\r\n00:02:17.095 --\u003e 00:02:18.847\r\nOh, man. Did he get loose?\r\n\r\n00:02:19.473 --\u003e 00:02:21.224\r\nI'm not going near that thing.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.308 --\u003e 00:02:23.060\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.271 --\u003e 00:02:27.439\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:02:30.067 --\u003e 00:02:31.401\r\n(ALL GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:02:31.568 --\u003e 00:02:33.195\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:44.289 --\u003e 00:02:45.415\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:48.418 --\u003e 00:02:52.381\r\nBatman? Come on.\r\nCan't you do any better than that?\r\n\r\n00:02:53.882 --\u003e 00:02:58.345\r\nYou want a piece of me?\r\nThink you can take the champ?\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:03:02.015\r\nYou're pumped full of sedative, Croc.\r\nYou won't get far.\r\n\r\n00:03:03.225 --\u003e 00:03:04.810\r\nFarther than you.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.268 --\u003e 00:03:06.978\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.163 --\u003e 00:03:26.164\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:30.627 --\u003e 00:03:31.878\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:03:39.886 --\u003e 00:03:41.138\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:03:54.693 --\u003e 00:03:56.695\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:03:59.072 --\u003e 00:04:00.824\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:16.590 --\u003e 00:04:18.049\r\n- (BIRDS CHIRPING)\r\n- (GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:04:32.647 --\u003e 00:04:34.483\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:09.476 --\u003e 00:05:10.769\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:11.645 --\u003e 00:05:13.230\r\n(EAGLE SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:05:27.577 --\u003e 00:05:28.870\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:06:01.528 --\u003e 00:06:03.071\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.985 --\u003e 00:06:43.278\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:59.419 --\u003e 00:07:00.795\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:15.602 --\u003e 00:07:16.937\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:07:30.659 --\u003e 00:07:32.494\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.553 --\u003e 00:07:53.848\r\n- GOLIATH: Looks like he's been hurt.\r\n- See his chains?\r\n\r\n00:07:53.932 --\u003e 00:07:55.183\r\n(The poor 9U)!-\r\n\r\n00:07:55.266 --\u003e 00:07:57.185\r\nIt's okay.\r\nWe'll take care of you.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.310 --\u003e 00:08:01.481\r\nOh, judgment,\r\nthou art fled to brutish beasts.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.815 --\u003e 00:08:04.442\r\nAnd men have lost their reason.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.318 --\u003e 00:08:06.945\r\nBring him, good Goliath.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.336 --\u003e 00:08:24.337\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:08:34.431 --\u003e 00:08:36.850\r\nRise and shine.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.603 --\u003e 00:08:43.481\r\n- Please try and drink some.\r\n- Yes, it's good for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.484 --\u003e 00:08:51.990\r\nAh, now, that's better, isn't it?\r\nSorry, we haven't been introduced.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.282 --\u003e 00:08:54.159\r\nRichard. At your service.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.367 --\u003e 00:08:58.455\r\nLike Richard Ill,\r\nI too am rudely stamped.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.997 --\u003e 00:09:00.957\r\nYou have to forgive\r\nour dramatic friend.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.499 --\u003e 00:09:03.001\r\nHe's nuts about Shakespeare.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.626 --\u003e 00:09:06.671\r\nThese two sylvan nymphs\r\nare May and June.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.005 --\u003e 00:09:09.007\r\n- Pleased to meet you.\r\n- Ditto.\r\n\r\n00:09:09.549 --\u003e 00:09:11.342\r\nAnd you've met Billy.\r\n\r\n00:09:12.427 --\u003e 00:09:16.222\r\nYou're the one that pulled me out\r\nof the drink, ain't you? I owe you.\r\n\r\n00:09:16.473 --\u003e 00:09:19.100\r\nAnd I'm Goliath.\r\nI helped haul you in.\r\n\r\n00:09:21.644 --\u003e 00:09:23.438\r\nSo I'll buy you a medal.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.230 --\u003e 00:09:28.401\r\nNo need to be shy.\r\nWe're all family here.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.485 --\u003e 00:09:31.196\r\nIt must have been fate\r\nthat led you to us.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.279 --\u003e 00:09:35.241\r\nYeah. What's a freak show\r\ndoing in the middle of nowhere?\r\n\r\n00:09:35.867 --\u003e 00:09:37.952\r\nYou're one to talk, lizard lips.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.495 --\u003e 00:09:42.582\r\nJune, he's a guest.\r\nOur circus days are over.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.083 --\u003e 00:09:46.419\r\nWe used the money we earned to buy\r\nthis farm so we could live in peace.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.045 --\u003e 00:09:51.257\r\nThis is a sanctuary,\r\nnot only for us but for all our kind.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.008 --\u003e 00:09:55.303\r\nIf you're willing to join in the\r\nwork, you too are welcome here.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.845 --\u003e 00:09:57.639\r\nIs that a fact?\r\n\r\n00:10:01.267 --\u003e 00:10:03.019\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:10:07.941 --\u003e 00:10:09.567\r\n- Hey.\r\n- You did it!\r\n\r\n00:10:09.651 --\u003e 00:10:13.488\r\n- Bravo. Well done.\r\n- I told you he was strong.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.905 --\u003e 00:10:16.658\r\nSo tell us, friend,\r\nfrom whence do you hail?\r\n\r\n00:10:17.242 --\u003e 00:10:20.954\r\nSee, I was part of this freak\r\nshow, same as you,\r\n\r\n00:10:21.037 --\u003e 00:10:24.415\r\nonly they kept me chained like an animal.\r\nDay and night.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.499 --\u003e 00:10:28.211\r\nForced me to live in a tank.\r\nMade me do tricks.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.294 --\u003e 00:10:30.296\r\n- How awful.\r\n- Jerks.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.630 --\u003e 00:10:34.801\r\nYeah. They fed me fish\r\nheads and stale bread.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.884 --\u003e 00:10:40.348\r\nWhen I tried to get away, they worked\r\nme over pretty good, put me in chains.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.641 --\u003e 00:10:42.725\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:10:47.897 --\u003e 00:10:50.483\r\nDon't worry.\r\nNobody will find you here.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.608 --\u003e 00:10:52.861\r\nHaven't seen a soul\r\nsince we moved in.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.319 --\u003e 00:10:56.030\r\nThat's good, real good.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.831 --\u003e 00:11:06.040\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:11:12.213 --\u003e 00:11:14.215\r\nAnd they say the\r\ncity's dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.969 --\u003e 00:11:20.054\r\nGOLIATH: No, I don't mind\r\nsleeping out on the straw.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.430 --\u003e 00:11:24.684\r\n- Go ahead and take my bedroom.\r\n- Don't put yourself out for me.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.934 --\u003e 00:11:26.853\r\nThe cat's too small anyway.\r\n\r\n00:11:27.061 --\u003e 00:11:28.980\r\nAnd tomorrow we'll go\r\nswimming, right, Croc?\r\n\r\n00:11:29.564 --\u003e 00:11:32.650\r\nThere's the coolest grottos along\r\nthe river. It's like another world.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.026 --\u003e 00:11:36.905\r\nYeah, sure, kid.\r\nToo bad I forgot my bathing suit.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.739 --\u003e 00:11:41.201\r\nThat's right. Our new friend here\r\nis going to need additional raiment.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.327 --\u003e 00:11:46.164\r\n- He means clothes.\r\n- Yeah? You guys got money?\r\n\r\n00:11:46.247 --\u003e 00:11:50.835\r\nJust a small nest egg leftover\r\nfrom the purchase of this mill.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.252 --\u003e 00:11:52.795\r\nFifty thousand.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.047 --\u003e 00:11:56.341\r\n(SIGHS) Thank you, Goliath.\r\n\r\n00:11:56.424 --\u003e 00:11:59.260\r\nIt's not something\r\nwe like to broadcast.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.178 --\u003e 00:12:03.932\r\nFifty grand?\r\nA guy could go to town on that.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.602 --\u003e 00:12:50.687\r\nBILLY: Croc?\r\n\r\n00:12:51.729 --\u003e 00:12:52.730\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:12:52.981 --\u003e 00:12:57.610\r\n- What you doing?\r\n- Looking for a blanket. I'm cold.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.986 --\u003e 00:12:59.529\r\nI'll find you one.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.907 --\u003e 00:13:04.033\r\nI got it, shorty.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.117 --\u003e 00:13:05.326\r\nYou know, Croc,\r\n\r\n00:13:05.410 --\u003e 00:13:08.329\r\nI know you feel a little funny being\r\nhere, but it's great.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.621 --\u003e 00:13:12.959\r\nIt really is. No one stares at\r\nyou, laughing, making you feel bad.\r\n\r\n00:13:13.084 --\u003e 00:13:14.419\r\nYou can be yourself.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.044 --\u003e 00:13:17.213\r\nYeah, great. Whatever.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.509 --\u003e 00:13:23.177\r\n(SNORING)\r\n\r\n00:13:29.350 --\u003e 00:13:30.351\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:13:31.394 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:32.478 --\u003e 00:13:33.521\r\n(MUFFLED PROTESTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:33.646 --\u003e 00:13:36.441\r\nCalm down. I won't hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.941 --\u003e 00:13:39.694\r\nI'm looking for someone.\r\nHalf man, half crocodile.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.654 --\u003e 00:13:44.574\r\n- He's in there, isn't he?\r\n- No. Stay away.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.493 --\u003e 00:13:48.745\r\nHe's one of us.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.828 --\u003e 00:13:50.621\r\nCroc, run!\r\n\r\n00:13:56.544 --\u003e 00:13:59.797\r\n- I don't want to hurt you.\r\n- Don't worry. You won't.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.391 --\u003e 00:14:11.392\r\n(GOLIATH GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:14:12.560 --\u003e 00:14:14.020\r\n(YELLING OUT IN PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.564 --\u003e 00:14:17.940\r\nYou.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.363 --\u003e 00:14:25.156\r\nRichard, help!\r\n\r\n00:14:34.874 --\u003e 00:14:37.752\r\nQuickly. Quickly. In there.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.805 --\u003e 00:14:51.682\r\nHa! Who's the freak now, Bats?\r\n\r\n00:14:52.475 --\u003e 00:14:54.894\r\n- Who is he?\r\n- A nutcase in a mask.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.977 --\u003e 00:14:58.106\r\n- He's the one who put me in the tank.\r\n- Don't listen to him.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.481 --\u003e 00:15:01.025\r\nHis name's Killer Croc.\r\nHe's dangerous.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.485 --\u003e 00:15:06.155\r\nQuiet! Don't think you're\r\ngonna fool my friends, do you?\r\n\r\n00:15:06.322 --\u003e 00:15:08.783\r\nThey know my story.\r\nI'm one of them.\r\n\r\n00:15:09.158 --\u003e 00:15:13.955\r\nYes. And his chains speak more\r\neloquently than any words of yours.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.539 --\u003e 00:15:19.085\r\nListen to me. He's an escaped\r\nconvict, a cold-blooded killer.\r\n\r\n00:15:19.335 --\u003e 00:15:20.670\r\nI said shut up!\r\n\r\n00:15:23.464 --\u003e 00:15:25.883\r\nWhat he said,\r\nit's not true, is it?\r\n\r\n00:15:26.134 --\u003e 00:15:28.177\r\nYou're being square with\r\nus, aren't you, Croc?\r\n\r\n00:15:28.678 --\u003e 00:15:33.516\r\n'Course I am. I ain't the one who\r\nattacked big boy in his sleep, am I?\r\n\r\n00:15:35.226 --\u003e 00:15:36.853\r\nWhat are we gonna do?\r\n\r\n00:15:38.396 --\u003e 00:15:39.772\r\nGet rid of him.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.274 --\u003e 00:15:42.650\r\nWhat do you mean?\r\n\r\n00:15:44.735 --\u003e 00:15:48.406\r\nIf he gets loose, he'll bring 'em\r\nall down on us. No one's safe.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.781 --\u003e 00:15:50.533\r\nThe bat's gotta go.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.417 --\u003e 00:16:03.921\r\nIt's your last hunt, Bats.\r\nAnd now you're the prey.\r\n\r\n00:16:05.673 --\u003e 00:16:07.592\r\nCroc, no. Don't do this.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.092 --\u003e 00:16:10.178\r\n- You can't.\r\n- It's not right.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.888 --\u003e 00:16:13.848\r\nI can and I will.\r\n\r\n00:16:16.434 --\u003e 00:16:17.810\r\nNo killing.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.187 --\u003e 00:16:20.396\r\nWhy, you dirty...\r\n\r\n00:16:23.065 --\u003e 00:16:26.611\r\nStay out of this!\r\nThis is between me and the bat.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.737 --\u003e 00:16:30.239\r\n- But you can't kill him.\r\n- He's still a human being.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.616 --\u003e 00:16:35.077\r\n- Who are you calling human?\r\n- Oh, Croc.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.620 --\u003e 00:16:39.582\r\nAlas, I fear that the chameleon\r\nhas shown his true colors.\r\n\r\n00:16:40.124 --\u003e 00:16:44.295\r\nI think you should leave, my friend.\r\nWe've had enough of these shenanigans.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.172 --\u003e 00:16:49.842\r\nWell, kid, looks like we're gonna\r\nhave to postpone that little swim.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.051 --\u003e 00:16:51.219\r\nWatch out!\r\n\r\n00:16:52.136 --\u003e 00:16:53.429\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:16:53.721 --\u003e 00:16:54.722\r\n(ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:59.685 --\u003e 00:17:00.686\r\n(GOLIATH GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.103 --\u003e 00:17:03.022\r\nThe bigger they are, eh, Bats?\r\n\r\n00:17:11.822 --\u003e 00:17:13.950\r\nThe evil that men do...\r\n\r\n00:17:15.117 --\u003e 00:17:16.536\r\nStuff the Shakespeare.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.619 --\u003e 00:17:18.996\r\nYou're lucky you're still\r\naround to recite it.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.747 --\u003e 00:17:21.666\r\nYou I'm not done with yet.\r\n\r\n00:17:28.756 --\u003e 00:17:29.882\r\nAll right.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.429 --\u003e 00:17:37.098\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.482 --\u003e 00:17:47.775\r\nCROC: Hey!\r\n\r\n00:17:48.776 --\u003e 00:17:52.280\r\nLookie here, Bats.\r\nGot a couple of souvenirs.\r\n\r\n00:17:55.741 --\u003e 00:17:57.410\r\nOne for you too.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.994 --\u003e 00:18:00.663\r\nDon't want you talking\r\nabout me when I'm gone.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.081 --\u003e 00:18:03.082\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.670 --\u003e 00:18:08.671\r\n(KILLER CROC YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.821 --\u003e 00:18:35.031\r\n(GOLIATH GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.795 --\u003e 00:18:51.505\r\n(GUN FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:18:58.012 --\u003e 00:19:02.933\r\nGive it up, Bats. You can't take me.\r\nI got the high ground. I got the gun.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.560 --\u003e 00:19:05.936\r\nI know a way in.\r\n\r\n00:19:29.752 --\u003e 00:19:30.753\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:19:42.348 --\u003e 00:19:43.349\r\n\u003ci\u003e“Yam!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:43.432 --\u003e 00:19:44.809\r\nYou're guano, bat.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.902 --\u003e 00:19:55.903\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:05.287 --\u003e 00:20:06.288\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:20:07.581 --\u003e 00:20:08.582\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:36.026 --\u003e 00:20:37.027\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:20:37.486 --\u003e 00:20:38.571\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:20:39.780 --\u003e 00:20:40.990\r\n(KILLER CROC GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:21:00.050 --\u003e 00:21:01.677\r\nShaw's over, folks.\r\n\r\n00:21:08.768 --\u003e 00:21:10.978\r\nOkay, guys. All set.\r\n\r\n00:21:11.771 --\u003e 00:21:14.648\r\nWhy, Croc?\r\nWhy did you turn on us like that?\r\n\r\n00:21:15.191 --\u003e 00:21:17.943\r\nWe could have helped you.\r\nWe could have done something.\r\n\r\n00:21:18.319 --\u003e 00:21:21.405\r\nYou said you can be yourself out\r\nhere, remember?\r\n\r\n00:21:22.156 --\u003e 00:21:24.450\r\nWell, I guess that's\r\nwhat I was doing.\r\n\r\n00:21:24.533 --\u003e 00:21:26.035\r\nBeing myself.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.811 --\u003e 00:21:53.813\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:18.420 --\u003e 00:22:19.630\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E08 - Avatar (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.147 --\u003e 00:00:24.191\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:03:07.104 --\u003e 00:03:10.190\r\nLUCIUS FOX: Without a doubt, this will\r\nbe one of the best museum exhibitions\r\n\r\n00:03:10.357 --\u003e 00:03:12.234\r\nGotham City has ever seen.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.526 --\u003e 00:03:15.445\r\nYou can be quite the\r\nhumanitarian on occasion, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.904 --\u003e 00:03:18.699\r\nIt's commendable.\r\nIt's inspiring.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.782 --\u003e 00:03:21.702\r\n- It's deductible.\r\n- The Scroll of Osiris.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.993 --\u003e 00:03:23.954\r\nPity only half of it exists.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.204 --\u003e 00:03:27.165\r\nIt's the oldest Egyptian\r\ndocument known to man.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.125 --\u003e 00:03:29.334\r\nYeah.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.127 --\u003e 00:03:32.504\r\n(GASPS) Oops!\r\nI gotta go meet Tammy at Charday's.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.380 --\u003e 00:03:35.424\r\nHmm. Such a pity.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.291 --\u003e 00:04:10.459\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:14.755 --\u003e 00:04:16.131\r\nNow, let's have a look at you.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.632 --\u003e 00:04:18.967\r\n\u003ci\u003e“Bu?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:19.342 --\u003e 00:04:22.179\r\nRA'S AL GHUL: You could've\r\nbeen my successor, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.763 --\u003e 00:04:26.349\r\nInstead, you will suffer the\r\nfate of all mortal flesh.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.030 --\u003e 00:04:42.949\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:05:11.853 --\u003e 00:05:13.063\r\nALFRED: Snake venom?\r\n\r\n00:05:13.438 --\u003e 00:05:16.733\r\nBATMAN: From an Egyptian cobra.\r\nExtremely deadly.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.942 --\u003e 00:05:20.278\r\n- You're certain it was Ra's Al Ghul?\r\n- None other.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.570 --\u003e 00:05:22.656\r\nBut I thought he died\r\nin the Pit months ago.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.281 --\u003e 00:05:24.282\r\nSo did I.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.658 --\u003e 00:05:27.536\r\nThat piece of papyrus is\r\nobviously very important to him.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.994 --\u003e 00:05:30.705\r\n- I have to find out why.\r\n- Where are you off to now?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.789 --\u003e 00:05:32.374\r\nJust in case the\r\nstockholders ask.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.291 --\u003e 00:05:36.127\r\nGibraltar. There's someone\r\nI've been meaning to look up.\r\n\r\n00:06:35.270 --\u003e 00:06:37.022\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:42.527 --\u003e 00:06:43.570\r\n(GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:06:47.490 --\u003e 00:06:48.825\r\nBeloved?\r\n\r\n00:06:57.334 --\u003e 00:06:59.377\r\nTALIA: My father? Alive?\r\n\r\n00:07:00.170 --\u003e 00:07:02.464\r\nIt was dear old dad, no mistake.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.048 --\u003e 00:07:06.551\r\nNo, he would have found me.\r\nHe would have told me he was alive.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.718 --\u003e 00:07:09.512\r\nI know the face of my most\r\npowerful enemy, Talia.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.763 --\u003e 00:07:12.390\r\nHe took quite a risk\r\nstealing that scroll from me.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.474 --\u003e 00:07:14.017\r\nWhy does he want it so badly?\r\n\r\n00:07:14.434 --\u003e 00:07:15.727\r\nIt's part of a map.\r\n\r\n00:07:16.478 --\u003e 00:07:17.979\r\nMy father has the other half.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.480 --\u003e 00:07:22.108\r\nAs long as I can remember he's\r\nbeen obsessed with finding...\r\n\r\n00:07:22.442 --\u003e 00:07:23.485\r\nFinding what?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.735 --\u003e 00:07:26.112\r\nThe tomb of the ancient\r\nqueen Thoth Khepera.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.696 --\u003e 00:07:28.949\r\nIt lies somewhere in\r\nthe Canyon of Tombs.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.366 --\u003e 00:07:31.076\r\nMany who've sought\r\nit have vanished.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.368 --\u003e 00:07:32.619\r\nAnd why does Ra's seek it?\r\n\r\n00:07:33.036 --\u003e 00:07:34.204\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.579 --\u003e 00:07:35.789\r\nYou must believe me.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.289 --\u003e 00:07:38.959\r\nI have to go after him, Talia.\r\nWill you help me?\r\n\r\n00:07:39.167 --\u003e 00:07:43.296\r\nYou are so like him,\r\nmaking me choose between the two of you.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.380 --\u003e 00:07:46.007\r\nOh, beloved,\r\nwhy has he forsaken me?\r\n\r\n00:07:46.341 --\u003e 00:07:47.842\r\nDoes he think I've betrayed him?\r\n\r\n00:07:48.051 --\u003e 00:07:50.387\r\nI can't pretend to know\r\nwhat Ra's thinks, Talia.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.221 --\u003e 00:07:55.183\r\nThe only thing he and I have ever\r\nagreed upon is our feelings towards you.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.107 --\u003e 00:08:05.443\r\nMy father used to have a\r\nhidden sanctuary in Cairo.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.527 --\u003e 00:08:08.446\r\n- Perhaps he still uses it.\r\n- It's worth a try.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.999 --\u003e 00:08:20.583\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.084 --\u003e 00:08:23.795\r\nArtifacts from the king's tomb.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.962 --\u003e 00:08:25.755\r\n- Every one's a valuable treasure.\r\n- In here.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.922 --\u003e 00:08:28.758\r\n- This place looks familiar.\r\n- VENDOR: Guaranteed authentic.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.679 --\u003e 00:08:34.681\r\n(SPEAKING EGYPTIAN)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.764 --\u003e 00:08:36.266\r\n(IN ENGLISH) How may I help you?\r\n\r\n00:08:36.558 --\u003e 00:08:37.600\r\nWe're just browsing.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.851 --\u003e 00:08:41.354\r\nYou could find no finer\r\nplace than this establishment\r\n\r\n00:08:41.563 --\u003e 00:08:44.816\r\nin which to obtain\r\nwondrous bargains.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.191 --\u003e 00:08:46.609\r\nThis, for example,\r\n\r\n00:08:46.943 --\u003e 00:08:49.904\r\na priceless relic from\r\nthe Seventh Dynasty.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.321 --\u003e 00:08:51.531\r\nThe only one of its kind.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.325 --\u003e 00:08:55.827\r\nAnother time, perhaps.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.870 --\u003e 00:08:57.871\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.706 --\u003e 00:09:01.541\r\nThis is the place.\r\nI'm sure of it.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.791 --\u003e 00:09:03.877\r\nThere's a secret entrance\r\nto a lower level,\r\n\r\n00:09:03.960 --\u003e 00:09:05.336\r\nbut I don't remember where.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.712 --\u003e 00:09:06.796\r\nThis might help us.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.965 --\u003e 00:09:10.565\r\n- (RAPID BEEPING)\r\n- An ultrasound imager.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.182 --\u003e 00:09:19.017\r\nEureka.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.735 --\u003e 00:09:29.736\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.819 --\u003e 00:09:30.820\r\n(TALIA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:31.154 --\u003e 00:09:34.783\r\nThis part of the store\r\nis closed to customers.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.630 --\u003e 00:09:51.132\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:00.934 --\u003e 00:10:02.018\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:04.229 --\u003e 00:10:06.648\r\n- We make a good team.\r\n- That we do.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.997 --\u003e 00:10:24.541\r\nTALIA: The completed scroll?\r\n\r\n00:10:24.624 --\u003e 00:10:27.043\r\nBRUCE: Yes,\r\nand a translation made by Ra's.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.628 --\u003e 00:10:31.047\r\nDid you really think I\r\nwould be foolish enough\r\n\r\n00:10:31.131 --\u003e 00:10:34.008\r\nnot to have this sanctum\r\nunder observation?\r\n\r\n00:10:37.053 --\u003e 00:10:39.931\r\nFather! You really are alive.\r\n\r\n00:10:40.014 --\u003e 00:10:41.933\r\nYes, Talia, I am alive.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.475 --\u003e 00:10:46.855\r\nNo thanks, I regret to say, are due\r\nyou for my current state of health.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:49.649\r\nNo, Father,\r\nyou can't believe that.\r\n\r\n00:10:49.899 --\u003e 00:10:52.235\r\nI only tried to\r\nsave the man I love.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.318 --\u003e 00:10:54.946\r\nYou've got a serious\r\npriority problem, Ra's.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.238 --\u003e 00:10:58.992\r\nWhat can be in that tomb that's more\r\nvaluable than the love of your daughter?\r\n\r\n00:10:59.492 --\u003e 00:11:01.035\r\nPower, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:11:01.411 --\u003e 00:11:06.166\r\nThe power once held by almighty Thoth\r\nKhepera, queen of two continents.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.666 --\u003e 00:11:08.334\r\nYou surprise me, Ra's.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.626 --\u003e 00:11:11.296\r\nThe world's oldest chauvinist\r\nchasing after a woman?\r\n\r\n00:11:11.588 --\u003e 00:11:15.049\r\nThoth Khepera was not simply a\r\nwoman, Detective,\r\n\r\n00:11:15.592 --\u003e 00:11:16.926\r\nnor merely a ruler.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.343 --\u003e 00:11:20.180\r\nThrough her flowed\r\nthe power of the gods.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.263 --\u003e 00:11:21.681\r\nWith no more than a gesture,\r\n\r\n00:11:21.764 --\u003e 00:11:24.142\r\nshe controlled the\r\nforce of life and death,\r\n\r\n00:11:24.392 --\u003e 00:11:29.314\r\nand with it she kept a nation\r\nunder her thumb for 1,000 years.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.606 --\u003e 00:11:32.358\r\nYou sound like a bad Saturday\r\nafternoon serial, Ra's.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.567 --\u003e 00:11:35.361\r\n- This is sheer nonsense.\r\n- No, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.445 --\u003e 00:11:37.655\r\nI know there is a power\r\nthere to be tapped.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.072 --\u003e 00:11:40.950\r\nMy 600 years of life\r\nare proof of that power.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.163 --\u003e 00:11:46.706\r\nFarewell, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:11:47.165 --\u003e 00:11:48.458\r\nFarewell, Talia.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.541 --\u003e 00:11:52.295\r\nIt is said that one finds\r\nimmortality in one's offspring.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.087 --\u003e 00:11:55.590\r\nAlas, I know that to be a lie.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.893 --\u003e 00:12:08.978\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:09.771 --\u003e 00:12:11.648\r\nThe air won't last much longer.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.106 --\u003e 00:12:14.192\r\nIt's not the end I would've\r\nchosen, beloved,\r\n\r\n00:12:14.609 --\u003e 00:12:17.028\r\nbut if we must die,\r\nI am glad we're together.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.362 --\u003e 00:12:18.613\r\nWe're not licked yet.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.501 --\u003e 00:12:33.878\r\nCover your ears,\r\nTalia, and pray.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.560 --\u003e 00:12:52.397\r\nTalia, I'll do whatever\r\nI have to to stop him.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.981 --\u003e 00:12:54.190\r\nYou must know that.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.399 --\u003e 00:12:56.901\r\nI do.\r\nAnd though it breaks my heart,\r\n\r\n00:12:57.402 --\u003e 00:12:59.195\r\nI will do what I must as well.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.844 --\u003e 00:13:25.596\r\nNo sign of Ra's.\r\nLooks like we beat him here.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.222 --\u003e 00:13:29.851\r\n- How did you know where to find it?\r\n- I saw the scroll's translation.\r\n\r\n00:13:30.059 --\u003e 00:13:31.185\r\nFor only a moment.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.270 --\u003e 00:13:33.438\r\nI'm a quick study.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.126 --\u003e 00:13:56.669\r\nThe queen's sarcophagus.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.378 --\u003e 00:13:59.297\r\nRA'S: It's not what it\r\nseems, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.630 --\u003e 00:14:00.757\r\nFather!\r\n\r\n00:14:01.007 --\u003e 00:14:04.469\r\nThat chest contains more\r\nthan a mummy's corpse.\r\n\r\n00:14:04.969 --\u003e 00:14:07.680\r\nRemember,\r\nThoth Khepera was immortal.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.889 --\u003e 00:14:09.974\r\nHer subjects deified her,\r\n\r\n00:14:10.183 --\u003e 00:14:14.187\r\nnamed her after the ancient gods of\r\ninfinite knowledge and eternal life.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.270 --\u003e 00:14:16.105\r\nAnd in a few short moments\r\n\r\n00:14:16.189 --\u003e 00:14:21.527\r\nI will be privy to those same\r\nsecrets of life and death.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.283 --\u003e 00:14:30.578\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:14:43.925 --\u003e 00:14:45.009\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.803 --\u003e 00:14:47.929\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:15:14.956 --\u003e 00:15:16.374\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:06.883 --\u003e 00:16:08.134\r\nWho are you?\r\n\r\n00:16:08.551 --\u003e 00:16:10.803\r\nI am Thoth Khepera.\r\n\r\n00:16:11.304 --\u003e 00:16:14.891\r\nThose who have joined me\r\nshare their knowledge with me.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.308 --\u003e 00:16:16.893\r\nWe are legion.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.518 --\u003e 00:16:19.812\r\nI am called Ra's Al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.688 --\u003e 00:16:24.150\r\nI have searched for\r\nyou for over 500 years.\r\n\r\n00:16:24.692 --\u003e 00:16:26.527\r\nTell me your secret.\r\n\r\n00:16:27.028 --\u003e 00:16:31.532\r\nGrant me the powers of the gods\r\nthat legend says you possessed.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.908 --\u003e 00:16:35.369\r\nThat knowledge can be\r\nyours if you join us.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.001 --\u003e 00:16:44.337\r\nCome forward, Ra's Al Ghul.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.004 --\u003e 00:16:48.633\r\nCome and know the mysteries\r\nof life and death.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.527 --\u003e 00:17:08.778\r\nFather.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.785 --\u003e 00:17:16.911\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:17.703 --\u003e 00:17:18.704\r\n(HISSES)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.934 --\u003e 00:17:43.938\r\n(DISTORTED VOICE) None\r\nmay defile me and live.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.004 --\u003e 00:18:09.088\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:09.171 --\u003e 00:18:10.172\r\nTalia!\r\n\r\n00:18:21.017 --\u003e 00:18:22.268\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:44.290 --\u003e 00:18:45.291\r\nRun!\r\n\r\n00:18:48.419 --\u003e 00:18:50.046\r\nKeep going and don't look back.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.129 --\u003e 00:18:52.965\r\nI'll do what I can\r\nto stop that thing.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.888 --\u003e 00:18:59.889\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:11.067 --\u003e 00:19:13.152\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.986 --\u003e 00:19:14.987\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:19:32.129 --\u003e 00:19:34.340\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:43.516 --\u003e 00:19:44.892\r\nInfidel!\r\n\r\n00:19:44.975 --\u003e 00:19:45.976\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:17.591 --\u003e 00:20:18.843\r\nDaughter.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.301 --\u003e 00:20:20.344\r\nFather.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.601 --\u003e 00:20:29.729\r\nMy apologies to you, daughter.\r\n\r\n00:20:31.105 --\u003e 00:20:35.317\r\nThough I had abandoned you in my heart,\r\nobviously, you have not done the same.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.496 --\u003e 00:20:51.041\r\n- What will you do now?\r\n- Take them back to the authorities.\r\n\r\n00:20:51.542 --\u003e 00:20:53.502\r\nYour father has\r\nmuch to answer for.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.586 --\u003e 00:20:54.795\r\n(GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:20:55.671 --\u003e 00:20:59.717\r\nI am truly sorry, beloved,\r\nbut he is my father.\r\n\r\n00:21:02.845 --\u003e 00:21:04.597\r\nPlease dismount.\r\n\r\n00:21:17.735 --\u003e 00:21:19.653\r\nAnother time, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:21:34.210 --\u003e 00:21:36.962\r\nYes, another time.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.644 --\u003e 00:21:53.646\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:17.795 --\u003e 00:22:18.796\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E09 - Trial (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:22.231 --\u003e 00:00:24.233\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.956 --\u003e 00:01:22.374\r\nJUDGE: The prisoner will stand.\r\n\r\n00:01:25.085 --\u003e 00:01:26.753\r\nPamela Lillian lsley,\r\n\r\n00:01:27.087 --\u003e 00:01:29.131\r\nDistrict Attorney\r\nVan Dorn has asked\r\n\r\n00:01:29.214 --\u003e 00:01:32.426\r\nthat the maximum sentence of life\r\nimprisonment be imposed upon you.\r\n\r\n00:01:32.843 --\u003e 00:01:35.929\r\nHowever, as your apprehension\r\ncame at the hands of the Batman,\r\n\r\n00:01:36.096 --\u003e 00:01:38.015\r\nand not a recognized\r\nagent of the law,\r\n\r\n00:01:38.098 --\u003e 00:01:42.352\r\nthis court has no choice but\r\nto return you to Arkham Asylum,\r\n\r\n00:01:42.436 --\u003e 00:01:45.897\r\nwhere it is hoped you will\r\ncomplete your rehabilitation.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.906 --\u003e 00:01:57.451\r\nHi, Red. Hi. Welcome home.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.786 --\u003e 00:02:00.829\r\nHi, Harley.\r\n\r\n00:02:04.291 --\u003e 00:02:05.626\r\n(KEYS JANGLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:19.181 --\u003e 00:02:22.184\r\nAw, things didn't go too\r\ngood, huh?\r\n\r\n00:02:22.643 --\u003e 00:02:24.519\r\n- Nope.\r\n- Well, cheer up.\r\n\r\n00:02:24.603 --\u003e 00:02:27.147\r\nWord is we're gonna\r\nthrow a little party.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.314 --\u003e 00:02:29.816\r\nAnd old Jervis here\r\nhas the invitations.\r\n\r\n00:02:35.697 --\u003e 00:02:39.576\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot only does Batman create\r\nthese so-called super-criminals,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:39.868 --\u003e 00:02:42.746\r\n\u003ci\u003ehe takes it upon himself\r\nto be their judge and jury\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:42.829 --\u003e 00:02:44.956\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith no regard for\r\nthe legal system.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:45.290 --\u003e 00:02:47.834\r\nFEMALE REPORTER: \u003ci\u003eIt sounds like\r\nyou want to put Batman on trial.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:48.001 --\u003e 00:02:50.087\r\nBelieve me,\r\nI'd like nothing better.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.630 --\u003e 00:02:54.383\r\n- Strong words.\r\n- It's got to stop, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.758 --\u003e 00:02:56.385\r\nAs Gotham's new\r\ndistrict attorney,\r\n\r\n00:02:56.468 --\u003e 00:03:00.097\r\nI can't allow your pet nut\r\nto run loose in my city.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.389 --\u003e 00:03:01.431\r\nI mean it.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.890 --\u003e 00:03:05.102\r\nJanet, it's a war zone out there,\r\nand Batman is our best weapon.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.435 --\u003e 00:03:10.482\r\nAnd I say he's a drug the city keeps\r\ntaking to avoid facing reality.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.565 --\u003e 00:03:11.566\r\n(BLINDS RATTLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:14.027 --\u003e 00:03:15.112\r\nSpeak of the devil.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.445 --\u003e 00:03:18.824\r\nThe East Side Skulls are ready to\r\ndeclare war on the other gangs.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.990 --\u003e 00:03:20.826\r\nOld news.\r\nMy department's already\r\n\r\n00:03:20.909 --\u003e 00:03:22.911\r\nplanning a sting to\r\ncatch the Skulls' leader.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.994 --\u003e 00:03:24.246\r\nDon't bother.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.248 --\u003e 00:03:27.624\r\nVery cute, mister.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.958 --\u003e 00:03:29.318\r\nYou want to support\r\nlaw and order?\r\n\r\n00:03:29.376 --\u003e 00:03:31.586\r\nYou take off that mask\r\nand put on a uniform.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.340 --\u003e 00:03:38.385\r\nYou hear me, Batman?\r\nThis is the last time!\r\n\r\n00:03:41.221 --\u003e 00:03:44.766\r\nThe next time I see him,\r\nit will be a whole different story.\r\n\r\n00:03:53.191 --\u003e 00:03:54.484\r\nHello, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.735 --\u003e 00:03:57.863\r\nJanet, I'm so glad we're able\r\nto meet on such short notice.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.322 --\u003e 00:04:02.200\r\nIt seems every place I look\r\nthere's our crusading DA\r\n\r\n00:04:02.284 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nleading the campaign to\r\nrid our city of Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.828 --\u003e 00:04:08.874\r\nOh, please. He's the last person\r\nI want to talk about tonight.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.791 --\u003e 00:04:10.792\r\nOh, sorry.\r\n\r\n00:04:11.293 --\u003e 00:04:14.212\r\nStill, even you have to admit\r\nBatman's come through now and then.\r\n\r\n00:04:14.421 --\u003e 00:04:16.590\r\nBut look at the lunatic\r\nfringe he's created.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.673 --\u003e 00:04:19.301\r\nThe Joker, Two-Face,\r\nPoison Ivy, and the rest.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.384 --\u003e 00:04:21.344\r\nBatman's responsible\r\nfor every one of them.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.595 --\u003e 00:04:24.097\r\nExcuse me, Ms.\r\nVan Dorn, but your office just called.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.181 --\u003e 00:04:26.016\r\nThey said it's an emergency.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.099 --\u003e 00:04:28.226\r\nI'm sorry, Bruce.\r\nI won't be a minute.\r\n\r\n00:04:31.980 --\u003e 00:04:33.064\r\nTake your time.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.318 --\u003e 00:04:38.278\r\n(BRUCE WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:04:43.617 --\u003e 00:04:45.410\r\nUh, excuse me, have you seen Ms.\r\nVan Dorn?\r\n\r\n00:04:45.869 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Not in the last half-hour, sir.\r\n- MAN: Look.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.789 --\u003e 00:04:49.873\r\nMust be trouble.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.081 --\u003e 00:04:51.082\r\n(PEOPLE MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:04:52.292 --\u003e 00:04:54.228\r\nMAN 1: Look at that.\r\nMAN 2: I've never seen that before.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.252 --\u003e 00:04:55.712\r\n(PEOPLE CHATTERING EXCITEDLY)\r\n\r\n00:05:00.634 --\u003e 00:05:01.802\r\nIt's Van Dorn's.\r\n\r\n00:05:02.302 --\u003e 00:05:04.513\r\nIt was dropped on the\r\nfront desk 20 minutes ago.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.263 --\u003e 00:05:06.306\r\nAlong with this.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.266 --\u003e 00:05:11.937\r\nBATMAN: \"Batman, come alone to\r\nwhere lives hang in the balance\"\r\n\r\n00:05:12.020 --\u003e 00:05:13.980\r\n\"or the law in Gotham dies.\"\r\n\r\n00:05:25.450 --\u003e 00:05:27.410\r\nYou there! Come into the light.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.162 --\u003e 00:05:30.205\r\nI said...\r\n\r\n00:05:31.873 --\u003e 00:05:33.033\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- (OBJECT CRASH ES)\r\n\r\n00:05:35.126 --\u003e 00:05:36.419\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:05:39.714 --\u003e 00:05:40.882\r\n(GRUNTS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:05:56.356 --\u003e 00:05:58.066\r\nOh, no, you don't.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.443 --\u003e 00:06:01.820\r\nTa-da!\r\n\r\n00:06:03.572 --\u003e 00:06:04.948\r\n(HARLEY SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.165 --\u003e 00:06:16.501\r\nLet me out. Do you hear me?\r\n\r\n00:06:16.585 --\u003e 00:06:18.837\r\nWhoever you are,\r\nlet me out this second.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.047 --\u003e 00:06:22.132\r\n(DOOR UNLOCKS)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.967 --\u003e 00:06:26.511\r\nWelcome to Arkham, Van Dorn.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.053 --\u003e 00:06:28.179\r\nTwo-Face.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.556 --\u003e 00:06:31.641\r\nDon't bother screaming for help.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.975 --\u003e 00:06:34.019\r\nThe white coats can't hear you.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.394 --\u003e 00:06:35.395\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:36.396 --\u003e 00:06:38.636\r\nTWO-FACE: Matter of fact,\r\nthey can't do much of anything,\r\n\r\n00:06:38.857 --\u003e 00:06:40.692\r\nthanks to the Mad Hatter.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.237 --\u003e 00:06:45.447\r\nYou're going to escape?\r\n\r\n00:06:45.947 --\u003e 00:06:47.115\r\nEventually.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.741 --\u003e 00:06:50.702\r\nWe've got some legal\r\nbusiness to settle first.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.119 --\u003e 00:06:54.915\r\n- What do you mean?\r\n- I'm talking about a trial.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.874 --\u003e 00:06:57.292\r\nMe, the prosecutor.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.959 --\u003e 00:06:59.336\r\nYou, the defense.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.836 --\u003e 00:07:01.338\r\nAnd your client...\r\n\r\n00:07:04.341 --\u003e 00:07:06.259\r\nls Batman.\r\n\r\n00:07:06.343 --\u003e 00:07:07.761\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.934 --\u003e 00:07:17.145\r\nThis is insane.\r\nMe defending you?\r\n\r\n00:07:17.228 --\u003e 00:07:19.731\r\nAs far as I'm concerned,\r\nyou belong in here with them.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.190 --\u003e 00:07:22.442\r\n(GROANS) Whatever.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.776 --\u003e 00:07:26.112\r\nYou've gotta go through with it.\r\nIt's their game and their rules.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.364 --\u003e 00:07:28.823\r\nLet's go. Move it.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.282 --\u003e 00:07:30.450\r\nIndeed.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.825 --\u003e 00:07:32.744\r\nCan't keep the judge waiting.\r\n\r\n00:07:34.663 --\u003e 00:07:36.456\r\nTWO-FACE: You've said it\r\nyourself, lady.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.957 --\u003e 00:07:39.084\r\nBatman made every one of us.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.250 --\u003e 00:07:43.797\r\nSo, we're placing him before\r\nthe bar to face ourjustice.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.005 --\u003e 00:07:45.131\r\nAnd me?\r\n\r\n00:07:45.548 --\u003e 00:07:47.384\r\nBasic 50/50 option.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.926 --\u003e 00:07:50.637\r\nYou get him off.\r\nYou both go free.\r\n\r\n00:07:51.638 --\u003e 00:07:52.806\r\nHe goes down,\r\n\r\n00:07:53.348 --\u003e 00:07:55.183\r\nyou take the fall with him.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.809 --\u003e 00:07:57.227\r\nMAD HATTER: Amusing idea, what?\r\n\r\n00:07:57.310 --\u003e 00:08:00.021\r\nKidnapping you to be\r\nBatman's attorney?\r\n\r\n00:08:00.438 --\u003e 00:08:03.692\r\nPersonally, I suggested a\r\nquick slug between the eyes.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.775 --\u003e 00:08:05.318\r\nBut I lost the coin toss.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.902 --\u003e 00:08:07.946\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:30.135 --\u003e 00:08:34.139\r\nI borrowed your belt, Bats,\r\nbut it doesn't do a thing for me.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.724 --\u003e 00:08:36.891\r\nKILLER CROC: Sit down.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.899 --\u003e 00:08:47.110\r\n\u003ci\u003eOYQZ. Dye;.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:49.487 --\u003e 00:08:53.074\r\nHe says, \"0yez,\" dirt bags!\r\nDummy up.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.533 --\u003e 00:08:54.534\r\nSheesh!\r\n\r\n00:08:54.617 --\u003e 00:08:56.286\r\nI gotta do everything for you.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.786 --\u003e 00:08:58.663\r\nCourt is now in session.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.122 --\u003e 00:09:01.207\r\nThe good people of Arkham Asylum\r\n\r\n00:09:01.291 --\u003e 00:09:05.587\r\nversus the self-righteous\r\nvigilante called Batman.\r\n\r\n00:09:05.879 --\u003e 00:09:08.048\r\nOur prosecutor is ready.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.298 --\u003e 00:09:12.635\r\nLikewise,\r\nour fair and impartial jury.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.011 --\u003e 00:09:14.429\r\n- Hang him.\r\n- Shoot him.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.512 --\u003e 00:09:16.056\r\nHit him with a rock.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.307 --\u003e 00:09:22.062\r\nAnd now all rise for the most honorable,\r\nmost benevolent, most merciful.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.270 --\u003e 00:09:24.189\r\nJudge Joker.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.272 --\u003e 00:09:26.232\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:09:29.736 --\u003e 00:09:30.904\r\nGuilty!\r\n\r\n00:09:32.072 --\u003e 00:09:34.991\r\nI was promised a chance\r\nto defend my client.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.075 --\u003e 00:09:36.910\r\nOh, very well.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.243 --\u003e 00:09:38.995\r\nLike it'll make a difference.\r\n\r\n00:09:39.079 --\u003e 00:09:42.916\r\nMr. Prosecutor,\r\nmake your opening statement.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.838 --\u003e 00:09:49.964\r\nLook at us.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.632 --\u003e 00:09:52.801\r\nWe're all freaks and monsters.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.384 --\u003e 00:09:54.969\r\nAnd who made us this way?\r\n\r\n00:09:55.762 --\u003e 00:09:57.055\r\nBatman.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.222 --\u003e 00:10:00.141\r\n(ALL SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:11.945 --\u003e 00:10:14.364\r\nGo on, lady.\r\nDefend him if you can.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.614 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nCall the first witness.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.449 --\u003e 00:10:18.701\r\nYo, Hat. On the stand.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.292 --\u003e 00:10:28.419\r\nProceed, counselor.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.632 --\u003e 00:10:35.051\r\nI suppose you,\r\nlike your friends,\r\n\r\n00:10:35.135 --\u003e 00:10:37.637\r\nclaim that Batman drove\r\nyou to be a criminal?\r\n\r\n00:10:37.720 --\u003e 00:10:38.930\r\nHe did.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.347 --\u003e 00:10:41.975\r\nAnd yet, as I recall your case,\r\n\r\n00:10:42.058 --\u003e 00:10:45.687\r\nyou brainwashed and kidnapped\r\na woman who rejected you.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.770 --\u003e 00:10:47.313\r\nBatman forced me to do it.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.480 --\u003e 00:10:50.567\r\nHe was going to take her away from me.\r\nI had no choice.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.900 --\u003e 00:10:54.112\r\nYou could have respected her\r\nwishes and left her alone.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.195 --\u003e 00:10:55.738\r\nI'd have killed her first!\r\n\r\n00:10:56.739 --\u003e 00:10:57.740\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.949 --\u003e 00:11:00.389\r\nI'd like that last statement\r\nstricken from the record, please.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.869 --\u003e 00:11:04.164\r\nRecord? Ls someone supposed\r\nto be writing this down?\r\n\r\n00:11:05.582 --\u003e 00:11:08.126\r\n(SIGHS) This is crazy.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.585 --\u003e 00:11:11.212\r\nThat's beside the point.\r\nJust keep it going.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.718 --\u003e 00:11:20.763\r\nLooks like Batman's hunch was wrong.\r\nThere's no sign of him or Ms. Van Dorn.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.847 --\u003e 00:11:22.599\r\nBut he was here, all right.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.850 --\u003e 00:11:25.351\r\nI object to this witness.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.435 --\u003e 00:11:27.854\r\nShe's obviously trying\r\nto influence the judge.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.857 --\u003e 00:11:34.068\r\n- What makes you say that?\r\n- Never mind.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.360 --\u003e 00:11:35.612\r\nDo you have a statement?\r\n\r\n00:11:35.695 --\u003e 00:11:39.324\r\nI just wanna say,\r\nif there was no Batman,\r\n\r\n00:11:39.407 --\u003e 00:11:40.992\r\nthere'd be no Joker.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.075 --\u003e 00:11:44.078\r\nAnd I'd never have\r\nmet my pudding.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.079 --\u003e 00:11:46.998\r\nThank you, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.708 --\u003e 00:11:50.293\r\nSad, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:11:50.460 --\u003e 00:11:53.129\r\nHarleen Quinzel was a\r\ndoctor here at Arkham\r\n\r\n00:11:53.213 --\u003e 00:11:55.256\r\nuntil the Joker\r\ntwisted her mind.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.715 --\u003e 00:11:58.343\r\nHa! You're just jealous\r\nbecause you don't have a fella\r\n\r\n00:11:58.426 --\u003e 00:12:02.889\r\nwho's as loving and loyal to\r\nyou as my pudding is to me.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.891 --\u003e 00:12:06.142\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:12:06.392 --\u003e 00:12:07.393\r\nUh-huh.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.727 --\u003e 00:12:10.480\r\nAnd I suppose it was\r\nthat same loyalty I saw\r\n\r\n00:12:10.563 --\u003e 00:12:13.233\r\nthe last time you escaped,\r\nand pudding here...\r\n\r\n00:12:14.359 --\u003e 00:12:16.861\r\nFinked on you in hopes\r\nof getting time off.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.947 --\u003e 00:12:21.366\r\nIs that true, pudding?\r\n\r\n00:12:23.117 --\u003e 00:12:25.828\r\n\"Finked\" is such an ugly word.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.704 --\u003e 00:12:29.374\r\nYou lousy scum-sucking creep!\r\n\r\n00:12:29.457 --\u003e 00:12:32.252\r\nThe witness is excused.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.669 --\u003e 00:12:34.128\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:34.212 --\u003e 00:12:35.546\r\nSlimy rat!\r\n\r\n00:12:38.091 --\u003e 00:12:40.510\r\n(HARLEY YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:40.760 --\u003e 00:12:42.387\r\nKILLER CROC: Knock it off, lady.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.720 --\u003e 00:12:44.264\r\n(PROTESTING INCOHERENTLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:44.722 --\u003e 00:12:47.308\r\nI'll kick that grin\r\noff your silly face.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.017 --\u003e 00:12:50.144\r\n(PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:51.145 --\u003e 00:12:54.524\r\nAnd so it's Batman's fault\r\nyou lead a life of crime.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.983 --\u003e 00:12:57.568\r\nHe should have let me\r\nbump off Harvey Dent.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.652 --\u003e 00:13:00.947\r\nWe'd all have been better\r\noff, wouldn't we, Harv?\r\n\r\n00:13:01.489 --\u003e 00:13:03.449\r\nWhy, you rotten little...\r\n\r\n00:13:03.533 --\u003e 00:13:04.826\r\nJANET: But, Ms. lsley,\r\n\r\n00:13:05.118 --\u003e 00:13:07.412\r\nisn't the real motivation\r\nfor your crimes\r\n\r\n00:13:07.495 --\u003e 00:13:08.955\r\nyour obsession with plants?\r\n\r\n00:13:09.122 --\u003e 00:13:10.832\r\nThat you prefer them to people?\r\n\r\n00:13:10.915 --\u003e 00:13:14.919\r\nI love plants, honey,\r\nbut a rose is a rose.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.378 --\u003e 00:13:17.588\r\nThen it doesn't bother\r\nyou when someone,\r\n\r\n00:13:17.672 --\u003e 00:13:21.009\r\nlet's say the judge\r\nhere, ruthlessly plucks\r\n\r\n00:13:21.259 --\u003e 00:13:26.097\r\na defenseless flower from\r\nthe warm green earth?\r\n\r\n00:13:26.180 --\u003e 00:13:27.223\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:13:27.307 --\u003e 00:13:30.101\r\nEven knowing he's given\r\nit his death sentence?\r\n\r\n00:13:30.643 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\nThat its petals must die?\r\n\r\n00:13:32.812 --\u003e 00:13:34.939\r\n- Stop it.\r\n- JANET: One by one.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.023 --\u003e 00:13:36.524\r\nWithering, falling.\r\n\r\n00:13:36.691 --\u003e 00:13:41.070\r\nOne by one, until it's all gone.\r\nHoney.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.154 --\u003e 00:13:42.405\r\n(IVY YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:13:46.826 --\u003e 00:13:48.745\r\nMs. Ivy, please.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.290 --\u003e 00:13:53.916\r\nYou're beautiful\r\nwhen you're angry.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.295 --\u003e 00:13:58.755\r\n(LAUGHS EVILLY)\r\n\r\n00:14:00.089 --\u003e 00:14:01.549\r\n(PEOPLE MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:14:08.473 --\u003e 00:14:11.809\r\nI used to believe Batman was\r\nresponsible for you people.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.934 --\u003e 00:14:15.605\r\nBut now I see nearly everyone here\r\nwould've ended up exactly the same,\r\n\r\n00:14:15.688 --\u003e 00:14:16.898\r\nBatman or not.\r\n\r\n00:14:17.357 --\u003e 00:14:18.792\r\nOh, the gimmicks\r\nmight be different.\r\n\r\n00:14:18.816 --\u003e 00:14:23.112\r\nBut you'd all be out there in some form\r\nor another, bringing misery to Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.321 --\u003e 00:14:26.366\r\nThe truth is you created him.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.619 --\u003e 00:14:31.259\r\n- GORDON: It's working.\r\n- (DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:31.537 --\u003e 00:14:33.206\r\nLooks like a tracking device.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.374 --\u003e 00:14:35.750\r\nIt's pointing north.\r\n\r\n00:14:36.250 --\u003e 00:14:37.502\r\nThe Somerset District.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.794 --\u003e 00:14:39.420\r\nNothing much out there except...\r\n\r\n00:14:40.380 --\u003e 00:14:41.506\r\nArkham.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.764 --\u003e 00:14:51.891\r\nJury, you've heard the evidence.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.183 --\u003e 00:14:54.268\r\nConsider your verdict.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.769 --\u003e 00:14:56.729\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:03.694 --\u003e 00:15:08.366\r\nYour Honor, in light of Ms.\r\nVan Dorn's stirring defense,\r\n\r\n00:15:08.741 --\u003e 00:15:11.953\r\nwe have no choice but\r\nto find the defendant...\r\n\r\n00:15:13.913 --\u003e 00:15:14.997\r\nNot guilty.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.081 --\u003e 00:15:17.625\r\n(CROWD SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.669 --\u003e 00:15:20.753\r\nAmazing.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.174 --\u003e 00:15:26.968\r\nWell done, counselor.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.427 --\u003e 00:15:30.346\r\nYou've proven that\r\nBatman didn't create us.\r\n\r\n00:15:30.471 --\u003e 00:15:33.975\r\nThat we, in fact,\r\nmessed up our own rotten lives.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.767 --\u003e 00:15:38.563\r\nAnd as we are so rotten,\r\nvile and depraved,\r\n\r\n00:15:38.938 --\u003e 00:15:41.983\r\nwe're going to waste you anyway.\r\n\r\n00:15:42.066 --\u003e 00:15:43.234\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:46.028 --\u003e 00:15:48.281\r\n(CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.955 --\u003e 00:15:57.015\r\n(IMITATING PORKY PIG STAMMERING)\r\n\r\n00:15:57.039 --\u003e 00:15:58.291\r\nThat's all, folks.\r\n\r\n00:15:58.458 --\u003e 00:16:00.126\r\nLet's mambo.\r\n\r\n00:16:31.741 --\u003e 00:16:33.618\r\nHelp us! Please!\r\n\r\n00:16:50.927 --\u003e 00:16:52.637\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:01.771 --\u003e 00:17:03.231\r\nLet me go.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.608 --\u003e 00:17:08.027\r\nAnything you say, Jannie-poo.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.455 --\u003e 00:17:22.166\r\n(IN IRISH ACCENT) And now\r\nfor the final confession.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.250 --\u003e 00:17:26.379\r\nThe big secret you've kept\r\nfrom us for so many years.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.462 --\u003e 00:17:29.882\r\nBrothers and sisters,\r\nat long last, I give you\r\n\r\n00:17:29.966 --\u003e 00:17:32.510\r\nthe man behind the bat.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.523 --\u003e 00:17:46.607\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:17:52.530 --\u003e 00:17:54.170\r\nMAN: What's going on?\r\nTWO-FACE: He's gone.\r\n\r\n00:17:54.532 --\u003e 00:17:57.368\r\nEveryone, spread out.\r\nDon't let him get away.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.910 --\u003e 00:17:59.745\r\nBATMAN: Who says I'm leaving?\r\n\r\n00:18:02.498 --\u003e 00:18:03.499\r\n(MUFFLED GASP)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.583 --\u003e 00:18:05.084\r\nWhat's going on?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.167 --\u003e 00:18:06.586\r\nGet the light.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.592 --\u003e 00:18:13.926\r\nNobody panic.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.635 --\u003e 00:18:16.596\r\n(MUFFLED PROTESTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:18.931 --\u003e 00:18:21.267\r\nOkay, start panicking.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.270 --\u003e 00:18:27.356\r\n(GROWLS) The only way\r\nout is through me.\r\n\r\n00:18:34.864 --\u003e 00:18:36.824\r\nHold on. You'll hit Croc.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.907 --\u003e 00:18:38.367\r\nWhat's your point?\r\n\r\n00:18:39.952 --\u003e 00:18:41.495\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:41.579 --\u003e 00:18:42.580\r\n(PUNCH THUDS)\r\n\r\n00:18:54.008 --\u003e 00:18:55.009\r\n(MUFFLED GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.969 --\u003e 00:18:59.138\r\nKILLER CROC: Watch where\r\nyou're shooting, clown.\r\n\r\n00:19:05.436 --\u003e 00:19:07.355\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.568 --\u003e 00:19:13.569\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:19.158 --\u003e 00:19:20.159\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.104 --\u003e 00:19:49.480\r\nI'm hit, boys!\r\n\r\n00:19:51.524 --\u003e 00:19:53.150\r\n(GRUNTING AT EACH STEP)\r\n\r\n00:19:58.698 --\u003e 00:20:00.658\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:18.134 --\u003e 00:20:19.719\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:23.723 --\u003e 00:20:24.849\r\nGORDON: Hold it.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.726 --\u003e 00:20:27.768\r\nNobody move.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.852 --\u003e 00:20:29.019\r\n(GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:33.232 --\u003e 00:20:36.068\r\nYoo-hoo! Look alive, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:20:37.945 --\u003e 00:20:39.947\r\nHere comes the judge.\r\n\r\n00:20:40.114 --\u003e 00:20:41.115\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:47.997 --\u003e 00:20:51.167\r\nOld Hanging Judge\r\nJoker, that's me.\r\n\r\n00:20:53.043 --\u003e 00:20:57.006\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:21:25.868 --\u003e 00:21:28.454\r\nI see now there's a need\r\nfor the things you do.\r\n\r\n00:21:29.955 --\u003e 00:21:33.459\r\nBut I'm still going to work toward\r\na city that doesn't need Batman.\r\n\r\n00:21:33.918 --\u003e 00:21:35.044\r\nMe too.\r\n\r\n00:21:48.599 --\u003e 00:21:50.601\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:22:15.042 --\u003e 00:22:16.085\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S02 E10 - Harlequinade (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:12.095 --\u003e 00:00:14.598\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.165 --\u003e 00:01:23.709\r\nHere it is, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:01:24.001 --\u003e 00:01:27.588\r\nEnough kaboom to turn Gotham\r\ninto the world's biggest pothole.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.879 --\u003e 00:01:30.757\r\nWhat say we start the\r\nbidding at one million?\r\n\r\n00:01:31.800 --\u003e 00:01:33.677\r\n- One million.\r\n- Two million.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.927 --\u003e 00:01:35.637\r\n- Three million.\r\n- Five.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.347 --\u003e 00:01:41.852\r\nGentlemen, please.\r\nDon't insult me with nickel-and-dime bids.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.644 --\u003e 00:01:46.106\r\nThe man who walks out with this bomb\r\nwalks out with Gotham in his pocket.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.523 --\u003e 00:01:48.900\r\nYours to pick clean\r\nor blow sky-high.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.151 --\u003e 00:01:51.486\r\nYour call. What am I bid?\r\n\r\n00:01:51.903 --\u003e 00:01:54.197\r\nJOKER: How about nothing?\r\n\r\n00:01:54.990 --\u003e 00:01:58.160\r\nZero, zip, zilch, nada.\r\n\r\n00:01:59.995 --\u003e 00:02:02.164\r\nMy personal check for bupkis.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.247 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nDrawn on the First\r\nNational Bank of Squadoo.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.917 --\u003e 00:02:07.210\r\n(JOKER LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.294 --\u003e 00:02:09.296\r\n(GUNS COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:02:11.256 --\u003e 00:02:12.716\r\nSorry, boys,\r\n\r\n00:02:12.883 --\u003e 00:02:14.509\r\nthis lot is sold.\r\n\r\n00:02:16.720 --\u003e 00:02:19.598\r\n(ALL SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:23.101 --\u003e 00:02:24.144\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:27.397\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:28.774 --\u003e 00:02:30.150\r\nWhoops.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.484 --\u003e 00:02:32.277\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:02:35.364 --\u003e 00:02:37.574\r\nYou really should loosen\r\nup, dear.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.741 --\u003e 00:02:39.576\r\nHave a laugh now and then.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.704 --\u003e 00:02:44.956\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:48.502 --\u003e 00:02:51.004\r\nThat's so much more pleasant.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.588 --\u003e 00:02:54.716\r\nMAYOR: \u003ci\u003eAlerting the public now would\r\nonly cause a panic, Commissioner.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:54.800 --\u003e 00:02:58.595\r\nBut if that madman plans to use the\r\nbomb, we've got to clear the city.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.679 --\u003e 00:03:01.890\r\nMAYOR: \u003ci\u003eIcan't evacuate 10 million\r\npeople on your suspicions.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:02.474 --\u003e 00:03:04.601\r\nWe don't even know if the\r\nbomb's still in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.060 --\u003e 00:03:06.812\r\nKeep me posted if\r\nyou find anything.\r\n\r\n00:03:08.230 --\u003e 00:03:10.357\r\nThe Joker will be extra\r\ncautious this time.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.607 --\u003e 00:03:11.775\r\nWe'll have to think like him.\r\n\r\n00:03:11.983 --\u003e 00:03:14.111\r\nOr recruit someone who does.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.866 --\u003e 00:03:21.827\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:24.705 --\u003e 00:03:26.415\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:03:26.707 --\u003e 00:03:27.833\r\nMs. Quinn.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.125 --\u003e 00:03:29.167\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:30.877 --\u003e 00:03:31.878\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:33.380\r\n(GAGGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:35.841 --\u003e 00:03:39.052\r\nDon't you knock before\r\nentering a lady's boudoir?\r\n\r\n00:03:39.678 --\u003e 00:03:42.639\r\n- I need help.\r\n- Well, you've come to the right place.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.973 --\u003e 00:03:44.391\r\nI recommend a lobotomy.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.559 --\u003e 00:03:47.144\r\nThe Joker's stolen a bomb.\r\n\r\n00:03:47.436 --\u003e 00:03:49.271\r\nIf I can't get to him in time\r\n\r\n00:03:49.438 --\u003e 00:03:52.482\r\nthis city and everyone in it is\r\ngoing up in a mushroom cloud.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.693 --\u003e 00:03:57.195\r\nSo you want me to turn\r\nsquealer on Mr. J. Ha!\r\n\r\n00:03:58.238 --\u003e 00:04:00.532\r\nSorry, B-man, no deal.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.158 --\u003e 00:04:03.285\r\nI've talked to Gordon\r\nand Dr. Bartholomew.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.827 --\u003e 00:04:06.788\r\nYou help me find the Joker,\r\nand they'll write your ticket out of here.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.955 --\u003e 00:04:08.123\r\nWhee!\r\n\r\n00:04:08.206 --\u003e 00:04:10.625\r\nIf you promise no double-cross.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.043 --\u003e 00:04:14.629\r\nAh, shoot,\r\ntake all the fun out of life.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.213 --\u003e 00:04:16.840\r\nI don't have time for jokes.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.841 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nOkay, okay, I promise.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.010 --\u003e 00:04:21.011\r\nShake?\r\n\r\n00:04:25.849 --\u003e 00:04:27.309\r\nOh, the irony of it.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.392 --\u003e 00:04:31.688\r\nThe grim, stalwart Dark Knight\r\nand his greatest female adversary\r\n\r\n00:04:31.772 --\u003e 00:04:33.899\r\nfighting together\r\nto save the city.\r\n\r\n00:04:40.864 --\u003e 00:04:42.449\r\nI sense a lack of trust.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.742 --\u003e 00:04:46.912\r\n\u003ci\u003eSure you don't need any help\r\nkeeping Zippy under control?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:47.162 --\u003e 00:04:48.246\r\nI'm fine.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.538 --\u003e 00:04:51.583\r\nBesides, I need you to be ready\r\nif Gordon's men get any leads.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.833 --\u003e 00:04:53.877\r\n- I'll signal if there's trouble.\r\n- You got \u003ci\u003eit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:54.419 --\u003e 00:04:56.755\r\n- HARLEY: I wanna listen to the radio.\r\n- Don't!\r\n\r\n00:05:00.801 --\u003e 00:05:02.469\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.227 --\u003e 00:05:11.269\r\nOops.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.520 --\u003e 00:05:13.355\r\nListen, and listen good.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.855 --\u003e 00:05:16.775\r\nYou don't touch\r\nanything, say anything\r\n\r\n00:05:16.858 --\u003e 00:05:18.902\r\nor do anything\r\nunless I tell you!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.152 --\u003e 00:05:21.279\r\n- Got it?\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.574 --\u003e 00:05:27.327\r\nSo far, Joker hasn't been seen\r\nat any of his old hideouts.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.786 --\u003e 00:05:30.664\r\nI want you to show me the last\r\nplace he used when he escaped.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.415 --\u003e 00:05:33.583\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.256 --\u003e 00:05:42.300\r\nThis used to be our\r\nspecial love nest.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.887 --\u003e 00:05:49.099\r\nHave a look around while I slip\r\ninto something more comfortable.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.724 --\u003e 00:05:50.809\r\nNo tricks.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.268 --\u003e 00:05:53.228\r\nHey, we have a deal, remember?\r\n\r\n00:06:11.621 --\u003e 00:06:14.416\r\n- (HYENAS GROWLING)\r\n- (YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.341 --\u003e 00:06:25.218\r\n(HYENAS SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.052 --\u003e 00:06:27.220\r\nWhee!\r\n\r\n00:06:28.263 --\u003e 00:06:31.683\r\nAh! I feel like a\r\nhuman being again.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.351 --\u003e 00:06:36.146\r\nHi, babies! Mommy's home!\r\n\r\n00:06:39.691 --\u003e 00:06:42.193\r\nAre you the sweetest babies?\r\n\r\n00:06:42.277 --\u003e 00:06:45.071\r\nYes, you are. Yes, you are.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.324 --\u003e 00:06:49.576\r\nHow do you like our ha-hacienda?\r\n\r\n00:06:49.993 --\u003e 00:06:51.119\r\nCharming.\r\n\r\n00:06:51.703 --\u003e 00:06:53.330\r\nEspecially these monitors.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.622 --\u003e 00:06:55.916\r\nBetween the cops,\r\ncity hall and the mayor's office,\r\n\r\n00:06:55.999 --\u003e 00:06:57.584\r\nJoker has the whole city wired.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.084 --\u003e 00:06:59.252\r\nHe's a genius.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.711 --\u003e 00:07:01.129\r\nWhat's the attraction, Quinn?\r\n\r\n00:07:01.880 --\u003e 00:07:03.798\r\nThis sick infatuation\r\nwith the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.007 --\u003e 00:07:06.051\r\nLook, Bats, when I was a doctor\r\n\r\n00:07:06.134 --\u003e 00:07:08.887\r\nI was always listening to\r\nother people's problems.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.763 --\u003e 00:07:15.143\r\nThen I met Mr. J., who listened to me\r\nfor a change and made everything fun.\r\n\r\n00:07:17.604 --\u003e 00:07:19.314\r\nYou think it's funny\r\nwhen he hurts people?\r\n\r\n00:07:19.981 --\u003e 00:07:21.191\r\nIt's just a joke.\r\n\r\n00:07:21.441 --\u003e 00:07:23.443\r\nHope you're still laughing\r\nwhen it's your turn.\r\n\r\n00:07:24.027 --\u003e 00:07:25.111\r\nHmph.\r\n\r\n00:07:27.447 --\u003e 00:07:29.532\r\nBATMAN: Meet us at the\r\nApex novelty factory.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.741 --\u003e 00:07:33.078\r\nQuinn says it's an old hideout.\r\nBut the Joker may be using it again.\r\n\r\n00:07:33.244 --\u003e 00:07:34.371\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm on my way.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:45.090 --\u003e 00:07:48.218\r\n- Grab on.\r\n- I can do it myself, thank you.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.803 --\u003e 00:07:51.596\r\nHa-ha! Ow!\r\n\r\n00:07:53.390 --\u003e 00:07:54.683\r\n(LAUGHS FLIRTINGLY)\r\n\r\n00:07:56.559 --\u003e 00:07:58.269\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.655 --\u003e 00:08:10.156\r\nSneak, sneak, sneak.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.657 --\u003e 00:08:11.950\r\n- Shh.\r\n- Shh.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.158 --\u003e 00:08:15.704\r\nWhat do you mean, \"Shh\"?\r\nNo one's been in this dump for years.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.748 --\u003e 00:08:20.583\r\n(JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:08:31.469 --\u003e 00:08:33.722\r\n(PANICKED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:08:37.225 --\u003e 00:08:38.351\r\nHARLEY: Uh-oh.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.062 --\u003e 00:08:42.230\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:44.566 --\u003e 00:08:46.860\r\nHey, guys, look who I got.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.277 --\u003e 00:08:48.403\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:49.154 --\u003e 00:08:50.447\r\nBOXY: Well, well.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.947 --\u003e 00:08:52.133\r\nIf it ain't the big, bad Batman\r\n\r\n00:08:52.157 --\u003e 00:08:54.242\r\ncome to break up Boxy\r\nBennett's little social club.\r\n\r\n00:08:55.368 --\u003e 00:08:57.704\r\nIt's gonna cost you,\r\nfreak, big time.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.038 --\u003e 00:09:00.832\r\nHi, Boxy. Long time no see.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.083 --\u003e 00:09:03.293\r\nHarley Quinn.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.668 --\u003e 00:09:06.548\r\nLast I heard, they tossed you in the\r\nsquirrel farm and swallowed the key.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.505 --\u003e 00:09:08.625\r\nWhat you doing with the Bat?\r\n\r\n00:09:09.632 --\u003e 00:09:10.925\r\n(GULPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:11.009 --\u003e 00:09:14.637\r\nCome on, you don't think\r\nI was working with Batman?\r\n\r\n00:09:14.888 --\u003e 00:09:18.683\r\nI know you'd blow us both\r\naway if you thought that.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.392 --\u003e 00:09:20.518\r\nYou thought right, sugar.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.813 --\u003e 00:09:24.856\r\nPhew.\r\n\r\n00:09:25.190 --\u003e 00:09:27.400\r\nSo, you ain't seen Mr. J.\r\nAround, have you?\r\n\r\n00:09:27.484 --\u003e 00:09:28.526\r\nNope.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.610 --\u003e 00:09:30.921\r\nYou know, I never could figure what\r\na cute little number like yourself\r\n\r\n00:09:30.945 --\u003e 00:09:32.614\r\nsaw in a slob like the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.156 --\u003e 00:09:36.034\r\nEspecially when there are\r\nsuave guys like me around.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.826 --\u003e 00:09:37.994\r\nNow, Boxy.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.578 --\u003e 00:09:41.164\r\nSure, my pudding's a\r\nlittle temperamental.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.249 --\u003e 00:09:46.753\r\nBut, gee, what relationship\r\ndoesn't have its ups and downs?\r\n\r\n00:09:49.339 --\u003e 00:09:50.715\r\n(ALL GASP \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e CONFUSION)\r\n\r\n00:09:52.383 --\u003e 00:09:53.426\r\nHa!\r\n\r\n00:09:55.220 --\u003e 00:09:56.262\r\nA flat.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.805 --\u003e 00:09:58.473\r\n(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:10:00.600 --\u003e 00:10:05.188\r\n(SINGING) \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e never knew\r\nThat our romance had \u003ci\u003eended.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:05.814 --\u003e 00:10:09.150\r\n\u003ci\u003eUntil you poisoned my food.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:10.151 --\u003e 00:10:12.612\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I thought it was a lark.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:13.071 --\u003e 00:10:15.782\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhen you kicked me in the park.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:16.616 --\u003e 00:10:20.161\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut now I think it was rude.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:22.205 --\u003e 00:10:26.501\r\n\u003ci\u003eI never knew that you\r\nand I were finished.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:27.335 --\u003e 00:10:30.213\r\n\u003ci\u003eUntil that bottle hit my head.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:31.798 --\u003e 00:10:34.425\r\n\u003ci\u003eThough I tried to be aloof.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:34.676 --\u003e 00:10:36.970\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhen you pushed me off the roof.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:38.263 --\u003e 00:10:41.349\r\n\u003ci\u003eI feel our romance is dead.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:43.309 --\u003e 00:10:47.814\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt wouldn't have been so\r\nbad If you had told me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:48.314 --\u003e 00:10:52.152\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat someone had taken my place.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:53.736 --\u003e 00:10:58.408\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut no No,\r\nyou didn't even scold me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:58.825 --\u003e 00:11:03.580\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou just tried to\r\ndisfigure my face.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:05.331 --\u003e 00:11:10.253\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou'll never know How this\r\nheart of mine is breaking.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:10.670 --\u003e 00:11:14.007\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt looks so hopeless, but then.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:15.341 --\u003e 00:11:18.261\r\n\u003ci\u003eLife used to be so placid.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:18.344 --\u003e 00:11:21.389\r\n\u003ci\u003eWon't you please\r\nput down that acid?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:21.472 --\u003e 00:11:27.562\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd say that we're\r\nsweethearts again\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:29.355 --\u003e 00:11:31.858\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.567 --\u003e 00:11:34.819\r\nMAN 1; Yeah.\r\nMAN 2; All right, baby!\r\n\r\n00:11:40.033 --\u003e 00:11:42.619\r\nWhoo! All right, B and R!\r\n\r\n00:11:50.460 --\u003e 00:11:51.794\r\nROBIN: Hey, UQW-\r\n\r\n00:11:54.297 --\u003e 00:11:55.465\r\nThey're all working together.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.013 --\u003e 00:12:03.014\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:08.853 --\u003e 00:12:10.063\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:12:10.146 --\u003e 00:12:11.814\r\nLet's go, Quinn!\r\n\r\n00:12:12.148 --\u003e 00:12:13.316\r\nQuinn!\r\n\r\n00:12:13.399 --\u003e 00:12:14.692\r\nHARLEY: Whee!\r\n\r\n00:12:14.776 --\u003e 00:12:16.486\r\nBombs away!\r\n\r\n00:12:17.278 --\u003e 00:12:18.655\r\n- Huh?\r\n- (ALL YELP)\r\n\r\n00:12:20.448 --\u003e 00:12:21.532\r\nYes!\r\n\r\n00:12:21.991 --\u003e 00:12:23.159\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:26.412 --\u003e 00:12:28.331\r\nDid you see the way I\r\nhandled those creeps?\r\n\r\n00:12:28.456 --\u003e 00:12:29.707\r\nPow! Barn!\r\n\r\n00:12:29.791 --\u003e 00:12:32.085\r\nOh, Batgirl, eat your heart out.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.835 --\u003e 00:12:35.505\r\nWhat was she before\r\nshe went bonkers?\r\n\r\n00:12:35.880 --\u003e 00:12:37.382\r\nA clinical psychiatrist.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.384 --\u003e 00:12:40.593\r\nFigures.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.808 --\u003e 00:12:48.518\r\n- Any word on the Joker?\r\n- Nothing.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.060 --\u003e 00:12:51.980\r\nI even checked with Gordon again,\r\nand the mayor still refuses\r\n\r\n00:12:52.063 --\u003e 00:12:53.773\r\nto let the cops\r\nevacuate the city.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.982 --\u003e 00:12:55.942\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.902 --\u003e 00:12:59.070\r\nOh, it's brilliant.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.446 --\u003e 00:13:02.407\r\nWay t0 go, Mr. J_!\r\n\r\n00:13:02.782 --\u003e 00:13:03.866\r\nWhat are you saying?\r\n\r\n00:13:04.284 --\u003e 00:13:06.202\r\nOh, come on, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.869 --\u003e 00:13:09.872\r\nYou've seen how my pudding\r\nkeeps an eye on Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.206 --\u003e 00:13:12.083\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat better way\r\nto tie up the cops\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:12.166 --\u003e 00:13:14.085\r\n\u003ci\u003ethan to tie up the mayor?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:19.716 --\u003e 00:13:20.925\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:13:27.223 --\u003e 00:13:29.976\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:13:36.733 --\u003e 00:13:39.902\r\nSee, do I know how Mr. J.\r\nThinks, or what? Ha!\r\n\r\n00:13:40.945 --\u003e 00:13:44.657\r\nAnd here you thought I was just\r\nanother bubble-headed blond bimbo.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.741 --\u003e 00:13:48.036\r\nWell, the joke's on you.\r\nI'm not even a real blond.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.830 --\u003e 00:13:52.123\r\nGood job.\r\n\r\n00:13:53.416 --\u003e 00:13:54.959\r\nHuh? Hey!\r\n\r\n00:13:58.588 --\u003e 00:14:01.841\r\n- What gives?\r\n- I can't risk you warning the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.800 --\u003e 00:14:05.011\r\nWould I do a thing like that?\r\n\r\n00:14:05.845 --\u003e 00:14:07.847\r\nHey, let me out! Come on!\r\n\r\n00:14:10.516 --\u003e 00:14:13.227\r\nBoy, you just can't\r\ntrust some people.\r\n\r\n00:14:21.569 --\u003e 00:14:25.698\r\nNothing like a moonlight dip,\r\neh, Mr. Mayor? (LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:26.032 --\u003e 00:14:29.077\r\nPlease, just make your ransom\r\ndemands and get on with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.079 --\u003e 00:14:33.790\r\nOh, no ransom this time, Hammy.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.082 --\u003e 00:14:37.001\r\n- You can't mean- -\r\nOh, yes, indeedy-do.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.126 --\u003e 00:14:41.798\r\nInstead of taking you,\r\nthe cops and the Batman down separately,\r\n\r\n00:14:41.881 --\u003e 00:14:44.217\r\nI'm going to blast\r\nyou all at once.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.843 --\u003e 00:14:47.929\r\nSend down the plane, boys.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.179 --\u003e 00:14:49.972\r\nWe're blowing town.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.223 --\u003e 00:14:51.307\r\nLiterally.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.724 --\u003e 00:14:52.975\r\n\u003ci\u003eYes, sir.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:53.768 --\u003e 00:14:55.728\r\nBut all those innocent people.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.020 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nSome joke on them, eh?\r\nThink of it as the ultimate punch line.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.692 --\u003e 00:15:03.903\r\n(JOKER LAUGHING MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:11.369 --\u003e 00:15:12.370\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:25.049 --\u003e 00:15:26.801\r\nHa!\r\n\r\n00:15:28.428 --\u003e 00:15:29.554\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:15:30.096 --\u003e 00:15:31.389\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:39.814 --\u003e 00:15:41.315\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.901 --\u003e 00:15:45.278\r\nWhat? Hey!\r\n\r\n00:15:49.574 --\u003e 00:15:53.286\r\nGee, it's amazing what you find\r\nin people's glove compartments.\r\n\r\n00:15:54.370 --\u003e 00:15:55.496\r\nHarley?\r\n\r\n00:15:55.746 --\u003e 00:15:58.332\r\nHi, pudding. Miss me?\r\n\r\n00:16:00.418 --\u003e 00:16:03.045\r\nYou clever little minx.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.421 --\u003e 00:16:05.298\r\nHow did you escape from Arkham?\r\n\r\n00:16:05.673 --\u003e 00:16:08.092\r\nBatman sprung me so\r\nI could find you.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.718 --\u003e 00:16:11.846\r\nHad me all locked up in\r\nhis bad old car, too.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.388 --\u003e 00:16:13.473\r\nAww.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.432 --\u003e 00:16:16.309\r\nQuinn, we had a deal!\r\n\r\n00:16:16.559 --\u003e 00:16:20.855\r\nDeal's off, B-man. No one ever\r\nsaid anything about hurting Mr. J.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.189 --\u003e 00:16:23.566\r\n(VEHICLE APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.912 --\u003e 00:16:37.038\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:16:40.791 --\u003e 00:16:43.419\r\n\u003ci\u003eAUTOMATED VOICE: 10-minute\r\ncountdown sequence has been engaged.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:43.503 --\u003e 00:16:44.754\r\nOh, my Lord.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.379 --\u003e 00:16:46.589\r\nCome, my dear.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.672 --\u003e 00:16:50.760\r\nWe'll get to a safe altitude,\r\nthen watch the fireworks.\r\n\r\n00:16:50.843 --\u003e 00:16:52.762\r\nIt's lucky you were\r\nhere, Harley.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.970 --\u003e 00:16:55.640\r\nThe countdown sequence didn't\r\nleave Joker enough time\r\n\r\n00:16:55.723 --\u003e 00:16:57.683\r\nto swing by Arkham\r\nand pick you up.\r\n\r\n00:16:58.184 --\u003e 00:16:59.477\r\nQuiet, brat.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.727 --\u003e 00:17:02.438\r\nYou were gonna come back for\r\nme, weren't you, pudding?\r\n\r\n00:17:02.647 --\u003e 00:17:04.941\r\nOf course, pumpkin pie.\r\n\r\n00:17:05.024 --\u003e 00:17:07.860\r\nIt's just that...\r\nWell, here you are,\r\n\r\n00:17:07.944 --\u003e 00:17:10.530\r\nso I can save myself a trip.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.988 --\u003e 00:17:12.448\r\nBut what about all our friends?\r\n\r\n00:17:12.532 --\u003e 00:17:17.537\r\nIvy and Two-Face and hat guy and\r\nlizard man and puppet head and-\r\n\r\n00:17:17.995 --\u003e 00:17:19.121\r\nWhat about them?\r\n\r\n00:17:19.413 --\u003e 00:17:20.957\r\nDon't forget your little pets.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.999 --\u003e 00:17:25.461\r\n(GASPS) The babies!\r\nWe can't leave the babies!\r\n\r\n00:17:25.836 --\u003e 00:17:27.797\r\nI'll buy you a goldfish!\r\n\r\n00:17:27.880 --\u003e 00:17:30.174\r\n'Let's go! “No!\r\n\r\n00:17:30.424 --\u003e 00:17:31.717\r\nWhy, you little-\r\n\r\n00:17:35.638 --\u003e 00:17:36.847\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:56.867 --\u003e 00:17:58.869\r\nYou know, Bats,\r\nI got a crazy idea.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.953 --\u003e 00:18:02.123\r\nMr. J. May not be the\r\nguy for me after all.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.206 --\u003e 00:18:03.666\r\n(HARLEY SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:18:16.679 --\u003e 00:18:17.805\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:37.325 --\u003e 00:18:38.367\r\nHa!\r\n\r\n00:18:43.122 --\u003e 00:18:46.167\r\n- Go around again!\r\n- But, boss...\r\n\r\n00:18:49.086 --\u003e 00:18:51.797\r\n- I said do it!\r\n- Yes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.056 --\u003e 00:19:01.390\r\n(TIMER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:02.266 --\u003e 00:19:03.392\r\n(BEEPING STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.476 --\u003e 00:19:05.476\r\n- Made it with time to spare.\r\n- (PLANE APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:15.613 --\u003e 00:19:16.989\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:19:34.882 --\u003e 00:19:38.094\r\nThat bomb's going off\r\neven if I go with it!\r\n\r\n00:19:38.177 --\u003e 00:19:40.429\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:19:48.062 --\u003e 00:19:50.564\r\nLaugh this off, pudding!\r\n\r\n00:20:10.334 --\u003e 00:20:11.377\r\nBOTH: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:20:13.087 --\u003e 00:20:14.130\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:38.946 --\u003e 00:20:40.322\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:20:49.582 --\u003e 00:20:52.960\r\n- Freeze, clown.\r\n- Quinn, stop!\r\n\r\n00:20:53.544 --\u003e 00:20:55.087\r\nHe's mine, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:20:59.633 --\u003e 00:21:01.552\r\nYou wouldn't dare.\r\n\r\n00:21:03.471 --\u003e 00:21:05.181\r\nYou don't have the guts.\r\n\r\n00:21:07.183 --\u003e 00:21:09.477\r\nNot in a million\r\nyears would you-\r\n\r\n00:21:10.770 --\u003e 00:21:11.812\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:21:16.233 --\u003e 00:21:17.485\r\n(BOTH SIGH IN RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:21:28.204 --\u003e 00:21:29.413\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:21:29.538 --\u003e 00:21:32.374\r\nBaby, you're the greatest.\r\n\r\n00:21:51.101 --\u003e 00:21:53.354\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E01 - Bane (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.089 --\u003e 00:00:08.133\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:50.861 --\u003e 00:01:52.029\r\n(WHISTLES)\r\n\r\n00:01:52.112 --\u003e 00:01:53.405\r\n(SNAPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:57.367 --\u003e 00:01:58.744\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:00.287 --\u003e 00:02:02.956\r\nYou really can't get\r\ngood help these days.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.042 --\u003e 00:02:06.501\r\n(CAR CREAKS)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.669 --\u003e 00:02:09.921\r\n(GRUNTS) Phew!\r\n\r\n00:02:13.050 --\u003e 00:02:14.718\r\n(CAR DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:02:16.678 --\u003e 00:02:20.182\r\nI understand your help is\r\nthe very best money can buy.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.265 --\u003e 00:02:22.851\r\nYou see,\r\nI'm the one who had you hired.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.852 --\u003e 00:02:25.812\r\nThen I owe you\r\nsomething special.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:29.358\r\nThis particular assignment is\r\none from which I will derive\r\n\r\n00:02:29.524 --\u003e 00:02:33.779\r\n- exquisite pleasure, Miss...\r\n- Call me Candice.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.404 --\u003e 00:02:37.532\r\nCall me Bane.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.741 --\u003e 00:02:38.992\r\n(KISSES)\r\n\r\n00:02:39.368 --\u003e 00:02:40.410\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:43.664 --\u003e 00:02:45.332\r\nCome on, boss. Hit it again.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.291 --\u003e 00:02:47.417\r\nAgain.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.751 --\u003e 00:02:49.086\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.379 --\u003e 00:02:53.674\r\nCome on, boss. No wonder Batman's\r\nrunning rings around you.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.634 --\u003e 00:02:57.344\r\n(GRUNTS LOUDLY)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.391 --\u003e 00:03:04.643\r\nJust can't get good\r\nhelp these days.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.519 --\u003e 00:03:07.187\r\nSo I have heard.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.688 --\u003e 00:03:09.731\r\nCandice,\r\nwhen Jake here comes around,\r\n\r\n00:03:10.065 --\u003e 00:03:11.483\r\ntell him he's fired.\r\n\r\n00:03:12.067 --\u003e 00:03:13.707\r\nNow, let's do a little\r\nbusiness, Mr. Bane.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.277 --\u003e 00:03:18.990\r\nThey'll never pin it on me, but that\r\nlittle fiasco cost me an easy $10 mil.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.658 --\u003e 00:03:21.785\r\nYou almost didn't get paid.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.244 --\u003e 00:03:25.122\r\nYou're lucky these diamonds didn't\r\nget nabbed in the smuggling bust.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.001 --\u003e 00:03:31.378\r\nNo, Mr. Thorne,\r\n\r\n00:03:32.337 --\u003e 00:03:33.630\r\nyou're the lucky one.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.214 --\u003e 00:03:35.382\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.926 --\u003e 00:03:41.513\r\nI'm making my secretary\r\navailable to you.\r\n\r\n00:03:41.805 --\u003e 00:03:44.808\r\nShe can provide any background\r\nyou might need on your target.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.016 --\u003e 00:03:46.977\r\nMy needs have already been met.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.440 --\u003e 00:03:53.692\r\nI'm paying you to\r\ngo after Batman,\r\n\r\n00:03:54.151 --\u003e 00:03:55.318\r\nnot Killer Croc.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.485 --\u003e 00:03:58.196\r\nBut the Batman will surely\r\nbe on the reptile's trail.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.572 --\u003e 00:04:00.282\r\nI will observe the bat in action\r\n\r\n00:04:00.449 --\u003e 00:04:04.077\r\nand when I understand how he thinks\r\nand fights, I will break him.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.327 --\u003e 00:04:07.998\r\nNow, where do I find\r\nthis Killer Croc?\r\n\r\n00:04:32.522 --\u003e 00:04:33.523\r\n(SNARLS)\r\n\r\n00:04:37.944 --\u003e 00:04:40.238\r\n(GUARDS SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:04:40.572 --\u003e 00:04:42.783\r\nLoad the truck.\r\nWe'll get the safe.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.014 --\u003e 00:05:07.015\r\n(GLASS BREAKS)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.560 --\u003e 00:05:11.603\r\nKILLER CROC: Batman.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.188 --\u003e 00:05:14.189\r\n(THUGS GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:05:17.275 --\u003e 00:05:18.475\r\nKILLER CROC: No time for this.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.028 --\u003e 00:05:21.029\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:05:33.416 --\u003e 00:05:34.876\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:05:48.932 --\u003e 00:05:50.600\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:06:12.664 --\u003e 00:06:15.709\r\nCome on in, Batman.\r\nThe water's fine.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.504 --\u003e 00:06:21.381\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.925 --\u003e 00:06:26.303\r\nHe is mine to destroy, monster.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.469 --\u003e 00:06:28.263\r\nOver my dead body.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.847 --\u003e 00:06:30.640\r\nAs you wish.\r\n\r\n00:06:32.809 --\u003e 00:06:34.352\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:06:42.152 --\u003e 00:06:43.153\r\n(SPUTTERING)\r\n\r\n00:06:43.987 --\u003e 00:06:45.906\r\n(KILLER CROC GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:48.742 --\u003e 00:06:49.826\r\nThat's Croc.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.118 --\u003e 00:06:51.161\r\n(KILLER CROC SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:06:52.913 --\u003e 00:06:53.914\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:59.252 --\u003e 00:07:00.879\r\nSomebody's helping us out.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.338 --\u003e 00:07:02.797\r\nSomebody tough.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.218 --\u003e 00:07:08.595\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.016 --\u003e 00:07:14.726\r\nHe could be a\r\ncrime-fighter, you know?\r\n\r\n00:07:15.018 --\u003e 00:07:17.854\r\nSomebody trying to be like us,\r\ntrying to help us clean up Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.021 --\u003e 00:07:20.899\r\nWhat do you think, Batman?\r\nDo you...\r\n\r\n00:07:21.232 --\u003e 00:07:22.317\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:07:24.319 --\u003e 00:07:26.488\r\nI think you're right about one\r\nthing, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.988 --\u003e 00:07:28.531\r\nWhoever did this was tough.\r\n\r\n00:07:28.698 --\u003e 00:07:31.201\r\nThis was done with bare hands.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.719 --\u003e 00:07:50.720\r\n(DOOR BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:07:50.804 --\u003e 00:07:52.097\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:07:52.681 --\u003e 00:07:55.475\r\nI didn't think you'd\r\nmind some company.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.142 --\u003e 00:07:57.894\r\nVisiting hours are over.\r\n\r\n00:07:59.646 --\u003e 00:08:00.689\r\nHmm...\r\n\r\n00:08:00.772 --\u003e 00:08:03.108\r\nHow do these\r\ntraction things work?\r\n\r\n00:08:03.566 --\u003e 00:08:06.778\r\nWhen my bones heal,\r\nI'll show you firsthand.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.821 --\u003e 00:08:09.322\r\nOkay, Okay-\r\n\r\n00:08:10.115 --\u003e 00:08:11.366\r\nWhat do you want?\r\n\r\n00:08:11.533 --\u003e 00:08:12.784\r\nWho did this, Croc?\r\n\r\n00:08:12.993 --\u003e 00:08:14.953\r\nWhy should I tell you?\r\n\r\n00:08:15.870 --\u003e 00:08:19.165\r\nIf you wanna suffer in\r\nsilence, that's fine by me.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.919 --\u003e 00:08:24.004\r\nAhhh!\r\n\r\n00:08:24.087 --\u003e 00:08:25.463\r\nOkay, Okay-\r\n\r\n00:08:26.214 --\u003e 00:08:27.424\r\nHe was huge.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.507 --\u003e 00:08:29.342\r\nHe had these tubes in his head.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.759 --\u003e 00:08:33.096\r\nPumped him up twice as big\r\nright in front of my eyes.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.889 --\u003e 00:08:38.351\r\nAnd he had an accent.\r\nSouth American or something.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.685 --\u003e 00:08:40.645\r\nSee? That wasn't so hard.\r\n\r\n00:08:41.104 --\u003e 00:08:43.356\r\nYou'll know hard, Bats,\r\n\r\n00:08:43.523 --\u003e 00:08:47.902\r\nonce he sucks that juice into\r\nhis brain and snaps you in two.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.278 --\u003e 00:08:49.696\r\nDon't bet on it, Killer.\r\n\r\n00:08:50.196 --\u003e 00:08:51.239\r\nLater, gator.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.450 --\u003e 00:08:55.660\r\n(DOOR BUZZES AND SLAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:55.827 --\u003e 00:08:59.539\r\n(BATS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:03.918 --\u003e 00:09:06.212\r\nYou seem to have a\r\nding in your door, sir.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.629 --\u003e 00:09:08.298\r\nHe trashed my car, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.757 --\u003e 00:09:11.593\r\nBetween a couple of guys,\r\nthat's real personal.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.843 --\u003e 00:09:15.430\r\nNice to see you haven't lost your sense\r\nof humor in the face of adversity.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.722 --\u003e 00:09:19.559\r\nSomething Croc said reminded me of a\r\nCuban prison experiment I heard about.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.101 --\u003e 00:09:22.854\r\nPefia Duro Prison,\r\nfor lifers only.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.229 --\u003e 00:09:25.982\r\n- Then we're looking for an escapee?\r\n- That's right.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.357 --\u003e 00:09:29.152\r\nAnd there's only been\r\none escape in 25 years,\r\n\r\n00:09:29.486 --\u003e 00:09:30.612\r\nthree years ago.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.906 --\u003e 00:09:37.243\r\nComputer, run background\r\nfile on Project Gilgamesh.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.535 --\u003e 00:09:39.370\r\nGilgamesh.\r\nNamed after the warrior?\r\n\r\n00:09:39.746 --\u003e 00:09:41.039\r\nThe ultimate warrior.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.498 --\u003e 00:09:45.001\r\n\u003ci\u003eA chemical plan to create super\r\nsoldiers out of hardened prisoners.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:45.168 --\u003e 00:09:47.921\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt was abandoned when they got\r\nmore than they bargained for.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:48.129 --\u003e 00:09:51.424\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"ALFRED: And what was that, sir?\r\nBATMAN\". They got Bane.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:00.642 --\u003e 00:10:01.684\r\nAfter he escaped,\r\n\r\n00:10:01.768 --\u003e 00:10:04.479\r\nBane went into business for\r\nhimself as a freelance assassin.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.771 --\u003e 00:10:08.066\r\nPrice per job, $5 million.\r\n\r\n00:10:08.149 --\u003e 00:10:09.400\r\nSo, the question is,\r\n\r\n00:10:09.567 --\u003e 00:10:11.069\r\nwho wants to eliminate me?\r\n\r\n00:10:11.528 --\u003e 00:10:13.863\r\nThat line is forming\r\naround the block, sir.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.322 --\u003e 00:10:15.907\r\nLet me put it this way.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.074 --\u003e 00:10:18.076\r\nWho has $5 million to spend?\r\n\r\n00:10:26.042 --\u003e 00:10:28.920\r\nBANE: I have anticipated\r\nhis every move.\r\n\r\n00:10:29.212 --\u003e 00:10:33.174\r\nVery soon now, I will allow you\r\nthe pleasure of drawing the mask\r\n\r\n00:10:33.258 --\u003e 00:10:36.094\r\nfrom Batman's decimated face.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.678 --\u003e 00:10:39.556\r\nWith Batman out of the\r\nway, Gotham could be yours.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.722 --\u003e 00:10:41.057\r\nSo could I.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.141 --\u003e 00:10:43.226\r\nAnd what about your employer?\r\n\r\n00:10:43.685 --\u003e 00:10:45.854\r\nWell, accidents do happen.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.229 --\u003e 00:10:47.939\r\nSee you tonight.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.443 --\u003e 00:10:54.028\r\nYou're here late, Candice.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.779 --\u003e 00:10:56.281\r\nJust leaving, Rupe.\r\n\r\n00:11:05.999 --\u003e 00:11:08.251\r\nHe's out there somewhere, Bane.\r\n\r\n00:11:08.751 --\u003e 00:11:12.088\r\nYes.\r\nProbably closer than we think.\r\n\r\n00:11:14.507 --\u003e 00:11:16.092\r\n(SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.912 --\u003e 00:11:44.913\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:50.627 --\u003e 00:11:51.836\r\nIt is over\r\n\r\n00:11:52.462 --\u003e 00:11:53.671\r\nbefore it begins.\r\n\r\n00:11:53.963 --\u003e 00:11:55.590\r\nI think not.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.798 --\u003e 00:11:56.799\r\n(BONES CRACK)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.883 --\u003e 00:11:57.884\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:23.534 --\u003e 00:12:24.702\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:27.121\r\n(STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:35.213 --\u003e 00:12:37.215\r\nBANE: You have courage\r\nfor one so small.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.590 --\u003e 00:12:39.592\r\nYou can yet be of use to me.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.118 --\u003e 00:13:06.202\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:06.286 --\u003e 00:13:08.997\r\nI'd like to speak to you\r\nabout your new boyfriend.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.748 --\u003e 00:13:13.710\r\n(VOICE SPEAKING\r\nINDISTINCTLY ON TV)\r\n\r\n00:13:13.793 --\u003e 00:13:15.211\r\nYou've been stood up.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.378 --\u003e 00:13:16.879\r\nHe knew you'd come.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.046 --\u003e 00:13:18.715\r\nHe was obsessed\r\nwith you in prison.\r\n\r\n00:13:19.257 --\u003e 00:13:20.883\r\nHe's read everything about you.\r\n\r\n00:13:21.509 --\u003e 00:13:24.053\r\nHe knows you better\r\nthan you know yourself.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.304 --\u003e 00:13:25.430\r\n(PHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.513 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\nBet it's for you.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.935\r\n\u003ci\u003eBANE: I've been watching\r\nyou, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:31.185 --\u003e 00:13:32.895\r\n\u003ci\u003eWere I a common sniper,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:32.979 --\u003e 00:13:34.772\r\n\u003ci\u003eyou'd\u003c/i\u003e have never\r\nreached the phone.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.148 --\u003e 00:13:36.607\r\nWhat do you want, Bane?\r\n\r\n00:13:36.899 --\u003e 00:13:39.861\r\n\u003ci\u003eSomething more\r\npersonal between foes.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:40.611 --\u003e 00:13:42.822\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat do you value most, Batman?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:43.239 --\u003e 00:13:44.615\r\n\u003ci\u003ePerhaps I should say\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:44.782 --\u003e 00:13:46.826\r\n\u003ci\u003ewhom do you value most?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:46.909 --\u003e 00:13:47.910\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:50.204 --\u003e 00:13:51.456\r\nRobin.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.206 --\u003e 00:13:53.374\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:30.453 --\u003e 00:14:32.038\r\nI want his mask, Bane.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.372 --\u003e 00:14:35.291\r\nPatience.\r\nSoon you will have them both.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.712 --\u003e 00:14:41.005\r\n(MOTOR WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.855 --\u003e 00:14:58.856\r\n(KISSES)\r\n\r\n00:14:58.940 --\u003e 00:15:00.650\r\nBeen nice hanging with you.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.485 --\u003e 00:15:03.486\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:20.211 --\u003e 00:15:22.338\r\nBANE: Welcome to my\r\narena, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:24.757 --\u003e 00:15:26.426\r\nPrepare to meet your master.\r\n\r\n00:15:27.635 --\u003e 00:15:29.220\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:15:38.229 --\u003e 00:15:40.064\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:44.527 --\u003e 00:15:45.528\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:45.611 --\u003e 00:15:47.864\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:56.581 --\u003e 00:15:57.623\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:59.500 --\u003e 00:16:00.877\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:13.848 --\u003e 00:16:15.308\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:16:25.860 --\u003e 00:16:27.320\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.409 --\u003e 00:16:35.995\r\nI will break you!\r\n\r\n00:16:42.043 --\u003e 00:16:45.755\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:09.237 --\u003e 00:17:10.238\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:17:15.117 --\u003e 00:17:16.744\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:18.371 --\u003e 00:17:20.122\r\nMy legs. Get the weights.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.086 --\u003e 00:17:26.295\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:30.341 --\u003e 00:17:31.926\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:48.693 --\u003e 00:17:51.320\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:55.324 --\u003e 00:17:56.325\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:01.956 --\u003e 00:18:05.251\r\nCome here, sweetie.\r\nI got something to discuss with you.\r\n\r\n00:18:12.091 --\u003e 00:18:13.884\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.685 --\u003e 00:18:24.562\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:26.439 --\u003e 00:18:28.566\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:36.115 --\u003e 00:18:40.953\r\nToys. You try to fight me\r\nwith pathetic little toys.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.374 --\u003e 00:18:47.418\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:48.878 --\u003e 00:18:50.296\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:50.755 --\u003e 00:18:51.756\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.677 --\u003e 00:18:58.554\r\nYou've got nothing.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.638 --\u003e 00:18:59.680\r\nBeg for mercy.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.181 --\u003e 00:19:01.766\r\nScream my name!\r\n\r\n00:19:02.475 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nNever.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.977 --\u003e 00:19:06.395\r\nYou are beaten.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.854 --\u003e 00:19:08.981\r\nNow I will break you.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.192 --\u003e 00:19:12.193\r\n(MACHINE WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.526 --\u003e 00:19:13.861\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:19:15.738 --\u003e 00:19:18.074\r\nNo! No! The venom!\r\n\r\n00:19:18.157 --\u003e 00:19:19.700\r\nCan't stop it!\r\n\r\n00:19:21.452 --\u003e 00:19:24.497\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:19:27.083 --\u003e 00:19:31.504\r\nNo! Help me!\r\n\r\n00:19:32.213 --\u003e 00:19:36.550\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:38.135 --\u003e 00:19:39.762\r\nYou can't do this to me!\r\n\r\n00:19:39.845 --\u003e 00:19:41.722\r\nI am invincible!\r\n\r\n00:19:42.098 --\u003e 00:19:44.225\r\nI am Bane!\r\n\r\n00:19:45.267 --\u003e 00:19:46.268\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:46.352 --\u003e 00:19:49.897\r\n(WHIRRING SLOWS AND STOPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:56.362 --\u003e 00:19:57.571\r\nBATMAN: Let her go.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.947 --\u003e 00:19:59.615\r\nI know where she's headed.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.247 --\u003e 00:20:08.708\r\nIs this the best you can throw at\r\nme, Rupert?\r\n\r\n00:20:16.841 --\u003e 00:20:19.677\r\nGo on, Candice, take his mask.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.969 --\u003e 00:20:21.887\r\nThought you might like to hear\r\nthis, Rupert.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.513 --\u003e 00:20:23.639\r\nIt's a new release.\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.560\r\nMaybe we'll call it,\r\n\"Better Luck Next Time.\"\r\n\r\n00:20:27.727 --\u003e 00:20:29.121\r\n\u003ci\u003eCANDICE: With Batman\r\nout of the way,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:29.145 --\u003e 00:20:30.438\r\n\u003ci\u003eGotham could be yours.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:31.147 --\u003e 00:20:32.273\r\n\u003ci\u003eSo could I.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:32.440 --\u003e 00:20:34.734\r\n\u003ci\u003eBANE: And what\r\nabout your employer?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:34.817 --\u003e 00:20:37.319\r\n\u003ci\u003eCANDICE: Well,\r\naccidents do happen.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:37.945 --\u003e 00:20:39.822\r\nTHORNE: Candice!\r\n\r\n00:20:46.996 --\u003e 00:20:48.998\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E02 - Second Chance (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.256 --\u003e 00:00:08.258\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:02:02.789 --\u003e 00:02:04.666\r\nROBIN: You think\r\nDr. Crest is right?\r\n\r\n00:02:04.958 --\u003e 00:02:07.628\r\nYou think this operation\r\nwill make Harvey okay again?\r\n\r\n00:02:07.794 --\u003e 00:02:09.046\r\nI don't know.\r\n\r\n00:02:10.547 --\u003e 00:02:12.549\r\nWe can only hope.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.344 --\u003e 00:02:17.429\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:25.020 --\u003e 00:02:26.730\r\nGive me that file.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.943 --\u003e 00:02:33.403\r\n- I'll get him.\r\n- Look out, Harvey!\r\n\r\n00:02:41.953 --\u003e 00:02:43.413\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:02:47.501 --\u003e 00:02:48.627\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:51.213 --\u003e 00:02:52.547\r\nHarvey.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.298 --\u003e 00:02:55.008\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.941 --\u003e 00:03:13.485\r\nDR.CREST: Your bad side is\r\nalmost completely submerged.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.652 --\u003e 00:03:16.196\r\nYou've done very well in\r\ntherapy, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.405 --\u003e 00:03:18.240\r\nYou're more in control now,\r\n\r\n00:03:18.407 --\u003e 00:03:22.244\r\nable to make decisions for\r\nyourself without relying on chance.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.452 --\u003e 00:03:24.871\r\nNow it's time for\r\nthe final step,\r\n\r\n00:03:25.288 --\u003e 00:03:28.291\r\nerasing the scars\r\nthat created Two-Face.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.458 --\u003e 00:03:31.128\r\nI believe that once\r\nyou are whole again,\r\n\r\n00:03:31.294 --\u003e 00:03:35.716\r\nyour mind will be strong enough\r\nto banish Two-Face permanently.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.882 --\u003e 00:03:39.511\r\n- Bruce Wayne picked up the tab for this?\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.678 --\u003e 00:03:41.972\r\nGood old Bruce.\r\nHe's never given up on me.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.806 --\u003e 00:03:44.850\r\nAlways been my best friend.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.475 --\u003e 00:03:49.479\r\nI remember when we used to close\r\nthe town at the Half Moon Club.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.646 --\u003e 00:03:51.398\r\nMost fun we ever had.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.357 --\u003e 00:03:54.568\r\nHeard they were tearing\r\nthe old place down.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.193 --\u003e 00:03:58.280\r\nI guess nothing\r\ngood lasts forever.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.407 --\u003e 00:04:02.033\r\nDOCTOR: He's ready. Let's do it.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.249 --\u003e 00:04:10.834\r\n- (DOOR OPENS)\r\n- (MAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:11.084 --\u003e 00:04:12.753\r\nNURSE: No! What are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:04:12.961 --\u003e 00:04:14.004\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:04:21.636 --\u003e 00:04:22.637\r\nCome on!\r\n\r\n00:04:24.473 --\u003e 00:04:26.850\r\nTHUG: Sorry,\r\nhis insurance don't cover this.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.979 --\u003e 00:04:33.690\r\nDon't hurt him.\r\nBoss wants to handle Dent personally.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.774 --\u003e 00:04:35.609\r\nSaid he wants to teach\r\nhim some respect.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.903 --\u003e 00:04:39.321\r\nTake a load off.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.446 --\u003e 00:04:40.864\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:04:48.997 --\u003e 00:04:50.165\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.129 --\u003e 00:04:57.547\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:57.631 --\u003e 00:05:00.008\r\nMan, talk about malpractice.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.847 --\u003e 00:05:07.682\r\nHey. Slow down.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.849 --\u003e 00:05:09.184\r\n(CAR STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:09.309 --\u003e 00:05:10.602\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:10.685 --\u003e 00:05:13.730\r\nYou take the sedan.\r\nI'll go after the other one.\r\n\r\n00:05:38.672 --\u003e 00:05:40.090\r\nClean your windshield, mister?\r\n\r\n00:05:40.590 --\u003e 00:05:42.467\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:46.763 --\u003e 00:05:48.431\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:05:52.561 --\u003e 00:05:53.562\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:02.487 --\u003e 00:06:03.655\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.990 --\u003e 00:06:06.992\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:28.763 --\u003e 00:06:30.181\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:06:39.816 --\u003e 00:06:40.942\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:49.034 --\u003e 00:06:50.702\r\nScratch one bat. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.513 --\u003e 00:07:12.265\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:07:13.558 --\u003e 00:07:15.018\r\n(MEN YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:27.989 --\u003e 00:07:29.240\r\n(MEN GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:07:41.294 --\u003e 00:07:43.838\r\nThe van was registered\r\nto Rupert Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.047 --\u003e 00:07:45.507\r\nBut Harvey was in the sedan.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.674 --\u003e 00:07:47.258\r\nIt was headed for Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.550 --\u003e 00:07:49.260\r\nThe Penguin's in Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.511 --\u003e 00:07:51.763\r\nHe's had a grudge against\r\nTwo-Face for a while now.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.013 --\u003e 00:07:53.723\r\nMaybe this is his revenge.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.932 --\u003e 00:07:55.517\r\nSorry I wasn't\r\nable to stop them.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.184 --\u003e 00:07:57.894\r\nI'm sure you did your best.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.186 --\u003e 00:08:01.147\r\nDon't gush all over me.\r\nIt's embarrassing.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.196 --\u003e 00:08:11.408\r\nSorry. Harvey's my friend.\r\nI'm worried about him.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.574 --\u003e 00:08:14.327\r\nRight,\r\nand I'm just the kid in tights.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.911 --\u003e 00:08:17.288\r\nI'll see you after I've\r\nchecked out Thorne.\r\n\r\n00:08:30.260 --\u003e 00:08:34.055\r\n\u003ci\u003eHARVEY: I remember when we used to\r\nclose the town at the Half Moon Club.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:34.347 --\u003e 00:08:36.850\r\n\u003ci\u003eMost fun we ever had.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:39.644 --\u003e 00:08:41.062\r\n(ENGINE STARTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:02.959 --\u003e 00:09:05.336\r\n(CLEARS THROAT) May \u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e help you?\r\n\r\n00:09:20.268 --\u003e 00:09:24.064\r\nFrankie here says they found you\r\nsnooping around my roof. Why?\r\n\r\n00:09:24.230 --\u003e 00:09:27.901\r\n- What are you trying to find?\r\n- Not \"what,\" Thorne, \"who.\"\r\n\r\n00:09:28.318 --\u003e 00:09:31.321\r\nSomebody grabbed Harvey Dent\r\nout of Gotham Central Hospital.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.821 --\u003e 00:09:33.490\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:33.573 --\u003e 00:09:36.159\r\nSomebody nabbed Two-Face,\r\nand you thought I did it?\r\n\r\n00:09:36.242 --\u003e 00:09:38.536\r\n(CHUCKLING) That's great.\r\n\r\n00:09:38.703 --\u003e 00:09:41.289\r\nI wish. I really hate that guy.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.498 --\u003e 00:09:43.208\r\nHe tried to put me\r\nout of business.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.625 --\u003e 00:09:45.251\r\nI've been planning what I'd do\r\n\r\n00:09:45.418 --\u003e 00:09:48.171\r\nif I ever got my hands on him\r\nagain, and I'll tell you-\r\n\r\n00:09:48.379 --\u003e 00:09:51.091\r\nNo, better yet,\r\nas long as you're here,\r\n\r\n00:09:51.299 --\u003e 00:09:52.425\r\nI'll show you.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.634 --\u003e 00:09:56.679\r\nBoys, take the Boy Wonder here\r\ndown to Gotham Gate Bridge\r\n\r\n00:09:56.930 --\u003e 00:09:59.057\r\nand see how well he flies.\r\n\r\n00:09:59.891 --\u003e 00:10:02.102\r\nThanks for giving an old\r\nman a good laugh, kid.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.185 --\u003e 00:10:04.813\r\n(CHUCKLES) Nice knowing you.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.110 --\u003e 00:10:11.694\r\n(CAR RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:24.833 --\u003e 00:10:26.334\r\n(CAR SLOWING DOWN)\r\n\r\n00:10:28.378 --\u003e 00:10:30.296\r\n(DOOR OPENS AND CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:10:30.839 --\u003e 00:10:32.632\r\n(KEYS JINGLING)\r\n\r\n00:10:41.891 --\u003e 00:10:44.644\r\nFRANKIE: You know, when I was a\r\nkid, I used to fish around here.\r\n\r\n00:10:45.270 --\u003e 00:10:47.230\r\nCan't do it anymore.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.397 --\u003e 00:10:50.233\r\nKnow why? Too much garbage.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.316 --\u003e 00:10:52.735\r\nYou wouldn't believe the stuff\r\npeople toss in the river.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.153 --\u003e 00:10:55.071\r\n- It's disgusting.\r\n- (THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:04.956 --\u003e 00:11:07.625\r\nPeople today got no\r\nrespect for Mother Nature.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.959 --\u003e 00:11:10.086\r\nSooner or later, just you wait.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.170 --\u003e 00:11:11.212\r\nThey'll be sorry.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.296 --\u003e 00:11:12.422\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:11:13.298 --\u003e 00:11:14.299\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:21.848 --\u003e 00:11:23.892\r\nNot all the garbage\r\nis in the river.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.230 --\u003e 00:11:30.523\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:30.899 --\u003e 00:11:32.483\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:36.654 --\u003e 00:11:38.364\r\nDance, my little ones.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.448 --\u003e 00:11:40.533\r\nDance for Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.954 --\u003e 00:11:46.331\r\nExcellent.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.414 --\u003e 00:11:48.666\r\nA terpsichorean triumph.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.334 --\u003e 00:11:50.668\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:51.044 --\u003e 00:11:53.171\r\nAnd what might you\r\nbe doing out there?\r\n\r\n00:11:53.504 --\u003e 00:11:55.215\r\nCatching insects for dinner?\r\n\r\n00:11:55.548 --\u003e 00:11:57.258\r\nI'm looking for Two-Face.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.508 --\u003e 00:12:00.678\r\nWhy? Did you lose him?\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:12:00.762 --\u003e 00:12:03.723\r\nSomebody kidnapped him from\r\nGotham Central tonight.\r\n\r\n00:12:03.932 --\u003e 00:12:06.434\r\nYou and he had a\r\ndisagreement some time ago.\r\n\r\n00:12:06.643 --\u003e 00:12:08.436\r\n- Didn't you?\r\n- It's true.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.645 --\u003e 00:12:11.314\r\nHarvey stole a rare avis\r\nright out from under my beak\r\n\r\n00:12:11.397 --\u003e 00:12:12.565\r\nseveral months ago.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.732 --\u003e 00:12:15.944\r\nA jewel-encrusted statuette\r\nof a two-headed roc.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.152 --\u003e 00:12:17.779\r\nIt was worth millions.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.029 --\u003e 00:12:22.909\r\nBut, my dear rodent, I'd never kidnap\r\na fellow rogue out of a sickbed.\r\n\r\n00:12:23.117 --\u003e 00:12:24.869\r\nIt just isn't done.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.078 --\u003e 00:12:27.705\r\n- Honor among thieves?\r\n- Absolutely.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.914 --\u003e 00:12:30.166\r\nIf I were going to attack\r\nHarvey, I'd do it\r\n\r\n00:12:30.250 --\u003e 00:12:34.045\r\nface-to-face, to-face.\r\nSo to speak.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.295 --\u003e 00:12:35.922\r\nLike this!\r\n\r\n00:12:36.256 --\u003e 00:12:38.049\r\n- (BIRD SCREECHING)\r\n- (LAUGHING MANIACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:12:41.052 --\u003e 00:12:42.512\r\n(BIRDS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:47.308 --\u003e 00:12:49.269\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:52.188 --\u003e 00:12:54.774\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.819 --\u003e 00:12:59.570\r\nOver here, you fools.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.821 --\u003e 00:13:02.490\r\nHe's down there. Down there.\r\n\r\n00:13:03.032 --\u003e 00:13:04.742\r\n(BIRDS SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:15.420 --\u003e 00:13:16.963\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:19.090 --\u003e 00:13:20.383\r\nAny luck with Thorne?\r\n\r\n00:13:20.800 --\u003e 00:13:22.427\r\nThorne didn't kidnap Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.677 --\u003e 00:13:24.012\r\nNeither did the Penguin.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.220 --\u003e 00:13:26.431\r\nBut I think I know who did.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.903 --\u003e 00:13:42.697\r\n(DIGITAL BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:13:44.907 --\u003e 00:13:46.951\r\nDoctors and nurses\r\nworking in the O.R.\r\n\r\n00:13:47.160 --\u003e 00:13:49.203\r\nwear paper socks\r\nover their shoes,\r\n\r\n00:13:49.454 --\u003e 00:13:52.457\r\nso this footprint had to be\r\nmade by one of the kidnappers.\r\n\r\n00:13:53.082 --\u003e 00:13:54.876\r\nMasonry dust.\r\n\r\n00:13:55.043 --\u003e 00:13:57.128\r\nI know where to find him now.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.420 --\u003e 00:13:59.547\r\nFind who? Who did this?\r\n\r\n00:13:59.797 --\u003e 00:14:01.758\r\nHarvey's worst enemy.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.966 --\u003e 00:14:03.426\r\nI'll take it from here.\r\n\r\n00:14:03.593 --\u003e 00:14:05.470\r\nWait a second.\r\nYou might need me.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.887 --\u003e 00:14:06.971\r\nNot this time, Robin.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.263 --\u003e 00:14:09.474\r\nThis is something\r\nI have to do alone.\r\n\r\n00:14:10.975 --\u003e 00:14:12.268\r\n(DOOR CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:14:14.270 --\u003e 00:14:15.980\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.994 --\u003e 00:14:32.455\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING) You\r\nmay as well come out.\r\n\r\n00:14:32.955 --\u003e 00:14:34.665\r\nI know everything now.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.791 --\u003e 00:14:36.292\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.130 --\u003e 00:14:42.382\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:46.052 --\u003e 00:14:47.553\r\nYou hated Harvey Dent\r\n\r\n00:14:47.887 --\u003e 00:14:50.181\r\nand would do anything\r\nto destroy him.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.140 --\u003e 00:14:52.350\r\nWhy not?\r\n\r\n00:14:52.558 --\u003e 00:14:54.477\r\nHe was gonna destroy me,\r\n\r\n00:14:54.727 --\u003e 00:14:57.355\r\njust like I'm gonna destroy you.\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.944 --\u003e 00:15:04.112\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:04.320 --\u003e 00:15:05.446\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:18.126 --\u003e 00:15:19.168\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.252 --\u003e 00:15:20.795\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:27.385 --\u003e 00:15:28.928\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:46.154 --\u003e 00:15:47.905\r\nYou kidnapped yourself.\r\n\r\n00:15:48.156 --\u003e 00:15:49.782\r\nI should've seen it right away.\r\n\r\n00:15:49.991 --\u003e 00:15:53.202\r\nOne red herring clue wasn't enough.\r\nYou had to leave two.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.369 --\u003e 00:15:56.539\r\nI couldn't let that\r\nwimp Dent destroy me.\r\n\r\n00:15:56.998 --\u003e 00:15:59.876\r\nI had to teach the\r\nlittle man some respect.\r\n\r\n00:16:00.209 --\u003e 00:16:03.671\r\nEverybody needs respect.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.754 --\u003e 00:16:05.506\r\nYou're your own worst\r\nenemy, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.007 --\u003e 00:16:09.552\r\nNo. I'm your worst enemy.\r\n\r\n00:16:09.802 --\u003e 00:16:10.887\r\nSee this?\r\n\r\n00:16:11.179 --\u003e 00:16:14.432\r\nIt's the remote control\r\nfor that detonator.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.308 --\u003e 00:16:18.144\r\nOnce my boys and I get\r\ndown to the ground,\r\n\r\n00:16:18.352 --\u003e 00:16:20.855\r\nI'll use it to set\r\noff that dynamite.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.314 --\u003e 00:16:25.359\r\nUnless, of course,\r\nthe coin says different.\r\n\r\n00:16:25.860 --\u003e 00:16:27.695\r\nWhat do you say, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:16:28.070 --\u003e 00:16:30.239\r\nFeefinglucky?\r\n\r\n00:16:30.990 --\u003e 00:16:33.326\r\nBATMAN: Looks like I\r\ndon't have much choice.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.537 --\u003e 00:16:37.663\r\nLet it hit the floor.\r\n\r\n00:16:37.747 --\u003e 00:16:39.081\r\nI wanna see it.\r\n\r\n00:16:42.919 --\u003e 00:16:44.378\r\nThat can't happen.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.011 --\u003e 00:16:54.138\r\nNo. It isn't possible.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.932 --\u003e 00:16:57.350\r\nIt can't land on edge.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.433 --\u003e 00:16:59.227\r\nIt has to be heads or tails.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.644 --\u003e 00:17:02.104\r\nHow can I decide if it\r\nisn't heads or tails?\r\n\r\n00:17:12.448 --\u003e 00:17:14.242\r\nOn edge, it's still on edge.\r\n\r\n00:17:19.664 --\u003e 00:17:21.123\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:31.676 --\u003e 00:17:33.135\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:34.845 --\u003e 00:17:36.138\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.684 --\u003e 00:17:41.352\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:43.646 --\u003e 00:17:45.606\r\nHeads or tails. I have to know.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.690 --\u003e 00:17:46.983\r\nHeads or tails.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.651 --\u003e 00:17:49.652\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:54.156 --\u003e 00:17:55.157\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:07.044 --\u003e 00:18:08.379\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.546 --\u003e 00:18:09.547\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.094 --\u003e 00:18:16.095\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:28.232 --\u003e 00:18:29.525\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.069 --\u003e 00:18:33.362\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:38.659 --\u003e 00:18:39.952\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:41.871 --\u003e 00:18:43.914\r\nHarvey. Pull yourself up.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.998 --\u003e 00:18:46.334\r\nI can't. I'll drop the coin.\r\n\r\n00:18:46.417 --\u003e 00:18:48.794\r\nDrop it. Save yourself.\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:50.838\r\nI... I don't know what to do.\r\n\r\n00:18:50.921 --\u003e 00:18:52.340\r\nThe coin won't tell me.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.423 --\u003e 00:18:54.300\r\nIt can't tell you anything.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.383 --\u003e 00:18:56.802\r\nI switched coins\r\nwhen you grabbed me.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.471 --\u003e 00:18:59.680\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:01.974 --\u003e 00:19:04.727\r\nGood thing I decided\r\nto tag along after all.\r\n\r\n00:19:06.354 --\u003e 00:19:07.855\r\nIt's a trick coin.\r\n\r\n00:19:07.938 --\u003e 00:19:09.774\r\nIt'll always land on edge.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.857 --\u003e 00:19:11.984\r\nIt's your decision now, Harvey.\r\n\r\n00:19:12.068 --\u003e 00:19:13.778\r\nLife or death.\r\n\r\n00:19:14.445 --\u003e 00:19:16.572\r\nThe coin or me.\r\n\r\n00:19:34.173 --\u003e 00:19:36.092\r\nBatman, help me.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.095 --\u003e 00:19:40.262\r\n(LIGHTNING CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.346 --\u003e 00:19:41.472\r\nNever.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.806 --\u003e 00:19:42.973\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:19:43.683 --\u003e 00:19:44.975\r\nHarvey!\r\n\r\n00:19:45.226 --\u003e 00:19:47.186\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.005 --\u003e 00:20:17.800\r\nBruce. Good old Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.092 --\u003e 00:20:19.635\r\nAlways there.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.927 --\u003e 00:20:21.303\r\nYou never give up on me.\r\n\r\n00:20:26.392 --\u003e 00:20:27.643\r\nDICK: He's right.\r\n\r\n00:20:27.727 --\u003e 00:20:29.937\r\n- You're always there for him.\r\n- Yes.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.396 --\u003e 00:20:32.314\r\nJust like you're\r\nalways there for me.\r\n\r\n00:20:32.398 --\u003e 00:20:35.276\r\n- Hey, what are friends for?\r\n- (LIGHTNING CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:43.159 --\u003e 00:20:45.161\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:10.019 --\u003e 00:21:11.061\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E03 - Riddler's Reform (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.256 --\u003e 00:00:08.258\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:02:01.330 --\u003e 00:02:02.748\r\nBring it out.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.831 --\u003e 00:02:04.333\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.878 --\u003e 00:02:08.879\r\nPhew.\r\n\r\n00:02:09.296 --\u003e 00:02:10.422\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:17.095 --\u003e 00:02:18.096\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:19.765 --\u003e 00:02:20.807\r\nTake it easy.\r\n\r\n00:02:24.019 --\u003e 00:02:25.020\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:27.481 --\u003e 00:02:29.316\r\nWell, well, well.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.483 --\u003e 00:02:31.109\r\nLook who's here.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.568 --\u003e 00:02:33.945\r\nUp to your old tricks\r\nalready, huh, Nygma?\r\n\r\n00:02:34.029 --\u003e 00:02:36.573\r\nWhatever are you talking\r\nabout, Batman?\r\n\r\n00:02:36.698 --\u003e 00:02:38.298\r\nThe last time you\r\ndelivered one of these,\r\n\r\n00:02:38.367 --\u003e 00:02:39.677\r\nit almost killed\r\nCommissioner Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:02:39.701 --\u003e 00:02:40.702\r\nWhat's your point?\r\n\r\n00:02:40.827 --\u003e 00:02:43.622\r\n- What's in the box?\r\n- None of your business.\r\n\r\n00:02:43.955 --\u003e 00:02:46.291\r\n- I'm making it my business.\r\n- MAN: Stop!\r\n\r\n00:02:47.042 --\u003e 00:02:48.543\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:02:51.254 --\u003e 00:02:52.881\r\nDon't worry, sir, we've got him.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.964 --\u003e 00:02:56.093\r\nHis name is Edward Nygma,\r\notherwise known as the Riddler.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.176 --\u003e 00:02:58.553\r\nI know who he is,\r\nyou young fool.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.804 --\u003e 00:03:00.806\r\nIt's all right, C.B.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.972 --\u003e 00:03:02.808\r\nThese are two old\r\nfriends of mine.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.974 --\u003e 00:03:05.227\r\nBefore you louts sink\r\nyour fists into me,\r\n\r\n00:03:05.310 --\u003e 00:03:08.605\r\nI'd like you to meet my new\r\npartner, Charles Baxter,\r\n\r\n00:03:08.730 --\u003e 00:03:12.567\r\npresident of the multimillion-dollar\r\nWacko Toy Corporation,\r\n\r\n00:03:12.943 --\u003e 00:03:15.696\r\nand the man who has\r\nlicensed my Riddler persona\r\n\r\n00:03:15.779 --\u003e 00:03:19.908\r\nand my exclusive puzzle technology\r\nfor his new line of toys.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.746 --\u003e 00:03:26.081\r\nWe're going to make a killing.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.540 --\u003e 00:03:27.791\r\nThat's what I'm afraid of.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.250 --\u003e 00:03:30.502\r\nNow, now,\r\nI know what you're thinking.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.669 --\u003e 00:03:33.505\r\nBut those silly riddle crimes\r\nare a thing of the past.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.755 --\u003e 00:03:35.966\r\nAncient history that's gone now.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.133 --\u003e 00:03:38.385\r\nI'm a new man. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:03:38.552 --\u003e 00:03:42.013\r\nBut you probably won't figure\r\nthat out until it's too late.\r\n\r\n00:03:42.264 --\u003e 00:03:44.391\r\nDo you know who you're\r\ndealing with here, Baxter?\r\n\r\n00:03:44.558 --\u003e 00:03:47.936\r\nYes, a man who's going to\r\nmake my company millions.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.103 --\u003e 00:03:49.688\r\nEveryone's heard of the Riddler.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.855 --\u003e 00:03:52.524\r\nYou can't buy that kind\r\nof market recognition.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.691 --\u003e 00:03:56.570\r\nLeave him alone, or I'll swear out a\r\ncomplaint against you for harassment.\r\n\r\n00:03:58.488 --\u003e 00:04:00.282\r\nHere's a little\r\nsomething for the kid.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.536 --\u003e 00:04:07.164\r\n\u003ci\u003eTV ANCHOR: Still no verdict\r\nin the trial of the Penguin.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:07.330 --\u003e 00:04:09.583\r\n\u003ci\u003eThough apprehended last\r\nmonth by the Batman,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:09.666 --\u003e 00:04:11.209\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe jury still\r\nremains unconvinced\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:11.293 --\u003e 00:04:13.462\r\n\u003ci\u003eof the felon's guilt\r\ndespite overwhelming...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:13.545 --\u003e 00:04:18.008\r\nAs far as I can tell, it looks like\r\na normal toy. No hidden gimmicks.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.175 --\u003e 00:04:19.259\r\nYou wanna look at it?\r\n\r\n00:04:21.970 --\u003e 00:04:23.054\r\nGuess not.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.722 --\u003e 00:04:25.974\r\n\u003ci\u003eFinally in the news,\r\nthere was a burglary\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:26.057 --\u003e 00:04:28.018\r\n\u003ci\u003elast night in the\r\nMarket Lane District.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:28.351 --\u003e 00:04:31.146\r\n\u003ci\u003eThieves made off with rare\r\nantiquities and artifacts\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:31.313 --\u003e 00:04:33.732\r\n\u003ci\u003efrom the Newman Import\r\n& Export Company.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:33.899 --\u003e 00:04:35.233\r\nWait. What's that?\r\n\r\n00:04:35.484 --\u003e 00:04:40.030\r\n\u003ci\u003eA Ming vase from the third\r\ncentury, an 800-year-old tapestry.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:40.113 --\u003e 00:04:42.115\r\n\u003ci\u003eI\u003c/i\u003e can't replace these.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.449 --\u003e 00:04:44.868\r\n\u003ci\u003eRIDDLER: Those were things\r\nof the past, Batman.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:45.035 --\u003e 00:04:47.162\r\n\u003ci\u003eAncient history that's gone now.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:47.329 --\u003e 00:04:48.747\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm a new man.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:48.914 --\u003e 00:04:52.042\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut you probably won't figure that\r\nout until it's too late. {LAUGHS.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:54.503 --\u003e 00:04:56.129\r\n- He did it.\r\n- Who?\r\n\r\n00:04:56.338 --\u003e 00:04:58.757\r\nThe Riddler.\r\nRemember what he said?\r\n\r\n00:04:59.257 --\u003e 00:05:03.261\r\n\"Things of the past.\" \"Ancient\r\nhistory that's gone now.\"\r\n\r\n00:05:04.221 --\u003e 00:05:05.222\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.431 --\u003e 00:05:09.643\r\nGee, I don't know.\r\nHis riddles aren't usually that subtle.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.976 --\u003e 00:05:12.979\r\nBesides, he's got a multimillion-dollar\r\ndeal with that toy company.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.146 --\u003e 00:05:15.857\r\nWhy would he throw it away\r\nover some stupid riddle crime?\r\n\r\n00:05:16.024 --\u003e 00:05:19.236\r\nBecause that's the way his\r\nwarped mind works. He's obsessed.\r\n\r\n00:05:19.611 --\u003e 00:05:20.862\r\nHey, look.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.741 --\u003e 00:05:26.952\r\n\u003ci\u003eGreetings, little riddle-tykes!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:28.703 --\u003e 00:05:30.580\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's time for riddle number\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:30.831 --\u003e 00:05:35.252\r\n3-1-7-5-3-7-0-1.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.629 --\u003e 00:05:40.715\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhere in the world can\r\nyou have the most fun?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:41.007 --\u003e 00:05:43.885\r\n\u003ci\u003eIn any store that sells Wacko\r\nToys, of course.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:43.969 --\u003e 00:05:48.056\r\nThat's because \u003ci\u003eWacko\u003c/i\u003e makes the entire\r\nline of Riddler games and puzzles,\r\n\r\n00:05:48.390 --\u003e 00:05:50.392\r\n\u003ci\u003elike the Riddler's Riddle-mid.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:50.559 --\u003e 00:05:53.103\r\n\u003ci\u003eHours of fun for only $19.95.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:53.395 --\u003e 00:05:55.981\r\n\u003ci\u003eSo grab your parents,\r\nor just their wallets,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:56.147 --\u003e 00:05:58.900\r\n\u003ci\u003eand run on down to\r\nyour nearest toy store.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:59.067 --\u003e 00:06:01.361\r\n\u003ci\u003eTell them the Riddler sent you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:02.445 --\u003e 00:06:03.864\r\nThis riddle number.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.030 --\u003e 00:06:05.824\r\nI wonder why he used that.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.991 --\u003e 00:06:07.742\r\nAnd why did he put\r\na map up there?\r\n\r\n00:06:08.076 --\u003e 00:06:09.953\r\nIt's got eight digits.\r\n\r\n00:06:11.204 --\u003e 00:06:12.706\r\nSo does a map coordinate.\r\n\r\n00:06:20.463 --\u003e 00:06:21.923\r\nDICK: 3-1-7-5,\r\n\r\n00:06:22.674 --\u003e 00:06:24.217\r\n3-7-0-1.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.053 --\u003e 00:06:29.180\r\nIt's the downtown\r\nFinancial District.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.057 --\u003e 00:06:33.018\r\nWhat's that building\r\nright there in the center?\r\n\r\n00:06:36.146 --\u003e 00:06:37.898\r\nThe First National Bank.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.799 --\u003e 00:07:07.552\r\n(SIGHS) It's after 10:00.\r\nHe should've been here by now.\r\n\r\n00:07:08.261 --\u003e 00:07:10.180\r\nYou know, maybe we're\r\nreading into this thing.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.263 --\u003e 00:07:12.140\r\nMaybe he wasn't sending\r\na riddle at all.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.355 --\u003e 00:07:20.148\r\nHe flipped it over.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.774 --\u003e 00:07:22.692\r\n- What?\r\n- The number.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.943 --\u003e 00:07:25.528\r\nHe flipped it upside-down when\r\nhe turned the chalkboard over.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.574 --\u003e 00:07:32.202\r\n- 10 Leslie?\r\n- It's an address.\r\n\r\n00:07:32.911 --\u003e 00:07:34.412\r\nWe're in the wrong place.\r\n\r\n00:07:36.539 --\u003e 00:07:37.958\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:42.253 --\u003e 00:07:44.589\r\nNot a sign of him\r\nanywhere, Mr. Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.006 --\u003e 00:07:46.841\r\nHe must be losing his touch.\r\n\r\n00:07:46.925 --\u003e 00:07:49.344\r\nAll right,\r\nhurry up and get out of there.\r\n\r\n00:07:57.560 --\u003e 00:07:58.561\r\n(ALL GREETING)\r\n\r\n00:08:02.357 --\u003e 00:08:03.984\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:09.531 --\u003e 00:08:10.699\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:08:10.865 --\u003e 00:08:11.866\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- (C0lNS JINGLE)\r\n\r\n00:08:16.496 --\u003e 00:08:17.580\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:39.769 --\u003e 00:08:40.812\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:42.897 --\u003e 00:08:44.065\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:47.736 --\u003e 00:08:48.903\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:53.575 --\u003e 00:08:54.576\r\nHad enough?\r\n\r\n00:08:56.870 --\u003e 00:08:57.996\r\nLook out!\r\n\r\n00:09:03.209 --\u003e 00:09:04.210\r\nRobin?\r\n\r\n00:09:04.377 --\u003e 00:09:05.378\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:08.048 --\u003e 00:09:09.257\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:09.799 --\u003e 00:09:10.842\r\nMy foot.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.471 --\u003e 00:09:15.472\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:09:16.181 --\u003e 00:09:17.348\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:20.060 --\u003e 00:09:21.061\r\nLet's go.\r\n\r\n00:09:22.437 --\u003e 00:09:23.646\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:09:25.523 --\u003e 00:09:26.649\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:26.733 --\u003e 00:09:28.276\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:09:28.359 --\u003e 00:09:31.446\r\nBut you better go on without me.\r\nI'll be okay.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.529 --\u003e 00:09:33.239\r\nGo! Go!\r\n\r\n00:09:40.288 --\u003e 00:09:41.581\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:49.964 --\u003e 00:09:51.132\r\nOh, no!\r\n\r\n00:09:51.257 --\u003e 00:09:52.467\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:52.550 --\u003e 00:09:53.760\r\nGive me that.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.427 --\u003e 00:09:55.678\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:58.348 --\u003e 00:09:59.349\r\n(GUN CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.520 --\u003e 00:10:05.063\r\nDo something!\r\n\r\n00:10:06.439 --\u003e 00:10:08.066\r\nHold on!\r\n\r\n00:10:09.818 --\u003e 00:10:11.402\r\n- (CREAKING)\r\n- (BOTH SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:17.784 --\u003e 00:10:18.952\r\nPull the brake!\r\n\r\n00:10:21.913 --\u003e 00:10:23.123\r\n(CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:10:32.257 --\u003e 00:10:33.550\r\n- (CRASHING)\r\n- (BOTH YELL)\r\n\r\n00:10:50.900 --\u003e 00:10:52.485\r\n(INDISTINCT CONVERSATIONS)\r\n\r\n00:10:54.028 --\u003e 00:10:55.822\r\nC.B.: Blast this thing.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.905 --\u003e 00:10:56.906\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:59.325 --\u003e 00:11:01.911\r\nHow do you solve this\r\ncontraption, Nygma?\r\n\r\n00:11:02.495 --\u003e 00:11:04.789\r\nEasy. You just have to be\r\n\r\n00:11:05.290 --\u003e 00:11:06.374\r\na genius.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.541 --\u003e 00:11:08.126\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:10.753 --\u003e 00:11:12.839\r\nWell, you are a genius, my boy.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.131 --\u003e 00:11:15.717\r\nSales are up 20%\r\nacross the country.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.800 --\u003e 00:11:18.303\r\nThese toys of yours\r\nare brilliant.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.764 --\u003e 00:11:25.894\r\nWhere did you find him, C.B.?\r\nHe's so adorable.\r\n\r\n00:11:26.519 --\u003e 00:11:27.520\r\nWho?\r\n\r\n00:11:28.855 --\u003e 00:11:29.939\r\nMe?\r\n\r\n00:11:30.356 --\u003e 00:11:32.775\r\n(CHUCKLES) Of course you, silly.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.067 --\u003e 00:11:37.197\r\nAnd you're so smart.\r\nI just love a man with brains.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.989 --\u003e 00:11:41.618\r\nGee, I bet you say that to\r\nall the geniuses. (CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:11:41.701 --\u003e 00:11:46.581\r\nOh, Mr. Riddler,\r\ncan you tell me what these do?\r\n\r\n00:11:50.084 --\u003e 00:11:53.713\r\nExcuse me, sir, but you have a\r\nphone call in the other room.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.719 --\u003e 00:12:01.095\r\n(WHISTLING TUNE)\r\n\r\n00:12:05.850 --\u003e 00:12:08.603\r\nYou're adorable.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.686 --\u003e 00:12:09.687\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:10.271 --\u003e 00:12:11.272\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.856 --\u003e 00:12:12.941\r\n\u003ci\u003eHello?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:14.484 --\u003e 00:12:15.985\r\nAdorable, huh?\r\n\r\n00:12:16.903 --\u003e 00:12:17.904\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:18.238 --\u003e 00:12:20.406\r\nI don't believe\r\nyou were invited.\r\n\r\n00:12:21.324 --\u003e 00:12:23.451\r\nI'm on to you, Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:12:24.619 --\u003e 00:12:27.038\r\n(SCOFFS) You're still\r\nchasing riddles.\r\n\r\n00:12:29.374 --\u003e 00:12:30.959\r\n\u003ci\u003eBATMAN: You're\r\nstill giving them.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:31.042 --\u003e 00:12:32.627\r\nRIDDLER: Is that\r\nwhat you believe?\r\n\r\n00:12:33.002 --\u003e 00:12:35.255\r\n\u003ci\u003eWell, how do you know what to\r\nbelieve, Batman?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:35.546 --\u003e 00:12:37.674\r\nMaybe I'm not\r\ngiving clues at all.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.840 --\u003e 00:12:40.426\r\nMaybe you're seeing\r\nthings that aren't there.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.593 --\u003e 00:12:43.263\r\nBut then again,\r\nmaybe I am giving you clues.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.429 --\u003e 00:12:46.015\r\nI could be giving you a clue right\r\nnow, couldn't I?\r\n\r\n00:12:46.224 --\u003e 00:12:49.936\r\nOf course, it's possible\r\nthat you're just paranoid.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.603 --\u003e 00:12:53.356\r\nBy the way,\r\ndid you see my latest toy?\r\n\r\n00:12:53.523 --\u003e 00:12:55.066\r\nIt's a two-way radio.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.149 --\u003e 00:12:56.693\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.944 --\u003e 00:13:02.615\r\nLadies and gentlemen,\r\nI'd like you to meet the great Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.699 --\u003e 00:13:05.034\r\nHe's here because he\r\nhasn't got a clue.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.118 --\u003e 00:13:06.786\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:13:09.497 --\u003e 00:13:10.873\r\nYou can play all you like.\r\n\r\n00:13:11.332 --\u003e 00:13:13.626\r\nBut you and I both know that\r\nI'm going to put you away\r\n\r\n00:13:13.793 --\u003e 00:13:15.837\r\nbecause you can't help yourself.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.004 --\u003e 00:13:17.213\r\nYou can't stop.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.300 --\u003e 00:13:22.051\r\nAnd I'll be waiting.\r\n\r\n00:13:23.428 --\u003e 00:13:24.595\r\n(THUNDERCLAP)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.680 --\u003e 00:13:27.932\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:13:33.229 --\u003e 00:13:34.522\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:39.485 --\u003e 00:13:40.737\r\nHe's right, you know.\r\n\r\n00:13:41.154 --\u003e 00:13:43.531\r\n- Who?\r\n- Batman.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.698 --\u003e 00:13:46.159\r\nHe is going to catch\r\nme, sooner or later.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.659 --\u003e 00:13:49.203\r\n(CHUCKLES) Gee, boss,\r\nyou're scaring me.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.370 --\u003e 00:13:50.830\r\nYou're talking kind of crazy.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.997 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nDon't you ever call me that!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.874 --\u003e 00:13:56.252\r\nI fooled the police, the doctors,\r\nthe parole board, all of them.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.336 --\u003e 00:14:00.214\r\nThere's only one person who's ever\r\nbeen able to challenge me. Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.381 --\u003e 00:14:02.759\r\nHe's the only one\r\nworthy of the game.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.967 --\u003e 00:14:06.512\r\nBut you said sooner or\r\nlater, he's gonna catch you.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.679 --\u003e 00:14:09.557\r\n- What are you gonna do?\r\n- I'm never going back to Arkham.\r\n\r\n00:14:11.768 --\u003e 00:14:15.313\r\nSo I guess there's\r\nonly one thing to do.\r\n\r\n00:14:15.396 --\u003e 00:14:16.564\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:20.526 --\u003e 00:14:21.861\r\nDIRECTOR: Give me lights.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.237 --\u003e 00:14:24.322\r\nSound check.\r\n\r\n00:14:24.614 --\u003e 00:14:26.032\r\nWe got speed.\r\n\r\n00:14:26.115 --\u003e 00:14:28.785\r\nDIRECTOR: All right,\r\nlet's have places, everyone.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.993 --\u003e 00:14:30.745\r\nHere's your script, Mr. Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.496 --\u003e 00:14:33.498\r\nI already know what\r\nI'm going to say.\r\n\r\n00:14:37.168 --\u003e 00:14:39.379\r\nDIRECTOR: Quiet on the set.\r\nWe're going live.\r\n\r\n00:14:40.922 --\u003e 00:14:41.964\r\nAction.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.423 --\u003e 00:14:45.218\r\nHey, folks. Wouldn't it be\r\ngreat to be a kid again,\r\n\r\n00:14:45.426 --\u003e 00:14:49.639\r\nenjoying all those wonderful moments\r\nof childhood with your favorite toys?\r\n\r\n00:14:49.806 --\u003e 00:14:51.808\r\n(WHISPERING) Not like\r\nthat, you'll break it.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.100 --\u003e 00:14:53.351\r\n(CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:14:53.434 --\u003e 00:14:57.939\r\nYes. Well, you can recapture\r\nyour childhood with Wacko Toys.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.231 --\u003e 00:14:59.607\r\nAll you have to do is pick up\r\n\r\n00:14:59.774 --\u003e 00:15:03.152\r\none of the Riddler's puzzles\r\nat your favorite store.\r\n\r\n00:15:03.319 --\u003e 00:15:08.032\r\nThen go back to where it all\r\nstarted, with toys.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.574 --\u003e 00:15:11.119\r\nCome on, be a kid again.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.163 --\u003e 00:15:16.457\r\nBRUCE: He's going to hit the\r\nGotham Convention Center.\r\n\r\n00:15:16.624 --\u003e 00:15:17.792\r\nHow did you figure that?\r\n\r\n00:15:18.209 --\u003e 00:15:20.461\r\nBecause of the clue he's\r\ndeliberately giving me.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.923 --\u003e 00:15:25.675\r\n- What clue?\r\n- He said,\r\n\r\n00:15:25.842 --\u003e 00:15:28.678\r\n\"Go back to where it\r\nstarted, with toys.\"\r\n\r\n00:15:30.096 --\u003e 00:15:31.389\r\nThe toy fair.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.379 --\u003e 00:16:04.380\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:36.579 --\u003e 00:16:37.580\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.010 --\u003e 00:16:52.470\r\n(STATIC)\r\n\r\n00:16:53.429 --\u003e 00:16:56.724\r\n\u003ci\u003eHello, Batman.\r\nThis is it, the end of the game.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:56.891 --\u003e 00:16:59.977\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm a little sad, actually.\r\nYou were a worthy opponent.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:00.061 --\u003e 00:17:03.189\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut then, I told you I'd make\r\na killing at the toy fair.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:06.776 --\u003e 00:17:09.028\r\n\u003ci\u003eTen, nine,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:09.487 --\u003e 00:17:11.614\r\n\u003ci\u003eeight, seven,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:12.615 --\u003e 00:17:14.617\r\n\u003ci\u003esix, five,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:15.618 --\u003e 00:17:16.869\r\n\u003ci\u003efour,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:17.870 --\u003e 00:17:19.664\r\nthree,\r\n\r\n00:17:19.956 --\u003e 00:17:21.749\r\n\u003ci\u003etwo...\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:37.265 --\u003e 00:17:39.517\r\nI always feel sad at funerals.\r\n\r\n00:17:39.976 --\u003e 00:17:43.354\r\nYes, truly,\r\npart of me has died tonight.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.938 --\u003e 00:17:46.566\r\nAnd so it is time to move on.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.109 --\u003e 00:17:49.193\r\n(MEN GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:17:53.656 --\u003e 00:17:56.242\r\nYou! I don't believe it.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.701 --\u003e 00:17:58.035\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:02.164 --\u003e 00:18:03.374\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:12.675 --\u003e 00:18:14.051\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.809 --\u003e 00:18:24.353\r\nThere's no way you could\r\nhave survived that explosion.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.520 --\u003e 00:18:27.106\r\n- How did you get out?\r\n- That's my little riddle.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.356 --\u003e 00:18:29.025\r\nPlease, you must tell me.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.067 --\u003e 00:18:32.987\r\nAll right, you win.\r\nYou tell me what I wanna know\r\n\r\n00:18:33.070 --\u003e 00:18:36.324\r\nand I'll tell you what\r\nyou wanna know. Okay?\r\n\r\n00:18:37.992 --\u003e 00:18:40.703\r\nYou mean, where you've hidden\r\neverything you've stolen?\r\n\r\n00:18:41.162 --\u003e 00:18:45.207\r\nCertainly. I'll even tell you how\r\nI committed all those robberies.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.374 --\u003e 00:18:46.375\r\nDeal?\r\n\r\n00:18:47.752 --\u003e 00:18:48.794\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:18:49.670 --\u003e 00:18:50.755\r\n(CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:18:51.422 --\u003e 00:18:53.382\r\n- Did you get that?\r\n- GORDON: We got it.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.928 --\u003e 00:19:00.389\r\nThis ought to be enough to\r\nprove a parole violation.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.473 --\u003e 00:19:04.185\r\nYou're going away for good this time.\r\nAll right, get him out of here.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.732 --\u003e 00:19:12.568\r\nMy compliments.\r\nThis is a great little idea.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.194 --\u003e 00:19:15.780\r\nWait a minute.\r\nAren't you gonna tell me how you did it?\r\n\r\n00:19:16.155 --\u003e 00:19:17.448\r\nThat's not fair!\r\n\r\n00:19:25.873 --\u003e 00:19:27.917\r\nHis accomplices\r\nplea-bargained immediately.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.167 --\u003e 00:19:30.007\r\nTold the police where\r\nall the stolen goods were\r\n\r\n00:19:30.086 --\u003e 00:19:32.672\r\nand even agreed to\r\ntestify against Nygma.\r\n\r\n00:19:32.880 --\u003e 00:19:36.217\r\nBut what I don't get is,\r\nhow did you escape from that explosion?\r\n\r\n00:19:38.469 --\u003e 00:19:39.637\r\nWell...\r\n\r\n00:19:42.848 --\u003e 00:19:44.725\r\n\u003ci\u003eBRUCE: All the\r\nexits were blocked.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:47.895 --\u003e 00:19:51.232\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd I was out of time.\r\nThere was only one thing to do.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:51.982 --\u003e 00:19:53.484\r\n\u003ci\u003eI jumped inside the safe.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:00.074 --\u003e 00:20:01.617\r\nDICK: (CHUCKLES) Nice\r\ngoing, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.076 --\u003e 00:20:03.703\r\nMan, I'd have never\r\nthought of that.\r\n\r\n00:20:03.911 --\u003e 00:20:05.246\r\nNeither would the Riddler.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.791 --\u003e 00:20:11.001\r\nRIDDLER: It's\r\nimpossible, I tell you!\r\n\r\n00:20:11.168 --\u003e 00:20:13.838\r\nImpossible! My trap was perfect!\r\n\r\n00:20:14.463 --\u003e 00:20:16.006\r\nHow did he do it?\r\n\r\n00:20:16.173 --\u003e 00:20:17.550\r\nI have to know!\r\n\r\n00:20:17.717 --\u003e 00:20:20.177\r\nSomebody tell me! It's not fair!\r\n\r\n00:20:20.261 --\u003e 00:20:22.221\r\nThere was no way, I tell you!\r\n\r\n00:20:22.388 --\u003e 00:20:26.267\r\nNo way he could have gotten out!\r\nSomebody tell me!\r\n\r\n00:20:26.350 --\u003e 00:20:30.229\r\nDo you hear me?\r\nSomebody tell me how he did it!\r\n\r\n00:20:30.521 --\u003e 00:20:32.356\r\nI have to know!\r\n\r\n00:20:32.523 --\u003e 00:20:35.109\r\nI have to know!\r\n\r\n00:20:35.484 --\u003e 00:20:36.777\r\n(WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:20:41.282 --\u003e 00:20:43.284\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:07.683 --\u003e 00:21:08.726\r\nEnglish-US-Template\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E04 - Baby-Doll (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.131 --\u003e 00:00:08.133\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:26.628 --\u003e 00:01:28.922\r\n- Night, Brian.\r\n- See you tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.383 --\u003e 00:01:32.801\r\n(GIRL SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:01:39.850 --\u003e 00:01:41.602\r\nHey, what's the matter?\r\n\r\n00:01:41.768 --\u003e 00:01:43.186\r\nAre you lost, honey?\r\n\r\n00:01:43.895 --\u003e 00:01:47.107\r\nMy big brother went away\r\nand left me by my lonesomes.\r\n\r\n00:01:47.608 --\u003e 00:01:50.986\r\nBig brothers aren't supposed to\r\ndo that to their baby sisters.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.029 --\u003e 00:01:54.740\r\nHere. Dry your eyes,\r\nand I'll help you find a policeman.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.906 --\u003e 00:01:58.619\r\n- He'll get you home safe and sound.\r\n- You're so nice to me.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.994 --\u003e 00:02:02.456\r\nBut then, you always was\r\nthe nicest one, Tippy.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.040 --\u003e 00:02:04.833\r\nYou! But how-\r\n\r\n00:02:05.000 --\u003e 00:02:06.168\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.044 --\u003e 00:02:08.211\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:08.920 --\u003e 00:02:11.173\r\nSorry I had to play\r\nroughs, Tippy.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.506 --\u003e 00:02:13.216\r\nI didn't mean to.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.179 --\u003e 00:02:18.805\r\nANCHOR: Gotham Insider asks,\r\n\r\n00:02:18.889 --\u003e 00:02:20.265\r\n\"Where are they \u003ci\u003enow?\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:20.349 --\u003e 00:02:23.685\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhen her sitcom, Love That\r\nBaby, premiered 20 years ago,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:23.852 --\u003e 00:02:26.813\r\n\u003ci\u003elittle Mary Louise Dahl\r\nbecame an overnight sensation.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:28.690 --\u003e 00:02:33.320\r\n\u003ci\u003eAs the adorable Baby-Doll, young Mary\r\nquickly captured the hearts of millions.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:34.404 --\u003e 00:02:35.697\r\nMEN: Whoa...\r\n\r\n00:02:39.076 --\u003e 00:02:42.704\r\n\u003ci\u003eWell, Baby, you'd better have a\r\npretty good explanation for this.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:43.789 --\u003e 00:02:45.582\r\n\u003ci\u003eI didn't mean to.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:45.999 --\u003e 00:02:48.710\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.587 --\u003e 00:02:52.631\r\nI remember this show\r\nfrom when I was a kid.\r\n\r\n00:02:53.173 --\u003e 00:02:54.508\r\nIt still stinks.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.675 --\u003e 00:02:58.804\r\nBe that as it may, three of the cast's\r\noriginal actors disappeared last week.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.144 --\u003e 00:03:07.270\r\nAnd these two?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.437 --\u003e 00:03:09.398\r\nGORDON: Ms.\r\nVance is in a show at Gotham Rep.\r\n\r\n00:03:09.773 --\u003e 00:03:12.025\r\nI have police bodyguards\r\nfollowing her everywhere.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.568 --\u003e 00:03:16.613\r\nBut that other one, Mary Dahl,\r\ndropped out of sight years ago.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.780 --\u003e 00:03:20.033\r\nIronically, the same thing that brought\r\nher fame turned her into a recluse.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.200 --\u003e 00:03:22.411\r\nI read about her once\r\nin a medical journal.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.577 --\u003e 00:03:24.913\r\nShe was born with\r\nsystemic hypoplasia,\r\n\r\n00:03:24.996 --\u003e 00:03:27.374\r\na rare condition that\r\nkept her from aging.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.792 --\u003e 00:03:31.169\r\nGORDON: Would you believe she\r\nwas 20 years old in that clip?\r\n\r\n00:03:31.753 --\u003e 00:03:33.422\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:33.505 --\u003e 00:03:35.465\r\nShe'd be about 30 now.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.426 --\u003e 00:03:40.178\r\nIt's obvious someone has a\r\nvendetta against these actors.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.345 --\u003e 00:03:41.945\r\nWe'll study this and\r\ncall you back if we-\r\n\r\n00:03:42.097 --\u003e 00:03:43.390\r\n\u003ci\u003eOFFICER: All units, all units!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:43.724 --\u003e 00:03:46.143\r\n- Gunfire reported at Gotham Rep.\r\n- (GUNFIRE IN BACKGROUND)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.226 --\u003e 00:03:47.894\r\n\u003ci\u003eThey're making a try for Vance.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:49.896 --\u003e 00:03:51.648\r\nStay down!\r\n\r\n00:03:54.067 --\u003e 00:03:55.652\r\nLet me go.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.027 --\u003e 00:03:58.613\r\n- Why are you doing this?\r\n- Quiet!\r\n\r\n00:03:58.780 --\u003e 00:04:00.866\r\nROBIN: The lady asked you a\r\nquestion, creep.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.116 --\u003e 00:04:02.159\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:03.034 --\u003e 00:04:04.411\r\nHow about an answer?\r\n\r\n00:04:09.833 --\u003e 00:04:11.209\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:13.962 --\u003e 00:04:15.422\r\n(TIRES SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:04:16.256 --\u003e 00:04:17.507\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:04:20.343 --\u003e 00:04:21.803\r\n- WOMAN: Ah!\r\n- Robin!\r\n\r\n00:04:25.932 --\u003e 00:04:27.559\r\n(TIRES SCREECHES)\r\n\r\n00:04:29.019 --\u003e 00:04:30.479\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:04:35.525 --\u003e 00:04:37.319\r\nNO. Help!\r\n\r\n00:04:42.073 --\u003e 00:04:44.034\r\n- They're getting away.\r\n- We'll get them.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.962 --\u003e 00:04:58.048\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- ROBIN: No!\r\n\r\n00:04:58.173 --\u003e 00:04:59.174\r\n(GIRL SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:05:02.135 --\u003e 00:05:03.345\r\nGIRL: Mommy!\r\n\r\n00:05:03.512 --\u003e 00:05:04.721\r\n(CROWD MURMURING)\r\n\r\n00:05:08.141 --\u003e 00:05:10.060\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.230 --\u003e 00:05:15.816\r\nGIRL: (SOBBING) I lost my mommy!\r\n\r\n00:05:16.483 --\u003e 00:05:17.692\r\nROBIN: It's okay.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.859 --\u003e 00:05:19.361\r\nOh, my baby.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.153 --\u003e 00:05:21.404\r\nMommy!\r\n\r\n00:05:21.571 --\u003e 00:05:22.989\r\nNaughty, naughty baby.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.156 --\u003e 00:05:25.075\r\nHaven't I told you\r\nnot to run off?\r\n\r\n00:05:25.492 --\u003e 00:05:27.619\r\nI didn't mean to.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.870 --\u003e 00:05:29.913\r\nHold it.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.039 --\u003e 00:05:32.874\r\nNaughty Mr. Batmans.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.083 --\u003e 00:05:34.376\r\nYou play too rough.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.710 --\u003e 00:05:37.087\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:05:41.591 --\u003e 00:05:42.759\r\nROBIN: I got 'em!\r\n\r\n00:05:43.844 --\u003e 00:05:45.178\r\nIt's me, dope.\r\n\r\n00:05:58.108 --\u003e 00:06:00.402\r\n(GROANING) Where am I?\r\n\r\n00:06:00.944 --\u003e 00:06:02.237\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:06:03.697 --\u003e 00:06:05.323\r\nIt can't be.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.202 --\u003e 00:06:12.372\r\n(GASPS) Tod, June, Brian?\r\n\r\n00:06:12.455 --\u003e 00:06:14.249\r\nTammy. She got you, too.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.416 --\u003e 00:06:16.084\r\nIs this some sort of bad joke?\r\n\r\n00:06:16.251 --\u003e 00:06:19.045\r\nWhat are we doing on the old set?\r\nAnd in these clothes?\r\n\r\n00:06:19.212 --\u003e 00:06:22.007\r\n- Welcome home, sister Suzy.\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.049 --\u003e 00:06:25.010\r\nI've missed you so.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.510 --\u003e 00:06:28.763\r\nMr. Happy-Head says he missed you, too.\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:29.014 --\u003e 00:06:30.849\r\nMary? Mary Dahl?\r\n\r\n00:06:31.016 --\u003e 00:06:32.350\r\nIs this a joke?\r\n\r\n00:06:32.559 --\u003e 00:06:35.312\r\nNo, sillies. I'm Baby, remember?\r\n\r\n00:06:35.478 --\u003e 00:06:39.274\r\nIt's Suzy and Tippy, and\r\nMumsy, and Daddy, and Baby,\r\n\r\n00:06:39.441 --\u003e 00:06:44.404\r\n\u003ci\u003etogether again\r\niorevers and avers.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:51.286 --\u003e 00:06:53.038\r\nI don't care what\r\nMayor Hill says.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.121 --\u003e 00:06:55.916\r\nThe people have a right to know,\r\nand if he won't talk to us-\r\n\r\n00:07:00.253 --\u003e 00:07:01.671\r\nI'll call you back, Marv.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.755 --\u003e 00:07:04.591\r\nSince when are you interested\r\nin has-been actors?\r\n\r\n00:07:04.841 --\u003e 00:07:07.761\r\nSince that one's been\r\nkidnapping her costars.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.928 --\u003e 00:07:08.970\r\nYou're serious?\r\n\r\n00:07:09.054 --\u003e 00:07:11.222\r\nShe's been picking them\r\noff, one by one.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.723 --\u003e 00:07:15.185\r\n- Any reason she'd have a grudge?\r\n- Actually, they should hate her.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.644 --\u003e 00:07:19.773\r\nDahl put them out of work when she quit\r\nthe series to become a dramatic actress.\r\n\r\n00:07:22.776 --\u003e 00:07:25.987\r\n\u003ci\u003eWhat, will these\r\nhands never be clean?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:26.154 --\u003e 00:07:28.865\r\n\u003ci\u003eHere's the smell\r\nof the blood still.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:29.240 --\u003e 00:07:33.370\r\n\u003ci\u003eAll the perfumes of Arabia will\r\nnot sweeten this little hand.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:33.662 --\u003e 00:07:35.121\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:36.247 --\u003e 00:07:37.499\r\nEw!\r\n\r\n00:07:37.624 --\u003e 00:07:39.125\r\nThat's what the critics said.\r\n\r\n00:07:39.334 --\u003e 00:07:43.004\r\nBaby's dramatic career flopped, and when\r\nshe tried to start her TV show again\r\n\r\n00:07:43.088 --\u003e 00:07:44.422\r\nthe networks turned her down.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.506 --\u003e 00:07:47.425\r\nThat still doesn't explain\r\nwhy she's after her old cast.\r\n\r\n00:07:47.676 --\u003e 00:07:50.261\r\nMaybe there's a clue\r\nin these old episodes.\r\n\r\n00:07:50.470 --\u003e 00:07:51.888\r\nYou can borrow them if you want.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.180 --\u003e 00:07:55.266\r\nAnd when you crack the case,\r\nyou can pay me back with an exclusive...\r\n\r\n00:07:56.685 --\u003e 00:07:57.978\r\nInterview.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.147 --\u003e 00:08:02.148\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.613 --\u003e 00:08:10.156\r\nBABY: Isn't this the best-est?\r\n\r\n00:08:10.907 --\u003e 00:08:14.452\r\nHaving breakfast,\r\njust like old times.\r\n\r\n00:08:14.828 --\u003e 00:08:18.331\r\n- Oh. Oh, it's swell, Baby.\r\n- Great.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.667 --\u003e 00:08:22.252\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:08:22.627 --\u003e 00:08:25.380\r\nHere comes Buster,\r\nbegging for scraps.\r\n\r\n00:08:31.469 --\u003e 00:08:33.847\r\n(DOG WHINING)\r\n\r\n00:08:35.890 --\u003e 00:08:37.017\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:08:37.267 --\u003e 00:08:38.685\r\nBad boy, Buster.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:39.936\r\n- Go away.\r\n- (DOG PANTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:40.770 --\u003e 00:08:41.980\r\n(CRASHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:43.023 --\u003e 00:08:44.816\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:45.984 --\u003e 00:08:48.611\r\nHey, guess what's today.\r\nAnybody know?\r\n\r\n00:08:50.321 --\u003e 00:08:52.657\r\nOh, Come on. Guess.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.451 --\u003e 00:08:55.910\r\n(WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:59.330 --\u003e 00:09:01.583\r\nIt's my births-day!\r\n\r\n00:09:01.666 --\u003e 00:09:03.752\r\nYaY, yay for me!\r\n\r\n00:09:04.085 --\u003e 00:09:06.254\r\nYou mean you had us brought here\r\n\r\n00:09:06.337 --\u003e 00:09:09.382\r\njust so you could throw\r\nyourself a surprise party?\r\n\r\n00:09:09.716 --\u003e 00:09:12.844\r\nThat's it. I always knew you\r\nwere a selfish little brat.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.386 --\u003e 00:09:15.221\r\nAlways throwing\r\nyour temper tantrums\r\n\r\n00:09:15.513 --\u003e 00:09:17.807\r\nand making life miserable\r\nfor the rest of us.\r\n\r\n00:09:17.891 --\u003e 00:09:20.226\r\nWell,\r\nthis time you've gone too far.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.310 --\u003e 00:09:22.645\r\nExpect a call from my lawyer.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.236 --\u003e 00:09:31.780\r\n\"HFya! \"(GRUNTs)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.697 --\u003e 00:09:36.034\r\n- Tod!\r\n- Isn't Mariams a treasure?\r\n\r\n00:09:36.117 --\u003e 00:09:38.828\r\nI couldn't gets through\r\nthe day without hers.\r\n\r\n00:09:39.079 --\u003e 00:09:41.414\r\nNaughty, naughty, Daddys.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.375 --\u003e 00:09:46.711\r\nMustn't yell at your\r\nBaby like thats.\r\n\r\n00:09:47.003 --\u003e 00:09:49.923\r\nYou're not my daughter.\r\nAnd we're not a family.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.423 --\u003e 00:09:51.966\r\nWe're actors, remember?\r\n\r\n00:09:52.258 --\u003e 00:09:56.137\r\nYou canceled our show because you whined\r\nyou weren't getting enough attention.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.221 --\u003e 00:09:58.556\r\nBut I knows now\r\nI made a boo-boo.\r\n\r\n00:09:59.099 --\u003e 00:10:00.475\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:10:03.895 --\u003e 00:10:05.688\r\n(MATURE VOICE) It was\r\nhard for me out there.\r\n\r\n00:10:05.772 --\u003e 00:10:08.775\r\nI studied and trained and\r\nauditioned, but no one wanted me.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.652 --\u003e 00:10:11.945\r\nAUDIENCE:\r\n\r\n00:10:17.575 --\u003e 00:10:21.121\r\nOver the years, I remembered how\r\nhappy I was with all of you around me,\r\n\r\n00:10:21.287 --\u003e 00:10:24.499\r\nand the folks at home\r\nwatching me each week. Me.\r\n\r\n00:10:25.375 --\u003e 00:10:26.626\r\n(GIRL'S VOICE) Baby-Doll.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.709 --\u003e 00:10:27.877\r\n(GIGGLES)\r\n\r\n00:10:29.295 --\u003e 00:10:32.882\r\nNow I'm Baby for good,\r\nand everyone will love me agains.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.966 --\u003e 00:10:34.342\r\nHugs, hugs!\r\n\r\n00:10:37.971 --\u003e 00:10:39.597\r\n- (RECORDER CLICKS)\r\n- AUDIENCE: Aww.\r\n\r\n00:10:44.727 --\u003e 00:10:48.565\r\nRemember that time Poison Ivy\r\nnearly smothered us in those vines\r\n\r\n00:10:49.023 --\u003e 00:10:50.775\r\nwith the really sharp thorns?\r\n\r\n00:10:51.151 --\u003e 00:10:53.987\r\n- Yes.\r\n- This is worse.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.404 --\u003e 00:10:55.947\r\nI did learn one thing, though.\r\n\r\n00:10:56.114 --\u003e 00:10:58.533\r\nBaby hasn't gotten every\r\nmember of her cast.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.159 --\u003e 00:11:01.953\r\nIn the last season,\r\nthe show's ratings began to drop,\r\n\r\n00:11:02.120 --\u003e 00:11:04.205\r\nso the producers\r\nintroduced a new character.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.706 --\u003e 00:11:06.541\r\nBaby's little cousin Spunky.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.712 --\u003e 00:11:11.713\r\n(CHUCKLING)\r\n\r\n00:11:11.796 --\u003e 00:11:12.797\r\nOh.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.173 --\u003e 00:11:17.510\r\nAccording to these, Dahl was furious\r\nshe was upstaged on her birthday episode\r\n\r\n00:11:17.594 --\u003e 00:11:19.137\r\nand walked off the series.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.638 --\u003e 00:11:23.183\r\nSo why hasn't she gone\r\nafter cousin Spunky?\r\n\r\n00:11:26.811 --\u003e 00:11:29.022\r\nMaybe she's waiting\r\nfor the right occasion.\r\n\r\n00:11:29.105 --\u003e 00:11:30.106\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:32.525 --\u003e 00:11:35.028\r\n(GUITAR PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:11:49.125 --\u003e 00:11:52.086\r\nExcuse me. Excuse me!\r\n\r\n00:11:52.545 --\u003e 00:11:55.256\r\nMy baby was taking a nap,\r\nand your music woke her up.\r\n\r\n00:11:55.506 --\u003e 00:11:57.342\r\nHey, I have to\r\npractice, you know?\r\n\r\n00:11:58.718 --\u003e 00:12:02.263\r\nYou're still a stinky\r\njerk-face, Spunky.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.722 --\u003e 00:12:04.432\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.143 --\u003e 00:12:08.478\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:12:11.814 --\u003e 00:12:13.399\r\nWake up, sleepyheads.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.944 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:12:17.278 --\u003e 00:12:19.489\r\nIt's time for my birthday party.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.697 --\u003e 00:12:21.074\r\n\"(GRUNTS) Yay!\"\r\n\r\n00:12:21.783 --\u003e 00:12:24.077\r\nWe're gonna have so much funs.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.580 --\u003e 00:12:30.917\r\n- Ready when you are, Ms. Dahl.\r\n- Goodies!\r\n\r\n00:12:32.043 --\u003e 00:12:35.505\r\nYou all remembers what happened\r\nthe last time I had a births-day.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.922 --\u003e 00:12:39.968\r\nPoopy old Spunkys pushed\r\nmy head in the cake.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.051 --\u003e 00:12:43.096\r\nEverybody laughed and laughed.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.429 --\u003e 00:12:46.557\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- Well, I'm laughing now.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.601 --\u003e 00:12:51.854\r\nWhat are you mad at me for?\r\nIt wasn't anything personal.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.939 --\u003e 00:12:55.525\r\nWe were just playing\r\ncharacters in a TV show.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.692 --\u003e 00:12:57.012\r\n(MATURE VOICE) It\r\nwas real to me.\r\n\r\n00:12:57.110 --\u003e 00:12:59.862\r\nEverybody loved Baby-Doll\r\nuntil you came along.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.029 --\u003e 00:13:01.948\r\nYou made them forget me.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.285 --\u003e 00:13:08.496\r\n(GIRL'S VOICE) Now\r\nBaby's gonna get evens.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.088 --\u003e 00:13:21.092\r\n- No, don't. Stop her.\r\n- WOMAN: Help! Wait!\r\n\r\n00:13:22.927 --\u003e 00:13:26.973\r\nIt's never too late to\r\nhave a happy childhood.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.193 --\u003e 00:13:42.822\r\nBlow out the candle, Spunky.\r\nBet your wish doesn't come trues.\r\n\r\n00:13:45.533 --\u003e 00:13:46.617\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:48.619 --\u003e 00:13:50.997\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.376 --\u003e 00:13:58.296\r\nCheater! Cheater!\r\nCheater! Cheater!\r\n\r\n00:14:03.134 --\u003e 00:14:04.218\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:14:04.719 --\u003e 00:14:07.722\r\nMr. Happy-Head says you're\r\nreally gonna get it nows.\r\n\r\n00:14:07.805 --\u003e 00:14:08.931\r\n(GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:14:10.725 --\u003e 00:14:11.726\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:15.021 --\u003e 00:14:16.272\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.106 --\u003e 00:14:18.191\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:14:21.986 --\u003e 00:14:23.363\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:14:24.822 --\u003e 00:14:25.823\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:33.039 --\u003e 00:14:34.665\r\nThanks, partner.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.749 --\u003e 00:14:36.209\r\nAnytime.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.712 --\u003e 00:14:41.881\r\nNo fairs. No fairs.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.090 --\u003e 00:14:44.467\r\nHe wasn't Spunky at alls.\r\n\r\n00:14:44.550 --\u003e 00:14:47.303\r\nI told Spunky what you were up to.\r\nWe switched places.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.470 --\u003e 00:14:50.556\r\nBatman rigged me with a\r\ntransmitter that led him here.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.640 --\u003e 00:14:54.352\r\nAh, aren't you Mr. Smarty-Heads.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.435 --\u003e 00:14:55.728\r\nMariam!\r\n\r\n00:15:02.360 --\u003e 00:15:03.611\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:05.822 --\u003e 00:15:09.117\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.580 --\u003e 00:15:16.290\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.836 --\u003e 00:15:22.088\r\nWow, lady, you're good.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.463 --\u003e 00:15:23.548\r\nIt's a living.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.923 --\u003e 00:15:25.258\r\nH I~ya!\r\n\r\n00:15:25.466 --\u003e 00:15:26.467\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:29.929 --\u003e 00:15:31.055\r\nH I~ya!\r\n\r\n00:15:43.234 --\u003e 00:15:45.945\r\nGet the hostages out.\r\nI'll go after Dahl.\r\n\r\n00:15:46.028 --\u003e 00:15:50.158\r\nRight. Hang on, folks.\r\nI'll have you back to reality in a second.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.957 --\u003e 00:15:59.083\r\n\u003ci\u003eYaw.!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.981\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:16:30.490 --\u003e 00:16:31.782\r\n(BELL DINGING)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.866 --\u003e 00:16:33.201\r\nMAN: Watch it, kid.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.620 --\u003e 00:16:37.205\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:16:46.631 --\u003e 00:16:47.632\r\nHmm.\r\n\r\n00:16:56.015 --\u003e 00:16:59.810\r\n- It's Batman.\r\n- Cool. Hey, Batman, down here.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.894 --\u003e 00:17:01.354\r\nHey, do you see what I see?\r\n\r\n00:17:01.812 --\u003e 00:17:04.232\r\n- Look at those people. It's Batman!\r\n- It's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:04.398 --\u003e 00:17:06.317\r\n- Look.\r\n- Wow, it's Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.526 --\u003e 00:17:08.152\r\n(EXCITED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:17:43.312 --\u003e 00:17:44.313\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:57.368 --\u003e 00:17:58.619\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.720 --\u003e 00:18:17.305\r\n(LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:18:22.184 --\u003e 00:18:25.980\r\n(CHUCKLING) Silly Mr. Batmans,\r\ncan't catch me.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.648 --\u003e 00:18:31.652\r\nDon't run away.\r\nI know you're scared, confused.\r\n\r\n00:18:31.902 --\u003e 00:18:35.656\r\n- I can help you.\r\n- Liar, liar, cape on fire.\r\n\r\n00:18:43.289 --\u003e 00:18:44.749\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:47.501 --\u003e 00:18:48.544\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:48.628 --\u003e 00:18:51.839\r\nNows we're playing by my rules.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.048 --\u003e 00:18:53.132\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:57.011 --\u003e 00:18:59.805\r\nGame's overs, Mr. Batman.\r\n\r\n00:19:00.181 --\u003e 00:19:01.432\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:19:01.515 --\u003e 00:19:02.975\r\nI wins.\r\n\r\n00:19:03.059 --\u003e 00:19:04.644\r\n(GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:07.229 --\u003e 00:19:09.065\r\n(GASPS) No fair!\r\n\r\n00:19:16.781 --\u003e 00:19:17.823\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:19:28.793 --\u003e 00:19:29.835\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:19:31.045 --\u003e 00:19:32.463\r\n(MATURE VOICE)\r\nThat's me in there.\r\n\r\n00:19:32.797 --\u003e 00:19:34.423\r\nThe real me.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.383 --\u003e 00:19:36.676\r\nThere I am.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.803 --\u003e 00:19:40.721\r\nBut it's not really real, is it?\r\n\r\n00:19:41.389 --\u003e 00:19:46.268\r\nJust made up and pretend like my\r\nfamily and my life and everything else.\r\n\r\n00:19:50.648 --\u003e 00:19:53.734\r\nWhy couldn't you just\r\nlet me make-believe?\r\n\r\n00:19:54.902 --\u003e 00:19:55.903\r\n(GUNSHOT)\r\n\r\n00:20:14.338 --\u003e 00:20:15.589\r\n(GUN CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:20:22.138 --\u003e 00:20:23.514\r\n(SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:20:32.732 --\u003e 00:20:33.733\r\n(SNIFFLES)\r\n\r\n00:20:34.442 --\u003e 00:20:36.485\r\nI didn't mean to.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.116 --\u003e 00:20:44.118\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.851 --\u003e 00:21:09.852\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E05 - Time Out of Joint (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.715 --\u003e 00:00:08.717\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.541 --\u003e 00:01:27.462\r\nSold, ladies and gentlemen, to Ms.\r\nVeronica Vreeland for $200,000.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.588 --\u003e 00:01:28.714\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:01:28.797 --\u003e 00:01:31.425\r\nBRUCE: Bored?\r\nWe've only been here 10 minutes.\r\n\r\n00:01:31.633 --\u003e 00:01:34.386\r\nDICK: Ten minutes for\r\nyou, 10 hours for me.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.970 --\u003e 00:01:36.972\r\nI know it's for a good\r\ncause, but...\r\n\r\n00:01:37.889 --\u003e 00:01:39.057\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:01:39.474 --\u003e 00:01:42.185\r\nAnd now, ladies and gentlemen,\r\nthis magnificent timepiece\r\n\r\n00:01:42.269 --\u003e 00:01:43.854\r\nfrom the reign of Louis XVI.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.479 --\u003e 00:01:46.690\r\nWho will start the\r\nbidding at $400,000?\r\n\r\n00:01:46.815 --\u003e 00:01:50.736\r\nYou've gotta be kidding.\r\nI wouldn't use that for a doorstop.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.503 --\u003e 00:02:11.131\r\nRight on time, as usual.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.679 --\u003e 00:02:20.766\r\nI have a bid of $500,000.\r\nDo I hear $550,000?\r\n\r\n00:02:21.850 --\u003e 00:02:22.976\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:24.686 --\u003e 00:02:25.979\r\nGood afternoon.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.230 --\u003e 00:02:29.232\r\nHave they sold\r\nthe Louis XVI yet?\r\n\r\n00:02:29.816 --\u003e 00:02:32.277\r\nNo, the bidding just started.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.361 --\u003e 00:02:33.362\r\nHow did you...\r\n\r\n00:02:37.032 --\u003e 00:02:38.450\r\nI gotta see my optometrist.\r\n\r\n00:02:41.828 --\u003e 00:02:44.790\r\nI have a bid of $585,000.\r\nDo I hear six?\r\n\r\n00:02:45.248 --\u003e 00:02:49.169\r\nCome, come. This is a one-of-a-kind item\r\nladies and gentlemen. Who'll give six?\r\n\r\n00:02:50.671 --\u003e 00:02:51.838\r\nSix hundred thousand.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.047 --\u003e 00:02:53.632\r\nSix hundred thousand?\r\n\r\n00:02:53.965 --\u003e 00:02:56.885\r\nI've heard that time is\r\nmoney, but this is ridiculous.\r\n\r\n00:02:57.260 --\u003e 00:02:59.346\r\nLike you said, it's for charity.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.430 --\u003e 00:03:04.643\r\nI have $600,000 from Mr. Bruce Wayne.\r\nDo I hear $650,000?\r\n\r\n00:03:05.268 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\nNeed I remind you, this timepiece\r\nwas once owned by Marie Antoinette.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.695 --\u003e 00:03:16.488\r\nRelax, Dick. It's almost over.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.863 --\u003e 00:03:20.283\r\nYou're not gonna believe this,\r\nbut I thought I just saw the Clock King.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.704 --\u003e 00:03:25.205\r\nWell, he was there.\r\n\r\n00:03:25.455 --\u003e 00:03:29.126\r\nI have $650,000.\r\nGoing, going, gone.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.003 --\u003e 00:03:33.588\r\n(GASPS) Blimey!\r\n\r\n00:03:47.561 --\u003e 00:03:50.772\r\nA trial run,\r\nand it went like clockwork.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.484 --\u003e 00:03:56.153\r\nHmm. Got one.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.580 --\u003e 00:04:10.459\r\n\u003ci\u003eI have $650,000.\r\nGoing, going, gone.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:12.919 --\u003e 00:04:14.629\r\n\u003ci\u003e(exams) Blimey!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:15.005 --\u003e 00:04:16.339\r\nBack up.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.677 --\u003e 00:04:22.429\r\nThere. Freeze \u003ci\u003eit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:27.893 --\u003e 00:04:29.978\r\nThat must be the hand\r\neveryone talks about.\r\n\r\n00:04:30.520 --\u003e 00:04:32.355\r\nThe one that's\r\nquicker than the eye.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.106 --\u003e 00:04:36.109\r\nSo we don't have another\r\ninvisible man running loose.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.193 --\u003e 00:04:37.277\r\nThen who could it be?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.028 --\u003e 00:04:40.489\r\nI think it's Temple\r\nFugate, the Clock King.\r\n\r\n00:04:41.198 --\u003e 00:04:42.365\r\nWhat makes you think that?\r\n\r\n00:04:42.699 --\u003e 00:04:44.242\r\nLet's just call it a hunch.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.618 --\u003e 00:04:46.161\r\nBetter warn Mayor Hill, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.495 --\u003e 00:04:48.747\r\nI doubt that time has\r\nhealed Fugate's wound.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.364 --\u003e 00:05:24.991\r\n6:15, sir. Time for breakfast.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.909 --\u003e 00:05:28.411\r\nI've also brought you your\r\nmedicine and the timer\r\n\r\n00:05:28.495 --\u003e 00:05:30.831\r\nso you can take your\r\npills on schedule.\r\n\r\n00:05:30.914 --\u003e 00:05:33.416\r\nYou think of everything,\r\ndon't you, Harold?\r\n\r\n00:05:33.500 --\u003e 00:05:35.544\r\nIt is my job, sir.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.961 --\u003e 00:05:38.296\r\nHow goes your\r\nresearch, if I may ask?\r\n\r\n00:05:38.380 --\u003e 00:05:39.464\r\nWell enough.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.798 --\u003e 00:05:42.384\r\nThe iron ball has dropped a\r\nmere tenth of a millimeter\r\n\r\n00:05:42.467 --\u003e 00:05:44.594\r\nsince the experiment\r\nbegan last week.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.095 --\u003e 00:05:47.389\r\nAn extreme temporal\r\ndiscontinuity.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.472 --\u003e 00:05:50.308\r\nAnd the accelerated effect\r\nis just as dramatic.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.392 --\u003e 00:05:53.979\r\nFive minutes ago,\r\nthat plant was a seed.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.604 --\u003e 00:05:56.481\r\nAmazing, Dr. Wakati.\r\n\r\n00:05:56.773 --\u003e 00:05:59.734\r\nWhy, the possible applications\r\nare mind-boggling.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.818 --\u003e 00:06:00.861\r\nIndeed.\r\n\r\n00:06:00.944 --\u003e 00:06:04.447\r\nWe could get rid of radioactive\r\nwaste in minutes instead of eons\r\n\r\n00:06:04.823 --\u003e 00:06:08.201\r\nput terminally ill people in\r\nstasis until a cure is found.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.827 --\u003e 00:06:14.541\r\nThe question is, is mankind civilized\r\nenough to make the proper use of it?\r\n\r\n00:06:15.166 --\u003e 00:06:16.501\r\nYou're right, Doctor.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.585 --\u003e 00:06:20.839\r\nIt's very important that this\r\ndevice be kept in the right hands.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.774 --\u003e 00:06:42.694\r\nI hope you're having a pleasant\r\nevening, Mr. Mayor,\r\n\r\n00:06:42.777 --\u003e 00:06:47.198\r\nbecause it's time for you and\r\nme to renew our acquaintance.\r\n\r\n00:07:05.383 --\u003e 00:07:07.427\r\nIt's going to be a big\r\nceremony, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:07:09.971 --\u003e 00:07:12.432\r\nFugate? No, I'm not worried.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.515 --\u003e 00:07:15.185\r\nI've got a platoon of\r\nofficers around the building.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.560 --\u003e 00:07:18.355\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe can't get in the door without\r\nbumping into a blue coat.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:19.147 --\u003e 00:07:22.317\r\nHe's still on the phone.\r\nYou really think our guy will show up?\r\n\r\n00:07:23.568 --\u003e 00:07:25.737\r\nSure as night follows day.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.278 --\u003e 00:08:09.114\r\n(CHUCKLES) What am I thinking?\r\n\r\n00:08:19.541 --\u003e 00:08:21.876\r\nGoing to be a nasty\r\nfall, dearie.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.681 --\u003e 00:08:35.921\r\n- What the...\r\n- (RAPID KNOCKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:36.057 --\u003e 00:08:37.183\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:08:37.350 --\u003e 00:08:38.727\r\nI think that's our cue.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.145 --\u003e 00:08:42.188\r\nYou! How did you get past-\r\n\r\n00:08:42.439 --\u003e 00:08:43.732\r\nGood evening, Mayor.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.982 --\u003e 00:08:46.151\r\nNice to see you again too.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.527 --\u003e 00:08:49.654\r\nAnd whose life are\r\nyou ruining now?\r\n\r\n00:08:49.821 --\u003e 00:08:51.072\r\nA poor pensioner,\r\n\r\n00:08:51.239 --\u003e 00:08:53.199\r\na malnourished orphan perhaps?\r\n\r\n00:08:57.120 --\u003e 00:08:58.371\r\nNaughty, naughty.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.040 --\u003e 00:09:01.041\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:09:01.124 --\u003e 00:09:02.751\r\nWhere did you...\r\n\r\n00:09:08.840 --\u003e 00:09:10.175\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.425 --\u003e 00:09:12.093\r\nEven if you could\r\nclimb the building,\r\n\r\n00:09:12.302 --\u003e 00:09:14.596\r\nyou won't be leaving this\r\nway, Mr. Mayor.\r\n\r\n00:09:14.804 --\u003e 00:09:17.891\r\nI've waited a long\r\ntime for this.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.558 --\u003e 00:09:20.351\r\nPlease, Fugate, don't hurt me.\r\n\r\n00:09:20.560 --\u003e 00:09:24.272\r\nIf it's any comfort, my revenge\r\nwill encompass more than just you.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.481 --\u003e 00:09:29.944\r\nI intend to pass a most timely\r\nsentence on the entire judicial system.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.236 --\u003e 00:09:31.738\r\nGet ready.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.698 --\u003e 00:09:34.908\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:09:34.991 --\u003e 00:09:36.284\r\nMy eyes!\r\n\r\n00:09:38.870 --\u003e 00:09:40.914\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:47.378 --\u003e 00:09:48.880\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:10:02.727 --\u003e 00:10:04.104\r\nRobin. Grab the hypo.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.649 --\u003e 00:10:09.192\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:13.238 --\u003e 00:10:14.697\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:37.679 --\u003e 00:10:39.139\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:44.978 --\u003e 00:10:46.187\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:10:48.022 --\u003e 00:10:49.524\r\nGet off me.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.150 --\u003e 00:10:51.192\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:10:56.156 --\u003e 00:10:57.740\r\nYou clumsy...\r\n\r\n00:10:57.907 --\u003e 00:10:59.617\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:59.951 --\u003e 00:11:01.494\r\nYou...\r\n\r\n00:11:07.709 --\u003e 00:11:09.002\r\nHey, you. Stop!\r\n\r\n00:11:14.591 --\u003e 00:11:16.593\r\nLook. Over there. That's him.\r\nLet's get him.\r\n\r\n00:11:16.676 --\u003e 00:11:18.219\r\n- Come on.\r\n- Stop.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.139 --\u003e 00:11:23.391\r\n- Hold it right there.\r\n- You're under arrest.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.474 --\u003e 00:11:24.559\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:11:26.477 --\u003e 00:11:27.937\r\n- Don't move.\r\n- Freeze.\r\n\r\n00:11:41.826 --\u003e 00:11:43.244\r\nThe Batmobile.\r\n\r\n00:11:44.787 --\u003e 00:11:45.914\r\nAh!\r\n\r\n00:11:46.539 --\u003e 00:11:47.916\r\n- Hey!\r\n- Where'd he go?\r\n\r\n00:11:48.082 --\u003e 00:11:49.417\r\n- Look out.\r\n- Hey, watch it.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.252 --\u003e 00:11:53.087\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:11:55.048 --\u003e 00:11:56.591\r\nIt was like a nightmare.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.050 --\u003e 00:11:59.385\r\nFirst he was here, then there.\r\n\r\n00:11:59.677 --\u003e 00:12:01.930\r\nMy heavens.\r\nIf you hadn't set that trap...\r\n\r\n00:12:02.597 --\u003e 00:12:05.683\r\nWell, at least we've got the pieces\r\nfrom Fugate's broken thingamajig.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.767 --\u003e 00:12:07.310\r\nMaybe we can find\r\nout how he made it.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.770 --\u003e 00:12:10.980\r\nI don't think Fugate\r\nmade that device.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.523 --\u003e 00:12:13.691\r\nHe's not a scientist.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.775 --\u003e 00:12:16.069\r\nWell,\r\nwe'll soon find out who did.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.445 --\u003e 00:12:19.989\r\nAll our patrol cars are\r\nequipped with tracking devices.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.198 --\u003e 00:12:22.450\r\nWe should be able to run\r\nFugate down pretty quickly.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.079 --\u003e 00:12:27.372\r\nHarold.\r\n\r\n00:12:29.582 --\u003e 00:12:30.667\r\nHarold.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.459 --\u003e 00:12:32.919\r\nWhat are you doing in my room?\r\n\r\n00:12:33.002 --\u003e 00:12:35.338\r\nI called for you\r\nbut got no answer.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.421 --\u003e 00:12:37.257\r\nI thought something\r\nmight be wrong.\r\n\r\n00:12:37.590 --\u003e 00:12:40.802\r\nThere is something\r\nwrong, old man.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.053 --\u003e 00:12:43.763\r\nWhy are you wearing that?\r\n\r\n00:12:43.930 --\u003e 00:12:47.183\r\nI'm afraid I haven't been\r\naltogether candid with you.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.101 --\u003e 00:12:49.936\r\nWhat...\r\nWhat are you going to do?\r\n\r\n00:12:50.770 --\u003e 00:12:54.649\r\nYou'll find out, my good\r\ndoctor, all in good time.\r\n\r\n00:13:00.238 --\u003e 00:13:02.448\r\nI want a dragnet over\r\na five-mile radius.\r\n\r\n00:13:04.534 --\u003e 00:13:07.704\r\nHe couldn't have gotten far.\r\nWith any luck, time is on our side.\r\n\r\n00:13:15.920 --\u003e 00:13:17.547\r\nYou think the police\r\nwill find him?\r\n\r\n00:13:18.631 --\u003e 00:13:20.508\r\nBATMAN: Doubtful,\r\nbut I have an idea.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.675 --\u003e 00:13:22.427\r\nWith his knowledge\r\nof train schedules.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.510 --\u003e 00:13:24.846\r\nHe would know when the next\r\ncommuter run would pass.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.263 --\u003e 00:13:27.515\r\nIt's no accident that he\r\nditched the car where he did.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.057 --\u003e 00:13:31.686\r\nOnly one train passed there in the last\r\nsix hours, heading for the mountains.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.186 --\u003e 00:13:34.105\r\nI don't get it.\r\nThere's nothing out that way.\r\n\r\n00:13:34.772 --\u003e 00:13:37.567\r\nNothing except Cranston Estates.\r\n\r\n00:13:44.073 --\u003e 00:13:45.950\r\nROBIN: So you say this\r\nguy lives out there?\r\n\r\n00:13:46.034 --\u003e 00:13:48.286\r\nWhat's his name,\r\nthis Professor Wataki?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.619 --\u003e 00:13:52.206\r\nWakati. He's the father of\r\nquantum temporal theory,\r\n\r\n00:13:52.290 --\u003e 00:13:54.292\r\n- the structure of time.\r\n- (DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:02.508 --\u003e 00:14:03.676\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:14:05.011 --\u003e 00:14:06.179\r\nROBIN: What's going on?\r\n\r\n00:14:06.262 --\u003e 00:14:08.097\r\nFugate's booby-trapped the car.\r\n\r\n00:14:08.473 --\u003e 00:14:10.391\r\nWe're trapped in time.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.487 --\u003e 00:14:24.197\r\nROBIN: What's going on?\r\n\r\n00:14:24.906 --\u003e 00:14:26.991\r\nWe've been put in a\r\nbubble of slow time.\r\n\r\n00:14:27.241 --\u003e 00:14:29.619\r\nThe outside world is moving\r\nmuch faster than we are.\r\n\r\n00:14:29.994 --\u003e 00:14:31.162\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.662 --\u003e 00:14:33.831\r\nHours are passing like minutes.\r\n\r\n00:14:35.333 --\u003e 00:14:37.502\r\nWhy didn't the car's sensors\r\npick up the booby trap?\r\n\r\n00:14:37.960 --\u003e 00:14:41.464\r\nHe probably set it just a nanosecond\r\nor two out of phase with reality.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.756 --\u003e 00:14:43.341\r\nBut that's the least\r\nof our problems.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.716 --\u003e 00:14:46.844\r\nE still equals MC\r\nsquared, last I heard.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.095 --\u003e 00:14:48.930\r\nMass increases with speed.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.263 --\u003e 00:14:51.516\r\nIf a car hits us while\r\nwe're frozen like this,\r\n\r\n00:14:51.599 --\u003e 00:14:53.643\r\nwe might trigger an\r\natomic explosion.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.649 --\u003e 00:15:01.109\r\nThere it is.\r\n\r\n00:15:02.819 --\u003e 00:15:03.820\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:15:13.287 --\u003e 00:15:14.622\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:27.301 --\u003e 00:15:30.763\r\nNearly as I can figure,\r\nwe've lost almost 48 hours.\r\n\r\n00:15:31.305 --\u003e 00:15:32.905\r\nThen we'd better not\r\nwaste any more time.\r\n\r\n00:15:58.458 --\u003e 00:16:00.293\r\nI think we've found\r\nthe professor.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.174 --\u003e 00:16:07.383\r\nHow do we get him out?\r\n\r\n00:16:08.301 --\u003e 00:16:10.136\r\nSame way we got ourselves out.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.768 --\u003e 00:16:19.103\r\nDon't, Harold.\r\n\r\n00:16:19.479 --\u003e 00:16:20.563\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:16:28.738 --\u003e 00:16:30.907\r\nJust make sure nobody\r\nfiddles with the props.\r\n\r\n00:16:32.742 --\u003e 00:16:33.910\r\nNo problem.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.266 --\u003e 00:16:59.852\r\n(HUMMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:05.191 --\u003e 00:17:07.735\r\nDR. WAKATI: He was the one\r\nperson in the world I trusted.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.818 --\u003e 00:17:11.030\r\nIs it any wonder I\r\nprefer being a recluse?\r\n\r\n00:17:11.906 --\u003e 00:17:14.116\r\nBATMAN: What else did he\r\nsay, Dr. Wakati?\r\n\r\n00:17:14.325 --\u003e 00:17:15.826\r\nHe was babbling.\r\n\r\n00:17:15.993 --\u003e 00:17:18.496\r\nSaid something about the Mayor,\r\n\r\n00:17:18.788 --\u003e 00:17:21.707\r\nabout how he was finally\r\ngoing to get his day in court.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.124 --\u003e 00:17:23.334\r\nDay in court?\r\n\r\n00:17:24.168 --\u003e 00:17:25.378\r\nThe new courthouse.\r\n\r\n00:17:25.836 --\u003e 00:17:28.130\r\nThe Mayor is dedicating\r\nit today at 10:00.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.048 --\u003e 00:17:31.634\r\nThat's two minutes from now.\r\nWe'd better call the cops and-\r\n\r\n00:17:31.801 --\u003e 00:17:33.970\r\nYou can't. I have no phones.\r\n\r\n00:17:35.221 --\u003e 00:17:38.307\r\nYour phone won't work, Batman.\r\nThis area is a dead zone.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.516 --\u003e 00:17:42.853\r\nI chose it so my experiments would be\r\nfree of electromagnetic interference.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.479 --\u003e 00:17:46.315\r\nIt'll take at least a half hour for\r\nus to make it back on the bikes.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.735 --\u003e 00:17:52.405\r\nYou have 30 seconds to\r\nshow us how to use these.\r\n\r\n00:18:08.879 --\u003e 00:18:11.591\r\nWow,\r\nfaster than a speeding bullet.\r\n\r\n00:18:14.385 --\u003e 00:18:17.555\r\nMAYOR HILL: \u003ci\u003eAnd so, my\r\nfriends, it is my privilege\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:17.763 --\u003e 00:18:21.767\r\n\u003ci\u003eto officially bring Gotham\r\nCity's new courthouse to order.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:22.018 --\u003e 00:18:26.939\r\nBy all means, Mr. Mayor,\r\nusher the new building in with a bang.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.818 --\u003e 00:18:32.111\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:18:34.071 --\u003e 00:18:35.489\r\n(LAUGHTER)\r\n\r\n00:18:36.198 --\u003e 00:18:39.160\r\nThis could be dangerous.\r\nBetter stand back.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.786 --\u003e 00:18:44.915\r\nOh, to savor the moment\r\nas long as possible.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.166 --\u003e 00:18:46.167\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:06.479 --\u003e 00:19:07.897\r\nNo. It can't be.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.906 --\u003e 00:19:18.449\r\nToo late. It's triggered.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.246 --\u003e 00:19:25.581\r\n(RAPID BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:27.249 --\u003e 00:19:28.876\r\nSlow down.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.269 --\u003e 00:19:49.397\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:50.523 --\u003e 00:19:51.857\r\n(PEOPLE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.950 --\u003e 00:20:02.159\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:20:08.999 --\u003e 00:20:11.544\r\nLooks like time just ran out.\r\n\r\n00:20:13.963 --\u003e 00:20:15.339\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:20:22.680 --\u003e 00:20:25.224\r\nIt's a shame that you've decided\r\nto keep this device a secret.\r\n\r\n00:20:25.641 --\u003e 00:20:28.769\r\nIt would seem that the world\r\nis not quite ready for it yet.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.061 --\u003e 00:20:30.813\r\nGee, that's too bad for Fugate.\r\n\r\n00:20:31.355 --\u003e 00:20:32.666\r\nI'm sure he'll wish\r\nhe had something\r\n\r\n00:20:32.690 --\u003e 00:20:34.734\r\n\u003ci\u003eto make the days pass\r\nquicker where he's going.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:47.913 --\u003e 00:20:49.915\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E06 - Harley's Holiday (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.924 --\u003e 00:00:09.176\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:18.620 --\u003e 00:01:20.620\r\n\u003ci\u003eDR. LELAND: You've made\r\nwonderful progress, Harley.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:20.831 --\u003e 00:01:22.624\r\nYou've passed your\r\ncompetency hearing\r\n\r\n00:01:22.708 --\u003e 00:01:25.669\r\nand tomorrow you'll be released,\r\nmentally sane and sound.\r\n\r\n00:01:26.003 --\u003e 00:01:30.299\r\nWhee! Who-hoo! Whoopie!\r\nYay! Yay! Yay!\r\n\r\n00:01:31.133 --\u003e 00:01:33.385\r\nI mean, thank you, Dr. Leland.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.885 --\u003e 00:01:37.097\r\nThat's okay. You have every\r\nreason to be proud of yourself.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.264 --\u003e 00:01:38.557\r\nSCARECROW: Unhand me!\r\n\r\n00:01:38.724 --\u003e 00:01:42.060\r\nI just wish the other inmates\r\ncould make your sort of progress.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.269 --\u003e 00:01:45.731\r\nI am the master of fear!\r\nThe lord of despair!\r\n\r\n00:01:45.897 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\nCower before me\r\nin witless terror!\r\n\r\n00:01:47.983 --\u003e 00:01:49.860\r\nHi, Professor Crane.\r\n\r\n00:01:50.193 --\u003e 00:01:54.323\r\nGood evening, child.\r\nWorship me, fools! Worship me!\r\n\r\n00:01:54.406 --\u003e 00:01:57.492\r\nScream hosannas of\r\nanguish to Scarecrow,\r\n\r\n00:01:57.576 --\u003e 00:02:00.120\r\nthe all-terrible god of fear!\r\n\r\n00:02:00.621 --\u003e 00:02:01.913\r\nI think he's getting better.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.707 --\u003e 00:02:05.542\r\nI hear you're\r\ngetting out tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:02:05.709 --\u003e 00:02:07.628\r\nYou got a problem with that?\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:02:08.378 --\u003e 00:02:09.755\r\nBATMAN: Congratulations.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.050 --\u003e 00:02:15.010\r\nYeah, so I made a few mistakes.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.177 --\u003e 00:02:18.472\r\nI've got my head back together,\r\nand I'm gonna live my life right.\r\n\r\n00:02:25.187 --\u003e 00:02:27.272\r\nFor your sake, I hope so.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.859 --\u003e 00:02:35.614\r\nI'll show you. Starting tomorrow,\r\nyou'll see I'm just as sane as anybody.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.449 --\u003e 00:02:38.492\r\nOh, my Lord!\r\n\r\n00:02:38.617 --\u003e 00:02:40.786\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:50.420 --\u003e 00:02:52.214\r\nGee, what's wrong with them?\r\n\r\n00:02:54.091 --\u003e 00:02:55.691\r\nI knew I shouldn't\r\nhave worn this outfit.\r\n\r\n00:02:56.176 --\u003e 00:02:58.387\r\nIt's so out of style,\r\nit's growing mold.\r\n\r\n00:02:58.845 --\u003e 00:03:01.348\r\nI probably look\r\nlike a total geek.\r\n\r\n00:03:07.896 --\u003e 00:03:10.691\r\nCome on, babies,\r\nwe're going shopping.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.735 --\u003e 00:03:15.278\r\n(BOTH WHINING)\r\n\r\n00:03:18.323 --\u003e 00:03:19.700\r\nI love it.\r\n\r\n00:03:19.783 --\u003e 00:03:21.034\r\nThat makes one of us.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.243 --\u003e 00:03:25.205\r\nReally, Brucie, a man of your social\r\nstanding needs a woman like me\r\n\r\n00:03:25.288 --\u003e 00:03:27.082\r\nto keep you in step\r\nwith the latest trends.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.791 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nWho dresses you anyway? Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:03:30.585 --\u003e 00:03:33.046\r\nWell, actually...\r\n\r\n00:03:34.548 --\u003e 00:03:37.134\r\n(HYENAS BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.300 --\u003e 00:03:39.761\r\nExcuse me, miss.\r\nYou can't bring those things in here.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.345 --\u003e 00:03:42.764\r\nIt's okay. They're housebroken.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.808 --\u003e 00:03:46.935\r\n- (PEOPLE GASPING)\r\n- (BOTH GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.523 --\u003e 00:03:52.649\r\n(HARLEY YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:55.068 --\u003e 00:03:57.028\r\n- Are you all right?\r\n- (HYENAS BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:58.989 --\u003e 00:04:01.950\r\nWow, I never saw\r\nthem do that before.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.951 --\u003e 00:04:04.870\r\nHey, don't I know you?\r\n\r\n00:04:05.245 --\u003e 00:04:06.955\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.914 --\u003e 00:04:10.083\r\nSomething about that chin.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.542 --\u003e 00:04:14.921\r\nI know! You're Bruce\r\nWayne, the boy billionaire.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.715 --\u003e 00:04:19.134\r\nUnattached, I see.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.426 --\u003e 00:04:20.719\r\n(VERONICA CLEARS THROAT)\r\n\r\n00:04:21.094 --\u003e 00:04:22.262\r\nMay I help you, miss?\r\n\r\n00:04:22.804 --\u003e 00:04:25.474\r\nUh-oh!\r\nEnter the jealous girlfriend.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.183 --\u003e 00:04:29.394\r\nHey, remember me?\r\nThat big charity bash a few years back?\r\n\r\n00:04:29.644 --\u003e 00:04:30.854\r\nThe one the Joker robbed?\r\n\r\n00:04:31.021 --\u003e 00:04:33.815\r\nI was the clown girl\r\nholding the gun on you!\r\n\r\n00:04:35.192 --\u003e 00:04:38.111\r\nOh, don't worry,\r\nI'm over the crime thing. See?\r\n\r\n00:04:42.699 --\u003e 00:04:46.536\r\nI'm rehabilitated and ready\r\nto live my life right.\r\n\r\n00:04:47.204 --\u003e 00:04:48.330\r\nHow nice for you.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.997 --\u003e 00:04:50.373\r\nGoodbye.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.875 --\u003e 00:04:55.337\r\nGee, you make one little mistake\r\nand they never let you forget.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.506 --\u003e 00:05:00.383\r\nAll I'm looking for is a\r\nfair chance to start over.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.636\r\nThat's not asking too\r\nmuch, is it?\r\n\r\n00:05:02.886 --\u003e 00:05:04.304\r\nWhy, no.\r\n\r\n00:05:09.100 --\u003e 00:05:10.143\r\nMiss?\r\n\r\n00:05:10.769 --\u003e 00:05:15.398\r\nI just wanna live a normal life\r\nwithout some cop always pouncing on me.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.649 --\u003e 00:05:17.567\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:05:17.818 --\u003e 00:05:19.236\r\nHey, what's the deal?\r\n\r\n00:05:19.569 --\u003e 00:05:20.612\r\nHold it.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.821 --\u003e 00:05:22.155\r\nI didn't do anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:22.447 --\u003e 00:05:24.407\r\nThat's a security alarm.\r\nJust give me back-\r\n\r\n00:05:24.491 --\u003e 00:05:26.117\r\n(SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:26.243 --\u003e 00:05:29.412\r\nThat's my dress.\r\nI paid for it fair and square.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.663 --\u003e 00:05:33.208\r\nI know. Just let me remove\r\nthe security tag and-Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:05:33.416 --\u003e 00:05:35.168\r\nIt's a frame-up, a fix.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.335 --\u003e 00:05:38.338\r\nYou ain't taking me back to the\r\nslammer, John Law.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.466 --\u003e 00:05:42.968\r\n(HYENAS SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:43.260 --\u003e 00:05:44.302\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:05:46.763 --\u003e 00:05:48.765\r\n- What in heaven?\r\n- Stay here.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.395 --\u003e 00:05:54.521\r\nShe ran in there.\r\n\r\n00:05:54.729 --\u003e 00:05:57.190\r\n- Oh, my. Did you see that?\r\n- What's going on?\r\n\r\n00:06:01.695 --\u003e 00:06:05.615\r\nMiss, please, I'm sure this has\r\nall been a simple misunderstanding.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.283 --\u003e 00:06:10.537\r\nYou don't wanna mess things up on\r\nyour first day out, do you? Miss?\r\n\r\n00:06:10.620 --\u003e 00:06:12.914\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.583 --\u003e 00:06:17.502\r\nI tried to play by the\r\nrules, but no,\r\n\r\n00:06:17.711 --\u003e 00:06:21.256\r\nthey wouldn't let me go straight.\r\nSociety is to blame.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.507 --\u003e 00:06:26.052\r\n- Back off, rich boy, I'm armed.\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:31.141 --\u003e 00:06:32.142\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.894 --\u003e 00:06:36.813\r\nScoot over, toots, I'm driving.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.105 --\u003e 00:06:38.815\r\n(WHISTLES) Come to Mommy!\r\n\r\n00:06:42.402 --\u003e 00:06:43.653\r\n(VERONICA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:47.991 --\u003e 00:06:49.534\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n- Hold on!\r\n\r\n00:06:49.993 --\u003e 00:06:51.453\r\n- (TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n- (SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:06:57.918 --\u003e 00:07:00.003\r\nOh! You're gonna pay for that.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.802 --\u003e 00:07:10.430\r\nGENERAL VREELAND: Let me get this\r\nright, Commissioner.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.139 --\u003e 00:07:13.892\r\nYou're saying that\r\nmilksop Bruce Wayne\r\n\r\n00:07:13.975 --\u003e 00:07:17.812\r\nallowed a crazy woman in a clown\r\nsuit to kidnap my Veronica?\r\n\r\n00:07:17.896 --\u003e 00:07:19.856\r\nWayne did what he\r\ncould, General Vreeland.\r\n\r\n00:07:20.065 --\u003e 00:07:23.151\r\nAnd for what it's worth, I don't think\r\nHarley Quinn means to hurt Veronica.\r\n\r\n00:07:23.234 --\u003e 00:07:24.736\r\nThis is her first\r\nday out of Arkham\r\n\r\n00:07:24.819 --\u003e 00:07:26.964\r\nand the threat of being sent\r\nback probably spooked her.\r\n\r\n00:07:26.988 --\u003e 00:07:30.700\r\nI want action, Gordon, not excuses.\r\nMy daughter's in danger.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.909 --\u003e 00:07:34.788\r\nI need SWAT teams, helicopters,\r\nfull military backup!\r\n\r\n00:07:38.625 --\u003e 00:07:40.001\r\nI... I'm sorry, Jim.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.377 --\u003e 00:07:43.380\r\nAll I want is my little Veronica\r\nreturned safe and sound.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.172 --\u003e 00:07:48.218\r\nIf you could just give this old\r\nsoldier a moment to compose himself.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.635 --\u003e 00:07:49.761\r\nCertainly, sir.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.648 --\u003e 00:08:03.358\r\nLieutenant,\r\nGeneral Vreeland here.\r\n\r\n00:08:03.733 --\u003e 00:08:05.360\r\nI'm calling a code red.\r\n\r\n00:08:08.571 --\u003e 00:08:11.011\r\nSounds like Harley didn't waste\r\nany time getting into trouble.\r\n\r\n00:08:11.324 --\u003e 00:08:12.534\r\nShe's good at that.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.286 --\u003e 00:08:18.456\r\nStill, I think she really\r\nwanted to do right this time.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.873 --\u003e 00:08:22.502\r\nIf we can find her first, maybe we\r\ncan stop her from ruining her chance.\r\n\r\n00:08:23.545 --\u003e 00:08:25.338\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:08:25.422 --\u003e 00:08:29.426\r\nAccording to the scanner,\r\nyour car should be right about here.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.551 --\u003e 00:08:31.511\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:36.182 --\u003e 00:08:37.267\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:39.769 --\u003e 00:08:41.479\r\nHa! I got you now.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.230 --\u003e 00:08:44.357\r\n(VERONICA SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:08:49.320 --\u003e 00:08:50.321\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:09:00.915 --\u003e 00:09:02.459\r\nPlease, Ms. Clown.\r\n\r\n00:09:02.542 --\u003e 00:09:04.711\r\nCall me Harley. Everyone does.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.961 --\u003e 00:09:07.255\r\nPlease, Harley, let me go.\r\nI'm rich.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.338 --\u003e 00:09:08.978\r\nI'll pay whatever you\r\nwant if you'll just-\r\n\r\n00:09:09.132 --\u003e 00:09:10.216\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.800 --\u003e 00:09:12.844\r\nUh-oh! Company-\r\n\r\n00:09:16.097 --\u003e 00:09:18.349\r\nHi, B-man. Wanna race?\r\n\r\n00:09:18.933 --\u003e 00:09:20.769\r\nStop the car now!\r\n\r\n00:09:21.269 --\u003e 00:09:22.896\r\nI think not.\r\n\r\n00:09:23.271 --\u003e 00:09:26.316\r\nWe wanna help you sort this\r\nout before it gets worse.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.649 --\u003e 00:09:29.819\r\nSure, like you helped poor\r\nProfessor Crane last night.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.653 --\u003e 00:09:33.823\r\nSorry, boys,\r\nyou ain't taking me back to Arkham.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.907 --\u003e 00:09:35.325\r\n(VERONICA SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:36.367 --\u003e 00:09:37.827\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:09:39.662 --\u003e 00:09:41.081\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:51.382 --\u003e 00:09:54.469\r\nI'm gonna get that little kook\r\nif it's the last thing I ever do.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.680 --\u003e 00:09:59.808\r\nThe scanner says she's\r\nheaded for the south side.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.225 --\u003e 00:10:02.852\r\nProbably to someone who can\r\nhide her until the heat's off.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.110 --\u003e 00:10:12.654\r\nThe last time I seen you,\r\nyou not only ruined my club\r\n\r\n00:10:12.946 --\u003e 00:10:15.240\r\nbut brought the freaking\r\nBatman down on my head as well.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.282 --\u003e 00:10:18.535\r\nGive me one good reason I\r\ndo not dust you right now.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.916 --\u003e 00:10:26.209\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'll\u003c/i\u003e buy that.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.086 --\u003e 00:10:31.131\r\nNo sweat, toots,\r\nBoxy will take care of us.\r\n\r\n00:10:31.548 --\u003e 00:10:33.716\r\nThat's what I'm afraid of.\r\n\r\n00:10:37.011 --\u003e 00:10:39.764\r\nSo, how soon can you\r\nsneak me out of town?\r\n\r\n00:10:39.848 --\u003e 00:10:41.015\r\nLeave us not be hasty.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.516 --\u003e 00:10:45.061\r\nWe have a friendship to renew and Ms.\r\nMoney-Bags to ransom off.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.608 --\u003e 00:10:52.735\r\nOh, no. We can't do that.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.986 --\u003e 00:10:54.779\r\nSee,\r\nI'm giving up the crime thing.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.863 --\u003e 00:10:56.906\r\nI only grabbed her\r\nbecause I needed a car.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.073 --\u003e 00:11:00.160\r\nOnce I'm gone,\r\nshe goes home safe and sound.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.954 --\u003e 00:11:04.497\r\nI'm calling the shots\r\nhere, sugar.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.873 --\u003e 00:11:07.250\r\nAnyone says different has\r\nto go through me, got it?\r\n\r\n00:11:07.333 --\u003e 00:11:08.543\r\nBATMAN: Got it.\r\n\r\n00:11:12.088 --\u003e 00:11:13.214\r\n(VERONICA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:13.298 --\u003e 00:11:15.675\r\nYou've stuck your cape into\r\nmy business for the last time.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.758 --\u003e 00:11:16.843\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:20.597 --\u003e 00:11:21.681\r\nTake 'em, boys.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.683 --\u003e 00:11:26.227\r\nTHUG 1: Get him! Get him!\r\nTHUG 2: Come back here!\r\n\r\n00:11:26.311 --\u003e 00:11:28.688\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:29.564 --\u003e 00:11:31.191\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:41.492 --\u003e 00:11:43.536\r\n(ALL GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:11:46.497 --\u003e 00:11:48.416\r\nWe're safe, thank goodness.\r\n\r\n00:11:50.376 --\u003e 00:11:51.419\r\nAhh!\r\n\r\n00:11:51.794 --\u003e 00:11:54.172\r\nBack off, freak,\r\nor the dame's history.\r\n\r\n00:11:54.255 --\u003e 00:11:55.590\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.841 --\u003e 00:11:58.635\r\nGet your own hostage.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.276 --\u003e 00:12:16.653\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:17.904 --\u003e 00:12:19.113\r\n(BOTH GASP)\r\n\r\n00:12:22.367 --\u003e 00:12:23.743\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:25.036 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nSorry, doll.\r\n\r\n00:12:26.537 --\u003e 00:12:28.957\r\nAs we gamblers say,\r\nyou just crapped out.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.425 --\u003e 00:12:41.636\r\n- Any last words?\r\n- Just one.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.178 --\u003e 00:12:43.805\r\nBabies!\r\n\r\n00:12:44.472 --\u003e 00:12:45.598\r\n(BOXY SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:12:46.099 --\u003e 00:12:48.601\r\nPlay nice with\r\nyour new chew toy.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.814 --\u003e 00:12:53.898\r\n(VERONICA YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.527 --\u003e 00:12:59.237\r\n(BOXY SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:08.997 --\u003e 00:13:10.832\r\nAhh!\r\n\r\n00:13:25.680 --\u003e 00:13:27.974\r\n- Harley's gone again.\r\n- So is Bennett.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.726 --\u003e 00:13:32.937\r\nDid you mean what you said back\r\nthere about sending me home?\r\n\r\n00:13:33.271 --\u003e 00:13:34.731\r\nSure. You're a good kid,\r\n\r\n00:13:35.023 --\u003e 00:13:38.026\r\nand I do kind of feel a little\r\nbit responsible for all this.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.443 --\u003e 00:13:39.527\r\nNo kidding.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.531 --\u003e 00:13:45.533\r\nSo, what will happen to you?\r\n\r\n00:13:45.908 --\u003e 00:13:47.827\r\nIf I'm lucky,\r\nI'll make it out of town\r\n\r\n00:13:47.910 --\u003e 00:13:50.121\r\nbefore Bats hauls my\r\nhiney back to the bin.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.747 --\u003e 00:13:52.790\r\nCan't you explain that it\r\nwas all just a mistake?\r\n\r\n00:13:53.249 --\u003e 00:13:56.836\r\nHa! With my past?\r\nI don't even believe it myself.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.759 --\u003e 00:14:04.177\r\nLook, let's make a deal.\r\n\r\n00:14:04.635 --\u003e 00:14:08.014\r\nYou get me out of this alive,\r\nand I'll drop all the charges.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.349 --\u003e 00:14:12.935\r\nYeah?\r\nHey, you're all right, toots.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.353 --\u003e 00:14:16.689\r\nFor the first time today,\r\nI think things are finally looking up.\r\n\r\n00:14:16.939 --\u003e 00:14:18.024\r\n(BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:14:18.316 --\u003e 00:14:20.276\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:22.278 --\u003e 00:14:24.655\r\n(TANK APPROACHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:31.704 --\u003e 00:14:33.956\r\nYou in the car,\r\nrelease your hostage immediately.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.374 --\u003e 00:14:35.416\r\nDaddy!\r\n\r\n00:14:35.958 --\u003e 00:14:37.001\r\nDaddy?\r\n\r\n00:14:40.254 --\u003e 00:14:41.506\r\n(Dy!\r\n\r\n00:14:42.632 --\u003e 00:14:44.550\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.055 --\u003e 00:14:51.391\r\nWait. What are you doing?\r\nThat's my father.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.808 --\u003e 00:14:54.811\r\nNo,\r\nthat's your father in a tank!\r\n\r\n00:15:08.616 --\u003e 00:15:09.867\r\nNo, you don't.\r\n\r\n00:15:29.554 --\u003e 00:15:31.973\r\n\u003ci\u003eDISPATCH: All units,\r\nsuspect Quinn has been sighted\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:32.056 --\u003e 00:15:33.307\r\n\u003ci\u003eheaded for Gotham City Square.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:53.911 --\u003e 00:15:57.290\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:02.462 --\u003e 00:16:04.380\r\nOh, great.\r\n\r\n00:16:21.105 --\u003e 00:16:22.565\r\n(BRAKES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:16:23.316 --\u003e 00:16:25.276\r\n- Got you now.\r\n- You screwy little-\r\n\r\n00:16:25.359 --\u003e 00:16:26.652\r\nTrouble-making clown.\r\n\r\n00:16:35.119 --\u003e 00:16:36.162\r\nVeronica?\r\n\r\n00:16:38.581 --\u003e 00:16:39.624\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:42.793 --\u003e 00:16:45.296\r\nHARLEY: Hey,\r\nbird-boy, look alive.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.463 --\u003e 00:16:46.881\r\n(VERONICA YELPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:47.298 --\u003e 00:16:49.717\r\nWell, that's my good\r\ndeed for the day.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.884 --\u003e 00:16:51.052\r\nBye.\r\n\r\n00:16:51.844 --\u003e 00:16:52.929\r\nWait!\r\n\r\n00:17:04.315 --\u003e 00:17:06.859\r\nMy little girl.\r\nI was so worried.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.109 --\u003e 00:17:08.110\r\nInoficed.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.821 --\u003e 00:17:11.864\r\nWhoa!\r\n\r\n00:17:13.908 --\u003e 00:17:15.409\r\nLeaving so soon, Boxy?\r\n\r\n00:17:15.826 --\u003e 00:17:17.245\r\nYou got nothing on me.\r\n\r\n00:17:20.289 --\u003e 00:17:22.124\r\nI'm sure I can find something.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.500 --\u003e 00:17:23.751\r\nMove it.\r\n\r\n00:17:33.594 --\u003e 00:17:35.314\r\nHARLEY: You don't know when to\r\nquit, do you?\r\n\r\n00:17:38.975 --\u003e 00:17:42.603\r\nListen to me.\r\nAll the work you've done, your freedom.\r\n\r\n00:17:43.062 --\u003e 00:17:45.439\r\nIf you run away,\r\nyou'll lose them, Harley.\r\n\r\n00:17:46.023 --\u003e 00:17:48.526\r\nYou're so close to winning\r\nback your real life.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.693 --\u003e 00:17:49.777\r\nWhy risk it now?\r\n\r\n00:17:53.447 --\u003e 00:17:55.741\r\nI'm having a bad day!\r\n\r\n00:17:55.825 --\u003e 00:18:00.162\r\nI'm sick of people trying to shoot\r\nme, run me over and blow me up!\r\n\r\n00:18:06.377 --\u003e 00:18:08.754\r\nI didn't even get to\r\nkeep my new dress,\r\n\r\n00:18:09.171 --\u003e 00:18:11.841\r\nand I actually paid for it!\r\n\r\n00:18:14.051 --\u003e 00:18:15.678\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:19.557 --\u003e 00:18:22.184\r\nI tried to be good.\r\nI really did.\r\n\r\n00:18:22.476 --\u003e 00:18:24.729\r\nBut if that's not good\r\nenough, fine!\r\n\r\n00:18:26.731 --\u003e 00:18:28.774\r\nLet's get back to basics.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.991 --\u003e 00:18:39.118\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:53.466 --\u003e 00:18:56.052\r\nTalk about grasping at straws.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.218 --\u003e 00:18:59.221\r\nOh, well,\r\nat least I'm going out on a joke.\r\n\r\n00:18:59.597 --\u003e 00:19:01.474\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.610 --\u003e 00:19:15.237\r\nI think I made a\r\nmess on your cape.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.073 --\u003e 00:19:18.115\r\n(HARLEY GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:23.996 --\u003e 00:19:26.791\r\nHome again, home\r\nagain, jiggity-jig.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.375 --\u003e 00:19:30.628\r\nNot for too long, though. Ms.\r\nVreeland dropped the kidnapping charges.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.878 --\u003e 00:19:34.507\r\nWith a little more hard work, you should\r\nbe ready to reenter society for good.\r\n\r\n00:19:34.674 --\u003e 00:19:35.716\r\n\u003ci\u003eY3Y'.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:19:36.175 --\u003e 00:19:38.177\r\nThere's one thing I gotta know.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.344 --\u003e 00:19:41.347\r\nWhy did you stay with me all day,\r\nrisking your butt for someone\r\n\r\n00:19:41.430 --\u003e 00:19:43.891\r\nwho's never given you\r\nanything but trouble?\r\n\r\n00:19:44.058 --\u003e 00:19:46.268\r\nI know what it's like to\r\ntry and rebuild a life.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.021 --\u003e 00:19:51.148\r\nI had a bad day too, once.\r\n\r\n00:19:53.901 --\u003e 00:19:56.779\r\nNice guys like you\r\nshouldn't have bad days.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.341 --\u003e 00:20:18.426\r\nCall me.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.926 --\u003e 00:20:20.845\r\nDon't press your luck.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.603 --\u003e 00:20:31.897\r\nAh, what are you looking at?\r\n\r\n00:20:39.071 --\u003e 00:20:41.365\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E07 - Make 'Em Laugh (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.924 --\u003e 00:00:08.967\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.372 --\u003e 00:01:22.833\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:01:26.920 --\u003e 00:01:28.005\r\n(ELEVATOR BELL DINGS)\r\n\r\n00:01:31.842 --\u003e 00:01:34.428\r\nMAN: We've waited\r\nweeks for reservations.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.936 --\u003e 00:01:45.981\r\n- Name?\r\n- King, party of one.\r\n\r\n00:01:46.398 --\u003e 00:01:50.694\r\nKing, King. No, I'm sorry,\r\nI don't show that reservation.\r\n\r\n00:01:50.986 --\u003e 00:01:54.489\r\nOh, yeah? Well,\r\nlet me show you something, fruitcake.\r\n\r\n00:01:56.325 --\u003e 00:01:57.534\r\nAhh!\r\n\r\n00:02:00.787 --\u003e 00:02:02.289\r\nHands up, chowhounds.\r\n\r\n00:02:02.623 --\u003e 00:02:08.712\r\nDrop your forks and prepare to cower\r\nbefore the uncanny Condiment King.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.795 --\u003e 00:02:11.465\r\n- Who is that?\r\n- Some kind of nutcase.\r\n\r\n00:02:11.548 --\u003e 00:02:14.593\r\n- Just ignore him.\r\n- MAN: Someone will call security.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.052 --\u003e 00:02:20.682\r\nHey. Hey! I don't believe this!\r\nI say cower, and you're still eating?\r\n\r\n00:02:21.099 --\u003e 00:02:22.893\r\nWell, all right then.\r\n\r\n00:02:23.393 --\u003e 00:02:25.103\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:28.815 --\u003e 00:02:29.983\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:30.067 --\u003e 00:02:32.319\r\nNow, see here, you.\r\n\r\n00:02:32.486 --\u003e 00:02:34.321\r\n(PANICKED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:02:37.783 --\u003e 00:02:39.201\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:02:39.284 --\u003e 00:02:40.535\r\nHot sauce.\r\n\r\n00:02:41.912 --\u003e 00:02:43.955\r\nAnyone else want to be a hero?\r\n\r\n00:02:44.164 --\u003e 00:02:46.333\r\nThen take out your\r\nwallets, cash and jewels\r\n\r\n00:02:46.500 --\u003e 00:02:49.086\r\nand toss them here on the table.\r\nCome on. Right now.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.547 --\u003e 00:02:55.109\r\n\u003ci\u003eDISPATCH: Disturbance reported at\r\nthe top of the Crown restaurant.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:55.133 --\u003e 00:02:59.012\r\n\u003ci\u003eSuspect is a male, costumed extremist\r\narmed with what appears to be\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:59.221 --\u003e 00:03:00.263\r\n\u003ci\u003ea ketchup gun.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:03.016\r\nIt's gonna be one\r\nof those nights.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.102 --\u003e 00:03:06.144\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:08.605 --\u003e 00:03:13.694\r\nSo long, suckers.\r\nParting is such sweet-and-sour sorrow.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.361 --\u003e 00:03:16.822\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:03:17.489 --\u003e 00:03:19.032\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:03:22.244 --\u003e 00:03:23.412\r\nWhat's this?\r\n\r\n00:03:23.870 --\u003e 00:03:26.998\r\nAh! The big, bad Bat-guy.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.499 --\u003e 00:03:31.378\r\nI knew you'd catch up to me sooner or\r\nlater. How I've relished this meeting.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.962 --\u003e 00:03:37.676\r\nYou, the dynamic Dark Knight, versus\r\nme, the conceptual Condiment King.\r\n\r\n00:03:38.051 --\u003e 00:03:39.094\r\nCome, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.553 --\u003e 00:03:42.889\r\nLet's see if you\r\ncan cut the mustard-\r\n\r\n00:03:42.973 --\u003e 00:03:44.099\r\n- Quiet.\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:44.766 --\u003e 00:03:46.059\r\n(BREATHING HEAVILY)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.268 --\u003e 00:03:49.354\r\n- You hit me.\r\n- Now, listen, Mustard Man,\r\n\r\n00:03:49.604 --\u003e 00:03:51.273\r\nor whatever you call yourself.\r\n\r\n00:03:51.815 --\u003e 00:03:55.193\r\nYou're obviously new at this,\r\nso I'm willing to go easy on you.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.402 --\u003e 00:03:58.864\r\nProvided you give back the loot and\r\nnever even think about doing this again.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.114 --\u003e 00:04:00.157\r\nDeal?\r\n\r\n00:04:01.283 --\u003e 00:04:04.161\r\n- Horseradish!\r\n- This is your last warning.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.411 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nLet's go, Batso. You and me.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.164 --\u003e 00:04:10.125\r\nI'm the prince of\r\npickles, sultan of sauce.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.959 --\u003e 00:04:13.336\r\nYou don't stand a chance.\r\nYou hear me?\r\n\r\n00:04:14.129 --\u003e 00:04:15.756\r\nLater, chump.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:17.883\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:04:20.260 --\u003e 00:04:21.470\r\nHang on.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.138 --\u003e 00:04:25.557\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.266 --\u003e 00:04:27.684\r\n- (THUDS)\r\n- (TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:04:33.398 --\u003e 00:04:34.858\r\nHarvey, call an ambulance.\r\n\r\n00:04:35.984 --\u003e 00:04:37.569\r\nI know this man.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.111 --\u003e 00:04:40.697\r\nHe's that TV comic,\r\nBuddy Standler.\r\n\r\n00:04:42.407 --\u003e 00:04:44.075\r\n\u003ci\u003eSUMMER: Still no\r\nclues in the mystery\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:44.159 --\u003e 00:04:45.827\r\n\u003ci\u003ebehind comedian Buddy Standler's\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:45.911 --\u003e 00:04:47.829\r\n\u003ci\u003eone-man crime spree last night.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:52.042\r\n\u003ci\u003eA rampage that ended with a trip to\r\nthe hospital for the famed TV comic.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:52.292 --\u003e 00:04:55.420\r\n\u003ci\u003eThough Standler himself is unable\r\nto account for his actions,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:55.587 --\u003e 00:04:57.923\r\n\u003ci\u003ehis manager had\r\nthese observations.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:04:58.173 --\u003e 00:05:02.511\r\n\u003ci\u003eI don't get it. Buddy's just\r\nthrown his entire career away.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:02.719 --\u003e 00:05:04.888\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe network's canceling his show\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:05.055 --\u003e 00:05:07.682\r\n\u003ci\u003eand the restaurant's suing\r\nhim for a million dollars.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:07.891 --\u003e 00:05:10.602\r\nWhy'd he do it?\r\nIt just doesn't make sense.\r\n\r\n00:05:10.811 --\u003e 00:05:14.523\r\nThat's too bad. I watch Standler's\r\nshow all the time. He's great.\r\n\r\n00:05:14.731 --\u003e 00:05:17.484\r\nAny idea what would have caused\r\nhim to go off the deep end?\r\n\r\n00:05:17.859 --\u003e 00:05:20.362\r\nNo, but talk about bad timing.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.779 --\u003e 00:05:22.405\r\nHe was supposed to\r\nbe one of the judges\r\n\r\n00:05:22.489 --\u003e 00:05:24.574\r\nfor the annual laugh-off\r\ncompetition tonight.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.950 --\u003e 00:05:26.701\r\nAlfred and I bought tickets.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.285 --\u003e 00:05:29.287\r\n\u003ci\u003eBy the way, where is Alfred?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:38.880 --\u003e 00:05:42.217\r\n- One side, mac.\r\n- I beg your pardon.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.681 --\u003e 00:05:50.141\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- Ooh. Pretty. I want it.\r\n\r\n00:05:51.852 --\u003e 00:05:54.980\r\n- Hey, you can't do that.\r\n- Sure I can, lady.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.188 --\u003e 00:05:57.190\r\nI'm the Pack Rat,\r\n\r\n00:05:57.440 --\u003e 00:06:00.694\r\n- and your trash is my treasure.\r\n- Hey!\r\n\r\n00:06:03.864 --\u003e 00:06:04.948\r\nMmm. Shiny.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.324 --\u003e 00:06:07.367\r\nSecurity!\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:13.915\r\nOh, no, you don't.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.710 --\u003e 00:06:17.711\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:06:26.803 --\u003e 00:06:29.014\r\nWhoa, dibs on the dummy hand.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.765 --\u003e 00:06:32.017\r\nGood heavens.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.774 --\u003e 00:06:42.110\r\nI've been looking\r\neveryplace for one of these.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.163 --\u003e 00:06:54.664\r\n- Yes?\r\n- ALFRED: Master Bruce?\r\n\r\n00:06:54.748 --\u003e 00:06:55.874\r\nAlfred?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.957 --\u003e 00:06:58.251\r\nI think you're needed at\r\nMayfield's right away, sir.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.335 --\u003e 00:07:00.253\r\nThere's a man with\r\na gun running amok.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.420 --\u003e 00:07:01.504\r\n- He's- - (GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:01.671 --\u003e 00:07:05.759\r\n\u003ci\u003eAward of advice, mac.\r\nNever rat on a rat.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:15.060 --\u003e 00:07:16.186\r\nBATMAN: Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:07:19.773 --\u003e 00:07:21.358\r\n- (GUNFIRE)\r\n- Alfred!\r\n\r\n00:07:35.038 --\u003e 00:07:37.540\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou'll get oatmeal and like it.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:38.041 --\u003e 00:07:42.545\r\nListen, Eddie, if they expect me to\r\njudge that stupid laugh-off again,\r\n\r\n00:07:42.629 --\u003e 00:07:44.756\r\nthey'd better be\r\nprepared to pay.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.839 --\u003e 00:07:45.882\r\n(KNOCKING ON DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:07:45.966 --\u003e 00:07:48.969\r\nHold on,\r\nI got somebody at the door.\r\n\r\n00:07:54.724 --\u003e 00:07:56.643\r\n- Yeah?\r\n- MAN: Pizza delivery.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.851 --\u003e 00:07:58.728\r\nI didn't order any pizza.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.812 --\u003e 00:08:00.230\r\n(SNIFFING)\r\n\r\n00:08:00.605 --\u003e 00:08:04.609\r\n- But I'll take it. How much?\r\n- It's on me.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.110 --\u003e 00:08:06.903\r\nLISA: Hey! (COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:08.029 --\u003e 00:08:10.115\r\n(SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:08:16.246 --\u003e 00:08:18.248\r\nOkay, everybody,\r\nempty your pockets.\r\n\r\n00:08:18.498 --\u003e 00:08:19.624\r\n(ALL GASP)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.708 --\u003e 00:08:22.919\r\nI want gum wrappers, loose string,\r\nthose little balls of lint.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.963 --\u003e 00:08:26.631\r\nNone of that cash stuff.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.215 --\u003e 00:08:28.466\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:08:29.551 --\u003e 00:08:31.052\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:08:32.137 --\u003e 00:08:35.724\r\nSo it's the rat versus\r\nthe bat and the brat.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:39.978\r\nOnly one will survive,\r\nand that's gonna be me.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.061 --\u003e 00:08:41.396\r\nEverybody, clear out.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.608 --\u003e 00:08:47.110\r\n(ULULATING)\r\n\r\n00:08:52.866 --\u003e 00:08:54.200\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.091 --\u003e 00:09:11.593\r\nCome on out.\r\n\r\n00:09:15.096 --\u003e 00:09:16.347\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:16.431 --\u003e 00:09:17.849\r\nMmm, mmm, mmm.\r\n\r\n00:09:18.516 --\u003e 00:09:19.976\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:30.278 --\u003e 00:09:32.197\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:38.286 --\u003e 00:09:40.371\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:09:52.008 --\u003e 00:09:53.259\r\nROBIN: It's Harry Loomis.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.551 --\u003e 00:09:55.053\r\nAnother famous comedian.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.303 --\u003e 00:09:56.429\r\nLook at his neck.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.687 --\u003e 00:10:05.980\r\nROBIN: A microchip?\r\n\r\n00:10:07.107 --\u003e 00:10:08.483\r\nMind control.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.192 --\u003e 00:10:12.946\r\nThis is beginning to point toward\r\nour old friend, the Mad Hatter.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.167 --\u003e 00:10:29.045\r\nWake up, Jervis.\r\nWe have to talk.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.839 --\u003e 00:10:32.715\r\nCome on, rise and shine.\r\n\r\n00:10:40.014 --\u003e 00:10:41.766\r\nWow, he's really out.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.083 --\u003e 00:11:08.209\r\nHere's what we know.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.460 --\u003e 00:11:13.381\r\nSomeone implants the Mad Hatter with\r\none of his own mind-control devices,\r\n\r\n00:11:13.631 --\u003e 00:11:15.800\r\nthen does the same\r\nthing to two comedians.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.967 --\u003e 00:11:17.218\r\nBut what's the connection?\r\n\r\n00:11:17.468 --\u003e 00:11:19.721\r\nLooks like it's three\r\ncomedians now, sir.\r\n\r\n00:11:21.931 --\u003e 00:11:24.392\r\n\"TV personality Lisa\r\nLorraine was abducted\"\r\n\r\n00:11:24.475 --\u003e 00:11:26.311\r\n\"from her apartment\r\nearly this evening.\"\r\n\r\n00:11:26.519 --\u003e 00:11:30.398\r\nAnd here's our common link.\r\nThis comedy competition.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.648 --\u003e 00:11:33.401\r\nROBIN: Sure.\r\nBuddy, Harry and Lisa judge it every year.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.860 --\u003e 00:11:35.445\r\nRemember, we taped the last one.\r\n\r\n00:11:35.904 --\u003e 00:11:37.113\r\nRight here, Master Dick.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.197 --\u003e 00:11:39.115\r\nAnd I've cued it to\r\nsomething you should see.\r\n\r\n00:11:45.413 --\u003e 00:11:47.207\r\n\u003ci\u003eWell,\r\nthat's it for our contestants.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:47.290 --\u003e 00:11:50.543\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow our panel of distinguished\r\njudges will choose\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:50.627 --\u003e 00:11:53.671\r\n\u003ci\u003ethe funniest person in Gotham.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:01.304 --\u003e 00:12:05.391\r\n\u003ci\u003eNot so fast, chuckles.\r\nYou haven't introduced me yet.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:05.600 --\u003e 00:12:07.644\r\n\u003ci\u003eSmiling Shecky Rimshot.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:07.727 --\u003e 00:12:09.229\r\n\u003ci\u003eBa-dum-boom.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:11.564 --\u003e 00:12:12.857\r\n\u003ci\u003eCome on, already.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:14.776 --\u003e 00:12:16.527\r\n\u003ci\u003eGood evening, ladies and germs.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:16.778 --\u003e 00:12:19.739\r\n\u003ci\u003eHey, did you hear about the guy\r\nwalked into a doctor's office\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:19.822 --\u003e 00:12:21.991\r\n\u003ci\u003ewith a frog on his head?\r\nDoctor says,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:22.075 --\u003e 00:12:24.929\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"That's the weirdest looking wart I've\r\never seen.\" Frog looks up and says,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:24.953 --\u003e 00:12:27.956\r\n\u003ci\u003e\"Yeah, I woke up this morning,\r\nthere was a big bump on my butt.\"\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:28.206 --\u003e 00:12:30.333\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:34.003 --\u003e 00:12:36.464\r\n\u003ci\u003eHey, then there's this\r\nguy who buys a new dog.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:36.547 --\u003e 00:12:38.341\r\n\u003ci\u003eHe takes it for a walk\r\nand the friend says-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:38.424 --\u003e 00:12:39.634\r\n- (BUZZER SOUNDS)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:12:39.801 --\u003e 00:12:43.096\r\n\u003ci\u003eSorry, pal.\r\nWe've already made our decision.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:43.304 --\u003e 00:12:47.267\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd for your information,\r\nregistration closed days ago.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:47.684 --\u003e 00:12:50.520\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm not leaving until\r\nI get that trophy.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:50.687 --\u003e 00:12:52.146\r\n(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:52.230 --\u003e 00:12:54.315\r\n\u003ci\u003eOh, yes, you are.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:54.399 --\u003e 00:12:57.193\r\n(LAUGHING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:12:58.820 --\u003e 00:13:00.697\r\n(IN BRITISH ACCENT) You\r\ncan't do this to me!\r\n\r\n00:13:00.780 --\u003e 00:13:02.782\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'm the greatest\r\ncomic in Gotham!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:04.033 --\u003e 00:13:06.911\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'll get even.\r\nI'll ruin you all.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:07.495 --\u003e 00:13:09.175\r\n- (GRUNTS)\r\n- BATMAN: Freeze \u003ci\u003eit\u003c/i\u003e right there.\r\n\r\n00:13:12.709 --\u003e 00:13:14.627\r\nI think I see what you\r\nmean, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:13:16.296 --\u003e 00:13:17.422\r\nWithout the hat...\r\n\r\n00:13:19.632 --\u003e 00:13:21.050\r\nAnd different hair...\r\n\r\n00:13:21.509 --\u003e 00:13:22.844\r\nROBIN: The Joker!\r\n\r\n00:13:37.150 --\u003e 00:13:38.901\r\n\u003ci\u003eHOST: He“ you, Maury,\r\nI'm dying here.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:38.985 --\u003e 00:13:40.278\r\nI got a full house,\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:43.573\r\nand all three of my celebrity judges\r\nare either missing or in jail.\r\n\r\n00:13:43.656 --\u003e 00:13:46.034\r\nYou gotta find me some\r\nreplacements quick.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.951 --\u003e 00:13:49.454\r\nJOKER: Ask and ye shall receive.\r\n\r\n00:13:49.871 --\u003e 00:13:51.581\r\nWhat in the... (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:52.498 --\u003e 00:13:57.128\r\nPermit me to introduce Judges\r\nKnuckles, Vinnie and Kowalski.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.545 --\u003e 00:14:00.298\r\nThey'll be presenting me\r\nwith the trophy tonight.\r\n\r\n00:14:00.798 --\u003e 00:14:03.843\r\n(CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY) Listen,\r\nyou can't just walk in here and take...\r\n\r\n00:14:04.010 --\u003e 00:14:06.012\r\nJOKER: Oh, but I already have.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.220 --\u003e 00:14:08.556\r\n(STRUGGLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:12.185 --\u003e 00:14:14.395\r\nThese little microchips\r\nare a wonder.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.729 --\u003e 00:14:18.983\r\nRemind me to thank the Mad Hatter\r\nif he ever wakes up. (LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:14:20.860 --\u003e 00:14:22.737\r\nWOMAN 1: Hey,\r\nstart the show already.\r\n\r\n00:14:23.112 --\u003e 00:14:26.157\r\n- Let's go already!\r\n- WOMAN 2: Start the show!\r\n\r\n00:14:26.616 --\u003e 00:14:31.287\r\nLadies and gentlemen, welcome to\r\nthe 10th annual Gotham Laff Off.\r\n\r\n00:14:31.371 --\u003e 00:14:32.663\r\n(AUDIENCE CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:14:32.747 --\u003e 00:14:35.416\r\nAnd now, it is my deepest\r\nhonor to present to you\r\n\r\n00:14:35.500 --\u003e 00:14:40.171\r\nthe evening's first and only\r\ncontestant, Smiling Shecky Rimshot.\r\n\r\n00:14:41.756 --\u003e 00:14:43.567\r\n(IN AMERICAN ACCENT) Hey,\r\nfolks, you're beautiful.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.591 --\u003e 00:14:46.511\r\nFunny thing happened to me on\r\nthe way to the theater last year.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.594 --\u003e 00:14:50.973\r\nIt seems three no-talent hacks\r\ntried to stop me from winning.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.182 --\u003e 00:14:52.517\r\nBut guess what!\r\n\r\n00:14:55.186 --\u003e 00:14:57.522\r\n(IN NORMAL ACCENT) I'm back.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.688 --\u003e 00:15:00.149\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:15:00.233 --\u003e 00:15:02.276\r\n(AUDIENCE GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:04.487 --\u003e 00:15:07.615\r\nOh! Such unhappy faces.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.074 --\u003e 00:15:10.201\r\nJudges, let's cheer them up.\r\n\r\n00:15:10.660 --\u003e 00:15:12.537\r\n(ALL LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.539 --\u003e 00:15:18.668\r\nMy high-octane laughing gas will\r\nhave you rolling in the aisles.\r\n\r\n00:15:25.508 --\u003e 00:15:27.051\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:15:33.683 --\u003e 00:15:35.977\r\nIt's just you and us, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:15:36.310 --\u003e 00:15:38.354\r\nNot quite, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:38.604 --\u003e 00:15:42.775\r\nI've got a new girl,\r\nand she'll really sweep you off your feet.\r\n\r\n00:15:45.194 --\u003e 00:15:46.195\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:47.113 --\u003e 00:15:48.406\r\nLisa Lorraine?\r\n\r\n00:15:51.409 --\u003e 00:15:54.871\r\nCall me Mighty Mom.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.079 --\u003e 00:15:56.372\r\nAin't she sweet?\r\n\r\n00:15:57.623 --\u003e 00:16:01.002\r\nMy very own happy homemaker.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.169 --\u003e 00:16:03.379\r\nBut I don't do windows.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.504 --\u003e 00:16:04.672\r\n(JOKER LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:16:04.755 --\u003e 00:16:06.007\r\nNot bad.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.299 --\u003e 00:16:09.302\r\nHoney, why don't you show\r\nour pals how you clean house?\r\n\r\n00:16:09.552 --\u003e 00:16:12.346\r\nIn other words, mop 'em up.\r\n\r\n00:16:13.764 --\u003e 00:16:16.809\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:20.521 --\u003e 00:16:23.441\r\nWho's first to get dusted?\r\n\r\n00:16:23.983 --\u003e 00:16:25.623\r\nThink you can get the\r\nbrain patch off her?\r\n\r\n00:16:25.818 --\u003e 00:16:26.819\r\nNo problem.\r\n\r\n00:16:29.322 --\u003e 00:16:30.615\r\n\"(GRUNTS) \"(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:33.451 --\u003e 00:16:37.121\r\n- Hey!\r\n- Naughty boy. Mama spank.\r\n\r\n00:16:38.623 --\u003e 00:16:40.458\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.586 --\u003e 00:16:46.756\r\nWhat did I tell you about playing\r\nwith your toys in the house?\r\n\r\n00:16:47.381 --\u003e 00:16:49.675\r\n- Get rid of it!\r\n- You're the boss.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.972 --\u003e 00:16:57.058\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:58.518 --\u003e 00:17:02.730\r\nNo! Not on my nice clean floor.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.813 --\u003e 00:17:05.566\r\nROBIN: Just hold still.\r\nLISA: Ow!\r\n\r\n00:17:05.816 --\u003e 00:17:07.151\r\nThat hurts.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.944 --\u003e 00:17:08.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:09.987 --\u003e 00:17:13.491\r\n- Don't worry. I'm back to normal.\r\n- Who can tell?\r\n\r\n00:17:37.890 --\u003e 00:17:41.143\r\n- Stay back.\r\n- You've hit a new low, Joker.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.561 --\u003e 00:17:45.106\r\nOnly you would ruin three\r\nlives for a silly piece of tin.\r\n\r\n00:17:45.606 --\u003e 00:17:47.692\r\nYou're dumber than you\r\nlook, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:17:49.944 --\u003e 00:17:53.823\r\nIt's not the trophy that\r\nmatters, it's the title.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.906 --\u003e 00:17:58.661\r\nI am the greatest clown this\r\ndismal burg has ever seen.\r\n\r\n00:17:58.869 --\u003e 00:18:02.415\r\nWhat would the common folk do\r\nwithout my pranks and antics?\r\n\r\n00:18:02.957 --\u003e 00:18:04.208\r\nLet's find out.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.709 --\u003e 00:18:06.627\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:12.049\r\nUP, up and away!\r\n\r\n00:18:29.692 --\u003e 00:18:31.319\r\nQuit rocking the boat!\r\n\r\n00:18:42.788 --\u003e 00:18:45.708\r\nJOKER: Oh! Too bad, Bat-sap.\r\n\r\n00:18:45.791 --\u003e 00:18:48.002\r\nBut you should have\r\nremembered the old saying,\r\n\r\n00:18:48.252 --\u003e 00:18:51.589\r\n\"Dying is easy, comedy is hard.\"\r\n\r\n00:18:52.298 --\u003e 00:18:54.717\r\n(LAUGHING MAN IACALLY)\r\n\r\n00:18:56.719 --\u003e 00:18:58.929\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- (CONTINUES LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:03.100 --\u003e 00:19:04.935\r\nROBIN: Mind if I join the party?\r\n\r\n00:19:06.604 --\u003e 00:19:07.897\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:12.276 --\u003e 00:19:14.654\r\nOw! You miserable brat.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.910 --\u003e 00:19:22.870\r\nGet this stupid thing off me.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.997 --\u003e 00:19:26.916\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:29.210 --\u003e 00:19:30.378\r\nQOps!\r\n\r\n00:19:31.921 --\u003e 00:19:32.963\r\nWatch it.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.756 --\u003e 00:19:36.425\r\nI think I'm getting airsick.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.431 --\u003e 00:19:43.974\r\n(SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:19:49.313 --\u003e 00:19:50.690\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:51.107 --\u003e 00:19:53.943\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:56.070 --\u003e 00:20:01.492\r\nI'll get you for this, Batman!\r\nNo one upstages me and lives.\r\n\r\n00:20:03.911 --\u003e 00:20:06.831\r\n- (GUNS COCKING)\r\n- Is there a problem, officers?\r\n\r\n00:20:07.623 --\u003e 00:20:08.749\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:20:10.334 --\u003e 00:20:11.544\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:11.711 --\u003e 00:20:13.087\r\n(PEOPLE LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:20:13.170 --\u003e 00:20:18.175\r\nWhat's so funny?\r\nI'll give you something to laugh about!\r\n\r\n00:20:20.928 --\u003e 00:20:22.680\r\n(GRUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:44.869 --\u003e 00:20:46.579\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E08 - Batgirl Returns (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.173 --\u003e 00:00:08.175\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.903 --\u003e 00:01:52.946\r\n(ELECTRICITY ZAPS)\r\n\r\n00:01:53.864 --\u003e 00:01:55.073\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:12.090 --\u003e 00:02:13.467\r\nBATGIRL: Back off, creeps.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.523 --\u003e 00:02:32.027\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.863 --\u003e 00:02:36.239\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:40.661 --\u003e 00:02:41.953\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:45.082 --\u003e 00:02:46.708\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:02:47.417 --\u003e 00:02:48.877\r\nBatgirl...\r\n\r\n00:02:49.920 --\u003e 00:02:51.046\r\nAre you all right?\r\n\r\n00:02:51.963 --\u003e 00:02:53.131\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:02:55.217 --\u003e 00:02:56.718\r\nThanks to you.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.435 --\u003e 00:03:06.687\r\nDICK'S VOICE: Barbara!\r\n\r\n00:03:07.312 --\u003e 00:03:09.064\r\n\u003ci\u003eHey, Babs!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:11.066 --\u003e 00:03:13.610\r\nYo, bookworm! You up there?\r\n\r\n00:03:14.986 --\u003e 00:03:16.279\r\nWhat is it, Dick?\r\n\r\n00:03:16.363 --\u003e 00:03:18.323\r\nAll work and no play, you know?\r\n\r\n00:03:18.573 --\u003e 00:03:20.200\r\nCome on, let's do a pizza run.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.283 --\u003e 00:03:21.785\r\nLove to, but I can't.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.244 --\u003e 00:03:25.372\r\nIf I don't ace these midterms,\r\nDad says he'll throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:03:25.622 --\u003e 00:03:28.125\r\nAnd with my dad,\r\nthat's no idle threat.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.878 --\u003e 00:03:33.505\r\nDICK: Okay, catch you later.\r\n\r\n00:03:35.590 --\u003e 00:03:37.342\r\n(SIGHS WEARILY) Math.\r\n\r\n00:03:37.759 --\u003e 00:03:39.678\r\nWhy did it have to be math?\r\n\r\n00:03:53.984 --\u003e 00:03:57.070\r\nHmm.\r\nMaybe I should take a break.\r\n\r\n00:04:21.428 --\u003e 00:04:23.180\r\nBATGIRL: Catwoman, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:04:25.849 --\u003e 00:04:27.100\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:34.274 --\u003e 00:04:37.277\r\nWell, well.\r\nLook what the bat dragged in.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.360 --\u003e 00:04:39.112\r\nGive up. I've caught you.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.362 --\u003e 00:04:40.906\r\nCaught me? At what?\r\n\r\n00:04:41.031 --\u003e 00:04:42.949\r\nReturning to the\r\nscene of your crime.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.117 --\u003e 00:04:46.244\r\nLook... Batgirl, is it?\r\n\r\n00:04:46.828 --\u003e 00:04:49.831\r\nI'm just trying to find out\r\nwho took the jade-cat statue.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.165 --\u003e 00:04:52.959\r\nIt's an art treasure.\r\nIt belongs to the world.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.293 --\u003e 00:04:55.462\r\nRight. Pull the other one.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.629 --\u003e 00:04:56.755\r\nLook.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.006 --\u003e 00:04:59.132\r\nBATGIRL: Huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:00.634 --\u003e 00:05:03.094\r\nLooks like the alarm cord\r\nwas eaten through with acid\r\n\r\n00:05:03.178 --\u003e 00:05:05.764\r\nlike the locks on the skylight.\r\nSo?\r\n\r\n00:05:06.890 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nThat's not my style.\r\n\r\n00:05:08.600 --\u003e 00:05:09.768\r\nNo finesse.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.353 --\u003e 00:05:12.395\r\n(CLAWS SCRAPING)\r\n\r\n00:05:13.563 --\u003e 00:05:14.815\r\nCATWOMAN: See?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.023 --\u003e 00:05:16.066\r\nOkay.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.608 --\u003e 00:05:18.920\r\nIf you're innocent,\r\ncome down to police headquarters with me\r\n\r\n00:05:18.944 --\u003e 00:05:20.403\r\nand tell them your story.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.487 --\u003e 00:05:23.031\r\nThat's also not my style.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.450 --\u003e 00:05:28.203\r\nOne way or another,\r\nyou're coming with me.\r\n\r\n00:05:28.703 --\u003e 00:05:31.832\r\nBats are just mice with\r\nwings, little girl.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.084 --\u003e 00:05:35.126\r\nBATGIRL: Robin!\r\n\r\n00:05:35.752 --\u003e 00:05:37.629\r\nJust came to\r\ninvestigate the robbery.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.921 --\u003e 00:05:39.798\r\nI didn't expect a convention.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.807 --\u003e 00:05:51.893\r\n- Come on! She's getting away.\r\n- Robin, wait! She's not...\r\n\r\n00:05:58.859 --\u003e 00:06:00.777\r\nHere, kitty, kitty.\r\n\r\n00:06:04.573 --\u003e 00:06:06.241\r\nBye-bye, birdie.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.535 --\u003e 00:06:09.619\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:06:09.703 --\u003e 00:06:11.580\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.374 --\u003e 00:06:17.168\r\nWe'll talk again, soon.\r\n\r\n00:06:19.629 --\u003e 00:06:21.631\r\nROBIN: Well,\r\nyou were a lot of help.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.756 --\u003e 00:06:24.843\r\nI tried to tell you she\r\ndidn't steal the jade cat.\r\n\r\n00:06:25.093 --\u003e 00:06:26.428\r\nHow do you know that?\r\n\r\n00:06:26.761 --\u003e 00:06:28.889\r\nI just know, that's all.\r\n\r\n00:06:29.055 --\u003e 00:06:31.099\r\nOh, well, thank you, Ms.\r\nPsychic.\r\n\r\n00:06:31.433 --\u003e 00:06:33.268\r\nAnd you call yourself\r\na crime-fighter.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.351 --\u003e 00:06:36.021\r\nBATGIRL: If you'd listened\r\ninstead of just barging in-\r\n\r\n00:06:36.146 --\u003e 00:06:38.148\r\nJust don't get in my way\r\nagain, okay?\r\n\r\n00:06:45.155 --\u003e 00:06:46.448\r\nDork.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.915 --\u003e 00:06:57.042\r\n- That was a great class.\r\n- You said it.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.125 --\u003e 00:06:58.835\r\nLet's go get a soda. (COUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:07:10.305 --\u003e 00:07:11.431\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:25.612 --\u003e 00:07:27.197\r\nCATWOMAN: Got the note, I see.\r\n\r\n00:07:31.826 --\u003e 00:07:33.703\r\nIf this is a trick, Catwoman-\r\n\r\n00:07:33.787 --\u003e 00:07:34.955\r\nNo trick.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.121 --\u003e 00:07:38.291\r\nI just wanted to tell you how\r\nimpressed I was with you last night.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.126 --\u003e 00:07:42.128\r\nYou're smart, and you're fast.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.088 --\u003e 00:07:45.090\r\nI thought maybe you'd\r\nlike to work together.\r\n\r\n00:07:45.715 --\u003e 00:07:47.926\r\nAfter all,\r\nagainst the two of us,\r\n\r\n00:07:48.009 --\u003e 00:07:50.512\r\nwhoever took the jade cat\r\ndoesn't stand a chance.\r\n\r\n00:07:53.014 --\u003e 00:07:55.266\r\nOkay. On one condition.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.767 --\u003e 00:07:57.894\r\nIf you're lying to\r\nme and I find out,\r\n\r\n00:07:58.019 --\u003e 00:07:59.479\r\nyou'll give yourself up.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.023 --\u003e 00:08:03.024\r\nDeal.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.286 --\u003e 00:08:19.207\r\nSo, you won't be back in time to help\r\nme look for your old flame Catwoman?\r\n\r\n00:08:19.290 --\u003e 00:08:21.042\r\nSorry, Dick. You're on your own.\r\n\r\n00:08:21.126 --\u003e 00:08:24.212\r\nThis WayneCorp merger is vital\r\nfor the European common market.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.295 --\u003e 00:08:25.797\r\nOkay, sure.\r\n\r\n00:08:25.880 --\u003e 00:08:29.175\r\nAfter all, who needs you when\r\nI've got Batgirl to help me?\r\n\r\n00:08:29.509 --\u003e 00:08:32.679\r\nWatch out for Selina.\r\nShe likes to play mind games.\r\n\r\n00:08:34.806 --\u003e 00:08:37.308\r\nI hope Batgirl isn't\r\nin over her head.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.685 --\u003e 00:08:40.228\r\nThe Stacked Deck?\r\n\r\n00:08:40.437 --\u003e 00:08:42.856\r\nThat's the sleaziest\r\ndive in Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.939 --\u003e 00:08:44.065\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:08:44.149 --\u003e 00:08:47.569\r\nThe only place to find\r\ninformation on the jade cat job.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.944 --\u003e 00:08:49.362\r\nYou're not afraid, are you?\r\n\r\n00:08:51.239 --\u003e 00:08:53.908\r\n(STAMMERS) No.\r\nOf course not. Let's go.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.534 --\u003e 00:08:56.411\r\nThe mouse has guts.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.248 --\u003e 00:09:02.292\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:09:20.602 --\u003e 00:09:21.978\r\nMAN 1; Hey! MAN 2; Here, kitty!\r\n\r\n00:09:22.062 --\u003e 00:09:23.414\r\nMAN 1; Oh, my!\r\nMAN 2; Kitty, kitty!\r\n\r\n00:09:23.438 --\u003e 00:09:27.776\r\nHey, kitten, how's about spending\r\none of your nine lives with me?\r\n\r\n00:09:27.859 --\u003e 00:09:29.986\r\nCrawl back in your litter\r\nbox, creep.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.111 --\u003e 00:09:31.321\r\n(GROWLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:36.910 --\u003e 00:09:38.912\r\nAnyone else wanna get fresh?\r\n\r\n00:09:40.622 --\u003e 00:09:42.040\r\nYou stay.\r\n\r\n00:09:43.124 --\u003e 00:09:45.919\r\nI got nothing to say to\r\nyou, lady.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.840 --\u003e 00:09:51.883\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:54.427 --\u003e 00:09:58.264\r\nDidn't anyone ever tell you it's\r\nimpolite to walk out on a lady?\r\n\r\n00:09:58.348 --\u003e 00:10:00.100\r\nThis is from the jade cat job.\r\n\r\n00:10:00.183 --\u003e 00:10:02.727\r\nResidue of the acid\r\nused on the locks.\r\n\r\n00:10:02.936 --\u003e 00:10:05.063\r\nThat's nice. Why tell me?\r\n\r\n00:10:05.146 --\u003e 00:10:06.981\r\nThey call you \"The Chemist.\"\r\n\r\n00:10:07.232 --\u003e 00:10:10.944\r\nYou know every acid,\r\nexplosive and poison by its first name.\r\n\r\n00:10:11.152 --\u003e 00:10:12.821\r\nAny idea where this was made?\r\n\r\n00:10:13.029 --\u003e 00:10:14.405\r\nCHEMIST: Hmm.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.614 --\u003e 00:10:16.991\r\nBasic corrosive compound.\r\n\r\n00:10:17.117 --\u003e 00:10:22.539\r\nProbably a local manufacturer,\r\nlike Axis, Phoenix, or...\r\n\r\n00:10:24.666 --\u003e 00:10:26.000\r\nCATWOMAN: Hey!\r\n\r\n00:10:27.001 --\u003e 00:10:28.002\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:10:33.508 --\u003e 00:10:35.093\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:38.388 --\u003e 00:10:39.722\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:10:41.850 --\u003e 00:10:43.434\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:45.812 --\u003e 00:10:47.397\r\nWas this part of your plan?\r\n\r\n00:10:47.480 --\u003e 00:10:48.773\r\nIt is now.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.733 --\u003e 00:10:52.235\r\n(INDISTINCT SHOUTING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:10:57.991 --\u003e 00:10:59.784\r\nI think it's closing time.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.125 --\u003e 00:11:08.418\r\n(ENGINE REVS)\r\n\r\n00:11:08.835 --\u003e 00:11:09.878\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:11:11.254 --\u003e 00:11:13.590\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:11:16.593 --\u003e 00:11:17.760\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.223 --\u003e 00:11:24.142\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:11:31.399 --\u003e 00:11:34.152\r\nThis is unit seven,\r\nin pursuit of Catwoman and Batgirl.\r\n\r\n00:11:34.235 --\u003e 00:11:37.155\r\nOh, Daddy, if you could\r\nsee your little girl now.\r\n\r\n00:11:51.044 --\u003e 00:11:52.921\r\n“Hang on! _l am!\r\n\r\n00:11:59.594 --\u003e 00:12:01.471\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.263 --\u003e 00:12:03.932\r\nBATGIRL: You could've\r\ngotten us killed.\r\n\r\n00:12:04.098 --\u003e 00:12:05.225\r\nBut I didn't.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.308 --\u003e 00:12:08.519\r\nAll that, and we didn't even get\r\nthe information we were looking for.\r\n\r\n00:12:08.603 --\u003e 00:12:09.896\r\nSure we did.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.979 --\u003e 00:12:13.399\r\nYou saw the way the chemist freaked\r\nwhen he recognized that acid.\r\n\r\n00:12:13.483 --\u003e 00:12:16.778\r\nI'm willing to bet only\r\none guy in Gotham makes it.\r\n\r\n00:12:16.945 --\u003e 00:12:18.738\r\nAn old friend of mine.\r\n\r\n00:12:19.113 --\u003e 00:12:21.699\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:26.913 --\u003e 00:12:28.081\r\n\u003ci\u003eOFFICER: This is unit seven.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:28.164 --\u003e 00:12:31.334\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe lost Catwoman and Batgirl\r\non the Bayshore Expressway.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:31.501 --\u003e 00:12:33.169\r\nWhat the heck is she up to?\r\n\r\n00:12:42.136 --\u003e 00:12:45.723\r\nBATGIRL: Hey, I recognize\r\nthis place from crime reports.\r\n\r\n00:12:45.807 --\u003e 00:12:47.642\r\nIt used to belong\r\nto Roland Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.725 --\u003e 00:12:49.686\r\nThis is where he\r\ninvented the Renuyu drug\r\n\r\n00:12:49.769 --\u003e 00:12:52.063\r\nthat turned Matt\r\nHagen into Clayface.\r\n\r\n00:12:56.609 --\u003e 00:12:59.112\r\nCATWOMAN: You do know\r\nyour police cases.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.904 --\u003e 00:13:02.240\r\nThis is also where\r\nDaggett developed a virus\r\n\r\n00:13:02.323 --\u003e 00:13:04.367\r\nthat nearly killed\r\nme and my cat.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.034 --\u003e 00:13:06.035\r\n(CLICKS)\r\n\r\n00:13:22.927 --\u003e 00:13:24.137\r\nAw.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.387 --\u003e 00:13:26.472\r\nIt's nice to be right.\r\n\r\n00:13:28.516 --\u003e 00:13:30.935\r\nDAGGETT: Yes, isn't it?\r\n\r\n00:13:31.644 --\u003e 00:13:34.981\r\nSelina Kyle,\r\nhow pleasant to see you again.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.315 --\u003e 00:13:37.608\r\nThe pleasure is all\r\nyours, Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:13:37.692 --\u003e 00:13:39.068\r\nWe'll be leaving now.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.152 --\u003e 00:13:40.945\r\nDAGGETT: On the\r\ncontrary, my dear,\r\n\r\n00:13:41.029 --\u003e 00:13:46.326\r\nyou and your lovely young friend\r\nhere will be staying forever.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.383 --\u003e 00:14:04.344\r\nWhy take the jade cat, Daggett?\r\n\r\n00:14:04.469 --\u003e 00:14:06.554\r\nThere were other more\r\nvaluable treasures.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.721 --\u003e 00:14:09.140\r\nBecause it's exactly what\r\nyou would have taken.\r\n\r\n00:14:09.390 --\u003e 00:14:11.934\r\nAlso,\r\nI need the money to start over.\r\n\r\n00:14:12.226 --\u003e 00:14:13.644\r\n(BATGIRL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:19.567 --\u003e 00:14:25.281\r\nMy legal fees after my last\r\nencounter with Batman left me broke.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.573 --\u003e 00:14:26.741\r\nThe money from this statuette\r\n\r\n00:14:26.824 --\u003e 00:14:29.452\r\nwill set me up quite\r\nnicely somewhere else\r\n\r\n00:14:29.660 --\u003e 00:14:34.165\r\nwhile the cops look for\r\na certain feline thief.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.457 --\u003e 00:14:36.084\r\nSo, what are you going to do?\r\n\r\n00:14:36.167 --\u003e 00:14:39.629\r\nLeave us hanging over one of these vats\r\nwith acid burning through the rope?\r\n\r\n00:14:39.921 --\u003e 00:14:41.172\r\n(LAUGHS)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.422 --\u003e 00:14:43.758\r\nIf there's one thing I've\r\nlearned over the years,\r\n\r\n00:14:43.841 --\u003e 00:14:48.888\r\nit's that you crime-fighting\r\ntypes are very resourceful.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.180 --\u003e 00:14:53.267\r\nSo I'll just have my men shoot you\r\nand throw your bodies into the vats.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.684 --\u003e 00:14:57.313\r\nThere's still enough acid residue\r\nin them to destroy the evidence.\r\n\r\n00:14:58.523 --\u003e 00:14:59.565\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:02.735 --\u003e 00:15:03.945\r\n(BOTH GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.240 --\u003e 00:15:08.324\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:09.450\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:15:14.580 --\u003e 00:15:15.873\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n- (GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:23.798 --\u003e 00:15:25.049\r\n(CATWOMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.806 --\u003e 00:15:33.141\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:15:33.433 --\u003e 00:15:36.477\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:49.907 --\u003e 00:15:51.033\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:15:55.413 --\u003e 00:15:56.747\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:58.207 --\u003e 00:16:00.084\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:00.209 --\u003e 00:16:01.627\r\nROBIN: Not bad.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.961 --\u003e 00:16:03.463\r\nNot bad yourself.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.671 --\u003e 00:16:04.881\r\nHow'd you find us?\r\n\r\n00:16:04.964 --\u003e 00:16:07.842\r\nMs. Kitty isn't the only one\r\nwith access to a chemical lab.\r\n\r\n00:16:08.134 --\u003e 00:16:09.510\r\nWhere's Catwoman?\r\n\r\n00:16:18.936 --\u003e 00:16:20.730\r\nCATWOMAN: Going\r\nsomewhere, Daggett?\r\n\r\n00:16:22.231 --\u003e 00:16:23.232\r\nGet away from me!\r\n\r\n00:16:30.781 --\u003e 00:16:31.824\r\n(SPLASH ES)\r\n\r\n00:16:37.371 --\u003e 00:16:38.956\r\nCATWOMAN: Nice catch.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.556 --\u003e 00:16:57.183\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:02.897 --\u003e 00:17:05.149\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:10.905 --\u003e 00:17:14.742\r\nNow you know how it feels to look\r\nthe Grim Reaper in the eye, Daggett.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.825 --\u003e 00:17:17.787\r\nThe same way I felt when you\r\npumped me full of your virus.\r\n\r\n00:17:17.870 --\u003e 00:17:19.080\r\nBATGIRL: No!\r\n\r\n00:17:19.455 --\u003e 00:17:21.958\r\nIf you let him fall,\r\nyou're no better than he is.\r\n\r\n00:17:22.041 --\u003e 00:17:23.376\r\nOh, grow up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.335 --\u003e 00:17:25.503\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:28.506 --\u003e 00:17:29.507\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:29.966 --\u003e 00:17:31.592\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.016 --\u003e 00:17:40.393\r\nCatwoman, wait!\r\n\r\n00:17:43.688 --\u003e 00:17:45.398\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:17:45.648 --\u003e 00:17:48.067\r\nRelax. You've had a busy day.\r\n\r\n00:18:23.227 --\u003e 00:18:24.395\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:18:37.491 --\u003e 00:18:38.701\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:42.913 --\u003e 00:18:43.956\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:52.423 --\u003e 00:18:55.092\r\nYou were going to keep that\r\nstatue all along, weren't you?\r\n\r\n00:18:55.551 --\u003e 00:18:56.802\r\nOf course.\r\n\r\n00:18:56.927 --\u003e 00:19:00.640\r\nHaven't you learned yet that only\r\nthe strong survive in this game?\r\n\r\n00:19:03.351 --\u003e 00:19:04.894\r\nOkay, I admit it.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.977 --\u003e 00:19:07.396\r\nI was just playing\r\nwith you at first.\r\n\r\n00:19:07.772 --\u003e 00:19:09.357\r\nBut you really impressed me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.482 --\u003e 00:19:11.067\r\nWe make a good team.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.359 --\u003e 00:19:13.486\r\nTogether we could\r\npick this town clean.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.569 --\u003e 00:19:15.905\r\nEven Batman wouldn't\r\nbe a match for us.\r\n\r\n00:19:15.988 --\u003e 00:19:19.533\r\nAnd the cops are a joke,\r\nespecially that senile fool Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:19:21.202 --\u003e 00:19:23.245\r\nWe had a deal, remember?\r\n\r\n00:19:23.496 --\u003e 00:19:24.497\r\nYou lost.\r\n\r\n00:19:24.830 --\u003e 00:19:26.374\r\nGive yourself up now.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.625 --\u003e 00:19:28.668\r\nFreeze!\r\n\r\n00:19:31.212 --\u003e 00:19:32.838\r\nOkay. You win.\r\n\r\n00:19:33.297 --\u003e 00:19:35.299\r\nAnd by the way,\r\nBatgirl's innocent.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.383 --\u003e 00:19:37.093\r\nShe was acting under coercion.\r\n\r\n00:19:47.561 --\u003e 00:19:49.021\r\nYou should've said yes.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.230 --\u003e 00:19:52.358\r\nIf I had,\r\nI'd be a rat with wings.\r\n\r\n00:19:57.363 --\u003e 00:20:00.116\r\nI knew you had Catwoman\r\non a leash all along.\r\n\r\n00:20:00.282 --\u003e 00:20:01.992\r\nYou're a lousy liar.\r\n\r\n00:20:02.076 --\u003e 00:20:03.661\r\nBut thanks for trying.\r\n\r\n00:20:06.330 --\u003e 00:20:07.373\r\n(OFFICER EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:08.082 --\u003e 00:20:09.208\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:20:15.548 --\u003e 00:20:17.675\r\n- Are you guys all right?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:20:20.052 --\u003e 00:20:21.762\r\nI said I'd let them take me,\r\n\r\n00:20:21.971 --\u003e 00:20:24.014\r\nbut I didn't say how far.\r\n\r\n00:20:28.352 --\u003e 00:20:29.478\r\n(EXCLAIMS)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.645 --\u003e 00:20:31.021\r\nIt's okay.\r\n\r\n00:20:31.480 --\u003e 00:20:33.149\r\nThere'll be another time.\r\n\r\n00:20:42.908 --\u003e 00:20:44.910\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:09.769 --\u003e 00:21:10.770\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E09 - Lock-Up (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:07.424 --\u003e 00:00:09.718\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:17.494 --\u003e 00:01:19.788\r\nSCARECROW: Don't take me back there!\r\nPlease!\r\n\r\n00:01:21.540 --\u003e 00:01:22.958\r\nLook at me, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:01:23.250 --\u003e 00:01:24.751\r\nI'm shaking with fear.\r\n\r\n00:01:24.960 --\u003e 00:01:27.087\r\nMe, the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:01:27.170 --\u003e 00:01:29.798\r\nI wasn't even going\r\nback to crime this time.\r\n\r\n00:01:29.881 --\u003e 00:01:32.342\r\nI just had to get away from him.\r\n\r\n00:01:35.470 --\u003e 00:01:36.638\r\n(WHIMPERS)\r\n\r\n00:01:39.516 --\u003e 00:01:41.393\r\nBOLTON: I'll take it from\r\nhere, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.603 --\u003e 00:01:45.439\r\nLyle Bolton, Chief of Security.\r\n\r\n00:01:45.981 --\u003e 00:01:48.567\r\nCongratulations,\r\nProfessor Crane.\r\n\r\n00:01:49.026 --\u003e 00:01:52.571\r\nYou're the first inmate to\r\nescape Arkham under my charge.\r\n\r\n00:01:52.738 --\u003e 00:01:55.657\r\n- (WHIMPERS)\r\n- You're also the last.\r\n\r\n00:01:56.575 --\u003e 00:02:00.579\r\nI won't let you and the people of\r\nGotham City down again, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:02:01.204 --\u003e 00:02:02.623\r\n(SINISTER LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:12.215 --\u003e 00:02:14.676\r\nThat Bolton's a 10\r\non the creep-o-meter.\r\n\r\n00:02:14.968 --\u003e 00:02:17.721\r\nBut it seems like he's doing a good\r\njob keeping the inmates in check.\r\n\r\n00:02:18.055 --\u003e 00:02:19.389\r\nMaybe too good.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.767 --\u003e 00:02:23.727\r\n(GAVEL BANGING)\r\n\r\n00:02:25.354 --\u003e 00:02:27.356\r\nI've called this\r\ninformal inquest\r\n\r\n00:02:27.439 --\u003e 00:02:30.359\r\nto address certain allegations\r\nbrought to my attention.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.859 --\u003e 00:02:32.944\r\nAre you sure this hearing\r\nwas necessary, Wayne?\r\n\r\n00:02:33.028 --\u003e 00:02:36.114\r\nBolton was brought to Arkham\r\non a Wayne Foundation grant.\r\n\r\n00:02:36.198 --\u003e 00:02:38.408\r\nWith his knowledge of\r\nhigh-tech security systems,\r\n\r\n00:02:38.492 --\u003e 00:02:40.452\r\nI felt he was the\r\nperfect man for the job.\r\n\r\n00:02:40.577 --\u003e 00:02:42.871\r\nIf anyone objects\r\nto my methods...\r\n\r\n00:02:44.247 --\u003e 00:02:46.375\r\nPlease, tell me.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.419 --\u003e 00:02:50.545\r\nMs. Quinn.\r\n\r\n00:02:50.629 --\u003e 00:02:53.548\r\nDo you have any complaints\r\nagainst Mr. Bolton?\r\n\r\n00:02:59.513 --\u003e 00:03:01.848\r\nI got nothing to say.\r\n\r\n00:03:01.932 --\u003e 00:03:04.518\r\nBut surely you must have\r\nsomething you wish to-\r\n\r\n00:03:04.601 --\u003e 00:03:06.687\r\nYou got a hearing\r\nproblem or something?\r\n\r\n00:03:06.770 --\u003e 00:03:11.817\r\nNo, nada, ixnay, zero,\r\nzilch, bupkes, nothing! Okay?\r\n\r\n00:03:13.235 --\u003e 00:03:16.279\r\nIt's all right.\r\nI promise, you can speak freely here.\r\n\r\n00:03:21.493 --\u003e 00:03:24.746\r\n- Mr. Bolton, he's a-\r\n- A hard worker!\r\n\r\n00:03:24.830 --\u003e 00:03:26.623\r\nA real stand-up guy.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.707 --\u003e 00:03:28.583\r\nNo complaints here, Chief.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.335 --\u003e 00:03:33.171\r\nProfessor Crane,\r\nyou've been sitting here for 10 minutes.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.422 --\u003e 00:03:36.299\r\n- Don't you have anything to say?\r\n- No, sir.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.925 --\u003e 00:03:40.178\r\nAnd yet yours was the\r\nloudest voice of protest.\r\n\r\n00:03:40.262 --\u003e 00:03:43.306\r\nYou must have some\r\nmisgivings about my methods.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.016 --\u003e 00:03:46.810\r\nIt seems I was mistaken.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.187 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\nWell then,\r\nbased on today's testimony,\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:53.984\r\nI propose extending\r\nMr. Bolton's contract\r\n\r\n00:03:54.067 --\u003e 00:03:55.907\r\n- for an additional 18 months.\r\n- (INMATES GASP)\r\n\r\n00:03:55.944 --\u003e 00:03:58.613\r\nNo! You can't!\r\nYou don't know what he's doing to us!\r\n\r\n00:03:58.739 --\u003e 00:03:59.781\r\nShut up!\r\n\r\n00:03:59.865 --\u003e 00:04:02.345\r\nDon't listen to jerk-face here.\r\nHe don't know what he's saying!\r\n\r\n00:04:02.576 --\u003e 00:04:04.035\r\nNo, it's all true!\r\n\r\n00:04:04.119 --\u003e 00:04:06.580\r\nIf we don't speak up now,\r\nwe'll never get another chance!\r\n\r\n00:04:06.663 --\u003e 00:04:08.749\r\nHe threatens us,\r\ntakes away our privileges,\r\n\r\n00:04:08.832 --\u003e 00:04:10.292\r\neven when we're good!\r\n\r\n00:04:10.375 --\u003e 00:04:12.377\r\nWe've heard enough\r\nof this nonsense.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.461 --\u003e 00:04:15.255\r\nHe says, \"Scum like us\r\nmust be kept in line.\"\r\n\r\n00:04:15.338 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nThat's why he chains us down at\r\nnight and electrifies our doors.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:22.053\r\nHe held me over a can\r\nfilled with termites.\r\n\r\n00:04:22.137 --\u003e 00:04:24.806\r\nYou hear me? Termites!\r\n\r\n00:04:24.890 --\u003e 00:04:26.266\r\nHe's an animal.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.349 --\u003e 00:04:27.869\r\nSCARFACE: A monster.\r\nCRANE: Keep him away!\r\n\r\n00:04:27.893 --\u003e 00:04:28.977\r\nShut up!\r\n\r\n00:04:29.060 --\u003e 00:04:30.312\r\nAll of you!\r\n\r\n00:04:30.395 --\u003e 00:04:31.897\r\n(ALL GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:53.376 --\u003e 00:04:54.669\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:04:56.129 --\u003e 00:04:57.631\r\nYou're all scum.\r\n\r\n00:04:57.714 --\u003e 00:05:01.259\r\nYou should be beaten within an\r\ninch of your misbegotten lives.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.510 --\u003e 00:05:02.803\r\nI've seen enough!\r\n\r\n00:05:02.886 --\u003e 00:05:05.138\r\nLyle Bolton, you're dismissed!\r\n\r\n00:05:05.222 --\u003e 00:05:07.015\r\nBefore I came here,\r\n\r\n00:05:07.349 --\u003e 00:05:11.353\r\nArkham was a revolving door\r\nfor every maniac in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.561 --\u003e 00:05:13.647\r\nI kept them in. Me!\r\n\r\n00:05:14.147 --\u003e 00:05:18.860\r\nNow I realize I was wrong to\r\npunish those pathetic miscreants!\r\n\r\n00:05:19.277 --\u003e 00:05:21.446\r\nThey're only symptoms.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.780 --\u003e 00:05:23.114\r\nYou're the cause!\r\n\r\n00:05:23.532 --\u003e 00:05:24.991\r\nThe gutless police,\r\n\r\n00:05:25.367 --\u003e 00:05:29.287\r\nmindless bureaucrats,\r\nand coddling doctors!\r\n\r\n00:05:29.496 --\u003e 00:05:34.709\r\nYou should all be locked\r\nup in a cage without a key!\r\n\r\n00:05:42.509 --\u003e 00:05:43.593\r\nMr. Bolton,\r\n\r\n00:05:43.677 --\u003e 00:05:47.806\r\nany comments about your dismissal\r\nand the charges of extreme behavior?\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.894\r\nThis city is an open wound\r\nbegging to be stitched.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.978 --\u003e 00:05:54.771\r\n\u003ci\u003eSince that day three weeks ago,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:54.855 --\u003e 00:05:57.983\r\n\u003ci\u003eLyle Bolton has been\r\nunavailable for further comment.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:58.775 --\u003e 00:06:00.986\r\nNext up on Gotham Insider,\r\n\r\n00:06:01.069 --\u003e 00:06:04.281\r\n\u003ci\u003eshe's gorgeous,\r\nshe's deadly and she's back in town.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:04.364 --\u003e 00:06:07.093\r\n- Once again, Poison \u003ci\u003eIvy\u003c/i\u003e has recently...\r\n- Look at the way these monsters\r\n\r\n00:06:07.117 --\u003e 00:06:09.119\r\nare turned into heroes.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.661 --\u003e 00:06:13.206\r\nIt all starts with the\r\npermissive, liberal media.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.290 --\u003e 00:06:15.292\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe villainous vixen\r\nof vines made off with-\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:06:30.932 --\u003e 00:06:33.268\r\nThanks for the\r\nexclusive, Mr. Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.476 --\u003e 00:06:36.521\r\nDo they always include\r\nsuch a sumptuous meal?\r\n\r\n00:06:36.646 --\u003e 00:06:39.524\r\nOnly when the topic is a\r\nsuccessful Wayne Corp merger.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.691 --\u003e 00:06:41.985\r\nI'm sorry, Mr. Wayne.\r\nYou have an urgent phone call.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:44.195\r\nIf you'll excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.045 --\u003e 00:07:01.421\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:07:01.504 --\u003e 00:07:02.756\r\nWhat the...\r\n\r\n00:07:04.633 --\u003e 00:07:05.634\r\nGreat.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.263 --\u003e 00:07:11.306\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:20.315 --\u003e 00:07:24.235\r\n(HONKING HORN)\r\n\r\n00:07:24.736 --\u003e 00:07:25.737\r\nSummer?\r\n\r\n00:07:31.034 --\u003e 00:07:33.203\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:56.226 --\u003e 00:07:57.268\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:07:57.352 --\u003e 00:08:00.563\r\nThe time has come to cleanse\r\nGotham of the real criminals.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.772 --\u003e 00:08:04.734\r\nYou apprehend them, Dark Knight,\r\nand Lock-Up will put them away.\r\n\r\n00:08:05.026 --\u003e 00:08:07.487\r\nTogether we can make\r\nthis city safe again.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.612 --\u003e 00:08:09.572\r\nBy kidnapping innocent victims?\r\n\r\n00:08:10.031 --\u003e 00:08:11.825\r\nI don't think so.\r\n\r\n00:08:12.283 --\u003e 00:08:14.619\r\nIf you're not part\r\nof the solution,\r\n\r\n00:08:15.036 --\u003e 00:08:16.871\r\nthen you're part of the problem.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.214 --\u003e 00:08:27.966\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:34.472 --\u003e 00:08:35.515\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:08:37.434 --\u003e 00:08:39.352\r\nYou disappoint me, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.436 --\u003e 00:08:42.814\r\nI thought you'd wanna see this\r\nmedia leech get her comeuppance.\r\n\r\n00:08:49.612 --\u003e 00:08:51.406\r\n(SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:09:00.957 --\u003e 00:09:02.876\r\n(BOTH SCREAM)\r\n\r\n00:09:05.128 --\u003e 00:09:06.629\r\n(BOTH GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:06.713 --\u003e 00:09:08.048\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:09:13.136 --\u003e 00:09:14.637\r\nJust what this town needs,\r\n\r\n00:09:14.721 --\u003e 00:09:17.015\r\nanother psycho in a\r\nHalloween costume.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.649 --\u003e 00:09:28.985\r\nThis is Lyle Bolton's handiwork.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.069 --\u003e 00:09:31.029\r\nNo one configures\r\na lock like him.\r\n\r\n00:09:31.112 --\u003e 00:09:34.324\r\nYou mean this Lock-Up nut is\r\nthe security creep from Arkham?\r\n\r\n00:09:34.407 --\u003e 00:09:35.700\r\nWithout a doubt.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.867 --\u003e 00:09:39.329\r\nAnother fine villain made possible\r\nby a grant from the Wayne Foundation.\r\n\r\n00:09:41.414 --\u003e 00:09:42.791\r\nOnly kidding.\r\n\r\n00:09:46.377 --\u003e 00:09:47.921\r\nBolton's last known address.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.004 --\u003e 00:09:49.464\r\nSee what you can find.\r\n\r\n00:09:59.182 --\u003e 00:10:01.935\r\nNice look. Early Alcatraz.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.119 --\u003e 00:10:20.495\r\n(MUFFLED GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:30.171\r\nDr. Bartholomew?\r\n\r\n00:10:42.475 --\u003e 00:10:43.518\r\nCommissioner?\r\n\r\n00:10:43.601 --\u003e 00:10:45.478\r\nI lit the signal, Bats.\r\n\r\n00:10:46.479 --\u003e 00:10:50.191\r\nThat nutcase took the commish\r\nand gave me these new cuff links.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.275 --\u003e 00:10:54.487\r\nTook me 15 minutes to hit the\r\nswitch on your overgrown flashlight.\r\n\r\n00:10:54.696 --\u003e 00:10:57.365\r\nYou got any idea what this is all\r\nabout, cowl-head?\r\n\r\n00:10:57.657 --\u003e 00:10:58.867\r\nI think so.\r\n\r\n00:10:59.033 --\u003e 00:11:00.451\r\nFirst Summer Gleeson,\r\n\r\n00:11:00.535 --\u003e 00:11:02.495\r\nthen Bartholomew,\r\nand now Gordon.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.579 --\u003e 00:11:04.455\r\nPut extra security\r\naround Mayor Hill.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.998 --\u003e 00:11:06.583\r\nYou mind letting\r\nme in on the joke?\r\n\r\n00:11:09.377 --\u003e 00:11:10.378\r\nTypical.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.673 --\u003e 00:11:16.426\r\nMAYOR HILL: You want me\r\nto hide during a crisis?\r\n\r\n00:11:16.801 --\u003e 00:11:18.136\r\nHow will that look\r\nto the voters?\r\n\r\n00:11:18.553 --\u003e 00:11:20.221\r\nThis is overkill, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.305 --\u003e 00:11:23.016\r\nI have the finest security\r\nsystem in the city.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.099 --\u003e 00:11:24.976\r\nIt's virtually impenetrable.\r\n\r\n00:11:25.059 --\u003e 00:11:26.436\r\nBATMAN: Virtually.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.730 --\u003e 00:11:30.315\r\nBut not completely.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.149 --\u003e 00:11:33.693\r\nIf we can slip through,\r\nso can Lock-Up.\r\n\r\n00:11:38.281 --\u003e 00:11:40.491\r\n(ALL COUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:11:43.703 --\u003e 00:11:44.746\r\nMayor!\r\n\r\n00:12:05.683 --\u003e 00:12:07.477\r\nForget to pay a parking ticket?\r\n\r\n00:12:11.189 --\u003e 00:12:12.607\r\n(DOOR OPENS)\r\n\r\n00:12:13.399 --\u003e 00:12:14.692\r\nMove it.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.153 --\u003e 00:12:18.238\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.285 --\u003e 00:12:25.536\r\nAhh!\r\n\r\n00:12:30.833 --\u003e 00:12:33.628\r\nI see your taste in prisoners\r\nis improving, Bolton.\r\n\r\n00:12:34.879 --\u003e 00:12:38.508\r\nYou have three seconds\r\nto release those bars.\r\n\r\n00:12:38.883 --\u003e 00:12:41.552\r\nIf you let us go now, Bolton,\r\nI can guarantee leniency.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.513 --\u003e 00:12:45.056\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.394 --\u003e 00:12:51.729\r\nI don't do leniency.\r\n\r\n00:12:59.654 --\u003e 00:13:01.030\r\nStill nothing.\r\n\r\n00:13:02.949 --\u003e 00:13:05.034\r\nJust as I suspected\r\nfrom the rust.\r\n\r\n00:13:05.118 --\u003e 00:13:07.912\r\nA high salt content\r\nlike seawater.\r\n\r\n00:13:07.996 --\u003e 00:13:12.250\r\nHey. What if F-84 is the\r\nserial number of a ship?\r\n\r\n00:13:14.294 --\u003e 00:13:15.878\r\nBingo.\r\n\r\n00:13:20.300 --\u003e 00:13:22.343\r\nThe Halsey was used\r\nas a temporary prison\r\n\r\n00:13:22.427 --\u003e 00:13:24.095\r\nwhile Stonegate was being built.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.762 --\u003e 00:13:25.805\r\nComputer.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.888 --\u003e 00:13:28.891\r\nName of security chief\r\nduring Operation Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:13:30.601 --\u003e 00:13:32.395\r\nROBIN: Well, blow me down.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.411 --\u003e 00:13:50.079\r\nI've horned in on\r\nhis power source.\r\n\r\n00:13:51.956 --\u003e 00:13:54.792\r\nShut down the security systems.\r\nI'll take care of Bolton.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.297 --\u003e 00:14:01.382\r\nYou brought this on\r\nyourself, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.818 --\u003e 00:14:21.986\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:14:26.991 --\u003e 00:14:28.910\r\nYou're resourceful, Dark Knight.\r\n\r\n00:14:28.993 --\u003e 00:14:31.621\r\nBut sooner or\r\nlater, you're mine.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.623 --\u003e 00:14:34.999\r\n(DISTANT EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:14:48.846 --\u003e 00:14:50.014\r\n(YELPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:51.307 --\u003e 00:14:53.476\r\nNo regard for authority.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.810 --\u003e 00:14:55.645\r\nWe'll soon change that.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.020 --\u003e 00:14:58.106\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:07.031 --\u003e 00:15:09.492\r\nYou think that was\r\nmy only defense?\r\n\r\n00:15:11.869 --\u003e 00:15:13.371\r\nIt's over, Bolton.\r\n\r\n00:15:15.206 --\u003e 00:15:16.374\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:16.874 --\u003e 00:15:18.167\r\nFace it, Bolton.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.376 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nYou've already lost.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.086 --\u003e 00:15:21.295\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:15:28.511 --\u003e 00:15:32.974\r\nAmazing what a little corrupted\r\ncomputer code will do.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.437 --\u003e 00:15:38.521\r\n(SUMMER GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:15:46.571 --\u003e 00:15:48.531\r\nI still have my prisoners.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.207 --\u003e 00:16:40.625\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:43.211 --\u003e 00:16:45.755\r\n- Commissioner? Mr. Mayor?\r\n- MAYOR HILL: Down here.\r\n\r\n00:16:49.175 --\u003e 00:16:50.801\r\nHang on, I'll get you out.\r\n\r\n00:16:52.011 --\u003e 00:16:53.846\r\n(THUNDER RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:16:59.560 --\u003e 00:17:01.896\r\nI was working with you, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:17:02.104 --\u003e 00:17:04.106\r\nYou apprehended the\r\nscum of the earth,\r\n\r\n00:17:04.190 --\u003e 00:17:06.067\r\nand I kept them locked away!\r\n\r\n00:17:06.984 --\u003e 00:17:08.819\r\nI've seen how you\r\ntreat your prisoners.\r\n\r\n00:17:08.903 --\u003e 00:17:10.571\r\nForgotten and scared.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.696 --\u003e 00:17:12.490\r\nWithout hope or compassion.\r\n\r\n00:17:12.573 --\u003e 00:17:15.493\r\nCan it be you actually\r\ncare for those creatures?\r\n\r\n00:17:15.576 --\u003e 00:17:17.828\r\nYou're just as\r\ncrazy as they are.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.499 --\u003e 00:17:23.334\r\nAlmost got it.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.417 --\u003e 00:17:25.127\r\nRobin, hurry!\r\n\r\n00:17:46.399 --\u003e 00:17:51.153\r\nI could have rid Gotham of the fools\r\nin city hall and the police department.\r\n\r\n00:17:51.320 --\u003e 00:17:53.656\r\nWe could have made\r\nour own order!\r\n\r\n00:17:53.739 --\u003e 00:17:56.784\r\nI was born to fight\r\nyour brand of order.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.867 --\u003e 00:17:58.828\r\nIf that's your decision.\r\n\r\n00:18:02.164 --\u003e 00:18:03.457\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:09.463 --\u003e 00:18:10.590\r\n(THUDS)\r\n\r\n00:18:17.430 --\u003e 00:18:18.723\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:35.197 --\u003e 00:18:36.574\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:36.949 --\u003e 00:18:39.410\r\nStay close.\r\nI think this is the way out.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.996 --\u003e 00:18:44.206\r\nWe could have been a team.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.923 --\u003e 00:18:54.342\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:19:17.365 --\u003e 00:19:18.491\r\nBatman?\r\n\r\n00:19:33.714 --\u003e 00:19:34.840\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:38.803 --\u003e 00:19:40.763\r\nI keep asking him to\r\nteach me that trick.\r\n\r\n00:19:55.945 --\u003e 00:19:58.572\r\nHARLEY: Hey, look, guys.\r\nThe big shot's back.\r\n\r\n00:19:58.781 --\u003e 00:20:00.783\r\n(INMATES CHATTERING)\r\n\r\n00:20:10.918 --\u003e 00:20:15.881\r\nNow you shall learn new lessons in fear.\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:20:23.681 --\u003e 00:20:27.560\r\nThey thought they could trap\r\nme in a world of lunatics,\r\n\r\n00:20:27.852 --\u003e 00:20:29.478\r\nbut I showed them.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.146 --\u003e 00:20:32.898\r\nNow,\r\nI can keep an eye on everyone.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.442 --\u003e 00:20:37.445\r\nThey'll never slip\r\npast me again.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.659 --\u003e 00:20:45.911\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S03 E10 - Deep Freeze (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:07.257 --\u003e 00:00:09.259\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.809 --\u003e 00:01:42.728\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:01:44.855 --\u003e 00:01:46.857\r\n(FOOTSTEPS THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:01:51.361 --\u003e 00:01:52.946\r\n(BLOWING WHISTLE)\r\n\r\n00:01:56.033 --\u003e 00:01:57.784\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:02:07.919 --\u003e 00:02:09.546\r\n(GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:02:15.510 --\u003e 00:02:16.720\r\nFire!\r\n\r\n00:02:32.569 --\u003e 00:02:34.029\r\n(DISTANT EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.112 --\u003e 00:02:36.114\r\n(MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:02:38.325 --\u003e 00:02:39.951\r\n(GUNS FIRING)\r\n\r\n00:02:40.744 --\u003e 00:02:42.162\r\n(EXPLOSION)\r\n\r\n00:02:42.996 --\u003e 00:02:44.581\r\nInteresting.\r\n\r\n00:02:45.457 --\u003e 00:02:47.292\r\n(GUNFIRE CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:57.135 --\u003e 00:02:58.845\r\nGuard? Guard?\r\n\r\n00:03:00.639 --\u003e 00:03:01.723\r\nGuard!\r\n\r\n00:03:06.520 --\u003e 00:03:09.231\r\n(YELLS) Help me!\r\n\r\n00:03:10.023 --\u003e 00:03:11.233\r\n(SHATTERS)\r\n\r\n00:03:15.821 --\u003e 00:03:17.489\r\nROBIN: You gotta give\r\nMr. Freeze credit.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.572 --\u003e 00:03:20.158\r\nThat's the most original\r\nbreakout this year.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.242 --\u003e 00:03:22.035\r\nYes, but I don't think\r\nhe was behind it.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.119 --\u003e 00:03:24.121\r\nLook at the expression\r\nof fear on his face.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.246 --\u003e 00:03:25.455\r\nThat's not easy to fake,\r\n\r\n00:03:25.539 --\u003e 00:03:28.333\r\nespecially for a man claiming\r\nto be dead to emotions.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.417 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nFreeze was taken\r\nagainst his will,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:32.796\r\nand obviously by someone\r\nwith expertise in robotics.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.963 --\u003e 00:03:36.425\r\nThen maybe we'd better\r\nconsult our own robot expert.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.598 --\u003e 00:03:45.267\r\nGreetings, dynamic duo.\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.685\r\nI'm your biggest fan.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.228 --\u003e 00:03:49.938\r\nWhat is it?\r\n\r\n00:03:51.022 --\u003e 00:03:52.149\r\nMwah!\r\n\r\n00:03:53.108 --\u003e 00:03:54.484\r\nI just wanna help.\r\n\r\n00:03:57.028 --\u003e 00:03:59.281\r\nJust wanna help.\r\nJust wanna help.\r\n\r\n00:04:00.657 --\u003e 00:04:01.867\r\nPoor little critter.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.950 --\u003e 00:04:03.994\r\nI never could get his\r\nprogramming right.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.077 --\u003e 00:04:05.287\r\nCute toy, Karl.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.370 --\u003e 00:04:08.415\r\nYou know I'm out of the\r\nrobot business, Batman.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.083 --\u003e 00:04:13.170\r\nAll I make anymore are little\r\nfriends to keep me company.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.253 --\u003e 00:04:14.463\r\nLike Tiny, here?\r\n\r\n00:04:15.714 --\u003e 00:04:18.216\r\nWell, if it isn't old M-9.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.300 --\u003e 00:04:20.343\r\n- It's one of yours?\r\n- Not really.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.469 --\u003e 00:04:23.555\r\nI once created a smaller\r\nprototype for Grant Walker.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.930 --\u003e 00:04:25.932\r\n- The guy who builds those theme parks?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:04:26.016 --\u003e 00:04:28.643\r\nI was one of Walker's\r\noriginal visioneers.\r\n\r\n00:04:28.727 --\u003e 00:04:31.438\r\nConstructing and programming\r\nthe animatronic figures\r\n\r\n00:04:31.521 --\u003e 00:04:33.440\r\nhe used in his park attractions.\r\n\r\n00:04:33.732 --\u003e 00:04:37.110\r\nThough it looks like old Grant's\r\nboys pumped up the design a bit.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.194 --\u003e 00:04:39.654\r\nBATMAN: I'm wondering how\r\nimproved these robots are.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.821 --\u003e 00:04:42.657\r\nAnd why one of them was\r\nsent to kidnap Mr. Freeze.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.441 --\u003e 00:05:18.026\r\nImpressive.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.109 --\u003e 00:05:19.402\r\nWALKER: \"impressive?\"\r\n\r\n00:05:19.486 --\u003e 00:05:22.030\r\nYou gaze upon all this and\r\ncan only say \"impressive\"?\r\n\r\n00:05:22.239 --\u003e 00:05:24.616\r\nThough perhaps I\r\nshouldn't be surprised.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.075 --\u003e 00:05:29.037\r\nI've made a hobby of studying\r\nyour chilly history, Victor Fries.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.246 --\u003e 00:05:30.789\r\nAnd you are?\r\n\r\n00:05:30.997 --\u003e 00:05:32.916\r\nGrant Walker,\r\nat your service, sir.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.083 --\u003e 00:05:36.586\r\nThis is Oceana,\r\nmy prototype vision of the future.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.878 --\u003e 00:05:39.673\r\nA vision that you shall\r\nhelp make a reality.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.840 --\u003e 00:05:41.049\r\nDoubtful.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.132 --\u003e 00:05:42.259\r\nWe'll see.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.342 --\u003e 00:05:44.344\r\nMake sure that our\r\nguest is comfortable.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.221 --\u003e 00:05:47.430\r\n(DEVICE BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:05:48.014 --\u003e 00:05:50.600\r\n\u003ci\u003eSir, we've picked up an unauthorized\r\ncraft entering our area.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:05:51.685 --\u003e 00:05:55.105\r\nCan't afford nosy trespassers\r\nat this stage of the game.\r\n\r\n00:05:55.188 --\u003e 00:05:57.858\r\nDispatch our usual\r\ndeterrents, Mr. Johnson.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.321 --\u003e 00:06:06.783\r\nI still don't see why a theme-park\r\nmogul would kidnap Mr. Freeze.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.867 --\u003e 00:06:09.744\r\nMen like Walker are obsessed\r\nwith getting their own way.\r\n\r\n00:06:09.828 --\u003e 00:06:12.622\r\nAnd they don't let little\r\nthings like the law stop them.\r\n\r\n00:06:12.706 --\u003e 00:06:13.790\r\n(COMPUTER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:06:13.874 --\u003e 00:06:15.500\r\nI'm picking something\r\nup on the scanner.\r\n\r\n00:06:15.584 --\u003e 00:06:17.502\r\nThree small objects\r\ncoming in fast.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.315 --\u003e 00:06:39.357\r\nHang on!\r\n\r\n00:06:52.871 --\u003e 00:06:54.456\r\n- (GROANS)\r\n- (COMPUTER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:07:02.172 --\u003e 00:07:03.423\r\nThe power shorted out.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.506 --\u003e 00:07:05.550\r\nAnd those things\r\nare coming back.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.558 --\u003e 00:07:15.310\r\nIntruder threat has\r\nbeen neutralized, sir.\r\n\r\n00:07:15.393 --\u003e 00:07:16.728\r\n\u003ci\u003eExcellent.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:07:28.114 --\u003e 00:07:30.075\r\nLooks like we're swimming home.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.158 --\u003e 00:07:32.911\r\nNot before we have a\r\ntalk with Mr. Walker.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.259 --\u003e 00:07:49.678\r\n(DOOR BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:07:57.185 --\u003e 00:08:00.647\r\nI think you'll find that suit is a\r\nperfect duplicate of your original.\r\n\r\n00:08:00.730 --\u003e 00:08:03.984\r\nAutomatic temperature control,\r\nincreased cybernetic strength.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.192 --\u003e 00:08:06.152\r\nEven the cold gun works.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.374 --\u003e 00:08:22.669\r\nYes. Logically,\r\nI should do the same to you.\r\n\r\n00:08:22.752 --\u003e 00:08:24.462\r\nJust hear me out, please.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.546 --\u003e 00:08:27.090\r\nAs I said,\r\nI've studied you and your work.\r\n\r\n00:08:27.173 --\u003e 00:08:29.300\r\nDo you realize that\r\nin your frozen state\r\n\r\n00:08:29.384 --\u003e 00:08:32.929\r\nyou'll age much slower\r\nthan an ordinary human?\r\n\r\n00:08:33.013 --\u003e 00:08:35.432\r\nYou're practically\r\nimmortal, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.515 --\u003e 00:08:39.978\r\nYes, eternal life trapped\r\nin this wretched shell.\r\n\r\n00:08:40.145 --\u003e 00:08:42.063\r\nWhat a miserable joke.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.188 --\u003e 00:08:46.151\r\nOh, miserable to you,\r\nbut a godsend to me.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.234 --\u003e 00:08:48.695\r\nLook at me, Mr. Freeze.\r\nI'm an old man.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.778 --\u003e 00:08:51.364\r\nI've created wonders\r\nin my lifetime,\r\n\r\n00:08:51.448 --\u003e 00:08:53.825\r\nbut there is still\r\nso much to do.\r\n\r\n00:08:53.992 --\u003e 00:08:56.036\r\nI want to change as you have.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.119 --\u003e 00:09:01.416\r\nTo become like you,\r\na being of blessed, eternal cold.\r\n\r\n00:09:01.791 --\u003e 00:09:03.460\r\nYou're insane.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.543 --\u003e 00:09:07.547\r\nOnly you have the know-how to duplicate\r\nthe accident that made you what you are.\r\n\r\n00:09:07.630 --\u003e 00:09:10.050\r\nWhat I long to become.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.468 --\u003e 00:09:13.428\r\n- (GROANING)\r\n- You want to live like this?\r\n\r\n00:09:13.511 --\u003e 00:09:15.805\r\nAbandoned and alone?\r\n\r\n00:09:15.889 --\u003e 00:09:19.017\r\nA prisoner in a world you can\r\nsee, but never touch?\r\n\r\n00:09:20.185 --\u003e 00:09:21.269\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:23.104 --\u003e 00:09:25.565\r\nOld and infirm as you are,\r\n\r\n00:09:25.648 --\u003e 00:09:30.195\r\nI'd trade 1,000 of my frozen\r\nyears for your worst day.\r\n\r\n00:09:30.570 --\u003e 00:09:32.030\r\nActually,\r\n\r\n00:09:32.113 --\u003e 00:09:35.075\r\nI had another kind\r\nof swap in mind.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.914 --\u003e 00:09:41.915\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:09:42.582 --\u003e 00:09:43.958\r\nNora.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.042 --\u003e 00:09:47.128\r\nI was a major investor in\r\nGothCorp a few years back\r\n\r\n00:09:47.212 --\u003e 00:09:50.131\r\nand put up some money for\r\ntheir cryogenics program.\r\n\r\n00:09:51.424 --\u003e 00:09:55.095\r\nI trust you know the young\r\nlady behind the glass.\r\n\r\n00:09:57.180 --\u003e 00:09:58.306\r\nMy wife.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.389 --\u003e 00:10:01.559\r\nThe GothCorp execs think\r\nshe perished in the fire,\r\n\r\n00:10:01.643 --\u003e 00:10:02.977\r\nbut my men got her out.\r\n\r\n00:10:03.061 --\u003e 00:10:06.314\r\nI have the technology to restore\r\nher, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.397 --\u003e 00:10:09.442\r\nAll you have to do\r\nis grant my wish.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.819 --\u003e 00:10:12.362\r\nVery well.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.030 --\u003e 00:10:15.740\r\n(INDISTINCT CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:10:20.745 --\u003e 00:10:21.955\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:37.178 --\u003e 00:10:38.596\r\n(BLADES WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:10:54.487 --\u003e 00:10:56.489\r\n- (MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n- (AUDIENCE APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:11:00.160 --\u003e 00:11:02.036\r\n\u003ci\u003eWelcome, friends.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:02.120 --\u003e 00:11:06.541\r\n\u003ci\u003eThanks to all our hard work,\r\nOceana's nearly up and running.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:06.666 --\u003e 00:11:10.712\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow, while most folks believe\r\nOceana's just another theme park,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:10.962 --\u003e 00:11:12.714\r\n\u003ci\u003ewe know better.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:12.922 --\u003e 00:11:16.426\r\n\u003ci\u003eFact of the matter is,\r\nit's not too nice out there anymore.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:16.509 --\u003e 00:11:19.053\r\n\u003ci\u003eCrime, hatred, violence.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:19.179 --\u003e 00:11:21.055\r\n\u003ci\u003eThings keep going on like that,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:21.389 --\u003e 00:11:23.766\r\n\u003ci\u003eit could mean the\r\nend of civilization.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:23.933 --\u003e 00:11:29.189\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat's why I decided to build a city\r\nwhere good folks can live in peace.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:29.606 --\u003e 00:11:32.358\r\n\u003ci\u003eA new Garden of\r\nEden, you might say,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:32.442 --\u003e 00:11:35.195\r\n\u003ci\u003efrom which a new race\r\nof people can spring.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:35.486 --\u003e 00:11:38.698\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow, of course you can't have\r\nspring without a little winter.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:38.990 --\u003e 00:11:41.242\r\n\u003ci\u003eAbout five years of it, I'd say.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:44.579 --\u003e 00:11:46.289\r\n\u003ci\u003eNow, don't anybody worry.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:46.372 --\u003e 00:11:49.918\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe'll all be warm\r\nas toast in here.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:50.001 --\u003e 00:11:53.296\r\n\u003ci\u003eAs for those folks\r\noutside, well, it's sad,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:53.379 --\u003e 00:11:56.674\r\n\u003ci\u003ebut I'm only speeding up what\r\nthey were doing to themselves.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:11:56.799 --\u003e 00:11:58.676\r\nBrother.\r\nHe's all heart, isn't he?\r\n\r\n00:11:58.760 --\u003e 00:12:00.220\r\nWalker's a madman.\r\n\r\n00:12:00.637 --\u003e 00:12:01.888\r\nROBIN: Whoa!\r\n\r\n00:12:04.933 --\u003e 00:12:06.017\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:07.352 --\u003e 00:12:08.603\r\n(ELECTRICITY BUZZING)\r\n\r\n00:12:11.272 --\u003e 00:12:12.273\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:12:19.113 --\u003e 00:12:20.448\r\n(CRASHES)\r\n\r\n00:12:22.325 --\u003e 00:12:23.326\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.628 --\u003e 00:12:36.130\r\n- MAN: Look.\r\n\u003ci\u003e- Every time I open a park,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:36.214 --\u003e 00:12:38.216\r\n\u003ci\u003eI get gate-crashers.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:38.299 --\u003e 00:12:41.344\r\nWe've seen your insane\r\nvision of the future, Walker.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.552 --\u003e 00:12:46.391\r\n\u003ci\u003eMy world will have no\r\ncrime, violence, or pain.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:46.557 --\u003e 00:12:48.977\r\nYou can add free will\r\nto that list too.\r\n\r\n00:12:49.060 --\u003e 00:12:51.104\r\n\u003ci\u003eA small price to pay for order.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:12:51.354 --\u003e 00:12:52.605\r\nYour order.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.689 --\u003e 00:12:54.190\r\nFor your select few.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.315 --\u003e 00:12:57.318\r\n\u003ci\u003eExcuse me, but I fail to\r\nsee the problem with that.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:20.758 --\u003e 00:13:24.345\r\nFreeze, I don't know what\r\nWalker said or promised you,\r\n\r\n00:13:24.554 --\u003e 00:13:26.514\r\nbut you can't help him go\r\nthrough with this plan.\r\n\r\n00:13:26.681 --\u003e 00:13:29.100\r\nI have no choice.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.027 --\u003e 00:13:40.445\r\n(BUZZES)\r\n\r\n00:13:46.701 --\u003e 00:13:47.702\r\n(BATMAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:47.785 --\u003e 00:13:49.537\r\nWALKER: I know it's a\r\nbit chilly in there,\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.332\r\nbut I figured you'd like to\r\nstick around and see the show.\r\n\r\n00:13:52.415 --\u003e 00:13:53.791\r\nHow are we doing?\r\n\r\n00:13:56.210 --\u003e 00:13:57.337\r\nReady.\r\n\r\n00:13:57.420 --\u003e 00:13:58.713\r\nLet's do it.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.511 --\u003e 00:14:06.929\r\n(MACHINE POWERS UP)\r\n\r\n00:14:12.101 --\u003e 00:14:13.936\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.230 --\u003e 00:14:17.857\r\n(SCREAMING LOUDER)\r\n\r\n00:14:28.451 --\u003e 00:14:30.119\r\nIncredible.\r\n\r\n00:14:30.203 --\u003e 00:14:33.164\r\nThis suit has more power\r\nthan I ever dreamed.\r\n\r\n00:14:33.456 --\u003e 00:14:34.457\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:35.958 --\u003e 00:14:37.126\r\nOh!\r\n\r\n00:14:37.210 --\u003e 00:14:38.419\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:14:38.503 --\u003e 00:14:39.754\r\nAre you all right, sir?\r\n\r\n00:14:39.837 --\u003e 00:14:42.298\r\n(CHUCKLES) This takes a\r\nlittle getting used to.\r\n\r\n00:14:42.382 --\u003e 00:14:45.718\r\nOnce Project Deep Freeze is\r\ncompleted, you won't need the suit.\r\n\r\n00:14:45.802 --\u003e 00:14:47.470\r\nWell, let's get that started.\r\n\r\n00:14:47.553 --\u003e 00:14:48.805\r\nComing, Mr. Freeze?\r\n\r\n00:14:49.055 --\u003e 00:14:50.848\r\nI've done what you wanted.\r\n\r\n00:14:50.932 --\u003e 00:14:53.017\r\nNow leave me alone with my wife.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.643 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nSuit yourself.\r\n\r\n00:14:56.062 --\u003e 00:14:57.814\r\nYou can't let Walker do this.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.980 --\u003e 00:14:59.941\r\nBillions of people will perish.\r\n\r\n00:15:00.024 --\u003e 00:15:01.776\r\nThat's not my concern.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.859 --\u003e 00:15:04.821\r\nAll that matters is I\r\nonce again have my wife\r\n\r\n00:15:04.904 --\u003e 00:15:06.572\r\nand the means to restore her.\r\n\r\n00:15:07.281 --\u003e 00:15:11.828\r\nShe'll wake up in a dead,\r\nfrozen world that you helped destroy.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.911 --\u003e 00:15:13.162\r\nShe'll hate you for that.\r\n\r\n00:15:13.246 --\u003e 00:15:14.497\r\nSilence.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.580 --\u003e 00:15:16.249\r\nYou think you're alone now?\r\n\r\n00:15:16.332 --\u003e 00:15:18.000\r\nWait until she learns the truth.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.084 --\u003e 00:15:20.670\r\nI said silence!\r\n\r\n00:15:21.671 --\u003e 00:15:22.964\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:31.472 --\u003e 00:15:33.141\r\nFREEZE: Forgive me.\r\n\r\n00:15:39.772 --\u003e 00:15:41.607\r\n(ICE CRACKING)\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:43.985\r\nCome. There is much to do.\r\n\r\n00:15:50.700 --\u003e 00:15:52.493\r\nThe cannon is operational, sir.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.632 --\u003e 00:16:08.009\r\nExcellent.\r\n\r\n00:16:10.803 --\u003e 00:16:14.056\r\nAh! You've come to join us after\r\nall, my friend.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.977 --\u003e 00:16:19.353\r\nWait. What are you doing?\r\n\r\n00:16:29.322 --\u003e 00:16:30.490\r\nStop him!\r\n\r\n00:16:30.990 --\u003e 00:16:32.450\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:50.259 --\u003e 00:16:51.260\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:53.846 --\u003e 00:16:55.139\r\n(WALKER GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:55.723 --\u003e 00:16:56.807\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:17:02.522 --\u003e 00:17:03.689\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:05.483 --\u003e 00:17:06.901\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:12.990 --\u003e 00:17:14.825\r\nThis is my dream.\r\n\r\n00:17:14.909 --\u003e 00:17:16.285\r\nMy vision!\r\n\r\n00:17:16.369 --\u003e 00:17:21.123\r\nI cheated death to make it\r\nreal, and you won't stop me.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.207 --\u003e 00:17:26.045\r\nYou may live forever, Grant Walker,\r\nbut your mad dream dies now.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.837 --\u003e 00:17:28.047\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:35.388 --\u003e 00:17:38.266\r\nWhat are you doing?\r\nThat's the main power core.\r\n\r\n00:17:38.349 --\u003e 00:17:40.977\r\nAn overload will blow this\r\ncity out of the water.\r\n\r\n00:17:41.060 --\u003e 00:17:42.186\r\nExactly.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.230 --\u003e 00:17:45.773\r\nNo!\r\n\r\n00:17:51.279 --\u003e 00:17:53.990\r\n\u003ci\u003eAttention,\r\nall residents of Oceana.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:54.073 --\u003e 00:17:56.033\r\n\u003ci\u003eYour city is doomed.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:56.242 --\u003e 00:17:59.412\r\n\u003ci\u003eIf you value your lives,\r\nyou will evacuate now.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:17:59.620 --\u003e 00:18:01.038\r\n\u003ci\u003eThat is all.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:18:01.122 --\u003e 00:18:02.915\r\n- (RUMBLING)\r\n- (PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.296 --\u003e 00:18:10.798\r\n- Mr. Walker!\r\n- Get out of here. Now!\r\n\r\n00:18:15.136 --\u003e 00:18:16.345\r\n(RUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:18:28.190 --\u003e 00:18:29.900\r\nThere's our ride.\r\n\r\n00:18:30.526 --\u003e 00:18:33.321\r\n- Let's go.\r\n- I'm staying with Nora.\r\n\r\n00:18:33.404 --\u003e 00:18:36.324\r\nDon't be a fool.\r\nThis whole place is going under.\r\n\r\n00:18:36.407 --\u003e 00:18:38.409\r\nI won't lose her again.\r\n\r\n00:18:39.744 --\u003e 00:18:41.329\r\nThere's nothing\r\nyou can do for her.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.412 --\u003e 00:18:42.622\r\nCome with us.\r\n\r\n00:18:44.415 --\u003e 00:18:46.751\r\nI am the least of your worries.\r\n\r\n00:18:47.835 --\u003e 00:18:49.587\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:18:50.630 --\u003e 00:18:52.089\r\nRobin!\r\n\r\n00:18:53.924 --\u003e 00:18:55.926\r\nTake the boy and go.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.762 --\u003e 00:18:59.639\r\n(SHIVERING)\r\n\r\n00:18:59.722 --\u003e 00:19:02.141\r\nRelax. You're going to be okay.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.572 --\u003e 00:19:19.283\r\nWe're together again, my love.\r\n\r\n00:19:54.318 --\u003e 00:19:55.736\r\n(MUFFLED SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:19:59.865 --\u003e 00:20:01.075\r\nMan...\r\n\r\n00:20:01.158 --\u003e 00:20:03.244\r\nIf I spent any more time\r\nin that immersion tank,\r\n\r\n00:20:03.327 --\u003e 00:20:04.370\r\nI'd be growing gills.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.453 --\u003e 00:20:06.956\r\nI'm just glad I was able to\r\nget you back here in time.\r\n\r\n00:20:07.039 --\u003e 00:20:08.290\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.457 --\u003e 00:20:10.257\r\nFor a while I thought\r\nI'd wind up like Walker,\r\n\r\n00:20:10.292 --\u003e 00:20:11.794\r\ntrapped in an ice cube forever.\r\n\r\n00:20:12.920 --\u003e 00:20:14.338\r\nWhat about Mr. Freeze?\r\n\r\n00:20:14.422 --\u003e 00:20:15.881\r\nYou think he's gone for good?\r\n\r\n00:20:15.965 --\u003e 00:20:17.049\r\nI'm not sure.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.133 --\u003e 00:20:20.761\r\nBut if Freeze's condition\r\nhas made him truly immortal,\r\n\r\n00:20:21.303 --\u003e 00:20:23.764\r\n\u003ci\u003ewe may not have seen\r\nthe last of him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:41.699 --\u003e 00:20:43.701\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.726 --\u003e 00:21:09.727\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S04 E01 - The Terrible Trio (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:07.174 --\u003e 00:00:09.468\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:21.290 --\u003e 00:01:23.166\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.542 --\u003e 00:01:25.460\r\nTHE FOX: A valiant\r\neffort, stout sentinel,\r\n\r\n00:01:25.544 --\u003e 00:01:28.088\r\nbut the game was\r\nours before it began.\r\n\r\n00:01:42.102 --\u003e 00:01:43.353\r\nTHE VULTURE: Time to fly.\r\n\r\n00:01:54.656 --\u003e 00:01:55.699\r\nWait, gentlemen.\r\n\r\n00:01:58.076 --\u003e 00:02:00.787\r\nSo, what do they pay you\r\nhere, Henry?\r\n\r\n00:02:01.163 --\u003e 00:02:07.461\r\nNine, ten dollars an hour?\r\nA grand total of, what, four, $425 a week?\r\n\r\n00:02:07.753 --\u003e 00:02:09.755\r\n- Fox, come on!\r\n- Let's see,\r\n\r\n00:02:09.838 --\u003e 00:02:13.717\r\nthat'd be $21,000 a year.\r\nCan that be right?\r\n\r\n00:02:16.470 --\u003e 00:02:19.598\r\nHere. In appreciation\r\nfor services rendered.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.182 --\u003e 00:02:22.768\r\n- (LAUGHS) We won't tell.\r\n- Beats a gold watch.\r\n\r\n00:02:22.851 --\u003e 00:02:23.894\r\n(THE FOX LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:02:24.311 --\u003e 00:02:25.312\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:27.189\r\nAh, ah, ah.\r\n\r\n00:02:27.314 --\u003e 00:02:30.942\r\nIt's business decisions like that\r\nthat got you where you are today.\r\n\r\n00:02:31.151 --\u003e 00:02:32.986\r\nCome, gentlemen. Let us away.\r\n\r\n00:02:33.487 --\u003e 00:02:34.767\r\n- (RUSTLING)\r\n- Did you hear that?\r\n\r\n00:02:46.500 --\u003e 00:02:47.751\r\nAllow me.\r\n\r\n00:02:54.841 --\u003e 00:02:56.635\r\nDon't worry about me. Get them!\r\n\r\n00:02:56.968 --\u003e 00:02:58.136\r\nIt'll be a pleasure.\r\n\r\n00:03:20.867 --\u003e 00:03:23.120\r\nHate to tell you,\r\nbut the costume party's over.\r\n\r\n00:03:23.203 --\u003e 00:03:25.956\r\nYou want me, Tweety Bird?\r\nCome on, then.\r\n\r\n00:03:26.957 --\u003e 00:03:28.625\r\nRobin! Stop!\r\n\r\n00:03:31.420 --\u003e 00:03:32.629\r\nHe smells it.\r\n\r\n00:03:34.172 --\u003e 00:03:35.257\r\nPlan B, then.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.302 --\u003e 00:03:40.345\r\nRobin!\r\n\r\n00:03:48.353 --\u003e 00:03:50.522\r\nSee?\r\nI told you this would be fun.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.912 --\u003e 00:04:07.998\r\nDICK: The Terrible\r\nTrio strikes again.\r\n\r\n00:04:08.415 --\u003e 00:04:12.085\r\nHow about those masks?\r\nThey look like refugees from Mardi Gras.\r\n\r\n00:04:12.586 --\u003e 00:04:15.338\r\nBRUCE: Predators of\r\nland, sea and air.\r\n\r\n00:04:15.756 --\u003e 00:04:17.716\r\nMaybe they're experts\r\nin those areas.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.049 --\u003e 00:04:21.386\r\nThe only thing these guys\r\nare experts in is arrogance.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.566 --\u003e 00:04:35.734\r\nThanks, Kevin.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.360 --\u003e 00:04:38.361\r\nPull!\r\n\r\n00:04:40.822 --\u003e 00:04:41.990\r\n\"Thanks, Kevin\"?\r\n\r\n00:04:42.073 --\u003e 00:04:44.117\r\nAwfully chummy with the\r\nhelp, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.201 --\u003e 00:04:47.245\r\nDo you thank the garbage man\r\nfor picking up your trash?\r\n\r\n00:04:47.537 --\u003e 00:04:48.914\r\nIf I happen to run into him.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.997 --\u003e 00:04:50.624\r\nDon't get Warren started, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:04:50.957 --\u003e 00:04:53.627\r\nYou know how he feels\r\nabout the servants.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.710 --\u003e 00:04:55.170\r\nGunther, Army, please.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.587 --\u003e 00:04:59.341\r\nI'm just trying to protect Bruce\r\nfrom his baser instincts. Pull!\r\n\r\n00:05:02.969 --\u003e 00:05:04.930\r\n(CROWD APPLAUDING)\r\n\r\n00:05:05.305 --\u003e 00:05:08.850\r\nSo this is all you do for kicks, Bruce?\r\nCharity work?\r\n\r\n00:05:08.934 --\u003e 00:05:11.019\r\nWell, I do have a nightlife.\r\n\r\n00:05:11.728 --\u003e 00:05:12.896\r\nPull!\r\n\r\n00:05:15.482 --\u003e 00:05:17.818\r\nBesides,\r\nit's important to help others.\r\n\r\n00:05:18.109 --\u003e 00:05:20.654\r\nIt may sound corny, but,\r\nhey, it's how I feel.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.904 --\u003e 00:05:24.366\r\nBut you must recognize that you\r\nare a superior animal, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.866 --\u003e 00:05:26.618\r\nA member of the elite. Pull!\r\n\r\n00:05:29.579 --\u003e 00:05:31.164\r\nTake my Delta brothers and me.\r\n\r\n00:05:31.540 --\u003e 00:05:33.500\r\nWhy, we've run with the bulls.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.750 --\u003e 00:05:35.293\r\nShot game from hot air balloons.\r\n\r\n00:05:35.544 --\u003e 00:05:36.962\r\nKilled a great white.\r\n\r\n00:05:38.255 --\u003e 00:05:39.798\r\nWARREN: We've done it all.\r\n\r\n00:05:41.341 --\u003e 00:05:43.343\r\nAh, therein lies the problem.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.468 --\u003e 00:05:47.347\r\nAfter all, what do the rajahs do when\r\nthere are no more tigers to hunt?\r\n\r\n00:05:47.597 --\u003e 00:05:50.308\r\nI'm sure you'll think of\r\nsomething, Warren.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.477 --\u003e 00:05:56.815\r\nDollar for dollar, that has to be\r\nthe dullest man in Gotham City.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.488 --\u003e 00:06:05.824\r\nIt should be obvious even to\r\nyou, Rebecca.\r\n\r\n00:06:05.991 --\u003e 00:06:08.243\r\nThat dress is not\r\nappropriate attire.\r\n\r\n00:06:08.493 --\u003e 00:06:11.121\r\nOh, Father,\r\nyou just don't quit, do you?\r\n\r\n00:06:12.289 --\u003e 00:06:13.957\r\nSheldon, nice to see you here.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.374 --\u003e 00:06:16.001\r\nThe pleasure's all ours, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:06:16.293 --\u003e 00:06:18.333\r\nRebecca and I wouldn't have\r\nmissed it for the world.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.587 --\u003e 00:06:20.797\r\n- Isn't that right, dear?\r\n- Right.\r\n\r\n00:06:22.382 --\u003e 00:06:23.633\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.801 --\u003e 00:06:26.136\r\n(CHUCKLES) Children.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.428 --\u003e 00:06:28.805\r\nI thought you'd never\r\nfinish that stupid game.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.682 --\u003e 00:06:33.435\r\nCareful, darling,\r\nPater is watching.\r\n\r\n00:06:34.895 --\u003e 00:06:36.479\r\nHe's always watching.\r\n\r\n00:06:37.188 --\u003e 00:06:41.109\r\nIf you think he's mad now, wait until\r\nhe gets this month's credit card bill.\r\n\r\n00:06:41.693 --\u003e 00:06:44.738\r\nAnd how much did that little\r\nfrock set Daddums back?\r\n\r\n00:06:45.238 --\u003e 00:06:46.823\r\nFive thousand.\r\n\r\n00:06:47.198 --\u003e 00:06:48.658\r\nI'd say it was worth it.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.909 --\u003e 00:06:50.702\r\nI don't know how\r\nI'm gonna tell him.\r\n\r\n00:07:07.510 --\u003e 00:07:10.096\r\nOh, Warren, you are a lifesaver.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.764 --\u003e 00:07:12.057\r\nWARREN: It's only money.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.307 --\u003e 00:07:13.558\r\nWith Daddy leaving town,\r\n\r\n00:07:13.642 --\u003e 00:07:16.478\r\nI should be able to slip this\r\ninto his account, no problem.\r\n\r\n00:07:18.647 --\u003e 00:07:19.689\r\nCatch you in the pool.\r\n\r\n00:07:30.158 --\u003e 00:07:32.953\r\nWell, old man,\r\nI'd say that fluttering sound you hear\r\n\r\n00:07:33.078 --\u003e 00:07:35.246\r\nis your check sprouting\r\nwings and flying away.\r\n\r\n00:07:35.330 --\u003e 00:07:39.501\r\nActually, I thought that daddy\r\nmight be willing to reimburse me.\r\n\r\n00:08:16.204 --\u003e 00:08:19.124\r\nAh, well,\r\nMing was a boring dynasty anyway.\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.542\r\nI don't know about this.\r\n\r\n00:08:20.875 --\u003e 00:08:24.295\r\nIt's one thing to steal from\r\nstrangers, but we know Fallbrook.\r\n\r\n00:08:24.838 --\u003e 00:08:27.674\r\nYes, adds a bit of extra\r\nspice, doesn't it?\r\n\r\n00:08:28.299 --\u003e 00:08:29.384\r\nSHELDON: Hands up!\r\n\r\n00:08:32.637 --\u003e 00:08:34.347\r\nShe said he'd be out of town.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.518 --\u003e 00:08:42.063\r\nHello, police? This is Sheldon\r\nFallbrook at the Gotham Park Towers.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.147 --\u003e 00:08:43.773\r\nI want to report-\r\n\r\n00:08:44.399 --\u003e 00:08:45.608\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:51.823 --\u003e 00:08:52.991\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:55.035 --\u003e 00:08:58.288\r\nThat's where you belong, old man.\r\nAt my feet.\r\n\r\n00:08:58.872 --\u003e 00:09:00.707\r\nCome on. The police\r\nwill be here any minute.\r\n\r\n00:09:04.586 --\u003e 00:09:05.879\r\n(wmn HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:06.588 --\u003e 00:09:07.630\r\n(SHOOTS GRAPPLING GUN)\r\n\r\n00:09:27.108 --\u003e 00:09:28.610\r\n- (CLEARING THROAT)\r\n- (SIREN WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:09:43.708 --\u003e 00:09:45.978\r\n\u003ci\u003eDISPATCH: (ON RADIO) All units,\r\npossible robbery in progress\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:46.002 --\u003e 00:09:48.505\r\n\u003ci\u003eat Gotham Park Towers,\r\n28th floor residence.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:09:48.588 --\u003e 00:09:50.048\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:01.059 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nI presume a good\r\ntime was had by all?\r\n\r\n00:10:04.312 --\u003e 00:10:05.396\r\nWarren, it's him.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.567 --\u003e 00:10:11.361\r\nHave a little backbone, Army.\r\n\r\n00:10:41.808 --\u003e 00:10:43.059\r\nMy turn.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.314 --\u003e 00:10:49.732\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:10:52.443 --\u003e 00:10:53.736\r\nHe's hooked us!\r\n\r\n00:11:10.879 --\u003e 00:11:12.672\r\n- I can't shake him.\r\n- What do we do?\r\n\r\n00:11:12.755 --\u003e 00:11:14.841\r\n- Quick! Dump the money!\r\n- What?\r\n\r\n00:11:15.258 --\u003e 00:11:17.135\r\nDump the money! Now!\r\n\r\n00:11:22.807 --\u003e 00:11:24.184\r\nWOMAN: Hey, free money!\r\n\r\n00:11:24.267 --\u003e 00:11:25.935\r\n(EXCITED CHATTER)\r\n\r\n00:11:51.294 --\u003e 00:11:52.587\r\n(GRUNTS IN FRUSTRATION)\r\n\r\n00:11:52.837 --\u003e 00:11:53.880\r\nAced it!\r\n\r\n00:11:53.963 --\u003e 00:11:57.425\r\nAnd once again,\r\nwe owe it all to the little people.\r\n\r\n00:12:02.513 --\u003e 00:12:03.556\r\nREBECCA: Daddy?\r\n\r\n00:12:05.266 --\u003e 00:12:06.809\r\nDaddy, can you hear me?\r\n\r\n00:12:07.352 --\u003e 00:12:08.770\r\nI'm so sorry.\r\n\r\n00:12:09.062 --\u003e 00:12:11.105\r\nYou might as well go on home, Ms.\r\nFallbrook.\r\n\r\n00:12:11.314 --\u003e 00:12:13.483\r\nNo telling when your father\r\nwill come out of this.\r\n\r\n00:12:14.317 --\u003e 00:12:16.819\r\nWOMAN: (ON PA) Dr. Forrest,\r\ndial 118, please.\r\n\r\n00:12:18.154 --\u003e 00:12:20.156\r\nBruce. It's nice of you to come.\r\n\r\n00:12:20.615 --\u003e 00:12:22.825\r\nIf there's anything I can\r\ndo, Rebecca...\r\n\r\n00:12:25.036 --\u003e 00:12:26.204\r\nWarren.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.750 --\u003e 00:12:32.335\r\nI came as soon as I heard.\r\n\r\n00:12:32.627 --\u003e 00:12:37.048\r\nMy poor Becky. Dreadful business.\r\nSo senseless.\r\n\r\n00:12:39.676 --\u003e 00:12:41.844\r\nCome,\r\nlet me take your mind off this.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.303 --\u003e 00:12:44.863\r\nWOMAN: \u003ci\u003e(ON\u003c/i\u003e PA) \u003ci\u003eDr. Kravitz,\r\nyou have\u003c/i\u003e a \u003ci\u003evisitor in the main lobby.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:02.782 --\u003e 00:13:06.035\r\nYou know, Becks, I don't think\r\nyou should be alone right now.\r\n\r\n00:13:06.244 --\u003e 00:13:08.804\r\nThe fellows and I were thinking\r\nabout the mountains this weekend.\r\n\r\n00:13:08.830 --\u003e 00:13:10.915\r\nA change of scenery\r\nmight do you good.\r\n\r\n00:13:32.520 --\u003e 00:13:35.106\r\nGUNTHER: So the police still\r\nhave no idea who the thieves are?\r\n\r\n00:13:35.815 --\u003e 00:13:37.483\r\nNo, I guess not.\r\n\r\n00:13:38.067 --\u003e 00:13:39.360\r\nBut I hope they find them soon.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.736 --\u003e 00:13:43.156\r\nYou know, I really shouldn't be here.\r\nI mean, what if my father wakes up?\r\n\r\n00:13:43.573 --\u003e 00:13:48.578\r\nCome off it, Rebecca. Anyone would\r\nthink you actually liked the old coot.\r\n\r\n00:13:48.995 --\u003e 00:13:50.747\r\nWell, he is my father.\r\n\r\n00:13:50.913 --\u003e 00:13:53.249\r\nDon't worry. We left the\r\nnumber here with the hospital.\r\n\r\n00:13:53.374 --\u003e 00:13:55.543\r\nAnd we're only an hour's\r\ndrive from the city.\r\n\r\n00:13:56.252 --\u003e 00:13:57.295\r\nWell...\r\n\r\n00:13:57.712 --\u003e 00:13:58.963\r\nTime for a feast.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.297 --\u003e 00:14:02.133\r\nWe're going to cheer you up\r\nwhether you like it or not.\r\n\r\n00:14:02.383 --\u003e 00:14:03.718\r\nYou're too sweet.\r\n\r\n00:14:13.811 --\u003e 00:14:16.272\r\nIt's Dad's stick pin.\r\nHow did it-\r\n\r\n00:14:21.986 --\u003e 00:14:23.071\r\nNo.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.540 --\u003e 00:14:36.042\r\nDICK: According to the computer,\r\n\r\n00:14:36.125 --\u003e 00:14:39.379\r\nthis is probably the ring that\r\nmade the mark on Fallbrook's jaw.\r\n\r\n00:14:39.504 --\u003e 00:14:43.299\r\nIt belongs to a frat,\r\nDelta Sigma Alpha, mostly rich boys.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.800 --\u003e 00:14:46.177\r\nLike Warren Lawford\r\nand his Delta brothers.\r\n\r\n00:14:46.427 --\u003e 00:14:49.013\r\nAll three of them\r\ninherited family fortunes.\r\n\r\n00:14:49.680 --\u003e 00:14:51.474\r\nLawford gets his from oil.\r\n\r\n00:14:51.808 --\u003e 00:14:54.310\r\nLydecker's father owned\r\nan aerodynamics firm.\r\n\r\n00:14:54.519 --\u003e 00:14:57.105\r\nAnd Hardwick's father\r\nwas a shipping magnate.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.522 --\u003e 00:14:59.690\r\nLand, air and water.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.982 --\u003e 00:15:01.526\r\nIt can't be a coincidence.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.901 --\u003e 00:15:04.028\r\nScoundrels like these\r\nare worse than the Joker.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.278 --\u003e 00:15:06.697\r\nAt least he's got\r\nmadness as an excuse.\r\n\r\n00:15:06.781 --\u003e 00:15:09.992\r\nBut they've got more money than the mint.\r\nWhy would they steal?\r\n\r\n00:15:10.785 --\u003e 00:15:14.414\r\nBecause we were bored!\r\nDon't you get it? It was a game.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.622 --\u003e 00:15:15.790\r\nA game?\r\n\r\n00:15:16.124 --\u003e 00:15:17.458\r\nWe've done everything else.\r\n\r\n00:15:17.708 --\u003e 00:15:20.002\r\nTreasure hunts, safaris,\r\ndeep-sea diving.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.169 --\u003e 00:15:23.756\r\nWe wanted a new challenge.\r\nYou know, the thrill of the chase.\r\n\r\n00:15:23.923 --\u003e 00:15:28.344\r\nAnd we were good at it.\r\nWe outfoxed the police and the Batman.\r\n\r\n00:15:28.636 --\u003e 00:15:31.305\r\nBut the people you\r\nhurt, my father...\r\n\r\n00:15:31.722 --\u003e 00:15:34.225\r\nWe never meant to hurt him, Becky.\r\nReally.\r\n\r\n00:15:34.559 --\u003e 00:15:36.686\r\nOf course not.\r\nAnd we'll pay him back.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.019 --\u003e 00:15:39.897\r\nSure we will.\r\nHey, we'll pay everybody back.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.481 --\u003e 00:15:44.527\r\n- You won't tell anyone, right?\r\n- No. Oh, no, of course not.\r\n\r\n00:15:51.868 --\u003e 00:15:55.580\r\n- You'll tell.\r\n- No, Warren. I won't, really.\r\n\r\n00:15:55.955 --\u003e 00:15:59.584\r\nShe's a liability,\r\none we can't afford.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.876 --\u003e 00:16:01.752\r\nWhoa, timeout, old man.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.836 --\u003e 00:16:03.963\r\nThis is getting extreme.\r\nThere are limits to-\r\n\r\n00:16:04.046 --\u003e 00:16:06.257\r\nHaven't you listened to\r\nanything I've told you?\r\n\r\n00:16:06.340 --\u003e 00:16:09.260\r\nWe are beyond limitations!\r\nBeyond restriction!\r\n\r\n00:16:09.594 --\u003e 00:16:11.888\r\nShe's your girlfriend,\r\nfor crying out loud!\r\n\r\n00:16:12.096 --\u003e 00:16:14.640\r\nShe's a spoiled, willful child.\r\n\r\n00:16:15.016 --\u003e 00:16:16.225\r\nAnd if we let her go...\r\n\r\n00:16:17.977 --\u003e 00:16:21.564\r\n- She will tell. Ow!\r\n- You're out of your minds, all of you!\r\n\r\n00:16:22.315 --\u003e 00:16:24.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:25.735 --\u003e 00:16:28.237\r\nIn for a penny, in for a pound.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.367 --\u003e 00:16:34.994\r\n(REBECCA WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:16:41.834 --\u003e 00:16:43.753\r\nWarren, for pity's sake.\r\n\r\n00:16:44.086 --\u003e 00:16:47.548\r\nEnough, Army!\r\nI want this done with, now!\r\n\r\n00:17:05.566 --\u003e 00:17:07.610\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:08.027 --\u003e 00:17:09.070\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:17:21.749 --\u003e 00:17:23.292\r\n- Take over.\r\n- Sure.\r\n\r\n00:17:23.376 --\u003e 00:17:25.211\r\nLeave me to steer\r\nwith a broken arm.\r\n\r\n00:18:09.505 --\u003e 00:18:10.756\r\n(THE SHARK GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:24.061 --\u003e 00:18:25.605\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:18:37.158 --\u003e 00:18:38.701\r\n(ENGINE REVVING)\r\n\r\n00:18:42.997 --\u003e 00:18:44.290\r\n(BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:45.643 --\u003e 00:19:48.938\r\nLet's go, Fox.\r\nYou've raided your last chicken coop.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.271 --\u003e 00:19:51.440\r\nWait, wait a minute.\r\nWe can make a deal.\r\n\r\n00:19:51.857 --\u003e 00:19:54.485\r\nA million dollars to let me go.\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:55.027 --\u003e 00:19:58.823\r\nTen million! Think about it.\r\nBuys a lot of Batarangs.\r\n\r\n00:19:59.448 --\u003e 00:20:01.117\r\nYour money's no good here.\r\n\r\n00:20:01.325 --\u003e 00:20:04.787\r\nOkay, fine. Go ahead.\r\nTake me in, hero.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.870 --\u003e 00:20:07.415\r\nI've got every judge\r\nin town in my pocket.\r\n\r\n00:20:07.707 --\u003e 00:20:11.877\r\nYou'll see. I'll get justice,\r\nthe best that money can buy!\r\n\r\n00:20:30.938 --\u003e 00:20:32.189\r\n(SNARLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:44.535 --\u003e 00:20:46.954\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S04 E02 - Showdown (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.215 --\u003e 00:00:08.217\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:41.184 --\u003e 00:01:44.146\r\nYou can put those away.\r\nThey will sleep for hours.\r\n\r\n00:01:44.229 --\u003e 00:01:46.023\r\nBATMAN: But I won't.\r\n\r\n00:01:50.027 --\u003e 00:01:51.028\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:01:56.908 --\u003e 00:01:58.285\r\n(GUNSHOTS CONTINUE)\r\n\r\n00:02:01.788 --\u003e 00:02:02.956\r\n(WHEEZING)\r\n\r\n00:02:09.379 --\u003e 00:02:10.756\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:02:11.715 --\u003e 00:02:12.924\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:02:14.635 --\u003e 00:02:16.970\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:02:22.142 --\u003e 00:02:23.518\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:02:29.733 --\u003e 00:02:31.360\r\n(HELICOPTER HOVERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:34.279 --\u003e 00:02:36.365\r\n- What did he want?\r\n- I'm not sure.\r\n\r\n00:02:42.537 --\u003e 00:02:44.539\r\nBut it appears he\r\nleft us a present.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.541 --\u003e 00:02:47.959\r\nHe's moving toward the airfield.\r\n\r\n00:02:48.377 --\u003e 00:02:51.046\r\nThat autogyro he's using\r\nisn't a long-range craft.\r\n\r\n00:02:51.380 --\u003e 00:02:54.007\r\nHe must be planning on\r\nrendezvousing with a bigger plane.\r\n\r\n00:02:57.219 --\u003e 00:02:59.137\r\n- There.\r\n- BATMAN: \"Lazarus.\"\r\n\r\n00:02:59.346 --\u003e 00:03:01.890\r\nIt's too easy.\r\nHe wants us to find him.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.057 --\u003e 00:03:03.600\r\nLet's check this out.\r\n\r\n00:03:05.268 --\u003e 00:03:08.814\r\nRA'S: \u003ci\u003eIanticipated meeting you\r\ntonight, Detective.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:09.356 --\u003e 00:03:13.735\r\n\u003ci\u003eI hope the story I have to tell you may\r\ncause you to reconsider your pursuit.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:14.736 --\u003e 00:03:17.197\r\n\u003ci\u003eThe year was 1883.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:17.489 --\u003e 00:03:20.867\r\n\u003ci\u003eYour government was\r\nruthlessly expanding westward.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:21.451 --\u003e 00:03:22.994\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:25.247 --\u003e 00:03:26.540\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:03:43.432 --\u003e 00:03:45.142\r\n(HAMMERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:46.309 --\u003e 00:03:47.436\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.356 --\u003e 00:03:52.357\r\n(SNARLING)\r\n\r\n00:03:55.110 --\u003e 00:03:56.445\r\n(DOG BARKING)\r\n\r\n00:03:59.823 --\u003e 00:04:01.116\r\n(DOOR CLOSES)\r\n\r\n00:04:11.293 --\u003e 00:04:12.711\r\nWhat will it be, stranger?\r\n\r\n00:04:14.171 --\u003e 00:04:16.423\r\nWater, ma'am, in a clean glass.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.923 --\u003e 00:04:17.924\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:04:18.049 --\u003e 00:04:19.259\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:04:19.342 --\u003e 00:04:21.553\r\nHorse done give out\r\non me 10 miles back,\r\n\r\n00:04:21.720 --\u003e 00:04:24.639\r\nand I'm hotter than a shaved\r\ncoyote with a heat rash.\r\n\r\n00:04:24.723 --\u003e 00:04:28.435\r\nAnother thing, ma'am.\r\nYou by any chance seen this feller?\r\n\r\n00:04:30.979 --\u003e 00:04:32.105\r\nYou a bounty hunter?\r\n\r\n00:04:32.272 --\u003e 00:04:34.274\r\nJust to pay for\r\nmy piano lessons.\r\n\r\n00:04:34.441 --\u003e 00:04:36.485\r\nI know that two-bit skunk.\r\n\r\n00:04:36.651 --\u003e 00:04:38.695\r\nHe hurt one of my\r\ngirls real bad.\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.240\r\nIf you could point me in his general\r\ndirection, I'd appreciate it.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.533 --\u003e 00:04:46.912\r\nThat I can and will.\r\nAnd this one's on the house.\r\n\r\n00:04:49.456 --\u003e 00:04:51.082\r\nSHERIFF: Well, well.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.249 --\u003e 00:04:53.627\r\nJonah Hex, his own bad self.\r\n\r\n00:04:53.710 --\u003e 00:04:57.714\r\nBeen here five minutes and you ain't\r\nkilled nobody nor set nothing on fire.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.131 --\u003e 00:04:59.508\r\nSlipping, ain't you?\r\n\r\n00:04:59.674 --\u003e 00:05:01.343\r\nI'm still a little bushed.\r\n\r\n00:05:01.885 --\u003e 00:05:07.307\r\nFact is, you look a little past it, Hex.\r\nNot tired, just all used up.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.557 --\u003e 00:05:09.726\r\nWell, if I get pushed,\r\n\r\n00:05:09.893 --\u003e 00:05:12.687\r\nI can still shoot a fly\r\nout from between its wings,\r\n\r\n00:05:12.854 --\u003e 00:05:14.773\r\nprovided the light's\r\nright, of course.\r\n\r\n00:05:15.941 --\u003e 00:05:17.859\r\nAnd it's a big, plump fly.\r\n\r\n00:05:23.782 --\u003e 00:05:26.284\r\nI ain't got nothing on you, Hex.\r\nYet.\r\n\r\n00:05:26.368 --\u003e 00:05:29.955\r\nJust remember them wanted posters\r\nsay, \"Dead or alive.\"\r\n\r\n00:05:30.664 --\u003e 00:05:33.291\r\nYou might try \"alive\" this time.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.750 --\u003e 00:05:35.460\r\nFirst time for everything.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.714 --\u003e 00:05:42.551\r\nBe back here around midnight.\r\nI can help you then.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.221 --\u003e 00:05:47.639\r\n(ANIMAL HOWLING)\r\n\r\n00:05:51.560 --\u003e 00:05:55.355\r\nDuvall comes into town now and then,\r\nstarts fights, bothers my girls,\r\n\r\n00:05:55.522 --\u003e 00:05:57.315\r\nchallenges men to duels.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.440 --\u003e 00:05:59.150\r\nI'm aware of his habits, missy.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.359 --\u003e 00:06:01.319\r\nWhat I ain't aware of\r\nis where he's holed up.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.736 --\u003e 00:06:03.029\r\nStrange thing, that.\r\n\r\n00:06:03.196 --\u003e 00:06:06.449\r\nHe ain't staying at the hotel,\r\nand the next town's 50 miles away.\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:10.120\r\nSounds like he likes to sleep on the\r\nground with the rest of the snakes.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.203 --\u003e 00:06:13.415\r\nHe ain't the type.\r\nMore the clean-sheet sort.\r\n\r\n00:06:13.498 --\u003e 00:06:14.916\r\nAnd he first showed up in town\r\n\r\n00:06:15.000 --\u003e 00:06:17.711\r\nabout the time folks started\r\nseeing the sky monster.\r\n\r\n00:06:18.003 --\u003e 00:06:19.045\r\nThe what?\r\n\r\n00:06:19.212 --\u003e 00:06:20.672\r\nNo one knows what it is,\r\n\r\n00:06:20.755 --\u003e 00:06:23.592\r\nand the sheriff's too\r\nyellow to investigate.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.134 --\u003e 00:06:28.096\r\nIt only comes out at night,\r\nlike a big boat or a log in the sky.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.179 --\u003e 00:06:30.473\r\nAbout the same time it showed,\r\n\r\n00:06:30.557 --\u003e 00:06:32.434\r\nfolks started seeing\r\nlights in the-\r\n\r\n00:06:33.226 --\u003e 00:06:34.269\r\nGet down.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.356 --\u003e 00:06:43.695\r\nWay I figure, that glow might some way\r\ntie in with the sky monster and Duvall.\r\n\r\n00:06:44.154 --\u003e 00:06:45.572\r\nReckon so.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.156 --\u003e 00:06:48.533\r\nI think you'd better start back\r\nnow, missy.\r\n\r\n00:06:48.617 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nGot a feeling things might\r\nget loud and busy soon.\r\n\r\n00:06:55.290 --\u003e 00:06:56.750\r\nGood luck, Jonah Hex.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.292 --\u003e 00:06:59.085\r\nRight nice sentiment, ma'am.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.045 --\u003e 00:07:03.882\r\nBut I never cottoned much to luck.\r\nI like to make my own.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.466 --\u003e 00:07:07.260\r\nI'll remember that\r\nwhen I see you next.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.974 --\u003e 00:07:13.975\r\n(BIRD SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:22.108 --\u003e 00:07:23.985\r\n(MACHINERY WORKING)\r\n\r\n00:07:37.290 --\u003e 00:07:39.459\r\nAll right,\r\nhurry up with that crane up there.\r\n\r\n00:07:43.380 --\u003e 00:07:45.548\r\nAll right, a little\r\nlower, a little lower.\r\n\r\n00:07:49.886 --\u003e 00:07:51.221\r\n(HORSE WHINNIES)\r\n\r\n00:08:00.355 --\u003e 00:08:02.148\r\n(BUBBLING)\r\n\r\n00:08:03.066 --\u003e 00:08:04.859\r\n(METAL CLANKING)\r\n\r\n00:08:15.453 --\u003e 00:08:16.454\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:17.914 --\u003e 00:08:19.874\r\nWork, you lazy good-for-nothing!\r\n\r\n00:08:22.877 --\u003e 00:08:26.631\r\nI've told you repeatedly,\r\nthis is not how I do things!\r\n\r\n00:08:27.173 --\u003e 00:08:28.883\r\nI beg your pardon, sir.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.050 --\u003e 00:08:32.262\r\nI was hoping to expedite the\r\ncompletion of the airship.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.429 --\u003e 00:08:37.100\r\nCommendable, but not at the\r\nexpense of my workforce.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.226 --\u003e 00:08:40.311\r\nGood men are hard to\r\nfind in these parts,\r\n\r\n00:08:40.395 --\u003e 00:08:42.022\r\nand there is still\r\nmuch to be done.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.188 --\u003e 00:08:45.316\r\nThe government's western\r\nexpansion is destroying this land.\r\n\r\n00:08:45.483 --\u003e 00:08:48.778\r\nDrastic steps must be taken\r\nto preserve the wilderness.\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:52.115\r\nAnd Ra's al Ghul is\r\nthe one to do it.\r\n\r\n00:08:52.407 --\u003e 00:08:54.367\r\nWho better than I?\r\n\r\n00:08:54.743 --\u003e 00:08:57.954\r\nI'll destroy the railroad and\r\nbomb other railroad junctions\r\n\r\n00:08:58.038 --\u003e 00:09:00.623\r\nas I move eastward\r\ntoward Washington.\r\n\r\n00:09:00.790 --\u003e 00:09:02.417\r\nOnce Washington is in flames,\r\n\r\n00:09:02.500 --\u003e 00:09:04.711\r\nI'll force the United\r\nStates government\r\n\r\n00:09:04.878 --\u003e 00:09:08.089\r\nto declare me master of America!\r\n\r\n00:09:08.173 --\u003e 00:09:09.674\r\n(CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:09:10.383 --\u003e 00:09:11.885\r\nWhatever you say.\r\n\r\n00:09:13.928 --\u003e 00:09:15.055\r\n(CRUMBLING)\r\n\r\n00:09:20.518 --\u003e 00:09:21.519\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:27.817 --\u003e 00:09:31.029\r\nIt would appear we have\r\nourselves a government spy.\r\n\r\n00:09:32.363 --\u003e 00:09:35.366\r\nA rather disreputable-looking\r\none at that.\r\n\r\n00:09:35.533 --\u003e 00:09:37.410\r\nWell, Mr. Spy,\r\n\r\n00:09:37.744 --\u003e 00:09:41.873\r\nI'd say your plan has failed\r\nand the railroad is doomed.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.165 --\u003e 00:09:43.875\r\nI ain't no spy.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.042 --\u003e 00:09:47.754\r\nI'm Jonah Hex, and I don't give a\r\ntinker's cuss about no railroad.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.421 --\u003e 00:09:50.965\r\nI've come to get\r\nyou, Arkady Duvall,\r\n\r\n00:09:51.591 --\u003e 00:09:54.260\r\non account of what you done\r\nto that girl back east.\r\n\r\n00:09:54.344 --\u003e 00:09:56.429\r\n(CHUCKLING) You mean to say\r\n\r\n00:09:56.596 --\u003e 00:10:00.308\r\nyou've tracked me across\r\n12 states because of that?\r\n\r\n00:10:00.391 --\u003e 00:10:03.978\r\nWell, there's also the\r\nmatter of a $200 reward.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.395 --\u003e 00:10:06.356\r\nThat part don't hurt\r\nmy feelings none.\r\n\r\n00:10:06.439 --\u003e 00:10:09.275\r\nYou're either a liar or a fool.\r\n\r\n00:10:09.484 --\u003e 00:10:11.486\r\nI've been known to be foolish,\r\n\r\n00:10:11.820 --\u003e 00:10:14.656\r\nbut ain't nobody calls me a\r\nliar and goes to bed happy.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.032 --\u003e 00:10:17.700\r\nGive him a lead bath.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.966 --\u003e 00:10:35.051\r\nPerhaps we can make\r\nboth sides match.\r\n\r\n00:10:35.135 --\u003e 00:10:36.302\r\nStop!\r\n\r\n00:10:37.011 --\u003e 00:10:39.097\r\nYou are becoming quite\r\nbold, Arkady.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.180 --\u003e 00:10:43.268\r\nWhipping my men, disposing of\r\ninterlopers without consulting me.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.434 --\u003e 00:10:46.312\r\nHe's a spy, sir, a railroad spy.\r\n\r\n00:10:48.398 --\u003e 00:10:50.650\r\nHe looks more like\r\na saddle bum to me.\r\n\r\n00:10:50.733 --\u003e 00:10:53.236\r\nImprison him.\r\nI will question him later.\r\n\r\n00:10:55.530 --\u003e 00:10:58.575\r\nAnd you, Arkady, will make no more\r\ndecisions without my approval.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.658 --\u003e 00:10:59.826\r\nUnderstood?\r\n\r\n00:11:07.792 --\u003e 00:11:08.960\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:11:29.480 --\u003e 00:11:30.481\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:11:40.617 --\u003e 00:11:41.784\r\nWhat?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.545 --\u003e 00:11:53.546\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:56.758 --\u003e 00:11:58.468\r\n(DOOR CREAKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:00.803 --\u003e 00:12:02.680\r\n(HORN TOOTING)\r\n\r\n00:12:13.483 --\u003e 00:12:14.901\r\n(MEN GRUNT)\r\n\r\n00:12:29.332 --\u003e 00:12:32.710\r\nGOVERNOR: Today on this\r\nmomentous period in history,\r\n\r\n00:12:32.877 --\u003e 00:12:35.755\r\nwe link our great western\r\nlands with the east.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.838 --\u003e 00:12:41.052\r\nBefore this great enterprise,\r\nenvisioned by myself,\r\n\r\n00:12:41.219 --\u003e 00:12:43.429\r\nthere was nothing\r\nhere but wilderness.\r\n\r\n00:12:43.513 --\u003e 00:12:46.557\r\nAnd from it, with bare hands,\r\n\r\n00:12:46.724 --\u003e 00:12:49.394\r\nhard work and dedication,\r\n\r\n00:12:49.852 --\u003e 00:12:53.189\r\nwe have hewn a civilized land.\r\n\r\n00:12:53.481 --\u003e 00:12:55.275\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:12:59.362 --\u003e 00:13:03.408\r\nAnd so it gives me great pleasure\r\nas the territorial governor\r\n\r\n00:13:03.491 --\u003e 00:13:05.868\r\nto drive the golden\r\nspike which will connect\r\n\r\n00:13:05.952 --\u003e 00:13:09.038\r\nthese two great sections of\r\nthe North American continent.\r\n\r\n00:13:10.498 --\u003e 00:13:11.833\r\n(MORTAR WHISTLING)\r\n\r\n00:13:31.936 --\u003e 00:13:34.564\r\n\u003ci\u003eRA'S: Run,\r\nif you value your lives!\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:13:37.108 --\u003e 00:13:40.445\r\nClear the area!\r\nMaintain at your peril!\r\n\r\n00:13:55.418 --\u003e 00:13:57.378\r\n(CROWD GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:01.382 --\u003e 00:14:02.508\r\nFire!\r\n\r\n00:14:13.644 --\u003e 00:14:15.438\r\n(HORSE WHINNIES)\r\n\r\n00:14:35.708 --\u003e 00:14:37.335\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:14:57.438 --\u003e 00:14:59.440\r\nRun for your lives!\r\n\r\n00:15:06.364 --\u003e 00:15:07.365\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:12.787 --\u003e 00:15:13.788\r\n(MEN SHOUTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:19.710 --\u003e 00:15:21.337\r\nDon't shoot, you fool!\r\n\r\n00:15:21.421 --\u003e 00:15:23.214\r\nThis ship is full\r\nof hydrogen gas!\r\n\r\n00:15:23.506 --\u003e 00:15:25.174\r\nDo you want to blow\r\nus all to atoms?\r\n\r\n00:15:32.515 --\u003e 00:15:33.516\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:15:37.228 --\u003e 00:15:38.229\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:15:52.577 --\u003e 00:15:54.495\r\nYou! I don't believe it!\r\n\r\n00:15:54.996 --\u003e 00:15:56.914\r\nGuess I'm just a bad penny.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.081 --\u003e 00:15:59.333\r\nWhy are you doing this?\r\n\r\n00:15:59.500 --\u003e 00:16:02.378\r\nBecause I don't like\r\nyou or your kind.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.296 --\u003e 00:16:04.672\r\nExcuse me.\r\n\r\n00:16:06.674 --\u003e 00:16:08.843\r\nNo! The hydrogen cells!\r\n\r\n00:16:15.933 --\u003e 00:16:17.894\r\n- (SCREAMING)\r\n- What happened?\r\n\r\n00:16:19.187 --\u003e 00:16:20.688\r\nIt was that scarred man.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.855 --\u003e 00:16:22.648\r\nHe turned our own cannons on us.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.239 --\u003e 00:16:33.159\r\nNow, let's you and me dance.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.951 --\u003e 00:16:36.120\r\nYou cannot defeat me.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.245 --\u003e 00:16:38.956\r\nI am a Heidelberg\r\nfencing champion.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.040 --\u003e 00:16:41.167\r\nMy heart's all aflutter.\r\n\r\n00:16:45.379 --\u003e 00:16:46.964\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:52.136 --\u003e 00:16:54.180\r\nI'll chop you to pieces.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.264 --\u003e 00:16:56.974\r\nTalk, talk, talk.\r\n\r\n00:16:57.350 --\u003e 00:16:58.935\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:08.402 --\u003e 00:17:10.446\r\nOrder the men to abandon ship.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.613 --\u003e 00:17:12.657\r\nAye, sir. But what about Duvall?\r\n\r\n00:17:12.740 --\u003e 00:17:14.784\r\nLeave that fool to his fate.\r\n\r\n00:17:32.969 --\u003e 00:17:33.970\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:38.599 --\u003e 00:17:40.268\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:46.440 --\u003e 00:17:47.733\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.011 --\u003e 00:18:18.222\r\n5000 in gold. Take it.\r\nLeave me be.\r\n\r\n00:18:18.723 --\u003e 00:18:20.641\r\nIt ain't about money, boy.\r\n\r\n00:18:20.808 --\u003e 00:18:24.353\r\nIt's about justice,\r\nand I aim to serve you some.\r\n\r\n00:18:24.770 --\u003e 00:18:26.564\r\nLet me live. Please.\r\n\r\n00:18:27.023 --\u003e 00:18:29.900\r\nI will, only because\r\nit's too much trouble\r\n\r\n00:18:29.984 --\u003e 00:18:32.278\r\nto haul your stinking\r\ncarcass back east.\r\n\r\n00:18:32.945 --\u003e 00:18:33.946\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:40.620 --\u003e 00:18:42.455\r\nI'm getting too old for this.\r\n\r\n00:18:48.711 --\u003e 00:18:51.922\r\nGreat story. But what's it\r\ngot to do with that rest home?\r\n\r\n00:18:52.632 --\u003e 00:18:53.883\r\nI think I know.\r\n\r\n00:18:57.928 --\u003e 00:18:59.889\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:19:08.314 --\u003e 00:19:11.734\r\nI assume you listened to my\r\naccount, Detective.\r\n\r\n00:19:11.817 --\u003e 00:19:12.943\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.405 --\u003e 00:19:17.490\r\nDuvall.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.615 --\u003e 00:19:20.201\r\nIt can't be.\r\nHe'd be over 100 years old.\r\n\r\n00:19:20.701 --\u003e 00:19:23.704\r\nHe was sentenced to 50\r\nyears of hard labor.\r\n\r\n00:19:23.871 --\u003e 00:19:26.540\r\nOf course, no one expected\r\nhim to live out that sentence.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.249 --\u003e 00:19:28.334\r\nNo one but me.\r\n\r\n00:19:28.417 --\u003e 00:19:29.960\r\nThe Lazarus pit.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.294 --\u003e 00:19:31.879\r\nWhen he was a young man,\r\n\r\n00:19:32.088 --\u003e 00:19:34.757\r\nthough even its powers\r\ncannot restore him now.\r\n\r\n00:19:34.840 --\u003e 00:19:38.969\r\nWhen his sentence was completed,\r\nArkady simply wandered away.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.679 --\u003e 00:19:42.932\r\nThe privations he had suffered\r\nhad left his mind shattered.\r\n\r\n00:19:43.015 --\u003e 00:19:46.185\r\nI had lost track of him until\r\nhe turned up in that rest home.\r\n\r\n00:19:46.352 --\u003e 00:19:49.230\r\nYou left Duvall to his\r\nfate a century ago.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.605 --\u003e 00:19:51.273\r\nWhy come back for him now?\r\n\r\n00:19:51.357 --\u003e 00:19:54.944\r\nDid you really think, Detective,\r\nthat in my 600 years of life,\r\n\r\n00:19:55.027 --\u003e 00:19:58.280\r\nI would've sired\r\nonly one offspring?\r\n\r\n00:20:00.533 --\u003e 00:20:03.327\r\nEven before the Phoenix\r\ndebacle, I had come to realize\r\n\r\n00:20:03.411 --\u003e 00:20:08.541\r\nthat Arkady was too unbalanced and\r\ncruel to wisely rule my empire.\r\n\r\n00:20:08.791 --\u003e 00:20:12.962\r\n- But you couldn't forget about him.\r\n- What father can ever forget his son?\r\n\r\n00:20:15.381 --\u003e 00:20:18.592\r\nCome now, Detective.\r\nI've still a few good years left.\r\n\r\n00:20:18.759 --\u003e 00:20:20.636\r\nWe will cross\r\nswords another day.\r\n\r\n00:20:21.345 --\u003e 00:20:24.557\r\nBut for now,\r\nlet me take my boy home.\r\n\r\n00:20:29.437 --\u003e 00:20:30.730\r\n(ENGINE STARTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:42.158 --\u003e 00:20:44.160\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:08.726 --\u003e 00:21:09.727\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S04 E03 - Catwalk (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.048 --\u003e 00:00:08.050\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:20.706 --\u003e 00:01:24.126\r\n\u003ci\u003eSEUNA: Poor baby.\r\nI used to be just like you.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:24.751 --\u003e 00:01:27.421\r\n\u003ci\u003eA child of the\r\nnight, wild and free.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:35.470 --\u003e 00:01:40.475\r\n\u003ci\u003eI was the cat who walked by herself,\r\nand the city was my hunting ground.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:41.143 --\u003e 00:01:43.645\r\n\u003ci\u003eI'd prowl through\r\nGotham each evening,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:01:43.895 --\u003e 00:01:47.816\r\n\u003ci\u003egoing where I liked and\r\ntaking whatever I wanted.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:05.667 --\u003e 00:02:06.793\r\n\u003ci\u003eUntil I met him.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:33.028 --\u003e 00:02:35.322\r\n\u003ci\u003eI gave him my best\r\nfight, but in the end,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:36.657 --\u003e 00:02:38.408\r\n\u003ci\u003ekitty got her claws clipped.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:46.333 --\u003e 00:02:49.628\r\n\u003ci\u003eHad to promise I'd be a good\r\nlittle pet and walk on a leash.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:51.546 --\u003e 00:02:53.048\r\n\u003ci\u003eEven if it killed me.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:03:09.356 --\u003e 00:03:11.692\r\nOh, you just say that to\r\nall the beautiful girls.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.985 --\u003e 00:03:16.238\r\nSelina? Excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:03:18.865 --\u003e 00:03:20.033\r\nSefina?\r\n\r\n00:03:25.330 --\u003e 00:03:28.500\r\n\"Extinction.\" I\r\ncan relate to that.\r\n\r\n00:03:29.000 --\u003e 00:03:30.460\r\nYou're in a cheery mood.\r\n\r\n00:03:30.669 --\u003e 00:03:33.213\r\nGiving up Catwoman hasn't been\r\neasy, Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:03:33.422 --\u003e 00:03:35.424\r\nI miss the excitement,\r\nthe danger.\r\n\r\n00:03:36.216 --\u003e 00:03:38.468\r\nSometimes I feel so tempted.\r\n\r\n00:03:39.636 --\u003e 00:03:41.138\r\nEven though you'd\r\nbe risking prison?\r\n\r\n00:03:41.430 --\u003e 00:03:43.181\r\nTell me I'm not in a cage now.\r\n\r\n00:03:43.348 --\u003e 00:03:44.558\r\nWOMAN: Bruce Wayne.\r\n\r\n00:03:44.933 --\u003e 00:03:47.227\r\nI wondered where you'd\r\nbeen hiding yourself.\r\n\r\n00:03:48.103 --\u003e 00:03:50.689\r\nAnd whom, may I ask,\r\nis your attractive date?\r\n\r\n00:03:50.981 --\u003e 00:03:53.942\r\n- Veronica Vreeland, meet Selina Kyle.\r\n- We've met.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.693 --\u003e 00:03:58.447\r\n- At the wildlife fundraiser last year?\r\n- Oh, of course.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.072 --\u003e 00:04:01.908\r\n- Love what you've done to your hair.\r\n- Thanks.\r\n\r\n00:04:02.617 --\u003e 00:04:05.662\r\nSince you're so devoted to\r\nwildlife, Selina,\r\n\r\n00:04:05.912 --\u003e 00:04:09.249\r\nI can't wait to hear what you think\r\nof the museum's new conservation hall.\r\n\r\n00:04:09.916 --\u003e 00:04:13.044\r\nI had it built in honor of my\r\ngrandfather, Stanton Vreeland.\r\n\r\n00:04:13.378 --\u003e 00:04:16.882\r\nHe was the first to realize the\r\nimportance of preserving rare animals.\r\n\r\n00:04:17.507 --\u003e 00:04:20.594\r\nNot surprising, considering how\r\nmany of them he obliterated.\r\n\r\n00:04:20.927 --\u003e 00:04:22.095\r\nExcuse me?\r\n\r\n00:04:22.429 --\u003e 00:04:24.473\r\nStanton Vreeland was\r\na playboy sportsman\r\n\r\n00:04:24.556 --\u003e 00:04:27.350\r\nwho'd blow away anything that\r\nwandered into his gunsight.\r\n\r\n00:04:27.768 --\u003e 00:04:30.645\r\nHe had to preserve animals or\r\nhe'd have nothing left to shoot.\r\n\r\n00:04:31.188 --\u003e 00:04:32.230\r\nIs that right?\r\n\r\n00:04:32.647 --\u003e 00:04:33.648\r\nUh-huh!\r\n\r\n00:04:33.940 --\u003e 00:04:37.027\r\nIn fact, most of these critters are\r\ngone thanks to trigger-happy jerks\r\n\r\n00:04:37.110 --\u003e 00:04:39.529\r\n- like old Grandpa.\r\n- SeHna.\r\n\r\n00:04:39.988 --\u003e 00:04:42.657\r\nBut, Bruce, Miss Vreeland\r\nasked me what I thought.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.116 --\u003e 00:04:44.576\r\nI think you've said enough.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.202 --\u003e 00:04:47.037\r\nYes, perhaps I have.\r\n\r\n00:04:51.041 --\u003e 00:04:54.753\r\nJust once I'd like to throw a\r\nparty without some kook showing up.\r\n\r\n00:04:54.961 --\u003e 00:04:56.546\r\nUh. Excuse me.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.637 --\u003e 00:05:05.514\r\nWell, that was pretty rude.\r\n\r\n00:05:05.847 --\u003e 00:05:07.390\r\nJust the cat in me, I guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.933 --\u003e 00:05:11.978\r\nLook, Bruce, it was sweet of you to\r\ninvite me, but I don't fit in here.\r\n\r\n00:05:12.312 --\u003e 00:05:14.773\r\nSometimes I feel like I\r\ndon't fit in anywhere.\r\n\r\n00:05:25.325 --\u003e 00:05:26.368\r\nTaxi.\r\n\r\n00:05:27.577 --\u003e 00:05:29.704\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:05:30.914 --\u003e 00:05:33.708\r\n- Your ride, Miss Kyle.\r\n- Hey. What the-\r\n\r\n00:05:36.920 --\u003e 00:05:39.714\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.465 --\u003e 00:05:44.553\r\n- Let me out, you big ape.\r\n- MAN: (CHUCKLES) She's a live one.\r\n\r\n00:05:44.761 --\u003e 00:05:47.264\r\nIn two seconds,\r\nthat'll be more than I can say about you.\r\n\r\n00:05:47.556 --\u003e 00:05:49.933\r\nCalm down, pussycat.\r\nWe're all friends here.\r\n\r\n00:05:50.350 --\u003e 00:05:53.520\r\nDummy, don't keep our\r\npretty guest in the dark.\r\n\r\n00:05:53.895 --\u003e 00:05:55.564\r\nMAN: Yes, sir, Mr. Scarf ace.\r\n\r\n00:05:56.439 --\u003e 00:05:57.482\r\nAh! That's better.\r\n\r\n00:05:57.816 --\u003e 00:05:58.817\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:59.568 --\u003e 00:06:00.610\r\nYou gotta be kidding.\r\n\r\n00:06:01.069 --\u003e 00:06:02.445\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:06:02.529 --\u003e 00:06:05.615\r\nWhat's she laughing at?\r\nMy fly ain't open, is it?\r\n\r\n00:06:06.074 --\u003e 00:06:08.034\r\n- No, sir.\r\n- So, what's the gag?\r\n\r\n00:06:08.577 --\u003e 00:06:12.664\r\nCome on. You know.\r\n\"What's the gag?\"\r\n\r\n00:06:12.831 --\u003e 00:06:14.040\r\nCan it, sister.\r\n\r\n00:06:14.332 --\u003e 00:06:17.669\r\nThis is Scarf ace you're dealing with\r\nand I don't stand for no disrespect.\r\n\r\n00:06:17.919 --\u003e 00:06:21.715\r\nI'd do as he says, ma'am.\r\nMr. Scarf ace can be quite insistent.\r\n\r\n00:06:21.798 --\u003e 00:06:23.717\r\nI don't think anyone's\r\ntalking to you.\r\n\r\n00:06:24.259 --\u003e 00:06:26.636\r\n- No, sir. No, sir.\r\n- Right.\r\n\r\n00:06:27.345 --\u003e 00:06:28.722\r\nSo, what do you want with me?\r\n\r\n00:06:29.180 --\u003e 00:06:30.682\r\nMy boys happened\r\nto be in the museum\r\n\r\n00:06:30.765 --\u003e 00:06:33.268\r\nwhen they saw your little\r\nset-to with Miss Ronnie V.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.977 --\u003e 00:06:35.687\r\nThey also seen you\r\nlicking your whiskers\r\n\r\n00:06:35.770 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nat the sight of Ronnie's\r\npretty sparklers.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.857 --\u003e 00:06:40.150\r\nYou're boring me, log.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.193 --\u003e 00:06:46.239\r\nSo, what if I could provide you with a\r\nfoolproof plan for snatching those rocks\r\n\r\n00:06:46.323 --\u003e 00:06:48.700\r\nwith no risk of\r\nyou getting caught?\r\n\r\n00:06:50.952 --\u003e 00:06:53.204\r\nPass. Kitty's been\r\nstaying in at night.\r\n\r\n00:06:53.788 --\u003e 00:06:56.875\r\nIt's not the greatest, but it beats\r\nthe pound, if you know what I mean.\r\n\r\n00:06:57.042 --\u003e 00:06:58.668\r\nNow that's a darn shame.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.835 --\u003e 00:07:02.172\r\nAnd I thought for sure you'd want a\r\nchance to get even with the Vreelands.\r\n\r\n00:07:02.756 --\u003e 00:07:04.507\r\nNot just for yourself,\r\nyou understand,\r\n\r\n00:07:04.591 --\u003e 00:07:07.344\r\nbut for all those poor\r\nlittle stuffed critters\r\n\r\n00:07:07.510 --\u003e 00:07:10.805\r\nwhat never had the\r\nchance to fight back.\r\n\r\n00:07:11.765 --\u003e 00:07:13.016\r\nOh! Barf.\r\n\r\n00:07:13.099 --\u003e 00:07:14.517\r\nIt's a 50-50 cut.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.726 --\u003e 00:07:16.728\r\nTake it or leave it.\r\nYou in, or what?\r\n\r\n00:07:37.415 --\u003e 00:07:38.792\r\nYou know what, Isis?\r\n\r\n00:07:40.669 --\u003e 00:07:42.712\r\nExtinction's for wimps.\r\n\r\n00:07:56.101 --\u003e 00:07:58.520\r\nMastodon, check.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.937 --\u003e 00:08:01.064\r\nCave bear, check.\r\n\r\n00:08:01.481 --\u003e 00:08:02.524\r\nSaber-tooth.\r\n\r\n00:08:02.607 --\u003e 00:08:03.608\r\n- (CREATURE MEOWS)\r\n- Huh?\r\n\r\n00:08:09.197 --\u003e 00:08:11.449\r\nWell, where did you come from?\r\n\r\n00:08:12.117 --\u003e 00:08:13.159\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:08:13.243 --\u003e 00:08:16.913\r\nAw, poor girl.\r\nMust've wandered in and got lost.\r\n\r\n00:08:17.372 --\u003e 00:08:18.665\r\nI'll let you out back.\r\n\r\n00:08:26.172 --\u003e 00:08:27.966\r\nExcuse me, Mr. Scarf ace,\r\n\r\n00:08:28.049 --\u003e 00:08:31.636\r\nbut isn't it cruel to take\r\nadvantage of that nice Miss Kyle?\r\n\r\n00:08:32.345 --\u003e 00:08:33.805\r\nHold my hat, will you?\r\n\r\n00:08:35.807 --\u003e 00:08:37.350\r\n“Bam! Ow!\r\n\r\n00:08:37.434 --\u003e 00:08:39.686\r\nThat's what you get\r\nfor going soft on me.\r\n\r\n00:08:39.769 --\u003e 00:08:41.229\r\nYes, sir.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.731 --\u003e 00:08:46.651\r\nThere. The guard's putting\r\nthe cat out like I planned.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.735 --\u003e 00:08:48.987\r\n\u003ci\u003eSCARFACE: Catwoman should\r\nhave all the time she needs\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:49.070 --\u003e 00:08:50.822\r\n\u003ci\u003eto lift the jewels and split.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:51.698 --\u003e 00:08:53.908\r\nThis one's for the Vreelands.\r\n\r\n00:08:56.745 --\u003e 00:08:59.873\r\nBut plans can change,\r\ncan't they, Rhino?\r\n\r\n00:08:59.956 --\u003e 00:09:01.624\r\nRight, boss.\r\n\r\n00:09:10.091 --\u003e 00:09:11.176\r\n“(GASPS) _Huh?\r\n\r\n00:09:11.384 --\u003e 00:09:13.344\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:14.888 --\u003e 00:09:17.348\r\nGreat. Someone else\r\nis hitting the place.\r\n\r\n00:09:19.809 --\u003e 00:09:21.978\r\nOkay, boys, to work.\r\n\r\n00:09:40.830 --\u003e 00:09:43.708\r\nSorry, kitty.\r\nYou're taking the fall.\r\n\r\n00:09:48.129 --\u003e 00:09:49.422\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:09:55.178 --\u003e 00:09:56.221\r\nHold it.\r\n\r\n00:09:56.638 --\u003e 00:09:58.139\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:09:59.307 --\u003e 00:10:01.142\r\nCould you please give me a hand?\r\n\r\n00:10:01.226 --\u003e 00:10:03.895\r\nThis dinosaur seems\r\nto have fallen on me.\r\n\r\n00:10:04.604 --\u003e 00:10:08.233\r\n- How did you...\r\n- It's a dull story, handsome.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.487 --\u003e 00:10:15.698\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:10:25.750 --\u003e 00:10:28.253\r\n(SIRENS WAILING)\r\n\r\n00:10:31.005 --\u003e 00:10:32.006\r\nThe Catwoman.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.590 --\u003e 00:10:33.633\r\nWatch out!\r\n\r\n00:10:33.758 --\u003e 00:10:36.386\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:10:37.011 --\u003e 00:10:38.346\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:10:41.766 --\u003e 00:10:44.435\r\n- Where is she?\r\n- Couldn't have missed her.\r\n\r\n00:10:53.403 --\u003e 00:10:55.613\r\nLooks like the hunt's on\r\nagain, Isis.\r\n\r\n00:10:57.574 --\u003e 00:11:00.034\r\nI think a quick trip\r\nout of town is in order.\r\n\r\n00:11:00.660 --\u003e 00:11:02.287\r\nMAN: Don't buy your ticket yet.\r\n\r\n00:11:03.872 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:11:05.081 --\u003e 00:11:06.499\r\nWhat a pleasant surprise.\r\n\r\n00:11:06.916 --\u003e 00:11:10.170\r\nThough I should warn you,\r\nbreaking and entering is against the law.\r\n\r\n00:11:10.670 --\u003e 00:11:14.382\r\nYou would know. Care to explain what\r\nyou were doing at the museum tonight?\r\n\r\n00:11:14.924 --\u003e 00:11:19.137\r\nLook, I was there earlier for a\r\nparty, and I kind of lost my temper.\r\n\r\n00:11:19.429 --\u003e 00:11:21.890\r\nI went back to apologize,\r\nand the place was empty,\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.433\r\nexcept for the burglars.\r\n\r\n00:11:23.808 --\u003e 00:11:27.228\r\nI happened to have my outfit in the car,\r\nand I thought if I nailed the robbers\r\n\r\n00:11:27.312 --\u003e 00:11:29.689\r\nI could work up some\r\npoints with the cops.\r\n\r\n00:11:30.190 --\u003e 00:11:31.357\r\nMaybe even with you.\r\n\r\n00:11:33.568 --\u003e 00:11:37.071\r\nI know how bad this looks for\r\nme, but it wasn't my fault.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.327 --\u003e 00:11:45.413\r\nWould you come back to the museum and\r\ntell your story to the authorities?\r\n\r\n00:11:45.496 --\u003e 00:11:48.708\r\nI suppose, if you're with me.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.250 --\u003e 00:11:53.254\r\n- After all, we do make a good team.\r\n- When we're on the same side.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.550 --\u003e 00:11:59.719\r\n(INAUDIBLE)\r\n\r\n00:12:10.521 --\u003e 00:12:12.482\r\nThe police are still\r\ntalking to the guard.\r\n\r\n00:12:12.857 --\u003e 00:12:14.692\r\nThat gives us a few\r\nminutes to look around.\r\n\r\n00:12:15.443 --\u003e 00:12:17.320\r\nI was looking at\r\nthis exhibit earlier.\r\n\r\n00:12:17.820 --\u003e 00:12:21.658\r\nIt's brand-new. Why would they\r\nremove the animals so soon?\r\n\r\n00:12:26.579 --\u003e 00:12:28.122\r\nThis lock's been sprung.\r\n\r\n00:12:28.206 --\u003e 00:12:31.125\r\nOur thief is clever,\r\nusing dummy cards to cover his tracks.\r\n\r\n00:12:31.459 --\u003e 00:12:35.004\r\nAn extinct-animal trophy is worth a\r\nfortune to the crook who can fence it.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.380 --\u003e 00:12:37.882\r\n\"All those poor little\r\nstuffed critters.\"\r\n\r\n00:12:38.091 --\u003e 00:12:40.009\r\nThat's what he was\r\nafter all along.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.510 --\u003e 00:12:42.220\r\nYou're not telling me something.\r\n\r\n00:12:42.887 --\u003e 00:12:45.014\r\nYou know what's wrong\r\nwith our relationship?\r\n\r\n00:12:45.556 --\u003e 00:12:47.976\r\nYou always let me get too close.\r\n\r\n00:12:48.643 --\u003e 00:12:50.687\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:51.604 --\u003e 00:12:55.692\r\nExcuse me. I have a date\r\nwith a scratching post.\r\n\r\n00:13:17.005 --\u003e 00:13:18.840\r\nWe don't have to\r\nmake this difficult.\r\n\r\n00:13:18.923 --\u003e 00:13:21.301\r\nBut somehow we always do.\r\n\r\n00:13:22.135 --\u003e 00:13:23.261\r\n(HISSES)\r\n\r\n00:13:23.344 --\u003e 00:13:24.554\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:13:25.638 --\u003e 00:13:26.681\r\nSefina?\r\n\r\n00:13:34.897 --\u003e 00:13:35.898\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:13:41.821 --\u003e 00:13:42.822\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:56.210 --\u003e 00:13:58.588\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:14:23.821 --\u003e 00:14:24.864\r\nCOP: In here!\r\n\r\n00:14:37.293 --\u003e 00:14:38.294\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:14:44.467 --\u003e 00:14:45.787\r\n\u003ci\u003eSCARF ACE: That's\r\nfight, Penguin.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:45.843 --\u003e 00:14:48.262\r\nI got your bird just\r\nlike I promised.\r\n\r\n00:14:48.846 --\u003e 00:14:50.890\r\nOf course, it'll cost you extra.\r\n\r\n00:14:53.142 --\u003e 00:14:55.395\r\nHey, you don't want it, fine.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.478 --\u003e 00:14:58.314\r\nI can always use it\r\nfor pillow stuffing.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.607 --\u003e 00:15:00.608\r\nAh...\r\n\r\n00:15:00.691 --\u003e 00:15:02.985\r\nSee there?\r\nI knew you'd be reasonable.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.488 --\u003e 00:15:09.200\r\nWhile I got you on the horn,\r\ncan I interest you in a Tasmanian tiger?\r\n\r\n00:15:09.409 --\u003e 00:15:11.285\r\nA steal at only two mil.\r\n\r\n00:15:11.661 --\u003e 00:15:12.829\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:15:13.996 --\u003e 00:15:16.040\r\n\u003ci\u003eSCARF ACE: No, huh'?\r\nThat's okay.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:16.457 --\u003e 00:15:19.377\r\nI got a client dying\r\nto get her paws on it.\r\n\r\n00:15:21.838 --\u003e 00:15:22.839\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:15:23.423 --\u003e 00:15:24.841\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:15:24.924 --\u003e 00:15:25.967\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:27.093 --\u003e 00:15:29.720\r\nI thought I saw a pussycat.\r\n\r\n00:15:33.391 --\u003e 00:15:35.017\r\n(WHIRRING)\r\n\r\n00:15:53.202 --\u003e 00:15:54.537\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:01.586 --\u003e 00:16:03.004\r\nLet go!\r\n\r\n00:16:05.339 --\u003e 00:16:06.966\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:07.049 --\u003e 00:16:10.636\r\nYou know, I never had much use for\r\nanimals, except Rhino here.\r\n\r\n00:16:10.887 --\u003e 00:16:12.388\r\nThanks, boss.\r\n\r\n00:16:12.555 --\u003e 00:16:15.266\r\nThen it hit me,\r\nsome rich geeks will pay big bucks\r\n\r\n00:16:15.349 --\u003e 00:16:17.518\r\nfor critters they can't\r\ngo out and shoot no more.\r\n\r\n00:16:17.935 --\u003e 00:16:20.104\r\nYou know what these\r\nthings are worth dead?\r\n\r\n00:16:20.188 --\u003e 00:16:21.772\r\nMore than my life, I bet.\r\n\r\n00:16:22.273 --\u003e 00:16:23.441\r\nYou win, kitten.\r\n\r\n00:16:23.900 --\u003e 00:16:27.361\r\nI needed a dummy to keep the cops\r\nbusy while I grabbed the stiffs.\r\n\r\n00:16:28.029 --\u003e 00:16:30.740\r\nSo you conned me into\r\nthat phony jewel robbery.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.823 --\u003e 00:16:33.117\r\nToo bad for you\r\nyou figured it out.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.618 --\u003e 00:16:38.664\r\nNow we're gonna find out if there really\r\nis more than one way to skin a cat.\r\n\r\n00:16:39.415 --\u003e 00:16:41.584\r\n- Rhino.\r\n- No!\r\n\r\n00:16:43.920 --\u003e 00:16:44.921\r\n(MEOWS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.174 --\u003e 00:16:49.258\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:49.342 --\u003e 00:16:50.426\r\n- (ISIS YOWLS)\r\n- Ow!\r\n\r\n00:16:50.510 --\u003e 00:16:51.886\r\nLousy fleabag.\r\n\r\n00:16:54.013 --\u003e 00:16:55.348\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:59.060 --\u003e 00:17:00.311\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:17:02.313 --\u003e 00:17:05.066\r\nOh, Great. Him, I don't need.\r\n\r\n00:17:06.817 --\u003e 00:17:09.320\r\nI don't know whether to\r\nbite you or kiss you.\r\n\r\n00:17:10.321 --\u003e 00:17:11.989\r\n(RHINO GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:14.116 --\u003e 00:17:15.284\r\nLater.\r\n\r\n00:17:16.702 --\u003e 00:17:18.162\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:17:22.333 --\u003e 00:17:23.709\r\nGet me out of here.\r\n\r\n00:17:27.088 --\u003e 00:17:28.089\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:29.298 --\u003e 00:17:30.758\r\nHurry!\r\n\r\n00:17:32.301 --\u003e 00:17:34.428\r\n- Oh, no.\r\n- Oh, yes.\r\n\r\n00:17:34.929 --\u003e 00:17:37.306\r\n- Put me down.\r\n- Sure.\r\n\r\n00:17:37.640 --\u003e 00:17:39.684\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:17:40.268 --\u003e 00:17:42.019\r\nUh-oh.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.103 --\u003e 00:17:43.521\r\nMr. Scarf ace!\r\n\r\n00:17:45.523 --\u003e 00:17:46.816\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:48.150 --\u003e 00:17:50.695\r\nLet's let the chips\r\nfall where they may.\r\n\r\n00:17:52.780 --\u003e 00:17:55.408\r\nGet me off of here.\r\nDummy, help me.\r\n\r\n00:17:57.243 --\u003e 00:17:59.036\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:03.165 --\u003e 00:18:05.376\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:18:11.048 --\u003e 00:18:13.801\r\nHelp, help!\r\nSomeone do something!\r\n\r\n00:18:14.427 --\u003e 00:18:16.178\r\nPlease, let me save him.\r\n\r\n00:18:16.721 --\u003e 00:18:19.098\r\nHmm, nah!\r\n\r\n00:18:20.182 --\u003e 00:18:23.311\r\nDummy, please!\r\n\r\n00:18:25.855 --\u003e 00:18:26.856\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.946 --\u003e 00:18:34.947\r\nPhew!\r\n\r\n00:18:36.907 --\u003e 00:18:38.117\r\nPhew!\r\n\r\n00:18:44.790 --\u003e 00:18:45.791\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:18:47.043 --\u003e 00:18:48.044\r\nHuh?\r\n\r\n00:18:50.296 --\u003e 00:18:51.672\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:19:00.806 --\u003e 00:19:04.310\r\n- That's one way to remove a splinter.\r\n- (SOBBING)\r\n\r\n00:19:07.063 --\u003e 00:19:10.232\r\nWhat's wrong, Ventriloquist?\r\nCat got your tongue?\r\n\r\n00:19:10.941 --\u003e 00:19:13.569\r\nPlease, I never hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:19:13.944 --\u003e 00:19:17.114\r\nScarf ace, he's another person.\r\nNot me, really.\r\n\r\n00:19:17.365 --\u003e 00:19:19.200\r\nBut he's inside you somewhere.\r\n\r\n00:19:19.533 --\u003e 00:19:22.495\r\nAnd I'm going to keep\r\nscratching until I find him.\r\n\r\n00:19:25.331 --\u003e 00:19:27.124\r\nDon't make it\r\nharder on yourself.\r\n\r\n00:19:27.291 --\u003e 00:19:30.211\r\n- He cost me my freedom.\r\n- No.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.628 --\u003e 00:19:33.089\r\nYou gave it up.\r\nFrom the very start I suspected\r\n\r\n00:19:33.172 --\u003e 00:19:35.292\r\nthere was more to this\r\nbusiness than you were telling.\r\n\r\n00:19:35.758 --\u003e 00:19:38.594\r\nSo I put a transmitter on your\r\ncat back at your apartment.\r\n\r\n00:19:39.095 --\u003e 00:19:41.347\r\nIt led me here in time\r\nto hear your confession.\r\n\r\n00:19:41.806 --\u003e 00:19:44.934\r\n- Why did you do it, Selina?\r\n- I have to be who I am.\r\n\r\n00:19:45.351 --\u003e 00:19:49.647\r\nI realize now I can't change that.\r\nLike I told someone else tonight...\r\n\r\n00:19:50.272 --\u003e 00:19:51.816\r\nIt's just the cat in me.\r\n\r\n00:19:55.861 --\u003e 00:19:56.904\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:20:00.950 --\u003e 00:20:03.953\r\nIt's priceless, Batman.\r\nThe last of its kind.\r\n\r\n00:20:04.203 --\u003e 00:20:06.956\r\nWill you take me in or let\r\nit become extinct again?\r\n\r\n00:20:07.331 --\u003e 00:20:10.000\r\nThe lady or the tiger, darling.\r\n\r\n00:20:10.084 --\u003e 00:20:11.252\r\nYour choice.\r\n\r\n00:20:35.234 --\u003e 00:20:38.362\r\nCATWOMAN: \u003ci\u003elam the cat\r\nwho walks by herself.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:20:44.076 --\u003e 00:20:46.078\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:16.984 --\u003e 00:21:21.984\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S04 E04 - A Bullet for Bullock (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.131 --\u003e 00:00:08.133\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:22.541 --\u003e 00:01:24.209\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:01:30.591 --\u003e 00:01:32.217\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:01:34.219 --\u003e 00:01:35.262\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:01:41.435 --\u003e 00:01:43.020\r\n(BREATHING DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:02:02.122 --\u003e 00:02:03.248\r\nCommissioner?\r\n\r\n00:02:03.874 --\u003e 00:02:05.250\r\nBULLOCK: Nope. Me.\r\n\r\n00:02:06.335 --\u003e 00:02:07.419\r\nI got a problem.\r\n\r\n00:02:08.337 --\u003e 00:02:09.963\r\nAnd you want my help?\r\n\r\n00:02:11.423 --\u003e 00:02:13.383\r\nLet's get something\r\nstraight from the get-go.\r\n\r\n00:02:13.592 --\u003e 00:02:16.762\r\nI think you're a freak and a menace,\r\nand those are your good points.\r\n\r\n00:02:17.304 --\u003e 00:02:20.140\r\nBut the commish says you serve a\r\npurpose, so I go along.\r\n\r\n00:02:21.016 --\u003e 00:02:24.144\r\nI appreciate your honesty.\r\nWhat's the problem?\r\n\r\n00:02:24.728 --\u003e 00:02:26.063\r\nSomebody's got it in for me.\r\n\r\n00:02:26.146 --\u003e 00:02:28.231\r\nTried to give me a fender\r\nmassage last night.\r\n\r\n00:02:28.482 --\u003e 00:02:30.776\r\nIt ain't the first time.\r\nLast week too.\r\n\r\n00:02:30.984 --\u003e 00:02:32.152\r\nAny Suspects?\r\n\r\n00:02:32.319 --\u003e 00:02:34.446\r\nSo many they could have\r\ntheir own zip code.\r\n\r\n00:02:34.946 --\u003e 00:02:37.032\r\nI've put a lot of guys away\r\nand they hate me for it.\r\n\r\n00:02:37.407 --\u003e 00:02:40.202\r\nLooks like one of them hates me\r\nenough to do something about it.\r\n\r\n00:02:41.119 --\u003e 00:02:44.039\r\nWhy me? Why not just\r\ngo to the department?\r\n\r\n00:02:44.623 --\u003e 00:02:46.166\r\nI step on a lot of toes.\r\n\r\n00:02:46.375 --\u003e 00:02:49.378\r\nI don't want Internal Affairs\r\nlooking at me too close.\r\n\r\n00:02:49.586 --\u003e 00:02:51.963\r\nThey might find some\r\nthings I don't want found.\r\n\r\n00:02:52.172 --\u003e 00:02:54.007\r\n- Are you on the take?\r\n- Watch it, freak!\r\n\r\n00:02:54.174 --\u003e 00:02:56.259\r\nI never took a dime from nobody!\r\n\r\n00:02:56.385 --\u003e 00:02:58.970\r\nI just bend the rules\r\na little sometimes.\r\n\r\n00:02:59.137 --\u003e 00:03:00.347\r\nYou understand.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.931 --\u003e 00:03:02.224\r\nWe're not all that different.\r\n\r\n00:03:02.391 --\u003e 00:03:05.727\r\nWe're on the same side,\r\nbut we're not the same.\r\n\r\n00:03:06.228 --\u003e 00:03:10.107\r\nI'll help you find out who's after you,\r\nbut you've got to collar them clean.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.273 --\u003e 00:03:12.984\r\nFile copies of my cases\r\nfrom five years back.\r\n\r\n00:03:13.151 --\u003e 00:03:14.986\r\nDon't wanna run them\r\non the system here.\r\n\r\n00:03:15.112 --\u003e 00:03:16.863\r\nYou find the guy then tell me.\r\n\r\n00:03:17.114 --\u003e 00:03:20.409\r\nI'll take it from there.\r\nSound fair, partner?\r\n\r\n00:03:46.935 --\u003e 00:03:47.936\r\nUgh.\r\n\r\n00:03:52.399 --\u003e 00:03:54.317\r\nThere's a doormat\r\noutside, Mr. Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:03:54.401 --\u003e 00:03:57.904\r\nReally? I thought you were the\r\ndoormat around here, Nivens.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.698 --\u003e 00:04:00.699\r\n(EXCLAIMS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e DISGUST)\r\n\r\n00:04:01.408 --\u003e 00:04:04.286\r\nDon't crowd me, dork,\r\nor I'll wipe my feet on you.\r\n\r\n00:04:05.412 --\u003e 00:04:06.455\r\nAhem.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.538 --\u003e 00:04:10.459\r\nTake out your garbage once in a while.\r\nYour apartment stinks.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.667 --\u003e 00:04:12.961\r\nI won't have roaches\r\nin my building!\r\n\r\n00:04:13.462 --\u003e 00:04:16.089\r\nAnd turn the heat down\r\nwhen you're out all day!\r\n\r\n00:04:16.173 --\u003e 00:04:17.966\r\nHappy holidays, Nivens.\r\n\r\n00:04:18.425 --\u003e 00:04:19.426\r\n(GROANS IN EXASPERATION)\r\n\r\n00:04:25.265 --\u003e 00:04:26.266\r\nHuh!\r\n\r\n00:04:30.937 --\u003e 00:04:32.105\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:04:40.238 --\u003e 00:04:41.907\r\nThank heaven for rent control.\r\n\r\n00:04:44.117 --\u003e 00:04:46.369\r\nALFRED: We are speaking of\r\nthe same person, are we not?\r\n\r\n00:04:46.453 --\u003e 00:04:50.832\r\nHarvey Bullock? The detective\r\nwho looks like an unmade bed?\r\n\r\n00:04:51.082 --\u003e 00:04:52.209\r\nThe same.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.626 --\u003e 00:04:56.087\r\nHe came to you for help?\r\nIt must be serious.\r\n\r\n00:04:56.880 --\u003e 00:05:00.300\r\nIt'll take the system a while to\r\ncollate and cross-index the names.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.550 --\u003e 00:05:01.927\r\nI'll be back later.\r\n\r\n00:05:03.762 --\u003e 00:05:06.139\r\nI thought you were through\r\nwith your rounds for tonight.\r\n\r\n00:05:07.224 --\u003e 00:05:10.977\r\nNot yet. I have a feeling Bullock's\r\ngoing to need a guardian angel.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.279 --\u003e 00:05:24.032\r\nStay sharp.\r\nThese perps are bad news.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.115 --\u003e 00:05:26.910\r\nScagged a couple of bank\r\nguards Christmas day.\r\n\r\n00:05:33.834 --\u003e 00:05:35.544\r\nPolice! Nobody move!\r\n\r\n00:05:35.877 --\u003e 00:05:36.878\r\n(MAN GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:05:40.465 --\u003e 00:05:41.758\r\nBULLOCK: Hey! Hold it!\r\n\r\n00:06:18.920 --\u003e 00:06:20.046\r\nGive it up, hairball!\r\n\r\n00:06:25.635 --\u003e 00:06:26.720\r\n(BREATHES DEEPLY)\r\n\r\n00:06:33.560 --\u003e 00:06:35.103\r\n(GRUNTS AND GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:06:38.064 --\u003e 00:06:39.190\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:06:40.025 --\u003e 00:06:42.819\r\nWatching your back.\r\nGood thing, too.\r\n\r\n00:06:43.361 --\u003e 00:06:45.989\r\nI asked you to find a\r\nname, not hold my hand.\r\n\r\n00:06:46.281 --\u003e 00:06:47.657\r\nYou're welcome.\r\n\r\n00:06:50.785 --\u003e 00:06:52.120\r\nI have some questions.\r\n\r\n00:06:52.495 --\u003e 00:06:55.248\r\nLater. After my shift.\r\nWhere do I find you?\r\n\r\n00:06:55.332 --\u003e 00:06:56.625\r\nBATMAN: I'll find you.\r\n\r\n00:06:59.669 --\u003e 00:07:00.754\r\nBULLOCK: Show-off.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.590 --\u003e 00:07:04.591\r\nOn your feet.\r\n\r\n00:07:04.716 --\u003e 00:07:06.885\r\nHarv? You need a hand up here?\r\n\r\n00:07:07.928 --\u003e 00:07:09.638\r\nJust reading this\r\njerk his rights.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.221 --\u003e 00:07:11.973\r\nYou got the right\r\nto remain silent.\r\n\r\n00:07:12.057 --\u003e 00:07:14.851\r\nIf you give up that right you'll\r\nprobably bore me to tears.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.935 --\u003e 00:07:17.228\r\nSo keep your trap\r\nshut, dog-breath.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.282 --\u003e 00:07:30.575\r\nQuestions, remember?\r\n\r\n00:07:32.369 --\u003e 00:07:35.038\r\nSheesh!\r\nYou take some chances, freak.\r\n\r\n00:07:37.165 --\u003e 00:07:39.668\r\n- Are these all the threats you received?\r\n- Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:07:40.001 --\u003e 00:07:41.670\r\nI'm thinking of\r\nstarting a scrapbook.\r\n\r\n00:07:44.214 --\u003e 00:07:45.614\r\nBATMAN: You dusted\r\nthem for prints?\r\n\r\n00:07:46.466 --\u003e 00:07:48.134\r\nYep. Nada.\r\n\r\n00:07:48.843 --\u003e 00:07:50.762\r\nHand-delivered to my mailbox.\r\n\r\n00:07:52.597 --\u003e 00:07:54.849\r\nSomeone's gone to a lot\r\nof effort to scare you.\r\n\r\n00:07:55.183 --\u003e 00:07:56.943\r\nBut I don't think they're\r\ntrying to kill you.\r\n\r\n00:07:58.019 --\u003e 00:08:01.481\r\nYeah? That attack last\r\nnight seemed pretty sincere.\r\n\r\n00:08:04.025 --\u003e 00:08:07.195\r\nA professional hit man would do you\r\nhere, not on the street.\r\n\r\n00:08:07.654 --\u003e 00:08:08.655\r\nSo what?\r\n\r\n00:08:08.738 --\u003e 00:08:12.033\r\nThe guy who gets whacked by an\r\namateur is just as stiff as a pro job.\r\n\r\n00:08:15.745 --\u003e 00:08:17.622\r\nWhen you gonna get me\r\nthat list of names?\r\n\r\n00:08:22.836 --\u003e 00:08:25.088\r\nI wonder how Gordon\r\nputs up with this.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.168 --\u003e 00:09:04.919\r\n(EXCLAIMS AND GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:09:07.797 --\u003e 00:09:09.007\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:09:09.716 --\u003e 00:09:10.884\r\n(SCREAMS)\r\n\r\n00:09:26.649 --\u003e 00:09:28.193\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:09:32.947 --\u003e 00:09:33.948\r\n(EXCLAIMS IN FRUSTRATION)\r\n\r\n00:09:39.496 --\u003e 00:09:42.624\r\nBullock? You okay?\r\nYou don't look so good.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.791 --\u003e 00:09:45.877\r\nI mean, you never look good,\r\nbut today you look worse.\r\n\r\n00:09:46.252 --\u003e 00:09:50.006\r\nAfter 15 years working in this cesspool,\r\nI'd like to see how good you look.\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:52.675\r\nWell, you're sure full\r\nof holiday spirit.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.759 --\u003e 00:09:54.219\r\nWhat are you doing\r\nfor New Year's?\r\n\r\n00:09:54.844 --\u003e 00:09:57.222\r\nSame thing I did for Christmas.\r\nMy laundry.\r\n\r\n00:09:58.306 --\u003e 00:09:59.557\r\n(SIGHS)\r\n\r\n00:10:10.151 --\u003e 00:10:12.987\r\n- BATMAN: Bullock.\r\n- You got what I want, pointy ears?\r\n\r\n00:10:13.696 --\u003e 00:10:16.491\r\nYou were right, Bullock.\r\nA lot of people don't like you.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.699 --\u003e 00:10:18.535\r\nThe list of suspects\r\nwas a long one.\r\n\r\n00:10:19.327 --\u003e 00:10:21.955\r\nDoes the name Vincent\r\nStarkey mean anything to you?\r\n\r\n00:10:22.497 --\u003e 00:10:24.040\r\nVinnie the Shark? Yeah.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.457 --\u003e 00:10:26.543\r\nThe dirtbag threatened\r\nme in open court.\r\n\r\n00:10:26.626 --\u003e 00:10:30.046\r\nRan a drug lab in South Gotham.\r\nI broke it up when I was in Vice.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.130 --\u003e 00:10:32.006\r\nHe got 10 to 20 in Stonegate.\r\n\r\n00:10:32.590 --\u003e 00:10:36.261\r\nStarkey was a model prisoner.\r\nHe only did eight years.\r\n\r\n00:10:36.970 --\u003e 00:10:38.346\r\nHe's out, Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:10:38.429 --\u003e 00:10:42.142\r\nI cost him an empire.\r\nHe'd love to see me take a dirt nap.\r\n\r\n00:10:42.642 --\u003e 00:10:43.768\r\nWhere do we find him?\r\n\r\n00:10:44.060 --\u003e 00:10:47.105\r\nI'm working on it.\r\nI want you to follow up on a lead.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:49.315\r\nHey, what am I,\r\nsome wet-eared rookie?\r\n\r\n00:10:49.524 --\u003e 00:10:52.152\r\nNobody tells me how to\r\nconduct an investigation.\r\n\r\n00:10:52.360 --\u003e 00:10:54.028\r\nDo you wanna live, Bullock?\r\n\r\n00:10:55.321 --\u003e 00:10:56.906\r\nThen pay attention.\r\n\r\n00:10:58.575 --\u003e 00:11:02.203\r\nSummer Gleeson did an exposé on\r\nSouth Gotham crack houses last week.\r\n\r\n00:11:02.537 --\u003e 00:11:04.257\r\nShe might have heard\r\nsomething about Vinnie.\r\n\r\n00:11:04.455 --\u003e 00:11:06.207\r\nSo, see the woman, huh?\r\n\r\n00:11:06.374 --\u003e 00:11:09.460\r\n- What are you gonna do?\r\n- Make a few inquiries.\r\n\r\n00:11:09.627 --\u003e 00:11:12.088\r\nInquiries? Like what?\r\n\r\n00:11:12.338 --\u003e 00:11:15.466\r\nHey, pal, this is my life\r\nwe're talking about here!\r\n\r\n00:11:15.633 --\u003e 00:11:17.844\r\nBats! Bats!\r\n\r\n00:11:19.637 --\u003e 00:11:20.763\r\n(TAPE WINDING)\r\n\r\n00:11:23.224 --\u003e 00:11:24.934\r\nBullock?\r\nWhat are you doing here?\r\n\r\n00:11:25.560 --\u003e 00:11:29.230\r\nNeed a favor, Gleeson.\r\nThat shoot you did down in crack town?\r\n\r\n00:11:29.772 --\u003e 00:11:32.108\r\nYou still owe me for the\r\nlast favor I did you.\r\n\r\n00:11:32.609 --\u003e 00:11:34.986\r\nHey, Summer,\r\nwhere's your Christmas spirit?\r\n\r\n00:11:35.236 --\u003e 00:11:36.571\r\nYou know you can trust me.\r\n\r\n00:11:37.030 --\u003e 00:11:39.532\r\nI trust you about as\r\nfar as I can throw you.\r\n\r\n00:11:42.327 --\u003e 00:11:43.870\r\nCome on, Gleeson.\r\n\r\n00:11:46.247 --\u003e 00:11:48.208\r\nYou're lucky I talk to you at\r\nall, Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:11:49.959 --\u003e 00:11:52.503\r\nTell you what.\r\nCome back in an hour.\r\n\r\n00:12:25.536 --\u003e 00:12:29.582\r\nHere you go, my friend.\r\nAnd a happy New Year to you.\r\n\r\n00:12:30.375 --\u003e 00:12:33.419\r\nFree enterprise.\r\nWhat makes America great.\r\n\r\n00:12:40.134 --\u003e 00:12:41.302\r\n(STAMMERS) Batman!\r\n\r\n00:12:42.011 --\u003e 00:12:43.096\r\nWhat... What do you want?\r\n\r\n00:12:43.263 --\u003e 00:12:45.932\r\nNot what, slime ball, who.\r\n\r\n00:12:46.015 --\u003e 00:12:47.183\r\nVinnie the Shark.\r\n\r\n00:12:47.976 --\u003e 00:12:49.978\r\nHe's not my connection anymore.\r\n\r\n00:12:50.353 --\u003e 00:12:51.646\r\nWrong answer.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.730 --\u003e 00:12:55.191\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.986 --\u003e 00:12:59.195\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:00.071 --\u003e 00:13:01.447\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:07.954 --\u003e 00:13:09.080\r\nTake two.\r\n\r\n00:13:09.414 --\u003e 00:13:11.416\r\n(WHIMPERS) Okay, okay, okay!\r\n\r\n00:13:20.800 --\u003e 00:13:22.135\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:22.760 --\u003e 00:13:24.804\r\nAren't you a piece of work.\r\n\r\n00:13:25.763 --\u003e 00:13:28.933\r\nYou gotta help me, Gleeson.\r\nI need to find Vinnie the Shark.\r\n\r\n00:13:29.017 --\u003e 00:13:32.061\r\nYou wanna find a shark?\r\nYou can jump in Gotham Bay!\r\n\r\n00:13:32.228 --\u003e 00:13:35.273\r\nYou've blown it big time, Bullock.\r\nDon't ever come to me again.\r\n\r\n00:13:35.940 --\u003e 00:13:39.652\r\nSummer, cut me some slack.\r\nThis guy's looking to whack me.\r\n\r\n00:13:39.736 --\u003e 00:13:42.739\r\nLook on the bright side.\r\nYou'll make the 6:00 news.\r\n\r\n00:13:46.409 --\u003e 00:13:47.577\r\n(SCOFFS)\r\n\r\n00:13:55.209 --\u003e 00:13:56.252\r\nTaxi.\r\n\r\n00:13:58.129 --\u003e 00:13:59.130\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:14:04.635 --\u003e 00:14:05.720\r\nGet in.\r\n\r\n00:14:06.471 --\u003e 00:14:07.513\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:14:07.764 --\u003e 00:14:09.432\r\n(TIRES SQUEALING)\r\n\r\n00:14:11.017 --\u003e 00:14:13.895\r\nYou got a serious attitude\r\nproblem, freak.\r\n\r\n00:14:14.062 --\u003e 00:14:15.646\r\nYou want the Shark or not?\r\n\r\n00:14:15.813 --\u003e 00:14:16.939\r\nYou know where he is?\r\n\r\n00:14:17.273 --\u003e 00:14:20.943\r\nHe's running rock crystal out of an\r\nabandoned auto plant out in Bayside.\r\n\r\n00:14:22.445 --\u003e 00:14:24.113\r\nNice starship you got here.\r\n\r\n00:14:25.281 --\u003e 00:14:26.366\r\nWhat's this for?\r\n\r\n00:14:27.075 --\u003e 00:14:28.826\r\nPassenger ejector seat.\r\n\r\n00:14:34.332 --\u003e 00:14:38.503\r\nSomething about this still bothers me.\r\nStarkey's not one to make idle threats.\r\n\r\n00:14:38.586 --\u003e 00:14:40.713\r\nWhy would he warn\r\nyou to leave town?\r\n\r\n00:14:41.172 --\u003e 00:14:42.924\r\nThe sicko wanted\r\nto see me sweat.\r\n\r\n00:14:43.174 --\u003e 00:14:44.675\r\nCome on,\r\nlet's get this over with.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.103 --\u003e 00:14:59.315\r\nCareful with that merchandise, boys.\r\nYou break it, you buy it. Capisce?\r\n\r\n00:15:17.667 --\u003e 00:15:18.709\r\nNobody move!\r\n\r\n00:15:20.294 --\u003e 00:15:23.714\r\nNice entrance.\r\nStill haven't lost your sense of timing.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.634 --\u003e 00:15:27.677\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:15:28.511 --\u003e 00:15:29.637\r\nDown!\r\n\r\n00:15:34.600 --\u003e 00:15:35.601\r\n\u003ci\u003e(census)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:37.353 --\u003e 00:15:39.981\r\nTaking out the Batman will\r\nmake me look good in Gotham.\r\n\r\n00:15:40.440 --\u003e 00:15:44.569\r\nBut the real pleasure's gonna\r\nbe taking you out, Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.703 --\u003e 00:15:56.372\r\nEight years I waited to do\r\nthis, Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.290 --\u003e 00:15:59.792\r\nNow it's payback time.\r\n\r\n00:16:03.963 --\u003e 00:16:06.048\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:16:08.926 --\u003e 00:16:10.303\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:18.895 --\u003e 00:16:20.188\r\n(GRUNTS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e PAIN)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.074 --\u003e 00:16:33.075\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:17:19.330 --\u003e 00:17:20.873\r\nMerry Christmas, Vinnie.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.249 --\u003e 00:17:22.708\r\nAnd happy New Year.\r\n\r\n00:17:26.921 --\u003e 00:17:28.589\r\nJust call me Santa.\r\n\r\n00:17:29.715 --\u003e 00:17:32.385\r\nAnd guess who's on top\r\nof my naughty list?\r\n\r\n00:17:33.928 --\u003e 00:17:36.889\r\n- No, Bullock!\r\n- Relax, cowl-head.\r\n\r\n00:17:36.973 --\u003e 00:17:39.058\r\nThis dirtbag don't\r\nget off that easy.\r\n\r\n00:17:39.517 --\u003e 00:17:42.061\r\n- The rest of the gang?\r\n- Taken care of.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.311 --\u003e 00:17:44.021\r\nGood. I'll radio for a wagon.\r\n\r\n00:17:44.105 --\u003e 00:17:45.189\r\nYou think it's over?\r\n\r\n00:17:46.023 --\u003e 00:17:48.776\r\nHad to be Vinnie.\r\nYeah. It's over.\r\n\r\n00:17:48.859 --\u003e 00:17:50.319\r\nIt's your call.\r\n\r\n00:17:50.987 --\u003e 00:17:53.322\r\nBy the way,\r\nI still think you're a freak.\r\n\r\n00:17:53.656 --\u003e 00:17:54.699\r\nBut...\r\n\r\n00:17:55.032 --\u003e 00:17:56.075\r\nThanks.\r\n\r\n00:18:04.250 --\u003e 00:18:05.418\r\nOkay, Vinnie.\r\n\r\n00:18:07.420 --\u003e 00:18:09.922\r\nThey say confession's\r\ngood for the soul.\r\n\r\n00:18:10.965 --\u003e 00:18:13.301\r\nYou wanna tell me why you\r\nsent me those letters?\r\n\r\n00:18:13.676 --\u003e 00:18:17.430\r\nYou've taken one too many shots to\r\nthe head, Bullock. What letters?\r\n\r\n00:18:17.638 --\u003e 00:18:21.100\r\nListen, scum-face,\r\nI don't feel like playing games.\r\n\r\n00:18:21.475 --\u003e 00:18:23.019\r\nI got a pile of paperwork,\r\n\r\n00:18:23.102 --\u003e 00:18:26.230\r\nand Internal Affairs is all\r\nover me like a cheap suit!\r\n\r\n00:18:26.314 --\u003e 00:18:27.440\r\nSo spill it!\r\n\r\n00:18:27.815 --\u003e 00:18:30.443\r\nWhat are you gonna do?\r\nSend me to jail?\r\n\r\n00:18:31.068 --\u003e 00:18:33.279\r\nI'm telling you,\r\nI don't know what you're talking about!\r\n\r\n00:18:34.447 --\u003e 00:18:35.531\r\nGet him out of here.\r\n\r\n00:18:39.160 --\u003e 00:18:41.412\r\nIt's just gotta be him, Montoya.\r\n\r\n00:18:41.954 --\u003e 00:18:43.497\r\nThere ain't nobody else.\r\n\r\n00:18:52.506 --\u003e 00:18:54.258\r\nYou should've taken my\r\nadvice, Bullock.\r\n\r\n00:18:54.342 --\u003e 00:18:57.970\r\nYou should've left town.\r\nI tried to scare you out.\r\n\r\n00:18:58.596 --\u003e 00:19:00.139\r\nI didn't want it\r\nto come to this.\r\n\r\n00:19:01.641 --\u003e 00:19:02.725\r\nI know you.\r\n\r\n00:19:04.185 --\u003e 00:19:05.478\r\nStay back!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.187 --\u003e 00:19:09.690\r\nYou wouldn't take the hints,\r\nso now I have to settle it this way.\r\n\r\n00:19:10.483 --\u003e 00:19:12.818\r\nIt's your fault.\r\nI tried to warn you.\r\n\r\n00:19:16.364 --\u003e 00:19:18.491\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.243 --\u003e 00:19:22.912\r\nI thought this wasn't over.\r\n\r\n00:19:30.002 --\u003e 00:19:32.296\r\n- Nivens?\r\n- Why wouldn't you move?\r\n\r\n00:19:32.755 --\u003e 00:19:34.256\r\nWhy wouldn't you get out?\r\n\r\n00:19:34.799 --\u003e 00:19:38.135\r\nYou and your late hours\r\nand your filthy habits.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.678 --\u003e 00:19:42.640\r\nDo you have any idea what your\r\napartment's worth these days?\r\n\r\n00:19:43.265 --\u003e 00:19:44.642\r\nYou wanted my apartment?\r\n\r\n00:19:45.184 --\u003e 00:19:47.561\r\nYou mean all this was\r\nabout rent control?\r\n\r\n00:19:47.728 --\u003e 00:19:50.398\r\nNo! I wanted you gone!\r\n\r\n00:19:51.107 --\u003e 00:19:53.609\r\nYou're not a tenant,\r\nyou're a pestilence!\r\n\r\n00:19:53.943 --\u003e 00:19:56.320\r\nYou insult me.\r\nYou treat me like dirt.\r\n\r\n00:19:56.570 --\u003e 00:20:00.366\r\nNo jury in the world\r\nwould've convicted me!\r\n\r\n00:20:00.866 --\u003e 00:20:04.537\r\n(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)\r\n\r\n00:20:04.870 --\u003e 00:20:06.914\r\nThey wouldn't have convicted me!\r\n\r\n00:20:08.457 --\u003e 00:20:11.085\r\nSomebody like Vinnie wants to pop\r\nme, that's no surprise.\r\n\r\n00:20:11.961 --\u003e 00:20:13.045\r\nBut this...\r\n\r\n00:20:14.213 --\u003e 00:20:17.049\r\nYou know, it's funny.\r\nI was thinking of moving anyway.\r\n\r\n00:20:17.133 --\u003e 00:20:19.218\r\nNeighborhood's really been\r\ngoing downhill lately.\r\n\r\n00:20:19.593 --\u003e 00:20:22.096\r\nLook,\r\nI guess I owe you for this.\r\n\r\n00:20:22.471 --\u003e 00:20:25.558\r\nForget it, Bullock.\r\nYou've got enough problems.\r\n\r\n00:20:34.734 --\u003e 00:20:36.652\r\n(NIVENS CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:20:43.367 --\u003e 00:20:45.369\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:10.144 --\u003e 00:21:11.145\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::Batman T.A.S - S04 E05 - The Lion and The Unicorn (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:06.131 --\u003e 00:00:08.133\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:12.656 --\u003e 00:01:13.949\r\n(SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:01:32.134 --\u003e 00:01:33.534\r\nBATMAN: That's good\r\nenough, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:01:33.635 --\u003e 00:01:36.471\r\nThe people I deal with out\r\nthere won't mind a little lint.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.931 --\u003e 00:01:40.559\r\nAjob worth doing and all that\r\nrot, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:01:43.312 --\u003e 00:01:45.022\r\nI do wish you would\r\nput on a shirt.\r\n\r\n00:01:45.105 --\u003e 00:01:47.274\r\nYou're apt to catch\r\ncold in this dank cave.\r\n\r\n00:01:53.739 --\u003e 00:01:57.784\r\nYes, folks, a perfect 10 for\r\nDick Grayson to take the gold.\r\n\r\n00:01:57.951 --\u003e 00:01:59.995\r\nAnd the crowd goes wild.\r\n\r\n00:02:00.078 --\u003e 00:02:01.330\r\n(MIMICKING CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:02:01.496 --\u003e 00:02:02.664\r\nDICK: Yeah!\r\n\r\n00:02:02.748 --\u003e 00:02:04.708\r\n- Did you hear me, Master Dick?\r\n- Yeah, all right!\r\n\r\n00:02:05.917 --\u003e 00:02:08.587\r\nYes, Alfred. Right away, Alfred.\r\n\r\n00:02:15.761 --\u003e 00:02:17.304\r\n(TIRES SCREECH)\r\n\r\n00:02:17.387 --\u003e 00:02:20.015\r\nI've fixed your supper.\r\nIt's upstairs, in the oven.\r\n\r\n00:02:20.390 --\u003e 00:02:23.518\r\n- What would we do without you, Alfred?\r\n- I shudder to think.\r\n\r\n00:02:29.900 --\u003e 00:02:31.193\r\n(RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:02:33.153 --\u003e 00:02:35.405\r\n- Good evening. Wayne Manor.\r\n- FREDERICK: Alfie?\r\n\r\n00:02:35.906 --\u003e 00:02:38.408\r\n- It's your cousin Freddie.\r\n- Frederick?\r\n\r\n00:02:38.867 --\u003e 00:02:42.037\r\n\u003ci\u003eI say, old thing,\r\ncould you meet me at the usual place?\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:42.287 --\u003e 00:02:43.830\r\n\u003ci\u003eIt's rather urgent.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:02:44.122 --\u003e 00:02:46.667\r\nYes, of course.\r\nI'll leave immediately.\r\n\r\n00:02:47.000 --\u003e 00:02:48.460\r\nNow what?\r\n\r\n00:02:51.088 --\u003e 00:02:52.255\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:04.893 --\u003e 00:03:06.937\r\nDICK: Hey,\r\nwas a butlers' strike called?\r\n\r\n00:03:07.229 --\u003e 00:03:09.856\r\nI came down for breakfast,\r\nand all I found was this.\r\n\r\n00:03:10.190 --\u003e 00:03:11.400\r\nWhere's Alfred?\r\n\r\n00:03:13.235 --\u003e 00:03:16.154\r\n\"Dear Master Bruce,\r\nmy apologies for leaving so abruptly.\r\n\r\n00:03:16.238 --\u003e 00:03:19.241\r\n\"I've just learned of a personal\r\nmatter involving a cousin of mine\"\r\n\r\n00:03:19.324 --\u003e 00:03:21.118\r\n\"that must be\r\nresolved immediately.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:21.201 --\u003e 00:03:23.829\r\n\"I shall endeavor to\r\nreturn in a few days.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:23.995 --\u003e 00:03:25.622\r\n\"Your obedient servant, Alfred.\"\r\n\r\n00:03:25.997 --\u003e 00:03:27.332\r\nMust be pretty important.\r\n\r\n00:03:28.041 --\u003e 00:03:29.721\r\nAlfred wouldn't leave\r\na dirty dish unwashed\r\n\r\n00:03:29.751 --\u003e 00:03:31.420\r\nif England were\r\nsinking into the sea.\r\n\r\n00:03:31.837 --\u003e 00:03:33.046\r\nI know.\r\n\r\n00:03:49.271 --\u003e 00:03:52.524\r\n- Frederick?\r\n- Hello. Is that Alfie?\r\n\r\n00:03:52.607 --\u003e 00:03:55.360\r\n- Mr. Pennyworth will do.\r\n- Right then.\r\n\r\n00:03:55.861 --\u003e 00:03:59.114\r\nIt's Freddie sent us.\r\nWants you to come with us.\r\n\r\n00:03:59.614 --\u003e 00:04:02.951\r\n- Frederick sent you?\r\n- That's right, old love. Come along now.\r\n\r\n00:04:03.118 --\u003e 00:04:05.579\r\n- We'll pop around and see him.\r\n- I think not.\r\n\r\n00:04:06.121 --\u003e 00:04:09.791\r\nFrederick knows I hate being called\r\nAlfie as much as he hates Freddie.\r\n\r\n00:04:10.542 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\n- What have you done with him?\r\n- Grab him, Bert.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.339 --\u003e 00:04:17.758\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:04:26.349 --\u003e 00:04:27.809\r\n(TELEPHONE RINGING)\r\n\r\n00:04:31.730 --\u003e 00:04:33.023\r\nHello?\r\n\r\n00:04:33.607 --\u003e 00:04:36.860\r\nGood evening, Master Bruce.\r\nI'm so sorry to have disturbed your rest.\r\n\r\n00:04:37.027 --\u003e 00:04:39.863\r\nAlfred. Are you all right?\r\nWhere are you?\r\n\r\n00:04:40.238 --\u003e 00:04:43.116\r\nI'm at the Yorkshire Arms\r\njust at the moment. In London.\r\n\r\n00:04:43.200 --\u003e 00:04:46.369\r\n- London, England?\r\n- There's only one, Master Bruce.\r\n\r\n00:04:46.787 --\u003e 00:04:49.164\r\nI seem to be in a bit\r\nof a sticky situation,\r\n\r\n00:04:49.331 --\u003e 00:04:50.971\r\n- and I was wondering\r\nif you- - (THUDDING)\r\n\r\n00:04:53.210 --\u003e 00:04:55.837\r\nCome along easy, gramps.\r\nWe don't want to hurt you.\r\n\r\n00:04:55.921 --\u003e 00:04:58.173\r\nI'm afraid I'll have\r\nto ring off now, sir.\r\n\r\n00:04:58.256 --\u003e 00:05:00.592\r\nIt seems I have\r\nunexpected guests.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.675 --\u003e 00:05:01.968\r\nAlfred, are you there?\r\n\r\n00:05:02.427 --\u003e 00:05:04.179\r\n- Alfred? Alfred!\r\n- (MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:05:11.561 --\u003e 00:05:14.648\r\nBefore he came to the States,\r\nAlfred did some work as an attache'\r\n\r\n00:05:14.815 --\u003e 00:05:16.274\r\nin the British\r\nSecurity Services.\r\n\r\n00:05:16.441 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nMore desk jobs than fieldwork,\r\nbut he acquired quite a reputation\r\n\r\n00:05:20.153 --\u003e 00:05:24.366\r\nfor defusing diplomatically dangerous\r\nsituations in high-security areas.\r\n\r\n00:05:24.533 --\u003e 00:05:26.409\r\nAnd I thought he was\r\njust a nice old guy\r\n\r\n00:05:26.618 --\u003e 00:05:28.498\r\nwho polished the silver\r\nand fixed me sandwiches.\r\n\r\n00:05:29.120 --\u003e 00:05:30.997\r\nHe's fixed more than\r\nthat in his time.\r\n\r\n00:05:32.249 --\u003e 00:05:34.626\r\nUnderneath Alfred's\r\nvery proper exterior\r\n\r\n00:05:34.709 --\u003e 00:05:36.962\r\nis a highly resourceful\r\ngovernment agent.\r\n\r\n00:05:37.754 --\u003e 00:05:39.214\r\nHe mentioned his cousin.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:41.675\r\nAs far as I know,\r\nhe has no living relatives.\r\n\r\n00:05:42.259 --\u003e 00:05:46.012\r\nAnd cousin can sometimes mean a fellow\r\nmember of an intelligence organization.\r\n\r\n00:05:46.805 --\u003e 00:05:48.765\r\nWell, I hear England's\r\nnice this time of year.\r\n\r\n00:05:49.724 --\u003e 00:05:51.434\r\n(POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:06:23.925 --\u003e 00:06:25.176\r\nEnd of the line, mate.\r\n\r\n00:06:26.469 --\u003e 00:06:28.096\r\nIt's good to see you\r\nagain, old man.\r\n\r\n00:06:28.346 --\u003e 00:06:30.307\r\nI'm sorry it has to be\r\nunder such circumstances.\r\n\r\n00:06:30.682 --\u003e 00:06:33.143\r\nExactly what circumstances\r\nare we talking about?\r\n\r\n00:06:33.727 --\u003e 00:06:35.770\r\nMy heavens! Red Claw.\r\n\r\n00:06:36.146 --\u003e 00:06:39.274\r\nSo pleased to make your\r\nacquaintance, Mr. Pennyworth.\r\n\r\n00:06:39.399 --\u003e 00:06:43.486\r\nIf you do exactly as I say,\r\nyou might live to see tomorrow.\r\n\r\n00:06:54.456 --\u003e 00:06:57.208\r\nBruce, over here.\r\nLooks like he put up a struggle.\r\n\r\n00:06:58.126 --\u003e 00:06:59.726\r\nPoor Alfred.\r\nHe must have been petrified.\r\n\r\n00:07:00.295 --\u003e 00:07:01.296\r\nI doubt it.\r\n\r\n00:07:01.546 --\u003e 00:07:03.423\r\nHe was pretty\r\nformidable in his day.\r\n\r\n00:07:03.965 --\u003e 00:07:05.216\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:07:10.388 --\u003e 00:07:12.807\r\nTwo blokes just came out\r\nof Pennyworth's room.\r\n\r\n00:07:14.726 --\u003e 00:07:15.769\r\nRight.\r\n\r\n00:07:19.940 --\u003e 00:07:21.066\r\nWhere they off to, then?\r\n\r\n00:07:22.400 --\u003e 00:07:24.027\r\nI don't know about this, Ernie.\r\n\r\n00:07:25.779 --\u003e 00:07:28.531\r\n- Where'd they go?\r\n- We're chasing a pair of poxy ghosts.\r\n\r\n00:07:29.449 --\u003e 00:07:30.450\r\n(BOTH YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:07:32.035 --\u003e 00:07:33.328\r\nStone the crows!\r\n\r\n00:07:36.706 --\u003e 00:07:37.832\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:07:46.758 --\u003e 00:07:47.926\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:07:48.593 --\u003e 00:07:49.761\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:07:55.767 --\u003e 00:07:56.893\r\n(STRAINING)\r\n\r\n00:08:01.106 --\u003e 00:08:02.691\r\n- Gotcha.\r\n- (GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:08:03.274 --\u003e 00:08:05.568\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n- May I see your license?\r\n\r\n00:08:07.112 --\u003e 00:08:08.279\r\n(TIRES SCREECHING)\r\n\r\n00:08:14.744 --\u003e 00:08:15.787\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:28.008 --\u003e 00:08:30.427\r\nWhen they wake up,\r\nthey'll tell us who they're working for.\r\n\r\n00:08:32.804 --\u003e 00:08:34.484\r\nI don't think we'll\r\nhave to wait that long.\r\n\r\n00:08:35.223 --\u003e 00:08:36.474\r\nBATMAN: Red Claw.\r\n\r\n00:08:37.851 --\u003e 00:08:40.729\r\n\u003ci\u003eRED CLAW: I've wasted\r\nenough courtesy on you two.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:08:41.271 --\u003e 00:08:43.481\r\nCourtesy? None that I've seen.\r\n\r\n00:08:43.815 --\u003e 00:08:44.816\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:08:44.899 --\u003e 00:08:47.193\r\nI want this missile\r\nsilo operational.\r\n\r\n00:08:47.652 --\u003e 00:08:51.197\r\nI intend for the British\r\ngovernment to give me £5 billion\r\n\r\n00:08:51.406 --\u003e 00:08:54.117\r\nto keep me from wiping\r\nLondon off the map.\r\n\r\n00:08:54.617 --\u003e 00:08:57.287\r\nYou understand, old man,\r\nI had no choice in the matter.\r\n\r\n00:08:57.662 --\u003e 00:08:59.289\r\nBut of course, dear boy.\r\n\r\n00:08:59.706 --\u003e 00:09:02.625\r\nEach of you holds half the\r\nfiring code for this missile.\r\n\r\n00:09:03.001 --\u003e 00:09:05.795\r\nI want that code. Or else.\r\n\r\n00:09:06.171 --\u003e 00:09:07.839\r\nMadam, impossible.\r\n\r\n00:09:08.089 --\u003e 00:09:11.301\r\nWe are both signatories to\r\nthe Official Secrets Act.\r\n\r\n00:09:11.384 --\u003e 00:09:13.720\r\nI've already thought of that.\r\n\r\n00:09:24.731 --\u003e 00:09:26.733\r\nStill no word from\r\nCastle Blairquhan.\r\n\r\n00:09:26.941 --\u003e 00:09:29.069\r\nOur post there has\r\nnever missed a check-in.\r\n\r\n00:09:29.402 --\u003e 00:09:32.739\r\nHere's more bad news.\r\nAgent Frederick has been listed missing.\r\n\r\n00:09:33.406 --\u003e 00:09:34.532\r\nI don't like this.\r\n\r\n00:09:34.699 --\u003e 00:09:37.619\r\nFrederick was part of the original\r\nsecurity team at Blairquhan.\r\n\r\n00:09:37.994 --\u003e 00:09:42.165\r\n- Him and that fellow from Clerical.\r\n- BATMAN: Pennyworth, Alfred Pennyworth.\r\n\r\n00:09:42.415 --\u003e 00:09:44.125\r\nOur apologies for intruding.\r\n\r\n00:09:44.209 --\u003e 00:09:45.877\r\nYou were saying\r\nsomething about a castle?\r\n\r\n00:09:46.086 --\u003e 00:09:47.712\r\nHow did you get in here?\r\n\r\n00:09:48.254 --\u003e 00:09:51.466\r\nWe don't have time for protocol.\r\nPennyworth is also missing.\r\n\r\n00:09:52.050 --\u003e 00:09:55.136\r\nWe have reason to think he and Frederick\r\nmight be in considerable danger.\r\n\r\n00:09:55.678 --\u003e 00:09:57.180\r\nWhat was the name\r\nof that castle?\r\n\r\n00:09:57.263 --\u003e 00:09:59.766\r\nAnd why should we give\r\nyou that information?\r\n\r\n00:10:00.183 --\u003e 00:10:02.560\r\nBecause I can give you Red Claw.\r\n\r\n00:10:07.732 --\u003e 00:10:11.694\r\nBlairquhan. Castle Blairquhan\r\non the west Scottish coast.\r\n\r\n00:10:12.195 --\u003e 00:10:14.405\r\nIt was the base for\r\nProject Excalibur.\r\n\r\n00:10:14.739 --\u003e 00:10:17.408\r\nBlairquhan is the last of\r\nour land-based missile silos.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.034 --\u003e 00:10:20.495\r\nDo you think that's\r\nwhat Red Claw is after?\r\n\r\n00:10:21.621 --\u003e 00:10:22.789\r\nM3: Apparently so.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.833 --\u003e 00:10:26.084\r\nTruth serum?\r\n\r\n00:10:26.501 --\u003e 00:10:30.130\r\nOf course. The old methods\r\nare still often the best.\r\n\r\n00:10:30.797 --\u003e 00:10:32.197\r\n- Fight it if you like.\r\n- (GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:10:32.257 --\u003e 00:10:34.384\r\nYou won't hold out for long.\r\n\r\n00:10:34.467 --\u003e 00:10:36.469\r\nBut it might be amusing.\r\n(COCKS GUN)\r\n\r\n00:10:37.720 --\u003e 00:10:39.722\r\nWell, anything to amuse a lady.\r\n\r\n00:10:39.889 --\u003e 00:10:43.268\r\nIf lady is the word I\r\nwant, which I doubt.\r\n\r\n00:10:43.726 --\u003e 00:10:45.854\r\nAw, sticks and stones.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.021 --\u003e 00:10:48.857\r\n- (FIRES GUN)\r\n- (GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:04.080 --\u003e 00:11:06.958\r\nWon't... I... I won't.\r\n\r\n00:11:07.375 --\u003e 00:11:11.254\r\nGive me your access code\r\nfor the missile activator.\r\n\r\n00:11:11.546 --\u003e 00:11:12.547\r\nNever.\r\n\r\n00:11:13.006 --\u003e 00:11:15.466\r\nYou'll get nothing but\r\ngibberish out of me, madam.\r\n\r\n00:11:15.800 --\u003e 00:11:19.679\r\nI come from haunts of coot and fern.\r\nI make a sudden sally.\r\n\r\n00:11:20.221 --\u003e 00:11:21.806\r\n(SCATTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:21.890 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nAnd bicker down the valley.\r\n\r\n00:11:24.142 --\u003e 00:11:27.812\r\nAnd people wonder why no one\r\ntakes Britain seriously anymore.\r\n\r\n00:11:28.271 --\u003e 00:11:30.648\r\nThe code, old man. Now.\r\n\r\n00:11:31.191 --\u003e 00:11:32.984\r\nFourteen...\r\n\r\n00:11:33.818 --\u003e 00:11:39.991\r\n14 Gurrier's Crescent,\r\nBlairquhan Upper.\r\n\r\n00:11:43.244 --\u003e 00:11:48.291\r\nAbsurdly simple like most passwords.\r\nNow, as for you.\r\n\r\n00:11:48.791 --\u003e 00:11:52.921\r\n(WEAKLY) \"Half a league, half a\r\nleague, half a league onward...\"\r\n\r\n00:11:53.463 --\u003e 00:11:57.050\r\nDesperate valor to the last.\r\nNot that it will help you.\r\n\r\n00:11:57.967 --\u003e 00:12:01.221\r\nSooner or later,\r\nthe serum always wins.\r\n\r\n00:12:01.387 --\u003e 00:12:02.639\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:12:15.360 --\u003e 00:12:16.569\r\n(GUN COCKING)\r\n\r\n00:12:16.653 --\u003e 00:12:17.695\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:22.784 --\u003e 00:12:23.785\r\n(SHUSHING)\r\n\r\n00:12:25.411 --\u003e 00:12:26.412\r\n(YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:12:37.882 --\u003e 00:12:39.342\r\nROBIN: Looks clear.\r\n\r\n00:12:55.775 --\u003e 00:12:56.776\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:12:57.068 --\u003e 00:12:58.069\r\n(MAN GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:13:04.701 --\u003e 00:13:07.578\r\nImpossible!\r\nHow could he have learned about this?\r\n\r\n00:13:09.706 --\u003e 00:13:11.082\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:13:47.327 --\u003e 00:13:48.369\r\n(CHUCKLES)\r\n\r\n00:14:17.106 --\u003e 00:14:20.485\r\n- That's one less thing to worry about.\r\n- (SCOFFS) Two less things.\r\n\r\n00:14:20.860 --\u003e 00:14:24.197\r\n- Dennis, you're always the humorist.\r\n- Did you hear that?\r\n\r\n00:14:25.365 --\u003e 00:14:26.657\r\n(BOTH YELL)\r\n\r\n00:14:34.791 --\u003e 00:14:36.084\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:14:41.714 --\u003e 00:14:46.219\r\n\u003ci\u003eLondoners. Your ancient city may\r\npride itself on having survived\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:46.469 --\u003e 00:14:48.971\r\n\u003ci\u003eplagues, fires, even the Blitz.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:49.514 --\u003e 00:14:54.268\r\n\u003ci\u003eBut unless £5 billion are delivered\r\nto me by midnight tonight,\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:54.519 --\u003e 00:14:56.813\r\n\u003ci\u003ethere will be nothing\r\nleft to survive.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:14:57.105 --\u003e 00:15:00.900\r\n\u003ci\u003eWe have Blairquhan Castle\r\nand its missile installation\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:01.317 --\u003e 00:15:03.986\r\nand the codes to\r\noperate the missile.\r\n\r\n00:15:04.654 --\u003e 00:15:06.948\r\n\u003ci\u003eYou have one hour.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:07.240 --\u003e 00:15:09.659\r\n\u003ci\u003eOtherwise,\r\nI'll be forced to plant this warhead\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:09.742 --\u003e 00:15:11.869\r\n\u003ci\u003ein the middle of\r\nTrafalgar Square.\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:12.662 --\u003e 00:15:15.289\r\n\u003ci\u003eAnd if! Do that, well...\r\n(CHUCKLES)\u003c/i\u003e\r\n\r\n00:15:15.873 --\u003e 00:15:18.292\r\nGod save the queen.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.044 --\u003e 00:15:23.714\r\nIs it smart to make demands before\r\nwe get the other half of the go code?\r\n\r\n00:15:23.923 --\u003e 00:15:26.217\r\nI will have the code\r\nin a matter of minutes.\r\n\r\n00:15:26.509 --\u003e 00:15:27.760\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:15:33.766 --\u003e 00:15:35.143\r\n(SHRIEKS)\r\n\r\n00:15:43.526 --\u003e 00:15:46.487\r\nGive me the code, or I'll-\r\n\r\n00:15:46.654 --\u003e 00:15:51.492\r\nThe lion and the unicorn\r\nfighting for the crown.\r\n\r\n00:15:53.161 --\u003e 00:15:56.873\r\nHe can't be resisting the drug this long.\r\nIt's impossible.\r\n\r\n00:15:57.748 --\u003e 00:16:00.751\r\n- The lion and the unicorn fighting...\r\n- Wait. He's not resisting.\r\n\r\n00:16:01.002 --\u003e 00:16:02.962\r\nThis doggerel is the code.\r\n\r\n00:16:04.422 --\u003e 00:16:07.175\r\n\"The lion and the unicorn\".\r\n\r\n00:16:12.346 --\u003e 00:16:13.556\r\nAt last!\r\n\r\n00:16:24.275 --\u003e 00:16:25.568\r\n(KNOCK AT DOOR)\r\n\r\n00:16:31.282 --\u003e 00:16:32.283\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:16:32.408 --\u003e 00:16:33.910\r\n(GROANING)\r\n\r\n00:16:35.661 --\u003e 00:16:37.413\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:16:42.418 --\u003e 00:16:43.419\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:16:45.171 --\u003e 00:16:46.589\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:51.677 --\u003e 00:16:53.095\r\nYou three, come with me.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.930 --\u003e 00:16:55.139\r\nWatch them.\r\n\r\n00:16:55.348 --\u003e 00:16:56.849\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:16:57.892 --\u003e 00:17:00.686\r\nFan out. This is the only\r\naccess to the control room.\r\n\r\n00:17:00.770 --\u003e 00:17:03.022\r\nThey'll have to\r\ncome through here.\r\n\r\n00:17:07.860 --\u003e 00:17:08.861\r\n(MAN YELLING)\r\n\r\n00:17:10.071 --\u003e 00:17:11.155\r\nTake them.\r\n\r\n00:17:21.874 --\u003e 00:17:22.875\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:17:23.209 --\u003e 00:17:24.252\r\n(GUNSHOTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:25.711 --\u003e 00:17:26.712\r\n(GUN CLICKING)\r\n\r\n00:17:38.015 --\u003e 00:17:39.183\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:17:39.600 --\u003e 00:17:41.644\r\nAnd here I thought all\r\nyou dusted was furniture.\r\n\r\n00:17:42.103 --\u003e 00:17:44.855\r\nA Louis Quinze. What a pity.\r\n\r\n00:17:50.152 --\u003e 00:17:51.654\r\nGoodness me.\r\n\r\n00:17:56.701 --\u003e 00:17:58.494\r\n(TIMER BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:18:11.507 --\u003e 00:18:13.259\r\n(ALARM BLARING)\r\n\r\n00:18:35.573 --\u003e 00:18:38.075\r\n- Dear Lord!\r\n- Do you two have the destruct code?\r\n\r\n00:18:38.159 --\u003e 00:18:39.452\r\n(BEEPING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:18:42.663 --\u003e 00:18:44.206\r\n(POWERING UP)\r\n\r\n00:19:19.241 --\u003e 00:19:20.284\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:19:21.952 --\u003e 00:19:23.287\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:19:40.096 --\u003e 00:19:41.097\r\n(YELLS)\r\n\r\n00:20:07.123 --\u003e 00:20:08.499\r\n(BEEPING)\r\n\r\n00:20:29.937 --\u003e 00:20:33.232\r\nI don't suppose you'd consider\r\ncoming out of retirement?\r\n\r\n00:20:33.315 --\u003e 00:20:36.026\r\nAnd taking up civil\r\nservice pay grades again?\r\n\r\n00:20:36.110 --\u003e 00:20:39.947\r\nHardly, old man. I've become\r\naccustomed to my style of living.\r\n\r\n00:20:40.030 --\u003e 00:20:43.409\r\nIt's a great pity.\r\nIt was just like old times.\r\n\r\n00:20:43.868 --\u003e 00:20:45.453\r\nGive my best to Whitehall.\r\n\r\n00:20:55.755 --\u003e 00:20:57.757\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:22.406 --\u003e 00:21:23.407\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E01 - Holiday Knights (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E02 - Sins of The Father (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E03 - Cold Comfort (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E04 - Never Fear (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E05 - You Scratch My Back (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E06 - Double Talk (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E07 - Joker's Millions (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E08 - Growing Pains (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E09 - Mean Seasons (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E10 - The Demon Within (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E11 - Over the Edge (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E12 - Torch Song (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S01 E13 - Love is a Croc (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E01 - The Ultimate Thrill (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E02 - Critters (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E03 - Cult of The Cat (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E04 - Animal Act (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E05 - Old Wounds (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E06 - Legends of The Dark Knight (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E07 - Girls Night Out (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E08 - Chemistry (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E09 - Judgement Day (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E10 - Beware The Creeper (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n", "dragon-ball-z-1989-2018-the-complete-uncut-series-16-dbz-movies-4-ovas-8-tv-spec::The New Batman Adventures - S02 E11 - Mad Love (1080p - BluRay).ia.mp4": "WEBVTT\r\n\r\n00:00:21.605 --\u003e 00:00:23.148\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:01:23.709 --\u003e 00:01:27.337\r\n- Hey, it's him.\r\n- Who, Mommy? Who?\r\n\r\n00:01:30.257 --\u003e 00:01:32.926\r\n- Mommy, who is it?\r\n- Why, that's Batman, honey.\r\n\r\n00:01:34.845 --\u003e 00:01:36.597\r\nUh, maybe it's not him.\r\n\r\n00:01:37.139 --\u003e 00:01:38.890\r\n(CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:40.267 --\u003e 00:01:44.354\r\nYahoo! (CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:01:45.606 --\u003e 00:01:47.899\r\n- What's his story?\r\n- Let's ask.\r\n\r\n00:02:03.790 --\u003e 00:02:05.751\r\nWhoo-hoo!\r\n\r\n00:02:06.877 --\u003e 00:02:08.003\r\nUh-oh!\r\n\r\n00:02:11.965 --\u003e 00:02:13.675\r\n(CONTINUES CACKLING)\r\n\r\n00:02:20.307 --\u003e 00:02:22.643\r\n(PEOPLE SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:02:52.130 --\u003e 00:02:54.091\r\n(SCREAMING CONTINUES)\r\n\r\n00:02:58.428 --\u003e 00:02:59.513\r\nMAN: They stopped it.\r\n\r\n00:03:00.514 --\u003e 00:03:01.640\r\n(SIGHS \u003ci\u003em\u003c/i\u003e RELIEF)\r\n\r\n00:03:02.182 --\u003e 00:03:03.725\r\n(LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:06.895 --\u003e 00:03:08.980\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:03:11.149 --\u003e 00:03:14.486\r\n- You okay?\r\n- Great. Never been better.\r\n\r\n00:03:14.569 --\u003e 00:03:19.825\r\nRight. Now, there's a window a few feet\r\nfrom here, and if you just follow me-\r\n\r\n00:03:19.908 --\u003e 00:03:22.119\r\nWindow? I'm not going in.\r\n\r\n00:03:22.202 --\u003e 00:03:24.579\r\nThis is gonna be the\r\nbest night of my life.\r\n\r\n00:03:24.663 --\u003e 00:03:27.207\r\n- It could also be the last.\r\n- Oh, come on.\r\n\r\n00:03:27.290 --\u003e 00:03:30.210\r\nThere's nothing to be afraid of.\r\nFear's a prison, you see,\r\n\r\n00:03:30.293 --\u003e 00:03:31.962\r\nand I've just broken out.\r\n\r\n00:03:32.045 --\u003e 00:03:34.297\r\n(SINGING)\r\n\r\n00:03:34.881 --\u003e 00:03:36.174\r\n- Tag!\r\n- (BATMAN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:03:37.050 --\u003e 00:03:38.635\r\nYOW!\r\n\r\n00:03:45.350 --\u003e 00:03:46.727\r\n(MAN LAUGHING)\r\n\r\n00:03:50.063 --\u003e 00:03:51.773\r\n(ALL CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:03:51.857 --\u003e 00:03:52.983\r\nMAN: That's awesome.\r\n\r\n00:03:56.153 --\u003e 00:03:57.612\r\nCome on.\r\n\r\n00:04:01.867 --\u003e 00:04:04.619\r\nGURU: And after that,\r\nBatman handed him over to the cops.\r\n\r\n00:04:04.953 --\u003e 00:04:06.747\r\nWasn't anything we could do.\r\n\r\n00:04:07.998 --\u003e 00:04:10.959\r\nSCARECROW: What's the use of\r\nproviding me with test patients\r\n\r\n00:04:11.042 --\u003e 00:04:13.128\r\nif you're going to lose them?\r\n\r\n00:04:13.211 --\u003e 00:04:15.922\r\nYou should have monitored\r\nhim more carefully.\r\n\r\n00:04:16.089 --\u003e 00:04:19.801\r\nWe... We tried, but we had no idea\r\nyour treatment would be that effective.\r\n\r\n00:04:19.885 --\u003e 00:04:23.305\r\nSCARECROW: All the more reason to keep\r\nthe subjects under close scrutiny.\r\n\r\n00:04:23.388 --\u003e 00:04:26.933\r\nWe don't want to give\r\nourselves away just yet. Do we?\r\n\r\n00:04:38.862 --\u003e 00:04:42.991\r\n- How was the inspection, Mr. Wayne?\r\n- Fine, Sara. Did I miss anything?\r\n\r\n00:04:43.074 --\u003e 00:04:45.869\r\nJust Seymour Grey.\r\nHe's been calling all morning.\r\n\r\n00:04:45.952 --\u003e 00:04:47.996\r\n- Who?\r\n- One of the clerks downstairs.\r\n\r\n00:04:48.079 --\u003e 00:04:50.707\r\nHe's sort of a quiet\r\nguy, usually.\r\n\r\n00:04:52.709 --\u003e 00:04:56.338\r\n- Oh, there's one more thing.\r\n- Let me guess.\r\n\r\n00:05:00.717 --\u003e 00:05:02.260\r\nPlaying hooky?\r\n\r\n00:05:03.386 --\u003e 00:05:05.263\r\nIt's summer vacation.\r\n\r\n00:05:06.932 --\u003e 00:05:08.308\r\nHow do you forget that?\r\n\r\n00:05:11.394 --\u003e 00:05:13.605\r\nNever mind.\r\nI forgot who I was talking to.\r\n\r\n00:05:13.688 --\u003e 00:05:15.690\r\nSo, what have you heard\r\nabout our Tarzan guy?\r\n\r\n00:05:15.774 --\u003e 00:05:17.442\r\nStill unconscious.\r\n\r\n00:05:17.526 --\u003e 00:05:19.986\r\nBut the police found out\r\nsomething interesting about him.\r\n\r\n00:05:20.070 --\u003e 00:05:21.655\r\nHe had acrophobia.\r\n\r\n00:05:21.738 --\u003e 00:05:23.198\r\nOh...\r\n\r\n00:05:23.406 --\u003e 00:05:26.993\r\n- It means fear of heights.\r\n- No joke? Then why-\r\n\r\n00:05:27.077 --\u003e 00:05:30.288\r\nYou can't put me off any longer, Wayne!\r\nI've got ideas!\r\n\r\n00:05:30.372 --\u003e 00:05:34.251\r\nIdeas that are going to\r\nrevolutionize cost accounting.\r\n\r\n00:05:34.334 --\u003e 00:05:36.086\r\nMr. Grey, I presume.\r\n\r\n00:05:36.211 --\u003e 00:05:39.589\r\nYeah, that's me,\r\nmousy Seymour Grey.\r\n\r\n00:05:39.673 --\u003e 00:05:43.426\r\nBeen sitting at the same desk 18\r\nyears, afraid to say anything.\r\n\r\n00:05:43.510 --\u003e 00:05:45.262\r\nAfraid of losing my job.\r\n\r\n00:05:45.345 --\u003e 00:05:48.181\r\nMr. Wayne, I'm so sorry.\r\nI've called security.\r\n\r\n00:05:48.265 --\u003e 00:05:52.352\r\nIt's all right, Sara.\r\nMr. Grey, now's not really the time.\r\n\r\n00:05:52.435 --\u003e 00:05:54.437\r\nOh, gonna try to intimidate\r\nme, huh?\r\n\r\n00:05:54.521 --\u003e 00:05:59.067\r\nWell, if you think I'm just gonna\r\ncrawl back to my desk, you're wrong.\r\n\r\n00:05:59.150 --\u003e 00:06:01.444\r\n'Cause I quit!\r\n\r\n00:06:06.533 --\u003e 00:06:08.326\r\nAnd one more thing.\r\n\r\n00:06:10.328 --\u003e 00:06:11.621\r\n(SARA GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:06:11.746 --\u003e 00:06:14.499\r\n(SARA GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:06:14.749 --\u003e 00:06:16.459\r\nMr. Grey!\r\n\r\n00:06:17.127 --\u003e 00:06:19.504\r\nI'm in the phone book, baby.\r\n\r\n00:06:33.935 --\u003e 00:06:38.064\r\nGURU: It paralyzes us,\r\nkeeps us from getting what we want.\r\n\r\n00:06:38.732 --\u003e 00:06:42.777\r\nKeeps us from experiencing\r\nlife to the fullest.\r\n\r\n00:06:42.861 --\u003e 00:06:47.949\r\nThat's what fear does.\r\nNow, how many of you\r\n\r\n00:06:48.033 --\u003e 00:06:51.828\r\nwant to banish it from your lives?\r\nAbandon it?\r\n\r\n00:06:52.078 --\u003e 00:06:54.080\r\n- Root it out of your psyches?\r\n- (CROWD CHEERING)\r\n\r\n00:07:07.677 --\u003e 00:07:08.803\r\n(YAWNS)\r\n\r\n00:07:08.887 --\u003e 00:07:11.890\r\nGURU: Well, folks,\r\nI can help you forget about your fear\r\n\r\n00:07:11.973 --\u003e 00:07:14.768\r\nand find the\r\nhappiness you deserve.\r\n\r\n00:07:42.921 --\u003e 00:07:44.381\r\n(BRUCE GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:08:19.207 --\u003e 00:08:20.625\r\n(GROWLS)\r\n\r\n00:08:21.543 --\u003e 00:08:23.336\r\nSCARECROW: Terrifying,\r\naren't they?\r\n\r\n00:08:26.631 --\u003e 00:08:29.592\r\n- What's going on?\r\n- That's what I'd like to know.\r\n\r\n00:08:29.676 --\u003e 00:08:31.886\r\nWho are you?\r\nWhy were you snooping around?\r\n\r\n00:08:31.970 --\u003e 00:08:35.932\r\nEasy, easy. I was just\r\nlooking for some loose cash.\r\n\r\n00:08:36.016 --\u003e 00:08:38.768\r\nI wasn't trying to move\r\nin on your operation.\r\n\r\n00:08:38.852 --\u003e 00:08:41.604\r\n- Whatever it is.\r\n- A thief.\r\n\r\n00:08:42.022 --\u003e 00:08:44.399\r\n- I thought as much.\r\n- Hey, be cool.\r\n\r\n00:08:46.443 --\u003e 00:08:48.862\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:08:48.945 --\u003e 00:08:50.530\r\nScared you, didn't I?\r\n\r\n00:09:02.250 --\u003e 00:09:04.377\r\nThey don't seem so frightening\r\nnow, do they?\r\n\r\n00:09:08.631 --\u003e 00:09:12.052\r\nThat's it, tough guy.\r\nCome and get me.\r\n\r\n00:09:27.192 --\u003e 00:09:29.319\r\nWelcome to the food chain.\r\n\r\n00:09:36.951 --\u003e 00:09:38.453\r\n(GASPING)\r\n\r\n00:09:50.507 --\u003e 00:09:53.384\r\n- What's taking him?\r\n- Could be any number of things.\r\n\r\n00:09:53.468 --\u003e 00:09:55.178\r\nInvestigations require time.\r\n\r\n00:10:01.601 --\u003e 00:10:03.561\r\nSuit up and get in the plane.\r\n\r\n00:10:10.693 --\u003e 00:10:13.404\r\n- You gonna tell me what's going on?\r\n- It's the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:10:13.488 --\u003e 00:10:16.074\r\nHe's developed a gas that\r\ntakes away people's fear.\r\n\r\n00:10:16.157 --\u003e 00:10:18.118\r\nNo more fear? Cool.\r\n\r\n00:10:18.576 --\u003e 00:10:21.996\r\nThe man on the ledge last night.\r\nThe one at my office.\r\n\r\n00:10:22.080 --\u003e 00:10:23.540\r\nImagine a whole city like that.\r\n\r\n00:10:24.582 --\u003e 00:10:26.042\r\nI see your point.\r\n\r\n00:10:28.586 --\u003e 00:10:29.671\r\nHey!\r\n\r\n00:10:44.227 --\u003e 00:10:45.353\r\nOoh.\r\n\r\n00:10:47.313 --\u003e 00:10:48.940\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:11:03.913 --\u003e 00:11:04.998\r\n(ROBIN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:11:09.794 --\u003e 00:11:13.882\r\nThis gas that takes away your fear,\r\nby any chance, did you breathe it?\r\n\r\n00:11:13.965 --\u003e 00:11:16.384\r\nYes, but I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:11:17.051 --\u003e 00:11:18.428\r\n(GRUNTS)\r\n\r\n00:11:22.182 --\u003e 00:11:23.600\r\nOh! Yeah?\r\n\r\n00:11:52.337 --\u003e 00:11:54.464\r\nThe gas canisters are in here.\r\n\r\n00:11:58.593 --\u003e 00:12:01.596\r\n- Here today, gone tonight.\r\n- (GUN COCKS)\r\n\r\n00:12:02.805 --\u003e 00:12:04.724\r\nIf I were you, I wouldn't move.\r\n\r\n00:12:05.099 --\u003e 00:12:06.601\r\nYou're not me.\r\n\r\n00:12:07.393 --\u003e 00:12:08.394\r\nBatman!\r\n\r\n00:12:15.652 --\u003e 00:12:16.945\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:24.786 --\u003e 00:12:26.079\r\nShoot him.\r\n\r\n00:12:27.080 --\u003e 00:12:28.373\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:12:33.253 --\u003e 00:12:34.545\r\nGet the gun.\r\n\r\n00:12:35.588 --\u003e 00:12:37.340\r\nHey, come back.\r\n\r\n00:12:41.803 --\u003e 00:12:43.304\r\nWhoa! Ahh!\r\n\r\n00:12:49.352 --\u003e 00:12:52.480\r\n- Where's the gas?\r\n- Go ahead. Throw me in jail.\r\n\r\n00:12:52.563 --\u003e 00:12:53.815\r\nIt won't do you any good.\r\n\r\n00:12:54.941 --\u003e 00:12:57.151\r\nWho said anything about jail?\r\n\r\n00:13:16.713 --\u003e 00:13:18.256\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:13:21.676 --\u003e 00:13:23.761\r\n- Batman!\r\n- Quiet.\r\n\r\n00:13:24.929 --\u003e 00:13:26.889\r\n(WHIMPERING)\r\n\r\n00:13:28.683 --\u003e 00:13:30.018\r\nHelp!\r\n\r\n00:13:36.232 --\u003e 00:13:37.442\r\n(GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:13:37.525 --\u003e 00:13:39.777\r\nYou didn't answer my question.\r\n\r\n00:13:40.361 --\u003e 00:13:42.613\r\nI CAN'T. HE'LL KILL ME.\r\n\r\n00:13:42.697 --\u003e 00:13:45.658\r\nDeath is death.\r\nDoes it matter who administers it?\r\n\r\n00:13:48.119 --\u003e 00:13:49.495\r\nYou're not really gonna...\r\n\r\n00:13:49.620 --\u003e 00:13:52.707\r\nNo.No! No!\r\n\r\n00:13:52.790 --\u003e 00:13:54.208\r\nMy question, remember?\r\n\r\n00:13:55.543 --\u003e 00:13:59.088\r\nHe took the gas down to the\r\n72nd Street subway station.\r\n\r\n00:13:59.172 --\u003e 00:14:01.466\r\n- Why?\r\n- He's gonna fill the tunnels with it.\r\n\r\n00:14:01.549 --\u003e 00:14:03.509\r\nJust in time for rush hour.\r\n\r\n00:14:05.553 --\u003e 00:14:08.181\r\nHelp me. Please!\r\n\r\n00:14:08.264 --\u003e 00:14:10.016\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:14:16.689 --\u003e 00:14:18.358\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:14:29.118 --\u003e 00:14:30.620\r\n(YELP$)\r\n\r\n00:14:49.472 --\u003e 00:14:52.767\r\nThis isn't the time for games.\r\nNow, untie me.\r\n\r\n00:14:52.850 --\u003e 00:14:55.144\r\nIt's no game.\r\nYou're out of control.\r\n\r\n00:14:55.269 --\u003e 00:14:56.869\r\nYou don't know what\r\nyou're talking about.\r\n\r\n00:14:57.063 --\u003e 00:14:59.190\r\nThat gas has affected\r\nyou more than you think.\r\n\r\n00:14:59.399 --\u003e 00:15:01.484\r\nI told you, I can handle it.\r\n\r\n00:15:01.734 --\u003e 00:15:04.445\r\nYou can't.\r\nYou're not even afraid to kill.\r\n\r\n00:15:05.113 --\u003e 00:15:06.989\r\nI'll be back for you\r\nas soon as I can.\r\n\r\n00:15:08.449 --\u003e 00:15:14.205\r\nRobin, it's hard for me to say\r\nthis, but you did the right thing.\r\n\r\n00:15:14.997 --\u003e 00:15:18.543\r\nI was out of control,\r\nand you've made me see that.\r\n\r\n00:15:18.626 --\u003e 00:15:19.877\r\nI did what I had to.\r\n\r\n00:15:20.420 --\u003e 00:15:22.880\r\n- What now?\r\n- I've got to stop the Scarecrow.\r\n\r\n00:15:22.964 --\u003e 00:15:25.633\r\n- I can help you. I know him.\r\n- But-\r\n\r\n00:15:25.716 --\u003e 00:15:28.386\r\nDon't worry,\r\nyou'll be the boss on this one.\r\n\r\n00:15:37.854 --\u003e 00:15:39.689\r\nYou almost fooled me.\r\n\r\n00:15:41.691 --\u003e 00:15:44.861\r\nUntie me, you little...\r\nUntie me!\r\n\r\n00:15:46.070 --\u003e 00:15:47.822\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:15:54.787 --\u003e 00:15:57.498\r\nMAN 1: Hurry up with that stuff.\r\nMAN 2: We're coming.\r\n\r\n00:15:59.667 --\u003e 00:16:01.252\r\n(MEN GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:12.638 --\u003e 00:16:14.599\r\nThis message is for the mayor.\r\n\r\n00:16:14.682 --\u003e 00:16:17.643\r\nYou'll soon see what Gotham\r\nCity will be like without fear.\r\n\r\n00:16:18.269 --\u003e 00:16:19.562\r\nAnd it won't be pretty.\r\n\r\n00:16:20.271 --\u003e 00:16:21.939\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:16:26.652 --\u003e 00:16:29.947\r\nFear is the glue that\r\nholds society together.\r\n\r\n00:16:30.031 --\u003e 00:16:33.409\r\nIt's what makes people\r\nsuppress their worst impulses.\r\n\r\n00:16:33.910 --\u003e 00:16:36.204\r\nFear is power.\r\n\r\n00:16:36.412 --\u003e 00:16:38.623\r\nAnd today,\r\nit will also be quite expensive\r\n\r\n00:16:38.706 --\u003e 00:16:41.209\r\nif you want the antidote.\r\n\r\n00:16:46.339 --\u003e 00:16:48.007\r\n(SCARECROW GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:48.299 --\u003e 00:16:51.636\r\nYou're not getting anything from\r\nanyone, except this.\r\n\r\n00:16:53.137 --\u003e 00:16:54.388\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:16:54.472 --\u003e 00:16:56.307\r\nGet him off me.\r\n\r\n00:16:59.101 --\u003e 00:17:02.563\r\n- What do we do now?\r\n- Leave, before his partner shows up.\r\n\r\n00:17:24.585 --\u003e 00:17:27.505\r\n(BOTH GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:00.037 --\u003e 00:18:01.664\r\nBetter odds, yeah?\r\n\r\n00:18:05.793 --\u003e 00:18:06.836\r\n(GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:18:08.838 --\u003e 00:18:10.214\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:15.803 --\u003e 00:18:17.263\r\n(SCREAMING)\r\n\r\n00:18:21.225 --\u003e 00:18:23.102\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:18:32.028 --\u003e 00:18:33.195\r\n(SCARECROW GASPS)\r\n\r\n00:18:33.279 --\u003e 00:18:34.989\r\nDon't do it.\r\n\r\n00:18:40.286 --\u003e 00:18:41.871\r\n(HORN HONKING)\r\n\r\n00:18:49.170 --\u003e 00:18:51.255\r\nFool. You'll get us killed.\r\n\r\n00:18:51.714 --\u003e 00:18:53.466\r\nYou're not trying to scare\r\nme, are you?\r\n\r\n00:19:00.264 --\u003e 00:19:01.724\r\nHiyah!\r\n\r\n00:19:01.891 --\u003e 00:19:03.517\r\nOw!\r\n\r\n00:19:06.812 --\u003e 00:19:09.023\r\n- You can't!\r\n- Watch me.\r\n\r\n00:19:09.106 --\u003e 00:19:10.858\r\n(ROBIN GROANS)\r\n\r\n00:19:13.903 --\u003e 00:19:15.529\r\n(CHOKING)\r\n\r\n00:19:18.908 --\u003e 00:19:20.242\r\n(couemue)\r\n\r\n00:19:35.508 --\u003e 00:19:38.052\r\nI can't stop it.\r\nYou're gonna have to jump.\r\n\r\n00:19:38.386 --\u003e 00:19:40.596\r\n- What about Scarecrow?\r\n- I'll take care of him.\r\n\r\n00:19:42.014 --\u003e 00:19:43.516\r\nI'll get him off the train.\r\n\r\n00:19:49.980 --\u003e 00:19:52.942\r\n(GRUNTING)\r\n\r\n00:20:24.306 --\u003e 00:20:27.685\r\nUm, last night when I tied you\r\nup, I didn't mean-\r\n\r\n00:20:27.768 --\u003e 00:20:30.271\r\nDon't apologize. You were right.\r\n\r\n00:20:30.354 --\u003e 00:20:32.606\r\nYeah, but it was kind of scary.\r\n\r\n00:20:33.023 --\u003e 00:20:34.692\r\nA little fear's a good thing.\r\n\r\n00:20:47.288 --\u003e 00:20:49.623\r\n(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)\r\n\r\n00:21:13.898 --\u003e 00:21:14.899\r\nEnglish - SDH\r\n"};
